(1288,'biology',100,551,1105,'The testes in humans are situated outside the abdominal cavity inside a pouch called scrotum. The purpose served is for<br>','[{"text": "Maintaining the scrotal temperature lower than the internal body temperature<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Escaping any possible compression by the visceral organs<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Providing more space for the growth of epididymis<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Providing a secondary sexual feature for exhibiting the male sex", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The testis are situated outside the abdominal cavity with in a pouch scrotum. It helps in maintaining the low temperature (2$2.5^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ ) which is necessary for spermatogenesis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1289,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Following is the data of four species $\\left(\\mathrm{S}_{1}-\\mathrm{S}_{4}\\right)$, present (+) or absent (-) in 5 different habitats $(\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{S}$ and $\\mathrm{T})$. Which species has the maximum diversity?<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{}&{\\rm{P}}&{\\rm{Q}}&{\\rm{R}}&{\\rm{S}}&{\\rm{T}}\\\\\n{{{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{1}}}}&{\\rm{ + }}&{\\rm{ - }}&{\\rm{ + }}&{\\rm{ + }}&{\\rm{ + }}\\\\\n{{{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{2}}}}&{\\rm{ + }}&{\\rm{ + }}&{\\rm{ - }}&{\\rm{ - }}&{\\rm{ + }}\\\\\n{{{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{3}}}}&{\\rm{ + }}&{\\rm{ + }}&{\\rm{ + }}&{\\rm{ - }}&{\\rm{ - }}\\\\\n{{{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{4}}}}&{\\rm{ - }}&{\\rm{ + }}&{\\rm{ - }}&{\\rm{ - }}&{\\rm{ - }}\n\\end{array}$','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'According to the data given, ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{1}}}$ has maximum diversity as it covers 4 habitats.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1290,'biology',103,968,2255,'Select the correct answer<br>I. Time-lag between the infection and appearance of AIDS symptoms may vary from a few months to many years (usually 15-20 years).<br>II. The HIV virus replicates to form viral DNA with the help of the enzyme reverse transcriptase.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Incorrect statement I: There is always a time-lag between the infection and appearance of AIDS symptoms. This period may vary from a few months to many years (usually 5-10 years).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1291,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Lichens is an intimate mutualistic relationship between','[{"text": "Fungus and cyanobacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungus and photosynthetic algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungus and roots of higher plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mycorrhizae is an intimate mutualistic relationship between Fungus and roots of higher plants. Lichens are mutual association between fungus and cyanobacteria/photosynthetic algae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1292,'biology',100,554,1109,'The secretory phase in the human menstrual cycle is also called<br>','[{"text": "Luteal phase and lasts for about 6 days<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Follicular phase and lasts for about 6 days<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Luteal phase and lasts for about 13 days<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Follicular phase and lasts for about 13 days", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In the menstrual cycle, the secretory phase is often called as luteal phase because at this time the anterior pituitary starts the secretion of $\\mathrm{LH}$. This phase lasts for a period of 13 days.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1293,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Biosphere reserves differ from National parks and wildlife sanctuaries because in the former','[{"text": "Human beings are not allowed to enter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "People are an integral part of the system", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Plants are paid greater attention than the animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Living organisms are brought from all over the world and preserved for posterity", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Biosphere reserves differ from National parks and wildlife sanctuaries because in the former people are an integral part of the system.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1294,'biology',103,968,2255,'HIV patients can come in contact with oppurtunistic infection like','[{"text": "Mycobacterium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viruses, fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parasites like Toxoplasma.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Due to decrease in the number of helper $\\mathrm{T}$ lymphocytes, the person starts suffering from infections that could have been otherwise overcome such as those due to bacteria especially Mycobacterium, viruses, fungi and even parasites like Toxoplasma.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1295,'biology',100,556,1113,'In a normal pregnant woman, the amount of total gonadotropin activity was assessed. The result expected was<br>','[{"text": "High level of circulating FSH and LH in the uterus to stimulate implantation of the embryo<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "High level of circulating hCG to stimulate endometrial thickening<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "High levels of FSH and LH in uterus to stimulate endometrial thickening<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "High level of circulating hCG to stimulate estrogen and progesterone synthesis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The placenta acts as an endocrine gland. It secretes progesterone, estrogen and human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG). This hCG allows the corpus luteum to secrete huge amounts of progesterone to sustain the pregnancy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1296,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Mycorrhizae are association between','[{"text": "Fungus and photosynthetic algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungus and roots of Angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungus and roots of Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mycorrhizae are association between<br>(2) Fungus and roots of Angiosperms<br>(3) Fungus and roots of Gymnosperms',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1297,'biology',106,1354,3256,'What are the reasons for more species richness in the tropics when compared to temperate?<br>i. $\\quad$ Speciation Time more $\\rightarrow$ Tropical Undisturbed $\\rightarrow$ Longer Evolutionary $\\rightarrow$ Period Diversification of species<br>ii. Constant (less seasonal) $\\rightarrow$ Local species<br>$\\rightarrow$ Tend to survive, no migration<br>iii. Warm Temperature $\\rightarrow$ Humid Environment $\\rightarrow$ Favourable survival of the species.<br>iv. Solar Radiation $\\rightarrow$ Productivity more $\\rightarrow$ Higher species diversity','[{"text": "Statement ii and iii are only correct reasons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement i and ii are only correct reasons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement i, ii, iii and iv are only correct reasons", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement iii and iv are only correct reasons", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'All the reasons are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1298,'biology',103,968,2255,'Development of vaccine is difficult for AIDS because its gene','[{"text": "Undergoes mutation at rapid rate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Undergoes reverse transcription", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Integrates into large number of host genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Integrates its genome into that of helper cells", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'From the most fundamental standpoint, efforts to develop an HIV vaccine have been hampered by the genetic diversity of the virus itself. The replication cycle of HIV is not only fast (a little more than 24 hours) but is prone to frequent errors, churning out mutated copies of itself that recombine into new strains as the virus is passed from person to person. Developing a single vaccine able to eradicate over 60 dominant strains as well as the multitude of recombinant strainsand on a global level-becomes all the more challenging when conventional vaccines can only protect against a limited number of viral strains.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1299,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Nostoc keeps symbiotic relation:','[{"text": "With the root of Pinus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "With coralloid root of Cycas", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "With the root of leguminous plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Nostoc keeps symbiotic relation With coralloid root of Cycas.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1300,'biology',100,551,1105,'The leydig cells found in the human body are the secretory source of<br>','[{"text": "Progesterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intestinal mucus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucagon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Androgens", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The hormone $\\mathrm{LH}$ secreted from the anterior pituitary stimulate the leydig cells to secrete androgens.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1301,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Read the following statements and select the correct option<br>I. India has more than 50, 000 genetically diverse varieties of rice<br>II. Genetic variations within a species increases with increase in size and environmental parameters of the habitat<br>III. Habitat loss and fragmentation is one of the major causes of biodiversity loss in the evil quartet<br>IV. Higher genetic diversity within a species is necessarily undergo mass scale destruction due to pathogenic attacks','[{"text": "I and IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and III are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only IV is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I and IV are incorrect.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1302,'biology',103,968,2255,'Select the correct statements.<br>I. AIDS was first reported in 1981 and the word \'syndrome\' in this means a group of symptoms.<br>II During HIV infection, the macrophages cells of body continues produce virus and in this way acts like a HIV factory.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement I: The word AIDS stands for Acquired Immuno Deficiency Syndrome. This means deficiency of immune system, acquired during the lifetime of an individual indicating that it is not a congenital disease. \'Syndrome\' means a group of symptoms. AIDS was first reported in 1981 and in the last twenty-five years or so, it has spread all over the world killing more than 25 million persons.<br>Statement II: After getting into the body of the person, the virus enters into macrophages where RNA genome of the virus replicates to form viral DNA with the help of the enzyme reverse transcriptase. This viral DNA gets incorporated into host cell\'s DNA and directs the infected cells to produce virus particles. The macrophages continue to produce virus and in this way acts like a HIV factory.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1303,'biology',100,553,1107,'Which of the following statements is false in respect of viability of mammalian sperm?<br>','[{"text": "Sperm is viable for only upto 24 hours<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Survival of sperm depends on the $\\\\mathrm{pH}$ of the medium and is more active in alkaline medium<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viability of sperm is determined by its motility<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sperms must be concentrated in a thick suspension", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The life span of a typical mammalian sperm is 48-72 hours (avg. of 2.4 hrs).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1304,'biology',105,1283,3104,'The following figure shows','[{"text": "Fig flower is pollinated by moth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Orchid flower is pollinated by bee", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Yucca</i> flower is pollinated by wasp", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fig flower is pollinated by wasp", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Fig inflorescence is pollinated by only species called the wasp and hence it is thought to be have co evolved during the same time.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/105_1304_question_1.png'),
(1305,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Mark the correct statement','[{"text": "Tropical rain forest has greatest biodiversity on earth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "According to Robert May estimates, the global species diversity is 7 million", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biodiversity is the greatest in Tropics", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of the statements are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1306,'biology',103,968,2255,'Which of the below statements are correct?<br>I. A widely used diagnostic test for AIDS is enzyme linked immuno-sorbent assay (ELISA).<br>II. 1st December is celebrated as World AIDS Day.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement I: A widely used diagnostic test for AIDS is enzyme linked immuno-sorbent assay (ELISA).<br>Statement II: First recognized in 1988, World AIDS Day falls on December 1 each year.World AIDS Day is dedicated to spreading awareness of the AIDS pandemic spread by the spread of HIV infection, and to mourning those who have died of the disease.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1307,'biology',100,554,1109,'Menstrual flow occurs due to lack of<br>','[{"text": "Oxytocin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasopressin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Progesterone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{FSH}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In the event of non-fertilization the endometrium lining is shed. This happens when the corpus luteum starts to degenerate which since then had been producing progesterone to maintain the endometrium.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1342,'biology',103,969,2256,'The property of normal cells by virtue of which contact with other cells inhibits their uncontrolled growth is called','[{"text": "Contact inhibition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metastasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Benign tumor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angiogenesis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Normal cells show a property called contact inhibition by virtue of which contact with other cells inhibits their uncontrolled growth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1308,'biology',105,1283,3104,'The female wasp uses the fruit of fig species for','[{"text": "Egg laying site to female wasp for oviposition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Developing seed as food for the developing wasp larvae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The female wasp uses the fruit of fig species for<br>(1) Egg laying site to female wasp for oviposition<br>(2) Developing seed as food for the developing wasp larvae',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1309,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Choose the correct statement with respect to extinction.<br>I. Species extinction in general is a dangerous sign<br>II. We deliberately want to make species extinct<br>III. Extinctions may occur due to anthropogenic actions<br>IV. The moment of extinction is when the death of the last individual of the species occurs','[{"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, IV are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1310,'biology',103,968,2255,'Match the column I with column II.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. AIDS reported first<br>B. Diagnosis test of AIDS<br>C. Group of retrovirus<br>D. Time-lag for HIV</div><div class="column-right">P. HIV<br>Q. 1981<br>R. 5-10 years<br>S. ELISA</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}  \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S} \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}  \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. AIDS was reported first - 1981 (AIDS was first reported in 1981)<br>B. Diagnosis test of AIDS - ELISA (A widely used diagnostic test for AIDS is enzyme linked immuno-sorbent assay (ELISA).<br>C. Group of retrovirus - HIV (AIDS is caused by the Human Immuno deficiency Virus (HIV), a member of a group of viruses called retrovirus, which have an envelope enclosing the RNA genome)<br>D. Time lag for HIV - 5-10 years (There is always a time-lag between the infection and appearance of AIDS symptoms. This period may vary from a few months to many years (usually 5-10 years).',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1311,'biology',100,556,1113,'Which one of the following is not the function of placenta?<br>','[{"text": "Facilitates removal of carbon dioxide and waste material from embryo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretes oxytocin during parturition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Facilitates supply of oxygen and nutrients to embryo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretes oestrogen", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Oxytocin is secreted by the neurohypophysis of the mother. The placenta acts as an endocrine gland secreting only progesterone, estrogen and human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1312,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Select the correct answer<br>i. The wasp pollinates the fig inflorescence while searching for suitable egg-laying sites<br>ii. The mutually beneficial system between the plant and its pollinator should also be safeguarded against \'teachers\'','[{"text": "Only i is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only ii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'i. The wasp pollinates the fig inflorescence while searching for suitable egg-laying sites',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1313,'biology',106,1355,3258,'Find out the correct statements w.r.t David Tilman\'s longterm ecosystem experiments<br>I. Plots with more species showed more year to year variation in total biomass<br>II. Increased biodiversity contribution to higher productivity<br>III. Plots with less species show less year to year variation in total biomass<br>IV. Less the species richness in a community, more is the productivity','[{"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "only II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only II is correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1314,'biology',103,968,2255,'Which of the following is correct regarding AIDS causative agent HIV?','[{"text": "HIV is enveloped virus containing one molecule of single-stranded RNA and one molecule of reverse transcriptase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "HIV is enveloped virus that contains two identical molecules of reverse transcriptase with ss-RNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "HIV is un-enveloped virus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "HIV does not escape but attacks the acquired immune response", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Retrovirus have an envelop consisting of a lipid bilayer derived from host cell membrane and projecting knob like glycoprotein spikes with pedicel formed of virus coded glycoprotein. This envelop encloses the RNA genome (single stranded RNA with two identical filaments and associated with a reverse transcriptase enzyme).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1315,'biology',100,551,1105,'The shared terminal duct of the reproductive and urinary system in the human male is<br>','[{"text": "Urethra", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ureter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vas deferens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasa efferentia", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Urethra is a common pathway for the passage of urine and seminal fluid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1316,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Pseudo copulation helps in pollination in','[{"text": "Fig plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Orchid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Cuscuta</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sea anemone", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pseudo copulation helps in pollination in Orchid',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1317,'biology',106,1355,3258,'According to David Tilman','[{"text": "Increase in diversity contributes to higher productivity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plots with more species showed less year to year variation in total biomass", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase in diversity, leads to more competition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statement 1 and 2 are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1328,'biology',100,555,1112,'Ectopic pregnancies are referred to as<br>','[{"text": "Implantation of embryo at other site other than the uterus<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Implantation of defective embryo in the uterus<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pregnancy terminated due to hormonal imbalance<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pregnancy due to genetic abnormality", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ectopic pregnancy is a medical complication of female reproductive tract where, the developing blastocyst attaches to the fallopian tube and embeds there causing painful complication. This may risk the life of mother as the developing foetus may cause the bursting of the tube.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1318,'biology',103,968,2255,'At which stage of HIV infection does one usually show symptoms of AIDS?','[{"text": "Within 15 days of sexual contact with an infected person", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "When the infected retro virus enters host cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "When HIV damages large number of T-lymphocytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "When the viral DNA is produced by reverse transcriptase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The progeny viruses released in the blood attack other helper T-lymphocytes. This is repeated leading to a progressive decrease in the number of helper Tlymphocytes in the body of the infected person. During this period, the person suffers from bouts of fever, diarrhoea and weight loss. Due to decrease in the number of helper $\\mathrm{T}$ lymphocytes, the person starts suffering from infections that could have been otherwise overcome such as those due to bacteria especially Mycobacterium, viruses, fungi and even parasites like Toxoplasma. The patient becomes so immuno-deficient that he/ she is unable to protect himself/herself against these infections.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1319,'biology',100,553,1108,'The main function of mammalian corpus luteum is to produce<br>','[{"text": "Estrogen only<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Progesterone<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Human chorionic gonadotropin<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Relaxin only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The main hormones secreted by corpus luteum is progesterone. It is required to maintain the endometrium thickening for a possible pregnancy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1320,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Best example of co-evolution','[{"text": "Fig trees and pollinator species of wasp", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fig trees and pollinator species of moth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sea anemone and clown fish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Orchids and bees", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Best example of co-evolution<br>(1) Fig trees and pollinator species of wasp',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1321,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Read the following statements<br>(I) The species diversity of animals is much less than that of plants<br>(II) Sacred grooves are the traditionally protected forest patches where even the cutting of a tree branch is not allowed<br>(III) Pollution adversely affects the health of an organism but doesn\'t reduce biodiversity<br>Which of the above statements is are correct?','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statements 1 and 3 are wrong.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1322,'biology',103,968,2255,'Which of the following are the measures taken to combat AIDS?<br>I. Making blood (from blood banks) safe from HIV<br>II. Ensuring the use of only disposable needles and syringes in public and private hospitals and clinics<br>III. Free distribution of condoms<br>IV. Controlling drug abuse<br>V. Advocating safe sex and promoting regular check-ups for HIV in susceptible populations','[{"text": "Only I, II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II, III, IV is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II, III, IV, V is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V is correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Making blood (from blood banks) safe from HIV, ensuring the use of only disposable needles and syringes in public and private hospitals and clinics, free distribution of condoms, controlling drug abuse, advocating safe sex and promoting regular check-ups for HIV in susceptible populations, are some such steps taken up.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1323,'biology',100,553,1108,'Which of the following is not associated with ovulation in human female?<br>','[{"text": "Release of secondary oocyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "LH surge", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decrease in estradiol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Full development of Graafian follicle", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During mid menstrual cycle there is a sudden increase in the levels of FSH and LH. LH surge results in ovulation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1324,'biology',105,1283,3104,'In____ , one petal of female flower bears an uncanny resemblance to the female bee in size, colour and markings','[{"text": "The Mediterranean orchid <i>Ophrys</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The Australian orchid <i>Ophrys</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The Madagascar orchid <i>Ophrys</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In The Mediterranean orchid Ophrys one petal of female flower bears an uncanny resemblance to the female bee in size, colour and markings.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1325,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Consider the following statements and select the option that correctly identifies the True (T) and False (F) ones<br>I. Ex-situ conservation of plants and animals provide resources for genetic engineering<br>II. In-situ conservation is adopted to protect endangered species from anthropogenic factors<br>III. In - situ conservation helps to maintain genetic diversity of all present species<br>IV. In order to acclimitise the offsprings produced in natural environment, they are shifted to ex-situ environment<br>&emsp; $\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{\\rm{I}}&{{\\rm{II}}}&{{\\rm{III}}}&{{\\rm{IV}}}\n\\end{array}$','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{F}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{T}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{T}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{F}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement 1 is true, Statement 2 is true, Statement 3 is true<br>Statement 4 is false.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1326,'biology',103,969,2256,'Study of cancer is called','[{"text": "Angiology", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytology", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oncology", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both \' 1 \' and \' 3 \'", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cancer is one of the most dreaded diseases of human beings and is a major cause of death all over the globe. Oncology is a branch of medicine that deals with the study, treatment, diagnosis and prevention of cancer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1327,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Plant offer following rewards to pollinators','[{"text": "Nectar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Plant offer nectar and pollen rewards to pollinators.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1329,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Which of the following is not a cause for loss of biodiversity?','[{"text": "Destruction of habitat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Invasion by alien species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Keeping animals in zoological parks", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Over-exploitation of natural resources", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Keeping animals in zoological parks helps in conservation of biodiversity. It gives a natural and safe environment with a supervision to check their decreasing numbers.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1331,'biology',100,555,1110,'Capacitation refers to changes in the<br>','[{"text": "Ovum after fertilization<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sperm after fertilization<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sperm before fertilization<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ovum before fertilization", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The sperm is activated before it penetrates the egg. This happens when the sperm is washed in the vaginal and cervical fluid in a process called capacitation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1332,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Morphological<br>B. Physiological adaptation<br>C. Chemical substance<br>D. Behavioural adaptation</div><div class="column-right">P. Altitude sickness<br>Q. Cactus<br>R. Caffeine<br>S. Basking of lizards</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{A - Q, B - P, C - R, D - S}}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1333,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Where among the following will you find pitcher plant?','[{"text": "Rain forest of North-East India", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sunderbans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thar desert", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Western Ghats", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In rainforest of North-East India pitcher plants are spotted because moist and humid climate is favourable to them.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1334,'biology',103,969,2256,'The spread of cancerous cells to distant sites is termed as','[{"text": "Metastasis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metachrosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metamorphosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metagenesis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cells actively divide and grow they also starve the normal cells by competing for vital nutrients. Cells sloughed from such tumors reach distant sites through blood, and wherever they get lodged in the body, they start a new tumor there. This property called metastasis is the most feared property of malignant tumors.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1335,'biology',100,554,1109,'Select the incorrect statement <br>','[{"text": "FSH stimulates the sertoli cells which help in spermiogenesis<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "LH triggers ovulation in ovary<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "LH and FSH decrease gradually during the follicular phase<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "LH triggers secretion of androgens from the Leydig cells", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'LH nad FSH increase during follicular phase.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1336,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Identify the organisms in the diagram','[{"text": "Fig and wasp", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bumble bee + orchid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mango + orchid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sea anemone + orchid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Bumble bee + orchid<br>It is mutualism. In Orchids, there is a relationship with pollinator insects ( bees and bumble bees). The Mediterranean orchid Ophrys employs sexual deficit to get pollination done by a species of bee. One petal of its flower bears and uncanny resemblance to the female of the bees in size, colour and markings.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/105_1336_question_1.png'),
(1337,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Match the animals given in column I with their location in column II:<br>Choose the correct match from the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Dodo<br>B. Quagga<br>C. Thylacine<br>D. Stellar’s sea cow</div><div class="column-right">P. Africa<br>Q. Russia<br>R. Mauritius<br>S. Australia</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-3, B-1, C-4, D-2',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1338,'biology',103,969,2256,'Normal cells are called cancerous when they show the following property','[{"text": "New blood vessels formation (angiogenesis)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uncontrolled cell division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contact inhibition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Normal cells shows contact inhibition, in which when they contact with other cells they inhibit their uncontrolled - growth. Angiogenesis is the creation and growth of new blood vessels throughout the body. This process is stimulated by cancer cells and helps the cancer cells travel through the body via these new blood vessels. The creation of new blood vessels also helps cancer cells spread to other tissues.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1339,'biology',100,556,1113,'Several hormones like hCG, hPL, estrogen, progesterone are produced by','[{"text": "Fallopian tube", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pituitary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Placenta", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Hormones of the Placenta: Estrogen, Progesterone & hCG. The placenta is an endocrine gland that is only present during pregnancy. It produces human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG), progesterone, estrogen, and human placental lactogen (hPL)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1340,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Mutualism<br>B. Commensalism<br>C. Parasitism<br>D. Predation</div><div class="column-right">P. Mosquito<br>Q. Tiger and deer<br>R. Cran and sea anemone<br>S. Fig and wasp</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{A - S, B - R, C - P, D - Q}}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
