(1343,'biology',100,551,1105,'Which of the following depicts the correct pathway of transport of sperms? <br>','[{"text": "Rete testis $\\\\rightarrow$ Vas deferens $\\\\rightarrow$ Efferent ductules $\\\\rightarrow$ Epididymis<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Efferent ductules $\\\\rightarrow$ Rete testis $\\\\rightarrow$ Vas deferens $\\\\rightarrow$ Epididymis<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rete testis $\\\\rightarrow$ Efferent ductules $\\\\rightarrow$ Epididymis $\\\\rightarrow$ Vas deferens<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rete testis $\\\\rightarrow$ Epididymis $\\\\rightarrow$ Efferent ductules $\\\\rightarrow$ Vas deferens", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Rete testis leads to vasa efferentia, leading to epididymis and furtehr to vasa deferentia and than ejaculatory duct and urethra.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1344,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Select the not false statement<br>I. Some organisms are able to maintain homeostasis by physiological (sometimes behavioural also) means which ensure constant body temperature, constant osmotic concentration etc. are called Regulators.<br>II. Snow leopards are found in Kerala forests and tuna fish are rarely caught beyond tropical latitudes in the ocean.<br>III. Water is the least important factor influencing the life of organisms','[{"text": "I is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Regulators are those organisms which regulate a constant body temperature',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1345,'biology',106,1356,3259,'The extinction of passenger pigeon was due to:','[{"text": "Increased number of predatory birds.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Over exploitation by humans.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Non-availability of the food.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bird flu virus infection.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Passenger pigeons were native birds to North America. They become extinct due to excessive hunting.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1346,'biology',100,555,1110,'Fertilization in humans is practically feasible only if.<br>','[{"text": "The sperms are transported into vagina just after the release of ovum in fallopian tube<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The ovum and sperms are transported simultaneously to ampullary isthmic junction of the fallopian tube<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The ovum and sperms are transported simultaneously to ampullary - isthmic junction of the cervix<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The sperms are transported into cervix within $48 \\\\mathrm{hrs}$ of release of ovum in uterus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sperms and ovum is present in ampullary region of fallopian tube at the same time.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1347,'biology',103,969,2256,'Which form of the tumor remains confirmed to their original location and do not spread to other parts of the body?','[{"text": "Benign tumor", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Malignant tumour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leukaemia", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Benign tumors normally remain confined to their original location and do not spread to other parts of the body and cause little damage.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1348,'biology',105,1278,3095,'Heat loss or heat gain____ A ____ Small animals have a____ B____ they tend to lose body heat very fast when it is cold outside; then they have to ____ C____ This is the main reason why very small animals are rarely found in polar regions.<br>Fill in the above blanks in the above statement','[{"text": "A- is a function of surface area", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B- Larger surface area relative to their volume", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C- Expend much energy to generate body heat through metabolism.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Articularly true for small animals like shrews and humming birds. Heat loss or heat gain is a function of surface area. Since small animals have a larger surface area relative to their volume, they tend to lose body heat very fast when it is cold outside; then they have to expend much energy to generate body heat through metabolism. This is the main reason why very small animals are rarely found in polar regions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1349,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Among the ecosystem mentioned below, where can one find maximum biodiversity?','[{"text": "Mangroves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Desert", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coral reefs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alpine meadows", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mangroves and alpine meadows can support only selected number of species. Same condition is in deserts as well.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1350,'biology',100,555,1112,'Match Column-I with Column-II and select the correct option using the codes given below<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Mons pubis<br>B. Antrum<br>C. Trophoecto- derm<br>D. Nebenkern</div><div class="column-right">1. Embryo formation<br>2. Sperm<br>3. Female external genitalia<br>4. Graafian follicle</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A} \\\\rightarrow 3, \\\\mathrm{~B} \\\\rightarrow 1, \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\rightarrow 4, \\\\mathrm{D} \\\\rightarrow 2$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A} \\\\rightarrow 1, \\\\mathrm{~B} \\\\rightarrow 4, \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\rightarrow 3, \\\\mathrm{D} \\\\rightarrow 2$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A} \\\\rightarrow 3, \\\\mathrm{~B} \\\\rightarrow 4, \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\rightarrow 2, \\\\mathrm{D} \\\\rightarrow 1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A} \\\\rightarrow 3, \\\\mathrm{~B} \\\\rightarrow 4, \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\rightarrow 1, \\\\mathrm{D} \\\\rightarrow 2$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-3, B-4, C-1, D-2',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1351,'biology',105,1278,3095,'In higher plants, which structure serve as means to tide over period of stress and also helps in dispersal','[{"text": "Seed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vegetative reproductive structures propagules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Spores", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In higher plants,<br>(1) Seed<br>(2) Vegetative reproductive structures propagules structure serve as means to tide over period of stress and also helps in dispersal.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1352,'biology',103,969,2256,'Which of the following properties is proposed by malignant tumors?','[{"text": "Metastasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uncontrolled cell division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Loss of contact inhibition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The malignant tumors, on the other hand are a mass of proliferating cells called neoplastic or tumor cells. Cells sloughed from such tumors reach distant sites through blood, and wherever they get lodged in the body, they start a new tumor there. This property called metastasis is the most feared property of malignant tumors.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
