(1356,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Read the statements and identify the correct option.<BR>I. Percentage of Phytophagous insects are nearly $45 \\%$<BR>II. Many plants produce and store chemicals that make the herbivore sick when they are eaten, inhibit feeding or digestion, disrupt its reproduction or even kill it.<BR>III. The Monarch butterfly is highly distasteful to its predator','[{"text": "I, II are wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I is wrong", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Percentage of Phytophagous insects are nearly $25 \\%$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1357,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Which of the below mentioned regions exhibit less seasonal variations?','[{"text": "Tropics", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Temperates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alpines", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Tropics get the same amount of illumination throughout the year and hence there is less seasonal variation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
