(1364,'biology',100,553,1107,'The difference between spermiogenesis and spermiation is<br>','[{"text": "In spermiogenesis spermatozoa from sertoli cells are released into the cavity of seminiferous tubules, while in spermiation spermatozoa are formed.<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In spermiogenesis spermatozoa are formed, while in spermiation spermatids are formed.<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In spermiogenesis spermatids are formed, while in spermiation spermatozoa are formed.<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In spermiogenesis spermatozoa are formed, while in spermiation spermatozoa are released from sertoli cells into the cavity of seminiferous tubules.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Spermiogenesis is the formation of spermatids from spermazoa, it is also called spermiogenesis. Spermiation is the release of the sperms from sertoli cells into the lumen of seminiferous tubule.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
