(1368,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Which of the following best describes the principle of competitive exclusion in wake of Mac Arthur\'s findings?','[{"text": "Competition between two species causes extinction of one species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two species occupying exactly the same niche can coexist in a community", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Competition in a population decreases survival of the best- adapted individuals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No two species can coexist in the same habitat", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Two species occupying exactly the same niche can coexist in a community best describes the principle of competitive exclusion in wake of Mac Arthur\'s findings.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4966,'biology',77,411,821,'Cell-cycle include','[{"text": "Interphase only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Division phase only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interphase and division phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DNA replication only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cell cycle includes interphase and division (M) phase',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1369,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Which of the following is not an invasive alien species in the Indian context?','[{"text": "<i>Lantana</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Cynodon</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Parthenium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Eichhornia</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Other species from the options were introduced into India from some other parts of the world.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1370,'biology',100,554,1109,'Match the items given in Column I with those in Column II and select the correct option given below :<br>\n<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A.  Proliferative phase<br>B. Secretory Phase<br>C. Menstruation</div><div class="column-right">1.Breakdown of endometrial lining<br>2. Follicular phase<br>3. Luteal phase</div></div>','[{"text": "A-2 B-3 C-1", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-1 B-3 C-2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-3 B-2 C-1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-3 B-1 C-2", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Proliferative phase is also called follicular phase as follicles gets developed during this phase. Secretory phase is also called as luteal phase mainly controlled by progesterone secreted by corpus luteum. Estrogen further thickens the endometrium maintained by progesterone. Decrease in progesterone level initiates menstruation and also involves breakdown of endometrial lining.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1371,'biology',103,969,2256,'Oncogene is another name for','[{"text": "Inducer gene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Jumping gene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Structural gene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cancer causing gene", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cancer causing viruses called oncogenic viruses have genes called viral oncogenes. Furthermore, several genes called cellular oncogenes (c-onc) or proto oncogenes have been identified in normal cells which, when activated under certain conditions, could lead to oncogenic transformation of the cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1372,'biology',105,1283,3102,'Which is not a characteristic of intestinal symbionts?','[{"text": "Feeding on extra food of host", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Providing vitamins to host", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaerobic respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aerobic respiration", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Intestinal symbionts exist inside our body. There is no availability of oxygen hence, they are not able to perform aerobic respiration.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1373,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Which one of the following is not a major characteristic feature of biodiversity hot spots?','[{"text": "Large number of species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abundance of endemic species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mostly located in the tropics", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mostly located in the polar regions", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Polar regions have poorest biodiversity because of low sunlight, very low temperature and negligible precipitation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1374,'biology',100,556,1113,'Hormones secreted by the placenta to maintain pregnancy are<br>','[{"text": "hCG, hPL, progestogens, estrogens<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "hCG, hPL, estrogens, relaxin, oxytocin<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "hCG, hPL, progestogens, prolactin<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "hCG, progestogens, estrogens, glucocorticoids", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Placenta is structural and functional unit between foetus and mothers body. It is formed by chorionic villi and uterine.<br>Placenta produces following hormones, human chorionic gonadotropic hormone (hCG), Human placental lactogen (hPL), estrogens, progesterone.Relaxin is hormone produced by ovary during later stages of pregnancy. Glucocorticoid is a hormone produced by adrenal cortex.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1375,'biology',105,1280,3097,'The population has certain attributes which an organism or individual does not. These are<br>i. Birth rate<br>ii. Death rate<br>iii. Sex ratio<br>iv. Age distribution','[{"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii and iv", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Population is a group of individuals of same species living together in a habitat, which have certain characteristic like birth rate, death rate, age distribution and sex ratio.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1376,'biology',103,969,2256,'The genes which can lead to the oncogenic transformation of the cells in which these are present, are called','[{"text": "Oncogenes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proto-oncogenes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellular oncogenes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (2) and (3)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Several genes called cellular oncogenes (c-onc) or proto oncogenes have been identified in normal cells which, when activated under certain conditions, could lead to oncogenic transformation of the cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1377,'biology',106,1356,3259,'What is common to the following plants:<br><em>Nepenthes, Psilotum, Rauwolfia </em>and<br><em>Aconitum</em>?','[{"text": "All are ornamental plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are phylogenic link species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are prone to over exploitation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are exclusively present in the Eastern Himalayas.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'These plants have various medicinal uses in traditional medicines and hence they are exploited and prone to increased exploitation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1378,'biology',103,969,2256,'Characteristics of cancer are','[{"text": "All viruses are oncogenic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All tumours are cancers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cancerous cells show property of contact inhibition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cancer cells show metastasis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Metastasis is a word used to describe the spread of cancer. Unlike normal cells, cancer cells have the ability to grow outside of the place in your body where they originated.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1379,'biology',100,555,1110,'Extrusion of second polar body from egg nucleus occurs :<br>','[{"text": "After entry of sperm but before fertilization<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "After fertilization<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Before entry of sperm into ovum<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Simultaneously with first cleavage", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'At the time of ovulation, the secondary oocyte is at metaphase-II stage. Penetration of the sperm into the oocyte induces the completion of Meiosis-II resulting in the production of ovum and second polar body. Then the nucleus of the sperm fuses with that of the ovum (amphimixis). So, the second polar body is extruded after the sperm penetration but before fertilization.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1380,'biology',105,1279,3096,'A person experience altitude sickness when they go to any high place like Rohtang pass near Manali and Mansarovar in China occupied Tibet, above a height','[{"text": "$>3500 \\\\mathrm{~m}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$>3500$ feet", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$>500 \\\\mathrm{~m}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$>500$ feet", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Altitude sickness is also called acute mountain sickness. It is a negative health effect on high altitudes above $3500 \\mathrm{~m}$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1381,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Amongst the animal groups given below, which one appears to be more vulnerable to extinction?','[{"text": "Insects", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mammals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphibians", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Reptiles", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'At present, $33 \\%$ of all amphibian species face threat of extinction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1382,'biology',100,551,1105,'Select the correct sequence for transport of sperm cells in male reproductive system.<br>','[{"text": "Testis $\\\\rightarrow$ Epididymis $\\\\rightarrow$ Vasa efferentia $\\\\rightarrow$ Rete testis $\\\\rightarrow$ Inguinal canal $\\\\rightarrow$ Urethra<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seminiferous tubules $\\\\rightarrow$ Rete testis $\\\\rightarrow$ Vasa efferentia $\\\\rightarrow$ Epididymis $\\\\rightarrow$ Vas deferens $\\\\rightarrow$ Ejaculatory duct $\\\\rightarrow$ Urethra $\\\\rightarrow$ Urethral meatus<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Seminiferous tubules $\\\\rightarrow$ Vasa efferentia $\\\\rightarrow$ Epididymis $\\\\rightarrow$ Inguinal canal $\\\\rightarrow$ Urethra<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testis $\\\\rightarrow$ Epididymis $\\\\rightarrow$ Vasa efferentia $\\\\rightarrow$ Vas deferens $\\\\rightarrow$ Ejaculatory duct $\\\\rightarrow$ Inguinal canal $\\\\rightarrow$ Urethra $\\\\rightarrow$ Urethral meatus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct sequence for transport of sperm cells in male reproductive system is Seminiferous tubules $\\rightarrow$ Rete testis $\\rightarrow$ Vasa efferentia $\\rightarrow$ Epididymis $\\rightarrow$ Vas deferens $\\rightarrow$ Ejaculatory duct $\\rightarrow$ Urethra $\\rightarrow$ Urethral meatus',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1383,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Though it is energetically expensive, tobacco plant produces nicotine because','[{"text": "It increases the taste of tobacco leaves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It stimulates the secretion of adrenaline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It decreases transpiratory water loss", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It protects it from herbivores", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The problem of predation is particularly severe for plants because, unlike animals, they cannot run away from their predators. Therefore, plants have morphological and chemical defences against herbivores. Manyplants produce and store chemicals that make the herbivore sick when they are eaten, inhibit feeding or digestion, disrupt its reproduction or even kill it. Examples: cardiac glycosides, nicotine, caffeine, quinine, strychnine, opium.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1384,'biology',103,969,2256,'Select the correct answer<br>I. Malignant tumors normally remain confined to their original location and do not spread to other parts of the body and cause little damage.<br>II. The Benign tumors, are a mass of proliferating cells called neoplastic or tumor cells.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statement I: The malignant tumors, on the other hand are a mass of proliferating cells called neoplastic or tumor cells. These cells grow very rapidly, invading and damaging the surrounding normal tissues. Cells sloughed from such tumors reach distant sites through blood, and wherever they get lodged in the body, they start a new tumor there. This property called metastasis is the most feared property of malignant tumors.<br>Statement II: A benign tumor is a mass of cells (tumor) that lacks the ability either to invade neighbouring tissue or metastasize (spread throughout the body).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1385,'biology',106,1356,3259,'What is common to <i>Lantana, Eichhornia</i> and African catfish?','[{"text": "All are endangered species of India.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are keystone species.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are mammals found in India.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the species are neither threatened nor indigenous species of India.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the species are neither threatened nor indigenous species of India.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1386,'biology',100,553,1108,'Meiotic division of the secondary oocyte is completed:<br>','[{"text": "At the time of copulation<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "After zygote formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "At the time of fusion of a sperm with an ovum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prior to ovulation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'At the time of fusion of a sperm with an ovum',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1387,'biology',103,969,2256,'Carcinoma refers to','[{"text": "Malignant tumours of the connective tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Malignant tumour of the skin or mucous membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Malignant tumour of the colon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Benign tumours of the connective tissue", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Carcinoma refers to malignant tumors of the Skin & Mucous membrane. It is cancer that arises in the epithelium, the tissue that lines the skin and internal organs of the body.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1388,'biology',105,1278,3095,'Which of the following organisms are indeed capable of thermoregulation and osmoregulation?','[{"text": "All birds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All mammals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Very few lower vertebrate and invertebrate species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'(1) All birds<br>(2) All mammals<br>(3) Very few lower vertebrate and invertebrate species organisms are indeed capable of thermoregulation and osmoregulation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1389,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Which of the following statements is correct?','[{"text": "<i>Parthenium</i> is an endemic species of our country.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "African catfish is not a threat to indigenous catfishes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Steller\'s sea cow is an extinct animal.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Lantana</i> is popularly known as carrot grass.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Stellars seacow is an extinct species.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1390,'biology',105,1283,3101,'An ecosystem resist change because it is in a state of','[{"text": "Imbalance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homeostasis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Shortage of light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Deficiency of light", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Homeostasis is a state of maintaining a constant environment inside our body.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1391,'biology',100,554,1109,'Which of the following hormone levels will cause release of ovum (ovulation) from the Graffian follicle?<br>','[{"text": "High concentration of progesterone<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Low concentration of LH<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Low concentration of FSH<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "High concentration of Estrogen", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'High concentration of Estrogen',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1392,'biology',103,969,2256,'Blood cancer is otherwise called as','[{"text": "Anaemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polycythemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leucopenia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leukemia", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Leukemia results from excessive formation of white blood cells (WBCs) or leucocytes in the bone marrow and lymphatic nodes, increasing their number in the blood. The blood contains millions of abnormal immature WBCs or leucocytes that are incapable of fighting out infections',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1393,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Which of the following forests is known as the \'lungs of the planet Earth\'?','[{"text": "Taiga forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tundra forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amazon rain forest", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rain forests of North East India", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Amazon rain forest is known as lungs of the planet.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1394,'biology',100,556,1113,'Match the following columns and select the correct option-<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Placenta<br>B. Zona pellucida<br>C. Bullo- urethral glands<br>D. Leydig cells</div><div class="column-right">P. Sulphur dioxide<br>Q. Human chorionic Gonadotropin<br>R. Layer of the ovum<br>S. Lubrication of the penis</div></div>','[{"text": "A - P, B - S, C - Q, D - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A -R, B - Q, C - S, D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q,B - R, C - S, D - P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - S, B - R, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'(a)(ii) ; (b)(iii) ; (c)(iv); (d)(i)',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1395,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Two opposite forces operate in the growth and development of every population. One of them is related to the ability to reproduce at a given rate. The force opposite to it is called','[{"text": "Fecundity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mortality", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Environmental resistance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Biotic control", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The environmental factors which can check the of growth population size constitute the environmental resistance.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1396,'biology',103,969,2256,'Sarcoma is cancer of','[{"text": "Epithelial tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesodermal tissue", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Endodermal tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sarcoma affects the tissue derived from mesoderm such as connective tissue. They include bone tumors, muscle tumor or cancer of lymph nodes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1397,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Which of the following group exhibit more species diversity?','[{"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bryophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Among plants; angiosperms and fungi show largest number of species.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1398,'biology',100,555,1110,'Receptors for sperm binding in mammals are present on:<br>','[{"text": "Corona radiata<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vitelline membrane<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Perivitelline space<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zona pellucida<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During fertilization in mammals, sperm must first bind in a species-specific manner to the egg $\\mathrm{s}$ thick extracellular coat, the zona pellucida. ZP3, one of three zona pellucida glycoproteins, serves as a structural glycoprotein, a sperm receptor, and an acrosome reaction-inducer.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1399,'biology',105,1277,3094,'Red and Green alage live in sea water at','[{"text": "Surface and Bottom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bottom and surface", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Middle layers of water & bottom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bottom and upper sandy layer of sea water", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Red -Bottom & Green algae - upper sandy layer of sea water.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1400,'biology',103,969,2256,'Which cancer affects lymph nodes?','[{"text": "Carcinoma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sarcoma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leukemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lymphoma", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sarcoma affects the tissue derived from mesoderm such as connective tissue. They includes bone tumors, muscle tumors or cancers of lymph nodes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1401,'biology',106,1357,3260,'The historic convention on Biological Diversity held in Rio de Janeiro in 1992 is known as:','[{"text": "CITES Convention", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The Earth Summit", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "G-16 Summit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "MAB Programme", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The Earth summit was held in Rio de Janeiro in 1992.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1402,'biology',100,556,1113,'Which of the following secretes the hormone, relaxin, during the later phase of pregnancy?<br>','[{"text": "Graafian follicle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpus luteum<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Foetus<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uterus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In Later phase of pregnancy ovary will produce Relaxin so the best answer is corpus luteum',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1403,'biology',103,969,2256,'Cancer cells are more easily damaged by radiation than normal cells because they','[{"text": "Do not undergo cell division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Undergoing rapid division", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Different in structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Are in G0 phase", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Radiation therapy is most harmful for the cells which are actively dividing and fastgrowing cells, cancer cells are one of them . The cancer cells are more easily damaged by the radiation than the normal cells as the radiations do not let them divide and grow, it makes the cancer cells dead. Therefore, this radiation easily damages the cancer cells because they undergo rapid division and do not stop by itself.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1487,'biology',105,1279,3096,'The reason of the altitude sickness is','[{"text": "The low atmospheric pressure of high altitudes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The high atmospheric pressure of high altitudes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The low atmospheric temperature of high altitudes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'At high altitudes there will be low atmospheric pressure',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1404,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Verhulst-Pearl Logistic Growth is described by the equation and the integral form of the exponential growth equation is as follows','[{"text": "$\\\\frac{{{\\\\rm{dN}}}}{{{\\\\rm{dt}}}}{\\\\rm{ = rN}}\\\\left( {\\\\frac{{{\\\\rm{K - N}}}}{{\\\\rm{K}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{,}}{{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{t}}}{\\\\rm{ = }}{{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{0}}}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{{\\\\rm{rt}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\frac{{{\\\\rm{dN}}}}{{{\\\\rm{dt}}}}{\\\\rm{ = rN,\\\\,}}{{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{t}}}{\\\\rm{ = }}{{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{0}}}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{{\\\\rm{rt}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{t}}}{\\\\rm{ = }}{{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{0}}}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{{\\\\rm{rt}}}}{\\\\rm{,}}\\\\frac{{{\\\\rm{dN}}}}{{{\\\\rm{dt}}}}{\\\\rm{ = rN}}\\\\left( {\\\\frac{{{\\\\rm{K - N}}}}{{\\\\rm{K}}}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{t}}}{\\\\rm{ = }}{{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{0}}}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{{\\\\rm{rt}}}}{\\\\rm{,}}{{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{t}}}{\\\\rm{ = }}{{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{0}}}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{n}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Verhulst-Pearl Logistic Growth is described by the equation $\\mathrm{dN} / \\mathrm{dt}=\\mathrm{rN}(\\mathrm{K}-\\mathrm{N} / \\mathrm{K})$, and the integral form of the exponential growth equation is as follows $\\mathrm{N}_{\\mathrm{t}}=\\mathrm{N}_{0} \\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{rt}}$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1405,'biology',106,1352,3254,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">There are 20,000 species of orchids, 3,00,000 species of beetles, 28,000 species of fishes.<br></div><div class="column-right">Biodiversity is the term popularised by the sociophysicist Edward Wilson</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement A is correct and statement B is wrong. Biodiversity is the term popularised by the sociobiologist Edward Wilson',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1406,'biology',100,557,1115,'Which of these is not an important component of initiation of parturition in humans?<br>','[{"text": "Increase in estrogen and progesterone ratio<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synthesis of prostaglandins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release of oxytocin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release of prolactin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Release of prolactin is not important for parturition',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1407,'biology',103,969,2256,'Which one of the following is not communicable disease','[{"text": "Tuberculosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diphtheria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cholera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cancer", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cancer or malignancy is a form of development that transforms normal cells into cancerous cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1408,'biology',105,1277,3094,'Select the correct answer<br>I. Water is another the most important factor influencing the life of organisms.<br>II. The salt concentrations (measused or salinity in parts per-thousand) is less than 15 in inland waters, $60-65$ in the sea and $>$ 100 in some hypersaline lagoons.<br>III. Many animals use the diurnal and seasonal variations in light intensity and duration as cues for timing their foraging, reproductive and migratory activities.','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I. Water is another the most important factor influencing the life of organisms.<br>III. Many animals use the diurnal and seasonal variations in light intensity and duration as cues for timing their foraging, reproductive and migratory activities.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1409,'biology',106,1352,3254,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">India has more than 50,000 genetically different strains of mango, and 1,000 varieties of rice.<br></div><div class="column-right">A single species might show high diversity at the genetic level over its distributional range.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement A is wrong and statement B is correct. India has more than 50,000 genetically different strains of rice, and 1,000 varieties of mango.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(1410,'biology',100,553,1108,'At which stage of life the oogenesis process initiated?<br>','[{"text": "Embryonic development stage<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Birth<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adult<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Puberty", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Oogenesis is initiated during the embryonic development stage when a couple of million gamete mother cells (oogonia) are formed within each foetal ovary; no more oogonia are formed and added after birth. These cells start division and enter prophase-I of the meiotic division and get temporarily arrested at that stage, called primary oocytes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1411,'biology',103,969,2256,'Breast cancer is the example of ____ disease','[{"text": "Deficiency", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hormonal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Allergic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Malignancy", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Malignant tumours : Cancerous cells from such tumour are carried by blood and lymph to other parts of the body, where they or secondary malignant growths. The spread of cancer cells to distant parts is called metastasis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1412,'biology',105,1278,3095,'Select the false answer<br>I. In summer, we shiver profusely causing evaporative cooling brings down the body temperature.<br>II. In winters, we sweat which is an exercise that produces heat and raises the body temperature','[{"text": "I is true, but II is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II is true, but I is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are false", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I. In summer, we shiver profusely causing evaporative cooling brings down the body temperature.<br>II. In winters, we sweat which is an exercise that produces heat and raises the body temperature Both are false statement.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1420,'biology',103,969,2256,'Mark odd one?','[{"text": "Cancer of Bone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cancer of Blood", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cancer of Muscle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cancer of cartilage", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In most blood cancers, the normal blood cell development process is interrupted by uncontrolled growth of an abnormal type of blood cell. These abnormal blood cells, or cancerous cells, prevent your blood from performing many of its functions, like fighting off infections or preventing serious bleeding.<br>Leukemia, a type of cancer found in your blood and bone marrow, is caused by the rapid production of abnormal white blood cells. The high number of abnormal white blood cells are not able to fight infection, and they impair the ability of the bone marrow to produce red blood cells and platelets.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1413,'biology',106,1352,3254,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left"><i>Rauwolfia vomitoria</i> shows genetic variation, growing in different Himalayan ranges might be in terms of the potency and concentration of the active chemical (vomitorin) that the plant produces.<br></div><div class="column-right">The Western Ghats have a greater amphibian species diversity than the Eastern Ghats.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement A is wrong and statement B is correct. The genetic variation shown by the medicinal plant Rauwolfiavomitoria growing in different Himalayan ranges might be in terms of the potency and concentration of the active chemical (reserpine) that the plant produces.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1414,'biology',100,553,1107,'Given below are two statements:<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The release of sperms into the seminiferous tubules is called spermiation.<br></div><div class="column-right">Spermiogenesis is the proces of formation of sperms from spermatogonia.<br><br>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:<br></div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are incorrect.<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The release of sperms into the seminiferous tubules is called spermiation. Spermiogenesis is the process of the formation of spermatozoa from spermatids.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1415,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Select the correct answer<br>I. Desert lizard bask in the sun and absorbs heat when their body temperature drops below the comfort zone, but move into shade when the ambient temperature starts increasing.<br>II. Migration is moving away permanently from the stressful habitat to more hospitable area and return when stressful period is over','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I. Desert lizard bask in the sun and absorbs heat when their body temperature drops below the comfort zone, but move into shade when the ambient temperature starts increasing. is correct answer.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1416,'biology',103,969,2256,'Cancer of muscle: Sarcoma:: Cancer of Skin : ____','[{"text": "Sarcoma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leukemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Melanoma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glucoma", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Carcinomas: Malignant growth of epithelial tissue or skin i.e, cancer of skin, lung, breast, stomach and pancreas.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1417,'biology',106,1353,3255,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Robert May places the Indian species diversity at about 7 million.<br></div><div class="column-right">Among animals, insects are the most species-rich taxonomic group, making upmore than 70 per cent of the total.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement B is correct and statement A is wrong. Robert May places the global species diversity at about 7 million. Among animals, insects are the most species-rich taxonomic group, making up more than 70 per cent of the total',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1418,'biology',100,553,1107,'Which of the following statements are true for spermatogenesis but do not hold true for oogensis?<br>(a) It results in the formation of haploid gametes<br>(b) Differentiation of gamete occurs after the completion of meiosis<br>(c) Meiosis occurs continuously in a mitotically dividing stem cell population<br>(d) It is controlled by the Luteinising hormone (LH) and Follicle Stimulating Hormone (FSH) secreted by the anterior pituitary<br>(e) It is initiated at puberty<br>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:<br>','[{"text": "(b) and (c) only<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(b), (d) and (e) only<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(b), (c) and (e) only<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(c) and (e) only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'(a) In both spermatogenesis and oogenesis, haploid gametes are formed.<br>(b) Differentiation of spermatids to spermatozoa (spermiogenesis) occurs only during spermatogenesis. The spermatozoon is morphologically much different from the spermatid. Oogenesis does not involve such morphological differention of the ovum.<br>(c) Meiosis is continuous during spermatogenesis. During oogenesis meiosis begins during embryonic stage and gets arrested at prophase - I. It resumes only after puberty. So, meiosis is discontinuous during oogenesis while it is continuous during spermatogenesis.<br>(d) Spermatogenesis is controlled by FSH and androgens (but not directly by LH). Oogenesis is also controlled by FSH only. LH stimulates ovulation but not oogenesis. Thus (d) does not hold good for both spermatogenesis and oogenesis.<br>(e) Spermatogenesis is initiated at puberty whereas oogenesis is initiated during embryonic stage itself.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1419,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Select the correct answer<br>I. The number of individuals of the same species that have come into the habitat from elsewhere during the time period under consideration is called immigration.<br>II. The number of individuals of the population who left the habitat and gone elsewhere during the time period under consideration is called emigration.','[{"text": "I is true, but II is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II is true, but I is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are true", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both I and II are false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I. The number of individuals of the same species that have come into the habitat from elsewhere during the time period under consideration is called immigration.<br>II. The number of individuals of the population who left the habitat and gone elsewhere during the time period under consideration is called emigration. Both are true statement',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1439,'biology',105,1283,3102,'Choose the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "Parasite might render the host more vulnerable to predation by making it physically better.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Majority of the parasites harm the host and reduce the population density", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Malarial parasite need a vector (mosquito) to spread to other host", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The human liver fluke depends on two intermediate hosts (a snail and a fish) to complete its life cycle.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Parasite might render the host more vulnerable to predation by making it physically better; is incorrect statement.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1421,'biology',106,1353,3255,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">According to the International Union for Conservation of Nature and Natural Resources (IUCN) (2007), the total number of plant and animal species described so far is slightly more than 1.5 million.<br></div><div class="column-right">For many taxonomic groups, species inventories are more complete in tropical countries than in temperate countries.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the statements are wrong. According to the International Union for Conservation of Nature and Natural Resources (IUCN) (2004), the total number of plant and animal species described so far is slightly more than 1.5 million. For many taxonomic groups, species inventories are more complete in temperate than in tropical countries.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1422,'biology',100,555,1111,'Consider the following statements with reference to female reproduction system:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The presence or absence of hymen is not a reliable indicator of virginity or sexual experience</div><div class="column-right">The sex of the foetus is determined by the father and not by the mother.<br>Choose the correct option from the following</div></div>','[{"text": "Both the statement A and statement B are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is wrong and statement B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statement A and statement B are wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct and statement B is wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both the statements A and statement B are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1423,'biology',103,969,2256,'In ____ , a piece of the suspected tissue cut into thin sections is stained and examined under microscope____ by a pathologist.','[{"text": "X-ray, MRI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biopsy, histopathological studies", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Biopsy, MRI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Histopathological studies, biopsy", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In biopsy, a piece of the suspected tissue cut into thin sections is stained and examined under microscope (histopathological studies) by a pathologist.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1424,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Select the correct answer<br>I. Any species growing exponentially under unlimited resource condition can reach enormous population densities in short time.<br>II. Darwin showed how even a slow growing animal like tiger could reach enormous numbers in the absence of check.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I. Any species growing exponentially under unlimited resource condition can reach enormous population densities in short time.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1425,'biology',106,1353,3255,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">More than 90 per cent of all the species recorded are animals.<br></div><div class="column-right">Plants (including algae, fungi, bryophytes, gymnosperms and angiosperms) comprise no more than 11 per cent of the total.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the statements are wrong.More than 70 per cent of all the species recorded are animals, plants (including algae, fungi, bryophytes, gymnosperms and angiosperms) comprise no more than 22 per cent of the total.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1426,'biology',100,551,1105,'The male sex accessory ducts include','[{"text": "Rete testis, urethra, epididymis and vas deferens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rete testis, vasa efferentia, seminal vesicle and vas deferens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rete testis, vasa efferentia, epididymis and vas deferens", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rete testis, vasa efferentia, epididymis and seminal vesicle", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Rete testis, Vasa efferentia, epididymis and vas deferens',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1427,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Which one is the correct statements for logistic model of population growth?<br>I. As population increases the competition goes on increasing.<br>II. All individuals have same effect on population growth.<br>III. There are limited natural resources.<br>IV. Population growth rate increases as the size of population approaches the carrying capacity.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statement for logistic population growth<br>I. As population increases the competition goes on increasing.<br>III. There are limited natural resources.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1428,'biology',103,969,2256,'Select the correct answer<br>i. Computed tomography uses $\\mathrm{X}$-rays to generate a three-dimensional image of the internals of an object.<br>ii. MRI uses strong magnetic fields and nonionising radiations to accurately detect pathological and physiological changes in the living tissue.<br>iii. Antibodies against cancer-specific antigens are also used for detection of certain cancers.','[{"text": "Only $i$ is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii, iii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statement i: Computed tomography uses X-rays to generate a three-dimensional image of the internals of an object.<br>Statement ii: MRI uses strong magnetic fields and non-ionising radiations to accurately detect pathological and physiological changes in the living tissue.<br>Statement iii: Antibodies against cancer -specific antigens are also used for detection of certain cancers.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1429,'biology',106,1353,3255,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The number of fungi species in the world is less than the combined total of the species of fishes, amphibians, reptiles and mammals.<br></div><div class="column-right">Conventional taxonomic methods are not suitable for identifying microbial species.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement B is correct and statement A is wrong..The number of fungi species in the world is more than the combined total of the species of fishes, amphibians, reptiles and mammals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1430,'biology',100,553,1107,'With reference to human sperm, match the Column – I with Column – II.<br>Choose the correct option from the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Head<br>B. Acrosome<br>C. Middle piece<br>D. Tail</div><div class="column-right">P. Filled with enzyme<br>Q. Contains mitochondria<br>R. Sperm motility<br>S. Contains haploid nucleus</div></div>','[{"text": "A – S, B – R, C – P, D – Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – S, C – R, D – P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – R, B – Q, C – S, D – P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – S, B – P, C – Q, D – R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-S, B-P, C-Q, D-R<br>Head - Contains haploid nucleus<br>Acrosome - Filled with enzyme<br>Middle piece - Contains mitochondria<br>Tails - Sperm motility',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1431,'biology',103,969,2256,'Which of the following is a non -invasive test for diagnosis of cancer?','[{"text": "PAP smear", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mammography", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Barium test", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PSA", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A Barium swallow is a test that may be used to determine the cause of painful swallowing, difficulty with swallowing, abdominal pain, bloodstained vomit, or unexplained weight loss. PAP smear is a screening procedure for cervical cancer.PSA test is a blood test used primarily to screen for prostrate cancer.<br>A mammography is an X-ray picture of the breast. It can be used to check for breast cancer in women who have no signs or symptoms of the disease.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1432,'biology',105,1283,3102,'Consider the following statements.<br>I. Brood parasitism in birds is an example of parasitism in which the parasitic bird lays its eggs in the nest of its host and host incubates them.<br>II. During the course of evolution, the eggs of the parasite bird have evolved to resemble the host\'s eggs in size and colour and reduce the chances of the host bird detecting the foreign eggs and removing them from the nest.','[{"text": "I is true, but II is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II is true, but I is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are true", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both I and II are false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I. Brood parasitism in birds is an example of parasitism in which the parasitic bird lays its eggs in the nest of its host and host incubates them.<br>II. During the course of evolution, the eggs of the parasite bird have evolved to resemble the host\'s eggs in size and colour and reduce the chances of the host bird detecting the foreign eggs and removing them from the nest. Both are true statement.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1433,'biology',106,1353,3255,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">India is one of the 12 mega diversity countries of the world.<br></div><div class="column-right">Nearly 45,000 species of plants and triple as many of animals have been recorded from India.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement A is correct and statement B is wrong. Nearly 45,000 species of plants and twice as many of animals have been recorded from India.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1434,'biology',100,552,1106,'In the female reproductive system, a tiny finger like structure which lies at the upper junction of the two labia minora above the urethral opening is called','[{"text": "Mons pubis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Clitoris", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vagina", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hymen", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Clitoris<br>Clitoris is a tiny finger like structure present at upper junction of labia minora and it is erectile in function.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1435,'biology',105,1283,3102,'Which statements are correct?<br>I. The human liverfluke, a nematode parasite, depends on two intermediate hosts (snail and fish) to complete its life cycle<br>II. Parasitic mode of life ensures free lodging and meals<br>III. The female mosquito is not considered parasite, however it needs our blood for reproduction.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Correct statement :<br>II) Parasitic mode of life ensures free lodging and meals<br>III. The female mosquito is not considered parasite, however it needs our blood for reproduction.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1436,'biology',103,969,2256,'Cancer of internal organs are detected by','[{"text": "Biopsy only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X-ray", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood test", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X ray, CT and MRI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Techniques like radiography (use of X-rays), CT (computed tomography) and MRI (magnetic resonance imaging) are very useful to detect cancers of the internal organs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1437,'biology',106,1353,3255,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">If we accept May\'s global estimates, only 33 per cent of the total species have been recorded so far.<br></div><div class="column-right">A large dfraction of these species faces the threat of becoming extinct even before we discover them</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement B is correct and statement A is wrong. If we accept May\'s global estimates, only 22 per cent of the total species have been recorded so far.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1438,'biology',100,554,1109,'Which of the following statements are correct regarding female reproductive cycle?<br>I. In non-primate mammals cyclical changes during reproduction are called oestrus cycle.<br>II. First menstrual cycle begins at puberty and is called menopause.<br>III. Lack of menstruation may be indicative of pregnancy.<br>IV. Cyclic menstruation extends between menarche and menopause.<br>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below','[{"text": "I and IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III and IV only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'First menstrual cycle that begins at puberty is called menarche.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1488,'biology',103,970,2257,'An opiate is type of drug that:','[{"text": "Relieves pain", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Causes stress", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Causes pain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Relieves anger", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A narcotic drug, also called a narcotic analgesic or opioid, is a medication prescribed by a doctor to relieve moderate to severe pain, either acute (short-term) or chronic (longerterm or continuous) pain.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1440,'biology',103,969,2256,'Match the following columns.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Biopsy<br>B. Oncogenic viruses<br>C. MRI<br>D. Computed tomography</div><div class="column-right">P. Use of X-rays to generate a three-dimensional image<br>Q. Strong magnetic fields and nonionising radiations<br>R. Viral oncogenes<br>S. A piece of the suspected tissue cut into thin sections, stained and examined under microscope</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - S,B - P,C - R,D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - S,B - R,C - Q,D - P}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R,B - S,C - P,D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q, B - S, C - P, D - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Biopsy - a piece of the suspected tissue cut into thin sections is stained and examined under microscope<br>B. Oncogenic viruses - viral oncogenes (Cancer causing viruses called oncogenic viruses have genes called viral oncogenes)<br>C. MRI - strong magnetic fields and nonionising radiations (MRI uses strong magnetic fields and non-ionising radiations to accurately detect pathological and physiological changes in the living tissue)<br>D. Computed tomography - uses X-rays to generate a three-dimensional image of the internals of an object.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1441,'biology',106,1354,3256,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The diversity of plants and animals is uniform throughout the world.<br></div><div class="column-right">In general, species diversity decreases as we move away from the equator towards the poles.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement B is correct and statement A is wrong. The diversity of plants and animals is not uniform throughout the world but shows a rather uneven distribution.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1442,'biology',100,552,1106,'Given below are two statements:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Vas deferens receives a duct from seminal vesicle and opens into urethra as the ejaculatory duct.</div><div class="column-right">The cavity of the cervix is called cervical canal which along with vagina forms birth canal.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are true.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is true.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement A and statement B both are correct.<br>Vas deferens receives a duct from seminal vesicle and opens into urethra as the ejaculatory duct. The cavity of cervix is called cervical canal which along with vagina forms the birth canal.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1443,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Which of the following is correct?','[{"text": "Very small animals are rarely found in polar regions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Archaebacteria can flourish in hot springs and deep sea hydrothermal vents where temperature is above $100^{\\\\circ} \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'(1) Very small animals are rarely found in polar regions<br>(2) Archaebacteria can flourish in hot springs and deep sea hydrothermal vents where temperature is above $100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1444,'biology',103,969,2256,'Treatment and detection of cancer can be done by','[{"text": "Chemotherapy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Radiography", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Surgery", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The common approaches for treatment of cancer are surgery, radiation therapy and immunotherapy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1445,'biology',106,1354,3256,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">With very few exceptions, tropics (latitudinal range of $23.5^{\\circ} \\mathrm{N}$ to $23.5^{\\circ} \\mathrm{S}$ ) harbour more species than temperate or polar areas.<br></div><div class="column-right">New York at $41^{\\circ} \\mathrm{N}$ has 205 species of birds.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement A is correct and statement B is wrong.New York at $41^{\\circ} \\mathrm{N}$ has 105 species.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1446,'biology',100,555,1112,'Read the Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct options given below:<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Endometrium is necessary for implantation of blastocyst<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In the absence of fertilization, the corpus luteum degenerates that causes disintegration of endometrium.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are  true and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is false but  Reason is true", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both Assertion and Reason are correct.<br>Implantation is embedding of the blastocyst into endometrium of uterus.<br>Correct explanation of reason is<br>Corpus luteum secretes large amount of progesterone which is essential for maintenance of endometrium of uterus. In absence of fertilisation, the corpus luteum degenerates hence the decrease in the level of progesterone hormone will cause disintegration of endometrium leading to menstrual phase.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1447,'biology',105,1283,3102,'Which of the following is correct?','[{"text": "In general, herbivores and plants appear to be more adversely affected by competition than carnivores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brood parasitism is seen in cuckoo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'(1) In general, herbivores and plants appear to be more adversely affected by competition than carnivores.<br>(2) Brood parasitism is seen in cuckoo',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1448,'biology',103,969,2256,'Select the incorrect option amongst the following.<br>i. Radiotherapy ____ tumor cells are irradiated lethally.<br>ii. Chemotherapy ____ drugs are used to kill cancerous cells.<br>iii. MRI ____ detect pathological and physiological changes in the living tissue<br>iv. Computed tomography ____uses X-rays to generate a four-dimensional image of the internals of an object.','[{"text": "i", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iv", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Incorrect statement iv: Computed tomography uses X-rays to generate a threedimensional image of the internals of an object.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1449,'biology',106,1354,3256,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Greenland at $71^{\\circ} \\mathrm{N}$ only 56 species of birds.<br></div><div class="column-right">Colombia located near the equator has nearly 1,400 species of birds</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. Colombia located near the equator has nearly 1,400 species of birds while Greenland at $71^{\\circ} \\mathrm{N}$ only 56 species.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1450,'biology',100,553,1107,'$2 \\mathrm{n}=16$ in a primary spermatocyte which is in metaphase of first meiotic division. What shall be the total number of chromatids in each of the secondary spermatocyte?','[{"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "16", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "24", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "32", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In spermatogenesis, primary spermatocyte undergoes meiosis I and as a result of which two haploid secondary spermatocytes are formed. It is given that $\\mathrm{n}=8$ that is the secondary spermatocyte possesses 8 chromosomes and 16 chromatids as each chromosome divides along its length into two chromatids.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1451,'biology',105,1279,3096,'In polar seas, aquatic $\\underline{a}$ like $\\underline{b}$ have a thick layer of fat called $\\underline{\\mathrm{c}}$ below their skin that acts as an $\\underline{\\mathrm{d}}$ and reduces loss of body heat.','[{"text": "a-fishes, b-sharks, c - clasper, d - conductor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a-mammals, b-seals,c-blubber, d - insulator", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a-fishes, b-seals, c - blubber, d - insulator", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a - mammals, b-seals, c - blubber, d- conductor", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'a - mammals, b - seals, $\\mathrm{c}$ - blubber, d - insulator.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1452,'biology',103,969,2256,'$\\alpha$ - interferon is given to the patients of cancer with the aim of','[{"text": "Potentiating immune system and destroying tumour cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metastasing cancerous cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Curing cancerous cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Preventing replication of ocogenes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The patients are given substances called biological response modifiers such as $\\alpha$-interferon which activates their immune system and helps in destroying the tumor.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1453,'biology',106,1354,3256,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">India, with much of its land area in the tropical latitudes, has more than 1,200 species of birds.<br></div><div class="column-right">A forest in a tropical region like Equador has up to 12 times as many species of vascular plants as a forest of equal area in a temperate region like the Midwest of the USA.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement $A$ is correct and statement $B$ is wrong.A forest in a tropical region like Equador has up to 10 times as many species of vascular plants as a forest of equal area in a temperate region like the Midwest of the USA.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1454,'biology',100,551,1105,'Column I contains terms and column II contains definitions. Match them correctly and choose the right answer.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Parturition<br>B. Gestation<br>C. Ovulation<br>D. Implantation<br>E. Conception</div><div class="column-right">P. Attachement\nof zygote to\nendometrium<br>Q. Release of\negg from\nGraffian\nfollicle<br>R. Delivery of\nbaby from\nuterus<br>S. Duration\nbetween\npregnancy and\nbirth<br>T. Formation of\nzygote by\nfusion of the\negg and\nsperms<br>U. Stoppage of\novulation and\nmenstruation</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q; B - S; C - P; D - T; E - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - S; B - R; C - P; D - T; E - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - T; B - P; C - Q; D - R; E - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R; B - S; C - Q; D - P; E - T}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Parturition, also called childbirth is a process of bringing forth a child from the uterus, or womb.<br>Gestation is defined as the time between conception and birth. A fetus grows and develops in the womb during gestation.<br>Ovulation is the release of eggs from the ovaries. In humans, this event occurs when the ovarian follicles rupture and release the secondary oocyte ovarian cells.<br>Implantation is the stage of pregnancy at which the embryo adheres to the wall of the uterus.<br>Conception is the time when sperm travels up through the vagina, into the uterus, and fertilizes an egg found in the fallopian tube to form zygote.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2011,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1455,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Read the following statements and find out the incorrect statement','[{"text": "Microbes / archaebacteria flourish in hot springs and deep sea hydrothermal vents where temperature exceed $100^{\\\\circ} \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Many fish thrive in Antarctic waters where the temperature is always below zero", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A large variety of marine invertebrates and fish live at great depths in the ocean where the pressure could be 100 times than the normal atmospheric pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Desert lizard have physiological ability that mammals have to deal with high temperature of their habitat", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Desert lizard have physiological ability that mammals have to deal with high temperature of their habitat is incorrect statement.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1456,'biology',103,969,2256,'$\\alpha$ - interferons are used in the treatment of','[{"text": "Bacterial infections", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Typhoid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pneumonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cancer", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Interferon alpha helps stimulate the body\'s immune system to fight some types of cancer by strengthening the immune system, reducing the ability of the cancer cells to defend themselves from the immune system and by slowing down or stopping the cancer cells from dividing.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1475,'biology',105,1283,3101,'The feeding efficiency of one species might be reduced due to the interfering and inhibitory presence of the other species, even if resources are abundant then it is called','[{"text": "Resource partitioning", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Competitive release", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interference competition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Competitive exclusion", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In competition, organisms use up resources directly. Once used, the resource is no longer available for other species to use. In interference competition, one organism prevents other organisms from using the resource.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1457,'biology',106,1354,3256,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Amazonian rain forest in North America has the greatest biodiversity on earth- it is home to more than 40,000 species of plants, 13,000 of fishes.<br></div><div class="column-right">There is more solar energy available in the tropics, which contributes to higher productivity</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The largely tropical Amazonian rain forest in South America has the greatest biodiversity on earth-it is home to more than 40,000 species of plants, 3,000 of fishes, 1,300 of birds, 427 of mammals, 427 of amphibians, 378 of reptiles and of more than 1,25,000 invertebrates.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1458,'biology',100,553,1108,'In humans, what is the ratio of number of gametes produced from one male primary sex cell to the number of gametes produced from one female primary sex cell?','[{"text": "$1: 1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1: 3$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1: 4$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4: 1$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Four viable sperm cells are produced from one primary sex cell, only one viable egg cell is produced, due to the unequal division of cytoplasm and the formation of polar bodies.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1459,'biology',105,1280,3097,'In a laboratory there are 40 fruit flies last week and during experiment 4 fruit flies died in a week. Calculate the death rate.','[{"text": "0.1 individual per fruitfly per year", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.36 individual per fruitfly per week", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.4 individual per fruitfly per week", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.1 individual per fruitfly per week", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The death rate in the population during that period is $4 / 40=0.1$ individuals per fruitfly per week.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1460,'biology',103,969,2256,'Which cancer affects lymph glands and spleen?','[{"text": "Carcinoma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sarcoma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leukemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lymphoma", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sarcoma affects the tissue derived from mesoderm such as connective tissue. They include bone tumors, muscle tumor or cancer of lymph nodes and spleen (also called lymphoma).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1461,'biology',106,1354,3256,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Scientists estimate that in rain forests there might be at least two million insect species waiting to be discovered and named.<br></div><div class="column-right">Tropical regions subjected to frequent glaciations in the past, temperate latitudes have remained relatively undisturbed for millions of years</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement A is correct and statement B is wrong. Temperate regions subjected to frequent glaciations in the past, tropical latitudes have remained relatively undisturbed for millions of years.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1462,'biology',100,553,1107,'The hormone which acts on Sertoli cells and stimulates the process of spermiogenesis is:','[{"text": "Androgen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "LH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GnRH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "FSH", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Spermiogenesis is the final stage of spermatogenesis where the spermatids need to mature into motile sperm cells (spermatozoa). The main hormones which regulate spermatogenesis are testosterone and FSH (follicle stimulating hormone) and the Sertoli cells possess receptors for both these hormones. Thus, the Sertoli cells, which nurse the sperm cells in the testes mature when the FSH secreted by the anterior pituitary binds to its receptors..',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1463,'biology',105,1283,3100,'No predator can become proficient at acquiring prey because ____','[{"text": "Predators are too large to be fast enough", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prey populations evolve antipredatory traits", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prey populations evolve more rapidly than predator populations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Predators are not as intelligent as their prey", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Predator & Prey both evolve to achieve their goals.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1464,'biology',103,970,2257,'A drug that speeds up your Central Nervous System is called a:','[{"text": "Opiate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimulant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inhalant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Depressant", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A stimulant is a medicine that increases neural activity in the brain by speeding up the central nervous system. Amphetamines, cocaine, crack, caffeine, nicotine, and ecstasy are a few stimulants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1465,'biology',106,1354,3256,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Speciation is generally a function of time.<br></div><div class="column-right">Constant environments promote niche specialisation and lead to a greater species diversity.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. Speciation is generally a function of time. Constant environments promote niche specialisation and lead to a greater species diversity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1476,'biology',103,970,2257,'Opioids are the drugs, which bind to specific opioid receptors present in our','[{"text": "Central nervous system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gastrointestinal system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Reproductive system", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Opioids are the drugs, which bind to specific opioid receptors present in our central nervous system and gastrointestinal tract.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1489,'biology',100,553,1107,'The process of conversion of non-motile spermatids into motile spermatozoa is called:','[{"text": "Spermiogenesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spermatogenesis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Spermiogenesis is the final stage of spermatogenesis. It is the development of haploid spermatids into sperms. No cell division occurs in spermiogenesis. Each spermatid becomes a single sperm cell. During this process, spherical spermatids transform into elongated, slender sperms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1466,'biology',100,551,1105,'Choose the correct sequence of events occur in human reproduction.','[{"text": "Gametogenesis $\\\\rightarrow$ Gestation $\\\\rightarrow$<br>Insemination $\\\\rightarrow$ Fertilization $\\\\rightarrow$<br>Implantation $\\\\rightarrow$ Parturition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametogenesis $\\\\rightarrow$ Insemination $\\\\rightarrow$<br>Gestation $\\\\rightarrow$ Implantation $\\\\rightarrow$<br>Fertilization $\\\\rightarrow$ Parturition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametogenesis $\\\\rightarrow$ Insemination $\\\\rightarrow$<br>Fertilization $\\\\rightarrow$ Implantation $\\\\rightarrow$<br>Gestation $\\\\rightarrow$ Parturition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gestation $\\\\rightarrow$ Gametogenesis $\\\\rightarrow$<br>Insemination $\\\\rightarrow$ Implantation $\\\\rightarrow$<br>Fertilization $\\\\rightarrow$ Parturition", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct sequence of events occur in human reproduction is: Gametogenesis insemination fertilisation implantation gestation parturition<br>Insemination is the process by which semen is released from the penis into the vagina during copulation (coitus).<br>Fertilisation is a process in which ovum fuses with the sperm to form the zygote that eventually forms the blastocyst.<br>About 6 days after fertilization, the blastocyst loosely attaches to the endometrium in a process called implantation.<br>The process of development of embryo is called gestation.<br>Labour or parturition is the process by which the foetus is expelled from the uterus through the vagina, also referred to as giving birth.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1467,'biology',105,1281,3098,'In 2000, for each of the 14 million people present in a country, 0.036 were born and 0.016 died during the year. Using exponential equation, the number of people present in 2010 is predicted as','[{"text": "14 million", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2.8 million", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "16.8 million", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.20 million", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Exponential equation<br>$\\begin{aligned}& \\mathrm{dN}-\\mathrm{dt}=(\\mathrm{b}-\\mathrm{d}) \\times \\mathrm{N} \\\\& \\mathrm{dN} / \\mathrm{dt}=(0.036-0.016) \\times 14 \\\\& =0.020 \\times 14 \\\\& \\mathrm{dN} / 10=0.28 \\\\& \\mathrm{dN}=0.28 \\times 10 \\\\& \\mathrm{dN}=2.8\\end{aligned}$<br>So, 14 million +2.8 million<br>$=16.8$ million',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1468,'biology',103,970,2257,'A drug that is sedative is called a:','[{"text": "Depressant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Opiate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimulant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hallucinogen", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Sedatives, or central nervous system depressants, are a group of drugs that slow brain activity. People use these drugs to help them calm down, feel more relaxed, and get better sleep.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1469,'biology',106,1354,3257,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The great German naturalist and geographer Alexander von Humboldt observed that within a region species richness increased with increasing explored area, without any limit.<br></div><div class="column-right">The relation between species richness and area for a wide variety of taxa (angiosperm plants, birds, bats, freshwater fishes) turns out to be a rectangular hyperbola.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1470,'biology',100,551,1105,'Which one of these is not an accessory gland in male reproductive system?','[{"text": "Prostate gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seminal vesicle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cowper\'s gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bartholin\'s gland", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In female reproductive system, Bartholin\'s (vestibular) glands are present on either side of the vaginal orifice which open by ducts into a groove between the hymen and labia minora. They produce a small quantity of mucus during sexual arousal and intercourse that adds to cervical mucus and provides lubrication.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1471,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Which one provide the evidence for the occurrence of competition in nature?','[{"text": "Resource partitioning", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Competitive release", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mac Arthur experiment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Competitive release is a situation in which an organism is relieved of the stresses associated with competition.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1472,'biology',103,970,2257,'A drug that alters your thoughts, moods and senses is a:','[{"text": "Depressant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimulant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inhalant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hallucinogen", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Hallucinogens are drugs that alter thoughts, perceptions, and feelings. While using these substances, people may experience hallucinations, where they have sensations or perceptions that are not real.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1473,'biology',106,1354,3257,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The species-area relationships among the entire continents, the Z values in the range of 0.6 to 1.2 .</div><div class="column-right">The species-area relationship of mammals in the tropical forests of different continents, the slope is found to be 1.15 .</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. After analysing the species-area relationships among very large areas like the entire continents, it is found that the slope of the line to be much steeper ( $Z$ values in the range of 0.6 to 1.2 ). For example, for frugivorous (fruit-eating) birds and mammals in the tropical forests of different continents, the slope is found to be 1.15 .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1474,'biology',100,551,1105,'Which one of the following characters favours the process of normal spermatogenesis in human male?','[{"text": "Descent of testes into scrotum.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Testes remain in the abdominal cavity.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Infection by mumps virus during childhood.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increased scrotal temperature.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Testes are male gonads which produce sperms and secrete hormones. The testes are contained in sacs called scrotum, which is connected to the abdomen via inguinal canals. The cremaster and dartos muscles of the scrotum help regulate the temperature (2$2.5^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ less than that of normal internal body temperature) of the testes. This is important for spermatogenesis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1477,'biology',106,1355,3258,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">For many decades, ecologists believed that communities with more species, generally, tend to be less stable than those with less species.<br></div><div class="column-right">A stable community should not show too much variation in productivity from year to year.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement A is wrong and Statement B is correct. For many decades, ecologists believed that communities with more species, generally, tend to be more stable than those with less species.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1478,'biology',100,552,1106,'Accessory ducts of reproductive system of human female include:','[{"text": "Oviduct, uterus and vagina", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oviduct, ovaries and ovarian ligaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oviduct, ovaries and mammary glands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovaries, uterus and vagina", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Female accessory ducts include oviducts, uterus and vagina.<br>Females have two fallopian (uterine) tubes, or oviducts, They provide a route for sperm to reach an ovum and transport secondary oocytes and fertilised ova from the ovaries to the uterus.<br>Uterus (womb) serves as part of the pathway for sperm deposited in the vagina to reach the uterine tubes. It is also the site of implantation of a fertilised ovum, development of the foetus during pregnancy, and labour.<br>The vagina extends from the exterior of the body to the uterine cervix. It is the receptacle for the penis during sexual intercourse, the outlet for menstrual flow and the passageway for childbirth.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1479,'biology',105,1277,3094,'In estuaries, salinity levels typically decline in the rainy season and rise during the summer. Which organisms are adapted to live in such environments?','[{"text": "Stenohaline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homeothermic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Euryhaline", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stenothermal", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Euryhaline organisms can tolerate wide range of salinities.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1480,'biology',103,970,2257,'Smack is chemically .....A.... which is white and odourless and crystalline in nature. This is obtained by .... B.... . Here A and B refers to','[{"text": "A - diacetylmorphine;$B$ - acetylation of morphine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - morphine;$B$ - acetylation of hashish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - diacetylmorphine;$B$ - acetylation of alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - diacetylmorphine;B - acetylation of hashish", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Smack is chemically diacetylmorphine which is a white, odourless, bitter crystalline compound. This is obtained by acetylation of morphine.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1481,'biology',106,1355,3258,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The \'rivet popper hypothesis\' is used by Stanford physiologist Paul Ehrlich.<br></div><div class="column-right">The biological wealth of our planet has been declining rapidly and the accusing finger is clearly pointing to human activities.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement B is correct and statement A is correct. The \'rivet popper hypothesis\' is used by Stanford ecologist Paul Ehrlich.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1482,'biology',100,553,1108,'In human females, the number of primary follicles left in each ovary at puberty is:','[{"text": "3000-30,000", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "30,000-60,000", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "60,000-80,000", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1,50,000-1,60,000", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'About 60,000-80,000 primary follicles are present in each ovary at puberty. Of these, very few mature and ovulate during a woman\'s reproductive lifetime.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1483,'biology',105,1280,3097,'In an area there are 200&nbsp;<em>Parthenium</em>&nbsp;plant but only a single huge banyan tree with a large canopy. The population density is measured in terms of','[{"text": "Number of biomass", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number of percent cover", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biomass or percent cover", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Number, biomass or percent cover", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In case of <em>Parthenium</em> plants and banyan tree, the percent cover or biomass is a more meaningful measure of the population size.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1484,'biology',103,970,2257,'Which of the following drug is extracted from the latex of poppy plant Papaver somniferum, generally taken by snorting and injection, is a depressant and slows down body functions?','[{"text": "LSD", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ganja", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Barbiturate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heroin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Heroin, commonly called smack is chemically diacetylmorphine which is a white, odourless, bitter crystalline compound. This is obtained by acetylation of morphine, which is extracted from the latex of poppy plant Papaver somniferum.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1485,'biology',106,1355,3258,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Paul Ehrlich showed that in his experiments, increased diversity contributed to higher productivity.<br></div><div class="column-right">David Tilman showed that in his experiments, increased diversity contributed to higher productivity.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement B is correct and statement A is wrong. Tilman found that plots with more species showed less year-to-year variation in total biomass. He also showed that in his experiments, increased diversity contributed to higher productivity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1486,'biology',100,555,1110,'Implantation is influenced by:','[{"text": "FSH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "LH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Progesterone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Relaxin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Progesterone is secreted by the corpus luteum.<br>It prepares the uterus for the implantation of a fertilized egg, controls the development of the foetus in the uterus.<br>The hormone is responsible for the increase in the cell lining of the uterus leading to implantation and maintenance of pregnancy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1490,'biology',106,1355,3258,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Paul Ehrlich was a German naturalist and geographer.<br></div><div class="column-right">Alexander von Humboldt was a Stanford ecologist.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the statements are wrong. Paul Ehrlich was a Stanford ecologist. Alexander von Humboldt was a German naturalist and geographer.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1491,'biology',105,1277,3094,'Read the following statements and find out the incorrect statement','[{"text": "Mango tree do not and cannot grow in tropical countries like Canada and Germany", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Snow leopards are not found in kerala forests", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tuna fish are rarely caught beyond tropical latitudes in the ocean", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mango tree do not and cannot grow in tropical countries like Canada and Germany is incorrect statement.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1492,'biology',103,970,2257,'Read the following statements<br>I. Heroin, commonly called smack, is obtained by acetylation of morphine.<br>II. Heroin is a depressant and slows down body functions<br>III. Heroin is obtained from the latex of the poppy plant Papaver somniferum&nbsp;<br>IV. Morphine is an effective sedative and pain killer.<br>Mark the option which includes correct statements.','[{"text": "I &amp; II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III &amp; IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, IV are correct.<br>III.Morphine is obtained from the latex of the<br>poppy plant Papaver somniferum is the corrected statement.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1493,'biology',100,554,1109,'If in a normal menstruating woman, menses occur on $5^{\\text {th }}$ April, what will be the expected date of ovulation?','[{"text": "$10^{\\\\text {th }}$ April", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$18^{\\\\text {th }}$ April", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$29^{\\\\text {th }}$ April", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$14^{\\\\text {th }}$ April", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ovulation, the rupture of the mature (Graafian) follicle and the release of the secondary oocyte into pelvic cavity, usually occurs on day 14 to 16 in a 28 days cycle. Thus, a woman whose menses occur on $5^{\\text {th }}$ April, the ovulation is likely to occur on $18^{\\text {th }}$ of April.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1494,'biology',106,1356,3259,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The colonisation of tropical Pacific Islands by humans is said to have led to the extinction of more than 2,000 species of native birds.<br></div><div class="column-right">The IUCN Red List (2004) documents the extinction of 748 species in last 500 years.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. The colonisation of tropical Pacific Islands by humans is said to have led to the extinction of more than 2,000 species of native birds. The IUCN Red List (2004) documents the extinction of 784 species (including 338 vertebrates, 359 invertebrates and 87 plants) in the last 500 years.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1495,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Mutualism examples are<br>i. A wasp pollinating a fig flower<br>ii. Rhizobium and its leguminous plant<br>iii. Lichen<br>iv. Mycorrhizae<br>v. Moth and yucca<br>vi. Ophyrus and bee','[{"text": "i, ii. iii. iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii, iv, vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii, iv, v, vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'It is an example of mutualism where both plant and animal are benefited. Plants need the help of animals for pollinating their flowers and dispersing their seeds. Plants offer rewards or fees in the form of pollen and nectar for pollinators and juicy and nutritious fruits for seed dispersers.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1496,'biology',103,970,2257,'\'Smack\' is a drug obtained from the','[{"text": "Latex of <i>Papaver somniferum</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Leaves of <i>Cannabis sativa</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flowers of <i>Dhatura pinata</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fruits of <i>Erythroxylum coca</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Smack also called heroin is an opioid drug obtained from latex of poppy(<i>Papaver somniferum</i>) plant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1497,'biology',100,553,1107,'Identifying the cells represents as P, Q, R and S in the given schematic representation of spermatogenesis.','[{"text": "P - Spermatozoa<br>Q - Spermatids<br>R - Secondary spermatocyte<br>S - Primary spermatocyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P - Primary spermatocyte<br>Q - Secondary spermatocyte<br>R - Spermatids<br>S - Spermatozoa", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "P - Secondary spermatocyte<br>Q - Spermatids<br>R - Spermatozoa<br>S - Primary spermatocyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P - Secondary spermatocyte<br>Q - Primary spermatocyte<br>$\\\\mathrm{R}$ - Spermatozoa<br>S - Spermatids", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/biology/100_1497_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/100_1497_question_1.png'),
(1498,'biology',106,1356,3259,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Some examples of recent extinctions include the dodo (Mauritius), quagga (Australia), thylacine (Africa), Steller\'s Sea Cow (Russia) and three subspecies (Bali, Javan, Caspian) of lion<br></div><div class="column-right">Extinctions across taxa are not random.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement B is correct and statement A is wrong. Some examples of recent extinctions include the dodo (Mauritius), quagga (Africa), thylacine (Australia), Steller\'s Sea Cow (Russia) and three subspecies (Bali, Javan, Caspian) of tiger. Careful analysis of records shows that extinctions across taxa are not random.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1499,'biology',105,1279,3096,'The adjustment of pupil of our eye to light intensity is an example of','[{"text": "Eutropy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Steady state", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adaptation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The pupil is an opening that lets light into your eye. Since most of the light entering your eye does not escapes your pupil appears black. In dim light your pupil expands to allow more light to enter your eye, in bright light it contracts.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1501,'biology',100,553,1108,'Identify the cells represented as p, q, r and s in the schematic representation of Oogenesis, shown below and choose the correct option.','[{"text": "p- Ovum, q- Oogonia, r - Primary oocyte, $\\\\mathrm{s}$ - Secondary Oocyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "p - Secondary Oocyte, q - Primary Oocyte, r - Ovum, s - Oogonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "p - Ovum, q - Secondary Oocyte, r - Primary Oocyte, s - Ovum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "p - Oogonia, q - Primary Oocyte, r - Secondary Oocyte, s - Ovum", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'p - Oogonia, q - Primary Oocyte,<br>r - Secondary Oocyte, s - Ovum',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/100_1501_question_1.png'),
(1502,'biology',106,1356,3259,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Some groups like amphibians appear to be more vulnerable to extinction.<br></div><div class="column-right">Presently, 12 per cent of all bird species, 23 per cent of all mammal species, 32 per cent of all amphibian species in the world face the threat of extinction.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. Careful analysis of records shows that extinctions across taxa are not random; some groups like amphibians appear to be more vulnerable to extinction. Presently, 12 per cent of all bird species, 23 per cent of all mammal species, 32 per cent of all amphibian species and 31per cent of all gymnosperm species in the world face the threat of extinction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1503,'biology',105,1283,3101,'A high density of Elephant population in an area can result in','[{"text": "Predation on one another", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutualism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intraspecific competition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Interspecific competition", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Intraspecific competition is the competition occurring between the same species hence there will be more number of same species in an area.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1504,'biology',103,970,2257,'The plant depicted in the diagram produces the drug.','[{"text": "LSD", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Smack", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coca", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ganja", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'It is Opium (poppy) plant',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/103_1504_question_1.png'),
(1505,'biology',100,552,1106,'When the fallopian tube is blocked at ampullary region, the ovum fails to move from','[{"text": "Isthmus to infundibulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovary to ampulla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isthmus to Uterus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Infundibulum to Isthmus", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The ampulla is located in between the infundibulum and isthmus. The infundibulum picks the secondary oocyte from the ovary with the help of fimbriae.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1506,'biology',106,1356,3259,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The last twenty years have witnessed the disappearance of 27 species.<br></div><div class="column-right">31per cent of all gymnosperm species in the world face the threat of extinction.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. The last twenty years alone have witnessed the disappearance of 27 species. 31per cent of all gymnosperm species in the world face the threat of extinction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1507,'biology',105,1283,3103,'Which of the following is not an example of commensalism?','[{"text": "Sea anemone and clown fish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Orchid on mango branch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tapeworm and man", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cattle egret and grazing cattle", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Commensalism is a symbiotic association between two organisms in which one benefits and the other derives neither benefit nor harm. Some of these include clownfish and sea anemones, epiphytes (orchid) on mango branch, cattle egret and grazing cattle Tapeworm is an endoparasite in man.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1508,'biology',103,970,2257,'Identify the molecule shown below','[{"text": "Chemical structure of morphine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chemical structure of marijuana", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemical structure of coca", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemical structure of LSD", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'It is chemical structure of morphine.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/103_1508_question_1.png'),
(1509,'biology',100,556,1114,'Match the months listed in Column - I write the organogenesis of foetus in Column - II<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. First month<br>B. Second month<br>C.  Fifth month<br>D. Six month</div><div class="column-right">P. Separation of eye lids<br>Q. Hairs on head<br>R. Heart<br>S. Limbs and Digits</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  P , D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  R, C  -  S , D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  Q, C  -  R , D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  Q , D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The heart is the organ that is formed after one month of pregnancy. and the first sign of a developing fetus is the sound of the heartbeat. The end of the second month marks the development of the limbs and digits. The second trimester or after 12 weeks the major organ systems such as the limbs, external genitalia are formed. The second trimester or the end of 24 weeks is characterized by the development of the hair,eye-lids',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1510,'biology',106,1356,3259,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">During the long period $(>3$ billion years) since the origin and diversification of life on earth there were five episodes of mass extinction of species.<br></div><div class="column-right">The current species extinction rates are estimated to be 100 to 1,000 times faster than in the pre-human times and our activities are not responsible for the faster rates.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statememt A is correct and statement B is wrong. the current species extinction rates are estimated to be 100 to 1,000 times faster than in the pre-human times and our activities are responsible for the faster rates.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1512,'biology',103,970,2257,'Which one includes all other three?','[{"text": "Cannabinoids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Marijuana", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ganja", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Charas", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cannabinoids are a group of chemicals, which interact with cannabinoid receptors present principally in the brain. The flower tops, leaves and the resin of cannabis plant are used in various combinations to produce marijuana, hashish, charas and ganja.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1513,'biology',100,553,1107,'In the given diagram of human sperm, identify the functions of the labelled parts, $a, b$ and $c$.','[{"text": "$a \\\\rightarrow$ Helps in penetration of sperm into ovum<br>$\\\\mathrm{b} \\\\rightarrow$ Helps in movement of sperm<br>$\\\\mathrm{c} \\\\rightarrow$ Provides energy for the movement of sperms into the female reproductive tract", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$a \\\\rightarrow$ Helps in penetration of sperm into ovum<br>$b \\\\rightarrow$ Provides energy for the movement of sperm<br>$\\\\mathrm{c} \\\\rightarrow$ Helps in movement of sperm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$a \\\\rightarrow$ Helps in movement of sperm<br>$b \\\\rightarrow$ Helps in penetration of sperm into<br>ovum<br>$\\\\mathrm{c} \\\\rightarrow$ Provides energy for the movement of sperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{a} \\\\rightarrow$ Provides energy for the movement of sperm<br>$b \\\\rightarrow$ Helps in movement of sperm<br>$\\\\mathrm{c} \\\\rightarrow$ Helps in penetration of sperm into ovum", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'a- acrosome - has enzymes that help in penetration of sperm into ovum.<br>b- mitochondria provides energy ,<br>c- tail - movement of sperm',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/100_1513_question_1.png'),
(1514,'biology',106,1356,3259,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Loss of biodiversity in a region may lead to incline in plant production and high resistance to environmental perturbations such as drought.<br></div><div class="column-right">Ecologists warn that if the present trend of extinction of species continue, nearly half of all the species on earth might be mutated within the next 100 years.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In general, loss of biodiversity in a region may lead to decline in plant production, lowered resistance to environmental perturbations such as drought. Ecologists warn that if the present trends continue, nearly half of all the species on earth might be wiped out within the next 100 years.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1515,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Ecotone is:','[{"text": "A polluted area", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The bottom of a lake", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A zone of transition between two communities", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A zone of developing community", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A zone of transition between two communities',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1516,'biology',103,970,2257,'Cannabinoid receptors are present principally in','[{"text": "Brain", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neuron", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GIT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "CVS", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cannabinoids are a group of chemicals, which interact with cannabinoid receptors present principally in the brain. Cannabinoid receptors are those receptors which are mainly present in the brain but are also present in nearly all the organs of the body. They are the receptors that are responsible for the physiological functions as well as the functioning of the body. They are primarily found in the nervous system and brain region.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1517,'biology',100,557,1115,'Under the influence of oxytocin which layer of the uterus exhibits strong contractions during parturition?','[{"text": "Endometrium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myometrium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Perimetrium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Oxytocin acts on the endometrium of the uterus causing the contraction of the myometrium resulting in delivery of the foetus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1518,'biology',106,1356,3259,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Once covering more than 6 per cent of the earth\'s land surface, tropical rain forests now cover no more than 4 per cent.<br></div><div class="column-right">The Amazon rain forest is called the \'lungs of the planet\'.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement B is correct and statement A is wrong. Once covering more than 14 per cent of the earth\'s land surface, tropical rain forests now cover no more than 6 per cent.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
