(1549,'biology',100,554,1109,'In the given columns, column-I contain various phases of menstrual cycle and column-II contain its features. Select the correct match from the options given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Menstrual phase<br>B. Luteal phase<br>C. Follicular phase<br>D. Ovulatory phase</div><div class="column-right">P. Breakdown of\nendometrial lining\nof uterus along\nwith its blood\nvessels which form\nliquid that comes\nout of vagina.<br>Q. A temporary\nendocrine gland is\nformed and\nsecretes a hormone\nwhich maintains\nendometrium and\nimplantation of\nfertilized ovum and\nother events of\npregnancy.<br>R. Secretion of\nluteinizing\nhormone at its\nmaximum level\nand induces\nbreakdown of\nmature follicle to\nrelease the female\ngamete<br>S. Formation of\nmature Graafian\nfollicle and\nregeneration of\nendometrium of\nuterus.</div></div>','[{"text": "A-S,  B-Q,  C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P,  B-R, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P,  B-S, C-Q,  D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P,  B-Q,  C-S,  D-R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'a-i; b-ii; c-iv; d-iii',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1550,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Amazon forest is estimated to produce, through photosynthesis, 60 per cent of the total oxygen in the earth\'s atmosphere.<br></div><div class="column-right">Philosophically or spiritually, we need to realise that every species has an intrinsic value, even if it may not be of current or any economic value to us.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement A is correct and statement B is wrong. Amazon forest is estimated to produce, through photosynthesis, 20 per cent of the total oxygen in the earth\'s atmosphere',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1551,'biology',105,1282,3099,'Which one of the following organisms reproduces sexually only once in its life time?','[{"text": "Banana & Bamboo", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mango & Tomato", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tomato & Banana", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eucalyptus & Banana", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Banana plant is a monocarpic plant which reproduces usually only once in its life-time.<br>Bamboo plants also reproduces only once in its life time.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1552,'biology',103,970,2257,'One major side effect of snorting cocaine (coke) is:','[{"text": "It interferes transport of dopamine Hallucinations", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It calms the body by sedation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It depresses the brain activity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It relieves anxiety act as tranquilizer", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cocaine (or) cocaalkaloids are generally interferes N.S producing sense of Euphoria and increase energy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1553,'biology',100,556,1114,'Which of the following is not a uterine function?','[{"text": "Waste removal for the developing embryo.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nutritional support of the growing embryo.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Place of fusion of male and female gametes.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mechanical protection of the developing embryo.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Male and female gametes are fused in ampullary- isthmic junction of fallopian tube. Fusion of gametes is not the function of uterine wall. Fertilisation occurs in the fallopian tube.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1554,'biology',106,1357,3260,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Four hotspots in India are - Western Ghats and Sri Lanka, Indo-Burma and Himalaya<br></div><div class="column-right">India has 14 biosphere reserves, 90 national parks and 484 wildlife sanctuaries.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the statements are wrong. Three hotspots in India are - Western Ghats and Sri Lanka, Indo-Burma and Himalaya. India has 14 biosphere reserves, 90 national parks and 448 wildlife sanctuaries.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1555,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Autecology is the:','[{"text": "Relation of heterogenous populations to its environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Relation of an individual of a species to its environment", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Relation of a community to its environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Relation of a biome to its environment", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Relation of an individual to its environment is called autoecology. An individual is closest to the species hence<br>\' b \' is the correct answer.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1557,'biology',100,555,1111,'Presence of X X or X Y chromosomes in zygote depends on','[{"text": "Amount of yolk in the ovum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sex chromosome of the fertilizing ovum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The length of the sperm\'s tail", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sex chromosome of the fertilizing sperm", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ovum contains the haploid set of chromosomes with one of the $\\mathrm{X}$ chromosomes. The haploid set of chromosomes in the male gamete, sperm has either the $\\mathrm{X}$ or $\\mathrm{Y}$ chromosome. Thus, the sex of the foetus depends on the male gamete fertilizing the ovum.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1558,'biology',106,1357,3260,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Zoological parks, botanical gardens and wildlife safari parks are methods of ex-situ conservation.<br></div><div class="column-right">The Earth Summit held in Rio de Janeiro in 1992.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. Zoological parks, botanical gardens and wildlife safari parks are methods of ex-situ conservation.The historic Convention on Biological Diversity (\'The Earth Summit\') held in Rio de Janeiro in 1992, called upon all nations to take appropriate measures for conservation of biodiversity and sustainable utilisation of its benefits.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1559,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Biosphere is:','[{"text": "A component in the ecosystem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Composed of the plants present in the soil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Life in the outer space", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Composed of all living organisms present on earth which interact with the physical environment", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The thin zone of interaction of hydrosphere, atmosphere and troposphere; where living beings are found; is called biosphere.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1560,'biology',103,970,2257,'Anesthesia given during surgery is obtained from','[{"text": "<i>Datura</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Papaver somniferum</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Cannabis</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alcohol", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Morphine is a very effective sedative and painkiller, and is very useful in patients who have undergone surgery. Morphine is obtained from plant Papaver somniferum .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1561,'biology',100,555,1112,'Finger like projection, called chorionic villi, appear on the ____ after the  implantation.','[{"text": "Ampulla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trophoblast", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Infundibulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inner cell mass", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'After implantation, the trophoblast develops finger-like projections on its outside known called as chorionic villi, which are surrounded by the uterine tissue and maternal blood.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1562,'biology',106,1357,3260,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The World Summit on Sustainable Development held in 2020 in Johannesburg, South Africa<br></div><div class="column-right">Seeds of different genetic strains of commercially important plants cannot be kept for long periods in seed banks.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the statements are wrong. The World Summit on Sustainable Development held in 2002 in Johannesburg, South Africa.Seeds of different genetic strains of commercially important plants can be kept for long periods in seed banks.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1563,'biology',105,1279,3096,'According to Allen\'s Rule, the mammals from colder climates have:','[{"text": "Shorter ears and longer limbs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Longer ears and shorter limbs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Longer ears and longer limbs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shorter ears and shorter limbs", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Joel Asaph and Allen proposed this rule in 1877. According to this rule; the body shape and proportions of endotherms vary according to climatic temperature. In colder climate, the surface area is minimized to prevent heat loss and it is maximized in warm climate to promote heat loss. Endotherms in cold climate usually have small ears and small legs.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1564,'biology',103,970,2257,'Which one of the following is a stimulant?','[{"text": "Smack", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cocaine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heroin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Coca alkaloid or cocaine is obtained from coca plant Erythroxylum coca, native to South America. It interferes with the transport of the neuro-transmitter dopamine. Cocaine, commonly called coke or crack is usually snorted. It has a potent stimulating action on central nervous system, producing a sense of euphoria and increased energy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1565,'biology',100,557,1115,'Which of these is not an important component of initiation of parturition in humans?','[{"text": "Release of oxytocin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release of prolactin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Increase in estrogen and progesterone ratio", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synthesis of prostaglandins", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The signals for child birth (parturition) originate from the fully developed foetus and placenta which induce mild uterine contractions called foetal ejection reflex. This causes quick release of oxytocin from the maternal posterior lobe of pituitary gland which induces labour pains. Prostaglandins, progesterone and estrogen also play a role. Prolactin is the hormone which induces lactation and has no role in parturition.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1566,'biology',106,1356,3259,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> There is threat to the indigenous cat fish in our rivers<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> African cat fish (alien species) produces toxic effect for agriculture','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The African Catfish (Clarias gariepinus) has been posing a threat to indigenous varieties of catfish in Indian waters. It affects the native species by way of genetic impact, disease introduction, predation, competition, etc.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1567,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Seals have a thick layer of fat (blubber) below their skin that acts as an','[{"text": "Thermostat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Capacitor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Resistor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insulator", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Blubber is the fatty layer present between the skin and muscle of whales and other cetaceans. It acts as an insulator and protects the animal from heat loss and serves as a food reserve.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1568,'biology',103,970,2257,'Plants with hallucinogenic properties are','[{"text": "<i>Atropa belladonna</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Datura", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Papaver", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Atropa belladonna and Datura are wellknown plants with hallucinogenic properties. Atropa belladonna is a highly poisonous plant, also known as deadly nightshade. The plant contains a high level of alkaloids that cause hallucinations.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1569,'biology',100,558,1116,'Intensely lactating mothers do not generally conceive due to the','[{"text": "Suppression of gonadotropins.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hypersecretion of gonadotropins.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Suppression of gametic transport.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Suppression of fertilization.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Suckling induces a reduction in gonadotropin releasing hormone, luteinizing hormone and follicle stimulating hormone release, resulting in amenorrhea.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1570,'biology',106,1357,3260,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In-situ conservation is a type of biodiversity conservation<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It is the conservation of resources outside their natural habitat','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In situ conservation is on site conservation or conservation of genetic resources in their natural habitats.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1571,'biology',105,1277,3094,'What will happen to a well growing herbaceous plant in the forest if it is transplanted outside the forest in a park?','[{"text": "It will grow normally", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It will grow well because it is planted in the same locality", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It may not survive because of change in its micro climate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It grows very well because the plant gets more sunlight.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'It may not survive because of change in its micro climate',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1572,'biology',103,970,2257,'Tick mark the incorrect match with respect to the drug, source and its action.<br>\\[\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {{\\rm{Drug}}\\;\\;\\;\\;}&amp;{\\;\\;}&amp;{{\\rm{Action}}} \\end{array}\\]<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {{\\\\rm{Smack}}\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{{\\\\rm{Depressant}}} \\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {{\\\\rm{Cocaine}}}&amp;{\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{{\\\\rm{Sense}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{euphoria}}} \\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}<br>{{\\\\rm{Cocaine}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{{\\\\rm{Lung\\\\,cancer}}}<br>\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {{\\\\rm{Hashish}}}&amp;{\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{{\\\\rm{Hallucinations}}} \\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cocaine - Lung cancer is wrong, smoking of tobacco causes lung cancer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1573,'biology',100,558,1116,'During pregnancy degeneration of corpus lutem is prevented by the hormone','[{"text": "hCG", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "HPL", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "LH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Relaxin", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Human chorionic gonadotropin is a hormone produced primarily by syncytiotrophoblastic cells of the placenta during pregnancy. The hormone stimulates the corpus luteum to produce progesterone to maintain the pregnancy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1574,'biology',106,1357,3260,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Gene bank is important for conservation of crop variety and wild genetic resources.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Their utility in future crop improvement and forestation programmes','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both assertion and reason are correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1575,'biology',105,1276,3093,'On earth life also exists','[{"text": "Scorching Rajasthan desert", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rain-soaked Meghalaya forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Torrential streams", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of them',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1576,'biology',100,555,1110,'Which of the following human developmental stage becomes embedded in the uterine endometrium by a process called implantation and leads to pregnancy?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Figure (3) refers to blastocysts stage.<br>Blastocyst is embedded in the uterine<br>endometrium by a process called implantation and leads to pregnancy. It possesses an inner cell mass which subsequently forms the embryo. The outer layer of the blastocyst consists of cells collectively called the trophoblast. This layer surrounds the inner cell mass and a fluid filled cavity known as the blastocoel. The trophoblast gives rise to the placenta.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1587,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Amensalism is an association between two species where:','[{"text": "One species is harmed and other is benefitted", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One species is harmed and other is unaffected", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One species is benefitted and other is unaffected", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the species are harmed.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'One species is harmed and other is unaffected.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1588,'biology',103,970,2257,'Tobacco is obtained from dried leaves of','[{"text": "<i>Nicotiana tobacum</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Erythroxylum coca</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Cannabis sativa</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Cannabis indica</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The use of Tobacco is believed to be originated from America where it was smoked by Red Indians. Then, it gradually spread to all parts of the world.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1577,'biology',103,970,2257,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Opioids<br>B. Cannabinoids<br>C. Cocaine<br>D.<i>Atropa belladona</i></div><div class="column-right">P. Marijuana<br>Q. <i>Smack</i><br>R. Coke<br>S. Hallucinogens</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. Opioids - smack (Heroin is commonly called smack)<br>B. Cannabinoids - marijuana (The flower tops, leaves and the resin of cannabis plant are used in various combinations to produce marijuana, hashish, charas and ganja)<br>C. Cocaine - coke (Cocaine, commonly called coke or crack is usually snorted)<br>D. Atropa belladonna - hallucinogen (well- known plants with hallucinogenic properties are Atropa belladona and Datura)',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1578,'biology',106,1357,3260,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In a seed bank seeds are stored for long time.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Gene bank is option for conservation of rare genes','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Reason is not the correct explanation of assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1579,'biology',105,1280,3097,'What parameters are used for tiger census in our country\'s national parks and sanctuaries?','[{"text": "Pug marks only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pug marks and faecal pellets", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Faecal pellets only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Actual head counts", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pug marks and faecal pellets',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1580,'biology',103,970,2257,'Select the correct option from the following<br>i. These days cannabinoids are also being abused by some sportspersons.<br>ii. Cannabinoids are generally taken by inhalation and oral ingestion','[{"text": "Only i is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement i: Cannabinoids bring about euphoria, excitement, increased energy, sometimes uncontrolled laughter and dilation of pupil of eyes. These days cannabinoids are taken by some sports persons.<br>Statement ii: Cannabinoids are a group of chemicals, which interact with cannabinoid receptors present principally in the brain. Generally taken by inhalation and oral ingestion, these are known for their effects on cardiovascular system of the body.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1581,'biology',100,553,1107,'Which of the following statements is wrong?','[{"text": "The male germ cells undergo meiotic division leading to sperm formation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The function of male sex accessory ducts and glands are maintained by the testicular hormones.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence or absence of hymen is not a reliable indication of virginity.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "FSH act on Leydig cells and stimulates release of some factors which help in spermiogenesis.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'FSH acts on Sertoli cells and stimulates secretion of some factors which help in the process of spermiogenesis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1582,'biology',106,1357,3260,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Wild ass sanctuary is a unique habitat of Indian wild ass<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It is the remnant gene pool in the world','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'India Wild Ass (Equus hemionus khur) is one of the three surviving species of Wild Ass in the world. The other two are found in central Asia and in Tibet.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1583,'biology',105,1277,3094,'Identify euryhaline, Eury thermal animals','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Salmon}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{fish}}}&{\\\\rm{ - }}&{{\\\\rm{Shark}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Shark}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{\\\\rm{ - }}&{{\\\\rm{Cutla}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Salmon}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{fish}}}&{\\\\rm{ - }}&{{\\\\rm{Pigeon}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Ray}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{fish}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{\\\\rm{ - }}&{{\\\\rm{Rana}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Salmon fish and pigeon',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1584,'biology',103,970,2257,'Smoking increases ____ content in blood and reduces the concentration of haembound oxygen.<br>Fill the blank suitably','[{"text": "Carbon dioxide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbaminohaemoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbon monoxide", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Carboxylic acid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Smoking increases carbon monoxide (CO) content in blood and reduces the concentration of haembound oxygen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1585,'biology',106,1357,3260,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In National Park wild life is strictly protected<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In National park, activity such as forestry, grazing, cultivation are not allowed.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'National parks are for the betterment of Wildlife & biodiversity and here activities like forestry, poaching, hunting & grazing or Cultivation are not permitted.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1586,'biology',100,552,1106,'An inverted pear-shaped sac with a thick lining and muscles in the pelvic area where a fertilized egg or zygote comes to grow into a baby is called','[{"text": "Oviduct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uterus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vagina", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vulva", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The uterus is a female reproductive organ located between the bladder and the rectum, in the pelvic area. The main purpose of the uterus is to nourish a foetus prior to birth. In menstruating females, the ovaries release eggs which travel via the fallopian tubes to the uterus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1589,'biology',106,1357,3260,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Biodiversity is important to maintain ecosystem and biosphere of the world<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Biodiversity provides food for mankind and their pets','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Biodiversity conservation is important to preserved the continuity of food chains.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1590,'biology',100,554,1109,'Which of the following events is not associated with ovulation in human female?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{LH}}$ surge", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abrupt decrease in estradiol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Full development of Graafian follicle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release of secondary oocyte", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the middle of cycle (about 14th day), LH surge induces rupture of Graafian follicle and thereby the release of secondary oocyte (ovulation). Estradiol (estrogen) secretion does not decrease abruptly.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1591,'biology',105,1283,3102,'An interaction where one species is harmed while the other is unaffected is called','[{"text": "Commensalism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Competition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amensalism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Parasitism", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In amensalism, one species is inhibited by toxic secretion of another species. Inhibitor species is neither benefited nor harmed.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1592,'biology',103,970,2257,'Match the columns I and II.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <i>Datura</i><br>B. Cocaine<br>C. Opioids<br>D. Cannabinoids</div><div class="column-right">P. <i>Erythroxylum coca</i><br>Q. <i>Papaver somniferum</i><br>R. Hallucinogens<br>S. <i>Cannabisativa</i></div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. Datura - hallucinogen (well-known plants with hallucinogenic properties are Atropa belladona and Datura)<br>B. Cocaine - Erythroxylum coca (Coca alkaloid or cocaine is obtained from coca plant Erythroxylum coca, native to South America)<br>C. Opioids - Papaver somniferum (opioids are extracted from latex of plant Ppapver somniferum)<br>D. Cannabinoids - Cannabis sativa (Natural cannabinoids are obtained from the inflorescences of the plant Cannabis sativa)',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1593,'biology',106,1354,3256,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Biodiversity is not uniform throughout the world<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Biodiversity increases as we move from equator to polar region','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'There is decrease in biodiversity as we move from equator to the poles.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1594,'biology',100,553,1107,'Which of the following shows the correct sequence of events leading to the formation of mature sperm?','[{"text": "Spermatogonium $\\\\rightarrow$ Secondary spermatocyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Primary spermatocyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Spermatids $\\\\rightarrow$ Sperms.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spermatogonium $\\\\rightarrow$ Spermatids $\\\\rightarrow$ Secondary spermatocyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Primary spermatocyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Sperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spermatids $\\\\rightarrow$ Primary spermatocyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Secondary spermatocyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Spermatogonium $\\\\rightarrow$ Sperms.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spermatogonium $\\\\rightarrow$ Primary spermatocyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Secondary spermatocyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Spermatids $\\\\rightarrow$ Sperms.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A spermatogonium divides into two primary spermatocytes. Each primary spermatocyte duplicates its DNA and subsequently undergoes${\\rm{ meiosis - I}}$ to produce two haploid secondary spermatocytes. Each of the two secondary spermatocytes further undergoes ${\\rm{meiosis II}}$ to produce two haploid spermatids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1595,'biology',105,1277,3094,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Temperature is the most important ecologically relevant environmental factor.<br></div><div class="column-right">Snow leopards are found in Kerala forests</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Temperature is the most relevant environment factor. The temperature varies seasonally. The physiological functions, morphology and the geographical distribution of many plants and animals is governed by temperature.<br>Statement A is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1596,'biology',103,970,2257,'Chronic bronchitis is caused by the use of','[{"text": "Alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tobacco", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Opium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contaminated food", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Tobacco smoke contains smoke carbon monoxide, polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons like benzopyrene and tar. Carbon monoxide combines with haemoglobin in RBCs and reduces its oxygen carrying capacity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1597,'biology',106,1356,3259,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Natural fragmentation of habitat leads to speciation.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Artificial fragmentation of habitat leads to extinction of species.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both are correct, reason is not the correct explanation of the assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1598,'biology',100,553,1108,'How many ova and sperms would be produced from 100 secondary oocytes and 100 secondary spermatocytes during gametogenesis in human?','[{"text": "100 ova, 100 sperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "100 ova, 200 sperms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "50 ova, 100 sperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "200 ova, 200 sperms", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A secondary oocyte produces one ovum and one polar body. A secondary spermatocyte produces two spermatids, each of which develops into a spermatozoon.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1599,'biology',105,1280,3097,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Species are groups of potentially interbreeding natural populations that are isolated from other such groups.<br></div><div class="column-right">Population ecology is an important area because it links ecology to population genetics and evolution.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Population ecology is the sub field of ecology that deals with the dynamics of species populations and how these populations interact with the environment. It is an important area because it links the ecology to population genetics and responsible for evolution.<br>So, statement B is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1600,'biology',103,970,2257,'Because of smoking which kind of change occurs in blood?','[{"text": "Proportion of $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ decrease and in $\\\\mathrm{Hb}$ also $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ decreases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proportion of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ decreases and in $\\\\mathrm{Hb}$ proportion of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ increases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proportion of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ increases and in $\\\\mathrm{Hb}$ proportion of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ decreases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proportion of $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ increases and in $\\\\mathrm{Hb}$ proportion of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ decreases", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Consuming tobacco in the form of cigarettes, bidis and cigar is referred to as smoking. Tobacco addiction is due to nicotine present in it. The habit of excessive smoking may also cause throat and lung cancer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1601,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Which one of the following is not used for ex situ plant conservation?','[{"text": "Field gene banks", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed banks", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shifting cultivation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Botanical Garden", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Besides shifting cultivation, all others are types of ex-situ plant conservation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1602,'biology',100,553,1108,'Second meiotic division in secondary oocyte results in the formation of','[{"text": "First polar body and a diploid ovum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "First polar body and a haploid ovum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Second polar body and a diploid ovum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Second polar body and a haploid ovum", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Second meiotic division in secondary oocyte results in the formation of a second polar body & a haploid ovum (ootid).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1603,'biology',105,1283,3104,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Symbiosis is a kind of positive interaction<br></div><div class="column-right">Symbiosis is shown by mycorrhizae.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mycorrhizae are symbiotic relationships that form between fungi and plantsSymbiosis is a term describing any relationship or interaction between two dissimilar organisms.<br>The specific kind of symbiosis depends on whether either or both organisms benefit from the relationship.<br>So, both statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1604,'biology',103,970,2257,'Nicotine stimulates____ to release adrenaline and nor-adrenaline into blood circulation, both of which ____ blood pressure and ____ heart rate.','[{"text": "Adrenal gland, decrease, increase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenal gland, increase, decrease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenal gland, increase, increase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adrenal gland, decrease, decrease", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Nicotine stimulates adrenal gland to release adrenaline and nor-adrenaline into blood circulation, both of which raise blood pressure and increase heart rate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1605,'biology',106,1357,3260,'An example of ex-situ conservation is','[{"text": "National park", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed bank", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Wild sanctuary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sacred Grove", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A seed bank stores seeds to preserve genetic diversity; hence it is a type of gene bank.<br>One reason is to have on-hand the genes that plant breeders need to increase yield, disease resistance, drought tolerance, nutritional quality etc. of plants used in agriculture.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1606,'biology',100,553,1108,'Which of the following is surrounded by zona pellucida?','[{"text": "Oogonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polar body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpus luteum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary oocyte", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The zona pellucida is a glycoprotein thick non-cellular membrane surrounding the plasma membrane of an oocyte or secondary oocytes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1607,'biology',105,1276,3093,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Niche comprises of invariably defined range of conditions that an organism can tolerate, diversity in the resources it utilises and a distinct functional role in the ecological system<br></div><div class="column-right">Ecological niche is the total interaction of a species with its environment</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each organism has an invariably defined range of condition that it can tolerate, diversity in the resources it utilises and a distinct functional role in the ecological system, all these together comprise its ecological niche.<br>The species that share a different habitat but the same ecological niche are considered as the ecological equivalents .<br>• Different types of habitat are formed with the evolution of the species along with their exploitation of natural<br>• The role of the species in a community of the ecotone is defined as Niche.<br>• It involves both the species interaction with each other and the environmental as well as the physical interactions.<br>• It also summons the abiotic factors along with the biotic factors.<br>So, both are correct statement',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1608,'biology',103,970,2257,'Smoking is associated with increased incidence of','[{"text": "Cancers of lung, urinary bladder and throat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bronchitis, emphysema", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coronary heart disease, gastric ulcer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Smoking is associated with increased incidence of cancers of lung, urinary bladder and throat, bronchitis, emphysema, coronary heart disease, gastric ulcer, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1609,'biology',106,1356,3259,'A species facing extremely high risk of extinction in the immediate future is called','[{"text": "Vulnerable", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endemic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Critically endangered", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Extinct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Such species are known as critically endangered species.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1610,'biology',100,554,1109,'Which of the following hormone is required for the maintenance of corpus luteum?','[{"text": "Progesterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "FSH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "LH", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{LH}}$ is a luteinizing hormone which stimulates the formation and maintenance of corpus luteum. Corpus luteum secretes progesterone hormone during the latter half of the menstrual cycle which maintains endometrium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1611,'biology',105,1283,3100,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Predation is an interspecific interaction with a feeding strategy.<br></div><div class="column-right">Predators help in maintaining species diversity in a community</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Predation is an interspecific interaction with a feeding strategy i.e., one species (prey) is eaten up by another (predator). The number of predator usually depends upon the population of prey, but the later is also controlled by predators.<br>Predators also help in maintaining species diversity in a community, by reducing the intensity of competition among competing prey species".<br>So, both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1612,'biology',103,971,2258,'During what age is considered as adolescence period?','[{"text": "Between 12-18 months of age", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Between 12-18 years of age", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Between 2-18 years of age", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Between 12-8 years of age", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The period between 12-18 years of age may be thought of as adolescence period.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1613,'biology',106,1357,3260,'In which of the following both pairs have correct combination?','[{"text": "In-situ conservation: National Park Ex-situ conservation: Botanical Garden", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In-situ conservation : Cryopreservation Ex-situ conservation: Wildlife sanctuary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In-situ conservation: Seed Bank Ex-situ conservation: Sacred groves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In-situ conservation: Tissue culture Ex situ conservation: Sacred groves", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ex-situ conservation is the preservation of components of biological diversity outside their natural habitats. This involves conservation of genetic resources, as well as wild and cultivated or species, and draws on a diverse body of techniques and facilities.<br>In-situ conservation is the on-site conservation or the conservation of genetic resources in natural populations of plant or animal species, such as forest genetic resources.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(1614,'biology',100,554,1109,'Which of the following hormones attains a peak level in the middle of menstrual cycle?','[{"text": "LH and estrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "FSH and progesterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "FSH and LH", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Estrogen and progesterone", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both ${\\rm{LH}}$ and ${\\rm{FSH}}$ attain a peak level in the middle of menstrual cycle (about 14th day) resulting in ovulation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1615,'biology',105,1283,3100,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The invasive cactus was brought under control only after a cactus-feeding predator (a moth)<br></div><div class="column-right">The prickly pear cactus introduced into Australia in early 1930s caused havoc by spreading rapidly into millions of hectares of rangeland.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'They soon became an invasive species by rapidly spreading into millions of hectares of rangeland. This invasive cactus was finally brought under control only after a cactus-feeding predator called Cactoblastis cactorum from its natural habitat was introduced into the country.<br>Statement A is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1616,'biology',103,971,2258,'Withdrawal syndrome is characterised by','[{"text": "Anxiety, shakiness", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nausea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sweating", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Dependence is the tendency of the body to manifest a characteristic and unpleasant withdrawal syndrome if regular dose of drugs/alcohol is abruptly discontinued. This is characterised by anxiety, shakiness, nausea and sweating, which may be relieved when use is resumed again. In some cases, withdrawal symptoms can be severe and even life threatening and the person may need medical supervision.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1617,'biology',100,555,1110,'Which of the following is associated with pregnancy?','[{"text": "Lack of menstruation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Occurrence of menstrual flow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Low levels of estrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Low levels of progesterone", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During pregnancy all events of the menstrual cycle stop and there is no menstruation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1618,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Cryopreservation of gametes of threatened species in viable and fertile condition can be referred to as','[{"text": "In-situ conservation of biodiversity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Advanced ex-situ conservation of biodiversity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In-situ conservation by sacred groves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In-situ cryo-conservation of biodiversity", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cryopreservation is a type of ex-situ conservation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1619,'biology',105,1283,3103,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In commensalism, one organism is benefied and other is unaffected.<br></div><div class="column-right">Epiphyte on a mango branch is an example of commensalism.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Commensalism is a relationship between species in which one benefits and the other is unaffected. Humans are host to a variety of commensal bacteria in their bodies that do not harm them but rely on them for survival (e.g. bacteria that consume dead skin).<br>Epiphytes are plants that grow on other plants but do not use their nutrients. As a result, the connection between a mango tree and an orchid is a commensalism, in which one species benefits while the other is unaffected.<br>So, both statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1620,'biology',103,971,2258,'Alcohol is considered a','[{"text": "Stimulant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hallucinogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Relaxant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Depressant", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Alcohol is a drug. It is classed as a depressant, meaning that it slows down vital functions- resulting in slurred speech, unsteady movement, disturbed perceptions and an inability to react quickly.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1621,'biology',100,555,1110,'Blastomeres are daughter cells formed in the process of','[{"text": "Cleavage, when zygote undergoes mitotic division.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fertilization, when sperm enters in the cytoplasm of ovum.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Implantation, when blastocysts attached to the uterine endometrium.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametogenesis, when male and female gametes are produced by testis and ovary respectively.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Blastomeres are a type of cells produced by cleavage (cell division) of the zygote after fertilization and are an essential part of blastula formation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1622,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Which of the following is the most important cause of animals and plants being driven to extinction?','[{"text": "Over-exploitation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alien species invasion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Habitat loss and fragmentation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Co-extinction", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Habitat loss and fragmentation is the most important cause of extinction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1623,'biology',105,1283,3104,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Plants need the help of insects and animals for pollinating their flowers and dispersing their seeds.<br></div><div class="column-right">Plants offer rewards in the form of pollen and nectar for pollinators.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Plants need the help of insects and animals for pollinating their flowers and dispersing their seeds. Plants offer rewards in the form of pollen and nectar for pollinators and juicy and nutritious fruits for seed dispersers.<br>So, both statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1624,'biology',103,971,2258,'Alcohol addiction causes','[{"text": "Hepatitis A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hepatitis B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liver cirrhosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Emphysema", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Drinking alcohol heavily for numerous years causes alcoholic cirrhosis. The more alcohol that you consistently consume, the more quickly you may develop cirrhosis. Experts say the risk of liver cirrhosis increases in men if they drink at least three to five standard drinks per day for 10 years. The risk for liver cirrhosis increases for women if they drink at least two standards drinks per day.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1625,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Red list contains data or information on','[{"text": "All economically important plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plants whose products are in international trade", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Threatened species", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Marine vertebrates only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Red list data contains information on threatened species.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1626,'biology',100,556,1114,'What is correct regarding major features of embryonic development at various months of pregnancy?','[{"text": "Brain becomes first functional organ at the end of 1st month of pregnancy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eye lashes separate at the end of 2nd month of pregnancy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Major organ are formed by the end of 12 th week of pregnancy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$1 \\\\mathrm{st}$ movement of foetus is noticed in 3rd month of pregnancy.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Most of the major organ systems are formed by the end of first trimester (12 weeks) of pregnancy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1627,'biology',105,1277,3094,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Many species of small plants (herbs and shrubs) growing in forests are adapted to photosynthesise optimally under very low light conditions because they are constantly overshadowed by tall, canopied trees.<br></div><div class="column-right">Plants are never dependent on sunlight to meet their photoperiodic requirement for flowering</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Many species of small plants (herbs and shrubs) growing in forests are adapted to photosynthesise optimally under very low light conditions because they are constantly overshadowed by tall, canopied trees. Many plants are also dependent on sunlight to meet their photoperiodic requirement for flowering.<br>They need less than the critical duration of light (about 8-10 hours) and a continuous dark period (about 14-16 hours) to flower. The dark period is very critical for SDP plants and has to be continuous. These plants will not flower if the dark period is briefly interrupted by light.<br>Statement A is correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1628,'biology',103,971,2258,'Cirrhosis is caused by','[{"text": "Tobacco", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Opium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alcohol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cocaine", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The liver is the store house of glycogen but alcohol causes the storage of fat in the liver, a condition called fatty liver syndrome. Gradually, the liver hardens and dries up called cirrhosis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1629,'biology',100,553,1108,'Choose the correct combination of labelling the hormonal control of female reproductive system.','[{"text": "A-GnRH, B-FSH, C-LTH, D-uterus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-GnRH, B-LH/FSH, C-estrogen or progesterone, D-uterus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-GnRH, B-STH, C-LH, D-uterus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-GnRH, B-ACTH, C-LH, D-uterus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-GnRH, B-LH/FSH, C-estrogen or progesterone, D-uterus',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/100_1629_question_1.png'),
(1630,'biology',106,1357,3260,'The region of Biosphere Reserve which is legally protected and where no human activity is allowed is known as:','[{"text": "Buffer zone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transition zone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Restoration zone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Core zone", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Biosphere Reserves are representative parts of natural and cultural landscapes extending over large area of terrestrial or coastal/marine ecosystems with multipurpose activities. It has 3 zones<br>Core zone : It includes protected areas and human interference is restricted here.<br>Buffer zone: Might be an area for experimental research, or may involve ways to manage natural vegetation, agricultural land, forests, fisheries, etc. Hence, limited human activity can be found here.<br>Transition zone: It is the outer area of the reserve. Here local communities, conservation agencies, scientists, civil associations, cultural groups, businesses and other stakeholders agree to work together to manage and use the area in a sustainable way that will benefit the people who live there.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1631,'biology',105,1283,3102,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The eggs of the parasitic bird have evolved to resemble the host\'s egg in size and colour to reduce the chances of the host bird detecting the foreign eggs and ejecting them from the nest.<br></div><div class="column-right">Koel is the host and crow is the parasite</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The eggs of the parasitic bird have evolved to resemble the host\'s egg in size and colour to reduce the chances of the host bird detecting the foreign eggs and ejecting them from the nest.<br>The Asian koel like many of its related cuckoo kin is a brood parasite that lays its eggs in the nests of crows and other hosts, who raise its young. They are unusual among the cuckoos in being largely frugivorous as adults. The name koel is echoic in origin with several language variants<br>So, statement A is correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1632,'biology',103,971,2258,'Name two diseases that can be transferred due to drug abuse?','[{"text": "Malaria and AIDS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AIDS and hepatitis A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AIDS and hepatitis B", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Malaria and hepatitis B", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Intravenous drug administration increases the risk of contracting a serious and sometimes incurable disease exponentially. HIV, AIDS and Hepatitis B \\\\& C are the most common blood-borne diseases that are linked to drug use. The reason that these diseases can be so easily spread is because people share needles and drug equipment. Infected blood is drawn into the syringe and then injected along with the drug by the next user of the syringe.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1633,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Which one of the following is related to Exsitu conservation of threatened animals and plants?','[{"text": "Biodiversity hot spots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amazon rainforest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Himalayan region", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wildlife safari parks", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ex-situ conservation means conservation of threatened animals and plants by bringing them out from their natural habitat and placing in special setting where they can be protected and given special care. Zoological parks, botanical gardens and wildlife safari parks serve this purpose.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1634,'biology',100,552,1106,'The given figure shows the diagrammatic sectional view of female reproductive system with few structures marked as A, B, C, and D. Select the option which shows the correct identification of the structure with its characteristics.','[{"text": "A: Infundibulum, funnel shaped structure surrounded by finger like projections.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B: Ampulla, wider part of oviduct where fertilization occurs.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "C: Isthmus, it has a narrow lumen and joins with uterus.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D: Fimbriae, it collects ovum before\\novulation.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The structure marked as ${\\rm{A, B, C }}$ and ${\\rm{D}}$ in the given figure of female reproductive system are respectively isthmus, ampulla, infundibulum and fimbriae. Isthmus is the narrower part of the tube that links to the uterus. Ampulla is the part behind the infundibulum, where fertilization of ovum takes place. Infundibulum is a funnel shaped structure whose edges possess finger like projection called fimbriae. Fimbriae help in the collection of ovum after ovulation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/100_1634_question_1.png'),
(1635,'biology',105,1283,3100,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left"><em>Calotropis</em> growing in abandoned fields, produces highly poisonous cardiac glycosides</div><div class="column-right">Cattle or goats browsing on this plant enjoy eating it.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The plant produces highly poisonous cardiac glycosides and that is why we usually do not see any cattle or goats browsing on this plant.<br>So, statement A is correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1636,'biology',103,971,2258,'With repeated use of the drugs, what happens to the tolerance level of the receptors?','[{"text": "Decreases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Same as usual", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fluctuates", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'With repeated use of drugs, the tolerance level of the receptors present in our body increases. Consequently the receptors respond only to higher doses of drugs or alcohol leading to greater intake and addiction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1637,'biology',100,556,1113,'Which of the following hormones is not secreted by human placenta?','[{"text": "Progestogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "HCG", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "LH", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Placenta also acts as an endocrine tissue and produces several hormones like human chorionic gonadotropin ( hCG ), human placental lactogen (hPL), estrogens, progestogens etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1638,'biology',106,1354,3257,'Alexander Von Humbolt described for the first time:','[{"text": "Laws of limiting factor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species area relationships", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Population growth equation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecological biodiversity", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'German naturalist and geographer Alexander Von Humboldt has observed that within a region, species richness gets increased when explored area is increased, but only up to a limit. He was first to work on species -area relationship',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1639,'biology',105,1283,3100,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Nearly 25 per cent of all insects are known to be phytophagous.<br></div><div class="column-right">The Monarch butterfly is highly tasteful to its predator</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Nearly, \'25\\% \' insects are known to be phytophagous (feeding on plant sap and other parts of plants.)<br>The monarch butterfly is highly distasteful to its predator (bird) because of a special chemical present in its body. Interestingly the butterfly acquires this chemical during its caterpillar stage by feeding on a poisonous weed.<br>So, only statement $\\mathrm{A}$ is correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1640,'biology',103,971,2258,'The side-effects of the use of anabolic steroids in females include<br>i. Masculinisation (features like males)<br>ii. Increased aggressiveness,<br>iii. Mood swings, depression<br>iv. Abnormal menstrual cycles<br>v. Excessive hair growth on the face and body,<br>vi. Enlargement of penis, deepening of voice<br>vii. Breast enlargement','[{"text": "Only i, ii, iii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii, iii, iv is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii, iii, iv, v, vi is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only i, ii, iii, iv, v is correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The side-effects of the use of anabolic steroids in females include masculinisation (features like males), increased aggressiveness, mood swings, depression, abnormal menstrual cycles, excessive hair growth on the face and body, enlargement of clitoris, deepening of voice',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1641,'biology',100,552,1106,'In human females, the endometrium of uterus consists of','[{"text": "Smooth muscle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glandular layer", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adipose layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cartilaginous layer", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The wall of the uterus has 3 layers of tissue. The external thin membranous perimetrium, middle thick layer of smooth muscle, myometrium and inner glandular layer called endometrium that lines the uterine cavity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1642,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Which one of the following is not a method of in situ conservation of biodiversity?','[{"text": "Biosphere Reserve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wildlife Sanctuary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Botanical Garden", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sacred Grove", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Botanical garden - ex - situ conservation (offsite conservation) i.e. living plants (flora) are conserved in human managed system.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1643,'biology',105,1279,3096,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Many desert plants have Sunken stoma to minimise water loss.<br></div><div class="column-right">In Opuntia stem is modified (or) reduced to spines</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Xerophytes are plants which can survive in dry or desert regions, i.e. with little water. Sunken stomata ensure less water loss, thus reduces the rate of transpiration. Hence, these are characteristically found in xerophytes.<br>Opuntia is a xerophytic plant, in which leaves are modified into spines and reduce the rate of transpiration and they cannot perform photosynthesis. So the photosynthesis is done by stem in opuntia.<br>Only statement A is correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1644,'biology',103,966,2249,'The main reason, why antibodies could not solve all the problems of bacteria mediated diseases is','[{"text": "Development of mutant strains resistant to antibodies", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inactivation of antibodies by bacterial enzymes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decreased efficiency of the immune system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insensitivity of the individual following prolonged exposure to antibiotics. Protozoan disease (Malaria)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bacteria develop mutant strains that become resistant to antibodies, so these antibodies become incapable of removing bacteria mediated diseases.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1645,'biology',100,553,1108,'If two primary spermatocytes and two primary oocytes undergo meiosis simultaneously, what will be the ratio of spermatozoa and ova produced at the end of the gametogenesis?','[{"text": "$2: 1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4: 1$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$6: 2$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1: 2$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'One spermatogonia differentiate and form primary spermatocyte. Primary spermatocyte undergoes meiosis -I and forms two secondary spermatocytes. Each secondary spermatocyte undergoes meiosis -II and forms two spermatids that transform into sperms. Hence, from one primary spermatocyte four sperms are produced.The production of ovum is called oogenesis in which an oogonia divides mitotically and differentiates into the primary oocyte. Primary oocyte divides by meiosis -I to form a secondary oocyte and first polar body. The secondary oocyte undergoes meiosis- II to form the ovum and second polar body, The two polar bodies released will degenerate. Hence, from one primary oocyte only one ovum is formed. There will be 8 spermatozoa and 2 ova formed respectively, which will give a ratio of $4: 1$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1646,'biology',106,1357,3260,'The Earth Summit held in Rio de Janeiro in 1992 was called','[{"text": "To reduce $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ emissions and global warming", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "For conservation of biodiversity and sustainable utilization of its benefits", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "To assess threat posed to native species by invasive weed species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "For immediate steps to discontinue use of CFCs that were damaging the ozone layer", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Earth Summit (Rio Summit)-1992, called upon all nations to take appropriate measures for conservation of biodiversity and sustainable utilisation of its benefits.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1647,'biology',105,1279,3096,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Desert lizards lack the physiological ability that mammals have to deal with the high temperatures of their habitat.<br></div><div class="column-right">Mammals from hotter climates generally have shorter ears and limbs to minimise heat loss.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Desert lizards lack the physiological ability that mammals have to deal with the high temperatures of their habitat. According to Allen\'s rule, in endothermal animals of colder areas, the extremities like feet, tail, ears, etc, tend to be smaller as compared to their relatives in warmer regions. This minimises heat loss. So, only statement A is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1648,'biology',103,969,2256,'Identify the correct statement<br>I. Computed tomography uses X-rays to generate a two-dimensional image of the internals of an object.<br>II. Bone marrow tests for decreased white cell counts in the case of leukemias<br>III. Non-ionising radiations like X-rays and gamma rays and ionizing radiations like UV cause DNA damage leading to neoplastic transformation.','[{"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I & II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II & III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ionising radiations like $X$-rays and gamma rays and non-ionizing radiations like UV cause DNA damage leading to neoplastic transformation. Bone marrow tests for increased white cell counts in the case of leukemias.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1649,'biology',100,552,1106,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The presence or absence of hymen is not a reliable indicator of virginity.</div><div class="column-right">The hymen is torn during the first coitus only.<br></div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is true but Statement B is false", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is false but Statement B is true", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Presence or absence of hymen is not a reliable indicator of virginity because hymen can also be broken by a sudden jolt, insertion of a vaginal tampon, active participation in some sports and in some women the hymen persists even after coitus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1650,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Which of the following is the most important cause for animals and plants being driven to extinction?','[{"text": "Habitat loss and fragmentation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Drought and floods", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Economic exploitation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alien species invasion", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Habitat loss and fragmentation is the most important cause driving animals and plants to extinction.<br>eg: Loss of tropical rainforest reducing the forest cover from $14 \\%$ to $6 \\%$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1651,'biology',105,1279,3096,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Zoo planktons diapause stage during unfavourable conditions.<br></div><div class="column-right">Kangaroo rats have a long Henle\'s loop to minimise water loss and to concentrate urine</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Under unfavourable conditions many zooplankton species in lakes and ponds enter a stage of suspended development<br>Diapause is a period during which growth or development is suspended and physiological activity is diminished, as in certain insects in response to adverse environmental conditions.<br>They mostly eat dry food and do not take in liquid water by drinking. The kangaroo rat\'s kidneys are well-organized and produce only small quantities of urine, which is highly concentrated. They are said to have very long loops of Henle. These long loops of Henle allows the water to be reabsorbed efficiently.<br>So, both statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1652,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which one is the best way to eradicate malaria?','[{"text": "Using mosquito repellent oils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Killing of <i>Culex</i> larvae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Killing of <i>Anopheles</i> larvae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Killing of adult <i>Anopheles</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Malaria is caused by Plasmodium vivax. It is transmitted by female Anopheles mosquito. Methods used to prevent Malaria include medications, eradication of larvae of Anopheles mosquito.<br>- The little guppy Poecilia reticulata has developed a big reputation.- The fish has been championed as a mosquito fighter and dumped into ponds and ditches to eat up the insect\'s larvae.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1653,'biology',100,553,1108,'Given below are two statements  one is labelled as  and the other is labelled as<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> FSH acts upon ovarian follicles in female and Leydig cells in male.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Growing ovarian follicles secrete estrogen in female while interstitial cells secrete androgen in male human being.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is false but Reason is true", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'FSH is a gonadotropin affects ovarian follicles in females and causes their growth but in males LH affects Leydig cells leading to secretion of androgens.Growing ovarian follicles secrete estrogen in females while interstitial cells secrete androgen in male human being.Hence, Assertion is false and Reason is true.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1654,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Which of the following regions of the globe exhibits highest species diversity?<br>','[{"text": "Madagascar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Himalayas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amazon forest", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Western Ghats of India", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Amazon forest exhibits highest species diversity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1703,'biology',105,1277,3094,'Temperature changes in the environment affect most of the animals which are','[{"text": "Homeothermic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aquatic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Poikilotherms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Desert living", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Poikilothermy is a condition of any animal whose body temperature fluctuates considerably with that of its environment. Homoiotherms on the either hand has the quality of maintaining a constant body temperature.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',1999,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1655,'biology',105,1283,3102,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Human liverflukeand plasmodium are digenetic parasites.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Most of the parasites harm the host and may reduce the population density.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Liver flukes spend their life cycle utilising two hosts. They live as an internal parasite in the vertebrates during their sexual reproduction phase while have asexual reproduction phase when they are prsesnt in molluscs. Hence they are digenetic organisms.<br>Reason: Majority of parasites harm the host: they may reduce the survival, growth and reproduction of the host and reduce the population density.<br>Both assertion and reason are true',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1656,'biology',103,965,2247,'Choose the correct option for typhoid<br>i. <i>Salmonella typhi</i> causes typhoid fever in human beings.<br>ii. <i>Salmonella typhi</i> generally enter the small intestine through bite of infected mosquito. <br>iii. Sustained high fever $\\left(39^{\\circ}\\right.$ to $\\left.40^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\right)$, weakness, stomach pain, constipation, headache and loss of appetite are some of the common symptoms of typhoid.<br>iv. Typhoid fever could be confirmed by Western blot test.','[{"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "all are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Salmonella typhi</i> generally enter the small intestine through contaminated food and water and migrates to other organs through blood.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1657,'biology',100,558,1116,'Given below are two statements One is labelled as  and the other is labelled as<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Breast-feeding during initial period of infant growth is recommended by doctors for bringing a healthy baby.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Colostrum contains several\nantibodies absolutely essential to develop\nresistance for the new born baby.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is false but Reason is true", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Breast-feeding during initial period of infant growth is recommended by doctors for bringing a healthy baby as colostrum contains several antibodies absolutely essential to develop resistance for the new born baby.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1658,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Which of the following is not a method of ex situ conservation?','[{"text": "National Parks", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Micropropagation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cryopreservation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In vitro fertilization", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In ex situ conservation, threatened animals and plants are taken out from their natural habitat and placed in special setting where they can be protected and given special care. Zoological parks, botanical gardens, in vitro fertilisation, micropropagation and cryopreservation serve this purpose. National parks are an example of in situ conservation. In situ conservation is the process of protecting organisms in their natural habitat. Biosphere reserves, national parks, sanctuaries and sacred groves are a part of in-situ conservation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1659,'biology',105,1279,3096,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Many desert plants have Sunken stoma to minimise water loss.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In Opuntia leaves are modified (or) reduced to spines','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Xerophytes are plants which can survive in dry or desert regions, i.e. with little water. Sunken stomata ensure less water loss, thus reduces the rate of transpiration.<br>Opuntia is a xerophytic plant, in which leaves are modified into spines and reduce the rate of transpiration and they can. t perform photosynthesis.<br>Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1660,'biology',103,965,2247,'Common cold differs from pneumonia in that pneumonia ...','[{"text": "Is communicable while common cold is deficiency disease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Can be prevented by vaccine while common cold has no vaccine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is caused by virus while common cold is caused by bacterium Haemophilus influenza", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Infects alveoli while common cold affects nose and respiratory passage but not lungs (Upper respiratory area).", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bacteria like Streptococcus pneumoniae and Haemophilus influenzae are responsible for the disease pneumonia in humans which infects the alveoli (air filled sacs) of the lungs. Rhino viruses represent a group of viruses which cause one of the most infectious human aliments- the common cold. They infect the nose and respiratory passage but not the lungs. <img src=\'/img/data/biology/103_1660_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1661,'biology',100,552,1106,'Which of the following is not a component of Fallopian tube?','[{"text": "Uterine fundus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Isthmus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Infundibulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ampulla", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The uterine fundus is the upper, dome shaped part of the uterus, above the opening of fallopian tubes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1662,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Habitat loss and fragmentation, over exploitation, alien species invasion and coextinction are causes for:<br>','[{"text": "Competition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biodiversity loss", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Natality", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Population explosion", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Habitat loss and fragmentation, overexploitation, invasion of alien species and, co-extinctions are the four major causes of biodiversity loss (evil quartet).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1748,'biology',106,1353,3255,'The highest number of species in the world is represented by','[{"text": "Fishes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reptiles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mammals", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The number of fungal species in the world is more than the combined total species of fishes, amphibians, reptiles and mammals.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1663,'biology',105,1283,3100,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Amensalism is an association between two species.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Where one species is harmed and other is unaffected','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ammensalism is an association between two species where one species is harmed and the other remains unaffected.<br>Amensalism is a negative interaction in which one species is unaffected and other is harmed.<br>Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1664,'biology',103,967,2254,'Obstacle to large scale transplantation of organs is','[{"text": "Insufficiency of organ donors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Immunological rejection of foreign bodies", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Religious or ethnic considerations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lack of effective surgical techniques", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The major obstacle in transplantation of organs is that the recipient body does not accept the donor\'s organ. The body defense mechanism reject and treat the transplanted organ as a foreign particle and react actively.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1665,'biology',100,553,1107,'Identify the correct option (A), (B), (C), (D) with respect to spermatogenesis.','[{"text": "FSH, Leydig cells, Sertoli cells, spermiogenesis.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ICSH, Interstitial cells, Leydig cells, spermiogenesis.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "FSH, Sertoli cells, Leydig cells, spermatogenesis.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ICSH, Leydig cells, Sertoli cells, spermatogenesis.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/biology/100_1665_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> (A) is FSH which is a pituitary hormone.<br>(B) is Leydig cells which are found in the interstitial space outside of the seminiferous tubules.<br>(C) is Sertoli cells which are found inside the seminiferous tubules.<br>(D) is Spermiogenesis which is a process that helps in transformation of spermatids into spermatozoa.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/100_1665_question_1.png'),
(1666,'biology',106,1357,3260,'In - situ conservation refers to:','[{"text": "Conserve only high risk species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Conserve only endangered species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Conserve only extinct species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protect and conserve the whole ecosystem", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In situ conservation is the process of protecting an animal species in its natural habitat. It protects and conserves the whole ecosystem, its biodiversity at all levels is protected. For example, we save the entire forest to save the tiger.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1667,'biology',105,1283,3102,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Hundreds of microbe species live in our intestine.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> All intestinal microbes live as parasites in humans','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Between 300 and 1000 different species live in the gut, with most estimates at about 500. However, all are not parasites.<br>Assertion is true but Reason is false',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1668,'biology',103,967,2254,'Which of the following explanation is/are related with bone marrow and thymus?<br>(a) Immature lymphocytes differentiate into antigen sensitive lymphocytes.<br>(b) Provide micro environment for the developement and maturation of T-lymphocyte.<br>(c) Provide the sites of interaction of lymphocyte with the antigen<br>(d) Act as filter of the body by trapping blood borne pathogens','[{"text": "a, b, c & d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a & b only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b & c only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The primary lymphoid organs are bone marrow and thymus where immature lymphocytes differentiate into antigensensitive lymphocytes. Both bone marrow and thymus provide micro-environment for the development and maturation of T-lymphocytes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1669,'biology',106,1355,3258,'According to David Tilman’s long term ecosystem experiments, the total biomass in plots with more species shows','[{"text": "High variation from year – to – year", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Average variation from year – to – year", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No variation from year – to – year", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Less variation from year – to – year", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Less variation from year to year',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1670,'biology',105,1277,3094,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> There is no loss of water by transpiration below the forest canopy<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Forest canopy is exposed to sunlight and wind fury and acts as effective wind and light barrier','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The second layer, the canopy, is formed by trees that grow between 60 and 150 feet tall (18-46 meters). The trees form a dense habitat that sustains most of the plant and animal life found in tropical rainforests.<br>The canopy layer also serves as a sunshade for the rainforest below, absorbing a majority of the sunlight. Only about two to five percent of the sunlight penetrates the canopy and reaches the forest floor. Hence below the canopy layer, transpiration is not possible.<br>Both Assertion and Reason are false',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1671,'biology',103,968,2255,'The word NACO stands for','[{"text": "National AIDS Control Organisation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Non-Governamental AIDS Control Organisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "National Agrochemical Organisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (2) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'NACO- National AIDS Control Organisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1672,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Among ‘The Evil Quartet’, which one is\nconsidered the most important cause driving\nextinction of species?','[{"text": "Habitat loss and fragmentation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Over exploitation for economic gain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alien species invasions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Co-extinctions", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Habitat loss and fragmentation is the most important cause driving animals and plants to extinction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1673,'biology',105,1276,3093,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The collective and continuous growth of animals and plants in an ecological area is called biome<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Coral reefs have lowest biomes','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The collective and continuous growth of plants in space is called as vegetation. A biome is defined as a major biological community-type, that recurs over a broad geographic scale under a particular set of environmental conditions.<br>Corals are small animals that belong to the phylum Cnidaria, together with anemones, jellyfish and hydroids. Coral reefs are almost exclusively found in tropical and sub-tropical waters across the globe. Coral reefs have been called as the rainforests of the ocean because of their rich biodiversity.<br>Both Assertion and Reason are false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1674,'biology',103,971,2258,'The symptoms or side effects of anabolic steroids which are seen in males, has an exception it is','[{"text": "Increased aggressiveness", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mood swings", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liver dysfunction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Excessive hair growth on face and body", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Side effects of using anabolic steroids in female includes masculanisation, increased aggressiveness, mood swings, depression, excessive hair growth on face & body, enlargement of clitoris, deeping voice, abnormal menstrual cycle etc.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1675,'biology',106,1357,3260,'The historic Convention on Biological\nDiversity, ‘The Earth Summit’ was held in Rio\nde Janeiro in the year','[{"text": "1985", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1992", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1986", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2002", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The historic convention on Biological Diversity, “The Earth Summit” was held in Rio de Janeiro in the year 1992. It called upon all nations to take appropriate measures for conservation of biodiversity and sustainable\nutilisation of its benefits.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1676,'biology',105,1279,3096,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Zoo planktons diapause stage during unfavourable conditions.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Kangaroo rats have a long Henle\'s loop to minimise water loss and to concentrate urine','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Under unfavourable conditions many zooplankton species in lakes and ponds enter a stage of suspended development Diapause is a period during which growth or development is suspended and physiological activity is diminished, as in certain insects in response to adverse environmental conditions.<br>They mostly eat dry food and do not take in liquid water by drinking. The kangaroo rat\'s kidneys are well-organized and produce only small quantities of urine, which is highly concentrated. They are said to have very long loops of Henle. These long loops of Henle allows the water to be reabsorbed efficiently.<br>Both Assertion and Reason are true',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1677,'biology',106,1356,3259,'The greatest threat to genetic diversity in agricultural crops is:','[{"text": "Extensive mixed cropping", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Introduction of high yielding varieties", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Extensive use of fertilisers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Extensive use of insecticides and pesticides", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Genetic diversity is the total number of genetic characteristics of a specific species, subspecies or group of species. Introduction of high yielding varieties is the greatest threat to genetic diversity in agricultural crops as they have the required traits and hence always are bred purely.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1678,'biology',103,967,2254,'Best match for transplants in order of preference is.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Parent $>$ Sibling $>$ Twin $>$ Unrelated donor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sibling $>$ Twin $>$ Parent $>$ Unrelated donor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Twin $>$ Unrelated donor $>$ Parent $>$ Sibling", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Twin $>$ Sibling $>$ Parent $>$ Unrelated donor", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'• The human leukocyte antigen (HLA) system or complex is a gene complex encoding the major histocompatibility complex (MHC) proteins in humans.<br>• These cell-surface proteins are responsible for the regulation of the immune system in humans.<br>• Human leukocyte antigen (HLA) typing is used to match patients and donors for bone marrow or cord blood transplants.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1679,'biology',105,1277,3094,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Sandy areas have a wide range of daily temperature<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Sand soil particles are good conductors of heat','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Sandy areas have a wide range of temperature. The reason is that sandy soil gets heated up more quickly than clayey soil. For this reason, in the sandy tracts of places like Rajasthan, it is warmer by the day and cooler by night. That makes a huge difference between the temperatures of day and night in deserts, nearly 15 to 20 degree celsius.<br>Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1680,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Choose the right one which denotes genetic diversity.','[{"text": "Chromosomes - nucleotides - genes individuals - populations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Populations - individuals - chromosomes nucleotides - genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genes - nucleotides - chromosomes individuals - populations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleotides - genes - chromosomes individuals - populations", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct order is (4) Nucleotides genes-chromosomes-individuals-populations.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1749,'biology',103,969,2256,'The genes which upon activation produce malignant neoplasms are called','[{"text": "<i>Pleiotrophic genes</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Multiple genes</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Neonatalgenes</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proto-oncogenes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Protooncogenes are responsible for cancer.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1681,'biology',103,966,2249,'Which is wrong?','[{"text": "Body\'s first line of defense is skin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Second line of defense is skin and phagocytic cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Third line of defense is immune system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lines of body defense are skin, phagocytic cells and immune system", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Second line of body defense is only Phagocytic cells which ingest and destroy all microbes that pass into body tissues. For example macrophages are cells derived from monocytes (a type of white blood cell).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1682,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Phenomenon when organisms resembling others for escaping from enemies is','[{"text": "Adaptation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mimicry", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Homology", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Analogy", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mimicry is the phenomenon of resemblance of one species with another. It is a means of adaptation and protection against predation. The species which is copied is called model, while the animal which copies another is known as mimic.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',1991,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1683,'biology',106,1357,3260,'One of the following statements is incorrect with reference to biodiversity. Identify it.','[{"text": "Biodiversity increases from higher altitudes to lower altitudes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Depletion in genetic diversity of crop plants is mainly due to the introduction of better varieties with high yield, disease resistance, etc.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The richest reservoirs of animal and plant life (species richness) with few or no threatened species are called \\"biodiversity hot spots\\".", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Biodiversity decreases from the equator to polar regions.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A biodiversity hot spot is a biogeographic region that is both a significant reservoir of biodiversity and is threatened with destruction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1684,'biology',103,966,2251,'Which is correctly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Anti tetanus and anti snake bite injections - Active immunity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Saliva in mouth and tears in eyes Physical barriers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mucus coating epithelium, urinogenital tract and $\\\\mathrm{HCl}$ in stomach - Physical barriers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polymorpho nuclear leucocytes and monocytes - Cellular barrier", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cellular barrier are certain types of leukocytes (WBC) of our body like polymorpho-nuclear leukocytes (PMNLneutrophils).<br>• Anti-tetanus and anti- snake bite injectionsacquired passive immunity.<br>• Saliva in mouth, tears from eyes all prevent microbial growth. They are part of innate immunity and grouped under physiological barriers.<br>• Mucus coating epithelium, urogenital tract and $\\mathrm{HCl}$ in stomach are examples of physiological barriers.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1685,'biology',105,1277,3094,'Soil water available for roots is','[{"text": "Surface water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hygroscopic water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gravitational water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Capillary water", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Water which is mainly held between the soil particles forming a septum of capillaries is called capillary water. It is most important form of water which is mainly taken by the plants.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',1991,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1686,'biology',106,1353,3255,'Given below is the representation of the extent of global diversity of vertebrates. What groups do the portions represent?','[{"text": "A-Mammals, B- Birds, C- Fishes, D- Amphibians, E- Reptiles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Fishes, B- Mammals, C- Birds, D- Reptiles, E- Amphibians", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Birds, B- Reptiles,C- Fishes, D- Mammals, E- Amphibians", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Fishes, B- Amphibians,  Mammals C- Birds, D- Reptiles", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A : Fishes; B : Mammals; C : Birds; D: Reptiles; E : Amphibians',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/106_1686_question_1.png'),
(1687,'biology',103,966,2251,'Which future development in vaccine production is most important in the fight to erdicate measles in developing countries?','[{"text": "A combined vaccine to combat it and other diseases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A vaccine containing only live measles viruses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A single vaccine, without the need for boosters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The measles vaccine is often incorporated with rubella and/or mumps vaccines. It is equally safe and effective in the single or combined form.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1688,'biology',105,1277,3094,'River water deposits','[{"text": "Loamy soil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alluvial soil", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Laterite soil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sandy soil", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'River water deposits alluvial soil. It is rich in nutrients and may contain heavy metals. These soils are formed when streams and rivers slow their velocity and suspended soil particles gets deposited on the riverbed.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',1992,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1689,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Find the wrongly matched pair.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Endemism - Species confined to one region and also found in other regions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alien species - Clarias gariepinus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lungs of the planet - Amazon rain forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hot spots - Regions with species richness", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Endemic species are restricted to a particular area or region.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1690,'biology',103,969,2256,'A metastatic cancerous tumor is termed \'sarcoma\' if the disorder is in','[{"text": "Fibroblasts", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Circulatory system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Immune system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epithelial cells", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Fibroblasts are the cells present in connective tissue. Sarcomas are cancers that are located in connective and muscular tissues derived from mesoderm. Thus, they include the cancers of bones, cartilages, tendons, adipose tissue, lymphoma, and muscles.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1691,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Tropical forests occur in India','[{"text": "Jammu and Kashmir", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rajasthan", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kerala and Assam", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The forest do not occur in India", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Tropical forest occurs in Assam, Western ghats and Western Himalayas. Major vegetation is of sal(Shorea robusta), shrubs, grasslands and desert communities in the region of decreasing rainfall.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',1994,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1692,'biology',106,1352,3254,'The variety of indigenous cows is an example for:','[{"text": "Genetic diversity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Species diversity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecological diversity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microbial diversity", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Genetic diversity is the total number of genetic characteristics of a specific species, subspecies or group of species. Genetic diversity within a species increases with environmental variability which results in the formation of polymorphs, races and subspecies in geographically isolated populations.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1693,'biology',103,966,2249,'Antigenic epitope fixes to paratope of antibody between?','[{"text": "One heavy and one light chain", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Two heavy chains", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two light chains", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fixes only an single heavy chain", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The antigen-binding site of the antibody molecule is called paratope. It binds antibody with epitope between one heavy and one light chain.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1694,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Desert plants are generally','[{"text": "Viviparous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Succulents", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Herbaceous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterophyllus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Desert plants are generally succulents or fleshy xerophytes. They are referred as drought resisting xerophytes eg: Opuntia, Bryophyllum, Euphorbia.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',1995,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1695,'biology',106,1353,3255,'So far 1.5 million species are identified, in which the number of fungi species identified is more than the combined total of:','[{"text": "Algae, lichens, mosses and ferns", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fishes, amphibians, reptiles and mammals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Molluscans and crustaceans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Molluscans, fishes and amphibians", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The estimated number of species of the fungi is about 2 to 4 million. This is the global estimated richness of the fungal species. This number is more than the combined total of the species of the fishes, amphibians reptiles and mammals.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1696,'biology',103,968,2255,'In full blown AIDS, opportunistic infections are caused by:','[{"text": "Mycobacterium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Toxoplasma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viruses and fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'People with AIDS may get life-threatening opportunistic infections, which are caused by viruses, bacteria, fungi and even parasites like Toxoplasma that usually don\'t make healthy people sick.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1697,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Which of the following plants do not have stomata','[{"text": "Hydrophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Xerophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Submerged", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Submerged hydrophytes are those plants which live completely inside the water,so there is no need of transpiration. Hence, the plants do not have stomata eg: Utricularia, Hydrilla.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',1995,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1698,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Select the option from the following which is not a major characteristic feature of biodiversity hotspots.','[{"text": "Large number of species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Destruction of habitats", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abundance of endemic species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Large number of exotic species", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A biodiversity hot spot is a biogeographic region that is both a significant reservoir of biodiversity and is threatened with destruction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1699,'biology',103,968,2255,'Identity the incorrect statements.<br>I. Ringworm is an integumentary disease.<br>II. Disease causing organisms are pathogens.<br>III. Most parasites are pathogens.<br>IV. A HIV infected cell can survive while viruses are being replicated and released','[{"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ringworm is one of the most common infectious diseases in man. Appearance of dry, scary lesions on various parts of the body such as skin, nails and scalp. Disease producing organisms or agents are called pathogens. All pathogens are parasite and also most parasites are pathogens. HIV enters into helper T-lymphocytes, replicates and produce progeny viruses.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1700,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Keystone species in an ecosystem are those which','[{"text": "Are present in maximum number", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Are most frequent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Attain a large biomass", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contribute to ecosystem properties", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Keystone species of an ecosystem are the species that exerts an important regulatory effect on other species in the community i.e contributes to ecosystem properties. It maintains higher species diversity in community by reducing the densities of strong competitors.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',1997,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1701,'biology',106,1357,3260,'The historic convention related to conservation of biological diversity is also known as:','[{"text": "Earth Summit", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Kyoto Protocol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "World Summit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Montreal Protocol", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The Convention on Biological Diversity (CBD), is a multilateral treaty. It has three main goals: the conservation of biological diversity; the sustainable use of its components; and the fair and equitable sharing of benefits arising from genetic resources. The Convention was opened for signature at the Earth Summit in Rio de Janeiro on June 1992.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1702,'biology',103,966,2249,'The body produces antibodies complementary to foreign antigens. The process by which the body comes up with the correct antibodies to a given disease is most like','[{"text": "Going to a tailor and having a suit made to fit you", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ordering the lunch special at a restaurant without looking at the menu", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Going to a shoe store and trying on shoes until you find a pair that fits", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Picking out a video that you haven\'t seen yet.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Antibody, also called immunoglobulin, a protective protein produced by the immune system in response to the presence of a foreign substance, called an antigen. Antibodies recognize and latch onto antigens in order to remove them from the body.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1801,'biology',103,965,2247,'Choose the pair of diseases/disorder that infect or harm the same structure or organ.<br>I. Amoebiasis, filarial<br>II. Pneumonia, emphysema<br>III. pneumonia, Common Cold<br>IV. Common cold, bronchitis','[{"text": "II only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pneumonia and emphysema both infects the alveoli.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1704,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Match Column I and Column II<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Narrowly utilitarian argument<br>B. Broadly utilitarian<br>C. Ethical argument<br></div><div class="column-right">P. Conserving biodiversity for major ecosystem services<br>Q. Every species has an intrinsic value and moral duty to pass our biological legacy in good order to future generation<br>R. Receiving benefits like food, medicine & industrial products</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - P,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{B - Q,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{C - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{B - R,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{C - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{B - P,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{C - Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{B - Q,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{C - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\rm{A - R,}}\\,{\\rm{B - P,}}\\,{\\rm{C - Q}}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1705,'biology',103,966,2249,'Researchers found that when laboratory rats were already infected with a virus, they were better be able to resist infection by a second completely different virus. The first infection apparently caused........ which protected the rats from the second infection.','[{"text": "Increased stress", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretion of interferon", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Production of antibodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Passive immunity", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Virus cause secretion of interferons by affected host cells which further protects the other cells from infection.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1706,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Which part of the world has high density of organisms','[{"text": "Deciduous forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Grasslands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Savannas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tropical rain forest", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The tropical rain forest are more diverse and highly densed with maximum productivity (approximately $12000 \\mathrm{kcal} / \\mathrm{m}^{2} / \\mathrm{yr}$ )',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',1999,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1707,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Identify the correct statement/s about ex situ conservation<br>I. Advanced ex situ conservation includes Cryopreservation of gametes<br>II. Plant tissue culture method<br>III. Seed bank<br>IV. In vitro fertilization','[{"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I & II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'i, ii, iii, iv is the correct sequence of ex situ conservation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1708,'biology',103,966,2251,'Choose the correct statement with respect to immunology.<br>I. One disulphide bond connects a heavy and a light chain of an antibody.<br>II. Vaccines can be antigens or antibodies.<br>III. Antitoxins are antibodies.<br>IV. Antigen binding site are at the amino end of antibody.','[{"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The immune system has the capability of self and non-self-recognition. Once they recognize antigens, they secrete antibodies. Antigen binding site are at the amino end of antibody. Many disulphide bond bridges connect a heavy and a light chain of an antibody. Antitoxins are preformed antibodies.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1709,'biology',105,1276,3093,'What is true for individuals of same species?','[{"text": "Live in same Niche", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Live in same habitat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interbreeding", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Live in different habitats", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A plant and its pollinator have a mutualistic relationship. The plant uses its pollinator to ensure cross pollination while pollinator uses the plant as food.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2002,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1710,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Identify the incorrect statement<br>I. Speciation is generally a function of time<br>II. Tropical environment is less seasonal, relatively more constant and predictable<br>III. Solar energy contributes to high productivity<br>IV Temperate regions have remained relatively undisturbed for millions of years','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The statement can be corrected as Tropical regions have remained relatively undisturbed for millions of years',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1711,'biology',103,966,2249,'A person underwent organ transplantation. Which of the following are correct.<br>i. The person underwent tissue matching and blood matching tissue before the graft was introduced.<br>ii. Cyclosporin $\\mathrm{A}$ is given to him life long<br>iii. Cell mediated immunity is responsible for graft rejection<br>iv. Graft rejection occurs because the body is able to differentiate self and non self.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "i, ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The person underwent tissue matching and blood matching tissue before undertaking any graft/transplant and even after this the patient has to take immune-suppressants (Cyclosporin A) all his/her life. The body is able to differentiate self and non-self and the cell-mediated immune response is responsible for the graft rejection.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1712,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Which type of association is found in between entomophilous flower and pollinating agent','[{"text": "Mutualism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Commensalism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cooperation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Co-evolution", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cuscuta commonly known as dodder or amarbel is a parasitic plant.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2002,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1713,'biology',106,1354,3257,'The given graph represents<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Population growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Enzyme activity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species area relationship", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Growth of organisms", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Graphical representation indicating species area relationship proposed by Alexander Von Humboldt.',NULL,'Medium','Graph/Figure',2022,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/106_1713_question_1.png'),
(1714,'biology',103,966,2252,'At new place you suddenly start sneezing and wheezing. The statement correctly correlate this condition.<br>I. This is exaggerated response of immune system.<br>II. Symptoms are watery eyes and running nose<br>III. Due to the release of chemicals like adrenaline, steroids and histamines<br>IV. Antibodies produced to these are IgE type<br>V. Rheumatoid arthritis is another example. Of the  said condition','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV are true", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct except V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The exaggerated response of the immune system to certain antigens present in the environment is called allergy. The antibodies produced to these are of IgE type. Symptoms include sneezing, watery eyes, running nose and difficulty in breathing.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1715,'biology',105,1283,3102,'Which of the following is a correct pair?','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{Cuscuta\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}& - &{{\\\\rm{Parasite}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{Dischidia\\\\,}& - &{{\\\\rm{Insectivorous}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{Opuntia\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}& - &{{\\\\rm{Predator}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{Capsella\\\\,\\\\,}& - &{{\\\\rm{Hydrophyte}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'According to the biological concept of species.<br>"Species is a group of organisms which can interbreed freely in nature and produce fertile offspring."',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2002,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1716,'biology',106,1353,3255,'IUCN stands for','[{"text": "Indian Union for Conservation of Nature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "International Union for Conservation of Nature", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Indian Union for Chemical Nomenclature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "International Union for Conservation of Nutrients", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN) is an international organization which works in the field of nature conservation and sustainable use of natural resources. It is also involved in data gathering and analysis, research, field projects and education.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1717,'biology',103,967,2254,'A person without thymus would not be able to','[{"text": "Reject a tissue transplant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Receive a tissue transplant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Develop an inflammatory response", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Produce antigens", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A person without thymus would not be able to reject a tissue transplant because as the immune system won\'t be developed, there will be no autoimmune response to reject the transplant. The T-lymphocytes which can distinguish between self and non-self, will not be produced. So, the transplant won\'t get rejected by the body.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1718,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Mycorrhiza is an example of','[{"text": "Endoparasitism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decomposers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Symbiotic relationship", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ectoparasitism", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mycorrhiza is a result of symbiosis between the roots of higher plants and fungi. In this association plants provide space and prepare food material to fungi in turn fungi help in absorption of water and minerals to plant.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2003,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1720,'biology',106,1354,3257,'Alexander Von Humbolt described for the first time:','[{"text": "Laws of limiting factor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species area relationships", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Population Growth equation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecological Biodiversity", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'German naturalist and geographer Alexander Von Humboldt has observed that within a region, species richness gets increased when explored area is increased, but only up to a limit. He was first to work on species -area relationship',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1721,'biology',103,966,2251,'Purpose of immunisation is','[{"text": "Formation of immunological memory", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Strengthening innate immunity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Promotion of phagocytosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Activation of complement system", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Purpose of immunisation is to develop the ability to quickly respond to a subsequent encounter because of immunological memory.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1722,'biology',105,1276,3093,'In which of the following habitats does the diurnal temperature of soil surface vary most','[{"text": "Scrub land", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Desert", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Grassland", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Deserts have very hot days and very cold nights. Due to the bare plant cover, the soil of desert is much more exposed to these fluctuations as compared to that of other areas. During day time the soil becomes hot and in night it frequently becomes cool.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2004,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1724,'biology',106,1354,3257,'Which one of the following shows concept of species- area relationship?','[{"text": "The number of species in an area increases with the size of the area.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Larger species require larger habitat areas than do smaller species.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Most species within any given area are endemic.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The larger the area, the greater the extinction rate.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'According to the concept of species area relationship, within a region, species richness gets increased when explored area is increased, but only up to a limit.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1725,'biology',103,967,2254,'Select the correct option.<br>i. The bone marrow is the main lymphoid organ where all blood cells including lymphocytes are produced.<br>ii. The thymus is a lobed organ located near the heart and beneath the sternum.<br>iii. Spleen also has a large reservoir of erythrocytes.','[{"text": "Only $i$ is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iii are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The primary lymphoid organs are bone marrow and thymus where immature lymphocytes differentiate into antigensensitive lymphocytes. The thymus is a lobed organ located near the heart and beneath the sternum. Spleen is a large bean shaped organ. It has a large reservoir of erythrocytes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1847,'biology',103,967,2254,'Which of the following is not a lymphoid tissue?','[{"text": "Spleen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tonsils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pancreas", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thymus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pancreas is a heterocrine gland',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1726,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Consider the following four conditions (I -IV) and select a correct pair of them as adaptation to environment in desert lizards<br>Conditions:<br>I. Burrowing in soil to escape high temperature<br>II. Losing heat rapidly from the body during high temperature<br>III. Bask in sun when temperature is low<br>IV. Insulating body due to thick fatty dermis','[{"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Desert lizards bask in the sun and absorb heat when their body temperature drops below the comfort zone, but move into shade when the ambient temperature starts increasing. Some species are capable of burrowing into soil to hide and escape from the above ground heat.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1728,'biology',106,1357,3260,'An example of ex situ conservation is','[{"text": "National park", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed Bank", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Wildlife sanctuary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sacred groove", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Seeds of different genetic strains of commercially important plants can be kept for long periods in seed banks. They are an eg. of ex situ conservation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1729,'biology',103,970,2257,'Choose the correct option for opioids<br>i. Opioids are the drugs, which bind to specific opioid receptors present in our central nervous system and gastrointestinal tract.<br>ii. Heroin commonly called smack is chemically diacetylmorphine which is a white, odourless, bitter crystalline compound.<br>iii. Opioids are obtained by acetylation of morphine, which is extracted from the latex of poppy plant Papaver somniferum.<br>iv. Heroin is a stimulant and improves body functions.','[{"text": "i and ii are wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii are wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only iv is wrong", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Heroin is a depressant and slows down body functions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1730,'biology',105,1281,3098,'A biologist studied the population of rats in a barn. He found that the average natality was 250, average mortality 240, immigration 20 and emigration 30 . The net increase in population is','[{"text": "10", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "15", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "05", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zero", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Zero',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1732,'biology',106,1357,3260,'In which of the following both pairs have correct combination?','[{"text": "In-situ conservation: National Park Ex-situ conservation: Botanical Garden", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In-situ conservation: Cryopreservation Ex-situ conservation: Wildlife sanctuary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In-situ conservation: Seed Bank Ex-situ conservation: Sacred groves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In-situ conservation: Tissue culture Ex situ conservation: Sacred groves", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ex-situ conservation is the preservation of components of biological diversity outside their natural habitats. This involves conservation of genetic resources, as well as wild and cultivated or species, and draws on a diverse body of techniques and facilities.<br>In-situ conservation is the on-site conservation or the conservation of genetic resources in natural populations of plant or animal species, such as forest genetic resources.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1733,'biology',103,969,2256,'Fill in the blanks<br>In ___ A ___, a piece of the suspected tissue is cut into thin sections, stained and examined under microscope for____B____  pathologist. In radiography____C____ are used In CT scan, ____D____ are used','[{"text": "A - biopsy; B - histopathological studies; C - X-rays; D - gamma rays.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - X-rays; B - histopathological studies; C - X-rays; D - X-rays", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Biopsy; B - histopathological studies; C - X-rays; D - Biopsy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Biopsy; B - histopathological studies; C - X-rays; D - X-rays", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In biopsy, a piece of the suspected tissue cut into thin sections is stained and examined under microscope (histopathological studies) by a pathologist. Techniques like radiography (use of X-rays), Computed tomography uses $\\mathrm{X}$-rays to generate a three-dimensional image of the internals of an object.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1734,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Presence of plants arranged into well defined vertical layers depending on their height can be seen best in :','[{"text": "Tropical rain forest", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Grassland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Temperate forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tropical savannah", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Tropical rain forest consist of dense vegetation, often forming three different layers the canopy, the understory, and the ground layer. Hence, we can find plants arranged in different layers according to their height.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1736,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Which vertebrate group is more vulnerable to extinction?','[{"text": "Birds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphibians", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mammals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fishes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Amphibians are more vulnerable to extinction because they are highly sensitive to environmental changes which lead to extinction. Threatened by habitat destruction and degradation, the spread of virulent diseases, climate change and trade, amphibians may be on the verge of a near total disappearance from global ecosystems.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1989,'biology',103,966,2249,'The cell mediated immunity inside the human body is carried out by','[{"text": "T-Lymphocytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B- Lymphocyes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thrombocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Erythrocytes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The cell mediated immunity inside the human body is carried out by T-Lymphocytes',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1737,'biology',103,970,2257,'What is true of the drug obtained from cannabis','[{"text": "Morphine leads to delusions and disturbed emotions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Barbiturates cause relaxation and temporary euphoria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hashish causes after thought perceptions and hallucinations", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Opium stimulates nervous system and causes hallucination", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The flower tops, leaves and the raisin of cannabis plant are used in various combinations to produce marijuana, hashish, charas and ganja. At high doses, mental effects can include anxiety, delusions, hallucinations, panic, etc.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1738,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Mycorrhizae are the example of :','[{"text": "Amensalism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antibiosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutualism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fungistasis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mutualism is a relationship between organisms in which both species involved benefit to some extent with neither species being harmed. Mycorrhizae are associations between fungi and the roots of higher plants. The fungi help the plant in the absorption of essential nutrients from the soil while the plant in turn provides the fungi with energy yielding carbohydrates.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1740,'biology',106,1354,3257,'Species richness means','[{"text": "Number of species per unit area", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number of individual in particular species per the total number of different species in a particular area", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Number of genetic variation in particular area", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number of genes in a particular species", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Species richness is the number of different species represented in an ecological community, landscape or region. Species richness is simply a count of species, and it does not take account the abundance of the species or their relative abundance distribution.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/106_1740_question_1.png'),
(1741,'biology',103,970,2257,'Identify the false statements-<br>I. Antigen-binding site of an antibody is found between two light peptide chains.<br>II. The pathogen of elephantiasis is transmitted to a healthy person through the bite of same mosquito species which also cause malarial disease.<BR>III. Lymphoid tissues are also located within the lining of the major tracts called mucosal lymphoid tissue.<br>IV. Increase intake of coffee or tea can cause indigestion, insomnia and disturb renal functions.<br>V. Anaphylactic shock is an autoimmune reaction which involves all the tissues of the body that results in drastic fall in blood pressure.','[{"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The antigen-binding site in an antibody is found between variable regions of light and heavy chains. The pathogen of elephantiasis is transmitted to a healthy person through the bite of the female mosquito vector(culex).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1742,'biology',105,1280,3097,'In a growing population of a country,','[{"text": "Reproductive and pre-reproductive individuals are equal in number.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reproductive individuals are less than the post-reproductive individuals.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pre-reproductive individuals are more than the reproductive individuals.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pre-reproductive individuals are less than the reproductive individuals", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Whenever the pre-reproductive individuals or the younger population size is larger than the reproductive group, the population will be an increasing population.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1744,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Biodiversity refers to the totality of ____ and ____ of a region.','[{"text": "Genes, species, ecosystem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ecosystem, genes, species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species, ecosystem, genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genes, ecosystem, species", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Biodiversity refers to the totality of Genes, species, ecosystem of a region.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1745,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which one is not correctly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "<i>Glossina palpalis</i> - Sleeping sickness", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Culex - Filariasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Aedes aegypti</i> - Chickengunya", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Anopheles</i> - Leishmaniasis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Anopheles is a major vector of Malaria. Leishmaniasis is a disease caused by parasites of the Leishmania type. It is spread by the bite of certain types of sandflies.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1746,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Natality refers to','[{"text": "Number of individuals leaving the habitat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Birth rate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Death rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number of individuals entering a habitat", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Natality (Birth rate) is the number of births during a given period in the population that are added to the initial density. Number of individuals leaving the habitat is Emigration.<br>Death rate is also called as Mortality. Number of individuals entering a habitat is Immigration',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1750,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Which one of the following population interactions is widely used in medical science for the production of antibiotics?','[{"text": "Parasitism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutualism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Commensalism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amensalism", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Amensalism is type of interaction between organisms of two different species, where one organism does not allow another organism to live near it is achieved by secretion of certain chemicals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1752,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Species diversity increase as one proceeds from','[{"text": "High altitude to low altitude and high latitude to low latitude.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Low altitude to high altitude and high latitude to low latitude.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Low altitude to high altitude and low latitude to high latitude.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "High altitude to low altitude and low latitude to high latitude.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The variety in the number and richness of the species of a region is called species diversity. Species diversity increases from high altitude to low altitude and from high latitude to low latitude.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1753,'biology',103,971,2258,'Which of the following statements is false.','[{"text": "Alcohol is stimulant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Psychoactive drugs alter activity of nervous system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adolescence is marked by accelerated physical growth, development of reproductive organs and changes in functioning of neuroendocrine system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hallucinogen can alter one\'s thoughts, feelings and perceptions", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Like caffeine, cocaine, amphetamines these drugs stimulate the nervous system, make a person more wakeful, alert active and cause excitement.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1754,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Which of the following is NOT an attribute of a population?','[{"text": "Natality", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mortality", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species interaction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sex ratio", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Species interaction',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1756,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Which of the following is not an example of recent extinction?','[{"text": "Steller\'s sea cow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dodo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Quagga", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pigeon", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pigeon is not an example of recent extinction. Examples of recent extinctions include dodo (Mauritius), quagga (Africa), Steller\'s sea cow (Russia), thylacine (Australia) and three subspecies of tiger (Bali, Java, Caspian).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1757,'biology',103,965,2247,'In hot summer and cold winter, the number of malaria cases as well as Anopheles declines. Reappearance of malaria in humid warm conditions is due to','[{"text": "Surviving malarial parasites in human carriers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Surviving sporozoites in surviving mosquitoes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monkeys", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mosquito larvae in permanent waters", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'• Mosquitoes that are not in the "floodwater" group lay their eggs on standing water.<br>• A difference between the two groups is that mosquito eggs in this category cannot withstand drying out.<br>• If the water dries up, or the eggs get stranded on the grass or soil, the egg dries and that will be the end, it will not hatch into larva.<br>• Females will lay their eggs on the water surface and the eggs will typically hatch in about 24 hours.<br>• Water is necessary to complete the life cycle, and soon the larva will change into pupa and then emerge into an adult that is hungry for blood.<br>• After the newly emerged female mates and finds a blood source.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1758,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Inspite of interspecific competition in nature, which mechanism the competing species might have evolved for their survival?','[{"text": "Resource partitioning", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Competitive release", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutualism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Predation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Resource partitioning is the division of limited resources by species to help avoid competition in an ecological niche. In any environment, organisms compete for limited resources, so organisms and different species have to find ways to coexist with one another.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1760,'biology',106,1357,3260,'A strict protection of biodiversity hotspots could reduce the ongoing mass extinction by almost','[{"text": "$20 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$25 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$30 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$35 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Although all the biodiversity hotspots put together cover less than 2 percent of the earth\'s land area, the number of species they collectively harbour is extremely high and strict protection of these hotspots could reduce the ongoing mass extinctions by almost 30 per cent.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1761,'biology',103,967,2254,'What is true about T-lymphocytes in mammals?','[{"text": "There are three main types of cells cytotoxic T-cells, helper T-cells and suppressor T-cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "These originate in lymphoid tissues", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They scavenge damaged cells and cellular debris", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These are produced in thyroid", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{T}$ lymphocytes are part of the immune system and develop from stem cells in the bone marrow. They help protect the body from infection. There are 3 main types of T cells: cytotoxic, helper, and suppressor.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1762,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Amensalism can be represented as:','[{"text": "Species A (-); $\\\\quad$ Species B (0)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Species A (+); $\\\\quad$ Species B (+)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species A (-); $\\\\quad$ Species B (-)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species A (+); $\\\\quad$ Species B (0)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Amensalism is association between organisms of two different species in which one is inhibited or destroyed and the other is unaffected.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1764,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Identify the incorrect match respect to recently extinct animals and their place of extinction according to IUCN Red list<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Dodo-Mauritius", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Quagga - Africa", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thylacine - Australia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Steller\'s Sea Cow - North America<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Steller\'s Sea Cow is extinct from Russia',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1765,'biology',103,966,2248,'Choose the appropriate definition for immunity with its types','[{"text": "Ability of the host to fight the disease causing organisms, conferred by the immune system is called immunity. Immunity is of two types:<br>(i) Innate immunity and<br>(ii) Acquired immunity.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inability of the host to fight the disease causing organisms, conferred by the immune system is called immunity. Immunity is of two types:<br>(i) Innate immunity and<br>(ii) Acquired immunity.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ability of the pathogen to fight the disease-causing organisms, conferred by the immune system is called immunity. Immunity is of two types:<br>(i) Innate immunity and<br>(ii) Cell mediated immunity.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ability of the host to fight the diseasecausing organisms, conferred by the immune system is called immunity. Immunity is of two types:<br>(i) Innate immunity and<br>(ii) In born immunity.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ability of being able to resist a particular disease especially through preventing development of a pathogenic microorganism or by counteracting the effects of its products. Two types of immunity exist - active and passive.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1766,'biology',105,1281,3098,'In the exponential growth equation $\\mathrm{Nt}=\\mathrm{N}_{0} \\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{rt}}$, e represents:','[{"text": "The base of number logarithms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The base of exponential logarithms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The base of natural logarithms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The base of geometric logarithms", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'e: in the exponential growth equation represents, the base of natural logarithm.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1768,'biology',106,1355,3258,'According to the hypothesis proposed by environmental biologists, a relatively constant environment in tropics promotes','[{"text": "Niche specialization and lesser species diversity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Niche specialization and greater species diversity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Niche diversity and lesser species specialization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Niche diversity and greater species specialization", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ecologists and evolutionary biologists have proposed various hypotheses. Some important ones are<br>1. Speciation is generally a function of time, unlike temperate regions subjected to frequent glaciations in the past, tropical latitudes have remained relatively undisturbed for millions of years and thus, had a long evolutionary time for species diversification.<br>2. Tropical environments, unlike temperate ones, are less seasonal, relatively more constant and predictable. Such constant environments promote niche specialisation and lead to a greater species diversity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1769,'biology',103,968,2255,'Which of the following is not a means of transmission of AIDS?','[{"text": "Sexual contact with uninfected person", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Transfusion of contaminated blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sharing infected needles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Child born to an HIV infected mother", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Transmission of AIDS generally occurs by sexual contact with infected person, by transfusion of contaminated blood and blood products, by sharing infected needles as in the case of intravenous drug abusers and from infected mother to her child through placenta.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1770,'biology',105,1279,3096,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> A person goes to high altitude and experiences \'altitude sickness\' with symptoms like breathing difficulty and heart palpitations.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Due to low atmospheric pressure at high altitude, the body does not get sufficient oxygen.<br><br>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below.<br>','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Higher altitude oxygen level would be less',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1772,'biology',106,1356,3259,'These are regarded as major causes of biodiversity loss:<br>A. Over exploitation<br>B. Co-extinction<br>C. Mutation<br>D. Habitat loss and fragmentation<br>E. Migration<br>Choose the Correct Option','[{"text": "A, C and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B, C and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and E only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and D only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Major causes of biodiversity losses are<br>(1) Habitat loss and fragmentation<br>(2) Over-exploitation<br>(3) Alien species invasions<br>(4) Co-extinctions<br>Hence correct option is A, B and D only.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1773,'biology',103,969,2256,'What is correct?','[{"text": "Malignant tumor may exhibit metastasis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Patients who have undergone surgery are given cannabinoids to relieve pain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Benign tumor show metastasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heroin accelerates body functions", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Benign tumors normally remain confined to their original location and do not spread to other parts of the body and cause little damage. In malignant tumors cells grow very rapidly, invading and damaging the surrounding normal tissues. This property is called metastasis. Heroin is a depressant and slows down body functions. Morphine is a very effective sedative and painkiller, and is very useful in patients who have undergone surgery.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1774,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Match Column - I with Column - II<BR>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Allen\'s Rule<br>B. Physiological adaptation<br>C. Behavioural adaptation<BR>D. Biochemical adaptation</div><div class="column-right">P. Kangaroo rat<br>Q. Desert lizard<BR>R. Marine fish at depth<BR>S. Polar seal</div></div>','[{"text": "A - S; B - Q; C - R; D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P; B - S; C - R; D - Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S; B - P; C - Q; D - R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - S; B - R; C - Q; D - P", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A - S; B - P; C - Q; D - R',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1776,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Tropical regions show greatest level of species richness because<br>A. Tropical latitudes have remained relatively undisturbed for millions of years, hence more time was available for species diversification.<br>B. Tropical environments are more seasonal.<br>C. More solar energy is available in tropics.<br>D. Constant environments promote niche specialization.<br>E. Tropical environments are constant and predictable.<br>choose the correct answer from the options given below.','[{"text": "A, C, D and E only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and E only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and D only", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Only statement B is incorrect because tropical environments unlike temperate ones, are less seasonal, relatively more constant and predictable.Thus statements A, C, D and E are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1777,'biology',103,971,2258,'Choose the correct option for the prevention and control of drug and alcohol abuse.<br>i. A child should not be pushed unduly to perform beyond his/her threshold limits; be it studies, sports or other activities. ii. Educating and counselling him/ her to face problems and stresses, and to accept disappointments and failures as a part of life.<br>iii. Help from parents and peers should be sought immediately so that they can guide appropriately.<br>iv. With the help of qualified psychologists, psychiatrists, and deaddiction and rehabilitation programmes to help individuals who have unfortunately got in the quagmire of drug/alcohol abuse.','[{"text": "i and iii are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iv are wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'All are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1778,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Which one of the following statements cannot be connected to Predation?','[{"text": "It might lead to extinction of a species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the interacting species are negatively impacted", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is necessitated by nature to maintain the ecological balance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It helps in maintaining species diversity in a community", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In predation, only one species (predator) benefits while the other (prey) is harmed. Both interacting species are negatively impacted in case of competition.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1780,'biology',106,1352,3254,'List of endangered species was released by','[{"text": "GEAC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "WWF", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "FOAM", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IUCN", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'List of endangered species was released by - IUCN.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1781,'biology',103,968,2255,'Enzyme responsible for replication of HIV in macrophages is','[{"text": "RNA polymerase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA ligase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA polymerase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reverse transcriptase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Enzyme responsible for replication of HIV in macrophages is Reverse transcriptase.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1782,'biology',105,1283,3100,'While explaining interspecific interaction of population, $(+)$ sign is assigned for beneficial interaction, (-) sign is assigned for detrimental interaction and (0) for neutral interaction. Which of the following interactions can be assigned $(+)$ for one species and (-) for another species involved in the interaction?','[{"text": "Amensalism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Commensalism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Competition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Predation", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In predation and parasitism, only one species is benefitted $(+)$ whereas other species is harmed (-).<br>$\\begin{array}{lcc} & \\text { Species A } & \\text { Species B } \\\\ \\text { Mutualism } & + & + \\\\ \\text { Competition } & - & - \\\\ \\text { Predation } & + & - \\\\ \\text { Parasitism } & + & - \\\\ \\text { Commensalism } & + & 0 \\\\ \\text { Amensalism } & - & 0\\end{array}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1784,'biology',106,1357,3260,'The type of conservation in which the threatened species are taken out from their natural habitat and placed in special setting where they can be protected and given special care is called','[{"text": "In-situ conservation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biodiversity conservation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Semi-conservative method", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sustainable development", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The type of conservation in which threatened species are taken out from their natural habitat and placed in special setting where they can be protected and given special care is called ex-situ conservation which is a type of biodiversity conservation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1785,'biology',103,968,2255,'With regard to the transmission of human immunodeficiency virus (HIV), which among of the following statements is not correct?','[{"text": "The chances of transmission from female to male are twice as likely from male to female.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The chances of transmission are more if a person suffers from other sexually transmitted infections.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "An infected mother can transmit the infection to her baby during pregnancy at child birth.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The risk of contacting infection from transfusion of infected blood is much higher than an exposure to contaminated needle.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Transmission of HIV-infection generally occurs by sexual contact with infected person, by transfusion of contaminated blood and blood products, by sharing infected needles as in the case of intravenous drug abusers and from infected mother to her child through placenta.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1786,'biology',105,1280,3097,'If \' 8 \' <i>Drosophila</i> in a laboratory population of \' 80 \' died during a week, the death rate in the population is ____ individuals per Drosophila per week','[{"text": "10", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{\\\\rm{.0}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "zero", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.1}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Per capita death rate (d)= No. of deaths/ total population size.<br>$\\mathrm{d}=8 / 80=0.1$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1788,'biology',106,1355,3258,'Match Column I with Column II<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Robert May<br>B. Alexander von Humboldt<br>C. Paul Ehrlich <br>D. David Tilman</div><div class="column-right">P. Species-Area relationship<br>Q. Long term ecosystem experiment using out door plots<br>R. Global species diversity at about 7 million<br>S. Rivet popper hypothesis</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  R, C  -  P, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  P, C  -  S, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  Q, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{R,}}\\,{\\rm{B}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{P,}}\\,{\\rm{C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S,}}\\,{\\rm{D}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{Q}}$ is the correct option. Robert May places the global species diversity at about 7 million.<br>Alexander von Humboldt gave species-area relationship.<br>Paul Ehrlich used an analogy "Rivet popper hypothesis" to explain the role of species in the ecosystem.<br>David Tilman performed long term ecosystem experiments using out door plots.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1789,'biology',103,968,2255,'Time lag between infection and appearance of AIDS symptoms can be few months to years','[{"text": "2-3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$5-10$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$>15$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1-2$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The time lag between infection and appearance of AIDS symptoms can be few months to 5-10 years.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1790,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Given below are two statements:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Gause’s ‘Competitive Exclusion\nPrinciple’ states that two closely related species\ncompeting for the same resources cannot coexist indefinitely and competitively inferior\none will be eliminated eventually</div><div class="column-right">In general, carnivores are more\nadversely affected by competition than\nherbivores<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the\ncorrect answer from the options given below:</div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are\\ntrue.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are\\nfalse", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is\\nfalse.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B\\nis true.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gause’s ‘Competitive Exclusion Principle’\nstates that two closely related species\ncompeting for the same resources cannot coexist indefinitely and the competitively\ninferior one will be eliminated eventaully.\nThus, statement A is correct.<br>\nStatement B is incorrect as in general,\nherbivores and plants appear to be more\nadversely affected by competition than\ncarnivores.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1792,'biology',103,970,2257,'Products of <i>Cannabis sativa</i> are abused by some sports persons because','[{"text": "These products are very effective sedative so they enhances muscle strength.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These products are very effective analgesics", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These products binds with the receptor of cardiovascular system to improve cardiovascular activity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "These products shows effects on cardiovascular system", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Products of cannabis sativa are generally taken by inhalation and oral ingestion, these are known for their effect on cardiovascular system of the body.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1793,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Match Column I (Interaction) with Column II (Species A and B) :<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Mutualism<br>B. Commensalism<br>C. Amensalism<br>D. Parasitism</div><div class="column-right">P. +(A), 0(B)<br>Q. –(A), 0(B)<br>R. +(A), –(B)<br>S. +(A), +(B)</div></div>','[{"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-P, C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'(+, +) Mutualism : In this interaction, both\nthe interacting species are benefitted.<br>\n(+, 0) Commensalism : Only one species is benefitted and the other species remains\nunharmed.\n<br>(–, 0) Amensalism : Neither species is\nbenefitted. One remains unharmed and the\nother is harmed.<br>\n(+, –) Parasitism : One species is benefitted\nand other is negatively affected',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1795,'biology',103,971,2258,'Hangover is','[{"text": "Feeling of giddiness and nausea in the morning after having alcohol in the night", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Increased desire to take alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Feeling of flushing after taking alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Development of gastritis and peptic ulcers due to alcohol addiction", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A hangover is a group of unpleasant signs and symptoms that can develop after drinking too much alcohol. It\'s symptoms include feeling of giddiness and nausea in the morning after having alcohol in the night.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1796,'biology',105,1283,3104,'Match Column I (Interacting species) with Column II (Name of interaction) :<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. A Leopard and a Lion in a forest/grassland<br>B. A Cuckoo laying\negg in a Crow’s\nnest<br>C. Fungi and root of\na higher plant in\nMycorrhizae<br>D. A cattle egret and\na Cattle in a field</div><div class="column-right">P. Competition<br>Q. Brood parasitism<br>R. Mutualism<br>S. Commensalism</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-S, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A leopard and a lion in a forest/grassland\nexemplify competition where both the species\nare competing for the same resources.<br>A cuckoo laying egg in a crow’s nest is brood\nparasitism where cuckoo is the parasitic bird\nthat lays its egg in the nest of crow (host bird).<br>\nFungi and root of a higher plant in mycorrhizae\nexemplify mutualism where both the species\nare benefitted. The fungi help the plant in the\nabsorption of essential nutrients from the soil\nwhile the plant in turn provides the fungi with\nenergy yielding carbohydrates.<br>A cattle egret and a cattle in a field exemplify\ncommensalism where one species benefits and\nthe other remains unaffected.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1798,'biology',103,971,2258,'Withdrawal syndrome does not include-','[{"text": "Calmness", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anxiety", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sweating", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nausea", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Withdrawal syndrome may include headaches, nausea, tremors, anxiety, hallucinations and seizures.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1799,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Match Column I  with Column II:<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Logistic growth<br>B. Exponential growth<br>C. Expanding age pyramid<br>D. Stable age pyramid</div><div class="column-right">P. Unlimited\nresource\navailability\ncondition<br>Q. Limited resource\navailability\ncondition<br>R. The percent\nindividuals of\npre-reproductive\nage is largest\nfollowed by\nreproductive and\npost reproductive\nage groups<br>S. The percent\nindividuals of\npre-reproductives\nand reproductive\nage group are\nsame</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Logistic growth occurs when there is\nlimited resource availability condition.\n<br>Exponential growth occurs when there is\nunlimited resource availability condition.\n<br>Expanding age pyramid reflects growing\npopulation where the percent individuals of\npre-reproductive age is largest followed by\nreproductive and post-reproductive age groups.\n<br>Stable age pyramid shows stable population\nwhere the percent individuals of prereproductive and reproductive age group are\nsame.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1802,'biology',105,1281,3098,'In the sigmoid growth curve given below, the alphabets indicate the sequence of events. Choose the correct option where the alphabet specifies the event.','[{"text": "A - Diminishing growth; B - Exponential growth; C - Slow growth; D - Stationary growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Stationary phase; B - Phase of slow growth; $\\\\mathrm{C}$ - Phase of rapid growth;<br>$\\\\mathrm{D}$ - Phase of diminishing growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Phase of slow growth; B - Phase of exponential growth; $\\\\mathrm{C}$ - Phase of diminishing growth; D - Stationary phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Phase of rapid growth; B - Phase of diminishing growth; C - Stationary phase; D - Phase of slow growth", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'It is an S-shaped logistic growth curve.<br>• \'A\' represents lag phase which is a slow growth adjustment phase. These cells increase in size, but no cell division occurs in the phase.<br>• \' B \' represents exponential growth. This is the time when the cells are dividing by binary fission and doubling in numbers after each generation time.<br>• \'C\' represents diminishing growth. The population growth experienced in the log phase begins to decline as the available nutrients become depleted and waste products start to accumulate.<br>• \' D \' is stationary phase. Bacterial cell growth reaches a plateau, or stationary phase, where the number of dividing cells equal the number of dying cells. This results in no overall populations growth.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/105_1802_question_1.png'),
(1804,'biology',103,964,2246,'The term \'Health\' is defined in many ways. The most accurate definition of the health would be:','[{"text": "Health is the state of body and mind in a balanced condition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Health is the reflection of a smiling face", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Health is a state of complete physical, mental and social well-being", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Health is the symbol of economic prosperity.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Social and mental wellbeing is as important as being physically fit.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1805,'biology',105,1283,3103,'The interaction between the organisms of one of the following pairs is an example for commensalism:','[{"text": "Wasps and fig tree", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cuckoo and crow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cattle or sheep and grass", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Orchid and mango tree", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Commensalism is an association in which one (commensal) is benefitted and the other (host) is unaffected. Ectocommensals, for example, orchids, grow on the branch of the mango tree. They benefit from this support by reaching positions where the light is better or where there is less competition for light. Mango tree remains unaffected.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1807,'biology',103,964,2246,'Diseases are broadly grouped into infectious and non-infectious diseases. In the list given below, identify the infectious diseases.<br>i. Cancer &emsp; &emsp; ii. Influenza<br>iii. Allergy &emsp; &emsp; iv. Small pox','[{"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iv", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'(ii) and (iv) Cancer and allergy are noninfectious diseases. They are not spread by any means.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1808,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Connel\'s field experiment on the rocky sea coast of Scotland, where larger Barnacle Balanus dominates the intertidal area and removes the smaller Barnacle Chthamalus. This happened due to','[{"text": "Predation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Competition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Parasitism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutualism", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'It was observed that in the deeper zones, Balanus barnacles could always outcompete Chthamalus barnacles. Balanus barnacles used the resources of the deeper zone more efficiently than Chthamalus organisms do, even though Chthamalus barnacles are able to survive there in the absence of its competitor.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1810,'biology',105,1283,3101,'In which type of interactions, both the interacting organisms do not live close together?','[{"text": "Predation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parasitism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutualism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Competition", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In competitive interactions, members of the species strive to obtain the same limited resources, that is, compete for resources. In this interaction both the interacting organisms need not to live close together. But, for rest of the interactions, predation, parasitism and mutualism, one organism depends on its survival on the other, thus they have to live close to each other.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1811,'biology',103,965,2247,'The disease chikungunya is transmitted by:','[{"text": "House fly", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aedes mosquito", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cockroach", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Female Anopheles", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Aedes aegypti (Tiger moquito)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1813,'biology',105,1280,3097,'A population is correctly defined as having which of the following characteristics?<br>(A) Inhabiting the same geography area<br>(B) Individuals belonging to same species<br>(C) Possessing a constant and uniform density and dispersion','[{"text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B and C only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and C only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B only", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A population is a group of individuals of the same species living in the same area or interbreeding and sharing genetic information.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1814,'biology',103,965,2247,'Many diseases can be diagnosed by observing the symptoms in the patient. Which group of symptoms are indicative of pneumonia?','[{"text": "Difficulty in respiration, fever, chills, cough, headache", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Constipation, abdominal pain, cramps, blood clots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nasal congestion and discharge, cough, constipation, headache", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "High fever, weakness, stomach pain, loss of appetite and constipation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Difficulty in respiration, fever, chills, cough, headache',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1816,'biology',105,1283,3104,'All the following interactions are mutualism, except:','[{"text": "Association of algae and fungi in lichens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Association of fungi and roots of higher plants in mycorhiza", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plant and animal relation for pollination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Association of cattle egret and grazing cattle", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mutualism is a relationship in which two species live together in close association, both benefiting from the relationship Cattle egrets and cattle show commensalism in which egrets are benefited from grazing by the cattle. As the cattle graze. the insects become visible and birds can easily catch them, while cattles are unaffected.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1817,'biology',103,964,2246,'When an apparently healthy person is diagnosed as unhealthy by a psychiatrist, the reason could be that:','[{"text": "The patient was not efficient at his work", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The patient was not economically prosperous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The patient shows behavioural and social maladjustment", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "He does not take interest in sports", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Option 1, 2 and 4 does not indicate a disease when dealt separately.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1819,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Mac Arthur\'s vision of 5 closely related species of warblers living on same tree were able to avoid competition and co-exist by behavioural difference. This is an example for:','[{"text": "Competitive release", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Resource partitioning", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Competitive exclusion principle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adaptive radiation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'One way for co-existence is through resource partitioning in which the for example, the time of feeding may be different.<br>Nevertheless, Gause\'s theory predicts that when two species co-exist on a long-term basis, one or more features of their niches will always differ, otherwise, the extinction of one species will inevitably result.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1820,'biology',103,969,2256,'In malignant tumors, the cells proliferate, grow rapidly and move to other parts of the body to form new tumors. This stage of disease is called:','[{"text": "Metagenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metastasis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Teratogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitosis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Metagenesis refers to alternation of generation.Teratogenesis refers to congenital deformities. And mitosis is a type of equational cell division. Hence, option \' 2 \' is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1822,'biology',103,966,2253,'Which of the following are the reason(s) for Rheumatoid arthritis? Choose the correct option.<br>i. The ability to differentiate pathogens or foreign molecules from self cells increases.<br>ii. Body attacks self cells<br>iii. More antibodies are produced in the body<br>iv. The ability to differentiate pathogens or foreign molecules from self cells is lost','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{i}$ and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{i}$ and iii", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The following statements are correct.<br>ii. Body attacks self cells<br>iv. The ability to differentiate pathogens or foreign molecules from self cells is lost.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1872,'biology',103,970,2257,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Smoking increases blood pressure.<br></div><div class="column-right">Nicotine causes tension that constricts the arteries, raising the blood pressure.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1823,'biology',105,1283,3104,'From the given options, identify the correct combination of population interactions that correspond to the symbols given here.<br>$\\begin{array}{lll}++ & -- & +\\mathrm{O}\\end{array}$','[{"text": "Parasitism Competition Mutualism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Predation Competition Commensalism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutualism Competition Commensalism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mutualism Parasitism Amensalism", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the species benefit in case of mutualism and protoco-operation; only one of the interacting species benefits in case of predation and parasitism and the interaction is detrimental to the other species and in case of competition, the interaction is detrimental to both the species.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1825,'biology',103,968,2255,'AIDS is caused by HIV. Among the following, which one is not a mode of transmission of HIV?','[{"text": "Transfusion of contaminated blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sharing the infected needles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shaking hands with infected person", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sexual contact with infected person", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'HIV infection involves exchange of body fluids.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1826,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Read the statements and choose the correct answer.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The Monarch butterfly feeds on poisonous weeds during its caterpillars stage.</div><div class="column-right">It helps butterfly to become distasteful to its predator.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is true, Statement B is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is true and Statement B is correct explanation.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statement A and B are false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement A and B are true, but Statement B is not the correct explanation of Statement A.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When the caterpillars of Monarch butterflies feed on plants of the milkweed family, for example, they do not break down the chemicals that protect these plants from most herbivores. Instead, they store them in fat within their bodies. As a result, the caterpillars and all developmental stages of the Monarch butterfly are protected against predators (birds) by this plant poison. A bird that eats a Monarch butterfly quickly regurgitates it. Although this is no help to the eaten insect, the bird will soon learn not to eat another butterfly with the bright orange and black pattern that characterizes the adult monarch. Such conspicuous coloration, which advertises an insect\'s toxicity, is called warning coloration or aposematic coloration.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1828,'biology',103,966,2248,'The substance produced by a cell in viral infection that can protect other cells from further infection is:','[{"text": "Serotonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Colostrum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interferons", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Histamine", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The substance produced by a cell in viral infection that can protect other cells from further infection is Interferons',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1830,'biology',105,1281,3098,'In the following equation of Verhulst - Pearl logistic growth, the letter \' r \' denotes<br>$\\frac{{{\\rm{dN}}}}{{{\\rm{dt}}}}{\\rm{ = rN}}\\left( {\\frac{{{\\rm{K - N}}}}{{\\rm{K}}}} \\right)$','[{"text": "Extrinsic rate of natural increase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intrinsic rate of natural increase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Carrying capacity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Population density", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'r= Intrinsic rate of natural increase and it depends on population density and how close it is to carrying capacity. It is the rate at which a population increases in size if no density dependent forces are regulating the population',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1832,'biology',103,970,2257,'\'Smack\' is a drug obtained from the:','[{"text": "Latex of <i>Papaver somniferum</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Leaves of <i>Cannabis sativa</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flowers of <i>Datura</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fruits of <i>Erythroxylum coca</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Latex of Papaver somniferum',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1833,'biology',105,1283,3102,'Identify the correct statement/s from the following<br>I. <i>Cuscuta</i> is a chlorophyllous endoparasite<br>II. The human liverfluke needs only one host to complete its life cycle<br>III. The life cycle of endoparasite is more complex due to their extreme specialisation<br>IV. During the course of evolution the host bird\'s eggs have evolved to resemble the eggs of the parasitic bird','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III & IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only the following statement is correct. The life cycle of endoparasite is more complex due to their extreme specialisation',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1834,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Relate Column A with Column B with regard to predatory behaviour<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <i>Calotropis</i><br>B. <i>Pisaster</i><br>C. Monarch butterfly<br>D. Frogs</div><div class="column-right">P. Invertebrates<br>Q. Distasteful<br>R. Cryptically coloured<br>S. Cardioglycoside</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - S,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{B - P,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{C - R,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - S,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{B - P,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{C - Q,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{D - R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{B - S,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{C - P,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{D - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - S,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{B - P,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{C - R,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{A - S,}}\\,{\\rm{B - P,}}\\,{\\rm{C - Q,}}\\,{\\rm{D - R}}$<br>A. Calotropis - S. Cardioglycoside<br>B. Pisaster - P. Invertebrates<br>C. Monarch butterfly - Q. Distasteful<br>D.Frogs -R. Cryptically coloured',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1835,'biology',103,966,2249,'Transplantation of tissues/organs to save certain patients often fails due to rejection of such tissues/organs by the patient. Which type of immune response is responsible for such rejections?','[{"text": "Auto-immune response", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Humoral immune response", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Physiological immune response", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell-mediated immune response", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cell-mediated immune response',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
