(1856,'biology',105,1283,3102,'Which of the following is an incorrect statement?','[{"text": "The human liver fluke depends on two intermediate hosts to complete its life cycle.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The malarial parasite needs vector (mosquito) to spread to other host.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parasites that feed on external surface of the host organism are called endoparasites.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cuscuta derives its nutrition from the host plant which it parasitises.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Parasites that feed on the external surface of the host organism are called ectoparasites. The most familiar examples of this group are the lice on humans and ticks on dogs.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1857,'biology',103,965,2247,'Haemozoin is a:','[{"text": "Precursor of haemoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Toxin released from <i>Streptococcus</i> infected cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Toxin released from <i>Plasmodium</i> infected cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Toxin released from <i>Haemophilus</i> infected cells", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Haemozoin causes chill and fever in a malaria patient.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1859,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Match the following.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Predation<br>B. Commensalism<br>C. Parasitism<br>D. Competition</div><div class="column-right">P. <em>Cuscuta </em>and\nhedge plants<br>Q. <em>Balanus </em>and\n<em>Chthamalus</em><br>R. Cactus and moth<br>S. Orchid and\nmango</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R, B - S, C - P, D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - S, B - R, C - Q, D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - P, B - R, C - Q, D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R, B - S, C - Q, D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{A - R, B - S, C - P, D - Q}}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1907,'biology',11,288,556,'Which of the following biomolecules is common to respiration - mediated breakdown of fats,carbohydrates and proteins?','[{"text": "Pyruvic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acetyl CoA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glucose-6-phosphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fructose 1,6-bisphosphate", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Acetyl CoA is common to respirationmediated breakdown of fats, carbohydrates and proteins',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1860,'biology',11,290,558,'Match column-I (Biological molecules) with column-II (Biological functions).<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Glycogen<br>B. Globulin<br>C. Steroids<br>D. Thrombin</div><div class="column-right">P. Hormone<br>Q. Biocatalyst<br>R. Antibody<br>S. Storage product</div></div>','[{"text": "A - P, B - Q, C - R, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - , B - Q, C - R, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S, B - R, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - R, B - Q, C - S, D - P", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Glycogen &ndash; Storage product<br>Globulin &ndash; Antibody<br>Steroids &ndash; Hormone<br>Thrombin &ndash; Biocatalyst',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1861,'biology',103,965,2247,'A person with sickle cell anaemia is','[{"text": "More prone to malaria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More prone to typhoid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Less prone to malaria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Less prone to typhoid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'People suffering from sickle cell anaemia are resistant to malaria because of different shape of RBCs in them.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1863,'biology',105,1283,3101,'In laboratory experiments, two species of the protist Paramoecium were grown alone and in the presence of the other species. The following graphs show growth of species 1 (left) and species 2 (right), both along and when in mixed culture.','[{"text": "Competitive exclusion occurred in these experiments.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both species are affected by interspecific competition but species 1 is less affected.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both species are affected by interspecific competition but species 2 is less affected.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both species are affected equally by interspecific competition.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both species are affected by interspecific competition but species 2 is less affected.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/105_1863_question_1.png'),
(1864,'biology',103,971,2258,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Parenting that combines with high levels of nurturance and consistent discipline, has been associated with lowered risk of substance (alcohol/drugs/ tobacco) abuse.<br></div><div class="column-right">Every child has his/her own choice and personality, which should not be respected and nurtured</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Only A is correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1865,'biology',11,286,553,'Following are the statements with reference to &lsquo;lipids&rsquo;.<br>(a) Lipids having only single bonds are called unsaturated fatty acids.<br>(b) Lecithin is a phospholipid<br>(c) Trihydroxy propane is glycerol<br>(d) Palmitic acid has 20 carbon atoms including carboxyl carbon.<br>(e) Arachidonic acid has 16 carbon atoms.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.','[{"text": "(a) and (b) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(c) and (d) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(b) and (c) only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(b) and (e) only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lecithin is a phospholipid Palmitic acid 20 carbon atoms including carboxyl',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1866,'biology',105,1283,3100,'The plant <i>Calotropis</i> produces highly poisonous ____ and that is why you never see any cattle or goats browsing on this plant.','[{"text": "Cardiac glycosidase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cardiac glycosides", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteases", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The plant Calotropis produces highly poisonous cardiac glycosides and that is why you never see any cattle or goats browsing on this plant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1868,'biology',103,968,2255,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">HIV virus is a Retro virus.<br></div><div class="column-right">It can form HIV DNA by reverse transcriptase</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1869,'biology',11,290,558,'Exoskeleton of arthropods is composed of:','[{"text": "Cellulose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chitin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glucosamine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cutin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In arthropods, exoskeleton is composed of chitin, which is present in the form of plates called sclerites.<br> These sclerites are joined by soft, flexible arthrodial membrane.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1871,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Gause\'s competitive exclusion principle states that','[{"text": "Humans are the most wide spread agents of disturbance.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In a competition for similar resource both the participants are benefitted.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In a competition, both the participants are excluded.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two closely related species competing for the same resources cannot co-exist indefinitely and competitively inferior one will be eliminated eventually.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Gause\'s principle states that similar species cannot coexist for long in the same ecological niche because competing for the same critical resources within an environment; one of them will eventually outcompete and displace the other.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1873,'biology',11,286,553,'Read the following statements on lipids and find out correct set of statements :<br>(a) Lecithin found in the plasma membrane is a glycolipid<br>(b) Saturated fatty acids possess one or more c=c bonds<br>(c) Gingely oil has lower melting point, hence remains as oil in winter<br>(d) Lipids are generally insoluble in water but soluble in some organic solvents(e) When fatty acid is esterified with glycerol, monoglycerides are formed <br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "(a), (d) and (e) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(c), (d) and (e) only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(a), (b) and (d) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(a), (b) and (c) only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Lecithin in plasma membrane is a phospholipid. Saturated fatty acids possess C-C bonds',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1875,'biology',105,1283,3104,'A wasp pollinating a fig flower is an example of','[{"text": "Commensalism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amensalism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parasitism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutualism", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'It is an example of mutualism where both plant and animal are benefited. Plants need the help of animals for pollinating their flowers and dispersing their seeds. Plants offer rewards or fees in the form of pollen and nectar for pollinators and juicy and nutritious fruits for seed dispersers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1876,'biology',103,969,2256,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Any agent that induces cancer is Carcinogenic or oncogenic agent.<br></div><div class="column-right">All cells carry c-onc or protooncogenes.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1877,'biology',11,293,561,'A dehydration reaction links two glucose molecules to produce maltose. If the formula for glucose is ${C_6}{H_{12}}{O_6}$ then what is the formula for maltose?','[{"text": "${C_{12}}{H_{24}}{O_{12}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${C_{12}}{H_{22}}{O_{11}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${C_{12}}{H_{24}}{O_{11}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${C_{12}}{H_{20}}{O_{10}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The formula for maltose is ${C_{12}}{H_{22}}{O_{11}}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1879,'biology',105,1281,3098,'The density of a population in a given habitat during a given period, fluctuates due to changes in four basic processes On this basis choose the correct option to fill up A and B boxes in the given diagram.','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}=$ Natality + Immigration, $\\\\mathrm{B}=$ Mortality + Emigration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}=$ Natality + Mortality $\\\\mathrm{B}=$ Immigration + Emigration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}=$ Birth rate + Death rate, $\\\\mathrm{B}=$ Mortality + Emigration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}=$ Natality + Emigration, $\\\\mathrm{B}=$ Mortality + Immigration", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Natality and immigration cause an increase in population size while mortality and emigration cause a decrease in population size.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/105_1879_question_1.png'),
(1880,'biology',103,971,2258,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Dependence is the tendency of the body to manifest a characteristic and unpleasant withdrawal syndrome<br></div><div class="column-right">Plasmodium enters the human body through the bite of infected female Anopheles mosquito.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1881,'biology',11,293,561,'Match column – I with column - II<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A Protein<br>B Unsaturated fatty acid<br>C Nucleic acid<br>D Polysaccharide</div><div class="column-right">P  C = C double bonds<br>Q  Phosphodiester bonds<br>R  Glycosidic bonds<br>S  Peptide bonds</div></div>','[{"text": "A - S, B - P, C - Q, D - R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - P, B - S, C - R, D - Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - P, C - S, D - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S, B - R, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A - S, B - P, C - Q, D - R',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1882,'biology',105,1283,3102,'Which of the following is not a parasitic adaptation?','[{"text": "Loss of unnecessary sense organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Absence of adhesive organs or suckers", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Loss of digestive system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "High reproductive capacity", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In addition to all other parasitic adaptations like loss of unnecessary sense organs, loss of digestive system and high reproductive capacity, parasites also show the presence of adhesive organs or suckers which help them to cling or attach to the host organism.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1884,'biology',103,971,2258,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Dependence leads the patient to ignore all social norms in order to get sufficient funds to satiate his/her needs.<br></div><div class="column-right">Excessive doses of drugs may lead to coma and death due to respiratory failure, heart failure or cerebral hemorrhage</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
