(1887,'biology',105,1278,3095,'Homeostasis is a condition where the organisms','[{"text": "Maintain a constant internal environment in everchanging external environment", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Do not maintain a constant internal environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Change their internal environment according to their external environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Change their internal environment when the external environment is constant", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Homeostasis can be defined as a self-regulating process by which a living organism can maintain internal stability while adjusting to changing external conditions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1888,'biology',103,965,2247,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left"><i>Salmonella typhi</i> causes Typhoid fever in human beings<br></div><div class="column-right">Widal test is used to confirm typhoid.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1889,'biology',11,288,556,'Which of the following are not polymeric?','[{"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polysaccharides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleic acids", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lipid is formed when glycerol molecule combines with fatty acid. Lipid is not a polymer because it contain any one molecule. Proteins are formed of units called amino acids. Polysaccharides contains units of monosaccharides. Nucleic acid is formed of nucleotides.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1890,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Match the type of adaptation given in Column-I with their examples given in Column-II. Select the option showing correct combination.<br>Choose the correct option from the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Biochemical adaptation<br>B. Behavioural adaptation<br>C. Physiological adaptation<br>D. Morphological adaptation</div><div class="column-right">P. Desert lizards<br>Q. Deep sea fishes<br>R. <i>Opuntia</i><br>S. Kangaroo rats</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q,B - R,C - S,D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - P,B - Q,C - R,D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q,B - P,C - S,D - R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - S,B - R,C - Q,D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Biochemical adaptation: A large variety of marine invertebrates and fish live at great depths in the ocean where the pressure could be $>100$ times the normal atmospheric pressure that we experience. They live under such high pressures because of the presence of some antifreeze proteins in their body.<br>• Behavioural adaptation: Some organisms show behaviour responses to cope up with variations in their environment. Desert lizards lack the physiological ability that mammals have to deal with the high temperatures of their habitat, but manage to keep their body. Temperature fairly constant by behavioural means. They bask in the sun and absorbs heat when their body temperature drops down the comport zone, but move into shade when the ambient temperatures starts increasing.<br>• Physiological adaptation: In the absence of external source of water, the kangaroo rat in North American deserts is capable of meeting all its water requirements through its internal fat oxidation (in which water is a byproduct). It also has the ability to concentrate its urine so that minimum volume of water is used to remove excretory products.<br>• Morphological adaptation: Many desert plants have a thick cuticle on their leaf surfaces and have their stomata arranged in deep pits (sunken) to minimise water loss through transpiration. Some desert plants like <i>Opuntia</i> have no leaves - they are reduced to spines and the photosynthetic function is taken over by the flattened stems.<br>',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1892,'biology',103,971,2258,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Those who take drugs intravenously are much more likely to acquire AIDS and Hepatitis B.<br></div><div class="column-right">The chronic use of drugs and alcohol damages nervous system and liver (cirrhosis).</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1893,'biology',11,290,558,'The two functional groups characteristic of sugars are','[{"text": "Carbonyl and phosphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbonyl and methyl", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydroxyl and methyl", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbonyl and hydroxyl", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sugar is a term which denotes Carbohydrates. Carbohydrates are polyhydroxy aldehyde, ketone or their derivatives, which means they have carbonyl and hydroxyl groups',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1895,'biology',105,1281,3098,'The equation of Verhulst-Pearl logistic growth is $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{dN}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=\\mathrm{rN}\\left[\\dfrac{\\mathrm{K}-\\mathrm{N}}{\\mathrm{K}}\\right]$<br>From this equation, K indicates:','[{"text": "Intrinsic rate of natural increase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biotic potential", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carrying capacity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Population density", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In the equation $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{dN}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=\\mathrm{rN}\\left[\\dfrac{\\mathrm{K}-\\mathrm{N}}{\\mathrm{K}}\\right]$<br>K represents carrying capacity',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
