(1934,'biology',11,290,558,'The chitinous exoskeleton of arthropods is formed by the polymerisation of','[{"text": "N-acetyl glucosamine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lipoglycans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Keratin sulphate chondroitin sulphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D-glucosamine", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The exoskeleton of arthropods is formed of chitin which is a structural polysaccharide. It is a complex carbohydrate which is formed by monomers of N-acetyl glucosamine by 1,4- $\\beta $ linkages.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
