(1943,'biology',11,286,553,'A phosphoglyceride is always made up of','[{"text": "A saturated or unsaturated fatty acid esterified to a glycerol molecule to which a phosphate group is also attached", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A saturated or unsaturated fatty acid esterified to a phosphate group which is also attached to glycerol molecule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only a saturated fatty acid esterified to a glycerol molecule to which a phosphate group is also attached", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only an unsaturated fatty acid esterified to a glycerol molecule to which a phosphate group is also attached", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Esters of fatty acids and glycerol containing a phosphate group is known as a phosphoglyceride.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1945,'biology',103,966,2248,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Innate immunity is non-specific defence.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It consists of four types of barriers.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Innate immunity refers to non-specific defense mechanisms that come into play immediately or within hours of an antigen\'s appearance in the body. Four barriers are physical, physiological, cellular and cytokine barriers.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1946,'biology',11,297,566,'Transition state structure of the substrate formed during a enzymatic reaction is','[{"text": "Transient and unstable", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Permanent and stable", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transient but stable", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Permanent but unstable", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The transition state is the transitory of molecular structure in which the molecule is no longer a substrate but not yet a product. The substrate binds to the enzyme at its active site forming an enzyme-substrate complex. This complex formation is a transient and unstable process and soon the product is formed at the active site.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1948,'biology',73,150,339,'In the taxonomic categories which heirarchial arrangement in ascending order is correct in case of animals?','[{"text": "Kingdom, Class, Phylum, Family, Order, Genus, Species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kingdom, Order, Class, Phylum, Family, Genus, Species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kingdom, Order, Phylum, Class, Family, Genus, Species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kingdom, Phylum, Class, Order, Family, Genus, Species", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Correct hierarchical arrangement in ascending order of taxonomic categories in animal taxonomy is:<br>Kingdom → Phylum →Class → Order →Family → Genus → Species',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1949,'biology',103,966,2249,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> T-lymphocytes mediate CMI response.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The above response makes it easy to transplant organs.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cell-mediated immunity (CMI) is an immune response that does not involve antibodies, but rather involves the activation of phagocytes, antigen-specific cytotoxic Tlymphocytes, and the release of various cytokines in response to an antigen. The immune response to a transplanted organ consists of both cellular(lymphocyte mediated) and humoral (antibody mediated) mechanisms. Although other cell types are also involved, the $\\mathrm{T}$ cells are central in the rejection of grafts',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1950,'biology',11,297,570,'The essential chemical components of many coenzymes are','[{"text": "Carbohydrates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vitamins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleic acids", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The essential chemical component of many coenzymes are vitamins, e.g., coenzymes NAD and NADP.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1952,'biology',73,150,339,'Which one of the following belongs to the family Muscidae?','[{"text": "Fire fly", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Grasshopper", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cockroach", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "House fly", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The housefly is classified in the phylum Arthropoda, class Insecta, order Diptera, family Muscidae. Fireflies belong to the Lampyridae family. Most grasshoppers belong to the family Acrididae. Cockroach belong to family Blattidae.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1963,'biology',11,297,570,'For its activity, carboxypeptidase requires:','[{"text": "Zinc", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Iron", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Niacin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Copper", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Carboxypeptidase is a metallo-enzyme which contains zinc. It has been reported that the enzyme can be de-activated by removal of zinc and that activity can be restored by the addition of zinc, cobaltous, ferrous, nickel and manganous ions but not by addition of cadmium, magnesium or calcium ions.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1953,'biology',103,966,2249,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> An antibody is represented by $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~L}_{2}$.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Each antibody is made of four peptide chains.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Immunoglobulins, also known as antibodies, are glycoprotein molecules produced by plasma cells (white blood cells). The Ig monomer is a "Y"-shaped molecule that consists of four polypeptide chains; two identical heavy chains and two identical light chains connected by disulfide bonds',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
