(2001,'biology',103,966,2253,'In higher vertebrates the immune system can distinguish self cells and non self. If this property is lost due to genetic abnormality and it attacks self cells, then it leads to.<br>','[{"text": "Allergic response", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Graft rejection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Auto immune disease", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Active immunity", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When the immune system cannot differentiate between self and non- self-cells then the immune system attacks and destroys self-cells and this is called auto immunity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2003,'biology',73,150,339,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Species are potentially interbreeding natural population that are isolated from other such group<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Reproductive isolation brings about distinctive morphological character','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct answer is ‘Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation for Assertion’.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2004,'biology',11,297,570,'An organic substance bound to an enzyme and essential for its activity is called','[{"text": "Isoenzyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coenzyme", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Holoenzyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apoenzyme", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Coenzymes are small molecules. They cannot by themselves catalyse a reaction but they can help enzymes to do so.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2005,'biology',103,966,2251,'Antivenom injection contains preformed antibodies while polio drops that are administered into the body contains','[{"text": "Activated pathogens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Harvested antibodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gamma globulin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Attenuated pathogens<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The oral polio vaccines consist of attenuated pathogens.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2007,'biology',73,149,338,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Each taxonomic group can have two or more names.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Name should be short, precise and easy to pronounce.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The scientific names ensure that each organism has only one name. Description of any organism should enable the people (in any part of the world) to arrive at the same name. They also ensure that such a name has not been used for any other known organism.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2008,'biology',11,286,553,'Which of the following is not a constituent of cell membrane','[{"text": "Proline", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phospholipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cholesterol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycolipids", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The principal components of the plasma membrane are lipids (phospholipids and cholesterol), proteins and carbohydrates.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2009,'biology',103,966,2253,'Which of the following is not an autoimmune disease?<br>','[{"text": "Alzheimer\'s", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rheumatoid disease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Psoriasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vitiligo", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Auto immune disease is a an illness that occurs when the body tissues are attacked by its own immune system. Alzheimer\'s disease is a progressive disease that destroys memory and other important mental functions. Alzheimer\'s disease is due to deficiency of neurotransmitter acetylcholine. It is not an auto immune disease.Rheumatoid arthritis (RA) is an autoimmune disease that can cause joint pain and damage throughout your body.Vitiligo is a condition in which the skin loses its pigment cells (melanocytes). Psoriasis is a long-lasting autoimmune disease characterized by patches of abnormal skin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2011,'biology',73,149,338,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> To give the scientific name of plant there is ICBN<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It uses articles, photographs and recommendations to name the plant','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The correct answer is ‘Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation for Assertion’.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2012,'biology',11,297,568,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Competitive inhibitor is also called substrate analogue.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It resembles the enzymes in structure.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Competitive inhibitor resembles the enzyme in it’s molecular structure.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2013,'biology',103,970,2257,'Which part of poppy plant is used to obtain the drug "Smack”?','[{"text": "Roots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Latex", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Flowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leaves<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Heroin is commonly called as \'Smack\'. Chemically it is diacetylmorphine, obtained by acetylation of morphine. It is extracted from latex of poppy plant (<i>Papaver somniferum</i>).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2015,'biology',73,150,339,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The complexity of classification increases from kingdom to species<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Common characters increases from kingdom to species','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The complexity of classification increases from kingdom to species because organisms are classified into two kingdoms-plantae and animalia. But species are the largest group of organisms that can interbreed to produce fertile offspring.<br>As we go higher from species to kingdom, the number of common characteristics goes on decreasing. Lower the taxa, more are the characteristics that the members within the taxon share. Higher the category, greater is the difficulty of determining the relationship to other taxa at the same level.<br>So, the correct answer is ‘Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation for Assertion’.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2016,'biology',11,290,558,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cellulose is a homopolymer.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It consists of glucose as a monomer','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and\nReason is correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2017,'biology',103,965,2247,'In which disease does mosquito transmitted pathogen cause chronic inflammation of lymphatic vessels?<br>','[{"text": "Ringworm disease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ascariasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Elephantiasis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amoebiasis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Elephantiasis is caused by filarial worm, <i>Wuchereria bancrofti</i> and it is transmitted to healthy person by Culex mosquito. It slowly develops in chronic inflammation of the organs in which they live for many years, usually the lymphatic vessels of the lower limbs.<br>Amoebiasis is caused by Entamoeba histolytica (protozoa), Ascariasis is caused by Ascaris (an intestinal parasite ) transmitted through contaminated food and water.Ringworms are generally caused by Fungi (belonging to genera Microsporum, Trichophyton and Epidermophyton) generally acquired from soil or by using towels, clothes or even the comb of infected individuals',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2019,'biology',73,150,339,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The “biological species” concept help us to ask how species are formed<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The concept of biological species focuses our attention on the question on how reproductive isolation comes about','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ernst Mayr proposed the biological species concept, which defines species as groups of actually or potentially inter-breeding natural populations which are reproductively isolated from other such groups.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2020,'biology',11,297,568,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> An example of non-competitive inhibitor is cyanide<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Cyanide kills animals by inhibiting cytochrome oxidase.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2021,'biology',103,966,2250,'Colostrum the yellowish fluid, secreted by mother during the initial days of lactation is very essential to impart immunity to the new born infants because it contains','[{"text": "Natural killer cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Macrophages", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Immunoglobulin A", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Colostrum has abundant IgA antibodies that provide naturally acquired passive immunity and protect the infant (from gastrointestinal infections) during first few months of life.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2024,'biology',11,297,569,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Enzymes are divided into different families .<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> All enzymes catalyse the same reactions.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Most of these enzymes have been classified into different groups based on the type of reactions they catalyse. Enzymes are divided into 6 classes each with 4-13 subclasses and named accordingly by a four-digit number.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2025,'biology',103,965,2247,'Identify the correct pair representing the causative agent of typhoid fever and the confirmatory test for typhoid.<br>','[{"text": "<i>Plasmodium vivax</i> / UTI test", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Streptococcus pneumoniae</i> / Widal test", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Salmonella typhi</i> / Anthrone test", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Salmonella typhi</i> / Widal test", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<i>Salmonella typhi</i> is the causative agent. Confirmatory test $=$ Widal test, it\'s based onantigen antibody reaction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2028,'biology',11,297,570,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> A coenzyme or metal ion tightly bound to enzyme protein is called prosthetic group.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> A complete catalytically active enzyme together with its bound prosthetic group is called apoenzyme','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'An apoenzyme is an inactive enzyme, activation of the enzyme occurs upon binding of an organic or inorganic cofactor. Therefore, the Assertion is true but Reason is false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2030,'biology',103,970,2257,'Drug called \'Heroin\' is synthesized by<br>','[{"text": "Methylation of morphine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acetylation of morphine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glycosylation of morphine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nitration of morphine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Heroin, commonly called smack and is chemically diacetylmorphine which is synthesized by acetylation of morphine.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2031,'biology',73,150,339,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The animal class, Carnivora, includes Felidae and Canidae.</div><div class="column-right">Order Primata comprising monkey, gorilla and gibbon is placed in class Mammalia</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Satement B is correct .The animal order, Carnivora, includes families like Felidae and Canidae.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2032,'biology',11,297,570,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Coenzyme is a non-protein group without which certain enzymes are inactive or incomplete.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Coenzymes not only provide a point of attachment of the chemical group being transformed, but also influence the properties of the group.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2034,'biology',103,966,2250,'Identify the wrong statement with reference to immunity.<br>','[{"text": "When ready-made antibodies are directly given, it is called \\"Passive immunity\\".", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Active immunity is quick and gives full response.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Foetus receives some antibodies from mother, it is an example for passive immunity.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "When exposed to antigen (living or dead) antibodies are produced in the host\'s body. It is called \\"Active immunity\\".", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Active immunity is quick and gives full response.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2035,'biology',73,150,339,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Three different genera Solanum, Petunia and Allium are placed in the family Solanaceae</div><div class="column-right">Felidae and Canidae, are two different genus.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both are wrong . Three different genera Solanum, Petunia and Datura are placed in the family Solanaceae. Felidae and Canidae,are two different families .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2036,'biology',11,297,568,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The enzyme work best at body temperature.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> High temperature denatures the enzyme permanently and freezing make them temporarily inactive.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'This optimal temperature is usually around human body temperature ($37.5^\\circ C$) for the enzymes in human cells. Above this temperature the enzyme structure begins to break down (denature) since at higher temperatures intra- and intermolecular bonds are broken as the enzyme molecules gain even more kinetic energy. At the point of freezing, molecular motion decreases drastically as solid formation occurs and molecules are locked into rigid crystalline formations. As a result, enzyme-substrate collisions are extremely rare once freezing occurs and enzyme activity is nearly zero below freezing. Therefore, both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2038,'biology',103,965,2247,'The infectious stage of <em>Plasmodium </em>that enters the human body is:','[{"text": "Sporozoites", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Female", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male gametocytes gametocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trophozoites", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<em>Sporozoites</em> is the infectious stage of Plasmodium',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2039,'biology',73,149,338,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The word systematics is derived from the Latin word ‘systema’ which means systematic arrangement of organisms.</div><div class="column-right">Linnaeus used Systema Naturae as the title of his publication.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2070,'biology',73,148,337,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Yeast and hydra reproduce through sexual reproduction called budding</div><div class="column-right">In bacteria, unicellular algae or Amoeba, reproduction is synonymous with growth</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Satement B is correct. Yeast and hydra reproduce through Asexual reproduction called budding.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2040,'biology',11,297,567,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Enzymes lower the activation energy of the reactant molecule to make its transition into product easier.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Enzymes are highly substrate specific.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Enzymes are highly substrate specific. The enzyme’s ability to make the reaction faster depends on the fact that it stabilises the transition state. The transition state’s energy or, in terms of a reaction, the activation energy is the minimum energy that is needed to break certain bonds of the reactants so as to turn them into products. Therefore, both Assertion and Reason are true and but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2042,'biology',103,965,2247,'Match the following diseases with the causative organism and select the correct option.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Typhoid<br>B. Pneumonia<br>C. Filariasis<br>D. Malaria</div><div class="column-right">P. Wuchereria<br>Q. Plasmodium<br>R. Salmonella<br>S. Haemophilus</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R, B - S, C - P, D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q, B - P, C - R,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - S, B - P, C - Q, D - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q, B - R, C - P, D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{A - R, B - S, C - P, D - Q}}$',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2043,'biology',73,149,338,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The scientific term for these categories is taxa.</div><div class="column-right">Characterisation, identification, classification and nomenclature are the processes that are basic to taxonomy</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2044,'biology',11,290,558,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Glucose is the main fuel in the living cells.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The cells draw glucose from the blood.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Glucose is the major fuel for most living\ncells. The oxidative breakdown of glucose by\nour body to produce energy is called respiration.\nTherefore, both Assertion and Reason are true\nand but Reason is not the correct explanation\nof Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2046,'biology',103,965,2247,'Match Column - I with Column - II<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Filariasis<br>B. Ameobiasis<br>C. Pneumonia<br>D. Ringworm</div><div class="column-right">P. Haemophilus influenzae<br>Q. Trichophyton<br>R. Wuchereria bancrofti<br>S. Entamoeba histolytica</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A -  S, B  -  P, C  -  R, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A -  R, B  -  S, C  -  P, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A -  P, B  -  Q, C  -  S, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A -  Q, B  -  R, C  -  P, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{A -  R, B  -  S, C  -  P, D  -  Q}}$',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2047,'biology',73,149,338,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The first word denoting the genus starts with a small letter while the specific epithet starts with a capital letter.</div><div class="column-right">Both the words in a biological name, when handwritten, both words are underlined together, or printed in italics to indicate their Italian origin.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both are wrong . The first word denoting the genus starts with a capital letter while the specific epithet starts with a small letter. Both the words in a biological name, when handwritten, are separately underlined, or\nprinted in italics to indicate their Latin origin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2048,'biology',11,293,561,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Macromolecules are formed from the micromolecule monomers by condensation.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> There is loss of water molecule for the addition of each micromolecule in the synthesis of macromolecules.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Most macromolecules are made from single sub-units, or building blocks, called monomers. The monomers combine with each other using covalent bonds to form larger molecules known as polymers. In the process, a water molecule is formed. Therefore, both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2050,'biology',103,966,2253,'Given below are two statements:<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Autoimmune disorder is a condition where body defense mechanism recognizes its own cells as foreign bodies.<br></div><div class="column-right">Rheumatoid arthritis is a condition where body does not attack self cells.<br><br>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Autoimmune disorder is a condition where body defense mechanism recognises its own cells are foreign bodies. Rheumatoid arthritis is an autoimmune disorder in which body attacks its own self cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2051,'biology',73,149,338,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Biological names are generally in italics and written in latin .</div><div class="column-right">They are Latinised or derived from Latin irrespective of their origin.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Satement B is correct . Biological names are generally in Latin and written in italics. They are Latinised or derived from Latin irrespective of their origin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2052,'biology',11,286,552,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Amino acids are amphoteric in their function.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> All amino acids are necessary for our body.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Amino acids are amphoteric, which means they have acidic and basic tendencies. The carboxyl group is able to lose a proton and the amine group is able to accept a proton. Nine amino acids are essential for humans and must be obtained through food because the body cannot synthesize them, Assertion is true and reason is false. ',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2054,'biology',73,149,338,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In Binomial nomenclature, the specific epithet tells us about the more common feature.</div><div class="column-right">In Binomial nomenclature, the generic name tells us about the more characteristic feature</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2055,'biology',103,966,2249,'Select the incorrect statement with respect to acquired immunity.<br>','[{"text": "Anamnestic response is elicited on subsequent encounters with the same pathogen.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anamnestic response is due to memory of first encounter.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acquired immunity is non-specific type of defense present at the time of birth.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Primary response is produced when our body encounters a pathogen for the first time.<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Non-specific type of defence present at the time of birth is termed innate immunity. Acquired immunity is gained by individual during their lifetime, when they interact with pathogen.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2056,'biology',11,297,570,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In the solutions of different pH, structure of amino acids changes.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It is because of the ionisable nature of $ - N{H_2}$ and $ - COOH$ groups.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2058,'biology',73,149,338,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The scientific names ensure that each organism has only one name.</div><div class="column-right">The vernacular names ensure that such a name has not been used for any other known organism.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement A is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2081,'biology',73,148,337,'Which of the following is a defining characteristic of living organisms?','[{"text": "Growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ability to make sound", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Response to external stimuli", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Rest of the characters may not be apparent at every instance of time. But response to external stimuli can always be confirmed as and when required. So, this is considered as a defining characteristic of living organisms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2059,'biology',103,965,2247,'Match the following columns and choose the correct option:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <i>Haemophilus influenzae</i><br>B.  <i>Entamoeba histolytica </i><br>C.  <i>Plasmodium falciparum </i><br>D.  <i>Wuchereria bancrofti </i></div><div class="column-right">P. Malignant malaria<br>Q. Elephantiasis<br>R. Pneumonia<br>S. Amoebiasis</div></div>','[{"text": "A - R, B - S, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - S, B - P, C - Q, D - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - R, B - P, C - Q, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - R, C - S, D - P", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-R, B-S, C-P, D-Q<br>Haemophilus influenza Pneumonia<br>Entamoeba histolytica Amoebiasis<br>Plasmodium falciparum Malignant malaria<br>Wuchereria bancrofti Elephantiasis',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2060,'biology',11,290,558,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cellulose is a polymer of glucose.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It is made of several glucose units.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2062,'biology',103,965,2247,'The toxic substance ‘haemozoin’ responsible for high fever and chill, is released in which of the following diseases?','[{"text": "Pneumonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Malaria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Typhoid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dengue", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Malaria<br>Haemozoin ganuales from RBC’S result in high fever & chill',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2063,'biology',73,148,337,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Metabolic reactions can be demonstrated outside the body in cell-free systems.</div><div class="column-right">An isolated metabolic reaction(s) outside the body of an organism, performed in a test tube is neither living nor non-living</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2064,'biology',11,292,560,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Haemoglobin is a quaternary protein.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It consists of four amino acid unit.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Quaternary structure is the fourth level of protein structure, which is not found in all proteins. It exists where two or more tertiary units also called a sub-unit combine to form one functioning protein. Eg: Molecule of Haemoglobin consists of four polypeptide chains i.e., two identical α-chains consisting of 141 amino acid residues and two identical β-chains consisting of 146 amino acid residues.Each chain is called a sub-unit and together they form the quaternary structure of the protein Haemoglobin. Therefore, the Assertion is true but Reason is false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2066,'biology',73,148,337,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The sum total of all the chemical reactions occurring in our body is metabolism.</div><div class="column-right">Not all plants, animals, fungi and microbes exhibit metabolism.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Satement A is correct . All plants, animals, fungi and microbes exhibit metabolism. The sum total of all the chemical reactions occurring in our body is metabolism.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2067,'biology',103,965,2247,'Identify the symptoms of pneumonia','[{"text": "Nasal congestion and discharge, cough, sore throat, headache", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Constipation, Abdominal pain, cramps, blood clots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "High fever, weakness, stomach pain, loss of appetite", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Difficulty in breathing, fever, chills, cough headache", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pneumonia is caused by Haemophilous influenza bacteria which leads to filling of alveoli & it leads to difficulty in breathing; fever; chills; cough & headache',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2068,'biology',11,297,568,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">When the binding of the chemical shuts off enzyme activity, the process is called inhibition and the chemical is called an inhibitor.</div><div class="column-right">When the inhibitor closely resembles the substrate in its molecular structure and inhibits the activity of the enzyme, it is known as Non-competitive inhibitor.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When the inhibitor closely resembles the substrate in its molecular structure and inhibits the activity of the enzyme, it is known as competitive inhibitor.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2071,'biology',103,970,2257,'Match Column I with Column II<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Heroin<br>B. Marijuana<br>C. Cocaine<br>D. Morphine</div><div class="column-right">P. Effect on cardiovascular system<br>Q. Slow down body function<br>R. Painkiller<br>S. Interfere with transport of dopamine</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-S, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Heroin belongs to the category of opioids\nand it is a depressant that slows down body\nfunctions.\n<br>• Marijuana is known for its effect on the\ncardiovascular system of the body.\n<br>• Cocaine interferes with the transport of the\nneurotransmitter dopamine.\n<br>Morphine is used is a sedative and painkiller',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2072,'biology',11,297,568,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Enzyme succinic dehydrogenase is inhibited by malonate by Non-competitive inhibition.</div><div class="column-right">Competitive inhibitors are often used in the control of bacterial pathogens.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Enzyme succinic dehydrogenase is inhibited by malonate by competitive inhibition.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2074,'biology',73,148,337,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Ernst Mayr, pioneered the currently accepted definition of a biological species</div><div class="column-right">Ernst Mayr, the Harvard University evolutionary biologist who has been called ‘The Darwin of the 21st century’</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Satement A is correct. Ernst Mayr, the Harvard University evolutionary biologist who has been called ‘The Darwin of the ${20^{th}}$ century’.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2075,'biology',103,968,2255,'In which blood corpuscles, the HIV undergoes replication and produces progeny viruses?','[{"text": "TH cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B-lymphocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Basophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eosinophils", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'HIV enters into helper T-lymphocytes (TH),\nreplicates and produces progeny viruses. The\nprogeny viruses released into blood attack\nother helper lymphocytes',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2076,'biology',11,297,569,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Enzymes are divided into six classes each with 4-13 subclasses</div><div class="column-right">Each Enzyme named accordingly by a Three -digit number.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Each enzyme is named accordingly by a four digit of.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2077,'biology',103,965,2247,'Match Column I with Column II.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Ringworm<br>B. Filariasis<br>C. Malaria<br>D. Pneumonia</div><div class="column-right">P. <i>Haemophilus influenzae</i><br>Q. <i>Trichophyton</i><br>R. <i>Wuchereria bancrofti</i><br>S. <i>Plasmodium vivax</i></div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'P. Ringworm is caused by\nTrichophyton.\n<br>Q. Filariasis is caused by Wuchereria\nbancrofti.\n<br>R. Malaria is caused by Plasmodium species.\n<br>S. Pneumonia is caused by Haemophilus\ninfluenzae.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2079,'biology',73,148,337,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Increase in mass and increase in number of individuals are twin characteristics of growth</div><div class="column-right">In majority of lower animals and plants, growth and reproduction are mutually exclusive events.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Satement A is correct. In majority of higher animals and plants, growth and reproduction are mutually exclusive events.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2080,'biology',11,297,569,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Enzymes which catalyse oxidoreduction between two substrates are called Oxidoreductases/ dehydrogenases.</div><div class="column-right">Enzymes which catalyse the linking together of 2 compounds are called Lyases.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ligases: Enzymes catalysing the linking together of 2 compounds',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2083,'biology',103,966,2248,'If the person shows the production of interferons in his body, chances are that he is suffering from:','[{"text": "Malaria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Measles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tetanus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anthrax", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Interferons are a group of signalling proteins made and released by host cells in response to the presence of several viruses. A virus-infected cell will release interferons causing nearly cells to heighten their anti-viral defences. Of the given options, only measles is a viral disease.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2084,'biology',11,297,570,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Non-protein constituents, which are bound to the enzyme and make the enzyme catalytically active, are called cofactors.</div><div class="column-right">The protein portion of the enzymes is called the Apoenzyme.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2086,'biology',103,966,2251,'Match the types of immunity listed in Column I with the examples listed in Column II. Choose the answer that gives the correct combination of alphabets of the two columns.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Natural active<br>B. Artificial passive<br>C. Artificial active<br>D. Natural passive<br></div><div class="column-right">P. Immunity\ndeveloped by\nheredity<br>Q. From mother to\nfoetus through\nplacenta<br>R. Injection of\nantiserum to\ntravellers<br>S. Fighting\ninfections\nnaturally<br>T.Induced by\nvaccination</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  T; B  -  ;S  C -  R; D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S; B  -  T;  C -  Q; D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S; B  -  R;  C -  T; D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P; B  -  Q;  C -  R; D  -  T}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Naturally acquired active immunity occurs when a person is exposed to a live pathogen, develops the disease, and then develops immunity.<br>Artificial passive immunity can be induced artifically when antibodies are given as a medication to a nonimmune individual.<br>Artifically acquired active immunity can be induced by a vaccine, a substance that contains the antigen.<br>Naturally acquired passive immunity occurs during pregnancy, in which certain antibodies are passed from the maternal blood into the foetal bloodstream in the form of IgG.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2010,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2088,'biology',11,297,570,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Co-enzymes are organic compounds but their association with the apoenzyme is only transient, usually occurring during the course of catalysis.</div><div class="column-right">Prosthetic groups are organic compounds and are distinguished from other cofactors in that they are loosely bound to the apoenzyme.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Prosthetic groups are organic compounds and are distinguished from other cofactors in that they are tightly bound to the apoenzyme.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2090,'biology',103,971,2258,'Every time, when the dosage of a drug has to be increased to achieve the same \'kick\' that initially occurred in response to a smaller dose, this condition is known as:','[{"text": "Tolerance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rebound effect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Addiction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Withdrawal symptoms", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Tolerance is the reduction or loss of the normal response to a drug or other substance that usually provokes a reaction in the body. Drug tolerance may develop after taking a particular drug over a long period of time. In such cases increased doses are necessary to produce the desired effect. Some drugs that cause tolerance also cause dependence.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2091,'biology',73,150,339,'The taxonomic unit ‘Phylum’ in the classification of animals is equivalent to which hierarchial level in classification of plants','[{"text": "Class", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Order", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Division", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Family", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In Animal kingdom, phylum comes just after the kingdom. Similarly, in the plant kingdom, division comes just after the kingdom.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2092,'biology',11,286,552,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Amino acids are monomers of nucleic acids<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Protein amino acids have an unlimited variety.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A monomer is the basic unit that binds chemically to other molecules to form a polymer. For proteins, the monomers are amino acids. For nucleic acids, the monomers are nucleotides which is made of a pentose sugar, a nitrogenous base and a phosphate group. Therefore, both Assertion and Reason are false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2093,'biology',73,149,338,'The term ‘systematics’ refers to:','[{"text": "Identification and study of organ systems", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Identification and preservation of plants and animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diversity of kinds of organisms and their relationship", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Study of habitats of organisms and their classification", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In fact, the need for a proper classification system was felt because of huge diversity of organisms. Based on certain relationships, organisms were classified into different group and sub-groups.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2095,'biology',103,969,2256,'Which of the following is not a character of cancerous tissues in our body?','[{"text": "Contact inhibition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neoplasia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metastasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inability for differentiation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Contact inhibition is a process of arresting cell growth when cells come in contact with each other. As a result, normal cells stop proliferating when they form a monolayer in a culture dish. Contact inhibition is a powerful anticancer mechanism that is lost in cancer cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2096,'biology',11,297,568,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Each enzyme shows its lowest activity at a particular temperature called the optimum temperature</div><div class="column-right">Enzyme activity increases both below and above the optimum value.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Each enzyme shows its highest activity at a particular temperature and pH called the optimum tem-perature and optimum pH. Activity declines both below and above the optimum value',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2097,'biology',73,150,339,'As we go from species to kingdom in a taxonomic hierarchy, the number of common characteristics','[{"text": "Will decrease", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Will increase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Remain same", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "May increase or decrease", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Number of common characters is maximum among members of a particular species. On the other hand, number of common characters is minimum among members of a particular kingdom.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2098,'biology',103,966,2248,'Interferons are the protein molecules produced from the :','[{"text": "Normal cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Infected host cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Macrophages", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B- lymphocytes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Interferons are produced by virus infected cells to inhibit viral replication in uninfected cells. They activate cytotoxic T cells and natural killer cells, inhibit cell division and suppress the formation of tumours.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2100,'biology',11,297,566,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">When ice melting to water is an example of chemical reaction.</div><div class="column-right">Hydrolysis of starch into glucose is a physical process.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'When ice melts into water, or when water becomes a vapour. These are also physical processes. Hydrolysis of starch into Glucose and fructose is a chemical process',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2101,'biology',73,150,339,'Match the following and choose the correct option:<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Family<br>B. Kingdom<br>C. Order<br>D. Species<br>E. Genus</div><div class="column-right">P.  tuberosum<br>Q.  Polymoniales<br>R.  Solanum<br>S.  Plantae<br>T.  Solanaceae</div></div>','[{"text": "P-D, Q-C, R-E, S-B, T-A", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "P-E, Q-D, R-B, S-A, T-C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P-D, Q-E, R-B, S-A, T-C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P-E, Q-C, R-B, S-A, T-D", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The order of taxa is as follows:<br>Kingdom Order Family Genus Species<br>Classification of potato:<br>Kingdom: Plantae<br>order: Polymoniales<br>Family: Solanaceae<br>Genus: <i>Solanum</i><br>Species: <i>tuberosum</i>.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2102,'biology',103,969,2256,'One of the following is incorrect about cancer cells.','[{"text": "They exhibit the property of contact inhibition.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They are metastatic.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They exhibit mass proliferation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are produced when cellular oncogenes of normal cells are activated.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Contact inhibition is a process of arresting cell growth when cells come in contact with each other. As a result, normal cells stop proliferating when they form a monolayer in a culture dish. Contact inhibition is a powerful anticancer mechanism that is lost in cancer cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2104,'biology',11,297,567,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The activity of an enzyme can be affected by a change in the conditions which alter the tertiary structure of the protein.</div><div class="column-right">These include temperature, pH, change in substrate concentration or binding of specific chemicals that regulate its activity.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2105,'biology',73,148,337,'All living organisms are linked to one another because','[{"text": "They have common genetic material of\\nthe same type", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They share common genetic material\\nbut to varying degrees", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All have common cellular organization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In fact, the whole theory of evolution is based on similarity of genetic materials which indicates towards common ancestry for living organisms.Variations in similarity of genetic material give biodiversity which we see all around us.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2107,'biology',103,965,2247,'The mature infective stages of malarial parasite which are transferred from mosquito to man are:','[{"text": "Sporozoites", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Merozoites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trophozoites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametocytes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The infective stage of Plasmodium is sporozoite, which is spindle-shaped. These sporozoites, present in the salivary glands of female Anopheles mosquito, enter the blood of the human being with the saliva of the mosquito when it bites a healthy human being.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2108,'biology',11,296,564,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Metabolism does not provide a mechanism for the production of energy.</div><div class="column-right">Living state and metabolism are synonymous</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Metabolism provides a mechanism for the production of energy',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2111,'biology',103,965,2247,'Internal bleeding, muscular pain, blockage of the intestinal passage and anaemia are some of the symptoms caused due to infection by:','[{"text": "<i>Wuchereria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Trichophyton</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ascaris</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Plasmodium</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ascaris worms cause three kinds of damage.<br>Larvae in the lung tissue cause Ascaris pneumonitis. Haemorrhage, edema and blockage of alveoli from worms, dead leucocytes and tissue debris are some of the effects.<br>Adults worms cause malnutrition by feeding mainly on the contents of the intestine. They also release toxic wastes that cause allergic reactions. A large number of worms can cause perforations. If this results in peritonitis, it can even be fatal.<br>Wandering worms cause abscesses in the liver.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2112,'biology',11,297,565,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Non protein catalysts are called ribozymes.</div><div class="column-right">Ribozymes are chemically deoxy ribo nucleic acids.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ribozymes are chemically Ribonucleic acids.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2114,'biology',73,150,339,'Genus represents','[{"text": "An individual plant or animal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A collection of plants or animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Group of closely related species of plants or animals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Taxon genus is just above the taxon species.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2253,'biology',11,297,566,'Which ofthe following reactions is not enzyme-mediated in biological system?','[{"text": "Almost all the reactions are catalysed by enzymes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Untwinding the two strands of DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrolysis of sucrose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Formation of peptide bond", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Almost all the reactions are catalysed by<br>enzymes',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2115,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which of the following is not correct with respect to malaria?','[{"text": "Sporozoites multiply in blood.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Malignant malaria is caused by <i>Plasmodium falciparum</i>.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RBC\'s rupture and release haemozoin which causes chills.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Female Anopheles mosquito is the vector.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Sporozoites (Infective stage of Plasmodium) initially multiply within the liver cells and then attack the red blood cells ( $\\mathrm{RBCs})$ resulting in their rupture.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2116,'biology',11,297,565,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Enzyme catalysts differ from inorganic catalysts in many ways.</div><div class="column-right">Enzymes work efficiently at high temperatures and high pressures, while Inorganic catalysts get damaged at high temperatures.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Inorganic catalysts work efficiently at high temperatures and high pressures, while enzymes get damaged at high temperatures',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2118,'biology',73,150,339,'Which ofthe following ‘suffixes’ used for units of classification in plants indicates a taxonomic category of ‘family’','[{"text": "–ales", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "–onae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "–aceae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "–ae", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'You can consider the names of families, e.g. Solanaceae, fabaceae, etc.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2119,'biology',103,970,2257,'Smack and Crack are produced from:','[{"text": "<i>Cannabis sativa</i> and <i>Atropa belladonna</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Papaver somniferum</i> and <i>Erythroxylon coca</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Cannabis sativa</i> and <i>Papaver somniferum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Erythroxylon coca</i> and <i>Atropa belladonna</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Smack is an opioid narcotic, which is extracted from the latex of poppy plant Papaver somniferum. It is also commonly called Brown Sugar. Cocaine commonly called coke or crack is obtained from the coca plant Erythroxylon coca. Crack is usually snorted.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2120,'biology',11,297,566,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Change in shape without breaking of bonds is called physical process.</div><div class="column-right">When bonds are broken and new bonds are formed during transformation is called chemical reaction.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2123,'biology',103,966,2248,'Identify the incorrect statement from the following.','[{"text": "B-cells produce antibody", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interferons kill viruses.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Response of T-cells is called cell mediated immunity.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Macrophages are the phagocytic cells.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Inteferons are produced by virus infected cells to inhibit viral replication in uninfected cells. They activate cytotoxic $\\mathrm{T}$ cells and natural killer cells, inhibit cell divison and suppress the formation of tumour.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2124,'biology',11,296,564,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Blood concentration of glucose in a normal healthy individual is nanograms/mL.</div><div class="column-right">Blood concentration of hormones is 4.2 mmol/L–6.1 mmol/L</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The blood concentration of glucose in a normal healthy individual is 4.2 mmol/L– 6.1 mmol/L, while that of hormones would be nanograms/mL.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2127,'biology',103,965,2247,'Some of the events occur during life cycle of <i>Plasmodium</i> are given below. Identify the correct statement.','[{"text": "The sporozoites reproduce sexually in liver cells.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The gametocytes develop in RBC.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Female mosquito takes up sporozoites with blood meal.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "When mosquito bites a man, gametocytes are injected.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The infective stage of Plasmodium is sporozoite, which is present in the salivary glands of female Anopheles mosquito, enter the blood of the human being with the saliva of the mosquito. Once they reach the human body they leave the blood and infect the hepatic cells within an hour where they multiply by asexual multiple fission called schizogony.<br>After repeated erythrocytic cycles in Plasmodium, some merozoites develop into sexually differentiated forms caleld gametocytes in the RBC to begin the gametogony. Their maturation takes place in spleen and bone marrow.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2128,'biology',11,296,564,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Living process is a constant effort to prevent falling into equilibrium.</div><div class="column-right">The living state is a non equilibrium steady state</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2130,'biology',103,965,2247,'A doctor identifies symptoms of nasal congestion, headache, sore throat, hoarseness, cough in a patient. The conclusion is that, the patient is infected by a pathogen:','[{"text": "Adeno virus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rhino virus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Plasmodium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Salmonella</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The common cold, or coryza, caused mainly by rhinoviruses. They generally transmit via aerosols of respiratory droplets or indirect contact with the infected. Primary site of infection is nose and respiratory tract. These viruses infect the upper respiratory tract but not the lungs. The symptoms are congestion, nasal discharge, sore throat, hoarseness, cough, headache, tiredness which usually last from 3 to 7 days.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2132,'biology',11,294,562,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Every metabolic reaction is a catalysed reaction.</div><div class="column-right">There is no uncatalysed metabolic conversion in living systems.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2134,'biology',103,970,2257,'Morphine is obtained from the :','[{"text": "Inflorescence of <i>Cannabis</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leaves of <i>Erythroxylum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Latex of Poppy plant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Root of <i>Atropa</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Morphine is obtained form latex of poppy plant (Papaver somniferum). They are analgesic and act on CNS to relieve pain. They are called pain killers also.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2136,'biology',11,294,562,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The catalyst decreases the rate of a given metabolic conversation.</div><div class="column-right">The proteins with catalytic power are named enzymes.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The catalyst increases the rate of a given metabolic conversation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2156,'biology',73,150,339,'Which of the following combinations is correct for wheat?','[{"text": "Genus: Triticum, Family: Poaceae, Order: Poales, Class: Monocotyledonae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genus: Triticum, Family: Poaceae, Order: Sapindales, Class: Dicotyledonae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus: Triticum, Family: Anacardiaceae , Order: Poales, Class: Monocotyledonae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus:Aestivum , Family: Poaceae, Order:Poales, Class: Dicotyledonae", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'For Wheat-Genus: <i> Triticum</i>, Family: Poaceae, Order: Poales, Class: Monocotyledonae.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(2139,'biology',103,966,2251,'Match the items of Column I with those of Column II and choose the correct answer. Select the code for the correct answer from the options given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Hepatitis B vaccine<br>B. Preformed antibodies<br>C. Colostrum<br>D. PMNL</div><div class="column-right">P. IgA<br>Q. Against snake venom<br>R. Neutrophils<br>S. Yeast<br>T. Basophils</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  Q, C  -  P, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  Q, C  -  S, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  Q, C  -  P, D  -  T}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  T, B  -  Q, C  -  S, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Human hepatitis B virus vaccine was prepared using antigen produced by recombinant technology in yeast<br>(Saccharomyces cerevisiae). The highly purified antigen had the correct amino acid sequence and assumed the appropriate conformational structure to present the immunologic determinants (epitopes) that are needed to stimulate an appropriate immune response.<br>Preformed antibodies, which are derived from the blood serum of previously infected people or animals, are often administered in an antiserum to another person in order to provide immediate, passive immunization against fastacting toxins or microbes, such as those in snakebites or tetanus infections.<br>Immunity can be naturally acquired from antibodies (IgA) transferred to a foetus across the placenta or to an infant in colostum and breast milk.<br>Neutrophils, also known as polymorphonuclear leucocytes (PMNLs), they are phagocytic and guard blood, skin and mucus membranes against infection. They respond quickly wherever tissue injury has occurred.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2140,'biology',11,295,563,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Metabolic pathways can lead to a more complex structure from a simpler structure are called degradation and hence are called catabolic pathways.</div><div class="column-right">Metabolic pathways can lead to a simpler structure from a complex structure are called biosynthetic pathways or anabolic pathways.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Metabolic pathways can lead to a more complex structure from a simpler structure are called deg-radation and hence are called anabolic pathways. Metabolic pathways can lead to a simpler structure from a complex structure are called biosynthetic pathways or catabolic pathways.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2141,'biology',73,150,339,'Organisms with their taxonomic categories in order with common name biological name<br>Man  → Homo sapiens  → Homo  → Hominidae  → Mammalia<br>II. Housefly  →  Musca domestica  →  Arthropoda  →  muscidae  →  Diptera<br>III. Mango  →  Mangifera indica Mangifera  →  Anacardiaceae  →  Dicotyledonae<br>IV. Wheat  → Triticum vulgare  →  Triticum  →  Poaceae  →  Monocotyledonae','[{"text": "I and II correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II only correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III and IV correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I , II and IV are correctly placed',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2143,'biology',103,968,2255,'During replication of retrovirus:','[{"text": "Viral protein is introduced in the host cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viral RNA is introduced into the host cell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Viral DNA is introduced into the host cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transcriptase enzyme is introduced into the host cell", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Viral glycoproteins bind to receptors in the host cell\'s plasma membrane causing infection. This causes the cell to transport the virus into its cytoplasm via receptor-mediated endocytosis. Inside the host cell, virus sheds its protein coat. A viral enzyme called reverse transcriptase reads the viral RNA strand and makes a DNA copy. The viral DNA copy then becomes integrated into the host cell\'s DNA and is duplicated along with the host cell\'s DNA during normal cell division.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2144,'biology',11,296,564,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Living organisms have ability to trap energy liberated during degradation and store it in the form of chemical bonds.</div><div class="column-right">The most important form of\nenergy currency in living systems is the bond energy in a chemical called adenosine triphosphate (ATP).</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2145,'biology',73,150,339,'Find the incorrect statements regarding taxonomic hierarchy.<br>a. From species to kingdom, the number of similarities increases<br>b. From species to kingdom, the number of dissimilarities decreases<br>c. Higher the taxa, higher are the similarities<br>d. Lower the taxa, higher are the dissimilarities','[{"text": "a and c only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b and d only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b and c only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b, c and d", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct. As we go higher from species to kingdom, the number of common characteristics goes on decreasing. Lower the taxa, more are the characteristics that the members within the taxon share. Higher\nthe category, greater is the difficulty of determining the relationship to other taxa at the same level.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2147,'biology',103,969,2256,'Identify the odd one from the following.','[{"text": "$\\\\alpha$ - Interferon", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oncogenic virus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proto-oncogenes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "UV rays", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Interferons are used in treatment of cancer and rest all options given cause cancer.<br>Oncogenic viruses are cancer causing viruses and are broadly divided into two large groups depending on the type of nucleic acid found within the mature virus particle: DNA tumour virus and RNA tumour virus.<br>Proto oncogenes are genes that when activated can push the cell toward the malignant state.<br>Both ionizing X-rays and non-ionizing ultraviolet (UV) radiation are leading cause of skin cancer, cause DNA damage<br>Hence interferons are odd one out.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2148,'biology',11,293,561,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In DNA double helix structure, the two strands of polynucleotides are parallel i.e., run in the same direction.</div><div class="column-right">In DNA double helix structure, the backbone is formed by the sugarphosphate- sugar chain.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'DNA exists as a double helix. The two strands of polynucleotides are antiparallel i.e., run in the op-posite direction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2149,'biology',73,150,339,'Choose the correct match<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Order - a group of related division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus - a group of related species", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Class - a group of related genera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Division - a group of related phyla", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct match is Genus is a group of related species.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2151,'biology',103,970,2257,'From which of the given plants is the drug whose skeletal structure is given below extracted?','[{"text": "<i>Papaver somniferum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Atropa belladonna</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Cannabis sativa</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Erythroxylum coca</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'It is also called marijuana, grass or pot. The chemical in marijuana is delta-9 tetrahydrocannabinol (THC).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/103_2151_question_1.png'),
(2152,'biology',11,293,561,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In DNA double helix structure, the pitch would be 34Å.</div><div class="column-right">In DNA double helix structure, the rise per base pair would be 3.4Å.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
