(2209,'biology',73,149,338,'Identify the correct statement given below','[{"text": "In binomial nomenclature, the name of an organism consists of three components", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Consciousness is the property shared by non-living organisms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellular organisation of the body is the defining feature of non-living forms.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Human beings are the only organisms, who is aware of himself, i.e. self-conscious", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The statement in option(4) is correct. Rest statements are incorrect and can be corrected as Cellular organisation of the body is the defining feature of living forms. All living organisms have the ability to sense their\nsurroundings and respond to various stimuli and are thus aware of their surroundings, i.e. show consciousness. A patient with dead dead brain has no consciousness (as brain is the main controlling organ of the body) and hence is considered to be dead.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2210,'biology',103,966,2248,'To which type of barriers under innate immunity does the saliva in the mouth belong?','[{"text": "Physical barriers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokine barriers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellular barriers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Physiological barriers", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The examples of physiological barriers are hydrochloric acid in stomach, saliva in mouth, lysozyme in tears, saliva, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2211,'biology',11,288,556,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Lipids come under completely acid soluble fraction.</div><div class="column-right">Lipids molecular weights exceed more than 800 Daltons.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Lipids comes under acid insoluble pool. They weigh less than 800 Da.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2213,'biology',73,148,337,'Select the correct statement from the following.<br>I. Reproduction is not an all inclusive characteristics of living organisms because many living organisms cannot reproduce.<br>II. Metabolic reactions can also be\ndemonstrated outside the body in isolated cell-free systems.<br>III. ‘Response to stimuli’ is a defining property of living organisms.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct statements',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
