(2269,'biology',11,286,552,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Based on number of amino and carboxyl groups, amino acids are classified as acidic, basic and neutral amino acids.</div><div class="column-right">Glutamic acid is an example of basic amino acid.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Glutamic acid is an example of acidic amino acid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2270,'biology',103,967,2254,'Which of the following statements is not applicable to spleen?','[{"text": "A large bean-shaped organ that mainly contains lymphocytes and phagocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A reservoir of erythrocytes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Graveyard of RBC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Quite large at the time of birth but keeps reducing in size with age", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The thymus is quite large at the time of birth but keeps reducing in size with age and by the time puberty is attained it reduces to a very small size.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2273,'biology',11,286,553,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Arachidonic acid has 20 carbon atoms excluding the carboxyl carbon</div><div class="column-right">Arachidonic acid is a saturated fatty acid.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Archidonic acid has 20 carbons including the carboxyl carbon.Archidonic acid is a unsaturated fatty acid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2274,'biology',103,968,2255,'There is always a time-lag between the infection and appearance of AIDS symptoms which is usually','[{"text": "Few months to 5-10 years", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 hour to 10 hours", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "10 days to 14 days", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 week to 6 months", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'There is always a time lag between the infection and appearance of AIDS symptoms. This period may vary from a few months to many years (usually 5-10 years).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2277,'biology',11,286,552,'An amino acid under certain conditions has both positive and negative charges simultaneously in the same molecule. Such a form of amino acid is called','[{"text": "Acidic form", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Basic form", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aromatic form", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zwitter ionic form", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The term ‘zwitterion’ comes from a German word which means a neutral molecule with positive and negative charges.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2278,'biology',103,968,2255,'AIDS is due to','[{"text": "Reduction in number of helper $T$ cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Excessive production of interferons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reduction in number of killer T cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autoimmunity", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Helper T-lymphocytes play a great role in regulating the immune system. Destruction of helper-T-lymphocytes leads to the development of a immune deficiency which makes the patient susceptible to wide variety of infections.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
