(2303,'biology',11,286,551,'It is said that elemental composition of living organisms and that of inanimate objects (like earth’s crust) are similar in the sense that all the major elements are present in both. Then what would be the difference between these two groups? Choose a correct answer from among the following :','[{"text": "Living organisms have more gold in them than inanimate objects", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Living organisms have more water in their body than inanimate objects", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Living organisms have more carbon, oxygen and hydrogen per unit mass than inanimate objects.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Living organisms have more calcium in them than inanimate objects.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Carbon, oxygen and hydrogen are the main components of organic compounds. This gives the biomoleclues for the correct answer.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2305,'biology',103,965,2247,'Match Column I with Column II :<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Typhoid<br>B. Leishmaniasis<br>C. Ringworm<br>D. Filariasis</div><div class="column-right">P. Fungus<br>Q. Nematode<br>R. Protozoa<br>S. Bacteria</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  R, C  -  P, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  P, C  -  S, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  S, C  -  R, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  R, C  -  P, D  -  Q}}$ is the correct option.<br>Typhoid - Caused by <i>Salmonella typhimurium</i>(Bacteria)<br>Leishmaniasis - Caused by protozoan<br><i>i.e., Leishmania donovani</i><br>Ringworm - Caused by fungi belonging to the genera <i>Microsporum, Trichophyton</i> and <i>Epidermophyton<br><i>Filariasis</i> - Caused by <i>Wuchereria bancrofti</i> and <i>Wuchereria malayi</i> (Nematode)',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2307,'biology',11,297,568,'Which one of the following statements regarding enzyme inhibition is correct?','[{"text": "Competitive inhibition is seen when a substrate competes with an enzyme for binding to an inhibitor protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Competitive inhibition is seen when the substrate and the inhibitor compete for the same active site on the enzyme", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Competitive inhibition is seen when the substrate and the inhibitor compete for the same site on the enzyme besides the active side", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-competitive inhibitors never bind to the enzyme", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The inhibitor closely resembles the substrate in its molecular structure and inhibits the activity of the enzyme, it is known as competitive inhibitor.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2309,'biology',103,966,2252,'Match Column I with Column II :<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Common cold<br>B. Haemozoin<br>C. Widal test<br>D. Allergy</div><div class="column-right">P. <i>Plasmodium</i><br>Q. Typhoid<br>R. Rhinoviruses<br>S. Dust mites</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  S, C  -  R, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  P, C  -  Q, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  Q, C  -  R, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{R,}}\\,{\\rm{B}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{P,}}\\,{\\rm{C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{Q,}}\\,{\\rm{D}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S}}$ is the correct option. Common cold is caused by Rhinoviruses.<br>•Haemozoin is released in blood due to ruptured RBCs after Plasmodium infection.<br>•Widal test is used to confirm the typhoid fever.<br>•Allergy is caused due to dust mites.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2311,'biology',11,297,568,'Select the option which is not correct','[{"text": "Malonate is a competitive inhibitor of succinic dehydrogenase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Addition of lot of succinate does not reverse the inhibition of succinic dehydrogenase by malonate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Increase in substrate concentration, increases the velocity of enzymatic reaction at first then it reaches maximum and further increment does not occur.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Addition of lot of succinate causes inhibition of succinic dehydrogenase by Malonate.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2313,'biology',103,970,2257,'Match Column I with Column II :<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Cocaine<br>B. Heroin<br>C. Morphine<br>D. Marijuana</div><div class="column-right">P. Effective sedative in surgery<br>Q. <i>Cannabis sativa</i><br>R. <i>Erythroxylum</i><br>S. <i>Papaver somniferum</i></div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  R, C  -  P, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  P, C  -  R, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  P, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{R,}}\\,{\\rm{B}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S,}}\\,{\\rm{C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{P,}}\\,{\\rm{D}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{Q}}$ is th correct option.<br>A. Cocaine- Obtained from plant <i>Erythroxylum coca</i>, stimulating action on CNS.<br>B. Heroin - Formed by the acetylation of morphine which is obtained from plant <i>Papaver somniferum</i>.<br>C. Morphine - Obtained from <i>Papaver somniferum</i>, is an effective sedative in surgery.<br>D. Marijuana - Obtained from <i>Cannabis sativa</i>, produces hallucinogenic effect and affects cardiovascular system of the body.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2315,'biology',11,297,568,'Select the correct statement:','[{"text": "A non-competitive inhibitor binds the enzyme at a site distinct from that which binds the substrate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In competitive inhibition, the inhibitor closely resembles the substrate in its molecular structure.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Competitive inhibition are often used in the control of bacterial pathogens.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2317,'biology',103,967,2254,'Given below are two statements:<br>Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Bone marrow is the main lymphoid organ where all blood cells including lymphocytes are produced.</div><div class="column-right">Both bone marrow and thymus provide micro environments for the development and maturation of T-lymphocytes.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statements A and B are correct. In humans, the bone marrow is the main lymphoid organ where all blood cells including lymphocytes are produced.Both bone-marrow and thymus provide micro environments for the development and maturation of lymphocytes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
