(2425,'biology',11,288,556,'Choose the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "Palmitic acid has sixteen carbon atoms including carboxyl carbon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Many lipids have both glycerol and fatty acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oils have high melting point", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The macromolecules from cytoplasm and organelles become the acid insoluble fractions", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only statement in option(c) is incorrect. Incan be corrected as Oils have lower melting point (e.g. gingelly oil).Rest of the statements are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2426,'biology',74,247,489,'Which among the following is not a prokaryote?','[{"text": "<i>Nostoc</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Mycobacterium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Saccharomyces</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Oscillatoria</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Saccharomyces is Yeast which belongs to the kingdom Mycota (fungi) whose members are eukaryotes. Nostoc and Oscillatoria are Cyanobacteria (blue green algae), Mycobacterium is a bacteria which belongs to Kingdom Monera. Members of Kingdom Monera are Prokaryotes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2427,'biology',73,150,339,'Human belong to the family','[{"text": "Hominidae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Primata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mammalia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chordata", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Humans belong to family hominidae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2429,'biology',11,288,556,'Choose the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "The acid insoluble fraction have four types of organic compounds, i.e.e proteins, nucleic acids, polysaccharides and lipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arachidonic acid has 20 carbon atoms including the carboxyl carbon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycerides are esters of fatty acid with glycerol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipids with molecular weight not exceeding 800 Da comes under acid soluble fraction", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Lipids weight less than 800 Da but comes under acid insoluble pool due to formation of vesicle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2430,'biology',74,253,504,'Viroids differ from viruses in having','[{"text": "DNA molecules without protein coat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RNA molecules with protein coat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RNA molecules without protein coat", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DNA molecules with protein coat", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Viroids are the smallest infectious pathogens which are composed of a short strand of circular, single-stranded RNA without protein coat.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2431,'biology',73,150,339,'Match the following columns and select the correct choice<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Family<br>B. Kingdom<br>C. Order<br>D. Species<br>E. Genus</div><div class="column-right">P. melongena<br>Q. Polymoniales<br>R. Datura<br>S. Plantae<br>T. Solanaceae</div></div>','[{"text": "A - T, B - S, C - Q, D - P, E - R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - T, B - Q, C - S, D - P, E - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P, B - Q, C - R, D - S, E - T", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P, B - Q, C - S, D - R, E - T", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A - T, B - S, C - Q, D - P, E - R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2433,'biology',11,290,558,'Identify the correct statement from those given below.','[{"text": "Cholesterol is the most abundant steroid in the animal tissue", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Arachidonic acid has twenty carbon atoms excluding carboxyl carbon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellulose is a homopolymer of fructose.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The acid insoluble pool represents roughly the cytoplasmic composition of cells", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cholesterol is the most abundant steroid in the animal tissue.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2435,'biology',73,150,339,'Which one of the following has least similar character?','[{"text": "Family", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kingdom", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Lower the taxa, more are the characteristics that the members within the taxon share. Higher the category, greater is the difficulty of determining the relationship to other taxa at the same level.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2437,'biology',11,297,570,'Organic compounds that are tightly bound to apoenzyme is','[{"text": "Metal ions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apoenzyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prosthetic group", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Co-enzymes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Prosthetic groups are organic compounds and are distinguished from other cofactors in that they are tightly bound to the apoenzyme.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2438,'biology',74,248,495,'Ciliates differ from all other protozoans in','[{"text": "using pseudopodia for capturing prey", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "having a contractile vacuole for removing\\nexcess water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "using flagella for locomotion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "having two types of nuclei", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ciliates have a larger macronucleus and a smaller micronucleus, Micronucleus takes part in reproduction. Macronucleus takes part in control of metabolic activities and growth Since ciliates have 2 nuclei, they exhibit nuclear dimorphism.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2439,'biology',73,150,339,'Which one of the following taxonomic categories tops the hierarchy of categories?','[{"text": "Genus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kingdom", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Class", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phylum", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Kingdom is the highest taxonomic category.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2441,'biology',11,297,570,'Prosthetic group is a part of holoenzyme. It is','[{"text": "Loosely attached organic part", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Loosely attached inorganic part", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Firmly attached non-protein organic part", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Prosthetic group is a part of holoenzyme. It is firmly attached non- protein organic part.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2442,'biology',74,247,489,'Select the mismatch :<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "<i>Rhodospirillum</i> - Mycorrhiza", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i> Anabaena</i> - Nitrogen fixer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i> Rhizobium </i>- Alfalfa", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Frankia </i>- Alnus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Rhodospirillum is a gram negative bacteria. Hence it will not match with the Mycorrhiza.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2443,'biology',73,150,339,'Which of the following covers a greater number of animals?','[{"text": "Class", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Order", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phylum", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Phylum is the highest taxonomic category compared to the others , so it will have a greater no. of organisms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2445,'biology',11,297,570,'Apoenzyme is','[{"text": "A vitamin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A metal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "An inorganic compound", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Always a protein", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Apoenzyme is always a protein.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2446,'biology',74,247,489,'Which of the following components provide sticky character to the bacterial cell ?','[{"text": "Nuclear membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasma membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycocalyx", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In bacteria, cell envelope consists of 3 layered structure i.e., outermost glycocalyx, middle cell wall and inner plasma membrane. Glycocalyx is considered a capsule when thepolysaccharides are more firmly attached to the cell wall. Capsules have a gummy, sticky consistency and provide protection as well as adhesion to solid surfaces and to nutrients in the environment.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2447,'biology',73,150,339,'Solanum, Datura and Nicotiana belong to the same<br>${\\rm{(a)&emsp; Species &emsp;  &emsp;  &emsp; (b)&emsp; Division}}$<br>${\\rm{(c)&emsp; Family  &emsp;  &emsp;  &emsp;  (d)&emsp; Genus}}$','[{"text": "a and b only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b and d only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b and c only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "c and d only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'b and c only - Solanum, Datura and Nicotiana belong to the same Division and Family.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2449,'biology',11,297,570,'The enzyme has a non- proteinous part. It is known as','[{"text": "Apoenzyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cofactor", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inorganic catalyst", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Active site", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Co- factor enzyme have a non proteinaceous part',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2450,'biology',74,253,504,'Which of the following statements is wrong for viroids?','[{"text": "They are smaller than viruses.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They cause infections.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Their RNA is of high molecular weight.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They lack a protein coat", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Viroids lack protein coat and are free RNAs. The RNA of viroids was of lower molecular weight.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2451,'biology',73,150,339,'In case of plants, classes with a few similar characters are assigned to higher category called','[{"text": "Class", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phylum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Division", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Family", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In classification of plants, classes with a few similar characters are assigned to a higher category called division, e.g. angiospermae. In animals, phylum is used in place of division.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2453,'biology',11,297,570,'How many types of cofactor can be identified?','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Three kinds of cofactors may be identified: prosthetic groups, co-enzymes and metal ions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2454,'biology',73,150,339,'Which one of the following taxonomic categories top the hierarchy of categories?','[{"text": "Order", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Division", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Class", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Division is at a higher taxonomic category.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2455,'biology',74,247,489,'Which of the following are found in extreme saline conditions?','[{"text": "Eubacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyanobacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mycobacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Archaebacteria", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Archaebacteria are those primitive group of bacteria that inhabit most extreme environments like extreme salty areas, hot springs, and marshy areas. Archaebacteria includes Methanogens, Halophiles and thermoacidophiles.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2457,'biology',11,297,568,'Identify A and B in the given diagram?','[{"text": "A - Velocity of reaction,<br> B - Concentration of substrate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Velocity of reaction,<br> B - Temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Velocity of reaction,<br> B - Km", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Temperature, B - Velocity of reaction", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A- velocity of reaction, B- Km',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/11_2457_question_1.png'),
(2458,'biology',73,150,339,'Class mammalia consists of','[{"text": "Order primata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Class primata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Order carnivora", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Order Primata comprising monkey, gorilla and gibbon is placed in class Mammalia along with order Carnivora that includes animals like tiger, cat and dog.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2459,'biology',74,249,497,'Which one of the following statements is wrong ?','[{"text": "Golden algae are also called desmids.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eubacteria are also called false bacteria.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phycomycetes are also called algal fungi.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyanobacteria are also called blue-green algae.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Eubacteria are also called as true bacteria. Eubacteria are prokaryotic cells that contain rigid cell wall made of peptidoglycan.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
