(2461,'biology',11,297,569,'Enzymes are divided into __classes each with ____subclasses and named accordingly by a _____digit number','[{"text": "4, 6. 13", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6, 4, 13", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6 , 4-13, 4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Enzymes are divided into 6 classes each with 4-13 subclasses and named accordingly by a four-digit number',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2462,'biology',73,150,339,'Higher taxa share','[{"text": "Least common characters", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Maximum common characters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No common characters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Character as a point is never considered", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Lower the taxa, more are the characteristics that the members within the taxon share. Higher the category, greater is the difficulty of determining the relationship to other taxa at the same level.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2463,'biology',74,246,488,'Study the four statements (A–D) given below and select the two correct ones out of them<br>1. Definition of biological species was given by Ernst Mayr<br>2. Photoperiod does not affect reproduction in plants.<br>3. Binomial Nomenclature system was given by R.H.Whittaker.<br>4. In unicellular organisms, reproduction is synonymous with growth.<br>Two correct statements are','[{"text": "1 and 4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 and 4", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement 1 and 4 are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2465,'biology',11,297,569,'Enzymes catalysing the breakdown of larger molecules into smaller molecules are','[{"text": "Hydrolases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Isomerases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ligase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Enzymes catalysing the breakdown of larger molecules into smaller molecules are Hydrolases.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2466,'biology',73,150,339,'Which one of the following has least similar characters?','[{"text": "Family", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Class", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Class being a higher taxonomic category as compared to others, it has least similar characters.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2467,'biology',74,248,491,'Select the wrong statement :','[{"text": "Diatoms are chief producers in the oceans.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diatoms are microscopic and float passively in water.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The walls of diatoms are easily destructible.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "‘Diatomaceous earth’ is formed by the cell walls of diatoms.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cell wall of the diatoms are silicious which is hard and almost impossible for destruction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2469,'biology',11,297,569,'Enzymes catalysing the linking together of 2 compounds, e.g., enzymes which catalyse joining of C-O, C-S, C-N, P-O etc. bonds','[{"text": "Hydrolases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lyase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ligase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (2) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ligases: Enzymes catalysing the linking together of 2 compounds, e.g., enzymes which catalyse joining of C-O, C-S, C-N, P-O etc. bonds.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2470,'biology',73,150,339,'Which of the following is a class','[{"text": "Insecta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mammalia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicotyledonae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Insecta, mammalia, and dicotyledonae are all classes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2472,'biology',74,249,496,'Which one of the following is wrong for fungi?','[{"text": "They are heterotrophic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are both unicellular and multicellular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are eukaryotic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All fungi possess a purely cellulosic cell wall", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Fungal cell walls are made of chitin and other polymers especially glucans and they do not contain cellulose. The composition of cell wall is one of the defining characters.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2473,'biology',11,297,569,'The enzyme that catalyses the conversion of glucose-6-phosphate into fructose-6- phosphate is','[{"text": "Oxidoreductase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isomerase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lyase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrolase", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The enzyme that catalyses the conversion of glucose-6-phosphate into fructose-6 phosphate is Isomerase',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2474,'biology',73,150,339,'Which order includes Convolvulaceae and Solanaceae','[{"text": "Poales", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polymoniales", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coniferales", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sapindales", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plant families like Convolvulaceae, Solanaceae are included in the order Polymoniales mainly based on the floral characters.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2476,'biology',74,248,490,'Chrysophytes, Euglenoids, Dinoflagellates and Slimemoulds are included in the kingdom','[{"text": "Protista", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Animalia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monera", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All single celled eukaryotes are placed under Protista. Chrysophytes, Dinoflagellates, Slime moulds, Euglenoids, come under Protista. Being eukaryotes, protistian cell body contains a well defined nucleus and membrane bound organelles.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2477,'biology',11,297,569,'Enzymes that catalyse the removal of groups from substrates by mechanism other than hydrolysis, addition of groups to double bonds are called','[{"text": "Lyases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ligases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrolases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dehydrogenases", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Lyases: Enzymes that catalyse removal of groups from substrates by mechanisms other than hydrolysis leaving double bonds.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2478,'biology',73,150,339,'Which of the following taxonomic catagories includes all the other categories?','[{"text": "Class", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Order", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Family", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Class is the highest taxonomic category among the given options as it includes order, family and genus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2480,'biology',74,249,496,'One of the major components of cell wall of most fungi is :','[{"text": "Peptidoglycan", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellulose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hemicellulose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chitin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Chitin is the main component of cell wall of fungi.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2481,'biology',11,297,569,'Electron transferring enzymes belong to','[{"text": "Transferases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxidoreductases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lyases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isomerases", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Electron transferring enzymes belong to oxidoreductase',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2482,'biology',73,150,339,'In hierarchical classification, class is placed between','[{"text": "Kingdom and phylum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Order and family", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phylum and order", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Family and genus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Class is located in between order and family.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2484,'biology',74,247,489,'Methanogens belong to :','[{"text": "Dinoflagellates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Slime moulds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eubacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Archaebacteria", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Methanogens are obligate anaerobes or organisms that live without oxygen. Methanogens are archaebacteria.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2485,'biology',11,297,569,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Oxidoreductases<br>B. Transferases<br>C. Hydrolases<br>D. Isomerases<br>E. Ligases</div><div class="column-right">P. Hydrolysis of bonds<br>Q. Oxidoreduction  between two  substrates<br>R. Linking together  of two  compounds<br>S. Transfer of a group<br>T. Inter-conversion of optical,  geometric or positional  isomers</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-T, D-S, E-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-T, B-Q, C-P, D-R, E-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-P, D-T, E-R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-T, B-S, C-Q, D-R, E-P", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-Q, B-S, C-P, D-T, E-R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2486,'biology',73,150,339,'The order-Carnivora includes family','[{"text": "Felidae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Convolvulaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Felidae and Canidae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Canidae", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The animal order, Carnivora, includes families like Felidae and Canidae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2488,'biology',74,247,489,'Select the wrong statement :-','[{"text": "Cyanobacteria lack flagellated cells.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mycoplasma is a wall-less microorganism.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacterial cell wall is made up of peptidoglycan.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pilli and fimbriae are mainly involved in motility of bacterial cells.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pili or fimbriae are often involved in adherence (attachment) of bacterial cells to surfaces in nature. They are not involved in motility.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
