(2619,'biology',74,249,499,'Which one of the following is wrongly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "<i>Cassia – Imbricate aestivation</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Root pressure – Guttation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i> Puccinia – Smut</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Root – Exarch protoxylem", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Smut is multicellular fungi which are characterised by large numbers of teliospores. They are mostly by Ustilaginomycetes.<br> Pathogens of smut are<i> Ustilago</i>. They cause plant disease in cereals and grasses which causes black powder. Rust is a group of parasitic fungi of the Phylum Basidiomycota. These species attack stems and leaves of cereal crops. Pathogens of rust are <i>Puccinia, Hemileia </i>.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2620,'biology',73,150,339,'Which is the correct sequence of taxonomic categories?','[{"text": "Species → genus → kingdom → phylum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species → order → phylum → kingdom", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genus → species → order → kingdom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Species → order → phylum → kingdom from lowest categories to highest',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
