(2681,'biology',73,149,338,'All the given options represent the basic process of taxonomy except','[{"text": "Classification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Identification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Specification", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nomenclature", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The basic components of taxonomy are<br>(a) Characterization<br>(b) Identification<br>(c) Classification<br>(d) Nomenclature, there is no specification.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2682,'biology',11,297,565,'All enzymes are proteins, except','[{"text": "Carbonic anhydrase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carboxypeptidase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aldolase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribozyme", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Almost all enzymes are proteins. There are some nucleic acids that behave like enzymes. These are called ribozymes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2683,'biology',74,248,490,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Members of Kingdom Protista are all eukaryotes.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Membrane bound organelles and an organized nucleus is absent in Protista','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Protista includes unicellular eukaryotes. Eukaryotes have a definite nucleus (true nucleus) and membrane bound organelles.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2685,'biology',73,149,338,'The basic components of taxonomy are<br> (a) Characterization           (b) Identification<br>(c) Classification &emsp; (d) Nomenclature','[{"text": "b,c,d only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a,b,d only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a,b,c,d", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "c,d only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The basic components of taxonomy are<br>(a) Characterization <br>(b) Identification<br>(c) Classification<br>(d) Nomenclature',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2686,'biology',11,297,565,'An enzyme like any protein has a','[{"text": "Primary structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tertiary structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'An enzyme like any protein has a primary structure, i.e., amino acid sequence of the protein. An enzyme like any protein has the secondary and the tertiary structure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2688,'biology',74,253,504,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Viroids are small RNA particles which are infectious and devoid of protein coat.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Viroids contain more than 900 nucleotides and genes are absent in them','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Viroids was discovered by Diener in 1971. Viroids are infectious particle which contains RNA but lacks protein coat around it, molecular weight of viroid is very less . Viroid is an obligate parasite.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2689,'biology',73,149,338,'Latin origin is indicated by','[{"text": "They are latinised", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "By printing in italics", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Written in bold", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both the words in a biological name, when handwritten, are separately underlined, or printed in italics to indicate their Latin origin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2690,'biology',11,297,565,'The crevice or pocket of an enzyme is found in which of the following structure?','[{"text": "Primary structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tertiary structure", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When you look at a tertiary structure you will notice that the backbone of the protein chain folds upon itself, the chain criss-crosses itself and hence, many crevices or pockets are made.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2692,'biology',74,249,496,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Heterothallism prevents inbreeding<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It helps fungi to adapt the unfavourable conditions','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Heterothallism prevents inbreeding and promotes outbreeding. It also helps fungi to overcome unfavourable conditions.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2693,'biology',73,149,338,'What are the basis of modern taxonomic studies?','[{"text": "Internal structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecological information", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Structure of cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'External and internal structure of an organisms along with the structure of its cells, developmental process and ecological information of an organism form the basis of modern taxonomic studies.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2694,'biology',11,297,565,'The crevice or pocket of an enzyme in which the substrate bind is called','[{"text": "Active site", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inactive site", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Socket", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'An active site of an enzyme is a crevice or pocket into which the substrate fits',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2696,'biology',74,249,496,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The fungi are widespread in distribution and they even live on or inside other plants and animals<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Fungi are able to grow anywhere, on land, water or on organisms, because they have a variety of pigments, including chlorophyll, carotenoids, fucoxanthin and phycoerythrin','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fungi are widespread in distribution which may be epiphytic, saprophytic, symbiotic and parasitic. Fungi lack chlorophyll pigments and autotrophic mode of nutrition.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2697,'biology',73,149,338,'First act of taxonomy is','[{"text": "Description", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Identification", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Naming", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Classification", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Taxonomy (taxis, “arrangement”, and nomia, “method”) is the science of defining groups of biological organisms on the basis of shared characteristics and giving names to those groups. In order to name the organism or a plant first it should be identified with its remarkable character.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2698,'biology',11,297,565,'Enzyme catalysis differ from inorganic catalysis in which way?','[{"text": "Inorganic catalysts can work efficiently at high temperature and high pressure", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inorganic catalysts can work efficiently at low temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inorganic catalysts can work efficiently at low pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Inorganic catalysts work efficiently at high temperatures and high pressures, while enzymes get damaged at high temperatures',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2700,'biology',74,254,505,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Prions are infectious proteins<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Viroids are tiny, naked molecules of RNA','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Prions are proteinaceous infectious particles, it was discovered by Stanley Prusiner. Viroids are tiny, naked molecules of RNA, they are a few hundred nucleotides long, they are infectious agents in plants.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2701,'biology',73,149,338,'Standardising the name of living organisms is known as','[{"text": "Classification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Identification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nomenclature", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Nomenclature is the process of standardising the name of living organism is known by same name all over the world.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2702,'biology',11,296,564,'The concentration of hormones in normal healthy individual is','[{"text": "mol/L", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "mmol/L", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "nanograms/mL", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "mm/L", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The concentration of hormones in normal healthy individual is nanograms/mL.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2704,'biology',74,248,493,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> <em>Euglena</em> is called as a plant animal<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Pellicle of <em>Euglena</em> is made up of cellulose and not protein','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The plant characters of <em>Euglena </em>are the presence of chloroplast and holophytic nutrition in the presence of light. Animal characters includes presence of pellicle made of proteins, presence of stigma and paraflagellar body, presence of a contractile vacuole and presence of longitudinal binary fission.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2705,'biology',73,149,338,'Organisms are given scientific names because','[{"text": "It ensures that each organism has only one  name", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It has a wide world acceptance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It avoids confusion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Description of any organism should enable the people (in any part of the world) to arrive at the same name. They also ensure that such a name has not been used for any other known organism',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2707,'biology',11,296,564,'Any chemical or physical process moves ______.','[{"text": "Spontaneously to nonequilibrium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non spontaneously to equilibrium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spontaneously to equilibrium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Non spontaneously to non equilibrium", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Any chemical or physical process moves Spontaneously to equilibrium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2708,'biology',74,249,500,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Deuteromycetes is known as fungi imperfectii<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In deuteromycetes, only asexual phase is known','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In deuteromycetes, sexual phase is absent or unknown',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2710,'biology',11,296,564,'The living state is a ___________to be able to perform work','[{"text": "Equilibrium steady state", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-equilibrium nonsteady state", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-equilibrium steady state", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Equilibrium non steady state", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The living state is a non-equilibrium steady state to be able to perform work',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2711,'biology',73,149,338,'The Latin binomial name for dog is properly written as','[{"text": "Canis familiaris", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Familiaris canis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kanis familiaris", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Canis familiaris</em>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'As per the rules of binomial nomenclature scientific name should be in Latin where genus name starts with a capital letter, species name starts with, small letter and it should be italicised',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2712,'biology',74,248,491,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cell wall of Chrysophytes are indestructible<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Cell wall of Chrysophyte have a layer of magnesium pectate embedded in it','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Chrysophytes include diatoms and golden algae. Their cell wall is embedded with silica and it is indestructible.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2714,'biology',11,296,564,'Select the incorrect statement from the following:','[{"text": "All biomolecules have turnover in cell.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metabolic reaction does not occur in isolation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metabolic pathways are either linear or circular.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Living state and metabolism are non synonymous", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The living state and metabolism are synonymous. Without metabolism there cannot be a living state.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2715,'biology',73,149,338,'The process by which anything grouped into convenient categories based on some easily observable characters is called','[{"text": "Classification", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "New Systematics", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nomenclature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Systematics", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The process by which anything grouped into convenient categories based on some easily observable characters is called classification.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2716,'biology',74,252,503,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Pasteur coined Contagium Vivum Fluidum<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Pasteur found that virus infected plant of tobacco can cause infection in an healthy plant','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'M. W Beijerinek, demonstrated that the extract of infected plants of tobacco can cause infection in healthy plants and called it as<i> ContagiumViviumFluidum</i>, which means infectious living fluid.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2718,'biology',11,296,564,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. All chemical reactions in living organisms<br>B. Proteins with catalytic power<br>C. Biosynthetic pathways<br>D. Degradation pathways</div><div class="column-right">P. Enzymes<br>Q. Anabolic pathways<br>R. Catabolic pathways<br>S. Metabolism</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-P, C-R, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-P, C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-S B-P, C-Q, D-R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2719,'biology',73,149,338,'In Mangifera indica, the word Mangifera is a','[{"text": "Genus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Variety", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Order", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In<i> Mangifera indica</i>, the word Mangifera is a Genus',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2720,'biology',74,246,488,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Two kingdom classification was insufficient<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Majority of organisms did not fall into either of the two categories of 2 kingdom classification','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Two kingdom classification was given by Linnaeus, the system did not distinguish between eukaryotes and prokaryotes, unicellular and multicellular, autotrophs and heterotrophs.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2721,'biology',11,296,564,'The tens and thousands of chemical compounds in a living organism, called biomolecules are also known as _____','[{"text": "Enzymes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Steroids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metabolites", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The tens and thousands of chemical compounds in a living organism, called biomolecules are also known as metabolites.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2723,'biology',73,149,338,'In Mangifera indica Linn. indica refers to','[{"text": "Genus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Author", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Family", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Specific epithet", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In<i> Mangifera indica</i> Linn. indica refers to species.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2725,'biology',74,249,497,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Phycomycetes, commonly called as sac fungi<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In phycomycetes, ascospore are produced endogenously in sac like asci','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ascomycetes are called as sac fungi, ascomycetes produces ascospores in sac-like structures called as asci.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2726,'biology',11,296,564,'Blood concentration of glucose in normal healthy individual is','[{"text": "2–3 mmol/L", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4.2 mmol/L– 6.1 mmol/L", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4.2 mol/L– 6.1 mol/L", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6.2 mmol/L– 8.1 mmol/L", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The blood concentration of glucose in a normal healthy individual is 4.2 mmol/L– 6.1 mmol/L',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2727,'biology',73,149,338,'In<i> Mangifera indica</i> L.,L is for','[{"text": "<i> Indica</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Mangifera</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linnaeus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In <i>Mangifera indica</i> Linn. indica refers to Linnaeus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2729,'biology',11,295,563,'Glucose is degraded to lactic acid in our skeletal muscle,_________.','[{"text": "Energy is taken in", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Energy is liberated", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Energy is lost and taken in also", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Glucose is degraded to lactic acid in our\nskeletal muscle, and energy is liberated.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2884,'biology',73,148,337,'An increase in the size or number of cells best describes','[{"text": "Homeostasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biological growth", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Asexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemical level of organisation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When an organism grows there will be increase in the number of cells as well as their size during cell division.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2730,'biology',74,252,503,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Viruses are not included in any kingdom of classification<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Viruses are not cells as they lack cytoplasm','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Viruses are considered as acellular organisms. Hence they are not included in any of the kingdoms.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2731,'biology',73,149,338,'In Binomial nomenclature','[{"text": "Both genus and species are printed in italics", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genus and species name starts with small alphabet also", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both in genus and species the first letter is capital", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus is written after the species", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both the words in a biological name, when handwritten, are separately underlined, or printed in italics to indicate their Latin origin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(2732,'biology',11,295,563,'In how many metabolic steps the breakdown of glucose to lactic acid occurs?','[{"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "9", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A little more than 10", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A little more than 10. Glycolysis is a ten\nstep reaction, lactic acid formation will take\nplace after reduction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2734,'biology',74,247,489,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Mycoplasma are pathogenic in plants and animals.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Mycoplasma lack cell wall and can survive without oxygen .','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Mycoplasma</i> are the simplest and freeliving prokaryotes, they can survive without oxygen. <i>Mycoplasma</i> live as saphrophytes but majority are parasites in plants and animals. They are parasitic due to the inability to produce required growth factors.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2735,'biology',73,149,338,'Botanical names of plants are written in Latin because:','[{"text": "Rules of nomenclature were framed by Italian botanist and they were speaking Latin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is to pronounce multiple meaning", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Latin is the national language of many countries", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Latin was a dead language, its words would convey meaning, it was the mother of many European languages and all the early botanical literature was in latin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Latin was a dead language, its words would convey meaning, it was the mother of many European languages and all the early botanical literature was in latin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2737,'biology',11,295,563,'The metabolic pathway from glucose to pyruvic acid is called as','[{"text": "Anabolism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycolysis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Photophsophorylation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The metabolic pathway from glucose to pyruvic acid is called as Glycolysis',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2738,'biology',74,249,496,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Fungi consists of intervening stage between plasmogamy and Karyogamy called as dikaryotic stage and it contain two haploid nuclei.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Fungal cellulose or chitin is basically made up of acetyl glucosamine','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During the sexual reproduction in fungi, two compatible haploid hyphae fuse, in members of Ascomycetes and Basidiomycetes, after fusion of incompatible hyphae (Plasmogamy) the nucleus do not fuse immediately. There will be two cells per nuclei in the stage. This is called Dikaryon Stage (n+n). Dikaryon stage will occur in between Plasmogamy and Karyogamy. Cell wall of fungi is made up of chitin and it is a homopolysachharide which includes N-acetyl glucosamine.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2739,'biology',73,149,338,'Given below is the botanical name of mango. Mark the option in which the name is correctly written','[{"text": "<i>Mangifera indica</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mangifera indica", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i> Mangifera Indica</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Magnifera Indica", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The first word denoting the genus starts with a capital letter while the specific epithet starts with a small letter. It can be illustrated with the example -<i> Mangifera indica</i>',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2949,'biology',74,249,496,'With respect to fungal sexual cycle, choose the correct sequence of events','[{"text": "Karyogamy, Plasmogamy and Meiosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis, Plasmogamy and Karyogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasmogamy, Karyogamy and Meiosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Meiosis, Karyogamy and Plasmogamy", "isCorrect": false}]',2,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2741,'biology',11,295,563,'The bond energy of which of the following chemicals is most important form of energy currency in living organisms?','[{"text": "Adenosine Triphosphate (ATP)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adenosine Diphosphate (ADP)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adenosine Tetraphosphate (ATP)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The bond energy of Adenosine Triphosphate\n(ATP) is the most important form of energy\ncurrency in living organisms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2742,'biology',73,149,338,'Nomenclature or naming is only possible when  the organism is described correctly and we  know to what organism the name is attached to. This is','[{"text": "Taxonomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Classification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Binomial system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Identification", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Nomenclature or naming is only possible when the organism is described correctly and we know to what organism the name is attached to. This is identification.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2743,'biology',74,249,498,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Budding occurs in yeast<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It is similar to fission process of bacteria','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Budding of vegetative cells is common in yeast, it is different from fission in which cell divides in transverse plane into two cells.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2745,'biology',11,296,564,'Biomolecules are constantly being changed ino some other biomolecules and are made from_____','[{"text": "Amino acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Some other biomolecules", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Biomolecules are constantly being changed into some other biomolecules and are made from some other biomolecules.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2746,'biology',73,149,338,'Scientific names are printed in _____ and are derived from _____','[{"text": "Italics and English", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Latin and Italics", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Italics and Italics", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Italics and Latin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the words in a biological name, when handwritten, are separately underlined, or printed in italics to indicate their Latin origin',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2747,'biology',74,247,489,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Eukaryotic cells have more DNA than prokaryotic cells<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Eukaryotes are more complex than prokaryotes genetically','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Genetically eukaryotes are more complex than prokaryotes and eukaryotic cells have more DNA than prokaryotes. In prokaryotes , DNA is not associated with any histone proteins, amount of DNA is low in prokaryotic cell and remains same throughout life. In eukaryotes, DNA is associated with histone proteins , amount of DNA is higher in eukaryotes.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2749,'biology',73,149,338,'In binomial nomenclature, the name of author appears before the','[{"text": "Genus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Family", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'According to binomial nomenclature, name of the author appears after the specific epithet (species name), i.e. at the end of the biological name and is written in an abbreviated form.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2750,'biology',11,295,563,'Identify, whether the given conditions are energy consuming or energy releasing .<br> I. Glucose  $ \\to $ lactic acid<br> II. Amino acids $ \\to $ proteins','[{"text": "I - Catabolic; II - Catabolic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I - Anabolic; II - Catabolic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I - Catabolic; II - Anabolic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I - Anabolic; II - Anabolic", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Glucose is degraded into lactic acid in\nskeletal muscles by a catabolic process\nthrough which energy is liberated. Assembly\nof a protein from amino acids requires energy\nand hence, it is an anabolic process.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2751,'biology',74,247,489,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Eubacteria have an outer cell wall.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Archaebacteria lack any cell wall like structure.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cell wall of eubacteria is composed of carbohydrate – protein complex and peptidoglycan. Cell wall of archaebacteria lacks peptidoglycan.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2753,'biology',73,149,338,'Specific epithet is','[{"text": "First word in the scientific name of a \\nspecies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Second word in the scientific name of a \\nspecies", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 & 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The first word in a biological name represents the genus while the second component denotes the specific epithet.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2754,'biology',11,295,563,'Bond energy, which is stored in our body in the form of ATP is utilized in','[{"text": "Biosynthetic phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osmotic work", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mechanical work", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2755,'biology',74,247,489,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Monera includes all prokaryotes<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Nuclei of monerans are not organized with nuclear membrane, nucleoplasm and nucleolus','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Prokaryotic cell lacks a true nucleus and membrane bound organelles, The genetic material of prokaryotic cell is dispersed in cytoplasm and is known as nucleoid.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2757,'biology',11,295,563,'Which of the following occurs through an anabolic pathway and requires energy?','[{"text": "Conversion of glucose into lactic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Formation of proteins from amino acids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Formation of acetyl CoA from pyruvate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Assembly of a protein from amino acids\nrequires energy input',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2758,'biology',73,149,338,'According to the binomial nomenclature, scientific name of an organism consists of','[{"text": "Specific epithet", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Generic name", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In binomial nomenclature ,each name has two components – the Generic name and the specific epithet.Both are scientific names.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2759,'biology',74,248,494,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The protoplasm of plasmodial slime mould is considered as purest in the world<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Protoplasm of plasmodium is differentiated into an outer enucleated and central nucleated proteins','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Vegetative part of slime moulds do not possess cell wall, it either occurs as a free-living amoeboid form of protoplasm (plasmodium) or an aggregation of amoeba (pseudoplasmodium). The protoplasm of plasmodial slime mould is considered as the purest in the living world. At maturity, it may contain several hundred to many nuclei.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2761,'biology',73,149,338,'Point out the correct method of showing scientific name of Coconut Palm','[{"text": "Coco Nucifera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cocos Nucifera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cocos nucifera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i> Cocos nucifera</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<i> Cocos nucifera</i> is the correct way of representing it.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2762,'biology',11,294,562,'Which of the following option shows the correct number of incorrect statements.<br>a- metabolic pathways are either linear or circular.<br>b- metabolic pathways do not crisscross each other.<br>c- All the metabolic reactions occur in an isolated condition.<br> d- metabolite flow is called dynamic state of body constituents.<br> e- There is no known single mishap in metabolite flow for healthy conditions.','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'b-metabolic pathways criss-cross each other.<br> d-Majorly metabolic reactions do not occur in an isolated condition.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2764,'biology',74,255,506,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In lichens, mycobiont and phycobiont are symbiotically associated, in which algae is predominant and fungi is a subordinate partner<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Fungus provides food and algae protects the fungal partner from unfavourable conditions','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Algal component of lichen is phycobiont, fungal component is mycobiont. Algal component provides food for fungal component and the fungal component provides shelter and absorbs mineral and water for its partner. The fungal component is predominant in this mutual relationship.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2765,'biology',73,149,338,'Binomial nomenclature means','[{"text": "One name given by two scientists", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two names, one scientific, other local", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two names, one latinised, other of a  person", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One scientific name consisting of a generic and a specific epithet", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The binomial name of Mango is Mangifera indica L. where Mangifera is genus name and indica is species name followed by the scientist abbreviation',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2766,'biology',11,294,562,'Majority of metabolic reactions do not occur in _A_ condition and are _B_ linked to some other reactions.','[{"text": "A - isolated B - always", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - isolated B - sometimes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - linked B - sometimes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Natural B - Always", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Majority of metabolic reactions do not occur in isolated condition and are always linked to some other reactions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2768,'biology',74,248,495,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Sporozoans may have silica on their surface<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Shells of sporozoans help in protection from acidic environment of host','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sporozoans are endoparasites, the body is covered with an elastic pellicle or cuticle.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2769,'biology',73,149,338,'Which naming system is practised by biologist all over the world?','[{"text": "Trivial system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Binomial system", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Artification system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Binomial system is practised by biologists all over the world.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2770,'biology',11,294,562,'Select the correct statement from the given statements.','[{"text": "Not every metabolic conversion is catalyzed in living system.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$C{O_2}$ dissolved in a water is a chemical process which is catalyzed in living system.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the proteins are catalysts.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteins with catalytic power are named as enzymes.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The proteins with catalytic power are named enzymes',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2772,'biology',74,247,489,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cyanobacteria are photosynthetic autotrophs<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Cyanobacteria have chlorophyll a and b similar to green plants','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cyanobacteria, also called as blue-green algae are photosynthetic autotrophs, they have chlorophyll similar to green plants. In addition to chlorophyll it also contains phycobilin and carotenoids.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2773,'biology',73,149,338,'Binomial nomenclature means writing the name of an organism in two words which designate','[{"text": "Order and family", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Family and genus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species and family", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus and species", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In binomial nomenclature ,each name has two components – the Generic name and the specific epithet.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2774,'biology',11,294,562,'Read the following statements carefully,<br> a- A simple bacterial cell contains thousands of organic compounds.<br> b- Dynamic state of body constituents is essential for living, as it’s stability leads\nto death.<br>c- interlinked metabolic reactions are very smooth and without single reported mishap for healthy condition.<br>Among the given statements select the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "c", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'None of them is correct',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2776,'biology',74,247,489,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Archaebacteria are able to survive in harsh habitats<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Presence of peptidoglycan in cell wall help to survive extreme conditions in archaebacteria','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Archaebacteria differs from other bacteria in having a different cell wall structure. This feature is responsible for its survival in extreme conditions. Archaebacteria is characterised by absence of peptidoglycan in the cell wall, it contains protein and non cellulosic polysaccharides.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2777,'biology',73,149,338,'Linnaeus is credited with','[{"text": "Binomial nomenclature", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Theory of biogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Discovery of microscope", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Discovery of blood circulation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Carolus Linnaeus, Swedish naturalist and explorer who was the first to frame principles for defining natural genera and species of organisms and to create a uniform system for naming them which is a binomial nomenclature.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2778,'biology',11,295,563,'The term metabolism means','[{"text": "Sum of all the enzymatically catalysed\\nchemical reactions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anabolic reactions only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Catabolic reactions only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Together all the catalysed chemical\nreactions are called metabolism',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2780,'biology',73,149,338,'ICBN stands for','[{"text": "International Code for Botanical Nomenclature", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "International Code for Biological Names", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Indian Code of Botanical Nomenclature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Indian Congress of Biological Names", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'International Code for Botanical Nomenclature',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2781,'biology',74,247,489,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Methanogen are present in gut of several ruminants<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Methanogen help in production of methane from dung of ruminants.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Methanogen occur in marshy areas, Some of the methanogen archaebacteria live as symbionts in the stomach of herbivores and help in the production of methane from dung of these animals. The presence of archaebacteria is helpful in fermentation of cellulose to the herbivores, mainly ruminants.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2782,'biology',11,295,563,'Metabolic pathways like acetic acid becomes cholesterol or glucose becomes lactic acid in our skeletal muscle. Identify what pathway is it?','[{"text": "Biosynthethic, Catabolic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Catabolic, Catabolic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biosynthethic, Anabolic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Catabolic, Anabolic", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Such type of reactions are biosynthetic and\ncatabolic.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2784,'biology',73,149,338,'ICZN stands for','[{"text": "International Code of Botanical \\nNomenclature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "International Code of Zoological Nomenclature", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "International Code of Viral Nomenclature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "International Code of Zoo Nomenclature", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'International Code of Zoological Nomenclature',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2785,'biology',74,247,489,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Chemosynthetic autotrophic bacteria oxidize various inorganic substances<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Energy released during oxidation is used in ATP production','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Chemoautotrophic bacteria are able to manufacture their organic food from inorganic raw materials with help of energy derived from exergonic chemical reactions involving oxidation of an inorganic substance present in external medium. The chemical energyobtained from oxidation reactions is trapped in ATP molecules.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2786,'biology',11,294,562,'Identify all the incorrect statements from the following.<br> a. All the chemical reactions in body are called as metabolism collectively.<br> b. Not every metabolic reaction results in the transformation of biomolecules.<br> c. Removal of  $C{O_2}$ from amino acid results in formation of amine<br>d. Removal of amino group in a nucleotide base is an example of metabolic reaction.<br>e. Hydrolysis of a glycosidic bond in diasaccharide is an example of anabolic reaction.','[{"text": "c, d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, c", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b, e", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'b- Each metabolic reaction results in the transformation of biomolecules.<br>e- Hydrolysis of a glycosidic bond in diasaccharide is an example of catabolic reaction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2788,'biology',73,149,338,'International code for botanical nomenclature is applicable to','[{"text": "Viruses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 &amp; 3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'International code for botanical nomenclature is applicable to plants only.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2789,'biology',74,255,506,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Lichens are symbiotic associations between lower plants and fungi.</div><div class="column-right">Lichens do not grow in polluted areas.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2790,'biology',11,294,562,'Find the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "Majority of metabolic reactions occur in an isolated condition.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metabolic reactions are always linked to some other reactions.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Series of interlinked reactions occurring in body is called as metabolic pathway.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metabolic pathways are similar to the automobile traffic i.e. traffic junctions.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Majority of metabolic reactions do not occur in an isolated condition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2792,'biology',73,149,338,'The number of species that are known and described, are approximately','[{"text": "0.5-1.0 million", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.7-1.8 million", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3.3-3.5 million", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "13-14 million", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The number of species that are known and described range between 1.7-1.8 million.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2804,'biology',73,148,337,'All living organisms – present, past and future, are linked to one another by the sharing of the common________, but to _______degrees','[{"text": "Genetic material, unchanging", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic material, varying", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Proteinaceous material, varying", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteinaceous material, unchanging", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All living organisms – present, past and future, are linked to one another by the sharing of the common genetic material, but to varying degrees.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
