(2940,'biology',74,249,497,'Membersof phycomycetes are found in<br> (i) Aquatic habitats<br>(ii) On decaying wood<br>(iii) Moist and damp places<br>(iv) As obligate parasites on plants<br>Choose from the following options','[{"text": "(i) and (iv)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(ii) and (iii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Phycomycetes belong to fungi. They live in aquatic habitats, moist and damp places, as obligate parasites on plants and on decaying wood.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2942,'biology',73,148,337,'Biological species concept was given by','[{"text": "Aristotle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "John Ray", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ernst Mayr", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Buffon", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The biological species concept is the most widely accepted species concept. It defines species in terms of interbreeding. <br>For instance, Ernst Mayr defined a species as \nfollows: “species are groups of interbreeding natural populations that are reproductively isolated from other such groups.”',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
