(2985,'biology',73,149,338,'The most important prerequisite in taxonomy based on field and lab tests that effects other aspects is','[{"text": "Identification", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nomenclature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Classification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Taxonomic studies would require correct classification and identification of organisms. Identification of organisms requires intensive laboratory and field studies.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2986,'biology',11,292,560,'In the primary structure of protein','[{"text": "Left end represents → 1st amino acid (C-terminal amino acid)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Right end represents → Last amino acid (N terminal amino acid)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Left end represents → 1st amino acid (N-terminal amino acid)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Right end represents → 1st amino acid (C-terminal amino acid)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The first amino acid is also called as N-terminal amino acid. The last amino acid is called the C- terminal amino acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2988,'biology',73,150,339,'X  being a higher category is the assemblage of families. Which exhibit a few "Y" characters. The "Z" characters are less in a number as compared to different genera included in a family. Identify " $\\mathrm{X}$ ", "Y", and "Z".','[{"text": "X - Order; Y - Similar; Z - Similar", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "X - Genus; Y - Similar; Z - Different", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X - Species; Y - Different; Z - Similar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X - Class; Y - Different; Z - Different", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Order being a higher category is the assemblage of families which exhibit a few similar characters. The similar characters are less in number as compared to different genera included in a family.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2989,'biology',74,246,488,'The five-kingdom classification was proposed by','[{"text": "R.H. Whittaker", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "C. Linnaeus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A. Roxberg", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Virchow", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Monera, Protista, Fungi, Plantae and Animalia are the five kingdoms according to R.H. Whittaker.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2990,'biology',11,292,560,'In a protein structure, the first amino acid and the last amino acid are respectively called as','[{"text": "Beta -amino acid,alpha -amino acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C-terminal amino acid, N-terminal amino\\nacid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alpha -amino acid, beta-amino acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "N-terminal amino acid, C-terminal amino\\nacid", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The first amino acid is also called as N-terminal amino acid. The last amino acid is called the C- terminal amino acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2992,'biology',73,150,339,'Choose the correct option for the following figure. &emsp;&emsp;$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {\\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,}&{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2}&{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3} \\end{array}$','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Genus}}\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{Order}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Phylum}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Phylum}}}&{{\\\\rm{Order}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Genus}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Order}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{Phylum}}}&{{\\\\rm{Genus}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Order}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{Genus}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Phylum}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'1.Genus 2.Order 3.Phylum',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/73_2992_question_1.png'),
(2993,'biology',74,255,506,'Find out the correct statement.','[{"text": "In lichens, the algal component is called phycobiont and fungal component is known as mycobiont, which are heterotrophic and autotrophic respectively.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viroid contains RNA of low molecular weight and protein coat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A virus contains both RNA and DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viruses are obligatory parasites", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Virus are obligatory parasites.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2994,'biology',11,292,560,'Sequence or positional information of amino acid is given by the','[{"text": "Secondary structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Primary structure", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tertiary structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Quaternary structure", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The sequence of amino acids i.e., the positional information in a protein – which is the first amino acid, which is second, and so on – is called the primary structure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2996,'biology',73,148,337,'Which is exclusive of humans?','[{"text": "Sense organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Self consciousness", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Respiratory organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Self consciousness is exclusive of humans.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2997,'biology',74,246,488,'Consider the following statements<br>I. <i>Paramecium</i> and<i>Amoeba</i> have cell wall<br>II.<i>Chlorella </i>and <i>Chlamydomonas</i> both were having cell wall<br>III. All prokaryotic organism were grouped together under kingdom Monera<br>IV. Unicellular eukaryotic organism were placed in Kingdom Protista<br> Which of the following statement is correct','[{"text": "I, II, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III and IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Paramecium and Amoeba have plasma membrane.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(2999,'biology',11,292,560,'Which of these is a type of secondary structure of proteins?','[{"text": "Line", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Helix", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Globule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spherical", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Helix represents seconds structure of\nprotein.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3000,'biology',73,148,337,'Untrue about metabolic reactions is','[{"text": "They can occur inside the organisms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They can occur in cell free systems", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They do not occur simultaneously", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They can occur outside the organisms", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'At a time several metabolic reactions occur simultaneously in a cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3001,'biology',74,248,493,'Read the following statements and select incorrect statement.','[{"text": "Instead of the cell wall, euglenoids have a protein rich layer called pellicle which makes their body flexible.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Many mycoplasma are pathogenic in animals and plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Toxins released by large number of red Dinoflagellates may even kill other marine animals such as fishes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3003,'biology',11,292,560,'What is the configuration of proteins in the primary structure?','[{"text": "Helix", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Line", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sheet", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Globule", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A protein is imagined as a line in it’s primary structure.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(3004,'biology',73,148,337,'Properties of tissues are not present in the constituent cells but arise as a result of ____ among cells.','[{"text": "Interactions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Irritability", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic material", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Properties of tissues are not present in the constituent cells but arise as a result of interactions among cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3016,'biology',73,149,338,'Identify the incorrect statement','[{"text": "Living world consists of amazing diversity of living organisms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Early man could easily perceive the difference between inanimate and living organisms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Systematic description of life forms is brought about by Identification, Nomenclature and Classification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Societies which indulged in \'anthropocentric\' view of biology registered huge progress in biology knowledge", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Societies which indulged in anthropocentric view of biology could register limited progress in biological knowledge.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3005,'biology',74,255,506,'Consider the following statements and select the correct option, stating which one is true (T) and which one is false (F)?<br>i. Blue green algae are the photosynthetic monerans.<br>ii. Genetic material in eukaryotes is circular, double stranded, helical DNA not enclosed by nuclear envelope<br>iii. Sexual reproduction in <em>Rhizopus</em> is oogamous and the mode of sexual fusion is gametangial contact type.<br>iv. <em>Noctiluca</em> is the first dinoflagellate to show bioluminescence.<br>v. The fungal component of lichen is called phycobiont and the algal component is called mycobiont.','[{"text": "i - T, ii - F, iii - F, iv - T, v - F", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i - T, ii - F, iii - F, iv - T, v - T", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i - T, ii - F, iii - T, iv - F, v - T", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i - F, ii - F, iii - F, iv - T, v - F", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'i. Blue green algae are the photosynthetic monerans- true<br>ii. Genetic material in eukaryotes is circular, double stranded, helical DNA not enclosed by nuclear envelope - false<br>iii. Sexual reproduction in <em>Rhizopus</em> is oogamous and the mode of sexual fusion is gametangial contact type - false<br>iv. <em>Noctiluca</em> is the first dinoflagellate to show bioluminescence- true<br>v. The fungal component of lichen is called phycobiont and the algal component is called mycobiont - true',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3007,'biology',11,292,560,'The primary structure of a protein is due to','[{"text": "Ionic bonds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrogen bonds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Disuphide bonds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peptide bonds", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The primary structure of protein is due to peptide bonds.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3008,'biology',73,148,337,'A human being and a cow can be differentiated in the following defined feature','[{"text": "Growth, Reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reproduction, Metabolism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellular organization, Reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Self consciousness", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All organisms are \'aware\' of their surroundings. Human being is the only organism who is aware of himself, i.e., has self consciousness.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3010,'biology',74,255,506,'Read the given statement about lichens and select the correct option<br>I. Algal partner obtains food from the fungus and the fungal partner obtains mineral nutrition<br>II. They constitute climax community in\necological succession<br>III. They represent an example of symbiosis<br>IV. They do not grow in polluted areas.','[{"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Lichens are composite organism that arises from algae or Cyanobacteria living among filaments of multiple fungi in symbiotic relationship. Algal partner is called as Phycobiont and Fungal partner is called as Mycobiont. Algae prepare food for fungi, and fungi provide shelter and absorb mineral nutrients and water for its partner.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3011,'biology',11,292,560,'Structure of molecules in inorganic chemistry refers to the________','[{"text": "Three-dimensional structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two- dimensional structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Molecular formula", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Primary structure", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In inorganic chemistry, the structure invariably refers to the molecular formulae (e.g., NaCl, MgCl2 , etc.).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3012,'biology',73,148,337,'The term not applicable to truely living organisms is','[{"text": "Self-replicating", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Evolving", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Self regulating", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inert system", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All living organisms are self-replicating, evolving and self-regulating interactive systems capable of responding to external stimuli.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3014,'biology',74,247,489,'Read the following statements and select the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "The cyanobacteria is an autrophic bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The cyanobacteria are unicellular, colonial or filamentous, freshwater/ marine or terrestrial algae.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mucor belongs to class phycomycetes of kingdom fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria are saprophytes always", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bacteria are saprophytes and parasite also.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3015,'biology',11,292,560,'Structure of molecules in physics refers to the _________','[{"text": "Primary structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two-dimensional structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three-dimensional structure", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Molecular formula", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Physicists conjure up the three dimensional views of molecular structures',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3018,'biology',74,252,503,'How many statements features are correct for bacteriophage?<br> i. They have polygonal head and envelope<br>ii. Contractile tail<br>iii. Tail sheath present<br>iv. Tail fibres are absent<br>v. Nucleic acid as double stranded circular DNA usually','[{"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iii, iv and v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All correct except iv", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bacteriophage contains 6 tail fibres which are helpful in attachment of the bacteriophage with the host.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3019,'biology',11,292,560,'Protein is described by biologists at _________ levels.','[{"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Biologists describe the protein structure at four levels.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3020,'biology',73,150,339,'Viable and visible taxon is','[{"text": "Order", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Family", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Class", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Species is an organism. Remaining are levels of classification.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3022,'biology',74,252,503,'Study the following statements and identify the correct option given below.<br>I. Viruses that infect plants have single-stranded RNA and viruses that infect animals have either single or double-stranded RNA or double-stranded DNA<br>II. Bacterial viruses or Bacteriophages are usually single-stranded RNA viruses.','[{"text": "I is true, but II is false", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I is false, but II is true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II are false", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bacterial viruses or bacteriophages (viruses that infect the bacteria) are usually double stranded DNA viruses',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3023,'biology',11,292,560,'Select the correct option<br>A. The first amino acid is also called as N-terminal amino acid.<br>B. Physicists conjure up the four dimensional views of molecular structures while biologists describe the protein structure at three levels.','[{"text": "Only A is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Physicists conjure up the three dimensional views of molecular structures while biologists describe the protein structure at four levels.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3024,'biology',73,150,339,'Two animals which are the members of the same order must also be the members of the same ____','[{"text": "class", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "family", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "genus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "species", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Class is a group of related orders. The lizards, birds and cattle belong to class reptilia, aves and mammals respectively.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3026,'biology',74,252,503,'How many of the given organisms are obligate parasites which take over the machinery of the host cell? TMV, <i>Nostoc</i>, Bacteriophage, HIV, <i>Oscillatoria</i>','[{"text": "Two", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Obligate Parasite is a parasitic organism that cannot complete its life-cycle without exploiting a suitable host. Viruses like TMV, Bacteriophage, HIV are obligate Parasites.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3027,'biology',11,292,560,'Proteins are heteropolymers of','[{"text": "Lipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amino acids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleotides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Proteins are heteropolymer of amino acids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3028,'biology',73,148,337,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The properties of tissues are not present in constituent cells<br></div><div class="column-right">The function of tissue is due to interaction between component cells</div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statements-A and Statements-B are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statements-A is correct, Statements-B is wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statements-A is wrong, Statements-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements-A and Statements-B are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All living phenomena are due to underlying interactions. Properties of tissues are not present in the constituent cells but arise as a result of interactions among the constituent cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3030,'biology',74,251,502,'Select from the following the total number of features belonging to animal kingdom.<br> 1. Multicellular, heterotrophic.<br>2. Most of them capable of locomotion.<br>3. Have definite shape and size.<br>\n4. Digestion of food in internal cavity.<br>5. Holozoic mode of nutrition.<br>6. Stored food reserve as glycogen or fat.<br>7. Higher forms shows sensory and neuromotor mechanism.<br>8. Some members are autotrophic.<br>9. Presence of cellulose cell wall.<br>10. Sexual reproduction generally by copulation of male and female followed by embryological development','[{"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "10", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 10.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3031,'biology',11,291,559,'Select the correct pair of substituted purines.','[{"text": "Cytosine and thymine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adenine and guanine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Uracil and cytosine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Guanine and uracil", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Adenine and guanine are substituted purins, while the rest, i.e. uracil, cytosine and thymine, are substituted pyrimidines.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3032,'biology',73,149,338,'Statements unrelated to Systema Naturae is/ are','[{"text": "Written by Linnaeus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Has description of systematic arrangement/ classification of animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Animal names in this book are coined following binomial nomenclature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Specific group of plants are described ahead of his time.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Binomial nomenclature system was given by Carolus Linnaeus. Systema Naturae is the title of his publication. He classified both plants and animals in his publication. Species Plantarum is also his publication and every species of plant known at the time are listed in it.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3034,'biology',74,249,496,'Select the organism with loose tissue level body organisation from the box<br>','[{"text": "iv, v, vi and vii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iii, iv ,vi and ix", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii, vii and viii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iv, vii and ix", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Fungi have loose tissue level body organisation. Puff balls and Agaricus are Basidiomycetes. Claviceps and Neurospora belongs to Ascomycetes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/74_3034_question_1.png'),
(3035,'biology',11,291,559,'Which purine base is found in RNA?','[{"text": "Thymine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uracil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytosine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adenine", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Purine base Adenine is found in both RNA and DNA.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3037,'biology',74,250,501,'Which of the following statement about plant is false?','[{"text": "Plants are autotrophs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plants show alternation of generations\\nduring their life cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plants are multicellular eukaryotes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plants are motile", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Plants are immotile.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3038,'biology',11,291,559,'Which of the following are substituted pyrimidine?','[{"text": "Cytosine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thymine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uracil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cytosine, Uracil and Thymine are Pyrimidines.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3040,'biology',74,249,499,'Karyogamy is delayed after Plasmogamy in the sexual life cycle of how many members?','[{"text": "Five", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Six", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Karyogamy is delayed after Plasmogamy in the members of Ascomycetes and Basidiomycetes. Mushrooms, Puffballs and Bracket fungi belongs to the class Basidiomycetes. Puccinia is the causal organism of wheat rust disease and Puccinia is a member of Basidiomycetes and Neurospora, Drosophila of plant kingdom.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/74_3040_question_1.png'),
(3041,'biology',11,291,559,'Which pyrimidine base is found in RNA only?','[{"text": "Thymine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uracil", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cytosine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pyrimidine base Uracil is found in RNA only.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3042,'biology',74,249,500,'Consider the statements<br>i. Organisms are known by only vegetative or asexual stage<br> ii. Most of the members are decomposers of litter<br>These statements are true for','[{"text": "Phycomycetes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ascomycetes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Basidiomycetes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Deuteromycetes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Deuteromycetes are also called as Impefect fungi as they don’t exhibit sexual reproduction. They are decomposers of litter and help in mineral cycling.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3043,'biology',11,291,559,'DNA contains','[{"text": "Ribose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2’ dioxyribose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5’ deoxyribose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2’ deoxyribose", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'DNA contains 2’ deoxyribose.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3044,'biology',74,249,496,'Read the following statements<br>I. Fungal Hyphae do the work as root hairs<br>II. In pinus roots, fungal hyphae are mainly external forming a wooly covering on outer surface','[{"text": "Both I and II are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Some fungi establish a close relationship with roots of higher plants and help them in obtaining nutrition from soil. This is referred as Mycorrhiza . Well marked Mycorrhiza is found in roots of Pinus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3045,'biology',11,291,559,'The sugar present in RNA is','[{"text": "Galactose - pentose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2’ deoxyribose - pentose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribose - pentose", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ribose - hexose", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A nucleic acid containing deoxyribose is called deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA) while that which contains ribose is called ribonucleic acid (RNA).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3046,'biology',74,249,500,'Which of the following is/are correct combinations with respect to their mycelium and mode of sexual reproduction :-<br>i.<i> Albugo</i> – Coenocytic mycelium and oogamy.<br>ii.<i> Rhizopus</i>– Aseptate mycelium and Isogamy.<br>iii. <i>Puccinia</i> – Septate mycelium and Anisogamy.<br>iv.<i> Trichoderma</i> – Aseptate mycelium and conidia formation','[{"text": "Only i and ii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii and iv", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Puccinia - plasmogamy, karyogamy is seen, and trichoderma is septate.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
