(3051,'biology',74,249,496,'The unique kingdom of heterotrophic organisms with loose tissue level organisation shows<br>i. Diversity in habitat<br>ii. Diversity in morphology of mycelium<br>iii. Chitin in cell wall<br>iv. Degeneration of sex organs from lower to higher group<br>v. Optimum in growth in cool and humid places','[{"text": "Only v is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii, iii and v are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii and v are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Fungi grows in warm and humid condition.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3052,'biology',11,291,559,'Identify the correct match<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Purine - Thymine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pyrimidine - Adenine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleic acid sugar - Glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterocycliccompounds - Purine", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Heterocyclic compounds in Nucleic acids are classified as Purines (Adenine and Guanine) and Pyrimidines (Cytosine, Uracil and Thymine).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3053,'biology',74,249,499,'Select the correct statement :-','[{"text": "Sporangiospores are exogenously produced in sporangium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Conidia after germination produced conidiophore.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In basidiomycetes asexual spores are generally not found.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<em>Alternaria</em> is a example of ascomycetes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In Basidiomycetes, asexual spores are not found and even the sex organs are absent.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3054,'biology',11,291,559,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Building block of nucleic acids<br>B. Building block of proteins<br>C. Building block of carbohydrates</div><div class="column-right">P. Monosaccharide<br>Q. Nucleotide<br>R. Amino acid</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Q, B-R, C-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3055,'biology',74,249,498,'How many statements are correct for truffles and morels?<br> i. They have septate monokaryotic mycelium<br> ii. Reproduce asexually by nonmotile endogenous spores<br> iii. Produce haploid exogenous sexual spores arranged in an orderly manner<br> iv. Their fruiting bodies are edible','[{"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Morels and truffels belongs to the Ascomycetes. In Ascomycetes, asexual spores are Conidia born exogenously on special branch called as Conidiophores. Sexual spores are called ascospores which are produced\nendogenously in sac like asci. These asci are arranged on different type of fruiting bodies called as Ascocarp.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3056,'biology',11,292,560,'The enormous diversity of protein molecules is mainly due to diversity of','[{"text": "Peptide bonds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "R groups on the amino acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amino groups on the amino acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amino acid sequences within the protein molecules", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The enormous diversity of protein molecules is mainly due to diversity of Amino acid sequences within the protein molecules',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3057,'biology',74,249,499,'Consider the following statements and consider them true or false category<br>I. The fungi constitute unique kingdom of heterotrophic organisms<br>II. The common mushroom and toad stools are fungi<br>III. White spots seen on mustard leaves are due to presence of parasitic fungus<br>IV. Some unicellular fungus (<em>Ustilago</em>) are used to make bread and beer<br>V. <em>Puccinia graminis tritici</em> is responsible for yellow rust of wheat <br>VI. <em>Penicillium</em> yields antibiotic penicillin<br>&emsp; &emsp; $True\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,False$','[{"text": "I II III VI &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; IV V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I II III IV &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; V VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II III VI &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; I IV V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV V &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; I II III VI", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<em>Ustilago</em> causes smut disease and it is multicellular. Some unicellular fungi like Yeast are used to make bread and beer In wheat, <em>Puccinia triticina</em> causes &lsquo;black rust&rsquo;, <em>P.recondita</em> causes &lsquo;brown rust&rsquo; and <em>P.striiformis</em> causes &lsquo;Yellow rust&rsquo;.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
