(3066,'biology',11,291,559,'Identify the building block for DNA and RNA','[{"text": "Nitrogen base", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleoside", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleotide", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sugar", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'For nucleic acids, the building block is a nucleotide. A nucleotide has three chemically distinct compounds, i.e. one is a heterocyclic nitrogenous base compound, second is a pentose monosaccharide and the third is a\nphosphoric acid or a phosphate group.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
