(3080,'biology',74,248,494,'Slime moulds - Under P conditions, they form an R called Q which may grow and spread over several feet. During unfavourable conditions, the plasmodium differentiates and formsfruiting bodies bearing spores at their tips. In the above mentioned incomplete statement, labeling represents','[{"text": "P - Aggregation, Q - Plasmodium, R - Suitable condition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P - Suitable condition, Q - Plasmodium, R - Aggregation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "P - Aggregation, Q - Plasmodium, R - Differentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P - Suitable condition, Q - Pseudoplasmodium, R - Aggregation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Slime moulds grows on decaying twigs and leaves. At suitable condition, they form aggregates and form a structure called Plasmodium. During unfavourable condition forms fruiting bodies having spores. Spores\nhave true walls, they are extremely resistant and survive for many years in the adverse conditions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
