(3122,'biology',74,247,489,'Study the following characters carefully and give answer :-<br> i. Bacterial structure is very simple because they are prokaryotic and unicellular<br> ii. Bacteria as a group show most extensive metabolic diversity<br>iii. Based on shape, bacteria are grouped into two categories only.<br> iv. Most of the bacteria do not have cell wall.','[{"text": "i, ii-correct ; iii, iv-incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iii, iv-correct ; i, ii-incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iv-correct ; ii, iii-incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iii-correct ; i, iv-incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bacteria are prokaryotes and unicellular. Extensive metabolic diversity can be observed in bacteria i.e., Some are phototrophs, getting energy from the sun. Others are chemotrophs, getting energy from chemical compounds. Some are autotrophs, fixing carbon from $C{O_2}$. Others are heterotrophs, getting carbon from organic compounds of other organisms. Bacterias may perform aerobic (oxygen requiring) or anaerobic (non-oxygen-based) metabolism, and some can switch between these modes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
