(3719,'biology',76,850,1892,'Which of the following is true about stomata?<br>i. Present on epidermis of leaves<br>ii. Regulate the process of transpiration and gaseous exchange<br>iii. Surrounded by guard cells<br>iv. It is an opening<br>v. It is sometimes secretory<br>vi. It is bean shaped in monocots','[{"text": "i, ii, iii, iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii, iv, v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv, v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Stomata is not secretory. In grasses, the guard cells are dumbbell shaped.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3720,'biology',75,717,1515,'Which of the following posses whorled phyllotaxy?','[{"text": "Alstonia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Guava", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both land 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "China rose", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'If more than two leaves arise at a node and form a whorl, it is called whorled, as in Alstonia',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3721,'biology',11,289,557,'Given below are two statements:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A protein is imagined as a line, the left end represented by first amino acid (C-terminal) and the right end represented by last amino acid (N-terminal).</div><div class="column-right">Adult human haemoglobin, consists of 4 subunits (two subunits of α type and two subunits of β type.)<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are true.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is true but Statement B is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is false but Statement B is true.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Protein is imagined as a line, the left end represented by the first amino acid and the right end is represented by the last amino acid. The first amino acid is also called N-terminal amino acid. The last amino acid is called the C-terminal amino acid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3722,'biology',74,249,496,'Which of the following interactions is fungi able to be in ?<br>i. Lichen ii. Parasite iii. Mycorrhizae<br> iv. Saprophyte<br>v. Predation<br>','[{"text": "i, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Fungi cannot predate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3723,'biology',11,290,558,'Benedict\'s reagent test is conducted to confirm the presence of:','[{"text": "Reducing sugars", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polysaccharides like starch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipids", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'For reducing and non-reducing sugars, Benedict\'s test and Fehling\'s test is done. Both these reagents contain an alkaline solution of copper sulphate $\\left(\\mathrm{Cu}^{+2}\\right)$. In the presence of reducing sugars, $\\mathrm{Cu}^{+2}$ is reduced to $\\mathrm{Cu}^{+}$which forms as a brick-red precipitate of copper(1) oxide.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3724,'biology',76,850,1892,'Which of the following is true about guard cells?','[{"text": "Outer wall is thick", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inner wall is thin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bean-shaped in dicots and dumb-bell- shaped in grasses", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The outer walls of guard cells (away from the stomatal pore) are thin and the inner walls (towards the stomatal pore) are highly thickened.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
