(3727,'biology',11,286,554,'Ribose sugar is present in:','[{"text": "RNA only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RNA polymerase and ATP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RNA and ATP", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "RNA polymerase, RNA and ATP", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ribose is an important sugar found in a variety of chemicals such as CoA, FAD, NAD, NADP and ATP besides being a constituent of nucleotides that form RNA.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3728,'biology',74,249,496,'The network of hyphae is known as','[{"text": "Mycelium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rhizoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coenocyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pseudomycelium", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The network of hyphae is known as Mycelium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3729,'biology',76,850,1892,'Guard cells are not','[{"text": "Opening for transpiration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chlorophyllous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "With thin outer wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parenchymatous cell", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Guard cells are modified epidermal cells. These cells have chlorophyll and perform photosynthesis. The outer walls of guard cells (away from the stomatal pore) are thin and inner wall (towards the stomatal pore) are highly thickened.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
