(3736,'biology',74,249,496,'Fungi are generally','[{"text": "Saprophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parasites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Photosynthetic", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Most fungi are heterotrophic and absorb soluble organic matter from dead substrates and hence are called saprophytes. Those that depend on living plants and animals are called parasites.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3737,'biology',11,286,554,'The nitrogen base found only in DNA is also called:','[{"text": "5-Methyl uracil", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\\\mathrm{Cl}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uracil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Guanine", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Four nitrogen bases present in DNA are adenine, guanine, cytosine and thymine (5-methyl uracil). Thymine is present only in DNA and is absent in RNA, as in RNA, uracil is present in place of thymine.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
