(3745,'biology',11,297,568,'What is the role of competitive inhibitor during enzyme action?','[{"text": "It enhances enzyme action.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It declines the enzyme action.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It alters the active site of the enzyme and prevents the binding of substrate.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It inhibits breaking of chemical bonds of the substrate.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Competitive inhibitors compete directly with a substrate for an enzyme\'s substrate binding site. They are structurally similar to the substrate which enables them to specifically bind to the active site. Thus, they weaken enzyme action.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
