(3833,'biology',76,850,1894,'Vascular bundles having xylem and phloem which lie at the same radius is termed as','[{"text": "Concentric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Radial", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Conjoint", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amphicribral", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The xylem and phloem are jointly situated along the same radius of vascular bundles are termed as conjoint. This type of arrangement can be seen in stems and leaves.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3834,'biology',11,297,565,'Enzymes do not occur in','[{"text": "Viruses", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Viruses are connecting link between living and non-living organisms. They are acellular, lack metabolism, hence enzymes are absent.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3835,'biology',75,718,1517,'The given diagram represents_','[{"text": "Cymose inflorescence where flowers are borne axially in basipetal manner.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Racemose inflorescence where flowers are borne axially in acropetal succession.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cymose inflorescence where flowers are borne laterally in acropetal succession.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Racemose inflorescence where flowers are borne laterally in acropetal succession.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In racemose type of inflorescences the main axis continues to grow, the flowers are borne laterally in an acropetal succession',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/75_3835_question_1.png'),
(3836,'biology',74,248,494,'Slime moulds are','[{"text": "Saprophytic fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parasite", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Saprophytic protists", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Autotrophic", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Slime moulds are saprophytic protists.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3837,'biology',76,850,1894,'Closed vascular bundle is present in','[{"text": "Monocot", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dicot", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In the monocotyledons, the vascular bundles have no cambium present in them. Hence, since they do not form secondary tissues they are referred to as closed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3838,'biology',11,297,566,'Study the following graph. In the above graph, Z indicates<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "The reaction is endothermic type", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Energy of colliding molecules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Activation energy in the presence and absence of enzyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Energy/ATP/Heat of the reaction", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Difference between the potential energy of substrate and product of a reaction is considered as reaction energy.',NULL,'Easy','Graph/Figure',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/11_3838_question_1.png'),
(3839,'biology',74,248,494,'Under favourable conditions slime moulds form','[{"text": "Protonema", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasmodium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mycelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fruiting bodies", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Under suitable conditions, they form an aggregation called plasmodium which may grow and spread over several feet.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3840,'biology',75,719,1518,'Based on the position of calyx, corolla and androecium in respect of the ovary on thalamus, the flowers are described as','[{"text": "Epigynous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypogynous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Perigynous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Based on the position of calyx, corolla and androecium in respect of the ovary on thalamus, the flowers are described as hypogynous, perigynous and epigynous',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3841,'biology',76,850,1894,'Conjoint vascular bundle is present in','[{"text": "Monocot stem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicot stem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leaf", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Stems and leaves show the vascular bundles with conjoint type of arrangement.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3842,'biology',11,290,558,'Exoskeleton of Arthropods is made up of unique complex polysaccharide known as','[{"text": "Hyaluronic Acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chitin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Waxes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellulose", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Chitin is a complex polysaccharide present in the exoskeletons of arthropods. It is also present in fungal cell wall.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3843,'biology',74,248,493,'Euglena posses all except','[{"text": "Pigments identical to those present in\\nhigher plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two equal flagella", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Two unequal flagella", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mixotrophic nutrition", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Euglena doesnot have equal flagella.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3844,'biology',11,286,553,'Lecithin, a small molecular weight organic compound found in living tissues, is an example of:','[{"text": "Amino acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phospholipids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glycerides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbohydrates", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Some lipids have phosphorous and a phosphorylated organic compound in them. These are phospholipids. They are found in cell membrane. Lecithin is one example.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3845,'biology',75,719,1518,'When the other floral parts are arranged at the base of the gynoecium, the flower is called','[{"text": "Hypogynous flower", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Perigynous flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epigynous flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Agynous flower", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In the hypogynous flower the gynoecium occupies the highest position while the other parts are situated below it.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3846,'biology',76,850,1894,'Vascular bundle is closed when ____ and is most commonly seen in ____','[{"text": "Cambium is present, monocot", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cambium is absent, monocots", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cambium is absent, dicots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cambium is present, dicots", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Vascular bundle is closed when Cambium is absent, and is most commonly seen in monocots.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3847,'biology',74,248,493,'Select the correct statement about the organism given in this diagram<br>','[{"text": "Autotrophic in absence of sunlight", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterotrophic in deprived sunlight", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Biflagellate- equal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are surrounded by protein rich layer known as cell wall", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Heterotrophic in deprived sunlight is the correct statement.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/74_3847_question_1.png'),
(3848,'biology',11,297,570,'The cofactor of the enzyme carboxypeptidase is:','[{"text": "Zinc", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Niacin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flavin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haem", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The cofactor of the enzyme carboxypeptidase is zinc.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3849,'biology',74,248,493,'Presence of which is true for Euglena','[{"text": "Chloroplasts - higher plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Flagella - single", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellulosic - cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell membrane - pellicle", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The pigments of euglenoids are identical to those present in higher plants',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3850,'biology',75,719,1518,'Identify the plants with hypogynous flowers is','[{"text": "Plum, Peach, Guava", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cucumber, Sun flower, Guava", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rose, Plum, Peach", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mustard, Brinjal, Chinarose", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The ovary in such flowers is said to be superior,i.e.hypogynous e.g., mustard, china rose and brinjal',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3851,'biology',76,850,1894,'When xylem and phloem are separated by a strip of cambium it is called','[{"text": "Open", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Closed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Half open", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Half closed", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When xylem and phloem are separated by a strip of cambium it is called open. Which shows that plant can show secondary growth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3852,'biology',11,297,568,'Inhibition of succinic dehydrogenase enzyme by malonate is a classical example of:','[{"text": "Cofactor inhibition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Feedback inhibition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Competitive inhibition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Enzyme activation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Because malonate shows close structural similarity with the substrate and it competes with the substrate for the substrate binding site of the enzyme succinic dehydrogenase.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3854,'biology',75,719,1518,'If gynoecium is situated in the centre and other parts of the flower are located on the rim of the thalamus almost at the same level, the flower is called','[{"text": "Hypogynous flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Perigynous flower", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Epigynous flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Agynous flower", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'If gynoecium is situated in the centre and other parts of the flower are located on the rim of the thalamus almost at the same level, it is called perigynous.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3855,'biology',11,289,557,'Match Column-I with Coulmn-II<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. GLUT-4<br>B. Insulinn<br>C. Trypsin<br>D. Collagen</div><div class="column-right">P. Hormone<br>Q. Enzyme<br>R. Intercellular ground substance<br>S. Enables glucose transport into cell</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  P, C  -  Q, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  Q, C  -  R, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  R, C  -  S, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{B - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{C - P,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S, B}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{P, C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{Q, D}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{R}}$ is the correct option.<br>${{\\rm{A}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{GLUT - 4}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{ - }}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{S}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Enables}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{glucose}}{\\mkern 1mu} }$<br>${\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{transport}}\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{into}}\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{cells}}}$<br>${{\\rm{B}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Insulin}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{ - }}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{P}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Hormone}}}$<br>${{\\rm{C}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Trypsin}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{ - }}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{Q}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Enzyme}}{\\mkern 1mu} }$<br>${{\\rm{D}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Collagen}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{ - }}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{R}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Intercellular}}\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{ground}}}$<br>${{\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{substance}}{\\rm{.}}}$',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3856,'biology',76,850,1894,'Match the columns I and II.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Radial<br>B. Exarch<br>C. Endarch<br>D. Conjoint</div><div class="column-right">P. Protoxylem towards centre<br>Q. Xylem and Phloem at same radius<br>R. Metaxylem towards centre<br>S. Xylem and Phloem in an alternate manner on different radii</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Radial- Xylem and phloem in an alternate manner on different radii<br>Exarch - Metaxylem towards centre.<br>Endarch - protoxylem towards centre.<br>Conjoint - Xylem and phloem at same radius',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3857,'biology',74,248,493,'Characteristic feature of euglenoids are<br> A. Presence of pellicle<br> B. Presence of two flagella<br>C. Photosynthetic in presence of sunlight<br>D. Heterotrophic in absence of sunlight','[{"text": "A and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, C and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements are correct for euglena.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(3858,'biology',11,293,561,'Match Column I with Column II :<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Lipase<br>B. Nuclease<br>C. Protease<br>D. Amylase</div><div class="column-right">P. Peptide bond<br>Q. Ester bond<br>R. Glycosidic bond<br>S. Phosphodiester bond</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  Q, C  -  R, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  R, B  -  Q, C  -  P, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  Q, B  -  S, C  -  P, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  S, B  -  P, C  -  R, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{Q,}}\\,{\\rm{B}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S,}}\\,{\\rm{C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{P,}}\\,{\\rm{D}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{R}}$ is the correct option.<br>A. Lipase - Digests ester bond found in lipids.<br>B. Nuclease - Helps in digestion of phosphodiester bonds found in nucleic acids.<br>C. Protease - Helps in digestion of peptide bond found in proteins.<br>D. Amylase - Digests/breaks the glycosidic bonds found in carbohydrates i.e., digest starch into smaller molecules, ultimately yielding maltose, which in turn is cleaved into two glucose molecules by maltase.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3859,'biology',76,850,1894,'Match the columns I and II.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Lateral meristem<br>B. Phloem<br>C. Sclerenchymatous cells<br>D. Closed vascular bundle</div><div class="column-right">P. Seed coats<br>Q. Vascular bundles without cambium<br>R. Albuminuous cells<br>S. Increase in girth</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Lateral meristem - increase in girth<br>Phloem - Albuminous cells<br>Sclerenchymatous cells - seed coats<br>Closed vascular bundles - Vascular bundles without cambium',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3860,'biology',75,719,1518,'Correct set of plants with perigynous flowers is','[{"text": "Plum, Peach, Guava", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cucumber, Sun flower, Guava", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rose, Plum, Peach", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mustard, Brinjal, Tomato", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'If gynoecium is situated in the centre and other parts of the flower are located on the rim of the thalamus almost at the same level, it is called perigynous. The ovary here is said to be half inferior, e.g., plum, rose, peach.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3861,'biology',74,248,493,'Mode of nutrition in euglenoids is','[{"text": "Autotropic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterotropic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Symbiotic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Euglena - Though they are photosynthetic in the presence of sunlight, when deprived of sunlight they behave like heterotrophs by predating on other smaller organisms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3875,'biology',75,719,1518,'Identify the plants with epigynous flowers is','[{"text": "Plum, Peach, Guava", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cucumber, Guava", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rose, Plum, Peach", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mustard, Brinjal, China rose", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the <i>epigynous</i> flowers, ovary is present inferior to calyx, corolla and androecium. The thalamus in this encloses the ovary inside it & the other three whorls are located above this,Cucumber, guava, sunflower',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3862,'biology',11,297,567,'Regarding catalytic cycle of an enzyme action, select the correct sequential steps :<br>I. Substrate enzyme complex formation.<br>II. Free enzyme ready to bind with another substrate.<br>III. Release of products.<br>IV. Chemical bonds of the substrate broken.<br>V. Substrate binding to active site.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :','[{"text": "V - I - IV - III - II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I - V - II - IV - III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II - I - III - IV - V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "V - IV - III - II - I", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The correct answer is option (1) which is V, I, IV, III, II.The catalytic cycle of an enzyme action can be described in the following steps.<br>(1) First, the substrate binds to the active site of the enzyme, fitting into the active site.<br>(2) The binding of the substrate induces the enzyme to alter its shape, fitting more tightly around the substrate.<br>(3) The active site of the enzyme, now in close proximity of the substrate breaks the chemical bonds of the substrate and the new enzymeproduct complex is formed.<br>(4) The enzyme releases the products of the reaction and the free enzyme is ready to bind to another molecule of the substrate and run through the catalytic cycle once again.<br>Options (2), (3) and (4) are incorrect as the steps mentioned are in the wrong sequence.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3863,'biology',74,248,493,'Euglenoids have flexible body because of','[{"text": "Cellulose rich pellicle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein rich pellicle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lipid rich pellicle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pectin rich pellicle", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Euglena - Instead of a cell wall, they have a protein rich layer called pellicle which makes their body flexible.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3864,'biology',76,850,1894,'The following diagram shows different type vascular bundles in plant cell. Identify A-C in the diagram?','[{"text": "A - Conjoint closed, B - Conjoint open, C - Radial", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Conjoint open, B - Radial, C - Conjoint closed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Radial, B - Conjoint closed, C - Conjoint open", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Conjoint open, B - Conjoint closed, C - Radial", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A - Radial, B - Conjoint closed,$\\mathrm{C}$ - Conjoint open typs of vascular bundles are represented here.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/76_3864_question_1.png'),
(3865,'biology',75,719,1518,'Ovary is half-inferior in the flowers of','[{"text": "Peach", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sunflower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brinjal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Guava", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ovary is half inferior in the flowers of Peach.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3866,'biology',74,248,493,'Habitat of euglenoids is','[{"text": "Fresh water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fresh stagnant water", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Marine water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypersaline lagoon", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Euglenoids - Majority of them are fresh water organisms found in stagnant water.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
