(3930,'biology',74,248,491,'Cell walls of diatoms are indestructible because of the presence of','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{CaC}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chitin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Silica", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cellulose", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Chrysophytes -The walls are embedded with silica and thus the walls are indestructible. Thus, diatoms have left behind large amount of cell wall deposits in their habitat; this accumulation over billions of years is referred to as &lsquo;diatomaceous earth&rsquo;.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3931,'biology',75,718,1517,'Read the following statements carefully select the correct statements for racemose type of inflorescence_____<br>P. Growth is limited.<br>Q. Flowers are born laterally in basipetal order.<br>R. Main axis continues to grow.<br>S. Flowers are born laterally in an acropetal order.','[{"text": "R and Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "R and S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Q and S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P and Q", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In racemose type of inflorescences the main axis continues to grow, the flowers are borne laterally in an acropetal succession',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
