(3952,'biology',77,413,826,'Which of the following options gives the correct sequence of events during mitosis?','[{"text": "Condensation → nuclear membrane disassembly → arrangement at equator → centromere division → segregation → telophase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Condensation  → crossing over → nuclear membrane disassembly  → segregation → telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Condensation  → arrangement at equator → centromere division  → segregation  → telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Condensation → nuclear membrane → disassembly → crossing over → segregationg → telophase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In mitosis, condensation takes place first by which chromosomes will be visible first. It occurs during early to mid prophase. Nuclear membrane disassembly begins at late prophase or transition to metaphase. During metaphase, chromosomes are arranged at the equator called as congression. During anaphase, Centromere division or splitting occurs which leads to formation of daughter chromosomes and during anaphase segregation also occurs by which daughter chromosomes will separate an move towards opposite polls. Telophase leads to the formation of two daughter nuclei.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
