(4013,'biology',75,719,1518,'Select the number of incorrect statements from the following statements__<br>i) When a flower can be divided into two equal radial halves in any radial plane passing through the centre, it is said to be actinomorphic.<br>ii) When flower can be divided into two similar halves in any vertical plane, it is zygomorphic.<br>iii) A flower is asymmetric (irregular) if it cannot be divided into two similar halves by any vertical plane passing through the centre.<br>iv) Family solanaceae have zygomorphic flowers.<br>v) A flower may be trimerous, tetramerous or pentamerous when floral appendages are in multiple of 3, 4 or 5 respectively.','[{"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When it can be divided into two similar halves only in one particular vertical plane, it is zygomorphic. Family Solanaceae have actinomorphic flowers.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
