(4014,'biology',77,413,826,'Select the correct option with respect to mitosis:','[{"text": "Chromatids separate but remain in the centre of the cell in anaphase.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromatids start moving towards opposite poles in telophase.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Golgi complex and endoplasmic reticulum are still visible at the end of prophase.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosomes move to the spindle equator and get aligned along equatorial plate in metaphase.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The key features of metaphase are: Spindle fibres attach to kinetochores of chromosomes. Chromosomes are moved to spindle equator and get aligned along metaphase plate through spindle fibres of both poles.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4015,'biology',76,853,1897,'Select the correct answer about anatomy of stem<br>I. Vascular bundles are conjoint and open in monocot.<br>II. Peripheral vascular bundles are generally smaller than the centrally located ones in dicots.','[{"text": "I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Each vascular bundle is conjoint, open in dicots. In monocotyledonous plant stem peripheral vascular bundles are generally smaller than the centrally located ones.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
