(4017,'biology',77,412,822,'At which stage of the cell cycle are histone proteins synthesised in a eukaryotic cell?','[{"text": "During entire prophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "During Telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "During S phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "During  ${G_2}$ stage of prophase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Histone proteins are basic proteins and are used in packing of eukaryotic (absent in prokaryotes) DNA. DNA and histones together comprise chromatin, forming bulk of the eukaryotic chromosomes. Histones are of\nfive major kinds  ${H_1},\\,{H_{2A}},\\,{H_{2B}},\\,{H_3}$  and  ${H_4}$. ${H_1}$  histones like neighbouring nucleosomes while others are elements of nucleosome structure. During S-phase of cell cycle synthesis of histone proteins takes place because at this stage number of chromosomes becomes double to that of somatic number.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
