(4037,'biology',77,413,824,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Synthesis of DNA takes place in the S-phase of interphase.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Every chromosome, during metaphase has two chromatids.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.<br>A typical cell cycle comparises of interphase and mitotic phase (M-phase). The interphase comprises of first growth phase or ${G_1}$ phase, synthesis phase or S phase and second drowth phase or ${G_2}$ phase. The DNA synthesis occurs during S phase in the process of DNA replication. In the mitotic phase, each chromosome has two sister chromatids. The two sister chromatids are clearly visible during metaphase stage because the chromosomes are highly coiled. The two sister chromatids are joined at the centromere.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4038,'biology',76,852,1896,'Identify the components labeled A-D in the given dicot stem diagram?','[{"text": "A-Pericycle, B- Cambium, C- Pith, D- Collenchyma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Cambium, B- Pith, C-Collenchyma, D- Pericycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Collenchyma, B- Pericycle, C- Cambium, D- Pith", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A- Pith, B-Collenchyma, C- Pericycle, D- Cambium", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The given diagram can be labelled as follow: A- Collenchyma, B- Pericycle, C- Cambium, D- Pith.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/76_4038_question_1.png'),
(4039,'biology',74,247,489,'Identify the organisms that produce their own food in kingdom Monera?<br>A. Algae<br>B. BGA<br>C. Cyanobacteria<br>D. Nitrifying bacteria<br>E. Mycoplasma<br>F. Nitrogen fixation bacteria','[{"text": "A, B, C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, C , D", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A, B, C, D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, C", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'BGA/ Cyanobacteria and nitrifying bacteria are autotrophs.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4040,'biology',77,412,822,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Interphase is also called inter-mitosis.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Interphase occurs between two dividing M-phase.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.<br>Cell cycle consists of two stages, a long non-individual growing I-phase and a short dividing M-phase. Interphase is series of changes that takes place in a newly formed cell and its nucleus before it becomes capable of division again. Therefore, it is also called intermitosis',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
