(4042,'biology',76,852,1896,'Carefully observe the given diagram and select the correct option.','[{"text": "It is section of monocot root.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is section of dicot root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is section of monocot stem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is section of dicot stem", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A large number of vascular bundles are arranged in a ring; the \'ring\' arrangement of vascular bundles is a characteristic of dicot stem.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/76_4042_question_1.png'),
(4043,'biology',77,415,828,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cancer cells are virtually immortal until the body in which they reside dies.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Cancer is caused by damage to genes regulating the cell division cycle.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cancer is caused by damage to genes regulating the cell division cycle. It results due to an uncontrolled growth of the cells. The cancer cells show uncontrolled cell growth. They have lost their cell differentiation ability. The also do not exhibit contact inhibition anymore. All these factors make the cancer cells immortal. Hence, these are virtually immortal cells until the body in which they reside dies.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4044,'biology',75,719,1518,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Receptacle<br>B. Gynoecium<br>C. Corolla</div><div class="column-right">P. Petal<br>Q. Swollen end of the pedicel<br>R. Reproductive Organ</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q},  \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R},  \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q},  \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P},  \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Q, B-R, C-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4045,'biology',74,247,489,'Identify the organism given in this diagram and its feature.','[{"text": "Cocci - rod shaped bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Mycoplasma</i>- no cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Nostoc</i>–Filamentous structure, helps in nitrogen fixation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Algae–Heterotrophic structure feeds on Nostoc", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Nostoc–Filamentous structure, helps in nitrogen fixation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/74_4045_question_1.png'),
(4056,'biology',76,852,1896,'The given diagram is transverse section of monocot stem. Identify labeled A in the given diagram?','[{"text": "Pith", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Medullary rays", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vascular bundles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Starch sheath", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The monocot stem has a large number of scattered vascular bundles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/76_4056_question_1.png'),
(4046,'biology',77,414,827,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cytokinesis is different in animal and plant cells.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Vesicles of golgi apparatus from cell plate in plant cells.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cytokinesis is the division of protoplast of a cell after the nuclear division. Each daughter cell comes to have its own nucleus. In animal cells, the furrow deepens centripetally and cleaves the cell into daughters, each having a daughter nucleus. The method is known as cleavage cytokinesis. In plant cells, cytokinesis takes place by two methods, cleavage and cell plate. Small vesicles produced by golgi apparatus collect at the equator of the phragmoplast. The membrane of the vesicles fuse to form two sheets on which enclose a matrix or film. Soon the film becomes solidified to form cell plate or middle lamella. The daughter protoplasts deposit cellulose, hemicelluloses and pectin on either side of the cell plate. They form the primary wall.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4047,'biology',76,852,1896,'The given diagram is transverse section of dicot stem. Identify labeled A in the given diagram?','[{"text": "Pith", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Medullary rays", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vascular bundle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Starch sheath <br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The given diagram is transverse section of Dicot stem. A is labelling pith.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/76_4047_question_1.png'),
(4048,'biology',75,719,1518,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Actinomorphic  symmetry<br>B. Zygomorphic symmetry<br>C. Irregular symmetry</div><div class="column-right">P. Cassia<br>Q. Mustard<br>R. Canna</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R},  \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Irregular is canna, zygomorphic is cassia, actinomorphic is mustard',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4049,'biology',74,247,489,'Function of (1) in the given diagram is','[{"text": "Excretion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fixing atmospheric nitrogen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Repoduction", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Heterocyst are involved in fixing atmospheric nitrogen into ammonia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/74_4049_question_1.png'),
(4050,'biology',77,418,834,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Mitotic division is an equational division.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Second meiotic division is homotypic.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mitosis is that type of division in which chromosomes replicate and become equally distributed both quantitatively and qualitatively into two daughter nuclei so that the daughter cells come to have the same number and type of chromosomes as are present in the parent cell. It is, therefore called equational division. The second division is known as homotypic or equational division, because the chromosome number remains the same as produced after the end of the first division.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4051,'biology',76,852,1896,'Carefully observe the given diagram and select the correct option.<br>I. It has sclerenchymatous hypodermis, scattered vascular bundles.<br>II. Phloem parenchyma is present<br>III. Water containing cavities are absent within the vascular bundles.<br>IV. Vascular bundles are conjoint and closed.','[{"text": "II, III, IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Given diagram represents transverse section of monocotyledonous stem. In monocotyledonous stem phloem parenchyma is absent. Water containing cavities are present within the vascular bundles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/76_4051_question_1.png'),
(4052,'biology',74,247,489,'Which of the following is ${N_2}$ fixing autotroph?','[{"text": "<em>Nostoc</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Anabaena</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<em>Escherichia coli</em>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<em>Nostoc</em> and <em>Anabaena</em> can fix atmospheric nitrogen in specialised cells known as heterocyst and are photosynthethic.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4053,'biology',75,719,1519,'Each flower normally has four floral whorls, namely<br>i. Calyx,<br>ii. Corolla,<br>iii. Androecium,<br>iv. Gynoecium,<br>v. Petals ,<br>vi. Sepals,<br>vii. Anther,<br>viii. Carpels','[{"text": "i, ii, vii, viii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "v, vi, vii, viii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A typical flower has four different kinds of whorls. These are calyx, corolla, androecium and gynoecium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(4054,'biology',77,418,834,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The stage between the two meiotic divisions is called interkinesis and is generally long lived.</div><div class="column-right">There is no replication of DNA during interkinesis</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The stage between the two meiotic divisions is called interkinesis and is generally short lived. There is no replication of DNA during interkinesis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4055,'biology',74,247,489,'<em>Oxygenic photosynthesis </em>takes place in','[{"text": "<em>Nostoc</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Anabaena</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "BGA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Oxygenic photosynthesis takes place in Cyanobacteria like <em>Nostoc</em>, <em>Anabaena</em> etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4057,'biology',77,419,835,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Meiosis is the mechanism by which conservation of specific chromosome number of each species is achieved across generations in sexually reproducing organisms.</div><div class="column-right">Meiosis also increases the genetic variability in the population of organisms from one generation to the next.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Meiosis is the mechanism by which conservation of specific chromosome number of each species is achieved across generations in sexually reproducing organisms, even though the process, per se, paradoxically,\nresults in reduction of chromosome number by half. It also increases the genetic variability in the population of organisms from one generation to the next.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4058,'biology',75,719,1519,'Which of the following has labelled incorrectly?','[{"text": "Pedicel and corolla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calyx and androecium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corolla and calyx", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Androecium and gynoecium.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Calyx and Corolla has labelled incorrectly',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/75_4058_question_1.png'),
(4059,'biology',74,247,489,'<em>Nostoc</em> and <em>Anabaena</em> are','[{"text": "Photoautotrophic bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "BGA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyanobacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4060,'biology',77,417,830,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The final stage of meiotic prophase I is diakinesis.</div><div class="column-right">Diakinesis is marked by terminalisation of chiasmata.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The final stage of meiotic prophase I is diakinesis. This stage is marked by terminalisation of chiasmata.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4061,'biology',76,852,1896,'The given diagram is transverse section of monocot stem. Identify labeled A in the given diagram?','[{"text": "Pith", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Medullary rays", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vascular bundles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ground Tissue", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The given diagram is transverse section of Monocot stem where label A is representing ground tissue.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/76_4061_question_1.png'),
(4062,'biology',75,719,1519,'The_____is the outermost whorl of the flower and the members are called','[{"text": "Corolla, sepals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calyx, sepals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Corolla, petals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calyx, petals", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The calyx is the outermost whorl of the flower and the members are called sepals.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4063,'biology',74,247,489,'Identify the correct statement about Heterocyst<br>i.<i> Nostoc </i>and <i>Anabaena </i>possess them<br>ii. It can fix atmospheric nitrogen<br>iii. These are specialized cells<br>iv. They are present in all BGA<br>v. They are present in certain cyanobacteria','[{"text": "i, ii, iii, v", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i , ii, iii, iv , v", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Nostoc and Anabaena can fix atmospheric nitrogen in specialised cells known as heterocyst. They are present in certain BGA /cyanobacteria only, not all.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4064,'biology',77,417,832,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">During metaphase-I, the bivalent chromosomes align on the equatorial plate.</div><div class="column-right">During anaphase-I, the microtubules from the opposite poles of the spindle attach to the kinetochore of homologous chromosomes.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During metaphase-I the bivalent chromosomes align on the equatorial plate and the microtubules from the opposite poles of the spindle attach to the kinetochore of homologous chromosomes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4065,'biology',77,417,833,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">During anaphase-I, both homologous chromosomes and sister chromatids separate.</div><div class="column-right">During Telophase-I, the nuclear membrane and nucleolus reappear.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During anaphase-I, the homologous chromosomes separate, while sister chromatids remain associated at their centromeres. During telophase I, the nuclear membrane and nucleolus reappear.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4066,'biology',74,247,489,'What indicates X and Y in this figure?<br>','[{"text": "X - Heterocyst, Y - Mucilaginous sheath", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "X - Mucilaginous sheath, Y - Heterocyst", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X - Heterocyst, Y - Heterocyst", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X - ATP , Y - Heterocyst", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'X - Heterocyst, Y - Mucilaginous sheath.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/74_4066_question_1.png'),
(4067,'biology',76,854,1898,'In a dorsiventral leaf, location of spongy tissue and palisade tissue is respectively on the ..... surfaces.','[{"text": "Adaxial and abaxial", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adaxial and adaxial", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abaxial and adaxial", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Abaxial and abaxial", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Dorsiventral (bifacial) leaves are commonly horizontal in orientation with distinct upper (adaxial) and lower (abaxial) surface. Mesophyll is distinguishable into palisade and spongy tissues. Spongy tissue can be seen at the lower side(abaxial) and palisade tissue is usually restricted to the upper (adaxial) side.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4068,'biology',75,719,1519,'Identify the function of the sepals','[{"text": "Green - photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protect the flower in the bud stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Since sepals are green they perform photosynthesis and also protect buds .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4069,'biology',77,417,830,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The beginning of diplotene is recognised by the dissolution of the synaptonemal complex</div><div class="column-right">In oocytes of all vertebrates, diplotene can last for months or years.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The beginning of diplotene is recognised by the dissolution of the synaptonemal complex. In oocytes of some vertebrates, diplotene can last for months or years.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4070,'biology',74,247,489,'Specialised organelles called heterocysts are present in','[{"text": "Cyanobacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chrysophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Archaebacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Heterocyst are cell and not organelles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4071,'biology',76,854,1898,'Vascular bundles in the leaves of dicots are surrounded by','[{"text": "Thin walled bundle sheath cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thick walled bundle sheath cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sclerenchymatous bundle sheath cells", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The vascular bundles are surrounded by a layer of thick-walled bundle sheath cells. These cells contain chloroplasts and are the site of photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4072,'biology',75,719,1519,'Identify the function of the petals','[{"text": "Green - photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protect the flower in the bud stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Attract insects for pollination", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Petals are usually brightly coloured to attract insects for pollination.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4073,'biology',77,417,830,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Crossing over is the exchange of genetic material between two non-homologous chromosomes.</div><div class="column-right">Crossing over is an enzyme-mediated process and the enzyme involved is called recombinase.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Crossing over is the exchange of genetic material between two homologous chromosomes. Crossing over is an enzymemediated process and the enzyme involved is called recombinase.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4074,'biology',74,247,489,'Which out of the following rightly define cyanobacteria?','[{"text": "Chemosynthetic autotrophic bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photosynthetic autotrophic bacteria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nitrifying bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Saprophytic", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Photosynthetic autotrophic bacteria, is cyanobacteria / blue green algae',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4075,'biology',77,417,830,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Chromosome synapsis is accompanied by the formation of complex structure called kinetochore complex.</div><div class="column-right">The kinetochore complex formed by a pair of synapsed homologous chromosomes is called a bivalent or a tetrad.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Electron micrographs of zygotene indicate that chromosome synapsis is accompanied by the formation of complex structure called synaptonemal complex. The complex formed by a pair of synapsed homologous\nchromosomes is called a bivalent or a tetrad.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4076,'biology',76,854,1898,'The correct location of stomata in isobilateral grass leaf is?','[{"text": "Towards adaxial surface", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Towards abaxial surface", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Equally distributed on adaxial and abaxial", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "More on the adaxial side", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In an isobilateral leaf, the stomata are present on both the surfaces of the epidermis which is distributed equally.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4077,'biology',75,719,1519,'The shape of corolla may be','[{"text": "Tubular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Funnel-shaped", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bell-shaped", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The shape and colour of corolla vary greatly in plants. Corolla may be tubular, bell- shaped, funnel-shaped or wheel-shaped.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4078,'biology',74,247,489,'Cyanobacteria are classified under which of the following kingdom?','[{"text": "Protista", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monera", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Kingdom monera includes cyanobacteria/ blue green algae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4079,'biology',77,417,830,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">During zygotene stage, the four chromatids of each bivalent chromosomes becomes distinct and clearly appears as tetrads.</div><div class="column-right">Pachytene stage is characterized by the appearance of recombination nodules, the sites at which crossing over occurs between non-sister chromatids of the homologous chromosomes.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During pachytene, the four chromatids of each bivalent chromosomes becomes distinct and clearly appears as tetrads. This stage is characterised by the appearance of recombination nodules, the sites at which crossing over occurs between non-sister chromatids of the homologous chromosomes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4080,'biology',74,247,489,'BGA can fix atmospheric nitrogen in structure called','[{"text": "Heterocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterocyst", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Homocyst", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Conidiophores", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'BGA / cyanobacteria can fix atmospheric nitrogen in specialised cells known as heterocyst.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
