(4169,'biology',77,412,822,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A typical eukaryotic cell divide once in approximately every 22 hours.</div><div class="column-right">Yeast for example, can progress through the cell cycle in only about 30 minutes.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A typical eukaryotic cell cycle is illustrated by human cells in culture. These cells divide once in approximately every 24 hours. Yeast can progress through the cell cycle in only about 90 minutes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
