(4180,'biology',77,411,821,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The sequence of events by which a cell duplicates its genome, synthesizes the other constituents of the cell and eventually divides into two daughter cells is termed cell cycle</div><div class="column-right">Cell division has to take place in a coordinated way to ensure correct division and formation of progeny cells containing intact genomes.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The sequence of events by which a cell duplicates its genome, synthesises the other constituents of the cell and eventually divides into two daughter cells is termed cell cycle. All the processes, i.e., cell division, DNA\nreplication, and cell growth, have to take place in a coordinated way to ensure correct division and formation of progeny cells containing intact genomes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
