(4223,'biology',77,417,830,'Select the correct statement from the following:','[{"text": "Prophase I is shorter and complex than prophase of mitosis.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "During zygotene the heterologous chromosome shows pairing.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chiasmata is a X shape structure formed in diplotene.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pachytene is characterized by the formation of synaptonemal complex.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'1. Prophase I is comparatively longer and more complex than prophase of mitosis <br>2. During zygotene, homologous chromosomes start pairing to form bivalents<br>3. Chiasmata marks the site where crossing\nover occurred. It is an X-shaped structure formed in diplotene.<br>4. Zygotene is characterised by the formation of synaptonemal complex.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4225,'biology',75,719,1521,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Monoadelphous<br>B. Diadelphous<br>C. Polyadelphous</div><div class="column-right">P. Citrus<br>Q. China rose<br>R. Pea</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R, B – P , C – Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – R , C – P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A – P, B – R , C – Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – P , C – R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The stamens may be united into one bunch or one bundle (monoadelphous) as in china rose, or two bundles (diadelphous) as in pea, or into more than two bundles (polyadelphous) as in citrus.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
