(4264,'biology',77,413,826,'i. Golgi body and ER are reformed.<br>ii. Golgi body and ER are disintegrated.<br>This occurs during which phase respectively?','[{"text": "Telophase and Prophase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Telophase and Anaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase and Telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase and Anaphase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Organelles like Golgi complex and endoplasmic reticulum disappear at the end of prophase while they are reformed at telophase.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4227,'biology',77,417,830,'Consider the following statements.<br>I. A bivalent consists of two chromatids.<br>II. Terminalisation of chiasmata is seen in diakinesis<br>Select the correct option.','[{"text": "Both I and II are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I is true, II is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I is false, II is true", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both I and II are false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A bivalent is a structure formed during zygotene after the synapsis of two homologous chromosomes or four chromatids.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4229,'biology',74,246,488,'In two kingdoms, the following are included in plant<br>(1) Bacteria, blue green algae<br>(2) Fungus, mosses and fern<br>(3) Gymnosperms and angiosperm','[{"text": "(1) Only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(2) and (3) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(3) Only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Earlier classification systems - 2-kingdom classification included bacteria, blue green algae, fungi, mosses, ferns, gymnosperms and the angiosperms under ‘Plants’.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4230,'biology',77,418,834,'Which of the following statement is incorrect?','[{"text": "Prophase II is simpler than prophase I.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In leptotene stage the chromosomes become gradually visible under light  microscope.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nuclear membrane reappears only in telophase II not in telophase I.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anaphase II is characterized by the splitting of centromere.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During telophase I as well telophase II, nuclear membrane and nucleolus reappear. In both the phases, chromosomes reach the pole and start uncoiling to become thin, long chromatin material.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4231,'biology',75,719,1521,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Mustard<br>B. Rose<br>C. Cucumber<br>D. Sterile stamen<br>E. Polypetalous</div><div class="column-right">P. Inferior ovary<br>Q. Superior ovary<br>R. Half inferior ovary<br>S. Petals free<br>T. Staminode</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{A - Q,B - R,C - P,D - T,E - S}}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4232,'biology',77,418,834,'Consider the following statements.<br>I.  During meiosis, the chromosome number reduces to half in anaphase-I stage.<br>II.  During anaphase-II stage, the amount of DNA in a cell gets reduced to haploid\nstate. <br>Select the correct option.','[{"text": "Both I and II are true", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I is true, II is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I is false, II is true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are false", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During anaphase-I of meiosis-I, homologous chromosomes separate which results in the chromosome number getting reduced by half. Whereas, during anaphase-II of meiosis-II, centromere splits and sister chromatids of homologous chromosomes separate which results in ploidy getting reduced to half.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4234,'biology',74,246,488,'Identify the kingdom which occupies two domains in 3-domains classification?','[{"text": "Plantae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protista", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monera", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Monera is divided into two domains.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4235,'biology',75,719,1521,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Racemose inflorescence<br>B. Cymose inflorescence<br>C. Epipetalous androecium<br>D. Epitepalous androecium</div><div class="column-right">P. Brinjal<br>Q. Lily<br>R. Liliaceae family<br>S. Fabaceae family</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P},  \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-S, B-R, C-P, D-Q',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4236,'biology',77,417,830,'The synaptonemal complex is formed during','[{"text": "Cytokinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Electron micrographs of Zygotene stage of Prophase-I of meiosis-I shows synapsis between homologous chromosomes accompanied by the formation of synaptonemal complex. This complex helps stabilise the synapsis between homologous chromosomes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4237,'biology',74,246,488,'Eukaryotic organisms find a place in which domain in the three domain classification ?','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{I}}^{{\\\\rm{st }}}}$domain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{I}}{{\\\\rm{I}}^{{\\\\rm{nd}}}}$ domain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{I}}^{{\\\\rm{st}}}}$ and ${\\\\rm{I}}{{\\\\rm{I}}^{{\\\\rm{nd}}}}$ domain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{II}}{{\\\\rm{I}}^{{\\\\rm{rd}}}}$ domain", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Eukaryotic organisms find a place in ${\\rm{II}}{{\\rm{I}}^{{\\rm{rd}}}}$ domain in the three domain classification .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4239,'biology',75,719,1522,'A carpel consists of','[{"text": "Stigma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Style", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A carpel consists of three parts namely stigma, style and ovary.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4240,'biology',77,416,829,'Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct about meiosis?','[{"text": "Meiosis involves pairing of homologous chromosomes and recombination between them.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis involves two sequential cycles of nuclear and cell division called meiosis-I and meiosis-II, but only a single cycle of DNA replication.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Specialised kind of cell division that reduces the chromosome number by half resulting in the production of haploid daughter cells is called meiosis. Meiosis involves two sequential cycles of nuclear and cell division\ncalled meiosis I and meiosis II but only a single cycle of DNA replication. In prophase I of meiosis I, homologous chromosomes pair and crossing over takes place between their non-sister chromatids.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4241,'biology',74,246,488,'Three domains of life include how many kingdoms?','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Three domains of life include 6-kingdom.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4243,'biology',77,417,832,'Which is the most essential step in meiosis leading to reduction','[{"text": "Crossing over between homologous chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Formation of chiasmata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Segregation of homologous chromosomes during anaphase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During anaphase I of meiosis I, homologous chromosomes separate from each other and start moving towards the pole. Since only one chromosome out of a pair reaches the pole, the number of chromosomes becomes half in daughter cells. This is an key event leading to reduction of chromosome number.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4244,'biology',75,719,1522,'Which of the following is correct about carpel?','[{"text": "Ovary is enlarged basal portion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stigma is usually at tip of style", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Style is elongated tube over ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4245,'biology',74,246,488,'Five kingdom classification was based on','[{"text": "Cell structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thallus organisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mode of nutrition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Five kingdom classification was based on cell structure, reproduction, phylogenetic relationship, thallus organisation and mode of nutrition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4246,'biology',77,419,835,'As compared to meiosis, in mitosis','[{"text": "Homologous chromosomes pair", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homologous chromosomes separate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaphase stage is absent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase is shorter", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Prophase of the first meiotic division is typically longer and more complex when compared to prophase of mitosis. It has been further subdivided into the following five phases based on chromosomal behaviour, i.e.,\nLeptotene, Zygotene, Pachytene, Diplotene and Diakinesis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4248,'biology',74,246,488,'Classification of organisms into plants and animals was easily done and was easy to understand, but, a large number of organisms did not fall into either category. The statement refers to which classification from the following','[{"text": "Aristotle classification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Whittakers classification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linnaeus classification", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The main criteria for classification used in 5 kingdom classification include cell structure, body organisation, mode of nutrition, reproduction and phylogenetic relationships.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4249,'biology',75,719,1522,'What is the receptive surface for pollen grains?','[{"text": "Ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stigma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Style", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Stigma serves as the landing platform for pollen grains.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4265,'biology',74,246,488,'Identify the kingdom that is undefined in terms of mode of nutrition but has all eukaryotic cells?','[{"text": "Monera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plantae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protista", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The boundaries of kingdom Protista is not well defined.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4250,'biology',77,419,835,'Which of the following is incorrect for meiosis cell division?','[{"text": "In meiosis, there is production of haploid cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The cells undergoing the division may be haploid or diploid in case of plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It leads to the formation of haploid gametes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synapsis of homologous chromosomes takes place during zygotene of prophase-I", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Meiosis is exclusive to diploid cells only, be it a plant cell or an animal cell. This is because diploid cells are ready to get reduced to half their chromosomal number to form a haploid cell. Meiosis cannot occur in haploid cells. Gamete formation in haploid organisms takes place only by mitosis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4251,'biology',74,246,488,'Whittaker’s classification included which of the following kingdom','[{"text": "Plantae and Animalia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monera and Protista", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The kingdoms defined by R.H. Whittaker were named Monera, Protista, Fungi, Plantae and Animalia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4253,'biology',77,419,835,'The number of chromosomes present in pollen grains is six. What shall be their number in leaf cells?','[{"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "24", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pollen grain is a haploid cell while leaf cells are diploid in nature. Pollen (n) = 6, therefore leaf cell (2n) = 6*2 = 12.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4254,'biology',75,719,1522,'Each ovary bears one or more ovules attached to a flattened, cushion-like_______','[{"text": "Ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Style", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stigma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Placenta", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Each ovary bears one or more ovules attached to a flattened, cushion-like placenta.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4255,'biology',74,246,488,'In which year Whittaker proposed the five kingdom classification?','[{"text": "1960", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1699", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1969", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1996", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'R.H. Whittaker (1969) proposed a Five Kingdom Classification.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4256,'biology',77,416,829,'For the production of 200 egg cells how many meiotic divisions are required?','[{"text": "50 divisions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "100 divisions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "200 divisions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "400 divisions", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'1 parent mother cell undergoes meiosis to give rise to 4 egg cells out of which only 1 egg cell is functional. So, technically 1 mother cell produces 1 egg cell. For the production of n egg\ncells, n meiotic divisions are required. Hence, for 200 egg cells, 200 meiotic divisions are required.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4258,'biology',75,719,1522,'When more than one carpel is present, they may be free are called ______. When carpels are fused, they are termed______','[{"text": "syncarpous, syncarpous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "apocarpous, apocarpous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "apocarpous, syncarpous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "syncarpous, apocarpous", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When more than one carpel is present, they may be free (as in lotus and rose) and are called apocarpous. They are termed syncarpous when carpels are fused, as in mustard and tomato.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4259,'biology',74,246,488,'Two-Kingdom classification was based on','[{"text": "Cell structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of cell-wall", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Type of cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 & 3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Two-Kingdom classification was based on cell wall.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4260,'biology',77,412,822,'Which of the following statements are correct for  ${G_1}$-phase?','[{"text": "Cell organelles do not increase in number", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It synthesises RNAs proteins and other biochemicals for cell growth and subsequent replication of DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell may enter  ${G_0}$ after this phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During  ${G_1}$  phase the cell is metabolically active and continuously grows by synthesising proteins and other biochemicals. The cells that do not divide further exit the cell cycle from  ${G_1}$  phase to enter  ${G_0}$ phase.  ${G_2}$ phase is characterised by the duplication of organelles like mitochondria, chloroplasts and Golgi body occurs.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4262,'biology',74,246,488,'Select the correct answer.<br>A. Aristotle was the earliest to attempt a more scientific basis for classification.<br>B. Before the 5-kingdom classification gross morphology, cell structure, nature of wall,\nmode of nutrition, habitat, methods of reproduction, evolutionary relationships were never considered.','[{"text": "A is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4263,'biology',75,719,1522,'Apocarpous condition is found in','[{"text": "Mustard", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lotus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Apocarpous condition is found in Rose and lotus',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4267,'biology',77,414,827,'Select the correct statement.','[{"text": "Cytokinesis occurs before the division of the nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Karyokinesis occurs before the division of the cytoplasm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Karyokinesis and cytokinesis occurs at the same time", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There is no specific rule", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The M Phase starts with the nuclear division, corresponding to the separation of daughter chromosomes (karyokinesis) and usually ends with division of cytoplasm (cytokinesis).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4268,'biology',75,719,1522,'Syncarpous condition is found in','[{"text": "Mustard", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lotus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Syncarpous</i> :  when <i>carpels</i> are fused,it is said to be syncarpous, as in mustard and tomato',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4269,'biology',74,246,488,'The kingdoms which becomes more organised in five kingdom classification than they were in two kingdom classification are','[{"text": "Protista and Monera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi and Plantae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plantae and Animalia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Animalia and Protista", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The kingdoms which becomes more organised in five kingdom classification then they are in two kingdom classification are Plantae and Animalia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4270,'biology',77,413,826,'Which of the following statement(events) is/ are true for mitotic telophase?','[{"text": "Nucleolus, GB and ER reform", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nuclear envelope develops around the chromosome clusters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosomes cluster at opposite spindle poles and their identity is lost as discrete elements.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'At the final stage of karyokinesis, i.e., telophase, the chromosomes that have reached their respective poles decondense and lose their individuality. Chromosomes cluster at opposite spindle poles and their identity is lost as discrete elements. Nuclear envelope develops around the chromosome clusters at each pole forming two daughter nuclei. Nucleolus, golgi complex and ER reform.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4272,'biology',75,719,1522,'After fertilization','[{"text": "Ovule develops into seed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovary matures to fruit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'After fertilisation, the ovules develop into seeds and the ovary matures into a fruit',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4273,'biology',74,246,488,'Two kingdom classification does not distinguish between','[{"text": "Eukaryote and prokaryote", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unicellular and multi-cellular organisms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photosynthetic (green algae) and nonphotosynthetic (fungi) organisms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Earlier classification systems - 2-kingdom classification included bacteria, blue green algae, fungi, mosses, ferns, gymnosperms and the angiosperms under ‘Plants’.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4274,'biology',77,413,825,'Which of the following is not true for anaphase?','[{"text": "Chromosomes move to equator", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Spindle poles move further apart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosomes move to opposite poles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centromeres split and chromatids separate", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Chromosomes align themselves at the equator to form metaphasic plate during metaphase. At the onset of anaphase, each chromosome arranged at the metaphase plate is split simultaneously at its centromere and the two daughter chromatids begin their migration towards the two opposite poles. These chromatids get separated due to the shortening of spindle fibres approaching towards the poles.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4276,'biology',75,719,1522,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Variation in length of filaments within flower<br>B. Apocarpous<br>C. Syncarpous</div><div class="column-right">P. Lotus<br>Q. Salvia<br>R. Tomato</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Q, B-P, C-R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4277,'biology',74,246,488,'Who proposed two kingdom system of classification?','[{"text": "Bentham and Linnaeus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aristotle and Linnaeus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "R.H . Linnaeus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carolus Linnaeus", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Carolus Linnaeus proposed Two Kingdom system of classification with Plantae and Animalia kingdoms was developed that included all plants and animals respectively.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4278,'biology',77,412,822,'The phase of cell cycle during which ‘DNA polymerase’ is used','[{"text": "S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${G_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${G_1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$M$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'DNA polymerase is responsible for the formation of new compies of DNA by addition of nucleotides. As we know, DNA replication takes place in S-phase of interphase. Thus, we conclude that DNA polymerase is an essential enzyme required during the S-phase.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4280,'biology',77,413,823,'Select the incorrect statement for prophase.','[{"text": "Chromosomal material condenses to form compact mitotic chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The assembly of mitotic spindle is initiated by the microtubules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase which is the first stage of mitosis follows the S immediately", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Prophase which is the first stage of karyokinesis of mitosis follows the  ${G_2}$ phase of interphase. Prophase is marked by the initiation of condensation of chromosomal material. Chromosomal material condenses to form compact mitotic chromosomes. Centrosome which had undergone duplication during interphase, begins to move towards opposite poles of the cell. Each centrosome radiates out microtubules and spindle assembly is initiated.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4281,'biology',74,246,488,'Identify the two Kingdoms mentioned in the Two-kingdom system of classification','[{"text": "Protista and Plantae kingdom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protista and Animalia kingdom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plantae and Monera kingdom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plantae and Animalia kingdom", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Carolus Linnaeus proposed Two Kingdom system of classification with Plantae and Animalia kingdoms was developed that included all plants and animals respectively.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4282,'biology',75,719,1522,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Apocarpous<br>B. Syncarpous<br>C. Diadelphous<br>D. Epiphyllous androecium</div><div class="column-right">P. Sesbania<br>Q. Lily<br>R. Mustard<br>S. Rose</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S},  \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P},  \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R},  \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R},  \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-S, B-R, C-P, D-Q',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(4283,'biology',77,415,828,'The number of mitotic divisions required to produce 128 cells from a single cell is','[{"text": "7", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "64", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'One mitotic division produces two identical daughter cells. Those two daughter cells will then be capable of division and produce four daughter cells. This arithmetic progression tells us that the n number of mitotic\ndivisions will be required to produce 2n cells. For the production of 128 cells, 128 = 27 i.e. 7 mitotic divisions would be required.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4284,'biology',74,246,488,'In how many groups did Aristotle divide the animals on the basis of presence/absence of red blood ?','[{"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Aristotle divided animals into two groups, those which had red blood and those that did not.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4286,'biology',75,719,1523,'Arrangement of ovules within the ovary is known as','[{"text": "Placentation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aestivation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Venation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hibernation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The arrangement of ovules within the ovary is known as placentation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4287,'biology',77,412,822,'Which one of the following statements is correct for cells in ${G_1}$ -stage of cell cycle?','[{"text": "Cells proliferate excessively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cells are metabolically inactive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cells are metabolically active, proliferate in normal condition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell is metabolically active and continuously grows", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${G_1}$  phase corresponds to the interval between mitosis and initiation of DNA replication. During  ${G_1}$  phase, the cell is metabolically active and continuously grows but does not replicate its DNA or proliferate.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4288,'biology',74,246,488,'Aristotle classified the plants on the basis of their morphological characters and categorised them into','[{"text": "Algae and herbs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae, bryophytes, pteridophytes,\\ngymnosperms and angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae and shrubs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trees, shrubs and herbs", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Aristotle used simple morphological characters to classify plants into trees, shrubs and herbs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4290,'biology',75,719,1523,'Select the correct answer','[{"text": "Placentation -Arrangement of ovules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phyllotaxy- arrangement of leaves at nodes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Venation - arrangement of veins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4291,'biology',77,412,822,'${G_1}$  phase is','[{"text": "End of  ${G_2}$-phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "End of S-phase and the start of mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Start of S-phase and the start of mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "End of mitosis and the start of S-phase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${G_1}$  phase is preceded by M-phase and followed by S-phase. Thus,  ${G_1}$ phase is the end of mitosis and start of S-phase.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4293,'biology',77,412,822,'Select the correct statements regarding S-phase','[{"text": "Occurs between  ${G_1}$  and  ${G_2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DNA replication begins in the cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centrioles duplicate in the nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "As DNA is doubled, number of chromosomes also doubles", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'S or synthesis phase occurs between  ${G_1}$ and  ${G_2}$ phases of interphase. It is characterised by the replication of DNA, where the amount of DNA becomes double but number of chromosomes remain same. In this stage, DNA duplicates in the nucleus while centriole duplicates in the cytoplasm.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4295,'biology',75,719,1523,'Identify the differnt type of placentation?<br>i. Axile, Central<br>ii. Free central, Basal<br>iii. Marginal, parietal','[{"text": "Only i", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only i, ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only i, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The placentation are of different types namely, marginal, axile, parietal, basal, central and free central',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4296,'biology',74,246,488,'Name the scientist who used scientific basis of classification for the first time ?','[{"text": "Bentham and Hooker", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aristotle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Whittaker", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linnaeus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Aristotle was the earliest to attempt a more scientific basis for classification. He used simple morphological characters to classify plants into trees, shrubs and herbs. He also divided animals into two groups, those which had red blood and those that did not.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4297,'biology',77,414,827,'Read the following statements and select the correct one.','[{"text": "M-phase represents the phase when the actual cell division or mitosis occurs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "S phase is included in M phase sometimes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitosis can be best studies in lab using pollen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It includes cytokinesis alone", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'1. M-phase also known as cell division proper is the phase when actual cell division occurs.<br>2. S-phase is a sub-phase of interphase. During this stage, DNA duplicates.<br>3. Mitosis can be best studied in rapidly\ndividing cells like the meristem of root tip of onion.<br>4. M-phase starts with nuclear division i.e. Karyokinesis and ends with cytoplasmic division i.e. Cytokinesis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4298,'biology',74,246,488,'Biological classification of plants based on morphological characters and animals - presence of red blood was first proposed by','[{"text": "Bentham and Hooker", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aristotle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Whittaker", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linnaeus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Biological classification of plants and animals was first proposed by Aristotle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4300,'biology',75,719,1523,'In marginal placentation the placenta forms a ridge along the______ suture of the ovary','[{"text": "Ventral", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Marginal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Basal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dorsal", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In marginal placentation the placenta forms a ridge along the ventral suture of the ovary and the ovules are borne on this ridge forming two rows, as in pea',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4301,'biology',77,412,822,'Which of the following is correct about interphase?','[{"text": "It includes  ${G_1}$, S,  ${G_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It lasts for more than 95 per cent in the duration of cell cycle in human cell.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is also known as resting phase.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Interphase represents the phase between two successive M phases. The interphase, though called the resting phase, is the time during which the cell is preparing for division by undergoing both cell growth and\nDNA replication in an orderly manner. The interphase lasts more than 95% of the duration of cell cycle. It is subdivided into –  ${G_1}$, S and  ${G_2}$ phases.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4302,'biology',74,247,489,'Which among the following are the smallest living cells, known without a definite cell wall, pathogenic to plants as well as animals and can survive without oxygen ?','[{"text": "Pseudomonas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mycoplasma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nostoc", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacillus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mycoplasma are smallest,  prokaryotic organisms which lack cell wall. They are pleomorphic in nature. These are pathogenic on both plants and animals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4304,'biology',75,719,1523,'In marginal placentation, the ovules are arranged','[{"text": "Along the inner wall of carpel in a syncarpous ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The ridge forming two rows.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In the middle of the ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "To the base of the ovary", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In marginal placentation the placenta forms a ridge along the ventral suture of the ovary and the ovules are borne on this ridge forming two rows, as in pea.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4374,'biology',74,248,492,'Major photosynthetic planktons are','[{"text": "Chrysophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dinoflagellate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) & (2)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The major photosynthetic planktons are:<br>(4) Both (1) & (2) - Chrysophytes and Dinoflagellates<br>Chrysophytes and Dinoflagellates are common examples of photosynthetic plankton found in aquatic environments.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4305,'biology',77,412,822,'Which one of the following is incorrect?','[{"text": "${G_1}$ Phase corresponds to interval between mitosis and initiation of DNA replication", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "During  ${G_1}$ Phase the cell is metabolically active", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA replication takes place during S-phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell growth in terms of cytoplasmic increase is a discontinuous process", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Although cell growth (in terms of cytoplasmic increase) is a continuous process, DNA synthesis occurs only during one specific stage in the cell cycle i.e. S-phase. ${G_1}$  phase corresponds to the interval between mitosis and initiation of DNA replication. During  ${G_1}$  phase the cell is metabolically active and continuously grows but does not replicate its DNA.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4306,'biology',74,252,503,'Given below are two statements:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">RNA mutates at a faster rate.</div><div class="column-right">Viruses having RNA genome and shorter life span mutate and evolve faster.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are true.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is true but Statement B is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is false but Statement B is true.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'RNA being unstable, mutate at a faster rate. Consequently, viruses having RNA genome and having shorter life span mutate and evolve faster.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4308,'biology',77,412,822,'Which of the following statement is correct:-','[{"text": "DNA is synthesized through out the cell cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interphase represents the phase between two alternate M phases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA replicates at S - stage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The interphase lasts more than 65% of the duration of cell cycle", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'DNA replication takes place only once during S-phase of interphase. Interphase represents the phase between two successive M-phases. It lasts for more than 95% of the duration of cell cycle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4309,'biology',75,719,1523,'Axile placentation is found in syncarpous ovaries, wherein the ovules are arranged along the','[{"text": "Base of the ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Margin of the ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Axis in the centre of the ovary", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When the placenta is axial and the ovules are attached to it in a multilocular ovary, the placentaion is said to be axile, as in china rose, tomato and lemon.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4310,'biology',74,252,503,'Which of the following statement is true about viruses?','[{"text": "Viruses are filterable facultative parasites.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viruses are capable of performing metabolic activities on their own.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All viruses known to man are obligate parasites.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Some viruses have cellular structure and are saprophytes.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Viruses are acellular infectious agents. They are too small to be seen with a light microscope. They do not have cell nucleus, organelles, or cytoplasm. They can replicate, or multiply, only inside a living host cell. They are called obligate intracellular parasites.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4311,'biology',77,411,821,'The cell cycle of mammalian cell and yeast, respectively, takes about','[{"text": "24 hrs, 90 min", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "90 min, 24 hrs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "30 min, 24 days", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Depends on the culture medium", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Duration of the cell cycle, for mammalian cell is 24 hrs. The cell cycle of yeast occurs in about 90 min. It is the period between two successive cell divisions and is called as generation time. It depends on the type of cell and external factors such as temperature, food and oxygen supplies.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4313,'biology',75,719,1523,'Ovary is one-chambered but it becomes two chambered due to the formation of false septum is found in','[{"text": "Argemone and mustard", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dianthus and primrose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rose and chinarose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pea and china rose", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ovary is one-chambered but it becomes twochambered due to the formation of the false septum, e.g., mustard and Argemone',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4314,'biology',74,248,492,'Identify the algae known for a biological activity called bioluminescence.','[{"text": "<i>Cyclotella</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Noctiluca</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Spirogyra</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Chlorella</i><br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Some marine dinoflagellate emits light and make the sea glow in dark (bioluminescence), for example, Noctiluca, Pyrocystis, etc.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4315,'biology',77,418,834,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Nuclear membrane disappears by the end of<br>B. Chromosomes align at the equator<br>C. Meiosis ends with<br>D. Splitting of the centromere of each chromosome</div><div class="column-right">P. Anaphase II<br>Q. Telophase II<br>R. Prophase II<br>S. Metaphase-II</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, \\tB-S, \\t C-R,\\t D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, \\tB-S, \\t C-Q,\\t D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, \\t B-P, \\t C-S,\\t D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, \\t B-R, \\t C-P,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Nuclear membrane disappears by the end of - (R) Prophase II<br>B. Chromosomes align at the equator - (S) Metaphase II<br>C. Meiosis ends with - (Q) Telophase II<br>D. Splitting of the centromere of each\nchromosome - (P) Anaphase II.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4317,'biology',74,247,489,'A bacterium is capable of withstanding extreme heat, dryness and toxic chemicals. This indicates that it is probably able to form:','[{"text": "Endospores", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Endotoxins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endogenous buds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A thick peptidoglycan wall", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The vegetative cells of some bacteria, such as Bacillus and Clostridium, produce resting stages called endospores. They are formed within cell. They contain very little water and are highly resistant to heat, drying, acids, bases, certain disinfectants and even radiation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4318,'biology',75,719,1523,'In which type of placentation, the ovules develop on the inner wall of the ovary or on peripheral part?','[{"text": "Marginal placentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parietal placentation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Axile placentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Free-central placentation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In parietal placentation, the ovules develop on the inner wall of the ovary or on peripheral part.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4319,'biology',77,411,821,'Which of the following statements are incorrect for cell cycle?','[{"text": "Cell cycle is cell division of a cell from the time of its formation to division into daughter cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DNA synthesis occurs only during one specific stage in the cell cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The replicated chromosomes (DNA) are distributed to daughter nuclei during cell division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The sequence of events by which a cell duplicates its genome, synthesises the other constituents of the cell and eventually divides into two daughter cells is termed cell cycle. It does not necessarily start from the time of the parent’s cell formation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4321,'biology',77,417,830,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Synaptonemal complex formation<br>B. Appears as tetrads<br>C. Chromosomes become gradually visible under the light microscope<br>D. X-shaped structures</div><div class="column-right">P. Pachytene<br>Q. Leptotene<br>R. Zygotene<br>S. Chiasmata</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, \\tB-P, \\t C-Q,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, \\t B-P, \\tC-R,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, \\t B-P, \\tC-R,\\t D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, \\t B-Q, \\tC-R,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. Synaptonemal complex formation - (R) Zygotene.<br>B. Appears as tetrads - (P) Pachytene<br>C. Chromosomes become gradually visible<br>under the light microscope - (Q) Leptotene<br>D. X-shaped structures - (S) Chiasmata',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4322,'biology',75,719,1523,'In a multicarpellary syncarpous unilocular ovary, if the ovules are borne on the central axis and septa are absent this is defined as','[{"text": "Marginal placentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parietal placentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Axile placentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Free-central placentation", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'When the ovules are borne on central axis and septa are absent, as in Dianthus and Primrose the placentation is called free central.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4323,'biology',74,254,505,'The agents which are known to cause CJD are:','[{"text": "A class of bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A class of viruses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shoot apex culture", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A slow but progressive dementing illness in human is known as Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease (CJD) and is characterized by mental degeneration, loss of motor function and eventual death. The disease is caused due to an infective agent which is a small proteinaceous infectious particle called prions.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4324,'biology',75,719,1523,'What is the type of placentation in which ovules are borne on central axis without septa','[{"text": "Free central, e.g. Primrose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Axile, e.g. China rose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Free central, e.g. Dianthus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In free cental ovules are borne on central axis without septa.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4325,'biology',74,254,505,'Bovine spongiform encephalopathy is a disease caused by prions in a:','[{"text": "Cow", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sheep", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Man", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Potato", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bovine spongiform encephalopathy (BSE) or mad cow disease occurs in dairy cattle. It is caused by prions (proteinaceous infectious particle). It has been observed to cause slow loss of neuronal function that leads to death.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4373,'biology',77,417,831,'Following diagram represents metaphse I, in which ____ are arranged at equator.','[{"text": "Bivalent chromosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tetravalent chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monovalent chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bivalent chromosomes formed in Zygotene stage of Prophase-I align at the equator to produce a double metaphasic plate during Metaphase-I.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/77_4373_question_1.png'),
(4326,'biology',77,417,833,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Terminalisation of chiasmata<br>B. Bivalent chromosomes align on the equatorial plate<br>C. Homologous chromosomes separation<br>D. Nuclear membrane and nucleolus reappear</div><div class="column-right">P. Metaphase I<br>Q. Anaphase I<br>R. Diakinesis<br>S. Telophase I</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, \\tB-P, \\t C-Q,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, \\tB-P, \\tC-R,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, \\t B-P, \\t C-R,\\t D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, \\t B-Q, C-R,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. Terminalisation of chiasmata - (R) Diakinesis<br>B. Bivalent chromosomes align on the equatorial plate - (P) Metaphase I<br>C. Homologous chromosomes separation - (Q) Anaphase I<br>D. Nuclear membrane and nucleolus reappear - (S) Telophase I',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4328,'biology',74,248,495,'When a fresh water protozoan is placed in marine water:','[{"text": "The contractile vacuole disappears", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The contractile vacuole increases in size", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A number of contractile vacuoles appear", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The contractile vacuole remains unchanged", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Contractile vacuole\'s job is to throw excess of water coming from outside to inside. In marine water, due to ex osmosis cell start loosing water anyway, means now there is need to preserve water not to throw it away. Therefore, contractile vacuole will disappear because presence of contractile vacuole will dehydrate the cell.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4329,'biology',77,417,830,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Pairing of chromosomes together<br>B. Pair of synapsed homologous chromosomes<br>C. Appearance of recombination nodules<br>D. Crossing over</div><div class="column-right">P. Bivalent<br>Q. Pachytene<br>R. Synapsis<br>S. Recombinase</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, \\tB-S, \\t C-Q,\\t D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, \\tB-S, \\t C-P,\\t D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, \\t B-P, \\t C-Q,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. Pairing of chromosomes together - (R) Synapsis<br>B. Pair of synapsed homologous chromosomes - (P) Bivalent<br>C. Appearance of recombination nodules - (Q) Pachytene.<br>D. Crossing over - (S) Recombinase.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4330,'biology',75,719,1523,'Basal placentation develops when the ovary has','[{"text": "Single ovule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Many ovules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Many locules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Single ovules in each locule", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In basal placentation, the placenta develops at the base of ovary and a single ovule is attached to it, as in sunflower, marigold.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4332,'biology',74,247,489,'Which of the following statement is not true for <i>Nostoc</i>?','[{"text": "It is prokaryotic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is autotrophic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is filamentous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is macroscopic", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Nostoc is a cyanobacteria. It belongs to kingdom Monera. They are photosynthetic they have filamentous unbranched form and convert atmospheric nitrogen to ammonia.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4333,'biology',77,417,830,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Diplotene<br>B. Zygotene<br>C. Pachytene<br>D. Leptotene</div><div class="column-right">P. 1<br>Q. 3<br>R. 4<br>S. 2</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, \\tB-Q, \\t C-R,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, \\tB-S, \\tC-Q,\\t D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-R, \\tB-Q, \\tC-P,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, \\t B-R, \\t C-Q,\\t D-P", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sub-stages of Prophase-I follow the order Leptotene, Zygotene, Pachytene, Diplotene and Diakinesis<br>A. Diplotene – (R) 4<br>B. Zygotene – (S) 2<br>C. Pachytene – (Q) 3<br>D. Leptotene – (P) 1',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
