(4336,'biology',74,247,489,'Which one does not belong to Monera?','[{"text": "Slime moulds", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mycoplasma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eubacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Archaebacteria", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All prokaryotic organisms are included in kingdom Monera. It includes bacteria, cyanobacteria (blue green alage), archaebacteria and some smaller groups, such as mycoplasmas, actinomycetes, rickettsias, etc. Slime moulds are eukaryotic and includes in kingdom Protista.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4338,'biology',77,417,830,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. zygotene<br>B. Leptotene<br>C. Diplotene<br>D. Pachytene</div><div class="column-right">P. Chromosomes become gradually visible under the light microscope<br>Q. Chromosomes start pairing together<br>R. Four chromatids of each bivalent chromosomes becomes distinct and clearly appears as tetrads<br>S. Dissolution of the synaptonemal complex</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-R,\\t D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-P, C-Q,\\t D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S,\\t D-R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A. Zygotene – (Q) Chromosomes start pairing together.<br> B. Leptotene – (P) Chromosomes become gradually visible under the light microscope.<br>C. Diplotene – (S) Dissolution of synaptonemal complex<br>D. Pachytene – (R) Four chromatids of each bivalent chromosomes becomes distant and clearly appears as tetrad.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4339,'biology',74,249,498,'A student while extracting DNA from <i>Aspergillus</i> fungus requires break open the cell wall. Name the enzyme used for the process?','[{"text": "Cellulase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysozyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pectinase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chitinase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Aspergillus is a fungus and its cell wall have chitin as a structurally important component. Thus, to break down the cell wall chitinase is required.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4341,'biology',77,418,834,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Formation of haploid gametes<br>B. Liquid endosperm in coconut<br>C. Growth of multicellular organisms<br>D. Between nonsister chromatids of homologous chromosomes</div><div class="column-right">P. Recombination<br>Q. Syncytium<br>R. Meiosis<br>S. Mitosis</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P,  B-R, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R,  B-Q, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R,  C-S,D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P,  B-S,  C-R, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. (R) Formation of haploid gametes/ Gametogenesis takes place by Meiosis<br>B. (Q) In some organisms, karyokinesis is not followed by cytokinesis as a result of which multinucleate condition arises leading to\nthe formation of syncytium (e.g., liquid endosperm in coconut).<br>C. (S) Mitosis plays a significant role in cellular growth of multicellular organisms.<br>D. (P) Recombination takes place between non-sister chromatids of homologous chromosomes during Pachytene stage of Prophase-I.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
