(4363,'biology',74,247,489,'The bacteria present in the gut of several ruminant animals','[{"text": "Are similar to other bacteria in cell wall structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Are anaerobes with peptidoglycan cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Are known as halophiles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Are responsible for production of biogas", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Methanogens are strictly anaerobes, they convert formic acid and carbon dioxide into methane/biogas . Methanogens live as symbionts inside rumen ( first chamber of stomach in ruminants). These are helpful to the ruminants in the fermentation of cellulose.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4364,'biology',77,417,833,'Name the following stages of meiosis_','[{"text": "A - Early prophase, B - Late prophase, C - Anaphase, D - Telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Prophase I, B - Metaphase I, C - Anaphase II, D - Telophase II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Prophase II, B - Metaphase II, C - Anaphase II, D - Telophase II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Prophase I, B - Metaphase I, C - Anaphase I, D - Telophase I", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The given figures represents the following stages – <br> A. Prophase-I, &emsp;  B. Metaphase-I<br>C. Anaphase-I,  &emsp; D. Telophase-I',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/77_4364_question_1.png'),
(4365,'biology',75,719,1523,'Which of the following type of placentation shows false septum___','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In parietal placentation, the ovules develop on the inner wall of the ovary or on peripheral part. Ovary is one-chambered but it becomes two- chambered due to the formation of the false septum',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4367,'biology',74,247,489,'Choose the features related to Cyanobacteria.<br>I. Symbionts in <i>Cycas</i> coralloid roots<br>II. Have mucilaginous sheath<br>III. Form blooms in polluted waters<br>IV. Have endospores','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I. Symbionts in Cycas coralloid roots: Cyanobacteria form a symbiotic relationship with Cycas plants. II. Have mucilaginous sheath: Many cyanobacteria have a protective, mucilaginous sheath. III. Form blooms in polluted waters: Cyanobacteria can proliferate and form harmful algal blooms in polluted water bodies. IV. Have endospores: Cyanobacteria do not typically form endospores. This statement is incorrect.<br>So, the correct options are (2) I, II, III.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4368,'biology',77,417,830,'In the phase shown by given diagram _','[{"text": "The homologous chromosome separates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bivalent chromosome separates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosomes start pairing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokinesis follows and this is called\\ndyad of cells", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The given figure represents Telophase I, showing the formation of dyad of cells after cytokinesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/77_4368_question_1.png'),
