(4372,'biology',75,719,1523,'Match the columns I and II, where column I represents type of placentation and column II represents it\'s example.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Marginal<br>B. Axile<br>C. Parietal<br>D. Free Central<br>E. Basal</div><div class="column-right">P. Argemone<br>Q. Pea<br>R. Lemon<br>S. Marigold<br>T. Primrose</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P},  \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Marginal - pea, axile - lemon, parietal <i>Argemone</i>, free central <i>Primrose</i>, basalmarigold.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4375,'biology',77,418,834,'Identify the correct statement','[{"text": "Interkinesis occurs before prophase I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interkinesis is generally short lived", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Replication of DNA occurs during interkinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interkinesis is followed by prophase-I", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The stage between the two meiotic divisions is called interkinesis and is generally short lived. There is no replication of DNA during interkinesis. Interkinesis is followed by prophase II.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4376,'biology',74,248,492,'Which of the following are the characters of dinoflagellates?<br>(i) They are planktonic golden yellow algae with soap box like structure.<br>(ii) They are marine red biflagellated protists.<br>(iii) They appear yellow, green, brown, blue and red in colour.<br>(iv) They are biflagellated organisms with pellicle.<br>(v) They are saprophytic (or) parasitic unicellular forms.','[{"text": "(ii) and (iii)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(ii) and (v)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i), (ii) and (iii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(ii), (iv) and (v)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Dinoflagellates are mostly single-celled organisms classified in the kingdom protista. Dinoflagellates characteristically have two flagella for locomotion and most have a rigid cell wall of cellulose',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4377,'biology',75,719,1523,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Inflorescence<br>B. Calyx<br>C. Corolla<br>D. Ovary<br>E. Placentation</div><div class="column-right">P. Polypetalous<br>Q. Racemose<br>R. Gamosepalous<br>S. Parietal<br>T. Unilocular</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P},  \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Q, B-R, C-P, D-T, E-S',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4379,'biology',77,419,835,'Select the option which correctly identifies the similarity between mitosis and meiosis cell division.','[{"text": "Pairing of homologous chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Required in all types of cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Duplication of DNA only once", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Separation of homologous chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the types of cell division. i.e. mitosis and meiosis are preceded by DNA replication which occurs in S-phase of interphase. Without replication of DNA cell division cannot proceed as equal distribution of DNA, is an essential function of cell division.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4380,'biology',74,249,496,'Choose the correct statements related to Fungi.<br>I. They show great diversity and morphology<br>II. They cause orange rot.<br>III. Toadstools are edible fungi.<br>IV. White spots on mustard leaves is due to parasitic fungus.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fungi show much diversity in morophology. Some cause orange rot, Albugo causes white spots on mustard leaves and toad stools are not edible but poisonous.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4381,'biology',75,720,1524,'Fruit is','[{"text": "Unripened ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ripened seed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A characteristic feature of flowering plant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The fruit is a characteristic feature of the flowering plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4383,'biology',77,419,835,'Which of the following is unique to mitosis and not a part of meiosis?','[{"text": "Homologous chromosomes behave\\nindependently", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chromatids are separated during anaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homologous chromosomes pair and form\\nbivalents", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homologous chromosomes cross over", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Meiosis is characterised by pairing of homologous chromosomes, crossing over and separation of homologous chromosomes. Because the homologous chromosomes separate, their number is reduced to half for\neach cell. In mitosis, there is not pairing of homologous chromosomes. They behave independently.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4384,'biology',74,249,498,'This is not a character of Ascomycetes','[{"text": "Sexual reproduction by gametogamy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Presence of Conidia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of Coprophiles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Asexual reproduction by budding", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The asexual spores are conidia produced exogenously on the special mycelium called conidiophores. Sexual spores are called ascospores which are produced endogenously in sac like asci.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4385,'biology',75,720,1524,'Fruit is','[{"text": "Developed after fertilisation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Developed before fertilisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Developed during the vegetative phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Fruit is a mature or ripened ovary, developed after fertilisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4386,'biology',77,419,835,'Which of the two events restore the normal number of chromosomes in life cycle :-','[{"text": "Mitosis and meiosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis and fertilisation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fertilisation and mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis and gametogenesis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Meiosis ensures the production of haploid phase in the life cycle of sexually reproducing organisms whereas fertilisation restores the diploid phase. These two events restore the normal number of chromosomes in life cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4388,'biology',77,419,835,'Meiosis is significant because it','[{"text": "Increases genetic variability", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Helps in the maintenance of specific\\nchromosome number", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is important for evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Meiosis is the mechanism by which conservation of specific chromosome number of each species is achieved across generations in sexually reproducing organisms. It also increases the genetic variability in the\npopulation of organisms from one generation to the next. Variations are very important for the process of evolution.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4389,'biology',75,720,1524,'Fruit developed without fertilization of the ovary, it is called','[{"text": "Parthenocarpy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Apomixis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "False fruit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polyembryony", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'If a fruit is formed without fertilisation of the ovary, it is called a parthenocarpic fruit',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4391,'biology',74,249,499,'Match column I (containing fungus name) with column II (common name) and choose the correct options.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <i>Puccinia</i><br>B. <i>Ustilago</i><br>C. <i>Agaricus<i/><br>D. <i>Saccharomyces</i></div><div class="column-right">P. Yeast<br>Q. Mushroom<br>R. Smut fungus<br>S. Rust fungus</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - P, B - Q, C - R, D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q, B - R, C - S, D -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A -  R, B -  S, C  - P, D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - S, B - R, C - Q, D - P}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Puccinia, Ustilago, Agaricus and Saccharomyces are commonly called as rust fungi, smut fungi, mushroom and yeast respectively.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4392,'biology',77,418,834,'Splitting of centromere and hence separation of chromatids occurs during','[{"text": "Prophase-II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaphase-I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaphase-II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metaphase-II", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During anaphase-II, the centromere splits and the sister chromatids of homologous chromosomes separate. This event is similar to the anaphase stage of mitosis. But during anaphase-I, the homologous chromosomes separate without the splitting of centromere.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4393,'biology',74,246,488,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">According to Whittaker, kingdom Protista includes <i>Chlorella</i> and <i>Paramoecium</i>.<br></div><div class="column-right">Paramoecium and Chlorella are unicellular and lack cell wall.</div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct, Statement B is wrong", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is wrong, Statement B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Protista includes unicellular eukaryotes. Both Chlorella and Paramoecium are unicellular and eukaryotic. Chlorella possess cell wall.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4395,'biology',75,720,1524,'Generally, what does the fruit consists of?','[{"text": "Pericarp and seeds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wall and seeds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mesocarp and seeds.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The pericarp may be dry or fleshy. When pericarp is thick and fleshy, it is differentiated into the outer epicarp, the middle mesocarp and the inner endocarp',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4396,'biology',77,418,834,'At the end of meiosis-II, number of cells formed are','[{"text": "two, haploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "four, haploid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "four, diploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "two, diploid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Meiosis starts with one diploid cell containing copies of chromosomes, one from the female parent and one from the male parent. The cell divides twice, so as to produce four haploid cells containing one copy of each chromosome.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4397,'biology',74,246,488,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The number and nature of other kingdoms have been understood differently by different scientists over time.<br></div><div class="column-right">Plant and Animal kingdoms are cons-tantly maintained in all the classifications so far since the time of Linnaeus.<br></div></div>','[{"text": "Both A and B statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both A and B statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct and B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect and B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Kingdom Plantae and Animalia are mentioned in all classifications so far but the organisms belong to them have been subjected to change in different classifications.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4398,'biology',77,418,834,'Meiosis II performs','[{"text": "Synthesis of DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Disjunction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Separation of chromatids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Separation of homologous chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Meiosis-I is responsible for separation of homologous chromosomes while Meiosis-II is responsible for separation of sister chromatids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4401,'biology',74,250,501,'Choose the correct statement.','[{"text": "The cell wall is present in all monerans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The cell wall is present in all protistans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All fungi are multicellular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The cell wall is present in all the members of Plantae", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All Plantae have cell wall but not all protistans like euglenoids and monerans like Mycoplasmas.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4402,'biology',77,418,834,'Meiosis II resembles a normal','[{"text": "Amitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When a dividing cell enters meiosis-II, chromosomal content in daughter cell remains same, just like in mitosis. Hence, meiosis-II is similar to mitosis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4404,'biology',75,720,1524,'In coconut and mango, the fruit is known as','[{"text": "Legume", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Berry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Drupe", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Achene", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In mango and coconut, the fruit is known as a drupe',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4405,'biology',74,247,489,'Choose the characters shown by the following organism. I. It has cell wall made of peptidoglycan<br>II. It releases oxygen during photosynthesis<br>III. If fixes Nitrogen <br>IV. It has Chlorophyll a','[{"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The diagram indicates Nostoc, Its cellwall is made up of peptidoglycan,has chlorophyll-a and performs photosynthesis and is a nitrogen fixer.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/74_4405_question_1.png'),
(4406,'biology',77,417,832,'In meiosis I, the centromere undergoes','[{"text": "No division", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Division during anaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Division during prophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Division during metaphase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In anaphase-I of meiosis-I, homologous chromosomes separate. Centromere splits in anaphase-II of meiosis-II.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4408,'biology',75,720,1524,'Coconut is developed from','[{"text": "Monocarpellary inferior ovary, one seeded", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monocarpellary superior ovary, one seeded", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Multicarpellary inferior ovary, one seeded", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multicarpellary superior ovary, one seeded", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Coconut and mango- They develop from monocarpellary superior ovaries and are one seeded',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4409,'biology',77,418,834,'During telophase II','[{"text": "The nuclear membrane and nucleolus reappear", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is followed by cytokinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In telophase-II, the nuclear membrane and nucleolus reappear, and cytokinesis follows forming tetrad of cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4410,'biology',74,248,493,'Identify the character of the following diagram.','[{"text": "It has only one flagellum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It has both chlorophyll a and b", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It has a cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipid membrane makes its body flexible", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Euglenoids resemble higher plants in having chlorophyll $\\mathrm{a}$ and $\\mathrm{b}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/74_4410_question_1.png'),
