(4457,'biology',75,721,1525,'Which of the following seed has two cotyledons____','[{"text": "Wheat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pea", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Barley", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maize", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The seed of pea has two cotyledons.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4459,'biology',77,417,830,'When paternal and maternal chromosomes exchange their genetic material with each other in cell division, this is called','[{"text": "Dysjunction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crossing over", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Synapsis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tetrad formation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Exchange of genetic material between two homologous chromosomes (one from paternal and another from maternal side) leads to crossing over which increases genetic variability.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4460,'biology',74,246,488,'Tissue organization is not seen in<br>I. Monera &emsp; &emsp;II. Protista<br>III. Fungi &emsp; &emsp;IV. Plantae','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Tissues are present only in Plantae, Fungi and Animalia but not in Monera and Protista as they are unicellular.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4461,'biology',75,721,1525,'Embryo consists of___','[{"text": "Cotyledons", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hilum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Micropyle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More than one options are correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Within the seed coat is the embryo, consisting of an embryonal axis and two cotyledons.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4462,'biology',77,417,830,'Tetrad is made of','[{"text": "Four homologous chromosomes, each\\nwith one chromatids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four non-homologous chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four homologous chromosomes with four\\nchromatids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two homologous chromosomes, each\\nwith two chromatids", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A bivalent/tetrad is a complex formed by a pair of synapsed homologous chromosome, each with two chromatids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4464,'biology',74,255,506,'Choose the correct statements.<br>I. All viruses have nucleic acid and a protein coat<br>II. Prions are misfolded proteins<br>III.Viroids have linear RNA<br>IV. Lichens are tracheates','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Viruses have both nucleic acid and protein, viroids have only RNA, Prions are misfolded proteins.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4465,'biology',77,417,830,'Recombination is seen in','[{"text": "Leptotene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygotene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pachytene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Diplotene", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Recombination is one of the key events of meiosis. During Pachytene of Prophase-I, recombination nodules appear and crossing over takes place. This crossing over leads to recombination of genetic material between two non-sister chromatids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4466,'biology',75,721,1525,'An embryonal axis is made up of___','[{"text": "Embryo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cotyledons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'None of the above',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4467,'biology',74,247,489,'Refer to the given figures of bacteria cell and Nostoc and choose the option which shows correct label for the structures marked as A, B, $\\mathrm{C}, \\mathrm{D}$ and $\\mathrm{E}$','[{"text": "A- Cell wall, B- Plasma membrane, C-DNA, D- <i>Heterocyst</i>, E-Mucilage sheath", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A- Plasma membrane, B- Cell wall, C- <i>Heterocyst</i>, D- Chromosome, E- Mucilage sheath", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Mucilage sheath, B- Cell wall, C- Plasma membrane, D- <i>Heterocyst</i>, E- Chromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Cell wall, B- Plasma membrane, C- Chromosome, D- Mucilage sheath, E- <i>Heterocyst</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The correct labeling in the figures of bacterial cell and Nostoc are - A- cell wall, B - cell membranes, C - DNA, D-heterocysts, E - mucilaginous sheath.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/74_4467_question_1.png'),
(4469,'biology',77,417,830,'Bivalents means','[{"text": "A tetrad", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synapsed homologous chromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dyad", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Homologous chromosomes come to lie side by side in pairs and this pairing is known as synapsis. The complex formed by a pair of synapsed homologous chromosomes is called a bivalent or a tetrad.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4470,'biology',75,721,1525,'Endosperm is formed as result of___','[{"text": "Syngamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Double fertilization", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dehiscence of cotyledons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed germination.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In seeds the endosperm formed as a result of double fertilisation.syngamy is fusion of the gametes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4471,'biology',74,252,503,'The given figure shows some structures labelled as A, B, C and D. Which structure has the protein coat that encloses the nucleic acid?','[{"text": "A", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The structure marked as A, B, C and D are respectively head, collar, sheath and tail fibres. In head (structure marked as A), the protein coat (called the capsid) made of small subunits called capsomeres, protect the nucleic acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/74_4471_question_1.png'),
(4472,'biology',77,417,830,'Synaptonemal complex involves','[{"text": "Chromosome pairing", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chromosome movement", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosome segregation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosome structure", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During zygotene, homologous chromosomes start pairing together. This association is called synapsis and is usually accompanied by the formation of synaptonemal complex. Synaptonemal complex is a protein lattice that stabilises the synapsis of homologous chromosomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4474,'biology',74,249,499,'Match Column I with Column II<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <i>Rhizopus</i><br>B.  <i>Ustilago</i><br>C.  <i>Puccinia</i><br>D.  <i>Agaricus</i></div><div class="column-right">P. Mushroom<br>Q. Smut fungus<br>R. Bread mould<br>S. Rust fungus</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  Q, C  -  S, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  Q, C  -  P, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Rhizopus</i> is a bread mould fungus. <i>Ustilago</i> is a smut fungi. <i>Puccinia</i> is known as <i>rust fungi</i>. <i>Agaricus</i> is commonly called mushroom. A - R, B - Q, C - S, D - P is the correct option.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4475,'biology',77,417,830,'Synaptonemal complex is visible in','[{"text": "Compound microscope", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Simple microscope", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Electron microscope", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Naked eyes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When we observe Zygotene under the electron microscope, we see that chromosomal synapsis is accompanied by the formation of a complex structure known as synaptonemal complex.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4476,'biology',75,721,1525,'Select the example which is monocotyledonous seed','[{"text": "Barley", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maize", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sugarcane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of the above',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4477,'biology',74,249,496,'Which one of the following is not a criterion for classification of fungi?','[{"text": "Morphology of mycelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mode of nutrition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mode of spore formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fruiting body", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The morphology of the mycelium, mode of spore formations and fruiting bodies form the basis for the division of the kingdom fungi into various classes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4478,'biology',77,417,830,'Synapsis and synaptonemal complex forms in','[{"text": "Diplotene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pachytene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diakinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During Zygotene, chromosomes start pairing together and this process of association is called synapsis. Electron micrographs of this stage indicate that chromosomal synapsis is accompanied by the formation of complex structure called synaptonemal complex.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4479,'biology',76,846,1888,'Choose the incorrect option.','[{"text": "Different organs of plants are similar in their internal structure.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Study of internal structure of plant is called anatomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tissues are organised into organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Different organs in a plant show differences in their internal structure.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4480,'biology',75,721,1525,'Read the following statements carefully and select the incorrect statements from given options<br>(a) At the one end of the embryonal axis are present the radicle and the plumule.<br>(b) Endosperm is formed as a result of syngamy.<br>(c) In some seeds such as bean, gram and pea endosperm is formed as result of double fertilization.<br>(d) Cotyledons store reserved food material.<br>(e) Bean, gram and pea are non-endospermous.','[{"text": "a, b, c", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b, d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "b, e", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'a) At the two ends of the embryonal axis are present the radicle and the plumule.<br>b) Endosperm is formed as a result of double fertilisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4481,'biology',77,417,830,'Pairing of homologous chromosomes is called','[{"text": "Disjunction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synapsis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Segregation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synapses", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The second stage of prophase I is called zygotene. During this stage, chromosomes start pairing together and this process of association is called synapsis. Such paired chromosomes are called homologous chromosomes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4483,'biology',75,721,1525,'How many of the following have dicotyledonous seeds, Select the number of examples___<br>Pea, bean, wheat, barley, sunflower, jowar, sugarcane, maize, gram.','[{"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pea, bean, sunflower, gram are dicots.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4484,'biology',77,417,830,'In which stage of meiosis- I, the chromosome is thin, long and thread-like?','[{"text": "Pachytene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygotene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leptotene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Diakinesis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Leptotene is the beginning of prophase where chromosomes appear as thin, long threads. Condensation and coiling of chromatin fibres begins in this stage.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4485,'biology',76,852,1896,'With respect to which factor, the pericycle of a root differs from that of the stem?','[{"text": "Sclerenchymatous in root and collenchymatous in stem.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parenchymatous in root and sclerenchymatous in stem.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sclerenchymatous in root and parenchymatous in stem.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collenchymatous in root and parenchymatous in stem.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In dicot root pericycle is parenchymous, takes part in the lateral formation and secondary growth, whereas in dicot stem, pericycle is discontinuous, sclerenchymatous, present in the form of patches over the vascular bundles.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4486,'biology',77,417,830,'Select the correct answer<br>i. 	 The compaction of chromosomes occurs during leptotene<br>ii.	 During leptotene stage the chromosomes become gradually visible under the electron microscope.','[{"text": "i is correct only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii is correct only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During leptotene stage, the chromosomes become gradually visible under the light microscope.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4487,'biology',75,721,1525,'Find the correct statement regarding seed__','[{"text": "The seed coat has three layers.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The funicle is a scar on the seed coat through which the seeds were attached to the fruit.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inner coat is tegmen and outer coat is testa.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cotyledons are generally without food reserve.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The seed coat has two layers, the outer testa and the inner tegmen is correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4488,'biology',76,847,1889,'Choose the correct statement.','[{"text": "Meristematic cells are capable of division", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All the cells in a plant body are capable of dividing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Permanent tissues have all cells same in function, but different in structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A group of cells having common origin generally performs different function", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Not all the cells in plant body are capable of dividing.e.g cells of permanent tissue.The newly formed cells become structurally and functionally specialised and lose the ability to divide. Such cells are termed permanent or mature cells and constitute the permanent tissues.A tissue is a group of cells having a common origin and usually performing a common function.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4489,'biology',77,417,830,'Which of the following represents the correct order in prophase I?','[{"text": "Zygotene, diplotene, pachytene, leptotene, diakinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leptotene, zygotene, pachytene, diplotene, diakinesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Leptotene, diplotene, pachytene, zygotene diakinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pachytene, leptotene, zygotene, diplotene, diakinesis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The following are 5 sub-stages of Prophase – I arranged in the order of their occurrence:<br>• Leptotene<br>• Zygotene<br>• Pachytene<br>• Diplotene<br>• Diakinesis',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4515,'biology',75,721,1525,'Plumule: coleoptile :: radicle:__','[{"text": "Rhizoptile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coleorhiza", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aleuroptile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Scutellum", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plumule: Coleoptile::Radicle: Coleorhiza',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4491,'biology',77,417,830,'Which of the following is the longest phase of meiosis?','[{"text": "Prophase II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metaphase I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metaphase II", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Prophase of the first meiotic division i.e. Prophase I is the longest and most complex phase of meiosis. It has been further subdivided into the following five phases based on chromosomal behaviour, i.e.,\nLeptotene, Zygotene, Pachytene, Diplotene and Diakinesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4492,'biology',76,848,1891,'Which of the following statements is correct?','[{"text": "Endarch -The protoxylem and metaxylem in stem lie towards pith and periphery, respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Exarch -The protoxylem and metaxylem in roots lie towards periphery and pith, respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In stems, the protoxylem lies towards the centre (pith) and the metaxylem lies towards the periphery of the organ. This type of primary xylem is called endarch. In roots, the protoxylem lies towards periphery and metaxylem lies towards the centre. Such arrangement of primary xylem is called exarch.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4493,'biology',75,721,1525,'Select the mismatched pair____<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Testa- outer seed coat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tegmen- inner seed coat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cotyledons- reserved food material.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endosperm- fertilisation of egg.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Endosperm-provide nutrition to Embryo',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4494,'biology',77,417,830,'Prophase I is divided into 5 phases based on the______','[{"text": "Cytoplasmic behaviour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleolar behaviour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nuclear behaviour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosomal behaviour", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Prophase I is subdivided into the following five phases based on chromosomal behaviour, i.e., Leptotene, Zygotene, Pachytene, Diplotene and Diakinesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4495,'biology',76,846,1888,'Most appropriate definition of tissue is','[{"text": "They are composed of only one type of cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Perform one common function", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A group of one or more types of cells performing one common function", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A tissue is a group of cells having a common origin and usually performing a common function. Tissues having all cells similar in structure and function are called simple tissues. Tissues having many different types of cells are called complex tissues.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4496,'biology',77,416,829,'Which statement is correct for meiosis?','[{"text": "Meiosis I is reduction division", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Meiosis II is reduction division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis I - equational and II -reduction divisions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis I and II both are equational divisions", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In meiosis I, the chromosomal number gets reduced by half and hence, known as reductional division. Meiosis II is similar to mitosis/equational division as the chromosomal content remains same.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4497,'biology',75,721,1525,'In which of the following seed endosperm is not totally consumed until mature state___','[{"text": "Gram", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bean", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Castor", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Castor is endospermic.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4498,'biology',76,847,1889,'Identify the false statement about primary meristem','[{"text": "They occur in grasses and regenerate parts removed by the grazing herbivores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It consists of root axillary buds.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They are formed early in life", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During the formation of leaves and elongation of stem, some cells \'left behind\' from shoot apical meristem, constitute the axillary bud.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4499,'biology',77,417,832,'Which of the follwoing is the most important events/ events for meiosis?<br>i.  Pairing of homologous chromosomes<br>ii. Recombination of homologous chromosomes<br>iii. Crossing over<br>iv. Disjunction<br>v. Separation of sister chromatids','[{"text": "i, ii, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv, v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, v", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Separation of sister chromatids is an event common to both mitosis and meiosis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4500,'biology',77,416,829,'Meiosis in plants can take place in :-','[{"text": "Megaspore mother cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microspore mother cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Meiosis takes place in specialised diploid\ncells. In plants, microspore mother cell produces 4 microspores/pollen grains while megaspore mother cells produces 4 megaspores/eggs out of which only one remains functional.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4501,'biology',76,848,1890,'Identify the correct statement from the following.','[{"text": "During the formation of primary plants body, specific regions of apical meristem produce dermal tissue, vascular tissue and ground tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Permanent tissues having all cells similar in structure and function are called simple tissues", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Permanent tissues having different type of cells are called complex tissues", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The meristems which occur at the tips of roots and shoots and produce primary tissues are called apical meristems. During the formation of the primary plant body, specific regions of the apical meristem produce dermal tissues, ground tissues and vascular tissues. Permanent tissues having all cells similar in structure and function are called simple tissues. Permanent tissues having many different types of cells are called complex tissues.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4502,'biology',75,721,1525,'The main chemical constituent of an aleurone layer is___','[{"text": "Lipid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sugar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Aleurone layer is made up of proteins .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4516,'biology',77,416,829,'Meiosis, generally results in','[{"text": "2 daughter cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4 daughter cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Remains the same", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Meiosis is a process in which a singular diploid cell is divided twice to give rise to four haploid daughter cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4503,'biology',77,416,829,'Meiosis I is initiated after the parental chromosomes have replicated to produce.','[{"text": "Non-identical sister chromatids at the G1 phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-identical sister chromatids at the S phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Identical sister chromatids at the G1 phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Identical sister chromatids at the S phase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'DNA replication takes place during S-phase before the cell enters meiosis-I. During S-phase, the chromatids duplicate to form identical sister chromatids of each chromosome. This way, the amount of DNA doubles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4504,'biology',76,848,1890,'Identify the type of plant tissue being represented by the set of statements given below.<br>I. They perform functions like photosynthesis, storage, secretion, etc.<br>II. Their cells are isodiametric (they may be spherical, oval, round, etc)<br>III. They may either be closely packed or have small intercellular spaces.<br>IV. Their cell walls are thin and made up of cellulose.','[{"text": "Collenchyma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parenchyma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Xylem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sclerenchyma", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Parenchyma forms the major component within organs. The cells of the parenchyma are generally isodiametric. They may be spherical, oval, round, polygonal or elongated in shape. Their walls are thin and made up of cellulose. They may either be closely packed or have small intercellular spaces. The parenchyma performs various functions like photosynthesis, storage, secretion.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4505,'biology',75,721,1525,'Read the following statements carefully and select the correct answer___<br>(a) Rarely monocotyledonous seeds are endospermic.<br>(b) In cereals seed coat is membranous and fused with the fruit wall<br>(c) The endosperm is bulky in mature seed of gram, bean and pea.<br>(d) The outer covering of endosperm separates the embryo by aleurone layer.','[{"text": "a and b are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a and c are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a and c are wrong", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "b and d are wrong.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The corrected statements are<br>a. Generally, monocotyledonous seeds are endospermic but some as in orchids are nonendospermic<br>c. In plants such as bean, gram and pea, the endosperm is not present in mature seeds and such seeds are called nonendospermous',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4506,'biology',77,416,829,'Meiosis is extremely necessary for','[{"text": "Growth of the cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fertilsation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametogenesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Meiosis ensures the formation of haploid gametes in the life cycle of a diploid cell by the process of gametogenesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4507,'biology',76,848,1890,'Which of the following is not a feature of sclereids (stone cells)?','[{"text": "They are spherical, oval or cylindrical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Highly thickended with lignified cell wall and narrow lumen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are a type of living tissue", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Commonly found in the fruits, wall of nuts, sead coats of legumes and leaves", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Sclerenchyma is usually dead and without protoplasts.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4508,'biology',77,416,829,'Meiosis involves','[{"text": "Two nuclear divisions and two DNA replication", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two nuclear divisions and one DNA replication", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One nuclear division and one DNA replication", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One nuclear division and two DNA replication", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Meiosis involves two sequential cycles of nuclear and cell division called meiosis-I and meiosis-II, but only a single cycle of DNA replication during S-phase of interphase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4509,'biology',75,721,1525,'The embryo is small and situated in a groove at the one end of the___','[{"text": "Plumule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cotyledon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endosperm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aleurone layer", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The embryo is small and situated in a groove at one end of the endosperm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4510,'biology',77,416,829,'Meiosis involves two cycles of','[{"text": "Cell division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nuclear divisions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA replication", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Meiosis involves two sequential cycles of nuclear and cell division called meiosis-I and meiosis-II, but only a single cycle of DNA replication (during S-phase of interphase).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4511,'biology',76,848,1890,'The collenchyma tissue is found in','[{"text": "Epidermis in most of the monocotyledonous plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epidermis in most of the dicotyledonous plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Epithelium in most of the dicotyledonous plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epithelium in most of the monocotyledonous plants", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The collenchyma occurs in layers below the epidermis in most of the dicotyledonous plants. It is found either as a homogeneous layer or in patches.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4512,'biology',75,721,1525,'Monocotyledonous embryo consists of___','[{"text": "One large and shield shaped cotyledon and aleurone layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Scutellum, plumule and radicle.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One large and shield shaped scutellum and long embryonal axis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed coat and endosperm", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Embryo consists of one large and shield shaped cotyledon known as scutellum and a short axis with a plumule and a radicle',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4513,'biology',77,416,829,'During meiosis, DNA replication occurs','[{"text": "Once during S-phase after meiosis -1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Twice, i.e. during interphase and M-phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Once during S-phase before meiosis -I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Once during S-phase before meiosis -II", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Meiosis requires only one cycle of DNA replication which takes place during S-phase of interphase before meiosis-I begins.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4514,'biology',76,854,1898,'Which would do maximum harm to a tree?','[{"text": "Loss of fruits", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Loss of half of its flowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Loss of all of its leaves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Loss of all its bark", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The bark is an outermost layer of the stem of woody plants. All the tissues outside the vascular cambium are called as bark. It protects the tree from external damage, bacterial infection and loss of water. If all the bark of the tree is removed then water loss will dry out the tree will also become vulnerable to infections.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4518,'biology',76,848,1891,'Consider the following statements.<br>I. Companion cells are specialised parenchymatous cells.<br>II. Sieve plates are necessary to allow conduction between sieve tube cells.','[{"text": "I is true, but II is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II is true, but I is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are true", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both I and II are false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The companion cells are specialised parenchymatous cells, which are closely associated with sieve tube elements. End walls of sieve tube element are perforated in a sieve-like manner to form the sieve plates.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4519,'biology',75,721,1525,'Select the incorrect statement among the following:<br>A. Monocot seeds are generally endospermic.<br>B. In maize, the seed coat is membranous and is generally fused with fruit wall.<br>C. In monocot seed, the single large shield shape cotyledon is known as scutellum.<br>D. In orchids, the seeds are non-endospermic.','[{"text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4520,'biology',77,416,829,'In meiosis, the chromosome number','[{"text": "Is reduced by half", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Increases twice", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sometimes increases, sometimes decreases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During meiosis, the chromosome number gets reduced by half. Thus, it leads to the production of haploid daughter cells. The sperm and the egg are haploid cells and when they fuse during fertilisation they produce a diploid cell called zygote.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4521,'biology',76,848,1890,'Identify the tissue from the following statements .<br>I. They provide mechanical support to growing parts of plants.<br>II. It consists of cells, which are thickened at the corners..<br>III. It often contains chloroplast.<br>IV. Intercellular spaces are absent.<br>V. These tissues are found as layers or patches.','[{"text": "Vascular tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collenchyma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Parenchyma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Simple sclerenchyma", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The epidermis is the outermost protective layer of the dicotyledonous stem which is covered with a thin layer of cuticle, it may bear trichomes and a few stomata. The collenchyma is found either as a homogeneous layer or in patches. It consists of cells which are much thickened at the corners due to a deposition of cellulose, hemicellulose and pectin.<br>Intercellular spaces are absent. They provide mechanical support to the growing parts of the plant such as young stem and petiole of a leaf. Pericycle is present on the inner side of the endodermis and above the phloem in the form of semi-lunar patches of sclerenchyma. Each vascular bundle is conjoint, open, and with endarch protoxylem.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4522,'biology',75,721,1525,'Which of the following term is used for mature integumented megasporangium','[{"text": "Fruit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo sac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ovary", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Seed is the mature integumented megasporangium',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4523,'biology',77,416,829,'Before undergoing meiosis, the amount of DNA of a cell','[{"text": "Halves in S phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Doubles in S phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Remains the same", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Doubles in  ${G_2}$  phase", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In S or Synthesis phase, DNA replication occurs. Before undergoing meiosis, the amount of DNA in S – phase doubles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4524,'biology',76,853,1897,'Select the incorrect statement among the following about monocots:','[{"text": "Pith is large and well developed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phloem parenchyma is absent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Have sclerenchymatous hypodermis.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In monocot, peripheral, vascular bundle, which are generally large and centrally located are small", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In monocotyledonous stem, Peripheral vascular bundles are generally smaller than the centrally located ones.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4525,'biology',77,416,829,'Identify the correct statement about meiosis?','[{"text": "First division is equational and the second is reductional", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "First division is reductional and the second is equational", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both divisions are reductional", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both divisions are equational", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In meiosis I, the chromosomal number gets reduced by half and hence, known as reductional division. Meiosis II is similar to mitosis/equational division as the chromosomal content remains same.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4526,'biology',75,721,1525,'In the mature bean, gram and pea seed the food material is stored in____','[{"text": "Radicle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endosperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cotyledon", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In plants such as bean, gram and pea, the cotyledons are often fleshy and full of reserve food materials and the endosperm is not present in mature seeds and such seeds are called nonendospermous.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(4527,'biology',77,416,829,'How many meiotic divisions are necessary to produce 600 pollen grains?','[{"text": "200", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "100", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "150", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "300", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each meiotic division in pollen mother cell (2n) results in the production of 4 pollen grains (n). Therefore, the number of meiotic divisions to give n pollen grains = n/4. For the production of 600 pollen grains, 600/4 = 150 meiotic division are required.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4528,'biology',76,852,1896,'The following features belong to which option?<br>I. Pericycle above phloem is in the form of semilunar patches of sclerenchyma.<br>II. Each vascular bundle is conjoint, open, and with endarch protoxylem.<br>III. Hypodermis is made up of collenchymas starch sheath. <br>IV. Epidermis may bear trichomes and few stomata.','[{"text": "Dicot root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monocot root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicot stem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Monocot stem", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The outer hypodermis, consists of a few layers of collenchymatous cells just below the epidermis, which provide mechanical strength to the young stem. Cortical layers below hypodermis consist of rounded thin walled parenchymatous cells with conspicuous intercellular spaces.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5826,'biology',75,716,1511,'The "Eyes" of the potato tuber are<br>','[{"text": "Root buds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flower buds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shoot buds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Axillary buds", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Eyes of potato are actually axillary buds that help in vegetative propagation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4529,'biology',75,721,1525,'Read the following statements carefully and select the correct statement____','[{"text": "In plants such as bean, gram and pea the endosperm is not present.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The plumule and radicle surrounds the sheath called coleoptile and coleorhiza respectively.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The outer covering of scutellum separates embryo from endosperm is called as aleurone layer.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The cotyledons of dicots are called as scutellum individually.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In plants such as bean, gram and pea, the endosperm is not present in mature seeds and such seeds are called nonendospermous',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4531,'biology',77,416,829,'Meiosis in plants occurs in','[{"text": "Root apex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anther", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In plants, meiosis takes place in anther to form pollen (n) and ovules too form egg (n).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4532,'biology',76,848,1891,'Mark the incorrect statement.<br>I. Sieve tube members have sieve plates where they join with other sieve tube members.<br>II. The sieve tube elements and companion cells are connected by pit fields present between their common longitudinal walls.<br>III. Companion cells help in maintaing the pressure gradient in sieve tube.<br>IV. Companion cells lie adjacent to sieve tube cells.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV and I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The companion cells are specialised parenchymatous cells, which are closely associated with sieve tube elements. The sieve tube elements and companion cells are connected by pit fields present between their common longitudinal walls. The companion cells help in maintaining the pressure gradient in the sieve tubes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4534,'biology',77,416,829,'The type of cells that undergo meiosis are','[{"text": "Somatic diploid cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diploid sex cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Haploid sex cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Meiosis occurs in diploid sex cells to gives rise to gametes such as sperm in males and eggs in females, both haploid cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4535,'biology',75,721,1525,'Choose correct pair','[{"text": "Endosperm-consumes food material", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endosperm- stores food material", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dicotyledonous seed- rice", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tegmen- outermost covering of seed.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Endosperm stores food material.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4537,'biology',76,850,1892,'Choose the correct option for epidermis.','[{"text": "Made of parenchymatous cell, usually single layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Functions in protection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cells with large vacuole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The epidermis is the outermost layer of the primary plant body. It is made up of elongated, compactly arranged cells, which form a continuous layer. Epidermis is usually single layered. Epidermal cells are parenchymatous with a small amount of cytoplasm lining the cell wall and a large vacuole.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4538,'biology',77,416,829,'Meiosis in animals occurs in','[{"text": "Testis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovaries", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Brain", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In animals, gametes are formed in testis (male) and ovaries (female). Meiosis occurs in testis and ovaries to produce sperms and eggs respectively.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4539,'biology',75,721,1525,'Label the following___','[{"text": "A-plumule,    B - cotyledons, C - radicle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-cotyledons, B - radicle,    C-plumule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-plumule,    B - radicle,    C - cotyledons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-cotyledons, B - plumule,    C - radicle", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A- cotyledons, B- plumule, C-radicle',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/75_4539_question_1.png'),
(4541,'biology',77,416,829,'Meiosis will always occurs in','[{"text": "Diploid cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Haploid cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both haploid and diploid cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Any cell", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Meiosis is a process in which a diploid cell is divided twice to give rise to four haploid cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4542,'biology',76,850,1892,'Select the incorrect statement from the following:','[{"text": "Epidermis is made up of elongated, compactly arranged cell, which forms non- continuous layer", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cuticle prevents loss of water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cuticle is absent in roots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sclerenchyma provides mechanical support to organs.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The epidermis is the outermost layer of the primary plant body. It is made up of elongated, compactly arranged cells, which form a continuous layer.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4544,'biology',77,416,829,'Meiosis is','[{"text": "Reductional division", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Equational division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiplicational division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Meiosis is a type of cell division in which each daughter cell receives half set of chromosomes. If the parent cell is diploid (2n), progeny produced is haploid (n). Since the number of chromosomes is halved in daughter\ncells, meiosis is known as reductional division.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4545,'biology',75,721,1525,'The following diagram shows___','[{"text": "Structure of the dicotyledonous seed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Structure of embryo sac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Structure of monocotyledonous seed", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Structure of the embryo sac.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The following diagram shows Structure of monocotyledonous seed',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/75_4545_question_1.png'),
(4547,'biology',76,850,1892,'Identify the incorrect statement<br>I. The stomatal aperture, guard cells and the surrounding subsidiary cells are together called stomatal apparatus.<br>II. Epidermal cells are parenchymatous cell with abundant cytoplasm.<br>III. Vessel members of xylem are interconnected through perforation in their common walls.<br>IV. Epidermis is usually single-layered','[{"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Epidermal cells are parenchymatous with a small amount of cytoplasm lining the cell wall and a large vacuole.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4548,'biology',77,415,828,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Some lower plants and some social insects haploid cells divide by<br>B. Significant contribution of mitosis<br>C. Essential for the cell to divide to restore<br>D. Cells of the upper layer of the epidermis</div><div class="column-right">P. Nucleocytoplasmic ratio.<br>Q. Mitosis<br>R. Continuously diving cells<br>S. Cell repair</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-P,\\t D-R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-Q,\\t D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-P,\\t D-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. (Q) Haploid cells of some lower plants and social insects divide by Mitosis.<br>B. (S) Mitosis significantly contributes in cell repair.<br>C. (P) It is essential for the cell to divide and restore its nucleo-cytoplasmic ratio.<br>D. (R) The cells of upper layer of epidermis continuously divide and get replaced constantly.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4549,'biology',75,721,1525,'The structure labelled as \' a \' is enclosed in a sheath which is called as__','[{"text": "Aleurone layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coleorhiza", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coleoptile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endocarp.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'a- radicle, which is enclosed in a sheath called Coleorhiza.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/75_4549_question_1.png'),
(4551,'biology',77,413,826,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Anaphase<br>B. Telophase<br>C. Metaphase<br>D. Prophase</div><div class="column-right">P. 1<br>Q. 2<br>R. 3<br>S. 4</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-S, C-Q,\\t D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-R,\\t D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S,\\t D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cell cycle progresses in the order –<br> Prophase, Metaphase, Anaphase, Telophase<br>A. (R) Anaphase – 3<br>B. (S) Telophase – 4<br>C. (Q) Metaphase – 2<br>D. (P) Prophase – 1',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4552,'biology',76,854,1898,'Which of the following is correct about dorsiventral leaf?','[{"text": "More stomata is present on abaxial surface", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Undifferentiated mesophyll", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nearly the same size of vascular bundle is present all over leaf, except main vein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reticulate venation", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The abaxial epidermis generally bears more stomata than the adaxial epidermis. The latter may even lack stomata.Mesophyll is differentiated.The size of the vascular bundles are dependent on the size of the veins. It is not of a same size all over leaf.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4554,'biology',77,414,827,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Cytokinesis in an animal cell<br>B. Multinucleate condition<br>C. Cytokinesis in plant cell</div><div class="column-right">P. Syncytium<br>Q. Cell-plate<br>R. Furrow in the plasma membrane</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, \\tB-P, \\t C-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, \\t B-R, \\tC-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, \\tB-P, \\t C-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, \\t B-R, \\t C-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A. Cytokinesis (Animal Cell) – (R) Furrow in plasma membrane<br>B. Multinucleate condition – (P) Syncytium<br>C. Cytokinesis (Plant Cell) – (Q) Cell plate',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
