(4561,'biology',76,850,1894,'Select the most suitable answer<br>a. The conjoint vascular bundles usually have the phloem located only on the outer side of xylem.<br>b. The conjoint vascular bundles usually have the xylem located only on the outer side of phloem.<br>c. When xylem and phloem within a vascular bundle are arranged in an alternate manner along the different radii, the arrangement is called radial such as in leaves.','[{"text": "a - true, c - true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b-false, c - false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a - true, b-false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More than one option is right", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'a- true , b - false , c- false',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4562,'biology',77,413,825,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Metaphase chromosome<br>B. Metaphase plate<br>C. Anaphase<br>D. Kinetochores</div><div class="column-right">P. Plane of alignment of the chromosomes at middle of the cell<br>Q. Small discshaped structures at the surface of the centromeres<br>R. Made up of two sister chromatids<br>S. Splitting of chromosome</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R,\\t B-P, \\t C-Q,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, \\tB-S, \\t C-P,\\t D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, \\tB-Q, \\t C-P,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, \\tB-P,\\t C-S,\\t D-Q", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. (R) Metaphase chromosome is made up of two sister chromatids, which are held together by the centromere.<br>B. (P) The plane of alignment of the chromosomes at metaphase is referred to as the metaphase plate.<br>C. (S) During anaphase, centromeres split and chromatids separate.<br>D. (Q) Small disc-shaped structures at the surface of the centromeres are called kinetochores. These structures serve as the\nsites of attachment of spindle fibres to chromosomes.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4565,'biology',77,413,824,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Beginning of Prophase<br>B. S-phase<br>C. End of prophase<br>D. Meta phase</div><div class="column-right">P. Disappear of nucleolus and nuclear envelope<br>Q. Initiation of condensation of chromosomal material<br>R. Centrosome duplication<br>S. Morphology of chromosomes is most easily studied.</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, \\tB-Q, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, \\tB-R, \\tC-P,\\t D-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-S, \\tB-Q, \\tC-P,\\t D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, \\t B-S, \\t C-P,\\t D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. (Q) Prophase is marked by the initiation of condensation of chromosomal material. <br>B. (R) During S or synthesis phase, DNA and centrosome duplication takes place.<br>C. (P) Prophase ends with disappearance of nucleolus and nuclear membrane.<br>D. (S) Condensation is complete at metaphase. Chromosome in their most condensed forms are easily observable under the microscope. This is the best stage to study their morphology.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
