(4575,'biology',76,852,1896,'The following features belong to which option?<br>I. Pith is small or inconspicuous.<br>II. Endoderm is made up of single layer of barrel-shaped cells without any intercellular spaces. <br>III. Fewlayersofthick-walled parenchymatous cell forms pericycle.<br>IV. Cambium present<br>V. 2 to 4 xylem and phloem patches.','[{"text": "Monocot root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicot stem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicot root", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Monocot stem", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In dicotyledonous root, the innermost layer of the cortex is called endodermis. It comprises a single layer of barrel-shaped cells without any intercellular spaces. Next to endodermis lies a few layers of thick-walled parenchymatous cells referred to as pericycle. The pith is small or inconspicuous. There are usually two to four xylem and phloem patches.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
