(4603,'biology',77,415,828,'The main difference between dividing an animal and plant cell lies in','[{"text": "Cell plate formation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chromosome movement", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Disapperance of nucleolus, ER, GB", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosome separation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Animal cell performs cytokinesis by appearance of furrow in the plasma membrane. Plant cells divide by the formation of a cell plate due to the presence of an inextensible cell wall.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4606,'biology',77,415,828,'Mitosis helps','[{"text": "Replacement of old cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Repair", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Restore the nucleo-cytoplasmic ratio", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The growth of multicellular organisms is due to mitosis. Cell growth results in disturbing the ratio between the nucleus and the cytoplasm. It therefore becomes essential for the cell to divide via mitosis to restore\nthe nucleo-cytoplasmic ratio. Mitosis also contributes in cell repair by replacing old, dead cells with new ones.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4607,'biology',75,722,1526,'What would we interpret if $\\%$ is given for a flower in its floral formula?','[{"text": "When it can be divided into two similar halves only in one particular vertical plane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only one vertical section divides it into equal vertical halves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cannot be divided into equal vertical halves by any vertical section", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "When it can be divided into two equal radial halves in any radial plane passing through the centre", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\%$ represents zygomorphic nature of flower, when it can be divided into two similar halves only in one particular vertical plane',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4609,'biology',76,850,1892,'Match the followings and choose the correct option from below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Meristem<br>B. Parenchyma<br>C. Collenchyma<br>D. Sclerenchyma<br>E. Epidermal tissue</div><div class="column-right">P. Photosynthesis, storage<br>Q. Mechanical support<br>R. Actively dividing cells<br>S. Stomata<br>T. Sclereids</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-R, C-T, D-Q, E-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q, D-T, E-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-T, D-P, E-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-T, B-S, C-R, D-Q, E-P", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Meristem - Actively dividing cells<br>Parenchyma - Photosynthesis, storage<br>Collenchyma - Mechanical support<br>Sclerenchyma - Sclereids<br>Epidermal tissue - Stomata',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4610,'biology',77,415,828,'Which cell division is responsible for the growth of tissue and individuals :–','[{"text": "Amitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitosis and meiosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitosis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mitosis usually results in the production of diploid daughter cells with identical genetic complement. The growth of tissue and individuals is due to mitosis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4612,'biology',75,722,1526,'The floral diagram given below represents____','[{"text": "Brassicaceae family", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fabaceae family", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Solanaceae family", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liliaceae family", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The given floral diagram represents Brassicaceae family',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/75_4612_question_1.png'),
(4613,'biology',77,415,828,'Identify the cell division that maintains genetic similarity','[{"text": "Amitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During mitosis, chromatids do no undergo crossing over. DNA content of the parental cell is equally divided between the two daughter cells, maintaining the genetic similarity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4614,'biology',76,848,1890,'Identify the simple tissue from the following','[{"text": "Parenchyma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Xylem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epidermis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phloem", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Parenchyma is a simple tissue made of only one type of cell. Epidermis, xylem & phloem are complex permanent tissue as they comprise more than one type of cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4616,'biology',77,415,828,'Zygote a product of fertilisation gives rise to a full blown organism. What is the secret that all the cells have the same genetic complement?','[{"text": "Meiosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endomitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitosis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mitosis results in the formation of two daughter cells with genetic content similar to each other as well as the parental cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4617,'biology',75,722,1526,'In the family of given floral diagram the androecium is____','[{"text": "Monoadelphous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diadelphous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tetradelphous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polyadelphous", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the family of given floral diagram the Androecium is diadelphous',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/75_4617_question_1.png'),
(4619,'biology',76,851,1895,'Epiblema of roots is equivalent to','[{"text": "Pericycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endodermis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epidermis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stele", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Outer layer of root is called epiblema. It is capable if absorption of water & minerals. It is similar to epidermis as both are external layer.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4620,'biology',77,415,828,'Cell which divides by mitosis is','[{"text": "Upper layer of epidermis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cells lining gut", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Somatic cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mitosis contributes in cell repair. The cells of the upper layer of the epidermis, cells of the lining of the gut, and blood cells are constantly replaced by mitosis. Mitotic divisions in the meristematic tissues – the apical and the lateral cambium, result in a continuous growth of plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4622,'biology',75,722,1526,'Tetradynamous stamens are typical of-','[{"text": "Brassicaceae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Solanaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liliaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fabaceae", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Brassicaceae has tetradynamous satmens',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4623,'biology',77,415,828,'Mitosis usually results in the','[{"text": "Production of diploid daughter cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Growth of multicellular organisms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Production of haploid daughter cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mitosis is exhibited by diploid cells with a few exceptions (Haploid - lower plants, social insects). Mitosis usually results in the production of diploid daughter cells with identical genetic complement. The growth of\nmulticellular organisms is due to mitosis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4626,'biology',77,414,827,'Furrow formation does not occur in plant cell during cytokinesis because of','[{"text": "Extensible cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inextensible cell membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Extensible cell membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inextensible cell wall", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Plant cells are enclosed by an inextensible cell wall, therefore they undergo cytokinesis by the formation of cell plate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4629,'biology',76,854,1898,'In which of the following pairs of parts of a flowering plant is epidermis absent?','[{"text": "Root tip and shoot tip", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Shoot bud and floral bud", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovule and seed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Petiole and pedicel", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Root a shoot tip lack epidermis as they continue to grow. Generally meristematic activity is more in these regions hence lacks epidermis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4630,'biology',77,414,827,'When karyokinesis is not followed by cytokinesis, it results in the formation of','[{"text": "Uninucleate cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "multinucleated cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "undifferentiated cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "diploid cells", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In some organisms, karyokinesis is not followed by cytokinesis as a result of which multinucleate condition arises leading to the formation of syncytium (e.g. liquid endosperm in coconut)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4633,'biology',77,414,827,'Cell furrow appears in the plasma membrane of animal cell during','[{"text": "Interphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Karyokinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokinesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "S phase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In an animal cell, cell furrow occurs on the plasma membrane during cytokinesis. This furrow gradually deepens and ultimately joins the centre, thus dividing the cell cytoplasm into two.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4634,'biology',76,848,1891,'A piece of wood having no vessels (trachea) must be belong to','[{"text": "Teak", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mango", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Palm", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Vessels are absent in gymnosperms. Pine tree is a gymnosperm. Palm, mango & Teak are all angiosperms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4637,'biology',77,414,827,'Cytokinesis occurs via cell plate formation in','[{"text": "Animal cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacterial cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plant cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mammalian cells", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cytoplasmic division or cytokinesis in plant cells occurs via cell plate formation because these cells are enclosed by an inextensible or flexible cell wall.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4639,'biology',76,848,1891,'In conifers, fibres are likely to be absent in','[{"text": "Secondary phloem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary Xylem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Primary phloem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leaves", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sclerenchyma is absent in secondary xylem, thus, secondary xylem is devoid of fibres.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4640,'biology',77,414,827,'Cell plate which appears during cytokinesis, ultimately transforms in :-','[{"text": "Secondary wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Primary wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Middle lamella", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Plasma membrane", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In plant cells, wall formation starts in the centre of the cell and grows outward to meet the existing lateral walls. The formation of the new cell wall begins with the formation of a simple precursor, called the cell-plate that represents the middle lamella between the walls of two adjacent cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4643,'biology',76,848,1891,'A vessel-less piece of stem possessing prominent sieve tubes would belong to','[{"text": "Pinus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eucalyptus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Grass", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trochodendron", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Trochodendron is a vessel less angiosperm.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4644,'biology',77,414,827,'Mitosis is further divided in ____ stages of cytoplasmic division?','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cytokinesis is a simple process without any further division into stages.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4647,'biology',77,413,826,'During telophase :-','[{"text": "Nuclear membrane is reformed", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleolus disappears", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Astral rays appear", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During telophase, nuclear membrane and nucleolus reappears.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4650,'biology',77,413,826,'Higher plants differ from animals in having','[{"text": "Disappearance of nuclear membrane\\nduring prophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anastral mitosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Centromere and kinetochore", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Disappearance of nucleous during prophase", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Centrosomes are exclusive organelles to animals that radiate out microtubules called asters. The two asters together with spindle fibres forms mitotic apparatus. Animals exhibit astral mitosis while plants exhibit anastral mitosis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4653,'biology',76,848,1891,'A transverse section of stem is stained first with safranin and then with fast green following the usual schedule of double staining for the preparation of a permanent slide. What would be the colour of the stained xylem and phloem?','[{"text": "Red and green", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Green and red", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Orange and yellow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Purple and orange", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Xylem has both primary & secondary cell wall. Secondary cell wall is lignified and attracts. Safranin & stains red. After staining xylem phloem picks up fast green stain & appear blue.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4654,'biology',77,413,826,'Nucleolus, golgi complex and endoplasmic reticulum reforms in','[{"text": "Prophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Telophase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During telophase, nuclear membrane and nucleolus reappears. Organelles like endoplasmic reticulum and Golgi complex reform.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4657,'biology',77,413,826,'In telophase :-','[{"text": "Chromosomes reach at their respective\\npoles decondense and loose their\\nindividuality", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chromosomes reach at their respective\\npoles condense and loose their\\nindividuality", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosomes reach the equator\\ndecondense and loose their individuality", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'At the beginning of the final stage of karyokinesis, i.e. telophase, the chromosomes that have reached their respective poles decondense and lose their individuality. The individual chromosomes can no longer be seen and each set of chromatin material tends to collect at each of the two poles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4658,'biology',76,854,1898,'Match the following and choose the correct option from below<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Cuticle<br>B. Bulliform cells<br>C. Stomata<br>D. Epidermis</div><div class="column-right">P. Guard cells<br>Q. Single layer<br>R. Waxy layer<br>S. Empty colourless cell</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-S, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cuticle - Waxy layer, Bulliform cells Empty colourless cell, Stomata - Guard cells, Epidermis - Single layer.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4661,'biology',77,413,825,'Out of the following phase of mitosis, during which phase the chromosomes may appear in the V, L, J or I-shaped structures?','[{"text": "Prophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaphase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Telophase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During anaphase, the sister chromatids separate and pulled to opposite poles by movement of spindle fibres attached to the centromere. The chromatids moving towards opposite poles appear to be of various\nshapes like V-shaped (metacentric), J-shaped (acrocentric), L-shaped (submetacentric) or I-shaped (telocentric), depending on the position of centromere.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4663,'biology',76,848,1890,'Cells of this tissue are living and show angular wall thickening. They also provide mechanical support. The tissue is','[{"text": "Xylem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sclerenchyma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collenchyma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Epidermis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cells of collenchymatous tissue are living and show angular wall thickening. They also provide mechanical support.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4664,'biology',77,413,826,'The metabolism of a cell which decreases during prophase again starts increasing during','[{"text": "Metaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Telophase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "S phase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'With the onset of telophase, the metabolic rate increases due to formation of a new daughter cell. The nuclear membrane and nucleolus reappear. Organelles like endoplasmic reticulum, Golgi complex reform and increase the metabolic activity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4667,'biology',76,850,1894,'A conjoint and open vascular bundle will be observed in the transverse section of','[{"text": "Monocot root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monocot stem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicot root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicot stem", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Dicots have open type of vascular bundle. Stem of both monocot & dicot are conjoint.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4668,'biology',77,413,825,'During anaphase the chromatids move towards the _____','[{"text": "Opposite poles by shortening of spindle\\n\\t fibres attached to centromeres", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Same poles by shortening of spindle fibres\\nattached to centromeres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Opposite poles by lengthening of spindle\\n\\t fibres attached to centromeres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Same poles by lengthening of spindle\\n\\t fibres attached to centromeres", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During anaphase, after the splitting of centromere, the sister chromatids migrate to opposite poles with the help of spindle fibres. These spindle fibres pull the chromatids towards the pole by shortening in length.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4671,'biology',77,413,825,'Which of the following phases are longest and shortest in mitosis?','[{"text": "Metaphase, Telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase, Anaphase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Telophase, Anaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase, Telophase", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In mitosis, prophase is the longest phase while anaphase is the shortest.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4674,'biology',77,413,825,'During anaphasic movements of chromosomes, centromere of each chromosome is directed towards','[{"text": "Pole", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Equatorial plate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During anaphasic movements, the centromeres are directed towards of chromosomes towards opposite poles of the cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4677,'biology',76,847,1889,'How many shoot apical meristems are likely to be present in a twig of a plant possessing, 4 branches and 26 leaves','[{"text": "26", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "30", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Apical means tip. A plant with 4 branches will have 5 Apical meristem reg <img src=\'/img/data/biology/76_4677_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4678,'biology',77,413,825,'Mitotic anaphase differs from metaphase in possessing','[{"text": "Half the number of chromosomes and half number of chromatids.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Half the number of chromosomes but same number of chromatids.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Same number of chromosomes but half number of chromatids.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'After the splitting of centromere and separation of sister chromatids during anaphase, the number of chromosome remains same while the number of chromatids is reduced to half.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4681,'biology',77,413,825,'During anaphase, the centromeres of chromosomes','[{"text": "Join to two form daughter chromosomes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Split into two form daughter centrosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Split into two form daughter\\n\\t chromosomes.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Join into two form daughter centrosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During anaphase, the centromeres of chromosomes split into two form daughter chromosomes. Spindle fibres attached to the centromeres shorten and pull the chromosomes to the opposite poles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4682,'biology',76,848,1890,'A plant tissue, when stained, showed the presence of hemicellulose and pectin in cell wall of its cells. The tissue represents','[{"text": "Collenchyma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sclerenchyma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Xylem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meristem", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Collenchyma consists of cells which are much thickened at the corners due to a deposition of cellulose, hemicellulose and pectin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4685,'biology',77,413,824,'At which stage of mitosis, the separation of daughter chromosomes occurs in','[{"text": "Telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Late prophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaphase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'At the onset of anaphase, each chromosome arranged at the metaphase plate is split simultaneously and the two daughter chromatids, now referred to as daughter chromosomes of the future daughter nuclei,\nbegin their migration towards the two opposite poles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4688,'biology',77,413,825,'Anaphase is characterized by','[{"text": "Splitting of centromere", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Unification of chromatids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Movement of chromatid to equator", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Key events taking place during anaphase are – <br>• Splitting of chromosome<br>•  Separation of sister chromatids<br>•  Migration of sister chromatids to opposite poles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4691,'biology',77,413,824,'Equatorial plate is found in','[{"text": "Metaphase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaphase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The metaphase is characterised by all the chromosomes coming to lie at the equator forming the equatorial plate. Here, each chromatid of a chromosome is attached at kinetochores to spindle fibres arising from\nboth the poles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4692,'biology',76,846,1888,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Different organs in a plant show differences in their internal structure.<br></div><div class="column-right">Within angiosperms, the monocots and dicots are also seen to be anatomically similar.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Within angiosperms, the monocots and dicots are also seen to be anatomically different.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4694,'biology',75,724,1528,'Which of the following is a potato family?','[{"text": "Liliaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Solanaceae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Brassicaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fabaceae", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Solanaceae is a large family, commonly called as the \'potato family\'.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4695,'biology',77,413,824,'Small disc-shaped structures at the surface of the structure in metaphase chromosome which holds the two sister chromatids is called as','[{"text": "Centromere", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centrosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centriole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kinetochore", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Small disc-shaped structures at the surface of the centromeres are called kinetochores. These structures serve as the sites of attachment of spindle fibres to the centrosome.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4697,'biology',76,847,1889,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Tissues are classified into two main groups, namely, meristematic and permanent tissues.<br></div><div class="column-right">Growth in plants is largely restricted to specialised regions of active cell division called meristems.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. Tissues are classified into two main groups, namely, meristematic and permanent tissues based on whether the cells being formed are capable of dividing or not. Growth in plants is largely restricted to specialised regions of active cell division called meristems.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4698,'biology',77,413,824,'In which stage of cell division the chromosomes are most condensed :-','[{"text": "Prophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meta phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Telophase", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During metaphase, condensation of chromosomes is completed. They can now be observed clearly under the microscope after reaching their most condensed form.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4699,'biology',75,724,1528,'From the given below vegetative characters of Solanaceae are?<br>A. Mostly herbs, shrubs<br>B. Rarely small trees<br>C. Aerial, Cylindrical stem<br>D. Mostly woody stem','[{"text": "A,C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A,B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A,B,C", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B,C", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Plants of Solanaceae are mostly herbs, shrubs and rarely small trees<br>Stem: herbaceous rarely woody, aerial; erect, cylindrical, branched, solid',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4701,'biology',76,847,1889,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Shoot apical meristem occupies the distant most region of the root axis.<br></div><div class="column-right">Axillary buds are present in the axils of leaves and are capable of forming a branch or a flower.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Shoot apical meristem occupies the distant most region of the shoot axis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4702,'biology',77,413,824,'In metaphase, the alignment of chromosome takes place at','[{"text": "Poles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both pole and equator", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Equator", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The metaphase is characterised by all the chromosomes coming to lie at the equator with each chromatid attached at kinetochores to spindle fibres from poles . The plane of alignment of the chromosomes at metaphase is referred to as the metaphase plate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4704,'biology',75,724,1528,'The stem of solanaceae is not?','[{"text": "Underground stem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aerial, Erect, Cylindrical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hollow, Hairy or Glabrous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unbranched, Solid, Offset", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Stem in Solanaceae are herbaceous rarely woody, aerial; erect, cylindrical, branched, solid or hollow, hairy or glabrous, underground stem in potato (<i>Solanum tuberosum</i>)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4705,'biology',77,413,824,'Metaphase is not characterized by','[{"text": "Complete condensation of chromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alignment of chromosome on metaphase\\nplate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Attachment of spindle fibre to kinetochore", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reappearance of nuclear membrane", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Telophase is characterised by the reappearance of nuclear membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4707,'biology',76,847,1889,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The meristem which occurs between mature tissues is known as intracalary meristem.<br></div><div class="column-right">Intracalary meristem occur in grasses and regenerate parts removed by the grazing herbivores.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The meristem which occurs between mature tissues is known as intercalary meristem.Intercalary meristem occur in grasses and regenerate parts removed by the grazing herbivores.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4708,'biology',77,413,824,'Which of the following initiates the start of metaphase?','[{"text": "Duplication of DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Formation of spindle fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Complete disintegration of nuclear envelope", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Duplication of chromosome", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The complete disintegration of the nuclear envelope marks the start of metaphase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4709,'biology',75,724,1528,'Which of the following is not correct about Solanaceae family?','[{"text": "Found in tropics, subtropics and temperate zones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Herbaceous stem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Exstipulated leaf", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Root with root nodules", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Solanaceae doesnot have root with nodules.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4711,'biology',76,847,1889,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Both apical meristems and intercalary meristems are primary meristems.<br></div><div class="column-right">Lateral meristem produce woody axis.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. Both apical meristems and intercalary meristems are primary meristems. The meristem that occurs in the mature regions of roots and shoots of many plants, particularly those that produce woody axis and appear later than primary meristem is called the secondary or lateral meristem.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4712,'biology',77,413,824,'The spindle fibre attaches to the','[{"text": "Centromere", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centrosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centriole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kinetochore", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Small disc-shaped structures at the surface of the centromeres are called kinetochores. These structures serve as the sites of attachment of spindle fibres to the chromosomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4739,'biology',77,413,823,'Spindle fibres are composed of :–','[{"text": "Actin filament", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microtubules", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collagen protein", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Spindle fibres arise from the centrosome and are composed of microtubules made up of tubulin protein. Spindle fibres are responsible for the separation of daughter chromosomes during cell division.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4714,'biology',75,724,1528,'Which of the following are the characteristics features of leaves of plants of Solanaceae family?<br>A. Reticulate venation<br>B. Stipulated leaf<br>C. Rarely pinnately compound leaves<br>D. Alternate phyllotaxy<br>E. Opposite, Simple','[{"text": "A, C, D", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A,B,C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A,B,E", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A,B,C,D", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Solanaceae has alternate, simple, rarely pinnately compound, exstipulate leaves ; venation reticulate',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4715,'biology',77,413,824,'In which stage of mitosis, the chromosomes are composed of two chromatids','[{"text": "Prophase and metaphase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metaphase and telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase and telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase and anaphase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The chromosomes are composed of two chromatids &nbsp;during prophase and metaphase. During anaphase, centromere splits and sister chromatids separate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4716,'biology',76,847,1889,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Fascicular vascular cambium, interfascicular cambium and cork-cambium are examples of lateral meristems.<br></div><div class="column-right">Secondary or lateral meristem is conical meristem.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Secondary or lateral meristems are cylindrical meristems.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4718,'biology',77,413,824,'Metaphase chromosome is made up of two sister chromatids, which are held together by the ______','[{"text": "Centromere", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Centrosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centriole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kinetochore", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Metaphase chromosome is made up of two sister chromatids, which are held together by the centromere.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
