(4725,'biology',77,413,824,'The complete disintegration of nuclear envelops in a cell cycle marks the','[{"text": "Start of prophase of mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Start of metaphase of mitosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "End of anaphase of mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "End of metaphase of mitosis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The complete disintegration of the nuclear envelope marks the initiation of the second phase of mitosis, i.e. metaphase. By this stage, condensation of chromosomes is completed and these can be observed clearly under the microscope.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4753,'biology',77,413,823,'Which does not occurs in prophase:','[{"text": "Formation of chromatin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Movement of centrioles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Appearance of sister chromatids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Compaction of chromosome", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Formation of chromatin after decondensation of chromosomes takes place during telophase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4726,'biology',76,848,1890,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The collenchyma performs various functions like photosynthesis, storage, secretion.<br></div><div class="column-right">The collenchyma occurs in layers below the epidermis in most of the dicotyledonous plants.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The parenchyma performs various functions like photosynthesis, storage, secretion.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4728,'biology',77,413,823,'During cell division chromosome move towards different poles due to:-','[{"text": "Centriole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kinetochores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microtubules", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cytokinesis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During cell division, chromosomes move towards different poles due to microtubules. Microtubules in the form of spindle fibres attach to kinetochores and shorten to pull chromatids towards the poles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4729,'biology',75,724,1528,'In the floral formula of Solanaceae family, Calyx $(\\mathrm{K})$ is represented as?','[{"text": "(5)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$(3+2)$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$(3+3)$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Calyx is represented as (5) in Solanaceae',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4731,'biology',76,848,1890,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Sclerenchyma are usually dead and without protoplasts.<br></div><div class="column-right">The fibresare thick-walled, elongated and pointed cells, generally occuring in groups</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct.Sclerenchyma consists of long, narrow cells with thick and lignified cell walls having a few or numerous pits. They are usually dead and without protoplasts. The fibres are thickwalled, elongated and pointed cells, generally occuring in groups, in various parts of the plant.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4732,'biology',77,413,823,'Spindle fibres are made up of','[{"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amino acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellulose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RNA", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Spindle fibres are made up of tubulin protein.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4734,'biology',75,724,1528,'How many sepals are there in the calyx of plants of Solanaceae family?','[{"text": "5, Polysepalous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6, Gamosepalous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5, Gamosepalous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "6, Polysepalous", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'5 sepals, United(Gamosepalous) are there in calyx of plants of Solanaceae family',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4735,'biology',76,848,1891,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Xylem functions as a conducting tissue for water and minerals from roots to the stem and leaves.<br></div><div class="column-right">Xylem is composed of four different kinds of elements, namely, tracheids, vessels, xylem sclereids and xylem parenchyma.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Xylem is composed of four different kinds of elements, namely, tracheids, vessels, xylem fibres and xylem parenchyma.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4736,'biology',77,413,823,'Cells at the end of prophase, when viewed under the microscope, do not show','[{"text": "Golgi body and ER", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleolus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nuclear envelope", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cells at the end of prophase, when viewed under the microscope, do not show Golgi complexes, endoplasmic reticulum, nucleolus and the nuclear envelope.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4738,'biology',75,724,1528,'Calyx of Solanaceae is not?','[{"text": "Persistent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Five sepals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fused sepals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vexillary aestivation", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Calyx in solanaceae has valvate aestivation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4741,'biology',76,848,1891,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Tracheidsare elongated or tube like cells with thick and chitinised walls and tapering ends. <br></div><div class="column-right">The inner layers of the cell wall of tracheids have thickening which is uniform.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Tracheids are elongated or tube like cells with thick and lignified walls and tapering ends.The inner layers of the cell walls of tracheids have thickenings which vary in form.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4742,'biology',77,413,823,'Longest phase of mitosis is :–','[{"text": "Prophase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Telophase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Prophase is the first and longest phase of mitosis. In this phase, chromosomal material condenses to form compact mitotic chromosomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4743,'biology',75,724,1528,'The floral formula has which of the following symbol to represent Corolla?','[{"text": "K", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Corolla is represented as" $\\mathrm{C}$ "',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4745,'biology',76,848,1891,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In flowering plants, tracheids and vessels are the main water transporting elements.<br></div><div class="column-right">Gymnosperms lack vessels in their xylem.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. In flowering plants, tracheids and vessels are the main water transporting elements. The presence of vessels is a characteristic feature of angiosperms. Gymnosperms lack vessels in their xylem.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4746,'biology',77,413,823,'Prophase is characterized by','[{"text": "Initiation of condensation of chromosomal material.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centrioles moving towards opposite pole.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Initiation of the assembly of mitotic spindle.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Prophase is marked by the initiation of condensation of chromosomal material. Centrosome which had undergone duplication during interphase, begins to move towards opposite poles of the cell. Each centrosome\nradiates out microtubules called asters. The two asters together with spindle fibres forms mitotic apparatus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4747,'biology',75,724,1528,'Which type of the following aestivation is seen in Solanaceae family?','[{"text": "Valvate aestivation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Imbricate aestivation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vexillary aestivation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Valvate aestivation is seen in Solanaceae family',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4749,'biology',76,848,1891,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In roots, the protoxylem lies towards the centre (pith) and the metaxylem lies towards the periphery of the organ.<br></div><div class="column-right">In stems, the protoxylem lies towards periphery and metaxylem lies towards the centre.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In stems, the protoxylem lies towards the centre (pith) and the metaxylem lies towards the periphery of the organ.In roots, the protoxylem lies towards periphery and metaxylem lies towards the centre.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4750,'biology',77,413,823,'In prophase :–','[{"text": "Centrioles duplicate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosomes are seen to be composed\\nof two chromatids attached together at the\\ncentrosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The chromosomal material becomes untangled during the process of chromatin condensation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During prophase, chromosomal material condenses to form compact mitotic chromosomes. Chromosomes are seen to be composed of two chromatids attached together at the centromere. Centrosome which had\nundergone duplication during interphase, begins to move towards opposite poles of the cell in this phase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4752,'biology',75,724,1528,'The corolla of Solanaceae family are?','[{"text": "Free petals (Polypetalous)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "United petals (Gamopetalous)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Free sepals (Polysepalous)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "United sepals (Gamosepalous)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Petals are united - gamosepalous.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4755,'biology',76,848,1891,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Phloem transports food materials, usually from leaves to other parts of the plant.<br></div><div class="column-right">Gymnosperms lack vessels, sieve tubes and companion cells.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. Phloem transports food materials, usually from leaves to other parts of the plant. Gymnosperms have albuminous cells and sieve cells. They lack sieve tubes and companion cells. Gymnosperms lack vessels in their xylem.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4756,'biology',77,413,823,'In which phase of mitosis the centriole moves to opposite poles of the cell ?','[{"text": "Prophase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Telophase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The centrosome which had undergone duplication during interphase, begins to move towards opposite poles of the cell during the prophase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4757,'biology',75,724,1528,'Androecium of Solanaceae family is not?','[{"text": "Epipetalous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Five stamens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epiphyllous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stamens are attached to the petals", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Androecium of Solanaceae family contain stamens five, epipetalous.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4759,'biology',76,848,1891,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Sieve tube elements are also long, tube-like structures, arranged in transverse plane and are associated with the companion cells.<br></div><div class="column-right">A mature sieve element possesses a peripheral cytoplasm, large vacuole and a nucleus.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sieve tube elements are also long, tubelike structures, arranged longitudinally and are associated with the companion cells.A mature sieve element possesses a peripheral cytoplasm and a large vacuole but lacks a nucleus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4760,'biology',77,413,823,'In which stage of cell cycle, initiation of condensation of chromosome takes place?','[{"text": "Prophase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Telophase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Prophase is marked by the initiation of condensation of chromosomal material. The chromosomal material becomes untangled during the process of chromatin condensation',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4762,'biology',75,724,1528,'Syncarpous, bilocular gynoecium is found in?','[{"text": "Fabaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Solanaceae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Liliaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Syncarpous, bilocular gynoecium is found in Solanaceae',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4763,'biology',77,413,823,'Which of the following is proper sequence of stages in mitosis?','[{"text": "Metaphase, telophase, prophase and anaphase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Telophase, anaphase, metaphase and prophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase, Anaphase, metaphase and telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase, metaphase, anaphase and telophase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mitosis has been divided into four phases of nuclear division proceeding in the order – Prophase, Metaphase, Anaphase and Telophase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4777,'biology',77,413,823,'Which of the following types of cell cycle is known as equational division?','[{"text": "Amitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mitosis is called as the equational division because it divides the parent cell into two identical daughter cells, each with a nucleus having the same chromosomal content as in the parent cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4764,'biology',76,848,1891,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The companion cells are specialised parenchymatous cells.<br></div><div class="column-right">The sieve tube elements and companion cells are connected by pit fields present between their common longitudinal walls.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. The companion cells are specialised parenchymatous cells, which are closely associated with sieve tube elements. The sieve tube elements and companion cells are connected by pit fields present between their common longitudinal walls.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4766,'biology',77,413,823,'The two daughter cells formed during mitosis contains___________ as compared to the parent cell','[{"text": "The same amount of DNA but half no. of chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The same amount of DNA and the same number of chromosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Half the amount of DNA and the half no. of chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Double the amount of DNA and double no. of chromosomnes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During mitosis, chromosomes and DNA content synthesised in parent cell is equally divided amongst the progeny. Hence, the two daughter cells formed during mitosis contain the same amount of DNA and the same number of chromosomes as compared to the parent cell',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
