(4787,'biology',77,412,822,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Separation of daughter chromosomes<br>B. Interphase<br>C. M Phase<br>D. Division of cytoplasm</div><div class="column-right">P. Cytokinesis<br>Q. Karyokinesis<br>R. 95% of the duration of cell cycle<br>S. 5% of the duration of cell cycle</div></div>','[{"text": "A-S, \\t B-R, \\t C-Q,\\t D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, \\t B-R, \\tC-S,\\t D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, \\t B-S, \\tC-R,\\t D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-P, D-P", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. (Q) Nuclear division corresponding to the separation of daughter chromosomes is known as karyokinesis. <br>B. (R) The interphase lasts more than 95% of the duration of cell cycle.<br>C. (S) The cell cycle is divided into two basic phases – Interphase and M-Phase. Interphase lasts for approximately 95% of the duration of cell cycle while in the remaining 5% of the duration, M-phase takes place.<br>D. (P) Division of cytoplasm of a cell is known as cytokinesis.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
