(4789,'biology',76,850,1892,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In grasses, the guard cells are dumb-bell shaped.<br></div><div class="column-right">The guard cells possess chloroplasts and regulate the opening and closing of stomata.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. Each stoma is composed of two bean shaped cells known as guard cells which enclose stomatal pore. In grasses, the guard cells are dumbbell shaped. The guard cells possess chloroplasts and regulate the opening and closing of stomata.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
