(4801,'biology',77,412,822,'What type of cells undergo Mitosis?','[{"text": "Haploid cells of plantsonly", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diploid cells of animals only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haploid and diploid cells of plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Haploid cells in animals only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In animals, mitotic cell division is only seen in the diploid somatic cells. However, there are few exceptions to this where haploid cells divide by mitosis, for example, male honey bees. Against this, the plants can show mitotic divisions in both haploid and diploid cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
