(4813,'biology',76,851,1895,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Endodermis comprises a single layer of barrel-shaped cells with intercellular spaces.<br></div><div class="column-right">The tangential as well as radial walls of the endodermal cells have a deposition of waterimpermeable, waxy material suberin in the form of casparian strips.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Endodermis comprises a single layer of barrel-shaped cells without any intercellular spaces.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4814,'biology',77,412,822,'In the ${G_0}$ phase, the cell undergoes','[{"text": "DNA duplication", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Active metabolism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Complete resting", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Slow metabolism", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cells in  ${G_0}$ stage remain metabolically active but no longer proliferate unless called on to do so.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4817,'biology',76,851,1895,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Initiation of lateral roots and vascular cambium during the secondary growth takes place in cells present in pericycle.<br></div><div class="column-right">The parenchymatous cells which lie between the xylem and the phloem are called conjuctive tissue.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. Next to endodermis lies a few layers of thick-walled parenchyomatous cells referred to as pericycle. Initiation of lateral roots and vascular cambium during the secondary growth takes place in these cells. The parenchymatous cells which lie between the xylem and the phloem are called conjuctive tissue.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4818,'biology',77,412,822,'The cells which do not divide enter ____ phase from ${G_1}$ phase.','[{"text": "Quiescent stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Directly ${G_2}$-phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${G_0}$ -phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The cells that do not divide further exit ${G_1}$ phase to enter an inactive stage called quiescent stage (${G_0}$) of the cell cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4820,'biology',75,724,1528,'<i>Belladonna</i> : Medicine ; chilli :____','[{"text": "Fibre", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spice", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Edible oil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ornament", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Belladonna</i>: medicine:: chilli: spice',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4821,'biology',77,412,822,'An onion root tip has 16 chromosomes in each cell. How many chromosomes the cell would have at S -phase?','[{"text": "28", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "16", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "62", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "7", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Chromosomes remain the same, DNA doubles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4823,'biology',76,851,1895,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">All tissues on the outerside of the endodermis such as pericycle, vascular bundles and pith constitute the stele.<br></div><div class="column-right">The anatomy of the monocot root is similar to the dicot root in many respects.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Tissues on the inner side of the endodermis such as pericycle, vascular bundles and pith constitute the stele.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4824,'biology',77,412,822,'If a cell has 2n number of chromosome in ${G_1}$ phase, what is the number of chromosome in cell after ${G_2}$-phase?','[{"text": "$n$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4n$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2n$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$3n$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Chromosomes remain the same, DNA doubles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4825,'biology',75,724,1528,'Which of the following is not a medicinal plant?','[{"text": "Belladonna", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ashwagandha", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tobacco", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Tobacco is a fumigatory plant',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4827,'biology',76,851,1895,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">As compared to the monocot root which have fewer xylem bundles, there are usually more than six (polyarch) xylem bundles in the dicot root.<br></div><div class="column-right">Pith is large and well developed in dicotyledons.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'As compared to the dicot root which have fewer xylem bundles, there are usually more than six (polyarch) xylem bundles in the monocot root.Pith is large and well developed in monocots.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4828,'biology',77,412,822,'Which among the following cells of human body are found in ${G_0}$ -phase of cell cycle?','[{"text": "Gastric cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red blood cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heart cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In human body, heart cells do not exhibit division. Therefore, these exit the cell cycle at ${G_1}$-phase to enter an inactive quiescent stage(${G_0}$).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5827,'biology',8,153,326,'Which one is female gametophyte?','[{"text": "Embryo sac", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Embryo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pistil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endosperm", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Embryo sac - Structure that provides female gamete is called female gametophyte.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4830,'biology',75,724,1528,'Flowers of Mustard resemble Makoi in<br>I) Number of Stamens<br>II) Number of Carpels<br>III) Placentation<br>IV) Superior ovary','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Same no. of carpels -2 and superior ovary.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4831,'biology',77,412,822,'Select the correct matching:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Cytokinesis – Nuclear division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Karyokinesis – Cytoplasmic division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "S phase – Synthesis phase of RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${G_1}$ Phase – Gap 1 Phase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${G_1}$ phase is also known as Gap 1 Phase',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4832,'biology',76,852,1896,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The cells arranged in multiple layers between epidermis and pericycle constitute the cortex.<br></div><div class="column-right">Cortex consists of three subzones.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. The cells arranged in multiple layers between epidermis and pericycle constitute the cortex. It consists of three sub-zones. The outer hypodermis, consists of a few layers of collenchymatous cells just below the epidermis. Cortical layers below hypodermis consist of rounded thin walled parenchymatous cells with conspicuous intercellular spaces. The innermost layer of the cortex is called the endodermis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4834,'biology',77,412,822,'During cell cycle, when does the following takes place respectively :-<br>A. RNA and protein synthesis for cell growth <br>B. RNA and protein synthesis for cell division','[{"text": "${G_1}$ and  ${G_2}$ - phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "S - phase and  ${G_2}$ - phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "M - phase and  ${G_2}$ - phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${G_1}$ and M - phase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During  ${G_1}$ phase, the cell is metabolically active and synthesises RNA and protein that help with cell growth. During the ${G_2}$ phase, RNA and proteins are synthesised in preparation for mitosis while cell growth continues.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4835,'biology',75,724,1528,'Floral formula of <i>Solanum melongena</i> is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/biology/75_4835_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(4837,'biology',76,852,1896,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Cortical layers below hypodermis consist of rounded thin walled parenchymatous cells with no intercellular spaces. <br></div><div class="column-right">The innermost layer of the cortex is called the endodermis.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cortical layers below hypodermis consist of rounded thin walled parenchymatous cells with conspicuous intercellular spaces.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4838,'biology',77,412,822,'How many times does the DNA replicates in one cell cycle?','[{"text": "Once", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Twice", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Many times", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Not at all", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'DNA replication occurs only once, during S-phase in the cell cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4840,'biology',75,724,1528,'Which is correct for the gynoecium of Solanaceae?','[{"text": "Tricarpellary, superior ovary, trilocular with many ovule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bicarpellary, superior ovary, unilocular, many ovule.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monocarpellary, superior ovary, unilocular with many ovules.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bicarpellary, ovary superior, bilocular", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Gynoecium: bicarpellary obligately placed, syncarpous; ovary superior, bilocular, placenta swollen with many ovules, axile',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4841,'biology',77,412,822,'S-phase is not characterized by','[{"text": "Duplication of centriole in nucleus of eukaryotic animal cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No increase in chromosome number", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA replication in cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During the S phase, DNA replication takes place in the nucleus, and the centriole duplicates in the cytoplasm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4842,'biology',76,853,1897,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Pericycle is present in the form of semi-lunar patches of sclerenchyma.<br></div><div class="column-right">The \'ring\' arrangement of vascular bundles is a characteristic of monocot stem.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The \'ring\' arrangement of vascular bundles is a characteristic of dicot stem.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4844,'biology',75,724,1528,'Select the appropriate example of a given floral diagram__','[{"text": "<i>Asparagus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sunhemp", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Trifolium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Belladonna</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The given floral diagram represents plant of Solanaceae family (Belladonna)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/75_4844_question_1.png'),
(4845,'biology',77,412,822,'In which phase of interphase, DNA content gets doubled?','[{"text": "${G_1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${G_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In S-phase, duplication of chromosomal material occurs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4847,'biology',76,853,1897,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The monocot stem has a sclerenchymatous hypodermis and large number of scattered vascular bundles.<br></div><div class="column-right">Vascular bundles are conjoint and open in monocotyledonous stem.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Vascular bundles are conjoint and closed in monocotyledonous stem.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4848,'biology',77,412,822,'The phase of mitosis in which the centriole duplicates in the cytoplasm?','[{"text": "S-phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${G_1}$ -phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${G_2}$ -phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In animal cells, during the S phase, DNA replication begins in the nucleus, and the centriole duplicates in the cytoplasm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4851,'biology',76,854,1898,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The phloem parenchyma is absent, and water-containing cavities are present within the vascular bundles in monocotyledonous stem.<br></div><div class="column-right">The abaxial epidermis generally bears more stomata than the adaxial epidermis in monocotyledonous leaves.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The adaxial epidermis generally bears more stomata than the abaxial epidermis in monocotyledonous leaves.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4852,'biology',77,412,822,'During  ${G_1}$ -phase of cell cycle,','[{"text": "DNA doubles but chromosomes remain same", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA reduces but chromosomes increase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA doubles and chromosomes also double", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No change in DNA content occurs", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'DNA replication does not occur in ${G_1}$- phase of cell cycle. Thus, the amount of DNA in the given cell remains the same.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4855,'biology',77,412,822,'Which of the following events occurs during  ${G_1}$ -phase of the cell cycle?<br>(i) Active metabolism<br>(ii) Growth and normal functioning of cell<br>(iii) DNA transcription<br>(iv) Elimination of unwanted cells<br>(v) DNA replication<br>(vi) Centriole duplicates in the cytoplasm','[{"text": "i , ii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, v, vi", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In the ${G_1}$-phase, a cell remains<br>metabolically active and continues to grow, i.e. <br>there is an increase in its cytoplasmic content <br>and function normally. The proteins required<br>for DNA replication are synthesised during<br>this phase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4857,'biology',76,854,1898,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In dorsiventral leaf, The adaxially placed palisade parenchyma is made up of elongated cells, which are arranged horizontally and parallel to each other.<br></div><div class="column-right">The veins are uniform in thickness in the reticulate venation of the dicot leaves.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In dorsivental leaf, the adaxially placed palisade parenchyma is made up of elongated cells, which are arranged vertically and parallel to each other.The veins vary in thickness in the reticulate venation of the dicot leaves.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4858,'biology',77,412,822,'Which of the following phases of cell cycle is also known as the resting phase?','[{"text": "${G_1}$ -phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interphase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "S-phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "M-phase", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The interphase is also called the resting phase. This is because it is the time during which the cell prepares for division by undergoing cell growth and DNA replication in an orderly manner.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4861,'biology',76,854,1898,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The vascular bundles are surrounded by a layer of thick walled bundle sheath cells, in dicotyledonous leaf.<br></div><div class="column-right">The mesophyll is not differentiated into palisade and spongy parenchyma in isobilateral leaf.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. The vascular bundles are surrounded by a layer of thick walled bundle sheath cells in dorsiventral leaf (leaf of dicotyledonous plant). In an isobilateral leaf (leaf of monocotyledonous plant), the mesophyll is not differentiated into palisade and spongy parenchyma.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4862,'biology',77,412,822,'Which out of the following changes of which stage are not visible under microscope','[{"text": "Telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interphase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anaphase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Changes in interphase are not visible with the help of light microscopy. Hence interphase is also known as resting phase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4865,'biology',77,412,822,'${G_1}$  phase is not characterized by','[{"text": "Continuous growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA replication", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Active metabolism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-replication of DNA", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${G_1}$ phase is characterized by high metabolic activity and rapid growth. Whereas S or synthesis phase marks the period during which DNA synthesis or replication takes place.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4866,'biology',76,854,1898,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In pulses, certain adaxial epidermal cells along the veins modify themselves into large, empty, colourless cells called bulliform cells.<br></div><div class="column-right">When bulliform cells are flaccid due to water stress, they make the leaves curl inwards to minimise water loss.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In grasses, certain adaxial epidermal cells along the veins modify themselves into large, empty, colourless cells called bulliform cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4869,'biology',77,412,822,'Interphase is also called resting stage because','[{"text": "Cell has stopped making proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell is metabolically inactive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No visible changes occur in the nucleus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "No visible changes occur in the cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Interphase is the time during which cell prepares itself for division by undergoing cell growth and DNA replication. Still it is known as the resting phase because the nucleus does not show any visible changes under light microscope and hence is at ‘rest’ with respect to cell division.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4870,'biology',76,854,1898,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The parallel venation in monocot leaves is reflected in the near similar sizes of vascular bundles including main veins.<br></div><div class="column-right">The growth of the roots and stems in length with the help of apical meristem is called the secondary growth.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The parallel venation in monocot leaves is reflected in the near similar sizes of vascular bundles (except in main veins)The growth of the roots and stems in length with the help of apical meristem is called the primary growth.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4872,'biology',77,412,822,'The interphase is divided into three phases, namely','[{"text": "${G_1}$ -phase, M-phase and  ${G_2}$ -phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "M-Phase, S-phase, and  ${G_1}$ phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${G_1}$ -phase, S-phase, and ${G_2}$ -phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "M-phase,${G_1}$ -phase, and ${G_2}$ -phase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The cell cycle is divided into two basic phases – Interphase and M-phase. The interphase is further divided into three subphases:<br>•  ${G_1}$ phase (Gap 1)<br>•	 S phase (Synthesis)<br>•  ${G_2}$ phase (Gap 2)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4876,'biology',77,412,822,'In cell cycle, which stage though called resting phase but is the most metabolically active','[{"text": "Interphase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${G_1}$ -phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${G_2}$ -phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "S-phase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The interphase, though called the resting phase, is the time during which the cell is preparing for division by undergoing both cell growth and DNA replication in an orderly manner. Hence, it is metabolically the most\nactive phase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4881,'biology',77,412,822,'What is the division of cytoplasm, in M-phase called?','[{"text": "Cytokinesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Karyokinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytodivision", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitosis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Division of cytoplasm in M-phase is known as cytokinesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4885,'biology',77,412,822,'The M Phase starts with ____and usually ends with division of cytoplasm______.','[{"text": "Cytokinesis, karyokinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleokinesis, cytokinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Karyokinesis, cytokinesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mitosis, cytokinesis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The M-Phase starts with the nuclear division i.e. Karyokinesis and usually ends with division of cytoplasm i.e. Cytokinesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4888,'biology',77,412,822,'What is the division of nucleus, in M-phase called?','[{"text": "Cytokinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleokinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Karyokinesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mitosis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Division of nucleus in M-phase corresponding to separation of daughter chromosomes is called as karyokinesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4891,'biology',77,412,822,'The sequence of cell cycle is','[{"text": "${G_1}$, S, ${G_2}$ and M", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${G_1}$, ${G_2}$, S and M", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "M,  ${G_1}$, ${G_2}$ and S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "S, M, ${G_1}$  and  ${G_2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The cell cycle proceeds with Interphase which is subdivided into an orderly manner of foremost ${G_1}$, S and lastly  ${G_2}$. Interphase is followed by M or Mitosis Phase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5828,'biology',8,153,326,'What does embryosac represents?','[{"text": "Megasporophyll", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Megagamete", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Megagametophyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Megaspore", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The embryo sac represents the megagametophyte.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4895,'biology',77,412,822,'What is the approximate percentage duration of cell cycle that comes under interphase in humans?','[{"text": "$100\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$95\\\\% $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$50\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$5\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In an average 24 hour duration of cell cycle of human cell, interphase lasts more than 95% of the total duration, while cell division (M-phase) lasts for only about an hour.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4899,'biology',77,412,822,'M-phase in human cell lasts for','[{"text": "24 hour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 hours", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 hour", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4 hours", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The M-phase represents the phase when the actual cell division or mitosis occurs. In the 24hour average duration of cell cycle of a human cell, cell division proper or M-phase lasts foronly about an hour.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4902,'biology',77,412,822,'Duration of a cell cycle in yeast is approximately','[{"text": "90 seconds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "90 minutes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "90 hours", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "45 minutes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Duration of a cell cycle in yeast is about 90 minutes',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4968,'biology',77,412,822,'Interphase is called "Resting phase". The word "Rest" refers to','[{"text": "Division of cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Division of nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Absence of any cell division", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cytokinesis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cell division does not occur in interphase for this reason it is considered as resting phase',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4905,'biology',77,412,822,'The cell cycle is divided into two basic phases. They are -','[{"text": "${G_1}$, S and  ${G_2}$- phases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Karyokinesis and cytokinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interphase and cytokinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interphase and M-phase/divisional phase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cell cycle consists of two basic stages. There is a long non-dividing stage called interphase where the cell prepares for division and a short dividing stage called M-phase/ divisional phase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4909,'biology',77,412,822,'Human cell can divide itself once approximately in','[{"text": "24 days", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "24 minutes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "24 seconds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "24 hours", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Human cells divide once in approximately every 24 hours.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4913,'biology',77,411,821,'During cell cycle, how many times DNA synthesis occurs?','[{"text": "In all the phases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During cell cycle, DNA synthesis occurs only once, i.e. during synthetic (S) phase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4915,'biology',77,411,821,'Which of the following is correct about cell cycle?','[{"text": "DNA synthesis occurs only during one specific stage in the cell cycle.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All events are under metabolic control.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The replicated chromosomes (DNA) are\\nthen distributed to daughter nuclei by a\\nsimple series of events during cell division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Events of cell cycle are under genetic control. The replicated chromosomes (DNA) are distributed to daughter nuclei by a complex series of events during cell division.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4919,'biology',77,411,821,'All organisms start their life with','[{"text": "Few cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Many cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Single cell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Any of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'All organisms, even the largest, start their life from a single cell. That cell further divides into two daughter cells which can themselves grow and divide to give rise to an entire cell population.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4923,'biology',77,411,821,'The sequence of events by which a cell duplicates its genome, synthesize the other constituent of cells and eventually divides itself into two daughter cells is termed as','[{"text": "Cell duplication", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell cycle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cell growth", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The sequence of events by which a cell duplicates its genome, synthesises the other constituents of the cell and eventually divides into two daughter cells is termed cell cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4926,'biology',77,411,821,'Cell growth is a continuous process in terms of','[{"text": "Increase in total cellular contents", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase in DNA content", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleoplasmic increase alone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytoplasmic increase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cell growth is a continuous process in terms of cytoplasmic increase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4929,'biology',77,417,830,'The complex formed by a pair of synapsed homologous chromosomes is called,','[{"text": "Triad", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bivalent", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Univalent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pentavalent", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The complex formed by a pair of\nhomologous chromosomes is called Bivalent',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4932,'biology',77,412,822,'Among eukaryotes, replication of DNA takes place in :','[{"text": "M phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "S phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{G}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}$ phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{G}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ phase", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Replication of DNA takes place in S-phase\nof cell cycle in eukaryotes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4935,'biology',77,417,830,'The process of appearance of recombination nodules occurs at which sub stage of prophase I in meiosis?','[{"text": "Zygotene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pachytene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Diplotene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diakinesis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The process of recombination occurs at\nPachytene stage of prophase I and is\ncharacterised by the appearance of\nrecombination nodules.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4938,'biology',77,412,822,'Match Column- I with Column- II :<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. M Phase<br>B.${{\\rm{G}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ Phase<br>C. Quiescent stage<br>D. ${{\\rm{G}}_{\\rm{1}}}$ Phase</div><div class="column-right">P. Proteins are synthesized<br>Q. Inactive phase<br>R. Interval between mitosis and initiation of DNA replication<br>S. Equational division</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-P, C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mitosis is also called equational division.<br>During ${{\\rm{G}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ phase DNA synthesis stops but cell synthesis RNA, proteins, etc. for next phase.<br>Quiescent stage is inactive phase in which non-dividing cells enters.<br>${{\\rm{G}}_{\\rm{1}}}$ phase is the interval between mitosis and initiation of DNA replication.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4942,'biology',77,412,822,'Given below are two statements:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">During ${{\\rm{G}}_{\\rm{0}}}$ phase of cell cycle, the cell is metabolically inactive.</div><div class="column-right">The centrosome undergoes duplication during S phase of interphase.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cells in the ${{\\rm{G}}_{\\rm{0}}}$ stage remain metabolically active but no longer proliferate unless called on to do so depending on the requirement of the organism.<br>In animal cells, during the S-phase, DNA replication begins in the nucleus, and the centriole duplicates in the cytoplasm.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4945,'biology',77,417,830,'Select the correct statements.<br>I. Tetrad formation is seen during Leptotene.<br>II. During Anaphase, the centromeres split and chromatids separate.<br>III. Terminalization takes place during Pachytene.<br>IV. Nucleolus, Golgi complex and ER are reformed during Telophase.<br>V. Crossing over takes place between sister chromatids of homologous chromosome.\n<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "I and III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III and V only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and V only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'• Tetrad formation is seen during zygotene stage<br>• During Anaphase, the centromeres split and chromatids separate.<br>• Terminalisation of chiasmata takes place during diakinesis.<br>• Nucleolus, golgi complex and ER are reformed during telophase.<br>• Crossing over takes place between non-sister chromatids of homologous chromosomes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4948,'biology',77,415,828,'Mitotic stages are not observed in:','[{"text": "<i>Cosmarium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>E. coli</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Saccharomyces</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Chlorella</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'E.coli is bacterium and it undergoes Binary fission and does not show mitotic or Meiotic type of cell division..',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4952,'biology',77,412,822,'The centrosome duplicates during the:','[{"text": "S-phase of cell cycle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "G1-phase of cell cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "G2-phase of cell cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prophase of cell cycle", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'S-phase is a part of interphase of cell cycle between $\\mathrm{G}_{1}$ and $\\mathrm{G}_{2}$. DNA content of a cell is doubled during this Phase. Centrosome also begins to divide, in Centriole containing cells, to form two centrosomes or centriole pair.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4955,'biology',77,417,830,'What is the function of the enzyme \'recombinase\' during meiosis?','[{"text": "Formation of synaptonemal complex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crossing over between non-sister chromatids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Condensation of chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alignment of bivalent chromosomes on equatorial plate", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Under the electron microscope, dense Bodies about $100 \\mathrm{~nm}$ in diameter are seen. These structures are called recombination. Nodules because they correspond to the sites Where crossing over (exchange of genetic Material) is taking place between non-sister Chromatids of the homologous chromosomes.Recombination nodules contain the enzyme recombinase that facilities genetic recombination, which is completed by the end of pachytene.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4979,'biology',76,848,1891,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Vascular tissues are complex tissues<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Xylem and phloem are meant for conduction of water and food respectively.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and but Reason is not correct explanation of Assertion. The complex tissues are made of more than one type of cells and these works together as a unit. Xylem and phloem constitute the complex tissues in plants.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4956,'biology',76,848,1891,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Phloem is a specialized complex tissue<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Phloem is a transport tissue characterized by the presence of sieve tubes, companion cells, phloem fibres and phloem parenchyma cells','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion. The complex tissues are made of more than one type of cells and these work together as a unit. Xylem and phloem constitute the complex tissues in plants. Phloem in angiosperms is composed of sieve tube elements, companion cells, phloem parenchyma and phloem fibres. Gymnosperms have albuminous cells and sieve cells. They lack sieve tubes and companion cells.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4958,'biology',77,412,822,'Cells in the quiescent stage :','[{"text": "Always become cancerous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Show indefinite proliferation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Remain metabolically inactive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Remain metabolically active", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Quiescence is the reversible state of a cell in which it does not divide but retains the ability tore-enter cell proliferation and thus is metabolically active. Some adult stem cells are maintained inaquiescent state and can be rapidly activated When stimulated.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4962,'biology',77,417,830,'The correct sequence of events in prophase I is:','[{"text": "Synapsis $\\\\rightarrow$ Crossing over $\\\\rightarrow$ Chiasmata $\\\\rightarrow$ Terminalisation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Crossing over $\\\\rightarrow$ Synapsis $\\\\rightarrow$ Chiasmata $\\\\rightarrow$ Terminalisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chiasmata $\\\\rightarrow$ Synapsis $\\\\rightarrow$ Crossing over $\\\\rightarrow$ Terminalisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chiasmata $\\\\rightarrow$ Crossing over $\\\\rightarrow$ Synapsis $\\\\rightarrow$ Terminalisation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The correct sequence of prophase-I of meiosis is Leptotene, zygotene, pachytene, diplotene, diakinesis. During prophase I, the chromosomes have already duplicated. During prophase I, they coil and become shorter and thicker and visible under the light microscope.<br>The duplicated homologous chromosomes pair, and crossing-over occurs. Crossing-over is the process that can give rise to genetic recombination. At this point, each homologous chromosome pair is visible as a bivalent, a tight grouping of two chromosomes, each consisting of two sister chromatids. The sites of crossing-over are seen as crisscrossed nonsister chromatids and are called chiasmata. The nucleolus disappears during prophase I. In the cytoplasm, the meiotic spindle, consisting of microtubules and other proteins, forms between the two pairs of centrioles as they migrate to opposite poles of the cell. The nuclear envelope disappears at the end of prophase I, allowing the spindle to enter the nucleus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4965,'biology',76,852,1896,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In some dicot stem, endodermis is also referred to as starch sheath<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The cells of endodermis are rich in starch grains.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion. The innermost layer of the cortex is called the endodermis. The cells of the endodermis are rich in starch grains and the layer is also referred to as the starch sheath.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4969,'biology',76,848,1890,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Simple permanent tissues have homogenous tissues<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Simple permanent tissue is made up of cells similar in structure and function','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion. A tissue is a group of cells having a common origin (homogenous) and usually performing a common function. A simple tissue is made of only one type of cells. Permanent tissues having all cells similar in structure and function are called simple tissues.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4972,'biology',77,412,822,'Which of the following statement related to $\\mathrm{G}_{0}$ stage of the cell cycle are correct?<br>I. It is a quiescent stage.<br>II. In this phase, cell cycle is stopped.<br>III. $\\mathrm{G}_{0}$ cells do not grow or proliferate but metabolically active.<br>IV. $\\mathrm{G}_{0}$ cells can divide in response to some stimulus.','[{"text": "I, and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements regarding $\\mathrm{G}_{0}$ stage of the cell are correct. $\\mathrm{G}_{0}$ stage or resting phase is a period in the cell cycle in which cells exist in a quiescent state. ${{\\rm{G}}_0}$ phase is viewed as either an extended $\\mathrm{G}_{1}$ phase, where the cell is neither dividing nor preparing to divide, or a distinct quiescent stage that occurs outside of the cell cycle. Some (like cells, nerve and heart muscle cells), become quiescent when they reach maturity (i.e., when they are terminally differentiated) but continue to perform their main functions for the rest of the organism\'s life.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4975,'biology',77,412,822,'In the somatic cell cycle','[{"text": "In ${{\\\\rm{G}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}$ phase, DNA content is double the amount of DNA present in the original cell.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA replication takes place in S-phase.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A short interphase is followed by a long mitotic phase.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "G1 phase is followed by mitotic phase.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the somatic cell cycle, DNA replication takes place in $\\mathrm{S}$ phase. $\\mathrm{S}$ Phase is the synthesis phase during which replication of chromosomes occur.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4978,'biology',77,413,823,'In which of the following phase chromosomes cluster at poles and lose their identity ?','[{"text": "Prophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{G}_{2}$ phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Telophase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anaphase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Chromosomes that have reached pole cluster and lose identity due to decondensation in telophase',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5012,'biology',77,412,822,'Given below is a schematic break - up of the phases/stages of cell cycle. Which one of the following is the correct indication of the stage/ phase in the cell cycle?','[{"text": "C-M -phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "D - synthetic phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-cytokinesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B - metaphase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$C$  in the diagram has one hour duration indicates that it is \' $M$ \' phase/ Apparent division phase',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/77_5012_question_1.png'),
(4982,'biology',77,413,825,'In anaphase of mitosis,','[{"text": "Chromosomes get arranged in middle of cell.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nuclear envelope disappears.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosome fibres become clear.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosomes aggregate at opposite poles to form daughter nuclei.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Anaphase is the stage of mitosis or meiosis when chromosomes are split and the sister chromatids move to opposite poles of the cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4985,'biology',77,414,827,'Which of the following statement(s) is/are true?','[{"text": "Cell plate represents the middle lamella between the walls of two adjacent cells.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "At the time of cytokinesis, organelles like mitochondria and plastids get distributed between the daughter cells.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokinesis in plant cell is centrifugal and takes place by cell-plate formation while animal cells by furrowing/ cleavage and is centripetal.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4988,'biology',77,413,825,'Match the description given in column-I with their stapes given in column-II and identify the correct answer.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Initiation of the\nassembly of\nmitotic spindle<br>B. Proteins are\nsynthesized in\npreparation for\nmitosis while\ncell growth\ncontinues.<br>C. Spindle fibres\nattach to\nkinetochores of\nchromosomes.<br>D. Movement of\nchromatids\ntowards opposite\npoles</div><div class="column-right">P. Anaphase<br>Q. Prophase<br>R. Interphase<br>S. Metaphase</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{A - Q,B - R,C - S,D - P}}$<br>Anaphase-Movements of chromatids towards opposite poles.Prophase - Initiation of assembly of mitotic spindle.<br>Interphase - Proteins are synthesized in preparation for mitosis while cell growth continues.<br>Metaphase - Spindle fibres attach to the kinetochores of chromosomes.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4989,'biology',76,848,1891,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Sclerenchyma cells do not have plasmodesmata<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The cell walls of some permanent tissues are heavily lignified.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and but Reason is not correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4992,'biology',77,417,832,'Number of bivalents are 8 in prophase I. What is the number of chromosomes during anaphase II?','[{"text": "8", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "13", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "32", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Meiosis II maintains the haploid number of chromosomes obtained after meiosis I while changing 2n DNA content to $\\mathrm{n}$, DNA during anaphase II will remain same i.e., 8 .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4994,'biology',76,847,1889,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Higher plants have meristematic regions for indefinite growth<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Higher plants have root and shoot apices','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion. Growth in plants is largely restricted to specialised regions of active cell division called meristems, the meristems which occur at the tips of roots and shoots and produce primary tissues are called apical meristems.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4995,'biology',77,417,830,'Which one is correct about crossing over/ genetic recombination?<br>(i) It occurs in tetrad stage which occurs in pachytene of prophase I of meiosis I.<br>(ii) It occurs between non-sister chromatids of homologous chromosomes. (iii) It is recombinase enzyme mediated process.<br>(iv) It is also the reciprocal transfer of genes between the non- homologous chromosomes','[{"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All except (iv)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(ii), (iii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(iii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Crossing over leads to recombination between homologous chromosomes.<br>Recombination is the rearrangement of genetic information within and among DNA molecules.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4998,'biology',77,419,835,'If a cell has a chromosome number after first meiosis equal to 48 . The chromosome number in the daughter cells after the completion of meiosis will be','[{"text": "48", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "24", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "36", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'If a cell has a chromosome number after first meiosis equal to 48 . The chromosome number in the daughter cells after the completion of meiosis will be 48 .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(4999,'biology',76,848,1891,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Xylem fibres are found in both the primary and secondary xylem and may possess simple or bordered pits, highly thickened walls and obliterated central lumen<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Bast fibres occur in groups, as sheets or cylinders, as in flax','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and but Reason is not correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5002,'biology',77,414,827,'Arrange the following events that occur in mitosis in sequential order<br>I. Chromosome attachment to spindle fibres<br>II. Splitting of centromere<br>III. Formation of cell plate<br>IV. Movement of chromosome to poles<br>V. Formation of two daughter nuclei','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, V, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, I, V, IV, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Chromosomes attach to spindle fibres in metaphase. Centromere splits and chromosomes move to the poles in anaphase. This is followed by formation of daughter nuclei and cytoplasmic division',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5004,'biology',76,848,1891,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Xylem functions in the transport of dissolved organic substances<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Xylem is the tissue characterized by the presence of tracheids, vessels, and companion cells.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both Assertion and Reason are false.Xylem functions as a conducting tissue for water and minerals from roots to the stem and leaves.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5006,'biology',77,417,830,'Match the description (given in column I) with correct stage of prophase I (given column II) and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Chromosomes\nare attached to\nspindle and\nmoved equator<br>B. Centromere\nsplits and\nchromatids apart<br>C. Pairing between\nhomologous\nchromosomes\ntake place<br>D. Crossing\nbetween\nhomologous\nchromosomes</div><div class="column-right">P. Pachytene<br>Q. Zygotene<br>R. Anaphase<br>S. Metaphase</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\rm{A - S,B - R,C - Q,D - P}}$',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5008,'biology',76,848,1891,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In <i>Zea mays</i> root, xylem is exarch<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The protoxylem lies towards periphery and metaxylem towards the centre.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion. In roots, the protoxylem lies towards periphery and metaxylem lies towards the centre. Such arrangement of primary xylem is called exarch.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5009,'biology',77,412,822,'In a mitotic cell cycle if the initial DNA content in $\\mathrm{G}_{1}$ phase is $10 \\mathrm{pg}$ then the amount DNA in the resulting daughter cell is','[{"text": "20 pg", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "10 pg", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "30 pg", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "40 pg", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The DNA content remains the same in mitosis, so the amount of DNA in the resulting daughter cell is also $10 \\mathrm{pg}$, which is the same as in the G1 phase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5013,'biology',76,847,1889,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Both apical and intercalary meristems are called primary meristems<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> They appear early in course of plants and contribute to the formation of primary plant body.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion. Both apical meristems and intercalary meristems are primary meristems because they appear early in life of a plant and contribute to the formation of the primary plant body.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5015,'biology',75,715,1507,'Match the columns I and II, and choose the correct combination with respect to \\(\\mathrm{k}\\). Esau.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Anatomy of seed plants<br>B. Dr Esau&rsquo;s plant Anatomy<br>C. Elected to National Academy of Sciences<br>D. National Medal of Sciences</div><div class="column-right">P. 1954<br>Q. 1957<br>R. 1960<br>S. 1989</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-Q, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. \'Anatomy of speed plants\' R. 1960<br>B. Dr. Esau\'s Plant Anatomy, P. 1954<br>C. Elected to National, Q. 1957<br>D. National Medal of science, S. 1989 from George Bush',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
