(5018,'biology',76,848,1890,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Permanent tissue is composed of mature cells<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Meristematic tissue is a group of actively dividing cells.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and but Reason is not correct explanation of Assertion. Following divisions of cells in both primary and as well as secondary meristems, the newly formed cells become structurally and functionally specialised and lose the ability to divide. Such cells are termed permanent or mature cells and constitute the permanent tissues.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5019,'biology',77,418,834,'Identify the given figures (A, B & C) showing meiotic phases and select the correct option.','[{"text": "A-Metaphase B-Anaphase C-Telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Metaphase-IB-Anaphase-I C-Telophase-I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Metaphase-II B-Anaphase-II C-Telophase-II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Anaphase-I B-Metaphase-I C-Telophase-I", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The given figures (A, B and C) showing meiotic phases are respectively metaphase I, anaphase I and telophaseI.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/77_5019_question_1.png'),
