(5032,'biology',77,412,822,'Which one is correct about S-phase (synthetic phase)?<br>i. It occurs between $\\mathrm{G}_{1}$ and $\\mathrm{G}_{2}$<br>ii. It marks the period during which DNA replicates<br>iii. At the end of this phase DNA is doubled but the number of chromosomes remains unchanged<br>iv. As the DNA is doubled in this phase number of chromosomes is also doubled<br>v. Centrioles replicate in this phase<br>vi. Amount of DNA changes from $2 \\mathrm{C}$ to $4 \\mathrm{C}$<br>vii. It is pre${{\\rm{G}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ and post ${{\\rm{G}}_{\\rm{1}}}$ phase','[{"text": "i, ii,iii,v, vi, vii are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii, iv, v, vi, vii are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only iv is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During the S-phase, DNA replication occurs (ii), resulting in a doubling of the DNA content (vi) from $2 \\mathrm{C}$ to $4 \\mathrm{C}$. The number of chromosomes remains the same (iii), and centrioles replicate in the S-phase (v). S-phase occurs between $\\mathrm{G}_{1}$ and $\\mathrm{G}_{2}$ (i), making statement vii also correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5033,'biology',76,854,1898,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Xerophytic leaves may contain stomatal crypts or sunken stomata.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Spongy parenchyma is more in xerophytic leaves.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Assertion is true but Reason is false Stomata occur individually and are sunken below the surface due to they are being overtapped by accessory or subsidiary cells.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5035,'biology',75,715,1509,'Fill in the blanks:<br>i. The __ 1 roots of carrot,turnip and __ 2 roots of sweet potato and&nbsp; <em>Asparagus</em>, get swollen and stores food.<br>ii.&nbsp;<em>Rhizophora</em>&nbsp;growing in___ 3 areas in which many roots come out of the ground and grow vertically upwards.','[{"text": "1--tap, 2--adventitious, 3--swampy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1--adventitious, 2--tap,3--swampy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1--adventitious, 2--tap ,3--dry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1--tap,2--adventitious,3--marshy", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The tap roots of carrot, turnip and adventitious roots of sweet potato and <em>Asparagus</em>, get swollen and stores food.<br><em>Rhizophora</em> growing in swampy areas in which many roots come out of the ground and grow vertically upwards.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5036,'biology',77,417,830,'Synapsis occurs between','[{"text": "Spindle fibres and centromeres.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RNA and ribosomes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A male and female gamete.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two homologous chromosomes.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The process of pairing of homologous chromosomes is called synapsis. Synapsis occurs during zygotene stage of meiosis-I.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5038,'biology',76,853,1897,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cambium is a lateral meristem and cause growth in width<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In monocot stem, cambium is present.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Assertion is true but Reason is false. In monocot stem vascular bundle are closed, i.e., cambium is absent.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5039,'biology',77,414,827,'Cell plate grows from','[{"text": "Wall to centre", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centre to walls", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One wall to another", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Simultaneously", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In plant cells, wall formation starts from the centre of the cell and grows outward to meet the existing lateral walls (centrifugal).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5040,'biology',75,715,1509,'Identify the mismatched pair.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Prop roots - Banyan", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stilt roots - Originate from stem\'s nodal part", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pneumatophores - Help in storing food", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Edible roots - Carrots", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'option (3) contains the mismatched pair that can be corrected as In some plants such as Rhizophora (growing in swampy areas), many roots came out of the ground and grow vertically upwards. Such roots are called pneumatophores, which help to get oxygen for respiration, i.e. respiratory roots.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5042,'biology',77,414,827,'Choose the incorrect one w.r.t cytokinesis in plants','[{"text": "In plant cells, wall formation starts in the centre of the cell and grows outward to meet the existing lateral walls.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The formation of the new cellwall begins with the formation of a simple precursor called the cell plate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The cytokinesis in a plant cell is achieved by the appearance of a furrow in the plasma membrane called the cell cleavage.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The cell-plate represents the middle lamella between the walls of two adjacent cells.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In plant cells the spindle fibres present at the equator move outwards and increase in number forming a barrel shaped structure called phragmoplast to trap golgi vesicles to form a cell plate.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
