(5049,'biology',75,715,1508,'The cells of region of meristematic activity of root are','[{"text": "Large, thick walled and with dense protoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Small,thin walled and with little protoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Very small, thin walled and with dense protoplasm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Very large thick walled and with little protoplasm", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The cells of the region of meristematic are very small, thin-walled and with dense protoplasm. They divide repeatedly.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5050,'biology',77,417,830,'Which of the following statement is not true for homologous chromosome pairs?','[{"text": "They come from only one of the individual\'s parents.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They usually contain slightly different versions of the same genetic information.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They segregate from each other during meiosis I.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They synapse during meiosis I.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A homologous chromosome is a set of one maternal chromosome and one paternal chromosome that pair up with each other inside a cell during meiosis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5052,'biology',76,851,1895,'Passage cells are thin walled cells found in<br>','[{"text": "Endodermis of roots facilitating rapid transport of water from cortex to pericycle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phloem elements that serve as entry points for substances for transport to other plant parts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testa of seeds to enable emergence of growing embryonic axis during seed germination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Central region of style through which the pollen tube grows towards the ovary", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In roots, endodermis is the innermost layer of cortex. Some of the endodermal cells present opposite to the xylem patches are thin walled and are called passage cells or transfusion cells. Passage cells help in transfer of water and dissolved salts from cortex directly into the xylem and ultimately to the pericycle.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5053,'biology',77,417,832,'The following events occur during the process of meiosis. Arrange the following events of meiosis in the correct sequence.<br>I. Terminalization<br>II. Crossing over<br>III. Synapsis<br>IV. Disjunction of genomes','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, II, I, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV, I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct sequence of the events in the meiosis is: III, II, I, IV.<br>III. Synapsis: Synapsis is the pairing of two homologous chromosomes that occurs during meiosis. It allows matching-up of homologous pairs prior to their segregation, and possible chromosomal crossover between them. It occurs in zygotene sage.<br>II. Crossing over: Crossing over is exchange of chromosomes segments between non-sister chromatids of homologous pair. Crossing over occurs during pachytene stage.<br>I. Terminalization: Terminalization of chiasmata occurs in diakinesis stage of meiosis<br>I. It is the disappearance of chiasmata of sliding towards the tips of the chromosomes due to tight condensation.<br>IV. Disjunction of genomes: The process of breakdown of homologous chromosomes is called disjunction. This process occurs in anaphase I.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5055,'biology',75,715,1509,'A type of modified ___A___ root that arises from the internode of stem, grows and becomes fleshy and tuberous, serving as storage for reserve food material is observed in ___B___<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{A}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{B}}$','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{Adventitious}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Sweet}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{potato}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Tap}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Sweet}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{potato}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Adventitious}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Ginger}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Tap}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Turmeric}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-adventitious root, B- Sweet potato',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5056,'biology',77,413,824,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Morphology of chromosome is easily understood in prophase.<br></div><div class="column-right">Chromosome is completely condensed in metaphase</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A and Statement-B are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is true but Statement-B is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is false but Statement-B is true.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A and Statement-B are false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Morphology of chromosome is best studied in metaphase due to maximum condensation',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5058,'biology',76,847,1889,'The length of different internodes in a culm of sugarcane is variable because of<br>','[{"text": "Shoot apical meristem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Position of axillary bud", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Size of leaf lamina at the node below each internode", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intercalary meristem", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Intercalary meristem is present away from the apical meristem and is situated at the base of the internodes which is responsible for the increase in length.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
