(5060,'biology',77,417,830,'Which one is correct about bivalent?<br>(i) Bivalent are tetrads.<br>(ii) A bivalent means 4 chromatids and 2 centromere.<br>(iii) One bivalent consists of 2 homologous chromosomes each and sister chromatids.<br>(iv) Bivalents formation occurs in zygotene.','[{"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only (iii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(iii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only (iv)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All the statements regarding bivalents are correct. A bivalent, sometimes referred to as a tetrad, is a pair of associated homologous chromosomes which are held together by a complex after chromosome replication. During meiosis the process of synapsis occurs in which bivalents are formed.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5063,'biology',77,412,822,'Read the following statements about cell division and select the correct statements.<br>I. $\\mathrm{M}$ phase represents the phase when actual cell division occurs and Interphase represents the phase between two successive ${\\rm{M}}$ phase.<br>II. In the 24 hours, average duration of cell cycle of a human cell, cell division proper lasts for only about an hour.<br>III. $\\mathrm{M}$ phase constitutes more than $95 \\%$ of the duration of cell cycle.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statements (i) and (ii) are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
