(5070,'biology',77,417,830,'The enzyme recombinase is required at which stage of Meiosis I?','[{"text": "Pachytene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Zygotene.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diplotene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diakinesis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During pachytene stage of meiosis-I, crossing over occurs.<br>Crossing over is the exchange of genetic material between two non-sister chromatids of homologous chromosomes & the enzyme involved in the process is called recombinase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
