(5076,'biology',77,417,830,'Given below are two statements:<br>Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Chromosomes become gradually visible under light microscope during leptotene stage.</div><div class="column-right">The beginning of diplotene stage is recognized by dissolution of synaptonemal complex.</div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are\\ntrue", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are\\nfalse", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is true but Statement B is\\nfalse", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is false but Statement B is\\ntrue", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During leptotene stage the chromosomes become gradually visible under the light microscope.<br>The beginning of diplotene is recognised by the dissolution of the synaptonemal complex and the tendency of the recombined homologous chromosomes of the bivalents to separate from each other except at the site of crossover.<br>Thus both statement A and B are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5077,'biology',76,850,1894,'In barley stem, vascular bundles are<br>','[{"text": "Open and scattered", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Closed and scattered", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Open and in ring", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Closed and radial", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The vascular bundles in Hordeum vulgare (barley) plant are scattered in ground tissues, many in number and vary in size smaller towards periphery and bigger towards center of the ground tissue, oval or rounded in outline, conjoint,collateral and closed.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5079,'biology',75,716,1511,'Read the following statements and fine out the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "Thorns are woody curved and pointed structures found in citrus and <i>Bougainvillea</i> for protecting them from browsing animals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tuber of potato is an underground stem having depressions called eyes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stem tendrils are found in gourd and grape-vines that are slender and spirally coiled and help plants to climb.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rhizome of ginger is fleshy horizontal underground stem possessing nodes and internodes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Thorns are woody straight and pointed structures found in citrus and Bougainvillea for protecting them from browsing animals',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5080,'biology',77,417,830,'Match Column I(Sub Phases of Prophase I) with Column II(Specific Characters) :<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Diakinesis<br>B. Pachytene<br>C. Zygotene<br>D. Leptotene<br></div><div class="column-right">P. Synaptonemal\ncomplex\nformation<br>Q. Completion of\nterminalisation\nof chiasmata<br>R. Chromosomes\nlook like thin\nthreads<br>S. Appearance of\nrecombination\nnodules</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  Q, C  -  R, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  Q, C  -  S, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  S, C  -  P, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{Q,}}\\,{\\rm{B}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S,}}\\,{\\rm{C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{P,}}\\,{\\rm{D}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{R}}$ is the correct option.<br>A. Diakinesis - Completion of terminalisation of chiasmata<br>B. Pachytene - Appearance of recombination nodules<br>C. Zygotene - Synaptonemal complex formation<br>D. Leptotene - Chromosomes look like thin threads',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5082,'biology',76,852,1896,'Anatomically fairly old dicotyledonous root is distinguished from the dicotyledonous stem<br>','[{"text": "Absence of secondary xylem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Absence of secondary phloem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of cortex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Position of protoxylem", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In dicotyledonous root, the condition of xylem is exarch as the protoxylem is away from the centre and metaxylem is towards the centre. In dicotyledonous stem (e.g.Cucurbita) the condition of xylem is endarch as the metaxylem is away from the centre and protoxylem is towards the centre.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5083,'biology',77,412,822,'Following are the stages of cell division :<br>A. Gap 2 phase<br>B. Cytokinesis<br>C. Synthesis phase<br>D. Karyokinesis<br>E. Gap 1 phase<br>Choose the correct sequence of stages from the options given below :','[{"text": "C - E - D - A - B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "E - B - D - A - C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B - D - E - A - C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "E - C - A - D - B", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct sequence of stages of cell division is Gap 1 phase $\\rightarrow$ Synthesis phase $\\rightarrow$ Gap 2 phase$\\rightarrow$ Karyokinesis $\\rightarrow$ Cytokinesis<br>The correct sequence will be<br>$\\rightarrow \\mathrm{E} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{A} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{D} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{B}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
