(5098,'biology',75,717,1514,'Fill in the blanks:<br>i. In a __1__ compound leaf a number of leaflets are present on a common__2__, the rachis, Which represents the midrib of the leaf as in__3__<br>ii. In __4__ compound leaves the leaflets are attached at common __5__ i.e, at the tip of petiole as in silk cotton','[{"text": "1-Pinnately, 2-point, 3-neem. 4-pinnately, 5-axis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-palmately, 2-point, 3-neem, 4-plamately, 5-axis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-plamately, 2-axis, 3-silk cotton, 4-pinnately, 5-point", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-Pinnately, 2-axis, 3-neem, 4-palmately, 5-point", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'i. In a pinnately compound leaf a number of leaflets are present on a common axis, the rachis, Which represents the midrib of which the midrib of the leaf as in neem.<br>ii. In palmately compound leave the leaflets are attached at common point, i.e, at the tip of petiole as in silk cotton.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5102,'biology',75,717,1513,'Which of the following statement is incorrect?','[{"text": "Arrangement of veins in leaf lamina is called phyllotaxy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In reticulate venation, veinlets form a network", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In parallel venation, veins run parallel to each other within a lamina", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leaves of dicotyledonous plants possess reticulate venation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The arrangement of veins and the veinlets in the lamina of leaf is termed as venation',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5105,'biology',75,717,1512,'Read the following statements and find out the correct statement.','[{"text": "The leaf is attached to the stem by the petiole while the leaf base help hold the blade to light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A typical leaf consist of three main parts: pulvinus, petiole and lamina", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A bud is present in the axil of petiole of compound leaf but not in the axil of the simple leaf.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The lamina (leaf blade) is the green expanded part of the leaf with veinlets.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A typical leaf consists of three main parts: leaf base, petiole and lamina. The leaf is attached to the stem by the leaf base and may bear two lateral small leaf like structures called stipules. A bud is present in the axil of leaf',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5107,'biology',76,850,1894,'Closed vascular bundles lack','[{"text": "Ground tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Conjunctive tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cambium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pith", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Closed vascular bundles lack cambium. In dicot stems, cambium is present between xylem and phloem and is helpful in formation of secondary growth. Whereas in monocots there is no cambium.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
