(5113,'biology',76,848,1891,'Companion cells are closely associated with<br>','[{"text": "Sieve elements", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vessel elements", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trichomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Guard cells", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Companion cells are characteristic elements of phloem tissue associated with the sieve tubes (sieve elements) in the angiosperms. The sieve tubes and companion cells are related ontogenically as they develop from the same mother cell.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5116,'biology',75,717,1516,'Read the following statements and find out the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "In Australian acacia, the leaves are used for storage of food", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Leaves are converted into spines for defence as in cacti", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leaves are converted into tendrils for climbing as in peas.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The fleshy leaves of onion and garlic store food.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In Australian acacia, the leaves are small and short-lived. The petiole in these plants expand, become green and sythesise food',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5119,'biology',75,717,1515,'Find out the correct matching:<br>A. Venation - Arrangement of veins and veinlets in the lamina of leaf<br>B. Phyllotaxy - Pattern of arrangement of leaves on stemor branch<br>C. Pinnately compound leaves - Leaf let attached to common axis rachis<br>D. Palmately compound leaves - Leaflet attached to a common point i.e. at the tip of petiole<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and C only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B,C and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5123,'biology',75,717,1515,'A vasculum has 1000 leaves. $15 \\%$ of these belong to China rose, $15 \\%$ to Mustard, $20 \\%$ to <i>Calotropis</i> 20\\% to Guava, and the remaining $30 \\%$ to Alstonia. If 6 leaves are present at each node of Alstonia, what is the total number of nodes seen in various twigs present in vasculum?','[{"text": "700", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1000", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "300", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "550", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$15 \\%$ of these belong to China rose , $15 \\%$ to Mustard $=300$ leaves, 300 nodes , $20 \\%$ to Calotropis $20 \\%$ to Guava= 400 leaves ${\\rm{(opposite\\, phyllotaxy)  = 200}}$ nodes, $30 \\%$ to Alstonia $=300$ leaves $=50$ nodes',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5124,'biology',76,848,1891,'Tracheids differ from other trachery elements in','[{"text": "Having casparian strips", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Being imperforate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lacking nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Being lignified<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Tracheids and vessels both are called tracheary elements because their main function is conduction of sap. They differ from each other in being imperforate. Tracheids are the specific cells which have pits to support upwards and lateral conduction of water sap.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5126,'biology',75,719,1523,'Read the following statements and find the suitable option.<br>I. Generally petals are green,leaf like and protect the flower in the bud stage.<br>II. Sepals are brightly coloured to attract insects for pollination.<br>III. In some flowers like lily, the calyx and corolla are not distinct and are termed as perianth<br>IV. Each ovary bears one or more ovules attached to a flattened, cushion like placenta.<br>V. A flower may be trimerous, tetramerous or pentamerous when the floral appendagesare in multiple of 3,4 or 5 , respectively','[{"text": "III, IV and V are true but I and II are false", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II and IV are true but III and II are false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, and V are true but I, II and III are false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, and IV are true but I, II and V are false", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Generally, sepals are green, leaf like and protect the flower in the bud stage. Petals are usually brightly coloured to attract insects for pollination.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
