(5198,'biology',75,722,1526,'Among the following how many features are seen in china-rose<br>i. Axile placentation<br>ii. Actinomorphic flowers<br>iii. Hypogynous flowers<br>iv. Stamens united into a bunch<br>v. Corolla with twisted aestivation<br>vi. Parietal placentation','[{"text": "iv, v, i, ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, i, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, v, iv, vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "except vi", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'China-rose shows all the features except Parietal placentation. It has axile placentation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5188,'biology',75,722,1526,'Read the following statements for floral formula of flower.<br>I. The position of the mother axis with regard to flower is represented by a dot on the top of floral diagram.<br>II. Outermost whorl represents the calyx<br>III. Floral formula shows cohesion and adhesion within parts of whorls.<br>Choose the option with correct statements.','[{"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5192,'biology',75,722,1526,'Features that can be shown in floral diagram but not floral formula<br>i. Aestivation<br>ii. Polarity of flower<br>iii. No.of thecae of anther<br>iv. Anthers as extrorse or introrse<br>v. Placentation<br>vi. Position of ovary','[{"text": "i, ii, iii, iv, v, vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iii, iv, v, vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Except vi", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Position of ovary is shown in the floral formula but not in floral diagram. Remaining five are shown only in the floral diagram but not in floral formula.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5202,'biology',75,717,1516,'The stem and the leaf are modified for the same purpose respectively in','[{"text": "<i>Acacia, Dionea</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cucurbita, <i>Pisum</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cactus, <i>Acacia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Acacia, Nepenthes</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The stem and leaf are modified in Curcurbita and pisum for support.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5207,'biology',76,850,1894,'When the vascular cambium is present between the xylem and phloem, then the vascular bundle is called,','[{"text": "Open", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Endarch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Closed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Exarch", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The cambium present between xylem and\nphloem in Vascular bundle is called open type,\npresent in Dicot stem',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5211,'biology',76,851,1895,'Given below are two statements :<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Endarch and exarch are the terms often used for describing the position of secondary xylem in the plant body.</div><div class="column-right">Exarch condition is the most common feature of the root system.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is true", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statement A is false and Statement B is true. Endarch and exarch are the terms often used for describing the position of primary xylem in the plant body. Primary xylem is of two types protoxylem and metaxylem. On the basis of relative position of protoxylem and metaxylem in the organ the arrangement of primary xylem can be endarch or exarch. Exarch type of primary xylem is seen in roots.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5215,'biology',76,852,1896,'Identify the plant parts whose transverse sections show a clear and prominent pith.','[{"text": "Dicot root and monocot root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicot stem and dicot root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicot stem and monocot stem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicot stem and monocot root", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The pith or medulla occupies central region of the stem and root, usually it is parenchymatous without chlorophyll. It contains starch forming leucoplasts. It is not distinct in moncot stem as vascular bundles are scattered throughout the ground tissue. In roots of monocots, pith is well-developed. In dicot roots, pith is scanty or lacking but in stem of dicots it is well-developed.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5221,'biology',76,851,1895,'Casparian strips are present in the____ of the root.','[{"text": "Epiblema", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cortex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pericycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endodermis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The Casparian strip is a ring-like thickening of certain parts of the endodermal cell walls in plant roots, which forces water and dissolved minerals to pass through the semipermeable plasma membrane of these cells, rather than their cell walls.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5225,'biology',76,851,1895,'Find out the wrong statement about angiosperm roots.','[{"text": "Cuticle is absent in young stages", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The apex is protected by root cap", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vascular bundles are collateral", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Xylem is centripetal in growth in the young roots", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Radial vascular bundles are characterstic feature of angiosperm roots. In this arrangement, xylem and pholem are arranged alternatively in different bundles on different radii. In collateral vascular bundles, the xylem and phloem lie on the same radius.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5231,'biology',76,854,1898,'The diagram given below represents the T.S. of dicot leaf. Identify the parts labelled as A, B, C and D, which denote their functions and choose the correct one given below.','[{"text": "A: Motor action B : Photosynthesis C: Conduction D: Transpiration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A: Motor action B: Conduction C: Photosynthesis D:Transpiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A: Transpiration B: PhotosynthesisC : Conduction D : Motor action", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A: Transpiration B: Conduction<br>$\\\\mathrm{C}$ : PhotosynthesisD : Motor action", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Buliform or motor cells labelled as A, on the upper epidermis of some monocot leaves, perform the motor action of rolling of leaves during dry conditions to reduce transpiration.- Undifferentiated mesophyll cells labelled as $\\mathrm{B}$, performs photosynthesis.- Vascular bundles labelled as C, perform conduction of water and nutrients.- Stomata labelled as D which are present on both surfaces performs transpiration and gaseous exchange.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2013,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/76_5231_question_1.png'),
(5232,'biology',75,724,1528,'Select from the following the total number of plant having epipetalous stamens.<br>Gram, Arhar, Moong, <i>Sesbania, Lupin</i>, Muliathi, Soyabean, Tomato, Brinjal, <i>Belladonna, Petunia</i>, Tobacco, Tulip, <i>Aloe, Colchicum, Asparagus</i>, Chilli, Ground nuts, Indigofera, Sunhemp','[{"text": "7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "10", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Tomato, brinjal, belladonna, Petunia, tobacco, chilli',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
