(5236,'biology',76,854,1898,'A student observes grass and Hibiscus plants in his garden during noon. To his surprise, only leaves of grass were found rolled inwards. The reason could be','[{"text": "Presence of more number on the grass leaves.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Undifferentiated mesophyll in grass leaves.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of Bulliform cells in the grass leaves.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Due to higher rate of transpiration.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In grasses, the transparent, colourless bulliform cells which are modified, curl inwards due to water stress.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
