(5452,'biology',75,717,1514,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A bud is present in the axil of petiole in both simple and compound leaves, and in the axil of leaflets of the compound leaf.<br></div><div class="column-right">In a palmately compound leaf a number of leaflets are present on a common axis, the rachis,</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A bud is present in the axil of petiole in both simple and compound leaves, but not in the axil of leaflets of the compound leaf.<br>In a pinnately compound leaf a number of leaflets are present on a common axis, the rachis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5455,'biology',8,153,323,'Each cell of sporogenous tissue in anther is','[{"text": "Microspore", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Potentital pollen or microspore mother\\ncell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Megaspore mother cell", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'As each cell of the sporogenous tissue is capable of giving rise to a microspore tetrad. Each one is a potential pollen or microspore mother cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5459,'biology',8,153,323,'In a flowering plant, archesporium gives rise to','[{"text": "Wall and the tapetum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only the wall of the sporangium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both wall and the sporogenous cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only tapetum and sporogenous cells", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In a flowering, archesporial cells consists of vertical rows of hypodermal cells located at four angles of anther. To form an outer primary parietal cell and inner sporogenous cell, they go through transverse division. Anther wall and sporogenous cells are formed after some periclinal divisions of primary parietal wall and forms sporogenous tissue.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5462,'biology',8,153,323,'Which one of the following produces both\nenzymes and nutrients?','[{"text": "Endothecium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tapetum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Epidermis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Middle layer", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Tapetum produces both hormones enzymes & nutrients.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5463,'biology',75,717,1515,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Phyllotaxy is the pattern of arrangement of leaflets on the rachis.<br></div><div class="column-right">In alternate type of phyllotaxy, doublate of leaf arises at each node in alternate manner, as in china rose, mustard and sun flower plants.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Phyllotaxy is the pattern of arrangement of leaves on the stem or branch.<br>In alternate type of phyllotaxy, a single leaf arises at each node in alternate manner, as in china rose, mustard and sun flower plants.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
