(5467,'biology',75,717,1515,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In opposite type, a pair of leaves arise at each internode and lie opposite to each other as in <i>Calotropis</i> and guava plants.<br></div><div class="column-right">If more than two leaves arise at a node and form a whorl, it is called whorled, as in <i>Alstonia</i>.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In opposite type, a pair of leaves arise at each node and lie opposite to each other as in Calotropis and guava plants.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5473,'biology',8,153,323,'Which of the following wall layers of anther\nplay a predominant role in its dehiscence','[{"text": "Tapetum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epidermis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Middle layers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endothecium", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The hypodermal layer of the anther wall present just beneath the epidermis is called as endothecium and remains in the mature anther. The endothecial cells over the junction of the two sporangia do not undergo secondary thickening. And such fibrous bands are important for supplying the mechanical force for anther dehiscence.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
