(5476,'biology',8,153,323,'In young anther the tissue occupying the centre\nof each microsporangium is called','[{"text": "Megaspore mother cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporogenous tissue", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Parietal tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When the anther is young, a group of compactly arranged homogenous cells called the sporogenous tissue occupies the centre of each microsporangium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5478,'biology',75,717,1515,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">If more than two leaves arise at a node and form a whorl, it is called whorled, as in <i>Alstonia</i>.<br></div><div class="column-right">Spines of certain insectivorous plants such as pitcher plant, venus-fly trap are also modified leaves.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Leaves of certain insectivorous plants such as pitcher plant, venus-fly trap are also modified leaves.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5480,'biology',8,153,323,'The innermost layer of pollen chamber, which\nact as nutritive layer is called','[{"text": "Tapetum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Perisperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endothelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endothecium", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Tapetum is the inner most layer of the microsporangium. It is the nutritive layer which nourishes the developing pollen grains.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5483,'biology',8,153,323,'Which one of the following statement is\ncorrect?','[{"text": "Endothecium produces the\\nmicrospores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tapetum nourishes the developing pollen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hard outer layer of pollen is called intine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporogenous tissue is haploid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Tapetum nourishes cells of pollen sac.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5485,'biology',75,718,1517,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A flower is a modified shoot wherein the shoot axial meristem changes to floral meristem.<br></div><div class="column-right">Internodes do not elongate and the axis gets condensed, during flower formation.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A flower is a modified shoot wherein the shoot apical meristem changes to floral meristem.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5486,'biology',8,153,323,'The function of innermost layer of pollen sac,\ntapetum is','[{"text": "Mechanical strength", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dehiscence", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protective", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nutritive", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Tapetum nourishes cells of pollen sac.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5489,'biology',75,718,1517,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">During flower formation, the apex produces different kinds of floral appendages laterally at successive nodes along with leaves<br></div><div class="column-right">When a shoot tip transforms into a flower, it is sometimes solitary.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The apex produces different kinds of floral appendages laterally at successive nodes instead of leaves.<br>When a shoot tip transforms into a flower, it is always solitary.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5490,'biology',8,153,323,'In the anther wall','[{"text": "Tapetum lies next to the epidermis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Middle layers lie between endothecium\\nand tapetum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tapetum lies just inner to the endothecium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Endothecium lies inner to the middle\\nlayers", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Periclinally the archesporial cells divide forming outer sub - epidermal parietal cells and inner sporogenous cells. Further the parietal cells separates next to periclinal walls producing a 3-5 layered microsporangial wall that consists of endothecium, middle layers and tapetum. Thus, the microsporangial wall consists of four kind of epidermal layer, endothecium, 1-3 middle layers and tapetum.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5493,'biology',8,153,323,'The outermost and innermost wall layers of microsporangium in an anther are respectively:','[{"text": "Epidermis and tapetum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Epidermis and endodermis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epidermis and middle layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endothecium and tapetum", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In an anther, the microsporangium is encircled by four wall layers, they are- the outermost protective epidermal layer, middle fibrous endothecial layers and the innermost\nnutritive tapetum layer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5495,'biology',75,718,1517,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In racemose type of inflorescences the main axis continues to grow, the flowers are borne laterally in basipetal order.<br></div><div class="column-right">In cymose type of inflorescence the main axis terminates in a flower, the flowers are borne in a acropetal succession.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In racemose type of inflorescences the main axis continues togrow, the flowers are borne laterally in an acropetalsuccession.<br>In cymose type of inflorescence the main axis terminates in a flower, the flowers are borne in a basipetal order.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5497,'biology',8,153,323,'In anther culture, the androgenic haploid plants are obtained from','[{"text": "Anther wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anther tapetum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Connective tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Young pollen grain", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Androgenic haploid plants are the haploid plants produced through anther or pollen culture. The male gametophyte produces the haploid plants in this case. Haploid plants are grown from immature pollen grain or microspores (male gametophytic cells).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5499,'biology',75,719,1518,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A typical flower has five different kinds of whorls arranged successively on the swollen end of the stalk or pedicel, these are calyx, corolla, androecium, gynoecium and perianth.<br></div><div class="column-right">Calyx, corolla and perianth are accessory organs, while androecium and gynoecium are reproductive organs.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A typical flower has four different kinds of whorls arranged successively on the swollen end of the stalk or pedicel, these are calyx, corolla, androecium and gynoecium.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5501,'biology',8,153,323,'Microsporogenesis is','[{"text": "Formation of microspores", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Formation of female gametes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Formation of tapetum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The process of formation of microspores from a pollen mother cell through meiosis is called microsporogenesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5504,'biology',8,153,323,'Another name for Pollen sac is','[{"text": "Embryo sac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anther", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microsporangium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Megasporangium", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The microsporangia develop further and become pollen sacs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5506,'biology',75,719,1518,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In some flowers like lily, the calyx and corolla are distinct and are termed as perianth.<br></div><div class="column-right">A flower having either only stamens or only carpels is unisexual.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In some flowers like lily, the calyx and corolla are not distinct and are termed as perianth.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5508,'biology',8,153,323,'The outer three layers of microsporangium perform the following functions?','[{"text": "Protection to developing pollen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Provides nourishment to developing\\npollen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Helps in the dehiscence of anther to\\nrelease pollen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The epidermis, endothecium, middle layers and the tapetum. The outer three wall layers perform the function of protection and help in dehiscence of anther to release the pollen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5510,'biology',75,719,1518,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">When a flower can be divided into two equal radial halves in any radial plane passing through the centre, it is said to be actinomorphic, e.g., mustard, datura, muliathi, chilli.<br></div><div class="column-right">When a flower can be divided into two similar halves only in one particular vertical plane, it is zygomorphic, e.g., pea, gulmohur, bean, <i>Cassia</i>.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Muliathi has zygomorphic flower.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5511,'biology',8,153,323,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The innermost wall layer is\nthe tapetum. It nourishes the\ndeveloping pollen grains.</div><div class="column-right">When the anther is young, a\ngroup of compactly arranged\nheterogenous cells called the\nsporogenous tissue occupies\nthe outer layer of each\nmicrosporangium</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When the anther is young, a group of compactly arranged homogenous cells called the sporogenous tissue occupies the centre of each microsporangium.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5514,'biology',75,719,1518,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Flowers with bracts-reduced petal found at the base of the pedicel- are called bracteate.<br></div><div class="column-right">A flower is asymmetric (irregular) if it cannot be divided into two similar halves by any vertical plane passing through the centre, as in cassia.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Flowers with bracts-reduced leaf found at the base of the pedicel- are called bracteates.<br>A flower is asymmetric (irregular) if it cannot be divided into two similar halves by any vertical plane passing through the centre, as in canna.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5515,'biology',8,153,323,'The outermost and innermost wall layers of microsporangium in an anther are respectively:','[{"text": "Endothecium and tapetum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epidermis and endodermis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epidermis and middle layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epidermis and tapetum", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The outermost and innermost wall layers of microsporangium in an anther are Epidermis and tapetum respectively.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5518,'biology',8,153,323,'Tapetal cells of stamens are','[{"text": "Diploid uninucleate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tetraploid binucleate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hexaploid tetranucleate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polyploid multinucleate", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cells of the tapetum possess dense cytoplasm and generally have more than one nucleus. The tapetum is a layer of nutritive cells found within the sporangium, particularly within the anther of flowering plants. The cells are usually bigger and normally have more than one nucleus per cell. As the sporogenous cells undergo mitosis, the nuclei of tapetal cells also divide. Sometimes, this mitosis is not normal due to which many cells of mature tapetum become multinucleate.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5552,'biology',8,153,324,'Pollen grains of different species show characteristic difference in ___','[{"text": "Shapes, size and colours only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shapes, sizes, colours and ploidy only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shapes, sizes, colour and design only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ploidy only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pollen grains of different species show characteristic difference in shapes, sizes, colour and design only.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5521,'biology',75,719,1518,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Mustard, china rose and brinjal are hypogynous.<br></div><div class="column-right">In the hypogynous flower the gynoecium occupies the lowest position while the other parts are situated below it.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In the hypogynous flower the gynoecium occupies the highest position while the other parts are situated below it.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5522,'biology',8,153,323,'Arrange the following wall layer of anther from inner side to the outside<br> i. Tapetum &emsp; ii. Endothecium<br> iii. Epidermis &emsp; iv. Middle layer','[{"text": "i, iv, ii, iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iii, ii, iv, i", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iv, i, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iv, iii, i", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The microsporangium is generally surrounded by four wall layers from outside to inside – the epidermis, endothecium, middle layers and the tapetum. Therefore the correct\norder is i, iv, ii, iii.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5525,'biology',75,719,1518,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">If gynoecium is situated in the centre and other parts of the flower are located on the rim of the thalamus almost at the same level, it is called perigynous.<br></div><div class="column-right">In epigynous flowers, the margin of thalamus grows upward enclosing the ovary partially and getting fused with it.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In epigynous flowers, the margin of thalamus grows upward enclosing the ovary completely and getting fused with it.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5526,'biology',8,153,324,'Pollen grains are produced inside the','[{"text": "Pistil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stamen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollen sacs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Filament", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In angiosperms, pollen grain is the male gametophyte. And microsporangium is the bilobed pollen sac structures. Inside which, microspore develop and mature into the pollen\ngrains are.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5529,'biology',8,153,324,'Male gametes in the angiosperms are formed by the division of','[{"text": "Microspore", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microspore mother cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Generative cell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vegetative cell", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The male gametes of angiosperms consist of two sperm cells within a pollen grain or a pollen tube. They are derived from a single generative cell, which is formed as the smaller cell by unequal cell division in the microspore after meiosis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5623,'biology',8,153,324,'Pollen grains are shed in 2 celled stage in','[{"text": "$ > 70\\\\% $ Angiosperm plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$ < 50\\\\% $Angiosperm plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$ > 60\\\\% $Angiosperm plant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$ < 40\\\\% $Angiosperm plant", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In over 60 per cent of angiosperms, pollen grains are shed at this 2-celled stage.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5532,'biology',75,719,1518,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The ovary isinferior in flowers of guava and cucumber.<br></div><div class="column-right">The ovary is superior in mustard, china rose and brinjal.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5533,'biology',8,153,324,'Number of meiotic divisions required to produce 200/400 seeds of pea would be','[{"text": "400/800", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "300/600", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "250/500", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "200/400", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Number of meiotic divisions required to produce 200/400 seeds of pea would be 250/500. 200 seeds of pea would be produced from 200 pollen grains and 200 eggs. 200 pollen grains will be formed by 50 microspore mother cell while 200 eggs will be formed by 200 megaspore mother cell so 250/500.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5536,'biology',75,719,1519,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Generally, sepals are green, leaf like and protect the flower in the bud stage.<br></div><div class="column-right">The calyx may be gamosepalous (petals united) or polysepalous (petals free).</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The calyx may be gamosepalous (sepals united) or polysepalous (sepals free).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5537,'biology',8,153,324,'Male gametophyte of angiosperm is','[{"text": "Microspore", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Microsporangium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucellus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stamen", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Microspore is haploid, uninucleate, minute spore produced in large numbers as a result of meiosis in microspore mother cells inside the microsporangia. These are the first cell of gametophytic generation in angiosperm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5540,'biology',8,153,324,'Pollen grains develop from','[{"text": "Sporogenous tissue", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Epidermis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endothecium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tapetum", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The microsporangia develops to form pollen sacs. When the anther is young, sporogenous tissue (a group of compactly arranged homogenous cells) captures the central position of each microsporangium. Cells of the sporogenous tissue further gives rise to microspore tetrad.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5634,'biology',8,153,324,'Pollen allergy is caused by pollens of','[{"text": "Rose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Clematis</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Parthenium</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sunflower", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pollen allergy occurs due to pollen of <em>Parthenium</em>, <em>Amaranthus </em>chenopodium etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5542,'biology',75,719,1519,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The shape and colour of corolla vary slightly in plants.<br></div><div class="column-right">Corolla may be tubular, bellshaped, funnel-shaped or wheel-shaped.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The shape and colour of corolla vary greatly in plants.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5545,'biology',8,153,324,'If there are 4 cells (PMC) in anthers, what will be the number of pollen grains?','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "16", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Microspores or pollen grains develop inside the anther, that is the fertile part of stamen or microsporophyll. The primary sporogenous cell produces microspore mother cells or pollen mother cells (MMC or PMC), inside the anther. On reduction division, every MMC produces 4 pollens or microspores. Accordingly, these four cells will produce 4 x 4 = 16 pollen grains.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5547,'biology',75,719,1520,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">When sepals orpetalsina whorl just touch one another at the margin, with overlapping, as in <i>Calotropis</i>, it is said to be valvate.<br></div><div class="column-right">In china rose, lady\'s finger and cotton, aestivation is called twisted.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When sepals or petals in a whorl just touch one another at the margin, without overlapping, as in Calotropis, it is said to be valvate.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5548,'biology',8,153,324,'Each cell of microspore tetrad is','[{"text": "Only diploid (2n)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only haploid (n)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Some haploid (n) and some diploid (2n)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sometimes (3n)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Microspore is haploid as it is formed by meiosis of pollen mother cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5553,'biology',75,719,1520,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">If the margins of sepals or petals overlap one another in any particular direction, the aestivation is called imbricate.<br></div><div class="column-right">In pea and bean flowers, there are five petals, the largest (wing) overlaps the two lateral petals (standard) which in turn overlap the two smallest anterior petals (keel).</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'If the margins of sepals or petals overlap one another but not in any particular direction as in Cassia and gulmohur, the aestivation is called imbricate.<br>In pea and bean flowers, there are five petals, the largest (standard) overlaps the two lateral petals (wings) which in turn overlap the two smallest anterior petals (keel).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
