(5655,'biology',75,721,1525,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The embryo is small and situated near a groove at one end of the endosperm.<br></div><div class="column-right">Monocotyledonous seed consists of one large and shield shaped cotyledon known as scutellum</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The embryo is small and situated in a groove at one end of the endosperm.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5657,'biology',8,153,324,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Pollen bank<br>B. Generative\ncell<br>C. Vegetative cell<br>D. Parthenium</div><div class="column-right">P. $\\left( { - {{196}^o}C} \\right)$<br>Q. Abudant food\nreserve<br>R. Spindle shaped\ncell<br>S. Carrot grass</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R, B – P, C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – R, C – P, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – P, B – R, C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A – Q, B – P, C – R, D – S", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A – P, B – R, C – Q, D – S',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5659,'biology',8,153,324,'Which of the following sequences is correct for microsporogenesis?','[{"text": "Micro S.M.C(2N)$\\\\xrightarrow{{Mitosis}}$Microspore<br>tetrad(N)$\\\\xrightarrow{{Meiosis}}$Microspore (N)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Micro S.M.C(2N)$\\\\xrightarrow{{Meiosis}}$<br>Microspora tetrad(N)$ \\\\to $Microspores(N)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Microspore tetrad (2N)$\\\\xrightarrow{{Mitosis}}$<br>Microspores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "MicroS.M.C (2N)$\\\\xrightarrow{{Mitosis}}$<br>Microsporate tetrad (N)$\\\\xrightarrow{{Mitosis}}$Microspores (2N)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Formation of microspores (N) from (2N) microspore mothercell through meiosis is called as microsporogenesis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5661,'biology',75,721,1525,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The plumule and radicle are enclosed in sheaths which are called coleorhiza and coleoptile respectively.</div><div class="column-right">In monocotyledonous seed, embryo consists of scutellum and short axis with plumule and radicle.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The plumule and radicle are enclosed in sheaths which are called coleoptile and coleorhiza respectively',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5664,'biology',8,153,324,'Number of meiotic divisions required to obtain 200 microspores','[{"text": "25", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "50", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "100", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "200", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'One microspore mother cell undergoes meiosis to give rise to 4 microspores, so to produce 200 microspores 50 meiotic divisions will be required.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5666,'biology',75,722,1526,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The floral formula is represented by some symbols.<br></div><div class="column-right">In the floral formula, Br stands for bracteate $\\mathrm{K}$ stands for corolla and $\\mathrm{C}$ for calyx.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In the floral formula, $\\mathrm{Br}$ stands for bracteate $\\mathrm{K}$ stands for calyx and $\\mathrm{C}$ for corolla.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5667,'biology',8,153,324,'Total number of meiotic division required for forming 100 zygotes/100 grains of wheat is','[{"text": "50", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "75", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "100", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "125", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'100 pollen grain and 100 female gametes are needed to produce 100 zygotes. From 100 microspores (from 25 meiotic divisions), 100 pollen grains are formed and from 100 megaspores (from 100 meiotic division) 100 gametes or eggs are produced. Therefore, number of meiotic division needed to form 100 zygotes/100 grains of wheat is 25 + 100 = 125.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5670,'biology',75,722,1526,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Fusion is indicated by line drawn above the symbols of the floral parts and adhesion by enclosing the figure within bracket.<br></div><div class="column-right">A floral diagram provides information about the colour of parts of a flower, their arrangement and the relation they have with one another.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Fusion is indicated by enclosing the figure within bracket and adhesion by a line drawn above the symbols of the floral parts.<br>Afloral diagram provides information about the number of parts of a flower, their arrangement and the relation they have with one another.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5671,'biology',8,153,324,'In an angiosperm, how many microspore mother cells are required to produce 100 pollen grains?','[{"text": "25", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "50", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "75", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "100", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Each MMC produces 4 pollen grains from 1 meiotic division. So to produce 100 pollen grains 25 meiotic divisions are required. $\\left( {25 \\times 4 = 100} \\right)$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5675,'biology',8,153,324,'Select the correct option from the following : <br>A. In some cereals such as rice and wheat, pollen grains lose viability within 30 hours of their release. <br>B. Some members of Rosaceae, Leguminoseae and Solanaceae, they maintain viability for months','[{"text": "Only A is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both A and B are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In some cereals such as rice and wheat, pollen grains lose viability within 30 minutes of their release, corrected statement A .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5677,'biology',75,722,1526,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The position of the mother axis with respect to the flower is represented by a dot below the floral diagram.<br></div><div class="column-right">Calyx, corolla, androecium and gynoecium are drawn in successive whorls, corolla being the outermost and the gynoecium being in the centre.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The position of the mother axis with respect to the flower is represented by a dot on the top of the floral diagram.<br>Calyx, corolla, androecium and gynoecium are drawn in successive whorls, calyx being the outermost and the gynoecium being in the centre.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5678,'biology',8,153,324,'Exine of pollen is<br> A. Hard outer layer of pollen grain<br> B. Most resistant organic matter known as layer which can withstand high temperature, strong acids and alkali.<br> C. Layer made up of sporopollenin.<br> D. Layer which cannot be degraded by any known enzyme.<br> Which one of the following is correct?','[{"text": "A and B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B, C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B, C, D", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A and C<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'All the statements are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5682,'biology',8,153,324,'Pollen grains<br> A. Represent male gametophytic phase of plant<br> B. Can cause severe allergies like asthma and bronchitis<br>C. Are rich in nutrient and are used as food\nsupplements<br> D. Contains two male gametes and vegetative cell<br>E. Are available in form of tablets and syrups in market of western countries','[{"text": "Only A is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only A, B and C are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All the information is true in all the statements.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5685,'biology',8,153,324,'Which of the following statements is false?<br> i. Pollen grains represents immatured male gametophyte<br> ii. In angisperms partially developed male gametophytes are pollinated<br> iii. Generative cell is siponogenous while vegetative cell is spermatogenous<br> iv. Formation and differentation of pollen grains is called microsporogenesis<br> v. Hay fever is a pollen allergy<br> vi. Pollen grains of some plants produce severe allergy and respiratory or bronchial diseases<br> vii. Pollen grains are poor in nutrients.','[{"text": "iii and vii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i and vii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "vi and vii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iv and v", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement III and VII is wrong. III Generative cell is spermatogenous (forms male gametes) while vegetative cell is siponogenous (forms tube nucleus). VII pollen grains are rich in nutrients.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5689,'biology',8,153,324,'Correct statements are :<br>I. In over 60 percent of angiosperms, generative cell divides inside pollen tube after pollination<br>II.&nbsp;<em>Parthenium</em>&nbsp;that came into India as a contaminant with imported rice has become ubiquitous in occurrence and causes pollen allergy<br>III. Pollen grains are rich in nutrients and so pollen consumption has been claimed to increase the performance of atheletes and race horses<br>IV. In some angiospermic families like Rosaceae Solanaceae and Leguminosae pollen lose viability within 30 minutes<br>V. Pollen banks and seed banks are good insitu conservation strategies','[{"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The statements can be corrected as<br>II. <em>Parthenium </em>that came into India as a contaminant with imported wheat has become ubiquitous in occurrence and causes pollen allergy<br>IV. Some members of Rosaceae, Leguminoseae and Solanaceae, they maintain viability for months.<br>V. Pollen banks and seed banks are good exsitu conservation strategies',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5694,'biology',8,153,324,'In flowering plants a mature gametophyte is derived from a pollen mother cell by','[{"text": "Two mitotic divisions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three mitotic divisions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A single meiotic division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One meiotic and two mitotic divisions", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In flowering plants a mature gametophyteis derived from a pollen mother cell by<br> One meiotic and two mitotic divisions. One microspore mother cell undergoes meiosis to give rise to 4 microspores. In the immature pollen grain, two mitosis occurs for formation of 2 male gametes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5696,'biology',8,153,324,'Generative cell was destroyed by laser but a normal pollen tube was still formed because','[{"text": "Vegetative cell is not damaged.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Contents of killed generative cell stimulate\\npollen growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Laser beam stimulates growth of pollen\\ntube", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The region of emergence of pollen tube is\\nnot harmed.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Generative cell was destroyed by laser but a normal pollen tube was still formed because vegetative cell is not damaged. Each microspore divides by mitotic division making\na smaller generative cell and a larger vegetative cell or tube cell. If generative cell is damaged then the normal pollen tube will be formed because pollen tube is formed by vegetative cell not by generative cell of microspore.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5709,'biology',75,724,1528,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In potato family gynoecium is bicarpellary and syncarpous.<br></div><div class="column-right">In potato family fruit is berry or capsule.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
