(5700,'biology',8,153,324,'The number of pollen grains, produced by each head inflorescence of family Asteraceae having 10 actinomorphic flowers (if each anther produces 20 pollen grains), are','[{"text": "500", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "300", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1000", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "800", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each flower has 5 Anthers and therefore there are 50 Anthers, each anther produces 20 pollen grains. So total pollen grain will be$10 \\times 5 \\times 20 = 1000$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5703,'biology',75,724,1528,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In <i>Belladonna</i> stamens are five which are epitepalous.<br></div><div class="column-right">In <i>Lupin</i> petals are five, which are united and show valvate aestivation.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In belladonnastamens are five which are epipetalous.<br>In lupine petals are five which are polypetalous and show vexillary aestivation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5704,'biology',8,153,324,'In angiosperms the following events occur during microgametogenesis <br>i. Mitotic division in microspore<br>ii. Meiotic division in microspore mother cell<br>iii. Formation of pollen grain<br>iv. Formation of microspores<br>v. Formation of mature male gametophyte<br>The correct sequence of events is','[{"text": "ii, i, iv, v, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii, ii, i, v, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iv, i, iii, v", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iv, v, ii, i, iii", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'ii, iv, i, iii, v, this is the correct sequence.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5707,'biology',8,153,324,'Which of the following statements is wrong?','[{"text": "Pollen grains remain viable for several\\nmonths because their outer covering is\\nmade of sporopollenin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "No enzyme can degrade sporopollenin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollen grains are well represented in fossil\\nstrata due to sporopollenin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollen wall has cavities containing\\nproteins", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When once they are shed, pollen grains have to land on the stigma before they lose viability if they have to bring about fertilisation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
