(5743,'biology',8,153,325,'The condition called ‘Syncarpous’ of the pistil is referred to as','[{"text": "Gynoecium containing single pistil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More than one pistil fused together", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "More than one pistil free from one another", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gynoecium containing many pistils", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When there are more than one, the pistils may be fused together (syncarpous) or may be free (apocarpous)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5746,'biology',75,719,1521,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Syngenesious condition is a characteristic feature of Compositae.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Stamens are united by their anthers only, filaments remaining free.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In Syngenesious condition only anthers are united in bundle but filaments remain free. Eg. Compositae family',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5747,'biology',8,153,325,'In a multicarpellary gynoecium, the pistils may be fused together in case of ___________ or may be free, in case of __________','[{"text": "Apocarpous, syncarpous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Syncarpous, apocarpous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Syncarpous, syncarpous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apocarpous, apocarpous", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When there are more than one, the pistils may be fused together (syncarpous) or may be free (apocarpous)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5751,'biology',75,719,1521,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> An incomplete flower can be perfect.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Perfect flowers (complete) are called neuter.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Complete flowers contain four flower parts: petals, sepals, stamen, and pistil. Incomplete flowers are missing one or more of these four parts. It is possible for a perfect flower to be incomplete. An incomplete flower can either be perfect, having the male as well as female sex organs or imperfect with either of the sexes missing. When both the essential organs are absent, the flower is spoken as neuter.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5752,'biology',8,153,325,'Plants have single ovule in ovary are','[{"text": "Wheat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Paddy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pine apple", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) & (2)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The number of ovules in an ovary may be one (wheat, paddy, mango)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5755,'biology',8,153,325,'More than one ovule is found in the ovary of','[{"text": "Wheat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mango", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Papaya", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rice", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The number of ovules in an ovary may be many (papaya, water melon,orchids).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5757,'biology',75,716,1511,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Corm is condensed form of rhizome growing more or less in vertical direction.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Sucker is an underground modification of stem.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Sucker is a subaerial stem modification',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5759,'biology',8,153,325,'Match the columns I and II w.r..t Ovary.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Syncarpous pistil <br>B.Apocarpous gynoecium<br>C. Single pistil</div><div class="column-right">P.&nbsp;<em>Michelia</em><br>Q.&nbsp;<em>Papaver</em><br>R. Monocarpellary</div></div>','[{"text": "A &ndash; R, B &ndash; P, C &ndash; Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A &ndash; Q, B &ndash; R, C &ndash; P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A &ndash; P, B &ndash; R, C &ndash; Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A &ndash; Q, B &ndash; P, C &ndash; R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A &ndash; Q, B &ndash; P, C &ndash; R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5762,'biology',75,720,1524,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The mesocarp of drupe is edible in mango.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Coconut is a fibrous drupe.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In mango edible fleshy part is mesocarp and the part where the seed is protected is called as endocarp.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5763,'biology',8,153,325,'Identify the type of ovary in diagram','[{"text": "Monocarpellary syncarpous of <em>Michelia</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monocarpellary apocarpous of <em>Papaver</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multicarpellary syncarpous of <em>Papaver</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multicarpellary apocarpous of <em>Michelia</em>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The diagram represents Multicarpellary apocarpous ovary of <em>Michelia</em>',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/8_5763_question_1.png'),
(5766,'biology',8,153,325,'From among the sets of terms given below, identify those that are associated with the gynoecium.','[{"text": "Stigma, ovule, embryo sac, placenta", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thalamus, pistil, style, ovule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovule, ovary, embryo sac, tapetum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovule, stamen, ovary, embryo sac", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Thalamus, tapetum and stamen are not associated with gynoecium.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5768,'biology',75,717,1516,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The leaf pitcher is a modification of lamina.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Leaf pitchers are found in Dischidia to catch the insects.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Leaf-pitcher is a device that is used to trap insects by the plants that grow in nitrogen deficient soil to fulfil their nitrogen requirements.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5770,'biology',8,153,325,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">When there are more than\none, the pistils may be fused\ntogether (syncarpous) or may\nbe free (apocarpous)</div><div class="column-right">Inside the ovary is the ovarian\ncavity (locule).</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5773,'biology',75,716,1511,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Ginger has a prostrate growing stem.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Shoot growth is not effected by gravity.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ginger is horizontal in position and generally branched and producing aerial leaves or shoots aboveground and adventitious roots on lower side in favourable season. Thus shoot growth is not effected by gravity.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5774,'biology',8,153,326,'The following structure represents<br>','[{"text": "Hemitropous ovule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Atropous ovule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anatropous ovule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Orthotropous ovule", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fig 2.7 from NCERT',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/8_5774_question_1.png'),
(5777,'biology',8,153,326,'Ovule of most angiosperms is','[{"text": "Orthotropus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anatropous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Campylotropus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphitropous", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Most angiosperms have inverted ovule where it is rotated by  $180^\\circ $.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5779,'biology',75,715,1509,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Vivipary is the phenomenon of producing young ones in advanced state of development.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It occurs in mangrove plants like Rhizophora and Sonneratia,Agave  and mammals.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Vivipary is the condition whereby the embryo (the young plant within the seed) grows first to break through the seed coat then out of the fruit wall while still attached to the parent plant. This condition is found in <i>Rhizophora</i> species.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5781,'biology',8,153,326,'Ovules are found attached at basal placentation in:','[{"text": "Liliaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Malvaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Asteraceae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cucurbitaceae", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The ovary where the placenta expands from its base and a single ovule appears attached to the base has a basal placentation. It is mostly seen in Asteraceae (marigold and\nsunflower)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5783,'biology',75,719,1518,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The first two whorls, calyx and corolla, are described as nonessential whorl.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> They serve secondary functions like protection of flower and attraction of insects for pollination.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Statement-A and Statement-B are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5785,'biology',8,153,326,'Basal part of pistil which is swollen is called','[{"text": "Stigma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Style", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovary", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The basal bulged part of the pistil is the ovary.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5788,'biology',8,153,326,'The slender elongated part of pistil is','[{"text": "Stigma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Style", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The style is the elongated slender part beneath the stigma.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5789,'biology',75,715,1509,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In turnip and beet, the root is known as napiform.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The root is broad at the base tapering smoothly from the base to tip.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The root is broad at the tip tapering smoothly from the tip to base.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5792,'biology',8,153,326,'With respect to following diagram identify?<br>i. Structure that serves as landing platform pollen<br>ii. Contains ovules<br>iii. Serves as a channel for growth of pollen tube<br>','[{"text": "i - C, ii - B, iii - A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i - A, ii - C, iii - B", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i - A, ii - B, iii - C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i - C, ii - A, iii - B", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'i - A, ii - C, iii - B',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/8_5792_question_1.png'),
(5794,'biology',75,722,1526,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\underline{G}$ is the symbol for inferior ovary<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Adhesion is indicated by enclosing the figure within the bracket','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\underline{G}$ is the symbol for Superior ovary. Fusion is indicated by enclosing the figure within bracket and adhesion by a line drawn above the symbols of the floral parts',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5796,'biology',8,153,326,'The tips on the ovule where integument are absent are called','[{"text": "Micropyle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Germ pore", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Integuments", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Integuments encircle the nucellus except at the tip where a small opening called the micropyle is organised.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5799,'biology',8,153,326,'What is the direction of micropyle in anatropous ovule?','[{"text": "Left", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Right", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inverted", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Upward", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When the funicle lies parallel to the body of the ovule and micropyle, the body of the<br> ovule has rotated by  $180^\\circ $, the ovule is called anatropous.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5800,'biology',75,717,1513,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> A simple leaf has undivided lamina.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Leaves showing pinnate and palmate venation have various type of incisions.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A leaf is said to be simple, when its lamina is entire or when incised, the incisions do not touch the midrib. When the incisions of the lamina reach up to the midrib breaking it into a number of leaflets, the leaf is called compound.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5803,'biology',8,153,326,'The ovule of an angiosperm is technically equivalent to :','[{"text": "Megaspore mother cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Megaspore", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Megasporangium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Megasporophyll", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The ovule of an angiosperm is technically equivalent to: Megasporangium',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5805,'biology',75,720,1524,'The fruit is chambered, developed from inferior ovary and has seeds with succulent testa in','[{"text": "Pomegranate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Orange", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Guava", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cucumber", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The fruit which is chambered, developed from the inferior ovary and has seed with succulent testa is Pomegranate <img src=\'/img/data/biology/75_5805_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5807,'biology',8,153,326,'The end opposite of the micropyle is called','[{"text": "Funicle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chalaza", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Integument", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hilum", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The end opposite of the micropyle is called Chalaza',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5810,'biology',8,153,326,'The mass of cell present inside the integuments of megasporangium having abundant food reserve is','[{"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucellus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sporogenous cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Enclosed within the integuments is a mass of cells called the nucellus. Cells of the nucellus have abundant reserve food materials.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5811,'biology',75,719,1523,'An example of axile placentation is<br>','[{"text": "Lemon", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Marigold", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Argemone</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Dianthus</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Axile placentation is found in multicarpellary syncarpous gynoecium. The fusion margin of carpels grown inward and meet in the centre of the ovary. Thus an axis forms in the centre of ovary, thus ovary becomes multichambered. The ovules are born at the central axis. Number of these chambers are equal to the number of carpel. Eg. Potato, China rose, Onion, Lemon, Orange, Tomato.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
