(5813,'biology',8,153,326,'Integumented megasporangium is','[{"text": "Ovule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pollen sac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollen grain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo sac", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Integumented megasporangium is Ovule',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5814,'biology',75,721,1525,'The scutellum observed in a grain of wheat or maize is comparable to which part of the seed in other monocotyledons<br>','[{"text": "Endosperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aleurone layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plumule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cotyledon", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In monocots, the seed consists of a single, large, shield-shaped cotyledon called scutellum. The scutellum is observed in a grain of wheat or maize is comparable to the cotyledons in other monocotyledons.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5816,'biology',8,153,326,'The point of attachment of funicle with chalazal end is called','[{"text": "Hilum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Placenta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Integument", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucellus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hilum is the junction at which funicle is attached to ovule.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5818,'biology',8,153,326,'The ovule is attached to the placenta of ovary wall by','[{"text": "Raphae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hilum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Micropyle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Funicle", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In flowering plants, the ovule can be found in the inner part of the flower called the gynoecium. One or more than one ovules are produced by the ovary of the gynoecium, and finally develops the fruit wall. The ovules are attached to the placenta inthe ovary through a stalked structure called a funicle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5821,'biology',8,153,326,'The embryo sac is located in an ovule inside the','[{"text": "Nucellus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Integuments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chalaza", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Micropyle", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Located in the nucellus is the embryo sac or female gametophyte.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5822,'biology',75,719,1523,'In unilocular ovary with a single ovule the placentation is','[{"text": "Basal", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Free Central", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Axile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Marginal<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In basal placentation, the placenta develops at the base of ovary and a single ovule is attached to it, as in sunflower, marigold.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5824,'biology',8,153,326,'Match the columns I and II w.r.t. ovule.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Funicle<br>B. Chalaza<br>C. Micropyle<br>D. Integuments</div><div class="column-right">P. Small opening\nof ovule<br>Q. Stalk of ovule<br>R. Basal part of\nthe ovule<br>S. Covering of\novule</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R, B – P, C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – R, C – P, D – S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A – P, B – R, C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – P, C – R, D – S", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A – Q, B – R, C – P, D – S',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5830,'biology',75,719,1518,'Flowers are Zygomorphic in :','[{"text": "Mustard", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gulmohur", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tomato", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Datura</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mustard - Actimomarphic, Gulmohur - Belongs to Caesalpinoideae with zygomorphic flower, Tomato - Actinomorphic, <i>Datura</i> -  Actinomorphic.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5831,'biology',8,153,326,'Starting from the innermost part, the correct sequence of parts in an ovule are,','[{"text": "Egg, nucellus , embryo sac, integument", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Egg, embryo sac, nucellus, integument", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Embryo sac, nucellus, integument, egg", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Egg, integument, embryo sac, nucellus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The sequence of parts in an ovule starting from the innermost part is egg, embryo sac, nucellus, integument. As can be seen in the figure showing structure of an ovule.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
