(5850,'biology',8,153,326,'In dicot plants, arrangement of nuclei in normal embryosac is','[{"text": "3+2+2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3+2+3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3+3+3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2+3+3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During the development the single nucleus of functional megaspore undergoes 3 mitotic divisions to form 8 nuclei. Among the 8 nuclei, 4 are present at Micropylar end\nand 4 are present at chalazal end. One nucleus from each comes to centre and forms 2 polar nuclei. 3 nuclei at Micropylar end forms egg apparatus and 3 nuclei at Micropylar end forms antipodals. Hence the arrangement is 3+2+3.<br>',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
