(5879,'biology',75,720,1524,'Flowers are unisexual in','[{"text": "Pea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cucumber", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "China rose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Onion<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cucumber is the member of the familycucurbitaceae. In the members of this family, the flowers are unisexual, with male and female flowers on different plants (dioecious) or on the same plant (monoecious).  <img src=\'/img/data/biology/75_5879_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5881,'biology',8,153,326,'Integuments of the ovule transforms into','[{"text": "Seed coat", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cotyledons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fruit wall", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The ovule develops into the seed. The integuments transform into the seed coat. Testa forms the outer integument and the tegmen becomes the inner integument. Both of these layers are hard, protective and quite rigid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
