(5925,'biology',8,153,326,'In a fertilised embryo sac, the haploid, diploid and triploid structures are:','[{"text": "Synergid, zygote and primary endosperm\\nnucleus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Synergid, antipodal and polar nuclei", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antipodal, synergid and primary\\nendosperm nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synergid, polar nuclei and zygote.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Synergid, zygote and primary endosperm nucleus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5913,'biology',8,153,326,'The functional megaspore undergoes :','[{"text": "3 meiotic divisions to form embryo sac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 meiotic divisions to form embryo sac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 mitotic divisions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2 mitotic divisions", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The functional megaspore undergoes 3 mitotic divisions to give rise 8 nucleate and 7-celled structure.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5914,'biology',75,719,1521,'The term \'polyadelphous\' is related to<br>','[{"text": "Gynoecium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Androecium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Corolla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calyx", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The term polyadelphous is related to androecium. In this condition, many stamens are present in more than 2 groups which are separated from each other.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5916,'biology',8,153,326,'Read the following statements.<br>I. Vegetative cell is bigger and contains abudant food reserve.<br>II. Generative cell is small and floats in the cytoplasm of the vegetative cell<br>III. In angiosperms, double fertilisation occurs<br>IV. Nucellus represents the junctions between ovule and funicle<br>Choose the option with correct set of statements','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The hilum represents the junction between ovule and funicle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5918,'biology',75,719,1523,'Free central placentation is found in','[{"text": "Dianthus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Argemone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brassica", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Citrus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Free central placentation is found in Dianthus',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5919,'biology',8,153,326,'Embryo sac is to ovule as _______ is to an anther.','[{"text": "Stamen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Filament", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollen grain", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Androecium", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Embryo sac is present in ovule, while pollen grains are present in anther.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5921,'biology',8,153,326,'Starting from the innermost part, the correct sequence of parts in an ovule are,','[{"text": "egg, nucellus, embryo sac, integument", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "egg, embryo sac, nucellus, integument", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "embryo sac, nucellus, integument, egg", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "egg, integument, embryo sac, nucellus.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Egg, embryo sac, nucellus, integument, this is the correct sequence from inside to outside.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5922,'biology',75,719,1521,'Proximal end of the filament of stamen is attached to the<br>','[{"text": "Connective", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Placenta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thalamus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anther", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A typical stamen consists of anther and filament. The proximal end of filament is attached to thalamus or petal of the flower whereas distal end bears anther.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5924,'biology',81,1049,2472,'If volume of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ liberated during respiration is more than the volume of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ used, the respiratory substrate will be','[{"text": "Carbohydrate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Organic acid", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Organic acids have more volume of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ liberated during respiration than the volume of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ used.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6209,'biology',81,1045,2468,'In Kreb\'s cycle, last $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ liberated gives','[{"text": "Succinate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxalosuccinate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\alpha$$-ketoglutarate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Succinyl Co A", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In Kreb\'s cycle, last $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ liberated gives Succinyl CoA.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5928,'biology',81,1049,2472,'More carbon dioxide is evolved than the volume of oxygen consumed when the respiratory substrate is','[{"text": "Fat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sucrose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Organic acid", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Organic acid evolves more carbon dioxide than volume of oxygen it consumes when broken down as respiratory substrate under aerobic conditions. Thus, its RQ is more than unity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5929,'biology',8,153,326,'From the statements given below choose the option that are true for a typical female gametophyte of a flowering plant:<br> i. It is 8-nucleate and 7-celled at maturity<br> ii. It is free-nuclear during the development<br> iii. It is situated inside the integument but outside the nucellus<br> iv. It has an egg apparatus situated at the chalazal end','[{"text": "i and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii and iv", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The statements can be corrected as<br> ii. It undergoes 3 nuclear divisions followed by cellwall deposition.<br>iv. It has an egg apparatus situated at the micropylar end.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5930,'biology',81,1049,2472,'If RQ is less than 1.0 in a respiratory metabolism, it would mean that','[{"text": "Carbohydrates are used as respiratory substrate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Organic acids are used as respiratory substrate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The oxidation of the respiratory substrate consumed more oxygen than the amount of $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ released", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The oxidation of the respiratory substrate consumed less oxygen than the amount of $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ released", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Respiratory quotient is the ratio of volume of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ evolved to the volume of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ consumed. Thus, is RQ is less than 1.0 in respiratory metabolism, means that respiratory substrates consume more oxygen than the amount of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ released.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5931,'biology',8,153,326,'In a flower, if the megaspore mother cell forms megaspores without undergoing meiosis and if one of the megaspores develops into an embryo sac, its nuclei would be:','[{"text": "Haploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diploid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A few haploid and a few diploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "With varying ploidy.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Since no meiosis takes place so no change in ploidy will take place.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5933,'biology',75,716,1511,'Stems modified into flat green organs performingthe functions of leaves are known as<br>','[{"text": "Scales", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cladodes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phyllodes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phylloclades", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Phylloclades are aerial modified stem, in which stem becomes thick, fleshy succulent, green and perform the function of photosynthesis. The leaves are reduced to spines in this.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5934,'biology',81,1049,2472,'On oxidation of ____ molecule maximum amount of energy is liberated.','[{"text": "Starch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fats", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vitamins", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Maximum amount of energy molecule is liberated on oxidation of fats.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5935,'biology',8,153,326,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Integuments encircle the\nnucellus except at the tip\nwhere a large opening called\nthe micropyle is present.</div><div class="column-right">Opposite the micropylar end,\nis the nucellus, representing\nthe basal part of the ovule.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Integuments encircle the nucellus except at the tip where a small opening called the micropyle. Opposite the micropylar end, is the chalaza, representing the basal part of the ovule.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6275,'biology',81,1044,2467,'Pyruvic dehydrogenase require the participation of','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NAD}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coenzyme A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Several coenzymes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of the above',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5937,'biology',8,153,326,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> 7-celled, 8 nucleate and\nmonosporic embryo sac is called\nPolygonum type of embryo sac.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It was discovered by Hofmeister\nfor the first time in Polygonum.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Embryo sac is the female gametophyte of angiosperms. It was observed by Hofmeister first time. Polygonum type of embryo sac is most simple, most primitive and normal, type of embryo sac. It is 7 celled, 8 -nucleate and monosporic embryo sac. It was discovered for the first time in Polygonum by Strasburger.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5938,'biology',81,1049,2472,'RQ for tripalmitin is','[{"text": "0.8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.7", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.9", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.5", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'RQ for tripalmitin is 0.7',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5940,'biology',75,719,1521,'How many plants among <i>Indigofera, Sesbania, Salvia, Allium, Aloe</i>, mustard, groundnut, radish, gram and turnip have stamens with different lengths in their flowers?<br>','[{"text": "Six", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Five", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only <i>Salvia</i>, mustard, radish and turnip have stamens of different length in their flowers. <img src=\'/img/data/biology/75_5940_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5941,'biology',8,153,326,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Megaspore mother cell undergoes meiosis to produce four haploid gametes of which all are functional.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Megaspore mother cell is 2n, meiosis gives diploid structure.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both Assertion and Reason are false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5942,'biology',81,1049,2472,'RQ for protein is','[{"text": "0.8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.9", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.5", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'RQ for protein is 0.9',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5944,'biology',75,719,1518,'Radial symmetry is found in the flowers of<br>','[{"text": "<i>Brassica</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Trifolium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pisum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Cassia</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The typical angiosperm flower is constructed of floral organs in sets of whorls. This usually results in flowers with radial (actinomorphic) or bilateral (zygomorphic) symmetry. Actinomorphic flowers have a radial symmetry where the flower can be divided equally on more than one plane.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5945,'biology',81,1049,2472,'RQ for carbohydrate is','[{"text": "0.8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.9", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'RQ for carbohydrate is 1',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5946,'biology',8,153,326,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Megaspore mother cell undergoes meiosis to produce four megaspores<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Megaspore mother cell and megaspore both are haploid','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Megaspore mother cell is diploid and megaspores are haploid.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5948,'biology',75,719,1520,'When the margins of sepals and petals overlaps one another without any particular direction, the condition is termed as<br>','[{"text": "Vexillary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Imbricate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Twisted", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Valvate", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When the margins of sepals and petals overlaps one another without any particular direction, the condition is termed as Imbricate e.g., <i>Cassia</i>, Gulmohar',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5949,'biology',81,1049,2472,'The respiratory quotient during cellular respiration would depend on the','[{"text": "Nature of enzymes involved", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nature of the substrate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amount of carbon dioxide released", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amount of oxygen utilised", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The respiratory quotient during cellular respiration would depend on the nature of the substrate',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5950,'biology',8,153,326,'In angiosperm functional megaspore develops into','[{"text": "Embryo sac", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ovule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endosperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollen sac", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In angiosperm functional megaspore develops into embryo sac.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5952,'biology',8,153,326,'Megasporangium is equivalent to','[{"text": "Ovule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fruit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucellus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo sac", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Megasporangium is equivalent to ovule.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5953,'biology',81,1049,2472,'Respiratory substrates are the organic substances which are respiration to liberate energy during','[{"text": "Oxidized", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Reduced", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synthesized", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Respiratory substrates are the organic substances which are oxidised during respiration to liberate energy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5955,'biology',75,720,1524,'Coconut fruit is a :','[{"text": "Berry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nut", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Capsule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Drupe<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A drupe is a fruit in which an outer fleshy part surrounds a pit of hardened endocarp with a seed inside. Example: Coconut, Mango',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5956,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Acetyl CoA is a precursor of synthesis','[{"text": "Protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fatty acids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Organic acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbohydrates", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Acetyl Co-A is a precursor of fatty acids synthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5957,'biology',8,153,326,'Filiform apparatus is characteristic feature of','[{"text": "Generative cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucellar embryo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aleurone layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synergids", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Filiform apparatus is characteristic feature of Synergids.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5959,'biology',75,715,1508,'Root hairs develop from the region of :','[{"text": "Elongation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Root cap", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meristematic activity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maturation", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Region of maturation is the region from where fine delicate thread-like structures called Root hairs, develop.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5960,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Identify the correct statement<br>I. Fatty acids would be broken down to acetyl CoA before entering the respiratory pathway when it is used as a substrate.<br>II. When the organism needs to synthesise fatty acids, acetyl CoA would be withdrawn from the respiratory pathway for it.','[{"text": "I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5961,'biology',8,153,326,'Ovule of an angiosperm is technically equivalent to','[{"text": "Megaspore", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Megasporophyll", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Megaspore mother cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Megasporangium", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ovule of an angiosperm is equivalent to megasporangium.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5975,'biology',8,153,326,'A typical angiosperm embryo sac at maturity is:','[{"text": "8-nucleate and 7-celled", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "7-nucleate and 8-celled", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "7-nucleate and 7-celled", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8-nucleate and 8-celled", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A typical angiosperm embryosac at maturity contains: 8 nucleate and 7 celled.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5963,'biology',8,153,326,'In majority of angiosperms','[{"text": "Egg has filiform apparatus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There are numerous antipodal cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reduction division occurs in the megaspore mother cell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A small central cell is present in the\\nembryo sac.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In majority of angiosperms reduction division occurs in the megaspore mother cell.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5964,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Respiratory pathway is best defined as','[{"text": "Catabolic pathway", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anabolic pathway", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphibolic pathway", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Because the respiratory pathway is involved in both anabolism and catabolism, it would hence be better to consider the respiratory pathway as an amphibolic pathway rather than as a catabolic one.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5966,'biology',75,716,1511,'In <i>Bougainvillea</i> thorns are the modifications of :','[{"text": "Adventitious root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Leaf", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stipules<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Axillary buds of stems get modified into woody, straight and pointed thorns. Hence thorns are a kind of stem modification. They are found in <i>Citrus, Bougainvillea</i> .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5967,'biology',8,153,326,'Functional megaspore in an angiosperm develops into?','[{"text": "Endosperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo sac", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Embryo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovule", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Process of formation of megaspores from megaspore mother cell (MMC) is called Megasporogenesis. Megaspore mother cell undergoes meiosis to form 4 haploid megaspores.Out of four megaspores, 3 gets degenerated and one megaspore enlarges to become functional megaspore. Functional megaspore develops into female gametophyte or embryo sac in angiosperms.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5968,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Identify which of the following never can enter any phase of respiration','[{"text": "Protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbohydrates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fats", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of the above',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5970,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Amino acid enters in the respiratory pathway as / at','[{"text": "Kreb\'s cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pyruvate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acetyl CoA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of the above',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5971,'biology',8,153,326,'The body of the ovule is fused within the funicle','[{"text": "Micropyle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucellus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chalaza", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hilum", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Hilum',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5972,'biology',75,715,1509,'Plants which produce characteristic pneumatophores and show vivipary belong to :<br>','[{"text": "Halophytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Psammophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesophytes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pneumatophores are specialised root structures that grow out from the water surface and grow vertically upwards. They help to get oxygen for respiration and Vivipary is the condition whereby the embryo (the young plant within the seed) grows first to break through the seed coat then out of the fruit wall while still attached to the parent plant. Both these conditions are found in mangroves (Mangroves are Halophytes).<br>e.g., <i>Avicennia germinans, Rhizophora species, Laguncularia raecemosa</i>.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5974,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Fatty acid for entry into Kreb\'s cycle is degraded to','[{"text": "Pyruvate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Citric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acetyl-CoA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "PGA", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fatty acid for entry into Kreb\'s cycle is degraded to acetyl Co-A.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5977,'biology',75,715,1509,'Pneumatophores occur in<br>','[{"text": "Carnivorous plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Free-floating hydrophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Halophytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Submerged hydrophytes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pneumatophores also called breathing roots are a type of root modification present in halophytes especially mangrove plants Ex: <i>Avicennia, Rhizopora</i>. They are negatively geotropic and bear pneumatothodes (lenticels) through which exchange of gases takes place.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5978,'biology',8,154,327,'In seed plant __________ are the carriers of male gametes','[{"text": "Pollen tube", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Air", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In seed plant Pollen tube are the carriers of male gametes',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5979,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Glycerol enters the respiratory pathway at','[{"text": "G-6-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PGA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PGAL", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "PA", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Glycerol would enter the pathway after being converted to PGAL.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5981,'biology',75,715,1509,'Sweet potato is a modified<br>','[{"text": "Tap root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adventitious root", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rhizome", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sweet potato is a modified adventitious root for storage of food. Tap root is a type of primary root which arises directly from radicle and it is further divided into secondary and tertiary roots. Rhizome is a modified underground stem modification present in turmeric, ginger.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5982,'biology',8,154,327,'Pollination occurs in','[{"text": "Pteridophytes and angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bryophytes and angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angiosperms and fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angiosperms and gymnosperms", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pollen grains are found only in angiosperms and gymnosperms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5983,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Usable energy available from respiration is approximately','[{"text": "$$55 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$100 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$45 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$50 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Usable energy available from respiration is approximately $$45 \\%$$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5985,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Before entering into the respiratory pathway fats breakdown into','[{"text": "Fatty acid and oxaloacetic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fatty acid and citric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fatty acid and pyruvic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fatty acid and glycerol", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Before entering into the respiratory pathway fats breakdown into Fatty acid and glycerol.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5986,'biology',8,154,327,'The term pollination signifies','[{"text": "Dehiscence of anther", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The transfer of pollen grains from anther to stigma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The transfer of pollen mother cell from anther to the stigma of the same flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Formation of pollinia", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Transfer of pollen grains (shed from the anther) to the stigma of a pistil is termed pollination.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5988,'biology',75,719,1523,'Placentation in which ovules develop on the inner wall of the ovary or in peripheral part, is<br>','[{"text": "Basal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Axile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parietal", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Free central", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In parietal placentation the ovules develop on the inner wall of ovary or in peripheral part.eg. Mustard, <i>Argemone</i> etc.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6598,'biology',8,157,334,'The early stages of embryo development is called as','[{"text": "Embryology", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seedology", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Palynology", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryogeny", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The early stages of embryo development (embryogeny) are similar in both monocotyledons and dicotyledons',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5989,'biology',81,1043,2466,'Which of the following is incorrect about fermentation?','[{"text": "It accounts for the partial breakdown of glucose.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It occurs in mitochondria.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The NADH to $$\\\\mathrm{NAD}^{+}$$formation reaction is vigorous.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Fermentation accounts for partial breakdown of glucose.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5990,'biology',8,154,327,'Self-pollination means','[{"text": "Transfer of pollen from anthers to stigma in the same flower", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Occurrence of male and female sex organs in the same flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Germination of pollen grains", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transfer of pollen from one flower to another on the different plants", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The transfer of pollen grains from the anther to the stigma of the same flower is called self pollination.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5992,'biology',75,720,1524,'Which one of the following statements regarding post-fertilization development in flowering plants is incorrect?','[{"text": "Ovary develops into fruit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote develops into embryo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Central cell develops into endosperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovules develop into embryo sac<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Following are the post-fertilisation changes.<br>• Ovule $\\rightarrow$ Seed<br>• Ovary $\\rightarrow$ Fruit<br>•  Zygote $\\rightarrow$ Embryo<br>• Central cell $\\rightarrow$ Endosperm',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5993,'biology',8,154,327,'Autogamy is','[{"text": "Transfer of pollen grains from anther to stigma of the same flower", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Transfer of pollen grains from anther to stigma of another flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollination between two flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maturation of anther and stigma at different times", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The transfer of pollen grains from the anther to the stigma of the same flower is called self pollination/ Autogamy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5994,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Match the columns I & II and choose the correct option.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Glycolysis <BR>B. Kreb’s cycle<BR>C. Electron transport system</div><div class="column-right">P. Inner mitochondrial membrane<BR>Q. Matrix of mitochondria<BR>R. Cytoplasm</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-R, B-Q, C-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5996,'biology',8,154,327,'Which characters should be possesed by autogamous flowers?','[{"text": "Synchrony in pollen release and stigma receptivity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The anthers and the stigma should lie close to each other", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The anthers and the stigma should lie on different flowers", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Autogamy in such flowers requires synchrony in pollen release and stigma receptivity and also, the anthers and the stigma should lie close to each other so that self pollination can occur.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5997,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Match the columns I & II and choose the correct option.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Net gain of ATP produced in fermentation<br>B. Total number of ATP molecules produced in glycolysis<br>C. Net gain of ATP produced in aerobic respiration<br>D. Number of ${\\rm{FAD}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ produced from one pyruvic acid in Kreb’s cycle</div><div class="column-right">P. 1<BR>Q. 38<BR>R. 4<BR>S. 2</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-S, B-R, C-Q, D-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(5998,'biology',75,719,1521,'Diadelphous stamens are found in:<br>','[{"text": "China rose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Citrus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pea", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "China rose and citrus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Diadelphous condition is found in Fabaceae family such as Pea.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6000,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Match the columns I & II and choose the correct option.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. During Kreb’s cycle, electron from NADH produced in<BR>B. Ubiquinone<BR>C. Role of oxygen<BR>D. Synthesis of ATP molecules</div><div class="column-right">P. Depends on the nature of the electron donor<BR>Q. Limited to the terminal stage of aerobic respiration<br>R. Mitochondrial matrix<br>S. Located in inner mitochondrial membrane</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-S, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-R, B-S, C-Q, D-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6001,'biology',8,154,327,'The flowers, which expose their mature anthers and stigma to the pollinating agents are called','[{"text": "Cleistogamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autogamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pseudogamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chasmogamous", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Chasmogamy, is a plant reproductive mechanism in which pollination occurs in chasmogamous flowers. Chasmogamous flowers have commonly showy with open petals encircling exposed reproductive parts. Chasmogamous stems from Greek for “open marriage”, named after the open arrangement of floral structures. Once chasmogamous flowers have reached maturity, they unfurl and their stamens and/or stigma are made available for pollination.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6004,'biology',8,154,327,'Which is correct about Oxalis?','[{"text": "It propagates as runner", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bears two types of flowers, chasmogamous and cleistogamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Produces assured seed-set even in the absence of pollinators", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct sentences about Oxalis are<br> (1) It propagates as runner<br> (2) Bears two types of flowers, chasmogamous and cleistogamous<br> (3) Produces assured seed-set even in the absence of pollinators. So option 4 is correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6005,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Match the columns I & II and choose the correct option.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Cytochrome c<BR>B. Complex IV<BR>C. Complex V<BR>D. Mobile electron carrier</div><div class="column-right">P. Ubiquinone<BR>Q. ATP synthase<BR>R. Small protein attached to the outer surface of the inner mitochondrial membrane<BR>S. Contains cytochromes a and a3 and 2 copper centres</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-S, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-S, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-R, B-S, C-Q, D-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6007,'biology',75,716,1511,'Identify the correct set of statements:<br><br>(a) The leaflets are modified into pointed hard thorns in Citrus and <i>Bougainvillea</i><br>(b) Axillary buds form slender and spirally coiled tendrils in cucumber and pumpkin<br>(c) Stem is flattened and fleshy in <i>Opuntia</i> and modified to perform the function of leaves<br>(d) <i>Rhizophora</i> shows vertically upward growing roots that help to get oxygen for respiration<br>(e) Subaerially growing stems in grasses and straw berry help in vegetative propagation<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "(a) and (d) Only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(b), (c), (d) and (e) Only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(a), (b), (d) and (e) Only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(b) and (c) Only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The pointed, hard thorns in Citrus and Bougainvillea are modified axillary buds.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
