(6011,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Here label A represents','[{"text": "Outer membrane of chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Outer membrane of mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inner membrane of chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inner membrane of mitochondria.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In the given diagram A represents Inner membrane of mitochondria.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_6011_question_1.png'),
(6012,'biology',8,154,327,'One advantage of Cleistogamy is','[{"text": "Seed set is not dependent on pollinators", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Seed dispersal is more efficient and widespread", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Each visit of a pollinator results in transfer of hundreds of pollen grains", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It leads to greater genetic diversity", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cleistogamy is the process of pollination and fertilization before the flower has opened. In such flowers anther and stigma are close to each other. When anther dehisce in the flower buds, pollen grains come in contact with the stigma to effect pollination. Thus cleistogamous flowers produce assured seed set even in the absence of pollinators.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6013,'biology',75,719,1521,'Which one of the following plants shows vexillary aestivation and diadelphous stamens?<br>','[{"text": "<i>Pisum sativum</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Allium cepa</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Solanum nigrum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Colchicum autummale</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Vexillary aestivation and diadelphous stamen is seen in Fabaceae members example Pisum sativum (Garden pea).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
