(6049,'biology',8,154,327,'Choose the correct statement from the following:','[{"text": "Cleistogamous flowers always exhibit autogamy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chasmogamous flowers always exhibit geitonogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cleistogamous flowers exhibit both autogamy and geitonogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chasmogamous flowers never exhibit autogamy", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cleistogamous flowers do not open at all and thus entry of pollens from another flower is not possible. Hence, cleistomgamous flowers always exhibit autogamy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
