(6055,'biology',8,154,327,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Attraction of flowers prevents insects from damaging other parts of the plant.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Pollination carried out by insects is called Anemophily.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The attraction of flower in plants is not to diverge the insect from damaging other part, but to bring about pollination (i.e, transfer of pollen to the stigma). The pollen grains in insect pollinated flowers are either sticky or provided with spinous outgrowths. The stigma is also sticky. Insect pollination is entomophily.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
