(6105,'biology',8,154,328,'Wind pollinated flowers are','[{"text": "Small, producing large number of dry pollen grains", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Large producing abundant nectar and pollen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Small, producing nectar and dry pollen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Small, brightly coloured producing large number of pollen grains", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pollination occuring by wind is called Anemophily. Anemophilous plants are characterized by small flowers, pollens, present in large numbers which are small, dry and light in weight.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6106,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Ubiquinone transfer its electron to','[{"text": "Complex III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Complex II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytochrome c", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxygen", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ubiquinone transfer its electron to Complex III.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6108,'biology',8,154,328,'Characteristics of wind pollinated pollen is, they are','[{"text": "Non-sticky", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Large number in production", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Wind pollinated flowers produce more pollen grains (for example: a single flower of Cannabis produces 5,00,000 pollen grains). Pollen grains are light, dry, non-sticky and rough.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6109,'biology',75,717,1512,'Which of the following statements are correct about the leaf?<br>I. Leaf is a lateral, generally flattened structure borne on the stem.<br>II. It develops at the node and bears a bud in its axil.<br>III. Leaves originate from root apical meristems and arranged in an acropetal order.<br>IV. They are the most important vegetative organs for reproduction.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement I and II are correct about leaf.<br>The remaining statements can be corrected as follows<br>III. Leaves originates from the shoot apical meristems and arranged in an acropetal order.<br>IV. Leaves are the most important vegetative organs for photosynthesis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6110,'biology',81,1046,2469,'The cytochrome','[{"text": "Are reduced as they pass electrons on to next molecule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Located in the matrix", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Has ATP synthase to make ATP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Are oxidised as they pass electrons on to next molecule", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The cytochrome are reduced as they pass electrons on to next molecule.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6112,'biology',8,154,328,'Select the most appropriate statement w.r.t. to wind pollination','[{"text": "Pollen grains are light, non-sticky", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Well-exposed stamens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Large often-feathery stigma to easily trap air-borne pollen grains", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Wind pollination also requires that the pollen grains are light and non-sticky so that they can be transported in wind currents. They often possess well-exposed stamens so that the pollens are easily dispersed into wind currents, and large often-feathery stigma to easily trap air-borne pollen grains.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6113,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Chemicals taking part in respiratory electron transport are','[{"text": "Flavin nucleotides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "FeS and UQ", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytochromes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of the above',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6114,'biology',75,717,1516,'Phylloclade and phyllode resemble one another in','[{"text": "Origin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Succulent nature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of nodes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Function", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both phylloclades and phyllodes perform photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6116,'biology',8,154,328,'Pollination by water is not seen in','[{"text": "Water lily", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Nelumbium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Eichhornia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In a majority of aquatic plants such as water hyacinth ,nelumbium (lotus)and water lily, the flowers emerge above the level of water and are pollinated by insects or wind as in most of the land plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6117,'biology',81,1046,2469,'How many complexes occurs in ETC?','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'5 complexes occurs in ETC.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6119,'biology',8,154,328,'Pollination by water takes place in','[{"text": "<i>Vallisneria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Hydrilla</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Zostera</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pollination by water is quite rare in flowering plants. Vallisnaria and Hydrilla grows in fresh water and several marine grasses such as Zostera use water for pollination.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6121,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Ubiquinone is located','[{"text": "Within the inner membrane of chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Within the inner membrane of mitochondria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Within the outer membrane of mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ubiquinone is located within the inner membrane of mitochondria.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6123,'biology',8,154,328,'Examples of water pollinated flowers are','[{"text": "<i>Zostera</i>, Lotus, Water lily", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Lotus, Vallisneria, Hyacinth</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Vallisneria</i>, Lotus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Vallisneria, Hydrilla, Zostera</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Lotus and water lily are entomophilous potamogeton has anemophily',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6124,'biology',75,717,1516,'In <i>Nepenthes</i> the pitcher is modified','[{"text": "Whole leaf", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leaf apex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lamina", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Petiole", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The lamina is modified in to broad pinkish pitcher of 1 to 10 inches in length.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6125,'biology',81,1046,2469,'The use of ETC is to','[{"text": "Release and utilise energy stored in $$\\\\mathrm{NADH}+\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Use the intermediate from TCA cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release and utilise energy stored in $$\\\\mathrm{FADH}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The use of ETC(electron transport chain) is to Release and utilise energy stored in NADH $$+\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$and to Release and utilise energy stored in $$\\mathrm{FADH}_{2}$$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6372,'biology',81,1043,2466,'Lactic acid fermentation occurs in','[{"text": "Some bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Muscle cell under anaerobic condition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Yeast", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lactic acid Fermentation occurs in some bacteria and muscle cells of animals under anaerobic condition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6127,'biology',8,154,328,'In Tapegrass (<i>Vallisneria</i>) -','[{"text": "The female flower reach the surface of water by long stalk and male flowers pollen grains are released on to the surface", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Monoecism is found", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollen grains or flowers are actively carried by water current", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In Vallisneria, the female flower reach the surface of water by the long stalk and the male flowers or pollen grains are released on to the surface of water.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6128,'biology',81,1046,2469,'ETS takes place in','[{"text": "Cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Matrix of mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inner membrane of mitochondria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Outer membrane of mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The metabolic pathway through which the electron passes from one carrier to another, is called the electron transport system (ETS) and it is present in the inner mitochondrial membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6129,'biology',75,718,1517,'The most important function of inflorescence is to help in','[{"text": "Forming large number of fruits", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Attracting insects for cross pollination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dispersal of seeds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release of pollen grains", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The most important function of inflorescence is it makes flower more conspicuous to pollinating agents (insects/ birds) so that chances of cross pollination are high.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6131,'biology',8,154,328,'Which plant will have the following characteristics required for pollination?<br> Female flowers remain submerged in water<br> Pollen grains are released inside the water.','[{"text": "Lotus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seagrasses", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Hyacinth</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Vallisneria</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In Vallisneria, the female flower reach the surface of water by the long stalk and the male flowers or pollen grains are released on to the surface of water',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6132,'biology',81,1046,2469,'During which stage in the complete oxidation of glucose are the greatest number of ATP molecules formed from ADP?','[{"text": "Link reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ETS", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glycolysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kreb\'s cycle", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During ETS, greatest number of ATP molecules formed from ADP in the complete Oxidation of glucose.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6134,'biology',8,154,328,'Pollen grains in many seagrasses species are__________ and they are carried __________inside the water; some of them reach the stigma and achieve pollination.','[{"text": "Short, ribbon like; passively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Long, ribbon like; passively", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Long, ribbon like; actively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Short, ribbon like; actively", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pollen grains in many such species are long, ribbon like and they are carried passively inside the water; some of them reach the stigma and achieve pollination.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6135,'biology',75,719,1519,'The perianth is the term used when','[{"text": "Androecium and gynoecium are similar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Androecium and calyx are similar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corolla and gynoecium are similar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calyx and corolla are together", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Perianth is the collective name of the nonessential floral organs if there is no distinction between sepals and petals.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
