(6138,'biology',8,154,328,'In most of the water-pollinated species, pollen grains are protected from wetting _____________','[{"text": "By a sticky covering", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "By a gelatinous covering", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "By a mucilaginous covering", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "By a plastic covering", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In most of the water-pollinated species, pollen grains are protected from wetting by a mucilaginous covering.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6139,'biology',81,1045,2468,'In the given diagram label \' $$U$$ \' represents conversion of','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NADH}+\\\\mathrm{H}^{+} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{NAD}{ }^{+}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NAD}^{+} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{NADH}+\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{FADH}_{2} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{FAD}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{ADP} \\\\rightarrow$$ ATP", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'U in the given diagram represents the conversion of $$\\mathrm{NAD}^{+}$$to $$\\mathrm{NADH}$$ and $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_6139_question_1.jpg'),
(6140,'biology',75,719,1519,'X is the outermost whorl of the flower and contains "Y". Y is green, leaf like and protect the other whorls of the flower.Identify $\\mathrm{X}$ and $\\mathrm{Y}$.','[{"text": "X - Calyx; Y - Sepals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "X - Corolla; Y - Petals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X - Gynoecium; Y - Fruit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X - Androecium; Y - Ovary", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Calyx of the flower contains sepals which are green in colour and look like leaf and protect the other whorls of the flower. Corolla is present inside the calyx and made up of petals. Petals are different in color and shapes and protects the other whorls present inside it. It attracts insects for pollination due to its color. Androecium is present inside the corolla and made up of stamens. Each stamen contains filament, anther and a connective.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6142,'biology',8,154,328,'Which of the following is false?','[{"text": "Wind-pollination is quite common in grasses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrophily is limited to about 30 genera mostly monocots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The tassels of the corn are the stigma and style which wave in the wind to trap pollen grains.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6143,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Which of the following step represents conversion of $$\\mathrm{FAD}^{+} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{FADH}_{2}$$','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{P}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{S}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{T}$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$$\\mathrm{T}$$ in the given diagram represents the conversion of $$\\mathrm{FAD}^{+}$$ to $$\\mathrm{FADH}_{2}$$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_6143_question_1.jpg'),
(6144,'biology',8,154,328,'The most common type of pollination is','[{"text": "Entomophily", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ornithophily", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Malacophily (by snails)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chiropterophily (by bats)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In most of the water-pollinated species, pollen grains are protected from wetting by a mucilaginous covering.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6146,'biology',75,719,1523,'How many plants in the list given below have marginal placentation?<br><i>Mustard, Gram, Tulip, Asparagus, Arhar, Sunhemp, Chilli, Colchicine, Onion, Moong, Pea, Tobacco, Lupin</i>','[{"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Five", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Six", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Marginal placentation is a placentation with ovules borne on the wall along the ventral suture of a simple ovary. Gram, arhar, sunhemp, moong, pea \\& lupin belong to Fabaceae family that bears marginal placentation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6147,'biology',81,1045,2468,'How many compounds in the given citric acid cycle are 4- carbon compounds?','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'3 compounds (Succinic acid, malic acid and oxaloacetic acid) in the given citric acid cycle are 4-carbon compounds.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_6147_question_1.jpg'),
(6148,'biology',8,154,328,'In order to attract insects for pollination','[{"text": "Petals are brightly coloured", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Petals are protected by calyx", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epicalyx is essential", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Petals have large surface area", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In order to attract insects for pollination petals should be brightly coloured.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6150,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Match the columns I & II and choose the correct option.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Glycerol enter Kreb’s cycle at<BR>B. Fatty acids enter Kreb’s cycle at<BR>C. Amino acids enter Kreb’s cycle at</div><div class="column-right">P. Pyruvic acid<BR>Q. Phosphogly-ceraldehyde<BR>R. Acetyl Co-A</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Q, B-R, C-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6151,'biology',75,719,1523,'Match the following placentation types given in Column I (Placentation Types) with their examples given in Column II (Examples) and choose the correct combination from the options given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Basal<br>B. Free central<br>C. Parietal<br>D. Axile<br>E. Marginal</div><div class="column-right">P. Dianthus<br>Q. Pea<br>R. Lemon<br>S. Marigold<br>T. Argemone</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S, E-T", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-T, E-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-P, C-T, D-R, E-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-T, D-P, E-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-S, B-P, C-T, D-R, E-Q<br>A. Basal - S. Marigold<br>B. Free central - P. Dianthus<br>C. Parietal - T. Argemone<br>D. Axile - R. Lemon<br>E. Marginal - Q. Pea',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
