(6185,'biology',8,154,328,'A moth species_________ and the plant _______cannot complete their life cycles without each other.','[{"text": "<i>Pronuba yuccasella, Amorphophallus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pronuba yuccasella, Yucca</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Pronuba yuccasella, Vallisneria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pronuba yuccasella, Zostera</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A similar relationship exists between a species of moth (Pronuba) and the plant Yucca where both species – moth and the plant – cannot complete their life cycles without each other. The moth deposits its eggs in the locule of the ovary and the flower, in turn, gets pollinated by the moth. The larvae of the moth come out of the eggs as the seeds start developing.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6186,'biology',75,719,1523,'Which of the following statements is correct?','[{"text": "Imbricate aestivation is found in the papilionaceous family.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Generally, sepals are green, leaf like and protect the flowers in the bud stage.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In cymose type of inflorescence, the main axis terminates in a flower, hence is limitless in growth.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In axile placentation ovary is one chambered but it becomes two chambered due to the formation of false septum", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Vexillary aestivation is found in papilionaceous family. In cymose type of inflorescence, the main axis terminates in a flower, hence is limited in growth. In parietal placentation ovary is one chambered but it becomes two cambered due to formation of the false septum.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
