(6196,'biology',8,154,328,'How many of the following are correct,<br> i. Majority of insect pollinated flowers are large, colourful, fragrant and rich in nectar<br> ii. The flowers pollinated by flies and beetles secrete foul odours to attract these animals<br> iii. Among the animals, insects, particularly bees are the dominant biotic pollinating agents<br> iv. Plant <i>Yucca</i> and moth Pronuba can not complete their life cycle without each other<br> v. In majority of angiosperms, the pollen grains are likely to come in contact with stigma of the same flower<br> vi. Condition present in Papaya, prevents both autogamy and geitonogamy','[{"text": "6", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All the statements are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
