(6205,'biology',81,1045,2468,'How many $$\\mathrm{NADH}_{2}$$ are produced per glucose molecule in Kreb\'s cycle?','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$$6 \\mathrm{NADH}_{2}$$ are produced per glucose molecule in Kreb\'s cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6206,'biology',8,154,328,'Which one of the following statement is in corret about pollination?','[{"text": "Salvinia is entomophilous pollination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hydrophily is by water and occurs in Zostera, Vallisneria and Ceratophyllum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Salvia is entomophilous pollination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ornithophily is by birds", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Salvinia is a pteridophyta, no flower is present , so no insect pollination.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6210,'biology',8,154,328,'Refer to the given characteristics of some flowers:<br> I. Flowers are small. They are often packed in inflorescence, are colourless, nectarless and odourless.<br> II. Well exposed stamens, Stigma-large, often feathery.<br> III. Pollen grains produced in large number, light and non-sticky.<br> IV. Flowers often have a single ovule in each ovary.<br>The above features are the characteristics of','[{"text": "Entomophily", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anemophily", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hydrophily", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chiropterophily", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Wind pollination requires that the pollen grains are light and non-sticky so that they can be transported in wind currents. They often possess well-exposed stamens (so that the pollens are easily dispersed into wind currents,and large often-feathery stigma to easily trap air-borne pollen grains. Wind pollinated flowers often have a single ovule in each ovary and numerous flowers packed into an inflorescence',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6212,'biology',81,1045,2468,'In Kreb\'s cycle, first $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is liberated during','[{"text": "Decarboxylation of acetyl Co-A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decarboxylation of oxalosuccinate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Decarboxylation of -ketoglutarate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxidation of pyruvic acid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In Kreb\'s cycle, first CO, is liberated during Decarboxylation of oxalosuccinate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6213,'biology',75,715,1509,'Based on the following figure find out the correct modification.','[{"text": "Modification of stem for storage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Modification of root for storage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Modification of root for respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Modification of stem for protection", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Modification of root for storage',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/75_6213_question_1.png'),
(6214,'biology',8,154,328,'Study the following and find correct statement(s).<br> I. Viola (common pansy), Oxalis, and Commelina produce two types of flowers – chasmogamous flowers and cleistogamous flowers<br> II. Water is a regular mode of transport for the male gametes among higher plant groups.<br> III. Distribution of bryophytes and pteridophytes are limited because of the need of water for transport of male gametes and fertilization','[{"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In higher plants pollination by various sources take place.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6216,'biology',81,1045,2468,'How many four-carbon compound are involved in Kreb\'s cycle?','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Oxalo acetic acid, succinyl CoA, malic acid, succinate and fumarate, total 5',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6217,'biology',75,719,1518,'The following diagram depicts the arrangement of floral leaves on thalamus in the flowers of','[{"text": "Mustard, China rose and brinjal", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Plum, rose and peach", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Guava, cucumber and the ray florets of sunflower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rose, China rose and sunflower", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The diagram given indicates hypogynous flower with superior ovary. Ex : Mustard, Chinarose, Brinjal.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/75_6217_question_1.png'),
(6219,'biology',8,154,328,'A particular species of plant produces light, non-sticky pollen in large numbers and its stigmas are long and feathery. These modifications facilitate pollination by:','[{"text": "Insects", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wind", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Animals", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Light and non-sticky pollens are ideal to be blown away by wind. Feathery stamens are able to sway with the wind which helps in release of pollens into air.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6220,'biology',81,1045,2468,'The first 5-C dicarboxylic acid in Kreb\'s cycle is','[{"text": "OAA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Succinic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\alpha$$-ketoglutaric acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Acetyl coenzyme A", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The first 5-C dicarboxylic acid in Kreb\'s cycle is alpha-ketoglutaric acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6371,'biology',75,719,1518,'Which of the following is an example of actinomorphic flower?','[{"text": "<i>Datura</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Cassia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pisum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Sesbania</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Datura</i> shows actinomorphic flower. In <i>Cassia, Pisum</i> and <i>Sesbania</i>, zygomorphic flowers are seen.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6222,'biology',8,154,328,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Six of the eight nuclei are surrounded by cell walls and organised into cells; the remaining two nuclei, called polar nuclei are situated below the egg apparatus in the large central cell</div><div class="column-right">The tallest flower of Amorphophallus (the flower itself is about 6 m in height)</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The tallest flower of Amorphophallus (the flower itself is about 6 feet in height)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6223,'biology',75,715,1508,'Region of meristematic activity is/has','[{"text": "Large, thick walled dead cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Distal end of root", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Proximal to elongation region", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epidermal cells with root hairs", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The part of the plant far away from root stem interface is called distal so root apex is distal and maturation region is proximal.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6224,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Which of the following is a \' $$4 \\mathrm{C}$$ \' compound?','[{"text": "Isocitric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Citric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\alpha$$-ketoglutaric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Succinyl CoA", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Succinyl CoA is a 4-C compound.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6226,'biology',8,154,328,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Some examples of water pollinated plants are&nbsp;<em>Vallisneria</em> and&nbsp;<em>Hydrilla</em> which grow in marine water and several fresh water species such as&nbsp;<em>Zostera</em>.</div><div class="column-right">The synergids have special cellular thickenings at the chalazal tip called filiform apparatus, which play an important role in guiding the pollen tubes into the synergid</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Some examples of water pollinated plants are Vallisneria and Hydrilla which grow in fresh water and several marine sea-grasses such as Zostera. The synergids have special cellular thickenings at the micropylar tip called filiform apparatus, which play an important role in guiding the pollen tubes into the synergid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6227,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Citric acid undergoes ____ and forms ____ ?','[{"text": "Isomerisation, isocitrate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Isomerisation, citrate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dehydration, isocitrate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxidation, isocitrate", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Citrate is isomerised to isocitrate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6228,'biology',75,719,1519,'Select the incorrect statement:','[{"text": "Flowers are morphological and embryological marvels and sites of sexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Several hormonal and structural changes take place prior to development of floral primordium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The distal end of the filament is attached to the thalamus or the petal of the flower.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Flowers are objects of aesthetic, ornamental, social, religious and cultural value", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The proximal end of the filament is attached to the thalamus or the petal of the flower.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6230,'biology',8,154,328,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Cleistogamous flowers produce assured seed-set even in the absence of pollinators.</div><div class="column-right">Wind-pollination is quite common in grasses</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6231,'biology',81,1045,2468,'TCA cycle is so called because','[{"text": "It is the short name of Krebs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Its common name for acetyl co enzyme A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Its common name for citric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Citric acid has 3 carboxylic acid", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'TCA(tricarboxylic acid cycle is so called because citric acid has 3 carboxylic acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6233,'biology',8,154,328,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Transfer of pollen grains from anther to the stigma of a different plant is Xenogamy.</div><div class="column-right">Although geitonogamy is functionally cross-pollination involving a pollinating agent, genetically it is similar to autogamy since the pollen grains come from the same plant.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6234,'biology',75,715,1509,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>I. From the region of elongation, some of the epidermal cells form root hairs.<br>II. Pneumatophores are seen in <i>Rhizophora</i>.<br>III. Adventitious roots are seen in the banyan tree.<br>IV. Maize and sugarcane have prop roots.','[{"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The zone of elongation region of a root increases length of the root. The external cells possess the power of Modifications of Stem absorption of water and minerals salts from the soil. The root hair zone represents the zone of differentiation or maturation because different types of primary tissues differentiate or mature in this region. Maize and sugarcane have stilt roots.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6235,'biology',81,1045,2468,'The enzyme required for the first reaction of TCA cycle is','[{"text": "Citrate synthetase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pyruvate dehydrogenase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isocitrate dehydrogenase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Succinyl thiokinase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The first reaction of TCA cycle is catalysed by the enzyme citrate synthase and a molecule of $$\\mathrm{CoA}$$ is released.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6237,'biology',8,154,328,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Pollination by water is more common amongst abiotic pollinations.</div><div class="column-right">Pollination by wind is quite rare in flowering plants and is limited to about 30 genera, mostly monocotyledons.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both are incorrect. Pollination by wind is more common amongst abiotic pollinations. Pollination by water is quite rare in flowering plants and is limited to about 30 genera, mostly monocotyledons.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6238,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Kreb\'s cycle starts with the formation of a ____ carbon compound by reaction between ____','[{"text": "Six, fumaric acid and pyruvic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Six, OAA and acetyl CoA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Five, OAA and acetyl CoA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Five, acetyl CoA and pyruvic acid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The TCA cycle starts with the condensation of acetyl group with oxaloacetic acid (OAA) and water to yield citric acid (6 carbon compound).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6239,'biology',75,716,1511,'Match the following stem modifications given in column I (Stem Modifications) with their examples given in column II (Found in) and select the correct combination from the options given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Underground stem<br>B. Stem tendril<br>C. Stem thorns<br>D. Flattened stem<br>E. Fleshy cylindrical stem</div><div class="column-right">P. <i>Euphorbia</i><br>Q. <i>Opuntia</i><br>R. Potato<br>S. Citrus<br>T. Cucumber</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-T, E-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-T, E-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-S, C-T, D-P, E-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-T, C-S, D-Q, E-P", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-R, B-T, C-S, D-Q, E-P<br>A. Underground stem - R. Potato<br>B. Stem tendril - T. Cucumber<br>C. Stem thorns - S. Citrus<br>D. Flattened stem - Q. Opuntia<br>E. Fleshy cylindrical stem - P. Euphorbia',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6276,'biology',75,720,1524,'In both Coconut and Mango<br>i. Mesocarp is fibrous<br>ii. Endocarp is hard and stony<br>iii. Fruit is developed from monocarpellary superior ovary<br>iv. Endosperm is edible','[{"text": "i, ii, iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iii", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The first three features are shown in both. Edible part in mango is mesocarp but not endosperm. Endosperm is edible in coconut.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6241,'biology',8,154,328,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In most of the water-pollinated species, pollen grains are protected from wetting by a suberised covering.</div><div class="column-right">Pollen grains in many hydrophilous species, are short, ribbon like and they are carried actively inside the water</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both are incorrect. In most of the water pollinated species, pollen grains are protected from wetting by a mucilaginous covering. Pollen grains in many species are long, ribbon like and they are carried passively inside the water.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6242,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Which formula for cellular respiration is correct?','[{"text": "1 glucose $$+6 \\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}=6 \\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}+6 \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}+38$$ ATP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 glucose $$+1 \\\\mathrm{O}_{2}=1 \\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}+1 \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}+38$$ ATP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 glucose $$+6 \\\\mathrm{O}_{2}=6 \\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}+6 \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}+38$$ ATP", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 glucose $$=6 \\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}+6 \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}+38$$ ATP", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'1 glucose $$+6 \\mathrm{O}_{2}=6 \\mathrm{CO}_{2}+6 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}+38$$ ATP',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6243,'biology',8,154,328,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Among the animals, insects, particularly bees are the dominant biotic pollinating agents.</div><div class="column-right">Continued self-pollination result in inbreeding depression.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6245,'biology',75,717,1515,'Study the following statements and select the correct option<br>I. Buds are present in the axil of leaflets of the compound leaf.<br>II. <i>Pulvinus</i> leaf-base is present in some fabaceae plants.<br>III. In <i>Alstonia</i>, the petioles expand, become green and synthesize food.<br>IV. Opposite phyllotaxy is seen in guava.','[{"text": "II and IV are correct but I and III are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and III are correct but II and IV are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV are correct but II and III are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III and IV are correct but I is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A bud is present in the axil of petiole in both simple and compound leaves, but not in the axil of leaflets of the compound leaf. In Australian Acacia, the petioles expand, become green and synthesize food.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6246,'biology',81,1045,2468,'In addition to glucose the cell needs ____ drive cellular respiration','[{"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbon dioxide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxygen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hydrogen", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In addition to glucose the cell needs oxygen to drive cellular respiration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6247,'biology',8,154,328,'Attractants and rewards are required for:','[{"text": "Entomophily", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hydrophily", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cleistogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anemophily", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pollination that occurs through agency of an insect is called Entomophily. Entomophilous flowers are usually brightly coloured and scented and often secrete nectar. Hence attractants and rewards are required for insects inorder to carry out pollination.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6249,'biology',81,1045,2468,'The organelle where cellular respiration takes place is','[{"text": "Chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cellular respiration takes place in mitochondria of each cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6250,'biology',75,717,1516,'In <i>Opuntia</i>, the function of phyotosynthesis is carried out by','[{"text": "Cladode", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phylloclade", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phyllode", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bulb", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Phylloclades are modification of stem. These are green fleshy leaf like structure having nodes and internodes. Stem performs the function of photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
