(6266,'biology',8,154,327,'Flowers which have single ovule in the ovary and are packed into inflorescence are usually pollinated by:','[{"text": "Bee", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wind", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pollination by wind is more common amongst abiotic pollinations. Wind pollination also requires that the pollen grains are light and non-sticky so that they can be transported in wind currents. Wind pollinated flowers often have a single ovule in each ovary and numerous flowers packed into an inflorescence. They often possess well-exposed stamens ( so that the pollens are easily dispersed into wind currents ) and large often-feathery stigma to easily trap air-borne pollen grains.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
