(6325,'biology',8,154,329,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In several species such as papaya, male and female flowers are present on different plants, that is each plant is either male or female (monoecy).</div><div class="column-right">The ability of the pistil to recognise the pollen followed by its acceptance or rejection is the result of a continuous dialogue between pollen grain and the pistil.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In several species such as papaya, male and female flowers are present on different plants, that is each plant is either male or female (dioecy).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6327,'biology',81,1044,2467,'Aerobic respiration uses','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{O}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Aerobic respiration uses oxygen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6328,'biology',8,154,329,'A dioecious flowering plant prevents both:','[{"text": "Autogamy and geitonogamy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Geitonogamy and xenogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cleistogamy and xenogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autogamy and xenogamy", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When the male and female flowers occur on separate plants the condition is called dioecious and it prevents both autogamy and geitonogamy.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6331,'biology',81,1043,2466,'Match the columns I & II and choose the correct option.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. End product of fermentation in yeast cells<BR>B. Net ATP produced in fermentation<BR>C. End product of fermentation in muscle cells during exercise<BR>D. Reducing agent in respiration process</div><div class="column-right">P. 2 molecules<BR>Q. ${\\rm{NADH  +  }}{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$<BR>R. Ethanol and ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<BR>S. Lactic acid and energy</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P,B-Q,C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6332,'biology',8,154,329,'A dicotyledonous plant bears flowers but never produces fruits and seeds. The most probable cause for the above situation is:','[{"text": "Plant is dioecious and bears only pistillate flowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plant is dioecious and bears both pistillate and staminate flowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plant is monoecious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plant is dioecious and bears only staminate flowers.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A pistillate flower can be pollinated from pollen grains from another flower, hence option ‘1’ is incorrect. A dioecious flower can show self or cross pollination and hence can be transformed into fruit. So, option ‘4’ is the correct answer.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6335,'biology',81,1043,2466,'How many glucose molecules are required for production of 38 ATP molecules in case of anaerobic respiration?','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "38", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "19", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'19 glucose molecules are required for production of 38 ATP molecules in case of anaerobic respiration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6336,'biology',8,155,330,'Self-incompatability _','[{"text": "Works the same-way in all plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Does not have potentital agricultural applications", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maintains variation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "On the same mechanism of transplant rejection seen in animal", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Another device to prevent inbreeding is self-incompatibility. This is a genetic mechanism and prevents self-pollen (from the same flower or other flowers of the same plant) from fertilising the ovules by inhibiting pollen germination or pollen tube growth in the pistil. Thus giving rise to variations.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6338,'biology',81,1043,2466,'Match the columns I & II and choose the correct option.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Aerobic respiration<BR>B. Alcoholic fermentation<BR>C. Lactic acid fermentation<BR>D. Common pathway for aerobic and anaerobic organisms</div><div class="column-right">P. Muscle cells during exercise<BR>Q. Glycolysis<BR>R. Yeast<BR>S. Kreb’s cycle</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-S, B-R, C-P, D-Q is correct',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6339,'biology',75,715,1508,'Choose the correct options in regions of root.','[{"text": "A- root cap; B- region of cell division; C - region of maturation; D - region of elongation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- root cap; B- region of cell division; C- region of elongation; D- region of maturation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A- region of maturation; B- region of elongation; C- root cap; D- region of cell division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- region of maturation; B- region of elongation; C - region of cell division;<br>D- root cap", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A- root cap; B- region of cell division; C-region of elongation; D - region of maturation',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/75_6339_question_1.png'),
(6340,'biology',8,155,330,'Self incompatibility means','[{"text": "Failure of pollen to fertilize the same flower of the same plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Failure of pollen to fertilize the flower of different plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2) are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Self-incompatibility is a widespread mechanism in flowering plants that prevents inbreeding and promotes outcrossing or it is failure of pollen to fertilize the same flower.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6342,'biology',81,1043,2466,'Yeast poisons themselves to death when alcohol concentration reaches to alcoholic fermentation.','[{"text": "$$7 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$10 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$13 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$20 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Yeasts poison themselves to death when the concentration of alcohol reaches about 13 percent.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6343,'biology',8,155,330,'Pollen pistil interaction is','[{"text": "Chemically mediated process", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dynamic process", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetically controlled process", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More than one option is correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The ability of the pistil to recognise the pollen followed by its acceptance or rejection is the result of a continuous dialogue between pollen grain and the pistil. This dialogue is mediated by chemical components of the pollen interacting with those of the pistil. Pollen-pistil interaction is a dynamic process involving pollen recognition followed by promotion or inhibition of the pollen',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6345,'biology',75,720,1524,'The given figure shows the parts of mango and coconut. Choose the option which shows the correct labelling of A, B, C and D marked in the figures.','[{"text": "Epicarp, Mesocarp, Seed, Endocarp", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Epicarp, Mesocarp, Ovule, Endocarp", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epicarp, Mesocarp, Ovary, Endocarp", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epicarp, Mesocarp, Embryo, Endocarp", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In mango and coconut, the fruit is known as drupe. Drupe develops from monocarpellary superior ovaries. In mango, the pericarp is differentiated into an outer thin epicarp, middle fleshy edible mesocarp and an inner stony hard endocarp. In coconut, the mesocarp is represented by the fibrous part.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/75_6345_question_1.png'),
(6346,'biology',81,1043,2466,'The number of net ATP produced when a molecule of glucose undergoes fermentation is','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "36", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "38", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During fermentation, the pyruvic acid is transformed to ethyl alcohol and a net of 2 ATP molecules are produced. This pyruvic acid comes from breakdown of glucose by glycolysis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
