(6381,'biology',75,720,1524,'Match Column I with Column II<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Rose<br>B. Pea<br>C. Cotton<br>D. Mango</div><div class="column-right">P. Twisted aestivation<br>Q. Perigynous flower<br>R. Drupe<br>S. Marginal placentation</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  S, C  -  P, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  Q, C  -  R, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  R, C  -  S, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Rose have half-inferior ovary, thus it is known as Perigynous flower.<br>In Pea, the placenta form a ridge along the ventral suture of the ovary and ovules are borne on this ridge forming two rows.<br>Therfore marginal placentation.<br>In Cotton, twisted aestivation is present.In Mango, fruit is drupe. $\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{S}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{D}-\\mathrm{R}$ is the correct option.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
