(6386,'biology',81,1043,2466,'Fermentation is a kind of','[{"text": "Biophysical process", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bio chemical process", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Excretory process", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fermentation is a kind of Biophysical and Biochemical process.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6387,'biology',75,719,1521,'Match Column I (Types of Stamen) with Column II (Example)<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Monoadelphous<br>B. Diadelphous<br>C. Polyadelphous<br>D. Epiphyllous</div><div class="column-right">P. <i>Citrus</i><br>Q. Pea<br>R. Lily<br>S. China-rose</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  S, B  -  Q, C  -  P, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  S, B  -  P, C  -  Q, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  P, B  -  Q, C  -  S, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  R, B  -  P, C  -  S, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In China rose monoadelphous androecium is present.<br>Diadelphous androecium is found in pea plant. Polyadelphous androecium is found in citrus. Epiphyllous androecium is found in lily.$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{S}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{D}-\\mathrm{R}$ is the correct option.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6388,'biology',8,155,330,'After penetrating stigmatic and stylar tissue, the pollen tube usually grows towards eggs because','[{"text": "Because no other path to follow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The filiform apparatus of synergids believed to attract the pollen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It grows under the control of egg nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Attracted by dissimilar electric charge", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In flowering plants, guidance of the pollen tube to the embryo sac is critical for successful fertilization. The target embryo sac may attract the pollen tube as the final step of guidance in the pistil. A single synergid cell was sufficient to an attraction signal, and two cells enhanced it. After fertilization, the embryo sac no longer attracts the pollen tube, despite the persistence of one synergid cell.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6390,'biology',81,1043,2466,'The metabolic fate of pyruvic acid formed after glycolysis is','[{"text": "Aerobic respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alcoholic fermentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lactic acid fermentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pyruvic acid is the key product of glycolysis. Its metabolic fate depends on the cellular need. There are three major ways in which different cells handle pyruvic acid produced by glycolysis. These are lactic acid fermentation, alcoholic fermentation and aerobic respiration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6391,'biology',8,155,330,'Synergid’s filiform apparatus','[{"text": "Guide the pollen tube", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Guide the style for development", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Present near the micropylar end", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Synergid’s filiform apparatus guide the pollen tube and are present near the micropylar end.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6393,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Number of carbon atoms in the molecule of product of given reaction is<br>$$2 \\times$$ Phosphoenolpyruvate','[{"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The number of carbon atoms in the molecule of product of given reaction is 3 .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_6393_question_1.png'),
(6394,'biology',8,155,331,'Artificial hybridization is achieved by','[{"text": "Emasculation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bagging", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Artificial hybridization is one major approaches of crop improvement programme. It is achieved by emasculation and bagging techniques.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
