(6396,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Following diagram represents final steps of glycolysis, which of the following label represents formation of energy currency<br>','[{"text": "P, Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "R, S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P, S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Q, R", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The following steps represents formation of energy currency (ATP):<br>a. 1, 3-bisphosphoglycerate to<br>3-phosphoglycerate<br>b. Phosphoenolpyruvate to Pyruvic acid',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_6396_question_1.png'),
(6397,'biology',8,155,331,'The necessity of bagging is','[{"text": "To avoid contamination of stigma with unwanted pollen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "To avoid self pollination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bagging is done for the emasculated flowers to prevent contamination of its stigma with undesired pollen grains.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6398,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Likely outcome of following reaction is<br>$$2 \\times$$ Triose bisphosphate<br>(1,3-biphosphoglyceric acid)','[{"text": "3-phosphoglyceric acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dihydroxy acetone phosphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The outcome of given reaction is 3-phosphoglycerate',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_6398_question_1.png'),
(6399,'biology',8,155,331,'While planning for an artificial hybridization programme involving dioecious plants, which of the following steps would not be relevant?','[{"text": "Bagging of female flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dusting of pollen on stigma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Emasculation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Collection of pollen", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Artificial hybridization is one of the major approaches of crop improvement programme. In such crossing experiments it is important to make sure that only the desired pollen grains are used for pollination and the stigma is protected from contamination. This is achieved by emasculation and bagging techniques. Emasculation is relevant in bisexual plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6400,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Byproduct formed due to following step is<br>$$2 \\times 2$$ - phosphoglycerate','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Methanol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2}$$ Gas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ Gas", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'By product of the given reaction is water $$\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)$$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_6400_question_1.png'),
(6401,'biology',8,155,331,'Emasculation is concerned with','[{"text": "Clonal selection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hybridization", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pure line selection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mass selection", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Emasculation is defined as removal of anthers from the flower before maturity to avoid self pollination and to favour cross pollination. Emasculation is an essential step in the process of hybridization. Done if female parent plant is having bisexual flowers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6402,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Which of the following steps consumes energy?','[{"text": "A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both A and B", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The following steps consumes energy:<br>a. Glucose to Glucose -6-phosphate<br>b. Fructose-6-phosphate to Fructose<br>-1, 6-bisphosphate',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_6402_question_1.png'),
(6403,'biology',8,155,331,'Emasculation is not required when flowers are _______','[{"text": "Bisexual", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intersexual", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unisexual", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Either 1 or 2", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Emasculation is not required if the flowers are unisexual.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6404,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Match the columns I & II and choose the correct option.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Key product of glycolysis<br>B. Glycolysis<br>C. End product of photosynthesis<br>D. Conversion of Phosphoglycerate to PEP</div><div class="column-right">P. 10 Step process<br>Q. Formation of water molecule<br>R. Pyruvic acid<br>S. Sucrose</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-P,C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6405,'biology',8,155,331,'What is emasculation?','[{"text": "Pollination between flowers of same plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollination between flowers of different plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Removal of stamens of plant to prevent self pollination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Artificial pollination", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Emasculation is removal of stamens of plant to prevent self pollination.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6406,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Match the columns I &amp; II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. In glycolysis, one molecule of glucose yields<br>B. Oxidative decarboxylation of pyruvic acid yields<br>C. Complete oxidation of pyruvate in aerobic respiration leaves</div><div class="column-right">P. Acetyl CO-A<br>Q. Three molecules of ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>R. Two molecules of pyruvate</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-R, B-P, C-Q',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6407,'biology',8,155,331,'Material used for bagging is','[{"text": "Gunny bag", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Woolen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Butter paper", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Emasculated flowers are covered with a bag of suitable size generally made up of butter paper to prevent contamination of its stigma with unwanted pollen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6408,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Match the columns I & II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Glucose → Glucose-6-phosphate<br>B. Fructose-6-phosphate → Fructose 1,6-bisphosphate<br>C. Glyceraldehyde -3-phosphate → 1,3 bisphospho glyceric acid<br>D. BPGA → 3-Phospho glyceric acid</div><div class="column-right">P. Phosphorylation<br>Q. Hexokinase<br>R. Formation of ATP<br>S. Formation of NADH + H+</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6409,'biology',8,155,331,'Emasculation is not necessary when the','[{"text": "Female parent produces bisexual flowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Female parent produces unisexual flowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "When there are no flowers produced", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (2) and (3)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Emasculation is removal of stamens of plant to prevent self pollination. It is not required in a plant that has female parent produces unisexual flowers and the plant that has no flowers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6410,'biology',81,1042,2465,'$$2 \\mathrm{NADH}\\left(\\mathrm{H}^{+}\\right)$$produced during glycolysis could possibly yield ATP in ETS','[{"text": "6", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Oxidative phosphorylation or ATP synthesis from NADH occurs only under aerobic condition and this results in the production of 6ATP molecules from $$2 \\mathrm{NADH}$$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6411,'biology',8,155,331,'Which of the following is false about emasculation?','[{"text": "During emasculation process, stigma is removed", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Emasculated flowers are bagged in order to prevent self-pollination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Emasuclation is the removal of stamens before maturation of selected bisexual flowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is one of the steps for artificial hybridization", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Emasculation is removal of stamens',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6412,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Match the columns I & II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Breakdown of glucose to pyruvic acid<br>B. Sucrose is converted into glucose and fructose by<br>C. Glycolysis occurs in</div><div class="column-right">P. Cytoplasm<br>Q. Glycolysis<br>R. Invertase enzyme</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Q, B-R, C-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6413,'biology',8,155,331,'Select the correct statement from the following<br> i. Emasculated flowers have to be bagged to prevent contamination of its stigma with unwanted pollen.<br> ii When the stigma becomes receptive, pollination is carried out using the desired pollen and the flower rebagged','[{"text": "Only i is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6414,'biology',81,1042,2465,'The end product of glycolysis','[{"text": "Pyruvic acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Acetyl coenzyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Citric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxaloacetic acid", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The end product of glycosidic is 2 molecules of Pyruvic acid',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6415,'biology',8,155,331,'Select the incorrect statement from the following<br> A. Emasculation is done after the anther dehisces.<br> B. Emasculation is done using a pair of forceps','[{"text": "Only A", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Emasculation is defined as removal of anthers from the flower before maturity',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6416,'biology',81,1042,2465,'What is true about the end products of glycolysis?','[{"text": "$$2 \\\\mathrm{ATP}+2 \\\\mathrm{NADH}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$2 \\\\mathrm{NADH}_{2}$$ only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$2 \\\\mathrm{ATP}+1 \\\\mathrm{NADH}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$1 \\\\mathrm{ATP}+1 \\\\mathrm{NADH}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The end product of glycosidic are 2 molecules of Pyruvic acid, 2ATP and ${\\rm{2NAD}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6417,'biology',8,155,331,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Pollen grains shed at two-celled condition, in such plants, the vegetative cell divides and forms the two male gametes during the growth of pollen tube in the stigma.</div><div class="column-right">Emasculated flowers have to be covered with a bag of suitable size, generally made up of butter paper</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pollen grains shed at two-celled condition, in such plants, the generative cell divides and forms the two male gametes during the growth of pollen tube in the stigma,',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6418,'biology',81,1042,2465,'How many times substrate level phosphorylation takes place in glycolysis','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The formation of ATP, by the transfer of phosphate from an organic compound to ADP, is called substrate level phosphorylation. In glycolysis, at two steps substrate level, phosphorylations occur and at each step two ATP are formed $$=4$$ ATP.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6419,'biology',8,156,332,'After entering one of the synergids, the pollen tube releases the two male gametes into the','[{"text": "Cytoplasm of the egg cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytoplasm of the synergid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cytoplasm of the antipodals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'After entering one of the synergids, the pollen tube releases the two male gametes into the cytoplasm of the synergid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6421,'biology',8,156,332,'Double fertilization is characteristic of','[{"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bryophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angiosperms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Double fertilization is a characteristic feature of angiosperms in which one male gamete fuses with egg (called syngamy) and other male gamete fuses with two two polar nuclei (called triple fusion) to form endosperm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6423,'biology',8,156,332,'Fusion of two dissimilar gametes is called','[{"text": "Fertilization", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Self-fertilization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Self-Pollination", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Plant fertilization is the union of male and female gametes (reproductive cells) to produce a zygote (fertilized egg) which is diploid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
