(6458,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Number of controlled steps required in glycolysis are:','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "10", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "9", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Number of controlled steps required in Glycolysis are 10.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6459,'biology',83,489,1003,'Cellular level of organisation is','[{"text": "Seen in sponges", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "When cells shows division of labour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seen in cnidaria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In sponges, the cells are arranged as loose cell aggregates, i.e., they exhibit cellular level of organisation. Some division of labour (activities) occurs among the cells. Cnidaria exhibits tissue level of organisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6460,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Growth is regarded as one of the most____ characteristics of a living being.','[{"text": "Fundamental and inconspicuous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fundamental and conspicuous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Superfluous and conspicuous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary and inconspicuous", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Growth is regarded as one of the most fundamental and conspicuous characteristics of a living being.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6461,'biology',8,156,332,'In angiosperms, triple fusion is required for the formation of','[{"text": "Seed coat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fruit wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endosperm", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In angiosperms, one male gamete fuses with the egg resulting in the formation of a diploid zygote. The other gamete fuses with the other two polar nuclei forming the two primary endopsperm nucleus(3n) this type of fertilization is called double fertilization.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6462,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Which of the following cellular metabolic processes doesnot require oxygen but is a part of aerobic and anaerobic respiration?','[{"text": "Glycolysis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fermentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "TCA cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Electron transport coupled with chemiosmosis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Glycolysis is independent of oxygen and occurs in both aerobic and anaerobic pathway.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6463,'biology',83,489,1003,'In tissue level of organisation the','[{"text": "Cells are arranged as loose cell aggregates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tissues are grouped to form organ system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cells performing the same function are arranged into groups", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tissue system is exhibited by members of platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The cells performing the same function are arranged into tissues, hence is called tissue level of organisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
