(6494,'biology',82,1262,3077,'What type of growth is it when new cells are always being added to the plant body by the activity of the meristem?','[{"text": "Transient growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Open growth", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Closed growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ceased growth", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The cells of meristems have the capacity to divide and self-perpetuate. The product, however, soon loses the capacity to divide and such cells make up the plant body. This form of growth wherein new cells are always being added to the plant body by the activity of the meristem is called the open form of growth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
