(6500,'biology',81,1040,2463,'The most common respiratory substrate is','[{"text": "Glucose", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sucrose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maltose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycogen", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The compounds that are oxidised during this process are known as respiratory substrates. Usually carbohydrates are oxidised to release energy, but proteins, fats and even organic acids can be used as respiratory substances in some plants, under certain conditions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6501,'biology',8,156,332,'What would be the number of chromosomes in the cells of the aleurone layer in a plant species with 8 chromosomes in its synergids?','[{"text": "16", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "24", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "32", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Synergids are two, short- lived, haploid cells lying close to the egg in mature embryosc of the flowering plant ovule. While the endosperm is triploid tissue formed after triple fusion. Thus if the synergid is 8 chromosomes, the aleurone layer (part of the endosperm) will have just triple of that of chromosomes in the synergids i.e., 24 chromosomes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6502,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Which of the following are responsible for the primary growth of the plants?','[{"text": "Root apical meristem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shoot apical meristem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The root apical meristem and the shoot apical meristem are responsible for the primary growth of the plants and principally contribute to the elongation of the plants along their axis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
