(6509,'biology',82,1262,3077,'In dicotyledonous plants and gymnosperms, the lateral meristems, vascular cambium and cork-cambium ____','[{"text": "Degenerate after completion of juvenile phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Appear early in life", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Appear later in life", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In dicotyledonous plants and gymnosperms, the lateral meristems, vascular cambium and cork-cambium appear later in life. These are the meristems that cause the increase in the girth of the organs in which they are active. This is known as secondary growth of the plant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
