(6513,'biology',82,1262,3077,'In which of the following plants the lateral meristems, vascular cambium and corkcambium appear later in life?','[{"text": "Algae and bryophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bryophytes and pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicotyledonous plants and gymnosperms", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In dicotyledonous plants and gymnosperms, the lateral meristems, vascular cambium and cork-cambium appear later in life. These are the meristems that cause the increase in the girth of the organs in which they are active. This is known as secondary growth of the plant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
