(6517,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Lateral meristem, vascular cambium and corkcambium are responsible for which of the following event in plants?','[{"text": "The increase in the girth of the organs in which they are active", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary growth of the plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Primary growth of the plants.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In dicotyledonous plants and gymnosperms, the lateral meristems, vascular cambium and cork-cambium appear later in life. These are the meristems that cause the increase in the girth of the organs in which they are active. This is known as secondary growth of the plant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6518,'biology',83,489,1004,'The layer absent in the embryos of diploblastic animals is','[{"text": "Ectoderm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoderm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesoderm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mesoglea", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Animals in which the cells are arranged in two embryonic layers, an external ectoderm and an internal endoderm, are called diploblastic animals. In these animals, an undifferentiated layer, mesoglea, is present in between the ectoderm and the endoderm. Mesoderm is present in triploblastic animals.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
