(6524,'biology',81,1040,2463,'Select the correct sentence<br>i. The strategy that the plant cell uses is to anabolise the glucose molecule in such a way that not all the liberated energy goes out as heat.<br>ii. The key is to oxidise glucose not in one step but in several large steps enabling some steps to be just large enough such that the energy released can be coupled to ATP synthesis.','[{"text": "i is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The corrected statements are i. The strategy that the plant cell uses is to catabolise the glucose molecule in such a way that not all the liberated energy goes out as heat.<br>ii. The key is to oxidise glucose not in one step but in several small steps enabling some steps to be just large enough such that the energy released can be coupled to ATP synthesis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6525,'biology',83,489,1004,'Diploblastic animals belong to the phylum','[{"text": "Arthropoda", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Annelida", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cnidaria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Animals in which the cells are arranged in two embryonic layers, an external ectoderm and an internal endoderm, are called diploblastic animals, e.g., coelenterates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6526,'biology',8,156,332,'What is the fate of the male gametes discharged in the synergid?','[{"text": "One fuses with egg other(s) degenerate (s) in the synergid.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All fuse with the egg.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One fuses with the egg, other(s) fuse(s) with synergid nucleus.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One fuses with the egg and other fuses with central cell nuclei.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'One fuses with the egg and other fuses with central cell nuclei.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6527,'biology',82,1262,3077,'How do we measure increase in protoplasm even if it is difficult to measure directly at cellular level?','[{"text": "By measuring some quantity which is more or less proportional to it", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "By calculating difference between increase in protoplasm and nucleoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is impossible to measure growth at cellular level", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Growth, at a cellular level, is principally a consequence of increase in the amount of protoplasm. Since increase in protoplasm is difficult to measure directly, one generally measures some quantity which is more or less proportional to it.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6528,'biology',81,1041,2464,'What are the several reasons why plants can get along without respiratory organs?','[{"text": "They do not present great demands for gas exchange", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Each plant part takes care of its own gas- exchange needs.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The distance that gasses must diffuse even in large, bulky plants is not great", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'They do not present great demands for gas exchange.Each plant part takes care of its own gas- exchange needs. The distance that gasses must diffuse even in large, bulky plants is not great, Therefore all are correct',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6529,'biology',83,489,1004,'Mark the incorrect statement for the phyla platyhelminthes to echinodermata.','[{"text": "All groups represent organ/ organ system level of organization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are triploblastic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are bilaterally symmetrical", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Adult echinoderms exhibit radial symmetry.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6530,'biology',8,157,333,'Post-fertilization events do not include<br>A. Formation of zygote and primary endosperm cell<br>B. Maturation of ovules in seed<br>C. Formation of ovary into fruit<br>D. Formation of embryo inside seed','[{"text": "Only A", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Double fertilization involves fertilization of egg and central cell by two sperms brought by same pollen tubes is a fertilsation event, not post fertilisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6531,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Among the following parameters how many of the following are used to measure growth at cellular level?<br>(a) increase in fresh weight,<br>(b) increase in dry weight,<br>(c) increase in length,<br>(d) increase in area,<br>(e) increase in volume,<br>(f) increase in cell number','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Growth is, measured by a variety of parameters some of which are: increase in fresh weight, dry weight, length, area, volume and cell number.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6532,'biology',81,1041,2464,'The released energy obtained by oxidation is stored as','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NADP}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ADP}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NAD}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ATP}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The energy released by oxidation during respiration is not directly used, but is stored as ATP, which is broken down whenever energy is needed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
