(6559,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Which of the following is the characteristics of cells in the meristematic phase?','[{"text": "Rich in protoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inconspicuous nuclei", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Large conspicuous nuclei", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The constantly dividing cells, both at the root apex and the shoot apex, represent the meristematic phase of growth. The cells in this region are rich in protoplasm, possess large conspicuous nuclei. Their cell walls are primary in nature, thin and cellulosic with abundant plasmodesmatal connections.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6560,'biology',81,1040,2463,'Select the correct answer<br>I. In green plants not all cells, tissues and organs photosynthesis.<br>II. In plants, only cells containing chloroplasts, that are most often located in the superficial layers, carry out photosynthesis.','[{"text": "I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Partly I is correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct. In green plants not all cells, tissues and organs photosynthesis. In plants, only cells containing chloroplasts, that are most often located in the superficial layers, carry out photosynthesis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6561,'biology',83,489,1004,'Given below is a diagrammatic sketch of germinal layers. Identify the part labelled A,B,C and D; select the correct option.','[{"text": "A - Ectoderm\\nB - Endoderm\\nC - Mesoderm\\nD - Mesoglea", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Ectoderm\\nB - Endoderm\\nC - Mesoglea\\nD - Mesoderm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Ectoderm\\nB - Mesoderm\\nC - Endoderm\\nD - Mesoglea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Ectoderm\\nB - Mesoglea\\nC - Mesoderm\\nD - Endoderm", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. Ectoderm<br>B. Endoderm<br>C. Mesoderm<br>D. Mesoglea',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_6561_question_1.png'),
(6562,'biology',8,157,333,'In a leaf cell of angiosperm contain 50 chromosome, the number of chromosome in egg cell, pollen grain, endosperm and integument would be','[{"text": "25, 25, 50, 50", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "25, 25, 75, 50", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "25, 25, 25, 50", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "25, 50, 50, 75", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In gamete formation, nuclear division results in the division of chromosomes. As a result half of the chromosomes are involved in the formation of gametophyte. Hence in an unfertilized ovule, egg cell is haploid \n(25), pollen grain (25) (male gametophyte )is haploid, integuments are diploid (50). After fertilization primary endosperm nucleus develops into triploid endosperm (75).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6563,'biology',82,1262,3077,'The cell wall of the cells in meristematic region are____','[{"text": "Primary in nature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thin and cellulosic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "With abundant plasmodesmatal connections", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The constantly dividing cells, both at the root apex and the shoot apex, represent the meristematic phase of growth. The cells in this region are rich in protoplasm, possess large conspicuous nuclei. Their cell walls are primary in nature, thin and cellulosic with abundant plasmodesmatal connections.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
