(6570,'biology',8,157,333,'Which of the following statement is true?<br>i. Pollen release and stigma receptivity are always synchronized in all species.<br>ii. Pollination does not  guarantee the transfer of right type of pollen.<br>iii. Micropyle represents the basal part of \novule.<br>iv. Most zygotes divide only after certain \namount of endosperm is formed.','[{"text": "i. iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i. ii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii. iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii. iii. iv", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The statement can be corrected as<br>i. Pollen release and stigma receptivity are always never synchronized in all species.<br>ii. Chalaza represents the basal part of ovule.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6571,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Increased vacuolation, cell enlargement and new cell wall deposition are the characteristics of cells in which of the following phase?','[{"text": "Dual phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meristematic phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Elongation phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Maturation phase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Further away from the apex, i.e., more proximal to the phase of elongation, lies the portion of axis which is undergoing the phase of maturation. The cells of this zone, attain their maximal size in terms of wall thickening and protoplasmic modifications.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
