(6705,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Identify the isomers from the following<br>i. Glucose-6- $$\\mathrm{PO}_{4}$$, fructose-6- $$\\mathrm{PO}_{4}$$<br>ii. Dihydroxy acetone phosphate and 3-phosphoglyceraldehyde<br>iii. PEPA and pyruvic acid<br>iv. Glucose, fructose','[{"text": "i, ii, iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The isomers from the given examples are: i). Glucose-6-phosphate and Fructose-6phosphate<br>ii). DHAP and PGA<br>iv). Glucose and fructose',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6706,'biology',82,1263,3078,'In the expression of exponential growth, $\\mathrm{W}_{1}=$ $\\mathrm{W}_{0} \\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{rt}}$, \'e\' represents____','[{"text": "Exponential growth rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Base of exponential logarithms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Base of natural logarithms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The exponential growth can be expressed as $\\mathrm{W}_{1}=\\mathrm{W}_{0} \\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{rt}}$<br>$\\mathrm{W}_{1}=$ final size (weight, height, number etc.)<br>$\\mathrm{W}_{0}=$ initial size at the beginning of the period<br>$r=$ growth rate $t=$ time of growth $e=$ base of natural logarithms',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6707,'biology',83,490,1006,'The common bath sponge belongs to the genus','[{"text": "<i>Sycon</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Spongilla</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Leucosolenia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Euspongia</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Spongillae are freshwater sponge, whereas  <i>Euspongia</i> is a common bath sponge.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6708,'biology',8,157,335,'Formation of fruits without fertilization is known as or the process of embryo sac formation without fertilization is known as','[{"text": "Parthenocarpy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Parthenogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polyembryony", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polygamy", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Although in most of the species, fruits are the results of fertilisation, there are a few species in which fruits develop without fertilisation. Such fruits are called parthenocarpic fruits. Banana is one such example.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6709,'biology',81,1040,2463,'Which process provides energy for daily activities to all organisms?','[{"text": "Photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fermentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellular respiration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Combustion of sugars", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cellular respiration provides energy for daily activities to all organisms.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6710,'biology',82,1263,3078,'In the expression of exponential growth, $\\mathrm{W}_{1}=$ $\\mathrm{W}_{0} \\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{rt}}$, \' $\\mathrm{r}$ \' means____','[{"text": "The measure of the ability of the plant to produce new plant material", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Efficiency index", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Relative growth rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The exponential growth can be expressed as $\\mathrm{W}_{1}=\\mathrm{W}_{0} \\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{rt}}$<br>$\\mathrm{W}_{1}=$ final size (weight, height, number etc.)<br>$\\mathrm{W}_{0}=$ initial size at the beginning of the period<br>r = growth rate t = time of growth e = base of natural logarithms<br>Here, ${\\rm{r}}$ is the relative growth rate and is also the measure of the ability of the plant to produce new plant material, referred to as efficiency index.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6711,'biology',8,157,335,'Morphologically the white fluffy edible mass of maize is','[{"text": "Perisperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed coat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endosperm", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Morphologically the white fluffy edible mass of maize is Endosperm',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6714,'biology',82,1263,3078,'Read the following statements carefully and select the wrong statement.','[{"text": "An idealised sigmoid growth curve is typical for growth of cells in culture, and many higher plants and plant organs.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A sigmoid curve is a characteristic of living organism growing in a natural environment.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The simplest expression of arithmetic growth is exemplified by a root elongating at a variable rate.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All above statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The simplest expression of arithmetic growth is exemplified by a root elongating at a constant rate',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6715,'biology',83,490,1006,'Which of the following statement is incorrect w.r.t sponges?','[{"text": "Choanocytes or collar cells line the spongocoel and the canals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sponges have paragastric cavity which helps in extracellular digestion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sponges are mostly asymmetrical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The larval stage in sponge is morphologically distinct from the adult", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Digestion in sponges is intracellular, food is carried to the other cells through amoebocytes',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
