(6730,'biology',83,490,1006,'Which of the following is the distinctive feature of sponges?','[{"text": "They are acellular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They possess spongocoel and osculum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They reproduce only asexually", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are all marine.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The presence of spongocoel and osculum are unique to sponges only.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6731,'biology',8,157,335,'Endospermic seeds are seen in','[{"text": "Castor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coconut", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Endosperm is a nutritive tissue that supplies food material to the growing embryo. It is developed from the primary endosperm nucleus. Castor retain a part of the endosperm. In coconut, water is free nuclear endosperm and white kernel is the cellular endosperm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6732,'biology',82,1263,3078,'Let\'s consider two leaves $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{B}$, having area $7 \\mathrm{~cm}^{2}$ and $20 \\mathrm{~cm}^{2}$ respectively. After 3 days of growth it is found that their area has become $14 \\mathrm{~cm}^{2}$ and $30 \\mathrm{~cm}^{2}$ respectively then which leaf has shown higher relative growth rate?','[{"text": "A", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both A and B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Data insufficient", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Relative growth rate is calculated as per unit initial parameter, leaf A has grown as twice as initial leaf size and leaf \' $\\mathrm{B}$ \' has grown only $50 \\%$ of initial size, therefore correct answer is leaf A.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
