(6740,'biology',82,1263,3078,'Given diagram represents which type of growth?','[{"text": "Arithmetic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Geometric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parabolic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hyperbolic", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Given diagram represents arithmetic type of growth. In arithmetic growth, following mitotic cell division, only one daughter cell continues to divide while the other differentiates and matures. The simplest expression of arithmetic growth is exemplified by a root elongating at a constant rate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/82_6740_question_1.png'),
