(6779,'biology',8,157,335,'Testa of the seed is produced from','[{"text": "Hilum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovary wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Funicle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Outer integument of ovule", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The seed coat (or testa) develops from the tissue, the integument, originally surrounding the ovule. The seed coat in the mature seed can be a paper-thin layer (e.g. peanut) or something more substantial (e.g. thick and hard in honey locust and coconut). The seed coat helps protect the embryo from mechanical injury and from drying out.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6780,'biology',81,1040,2463,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The breaking of $$\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$$ bonds of complex organic molecules by oxidation of cells leading to the release of a lot of energy is called cellular respiration<br></div><div class="column-right">Glucose is the favoured substrate for respiration</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6781,'biology',82,1262,3077,'What happens after differentiation in the cells derived from root apical and shoot apical meristem and cambium?','[{"text": "Further differentiate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Starts doing specific function", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The cells derived from root apical and shoot apical meristems and cambium differentiate and mature to perform specific functions. This act leading to maturation of cells is termed as differentiation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
