(6783,'biology',8,157,335,'Hilum is a scar on the','[{"text": "Seed, where micropyle was present", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fruit, where it was attached to pedicel", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed, where funicle was attached", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fruit, where style was present", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ovule is integumented megasporangium found in spermatophytes which develop into seed fertilization. Ovule occurs inside the ovary where it is attached to the placenta. Ovule is stalked. Stalk is called Funicle. Point of attachment of body of the ovule with the funicle is known as hilum. It is present on scar in a mature seed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6784,'biology',81,1041,2464,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">During oxidation within a cell, all the energy contained in respiratory substrates is not released free into the cell, or in a single step<br></div><div class="column-right">Energy is released in a series of slow step-wise reactions controlled by enzymes, and it is trapped as chemical energy in the form of ATP</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6785,'biology',82,1265,3080,'If a part of the  pith from the stem of a plant is used as an explant and cultured on nutrient medium, which of the following processes is responsible for the formation of an undifferentiated mass of cells called callus?','[{"text": "Growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Differentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dedifferentiation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Redifferentiation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The living differentiated cells, that have lost the capacity to divide can regain the capacity of division under certain conditions. This phenomenon is termed as dedifferentiation. If a part pith from the stem of a plant is used as an explant and cultured on nutrient medium, dedifferentiation is responsible for the formation of an undifferentiated mass of cells called callus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6786,'biology',83,491,1007,'The skeleton of corals is composed of','[{"text": "Spicules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calcium sulphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calcium carbonate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Spongin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Some of the cnidarians, e.g., corals have a skeleton composed of calcium carbonate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6787,'biology',8,157,335,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Outer \ninteguments<br>B. Inner \ninteguments<br>C. Ovary<br>D. Ovules<br>E. Ovary wall</div><div class="column-right">P. Testa<br>Q. Fruit<br>R. Tegman<br>S. Pericarp<br>T. Seed</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R, B – P , C – Q, D – T, E – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – R, C – P, D – T, E – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – P, B – R, C – Q, D – T, E – S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A – Q, B – T, C – P, D – R, E – S", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A – P, B – R, C – Q, D – T, E – S',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6788,'biology',81,1041,2464,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">ATP do not act as energy currency of the cell<br></div><div class="column-right">Energy trapped in ATP is utilised in various energyrequiring processes of the organisms</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'It is important to understand that the energy released by oxidation in respiration is not (or rather cannot be) used directly but is used to synthesise ATP, which is broken down whenever (and wherever) energy needs to be utilised. Hence, ATP acts as the energy currency of the cell.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6789,'biology',82,1265,3080,'Arrange the following events in correct sequence, in the life cycle of a typical dicot plant.<BR>p) Differentiation<BR>q) Redifferentiation.<br>r) Dedifferentiation<br>s) Divisions in primary meristem.','[{"text": "p, q, r, s", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "s, p, r, q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "s, r, p, q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "q, p, r, s", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the life cycle of a typical dicot plant, events occur as per following sequence:<br>(s) Divisions in primary meristem,<br>(p) Differentiation,<br>(r) Dedifferentiation,<br>(q) Redifferentiation',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6792,'biology',81,1041,2464,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Plants require $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ for respiration to occur and they also give out $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$<br></div><div class="column-right">Plants have systems in place that ensure the availability of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plants require $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ for respiration to occur and they also give out $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6793,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Different stages of development in plants are as follow, select the correct sequence','[{"text": "Bolting -Flowering -Juvenility Germination.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Internode elongation- Flowering - Fruiting - Juvenility", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Germination-Juvenility-Flowering -Fruiting.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Maturity - Flowering - Juvenility -Germination.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct sequence of different stages of development in plants is as follow, Germination-Juvenility-Flowering -Fruiting.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6794,'biology',83,491,1007,'Absence of circulatory system in hydra is compensated by','[{"text": "Pseudocoelomic fluid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of tentacles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gastro vascular cavity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The gastrovascular cavity compensates for the absence of circulatory system in Cnidarians.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6795,'biology',81,1041,2464,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">During the process of respiration, oxygen is utilised, and carbon dioxide, water and energy are released as products<br></div><div class="column-right">The combustion reaction does not require oxygen</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Combustion reactions requires oxygen.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6796,'biology',8,157,335,'What is the function of micropyle in the seed?','[{"text": "It facilitates entry of water into the seed during germination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It facilitates entry of oxygen and water into the seed during germination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It facilitates entry of oxygen into the seed during germination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It has no use", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The function of micropyle in the seed is it facilitates entry of oxygen and water into the seed during germination',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6797,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Select the option showing correct sequence of developmental process in a plant cell.','[{"text": "Subsidiary cell - mitochondrial division - redifferentiation - Mature cell.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mature cell- Nucleoplasmic growth - Maturation - Meristematic cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meristematic cell - Plasmatic growth - differentiation- mature cell.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Guard cell- Senescence -Plasmatic growth- Meristematic cell.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Correct sequence of developmental process in a plant cell is as follow<br>Meristematic cell - Plasmatic growth - differentiation- mature cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6798,'biology',83,491,1007,'In which of the following polyp phase does not occurs?','[{"text": "<i>Hydra</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Obelia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Physalia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Aurelia</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Aurelia is umbrella-shaped and freeswimming and thus exhibits medusa phase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6799,'biology',81,1042,2465,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">All living organisms retain the enzymatic machinery to partially oxidise glucose with the help of oxygen<br></div><div class="column-right">The breakdown of glucose to lactic acid is called glycolysis</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All living organisms retain the enzymatic machinery to partially oxidise glucose without the help of oxygen. The breakdown of glucose to Pyruvic acid is called glycolysis and the breakdown of glucose to lactic acid is called anaerobic respiration (Fermentation).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6800,'biology',8,157,335,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. False fruits<br>B. Parthenocarpic \nfruit<br>C. Dry fruit<br>D. Fleshy fruit</div><div class="column-right">P. Mustard<br>Q. Orange<br>R. Banana<br>S. Apple</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R, B – P, C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – S, B – R, C – P, D – Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A – P, B – R, C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – P, C – R, D – S", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A – S, B – R, C – P, D – Q',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6801,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Which of the following events occur due to the plants growth and development?','[{"text": "Increase in length", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leaves, flowers, fruits, arise in an orderly pattern", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Falling of leaves and fruits", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of the given events occur due to the plants growth and development. During growth size increases. Development is the sum of two processes: growth and differentiation. The development of a mature plant from a zygote (fertilised egg) follow a precise and highly ordered succession of events. During this process a complex body organisation is formed that produces roots, leaves, branches, flowers, fruits, and seeds, and eventually they die.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6802,'biology',83,491,1007,'Recognise the figure and find out the correct matching.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "a - asexually,\\nb - sexually", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a - sexually,\\nb - asexually", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a - sexually,\\nb - parthenogenetically", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a - asexually,\\nb - parthenogenetically", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Those cnidarians which exist in both forms exhibit alternation of generation (Metagenesis), i.e., polyps produce medusae asexually and medusae form the polyps sexually(e.g., Obelia).<br>a - asexually<br>b - sexually <img src=\'/img/data/biology/83_6802_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_6802_question_1.png'),
(6803,'biology',81,1042,2465,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In aerobic respiration, glycolysis is the only process in respiration<br></div><div class="column-right">Glycolysis occurs in the cytoplasm of the cell and is present in all living organisms</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In aerobic respiration glycolysis, link reaction, Kreb\'s cycle and ETS are the processes in respiration. In anaerobic respiration, glycolysis is the only process in respiration.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6804,'biology',8,157,335,'Parthenogenesis is a type of','[{"text": "Budding", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Regeneration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Asexual reproduction", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Parthenocarpic fruits are seedless. They are produced by asexual reproduction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6805,'biology',82,1266,3081,'What do you call an expansion of leaf?','[{"text": "Growth", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Redifferentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wilting", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centrifugation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Expansion of leaf can be called as growth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6806,'biology',83,491,1007,'Metagenesis is seen in','[{"text": "<i>Hydra</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Physalia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Obelia</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Adamsia</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Metagenesis or alternation of generation is seen in Obelia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6807,'biology',81,1042,2465,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In glycolysis, a chain of ten reactions, under the control of different enzymes, takes place to produce pyruvate from glucose<br></div><div class="column-right">Pyruvic acid is then the key product of glycolysis</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(6808,'biology',8,157,335,'Example for false fruits are','[{"text": "Apple", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cashew nut", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Strawberry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A false fruit or pseudo-carp is derived from the floral parts other than ovary, e.g., peduncle in cashew-nut, thalamus in apple.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6809,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Plant growth is unique which statement supports this statement?','[{"text": "The plant retains the regeneration power.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Capacity of the plants of unlimited growth", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "There is change in offspring\'s characters.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plant growth is unique because plants retain the capacity for unlimited growth throughout their life. This ability of the plants is due to the presence of meristems at certain locations in their body. The cells of such meristems have the capacity to divide and self-perpetuate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6810,'biology',83,491,1007,'The phenomenon of metagenesis occur in','[{"text": "<i>Obelia</i> - cnidaria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Aurelia</i> - cnidaria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Musca</i> - cnidaria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Obelia</i> - ctenophora", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Metagenesis or alternation of generation is seen in the cnidarian, Obelia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6811,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In glycolysis, conversion of BPGA to PGA is an energy yielding process, this energy is trapped by the formation of ATP<br></div><div class="column-right">Another ATP is synthesised during the conversion of PEP to pyruvic acid in the glycolytic pathway</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6812,'biology',8,157,335,'The following diagram represents false fruit of apple, strawberry. Identify the parts labelled P, Q, R, S.','[{"text": "P - Achene, Q - Thalamus, R - Mesocarp, S - Endocarp", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P - Achene, Q - Mesocarp, R - Endocarp, S - Thalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P - Achene, Q - Thalamus, R - Endocarp, S - Mesocarp", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "P - Achene, Q - Endocarp, R - Thalamus, S - Mesocarp", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fg 2.15 from NCERT',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/8_6812_question_1.png'),
(6813,'biology',83,491,1007,'Select the correct answer<br>i. Metagenesis in <i>Obelia</i>-polyp and medusae are diploid<br>ii. Alternation of generations in plants - one is haploid and other is diploid<br>Select the correct answer','[{"text": "Only i is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct. Alternation of generation in Obelia is seen between polyp and medusa. Alternation of generation in plants is amongst a diploid sporophyte and haploid gametophyte.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6814,'biology',82,1265,3080,'Which type of growth is responsibility of meristems?','[{"text": "Plasmal growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Primary growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (2) and (3)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Plant growth is unique because plants retain the capacity for unlimited growth throughout their life. This ability of the plants is due to the presence of meristems at certain locations in their body. The cells of such meristems have the capacity to divide and self-perpetuate. Meristem is responsible for both primary and secondary growth in plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6839,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Select the correct character related to the cell found in phase of elongation.','[{"text": "Cell wall is thin and cellulosic.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abundant plasmodesmatal connections.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increased vacuolation of cell.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cell wall becomes very much thickened.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Increased vacuolation, cell enlargement and new cell wall deposition are the characteristics of the cells found in elongation phase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6815,'biology',81,1043,2466,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Under anaerobic conditions either lactic acid fermentation or alcohol fermentation occurs<br></div><div class="column-right">Fermentation takes place under anaerobic conditions in many prokaryotes and multicellular eukaryotes</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Fermentation takes place under anaerobic conditions in many prokaryotes and unicellular eukaryotes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6816,'biology',8,157,335,'Development of seedless fruit in an unfertilized flower is','[{"text": "Polyembryony", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporophytic budding", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parthenocarpy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Micropropagation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Parthenocarpy is the natural or artificially induced production of fruit without fertilization of ovules.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6817,'biology',83,491,1007,'Alternation of generation is also called','[{"text": "Metamorphosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metastasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metakaryocyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metagenesis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Metagenesis is also known as alternation of generation. It is seen in the coelenterate, Obelia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6818,'biology',82,1264,3079,'Meristem contributes in ____ of plant?','[{"text": "Increase in girth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Elongation along the axis (3) Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Meristem is responsible for both primary and secondary growth in plants. Primary growth of the plants contribute to the elongation of the plants along their axis. Secondary growth of the plant causes the increase in the girth of the organs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6819,'biology',81,1043,2466,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In lactic acid and alcohol fermentation, less than 7 percent of the energy in glucose is released and all of it is trapped as high energy bonds of ATP<br></div><div class="column-right">Yeast poison themselves to death when the concentration of alcohol reaches about 13 percent</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In both lactic acid and alcohol fermentation not much energy is released; less than seven per cent of the energy in glucose is released and not all of it is trapped as high energy bonds of ATP.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6820,'biology',8,157,335,'Parthenocarpic tomato fruits can be produced by','[{"text": "Raising the plants from vernalized seeds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Treating the plants with low concentration of Gibberellic acid and auxins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Treating the plants with phenyl mercuric acetate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Removing androecium of flowers before pollen grains are released.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Parthenocarpic fruits are seedless. Flower is emasculated and auxins are applied to the stigma of the flower which forms Parthenocarpic fruits. Auxins should be applied after anthesis and Gibberlic acid should be applied before anthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6821,'biology',83,491,1007,'Medusa of <i>Obelia</i> is','[{"text": "Asexually reproductive structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sexually reproductive structure", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The medusa is umbrella-shaped and freeswimming that reproduces sexually to form polyps.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6822,'biology',82,1262,3077,'The cells representing the phases of elongation can be found at which location?','[{"text": "Shoot Apex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Root Apex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cells proximal to both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The cells representing the phases of elongation can be found at Shoot apex and Root apex.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6823,'biology',81,1044,2467,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Aerobic respiration is the process that leads to a complete oxidation of organic molecules in the presence of oxygen<br></div><div class="column-right">This type of respiration is most common in lower organisms</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Aerobic respiration is most common in higher organisms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6824,'biology',8,157,335,'An example for naturally occurring parthenocarpic fruit','[{"text": "Apple", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mango", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Guava", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Banana", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Banana is an eg. of naturally occurring parthenocarpic fruit.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6825,'biology',83,491,1007,'What do the given figures $A$ and $B$ represent and identify their habitats. Choose the correct option.','[{"text": "A - Polyp-free swimming, B - Medusa-sessile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Medusa-free swimming, B - Polyp-sessile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Polyp-sessile, B - Medusa-free swimming", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Medusa-sessile, B - Polyp-free swimming", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The given diagram represents -<br>A - Polyp (sessile)<br>B - Medusa (free-living)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_6825_question_1.png'),
