(6837,'biology',83,491,1007,'Highest degree of polymorphism is found in','[{"text": "Arthropoda", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cnidarians", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protozoa", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cnidarians show the highest degree of polymorphism among invertebrate organisms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6838,'biology',81,1045,2468,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The continued oxidation of acetyl CoA via the TCA cycle requires the continued replenishment of citric acid<br></div><div class="column-right">In addition it also requires regeneration of NADH and $$\\mathrm{FADH}_{2}$$ from NAD $${ }^{+}$$and $$\\mathrm{FAD}^{+}$$</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The continued oxidation of acetyl CoA via the TCA cycle requires the continued replenishment of oxaloacetic acid, the first member of the cycle.In addition it also requires regeneration of $$\\mathrm{NAD}^{+}$$and $$\\mathrm{FAD}^{+}$$from $$\\mathrm{NADH}$$ and $$\\mathrm{FADH}_{2}$$ respectively.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6840,'biology',8,157,335,'Select the correct statement from the following<br>A. Seeds have better adaptive strategies for dispersal to new habitats and help the species<br>B. Seeds have sufficient food reserves to nourish the seedlings till they are capable of photosynthesis<br>C. The hard seed coat of seed provides protection to the young embryo.<br>D. Seeds are products of asexual reproduction, therefore leading to variations.','[{"text": "A,B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B,C,D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A,B,C", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A,B,C,D", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Seeds are products of sexual reproduction.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6841,'biology',83,491,1007,'Read the following statements:<br>I. Polyp is sessile and cylindrical form like <i>Adamsia</i><br>II. Medusa is umbrella shaped and free-living like <i>Aurelia</i><br>III. Polyp produce medusae sexually and medusae form the polyp asexually (e.g : <i>Obelia</i>).<br>IV. Metagenesis is seen in Jelly fish<br>Find the incorrect statement :','[{"text": "I,III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I,II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III,IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II,III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Polyp produces medusae asexually and medusae form the polyp sexually (e.g : Obelia). Metagenesis is seen in Obelia.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6842,'biology',81,1046,2469,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The metabolic pathway through which the proton passes from one carrier to another is called electron transport system (ETS)<br></div><div class="column-right">ETS is present in the inner mitochondrial membrane</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The metabolic pathway through which the electron passes from one carrier to another, is called the electron transport system (ETS).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6843,'biology',82,1264,3079,'Which of the following is not necessary for plant growth?','[{"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxygen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nutrients like some nitrogen compounds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of the given things like oxygen, water, nutrients like some nitrogen compounds are essential for plant growth. Plant growth and further development is intimately linked to the water status of the plant. Oxygen helps in releasing metabolic energy essential for growth activities. Nutrients (macro and micro essential elements) are required by plants for the synthesis of protoplasm and act as source of energy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6844,'biology',8,157,335,'Parthenogenesis is','[{"text": "Development of fruit without fertilization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Development of fruit without hormones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Development of embryo without fertilization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Development of embryo from egg without fertilization", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Parthenogenesis is most simply defined as reproduction without fertilization or development of embryos from eggs without fertilization.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
