(6846,'biology',81,1046,2469,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Cytochrome c is a small protein attached to the outer surface of inner membrane and acts as a mobile carrier for transfer of electrons between complex III and IV<br></div><div class="column-right">Complex IV refers to cytochrome b oxidase complex containing cytochrome a and a3 and three copper centres</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Complex IV refers to cytochrome c oxidase complex containing cytochromes a and a3, and two copper centres.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6847,'biology',82,1264,3079,'____ of cells helps in extension growth.','[{"text": "Plasticity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Turgidity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Elasticity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The plant cells grow in size by cell enlargement which in turn requires water. Turgidity of cells helps in extension growth. Thus, plant growth and further development is intimately linked to the water status of the plant. Water also provides the medium for enzymatic activities needed for growth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6848,'biology',8,157,335,'Banana fruits are seedless because','[{"text": "Triploid plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fruits are artificially ripened", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vegetative propagation of plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are parthenocarpically produced", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bananas are the most commonly available seedless fruits. Bananas are seedless because the parent banana tree is triploid (3X chromosome sets) even though pollination is normal.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6849,'biology',83,491,1007,'Which of the following is a correct statement regarding cnidarians?','[{"text": "They are all marine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are triploblastic with blind sac body plan.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gastrovascular cavity serves for digestion only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cnidarians exhibit two basic body forms called polyp and medusa", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Coelenterates are both marine and freshwater. They are diploblastic animals with a blind sac body plan. Gastrovascular cavity serves not only for digestion but also for circulation, excretion, reproduction, etc.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
