(6905,'biology',81,1043,2466,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Fermentation is the incomplete oxidation of glucose into lactic acid or ethanol<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It takes place under anaerobic conditions in prokaryotes only','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fermentation is an incomplete oxidation of glucose into lactic acid under anaerobic conditions. Fermentation process will occur in eukaryotes also, it occurs in yeast, in animal cells like muscles. Fermentation takes place under aerobic conditions in many prokaryotes, unicellular eukaryotes and germinating seeds.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6906,'biology',8,157,335,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">As the seed matures, its water content is reduced and seeds become relatively dry (10-15 per cent moisture by mass).</div><div class="column-right">As ovules mature into seeds, the ovary develops into a fruit</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6907,'biology',83,492,1008,'Bioluminescent property is well marked in','[{"text": "Ctenophores", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coelenterates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Branchiostoma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bioluminescent property is well marked in ctenophores.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6908,'biology',82,1265,3080,'Tumour is a product of____.','[{"text": "Dedifferentiation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Re-differentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Differentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Tumours are the result of dedifferentiation. Tumour is formed when a differentiated cell regains the capacity to divide and shows unrestrained growth. Tumours, also known as tumour cells, are the result of uncontrolled and abnormal cell growth in an organ, skin, or membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6909,'biology',81,1048,2471,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Respiratory pathway is an amphibolic pathway<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In respiratory pathway there is catabolism and anabolism by respiratory intermediates','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Amphibolic pathway is a pathway that functions for both catabolism (break down) and anabolism (building up) reactions. Respiration is catabolic process, but the pathway produces various intermediates which are raw materials for building up metabolites. Since respiratory pathway is involved in both anabolism and catabolism, it is considered as an amphibolic pathway.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6910,'biology',8,157,335,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The oldest is that of date palm, <i>Phoenix dactylifera </i>excavated from Arctic Tundra</div><div class="column-right">A recent record of 2000 years old viable seed is of a lupine, <i>Lupinus arcticus </i>discovered during the archeological excavation at King Herod’s palace near the Dead Sea</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both are incorrect. The oldest is that of a lupine, Lupinus arcticus excavated from Arctic Tundra. A recent record of 2000 years old viable seed is of the date palm, Phoenix dactylifera discovered during the archeological excavation at King Herod’s palace near the Dead Sea.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6911,'biology',83,492,1008,'The members of following phylum are exclusively marine, radially symmetrical and diploblastic','[{"text": "Porifera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Echinodermata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hemichoradata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ctenophora", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The members of Phylum Ctenophora are exclusively marine, diploblastic and show radial symmetry.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6912,'biology',82,1265,3080,'What would you call the parenchyma cells that are made to divide under controlled laboratory conditions during plant tissue culture?','[{"text": "Dedifferentiation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Re-differentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Differentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The parenchyma cells that are made to divide under controlled laboratory conditions during plant tissue culture are product of dedifferentiation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6913,'biology',81,1046,2469,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Oxidation of one molecule of $$\\mathrm{NADH}$$ gives rise to 3 molecules of ATP and one molecule of $$\\mathrm{FADH}_{2}$$ produces 2 molecules of ATP in ETS<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The number of ATP molecules synthesised depend on the nature of electron donor','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6914,'biology',8,157,335,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Tiny seeds are produced by <i>Ficus, Orobanche </i>and <i>Striga</i>.</div><div class="column-right">In many <i>Citrus</i> and Mango  varieties some of the nucellar cells surrounding the embryo  sac start dividing, protrude  into the embryo sac and  develop into the embryos.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6915,'biology',83,492,1008,'Ctenophore commonly known as?','[{"text": "sea walnuts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "comb jellies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adamsia", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ctenophores are commonly known as sea walnuts or comb jellies.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6916,'biology',82,1265,3080,'We may say that even differentiation in plants is ____A____, because cells/tissues arising out of the same meristem have____B____ structures at maturity','[{"text": "A - open,&emsp;&emsp;B - same", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - open,&emsp;&emsp;B - different", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - close,&emsp;&emsp;B - same", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - close,&emsp;&emsp;B - different", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'We may say that even differentiation in plants is open, because cells/tissues arising out of the same meristem have different structures at maturity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6917,'biology',81,1046,2469,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In electron transport system, the electrons are passed on to oxygen, resulting in the formation of $$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$$<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Oxygen is the ultimate acceptor of electrons','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Oxygen is the last electron acceptor of respiratory chain. In electron transport system, electrons are passed on from one carrier to another and ultimately to oxygen and at the end of the chain, one molecule of water is produced.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6918,'biology',8,157,335,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Some fruits are seedless or contain non-viable seeds.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> They are produced without fertilisation.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6920,'biology',82,1265,3080,'Read the following statements and select the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "Cells positioned away from root apical meristems differentiate as root-cap cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The final structure at maturity of a cell/ tissue is also determined by the location of the cell within.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cells those pushed to the periphery from root apical meristems mature as pith cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cells positioned away from root apical meristems differentiate as root-cap cells, while those pushed to the periphery mature as epidermis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6921,'biology',81,1041,2464,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Plants have no specialized respiratory organs<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> There is very little transport of gases from one plant part to another.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Plants do not have specialized structures or organs for respiration as in animals. Because the parts of plant will take care of its own gas exchange needs and there is a very little transport of gasses from one part of the plant to the another. Plants do not demand much as roots, leaves and stems respire at lower rate than animals. But plants have presence of stomata and lenticels for respiration.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6922,'biology',8,157,335,'Perisperm differs from endosperm in','[{"text": "Having no reserve food", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Being a diploid tissue", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Being a haploid tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Its formation by fusion of secondary nucleus with several sperms", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Perisperm differs from endosperm in being a diploid tissue',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6923,'biology',83,492,1008,'Which type of symmetry is common in ctenophores?','[{"text": "Pentamerous symmetry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Radial", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bilateral", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No symmetry", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ctenophores exhibit radial symmetry.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6924,'biology',82,1266,3081,'All the changes that an organism goes through during its life cycle from germination of the seed to senescence is termed as____.','[{"text": "Directional movement", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Development", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Redifferentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dedifferentiation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All the changes that an organism goes through during its life cycle from germination of the seed to senescence is termed as development.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6925,'biology',81,1042,2465,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Glycolysis is also called as EMP pathway<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It is the only process of respiration in aerobic organisms','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Glycolysis is also known as EMP pathway, in glycolysis, glucose undergoes partial oxidation which will result in the formation of 2 molecules of pyruvic acid. Glycolysis occurs in the cytoplasm of a cell. Aerobic respiration includes Glycolysis, Oxidative decarboxylation of pyruvic acid, Kreb\'s cycle and terminal oxidation, oxidative phosphorylation.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6926,'biology',8,157,335,'Persistent nucellus in the seed is known as','[{"text": "Chalaza", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Perisperm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hilum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tegmen", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Persistent Nucellus is called Perisperm e.g.: Black pepper, Beet',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6927,'biology',83,492,1008,'Which phylum includes \'sea walnuts\'?','[{"text": "Porifera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coelenterata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ctenophora", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Planarians", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ctenophores are commonly known as sea walnuts.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6928,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Plants follow different pathways in response to environment or phases of life to form different kinds of structures. Which term is used for this ability?','[{"text": "Rejuvenation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Differentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Elasticity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasticity", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Plants follow different pathways in response to environment or phases of life to form different kinds of structures. The term plasticity is used for this ability. Heterophylly in cotton, coriander and larkspur are the examples of plasticity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6929,'biology',81,1046,2469,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Complex II and complex III of ETS are NADH dehydrogenase complexes<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Cytochrome c, acts as a mobile carrier for transfer of electrons between complex II and III','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Complex II of ETS is succinate dehydrogenase complex, complex III is cytochrome bc1 complex. Cytochrome $$\\mathrm{c}$$ is protein attached to the outer surface of inner mitochondrial membrane, it acts as an electron carrier for transfer between complex III and complex IV.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6930,'biology',8,157,335,'The plant parts which consist of two generations-one within the other:<br>a) Pollen grains inside the anther<br>b) Germinated pollen grain with two male gametes<br>c) Seed inside the fruit<br>d) Embryo sac inside the ovule','[{"text": "(a), (b) & (c)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(c) & (d)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(a) & (d)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(a) only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'(a) & (d)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6931,'biology',83,492,1008,'Ctenophores have  _________for locomotion','[{"text": "Ten comb plates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eight comb plates", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Six comb plates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Five comb plates", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The body of Ctenophores bear eight external rows of ciliated comb plates, which help in locomotion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6932,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Heterophylly in cotton, coriander and larkspur are the examples of____','[{"text": "Rejuvenation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Differentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Elasticity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasticity", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Plants follow different pathways in response to environment or phases of life to form different kinds of structures. The term plasticity is used for this ability. Heterophylly in cotton, coriander and larkspur are the examples of plasticity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6933,'biology',81,1042,2465,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Conversion of 1,3<br>biphosphoglycerate to 3-phosphoglycerate is an energy yielding step<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> This energy is trapped by formation of ATP','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Conversion of 1,3 biphosphoglycerate to 3 phosphoglycerate is an energy yielding step, one among the 2 phosphates of biphosphoglycerate is linked by high energy bond, it can synthesise ATP to form 3-phosphoglycerate. Direct synthesis of ATP from metabolite is substrate level phosphorylation.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6934,'biology',8,157,335,'Which part of the fruit, labelled in the given figure makes it a false fruit?','[{"text": "B → Endocarp", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C → Thalamus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "D → Seed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A → Mesocarp", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'As thalamus is involved in fruit formation. Therefore, it is a false fruit.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/8_6934_question_1.png'),
(6935,'biology',83,492,1008,'Which of the following is/are known to emit light?','[{"text": "<i>Pleurobranchia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ctenoplana</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Balanoglossus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ctenophores like Ctenoplana and Pleurobrachia exhibit bioluminescence.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6936,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Which of the following plants show plasticity?','[{"text": "Cotton", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coriander", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Larkspur", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Plants follow different pathways in response to environment or phases of life to form different kinds of structures. The term plasticity is used for this ability. Heterophylly in cotton, coriander and larkspur are the examples of plasticity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6937,'biology',81,1049,2472,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> When carbohydrates are used as substrate and completely oxidised, R.Q is 1<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> When proteins are used in respiration as substrate the R.Q is greater than 1.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'R.Q (respiratory quotient) depends on the type of respiratory substrate used during respiration. When carbohydrates is used as substrate and is completely oxidised the R.Q will be 1 , because equal amount of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ are evolved and consumed. When proteins are used as respiratory substrate, R.Q will be around 0.9 (which bis less than 1).',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6938,'biology',8,158,336,'What is Apomixis?','[{"text": "Effect of low temperature on the growth of plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Development of plants in darkness", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Development of plants without the fusion of gametes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Plant’s inability to perceive stimulus for flowering", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Apomixis as defined by Hans Winkler is replacement of the normal sexual reproduction by asexual reproduction, without fertilization. Apomixis is a genetically controlled reproductive process by which embryos and seeds develop in the ovule without female meiosis and egg cell fertilization.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6939,'biology',83,492,1008,'Radial symmetry and lack of cnidoblasts are the characteristics of','[{"text": "<em>Ctenoplana</em> and <em>Pleurobrachia</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<em>Aurelia</em> and <em>Ctenoplana</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Ctenoplana</em> and star fish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Star fish and <em>Pleurobrachia</em>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Radial symmetry and lack of cnidoblasts are the characteristics of members of Ctenophora. Some examples of Ctenophora are - <em>Ctenoplana</em>, Pleurobrachia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6940,'biology',82,1266,3081,'In plants showing plasticity,','[{"text": "Heterophyllous development is according to environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The leaves of the juvenile plant are different in shape from those in mature plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Leaves of the plants are stretchable", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Plants follow different pathways in response to environment or phases of life to form different kinds of structures. This ability is called plasticity, e.g., heterophylly in cotton, coriander and larkspur. In such plants, the leaves of the juvenile plant are different in shape from those in mature plants. On the other hand, difference in shapes of leaves produced in air and those produced in water in buttercup also represent the heterophyllous development due to environment. This phenomenon of heterophylly is an example of plasticity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6941,'biology',81,1045,2468,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> First step of TCA cycle is the condensation of pyruvate with oxaloacetic acid and water<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> This reaction is catalysed by the enzyme pyruvate synthase','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'TCA cycle starts with condensation of acetyl group with oxaloacetic acid and water to yield citric acid. This reaction is catalysed by citrate synthase enzyme and a molecule of CoA ( coenzyme A) is released.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6943,'biology',83,492,1008,'Identify feature of phylum-ctenophora','[{"text": "The presence of 6 comb plates and appearance like jellies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The presence of 8 comb plates", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The presence of tentacles only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Asexual reproduction only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The body of Ctenophores bear eight external rows of ciliated comb plates, which help in locomotion. This is an identifying feature of phylum Ctenophora.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6944,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Growth, differentiation and development are','[{"text": "Clearly non-related events in the life of a plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Very closely related events in the life of a plant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sometimes related events depending on environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Growth, differentiation and development are very closely related events in the life of a plant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6945,'biology',81,1047,2470,'How many ATP molecules could maximally be generated from one molecule of glucose, if the complete oxidation of one mole of glucose to $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$$ yields ${\\rm{686}}\\,{\\rm{kcal}}$ and the useful chemical energy available in the high energy phosphate bond of one mole ATP is ${\\rm{12}}\\,{\\rm{kcal}}$ ?','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "30", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "57", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'One mole of ATP liberates ${\\rm{12}}\\,{\\rm{kcal}}$ of energy. So ${\\rm{686}}\\,{\\rm{kcal}}$ will be liberated by ${\\rm{686/12 = 57}}{\\rm{.1}}$ ATP molecules.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6946,'biology',8,158,336,'Adventive polyembryony is common in','[{"text": "Wheat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apple", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mango", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Orobanche", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Adventive polyembryony is formation of multiple embryos from nucellus or integument. e.g., Mango, Citrus, Opuntia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6947,'biology',83,492,1008,'Phylum-ctenophora is similar to _________ in having radially symmetrical, diploblastic organisms with tissue level of organisation','[{"text": "Cephalopoda", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ascelminthes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cnidaria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Turbellaria", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Organisms in phylum Ctenophora are similar to that of phylum Cnidaria in being diploblastic and possessing tissue level of organisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6948,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Broadly, the sum of growth and differentiation is considered as','[{"text": "Plasticity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dedifferentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Development", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Broadly, the sum of growth and differentiation is considered as development.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6949,'biology',81,1041,2464,'The overall goal of glycolysis, Kreb\'s cycle and the electron transport system is the formation of','[{"text": "Sugars", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleic acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ATP in one large oxidation reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ATP in small stepwise units<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Glycolysis, Kreb\'s cycle and electron transport system, they all give ATP which is the main energy currency of our body. Glycolysis takes place in cytoplasm, Kreb\'s cycle also takes place in cytoplasm and ETS takes place in the mitochondria.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6950,'biology',8,158,336,'Nucellar embryo is','[{"text": "Apomictic diploid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Apomictic haploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphimictic haploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphimictic diploid", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Substitution of usual sexual reproduction by form of reproduction which does not include syngamy and meiosis is called apomixis. Here embryo is developed by some other tissue like nucellus or integument. As nucellus is diploid tissue ,therefore nucellar embryo is apomictic diploid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6951,'biology',83,492,1008,'Ctenophores are','[{"text": "Dioecious (unisexual)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monoecious (hermaphrodite)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Multicellular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Asexual", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sexes are not separate in ctenophores. They are monoecious (hermaphrodites).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6952,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Development in plants is under control of which factors?','[{"text": "Intrinsic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Extrinsic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Environmental only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Development in plants is under control of both intrinsic and extrinsic factors.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6953,'biology',81,1046,2469,'All enzymes of TCA cycle are located in the mitochondrial matrix except one which is located in inner mitochondrial membranes in eukaryotes and in cytosol in prokaryotes. This enzyme is<br>','[{"text": "Isocitrate dehydrogenase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Malate dehydrogenase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Succinate dehydrogenase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lactate dehydrogenase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mitochondria contains various enzymes participating in Kreb\'s cycle. The membrane extrinsic, water-soluble domain, known as succinate dehydrogenase (SDH), contains the fumarate/succinate active site with a covalently bound FAD group and three iron-sulfur clusters: [2Fe-2S]2+/1+, [4Fe-4S]2+/1+, and $$[3 \\mathrm{Fe}-4 \\mathrm{~S}] 1+/ 0$$. The enzyme catalyses the interconversion of fumarate and succinate, and is closely related to fumarate reductase.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6954,'biology',8,158,336,'Apomictic embryos in Citrus arise from','[{"text": "Diploid cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synergids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antipodal cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maternal sporophytic tissue in ovule", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Nucellus turns into embryo in citrus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6955,'biology',83,492,1008,'Reproduction in <em>Ctenoplana</em> is by','[{"text": "Asexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sexual reproduction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Binary fission", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Budding", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Reproduction in Ctenophora takes place by sexual means.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6956,'biology',82,1266,3081,'The intrinsic factors which control development in plants are____.','[{"text": "Genetic only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemicals such as plant growth regulators only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Genetic factors and chemicals like plant growth hormone include intrinsic factors that control plant development.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6957,'biology',81,1046,2469,'The chemiosmotic coupling hypothesis of oxidative phosphorylation proposes that adenosine triphosphate (ATP) is formed because<br>','[{"text": "There is a change in the permeability of the inner mitochondrial membrane toward adenosine diphosphate (ADP)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A proton gradient forms across the inner membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "High energy bonds are formed in mitochondrial proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ADP is pumped out of the matrix into the intermembrane space", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Proton motive force develop between perimitochondrial space and matrix across inner mitochondrial membrane.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6958,'biology',8,158,336,'The polyembryony commonly occurs in','[{"text": "Tomato", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Potato", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Citrus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Turmeric", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Polyembryony refers to the formation of more than one embryo within a seed of a flowering plant. eg. Citrus',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6959,'biology',83,492,1008,'In ctenophores fertilisation is _____ with _______development..','[{"text": "External, direct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Internal, indirect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "External, indirect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Internal, direct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fertilisation in Ctenophora is external with indirect development.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6960,'biology',82,1266,3081,'The extrinsic factors which control development in plants are____.','[{"text": "Genetic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemicals such as plant growth regulators", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nutrition", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Light, temperature, water, oxygen, nutrients are considered as extrinsic factors for development of plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6961,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Aerobic respiratory pathway is appropriately termed<br>','[{"text": "Anabolic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parabolic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Catabolic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphibolic", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Amphibolic pathway is a kind of pathway which serves as both anabolic and catabolic process. Aerobic respiratory pathway involves both catabolism of carbohydrates and fatty acids and synthesis of anabolic precursors for amino acid synthesis, secondary metabolites and various intermediatory metabolic products.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6962,'biology',8,158,336,'In a type of apomixes known as adventives embryony, embryos develop directly from','[{"text": "Nucellus or integument", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Zygote", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synergids or antipodals in embryo sac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Accessory embryo sacs in the ovule", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Development of embryos directly from sporophytic tissues like nucellus, and integuments is called adventive embryony which is also a type of apomixis. Eg: Citrus',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6963,'biology',83,492,1008,'Cnidarians and ctenophores share common characteristics such as','[{"text": "Diploblastic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both extracellular and intracellular digestion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tissue level of organisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the mentioned characteristics are common in both Cnidaria and Ctenophora.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6964,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Read the following factors affecting plant development and select the number of extrinsic factors.<br>Light, genes, temperature, plant growth regulators, water, oxygen, nutrition','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Light, temperature, water, oxygen, nutrients are considered as extrinsic factors for development of plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6965,'biology',81,1043,2466,'The energy releasing metabolic process in which substrate is oxidised without an external electron acceptor is called','[{"text": "Fermentation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aerobic respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photorespiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycolysis<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Fermentation is the energy releasing metabolic process in which substance is oxidised without an external electron acceptor.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6966,'biology',8,158,336,'Seed formation without fertilization in flowering plants involves process of','[{"text": "Apomixis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sporulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Budding", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Somatic hybridization", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Apomixis is a reproductive process in plants that superficially resembles normal sexual reproduction in which there is no fusion of gametes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6967,'biology',83,492,1008,'Comb plates are found in','[{"text": "<i>Obelia</i> (Sea-fur )", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pleurobranchia</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Physalia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Comb plates are found in Pleurobrachia (Ctenophora).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6968,'biology',81,1046,2469,'In mitochondria, protons accumulate in the<br>','[{"text": "Matrix", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inner membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Outer membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inter membrane space", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In respiration, Protons accumulate in the intermembrane space of the mitochondria where electrons move through the ETS.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6969,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Suppose the meristem ceases to divide then what will happen?','[{"text": "Plant grows during juvenile phase only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plant growth ceases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Plant grows in length and girth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plant grows in mature phase only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Suppose the meristem ceases to divide then plant growth will also cease. Plant growth is unique because plants retain the capacity for unlimited growth throughout their life. This ability of the plants is due to the presence of meristems at certain locations in their body. The cells of such meristems have the capacity to divide and self-perpetuate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6981,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Which of the following leaves produced in air and those produced in water shows difference in shape?','[{"text": "Coriander", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Buttercup", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coconut", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Commelina</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Difference in shapes of leaves produced in air and those produced in water in buttercup represent the heterophyllous development due to environment.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6970,'biology',8,158,336,'Similarity between apomixes and vegetative reproduction is','[{"text": "Both occur round the year", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are applicable only to dicot plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both bypass the flowering phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both produce progeny identical to the parent", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Apomixis (asexual seed formation) is the result of a plant gaining the ability to bypass the most fundamental aspects of sexual reproduction: meiosis and fertilization. Embryos develop simply by division of a diploid cell. So the progenies produced are identical to the parent. In vegetative reproduction also progenies produced are identical to the parent.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6971,'biology',83,492,1008,'In sea -walnuts and comb -jellies the fertilization is','[{"text": "Internal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "External", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In sea-walnuts or comb-jellies, the fertilization is external.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6972,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Which of the metabolites is common to respiration -mediated breakdown of fats, carbohydrates and proteins?<br>','[{"text": "Acetyl CoA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pyruvic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fructose1.6-biphosphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose-6-Phosphate", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Acetyl CoA is he metabolite that is common to respiration by breakdown of fat, carbohydrate and protein. Fats are first broken down into glycerol and fatty acids, carbohydrates are converted into simple sugars like glucose. Proteins are converted into individual amino acids. Glycerol, fatty acids, simple sugars and amino acids are then converted into Acetyl CoA which enters Kreb\'s cycle',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6973,'biology',82,1265,3080,'When new cells added to the plant body by the activity of meristems is called as','[{"text": "Random growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Indirect growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Closed growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Open growth", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'When new cells are always added to the plant body by the activity of meristems is called as open growth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6974,'biology',8,158,336,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Asteraceae<br>B. Mango<br>C. Ficus<br>D. Achene</div><div class="column-right">P. Polyembryony<br>Q. Apomixis<br>R. Tiny seed<br>S. Strawberry</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R, B – P, C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – S, B – R, C – P, D – Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – P, B – R, C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – P, C – R, D – S", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A – Q, B – P, C – R, D – S',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6975,'biology',83,492,1008,'Choose the false option-','[{"text": "Sponges : Mostly asymmetrical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cnidaria, Ctenophora and larval Echinoderms : Radial symmetry", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Annelids, Arthropods, Molluscs and Chordates : Bilateral symmetry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Adult echinoderms exhibit radial symmetry.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6976,'biology',81,1044,2467,'In which one of the following processes $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is not released?<br>','[{"text": "Aerobic respiration in plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alcoholic fermentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aerobic respiration in animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lactate fermentation", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Lactic acid fermentation produces lactic acid only as pyruvic acid produced in glycolysis is directly reduced by NADH to form lactic acid, without producing carbon dioxide. <br>${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}\\mathop {{\\rm{COCOOH  +  }}}\\limits_{{\\rm{Pyruvic}}{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\rm{acid}}} {\\rm{NAD}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ $\\xrightarrow{\\begin{subarray}{l} \n  {\\text{Lactatedehy - }} \\\\ \n  {\\text{drogenase}} \n\\end{subarray} }$ <br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}\\mathop {{\\text{CHOHCOOH}}}\\limits_{{\\text{Lactic}}\\,{\\text{acid}}} {\\text{ + NAD}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6977,'biology',82,1266,3081,'The shape of leaves of juvenile plant differ in shape from those of mature plant in','[{"text": "Buttercup", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cotton", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Wheat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Banyan", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The leaves of the juvenile plant are different in shape from those in mature plantse e.g. Heterophylly in cotton, coriander and larkspur.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6978,'biology',8,158,336,'The process by which haploid embryo is formed from haploid egg without fertilization is called','[{"text": "Apospory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Agamospermy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vegetative reproduction", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Apospory is the production of gametophyte directly from diploid cells of the sporophytes without the spore formation Apogamy is a type of reproduction, occurring in some ferns, in which the sporophyte develops from the gametophyte without the fusion of gametes.<br>Vegetative reproduction is a form of asexual reproduction of a plant. Only one plant is involved and the offspring is the result of one parent.<br>Agamospermy is a asexual reproduction in which seeds are produced from unfertilized ovules.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6979,'biology',83,492,1008,'Select the correct one (s) for ctenophora-','[{"text": "They have similarities with cnidaria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have 8 external rows of ciliated comb plates for locomotion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bioluminescence", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6980,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Which of the following biomolecules is common to respiration mediated breakdown of fats, carbohydrates and proteins?<br>','[{"text": "Fructose 1,6-biphosphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pyruvic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acetyl CoA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glucose -6-Phosphate", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Carbohydrates are first converted into glucose before they are used for respiration. Proteins are being degraded by proteases to amino acids and depending on structure they enter pathways within Kreb\'s cycle as acetyl CoA or as Pyruvate. Fats are broken down into glycerol and fatty acids. If fatty acids are to be respired they would have degraded to acetyl CoA and enter the pathway. Thus acetyl CoA is the common metabolite of all three i.e., carbohydrates, proteins and fats.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7118,'biology',83,494,1010,'The first phylum to have a organ-system level of body organisation','[{"text": "Platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arthropoda", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aschelminthes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Annelida", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Roundworms are the first animals to have organ-system level of body organisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6982,'biology',8,158,336,'The phenomenon observed in some plants wherein parts of the sexual apparatus is used for forming embryos without fertilisation is called:','[{"text": "Parthenocarpy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apomixis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vegetative propagation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sexual reproduction.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When seeds are produced without fertilization, this phenomenon is called apomixes. In parthenocarpy, seeds are not produced which means embryos are not produced. Hence, option ‘2’ is the correct answer.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6983,'biology',83,492,1008,'i. Extracellular and intracellular digestion<br>ii. Exclusively marine, radially symmetrical, diploblastic, tissue level of organization<br>iii. Bisexual, external fertilization and indirect development<br>iv. No asexual reproduction<br>v. Presence of 8 comb plates<br>The above characters are shown by-','[{"text": "Ctenophora", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Porifera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cnidaria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rotifers", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The above characteristics represent the Phylum Ctenophora.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6984,'biology',81,1044,2467,'Respiratory enzymes occur in bacterium is located in','[{"text": "Plasma membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Golgi apparatus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Respiratory enzymes in bacterium are located on the plasma membrane.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6985,'biology',8,158,336,'The phenomenon wherein, the ovary develops into a fruit without fertilisation is called:','[{"text": "Parthenocarpy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Apomixis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Asexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The phenomenon wherein, the ovary develops into a fruit without fertilisation is called parthenocarpy',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6986,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Fill in the blanks____','[{"text": "A-Cell division, B- Differentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Differentiation, B- Maturation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Plasmatic growth, B- Maturation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A- Elongation, B- Maturation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The given flow chart represents sequence of the developmental process in a plant cell. In which missing labels are A- Plasmatic growth, B- Maturation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/82_6986_question_1.png'),
(6987,'biology',83,492,1008,'The following represents.','[{"text": "Adamsia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pleurobrachia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aurelia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Taenia", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The given diagram represents Pleurobrachia from Phylum Ctenophora.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_6987_question_1.png'),
(6988,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Oxidative phosphorylation is','[{"text": "Oxidation of phosphate group in ATP.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Formation of ATP by energy released from electrons removed during substrate oxidation.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Formation of ATP by transfer of phosphate group from a substrate to ADP.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Addition of phosphate group to ATP.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Oxidative phosphorylation is the process in which ATP is formed as a result of the transfer of electrons from NADH or $$\\mathrm{FADH}_{2}$$ to $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ by a series of electron carriers. This process, which takes place in mitochondria, is the major source of ATP in aerobic organisms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6989,'biology',8,158,336,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In apomixis, plants of new genetic variations are not produced.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In apomixis, reductional division \ntakes place','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In apomixis, mitotic division takes place.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6990,'biology',82,1266,3081,'The given diagram depicts cartoon of','[{"text": "Heterophylly in buttercup due to environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterophylly in coriander due to environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasticity in larkspur leaf due to life phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Elasticity in cotton due to life phase.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The given diagram depicts cartoon of plasticity in Larkspur leaf due to life phase',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/82_6990_question_1.png'),
