(6992,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Which statement is wrong for Kreb\'s cycle?<br>','[{"text": "There is one point in the cycle $$\\\\mathrm{FAD}^{+}$$that is reduced to $$\\\\mathrm{FADH}_{2}$$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "During conversion of succinyl CoA to succinic acid, a molecules of GTP is synthesised.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The cycle starts with condensation of acetyl group (acetyl CoA) with pyruvic acid to yield citric acid.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "There are three points in the cycle where $$\\\\mathrm{NAD}^{+}$$is reduced to $$\\\\mathrm{NADH}+\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Kreb\'s cycle starts with condensation of acetyl group (acetyl CoA) with oxalo acetic acid to yield citric acid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
