(6996,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Which of these statements is incorrect?<br>','[{"text": "Glycolysis operates as long as it is supplied with NAD that can pick up hydrogen atoms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycolysis occurs in cytosol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Enzymes of TCA cycle are present in mitochondrial matrix", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxidative phosphorylation takes place in outer mitochondrial membrane", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Oxidative phosphorylation takes place in inner mitochondrial membrane.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6997,'biology',8,152,322,'Flower is a modified shoot because','[{"text": "Epicalyx is present in some flowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In some flowers thalamus become\\nelongated and show distinct nodes and\\ninternodes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Essential organs are present in some\\nflowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flowers aggregate to form inflorescence", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During the season of flowering, the floral meristem is raised by the apical meristem. The axis of the stem becomes compressed, although the internodes stay near each other.\nRather leaves of different floral appendages\nappear from the node. From this , it can be\nconcluded that the flower is a modified shoot.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(6998,'biology',83,493,1009,'Number of germ layers present in the embryonic stage of platyhelminthes?','[{"text": "One", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Platyhelminthes is triploblastic in nature i.e. it bears 3 germinal layers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
