(7011,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Extrinsic factor for growth<br>B. Intrinsic factors for growth<br>C. Heterophylly in cotton, coriander, larkspur, buttercup</div><div class="column-right">P. Plasticity<br>Q. Light, temperature, water<br>R. Genetics and plant growth regulators</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Extrinsic factor in growth - Light, temperature, water Intrinsic factor in growth - Genetics and plant growth regulators<br>Heterophylly in Cotton, Coriander, Larkspur, Buttercup - Plasticity',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7012,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Which one of the following is not true regarding the release of energy during ATP synthesis through chemiosmosis? It involves :<br>','[{"text": "Breakdown of electron gradient", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Movement of protons across the membrane to the stroma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reduction of NADP to $$\\\\mathrm{NADPH}_{2}$$ on the stroma side of the membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Breakdown of proton gradient", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Breakdown of electron gradient is not true regarding the release of energy during ATP synthesis through chemiosmosis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7013,'biology',8,156,332,'Primary endosperm nucleus is formed by\nfusion of','[{"text": "Ovum and male gamete", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One polar nucleus and male gamete", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two polar nuclei and two male gametes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two polar nuclei and one male gamete", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Primary endosperm nucleus is formed\nby fusion of two polar nuclei and one male\ngamete. This is called triple fusion',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7014,'biology',83,493,1009,'An acoelomate animal with bilateral symmetry is','[{"text": "<i>Aurelia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Obelia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Taenia</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Physalia</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Platyhelminthes are acoelomate animals showing bilateral symmetry. Taenia is one of its examples. Platyhelminthes like Fasciola have 3 germinal layers and hence are triploblastic.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7015,'biology',82,1267,3082,'Which of the following is a characteristic of a PGR?','[{"text": "They are small", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Simple molecules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are of diverse chemical composition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The plant growth regulators (PGRs) are small, simple molecules of diverse chemical composition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7016,'biology',81,1043,2466,'What amount of energy is released from glucose during lactic acid fermentation','[{"text": "More than 18\\\\%", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "About $$10 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Less than $$7 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Approximately $$15 \\\\%$$<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Less than $$7 \\%$$ of energy is released from glucose during lactic acid fermentation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7017,'biology',8,154,328,'Large, colourful, fragrant flowers with nectar are seen in','[{"text": "Insect pollinated plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bird pollinated plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bat pollinated plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wind pollinated plants", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Large, colourful, fragrant flowers with\nnectar attract biotic pollinators (insects), thus,\nthey are seen in insect pollinated plants.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7018,'biology',83,493,1009,'Which one of the following kind of animals are triploblastic?','[{"text": "<i>Fasciola</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sponge", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flatworms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Platyhelminthes (flatworms) like Fasciola have 3 germinal layers and hence are triploblastic.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7019,'biology',82,1267,3082,'Which of the following are phytohormones?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{ABA, IAA}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{GA}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{ABA}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The plant growth regulators (PGRs) are small, simple molecules of diverse chemical composition. They could be indole compounds (indole-3-acetic acid, IAA); adenine derivatives (N6 -furfurylamino purine, kinetin), derivatives of carotenoids (abscisic acid, ABA); terpenes (gibberellic acid, GA3 ) or gases (ethylene, ${{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ ). Plant growth regulators are variously described as plant growth substances, plant hormones or phytohormones in literature',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7020,'biology',81,1042,2465,'What is the net gain of ATP when each molecule of glucose is converted to two molecules of pyruvic acid?','[{"text": "Six", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Eight", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Net gain of ATP when one molecule of glucose is partially oxidized to 2 molecules of pyruvic acid is two.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7021,'biology',8,154,328,'What is the function of tassels in the corn\ncob?','[{"text": "To attract insects", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "To trap pollen grains", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "To disperse pollen grains", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "To protect seeds", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Tassels in the corn cob represents stigma\nand style which wave in the wind to trap pollen\ngrains.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7022,'biology',83,493,1009,'In platyhelminthes, digestive system is incomplete because','[{"text": "It has suckers and hooks in parasitic form", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It absorbs food from general body surface", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It has only one opening that serves as mouth and anus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In platyhelminthes, the digestive system is incomplete because it has only one opening that serves as mouth and anus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7023,'biology',82,1267,3082,'$\\mathrm{ABA}$ is a derivative of?','[{"text": "Adenine derivatives", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Terpenes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anthocyanin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carotenoids", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Abscisic acid, ABA is a derivative of carotenoids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7024,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Read the Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct options given below:<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> ATP is used at two steps in glycolysis.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> First ATP is used in converting glucose into glucose-6-phosphate and second ATP is used in conversion of fructose-6-phosphate into fructose-1, 6-diphosphate.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are  true and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is false but  Reason is true", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'ATP in glycolysis is used at two steps of conversion that are<br>Glucose → Glucose-6-phosphate<br>Fructose-6-phosphate → Fructose-1,6-bisphosphate<br>The reason of the utilisation of ATP is for phosphorylation the substrates.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7025,'biology',8,156,332,'In angiosperm, the haploid, diploid and triploid structures of a fertilized embryo sac sequentially are :','[{"text": "Synergids, primary endosperm nucleus\\nand zygote", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antipodals, synergids, and primary\\nendosperm nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synergids, zygote and primary endosperm\\nnucleus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Synergids, antipodals and polar nuclei", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Synergids are the cells of gametophyte and\nhence these are haploid. Zygote is formed by\nfusion of two gametes and thus it is diploid.\nPrimary endosperm nucleus is formed by the\nfusion of diploid secondary nucleus with a\nmale gamete.\nTherefore, it is triploid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7026,'biology',83,493,1009,'Body plan of a <i>Fasciola</i> is','[{"text": "Cell aggregate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blind sac", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tube within tube", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Fasciola possesses blind sac body plan due to the presence of an incomplete digestive system. It bears only one opening that acts as both mouth and anus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7027,'biology',82,1267,3082,'$\\mathrm{N}_{6}$-furfurylamino purine is a derivative of?','[{"text": "Cytosine derivatives", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Terpenes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anthocyanin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adenine", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'N6 -furfurylamino purine is a derivative of adenine.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7028,'biology',8,154,329,'Which one of the following is not a device to promote cross-pollination?','[{"text": "Herkogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cleistogamy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dichogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterostyly.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The flowers that do not open on maturity and remain closed are called cleistogamous flowers.It promotes autogamy and assured seed set, seen in viola, oxalis, commelina.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7029,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Match Column I with Column II :<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Oxidative decarboxylation<br>B. Glycolysis<br>C. Oxidative phosphorylation<br>D. Tricarboxylic acid cycle</div><div class="column-right">P. Citrate synthase<br>Q. Pyruvate dehydrogenase<br>R. Electron transport system<br>S. EMP pathway</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R, B – S, C – Q, D – P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – S, C – P, D – R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – R, B – P, C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – S, C – R, D – P", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pyruvate, which is formed by the glycolysis in the cytosol, after it enters mitochondrial matrix undergoes oxidative decarboxylation catalyzed by pyruvate dehydrogenase.<br>The scheme of glycolysis was given by Gustav Embden, Otto Meyrhof and J. Parnas, and is often referred to as the EMP pathway.<br>In electron transport system, the energy of oxidation-reduction is utilized for the production of proton gradient required for phosphorylation, thus, this process is also called oxidative phosphorylation.<br>The TCA (tricarboxylic acid cycle) starts with the condensation of acetyl group with oxaloacetic acid to give citric acid. The reaction is catalysed by the enzyme citrate synthase.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7031,'biology',82,1267,3082,'Which one includes growth inhibitors?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{ABA, cytokinin}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{ABA}, \\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{4}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{GA, IAA}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The PGRs of the other group called plant growth inhibitors play an important role in plant responses to wounds and stresses of biotic and abiotic origin. They are also involved in various growth inhibiting activities such as dormancy and abscission. The PGR abscisic acid belongs to this group. The gaseous PGR, ethylene, is largely an inhibitor of growth activities.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7032,'biology',8,153,324,'Sporopollenin, a chemical substance is found in:','[{"text": "Exine of pollen grain", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Intine of pollen grain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tapetum of anther", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endothecium of anther", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Sporopollenin is one of the most chemically inert biological polymers. It is a major component of the touch outer (exine) walls of plant spores and pollen grains. It is chemically very stable and is usually well preserved in soils and sediments.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7033,'biology',81,1049,2472,'In succulent plants like <i>Opuntia</i>, the RQ value will be:','[{"text": "Infinity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zero", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Less than 1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More than 1", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The respiratory quotient, is defined as the volume of carbon dioxide released over the volume of oxygen absorbed during respiration and is denoted as RQ. In some succulent plants like Opuntia, Bryophyllum, etc carbohydrates are incompletely oxidised to organic acids in dark without the evolution of , hence the value of RQ remains zero.<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{6}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{12}}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{ + 3}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}\\\\\n{{\\rm{Glucose}}}\n\\end{array} \\to \\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{4}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{6}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{5}}}}\\\\\n{{\\rm{Malic}}\\,{\\rm{acid}}}\n\\end{array}{\\rm{ + 3}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$<br>${\\rm{RQ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{Vol}}{\\rm{.}}\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{{{\\rm{Vol}}{\\rm{.}}\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{O}}}{{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7034,'biology',83,493,1009,'Alimentary canal is incomplete in','[{"text": "Arthropoda", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nematoda", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Annelida", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Members of Phylum Platyhelminthes bear an incomplete alimentary canal with only one opening that acts both as mouth as well as anus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7035,'biology',82,1267,3082,'Which of the following is shown by growth promoters?<BR>1) Cell division<BR>2) Cell enlargement<BR>3) Pattern formation<BR>4) Dormancy and abscission<BR>5) Tropic growth and flowering<br>6) Fruiting and seed formation','[{"text": "$1,2,3$ only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1,2,3,5,6$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$1,2,4,5$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1,3,4,5,6$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'One group of PGRs known as plant growth promoters are involved in growth promoting activities, such as cell division, cell enlargement, pattern formation, tropic growth, flowering, fruiting and seed formation, e.g., auxins, gibberellins and cytokinins.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7036,'biology',8,154,328,'Match the entries in Column I(Name of pollination) with those of Column II(Type of pollination) and choose the correct answer.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Cleistogamy<br>B. Geitonogamy<br>C. Entomophily<br>D. Xenogamy</div><div class="column-right">P. Insect\npollination<br>Q. Bud pollination<br>R. Pollination\nbetween\nflowers in the\nsame plant<br>S. Wind pollination<br>T. Cross pollination</div></div>','[{"text": "A - R, B - P, C - T, D - Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P, B - T, C - Q, D - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - R, C - P, D - T", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - T, B - S, C - R, D - Q", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<br>• Anthers and stigma in intersexual or perfect flowers ripen much before the opening of the buds. Thus, self-pollination or cleisto gamy is a necessity for them.<br>• Transfer of pollen grain from the anther of the flower of one plant to the stigma of another flower of the same plant is known as geitonogamy.<br>• Insect pollination is also known as entomophily and such flowers are called entomophilous flowers.<br>•Transfer of pollen grains from the anther of one flower to the stigma of flower of a different plant is known as xenogamy. Hence, it is crosspollination.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7037,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Oxalosuccinic acid, an intermediary compound of Kreb\'s cycle is a:','[{"text": "4 carbon compound", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 carbon compound", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5 carbon compound", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6 carbon compound", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Oxalosuccinic acid is an unstable 6-carbon intermediate in the tricarboxylic acid cycle.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7038,'biology',83,493,1009,'Which process is likely to occur in tapeworms?','[{"text": "Aerobic respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycolysis only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ETS only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaerobic respiration", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In tapeworm, anaerobic respiration occurs due to the lack of oxygen inside the host\'s body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7039,'biology',82,1267,3082,'Which one includes growth promoters?','[{"text": "Auxin, cytokinin, ${\\\\rm{ABA}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Auxin, cytokinin, $\\\\mathrm{GA}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{ABA}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{GA}, \\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plant growth promoters are involved in growth promoting activities, such as cell division, cell enlargement, pattern formation, tropic growth, flowering, fruiting and seed formation, e.g., auxins, gibberellins and cytokinins.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7040,'biology',8,153,326,'The embryo sac of an angiosperm is made up of:','[{"text": "8 cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "7 cells and 8 nuclei", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "8 nuclei", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8 cells and 7 nuclei", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A typical angiospermic mature embryo sac or megagametophyte is 7-celled (central cell has two nuclei) and 8-nucleate. An egg surrounded by 2 synergids at the micropilar end of the ovule, 3 antipodals at the chalazal end of the ovule, 2 polar nuclei of the central cell at the centre of the embryo sac.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7075,'biology',82,1267,3083,'F.W. Went isolated auxins from the','[{"text": "Coleoptiles of oat seedlings", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coleoptiles of rice seedlings.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungal pathogen.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coleoptiles of canary grass.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Auxin was isolated by F.W. Went from tips of coleoptiles of oat seedlings.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7041,'biology',81,1046,2469,'The following is a scheme showing electron transport system. Identify the electron carrier molecules indicated as A and B. Choose the correct option.','[{"text": "A - Cytochrome C; B - Coenzyme Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Coenzyme Q; B - Cytochrome C", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - FMN; B - Fe-S protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Fe-S protein; B - FMN", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/biology/81_7041_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2010,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_7041_question_1.png'),
(7042,'biology',83,493,1009,'Excretory organ of <i>Planaria</i> is','[{"text": "Nephridia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flame cell/solenocytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metanephridia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renette cell", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Excretory organ of Planaria is flame cells / solenocytes/ protonephridia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7043,'biology',82,1267,3082,'Which of the following is not a plant growth promoter?','[{"text": "Auxins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gibberellins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethylene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abscisic acid", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Abscicic acid is not a plant growth promoter it is a plant growth inhibitor.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7044,'biology',8,152,322,'The diagram given below denotes the various parts of a typical flower. Identify the labelled parts A, B, C and D and choose the correct option:','[{"text": "A - Petals; B - Sepals; C - Stamens; D Pistil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Sepals; B - Pistil; C - Petals; D Stamens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Sepals; B - Pistil; C - Stamens; D Petals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Sepals; B - Petals; C - Pistil; D Stamens", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The four whorls of a typical flower are calyx (sepals), corolla (petals), androecium (stamens) and gynoecium (pistils/carpels). Sepals labelled as A and petals labelled as D form the outer whorls. Stamens labelled as C and pistils labelled as B form the inner whorls. The inner two whorls are the reproductive organs in which the gametes are formed. Hence, flowers serve as sites of sexual reproduction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/8_7044_question_1.png'),
(7045,'biology',81,1044,2467,'Pyruvate dehydrogenase complex needed for the conversion of pyruvic acid to acetyl CoA is located in:','[{"text": "Intermembranal space of mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Matrix of mitochondria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Grana of chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Acetyl CoA is formed from pyruvate by its oxidative decarboxylation by the enzyme pyruvate dehydrogenase, in the mitochondrial matrix.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7046,'biology',83,493,1009,'Flame cells help in____________ in platyhelminthes','[{"text": "Excretion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osmoregulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Digestion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Specialised cells called flame cells (also known as solenocytes) help in osmoregulation and excretion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7047,'biology',82,1267,3082,'Find out the<br>i. Gaseous hormone from the following.<br>ii. Hormone that could fit either of the groups, but it is largely an inhibitor of growth activities','[{"text": "Ethylene, auxins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethylene, gibberellins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokinins, ethylene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethylene, ethylene", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The gaseous PGR, ethylene, could fit in both groups called plant growth promoter and plant growth inhibitor, but it is largely an inhibitor of growth activities.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7048,'biology',8,156,332,'With respect to angiosperms, identify the incorrect pair from the following','[{"text": "Antipodals - 2n", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vegetative cell of male gametophyte-n", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Primary endosperm nucleus - 3n", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cells of nucellus of ovule - 2n", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The three haploid cells situated at the chalazal end are called antipodals or antipodal cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7049,'biology',81,1043,2466,'During lactic acid fermentation:','[{"text": "Neither $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ is used, nor $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ is liberated", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ is used, $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ is liberated", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ is not used, $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ is liberated", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ is used, $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ is not liberated", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Lactic acid fermentation creates ATP, which is a molecule both animals and bacteria need for energy, when there is no oxygen present. This process breaks down glucose into two lactate molecules. There is no release of Carbondioxide.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7050,'biology',83,493,1009,'Following organism does not have organ system level of organization :','[{"text": "Liver fluke", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ascaris", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Silver fish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leech", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Liver fluke belongs to phylum\n\nPlatyhelminthes which exhibits organ level of organisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7051,'biology',82,1267,3083,'The discovery of PGRs started with the observation of the following scientists:','[{"text": "Charles Darwin and his son Francis Darwin.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Charles Darwin and his son James Darwin.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Charles Darwin and his grandson Francis Darwin.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The discovery of each of the five major groups of PGRs have been accidental. All this started with the observation of Charles Darwin and his son Francis Darwin when they observed that the coleoptiles of canary grass responded to unilateral illumination by growing towards the light source (phototropism). After a series of experiments, it was concluded that the tip of coleoptile was the site of transmittable influence that caused the bending of the entire coleoptile. Auxin was isolated by F.W. Went from tips of coleoptiles of oat seedlings.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7052,'biology',8,154,329,'In castor and maize plants:','[{"text": "Autogamy is prevented but not geitonogamy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both autogamy and geitonogamy are prevented", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male and female flowers are borne by different plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The anthers and stigma are placed at different positions to encourage cross pollination", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'If a plant bears both male and female flowers on the same plant, it is called monoecious (e.g., cucurbits, maize, castor). In such cases, autogamy is prevented but geitonogamy can take place.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7053,'biology',81,1045,2468,'The site of Kreb\'s cycle is:','[{"text": "Cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondrial matrix", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Intermembrane space of mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Racker\'s particles", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The Kreb\'s cycle or tricarboxylic acid (TCA) cycle the oxidation of the acetyl group of acetyl CoA to $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$. All enzymes of Krebs\' cycle are located in the mitochondrial matrix except one, succinate dehydrogenase which is located in the inner mitochondrial membrane in eukaryotes. Thus, it takes plac in the mitochondrial matrix.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7054,'biology',83,493,1009,'Name the platyhelminth which possesses high regeneration capacity?','[{"text": "<i>Fasciola</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Taenia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Hookworm</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Planaria</i>.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Some members of Platyhelminthes like Planaria possess high regeneration capacity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7055,'biology',82,1267,3083,'Charles Darwin used which plant in the discovery of plant growth regulator?','[{"text": "Larkspur", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Buttercup", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tobacco", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Canary grass", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The discovery of each of the five major groups of PGRs have been accidental. All this started with the observation of Charles Darwin and his son Francis Darwin when they observed that the coleoptiles of canary grass responded to unilateral illumination by growing towards the light source (phototropism). After a series of experiments, it was concluded that the tip of coleoptile was the site of transmittable influence that caused the bending of the entire coleoptile. Auxin was isolated by F.W. Went from tips of coloptiles of oat seedlings.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7056,'biology',8,153,324,'The germ pores in the pollen grain are the regions:','[{"text": "That can withstand high temperature and strong acids and alkalies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Through which sperms are released into the female gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Which are made up of lignin and suberin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Which lack sporopollenin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The exine is thin at several places and consists of apertures known as germ pores. At these places, sporopollenin is absent. The function of germ pores is to allow pollen tubes to emerge during germination of pollen grain.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7057,'biology',81,1043,2466,'Select a suitable name for this process.<br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n{\\rm{(}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{6}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{12}}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{ + 2ADP + 2Pi}} \\to \\\\\n\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{OH + 2ATP + 2C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}} \\uparrow )\n\\end{array}$','[{"text": "Alcoholic fermentation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Photorespiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lactate fermentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aerobic respiration", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In yeast, anaerobic respiration occurs in sugary solution causing fermentation. Pyruvate undergoes oxidative decarboxylation in the presence of enzyme pyruvate decarboxylase to yield $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ and acetaldehyde, which is then reduced by NADH in the presence of dehydrogenase to yield $\\mathrm{NADH}^{+}$and ethanol.<br>Glucose $\\rightarrow$ Pyruvate $\\rightarrow$ Acetaldehyde$\\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{NADH}+\\mathrm{H}^{+}}$Ethanol $+\\mathrm{CO}_{2}+\\mathrm{NAD}^{+}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7058,'biology',83,493,1009,'Given are the four matches of phyla with their characteristics\ni. Coelenterata - Nematocytes\nii. Porifera - Choanocytes\niii. Ctenophora - Solenocytes\niv. Platyhelminthes - Nephrocytes\nMark the option that has both incorrect matches<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "i, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii, iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Platyhelminthes bear solenocytes while nephrocytes are found in Arthropods. Hence, (iii) and (iv) are incorrect.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7059,'biology',82,1267,3083,'Hormone involved in phototropism is','[{"text": "Ethylene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gibberlin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Auxin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2, 4-D", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Auxin hormone is involved in phototropism, i.e. the bending of plant towards the direction of light.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7060,'biology',8,157,335,'In this diagram showing the L.S. of an embryo of grass, identify the answer having the correct combination of alphabets with the right part:','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}<br>{\\\\rm{A}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Root}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{cap,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{B}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Coleoptile,}}\\\\\\\\<br>{\\\\rm{C}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Scutellum,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{D  - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Coleorhiza,}}\\\\\\\\<br>{\\\\rm{E}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Epiblast, }}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{F}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Shoot\\\\,apex}}<br>\\\\end{array}$<br><br><br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}<br>{\\\\rm{A}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Shoot}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{apex,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{B}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Epiblast,}}\\\\\\\\<br>{\\\\rm{C}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Coleorhiza,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{D}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Scutellum,}}\\\\\\\\<br>{\\\\rm{E}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Coleoptile,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{F}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Radicle}}<br>\\\\end{array}$<br><br><br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}<br>{\\\\rm{A}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Epiblast,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{B}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Scutellum,}}\\\\\\\\<br>{\\\\rm{C}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Coleoptile,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{D}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Radicle,}}\\\\\\\\<br>{\\\\rm{E}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Coleorhiza,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{F}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Shoot}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{apex}}<br>\\\\end{array}$<br><br><br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}<br>{\\\\rm{A}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Epiblast,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{B}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Radicle,}}\\\\\\\\<br>{\\\\rm{C}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Coleoptile,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{D}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ -  Scutellum,}}\\\\\\\\<br>{\\\\rm{E}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Coleorhiza,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{F}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Shoot}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{apex}}<br>\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/biology/8_7060_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/8_7060_question_1.png'),
(7061,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Oxidative decarboxylation occurs during the formation of:','[{"text": "Citric acid and Succinic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Citric acid and Oxaloacetic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acetyl CoA and Succinyl CoA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oxaloacetic acid and Oxalosuccinic acid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Acetyl CoA is formed form pyruvate by its oxidative decarboxylation<br>Pyruvicacid $+\\mathrm{CoA}+\\mathrm{NAD}^{+} \\xrightarrow[\\text { Pyruvate dehydrogenase }]{\\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}}$<br>AcetylCoA $+\\mathrm{CO}_{2}+\\mathrm{NADH}+\\mathrm{H}^{+}$<br>Oxidative decarboxylation of<br>${\\rm{\\alpha  - Ketoglutarate}}\\,{\\rm{takes}}\\,{\\rm{place}}\\,{\\rm{to}}\\,{\\rm{form}}\\,{\\rm{succinyl}}\\,{\\rm{CoA}}$<br>${\\rm{\\alpha  - Ketoglutarate}}\\,{\\rm{ + NA}}{{\\rm{D}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{ + CoASH}}$<br>$\\xrightarrow[{\\alpha  - {\\text{Ketoglutarate}}\\,{\\text{dehydrogenase}}}]{{{\\text{ TPP  Lipoic acid M}}{{\\text{g}}^{{\\text{2  +  }}}}}}$<br>${\\rm{Succinyl CoA + NADH + }}{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{ + C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7062,'biology',83,493,1009,'Which of these is an endoparasite?','[{"text": "<i>Taenia saginata</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Taenia solium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Fasciola hepatica</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Taenia and Fasciola both genuses belong to Phylum Platyhelminthes. This phylum is characterised by organisms that are endoparasites.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7063,'biology',82,1267,3083,'In coleoptile tissue, auxin is','[{"text": "Transported because it is used where it is made", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transported by diffusion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transported from base to tip by as mosses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Produced by growing apices of stem which migrate to the region of its action", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Coleoptile tissue, auxin is produced by growing apices of stem which migrates to the region of its action.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7064,'biology',8,155,331,'Continued self-pollination results in:','[{"text": "Inbreeding depression", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Self incompatibility", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Formation of unisexual flowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametes loose vigour", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Majority of flowering plants produce hermaphrodite flowers and pollen grains are likely to come in contact with the stigma of the same flower continued self-pollination results in decrease in vitality and productivity in the offspring known as inbreeding depression.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7065,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Given below is an electron acceptor. Mention its status, which is labelled as (A).<br>$\\mathrm{Cyt}^{++} \\xrightarrow{2 \\mathrm{e}} \\mathrm{Cyt}^{+++} \\text {(A) }$','[{"text": "Oxidised", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Reduced", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phosphorylation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrated", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Oxidation is a process in which electrons are lost. The product formed by losing electrons is called oxidised product.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7066,'biology',83,493,1009,'Parasitic forms of platyhelminthes have well developed','[{"text": "Sensory system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Digestive system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reproductive system", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Platyhelminthes generally bear a complex reproductive system as they have to reproduce under hostile conditions inside the host\'s body. Usually the presence of numerous testes but only one or two ovaries is exhibited.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7067,'biology',82,1267,3083,'Coleoptiles responded to ____','[{"text": "Soil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Touch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Light", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Charles Darwin and his son Francis Darwin observed that the coleoptiles of canary grass responded to unilateral illumination by growing towards the light source (phototropism).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7068,'biology',8,157,335,'Which among these is not a post fertilization event?','[{"text": "Gametogenesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Embryogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fruit formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed formation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Gametogenesis is a pre-fertilization event in which cells undergo meiosis to form gametes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7069,'biology',81,1043,2466,'Choose the correct combination of labelling the molecules involved in the pathway of anaerobic respiration in Yeast.','[{"text": "A - Ethanol, B - $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{C}$ - Acetaldehyde", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$, B - Ethanol, $\\\\mathrm{C}$ - Acetaldehyde", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Acetaldehyde, $\\\\mathrm{B}$ - $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{C}$ - Ethanol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Ethanol, B - Acetaldehyde, $\\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{A}$ - Ethanol, $\\mathrm{B}$ - Acetaldehyde, $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_7069_question_1.png'),
(7070,'biology',83,493,1009,'Which of the following does not belong to phylum-Platyhelminthes?','[{"text": "<i>Fasciola</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Taenia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Hookworm</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Planaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Hookworm belongs to phylum Aschelminthes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7071,'biology',82,1267,3083,'As a response to stimuli the coleoptiles caused ____','[{"text": "Bending", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Flowering", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Budding", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'As a response to stimuli the coleoptiles caused bending towards light.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7072,'biology',8,154,327,'Which of the following characters is not required for autogamy?','[{"text": "Flowers require synchrony in pollen release and stigma maturation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anthers and stigma should lie close to each other.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flowers should be bisexual.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Required pollination agents.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Transfer of pollen grains from the anther of a flower to the stigma of the same flower is known as autogamy. Hence, it is selfpollination. In this, only one bisexual flower is involved. The stigma should be receptive at the time of pollen release. Stamens and carpels should mature at the same time. The stigma and anther should be located close to each other to allow self-pollination. It does not require any pollination agents.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7073,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Hibernating animals have tissues containing mitochondria with a membrane protein that accelerates electron transport while blocking the synthesis of ATP. What is the consequence of this?','[{"text": "Energy is saved because glycolysis and the citric acid cycle shuts down.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The energy of respiration is converted into heat.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hibernating animals can synthesize fat instead of wasting energy of respiration.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pyruvate is converted to lactic acid by anaerobic fermentation.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In mammals there are two types of adipose tissues: white and brown. Brown fat cells contain a great many mitochondria, and brown adipose tissue is well supplied by blood capillaries. Brown adipose tissue produces considerable amount of heat, because their lipids are respired with little or no ATP formation; most energy is released as heat. This heat is transported in the blood to the body organs.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7074,'biology',83,493,1009,'Flatworms resemble <i>Ctenoplana</i> in','[{"text": "Body plan", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Symmetry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coelom", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Germ layers", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ctenoplana (Cnidaria) and flatworms are both acoelomate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7076,'biology',8,153,324,'Among the following statements related to pollens, choose the correct one.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In $40 \\%$ of angiosperms pollen grains are shed at 3-celled stage.<br></div><div class="column-right">Intine is made of cellulose and pectin and it is discontinuous with germ pores.</div></div>','[{"text": "Both statements A and B are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements A and B are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct and Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect and Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In some species (about 40%), this division occurs before the release of pollen from the anther. These cells are three- celled when the pollen grain is shed. The inner layer, intine is thin and continuous. It is deposited by the cytoplasm like the primary cell wall.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7077,'biology',81,1042,2465,'The number of ATP molecules utilized for the breakdown of one molecule of glucose during glycolysis is:','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The net reaction of glycolysis for one molecule of glucose is:<br>Glucose $+2 \\mathrm{ADP}+2 \\mathrm{Pi}+2 \\mathrm{NAD}^{+} \\rightarrow 2$ Pyruvate + $2 \\mathrm{ATP}+2 \\mathrm{NADH}+2 \\mathrm{H}^{+}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7078,'biology',83,493,1009,'Which of the followng is true about phylumplatyhelminthes','[{"text": "Presence of sucking mouth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mostly free-living in nature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fertilisation is internal and development is through many larval stages", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Most Platyhelminthes are parasitic in nature.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7079,'biology',82,1267,3083,'<i>Gibberella fujikuroi</i> causes which disease in wheat plants?','[{"text": "Foolish seeding", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bakane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Gibberella fujikuroi causes bakane in rice, not in wheat.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7080,'biology',8,153,324,'When pollen grain is shed at 3-celled stage, name the cells it contains.','[{"text": "1 vegetative cell and 2 male gametes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2 vegetative cells and 1 male gamete", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 generative cells and 1 male gamete", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 male gametes and 1 generative cell", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pollen grain contains the male gametes that must reach the female ovum to produce a seed. When it is shed in the three celled stage it has the following cells: One vegetative cell and two male gametes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7081,'biology',81,1045,2468,'During Citric Acid cycle, the various organic acid undergo decarboxylation. Which of the following organic acids of the above cycle have $4 \\mathrm{C}, 5 \\mathrm{C}$ and $6 \\mathrm{C}$ respectively?','[{"text": "Oxaloacetic acid, Citric acid and Succinic acid.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Succinic acid, $\\\\alpha$-Ketoglutaric acid and Citric acid.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pyruvic acid, Malic acid and $\\\\alpha$ -<br>Ketoglutaric acid.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pyruvic acid, $\\\\alpha$-Ketoglutaric acid and Citric acid.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Succinic acid-4-C, alpha- ketoglutaric acid - 5C , Citric acid - 6-C',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7082,'biology',83,493,1009,'What is common amongst tapeworm, liver fluke and planarian?','[{"text": "They are all parasites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are all unsegmented, acoemolate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are dorso-ventrally flattened", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'All three of these organisms are parasitic worms that possess an unsegmented and dorsoventrally flattened body. Platyhelminthes are acoelomates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7083,'biology',8,154,327,'Even in the absence of pollinators, assured seed set will be there in:','[{"text": "Chasmogamous flowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Geitonogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cleistogamous flowers", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Xenogamy", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The stigma and anther should be located close to each other to allow self-pollination. The flowers that open after maturation or anthesis and expose their stamen and stigma are called chasmogamous flowers. the flowers that do not open on maturity and remain closed are called cleistogamous flowers.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7084,'biology',82,1267,3083,'Who reported that the symptoms reappeared in uninfected plants treated with sterile filtrate of gibberella?','[{"text": "Charles Darwin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "F. Skoog", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "F.W. Went", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "E. Kurosawa", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'E. Kurosawa (1926) reported the appearance of symptoms of the disease in rice seedlings when they were treated with sterile filtrates of the fungus. The active substances were later identified as gibberellic acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7085,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Match the location of the cell given in Column I with its function in Column II<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Mitochondrial matrix<br>B. Cytoplasm<br>C. ${{\\rm{F}}_0}$ and ${{\\rm{F}}_1}$<br>D. Inner mitochondrial membrane</div><div class="column-right">P. Kreb’s cycle<br>Q. ETC<br>R. Glycolysis<br>S. ATP synthesis</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{P} ; \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{R} ; \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{S} ; \\mathrm{D}-\\mathrm{Q}$',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7086,'biology',83,493,1009,'Match the columns I and II<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <em>Taenia</em><br>B. <em>Fasciola</em><br>C. <em>Pleurobrachia</em></div><div class="column-right">P. Ctenophora<br>Q. Tapeworm<br>R. Liver fluke</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$,", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. <em>Taenia</em> - Q. Tapeworm<br>B. <em>Fasciola</em> - R. Liver fluke<br>C. <em>Pleurobrachia</em> - P. Ctenophora',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7087,'biology',8,154,329,'In some plants, stigma and anther mature at different times because:','[{"text": "It attracts pollinators", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "If facilitates self-pollination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It prevents cross pollination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It facilitates cross pollination", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In dichogamy, the male and female parts of a bisexual flower mature at different times and xenogamy (cross-pollination) is favored. If the stamens mature before the pistil, the condition is known as protandry, while if the carpels mature before stamens, the condition is known as protogyny.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7088,'biology',82,1267,3083,'Bacterial pathogen responsible for foolish seedling disease of rice seedlings is','[{"text": "<i>Gibberella kurosawa.</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Gibberella fujikuroi.</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Gibberella moniliformae.</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The \'bakanae\' (foolish seedling) disease of rice seedlings, was caused by a fungal pathogen Gibberella fujikuroi.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7089,'biology',81,1049,2472,'Respiratory quotient of glucose is','[{"text": "0.9", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.0", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.7", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Respiratory quotient of glucose is 1.0 .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7090,'biology',83,493,1009,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <em>Taenia</em><br>B. <em>Planaria</em><br>C. <em>Pleurobrachia</em> <br>D. <em>Aurelia</em></div><div class="column-right">P. High regeneration capacity<br>Q. Bioluminesce-nce<br>R. Hooks and suckers<br>S. Gastrovascular system</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. <em>Taenia</em> - R. Hooks and suckers<br>B. <em>Planaria </em>- P. High regeneration capacity<br>C. <em>Pleurobrachia</em> - Q. Bioluminescence<br>D. <em>Aurelia</em> - S. Water vascular system',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7091,'biology',82,1267,3083,'Miller observed callus from which plant?','[{"text": "Tomato", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tobacco", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rice plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oats", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'F. Skoog and his co-workers observed that from the internodal segments of tobacco stems the callus (a mass of undifferentiated cells) proliferated only if, in addition to auxins the nutrients medium was supplemented with one of the following: extracts of vascular tissues, yeast extract, coconut milk or DNA. Miller et al. (1955), later identified and crystallised the cytokinesis promoting active substance that they termed kinetin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7092,'biology',8,158,336,'Now-a-days agricultural practice is expensive to the farmers as they need to purchase hybrid seeds every year. Which of the following strategies can be employed to overcome this problem?','[{"text": "Synthetic seeds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Production of Apomictic seeds", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Conventional plant breeding", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parthenocarpy", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Apomixis is a type of asexual reproduction that resembles sexual reproduction. In this, seeds are produced without fertilization. Hence, all the individuals produced apomictically are gentically similar to the parent. It would drastically reduce the cost of hybrid production, so that plant breeders produce new varieties of seeds more quickly and more cheaply.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7093,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Match the compounds given in Column-I with the number of carbon atoms present in them which are listed under Column II. Choose the answer which gives the correct combination of alphabets of the two columns.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Oxaloacetate<br>B. Phosphoglyceraldehyde<br>C. Isocitrate<br>D. ${\\rm{\\alpha  - }}$Ketoglutarate</div><div class="column-right">P. 6-C compound<br>Q. 5-C compound<br>R. 4-C compound<br>S. 3-C compound</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{T} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{T} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'• Oxaloacetic acid $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{4} \\mathrm{H}_{4} \\mathrm{O}_{5}\\right)$ is a<br>4-Carbon compound.<br> • Phosphoglyceraldehyde $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{3} \\mathrm{H}_{7} \\mathrm{O}_{6}\\right)$ is a 3Carbon compuond.<br> • Isocitrate $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{7} \\mathrm{O}_{6}\\right)$ is a 6-Carbon compuond.<br> • $\\alpha$-Ketoglutarate $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{5} \\mathrm{H}_{6} \\mathrm{O}_{5}\\right)$ is a 5 -carbon compound.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7094,'biology',83,494,1010,'Aschelminthes are usually','[{"text": "Dioecious", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hermaphrodites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monoecious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homosexual", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In Aschelminths, sexes are separate (dioecious), i.e., males and females are distinct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7095,'biology',82,1267,3083,'Kinetin -identified and crystallised by','[{"text": "Darwin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cousins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "E Kurosawa", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Skoog and Miller", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'F. Skoog and his co-workers observed that from the internodal segments of tobacco stems the callus (a mass of undifferentiated cells) proliferated only if, in addition to auxins the nutrients medium was supplemented with one of the following: extracts of vascular tissues, yeast extract, coconut milk or DNA. Miller et al. (1955), later identified and crystallised the cytokinesis promoting active substance that they termed kinetin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7106,'biology',83,494,1010,'Body plan in aschelminthes is','[{"text": "Cell aggregate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tube within a tube", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Blind sac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Aschelminthes possesses a complete digestive system consisting of two openings, mouth and anus. This type of body plan is known as tube within tube.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7096,'biology',8,155,331,'Identify the correct order of steps involved in artificial hybridization in plants.','[{"text": "Artificial pollination $\\\\rightarrow$ Emasculation $\\\\rightarrow$ Rebagging $\\\\rightarrow$ Bagging", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rebagging $\\\\rightarrow$ Artificial pollination $\\\\rightarrow$ Bagging $\\\\rightarrow$ Emasculation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Emasculation $\\\\rightarrow$ Bagging $\\\\rightarrow$ Artificial pollination $\\\\rightarrow$ Rebagging", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bagging $\\\\rightarrow$ Artificial pollination $\\\\rightarrow$ Rebagging $\\\\rightarrow$ Emasculation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Artificial hybridization of plant involves following steps:<br>• Anthers or stamens are removed, or pollen grains are killed in a bisexual flower of a plant to be used as the female parent in a cross, a process called emasculation.<br>• Emasculated flower is immediately bagged to avoid pollination by any foreign pollen grains. These bags are made up of butter paper, fine cloth or polythene depending on the inflorescence. Bagged flowers are then tagged.<br>• Mature and fertile pollen grains are collected from male parent, bag is opened, and pollen grains are dusted on receptive stigma with the help of brush and artificial pollination is done.<br>• Then, bagging is repeated.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7097,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Consider the following statement regarding photosynthesis and respiration in plants and select the correct option.<br>I. RuBisCO has high affinity to oxygen in $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ low concentration.<br>II. The Calvin pathway occurs in the chloroplast of bundle sheath cells of $\\mathrm{C}_{4}$ plants.<br>III. Yeast position themselves when the concentration of alcohol reaches $7 \\%$.<br>IV. Oxygen is a final hydrogen acceptor during aerobic respiration.','[{"text": "Statement II & IV are correct, I is wrong.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statements I & II are correct, IV is wrong.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I & III are correct, II is wrong.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statements I and IV are correct, III is wrong.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statement I, II and IV are correct. Option III is incorrect. Yeast poison themselves at a concentration of $13 \\%$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7098,'biology',83,494,1010,'All roundworms having','[{"text": "Triploblastic body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bilateral symmetry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Circular in cross-section", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The body of the aschelminthes is circular in cross-section, hence, the name roundworms. Roundworms have organ-system level of body organisation. They are bilaterally symmetrical, triploblastic and pseudocoelomate animals.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7099,'biology',82,1267,3083,'Which three different kinds of inhibitors were found in mid-1960s?','[{"text": "Inhibitor-I, Abscission-II and dormin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inhibitor-B, Abscission-III and dormin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inhibitor-I, Abscission-III and dormin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inhibitor-B, Abscission-II and dormin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During mid-1960s, three independent researchers reported the purification and chemical characterisation of three different kinds of inhibitors: inhibitor-B, abscission II and dormin. Later all the three were proved to be chemically identical. It was named abscisic acid (ABA).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7100,'biology',8,155,330,'Identify the correct order of events in pollen-pistil interaction form the options given below<br>I. Release of male gametes into the embryo sac.<br>II. Deposition of pollen grains on stigma.<br>III. Entry of pollen tube into embryo sac.<br>IV. Development of pollen tube.<br>V. Entry of pollen tube into the Ovule.','[{"text": "IV - III - II - I - V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II - IV - V - III - I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II - IV - III - V - I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "V - IV - III - II - I", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II,IV, V, III, I , the pollen grains are deposited on the stigma, if it is compatible, pollen tube development occurs followed by entry of tube into ovule and then into embryo sac followed by release of male gametes',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7101,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Cellular respiration includes the various pathways by which carbohydrates and other metabolites are broken down with the consecutive buildup of','[{"text": "ATP", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "vitamins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "fats", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cellular respiration includes the various pathways by which carbohydrates and other metabolites are broken down with the consecutive buildup of ATP.<br>ATP is used for various chemical reactions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7102,'biology',83,494,1010,'All flatworms differ from all round worms in having','[{"text": "Presence of mesoderm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Triploblastic body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bilateral symmetry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of dorso- ventrally flattened body", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Flatworms have dorsoventrally flattened bodies while roundworms have circular cross sections.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7103,'biology',82,1267,3083,'Name the scientist who confirmed the release of a volatile substance from ripened oranges that hastened the ripening of stored unripened bananas?','[{"text": "Darwin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cousins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "E Kurosawa", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Skoog and Miller", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'H.H. Cousins (1910) confirmed the release of a volatile substance from ripened oranges that hastened the ripening of stored unripened bananas. Later this volatile substance was identified as ethylene, a gaseous PGR.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7104,'biology',8,156,332,'Identify the mismatch<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Antipodals - Haploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote - Diploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synergids - Diploid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Primary Endosperm Nucleus Triploid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Synergids is haploid,it is a part of female gametophyte,',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7105,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Glycolysis occurs in the ____ and the product is','[{"text": "cytosol; pyruvate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "cytosol; glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "mitochondrion; pyruvate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "chloroplast; glucose", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Glycolysis occurs in the cytoplasm and does not use oxygen. Thus, it is an anaerobic pathway. In this process, glucose is partially oxidized/converted into two molecules of pyruvate/ pyruvic acid. In aerobic respiration pyruvate enters mitochondrion through a specific transport protein. It undergoes oxidative decarboxylation and dehydrogenation to produce $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ and NADH.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7107,'biology',81,1042,2465,'In which of the following reaction of glycolysis, a molecule of water is removed from the substrate?.','[{"text": "Fructose-6-phosphate Fructose to 1,6-phosphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3-phosphate glyceraldehyde to 1,3biphosphoglyceric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PEP to Pyruvic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2-phosphoglycerate to PEP", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During glycolysis, dehydration occurs in the presence of enzyme enolase and cofactor $\\mathrm{Mg}^{2}+$. 2-phosphoglycerate loses a molecule of water and is changed into phosphoenol pyruvate (PEP).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7108,'biology',8,153,323,'How many microsporangia are located at the corners of a typical bilobed anther of angiosperm','[{"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Microsporangium is a sporangial structures which produces spores. They are also called as pollen sacs. Anther of gymnosperms and angiosperms shows two anther lobes. Each anther lobes develops into two microsporangium. Thus, anther has four pollen sacs at four corners of it.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7109,'biology',82,1267,3083,'The given diagram gives an idea of experiment used to demonstrate that tip of the coleoptile is the source of auxin. In the given diagram arrows are used to show','[{"text": "The direction of wind", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The direction of light", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The direction of growth of leaves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The given diagram gives an idea of experiment used to demonstrate that tip of the coleoptile is the source of auxin. In the given diagram arrows are used to show the direction of light.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/82_7109_question_1.png'),
(7110,'biology',83,494,1010,'In aschelminthes. the mesoderm is present as scattered pouches in between the ectoderm and endoderm, it is called','[{"text": "Coelom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Enterocoel", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haemocoel", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pseudocoel", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In aschelminthes, the mesoderm is present as scattered pouches in between the ectoderm and endoderm , it is called pseudocoel.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7111,'biology',81,1044,2467,'Which of the following are not used in the conversion by pyruvate to acetyl CoA?<br>(i) Oxidative dehydrogenation<br>(ii) Oxidative dehydration<br>(iii) Oxidative phosphorylation<br>(iv) Oxidative decarboxylation','[{"text": "(i), (ii) and (iii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i) and (ii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(ii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(i) and (iii)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The conversion of pyruvate to acetyl CoA involves oxidative decarboxylation (removal of a carboxyl group) and removal of hydrogen which is taken up by $\\mathrm{NAD}^{+}$to become $\\mathrm{NADH}^{+}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7112,'biology',8,153,323,'Consider the following statemetns & choose the correct answer from the given options.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Innermost layer of microsporangium is tapetum.<br></div><div class="column-right">Cells of tapetum possess dense cytoplasm more than one nucleus and nourishes developing pollen grains</div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statements A & B are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements A & B are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is correct & B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement B is correct & A is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both the statements are correct, tapetum is the inner most layer of the microsporangium and it more than one nucleus and nourishes the pollen grain.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7113,'biology',82,1267,3083,'Who among the following conducted an experiment depicted by following diagram____','[{"text": "F. Skoog and his co-workers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "E. Kurosawa", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cousins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Charles Darwin and his son Francis Darwin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The given diagram gives an idea of experiment used to demonstrate that tip of the coleoptile is the source of auxin. In the given diagram arrows are used to show the direction of light. This experiment was carried out by Charles Darwin and his son Francis Darwin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/82_7113_question_1.png'),
