(7115,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Select the incorrect statement about NADH during cellular respiration.','[{"text": "It is synthesized in glycolysis.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is transferred into the mitochondria.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It undergoes oxidative phosphorylation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is reduced to $\\\\mathrm{NAD}^{+}$.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cellular respiration is the mechanism of breakdown of food materials within the cell to release energy and the trapping of this energy for synthesis of ATP. In cellular respiration, NADH is oxidised to $\\mathrm{NAD}^{+}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
