(7119,'biology',81,1042,2465,'In Glycolysis, $\\mathrm{NADH}+\\mathrm{H}^{+}$is formed from NAD, when','[{"text": "2-phosphoglycerate is converted to pyruvic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "triose phosphate is converted to 2-phosphoglycerate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2-phosphoglycerate is converted to 2-phosphopyruvate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3- phosphoglyceraldehyde (PGAL) is converted to 1,3- biphosphoglycerate (BPGA)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In the presence of enzyme Glyceraldehyde3 phosphate dehydrogenase, glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate loses hydrogen to NAD to form $\\mathrm{NADH}_{2}$ and accepts inorganic phosphate to form 1,3-bisphosphoglycerate',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
