(7128,'biology',8,152,322,'A typical bisexual flower has ____ different kinds of whorl.','[{"text": "Two", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Five", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A typical flower has four different kind of whorl. These are calyx (green leafly sepals) corolla (bright colored petals), and androecium (male reproduction organ) and gynoecium (female reproduction organ).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7129,'biology',83,494,1010,'A pseudocoelomate, bilaterally symmetrical human parasite, oviparous and the transmission is by a arthropoda vector. It is','[{"text": "Filarial worm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hook worm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Earth worm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tapeworm", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The given characteristics are that of nematodes. Filariasis is transferred by Culex mosquito that acts as a vector of filarial worm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7130,'biology',82,1268,3084,'2, 4-D stands for ____','[{"text": "2, 4-Dichloromethoxy acetate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2, 4-Di fluorophenoxy acetate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2, 4-Diphospho phenoxy acetate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2, 4-Dichlorophenoxy acetate", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The fullform of 2, 4-D stands for 2 , 4-dichlorophenoxy acetate which is synthetic auxins.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7131,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Term protoplasmic respiration is used for oxidation of','[{"text": "Carbohydrates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fats", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vitamins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'It is said to be protoplasmic respiration when the respiratory substrate is protein.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7132,'biology',8,153,323,'Microsporogenesis occurs','[{"text": "On margins of leaves.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inside the ovule.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inside the anther.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In non- essential floral organs.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Microsporogenesis is the process of formation of microspores or pollen grains, from a pollen mother cell through meiosis is micro sporogenesis Each cell of sporogenous tissue serve as microspore mother cell (MMC). These MMCs undergo meiosis and form microspore tetrad and become haploid, microspores or pollen grains. As anthers mature microspores of the tetrad separate from each other and develops into pollen grains. Each microsporangium contains numerous pollen grains which are released after dehiscence of anther wall.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7133,'biology',83,494,1010,'A pseudocoelomate, bilaterally symmetrical human parasitic, which is oviparous and the transmission is by contaminated soil. It is','[{"text": "Filarial worm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hook worm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fish worm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tapeworm", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Hookworm is a parasitic nematode transferred via contaminated soil.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7134,'biology',82,1271,3087,'Ethylene is used to initiate flowering and for synchronizing fruit set in which fruit?','[{"text": "Apple", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pineapple", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cherry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mango", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Auxins promote flowering e.g. in pineapples and ethylene is used to initiate flowering and for synchronising fruit-set in pineapples.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7135,'biology',81,1045,2468,'The number of ATP molecules produced by electron transport system from Kreb\'s cycle intermediate in a single turn is','[{"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "11", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "16", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "14", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The number of ATP molecules produced by electron transport system from Kreb\'s cycle intermediate in a single turn is 11 .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7136,'biology',8,153,324,'One of the most resistant known biological material is.','[{"text": "Lignin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hemicellulose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporopollenin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lignocellulose", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Sporopollenin is the tough resistant biopolymer that coats the outer walls of pollen grains spores and related micro-organisms. It is considered "the most resistant organic material known" and accounts for the morphology and microstructure and for geological preservation of polymorphs (an organic microfossils).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7137,'biology',83,494,1010,'What is true about excretion in adult <em>Ascaris</em>','[{"text": "Occurs by Nephridia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "An excretory tube removes body wastes from the body cavity through the excretory pore.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Occurs by malpighian tubules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Occurs by green glands", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In adult <em>Ascaris</em>, an excretory tube removes body wastes from the body cavity through the excretory pore.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7138,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Auxins promote flowering in','[{"text": "Tomatoes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pineapples", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oranges", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apples", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Auxins promote flowering e.g. in pineapples.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7139,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Number of carbon atoms present in oxaloacetic acid, ketoglutaric acid and citric acid are','[{"text": "$4,5,6$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$6,4,5$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$5,6,4$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4,6,5$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Oxalo acetic acid has 4 carbon atoms, ketoglutaric acid has 5 carbon atoms and citric acid has 6 carbon atoms.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7140,'biology',8,153,324,'Pollen grain is liberated at','[{"text": "One celled stage.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two celled stage.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three celled stage.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two or three celled stage.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pollen grain is liberated at 2 or 3 celled stage. If pollen grain is released at the 2-celled stage (i.e., vegetative and generative cells) then generative cell divides meiotically to produce two male gametes, but when pollen grains are released at 3-celled stage then two male gametes are already present.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7141,'biology',83,494,1010,'<i>Ascaris</i> is characterised by','[{"text": "Coelomates but presence of metamerism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pseudocoelomate, no metamerism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coelomates but the absence of metamerism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coelomates and pseudo-metamerism", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ascaris is a pseudocoelomate that does not exhibit metamerism.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7142,'biology',82,1268,3084,'What promotes the abscission of older mature leaf?','[{"text": "Abscisic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Auxin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ethylene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokinins", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Auxins help to prevent fruit and leaf drop at early stages but promote the abscission of older mature leaves and fruits.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7143,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Terminal cytochrome of respiratory chain which donates electrons to oxygen is','[{"text": "cyt.b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "cyt. c", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "cyt. a", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "cyt. $\\\\mathrm{a}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Terminal cytochrome of respiratory chain is cyt-a3. cyt-a3 possesses two copper centres. It helps in transfer of electrons to oxygen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7144,'biology',8,154,327,'Transfer of pollen grains from the anther to the stigma of another flower of the same plant is called','[{"text": "Geitonogamy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Xenogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cleistogamy", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Autogamy and geitonogamy are types of self - pollination. Geitonogamy is the fertilization of a flower by pollen from another flower on the same (or a genetically identical) plant. It occurs between bisexual flowers or unisexual flowers of the same plant. While autogamy is a kind of pollination in which the pollen from the anthers of a flower are transferred to the stigma of the same flower.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7145,'biology',83,494,1010,'<i>Ascaris lumbricoides</i> is an endoparasite of man and inhabits','[{"text": "Liver", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lymph nodes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Digestive system", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ascaris lumbricoides is an endoparasite of man and it inhabits the small intestine of humans.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7146,'biology',82,1268,3084,'What can help removing apical dominance?','[{"text": "Removal of shoot tips", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Treatment with auxin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Treatment with cytokinin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Removal of shoot tips and treatment with cytokinins can help removing apical dominance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7147,'biology',81,1046,2469,'In the electron transport system present in the inner mitochondrial membrane, complexes I and IV are respectively','[{"text": "NADH dehydrogenase and succinate dehydrogenase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{FAD}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_2}$ and NADH dehydrogenase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "NADH dehydrogenase and ATP synthase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "NADH dehydrogenase and cytochrome oxidase complex", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Complex - I - NADH dehydrogenase Complex - IV - Cytochrome oxidase',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7148,'biology',8,153,324,'In angiosperms the following events occur during microgametogenesis<br>i. Mitotic division in microspore<br>ii. Meiotic division in microspore mother cell<br>iii. Formation of pollen grain<br>iv. Formation of microspores<br>v. Formation of mature male gametophyte<br>The correct sequence of events is','[{"text": "ii, i, iv, v, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii, ii, i, v, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iv, i, iii, v", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iv, v, ii, i, iii", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'ii, iv, i, iii, v',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7149,'biology',83,494,1010,'<i>Female Ascaris</i> can be differentiated from male by','[{"text": "Presence of female gonapophysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of penial setae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shorter size", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Longer than male and straight posterior end", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Female Ascaris is longer in length than the male. The female also bears a straight posterior end. While the male bears penial setae at its curved end.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7150,'biology',82,1268,3084,'The process of removal of shoot tip to avoid apical dominance is called ____','[{"text": "E-dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decapitation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Capitation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Removal of shoot tips to remove apical dominance is called as decapitation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7151,'biology',8,153,326,'An ovule, which becomes curved so that the nucellus and embryo sac lie at right angles to the funicle is','[{"text": "Hemitropous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Campylotropous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anatropous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Orthotropous", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In campylotropous the body of the ovule is curved but the embryo sac is straight.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7152,'biology',81,1049,2472,'If R. Q. is less than 1.0 in a respiratory metabolism, it means that','[{"text": "carbohydrates are used as respiratory substrate.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "organic acids are used as respiratory substrate.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "the oxidation of the respiratory substrate consumed more oxygen than the amount of $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ released.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "the oxidation of the respiratory substrate consumed less oxygen than the amount of $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ released.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The ratio of the volume of carbon dioxide evolved to that of oxygen consumed by an organism, tissue, or cell in a given time is called respiratory quotients.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7153,'biology',83,494,1010,'The posterior end of male <i>Ascaris</i> has','[{"text": "Penial setae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Straight end", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Curved tail", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The male bears penial setae at its curved end.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7154,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Decapitation is widely used for','[{"text": "Tea plantation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hedge making", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Parthenocarpy", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Removal of shoot tips (decapitation) usually results in the growth of lateral buds. Decapitation is widely applied in tea plantations, hedge-making.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7155,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Net gain of ATP after glycolysis (without E.T.S)','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "10 ATP", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The net gain of ATP after glycolysis, without considering the electron transport system (ETS), is 2 ATP molecules produced. Glycolysis generates 4 ATP molecules during its energy-yielding steps but consumes 2 ATP molecules during its preparatory steps, resulting in a net gain of 2 ATP.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7156,'biology',8,153,325,'Ovules are attached to a parenchymatous cushion called','[{"text": "Nucellus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Obturator", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Conducting tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Placenta", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Placenta is the surface of the carpel to which the ovules (potential seeds) are attached. The placenta is usually located in a region corresponding somewhat to the margins of a leaf but is actually submarginal in position.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7157,'biology',83,494,1010,'Anus and genital aperture is common in ascaris','[{"text": "Male <i>Ascaris</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Female cockroach", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Female <i>Ascaris</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male cockroach", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In female Ascaris, there is the genital pore or vulva; males do not have a separate genital opening. Distinct sexual dimorphism is observed between male and female Ascaris.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7158,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Auxin was first isolated from ____','[{"text": "Frog\'s urine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zeatin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Human urine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Auxin was first isolated from human urine.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7170,'biology',82,1268,3084,'2, 4-D does not show herbicidal action on','[{"text": "Rose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mature dicotyledonous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mature monocotyledonous", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'2, 4-D, widely used to kill dicotyledonous weeds, does not affect mature monocotyledonous plants. It is used to prepare weed-free lawns by gardeners.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7159,'biology',81,1040,2463,'Read the following statements and identify the correct statements<br>i. Cellular respiration is the mechanism of breakdown of food material within the cell to release energy.<br>ii. The compounds that are oxidized during the process are known as respiratory substrate iii. Respiration causes the breaking of $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$ bond of complex compounds through oxidation within the cells leads in energy release','[{"text": "Only (i)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (i) and (ii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (i) and (iii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "all the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct Cellular respiration involves the breakdown of food materials within the cell to release energy. The compounds that are oxidized during the process are known as respiratory substrates, and respiration indeed involves the breaking of $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$ bonds in complex compounds through oxidation, leading to energy release.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7160,'biology',8,157,333,'Endosperm is generally','[{"text": "Diploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Triploid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Haploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polyploid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Endosperms is produced inside the seeds of most flowering plants around the time of fertilization. It is formed when the two sperm nuclei inside a pollen grain reach the interior of an embryo sac or female gametophyte. One sperm nucleus fertilizes the egg,forming a zygote, while the other sperm nucleus usually fuses with the two polar nuclei at the centre of the embryo sac, forming a primary endosperm cell (its nucleus is often called the triple fusion nucleus). About $70 \\%$ of angiosperm species have endosperm cells that are polyploid. These are typically triploid (containing three sets of chromosomes) but can vary widely from diploid (2n) to $15 n$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7161,'biology',83,494,1010,'An arthropod -intermediate host is present in','[{"text": "Earthworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ancylostoma</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Wuchereria</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Enterobius</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Wuchereria is transmitted by mosquitoes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7162,'biology',82,1268,3084,'The name \'Auxin\' was given to which chemical?','[{"text": "Indole-2-butyric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Indole-2-acetic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Indole-4-butyric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Indole-3-acetic acid", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The name \'Auxin\' was given to Indole-3-acetic acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7163,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Identify the products formed due to breakage of $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$ bonds during aerobic breakdown of Glucose<br>I. Trioses<br>II. Acetyl Co.A<br>III. Succinyl Co. A<br>IV. $\\alpha$-keto glutaric acid','[{"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The products formed due to the breakage of $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$ bonds during aerobic glucose breakdown include trioses (3-carbon compounds), acetyl CoA, succinyl CoA, and $\\alpha$-ketoglutaric acid. These products are intermediates in various stages of the citric acid cycle (TCA or Krebs cycle), which is part of the aerobic respiration process.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7164,'biology',8,154,327,'Cleistogamous flowers are','[{"text": "Wind pollinated", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Self-pollinated", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cross-pollinated", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insect pollinated", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In some plants, bisexual flowers are formed which never open throughout the life. Such flowers are called cleistogamous flowers such as Commelina viola. So only self-pollination takes place in these plants. Self-pollination is a rule in cleistogamous flowers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7165,'biology',83,494,1010,'<i>Wuchereria bancrofti</i> belongs to phylum','[{"text": "Platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Annelida", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aschelminthes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coelenterata", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Wuchereria bancrofti belongs to Phylum Aschelminthes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7166,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Which of the following PGR is widely used to kill dicotyledonous weeds?','[{"text": "IAA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "NAA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2, 4-D", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ABA", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'2, 4-D, widely used to kill dicotyledonous weeds, does not affect mature monocotyledonous plants. It is used to prepare weed-free lawns by gardeners.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7167,'biology',8,154,328,'In flowering plants both male and female gametes are non-motile. The method to bring them together for fertilization is','[{"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Air", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Apomixis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In flowering plants, both male and female gametes are non-motile. The method to bring them together for fertilization is called pollination. Pollination is the process by which pollen is transferred from the anther (male part) to the stigma (female part) of the plant, thereby enabling fertilization and reproduction. Pollination takes place in the angiosperms, the flower bearing plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7168,'biology',81,1043,2466,'The following is a simplified scheme showing the fate of glucose during aerobic and anaerobic respiration. Identify the end products that are formed at stages indicated as A, B, C and D. Identify the correct option from those given below.','[{"text": "A = Carbondioxide and water,\\nB = pyruvic acid, C = ethyl alcohol and\\ncarbondioxide, D = lactic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A = pyruvic acid, B = carbondioxide,\\nC = ethyl alcohol and carbondioxide,\\nD = lactic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A = pyruvic acid, B = ethyl alcohol and\\ncarbondioxide, C= lactic acid,\\nD = carbondioxide and water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A = pyruvic acid, B = carbondioxide,\\nC = lactic acid, D = ethyl alcohol and\\ncarbondioxide", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{A}=$ pyruvic acid,$\\mathrm{B}=$ carbon-di-oxide, $\\mathrm{C}=$ lactic acid, $\\mathrm{D}=$ ethyl alcohol and carbondi-oxide.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_7168_question_1.png'),
(7169,'biology',83,494,1010,'<em>Elephantiasis</em> causing organism belongs to the phylum','[{"text": "Arthropoda", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Porifera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aschelminthes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<em>Elephantiasis</em> is caused by filarial worm, <em>Wuchereria bancrofti</em>. It belongs to the phylum <em>Aschelminthes</em>.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7231,'biology',83,495,1011,'The excretory organs of Annelida is','[{"text": "Nephridia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Malphigian tubules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Choanocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Nephridia (sing. nephridium) help in osmoregulation and excretion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7171,'biology',8,154,328,'Bees are important to agriculture as they','[{"text": "Produce wax", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Perform pollination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prevent pollination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Produce honey", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Bees are important to agriculture as they perform pollination. Bees are responsible for over $80 \\%$ of all pollination done by insects. Plants pollinated by insects are colorful with fragrance and abundant nectar which attracts insects.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7172,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Identify the products $\\mathrm{a}, \\mathrm{b}, \\mathrm{c}$ and $\\mathrm{d}$ and find out the correct option','[{"text": "a-pyruvic acid, b-ethyl alcohol +, c-${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_2}$,\\nd - lactic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a-pyruvic acid, b- lactic acid , c-ethyl\\nalcohol+ , d-${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a-pyruvic acid, b-NADH2, c-lactic acid,\\nd-ethyl alcohol +${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a- pyruvic acid, b- PGA c-ethyl alcohol+,\\nd-lactic acid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/biology/81_7172_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_7172_question_1.png'),
(7173,'biology',83,494,1010,'Which of the following is mismatch?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "<em>Fasciola</em>- Liver fluke", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Ascaris</em> - <em>Hirudinaria</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<em>Ancylostoma</em> - Hookworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Wuchereria</em> - Filaria worm", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Leech - <em>Hirudinaria</em>',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7174,'biology',82,1271,3087,'Rise in the rate of respiration is called','[{"text": "Respiratory climax", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Respiratory quotient", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Respiratory climactic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Rise in the rate of respiration is called respiratory climactic.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7175,'biology',8,154,327,'Choose the correct statement','[{"text": "Chasmogamous flowers never exhibit autogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cleistogamous flowers exhibit both autogamy and geitonogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chasmogamous flowers always exhibit geitonogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cleistogamous flowers always exhibit autogamy", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cleistogamous flowers are the flowers which don\'t open. In Cleistogamous flowers, reproductive structures are smaller and the pollen are produced in less in number. In Cleistogamous flower the anthers and stigma lie close to each other with in the closed flowers. When anthers dehisces in the flower buds, pollen grains come in contact with the stigma for effective pollination. Thus, these flowers are invariably autogamous as there is no chance of cross-pollen landing on the stigma.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7176,'biology',81,1040,2463,'During the process of respiration, which of the followings are released as products?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}$ only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CO}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}$ and energy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}$ and energy", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Respiration is a metabolic process in which energy is produced with the intake of oxygen and the release of carbon dioxide from the oxidation of complex organic substances along with water.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7177,'biology',83,494,1010,'Give the correct matching of causative agents and disease.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "<i>Wuchereria</i> - Filariasis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Anopheles</i> - Malaria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Glossina</i> - Kala-azar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Leishmania</i> - Sleeping sickness", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The causative agent of Filariasis is Wuchereria bancrofti.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7178,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Auxin helps in?','[{"text": "Phloem differentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Xylem differentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Auxin controls xylem differentiation and helps in cell division.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7179,'biology',81,1043,2466,'Select the correct statement.','[{"text": "There is complete breakdown of organic substrate in anaerobic respiration.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Very little $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ is evolved during anaerobic respiration.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anaerobic respiration is more efficient in releasing energy to maintain cellular activities", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Very little $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ is evolved during anaerobic respiration.<br>In anaerobic respiration, less $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ is produced compared to aerobic respiration, as the organic substrate is not completely oxidized in the absence of oxygen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7180,'biology',8,154,327,'One advantage of cleistogamy is :','[{"text": "It leads to greater genetic diversity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed dispersal is more efficient and wide spread", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed set is not dependent on pollination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Each visit of a pollinator results in transfer of hundred of pollen grains", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is (3) seed set is not dependent on pollination. Cleistogamous flowers are adapted for self-pollination, and they produce seeds without the need for external pollinators, making seed set more independent of pollination events. This adaptation can be advantageous in certain ecological contexts.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7181,'biology',83,494,1010,'Read the following statements carefully<br>I. They are triploblastic<br>II. Alimentary canal is complete with a well developed muscular pharynx<br>III. An excretory tube removes body wastes from the body cavity through excretory pore (Rennette cells excretory organ)<br>IV. They are dioecious<br>iv. Fertilisation is internal<br>Above features belong to which phylum?','[{"text": "Arthropoda", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Annelida", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Echinodermata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aschelminthes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The given characteristics point towards the Phylum Aschelminthes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7182,'biology',82,1270,3086,'Natural kinetin occurs in','[{"text": "Coconut milk", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pineapple", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corn", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cytokinins have specific effects on cytokinesis, and were discovered as kinetin (a modified form of adenine, a purine) from the autoclaved herring sperm DNA. Kinetin does not occur naturally in plants. Search for natural substances with cytokinin-like activities led to the isolation of zeatin from corn-kernels and coconut milk.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7183,'biology',81,1042,2465,'The enzymes, involved in the chemical reactions of glycolysis are located','[{"text": "in the fluid matrix of cytoplasm.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "in the mitochondrial matrix.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "in the nuclear sap.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "on the cristae of a mitochondria.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Glycolysis occurs in the cytosol, where the glucose molecule is converted into two molecules of the $3 \\mathrm{C}$ compound, pyruvate. The enzymes are located in the fluid matrix of cytoplasm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7184,'biology',8,154,329,'The terms homothallic and monoecious are used to denote','[{"text": "Bisexual condition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Unisexual condition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Staminate flowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pistillate flowers", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Homothallic and monoecious are used to denote bisexual condition. The example includes fungi and plants. Heterothallic and dioecious are used to denote unisexual condition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7185,'biology',83,494,1010,'Given below are four statements regarding aschelminthes<br>I. They are bilaterally symmetrical and triploblastic<br>II. They are dioecious<br>III. All are plants or animal parasites<br>IV. They are acoelomate<br>\nMark the option that has both the correct statements','[{"text": "II,IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I,III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II,III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I,II", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Organisms in phylum Aschelminthes are exclusively animal parasites. They are pseudocoelomates.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7186,'biology',82,1270,3086,'The naturally available cytokinin like substance in plants is','[{"text": "Kinetin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zeatin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Kinetin does not occur naturally in plants. Search for natural substances with cytokininlike activities led to the isolation of zeatin from corn-kernels and coconut milk.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7187,'biology',8,153,323,'Another name for Pollen sac is','[{"text": "Embryo sac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anther", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Microsporangium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Megasporangium", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pollen sacs are also called the microsporangia Anther consists of four microsporangia..',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7188,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Which of the following statement regarding the process of glycolysis is correct?','[{"text": "Glucose undergoes complete oxidation to form two molecules of pyruvic acid.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose undergoes partial oxidation to form onemolecule of pyruvic acid.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose undergoes complete oxidation to form one molecule of pyruvic acid.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose undergoes partial oxidation to form two molecules of pyruvic acid.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Glycolysis occurs in cytoplasm, is a common phase of aerobic and anaerobic respiration. It is a partial breakdown of glucose molecule into two molecules of pyruvic acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7189,'biology',83,494,1010,'Which of the following is a characteristic feature of phylum aschelminthes?','[{"text": "They are dioecious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bilaterally symmetrical, triploblastic animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Complete alimentary canal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of the options depict characteristics of Aschelminthes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7190,'biology',81,1044,2467,'The formation of acetyl coenzyme A from pyruvic acid produces (in addition to acetyl coenzyme A) one molecule of A, one molecule of B. Identify A, B.<br>&emsp; ${\\bf{A}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\bf{B}}$','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{NADH}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{NADH}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In the presence of an enzyme complex, pyruvate dehydrogenase complex, Sulphur containing $\\mathrm{CoA}$ and $\\mathrm{NAD}+$, pyruvate undergoes oxidative decarboxylation or both oxidation (removal of hydrogen) and decarboxylation (removal of $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7191,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Which of the following PGR is widely used as herbicide?','[{"text": "Auxin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gibberellic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokinins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethylene", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Auxins are widely used as herbicides. 2, 4-D, widely used to kill dicotyledonous weeds, does not affect mature monocotyledonous plants. It is used to prepare weed-free lawns by gardeners.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7192,'biology',83,494,1010,'Which one of the following statements about certain given animals is correct?','[{"text": "Molluscs are pesudocoelomates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Annelida are pseudocoelomates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ctenophores are coelomates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Roundworms are pseudocoelomates", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Organisms in phylum Achelminthes, commonly known as roundworms are pseudocoelomates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7193,'biology',8,153,323,'The functions of tapetum is to','[{"text": "Produce ubisch bodies.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Produce pollen grains.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Provide nourishment to the developing pollen grains.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The tapetum is a layer of nutritive cells found within the sporangium, particularly within the anther, of flowering plants. Its main function is to provide nutrition to the developing microspore mother cells and pollen grains. A small, granular structure that is found in the extracellular matrix of cell of the secretory tapetal layer that surrounds developing pollen grains.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7194,'biology',81,1043,2466,'During respiration, yeast converts glucose to','[{"text": "Ethanol and water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethanol and oxygen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethanol and $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lactic acid and $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In fermentation, yeast converts glucose, to ethanol and carbon dioxide.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7195,'biology',82,1269,3085,'Different types of gibberellins is reported from what kind of organisms?','[{"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Higher plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gibberellins are another kind of promotory PGR. There are more than 100 gibberellins reported from widely different organisms such as fungi and higher plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7196,'biology',83,494,1010,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Ctenophora<br>B. Flattened body<br>C. Circular in cross-section</div><div class="column-right">P. Aschelminthes<br>Q. Sea walnuts<br>R. Platyhelminthes</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Ctenophora - Q. Sea walnuts<br>B. Flattened body - R. Platyhelminthes<br>C. Circular in cross-section - P. Aschelminthes',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7197,'biology',8,153,324,'Exine of pollen grain is formed of','[{"text": "Callose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pecto-cellulose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ligno-cellulose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporopollenin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Exine is tough, cutinized layer often with spinous outgrowth but sometimes smooth. Exine is composed of sporopollenin which is resistant to physical and biological decomposition. It protect the pollens from environmental extremes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7198,'biology',81,1045,2468,'During aerobic breakdown of Glucose what is the series of intermediates formed with respect to no. of carbon atoms that they have<br>I. 3C compound<br>II. 4C compound<br>III. 5C compound<br>IV. 2C compound<br>V. 6C organic acid','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V, I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, III, II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, V, IV, III, II", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct series of intermediates formed during the aerobic breakdown of glucose with respect to the number of carbon atoms they have is:<br>The intermediates formed in glycolysis and the Krebs cycle during glucose breakdown are as follows: (I) 3C compound, (IV) 2C compound, (V) 6C organic acid, (III) 5C compound, and (II) 4C compound.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7199,'biology',82,1269,3085,'Which of the following was first reported gibberellins to be discovered?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{GA}_{1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{GA}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{GA}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{GA}_{100}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gibberellic acid (${\\rm{G}}{{\\rm{A}}_{\\rm{3}}}$) was one of the first gibberellins to be discovered and remains the most intensively studied form.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7200,'biology',83,494,1010,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Round worm<br>B. <em>Ancylostoma</em><br>C. <em>Wuchereria</em></div><div class="column-right">P.Hook worm<br>Q. Filaria worm<br>R. <em>Ascaris</em></div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$,", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. Round worm - R. <em>Ascaris</em><br>B. <em>Ancylostoma</em> - P. Hook worm<br>C.<em> Wuchereria</em> - Q. Filaria worm',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7201,'biology',8,157,333,'Milky water of green coconut is','[{"text": "Liquid chalaza", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liquid nucellus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liquid endosperm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Liquid female gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Coconut water is the clear liquid inside young green coconuts. Milky water of green coconut is called liquid endosperm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7202,'biology',81,1044,2467,'Acceptor of acetyl Co-A in Kreb\'s cycle is','[{"text": "malic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "fumaric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\alpha$-keto glutaric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "oxaloacetic acid", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Oxaloacetic acid is the acceptor of acetyl coA in Krebs\' cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7203,'biology',82,1269,3085,'How can gibberellins help to extend the market period?','[{"text": "It delays senescence", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Increases ripening period", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increases flowering time", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It promotes senescence", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Some of the gibberellins are commercially used in the delayed ripening of fruits. ${\\rm{G}}{{\\rm{A}}_{\\rm{7}}}$ delays senescence so that fruit can be left on the tree for longer period. It extends period of marketing.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7204,'biology',83,494,1010,'Identify male and female organism.','[{"text": "A - female <i>Ascaris</i>, B - male <i>Ascaris</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - male <i>Ascaris</i>, B - female <i>Ascaris</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - male <i>Hirudinaria</i>, B - female <i>Hirudinaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - male <i>Nereis</i>, B - female <i>Nereis</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the given figure, A represents male Ascaris while B represents female Ascaris.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_7204_question_1.png'),
(7205,'biology',8,154,327,'Both chasmogamous and cleistogamous flowers are present in','[{"text": "<i>Helianthus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Commelina</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Rosa</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Gossypium</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The answer is (2) Commelina. Commelina plants have both chasmogamous (open, visible) and cleistogamous (closed, inconspicuous) flowers in the same inflorescence. Chasmogamous flowers are for cross-pollination, while cleistogamous flowers often self-pollinate without opening.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7206,'biology',81,1048,2471,'Which of the following is amphibolic in nature?','[{"text": "Glycolysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxidative decarboxylation of pyruvate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "TCA cycle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oxidative phosphorylation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Krebs cycle (also called as tricarboxylic acid cycle, TCA) is amphibolic or having both catabolic and anabolic rates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7207,'biology',82,1270,3086,'Addition of what to auxins in nutrients medium causes proliferation of callus?','[{"text": "DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Yeast extract", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coconut milk", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Addition of DNA, Coconut milk and yeast extract with auxins in nutrients medium causes proliferation of callus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7208,'biology',83,495,1011,'The phylum - Annelida is named so because of','[{"text": "Metamerism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They possess longitudinal and circular muscles which help in locomotion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dorsally placed neural system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The presence of Nephridia", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The body surface of Annelids is distinctly marked out into segments or metameres and, hence, the phylum name Annelida (Latin, annulus : little ring)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7209,'biology',8,154,328,'Pollination by water occurs in','[{"text": "<i>Vallisneria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Zostera</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Salvia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pollination by water (called hydrophily) occurs in Vallisneria. In vallisneria (ribbon weed), female flower reaches on the surface of water and assumes horizontal position due to elongation of its stalk, male flowers or pollen grains are released on to the surace of water. They are carried passively by water currents & some of which eventually reach to the stigma. In zostera pollination by Hypohydrophily.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(7210,'biology',81,1044,2467,'Select the incorrect statement w.r.t aerobic respiration<br>I. In the complete oxidation of a molecule of pyruvate by the stepwise removal of all the hydrogen atoms, six $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ molecules are released.<br>II. Glycolytic catabolism of carbohydrate takes place in the mitochondrial matrix.<br>III. The reaction catalysed by pyruvic dehydrogenase requires the participation of several coenzymes, including $\\mathrm{NAD}^{+}$ and coenzyme A.<br>IV. In the process catalysed by Pyruvate dehydrogenase, two molecules of NADH are produced from two molecules of pyruvic acid.','[{"text": "I & III are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II & IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I & II are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III & IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'From a pyruvate molecule there is stepwise removal of $3 \\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ molecules. Glycolysis takes place in cytoplasm.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7211,'biology',82,1269,3085,'On spraying gibberellins on sugarcane crops what major change will it bring?','[{"text": "Increase flowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase length of stem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Increase root strength", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Spraying sugarcane crop with gibberellins increases the length of the stem, thus increasing the yield by as much as 20 tonnes per acre.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7212,'biology',83,495,1011,'Metamerism is the characteristic of-','[{"text": "Platyheminthes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Annelida (e.g. earthworm)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Porifera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mollusca", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The body surface of Annelids is distinctly marked out into segments or metameres. This phenomenon is known as metamerism.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7213,'biology',8,154,328,'Which one of the following statements are not true?','[{"text": "Pollen grains of some plants cause severe allergies and bronchial afflications in some people", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollination by wind is more common among the abiotic pollinations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Honey is made by bees by digesting pollen collected from flowers", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Wind and water pollinated flowers do not produce nectar and are not very colourful", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Honey is made from nectar through process of regurgitation and evaporation. Later the aqueous solution is still high in water. Hence the process continuous by evaporation. Bees produce honey as a food source.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7214,'biology',81,1046,2469,'In the electron transport system, the final acceptor of proton is','[{"text": "cytochrome b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "cytochrome $a_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "oxygen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ubiquinone (substance A)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In the electron transport system, the final acceptor of proton is oxygen. Oxygen functions as the terminal acceptor of electrons and is reduced to water along with the hydrogen atoms in mitochondrial matrix. It drives whole process by removing hydrogen from system.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7215,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Which of the following PGR can induce parthenocarpy?','[{"text": "Abscisic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2,4 -D", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ethylene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokinins", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Auxins(2, 4-D) induce parthenocarpy, e.g., in tomatoes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7216,'biology',83,495,1011,'Which of the following animals have organ system level of body organisation, and true coelomates?','[{"text": "Coelenterata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Annelida", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Porifera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aschelminthes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Annelida',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7217,'biology',8,154,328,'Xenogamy involves:','[{"text": "Pollination of a flower by the pollen from another flower of the same plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollination of a flower by the pollen from another same flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollination of a flower by the pollen from a flower of another plant in the same population", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pollination of a flower by the pollen from a flower of another plant belonging to a distinct population", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Xenogamy is pollination of a flower by the pollen from a flower of another plant in the same population.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7218,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Which of the following statement is correct in relation to the ETS?','[{"text": "It is present in the mitochondrial matrix.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxidation of one molecule of NADH gives rise to 2 molecules of ATP, while that of one molecule of ${\\\\rm{FAD}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ produces 3 molecules of ATP.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxygen acts as the final hydrogen acceptor.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In respiration, light energy is utilized for the production of proton gradient.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'ETS (Electron transport system or chain) is a series of coenzymes and coenzymes that takes part in the passage of electrons from a chemical to its ultimate acceptor. ETS is present in the inner mitochondrial membrane, oxidation of one molecule of NADH gives rise to 3 molecules of ATP, while that of one molecule of FADH2 produces 2 molecules of ATP. In respiration, energy of oxidation reduction is utilized for the production of proton gradient.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7219,'biology',82,1268,3084,'NAA stands for____.','[{"text": "Nitrogen acetic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "N-acetic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Naphthalene acetic acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nitro acetic acid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'NAA stands for Napthaline acetic acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7220,'biology',83,495,1011,'Which of the following animals are triploblastic and have metamerically segmented body?','[{"text": "Echinodermata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Annelida", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mollusca", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aschelminthes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Annelida possesses three germinal layers and hence is triploblastic. One of this phylum\'s unique features is the presence of metamerism.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7221,'biology',8,156,332,'Vegetative fertilization involves fusion of','[{"text": "Two polar nuclei", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A male gamete and a synergid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A male gamete and antipodal cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleus of a male gamete and secondary nucleus", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The fusion of male and female gametes is called fertilization. Fertilization in angiosperms involves two nuclear fusions, one between one of the male gametes and the egg and the other between the second male gamete and the secondary nucleus of the polar nuclei. The first of these fusions called generative fertilization or syngamy which leads to the formation of a zygote and the second known as vegetative fertilization which leads to the formation of a triploid primary endosperm nucleus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7222,'biology',81,1049,2472,'Consider the following statements with respect to respiration<br>I. $\\mathrm{C}_{51} \\mathrm{H}_{98} \\mathrm{O}_{6}$ is the chemical formula of Tripalmitin, a fat<br>II. Glycolysis occurs in the cytoplasm of the cell<br>III. Electron transport system is present in the outer mitochondrial membrane<br>IV. Respiratory quotient =<br>$\\frac{{{\\rm{Voulme}}\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{evolued}}}}{{{\\rm{Voulme}}\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{consumed}}}}$<br> Regarding the above statements,','[{"text": "Statement I and II are correct and Statement III and IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement I and III are correct and Statement II and IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement II and III are correct and Statement I and IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I and II are incorrect and Statement III and IV are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Electron transport system is present in the inner mitochondrial membrane.<br>Respiratory quotient is ratio of volume of carbon dioxide evolved by volume of oxygen consumed.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7223,'biology',82,1269,3085,'Spraying of gibberellins over sugarcane can increase the yield by how much?','[{"text": "20 tonnes/acre", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "20 kg /acre", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "20 tonnes/sq.feet", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "200 tonnes/acre", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Spraying sugarcane crop with gibberellins increases the length of the stem, thus increasing the yield by as much as 20 tonnes per acre.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7224,'biology',83,495,1011,'In Annelida, locomotion takes by','[{"text": "Nephridia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Longitudinal and circular muscles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ommatidia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cartilage", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In Annelids, locomotion takes place by muscular movement. They possess longitudinal and circular muscles which help in locomotion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7225,'biology',8,157,335,'Choose the correct option for A, B, C and D of a monocot embryo.','[{"text": "A- Scutellum; B- Epiblast; C- Coleoptile; D- Coleorhiza", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Scutellum; B- Coleoptile; C- Epiblast; D- Coleorhiza", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A- Coleoptile; B- Scutellum; C-Epiblast; D- Coleorhiza", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Scutellum; B- Coleoptile; C- Coleorhiza; D- Epiblast", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Scutellum; B-Coleoptile; C-Epiblast; D- Coleorhiza',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/8_7225_question_1.png'),
(7226,'biology',81,1043,2466,'Which of the following statement about cellular energy-harvesting pathway is incorrect?','[{"text": "Pyruvate oxidation can only occur under aerobic conditions.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autotrophs can produce their own food but must obtain energy from it by glycolysis & cellular respiration.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fermentation usually occurs under aerobic conditions.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fermentation represents anaerobic mode of respiration. In fermentation the incomplete oxidation of glucose is achieved by sets of reactions where pyruvic acid is converted to $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ and ethanol.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7227,'biology',82,1269,3085,'What change does GA bring in juvenile conifers?','[{"text": "Hastens maturity period and early seed production", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hastens germination period and early germination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hastens dormancy period and early seed production", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lessens maturity period and early seed production", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Spraying juvenile conifers with GAs hastens the maturity period, thus leading to early seed production.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7228,'biology',83,495,1011,'Circulatory system is first complete in which phylum','[{"text": "Annelida", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Arthropoda", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aschelminthes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Circulatory system is first complete in phylum Annelida.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7229,'biology',8,155,330,'The role of Filiform apparatus in synergids is','[{"text": "Protect the egg apparatus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endosperm formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Guide the entry of pollen tube.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prevention of gamete entry", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In embryo sac, the synergids have special cellular thickenings at the micropylar tip called filiform apparatus, which play an important role in guiding the pollen tubes into the synergid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7230,'biology',81,1042,2465,'Arrange the steps of glycolysis in correct order<br>i. Conversion of BPGA to 3-Phosphoglyceric acid<br>ii. Conversion of 3-Phosphoglyceric acid to 2- Phosphoglycerate<br>iii. Splitting of Fructose 1,6 -biphosphate into dihydroxy acetone phosphate and 3 - Phosphoglyceraldehyde<br>iv. Conversion of 3-Phosphoglyceraldehyde to 1,3-biphosphoglycerate','[{"text": "iii, iv, i, ii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iii,i, ii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii, ii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iv, ii, iii, i", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'iii , iv, i, ii<br>iii. Splitting of Fructose 1,6 -biphosphate into dihydroxy acetone phosphate and<br>3 - Phosphoglyceraldehyde<br>iv. Conversion of 3-Phosphoglyceraldehyde to 1,3-biphosphoglycerate i. Conversion of BPGA to 3-Phosphoglyceric acid<br>ii. Conversion of 3-Phosphoglyceric acid to 2Phosphoglycerate',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7232,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Natural auxins and synthetic auxins are extensively used in','[{"text": "Agriculture", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Horticulture", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Auxins like IAA and indole butyric acid (IBA) have been isolated from plants. NAA (naphthalene acetic acid) and 2, 4-D (2, 4-dichlorophenoxyacetic) are synthetic auxins. All these auxins have been used extensively in agricultural and horticultural practices.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7233,'biology',8,154,327,'Transfer of pollen grains from the anther to the stigma of another flower of the same plant, is called','[{"text": "Xenogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cleistogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Geitonogamy", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Geitonogamy : Transfer of pollen grains from the anther to the stigma of another flower of the same plant.<br>Xenogamy: The transfer of pollen grains from anther to the stigma of another flower of different plant of the same species.<br>Autogamy: The transfer of pollen grain from another to the stigma of the same flower.<br>Cleistogamy: A condition in which flower does not open.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7234,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Choose the correct combination of $\\mathrm{A}$ to $\\mathrm{E}$ carbon compounds in the substrate molecules involve in T.C.A. cycle. &emsp;${\\,\\,\\bf{A}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\bf{B}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\bf{C}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\bf{D}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\bf{E}}$','[{"text": "$4 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 6 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 5 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 4 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 4 \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$6 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 5 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 4 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 3 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 2 \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 5 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 6 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 4 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 4 \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 6 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 4 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 4 \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\quad 5 \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The correct combination is (3) 4C, 6C, 5C, 4C,4C.<br>Explanation:<br>- A (OAA - Oxaloacetate) has 4 carbon atoms.<br>- $\\mathrm{B}$ (Citric acid) is formed by the addition of a 2-carbon acetyl group to a 4-carbon oxaloacetate, making it a 6-carbon compound.<br>- $\\quad \\mathrm{C}(\\alpha$-ketoglutaric acid $)$ is a 5-carbon compound.<br>- D (Succinic acid) is a 4-carbon compound.<br>- E (Malic acid) is also a 4-carbon compound.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/81_7234_question_1.png'),
(7235,'biology',83,495,1011,'Neural system of annelida consists of','[{"text": "Single ganglia (sing. ganglion) connected by lateral nerves to a double ventral nerve cord.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Paired ganglia (sing. ganglion) connected by medial nerves to a double ventral nerve cord.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Paired ganglia (sing. ganglion) connected by lateral nerves to a double ventral nerve cord.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Paired ganglia (sing. ganglion) connected by lateral nerves to a double dorsal nerve cord.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Neural system in Annelids consists of paired ganglia (sing. ganglion) connected by lateral nerves to a double ventral nerve cord.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7236,'biology',82,1269,3085,'Gibberellins promotes bolting in which plants?','[{"text": "Beet", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cabbage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plant with Rosette habit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Gibberellins promotes bolting (internode elongation just prior to flowering) in beet, cabbages and many plants with rosette habit',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7237,'biology',8,157,335,'Match the content of Column I with Column II:<br>Choose the correct option from the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Polyembryony<br>B. Perisperm<br>C. False fruit<br>D. Parthenocarpy</div><div class="column-right">P. Black pepper<br>Q. Banana<br>R. Lemon<br>S. Apple</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R,B - P,C - S,D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - P,B - R,C - S,D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q,B - P,C - S,D - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R,B - S,C - P,D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{A - R,B - P,C - S,D - Q}}$<br>Polyembryony: The occurrence of more than one embryo in a seed.<br>Eg: Lemon.<br>Perisperm: The persistent nucellus is called perisperm.<br>Eg: Black pepper and beet.<br>False fruit: When fruit is formed from any other parts of the flower except ovary. In apple, cashew and strawberry, thalamus contributes to the formation of edible part.<br>Parthenocarpy: When fruits are produced without undergoing fertilization.<br>Eg: Banana',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7238,'biology',81,1044,2467,'Which is the intermediate compound that links the end product of Glycolysis with TCA Cycle?','[{"text": "Acetyl CoA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pyruvic Acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "OAA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Citric Acid", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pyruvate is the end product of glycolysis. Pyruvate undergoes oxidative decarboxylation to form acetyl coenzyme A (a 2-C compound), which then enters TCA (Krebs\'s) cycle, occuring in the matrix part of mitochondria.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7239,'biology',83,495,1011,'The segmental appendages of <em>Nereis</em> are','[{"text": "Setae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parapodia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tentacles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Suckers", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Segmental appendages that are found in Nereis are parapodia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7240,'biology',82,1271,3087,'Which PGR responsible for senescence in leaves and flowers?','[{"text": "Auxins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gibberellins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokinins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethylene", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'PGR ethylene is responsible for senescence in leaves and flowers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7241,'biology',8,154,328,'Identify the set of correct statements:<br>I. The flowers of <i>Vallisneria</i> are colourful and produce nectar.<br>II. The flowers of water lily are not pollinated by water.<br>III. In most of water-pollinated species, the pollen grains are protected from wetting<br>IV. Pollen grains of some hydrophytes are long and ribbon like.<br>V. In some hydrophytes, the pollen grains are carried passively inside water.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.','[{"text": "III, IV and V only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III and IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV and V only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV and V only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Flowers of <i>Vallisneria</i> are not colourful and do not produce nectar. Water lily is pollinated by insect or wind. In water-pollinated species, pollen grains are protected from wetting by a mucilaginous covering. In some hydrophytes such as <i>Vallisneria</i> pollen grains are carried passively by water current.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7242,'biology',81,1045,2468,'Identify the step in tricarboxylic acid cycle, which does not involve oxidation of substrate.','[{"text": "Malic acid $\\\\rightarrow$ Oxaloacetic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Succinic acid $\\\\rightarrow$ Malic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Succinyl-CoA $\\\\rightarrow$ Succinic acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Isocitrate $\\\\rightarrow \\\\alpha$-ketoglutaric acid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Oxidation involves the loss of electrons (often as part of hydrogen) from a molecule, leaving to an increase in its oxidation state. This process is typically associated with the transfer of electrons to an electron acceptor which is reduced in the process.The conversion of succinyl CoA to succinic acid involves hydration and formation of GTP.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7243,'biology',83,495,1011,'<i>Nereis</i> possesses lateral appendages called parapodia which help in','[{"text": "Respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Swimming", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Locomotion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Nereis possess lateral appendages, parapodia, which help in swimming.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7244,'biology',82,1271,3087,'Large amounts of ethylene is synthesized in','[{"text": "Flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Newly grown leaf", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ripening fruit", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ethylene is a simple gaseous PGR. It is synthesised in large amounts by tissues undergoing senescence and ripening fruits.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7245,'biology',8,154,328,'Identify the correct description about the given figure:','[{"text": "Wind pollinated plant inflorescence showing flowers with well exposed stamens.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Water pollinated flowers showing stamens with mucilaginous covering.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cleistogamous flowers showing autogamy.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Compact inflorescence showing complete autogamy", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The given diagram shows a wind pollinated plant showing compact inflorescence and well exposed stamens.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/8_7245_question_1.png'),
(7246,'biology',81,1046,2469,'Match Column I with Column II<br>Choose the correct answer from the options\ngiven below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Citric acid cycle<br>B.Glycolysis<br>C. Electron transport system<br>D. Proton gradient</div><div class="column-right">P. Cytoplasm<br>Q. Mitochondrial matrix<br>R. Intermembrane space of mitochondria<br>S. Inner mitochondrial membrane</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  Q, C  -  R, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  P, C  -  S, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  P, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{Q,}}\\,{\\rm{B}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{P,}}\\,{\\rm{C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S,}}\\,{\\rm{D}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{R}}$ is the correct option.<br>Citric acid cycle occurs in mitochondrial matrix.<br>Glycolysis occurs in cytosol in most of the organism.<br>Electron transport system is present in the inner mitochondrial membrane.<br>Proton gradient is formed across the intermembrane space of mitochondria.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7247,'biology',83,495,1011,'Which statement regarding <i>Nereis</i> is wrong?','[{"text": "It has nephridium for excretion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is metamerically segmented", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is dioecious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It has circular muscles for swimming", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Nereis possess lateral appendages, parapodia, which help in swimming.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7248,'biology',82,1271,3087,'What are the influences of ethylene on plants?','[{"text": "Apical hook formation in dicot seedling", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Swelling of the axis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Horizontal growth of seedlings", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Influences of ethylene on plants include horizontal growth of seedlings, swelling of the axis and apical hook formation in dicot seedlings. Ethylene promotes senescence and abscission of plant organs especially of leaves and flowers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7249,'biology',83,495,1011,'Which of the following is related with <i>Nereis</i>?','[{"text": "Parapodia present", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dioecious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monoecious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Nereis, an aquatic form, is dioecious and it possesses lateral appendages, parapodia, that assist in swimming.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
