(7337,'biology',82,1272,3088,'What are the actions of ABA?','[{"text": "General plant growth inhibitor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inhibitor of plant metabolism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimulates the closure of stomata in epidermis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'ABA acts as a general plant growth inhibitor and an inhibitor of plant metabolism. ABA inhibits seed germination. ABA stimulates the closure of stomata and increases the tolerance of plants to various kinds of stresses. Therefore, it is also called the stress hormone.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
