(7416,'biology',84,579,1158,'The tubular gland of the stomach consists of','[{"text": "Striated epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cuboidal epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ciliated epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Columnar epithelium", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Columnar epithelium cells are specialised for function of secretion in tubular gland of stomach.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7417,'biology',83,497,1013,'The animal\'s body belonging to phylum Mollusca is divided into','[{"text": "Head, thorax and abdomen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Head, muscular foot and abdomen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Head, muscular foot and visceral hump", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Head, abdomen and visceral hump", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Body is covered by a calcareous shell and is unsegmented with a distinct head, muscular foot and visceral hump.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7419,'biology',82,1273,3089,'Short day plant also called','[{"text": "Short night plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Long night plant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Intermediate night plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Short day plant is also called as long night plant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7420,'biology',84,579,1158,'Endometrium refers to the inner lining of','[{"text": "Uterus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bones and blood vessels", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intestine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Endometrium is the inner epithelial layer of mammalian uterus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7421,'biology',83,497,1013,'Visceral hump is present in','[{"text": "Antedon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cockroach", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aplysia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aurelia", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'It is present in mollusca only.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7423,'biology',82,1273,3089,'According to hypothesis, which substances are responsible for photoperiodism?','[{"text": "Flower itself", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abscisic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gibberellins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hormonal substance", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'It has been hypothesised that there is a hormonal substance(s) that is responsible for flowering. This hormonal substance migrates from leaves to shoot apices for inducing flowering only when the plants are exposed to the necessary inductive photoperiod.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7424,'biology',84,579,1158,'Some of the A or B cells get specialised for secretion and are called glandular epithelium','[{"text": "A - Ciliated, B - Squamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Squamous, B - Columnar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Columnar, B - Cuboidal", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Cuboidal, B - Ciliated", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Some of the columnar or cuboidal cells get specialised for secretion and are called glandular epithelium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7425,'biology',83,497,1013,'The feeding organ in phylum-Mollusca is','[{"text": "Cnidoblast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prostomium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mouth and teeth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Radula", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The mouth of molluscs contains a file-like rasping organ for feeding, called radula.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7427,'biology',82,1273,3089,'Name the term used for the response of plants to periods of day/night?','[{"text": "Photoperiodism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aestivation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vernalization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dormancy", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Photoperiodism is the term used for the response of plants to periods of day/night.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7428,'biology',84,579,1158,'The inability to absorb nutrients may be due to damage of which type of epithelium?','[{"text": "Simple glandular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stratified squamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ciliated columnar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brush bordered columnar", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The inability to absorb nutrients may be due to damage brush - bordered columnar epithelium as columnar epithelium mainly helps in absorption and secretion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7429,'biology',83,497,1013,'In molluscs mouth contains a file like rasping organ called-','[{"text": "Radula", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mantle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prostomium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Operculum", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The mouth of molluscs contains a file-like rasping organ for feeding, called radula.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7431,'biology',82,1274,3090,'When flowering is either quantitatively or qualitatively dependent or exposure to low temperature it is called phenomenon.','[{"text": "Photoperiodism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aestivation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vernalization", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dormancy", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When flowering is either quantitatively or qualitatively dependent or exposure to low temperature it is called vernalization phenomenon.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7432,'biology',84,579,1158,'The columnar epithelium in human body is found in<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Stomach", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fallopian tube", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The columnar epithelium is composed of a single layer of tall and slender cells which possess microvilli on their free surfaces. These are found in the lining of the stomach and intestine and help in secretion and absorption.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7433,'biology',83,497,1013,'Molluscs are -','[{"text": "Unsegmented", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Soft bodied", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shelled", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the given characteristics match that of Molluscs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7435,'biology',82,1274,3090,'Which of the plants don\'t have winter and spring varieties?','[{"text": "Wheat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rice", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Barley", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rye", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Rice plants don\'t have winter and spring varieties. Wheat, Barley and rye have spring and winter varieties.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7436,'biology',83,497,1013,'The main body parts common to all molluscs are the-','[{"text": "Radula and the mantle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Visceral mass, shell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Visceral mass (hump) and mantle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Radula, visceral mass", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Radula and hump are both common to all molluscs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7437,'biology',84,579,1158,'Which of the following epithelium types helps in the secretion and absorption of nutrients?','[{"text": "Columnar ciliated epithelium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cuboidal epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neurosensory epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Germinal epithelium", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The columnar ciliated epithelium mainly helps in absorption and secretion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7439,'biology',82,1274,3090,'Hormone, which replaces the requirement of vernalisation is','[{"text": "Ethylene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ABA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gibberllin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cytokinin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Hormone, which replaces the requirement of vernalisaton is Gibberellin. Gibberellin overcomes vernalization requirement (low temperature) for flowering. Gibberellins affect several reproductive processes in plants. They stimulate flowering, particularly in long-day plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7440,'biology',83,497,1013,'Closed circulatory system is found in','[{"text": "Snake", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cuttle fish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cockroach", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Closed circulatory system is found in cephalopod molluscs like cuttlefish and in reptiles like snake.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7441,'biology',84,579,1158,'The type of tissue lining in the tracheal passage and the bronchioles is','[{"text": "Columnar ciliated epithelium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cuboidal epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neurosensory epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Germinal epithelium", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Columnar ciliated epithelium comprises of columnar cells, which have cilia on the free surfaces. This epithelium lines most of the respiratory tract like nasal passage and bronchioles and Fallopian tubes (oviducts). It also lines the ventricles of the brain and the central canal of the spinal cord. It is also present in tympanic cavity of the middle ear and auditory tube.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7443,'biology',82,1274,3090,'When are winter varieties planted?','[{"text": "Spring", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Winter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autumn", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Winter varieties are planted in autumn. They germinate, and over winter come out as small seedlings, resume growth in the spring, and are harvested usually around mid-summer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7444,'biology',83,497,1013,'Which one belongs to mollusca?','[{"text": "Dog Fish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Devil Fish", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Jelly Fish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Silver Fish", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Devil fish is the common name used for Octopus. It belongs to Phylum Mollusca.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7445,'biology',84,579,1158,'Match the columns I and II<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Squamous epithelium<br>B. Cuboidal epithelium<br>C. Columnar epithelium<br></div><div class="column-right">P. Ducts of glands <br>Q. Air sacs of lungs<br>R. Lining of stomach</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Squamous epithelium - Air sacs of lungs Cuboidal epithelium - Ducts of glands<br>Columnar epithelium - Lining of stomach',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7447,'biology',82,1274,3090,'When is the harvesting of winter varieties done?','[{"text": "Spring", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Winter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mid-summer", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Autumn", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Winter varieties are planted in autumn. They germinate, and over winter come out as small seedlings, resume growth in the spring, and are harvested usually around mid-summer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7448,'biology',83,497,1013,'Which of the following is commonly called \'Apple snail\'','[{"text": "<i>Limulus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Dentalium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pila</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Chaetopleura</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pila is commonly known as apple snail.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7449,'biology',84,579,1158,'Identify the type of epithelium marked as $a, b, c$.','[{"text": "a - squamous, b - columnar, c - cuboidal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a - cuboidal, b - columnar, c - squamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a - squamous, b - cuboidal, c - columnar", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a - columnar, b - cuboidal, c - squamous", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Given diagrams are showing different types of epithelium, which can be labelled as:<br>a - squamous, b - cuboidal, c - columnar.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/84_7449_question_1.png'),
(7451,'biology',82,1274,3090,'Biennials are what kind of plants?','[{"text": "Dicarpous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monocarpellary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polycarpic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monocarpic", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Biennial plants are monocarpic plants that normally flower and die in the second season. Sugarbeet, cabbages, carrots are some of the common biennials.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7452,'biology',83,497,1013,'Pearls are obtained from','[{"text": "<i>Sepia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pinctada</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Dentalium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pila</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pinctada is a mollusc which is known to provide the pearls we use to this date.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7453,'biology',84,579,1158,'Which type of tissues forms glands?','[{"text": "Connective", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nervous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Muscular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epithelial", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Some of the columnar epithelial or cuboidal epithelial cells get specialised for secretion and are called glandular epithelium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
