(7455,'biology',82,1274,3090,'Which of the following are examples of common biennials?','[{"text": "Sugarbeet", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cabbages", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carrot", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Biennial plants are monocarpic plants that normally flower and die in the second season. Sugarbeet, cabbages, carrots are some of the common biennials.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7456,'biology',83,497,1013,'Which of the following is not a characteristic feature of phylum mollusca?','[{"text": "They are bilaterally symmetrical, triploblastic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unsegmented animals, coelomate animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are usually monoecious and oviparous with indirect development", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Respiratory organs are feather like gills in all molluscs and are present in the mantle cavity", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Molluscs are usually dioecious and oviparous with indirect development.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7457,'biology',84,579,1158,'The tissue, which forms the glands are a type of','[{"text": "Columnar cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cuboidal cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Some of the columnar epithelial or cuboidal epithelial cells get specialised for secretion and are called glandular epithelium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7459,'biology',82,1273,3089,'Observe the following diagram carefully and classify the plants with respect to photoperiodism____','[{"text": "P-Day neutral plants, Q- Short day plants, R- Long day plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P- Long day plants, Q- Short day plants, R- Day neutral plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "P- Short day plants, Q- Long day plants, R- Day neutral plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P-Short day plants, Q- Day neutral plants, R- long day plants.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The given diagram is showing photoperiodism : P- Long day, Q- short day and R- day neutral plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/82_7459_question_1.png'),
(7460,'biology',84,579,1158,'Goblet glands are','[{"text": "Unicellular endocrine glands of intestine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unicellular exocrine glands of intestine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Multicellular endocrine glands of gut", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multicellular exocrine glands of gut", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Goblet glands are unicellular exocrine glands of intestine.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7461,'biology',83,497,1013,'What is true about mollusca?','[{"text": "The presence of water vascular cavity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The presence of mantle cavity and unsegmented body", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The presence of organ level of organisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The presence of chitinous exoskeleton", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Molluscs exhibit organ system level of organisation. Mantle cavity is present and body is soft, unsegmented.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7463,'biology',82,1273,3089,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Long day plants<br>B. Short day plants<br>C. Day-neutral plants</div><div class="column-right">P. Needs light exposure below critical period for flowering<br>Q. Needs light exposure above critical period for flowering<br>R. Flowering is not related with the exposure to light</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Long day plants - Needs light exposure above critical period for flowering<br>Short day plants - Needs light exposure above critical period for flowering<br>Day neutral plants - Flowering is not related with the exposure to light',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7464,'biology',83,497,1013,'Select the correct answer about mollusca?<br>I. The space between the hump and the mantle is called the mantle cavity in which feather like gills are present.<br>II. A tough and spongy layer of skin forms a mantle over the visceral hump.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A soft and spongy layer of skin forms a mantle over the visceral hump.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7465,'biology',84,579,1158,'Goblet cells of respiratory tract are a type of','[{"text": "Intercellular gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multicellular gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unicellular gland", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Goblet cells are a type of unicellular gland. Some of the columnar or cuboidal cells get specialised for secretion and are called glandular epithelium. They may be unicellular, e.g., goblet cells of alimentary canal or multicellular, e.g., salivary glands',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7467,'biology',82,1274,3090,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Site of perception of light/dark duration<br>B. Harvested in mid-summer<br>C. Biennial plants</div><div class="column-right">P. Leaves<br>Q. Sugarbeet, cabbages, carrots<br>R. Winter variety of crop</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P},  \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Site of perception of light/dark duration Leaves<br>Harvested in mid-summer - Winter variety of crop<br>Biennial plants - Sugarbeet, Cabbages, carrots',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7468,'biology',83,497,1013,'Choose the correct option for phylum-Mollusca','[{"text": "Body is covered by a calcareous shell and segmented", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Feather-like gills present for digestion and respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The anterior head region has sensory tentacles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mostly terrestrial, triploblastic and acoelomates", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Body is covered by a calcareous shell and is unsegmented. The space between the hump and the mantle is called the mantle cavity in which feather like gills are present. They have respiratory and excretory functions. The anterior head region has sensory tentacles. They are exclusively marine, triploblastic and coelomates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7469,'biology',84,579,1158,'Goblet cells secrete','[{"text": "Serum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mucous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sebum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Milk", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Goblet cells are a type of unicellular gland. Goblet cells secrete mucous consisting of cluster of cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7471,'biology',82,1274,3090,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Site of perception of light/dark duration<br>B. Exposure to low temperature<br>C. Spring variety<br>D. Winter variety</div><div class="column-right">P. Vernalisation<br>Q. Leaves<br>R. Planted in the spring<br>S. Planted in autumn</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Site of perception of light/dark duration - Leaves<br>Exposure to low temperature - vernalisation<br>Spring variety - planted in spring<br>Winter variety - planted in autumn',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7472,'biology',83,497,1013,'Which of the following is incorrect match?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$Loligo\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\, - \\\\,{\\\\rm{Squid}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$Sepia\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\, - \\\\,{\\\\rm{Cuttle fish}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$Mango\\\\,snail - \\\\,{\\\\rm{Pila}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$Denta\\\\lim \\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\, - \\\\,{\\\\rm{Tusk shell}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pila is commonly known as apple snail.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7473,'biology',84,579,1158,'Which of the following are multicellular glands?','[{"text": "Salivary glands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Goblet cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sebaceous glands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Salivary gland and sebaceous glands are multicellular glands.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7475,'biology',82,1275,3091,'Certain seeds which fail to germinate even when external conditions are favourable is due to','[{"text": "Photoperiodism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed dormancy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vernalisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasticity", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Certain seeds which fail to germinate even when external conditions are favourable is due to seed dormancy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7476,'biology',84,579,1158,'Categorisation of glands can be done on the basis of','[{"text": "Mode of pouring of their secretion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mode of forming the secretion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mode of action", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'On the basis of pouring of secretions, glands are classified into two categories, i.e. endocrine and exocrine. Endocrine glands do not have ducts and their products called hormones are secreted directly into the fluid bathing the gland. Exocrine glands release their products through ducts or tubes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7477,'biology',83,497,1013,'Similarity between annelids and mollusca is','[{"text": "Triploblastic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coelomates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bilaterally symmetrical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the mentioned features are that of both annelids and molluscs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7780,'biology',83,500,1017,'Which of the following is a cephalochordate?','[{"text": "<em>Branchiostoma</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphioxus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lancelet", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Example of Cephalochordata - <em>Branchiostoma</em> (Amphioxus or Lancelet).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7479,'biology',82,1275,3091,'Which of the following is/are factor causing seed dormancy?','[{"text": "Impermeable and hard seed coat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemical inhibitors like abscisic acids, phenolic acids and para-ascorbic acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Immature embryos", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Impermeable and hard seed coat; presence of chemical inhibitors such as abscissic acids, phenolic acids, para-ascorbic acid; and immature embryos are some of the reasons which causes seed dormancy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7480,'biology',83,497,1013,'Select the incorrect example of mollusca?','[{"text": "<i>Aplysia</i> (Seahare)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Chaetopleura</i> (Chiton)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pinctada</i> (Pearl oyster)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pinctada</i> (Coral oyster)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pinctada is commonly known as pearl oyster.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7481,'biology',84,579,1158,'Which of the following secretions are released through ducts in human body?','[{"text": "Milk", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mucus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Digestive enzymes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Exocrine glands release their products through ducts or tubes. The secretions of exocrine glands include ear wax, mucus, saliva, oil, milk, digestive enzymes etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7483,'biology',82,1275,3091,'Which of the following method would help in breaking seed dormancy?','[{"text": "Mechanical abrasions using knives, sandpaper, etc", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microbial action", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Changing the environmental conditions like light and temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Seed dormancy can be overcome through natural means and various other man-made measures. For example, the seed coat barrier in some seeds can be broken by mechanical abrasions using knives, sandpaper, etc. or vigorous shaking. In nature, these abrasions are caused by microbial action, and passage through digestive tract of animals. Effect of inhibitory substances can be removed by subjecting the seeds to chilling conditions or by application of certain chemicals like gibberellic acid and nitrates. Changing the environmental conditions, such as light and temperature are other methods to overcome seed dormancy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7484,'biology',83,497,1013,'Which of the following is unsegmented and has a radula?','[{"text": "Earthworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Limulus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Sepia</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Antedon</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Radula is a characteristic feature of molluscs. They have soft, unsegmented bodies.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7485,'biology',84,579,1158,'Which of the following gland do not have duct?','[{"text": "Salivary gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mammary gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intestinal gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroid gland", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Exocrine glands secrete mucus, saliva, earwax, oil, milk, digestive enzymes and other cell products. These products are released through ducts or tubes. In contrast, endocrine glands do not have ducts. Their products called hormones are secreted directly into the fluid bathing the gland. Pituitary, pineal, thyroid, adrenal, pancreas, parathyroid, thymus and gonads (testis in males and ovary in females) are the organised endocrine bodies in our body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7487,'biology',83,497,1013,'<i>Loligo</i> is also called as','[{"text": "Tusk shell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cuttlefish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Squid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Apple snail", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Loligo is commonly known as Squid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7488,'biology',84,579,1158,'Mammary glands are','[{"text": "Unicellular endocrine glands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unicellular exocrine glands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multicellular endocrine glands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multicellular exocrine glands", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mammary glands are multicellular exocrine glands. Mammary glands secrete milk ducts or tubes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7489,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Read the following statements about the<br>I. Phase of maturation-Cells attain their maximal size, proper wall thickening and protoplasmic modifications, the cells in this region are rich in protoplasm, possess large conspicuous nucleus.<br>II. Phase of elongation- It is characterised by rapid cell division, the cells proximal (just next, away from the tip) to the meristematic zone<br>Choose the correct option.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are wrong", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the given statements are wrong. Phase of maturation: The cells of maturation zone, attain their maximal size in terms of wall thickening and protoplasmic modifications.<br>Phase of elongation : Increased vacuolation, cell enlargement and new cell wall deposition are the characteristics of the cells in phase of elongation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7491,'biology',83,497,1013,'In which one of the following the genus name, its two characters and its phylum are not correctly matched, whereas the remaining three are correct?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Genus name : <i>Asterias</i><br>Two Characters :<br>(i) Spiny Skinned ;<br>(ii) Water vascular system<br>Phylum: Echinodermata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus name :<i>Pila</i><br>Two Characters :<br>(i) Body segmented;<br>(ii) Mouth with Radula<br>Phylum : Mollusca", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genus name : <i>Sycon</i><br>Two Characters :<br>(i) Pore bearing;<br>(ii) Canal system<br>Phylum : Porifera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus name : <i>Periplaneta</i><br>Two Characters :<br>(i) Jointed appendages;<br>(ii) Chitinous exoskeleton<br>Phylum : Arthropoda", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Body of molluscs is unsegmented.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7492,'biology',84,579,1158,'Endocrine glands','[{"text": "Do not have ducts", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Have ducts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Have ducts sometimes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Endocrine glands do not have ducts. Their products called hormones are secreted directly into the fluid bathing the gland.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7493,'biology',82,1272,3088,'Identify the correct match<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Ethylene- Lateral dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ABA- promotes flowering", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Auxins- stem elongation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethylene- root formation", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ethylene promotes root formation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7495,'biology',84,579,1158,'The skin becomes oily due to the secretion of','[{"text": "Sudoriferous glands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sebaceous glands", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sweat glands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ceruminous glands", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The skin becomes oily due to the secretion of sebaceous gland. The glands secrete sebum through the sebaceous duct into the follicle and onto the surface of the skin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7496,'biology',83,497,1013,'Among the given figures $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{C}$ and $\\mathrm{D}$, identify the animals which is/ are dioecious, coelomate with segmentation?<br>Identify the correct options','[{"text": "A and $\\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and D", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "C and D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B and C", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Figure A represents grasshopper, an arthropod and figure D represents Nereis, an annelid. Both are dioecious, coelomate and echibit metameric segmentation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_7496_question_1.png'),
(7497,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Identify the correct statement.<br>I. Elongation of a plant along the axis is called primary growth<br>II. Increase in girth of plants occurs due to the apical meristem.<br>III. Secondary growth of plants occurs due to the lateral meristem.<br>IV. Vascular cambium and cork cambium are the lateral meristems of plants.','[{"text": "I, III and, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Increase in girth of plants occurs due to the lateral meristem.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7499,'biology',84,579,1158,'Which of the following statements is false about the glands?','[{"text": "Exocrine glands posses duct for secretion of mucus, milk, saliva, earwax, digestive enzymes, oil and other cell products", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Goblet cells secrete mucus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endocrine glands secretes a variety of enzymes only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glandular epithelium consists of specialized columnar or cuboidal cells", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Endocrine glands secrete only hormones directly into the fluid bathing the gland.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7500,'biology',83,497,1013,'The figure shows four animals 1, 2, 3 and 4. Select the correct answer with respect to a common characteristics of two of these animals:','[{"text": "3 and 4 have a true coelom", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 4 respire mainly through body wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 and 3 show radial symmetry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2 have Cnidoblasts for self defense", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Figure 2 represents Aurelia (Coelentrata) and Figure 3 represents Octopus (Mollusca). Both are true coelomates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_7500_question_1.png'),
(7501,'biology',82,1272,3088,'Identify the mismatch<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Promotion of flowering in pineapple Ethylene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Seed dormancy - ABA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apical dominance - Auxins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Senescence in leaves - Ethylene", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Auxins promote flowering e.g. in pineapples.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7503,'biology',84,579,1158,'Identify the correct heterocrine glands','[{"text": "Thyroid, Ovary, Pancreas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testis, Pancreas, Ovary", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pancreas, Ovary, Adrenal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovary, Thymus, Testis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Heterocrine glands (also known as mixed glands) are the glands which function as both exocrine gland and endocrine gland. These include the pancreas and the gonads (testes and ovaries).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7504,'biology',83,497,1013,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <em>Chaetopleura</em><br>B. <em>Dentalium</em><br>C. <em>Aplysia</em><br>D. Devil fish</div><div class="column-right">P. Tusk shell<br>Q. Seahare<br>R. Chiton<br>S. Octopus</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. <em>Chaetopleura</em> - R. Chiton<br>B.<em> Dentalium</em> - P. Tusk shell<br>C.<em> Aplysia</em>-Q. Seahare<br>D. Devil fish - S. Octopus',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7506,'biology',82,1269,3085,'How many of the following are the effects influenced by gibberellin?<br>1) Apple - elongation and improve its shape<br>2) Pineapple - elongation and improve its shape<br>3) Brewing and baking<br>4) Tissue culture<br>5) Kill dicot weeds','[{"text": "1, 3, 5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1, 3, 4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2, 3, 4", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Apple - elongation and improve its shape is the only correct effect brought by gibberellin.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7507,'biology',84,579,1158,'Match the columns I and II<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Unicellular  gland<br>B. Multicellular exocrine gland<br>C. Endocrine gland</div><div class="column-right">P. Thymus<br>Q. Goblet cells<br>R Salivary gland</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Unicellular gland - Goblet cells<br>Multicellular gland - Salivary gland<br>Endocrine gland - Thymus',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7508,'biology',83,497,1013,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <em>Pila</em><br>B. <em>Pinctada</em><br>C. <em>Sepia</em></div><div class="column-right">P. Cuttlefish<br>Q. Apple snail<br>R. Pearl oyster</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. <em>Pila </em>- Q. Apple snail<br>B. <em>Pinctada</em> - R. Pearl oyster<br>C. <em>Sepia </em>- P. Cuttlefish',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7510,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Select the correct statements regarding auxins.<br>I. Auxins promote flowering e.g. in pineapple and promote abscission of new leaves and fruits.<br>II. Auxin controls dicot weed','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Auxins promote flowering e.g. in pineapples. They help to prevent fruit and leaf drop at early stages but promote the abscission of older mature leaves and fruits',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7511,'biology',84,579,1158,'Select the correct answer<br>I. Compound epithelium is made of more than one layer (multi-layered) of cells.<br>II. Compound epithelium has a limited role in secretion and absorption.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct. Compound epithelium is made of more than one layer (multi-layered) of cells. Compound epithelium has a limited role in secretion and absorption.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7512,'biology',83,497,1013,'Match the columns I and II wrt to excretion.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Gills<br>B. Malpighian tubule<br>C. Nephridia<br>D. Flame cells</div><div class="column-right">P. Arthropoda<br>Q. Annelida<br>R. Mollusca<br>S. Platyhelminthes</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P},  \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q},  \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. Gills - R. Mollusca<br>B. Malpighian tubules - P. Arthropoda<br>C. Nephridia - Q. Annelida<br>D. Flame cells - S. Platyhelminthes',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7514,'biology',82,1269,3085,'Identify the correct function of GA.<br>I. Acts as general plant growth inhibitor and an inhibitor of plant metabolism.<br>II. Plays an important role in seed development, maturation and dormancy<br>III. Helps seeds withstand desiccation and other factors unfavourable for growth.','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the given functions are of abscisic acid. (ABA)',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7515,'biology',84,579,1158,'The given image depicts','[{"text": "Squamous epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multicellular glandular epithelium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Compound epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unicellular glandular epithelium", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The given image depicts multicellular Glandular epithelium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/84_7515_question_1.png'),
(7516,'biology',83,498,1014,'All are marine without any exception with organ-system level of organisation?','[{"text": "Chordata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pisces", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Echinodermata", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Porifera", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Echinoderms are exclusively marine animals that possess organ system level of organisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7518,'biology',82,1271,3087,'How many of the following are the effects influenced by ethylene?<br>1) Synchronising fruit set in pineapples<br>2) Xylem differentiation<br>3) Promotes female flowers in cucumbers<br>4) Produce new leaves and chloroplasts in leaves<br>5) Bolting in cabbage','[{"text": "1, 3, 5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1, 3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1, 2, 4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2, 3, 4", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ethylene is used to initiate flowering and for synchronising fruit-set in pineapples and also it promotes female flowers in cucumbers thereby increasing the yield. Auxin controls xylem differentiation and helps in cell division. Cytokinins help produce new leaves and chloroplasts in leaves. Gibberellins also promotes bolting (internode elongation just prior to flowering) in beet, cabbages and many plants with rosette habit.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7519,'biology',84,579,1158,'The stratified epithelium in which the outermost layer becomes keratinised is found in','[{"text": "Skin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cheeks", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vagina", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pharynx", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The stratified epithelium in which the outermost layer becomes keratinised is found in skin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7520,'biology',83,498,1014,'Which of the following is distinctive feature of phylum echinodermata.','[{"text": "Presence of cnidoblast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Body with pores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water vascular system with radial symmetry", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The most distinctive feature of echinoderms is the presence of a water vascular system which helps in locomotion, capture and transport of food and respiration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7522,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Choose the not incorrect statement:','[{"text": "In beans, hypocotyl elongates faster", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Growth of pollen tube is measured in the terms of its length", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One single maize root apical meristem can give rise to more than 17,500 new cells per hour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are not incorrect i.e. all the statements are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7523,'biology',84,579,1158,'Compound epithelium','[{"text": "Plays major role in secretion and absorption", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Provides protection against chemical and mechanical stresses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Covers dry surface of skin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The main function of compound epithelium is to provide protection against chemical and mechanical stresses. They cover the dry surface of the skin, the moist surface of buccal cavity, pharynx, inner lining of ducts of salivary glands and of pancreatic ducts.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7524,'biology',83,498,1014,'Characteristic feature of phylum - Echinodermata is','[{"text": "Radial symmetry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water vascular system", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Jointed appendages", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The most distinctive feature of echinoderms is the presence of a water vascular system which helps in locomotion, capture and transport of food and respiration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7526,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Which of the following effects of auxin on plants is the basis for their commercial application?','[{"text": "Callus formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Curvature of stem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Induction of root formation in stem cuttings", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Induction of shoot formation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Auxins help to initiate rooting in stem cuttings, an application widely used for plant propagation which forms the basis for their commercial application.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7527,'biology',83,498,1014,'Great power of regeneration and exclusively marine animals belong to the phylum','[{"text": "Mollusca", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Echinodermata", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cyclostomata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Annelida", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All echinoderms are marine with high regeneration capacity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7528,'biology',84,579,1158,'Compound squamous epithelium occurs in','[{"text": "Dry surface of the skin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The moist surface of buccal cavity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inner lining of ducts of salivary glands and of pancreatic ducts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The main function of compound epithelium is to provide protection against chemical and mechanical stresses. They cover the dry surface of the skin, the moist surface of buccal cavity, pharynx, inner lining of ducts of salivary glands and of pancreatic ducts.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7530,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Identify the correct functions of auxin','[{"text": "Cell division and controls xylem differentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Promotes flowering in pineapples", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apical dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Auxins help to initiate rooting in stem cuttings, an application widely used for plant propagation. Auxins promote flowering e.g. in pineapples. They help to prevent fruit and leaf drop at early stages but promote the abscission of older mature leaves and fruits. In most higher plants, the growing apical bud inhibits the growth of the lateral (axillary) buds, a phenomenon called apical dominance.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7531,'biology',83,498,1014,'In echinoderms adult  are _________  symmetrical but larvae  are _________  symmetrical?','[{"text": "Radially, bilaterally", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Radially, asymmetrical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bilaterally, radially", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bilaterally, assymetrical", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The adult echinoderms are radially symmetrical but larvae are bilaterally symmetrical.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7532,'biology',84,579,1158,'Compound epithelium that provides protection against chemical, mechanical, thermal or osmotic stresses includes','[{"text": "Pharynx", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Skin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Buccal cavity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Compound epithelium that provides protection against chemical mechanical thermal or Osmotic stresses includes skin, buccal cavity, pharynx, inner lining of ducts of salivary glands and of pancreatic ducts.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7534,'biology',82,1267,3083,'When a green plant is exposed to light on only one side, bends towards the source of light as it grows. What is the possible reason for this','[{"text": "Green plants are phototropic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Such an event never occurs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Auxin causes the following", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Green plants need light to perform photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When a green plant is exposed to light on only one side, plant bends towards the source of light as it grows. The possible reason for this is auxin causes following.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7535,'biology',84,579,1158,'Select the correct answer<br>I. All cells in epithelium are held together with little intercellular material.<br>II. In nearly all animal tissues, specialised junctions provide both structural and functional links between its individual cells.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct. All cells in epithelium are held together with little intercellular material. In nearly all animal tissues, specialised junctions provide both structural and functional links between its individual cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7536,'biology',83,498,1014,'Calcareous ossicles of echinodermates is','[{"text": "Endoskeleton", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Exoskeleton", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both endoskeleton and exoskeleton", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There is no skeleton", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Echinoderms have an endoskeleton of calcareous ossicles and, hence, the name Echinodermata (Spiny bodied).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
