(7718,'biology',82,1263,3078,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The simplest expression of arithmetic growth is exemplified by a root elongating at a constant rate.<br></div><div class="column-right">A parabolic growth curve is a characteristic of living organism growing in a natural environment.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A sigmoid growth curve is a characteristic of living organism growing in a natural environment.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7720,'biology',84,579,1159,'The type of tissue present in the pinna and tip of human nose','[{"text": "Cartilage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stratified epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Muscle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nervous tissue", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cartilage is the type of connective tissue which is highly flexible and less vascular. Cartilage smoothens bone surfaces at joints and is also present at the tip of the nose, outer ear, trachea, and larynx.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7721,'biology',83,500,1016,'Which among the following is true?','[{"text": "All vertebrates have open circulatory system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chordates have ventral hollow nerve cord", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All vertebrates are chordates.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All chordates are vertebrates", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Chordates have a dorsal hollow nerve cord. All vertebrates have a closed circulatory system. All chordates are not vertebrates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7736,'biology',84,579,1159,'Which of the following statements is incorrect?','[{"text": "Cartilage is present below skin, outer ear joints, attaches bone to bone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cartilage may be replaced by bones in adult", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cartilage has no rich blood supply", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cartilage is surrounded by perichondrium", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cartilage is present in the tip of nose, outer ear joints, between adjacent bones of the vertebral column, limbs and hands in adults.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
