(7829,'biology',82,1265,3080,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Differentiation in plants is closed.<br></div><div class="column-right">Differentiation results in development of structures that is commensurate with the function the cells finally has to perform.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Differentiation in plants is open and development is flexible.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7831,'biology',83,500,1018,'Which of the following group does not represent a class?','[{"text": "Amphibia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyclostomata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pisces", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pisces is a superclass.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7832,'biology',84,579,1160,'Smooth muscle fibres are','[{"text": "Spindle shaped, unbranched, unstriated, uninucleated and involuntary", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cylindrical, striated unbranched, multinucleate and voluntary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cylindrical, unbranched, non-striated, multinucleated and involuntary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spindle shaped, unbranched, non-striated, multinucleated and involuntary", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Smooth muscle fibres are spindle shaped, their fibres are unbranched, uninucleate, bounded by plasmalemma, they donot get fatigued and involuntary in function. They are present in the oesophagus, urinogenital tract, urinary bladder, vessels, iris of eye, dermis of skin, and arrector pili muscles of hair.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7833,'biology',82,1267,3082,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">PGR has diverse physiological effects on plants.<br></div><div class="column-right">Diverse PGRs manifest similar effects.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7835,'biology',83,501,1019,'The cyclostomes are','[{"text": "Marine and non migratory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fresh water form and non migratory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fresh water form and migrate character", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Marine and migrate to fresh water for spawning", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cyclostomes are marine but migrate for spawning to fresh water.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7836,'biology',84,579,1160,'Which of the following statements is false about the muscles?','[{"text": "The smooth muscle fibres are fusiform", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wall of blood vessels, stomach and intestine contain striated muscles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cell junctions hold smooth muscle fibres togetherand they are bundled together in a connective tissue sheath", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Wall of blood vessels, stomach and intestine contain smooth muscles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7837,'biology',82,1262,3077,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> As whole plant growth is indefinite.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Plants retain the capacity of continuous growth throughout their life.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The tissues in shoot tips are meristematic in nature.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7839,'biology',83,501,1019,'Lamprey (<i>Petromyzon</i>) and <i>Myxine</i> (Hag fish) are','[{"text": "Chondrichthyes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osteichthyes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphibia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Agnatha/Cyclostomata", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Class Cyclostomata includes Petromyzon (Lamprey) and Myxine (Hagfish).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7840,'biology',84,579,1160,'Find out incorrect statement','[{"text": "Smooth muscles are present in viscera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Smooth muscles are involuntary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Striated muscles are involuntary", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Myocardium has involuntary muscles", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Skeletal muscles are closely associated with the skeletal components of the body. They have a striped appearance under the microscope and hence are called striated muscles. As their activities are under the voluntary control of the nervous system, they are known as voluntary muscles too.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7841,'biology',82,1270,3086,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cytokinins are anti-senescent<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Effects of cytokinins in antagonistic to ethylene.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When cytokinins are added directly to the abscission layer, senescence of the zone is retarted. As they act as anti-senescent, they act as antagonistic to ethylene which accelerates senescence',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7843,'biology',83,501,1019,'Mark the incorrect statement about the members of the class cyclostomata','[{"text": "Circulation is of closed type", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Body devoid of scales and unpaired fins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Have a sucking and circular mouth without jaws", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All the mentioned features are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7844,'biology',84,579,1160,'Muscles which do not get tired are','[{"text": "Striated", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Smooth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cardiac", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Normal muscles like the skeletal muscles get fatigued (strenuous activities like exercise, sports etc.) due to the formation of lactic acid as a result of anaerobic glycolysis. But cardiac muscles do not form lactic acid due to the presence of rich capillary network which provides enough oxygen to the muscles. Anaerobic processes never occur in cardiac muscles, hence lactic acid is never formed enabling heart muscles to perform their function without fatigue. Hence we can say cardiac muscles do not get tired.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7845,'biology',82,1263,3078,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> On plotting the length of the root against time a linear curve is obtained<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> An elongating root at constant rate exemplifies arithmethic growth','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In arithmetic growth, following mitotic division only one daughter cell continues to divide and other differentiates and matures. It is exemplified by a root elongating at constant rate.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7847,'biology',83,501,1019,'Which of the following statement is incorrect w.r.t. class cyclostomata?','[{"text": "The members are ectoparasites on some fishes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Their body is devoid of scales and paired fins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Circulation is of closed ype", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are freshwater organism but migrate for spawning to marine water", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cyclostomes are marine but migrate for spawning to fresh water.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7848,'biology',84,579,1160,'Cardiac muscle cells differ from striated muscle cells in having','[{"text": "Myofibrils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No sarcoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A centrally located nucleus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fewer mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The cardiac muscle fibres are uninucleate and their nuclei are centrally placed. Striated muscle fibres are multinucleate and their nuclei lie at irregular intervals.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7849,'biology',82,1270,3086,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cytokinins increases shelf-life of fruits and vegetables<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Cytokinins induces cell division','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cytokinins cause delay in senescence of plant tissue, it is negative senescence regulator, if a small spot on a leaf treated with cytokinin, that spot remain green after surrounding tissues on the same leaf begin to senescence. Cytokinin is involved in the formation, maintenance and growth of shoot apical meristem; it is a positive regulators of cell division in shoot apical meristem and negative regulator in the root apical meristem.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7851,'biology',83,501,1019,'Which of the following options about the class-Cyclostomata is incorrect?','[{"text": "Cranium and vertebral column are cartilaginous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoparasites", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gill slits for respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sucking and cicular mouth", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All living members of the class Cyclostomata are ectoparasites on some fishes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7852,'biology',84,579,1160,'Cardiac muscles contract','[{"text": "Slowly and get fatigued", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Quickly and donot get fatigued", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Slowly and donot get fatigued", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Quickly and get fatigued", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cardiac muscles contract quickly and donot get fatigued. cardiac muscles do not form lactic acid due to the presence of rich capillary network which provides enough oxygen to the muscles. Anaerobic processes never occur in cardiac muscles, hence lactic acid is never formed enabling heart muscles to perform their function without fatigue.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7853,'biology',82,1266,3081,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The sum of growth and differentiation is development.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Development in plants is under the control of extrinsic factors only.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In the life of a plant, growth, differentiation and development are closely related events. Development is sum of growth and differentiation. Development in plants is under control of intrinsic and extrinsic factors. Intrinsic factors include intracellular genetic factors and intercellular factors. Extrinsic factors are light, temperature, water, oxygen and nutrition etc.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7855,'biology',83,501,1019,'Hagfish has','[{"text": "6-15 pairs of gill slits", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Closed type circulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bony skeleton", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Hagfish, a cyclostome, bears 6 to 15 pairs of gill slits and possesses a closed type of circulation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7856,'biology',84,579,1160,'In the cardiac muscles, identify the correct statement','[{"text": "Cell junction fuse the plasma membrane of adjacent cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contraction of one cell affects the other cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intercalated discs help in the communication among cardiac cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the given statements are correct. Cell junctions fuse the plasma membranes of cardiac muscle cells and make them stick together . Communication junctions (intercalated discs) at some fusion points allow the cells to contract as a unit, i.e., when one cell receives a signal to contract, its neighbours are also stimulated to contract.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7857,'biology',82,1274,3090,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The promotion of flowering by a period of low temperature is vernalisation.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It prevents precocious reproductive development late in growing season.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'There are plants for which flowering is either, quantitatively and qualitatively dependent on exposure to low temperature. This is termed as vernalization.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7859,'biology',83,501,1019,'Which of the following statements is not true about jawless fishes of the Agnatha?','[{"text": "They have notochord throughout their lives", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They include hag fish and lampreys", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Circulation is of open type", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The are known as cyclostomes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cyclostomates bear a closed type of circulation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7860,'biology',84,579,1160,'Intercalated discs are the communication junctions found in','[{"text": "Striped muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myocardium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Striated muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adipose tissue", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Communication junctions (intercalated discs) at some fusion points are found in cardiac muscles which allow the cells to contract as a unit, i.e., when one cell receives a signal to contract, its neighbours are also stimulated to contract.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7861,'biology',82,1268,3084,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Auxins help to prevent fruit and leaf drop at early stages.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Auxins promote the abscission of older mature leaves and fruits.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Auxin delays abscission of young leaves and fruits. Its effect is through nonformation of abscission zone below a leaf or fruit.<br>Abscission zone cuts off nutrients and water supply. However, auxin promotes the abscission of mature or older leaves and fruits.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7863,'biology',83,501,1019,'Lamprey is not a fish since it does not have','[{"text": "Closed blood vascular system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cranium and vertebral column", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Body scales", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Lamprey is devoid of scales, hence it is not a fish.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7864,'biology',84,579,1160,'Cardiac muscles are different from skeletal muscles as they are','[{"text": "Voluntary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Involuntary", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Smooth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Striated", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cardiac muscles are present in heart. They are involuntary, striated and have intercalated discs which differentiate them from skeletal muscles which are striated, voluntary and do not contain intercalated discs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7865,'biology',82,1268,3084,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The apical bud is the only source of auxins.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Removal of apical bud is the only way to promote lateral bud growth.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The apical bud is not the only source of auxins. Young developing leaves also produce auxins and it has been shown that auxins from this source may inhibit lateral bud growth.<br>When the apical bud is removed, the lateral buds sprout. However, if a paste of auxin is painted on the cut end of the decapitated shoot, the lateral buds remain inhibited, as if the apical bud is present.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7867,'biology',83,501,1019,'Jawless vertebrates belong to the group','[{"text": "Gnathostomata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Agnatha", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prototheria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lagomorpha", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Jawless vertebrates belong to the group Agnatha.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7868,'biology',84,579,1160,'Intercalated discs are the characteristic feature of _____ tissue.','[{"text": "Epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Connective", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Muscular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cardiac muscles", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Intercalated discs are the characteristic feature of cardiac muscle tissue which allow allow the cells to contract as a unit, i.e., when one cell receives a signal to contract, its neighbours are also stimulated to contract.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7869,'biology',82,1269,3085,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Gibberellins induce flowering in long day plants.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Genetically tall plant become dwarf by application of Gibberellin.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Application of GA can induce flowering in long day plants. It has no favourbale effect on size of flower and fruit in certain plants. The genetically dwarf plants can be made tall by application of GA.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7871,'biology',83,501,1019,'Which of the following characters are correct about the cyclostomata?','[{"text": "All living members of the class cyclostomata are ectoparasites on some fishes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cranium and vertebral column are cartilaginous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No paired fins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the mentioned features are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7872,'biology',84,579,1160,'Which of the following is correct?','[{"text": "Cardiac muscles are voluntary muscles found in the myocardium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Communication junctions called intercalated discs at some fusion points allow these cells to contract as a unit", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They show the absence of alternate light and dark bands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The cardiac fibres are multinucleate", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cardiac muscles are involuntary muscles found in the myocardium. Cardiac muscles do not show the absence of alternate light and dark bands. cardiac muscle cells are mononucleated in humans. However, cardiac muscle cells are functionally syncytium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7874,'biology',82,1268,3084,'How does pruning help in making the hedge dense<br>','[{"text": "It induces the differentiation of new shoots from the root stock", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It frees axillary buds from apical dominance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The apical shoot grows faster after pruning", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is released from wound hormones", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pruning frees axillary buds from apical dominance caused due to auxin hence help in making the hedge dense.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7875,'biology',83,501,1019,'Recognize the figure<br>The represented animal in the diagram -','[{"text": "Has 4 pairs of gills", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Has jaw that are very powerfull", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is a jawless vertebrate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Has persistent notochord", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Petromyzon is jawless vertebrate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_7875_question_1.png'),
(7876,'biology',84,579,1160,'Which of the following statements is correct about the cardiac muscles?<br>i. It is present in heart<br>ii. The plasma membranes of adjacent cardiac cells interlock at intercalated disc<br>iii. Gap junctions allow the cardiac cells to contract as a unit','[{"text": "i and ii only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'All the statements given about cardiac muscles are correct. Cardiac muscle tissue is a contractile tissue present only in the heart. Cell junctions fuse the plasma membranes of cardiac muscle cells and make them stick together . Communication junctions (intercalated discs) at some fusion points allow the cells to contract as a unit, i.e., when one cell receives a signal to contract, its neighbours are also stimulated to contract.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7878,'biology',82,1269,3085,'Parthenocarpic tomato fruits can be produced by<br>','[{"text": "Removing androecium of flowers before pollen grains are released", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Raising the plants from vernalised seeds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Treating the plants with low concentration of gibberellic acid & auxins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Treating the plants with phenyl mercuric acid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Parthenocarpy is the development of fruits without prior fertilization which results in the formation of seedless fruits. In some plant species, parthenocarpic fruits may be produced naturally or they may be induced by treatment of the unpollinated flowers with auxin',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7879,'biology',83,501,1019,'Which of the following is not correct about Lamprey?','[{"text": "Closed circulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Larval stage absent in their life cycle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sucking and circular mouth without jaw", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lamprey is marine but migrate for spawning to fresh water", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Lamprey (Petromyzon) has a larval stage called Ammocoete larva.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7880,'biology',84,579,1160,'Identify the labelled parts (A) and (B) in the figure.','[{"text": "A - Cardiac muscle tissue, B - Smooth muscle tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Skeletal muscle tissue, B - Cardiac muscle tissue", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Smooth muscle tissue, B - Cardiac muscle tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Cardiac muscle tissue, B - Skeletal muscle tissue", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The given diagram represents muscle tissue as<br>(A) - Skeletal (striated) muscle tissue (B) Cardiac muscle tissue.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/84_7880_question_1.png'),
(7882,'biology',82,1272,3088,'Which one of the following pairs is not correctly matched?<br><div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Gibberellic acid - Leaf fall", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cytokinin - Cell division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IAA - Cell wall elongation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ABA - Stomatal closure", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Gibberellic acid is a simple weak acidic plant growth hormone which promotes cell elongation of leaves and stem and generally not involve in abscission.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7883,'biology',83,501,1019,'In which of the following notochord is absent?','[{"text": "Adult tunicate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<em>Myxine</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lamprey", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Larval tunicates", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In Tunicata, only larval tails possess a notochord.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7887,'biology',83,501,1019,'Which of the following is correct w.r.t classification of <i>Myxine</i>?','[{"text": "Chordata, Vertebrata, Agnatha, Cyclostomata", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chordata, Agnatha, Pisces, Cyclostomata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chordata, Vertebrata, Gnathostomata, Chondrichthyes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chordata, Vertebrata, Gnathostomata, Tetrapoda", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Myxine belongs to Class Cyclostomata, Division Agnatha, Subphylum Vertebrata and Phylum Chordata.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
