(7898,'biology',82,1267,3083,'Phototropic curvature is the result of uneven distribution of','[{"text": "Gibberellins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phytochrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokinin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Auxin<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Phototropic curvature is the result of uneven distribution of auxin. Charles Darwin and Francis Darwin observed that the coleoptiles of canary grass responded to unilateral illumination by growing towards source of light. After many trials they concluded that auxin was responsible for bending of coleoptiles.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
