(7947,'biology',82,1270,3086,'You are given a tissue with its potential for differentiation in an artificial culture. Which of the following pairs of hormones would you add to the medium to secure shoots as well as roots?','[{"text": "IAA and gibberellin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "auxin and cytokinin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "auxin and abscisic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "gibberellins and abscisic acid<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Root and shoot formation during tissue culture requires hormones. Cytokinin and auxin in fixed proportions. A low auxin to cytokinin ratio promotes shoot formation whereas a high auxin to cytokinin ratio promotes rooting of callus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
