(7964,'biology',82,1268,3084,'The plant hormone used to destroy weeds in a field is:','[{"text": "IAA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "NAA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2, 4-D", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IBA<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'2, 4-D is a herbicide or weedicide used to destroy weeds of broad leaved dicot plants.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7965,'biology',83,502,1020,'Read the following statements and find out the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "In fighting fish gills are covered by operculum while in sting ray gill cover is absent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dog fish have teeth that are modified placoid scales", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mouth of flying fish is terminal while that of great white shark is ventral.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Air bladder present in saw fish which regulates buoyancy, while in Angel fish air bladder is absent", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Air bladder is not present in sawfish, while in some fish air bladder is present.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7968,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Which one of the following plants does not show plasticity?','[{"text": "Coriander", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Buttercup", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maize", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cotton<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Maize do not show plasticity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7969,'biology',83,502,1020,'Read the following four features (i-iv)<br>i. Gills-slits are covered by "operculum"<br>ii. The skin is tough, containing minute placoid scales.<br>iii. In male, pelvic fins bear claspers<br>iv. Air bladder is present which regulates buoyancy.<br>Out of these how many features are not exhibited by cartilaginous fishes?','[{"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In Chondrichthyes, gill slits are not covered by an operculum and an air bladder is absent.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7972,'biology',82,1271,3087,'The gaseous plant growth regulator is used in plants to<br>','[{"text": "promote root growth and root hair formation to increase the absorption surface", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "help overcome apical dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "kill dicotyledonous weeds in the fields", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "speed up the malting process", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Gaseous plant growth regulator is ethylene which promotes root growth and root hair formation to increase the absorption surface.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7973,'biology',83,503,1021,'In which of the following animal the notochord is replaced by bony vertebral column in the adult?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "<em>Scoliodon</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Branchiostoma</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hagfish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Clarias</em>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Notochord is replaced by bony vertebral column in Osteichthyes like <em>Clarias</em>.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7976,'biology',82,1271,3087,'Production of Cucumber has increased manifold in recent years. Application of which of the following phytohormones has resulted in this increased yield as the hormone is known to produce female flowers in the plants:','[{"text": "Gibberellin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethylene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cytokinin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ABA", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Increase in yield of cucumber is due to ethylene.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7977,'biology',83,503,1021,'In which of the following fish the skin is tough containing minute ctenoid scales?','[{"text": "<i>Exocoetus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Hippocampus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Labeo</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In Osteichthyes, the skin is tough containing minute ctenoid scales. Examples are - Exocoetus, Clarias and Labeo.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7980,'biology',82,1265,3080,'In tissue culture experiments, leaf mesophyll cells are put in a culture medium to form callus. This phenomenon may be called as','[{"text": "Differentiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dedifferentiation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Development", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Senescence", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In tissue culture experiments, leaf\nmesophyll cells are put in a culture medium\nto form callus. Dedifferentiation is a process\nby which the living differentiated plant cells,\nthat have lost the capacity to divide, regain the\ncapacity of division under appropriate\nconditions.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7982,'biology',83,503,1021,'Which of the following is a characteristic feature of osteichthyes?','[{"text": "Internal fertilisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gills are covered by an operculum on each side", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pelvic fins of bear claspers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viviparous", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Osteichthyes have four pairs of gills which are covered by an operculum on each side.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7984,'biology',82,1269,3085,'Spraying of which of the following phytohormone on juvenile conifers helps hastening the maturity period, that leads early seed production?','[{"text": "Indole-3-butyric Acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gibberellic Acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Zeatin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abscisic Acid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Spraying juvenile conifers with gibberellins\n(GAs) hastens the maturity period, thus leading\nto early seed production.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7985,'biology',83,503,1021,'Bony fishes can stay at a particular depth in water beating their pectoral and pelvic fins due to the presence of','[{"text": "Pneumatic bones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ctenoid scales", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Air bladder", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Streamlined body", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In Osteichthyes, body is streamlined so that fishes can stay at a particular depth. Air bladder is present which regulates buoyancy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7988,'biology',82,1271,3087,'Which hormone promotes internode/petiole elongation in deep water rice?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{G}}{{\\\\rm{A}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kinetin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethylene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2, 4-D", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ethylene promotes rapid internode/petiole elongation in deep water rice plants.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7989,'biology',83,503,1021,'The number of gills present in osteichthyes is','[{"text": "2 pairs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6 pairs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4 pairs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5 pairs", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Osteichthyes have four pairs of gills which are covered by an operculum on each side.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7992,'biology',82,1269,3085,'Genetically dwarf plants can be induced to grow tall by using:','[{"text": "Auxins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokinnis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gibberellins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phycobilins", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gibberellins is mainly involved in inducing bolting in rosette plants, elongating internodes in dwarf plants, overcoming dormancy, clongating stems and fruits, etc.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7993,'biology',83,503,1021,'Select the correct answer about osteichthyes<br>I. Mouth is mostly terminal<br>II. Skin is covered with cycloid/ctenoid scales','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7996,'biology',83,503,1021,'Heart is two-chambered','[{"text": "Chondrichthyes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osteichthyes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphibia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Heart is two-chambered in both classes of Superclass Pisces.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(7998,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Which of the following hormones does not naturally occur in plants?','[{"text": "IAA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ABA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2,4 - D", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'2,4-D is a synthetic auxin. They elicit auxin-like functions and have been produced synthetically.<br>IAA(Indole acetic acid) is a natural auxin. ABA (Abscisic acid) and GA(Gibberelic acid) are natural plant growth hormones.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8002,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Compare the statements A and B.<br>Select the correct description.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Auxins promote apical dominance by suppressing the activity of lateral buds.<br></div><div class="column-right">In moriculture, periodic pruning of shoot tips is done to make mulberry plants bushy.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct, and Statement B is wrong.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is wrong and Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements ar correct, and Statement A is not the reason for Statement B.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct, and Statement A is the reason for Statement B.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The presence of auxin in the apical bud, can be tested by applying some auxin containing paste on the cut portion of the shoot. It can be seen that the axillary bud is prevented from growing, hence confirming the role of auxin in apical dominance. If axillary bud resumes growth, the plant will have many branches and hence many leaves. This is commonly used to produce bushy plants.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8005,'biology',82,1269,3085,'The rosette habit of cabbage can be changed by application of:','[{"text": "IAA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ABA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethaphon", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The rosette plants (cabbage, spinach, etc.) generally do not flower into rosette form as they undergo a phenomenon called bolting just before flowering. In bolting, extensive internode elongation takes place, which prevents rosette formation. On application of gibberellin to certain cabbage plants, bolting is favoured and after some days, stem elongation was observed to a greater extent.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8006,'biology',83,503,1021,'Air bladder is present in','[{"text": "Rays", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Starfish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shark", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gold fish", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Gold fish belongs to Actinopterygii and possesses air bladder or swim bladder which provides buoyancy to the body. Rays and sharks lack swim bladder. Starfish is an invertebrate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8009,'biology',82,1272,3088,'Perishable vegetables can be maintained fresh for a longer period by spraying on them with a solution of:','[{"text": "ABA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokinin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ethephon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenyl mercuric acetate", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Commercially, cytokinins have been (i) used in tissue culture to form new plant varieties by morphogenesis, (ii) used to prolong the shelf-lives of vegetables such as cabbage, lettuce, etc., (iii) applied to cut flowers to keep them fresh; (iv) applied to help the plant develop resistance to certain pathogens and extreme temperature variations.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8010,'biology',83,503,1021,'Bony fishes can stay at any particular depth in water without spending energy due to','[{"text": "Operculum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of scutes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pneumatic bones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Swim bladder", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bony fishes can stay at any particular depth in water without spending energy due to presence of air bladder.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8025,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Which of the following statement is correct w.r.t growth in plants?<br>I. Plants retain the capacity for unlimited growth throughout their life<br>II. Meristem cells in plants have the capacity to divide and self-perpetuate<br>III. Presence of meristems at certain locations in their body enable plants to grow<br>IV. New cells are always being added is open form of growth','[{"text": "I, II & III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both II & III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III & IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both III & IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Plants retain the capacity for unlimited growth throughout their life, meristem cells in plants have the capacity to divide and self perpetuate, presence of meristems at certain locations in their body enable plants to grow, growth wherein new cells are always being added is open form of growth.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8013,'biology',82,1272,3088,'Match the entries in Column I with those of Column II and choose the correct answer.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Cytokinin<br>B. Auxins<br>C. Abscisic acid<br> D. Ethylene <br></div><div class="column-right">P. Stress hormone<br>Q. Ripening of fruits<br>R. Apical dominance<br>S. Bolting <br> T.Richmond Lang effect</div></div>','[{"text": "A - T, B - R, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - T, B - R, C - Q, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - R, B - S, C - Q, D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - Q, C -T,D - R", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'•Richmond Lang effect is retardation of ageing due to cytokinin. They retarded the rate of destruction of chlorophyll and yellowing of leaves.<br>• Auxin is mainly involved in root initiation, inducing parthenocarpy, promoting apical dominance and shortening of internodes.<br>• Abscisic acid serves to increase plant tolerance to several stresses, such as drought, waterlogging, etc., hence, it is also known as stress hormone.<br>• Ethylene is primarily involved in ripening and senescence apart from other processes such as development of roots and shoots.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8014,'biology',83,503,1021,'Air bladder occurs in','[{"text": "<i>Torpedo</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Exocoetus</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Scoliodon</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Trygon</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Air bladder is present in Osteichthyes eg. Exocoetus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8017,'biology',82,1272,3088,'One hormone hastens maturity period in juvenile confiers, a second hormone controls xylem differentiation, while the third increases the tolerance of plants to various stresses.<br>They are respectively.','[{"text": "Auxin, Gibberellins, Cytokinin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Auxin, Gibberellins, ABA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gibberellin, Auxin, Cytokinin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gibberellin, Auxin, ABA", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Spraying juvenile conifers with gibberellins hastens the maturity period, thus leads to early seed production. Auxin controls xylem differentiation. Abscisic acid (ABA) increase the tolerance of plants to various kinds of stresses therefore, also known as stress hormone.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8018,'biology',83,503,1021,'Out of the following set of characters, how many are found in bony fish?<br>Bladder, claspers, cloaca, operculum, ctenoid scales, placoid scales, homocercal tail fin','[{"text": "Two", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Five", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Bony fishes have swim bladder, operculum, homocercal tail fin and ctenoid scales.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8021,'biology',82,1272,3088,'Identify the incorrect statement/s<br>I. Kinetin is a derivative of Adenine which is a pyrimidine.<br>II. The technique of decapitation it widely used in tea plantations.<br>III. Ethylene is a gaseous plant hormone.<br>IV. Use of $\\mathrm{GA}_{3}$, hastens the malting process in brewing industry.<br>V. $\\mathrm{ABA}$ is a growth promoter.','[{"text": "I,II,III,IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II,III,IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Kinetin is a derivative of adenine which is a purine. Abscisic acid is a growth inhibitor.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8022,'biology',83,503,1021,'Bony fishes have','[{"text": "External fertilisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Are mostly oviparous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Show direct development", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All mentioned features are characteristics of bony fishes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8026,'biology',83,503,1021,'Which of the following feature of bony fish is missing in cartilaginous fish?','[{"text": "Paired fins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Placoid scales", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Poikilothermic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Operculum", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Operculum is present in bony fishes only, not cartilaginous fishes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8029,'biology',82,1263,3078,'In ____ growth, following mitotic cell division, one daughter cell continues to ____ while the other differentiates and the simplest expression of this growth is exemplified by a root elongating at ____ rate. Which of the following is<br>correct fill up of the above paragraph in sequence?','[{"text": "Geometric, mature, divide, constant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arithmetic, divide, mature, constant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Geometric, divide, mature, exponential", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arithmetic, mature, divide, exponential", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In arithmetic growth, following mitotic cell division, one daughter cell continues to divide while the other differentiates and mature the simplest expression of this growth is exemplified by a root elongating at constant rate".',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8030,'biology',83,503,1021,'Which of the following you would like to select bony fishes for aquarium?','[{"text": "Sea horse", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Betta</i>(fighting fish), <i>Pterophyllum</i> (Angel fish)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dog fish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Saw fish", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Betta(fighting fish) and Pterophyllum (Angel fish) are the fishes seen in the aquarium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8033,'biology',83,503,1021,'Following are few examples of bony fishes. Choose the odd one out as marine bony fish.','[{"text": "Flying fish", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Catla</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Clarias</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Labeo</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Exocoetus (Flying fish) is a marine bony fish.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8034,'biology',82,1263,3078,'The maximum growth rate occurs in','[{"text": "Senescent phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lag phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Exponential phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stationary phase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Exponential phase or lag phase is characterized by rapid growth in population which continues till enough food is available.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(8037,'biology',83,503,1021,'Which one is a true fish?','[{"text": "Salmon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sea horse", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bombay duck", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'True fishes are also referred to as fin fishes to distinguish them from other aquatic life forms.Salmon, sea horse and Bombay duck are all true fishes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8038,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Growth can be measured in various ways. Which of these cannot be used as parameters to measure growth','[{"text": "Increase in cell number", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase in cell size", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase in length and weight", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase in leaf fall", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Increase in leaf fall is not a parameter used for growth measurement.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8041,'biology',83,503,1021,'Scientific name of \'Magur\' is','[{"text": "<i>Clarias</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Catla catla</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Labeo rohita</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Naja naja</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Scientific name of \'Magur\' is Clarias.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8042,'biology',82,1266,3081,'How many of the following are extrinsic factors that affect growth and development?','[{"text": "Five", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nine", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The extrinsic factors responsible for growth and development are Light,<br>Temperature, Oxygen, Carbon dioxide and<br>Nutrition.<br>Light, Temperature, Oxygen, Carbon dioxide, Nutrition, Auxin, Gibberellins, Cytokinin, Ethylene',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8045,'biology',83,503,1021,'<em>Gambusia</em> is','[{"text": "Is an echinodermata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parasitic fish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fish predating on mosquito larvae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "An urochordata", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gambusia is a fish predating on mosquito larvae. It clears mosquito breeding grounds and avoids diseases where mosquito is the vector.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8046,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Heterophylly can be seen in','[{"text": "Coriander", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Larkspur", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Buttercup", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Heterophyll is the presence of differently shaped leaves on the same shoot or on different shoots of the same plants. It can be seen in coriander, buttercup and larkspur.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8049,'biology',83,503,1021,'Sea horse is','[{"text": "A marine mammal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A marine fish", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Antelope", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hippopotamus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sea horse or Hippocampus is a marine fish.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8050,'biology',82,1267,3083,'During mid-1960s, three independent researchers reported the purification and chemical characterization of three different kinds of inhibitors: inhibitor-B, abscission II and dormin. Later all the three were proved to be chemically identical. It was named','[{"text": "Naphthalene acetic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Indole butyric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abscisic acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Indole acetic acid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During mid-1960s, three independent researchers reported the purification and chemical charcterisation of three different kinds of inhibitors: inhibitor - B, abscission II and dormin. later all the three were proved to be chemically identical. It was named Abscisic acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8053,'biology',83,503,1021,'Scientific names of which two fish are correctly matched:<br>i. Fighting fish -<i>Pterophyllum</i><br>ii. Magur - <i>Clarias</i><br>iii. Sea horse - <i>Hippocampus</i><br>iv. Flying fish - <i>Draco</i><div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Common name of Clarias is Magur and that of Hippocampus is sea horse.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8054,'biology',82,1270,3086,'Which of the following is not a function of cytokinin?','[{"text": "Promotes apical dominance.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Promotes chloroplast development.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Promotes movement of nutrients.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Delay leaf senescence.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cytokinins are mildly basic growth hormones which are usually amino purine derivatives and promotecell division in plants. Cytokinins inhibit apical dominance while auxins promote apical dominance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8057,'biology',83,503,1021,'Which of the following statement is incorrect?','[{"text": "All vertebrates have a ventral heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All vertebrates have an endoskeleton derived from mesoderm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Placoid scales cover the body of sharks and lampreys", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Skin in fishes is covered with cycloid/ ctenoid scales", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Placoid scales cover body of shark only, body of lamprey is devoid of any scales.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
