(8078,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Cell / Tissue arising out of the same meristem have different structures at maturity the phenomena in plants is called','[{"text": "Open growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Open differentiation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Indeterminate growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Determinate differentiation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cell / Tissue arising out of the same meristem have different structures at maturity the phenomena in plants is called Open differentiation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8081,'biology',83,504,1022,'Which of the following is incorrect statement about frog?','[{"text": "Body is divisible into head and trunk", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The skin is moist without scales", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A tympanum represents the ear", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Body is divisible into head, trunk and abdomen", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In amphibians, body is divisible into head and trunk. Tail may be present in some.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8082,'biology',82,1262,3077,'Identify the correct and incorrect statements from the following<br>I. 17500 new cells are produced per hour by a single maize root apical meristem<br>II. With the help of length, growth of pollen tube is measured<br>III. The growth of the leaf is measured in term of volume<br>IV. Cells in a watermelon may increase in size by upto 350000 times','[{"text": "II, III are correct and I, IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I,II,III are correct and IV is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I,II,IV are correct and III is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV are correct and II, III are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Growth of leaf is measured in term of surface area.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8084,'biology',83,504,1022,'Which of the following statements are true about amphibians?','[{"text": "They are cold-blooded", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Respiration occurs through gills, skin and lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are poikilotherms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Poikilotherms means cold bloeded animals and amphibians are cold blooded and respiration occurs through gills, skin and lungs',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8086,'biology',82,1266,3081,'Development in plant is','[{"text": "Includes plasmatic growth followed by differentiation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only under control of intrinsic factors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Not influenced by environmental factors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Governed by intercellular factors like genetic factors", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Plant development is an umbrella term for broad spectrum of processes; it includes all changes that an organism goes through its lifecycle from germination to senescence. It includes plasmatic growth followed by differentiation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8088,'biology',83,504,1022,'Heart in amphibians is','[{"text": "Two-chambered with one auricle and one ventricle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three-chambered with one auricle and two ventricles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three-chambered with two auricles and one ventricle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Four-chambered with two auricles and two ventricles", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The heart is three chambered (two auricles and one ventricle).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8094,'biology',82,1267,3083,'Which one of the following is chemically identical to ABA?','[{"text": "Indole-3-acetic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kinetin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dormin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2,4-D", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During mid- 1960s, three independent researchers reported the purification and chemical characterization of three different kinds of inhibitors : inhibitor - B, abscission II and Dormin. Later all the three were proven to be chemically identical. It was named abscisic acid (ABA). ABA plays an important role in seed development, maturation & dormancy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8095,'biology',83,504,1022,'Amphibians show _______ fertilization and are _______ .','[{"text": "Internal and oviparous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Internal and viviparous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "External and viviparous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "External and oviparous", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Amphibians are oviparous and development is indirect. It occurs in water.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8098,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Which of the following is not an influence of auxins?','[{"text": "Apical dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parthenocarpy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phototropism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fruit ripening", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Auxins inhibit the growth of axillary buds and promote apical dominance. It induces parthenocarpic development of fruits and such fruits are seedless and auxin is also responsible for phototropism and geotropisms. Ripening and maturity of fruits are related to ethylene.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8099,'biology',83,504,1022,'Which of the following is incorrect?','[{"text": "<i>Bufo</i>-frog", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Hyla</i>-tree lizard", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ichthyophis</i> - limbless reptile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are wrong", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are wrong',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8102,'biology',82,1269,3085,'Dwarfness can be controlled by treating the plant with ____','[{"text": "Cytokinin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gibberellic acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Auxin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anti-gibberellin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When GA is sprayed on rosette plants, there is a rapid expansion of internodes and flowers with long stalks are produced. This phenomenon is called bolting. If GA is sprayed on single gene dwarf plant, genetic dwarfism can be overcome and plant becomes long, e.g., in maize and pea etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8104,'biology',83,504,1022,'Which of the following statements is not incorrect for the class-amphibia?','[{"text": "Skin is dry without glands with no exception", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have feathers, beak, forelimbs modified into wings and hind limb have scales", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Air sacs in lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three chambered heart", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Three chambered heart',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8106,'biology',82,1267,3082,'6-furfuryl amino purine, 2, 4-dichlorophenoxy acetic acid and indole- 3 acetic acid are examples respectively for','[{"text": "synthetic auxin, kinetin and natural auxin.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "gibberellin, natural auxin and kinetin.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "natural auxin, kinetin and synthetic auxin.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "kinetin, synthetic auxin and natural auxin.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'6-furfuryl amino purine, 2,4 dichlorophenoxy acetic acid and indole 3 acetic acid are the examples of kinetin, synthetic auxins and natural auxins respectively. Kinetin stimulates cell division in plants. 2, 4 dichlorophenoxy acetic acid is a common systemic herbicide used in the control of broadleaf weeds. Indole - 3 acetic acid induces cell elongation and cell division and results in plant growth and development.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8108,'biology',83,504,1022,'Which of the following is an example of amphibia?','[{"text": "<i>Hyla</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Rana</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Bufo</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the given examples belong to class Amphibia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8110,'biology',82,1271,3087,'Senescence in plants can be promoted by applying.','[{"text": "Auxins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokinins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethylene", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ethylene promotes abscission and senescence of leaves, flowers etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
