(8124,'biology',82,1267,3083,'Experiments done by Charles Darwin and his son on plant phototropism showed that','[{"text": "Within coleoptiles, auxin moves laterally away from the source of the light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Auxin is produced in the tip of the coleoptiles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More cell elongation takes place on the shaded side of the plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The tip of the coleoptiles is the light receptor of the plant", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Experiments done by Charles Darwin and his son on plant phototropism showed that the tip of the coleoptiles is the light receptor of the plant',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8127,'biology',83,505,1023,'The class name-Reptilia refers to','[{"text": "Presence of two pair of limbs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Their creeping or crawling mode of locomotion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Presence of dry and cornified skin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The class name Reptilia refers to their creeping or crawling mode of locomotion (Latin, repere or reptum, to creep or crawl).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8128,'biology',82,1263,3078,'In sigmoid curve, the numericals indicate the sequence of events, choose the correct option where the numerals specify the event.','[{"text": "1= Phase of slow growth, 2= Phase of\\nexponential growth, 3 = Phase of\\ndiminishing phase, 4 = Stationary phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1= Phase of diminishing phase,\\n2= Phasof exponential growth,<br>3= Phase of slow growth,\\n4 = Stationary phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 = Stationary phase, 2 = Phase of\\ndiminishing Phase, 3= Phase of\\nexponential growth, 4= phase of slow\\ngrowth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 = Phase of slow growth, 2 = Stationary\\nphase,3 = Phase of diminishing phase,\\n4= Phase of exponential growth", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In the diagram numericals (1-4) represents, $1=$ Phase of slow growth, $2=$ Phase of exponential growth, $3=$ Phase of diminishing phase, $4=$ Stationary phase.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/82_8128_question_1.png'),
(8132,'biology',82,1269,3085,'Auxins : Apical dominance : : Gibberellins :','[{"text": "Adventitious shoot formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Accelerates abscission", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Closure of stomata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bolting<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Application of gibberellins promotes bolting (internode elongation just prior to flowering) in beet, cabbages and many plants with rosette habit.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8135,'biology',83,505,1023,'Reptiles are different from amphibians in','[{"text": "Skin type", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Structure of the heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fertilisation process", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Body of reptiles is covered by dry and cornified skin, epidermal scales or scutes. The amphibian skin is moist (without scales). The heart of amphibians is three chambered (two auricles and one ventricle). Heart in reptiles is usually three-chambered, but four-chambered in crocodiles. Fertilisation is internal in reptiles and external in amphibians.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8136,'biology',82,1268,3084,'Auxin is used by gardeners to prepare weed free lawns. But no damage is caused to grass as auxin','[{"text": "Promotes apical dominance.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Promotes abscission of mature leaves only.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Does not affect mature monocotyledonous plants.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Can help in cell division in grasses, to produce growth.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Auxin does not affect mature monocot plants. In monocots, especially grasses show limited translocation and cause rapid degradation of external auxin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
