(8214,'biology',83,506,1024,'Which of the following is strictly an avian character','[{"text": "Homeothermic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of four chambered heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only right systemic arch persists and presence of pneumatic bones", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Twelve pairs of cranial nerves", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'4 chambered heart is present in birds, mammals and crocodiles. Birds and mammals are homeothermic. Reptiles, birds and mammals have 12 pairs of cranial nerves.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
