(8223,'biology',83,506,1024,'Which of the following characters does not fit for aves?','[{"text": "Beak has teeth", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alimentary canal has 2 additional chambers, crop and gizzard", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hind limbs are modified for walking, swimming or clasping. Fore limbs are modified into wings", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Skin is dry, without glands except oil / preen glands at the base of tail", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Beak is present in birds but without teeth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8224,'biology',86,979,2283,'Prawn respires with ____ and cockroach with ____','[{"text": "Trachea, gills", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gills, trachea", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Moist skin, gills", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Simple diffusion", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In majority of crustaceans gills are the chief respiratory organs. In prawn gills are enclosed in a gill chamber on each side of the cephalothorax and are covered by a carapace, inner side of which is called branchiostegite and has vascularised respiratory epithelium. Air enters the respiratory system of a cockroach through these external openings, which act as muscular valves, leading to the internal respiratory system. The internal respiratory system is a densely networked array of air tubes called trachea. This network of trachea equalises pressure throughout the system.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
