(8244,'biology',86,979,2283,'Identify the correct statement:','[{"text": "Higher invertebrates like sponges, coelenterates, flatworms, etc., exchange gases by simple diffusion over their entire body surface.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aquatic arthropods and molluscs use network of tracheal tubes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Moist cuticle and skin is used by earthworm.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Terrestrial amphibians and the larval stages of amphibians respire with gills, while aquatic amphibians use lungs and moist skin.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lower invertebrates like sponges, coelenterates, flatworms, etc., exchange gases by simple diffusion over their entire body surface. Gills (branchial respiration) are used by most of the aquatic arthropods and molluscs. Moist cuticle and skin is used by earthworm for respiration. Vascularised bags called lungs (pulmonary respiration) are used by the terrestrial forms for the exchange of gases.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
