(8368,'biology',86,979,2284,'Respiratory or exchange part of the respiratory system is the site of','[{"text": "Actual diffusion of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ between tissues and atmospheric air.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Actual diffusion of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ between blood and atmospheric air.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Actual diffusion of $$\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ between blood and atmospheric air.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Actual diffusion of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}$$ between blood and atmospheric air.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Respiratory or exchange part of the respiratory system consists of alveoli and their ducts serve for actual diffusion of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ between blood and atmospheric air. These serve to get rid of the body $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and pick up oxygen from the atmosphere. This system is derived from the endoderm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8369,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which one of the following categories of animals, is correctly described with no single exception in it?','[{"text": "All reptiles possess scales, have a three chambered heart and are cold blooded (poikilothermous)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All sponges are marine and are lined by collared cells.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All bony fishes have four pairs of gills and an operculum on each side.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All mammals are viviparous and possess diaphragm for breathing", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Some freshwater sponges exist as well, for example, Spongilla. Some reptiles like crocodiles possess a 4 chambered heart. Mammals like Ornithorhyncus are oviparous.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
