(8388,'biology',86,979,2284,'Select the correct answer.<BR>A. The anatomical setup of lungs in thorax is such that any change in the volume of the thoracic cavity will be reflected in the abdominal cavity.<BR>B. This arrangement is essential for breathing, as we can directly alter the pulmonary volume.','[{"text": "A is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The anatomical setup of lungs in thorax is such that any change in the volume of the thoracic cavity will be reflected in the lung (pulmonary) cavity. Such an arrangement is essential for breathing, as we cannot directly alter the pulmonary volume.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
