(9680,'biology',87,1132,2704,'Coronary artery disease, often referred to as','[{"text": "Arteriosclerosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myocardial infarction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Atherosclerosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Myocarditis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Coronary Artery Disease, often referred to as atherosclerosis',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8410,'biology',83,496,1012,'Which one of the following statements is incorrect?','[{"text": "In ctenophores, locomotion is mediated by comb plates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In cockroaches and prawns excretion of waste material occurs through malpighian tubules", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Earth worms are hermaphrodites and yet cross fertilization take place among them.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In Fasciola flame cells take part in excretion", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In cockroaches excretion of waste material occurs through malpighian tubules and in prawn by green glands.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8412,'biology',86,979,2284,'Which is the correct sequence of steps in respiration?<br>i. Transport of gases by the blood<br>ii. Breathing or pulmonary ventilation<br>iii. Cellular respiration<br>iv. Diffusion of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ between blood and tissues<br>v. Diffusion of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ across alveolar membrane','[{"text": "ii $$\\\\rightarrow$$ iv $$\\\\rightarrow$$ i $$\\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{v} \\\\rightarrow$$ iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii $$\\\\rightarrow$$ i $$\\\\rightarrow$$ v $$\\\\rightarrow$$ iii $$\\\\rightarrow$$ iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii $$\\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{v} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{i} \\\\rightarrow$$ iv $$\\\\rightarrow$$ iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii $$\\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{v} \\\\rightarrow$$ iv $$\\\\rightarrow$$ i $$\\\\rightarrow$$ iii", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Respiration involes the following steps<br>(i) Breathing or pulmonary ventilation by which atmospheric air is inhalled in and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ rich alveolar air is released out .<br>(ii) Diffusion of gases $$\\left(\\mathrm{O}_{2}\\right.$$ and $$\\left.\\mathrm{CO}_{2}\\right)$$ across alveolar membrane.<br>(iii) Transport of gases by the blood.<br>(iv) Diffusion of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ between blood and tissues (v) Utilisation of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ by the cells for catabolic reactions and resultant release of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ (cellular respiration)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8414,'biology',83,496,1012,'Which of the following is incorrect matching?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Protonephridia --- Some rotifers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haemocoel --- Prawn and <em>Pila</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acoelomate --- Hookworm", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Hook worm -pseudocoelomate',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8416,'biology',86,979,2284,'The space at the back of the mouth, that leads either to the airway or the oesophagus is the:','[{"text": "Larynx-A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Conchae-C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nasal cavity-C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pharynx-B", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The pharynx is the part of the throat that is behind the mouth and nasal cavity and above the oesophagus and the trachea, or the tubes going down to the stomach and the lungs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/86_8416_question_1.png'),
(8418,'biology',83,494,1010,'Which of the following is incorrect matching?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "<i>Ascaris,Wuchereria</i>, HookWorm-Aschelminthes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Taenia, Fasciola, Dugesia, Schistosoma</i> - Platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eye worm, Filarial worm, seatworm-Aschelminthes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pinworm, flatworm, liver fluke-Platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pinworm -Aschelminthes<br>Flatworm, liver fluke -Platyhelminthes',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8420,'biology',86,979,2284,'Identify diaphragm in the diagram given below','[{"text": "A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{C}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The diaphragm is the primary muscle used in the process of inspiration, or inhalation. It is a domeshaped sheet of muscle that is inserted into the lower ribs. Lying at the base of the thorax (chest), it separates the abdominal cavity from the thoracic cavity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/86_8420_question_1.png'),
(8422,'biology',83,493,1009,'In contrast to annelida the platyhelminthes show:','[{"text": "Triploblastic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bilateral symmetry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of hooks and suckers", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Platyhelminthes, due to their parasitic nature, bear hooks and suckers.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8424,'biology',86,979,2284,'The figure below shows ventral view of human thorax. Labelled A, B & C find the correct option','[{"text": "B - The rib cage and A- diaphragm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Sternum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B - Bronchiole, A - Lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Manubrium, C - Lungs", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Lungs are protected by the rib cage, which is made up of 12 sets of ribs. These ribs are connected to your spine in your back and go around the lungs to keep them safe. Beneath the lungs is the diaphragm a dome-shaped muscle that works with the lungs to allow us to inhale (breathe in) and exhale (breathe out) air.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/86_8424_question_1.png'),
(8426,'biology',83,506,1024,'Find out correct option?','[{"text": "In most of the birds copulatory organ is absent, so fertilization is external.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In annelida, neural system consist of paired ganglia connected by lateral nerves to a double ventral nerve cord.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sponges reproduce sexually by fragmentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Platyhelminthes are pseudocoelomate.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In birds, Fertilization is internal. Platyhelminthes are acoelomates. In sponges fragmentation is a mode of asexual reproduction.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8428,'biology',86,979,2284,'The figure shows diagrammatic view of human respiratory system with labels A, B, C and D. Select the option, which gives correct identification and main functional and/or characteristic.','[{"text": "A-trachea-long tube supported by complete cartilaginous rings for conducting inspired air", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B-pleural membrane-surround ribs on both sides to provide cushion against rubbing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C-alveoli-thin walled vascular bag-like structures for exchange of gases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D-lower end of lungs-diaphragm pulls it down during inspiration.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'B - Alveoli are thin-walled vascular baglike structures for exchange of gases.<br>A - Trachea or wind pipe is an air conducting tube through which transport of gases takes place.<br>C - Pleural membrane is double layered which reduces friction on the lung surface.<br>D - Diaphragm is involving in the inspiration and expiration process of breathing.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/86_8428_question_1.png'),
(8431,'biology',83,506,1024,'Which of the following class is incorrectly matched with its general characters?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Osteichthyes : Four pairs of gills are covered with an operculum and skin is covered with cycloid scales.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyclostomata: Lack jaws and paired fins and body is covered with placoid scales.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Reptilia : Tympanum represents ear and fertilisation is internal.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aves : Endoskeleton is fully ossified and long bones are hollow with air cavities called as pneumatic bones.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cyclostomes are devoid of scales.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8432,'biology',86,980,2285,'The most important function of diaphragm of mammals is','[{"text": "To divide the body cavity into components", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "To protect lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "To aid in breathing", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "To aid in ventilation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The main function of the diaphragm is as a muscle of respiration, meaning that it aids with breathing. It is aided by other muscles and accessory muscles of breathing when a person experiences shortness of breath. When the diaphragm contracts, the lungs expand and air is inhaled. When the diaphragm relaxes, it restores the pressure in the pleural cavity and the lungs recoil thereby pushing out air (exhalation).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8434,'biology',83,495,1011,'Nephridia of earthworm perform function similar to','[{"text": "Gills of prawn", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trachea of insects", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flame cells of <i>Planaria</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nematoblasts of <i>Hydra</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Nephridia of earthworms are responsible for excretion. Similarly, flame cells in Planaria perform excretion.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8436,'biology',86,980,2285,'Thoracic cavity is enlarged by contraction of','[{"text": "Intercostal muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diaphragm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Inspiration is initiated by the contraction of diaphragm which increases the volume of thoracic chamber in the antero-posterior axis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8439,'biology',83,500,1016,'Just as mammalia is to chordata, so is','[{"text": "Cetacea to Vertebrata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ophidia to Snakes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trematoda to Platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Periplanata to Insecta", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Phylum Platyhelminthes consists of three classes viz. Turbellaria, Trematoda and Cestoda. Similarly, Mammalia is a class of phylum Chordata.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8440,'biology',86,980,2285,'Read the following statements and fill in the blanks with correct options:<br>Contraction of ____ I____ increases the volume of thoracic chamber in anteroposterior axis.<br>Contraction of ___ II____lifts up the ribs and the sternum causing an increase in the volume of the thoracic chamber in the dorsoventral axis.<BR> $\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{I}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}&{\\,\\,}&{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{II}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}\n\\end{array}$','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Diaphragm\\\\,}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{Internal}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{intercostal}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{muscle}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Diaphragm}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,}&{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{External}}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\\\,{\\\\rm{intercostal}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{muscle}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{External}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{Phrenic}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{muscles}}}\\\\\\\\\\n{{\\\\rm{intercostal}}\\\\,\\\\,}&{\\\\,\\\\,}&{}\\\\\\\\\\n{{\\\\rm{muscle}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{\\\\,\\\\,}&{}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Abdominal}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\,\\\\,}&{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Diaphragm}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{muscles}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\,\\\\,}&{}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Inspiration is initiated by the contraction of diaphragm which increases the volume of thoracic chamber in the antero-posterior axis. The contraction of external inter-costal muscles lifts up the ribs and the sternum causing an increase in the volume of the thoracic chamber in the dorso-ventral axis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8442,'biology',83,496,1012,'Which one of the following structures possess chitin?','[{"text": "Exoskeleton of arthropods, bacterial cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoskeleton of arthropods, bacterial cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Exoskeleton of arthropods, fungal cell wall", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Exoskeleton of arthropods, fungal cell wall',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8444,'biology',86,980,2285,'Movement of the air into and out of the lungs is carried out by','[{"text": "Active transport", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pressure gradient", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Osmosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diffusion", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The movement of the air into and out of the lungs is carried out by creating a pressure gradient between the lungs and the atmosphere.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8446,'biology',83,500,1016,'Besides annelida and arthropoda segmentation is found in','[{"text": "Cestoda", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chordata", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Acanthocephali", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mollusca", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Segmentation of the body is seen in Annelida, Arthropoda and chordata.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8448,'biology',86,980,2285,'Pressure within the lungs is called','[{"text": "Inter-pulmonary pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intra-pulmonary pressure", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alveolar pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interstitial pressure", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pressure within the lungs is called intrapulmonary pressure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8450,'biology',83,493,1009,'Which one of the following pairs is correctly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Uricotelism - Aquatic habitat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parasitism - Presence of digestive system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Streamlined body - Aquatic adaptation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Excessive perspiration - Xeric adaptation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fishes and other aquatic organisms have a streamlined body as an adaptation towards aquatic mode of life.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8452,'biology',86,980,2285,'Inhalation is the process of intake of air through the respiratory tract. Which figure illustrates the process of inhalation?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Inhalation is the process of expulsion of air through the respiratory tract. Figure 2 illustrates the process of inhalation. The contraction of external inter-costal muscles lifts up the ribs and the sternum causing an increase in the volume of the thoracic chamber in the dorsoventral axis. The overall increase in the thoracic volume causes a similar increase in pulmonary volume. An increase in pulmonary volume decreases the intra-pulmonary pressure to less than the atmospheric pressure which forces the air from outside to move into the lungs, i.e., inspiration',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(8454,'biology',83,504,1022,'How many organisms in the list given below respire through gills?','[{"text": "Six", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Molluscans like Snails, clams, octopus respire through gills. Aquatic arthropods, fishes and tadpoles respire through gills.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_8454_question_1.png'),
(8456,'biology',86,980,2285,'Name the muscles of the ribs','[{"text": "External and internal intercostals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Internal intercostals only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "External intercostals only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diaphragm", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The muscles of the ribs are external and internal intercostals.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8457,'biology',83,500,1017,'Read the following statements and find out the correct statement.','[{"text": "<em>Branchiostoma</em> (Amphioxus) belongs to phylum Cephalochordata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Ascidia</em>, <em>Salpa </em>and <em>Doliolum</em> belongs to phylum Urochordata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In vertebrates notochord is only present in the embryonic stage which is replaced by vertebral column in adult forms.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<em>Ascidia, Salpa</em> and<em> Doliolum</em> belong to subphylum Urochordata.<em>Branchiostoma </em>(Amphioxus or Lancelet) belongs to subphylum Cephalochordata. All chordates are not vertebrates but all vertebrates are chordates',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8460,'biology',86,980,2285,'By the contraction in diaphragm volume of thoracic chamber increases in the','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Dorso}}\\\\,}&{\\\\rm{ - }}&{{\\\\rm{ventral}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{axis}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Antero}}}&{\\\\rm{ - }}&{{\\\\rm{posterior}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{axis}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Dorso}}\\\\,}&{\\\\rm{ - }}&{{\\\\rm{posterior}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{axis}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Antero}}}&{\\\\rm{ - }}&{{\\\\rm{ventral}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{axis}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Inspiration is initiated by the contraction of diaphragm which increases the volume of thoracic chamber in the antero-posterior axis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8461,'biology',83,493,1009,'Which characters are developed first time in the members of phylum platyhelminthes\ni. Coelom\nii. Bilateral symmetry\niii. Excretory\niv. Triploblastic','[{"text": "Only ii, iii and iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only i, ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only i, ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All i, ii, iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Platyhelminthes members are having a bilateral symmetry, developed excretory structures and are triploblastic.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8464,'biology',86,980,2285,'By the contraction in external intercostal muscles volume of thoracic chamber increases in the','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Dorso}}\\\\,}&{\\\\rm{ - }}&{{\\\\rm{ventral}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{axis}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Antero}}}&{\\\\rm{ - }}&{{\\\\rm{posterior}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{axis}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Dorso}}\\\\,}&{\\\\rm{ - }}&{{\\\\rm{posterior}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{axis}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Antero}}}&{\\\\rm{ - }}&{{\\\\rm{ventral}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{axis}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The contraction of external inter-costal muscles lifts up the ribs and the sternum causing an increase in the volume of the thoracic chamber in the dorso-ventral axis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8465,'biology',83,496,1012,'Two common characters found in Centipede, Honeybee, Sliver fish, Scorpion, Cockroach and crab are','[{"text": "Green glands and tracheae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Jointed legs and chitinous exoskeleton", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Compound eyes and anal cerci", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Book lungs and antennae", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Common characters found in Centipede, Honey bee, Sliver fish, Scorpion, and Cockroach are jointed legs and chitinous exoskeleton.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8468,'biology',86,980,2285,'Inspiration can occur, when','[{"text": "Pressure with in the lungs is less than the atmospheric pressure", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pressure with in the lungs is more than the atmospheric pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pressure with in the lungs and atmospheric air is same", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No effect of pressure on inspiration", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'An increase in pulmonary volume decreases the intra-pulmonary pressure to less than the atmospheric pressure which forces the air from outside to move into the lungs, i.e., inspiration',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8469,'biology',83,503,1021,'Mark the correct match of the animals and its common name<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$Myxine\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\, - \\\\,{\\\\rm{hagfish}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$Ascidia\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\, - \\\\,{\\\\rm{lancelet}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$Pterophyllum\\\\,\\\\, - \\\\,{\\\\rm{flying}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{fish}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$Trygon\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\, - \\\\,{\\\\rm{dog}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{fish}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Lancelet is a chordate but not a vertebrate. It is a cephalochordate having a highly developed notochord as a skeletal structure.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8472,'biology',86,980,2285,'During inspiration muscle of diaphragm','[{"text": "Contracts", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Expands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No effect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coil-like string", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The diaphragm is the major muscle responsible for breathing. It is a thin, domeshaped muscle that separates the abdominal cavity from the thoracic cavity. During inhalation, the diaphragm contracts, so that its centre moves caudally (downward) and its edges move rostrally (upward).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8473,'biology',83,503,1021,'Which one of the following matching pairs is wrong?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Silver fish - Arthopoda", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shell fish - Pisces", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cuttle fish - Mollusca", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Starfish - Echinodermata", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Shellfish are a group of aquatic animals that belong to either Mollusca, Crustaceans or Echinoderms.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8476,'biology',86,980,2285,'Relaxation of the diaphragm and the intercostal muscles results in-','[{"text": "Reducing the thoracic volume", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diaphragm and sternum return to their normal position", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase pulmonary volume", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Relaxation of the diaphragm and the inter-costal muscles returns the diaphragm and sternum to their normal positions and reduce the thoracic volume and thereby the pulmonary volume. This leads to an increase in intra-pulmonary pressure to slightly above the atmospheric pressure causing the expulsion of air from the lungs, i.e., expiration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8477,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which of the following represents the correct combination without any exception? <br>  <br><b> &emsp; Characteristics</b> &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; <b>Class</b>','[{"text": "$\\\\rm{Sucking} \\\\, and $ &emsp; &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{Cyclostomata} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{circular \\\\,  mouth;}$ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{jaws \\\\, absent,} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\,  \\\\rm{integument} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{without} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{scales} $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\rm{Mouth \\\\, ventral;}$ &emsp; &emsp; $\\\\rm{Chondrichthycs}$ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{gills \\\\, without}$ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{operculum;}$ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{skin \\\\, with \\\\,  placoid}$ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{scales; \\\\, persistent} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{notochord} $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\rm{Mammary \\\\, gland;} $ &emsp; &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\rm{Mammalia} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{hair \\\\, on \\\\, body;} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{pinnae; \\\\, two \\\\, pairs} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{of \\\\, limbs} $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\rm{Body \\\\, covered} $ &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{Aves} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{with \\\\, feathers;} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{skin \\\\, moist} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{\\\\& \\\\, glandular, \\\\, force} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{- \\\\, limbs \\\\, form \\\\, wings;} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{lungs \\\\, with \\\\, air \\\\, sacs} $", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Fishes belonging to class Chondrichthyes bear a ventral mouth. Operculum is absent. Skin is covered by placoid scales. Teeth are modified placoid scales. Notochord is persistent throughout life.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8480,'biology',86,980,2285,'Inspiration is initiated by','[{"text": "The relaxation of diaphragm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The contraction of diaphragm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Decrease in volume of thoracic chamber", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The contraction of lungs", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Inspiration is initiated by the contraction of diaphragm which increases the volume of thoracic chamber in the antero-posterior axis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8481,'biology',83,495,1011,'In which of the following, metamerically segmented body present?','[{"text": "<em>Taenia</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Ctenoplana</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Nereis</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<em>Pila</em>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<em>Nereis</em>, an annelid, bears a metamerically segmented body.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8544,'biology',83,497,1013,'Jellyfish differs from cuttlefish as well as starfish because it is','[{"text": "Unsegmented", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Marine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Without tissues", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diploblastic", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Jellyfish (Cnidaria) is diploblastic.<br>Cuttelefish (Mollusca) and Starfish (Echinodermata) are triploblastic.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8484,'biology',86,980,2285,'Decreased intrapulmonary pressure during inspiration is caused due to','[{"text": "Increased pulmonary volume and thoracic volume", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contraction of diaphragm and intercostal muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribs and sternum are raised", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Inspiration is initiated by the contraction of diaphragm. It is achieved by the contraction of the external intercostal muscles which up lift the ribs and the sternum. The ovarall increase in the thoracic volume causes a similar increase in the pulmonary volume. This decreases the intrapulmonary pressure forcing the air from outside to move into the lungs (i.e. inspiration).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8485,'biology',83,494,1010,'Select the incorrect statement about the phylum aschelminthes.','[{"text": "Sexes are separate (dioecious )", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alimentary canal is complete with well developed muscular pharynx", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fertilization is external", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Often females are longer than males", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In Aschelminthes, Fertilisation is internal and development may be direct (the young ones resemble the adult) or indirect.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8488,'biology',86,980,2285,'Exhalation is the process of expulsion of air through the respiratory tract. Which figure illustrates the process of exhalation?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Exhalation is the process of expulsion of air through the respiratory tract. Figure in option 4 illustrates the process of exhalation. Relaxation of the diaphragm and the inter-costal muscles returns the diaphragm and sternum to their normal positions and reduce the thoracic volume and thereby the pulmonary volume. This leads to an increase in intra-pulmonary pressure to slightly above the atmospheric pressure causing the expulsion of air from the lungs, i.e., expiration',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8489,'biology',83,504,1022,'What will you look for to identify the sex of the following?','[{"text": "Female cockroach - Anal cerci", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male frog - A copulatory pad on the first digit of the hind limb", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Female <i>Ascaris</i> - Sharply curved posterior end", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male shark - Claspers borne on pelvic fins", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The sexual dimorphism in sharks is evident due to the presence of copulatory organ, the claspers in the pelvic region are at the base of pelvic fins.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8492,'biology',86,980,2285,'Expiration involves','[{"text": "Relaxation of diaphragm and external intercostal muscles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Contraction of diaphragm and external intercostal muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contraction of diaphragm muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contraction of intercostal muscles", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During expiration or exhalation the inner intercostal muscles contract bringing the ribs back to the original position and the diaphragm is also raised back. This reduces the space in the chest cavity and increases the pressure. This expels the air out of the lungs',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8493,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which of the following groups of animals is correctly matched with its one characteristics feature without even a single exception?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Reptilia - possess 3-chambered heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mammalia - give birth to young ones.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chondrichthyes - possess cartilaginous bony endoskeleton.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chordata - possess a mouth provided with an upper and a lower jaw.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In class Mammalia, members of subclass Prototheria are egg laying mammals<br>(Ornithorhyncus and Echidna), in class Reptilia, crocodile is an exception, it has 4 chambered heart. In phylum Chordata, organisms that belong to division Gnathostomata have upper jaw and lower jaw, members of protochordata and division agnatha do not have jaws.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8545,'biology',86,981,2286,'Volume of air inspired during a normal respiration is called','[{"text": "RV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "TV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ERV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IRV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Volume of air inspired or expired during a normal respiration is called TV.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8496,'biology',86,980,2285,'Expiration occurs when','[{"text": "Intrapulmonary pressure is less than the atmospheric pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intrapulmonary pressure is greater than the atmospheric pressure", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Intrapulmonary pressure is equal to the atmospheric pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intrapulmonary pressure is slightly lower than atmospheric pressure", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Expiration takes place when the intrapulmonary pressure is higher than the atmospheric pressure, i.e. there is positive pressure in the lungs with respect to the atmospheric pressure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8497,'biology',83,499,1015,'Given below are four matching of the animal and their kind of excretory organs<br>Animals &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; &emsp;Excretory organs<br>i. <i>Pleurobrachia</i> &emsp; - Flame cells<br>ii. <i>Meandrina</i> &emsp; &emsp;- Excretory system<br>iii. <i>Anopheles</i> &emsp; &emsp;- Malpighian tubules<br>iv. <i>Balanoglossus</i> &emsp; - Proboscis gland<br>How many of the matchings are correct?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'An excretory system is absent in Pleurobrachia (phylum Ctenophora)',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8500,'biology',86,980,2285,'During expiration, there is','[{"text": "Increase in the thoracic volume and reduction in the pulmonary volume.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reduction in the thoracic volume and reduction in the pulmonary volume.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Reduction in the thoracic volume and increase in the pulmonary volume.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Relaxation of the diaphragm and the intercostal muscles returns the diaphragm and sternum to their normal positions and reduce the thoracic volume and thereby the pulmonary volume. This leads to an increase in intrapulmonary pressure to slightly above the atmospheric pressure causing the expulsion of air from the lungs, i.e., expiration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8501,'biology',83,500,1018,'Which of the following statement is correct?<br>I. In urochordates like ascidia, salpa, doliolum notochord is present in only larval tail.<br>II. In cephalochordates like branchiostoma (Amphioxus or Lancelet notochord extends from head to tail and is persistent throughout the life<br>III. All vertebrates are chordates but all chordates are not vertebrates<br>IV. Notochord is replaced by vertebral column<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "All are wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II and IV are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only II is wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'All the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8504,'biology',86,980,2285,'Expiratory muscle contract at the time of','[{"text": "Deep inspiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Normal inspiration and expiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Forceful expiration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Normal expiration", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When forceful exhalation is required, or when the elasticity of the lungs is reduced (as in emphysema), active exhalation can be achieved by contraction of the abdominal wall muscles (rectus abdominus, transverse abdominus, external oblique muscle and internal oblique muscle).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8505,'biology',83,493,1009,'Which of the following is correct set of animals with blind sac body plan?','[{"text": "<i>Ophiura, Fasciola, Adamsia</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Hydra, Planaria, Ascaris</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Wuchereria, Pennatula, Clonorchis</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Obelia, Hydra, Ascaris</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Alimentary canal is absent in Taenia. Ascaris and Wuchereria have a tube-withintube body plan.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8508,'biology',86,980,2285,'Additional muscles which support to increase the strength of breathing are found in','[{"text": "Ribs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abdomen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Diaphragm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heart", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Additional muscles which impact the ability of humans to increase the strength of respiration are found in the abdomen. This is due to the fact that we can voluntarily take deep breathe by an effort. In the process of deep inspiration or expiration, chest distention is brought about by the external intercostal muscles and the abdominal muscles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8509,'biology',83,491,1007,'Which statement is true about coelenterates?','[{"text": "Metagenesis is observed in a few cnidarians", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They have only sexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are diploblastic, having system level organisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have Cnidoblast cells in their gametes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both sexual and asexual modes of reproduction are available. They have tissue level of organisation. They have cnidoblasts on their body wall and tentacles.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8512,'biology',86,980,2285,'The human respiratary cycles per minute is','[{"text": "12 - 16 times/min", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "18 - 20 times/min", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "20 - 25 times/min", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12 - 20 times/min", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'On an average, a healthy human breathes 12-16 times/minute.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8513,'biology',83,492,1008,'Which one of the following living organisms completely lacks a cell wall?','[{"text": "<i>Funaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Cyanobacteria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pleurobrachia</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Chlorella</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pleurobrachia is an animal and hence lacks a cell wall.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8516,'biology',83,500,1016,'Which of the following is incorrect?','[{"text": "Chordates have a ventral heart.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Most members of porifera are asymmetrical.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Segmentation is absent in mollusca.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neurons are absent in coelenterate.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Diffuse nervous system first appears in Coelenterates.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8517,'biology',86,980,2285,'Which of the following diagram is correct representation of inspiration?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Diagram in option 2 shows the correct representation of inspiration. The contraction of external inter-costal muscles lifts up the ribs and the sternum causing an increase in the volume of the thoracic chamber in the dorsoventral axis. The overall increase in the thoracic volume causes a similar increase in pulmonary volume. An increase in pulmonary volume decreases the intra-pulmonary pressure to less than the atmospheric pressure which forces the air from outside to move into the lungs, i.e., inspiration',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8520,'biology',83,494,1010,'Which of the following is a character of phylum aschelminthes?','[{"text": "Triploblastic, bilaterally symmetrical, segmented and pseudocoelomate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Triploblastic, segmented and pseudocoelomate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Triploblastic, unsegmented and pseudocoelomate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Triploblastic, radially symmetrical and acoelomate", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Members of Phylum Aschelminthes are triploblastic, unsegmented and pseudocoelomate.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8521,'biology',86,980,2285,'Which one of the following statement is correct?','[{"text": "Chest expands because air enters into the lungs.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Air enters into the lungs because chest has high volume", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The muscle of the diaphragm contracts because air enter into the lungs.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When you breathe in, or inhale, your diaphragm contracts (tightens) and moves downward. This increases the space in your chest cavity, into which your lungs expand. The intercostal muscles between your ribs also help enlarge the chest cavity. They contract to pull your rib cage both upward and outward when you inhale.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8524,'biology',83,495,1011,'Which of the following animals does not have segmentation?','[{"text": "Lobster", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Earthworms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flatworms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Silk worm", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Body of flatworms is not segmented.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8525,'biology',86,980,2285,'In fever, breathing rate','[{"text": "Increase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Decrease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Fever causes an increase in the heart rate, breathing rate and blood circulation to the skin. This is how the body tries to reduce the heat caused by fever.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8528,'biology',83,494,1010,'<em>Ascaris</em> is characterized by','[{"text": "Sexes are separate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fertilisation is internal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alimentary canal is complete with a welldeveloped muscular pharynx.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<em>Ascaris</em> is characterized by all the above factors .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8529,'biology',86,980,2285,'What will be the $$\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ in the atmospheric air compared to those in the alveolar air?','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ higher, $$\\\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ lesser", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ lesser, $$\\\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ higher", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ higher, $$\\\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ higher", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ lesser, $$\\\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ lesser", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$$\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ higher and $$\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ is lower in the atmospheric air compared to those in the alveolar air.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8532,'biology',83,503,1021,'Which of the following are correctly matched with respect to their taxonomic classification?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Fighting fish,angel fish, devil fish - Osteichthyes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dog fish, saw fish, great, devil fish - Chondrichthyes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Star fish, Cuttle fish, devil fish - Mollusca,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Silver fish, cray fish, Jelly fish - Arthropoda", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Examples of Chondrichthyes: Scoliodon (Dog fish), Pristis (saw fish), Carcharodon (Great white shark), Trygon(Sting ray), Torpedo.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8533,'biology',86,980,2285,'Among mammals, the efficiency of ventilation of lungs as compared to reptiles and birds is better developed by the presence of','[{"text": "Ribs and costal muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ribs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only costal muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diaphragm", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The ventilation of bird lungs is similar to that of reptiles, their effectiveness is increased by the presence of air sacs. Although no gas exchange occurs in the air sacs, their arrangement increases the efficiency of lung ventilation by enabling fresh air to pass in one direction through the lungs during both inhalation and exhalation. Ventilation of mammalian lungs is assisted by the diaphragm - a muscular partition that divides the thoracic cavity from the abdominal cavity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8536,'biology',83,495,1011,'Select the option which gives a common characteristic of two animals.','[{"text": "Tapeworm and roundworm are acoelomates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sea hare and sea horse have ventral nerve cord", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Earthworm and silkworm are metamerically segmented", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sea walnut and sea cucumber have comb plates for locomotion", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Earthworm (Annelida) and silkworm(Arthropoda) are metamerically segmented animals.<br>(1) Roundworm is a pseudocoelomate (not acoelomate).<br>(2) Sea horse is a chordate. It has dorsal nerve cord.<br>(3) Comb plates are present only in ctenophores (sea walnuts or comb jellies) but not in sea cucumbers (echinoderms).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8537,'biology',86,981,2286,'Which instrument helps in clinical assessment of pulmonary functions?','[{"text": "Syphygmomanometer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Setethoscope", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spirometer", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Electro cardiograph", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The volume of air involved in breathing movements can be estimated by using a spirometer which helps in clinical assessment of pulmonary functions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8540,'biology',83,497,1013,'Each of the following four sets (i-iv) contains three animals of a phylum and one odd animal that belongs to another phylum. Select the option that identifies the odd animal in each series.\ni. <i>Adamsia, Gorgonia, Euspongia, Physalia</i>\nii. <i>Ascaris, Ancylostoma, Wuchereria, Fasciola</i>\niii. <i>Ophiura, Pila, Sepia, Aplysia</i>\niv. <i>Locusta, Loligo Limulus, Laccifer</i>','[{"text": "<i>Euspongia, Fasciola, Ophiura, Loligo</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Adamsia, Fasciola, Aplysia, Locusta</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Euspongia, Ascaris, Ophiura, Loligo</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Gorgonia, Fasciola, Pila, Limulus</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'i. Euspongia belongs to porifera. Other three belong to Cnidaria.<br>ii. Fasciola belongs to platyhelminthes, other three belong to Ascheminthes.<br>iii. Ophiura belongs to Echinodermata. Other three belong to Mollusca.\n\niv. Loligo belongs to Mollusca. Other three belong to Arthropoda.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8541,'biology',86,981,2286,'A spirometer can be used to directly measure','[{"text": "Residual volume", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vital capacity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Functional residual capacity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Total lung capacity", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The volume of air involved in breathing movements can be estimated by using a spirometer which helps in clinical assessment of pulmonary functions. A spirometer can be used to directly measure vital capacity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8548,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which of the following is not a correct combination of three animals and their common feature?','[{"text": "$Obelia$ &emsp; &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{Umbrella-shaped \\\\, adult} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, Physalia $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, Aurelia $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$Planaria$ &emsp; &emsp; $\\\\rm{Ventral \\\\, nerve\\\\,  cord}$ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, Hirudinaria $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, Wuchereria $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$Ascaris $ &emsp; &emsp; &emsp;$\\\\, \\\\rm{Organ-system\\\\,  level} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, Nereis $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, Apis $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$Pristis $ &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, \\\\rm{Viviparous} $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, Felis $ <br> &emsp; $\\\\, \\\\, Canis $", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Obelia and Physalia are polyp forms (cylindrical and sessile).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
