(8552,'biology',83,497,1013,'Which is correct for the gills of mollusca?<br>i. Feather like<br>ii. Respiratory and excretory in function<br>iii. Present in mantle cavity<br>iv. Covered with very thin calcareous shell','[{"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii and iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The space between the hump and the mantle is called the mantle cavity in which featherlike gills are present. They have respiratory and excretory functions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8553,'biology',86,981,2286,'Find out the tidal volume (approximate value) for a healthy human in an hour.','[{"text": "250 litres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "450 litres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "360 litres", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "150 litres", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Tidal Volume (TV): The volume of air inspired or expired during a normal respiration is called Tidal Volume. It is approximately 500 $$\\mathrm{ml}$$ in a healthy man. This means that a healthy adult can inspire or expire about 6 to 8 litre of air per minute.<br>Tidal Volume $$=500 \\mathrm{ml}$$<br>Respiration rate $$=12$$ per minute<br>Hence, Tidal Volume in 1 hour ${\\rm{ = 500ml}}\\,{\\rm{x}}\\,{\\rm{12}}\\,{\\rm{x}}\\,{\\rm{60minute}}$ $$=360000 \\mathrm{ml}=360$$ litre',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8556,'biology',83,497,1013,'Which of the following is an incorrect match w.r.t. animal and its features/description?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "<i>Sycon</i> - Cellular level of organization, radial present for balancing, planula larva in life cycle. Intracellular digestion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Obelia</i> - Diploblastic, polymorphic, exhibits metagenesis, carnivorous, sense organs, statocyst symmetry, calcareous spicules, intracellular", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Hirudinaria</i> - Schizocoelomate, organsystem level of organisation, sangvivorous, metameric segmentation, temporary clitellum, coelom is filled with bortroidal tissue, trochophore larva in life cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Octopus - Unsegmented, bilateral symmetry, closed circulatory system eight oral arms, male has hectocotylized arm, internal fertilization, direct development", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Digestion is extracellular and intracellular in cnidarians. Calcareous spicules are present in poriferans.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8557,'biology',86,981,2286,'Tidal volume is','[{"text": "Volume of air inspired in normal breathe", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Additional volume of air, a person can inspire by forcible inspiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Volume of air expired in normal breathe", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Volume of the air inspired or expired during normal breathe is called tidal volume. It is about $$500 \\mathrm{~mL}$$. of air in average young adult man.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8559,'biology',83,496,1012,'Read the following characteristics of the phylum arthropoda<br>How many informations are correct?','[{"text": "Seven", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Five", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Six", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Arthropods have Bilateral symmetry, Open type of circulatory system, coelomates and triploblastic with an organ system level of organization.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_8559_question_1.png'),
(8562,'biology',86,981,2286,'Approximate volume of air, a healthy man can inspire or expire per minute is','[{"text": "5000 to 6000 mL", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6000 to 8000 mL", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1200 to 7000 mL", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "7000 to 9000 mL", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Volume of air inspired or expired during a normal respiration. It is approx. 500 mL., i.e., a healthy man can inspire or expire approximately 6000 to 8000 mL of air per minute.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
