(8583,'biology',83,507,1025,'Study the statements and select the correct option<br>I. <i>Torpedo</i> has electric organs that can stun the prey<br>II. Bony fishes have to swim continuously<BR>III. Amphibian skin has thick scales<br>IV. Birds are poikilothermous<br>V. Prototherian mammals are oviparous','[{"text": "I, and V are true, while II, III and IV are false", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, and V are true, while III and IV are false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II are true, while III, IV and V are false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV and III are true, while I and III are false", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bony fishes are provided with an air bladder, hence they need not swim continuously. Skin of amphibians is moist and it lacks scales. Birds are homeothermic.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
