(8607,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which one of the following statements about crocodile, crow and cat is correct?','[{"text": "Crocodile has three-chambered heart whereas the other two have fourchambered heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crow is oviparous whereas the other two are viviparous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crocodile is cold-blooded whereas the other two are warm-blooded", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All the three exhibit external fertilization and direct development", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Crocodile is a reptile. Crow is a bird. Cat is a mammal. Only birds and mammals are warmblooded. Reptiles are cold-blooded.<br>(1) Crocodile also has four-chambered heart.<br>(2) Crocodile is also oviparous.<br>(4) All the three exhibit internal fertilization.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
