(8712,'biology',86,982,2287,'In alveoli of the lungs, the air at the site of gas exchange, is separated from the blood by','[{"text": "Alveolar epithelium only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alveolar epithelium and capillary endothelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alveolar epithelium, capillary endothelium and basement membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alveolar epithelium, capillary endothelium, a thin layer of tunica media and tunica adventitia", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Alveoli: It is the primary site of gas exchange between air and blood. It is a very thin layer ${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.1 - 1}}{\\rm{.5\\mu }}$ allowing for rapid and efficient gas exchange. It has a rich capillary network that anastomoses through the wall of the alveoli, total endothelial surface area of about $$125 \\mathrm{~m}^{2}$$ for gas exchange. The blood- air barrier consists of:-<br>a. Endothelial cell of capillary.<br>b. Basement membrane between endothelial and epithelial cells.<br>c. Epithelial cell (simple squamous) of alveolar lining.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
