(8744,'biology',86,982,2287,'The solubility of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ in the blood is','[{"text": "10-15 times higher than that of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "20-25 times higher than that of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "30-35 times higher than that of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "40-45 times higher than that of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The solubility of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is $$20-25$$ times higher than that of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$. Therefore, the amount of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ that can diffuse through the diffusion membrane per unit difference in partial pressure is much higher as compared to that of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
