(8756,'biology',86,982,2287,'The total thickness of the diffusion membrane of alveolus capillary is','[{"text": "Less than $$1 \\\\mathrm{~cm}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Less than $$2 \\\\mathrm{~cm}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Less than $$1 \\\\mathrm{~mm}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "More than $$1 \\\\mathrm{~mm}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The diffusion membrane is made up of three major layers namely, the thin squamous epithelium of alveoli, the endothelium of alveolar capillaries and the basement substance in between them. However, its total thickness is much less than a millimetre.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8757,'biology',84,583,1167,'Hibernation in frog is_____','[{"text": "Spring sleep", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rainy season sleep", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Winter sleep", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Summer sleep", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Hibernation is winter sleeping, where organism will remain dormant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8758,'biology',83,498,1014,'The scientific and common names of certain animals are given below. Mark the correct option<br>Scientific name &emsp; &emsp;  Common name<br>A. <i>Antedon</i> &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; &emsp;-Brittle star<br>B. <i>Loligo</i> &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; &emsp;- Cuttle fish<br>C. <i>Dentalium</i> &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; - Tusk shell<br>D. <i>Euspongia</i> &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; - Bath sponge<br>Option','[{"text": "A is wrong but $\\\\mathrm{B}, \\\\mathrm{C}$ and $\\\\mathrm{D}$ are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and C are wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\\\mathrm{B}$ are wrong but $\\\\mathrm{C}$ and $\\\\mathrm{D}$ are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A and B are correct but C and D are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Loligo is a squid. Cuttle fish is the common name of Sepia. Common name for Antedon is feather star.Brittle star is common name for members of Ophiuroidea order.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8760,'biology',86,982,2287,'Which is not true?','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ of oxygented blood is $$95 \\\\mathrm{~mm} \\\\mathrm{Hg}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ of alveolar air is $$40 \\\\mathrm{~mm} \\\\mathrm{Hg}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ of alveolar air is $$104 \\\\mathrm{~mm} \\\\mathrm{Hg}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ of deoxygenated blood is $$95 \\\\mathrm{~mm} \\\\mathrm{Hg}$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The $$\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ of deoxygenated blood is ${\\rm{45}}\\,{\\rm{mmHg}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8761,'biology',84,583,1167,'Croaking of frog is','[{"text": "Hunger call", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Danger call", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mating call for female", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Musical note", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Croaking sound of frog is produced due to presence of vocal cords. These vocal sacs are present only in a male frog. Production of croaking sound in frog is a courtship behavior in frogs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8764,'biology',86,982,2287,'The direction of concentration gradient for $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is from','[{"text": "Tissues to blood and alveoli to blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood to tissues and tissues to alveoli", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alveoli to blood and blood to tissues", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tissues to blood and blood to alveoli", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The direction of concentration gradient for $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is from tissues to blood and blood to alveoli.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8765,'biology',84,583,1167,'The frogs have the ability to change its colour to hide them from their enemies. This protective colouration is called','[{"text": "Hibernation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mimicry", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aestivation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Camouflage", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Frogs have the ability to change the colour to hide them from their enemies (camouflage). This protective coloration is called mimicry.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8766,'biology',83,506,1024,'Consider the following characters and choose the option which have characters those are not present in aves<br>i. Scales on all over the body<br>ii. Endoskeleton is fully ossified<br>iii. Skin is dry without glands except some oil gland<br>iv. Glands on body to feed their young ones','[{"text": "i, ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iv", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Scales are present only on the hind limbs of birds. Birds do not have any gland to feed their young ones. It is the mammals that have mammary glands to feed their young ones.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8768,'biology',86,982,2287,'At which of the following sites is the partial pressure of carbon dioxide $$\\left(\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}\\right)$$ highest?','[{"text": "Exhaled gas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alveolar gas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arterial blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Venous blood", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The partial pressure of carbon dioxide $$\\left(\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}\\right)$$ is highest in venous blood i.e. (deoxygenated blood) which is ${\\rm{45}}\\,{\\rm{mmHg}}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8769,'biology',84,583,1167,'Frogs possesses all of the following habits except','[{"text": "Mimicry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aestivation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hibernation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of claspers", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Frogs have the ability to change the colour to hide them from their enemies (camouflage). This protective coloration is called mimicry. Frogs are not seen during peak summer and winter. During this period they take shelter in deep burrows to protect them from extreme heat and cold. This is known as summer sleep (aestivation) and winter sleep (hibernation) respectively. Presence of claspers is not characteristic habit of frog.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8770,'biology',83,496,1012,'Which of the following in not a matching pair of the kind of excretory organ in animal and its phylum?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Animal : <em>Musca</em><br>organ : Excretory Malpighian tubules<br>Phylum : Arthropoda", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Animal : <em>Ancylostoma</em><br>Excretory organ : Renette cell<br>Phylum : Aschelminthes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Animal : <em>Taenia solium</em><br>Excretory organ : Flame cell<br>Phylum : Ctenophora", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Animal : <em>Palaemon</em><br>Excretory organ : Green gland<br>Phylum : Arthropoda", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<em>Taenia solium</em> belongs to Phylum Platyhelminthes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8772,'biology',86,982,2287,'At which of the following sites is the partial pressure of oxygen $$\\left(\\mathrm{pO}_{2}\\right)$$ highest?','[{"text": "Exhaled gas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anatomical dead space at the end of expiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anatomical dead space at the end of inspiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alveolar gas", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The partial pressure of oxygen $$\\left(\\mathrm{pO}_{2}\\right)$$ is highest in alveolar gas which is ${\\rm{104}}\\,{\\rm{mmHg}}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8773,'biology',84,583,1167,'The frog is poikilothermal animal because','[{"text": "Its body temperature is higher than that of the surrounding environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Its body temperature is constant irrespective of the fluctuation in the temperature of environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Its body temperature is non constant and fluctuates with temperature of environment", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The frog is poikilothermal animal because its body temperature is non constant and fluctuates with temperature of environment.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8774,'biology',83,494,1010,'How many characters in the list given below are true regarding aschelminthes.<br>i. Circular in cross section, hence the name flatworms.<br>ii. Pseudocoelomate animals<br>iii. Alimentary canal is complete with muscular pharynx.<br>iv. Sexes are separate (Dioecious)<br>v. Fertilization is external<br>vi. Development is indirect only','[{"text": "Three", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Five", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Aschelminthes are pseudocoelomate animals, alimentary canal is complete with muscular pharynx and the sexes are separate .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8776,'biology',86,982,2287,'Which of the following statements about the partial pressure of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is true?','[{"text": "It is higher in alveoli than in pulmonary artery", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is higher in systemic veins than in systemic arteries", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is higher in the systemic arteries than in tissues", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is higher in the pulmonary veins than in pulmonary arteries", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The partial pressure of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is higher in systemic veins (contains deoxygenated blood) than in systemic arteries(contains oxygenated blood).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8777,'biology',84,583,1167,'Select the correct answer<br>i. Body of a frog is divisible into head and trunk<br>ii. A neck and tail are sometimes absent','[{"text": "Only $\\\\mathrm{i}$ is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only ii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Body of a frog is divisible into head and trunk. A neck and tail are absent.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8778,'biology',83,496,1012,'Which is a character of arthropods?<br>i. Open circulatory system<br>ii. Sensory organs like eyes, antennae and statocysts<br>iii. Internal fertilization and mostly oviparous<br>iv. Development always direct','[{"text": "ii, iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii and iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii and iv", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Development in arthropods is indirect.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8780,'biology',86,982,2287,'Which vein contains the oxygenated blood in humans?','[{"text": "Cardiac vein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hepatopancreatic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Portal vein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pulmonary vein", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pulmonary vein is the only vein in body, which carries oxygenated blood rather than deoxygenated blood. It carries the blood from the lungs to the left auricle of heart. From left auricle, blood goes to the left ventricle, which then distributes that blood all over the body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8781,'biology',84,583,1167,'In order to protect from water, eye of a frog is provided with a transparent','[{"text": "Nictitating membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Upper eye lid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cornea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lower eye lid", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In frogs eyes are bulged and covered by a nictitating membrane that protects them while in water.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8783,'biology',83,491,1007,'Given below are types of cells present in some animals. Which of the following cells can differentiate to perform different functions?','[{"text": "Choanocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interstitial cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gastrodermal cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nematocytes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Other cells in the options cannot differentiate. But interstitial cells in testes and ovary can differentiate.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8784,'biology',86,982,2287,'Name of artery which carries deoxygenated blood.','[{"text": "Pulmonary artery", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pulomnary trunk", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Systemic artery", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vena cava", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pulmonary artery carries deoxygenated blood from the right ventricle to the lungs for the oxygenation of deoxygenation blood.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8785,'biology',84,583,1167,'The skin of frog is slippery and smooth due to the presence of','[{"text": "Mucus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Saliva", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Waxy skin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The skin is smooth and slippery due to the presence of mucus. The skin is always maintained in a moist condition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8797,'biology',84,583,1167,'Male frog can be distinguished from female frog by the presence of','[{"text": "Vocal sacs and copulatory pad on the first digit of the forelimb", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A neck and tail is present", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nictating membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Copulatory pad on the first digit of the hindlimb", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Male frogs can be distinguished by the presence of sound producing vocal sacs and also a copulatory pad on the first digit of the fore limbs which are absent in female frogs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8787,'biology',83,505,1023,'Which of the following pairs of animals has non glandular skin?','[{"text": "Snake and Frog", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chameleon and Turtle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Frog and Pigeon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crocodile and Tiger", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Glandular skin is present in frog, snake and crocodile. Mammals too have glandular skin. Hence, option \' 2 \' is the correct option.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8788,'biology',86,982,2287,'Identify the correct statement.','[{"text": "In lungs, gaseous exchange takes place by active transport.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The solubility of oxygen is 20-25 times higher than that of carbon dioxide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The thickness of diffusion membrane is more than a millimetre.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The amount of $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ that can diffuse through the diffusion membrane per unit difference in partial pressure is much higher compared to that of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'As the solubility of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is 20-25 times higher than that of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$, the amount of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ that can diffuse through the diffusion membrane per unit difference in partial pressure is much higher compared to that of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8789,'biology',84,583,1167,'The hindlimbs and forelimbs of frogs are','[{"text": "Four digits", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Five digits", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four and five digits, respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Five and four digits, respectively", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The hind limbs end in five digits and they are larger and muscular than fore limbs that end in four digits. Feet have webbed digits that help in swimming',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8791,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which one of the following sets of animals belong to a single taxonomic group?','[{"text": "Cuttlefish, Jellyfish, Silverfish, Dogfish, Starfish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bat, Pigeon, Butterfly", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monkey, Chimpanzee, Man", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Silkworm, Tapeworm, Earthworm", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In option \' 3 \' all organisms belong to class mammalia.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8792,'biology',86,982,2287,'The figure given below shows a small part of human lung where exchange of gas takes place. In which of the options given below, the one part A, B, C or D is correctly identified along with its function.','[{"text": "A-alveolar cavity - main site of exchange of respiratory gases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "D - capillary wall - exchange of gases takes place here", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B - Red blood cell - transport of $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ mainly haemoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C-arterial capillary - passes oxygen to tissues", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Option (1) is correctly mentioned as alveoli which are the primary sites of exchange of gases. The exchange of gases $$\\left(\\mathrm{O}_{2}\\right.$$ and $$\\left.\\mathrm{CO}_{2}\\right)$$ between the alveoli and the blood occurs by simple diffusion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/86_8792_question_1.png'),
(8793,'biology',84,583,1167,'The forelimb of male frog is distinct from female frog by the presence of','[{"text": "Fore arm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thumb", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Web feet", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Copulatory pad", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Male frogs can be distinguished by the presence of sound producing vocal sacs and also a copulatory pad on the first digit of the fore limbs which are absent in female frogs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8795,'biology',83,496,1012,'Which one of the following statements is incorrect?','[{"text": "In cockroaches and prawns excretion of waste material occurs through malpighian tubules.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In ctenophore, locomotion is mediated by comb plates.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In fasciola flame cells take part in excretion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Earthworms are hermaphrodites and yet cross fertilization take place among them.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In prawns, excretion takes place through green glands.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8796,'biology',86,983,2288,'About $$97 \\%$$ of oxygen is transported by RBC. The remaining $$3 \\%$$ is','[{"text": "Dissolved in plasma and transported", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Retained in lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Attached to cell membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inside mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'About $$97 \\%$$ of oxygen is transported by $$\\mathrm{RBC}$$. The remaining $$3 \\%$$ is dissolved in plasma and transported.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8799,'biology',83,505,1023,'Which one of the following is not a poisonous snake?','[{"text": "Cobra", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viper", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Python", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Krait", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Python is a non-poisonous snake.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8800,'biology',86,983,2288,'Which of the following statement is incorrect about transport of gases?','[{"text": "About 97 percent of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ is transported by $\\\\mathrm{RBC}$ in the blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 percent of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ is carried in dissolved state through the plasma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "70 percent carbon dioxide is carried in dissolved state in plasma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "20-25 percent of $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ is transported by $\\\\mathrm{RBC}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'70 percent carbon dioxide is carried in dissolved state in plasma is incorrect. Nearly 20-25<br>per cent of $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ is transported by RBCs whereas 70 per cent of it is carried as bicarbonate.<br>About 7 per cent of $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ is carried in a dissolved state through plasma.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8801,'biology',84,583,1167,'Which of the following is false about the frog?<br>i. The frog never drinks water but absorb it through the skin.<br>ii. On either side of the eyes a membranous tympanum (ear) receives sound signals <br>iii. The forelimbs and hind limbs help in swimming, walking, leaping and burrowing<br>iv. Feet have webbed digits that help in swimming','[{"text": "Only i and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only i and vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements given are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8803,'biology',83,489,1004,'Body cavity is the cavity present between body wall and gut wall. In some animals, the body cavity is not lined by mesoderm. Such animals are called','[{"text": "Acoelomate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pseudocoelomate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coelomate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haemocoelomate", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When body cavity is present but not lined by mesoderm, the condition is known to be pseudocoelomate. Mesoderm here is present in scattered pouches.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8804,'biology',86,983,2288,'What percentage of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ flows in blood in the form of bicarbonates?','[{"text": "$$7 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$23 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$50 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$70 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The majority (70 %) of carbon dioxide travels in the blood stream as bicarbonate ions.<BR>The reaction that describes the formation of bicarbonate ions in the blood is:<br>$$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{CO}_{3} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}^{+}+\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$<br>This means that carbon dioxide reacts with water to form carbonic acid, which dissociates in solution to form hydrogen ions and bicarbonate ions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8805,'biology',84,583,1168,'Adult frog is','[{"text": "Herbivores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carnivores", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Omnivores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Saprophyte", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Frogs are Carnivores as they eat live prey.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8807,'biology',83,489,1005,'In some animal groups, the body is found divided into compartments with serial repetition of at least some organs. This characteristic feature is named','[{"text": "Segmentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metamerism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metagenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metamorphosis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Segments in such animals are called metameres and this phenomenon is called metamerism.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8808,'biology',86,983,2288,'$$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is carried in blood as','[{"text": "Magnesium carbonate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sodium carbonate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Potassium carbonate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sodium bicarbonate", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is carried in blood as sodium bicarbonate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8809,'biology',84,583,1168,'. The alimentary canal of frog is _________and the length of intestine is _______','[{"text": "short, reduced", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "long, reduced", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "long, increased", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "short, increased", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The digestive system consists of alimentary canal and digestive glands. The alimentary canal is short because frogs are carnivores and hence the length of intestine is reduced.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8811,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which one of the following sets of animals share a four-chambered heart?','[{"text": "Amphibian, Reptiles, Birds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crocodiles, Birds, Mammals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Crocodiles, Lizards, Turtles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lizards, Mammals, Birds", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Amphibians have two-chambered heart, while most of the reptiles have a three chambered heart.Crocodiles, birds and mammals have four chambered heart.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8812,'biology',86,983,2288,'Oxyhaemoglobin dissociates at','[{"text": "All times irrespective of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ concentration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Low $$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ in tissues", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Equal $$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ in tissues", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "High $$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ in tissues and blood", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the tissues, where low $$\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$, high $$\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$, high $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$concentration and higher temperature exist, the conditions are favourable for dissociation of oxygen from the oxyhaemoglobin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
