(8813,'biology',84,583,1168,'Put the organs of the digestive system of the frog in its proper order<br>1. pharynx 2. stomach 3. Mouth 4. intestine, 5. Oesophagus, 6. cloaca 7. rectum','[{"text": "$3,1,5,2,4,7,6$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$3,1,5,2,4,6,7$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1,3,5,2,4,7,6$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3,1,2,5,4,7,6$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The mouth of frog opens into the buccal cavity that leads to the oesophagus through pharynx. Oesophagus is a short tube that opens into the stomach which in turn continues as the intestine, rectum and finally opens outside by the cloaca.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8815,'biology',83,507,1025,'Birds and mammals share one of the following characteristics as a common feature.','[{"text": "Pigmented skin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pneumatic bones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viviparity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Warm blooded", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pneumatic bones and viviparity is present in birds but not in mammals. Pigmented skin is present only in mammals. Hence, \' 4 \' is the correct option.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8816,'biology',86,983,2288,'Which of the following statement is incorrect about transport of gases?','[{"text": "About 97 percent of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ is transported by $$\\\\mathrm{RBC}$$ in the blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 percent of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ is carried in dissolved state through the plasma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "70 percent carbon dioxide is transported as bicarbonates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "10-15 percent of $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is transported by $$\\\\mathrm{RBC}$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Nearly 20-25 per cent of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is transported by RBCs whereas 70 per cent of it is carried as bicarbonate. About 7 per cent of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is carried in a dissolved state through plasma.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8817,'biology',84,583,1168,'Food in the frog is captured by  the_________.','[{"text": "Dry tongue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bilobed tongue", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rosy tongue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hairy tongue", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Frog captures food by the bilobed tongue.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8819,'biology',83,498,1014,'Which one of the following statements is incorrect?','[{"text": "Mesoglea is present in between ectoderm and endoderm in <i>Obelia</i>.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Asterias</i> exhibits radial symmetry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Fasciola</i> is a pseudocoelomate animal", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Taenia</i> is a triploblastic animal", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fasciola is an acoelomated animal.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8820,'biology',86,983,2288,'Oxyhaemoglobin is converted into haemoglobin during the internal respiration because','[{"text": "Oxyhaemoglobin is unstable", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxygen tension in tissue is less than capillary blood reaching tissue", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ tension is low in blood that reaches tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "An enzyme splits oxyhaemoglobin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'One hemoglobin molecule contains ironcontaining heme molecules, and because of this, each hemoglobin molecule is capable of carrying up to four molecules of oxygen. As oxygen diffuses across the respiratory membrane from the alveolus to the capillary, it also diffuses into the red blood cell and is bound by hemoglobin. The following reversible chemical reaction describes the production of the final product, oxyhemoglobin $$(\\mathrm{Hb}-$$ $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ ), which is formed when oxygen binds to hemoglobin.So, the correct option is \'Oxygen tension in tissues is less than capillary blood reaching tissues\'.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8823,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which one of the following is oviparous?','[{"text": "Platypus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Flying fox (Bat)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Elephant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Whale", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Platypus and echidna are oviparous mammals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8824,'biology',86,983,2288,'Oxygen in expired air','[{"text": "$$10 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$16 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$19 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$4 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The permanent gases in gas we exhale are $$4 \\%$$ to $$5 \\%$$ by volume more carbon dioxide and $$4 \\%$$ to $$5 \\%$$ by volume less oxygen than was inhaled. This expired air is typically composed of: $$78.04 \\%$$ nitrogen. $$13.6 \\%-16 \\%$$ oxygen',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8825,'biology',84,583,1168,'In frog, excess bile juice secreted by the liver is stored in','[{"text": "Intestine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pancreas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gall bladder", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stomach", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In frog Liver secretes bile that is stored in the gall bladder.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8827,'biology',83,489,1003,'Match the following list of animals with their level of organisation.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Organ level<br>B. Cell aggregate level<br>C. Tissue level<br>D. Organ system level</div><div class="column-right">1. <em>Pheretima</em><br>2.<em> Fasciola</em><br>3. <em>Spongilla</em><br>4. <em>Obelia</em></div></div>','[{"text": "1-B, 2-C, 3-D, 4-A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-B, 2-D, 3-C, 4-A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-D, 2-A, 3-B, 4-C", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1-A, 2-D, 3-C, 4-B", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A. Organ level - 2. <em>Fasciola</em><br>B. Cell aggregate level - 3. <em>Spongilla</em><br>C. Tissue level - 4. <em>Obelia</em><br>D. Organ system level - 1. <em>Pheretima</em>',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8828,'biology',86,983,2288,'A molecule of haemoglobin carries how many oxygen molecules?','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each haemoglobin molecule can carry a maximum of four molecules of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$. Thus, chemical formula of oxyhaemoglobin is $$\\mathrm{Hb}$$ $$\\left(\\mathrm{O}_{2}\\right) 4$$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8829,'biology',84,583,1168,'In frogs, digested food is absorbed by','[{"text": "Villi and microvilli in intestine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Villi in rectum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Typhlosole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Villi and microvilli in stomach and intestine", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In frogs digested food is absorbed by the numerous finger-like folds in the inner wall of intestine called villi and microvilli.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8831,'biology',83,498,1014,'Match the column A with column B and choose the correct option<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Porifera<br>B. Aschelminthes<br>C. Annelida<br>D. Arthropoda<br>E. Echinodermata</div><div class="column-right">1. Canal system<br>2. Water-vascular system<br>3. Muscular pharynx<br>4. Jointed appendages<br>5. Metameres</div></div>','[{"text": "A-2, B-3, C-5, D-4, E-1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-2, B-5, C-3, D-4, E-1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-1, B-3, C-5, D-4, E-2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-1, B-5, C-3, D-4, E-2", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A. Porifera - 1. Canal system<br>B. Aschelminthes - 3. Muscular pharynx<br>C. Annelida - 5. Metameters<br>D. Arthropoda - 4. Jointed appndages<br>E. Echinodermata - 2. Water-vascular system',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8832,'biology',86,983,2288,'Haemoglobin has maximum affinity for----than $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Haemoglobin has maximum affinity for $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ (200-250 times higher as compared to $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ ).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8833,'biology',84,583,1168,'In frog, the duodenum receives bile from gall bladder and pancreatic juices from the pancreas through a','[{"text": "Stenson\'s duct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Common bile duct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cystic duct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hepatic duct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In frog, the duodenum receives bile from gall blader and pancreatic juices from the pancreas through a common bile duct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8845,'biology',84,583,1168,'In water, the aquatic respiratory organ in frog is/are','[{"text": "Skin, lungs and buccal cavity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Skin only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lungs and buccal cavity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Buccal cavity only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In water, the aquatic respiratory organ is Skin (cutaneous respiration).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8835,'biology',83,500,1017,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Notochord is persistent only at larval stage, after that it diappearsin urochordates</div><div class="column-right">Insects blood has no role in transport of oxygen</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Notochord is persistent only at larval stage, after that it diappearsin urochordates is correct. Hemolymph, is a fluid, analogous to the blood in vertebrates, which circulates in the interior of the arthropod body remaining in direct contact with the animal\'s tissues. It contains hemocyanin, a copper-based protein that turns blue in colour when oxygenated, instead of the iron-based haemoglobin in red blood cells found in vertebrates, thus giving hemolymph a blue-green colour rather than the red colour of vertebrate blood.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8836,'biology',86,983,2288,'Amount of oxygen present in one gram of haemoglobin is','[{"text": "$$1.34 \\\\mathrm{ml}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$20 \\\\mathrm{ml}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$13.4 \\\\mathrm{ml}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Amount of oxygen present in one gram of haemoglobin is ${\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.34}}\\,{\\rm{ml}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8837,'biology',84,583,1168,'The given figure depicts','[{"text": "Digestive system of cockroach", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nervous system of earthworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Digestive system of earthworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Digestive system of frog", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The given figure depicts digestive system of frog.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/84_8837_question_1.png'),
(8839,'biology',83,498,1014,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Echinodermata are triploblastic radially symmetrical in larval stage and coelomate animals</div><div class="column-right">The body wall of Ascaris has cuticle but lacks circular muscles</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Echinodermata adult is radially symmetrical. There is a stiff cuticle and no circular muscles, hence nematodes possess poor powers of locomotion.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8840,'biology',86,983,2288,'Determination of oxygen carried by haemoglobin is done by','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pH}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Partial pressure of oxygen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Partial pressure of carbon dioxide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Binding of oxygen with haemoglobin is primarily related to partial pressure of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$. Partial pressure of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$, hydrogen ion concentration and temperature are the other factors which can interfere with this binding.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8841,'biology',84,583,1168,'In frog, cutaneous respiration occurs','[{"text": "Only on land", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Everywhere", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only during aestivation or hibernation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only in water", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Frogs respire on land and in the water by two different methods. In water, skin acts as aquatic respiratory organ (cutaneous respiration). Dissolved oxygen in the water is exchanged through the skin by diffusion. On land, the buccal cavity, skin and lungs act as the respiratory organs. The respiration by lungs is called pulmonary respiration. Hence in frog, cutaneous respiration occurs everywhere.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8843,'biology',83,500,1017,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Protochordates are often called invertebrate chordates</div><div class="column-right">They are connecting link between invertebrates and chordates</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Protochordates are often called invertebrate chordates and they are connecting link between vertebrates and early chordate ancestors. They lack a vertebral column.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8844,'biology',86,983,2288,'The combination of oxygen with haemoglobin is called','[{"text": "Oxidation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxygenation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Reduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The red respiratory protein of red blood cells that transports oxygen as oxyhaemoglobin (Also called oxygenated haemoglobin) from the lungs to the tissues, where the oxygen is readily released and the oxyhaemoglobin becomes haemoglobin. The compound formed when a molecule of haemoglobin binds with a molecule of oxygen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8847,'biology',83,506,1024,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Avian bones are pneumatic</div><div class="column-right">This makes body light for flight in the air</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The pneumatic or hollow bones of birds are an adaptation towards aerial mode of life. They reduce the extra weight of the body and make them buoyant.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8848,'biology',86,983,2288,'The direction of concentration gradient for oxygen is from','[{"text": "Tissues to blood and blood to alveoli", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tissues to blood and alveoli to blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alveoli to blood and blood to tissues", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Blood to tissues and tissues to alveoli", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The direction of concentration gradient for oxygen is from alveoli to blood and blood to tissues',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8849,'biology',84,583,1168,'In frog, if a hole is punched in the floor of its buccal cavity, then frog will not die, reason is','[{"text": "Cutaneous respiration occurs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Respiration other than lungs will continue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "buccal respiration does not stop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It can store oxygen for future also", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In frog, if a hole is punched in the floor of its buccal cavity, then frog will not die, reason is cutaneous respiration occurs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8850,'biology',83,489,1005,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Segmentation in tapeworms is called pseudometamerism</div><div class="column-right">Echinodermata are marine with cellular level of organisation</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Echinodermata are marine with organ system level of organisation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8852,'biology',86,983,2288,'Every $$100 \\mathrm{ml}$$ of oxygenated blood delivers following amount of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ to the tissues under normal physiological conditions','[{"text": "More than $$50 \\\\mathrm{ml}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$15 \\\\mathrm{ml}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$50 \\\\mathrm{ml}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$5 \\\\mathrm{ml}$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Every $$100 \\mathrm{ml}$$ of oxygenated blood can deliver around $$5 \\mathrm{ml}$$ of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ to the tissues under normal physiological conditions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8853,'biology',84,583,1168,'The respiration by lungs in frog is called','[{"text": "Pulmonary respiration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cutaneous respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Buccal respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellular respiration", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The respiration by lungs in frog is called pulmonary respiration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8854,'biology',83,496,1012,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Arthropods are the most successful of all the animal groups</div><div class="column-right">They exhibit the greatest adaptive radiations and diversity of habitats</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Arthropods success and diversity is due to mainly two factors. First, arthropod jointed appendages are susceptible to adaptive specialisation. Legs, mouthparts antennae, claws pincers, swimming paddles, and gills represent some of the specialisations. Second, their exoskeleton provides protection and mechanical advantage. The exoskeleton serves as an external armor for protection against the environment and predators.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8856,'biology',86,983,2288,'Reduction of the pulmonary diffusing capacity to one-fourth of its normal value would be expected to have what effect on systemic arterial oxygen and carbon dioxide partial pressures (compared to normal)?','[{"text": "Decrease $$\\\\mathrm{Pa}-\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and decrease $$\\\\mathrm{Pa}-\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decrease $$\\\\mathrm{Pa}-\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and increase $$\\\\mathrm{Pa}-\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase $$\\\\mathrm{Pa}-\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and decrease $$\\\\mathrm{Pa}-\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decrease $$\\\\mathrm{Pa}-\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ but no change in $$\\\\mathrm{Pa}-\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$$\\mathrm{Pa}-\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ decreases when $$\\mathrm{pO} 2$$ decreases to less than one-third its normal value. But $$\\mathrm{pCO} 2$$ is so high normally that even a decrease to one-fourth will still permit carbon dioxide to equilibrate in the time that blood passes through pulmonary capillaries.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8857,'biology',84,583,1168,'During aestivation and hibernation in frogs, gaseous exchange takes place through','[{"text": "Lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Skin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During aestivation and hibernation in frogs, gaseous exchange takes place through skin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8858,'biology',83,507,1025,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Mammals and birds use metabolic heat to regulate their body temperature</div><div class="column-right">These animals are ectothermic</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mammals and birds are endothermic animals, as they use metabolic heat to regulate their body temperature.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8860,'biology',86,983,2288,'The sigmoid shape of the dissociation curve is because:-','[{"text": "The curve shows the equilibrium of oxyhaemoglobin and haemoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In the lungs, the partial pressure of oxygen is high", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tissues have a low oxygen concentration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Binding of oxygen to haemoglobin. As the first oxygen molecule binds to haemoglobin, it increases the affinity for the second molecule of oxygen to bind. Subsequently, haemoglobin attracts more oxygen", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Haemoglobin molecule can bind to four oxygen molecules reversibly. The dissociation curve is the curve that results from the interaction of oxygen molecules with haemoglobin molecule. It indicates the oxygen saturation and partial pressure of oxygen in the blood. The binding of the first molecule is difficult. As the first oxygen molecule binds to haemoglobin, it increases the affinity of the haemoglobin molecules for the second molecule of oxygen to bind. Subsequently, haemoglobin attracts more oxygen and hence, the curve is sigmoid shape or S-shape',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8861,'biology',84,583,1168,'Which of the following is TRUE about the respiration of frog?','[{"text": "In water, skin acts as aquatic respiratory organ (cutaneous respiration)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Frogs respire on land and in water by the same method", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "On land, only the lungs act as respiratory organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dissolved oxygen in water is exchanged through the skin by active transport", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In water, skin acts as aquatic respiratory organ (cutaneous respiration). Dissolved oxygen in the water is exchanged through the skin by diffusion.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8862,'biology',83,494,1010,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Tapeworm,roundworm and pinworm are all endoparasites of human intestine</div><div class="column-right">Improperly cooked food is the source of all intestinal infections</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Some parasites that live inside the body of host are called endoparasites.\n\nIntestinal worms live at the expense of host by sucking vital nutrients from their body.\n\nRoundworms, tapeworms, hookworms, thread worms, pin worms and whip worms are the most common endoparasites of humans.\n\nInfection to parasites can occur if uncooked or contaminated food is consumed.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8864,'biology',86,983,2288,'Which of the following would have the same $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ content?','[{"text": "Blood entering the lungs - blood leaving the lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood entering the right side of the heart blood leaving the left side of the heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood entering the right side of the heart blood leaving the right side of the heart", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Blood entering the tissue capillaries blood leaving the tissue capillaries", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Blood entering the right side of the heart i.e. right atrium is a deoxygenated blood having partial pressure of $$40 \\mathrm{~mm} \\mathrm{Hg}$$. Blood,leaving the right side of the heart i.e., right ventricle will also have almost same partial pressure as the blood is moving from right atrium to right ventricle and also no exchange of gases occurs in this path.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8865,'biology',84,583,1168,'Which of the following statement is correct about frog?<br>i. During aestivation and hibernation gaseous exchange takes place through skin<br>ii. A pair of elongated pink hollow lungs are found in thorax.','[{"text": "Only i is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lungs are pair of elongated pink hollow structures found in thorax. During aestivation and hibernation gaseous exchange takes place through skin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8866,'biology',83,499,1015,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Echinodermata has endoskeleton of calcareous ossicle</div><div class="column-right">Hemichordata are bilaterally symmetrical, triploblastic and coelomate</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8868,'biology',86,983,2288,'With decrease in temperature, oxyhaemoglobin curve will become','[{"text": "More steep", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Straight", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parabola", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'At decreased temperature and rise in $$\\mathrm{pH}$$, the oxygen haemoglobin curve becomes steeper as the curve shifts to the left. This indicates that at these conditions, the $$\\mathrm{Hb}$$ has a higher affinity for oxygen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8869,'biology',84,583,1168,'Match the columns I and II in the frog.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Cutaneous respiration<br>B. Pulmonary respiration<br>C. Buccal respiration</div><div class="column-right">P. Lungs<br>Q. Skin<br>R. Buccal cavity</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'cutaneous respiration - Skin<br>Pulmonary respiration - lungs<br>Buccal respiration - Buccal cavity',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8870,'biology',83,503,1021,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Osteichthyes show presence of placoid scales</div><div class="column-right">Mouth terminal and gills covered by operculum is seen in osteichthyes</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Osteichthyes show presence of ctenoid scales',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8872,'biology',86,983,2288,'At a given $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ concentration, dissociation of oxyhaemoglobin will increase if','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pH}$$ of blood rises", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ concentration of blood falls", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pH}$$ of blood falls", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Free fatty acid concentration of blood falls", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Factors which shift oxygen dissociation curve to right<br>a. Decrease in $$\\mathrm{pO} 2$$.<br>b. Increase in ${\\rm{pC}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ (Both effect).<br>c. Increase in body temperature.<br>d. Increase in $$\\mathrm{H}+$$ ion concentration.<br>e. Decrease in $$\\mathrm{pH}$$.<br>f. Increse in 2,3 diphosphoglycerate<br>Right shifting indicates dissociation of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ from $$\\mathrm{Hb}$$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8873,'biology',83,489,1004,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">All triploblastic animals are eucoelomates</div><div class="column-right">They have a false coelom</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Eucoelomates are organisms having a true coelom. Coeloms developed in triploblasts but were subsequently lost in several lineages. The lack of a coelom is correlated with a reduction in body size.Coelom is sometimes incorrectly used to refer to any developed digestive tract. Some organisms may not possess a coelom or may have a false coelom (pseudocoelom).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8874,'biology',84,583,1167,'Amphibian heart is','[{"text": "3- chambered", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2- chambered", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1- chambered", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4- chambered", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Heart is a muscular structure situated in the upper part of the body cavity. Amphibian heart has three chambers, two atria and one ventricle and is covered by a membrane called pericardium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9481,'biology',84,579,1159,'The supportive skeletal structures in the human external ears and in the nose tip are example<br>','[{"text": "Areolar tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cartilage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ligament", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The supportive skeletal structures in the human external ears and in the nose tip are examples of cartilage.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8876,'biology',86,983,2288,'Bicarbonate ion is produced inside','[{"text": "Lymphocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Basophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neurophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Erythrocytes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In erythrocytes which are also known as red blood cell is the cell where bicarbonate ion production takes place. In the cell, some carbon dioxide binds to hemoglobin forming carbaminoglobin. Then carbonic anhydrase enzyme present in red blood cell quickly converts carbon dioxide and water into bicarbonate and hydrogen ions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8877,'biology',83,503,1021,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Coral reefs serve as stable marine ecosystems</div><div class="column-right">Both marine and freshwater forms with bony endoskeleton are present in osteichthyes</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Coral reefs provide shelter for a wide variety of marine life. They are a valuable source of organisms for potential medicines, they create sand for beaches, and serve as a buffer for shorelines. Coral reefs are built by millions. Both marine and freshwater forms with bony endoskeleton are present in Osteichthyes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8878,'biology',84,583,1169,'The vascular system of the frog is','[{"text": "Open type", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Closed type", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Double circulatory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Half open", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The vascular system of frog is welldeveloped closed type. Frogs have a lymphatic system also. The blood vascular system involves heart, blood vessels and blood.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8880,'biology',86,983,2288,'At higher $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ concentration, oxygen dissociation curve of haemoglobin will','[{"text": "Move to left", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Move to right", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Become irregular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Move upwardly", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'At higher $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ concentration, oxygen dissociation curve of haemoglobin will move to right.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8881,'biology',83,499,1015,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In hemichordata, sexes are separate, fertilisation is external and development is indirect</div><div class="column-right">Hemichordata has circulation is of open type</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8882,'biology',84,583,1169,'The three chambered heart of the frog is not as efficient as the mammalian heart because','[{"text": "both oxygenated and deoxygenated blood mix in the ventricle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "muscles of the heart are not so strong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ventricle can not pump blood properly", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "it cannot hold enough quantity of blood", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The three chambered heart of the frog is not as efficient as the mammalian heart because both oxygenated and deoxygenated blood mix in the ventricle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8884,'biology',86,983,2288,'Bicarbonate formed inside erythrocytes passes out into plasma while chloride of plasma pass into erythrocytes. the phenomenon is called','[{"text": "Bicarbonate shift", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbonation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbonchlorosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hamburger phenomenon", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bicarbonate formed inside erythrocytes passes out into plasma while chloride of plasma pass into erythrocytes. the phenomenon is called hamburger phenomenon.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8885,'biology',83,490,1006,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Sponges have remarkable power of regeneration</div><div class="column-right">They possess choanocytes which are totipotent cells</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The power of regeneration is very great in sponges.Any cut part will regenerate the whole sponge. This Power of regeneration in sponges is due to cells called Archeocytes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8886,'biology',84,583,1169,'The blood vascular system of the frog consists of','[{"text": "Heart, Blood vessels and blood without haemoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood vessels and sinus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haemolymph, blood vessels and myogenic heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood vessel, heart and blood containing RBCs and WBCs", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The vascular system of frog is welldeveloped closed type. Frogs have a lymphatic system also. The blood vascular system involves heart, blood vessels and blood(containing RBCs and WBCs). The lymphatic system consists of lymph, lymph channels and lymph nodes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8888,'biology',86,983,2288,'Dissociation curve shift to the left when','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ concentration increases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ concentration increases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ concentration decreases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$concentration increases", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Dissociation curve shift to the left when $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ concentration increases.<br>Factors which shift oxygen dissociation curve to left<br>a. Increase in $$\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$.<br>b. Decrease in $$\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ (Both effect).<br>c. Decrease in body temperature.<br>d. Decrease in $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$ion concentration.<br>e. Increase in $$\\mathrm{pH}$$.<br>f. Decrese in 2,3 diphosphoglycerate Left shifting indicates association of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ with $$\\mathrm{Hb}$$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
