(8890,'biology',84,583,1169,'Three-chambered heart of the frog contains','[{"text": "Two ventricles and one atrium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two atria and one ventricle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One auricle and one ventricles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One auricle, one ventricle, one sinus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Amphibian heart has three chambers, two atria and one ventricle and is covered by a membrane called pericardium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8892,'biology',86,983,2288,'In the process of transport of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ which phenomenon occurs between RBCs and plasma?','[{"text": "Osmosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adsorption", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloride shift", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Absorption", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bicarbonate diffuses out of the red blood cells into the plasma in venous blood and visa versa in arterial blood. Chloride ion always diffuses in an opposite direction of bicarbonate ion in order to maintain a charge balance. This is referred to as the chloride shift.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8893,'biology',83,491,1007,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Cnidarians are a great nuisance to the humans swimming in the sea</div><div class="column-right">They can sting and even paralyse people swimming in sea</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cnidarians like Jellyfish are the most frequent stingers in sea waters. They are a nuisance as they sting people taking a bath or swimming in the sea.Their stings penetrate human skin and introduce the toxins which produce the pain and even cause paralysis. .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
