(8992,'biology',87,1122,2693,'Select the true statement from the following:<br>1) Blood is the most commonly used body fluid by most of the higher organisms for transport.<br>2) Lymph also transports exactly the same substances like blood','[{"text": "1 is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2 is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Lymph does not transport exactly the same substances like blood.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8993,'biology',83,491,1007,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> <em>Hydra</em>, <em>Obelia</em> and adult echinoderms have radial symmetry.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Their body can be dived into two equal halves in any plane passing through central axis of the body.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When any plane passing through the central axis of the body divides the organism into two identical halves, it is called radial symmetry. Examples of radially symmetrical animals are - Ctenophora, Cnidaria, adult echinoderms.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
