(8997,'biology',83,491,1007,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Coelenterates are diploblastic.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Coelenterates contain mesoglea in between ectoderm and endoderm.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason  are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Coelentrates are diploblastic animals. Endoderm and ectoderm are the two germinal layers present and in between them an undifferentiated layer called mesoglea is present.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8998,'biology',84,583,1171,'In female frogs.','[{"text": "Ovaries are present inside the kidneys", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovaries are functionally connected with kidneys", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovaries are not connected with kidney functionally", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ovaries and oviducts are present around the digestive system", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The female reproductive organs of frog include a pair of ovaries. The ovaries are situated near kidneys and there is no functional connection with kidneys.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(8999,'biology',86,984,2289,'Neural signal from which centre can reduce the duration of inspiration is (Inspiration inhibition)','[{"text": "Chemosensitive area", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Respiratory rhythm centre", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Receptors associated with aortic arch and carotid artery", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pneumotaxic centre", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Acentre present in the pons regin of the brain called pneumotaxic centre can moderate the functions of the respiratory rhythm centre. Neural signal from this centre can reduce the duration of inspiration and thereby alter the respiratory rate. In human beings, in each breath, inspiration accounts for 2 seconds and expiration for 3 seconds.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9000,'biology',87,1122,2693,'The nature of plasma is ____ constituting nearly ____ percent of the blood.','[{"text": "Straw coloured, viscous fluid, 90", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red coloured, viscous fluid, 90", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Straw coloured, viscous fluid, 55", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Red coloured, viscous fluid, 55", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Plasma is a straw coloured, viscous fluid constituting nearly $55 \\%$ of the blood.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9001,'biology',83,492,1008,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In ctenoplana, digestion is chiefly extracellular.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Digestive tract is incomplete in ctenophores.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason  are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Digestive tract in ctenophores consists of mouth, pharynx or stomodaeum, stomach or infundibulum, anal canals and two anal pores. Since there are mouth and anal pores present, the digestive tract is complete. Thus, digestion is both extracellular and intracellular.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9002,'biology',84,583,1171,'Select the correct answer about the frog<br>I. A mature female can lay 250 to 300 ova at a time.<br>II. Fertilisation is internal.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'None of the given statements are correct. A mature female frog can lay 2500 to 3000 ova at a time. Fertilisation is external and takes place in water.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9003,'biology',86,984,2289,'Pneumotaxic centre of the brain, i.e. pons region can','[{"text": "Moderate the function of respiratory system directly", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decrease the heart rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase the heart rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Moderate the function of respiratory rhythm centre", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Respiratory centre present in the pons region of the brain is called pneumotaxic centre. It can moderate the functions of respiratory rhythm centre.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
