(9027,'biology',86,984,2289,'An area situated adjacent to the respiration rhythm centre is highly sensitive to','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrogen ions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and Hydrogen ions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oxygen only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A chemosensitive area is situated adjacent to the rhythm centre which is highly sensitive to $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and hydrogen ions. Increase in these substances can activate this centre, which in turn can signal the rhythm centre to make necessary adjustments in the respiratory process by which these substances can be eliminated.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9028,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Plasma<br>B. Water<br>C. Proteins<br>D. Formed elements</div><div class="column-right">P. 90-92% of plasma<br>Q. 6-8% of plasma<br>R. Nearly 55% of the blood<br>S. 45% of the blood</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Plasma - Nearly $$55 \\%$$ of blood Water $$-90-92 \\%$$ of plasma Proteins $$-6-8 \\%$$ of plasma Formed elements $$-45 \\%$$ of the blood.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9029,'biology',83,500,1017,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Branchiostoma belong to sub phylum cephalochordata.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Notochord extends from head to tail region and is persistent throughout their life.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason  are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When notochord extends from head to tail region and is persistent throughout their life, organism belongs to subphylum Cephalochordata. Examples are Branchiostoma.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9031,'biology',86,984,2289,'The area found adjacent to the rhythm centre in the brain is highly sensitive to the increased concentration of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and hydrogen ions is ____ in nature','[{"text": "Thermosensitive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Barosensitive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Touch sensitive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemosensitive", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The area found adjacent to the rhythm centre in the brain is highly sensitive to the increased concentration of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and Hydrogen ions is chemosensitive in nature.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9032,'biology',87,1122,2693,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Globulins<br>B. Fibrinogen<br>C. Albumin</div><div class="column-right">P. Osmotic balance<br>Q. Involved in defense mechanisms of the body<br>R. Blood coagulation<br></div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Globulins - Involved in defence mechanism of body<br>Fibrinogen - Blood coagulation Albumin - Osmotic balance',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9033,'biology',83,506,1024,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Birds have pneumatic bones .<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> This reduces the body weight for flight.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason  are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pneumatic bones is a flight adaptation acquired by birds. Endoskeleton is fully ossified (bony) and the long bones are hollow with air cavities (pneumatic).',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9034,'biology',84,579,1158,'Which of the following is false about columnar epithelium?<br>i. It is made of tall and slender cells<br>ii. Free surface may have microvilli<br>iii. They are found in stomach and intestine and help in protection <br>iv. Ciliated epithelium is mainly present in hollow structure like bronchioles and fallopian tubes/ oviducts<br>v. They have apical nuclei<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Only v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only i", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only iii and v", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The columnar epithelium is composed of a single layer of tall and slender cells. Their nuclei are located at the base. Free surface may have microvilli. They are found in the lining of stomach and intestine and help in secretion and absorption. If the columnar or cuboidal cells bear cilia on their free surface they are called ciliated epithelium',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9035,'biology',86,984,2289,'A. Increase in $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and hydrogen ions can activate chemosensitive area, which in turn can signal the rhythm centre to make necessary adjustments<br>B. Increase in $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and hydrogen ions can activate rhythm centre, which in turn can signal the chemosensitive area to make necessary adjustments','[{"text": "A is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A chemosensitive area is situated adjacent to the rhythm centre which is highly sensitive to $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and hydrogen ions. Increase in these substances can activate this centre, which in turn can signal the rhythm centre to make necessary adjustments in the respiratory process by which these substances can be eliminated.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9036,'biology',87,1122,2694,'The difference between the RBC of man and frog is','[{"text": "Human RBC have more haemoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Frog mature RBC is enucleated", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Human mature RBC is enucleated", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Human mature RBC have more haemoglobin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mature human RBCs are devoid of nucleus (enucleated) and are biconcave in shape. Frog RBCs are nucleated.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9037,'biology',83,507,1025,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Bats and whales are classified as vertebrates<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Bats and whales have a bony vertebral column','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason  are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bats and whales belong to subphylum Vertebrata. Notochord gets replaced by vertebral column in embryonic stage.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9038,'biology',84,579,1158,'Select the correct option by reading the statements regarding cell junctions.<br>I. Tight junctions help to stop substances from leaking across tissues.<br>II. Adhering junctions provide cementing to keep neighbouring cells together.<br>III. All the cells of the epithelium are held together with little intercellular materials.<br>IV. Gap junctions provide cytoplasmic channels between cells for passage of ions, small molecules and some time big molecules.','[{"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III and IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements regarding cell junction are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(9039,'biology',86,984,2289,'Which of the following gases is quite insignificant for the regulation of respiration rhythm?','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The role of oxygen in the regulation of respiratory rhythm is quite insignificant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9040,'biology',87,1122,2694,'The most abundant cell in human blood are','[{"text": "Neutrophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lymphocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{RBC}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Erythrocytes or red blood cells (RBC) are the most abundant of all the cells in blood.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9053,'biology',83,496,1012,'Metameric segmentation is the characteristic of','[{"text": "Mollusca and chordata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Annelida and arthropoda", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Echinodermata and annelida", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Platyhelminthes and arthropoda", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Metamerism or segmentation is a phenomenon that occurs in annelids and arthropods.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9041,'biology',83,507,1025,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Duck-bill platypus is a mammal.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Platypus lays eggs but bears mammary glands.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason  are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Duck bill platypus is a egg-laying mammal. It bears mammary glands but exhibits oviparity',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9042,'biology',84,579,1158,'Which of the following statements is false about the compound epithelium?<br>I. It consists of several layers of pseudostratified layers.<br>II. It covers the dry surface of the skin, the moist surface of buccal cavity, pharynx, inner lining of ducts of salivary, glands and pancreatic ducts<br>III. It provides protection against chemical and mechanical stresses<br>IV. Being multilayered it has a great role in secretion and absorption','[{"text": "Only IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I and IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Compound epithelium is made of more than one layer (multi-layered) of cells and thus has a limited role in secretion and absorption',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9043,'biology',86,984,2289,'The impulse for voluntary muscles for forced breathing starts in','[{"text": "Medulla oblongata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vagus nerve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cerebellum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cerebal cortex", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The motor cortex within the cerebral cortex of the brain controls voluntary respiration (the ascending respiratory pathway). Voluntary respiration may be overridden by aspects of involuntary respiration, such as chemoreceptor stimulus and hypothalamus stress response. The phrenic nerves, vagus nerves and posterior thoracic nerves are the major nerves involved in respiration. Voluntary respiration is needed to perform higher functions, such as voice control.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9044,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Number of erythrocytes in $$\\mathrm{mm}^{3}$$ of blood are','[{"text": "4.5 to 5 million", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5 to 5.5 million", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5.5 to 6.5 million", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 million", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A healthy adult man has, on an average, 5 millions to 5.5 millions of RBCs $$\\mathrm{mm}^{3}$$ of blood.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9045,'biology',83,492,1008,'Biradial symmetry and lack of Cnidoblasts are the characteristics of:','[{"text": "<i>Hydra</i> and starfish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ctenoplana</i> and <i>Beroe</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Aurelia</i> and <i>Paramecium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Starfish and sea anemone", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Ctenoplana</i> and <i>Beroe</i> belong to phylum Ctenophora. They show biradial symmetry. Cnidoblasts are absent in them.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9046,'biology',84,579,1158,'Which of the following is incorrect with respect to endocrine glands?','[{"text": "They produce secretions called hormones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These glands do have ducts", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adrenals is an example of endocrine glands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endocrine glands are under the direct or indirect control of the hypothalamus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Endocrine glands do not have ducts. Their products called hormones are secreted directly into the fluid bathing the gland.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9047,'biology',86,985,2290,'Lungs are not affected by the disease','[{"text": "Pneumonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polio", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bronchitis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Asthma", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Polio affects lower limbs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9048,'biology',87,1122,2694,'A healthy individual has ____ gms of haemoglobin in every____ ml of blood','[{"text": "$$12-16,1000$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$2-6,100$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$12-16,100$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$12-16,10000$$<br>gms of $$\\\\mathrm{ml}$$ of blood", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A healthy individual has $$12-16$$ gms of haemoglobin in every $$100 \\mathrm{ml}$$ of blood',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9049,'biology',83,496,1012,'Open blood vascular system without haemoglobin is found in:','[{"text": "Nereis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydra", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cockroach", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Earthworm", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In cockroach the circulatory system is open. Hemolymph is present which is devoid of hemoglobin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9050,'biology',84,579,1158,'Commonly found cell type in the epithelial lining of intestine, urinary tract and respiratory tract is a goblet cell. It is a','[{"text": "Supportive cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretory unicellular gland", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mitogenic cell capable of producing other cell types", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Modified columnar epithelial cell with unknown functions", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Commonly found cell type in the epithelial lining of intestine, urinary tract and respiratory tract is a goblet cell. It is a secretory unicellular gland.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9051,'biology',86,985,2290,'Which one of the following organs in the human body is most affected due to shortage of oxygen?','[{"text": "Intestine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Skin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brain", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The brain represents just $$2 \\%$$ of body weight, yet it uses about $$20 \\%$$ of the body\'s oxygen supply. Without it, the brain can\'t perform even the most basic functions. The brain relies on glucose to power neurons that control everything from conscious functions like planning and thought to automatic unconscious processes like heart rate and digestion. Without oxygen, the brain\'s cells cannot metabolise glucose, and therefore cannot convert glucose into energy. When your brain is deprived of oxygen, then, the ultimate cause of brain death is inadequate energy to power the brain\'s cells',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9052,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Pulmonary vein is rich in','[{"text": "Oxygen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Carbon dioxide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haemoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number of RBC", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The deoxygenated blood pumped into the pulmonary artery is passed on to the lungs from where the oxygenated blood is carried by the pulmonary veins into the left atrium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9054,'biology',84,579,1159,'How many of the following statements are related to bone?<br>i. It is a specialized connective tissue having hard and pliable ground substance rich in calcium salts and collagen fibres which give bone its strength.<br>ii. It is the main tissue that provides structural frame to the body<br>iii. It supports and protects softer tissues and organs<br>iv. The bone cells, osteocytes are present in the spaces called lacunae.<br>v. They also interact with smooth muscles attached to them to bring about movements','[{"text": "Two", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Five", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bone is a specialized connective tissue having hard and non-pliable ground substance rich in calcium salts and collagen fibres which give bone its strength. They also interact with skeletal muscles attached to them to bring about movements.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9055,'biology',86,985,2290,'Asthma is respiratory disease caused due to','[{"text": "Infection of trachea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Infection of lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bleeding into pleural cavity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spasm in bronchi and bronchioles", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Broncho spasms appear as the feature of asthma, chronic bronchitis and anaphylaxis. Bronchospasms are a possible side effect of some drugs: pilocarpine When a person has an asthma attack, a Bronchospasm occurs. This narrows the bronchus diameter and causes the mucosa to swell and inflame. The bronchial glands secrete a massive amount of sticky mucus that is often difficult to dislodge. The mucus is an irritant that plugs the bronchus, adding to the obstruction of the normal flow of air, and giving rise to uncontrollable coughing.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9056,'biology',87,1122,2694,'The true statement about RBC is','[{"text": "RBCs have an average life span of 120 days.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RBCs are destroyed in the spleen (graveyard of RBCs).", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RBCs are biconcave in shape", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'RBCs are devoid of nucleus in most of the mammals and are biconcave in shape. RBCs have an average life span of 120 days after which they are destroyed in the spleen (graveyard of RBCs).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9057,'biology',83,496,1012,'Two common characters found in centipede, cockroach and crab are:','[{"text": "Book lungs and antennae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green gland and trachea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Compound eyes and anal cerci", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Jointed legs and chitinous exoskeleton", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Centipede, Cockroach and Crab are arthropods having jointed legs and chitinous exoskeleton.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9058,'biology',86,985,2290,'Which of the following is an allergic respiratory disorder?','[{"text": "Asthma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Emphysema", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaphyllaxis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cystic fibrosis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Asthma is a difficulty in breathing causing wheezing due to inflammation of bronchi and bronchioles. It is an allergic respiratory disorder.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9059,'biology',84,579,1161,'Identify the wrong statement among the given statements','[{"text": "Neurons are responsible for conduction of nerve impulse.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nephrons, the unit of neural system are excitable cells.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Skeletal muscles are attached to bones.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neuroglia make up more than onehalf the volume of neural tissue in our body", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Each kidney of frog is composed of several structural and functional units called uriniferous tubules or nephrons. Neurons, the unit of neural system are excitable cells.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9060,'biology',83,497,1013,'Which one of the following is a matching set of a phylum and its three examples?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Mollusca - <i>Loligo, Teredo, Octopus</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cnidaria - <i>Bonellia, Physalia, Aurelia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Porifera - <i>Spongilla, Euplectella, Pennatula</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Platyhelminthes -<i>Planaria, Schistosoma, Enterobius</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Loligo, Teredo</i> and <i>Octopus</i> belong to phylum Mollusca.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9061,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Leucocytes are known as WBC as they are colourless due to','[{"text": "Presence of nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "White pigment present in them", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lack of haemoglobin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Leucocytes are also known as white blood cells (WBC) as they are colourless due to the lack of haemoglobin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9062,'biology',84,579,1161,'Identify the correct option by reading the correct statement<br>I. Striated muscle fibres are bundled together in a parallel fashion.<br>II. Neuroglial cells protect and support the neurons.<br>III. Biceps are involuntary and striated.<br>IV. Skeletal muscle tissue is closely attached to skeletal bones.','[{"text": "Statement I and IV are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I, II and IV are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement I, II and III are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I, III and IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Biceps are voluntary and striated.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9063,'biology',86,985,2290,'"Emphysema" is a condition in which','[{"text": "Respiratory centre inhibited", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lot of fluid in the lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The walls separating the alveoli break", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lungs have more $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Emphysema is a type of COPD (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease) involving damage to the air sacs (alveoli) in the lungs. As a result, your body does not get the oxygen it needs. Emphysema makes it hard to catch your breath. You may also have a chronic cough and have trouble breathing during exercise. The most common cause is cigarette smoking',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9064,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Leucocytes are nucleated and are relatively lesser in number which averages ____ $$\\mathrm{mm}^{3}$$ of blood.','[{"text": "$$600-800$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$60000-80000$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$6000-8000$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$6000-80000$$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Leucocytes are nucleated and are relatively lesser in number which averages 6000-8000 $$\\mathrm{mm}^{3}$$ of blood.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9503,'biology',88,1151,2758,'The structures from which the collecting duct receives the filtrate','[{"text": "PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DCT", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Henle\'s loop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Efferent arteriole", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The DCTs of many nephrons open into a straight tube called collecting duct. The collecting duct hence receives the filtrate from DCTs of a group of nephrons in the kidney.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9065,'biology',83,495,1011,'Earthworms are:','[{"text": "Ammonotelic when plenty of water is present", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Uricotelic under conditions of water scarcity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uricotelic when plenty of water is available", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ureotelic when plenty of water is available", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The presence of ammonia in blood is toxic, hence requires plenty of water for rapid elimination.Earthworms when kept in moist environment produce urea instead of ammonia however, if they are kept immersed in water then they tend to produce ammonia as an excretory product.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9066,'biology',86,985,2290,'Which of the following symptoms is incorrect regarding emphysema?','[{"text": "Surface area of gas exchange decreases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Loss of elasticity in the walls of alveolar sacs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alveolar septa collapse", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Regular coughing with thick greenish yellow sputum", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Emphysema is a chronic disorder in which alveolar walls are damaged i.e. alveolar septa collapses, due to which respiratory surface is decreased. One of the major causes of this is cigarette smoking.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9068,'biology',83,497,1013,'Which of the following pairs is mismatched:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "<i>Kenia laca</i> - Lac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Bombyx mori</i>\\n- Silk", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pila globosa</i>\\n- Pearl", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Apis indica</i>\\n- Honey", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pearl is formed by bivalves like mussel.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9069,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Basophil secrete','[{"text": "Histamine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Serotonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heparin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Basophils secrete histamine, serotonin, heparin, etc., and are involved in inflammatory reactions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9071,'biology',86,985,2290,'Which of the following statement are false with respect to "Emphysema"','[{"text": "Emphysema means \\"full of air\\" or \\"inflation\\"", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Emphysema is a chronic disorder due to cigarette smoking.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The surface area of alveoli decreases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'None of the given option is incorrect. Emphysema is a chronic disorder in which alveolar walls are damaged i.e. alveolar septa collapses, due to which respiratory surface is decreased. One of the major causes of this is cigarette smoking.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9072,'biology',83,497,1013,'Which one of the following is a matching pair of a body feature and the animal possessing it<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Pharyngeal gill slits - <em>Chameleon</em> absent in embryo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ventral heart - Scorpion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Post anal tail - <em>Octopus</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ventral central - Leech nervous system", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In Leech the entire central nervous system is enclosed within the ventral haemocoelomic channel.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9073,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Which of the following is associated with allergic reactions?','[{"text": "Neutrophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eosinophils", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Leucocyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lymphocytes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Eosinophils (2-3 percent) resist infections and are also associated with allergic reactions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9075,'biology',86,985,2290,'Occupational respiratory disorders can be prevented by','[{"text": "Wearing protective masks", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Avoid areas with increased levels dust and smoke areas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 an 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Shifting to areas with increased levels dust and smoke areas", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Occupational respiratory disorders can be prevented by wearing protective mask and avoiding areas with increased levels dust and smoke areas.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9076,'biology',83,495,1011,'Which one of the following is not a characteristic of phylum Annelida?','[{"text": "Segmentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pseudocoelom", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ventral nerve chord", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Closed circulatory system", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Annelids are coelomates having a true coelom.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9078,'biology',86,985,2290,'In occupational respiratory disorders long exposure can give rise to','[{"text": "Inflammation leading to fibrosis-proliferation of fibrous tissues", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inflammation leading to cyanosis-proliferation of fibrous tissues", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inflammation leading to fibrosis-proliferation of elastic tissues", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inflammation leading to fibrosis-degeneration of fibrous tissues", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In certain industries, especially those involving grinding or stone-breaking, so much dust is produced that the defense mechanism of the body cannot fully cope with the situation. Long exposure can give rise to inflammation leading to fibrosis (proliferation of fibrous tissues) and thus causing serious lung damage. Workers in such industries should wear protective masks.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9080,'biology',83,495,1011,'Earthworms have no skeleton but during burrowing the anterior end becomes turgid and acts as a hydraulic skeleton. It is due to:','[{"text": "Setae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coelomic fluid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gut peristalsis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'An earthworm does not have a skeleton. It has bristles on each segment called setae that help the earthworm move. Earthworms have rings of muscles that are filled with fluid, making their entire body hydrostatic.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9081,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Identify the correct percent of WBCs?','[{"text": "Neutrophils - 60-65 percent", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Basophils - 00.5-1 percent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monocytes - 60-80 percent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Neutrophils are the most abundant cells (60-65 per cent) of the total WBCs and basophils are the least (5-20 per cent) among them. and monocytes (6-8 per cent)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9083,'biology',86,985,2290,'Match the column:<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Asthma<br>B. Emphysema<br>C. Occupational respiratory disorders</div><div class="column-right">P. Inflammation of bronchi and bronchioles<br>Q. Chronic disorder in which alveolar walls are damaged due to which respiratory surface is decreased.<br>R. Long exposure of chemicals can give rise to inflammation leading to fibrosis (proliferation of fibrous tissues).</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - P, B - Q, C - R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q, B - P, C - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R, B - P, C - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R, B - Q, C - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Asthma - Inflammation of bronchi and bronchioles<br>Emphysema - chronic disorder in which alveolar walls are damaged due to which respiratory surface is decreased<BR>Occupational respiratory disorder - Long exposure can give rise to inflammation leading to fibrosis (proliferation of fibrous tissues).',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9084,'biology',83,494,1010,'<i>Ascaris</i> is characterised by','[{"text": "Presence of true coelom and metamerism (metamerisation)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of neither true coelom nor metamerism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Absence of true coelom but presence of metamerism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of true coelom but absence of metamerism", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ascaris does not have a true coelom as it is pseudocoelomate and metamerism is also absent.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9085,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Which of the following cells are responsible for immune responses of the body?','[{"text": "T-lymphocyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B-lymphocyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neutrophils", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lymphocytes are of two major types - \'B\' and \' $$\\mathrm{T}$$ \' forms. Both $$\\mathrm{B}$$ and $$\\mathrm{T}$$ lymphocytes are responsible for immune responses of the body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9087,'biology',86,981,2286,'Study the spirogram shown below and choose the option that correctly gives the inspiratory reserve volume (IRV), inspiratory capacity (IC), vital capacity (VC) and functional residual capacity (FRC).<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {{\\\\rm{IRV - 2}}{\\\\rm{.5L,}}}&amp;{{\\\\rm{IC - 3L,}}\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{{\\\\rm{VC - 5L,}}}&amp;{{\\\\rm{FRC - 3L}}} \\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {{\\\\rm{IRV - 3L,}}\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{{\\\\rm{IC - 2}}{\\\\rm{.5L,}}}&amp;{{\\\\rm{VC - 5L,}}}&amp;{{\\\\rm{FRC - 3L}}} \\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {{\\\\rm{IRV - 2}}{\\\\rm{.5L,}}}&amp;{{\\\\rm{IC - 3L,}}\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{{\\\\rm{VC - 4L,}}}&amp;{{\\\\rm{FRC}}} \\\\end{array}{\\\\rm{ - 2L}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {{\\\\rm{IRV - 2}}{\\\\rm{.5L,}}}&amp;{{\\\\rm{IC - 3L,}}\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{{\\\\rm{VC - 6L,}}}&amp;{{\\\\rm{FRC - 3L}}} \\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'As per the given spirogram:&lt;br&gt; IRV &minus; 2.5L, IC &minus; 3L, VC &minus; 5L, FRC &minus; 3L&lt;br&gt; &nbsp; <img src=\'/img/data/biology/86_9087_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;',NULL,'Hard','Graph/Figure',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/86_9087_question_1.png'),
(9088,'biology',83,494,1010,'Which one of the following groups of animals is bilaterally symmetrical and triploblastic?','[{"text": "Sponges", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ctenophores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coelenterates (Cnidarians)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aschelminthes (round worms)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The body of nematodes is bilaterally symmetrical and triploblastic. Sponges have no true tissue or loose tissue organization. Body is asymmetrical or radially symmetrical. Ctenophores and Cnidarian body is Diploblastic i.e. have two layers: gastrodermis(derived from endoderm) and epidermis (derived from ectoderm) and show Radial symmetry.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9089,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Capacity of leucocytes to digest foreign matter is known as','[{"text": "Leucopenia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diapedesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phagocytosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Leukemia", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Neutrophils and monocytes are phagocytic cells which destroy foreign organisms entering the body.Phagocytosis is the capacity of leucocytes to digest foreign matter.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9091,'biology',86,979,2284,'Mark the correct statement','[{"text": "Tracheal rings are of hyaline cartilage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ventral side of thoracic chamber is formed by sternum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Expiration occurs when there is positive pressure in lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of these are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9092,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which one of the following statements about all the four of <i>Spongilla</i>, Leech, Dolphin and Penguin is correct?','[{"text": "Spongilla has special collared cells choanocytes, not found in the remaining three.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Penguin is homoeothermic while the remaining three are poikilothermic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leech is a freshwater form while all others are marine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are bilaterally symmetrical", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Spongilla</i> has special collared cells choanocytes, not found in the remaining three.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
