(9095,'biology',86,983,2288,'Read the following statements :-<br>I. High $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$concentration and higher temperature are favourable for dissociation of oxygen from oxyhaemoglobin<br>II. Partial pressure of oxygen in alveoli is higher than in tissue<BR>III. The maximum volume of air a person can breathe in, after a forced expiration is vital capacity<br>IV. In alveoli low $$\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ and high $$\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ are the factors for dissociation of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ from carbaminohaemoglobin<br>How many statements are correct?','[{"text": "One", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'All the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9096,'biology',83,493,1009,'Which one of the following kinds of animals are triploblastic?','[{"text": "Corals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sponges", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ctenophores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flatworms", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Flatworms are triploblastic animals belonging to phylum Platyhelminthes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9097,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Find the correct descending order to the percentage proportion of leucocytes in human blood.','[{"text": "Eosinophils $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Basophils $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Lymphocytes $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Neutrophils $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Monocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neutrophils $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Monocytes $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Lymphocytes $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Eosinophils $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Basophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neutrophils $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Lymphocytes $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Monocytes $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Eosinophils $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Basophils", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lymphocytes $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Eosinophils $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Basophils $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Neutrophils $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Monocytes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Of the total WBCs<br>Neutrophils are 60-65 percent,<BR>Lymphocytes are 20-25 percent,<BR>monocytes are 6-8 percent,<br>Eosinophils are 2-3 percent,<BR>Basophils are 0.5-1 percent.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9099,'biology',86,981,2286,'Listed below are the lung volumes of a healthy adult woman. Tidal volume- $$500 \\mathrm{~mL}$$<br>Inspiratory reserve volume $$-2,000 \\mathrm{~mL}$$<br>Expiratory reserve volume $$-700 \\mathrm{~mL}$$<br>Residual volume $$-1,100 \\mathrm{~mL}$$<br>Which one of the following is the correct matching of two lung capacities in that person?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Inspiratory capacity $$-2,500 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$<br>Expiratory capacity $$-1,800 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Functional residual capacity $$-2,300 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$<br>Vital capacity $$-3,200 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Total lung capacity $$-3,200 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$<br>Functional residual - 1,800 mL capacity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vital capacity $$-3,200 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$<br>Total lung capacity $$-4,300 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{TV = 500\\,mL; IRV = 2,000}}\\,{\\rm{mL}}$,<br>${\\rm{ERV = 700\\,mL;RV = 1,100\\,mL}}$<br>${\\rm{IC = TV + IRV = 500 + 2,000 = 2,500\\,mL}}$<br>${\\rm{EC = TV + ERV = 500 + 700 = 1,200\\,mL}}$<br>${\\rm{FRC = ERV + RV = 700 + 1,100 = 1,800\\,mL}}$<br>${\\rm{VC = IRV + TV + ERV = 2,000 + 500 + 700 = }}$<br>$\\,{\\rm{3,200}}\\,{\\rm{mL}}$<br>${\\rm{TLC = VC + RV = 3200 + 1100 = 4,300}}\\,{\\rm{mL}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9100,'biology',83,500,1017,'One example of animals having a single opening to the outside that serves both mouth as well as anus is:','[{"text": "Octopus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Asterias</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Fasciola</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Ascidia</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In <i>Fasciola</i>, the alimentary canal is incomplete. It has a single mouth which leads into the blind gut; it has no anus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9101,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Platelets are','[{"text": "Cell fragments of megakaryocyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cell fragments of microkaryocyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell fragments of thrombocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell fragments of lymphocyte", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Platelets also called thrombocytes, are cell fragments produced from megakaryocytes (special cells in the bone marrow).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9102,'biology',86,979,2284,'Which of the following statement is false?','[{"text": "Exchange part of the respiratory system is the actual site at which $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ exchange takes place", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Conducting part of the respiratory system clears the air from foreign particles, humidifies and brings it to the body temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The conducting part of the respiratory system transports the atmospheric air to alveoli", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
