(9105,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Platelets count is','[{"text": "$$4000-8000 / \\\\mathrm{mm}^{3}$$ in blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.5 to $$3.5 \\\\mathrm{lac} / \\\\mathrm{mm}^{3}$$ in blood", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3.5 to 5.5 thousand $$/ \\\\mathrm{mm}^{3}$$ in blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.5 to $$3.5 \\\\mathrm{millions} / \\\\mathrm{mm}^{3}$$ in blood", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Blood normally contains $$1,500,00$$ $$3,500,00$$ platelets $$\\mathrm{mm}^{3}$$.i.e. 1.5 to $$3.5 \\mathrm{lac} / \\mathrm{mm}^{3}$$ in blood.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9106,'biology',86,979,2284,'Which of the following is incorrect about human lungs?','[{"text": "The pleural fluid lubricates the surface of the lungs and prevents friction between the membranes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Right lung has 3 lobes and left lung has 2 lobes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lungs are covered by outer parietal pleura and inner visceral pleura", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Situated in thoracic chamber and rest below diaphragm", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The lungs are situated in the thoracic chamber and rest above diaphragm which is anatomically an air-tight chamber.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9108,'biology',83,507,1025,'In which of the following the genus name, its two characters and its class/phylum are correctly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Genus name: <i>Aurelia</i><br>Two characters :<br>i) Cnidoblast<br>ii) Organ level of organisation<br>Class/Phylum : Coelenterata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus name :<i>Ascaris</i><br>Two characters :<br>i) Body segmented<br>ii) Males and females distinct<br>Class/Phylum Annelida", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus name : <i>Salamandra</i><br>Two characters :<br>i) A tympanum represents ear<br>ii) Fertilisation is external<br>Class/Phylum : Amphibia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genus name :<i>Pteropus</i><br>Two characters :<br>i) Skin possess hair<br>ii) Oviparous<br>Class/Phylum : Mammalia", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<i>Salamandra</i> is a tailed amphibian. It has a tymphanum which represents ear.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9176,'biology',83,506,1024,'Which one of the following organisms bears hollow and pneumatic long bones?','[{"text": "Neophron", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hemidactylus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Macropus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ornithorhynuchus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Birds have hollow bones. These bones make birds light-weighted which works in their favour while flying. Among the given options, only Neophron is a bird',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9109,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Identify the different types of cells $$(A-C)$$ in the given diagram?','[{"text": "A- Platelets, B- Eosinophil, C- Red Blood Cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Eosinophil, B- Red Blood Cells, C- Platelets", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Red Blood Cells, B- Platelets, C- Eosinophil", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A- Platelets, B- Red Blood Cells, C- Eosinophil", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Given diagram depicts : A-Red Blood Cells, B- Platelets, C-Eosinophil',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/87_9109_question_1.png'),
(9110,'biology',86,980,2285,'Read the following steps of inspiration.<br>i. Increases thoracic volume<br>ii. air move into lungs<br>iii. contraction in diaphragm and EICM<br>iv. Increases pulmonary volume<br>v. Lungs expand<br>vi. decreases the intra pulmonary pressure (IPP)<br>Find out the correct sequence of these steps.','[{"text": "iii, v, iv, i, vi, ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii, iv, i, v, vi, ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii, i, v, iv, vi, ii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv, v, vi", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Inspiration is initiated by contraction of diaphragm and external inter- costal muscles raising the ribs and chest bone upward and forwards increasing the dorsoventral dimension of the chest cavity. Both these actions increase the volume of thoracic cavity which in turn increases the Intrapleural volume. Lungs expands and increase in pulmonary volume leads to decreases the intra pulmonary pressure. As a result air rushes in from the region of higher pressure to the region of lower pressure until the air pressure in the lungs equals to the atmospheric pressure',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9112,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which one of the following organisms is scientifically or correctly named, correctly printed according to the International Rules of Nomenclature and correctly described?','[{"text": "<i>Musca domestica</i> - the common house lizard, a reptile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Plasmodium falciparum</i> - A protozoan pathogen causing serious type of malaria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Felis tigris</i> - the Indian tiger, well protected in Gir forests", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>E. coli</i> - full name Entamoeba coli, a commonly occurring bacterium in human intestine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Plasmodium falciparum</i> causes malaria. Musca domestica is the house fly, <i>E.coli is Escherichia coli</i> and Indian tiger is <i>Panthera tigris</i>.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9113,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Identify the most abundant cells of the total WBCs in the given diagram?','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Given diagram depicts : 1-Red Blood Cells, 2-Platelets, 3-Eosinophil where RBCs are most abundant cells in human blood.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/87_9113_question_1.png'),
(9115,'biology',86,985,2290,'Which one of the following is the correct statement regarding the process of respiration in humans?','[{"text": "Workers in grinding and stone breaking industries may suffer from lung fibrosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "about $$90 \\\\%$$ of $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is carried out by haemoglobin as carbomino -haemoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cigarette smoking may lead to inflammation of nasopharynx", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neural signals from the pneumotoxic centre in the pons region of the brain can increase the duration of inspiration", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$$23 \\%$$ of carbon dioxide is transported as carbaminohaemoglobin. Cigarette smoking leads to Emphysema. Neural signal from pneumotoxic centre in the pons region of the brain will reduce rate of respiration and respiratory rate. Lung fibrosis is an occupational respiratory disorder where due to continuous exposure to certain particles there is inflammation of lungs.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
