(9123,'biology',86,983,2288,'Read the following statement and identify the correct option<br>I. Thoracic activity is anatomically an air tight chamber<br>II. Healthy man can inspire approximately $$500 \\mathrm{ml}$$ of air per minute<br>III. The contraction of internal intercoastal muscles lifts up the ribs and sternum<br>IV. RBC transport oxygen only','[{"text": "Statement II and IV are correct while statement I and III are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement II and III are correct while statement I and IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement II is correct while statement I, III and IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I is correct while statement II, III and IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$$\\mathrm{RBC}$$ transports both $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2} \\cdot 97 \\%$$ $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ is transported by RBC. $$20-25 \\% \\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is transported by RBC. Contraction of external intercoastal muscle will lift ribs and sternum. A healthy man can inspire or expire approximately ${\\rm{6000}}$ to $$8000 \\mathrm{~mL}$$ of air per minute.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
