(9147,'biology',86,983,2288,'An increase in ____ (1) ____ in the blood causes an increase in ____(2)____, leading to an ____ (3)____ in breathing rate.<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{{\\rm{a}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}&{{\\rm{b}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}&{\\rm{c}}\n\\end{array}$','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}}&{{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}}&{{\\\\rm{decrease }}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{pH}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{increase}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{increase}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{increase}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ combines with $$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$$ to form $$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{CO}_{3}$$ which dissociates into $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$and $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}$$. Chemoreceptors detect elevated $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ levels and activate respiratory rhythm centre. Rapid and deep breathing (hyperventilation) occurs to exhale more $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ until $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$are lowered to normal level.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9148,'biology',83,490,1006,'In case of poriferans, the spongocoel is lined with flagellated cells called:','[{"text": "Oscula", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Choanocytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mesenchymal cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ostia", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Choanocytes or the collar cells are flagellated cells which line the spongocoel and canals in the poriferans.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9149,'biology',87,1123,2695,'$$\\mathrm{ABO}$$ grouping is based on how many antigens present or absent on RBCs','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$$\\mathrm{ABO}$$ grouping is based on the presence or absence of two surface antigens (chemicals that can induce immune response) on the RBCs namely $$\\mathrm{A}$$ and $$\\mathrm{B}$$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9151,'biology',86,983,2288,'Select the correct statement about oxygen transport in blood','[{"text": "During acidosis, haemoglobin is able to carry oxygen more efficiently", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Foetal haemoglobin has higher affinity for oxygen in comparison to maternal haemoglobin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "During normal activity, a molecule of haemoglobin returning to the lungs carries one molecule of oxygen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increased BPG levels in the red blood $$\\\\backslash$$ cell enhance oxygen carrying capacity of blood.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During acidosis, i.e., acidic condition there will be dissociation of oxyhaemoglobin. One haemoglobin carries 4 oxygen molecules. Increased levels of BPG will reduce oxygen carrying capacity of blood. Foetal',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9152,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which among these is the correct combination of aquatic mammals?','[{"text": "Dolphins, Seals, Trygon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Whales, Dolphins, Seals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Trygon, Whales, Seals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seals, Dolphins, Sharks", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Aquatic mammals include dolphin, Seal and whales. Dolphin and whales come under Order Cetacea of class Mammalia. Cetacea is the order for aquatic mammals. Seal is a aquatic mammal of order Carnivora.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9153,'biology',87,1123,2695,'A person with antigen $$B$$ in $$\\mathrm{RBC}$$ and antibody A in plasma','[{"text": "Belongs to blood group $$\\\\mathrm{A}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Belongs to blood group $$\\\\mathrm{B}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Belongs to blood group $$\\\\mathrm{O}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Belongs to blood group $$\\\\mathrm{AB}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A person with antigen B in RBC and antibody A in plasma belongs to blood group B.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9155,'biology',86,983,2288,'Which of the following factors are favourable for the formation of oxyhaemoglobin?<br>i. High $$\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$<br>ii. Lesser $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$concentration and lower temperature<br>iii. Higher $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$concentration and higher temperature<br>iv. High $$\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$','[{"text": "i, ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Formation of oxyhaemoglobin is favourable when there is high partial pressure of oxygen $$\\left(\\mathrm{PO}_{2}\\right)$$, lower concentration of $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$ ions and a high temperature',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9156,'biology',83,499,1015,'An important characteristic that hemichordates share with chordates is','[{"text": "Ventral tubular nerve cord", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pharynx with gill slits", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pharynx without gill slits", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Absence of notochord", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Hemichordata are soft-bodied, wormlike marine organisms which are often found in U shaped burrows on sandy or muddy sea bottoms and any animal that has a spinal cord is a chordate Both chordates, and hemichordates are deuterostomes with pharyngeal gill slits and most have a dorsal (and sometimeshollow) nerve cord',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9157,'biology',87,1123,2695,'A patient with blood group \' $$A B$$ \' needs blood for his surgery. Which blood group the doctor should effectively use in this case?','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{AB}$$ only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{B} / \\\\mathrm{O}$$ only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{A} / \\\\mathrm{O}$$ only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{AB} / \\\\mathrm{A} / \\\\mathrm{B}$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'AB is universal recipient.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10203,'biology',9,24,44,'The algae which possess chlorophyll a, c, belong to','[{"text": "Green algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brown algae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red algae", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Brown algae possess chlorophyll a, c, carotenoids and xanthophylls.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9159,'biology',86,981,2286,'Identify the correct and incorrect match about respiratory volumes and capacities and mark the correct answer.<br>i. Inspiratory capacity \\[{\\rm{(IC) }}\\] $$=\\mathrm{TV}+\\mathrm{RV}$$<br>ii. Vital capacity \\[{\\rm{(V}}{\\rm{.C}}{\\rm{.)}}\\] $$=\\mathrm{TV}+\\mathrm{IRV}+\\mathrm{ERV}$$<br>iii. Residual volume \\[{\\rm{(R}}{\\rm{.V}}{\\rm{.)}}\\] $$=\\mathrm{VC}-\\mathrm{IRV}$$<br>iv. Tidal volume \\[{\\rm{(TV)}}\\] \\[{\\rm{ =  IC  -  IRV}}\\]<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "i, iii incorrect and ii and iv correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii, iii incorrect and iv correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iv correct and iii incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii correct and ii, iv incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Inspiratory capacity is the total volume of air a person can inspire after normal expiration. Therefore Inspiratory capacity $$=$$ $$\\mathrm{TV}+$$ ${\\rm{IRV}}$ Residual volume $$=$$ Volume of air that remains in lungs even after forcible expiration.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9160,'biology',87,1123,2695,'Blood group $$\\mathrm{O}$$ can be given to people with blood group','[{"text": "B and AB blood group", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AB", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "O and AB blood group", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of them $$\\mathrm{O}$$ is universal donor.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9161,'biology',83,500,1017,'Which of the following animals do not undergo metamorphosis?','[{"text": "Moth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tunicate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Earthworm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Starfish", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Metamorphosis is transformation of larva into adult. Animal that perform metamorphosis are said to have indirect development. In earthworm there is no larval stages, development is direct and metamorphosis is direct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9163,'biology',86,984,2289,'Spontaneous respiration ceases after transection of the','[{"text": "Brainstem above the pons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spinal cord below the diaphragm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brainstem at the inferior end of the medulla", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Spinal cord above the conus medullaris", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Respiratory centres are present in medulla oblongata (respiratory rhythm centre) and pons (pneumotaxic centre and apneustic centre). If brain is transected (cut across) below the medulla oblongata, impulses from the respiratory centre cannot reach the respiratory muscles.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9164,'biology',83,506,1024,'Identify the vertebrate group of animals characterized by crop and gizzard in its digestive system','[{"text": "Aves", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Reptilia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphibia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osteichthyes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Digestive tract of birds has additional chambers called crop and gizzard. Crop stores food and softens it. Gizzard crushes it.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9165,'biology',87,1123,2695,'How many people are $$\\mathrm{Rh}+$$ ve in human population?','[{"text": "$$80 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$50 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$60 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$100 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The $$\\mathrm{Rh}$$ antigen similar to one present in Rhesus monkeys (hence Rh), is observed on the surface of RBCs of majority (nearly 80 per cent) of humans.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9177,'biology',87,1123,2695,'Erythroblastosis fetalis is','[{"text": "Hemolytic disease of newborn", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rh incompatibility", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Erythroblastosis fetalis is a special case of $$\\mathrm{Rh}$$ incompatibility (mismatching) has been observed between the Rh-ve blood of a pregnant mother with $$\\mathrm{Rh}+\\mathrm{ve}$$ blood of the foetus causing hemolytic disease of newborn.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10204,'biology',88,1157,2764,'What kind of a gland is liver?','[{"text": "Endocrine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Exocrine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterocrine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Liver, the largest exocrine gland in our body, as it has ducts.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9167,'biology',86,985,2290,'Which of the following sets of changes is present in a man suffering from chronic pulmonary emphysema, compared with a healthy non-smoker?<BR>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{{\\rm{No}}{\\rm{. of \\,alveoli}}}&{{\\rm{arterial\\, p}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}&{{\\rm{Respiratory}}}\\\\\n{}&{}&{{\\rm{surface}}}\n\\end{array}$','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Decreases}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{increases}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{decreases}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Increases}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{decreases}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{decreases}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Decreases}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{decreases}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{decreases}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Decreases}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{decreases}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{increases}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Emphysema is a chronic disorder in which alveoli become fewer and larger as the alveolar walls are damaged. Respiratory surface is decreased. Hence gas exchange is affected leading to low arterial $$\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9168,'biology',87,1123,2695,'$$\\mathrm{Rh}$$ incompatibility in first pregnancy occurs when','[{"text": "Foetus develop its heart completely", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "During the delivery of first child", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "When foetal organs completely develop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Never occur in the first pregnancy", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During the delivery of the first child, there is a possibility of exposure of the maternal blood to small amounts of the $$\\mathrm{Rh}+\\mathrm{ve}$$ blood from the foetus. In such cases, the mother starts preparing antibodies against $$\\mathrm{Rh}$$ antigen in her blood. In case of her subsequent pregnancies, the $$\\mathrm{Rh}$$ antibodies from the mother<br>( $$\\mathrm{Rh}-\\mathrm{ve})$$ can leak into the blood of the foetus $$(\\mathrm{Rh}+\\mathrm{ve})$$ and destroy the foetal RBCs',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9169,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which one of these animals is not a homeotherm?','[{"text": "<em>Camelus</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Chelone</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<em>Macropus</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Psittacula</em>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<em>Chelone</em> (Turtle) is a reptile and is not a homeotherm. <em>Camelus</em> (Camel), <em>Macropus</em> (Kangaroo) are mammals. <em>Psittacula</em> (Parrot) is a bird. Birds and mammals are homeotherm.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9171,'biology',86,983,2288,'In the oxygen - haemoglobin dissociation curve given below, the shift from curve A to B could be caused by<BR>i. Fall in pH<BR>ii. Increase in carbon dioxide level in blood<BR>iii. Rise in pH<BR>iv. Fall in carbon dioxide level in blood<BR>v. Rise in temperature<BR>vi. Fall in temperature','[{"text": "iii, iv and vi", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii and v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii and vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii, iv and v", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The oxyhaemoglobin dissociation curve shifts right wards due to rise in level of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$, rise in temperature, rise in level of 2,3-diphosphoglycerate and fall in $$\\mathrm{pH}$$. All these factors therefore decreases the oxygen affinity and increase release of oxygen into tissues.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/86_9171_question_1.png'),
(9172,'biology',87,1123,2695,'People having $$\\mathrm{O}$$ blood group are known as?','[{"text": "Universal recipient", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Universal donor", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'From the above mentioned table it is evident that group \' $$\\mathrm{O}$$ \' blood can be donated to persons with any other blood group and hence \'O\' group individuals are called \'universal donors\'',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9173,'biology',83,497,1013,'Match the following organisms with their respective characteristics :<br>Select the correct option from the following :<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">1. <em>Pila</em><br>2. <em>Bombyx</em><br>3. <em>Pleurobrachia</em><br>4.<em>Taenia</em></div><div class="column-right">P. Flame cells<br>Q. Comb plates<br>R. Radula<br>S. Malphigian tubules</div></div>','[{"text": "1-R, 2-Q, 3-P, 4-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-R, 2-S, 3-Q, 4-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1-Q, 2-S, 3-R, 4-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-R, 2-Q, 3-S, 4-P", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<em>Pila</em> is a Mollusc. The mouth contains a file - like rasping organ for feeding called radula.<br><em>Bombyx</em> is an Arthropod. In Bombyx excretion takes place through malpighan tubules.<br><em>Pleurobrachia&nbsp;</em>is Ctenophore. The body bears eight external rows of ciliated comb plates, which help in locomotion.<br><em>Taenia&nbsp;</em>is a platyhelminth specialised cells called flame cells helps in osmoregulation and excretion',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9175,'biology',86,980,2285,'Following diagram depicts the mechanism of breathing. In which of the following options, all the parts A, B, C and D are correctly labelled?','[{"text": "A - Air expelled form lungs<br>B - Ribs and Sternum raised<br>C - Diaphragm contracted<br>D - Volume of thorax decreased", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Air expelled form lungs<br>B - Ribs and Sternum raised<br>C - Diaphragm relaxed<br>D - Volume of thorax decreased", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Air entering into lungs<br>B - Ribs and Sternum raised<br>C - Diaphragm contracted<br>D - Volume of thorax decreased", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Air expelled form lungs<br>B - Ribs and Sternum lowered<BR>C - Diaphragm relaxed and arched upwards<br>D - Volume of thorax decreased", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Air is exhaled out from lungs when the phrenic muscles of diaphragm relax and it returns to its original dome shape. Ribs and sternum are therefore, lowered and the volume of thorax decreases.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/86_9175_question_1.png'),
(9179,'biology',86,979,2283,'Select the correct combination of the animal and its respiratory organ.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Prawn<br>B. Earthworm<br>C. Cockroach<br>D. Scorpio<br>E. Starfish</div><div class="column-right">1. dermal bronchiae<br>2. Tracheae<br>3. Moist skin<br>4. Gills<br>5. Book lungs</div></div>','[{"text": "A- 4, B- 3, C- 2, D- 5, E-1", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A- 3, B- 4, C- 5, D- 2, E-1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- 2, B- 5, C- 4, D- 3, E-1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- 1, B- 2, C- 3, D- 4, E-5", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In prawns, respiration takes place through gills (Branchial respiration).<br>Earthworm respires through moist skin, cockroach uses trachea, Scorpio uses booklungs while starfish uses dermal branchiae.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9180,'biology',83,498,1014,'Read the following statements.<br>I.Metagenesis is observed in Helminths<br>II.Echinoderms are triploblastic and coelomate animals.<br>III.Round worms have organ-system level of body organization<br>IV.Comb plates present in ctenophores help in digestion<br>V.Water vascular system is characteristic of Enhinoderms<br>Choose the correct answer from the options give below.','[{"text": "(III), (IV) and (V) are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I), (II) and (III) are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I), (IV) and (V) are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(II), (III) and (V) are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Metagenesis is observed in coelenterates. Comb plates play a crucial role in locomotion.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9181,'biology',87,1123,2695,'Rh positive mother and $$\\mathrm{Rh}$$ positive father have a child, expect the possibilty of that child?','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{Rh}+$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{Rh}$$ -", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'If a woman who is Rh negative and a man who is Rh positive conceive a baby, the fetus may have Rh-positive blood, inherited from the father. (About half of the children born to an Rh-negative mother and Rh-positive father will be Rh-positive.) It is possible that child may have Rh -ve blood. Rh incompatibility usually isn\'t a problem if it\'s the mother\'s first pregnancy. That\'s because the baby\'s blood does not normally enter the mother\'s circulatory system during the pregnancy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9183,'biology',86,979,2284,'A person suffers from punctures in his chest cavity in an accident, without any damage to the lungs. Its effect could be','[{"text": "Reduce breathing rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No change in breathing rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cessation of breathing", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "First increases then reduced breathing rate", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Punctures in chest cavity causes collapse of lungs resulting in apnoea (cessation of breathing). Breathing occurs due to negative intrapleural prssure created by use of respiratory muscles.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9184,'biology',83,495,1011,'Match Column - I with Column - II.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">a. Metamerism<br>b. Canal system<br>c. Comb plates<br>d. Cnidoblasts</div><div class="column-right">p. Coelenterata<br>q. Ctenophora<br>r. Annelida<br>s. Porifera</div></div>','[{"text": "a - s; b - r; c - p; d - q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a - r; b - s; c - p; d - q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a - r; b - s; c - q; d - p", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a - s; b - p; c - q; d - r", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Metamerism is first seen in annelids in animal kingdom. Each segment usually contains appendages, muscles, nerves, blood vessels, excretory organs and a pair of coelomic sacs which are repeated in almost all segments. In annelids the metameric segmentation is both external and internal. Body of all sponges is the perforated by large number of apertures through which water enters Inside body and flows through a system of criss-crossing canals collectively forming the canal system which is a characteristic feature of poriferans. Comb plates are found in the members of the phylum Ctenophora. Cnidoblasts are the distinctive feature of the phylum Cnidaria. These are present on the body surface and tentacles.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9185,'biology',87,1123,2695,'In case of emergency, which blood group could be safely transfused?','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{AB} \\\\mathrm{Rh}-$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{O} \\\\mathrm{Rh}-$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{AB} \\\\mathrm{Rh}+$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{ORh}+$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In case of emergency, O Rh - ve blood group could be safely transfused.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9735,'biology',88,1151,2758,'The two U shaped structures in the kidney are','[{"text": "Vasa recta and loop of Henle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Afferent arteriole and loop of Henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Efferent arteriole and loop of Henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peritubular network and Bowman\'s capsule", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The two U-shaped structures in the kidney are Peritubular network/ Vasa recta and loop of Henle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9187,'biology',86,979,2284,'Read the following statements. Which of the following are correct?<br>I. Lungs are covered with three-layered membrane called pleura.<br>II. Right primary bronchus divides into secondary bronchi<br>III. Respiratory bronchioles, alveolar ducts alveoli constitute the exchange part of the respiratory tract.<br>IV. Left lung has three lobes, while the right lung has two','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lungs are covered by a double layered pleura, with pleural fluid between them. It reduces friction on the lung-surface. Left lung has 2 lobes and right lung has 3 lobes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9188,'biology',83,500,1018,'Given below are two statements: one is labelled as Assertion and the other is labelled as Reason.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> All vertebrates are chordates but all chordates are not vertebrates.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Notochord is replaced by vertebral column in the adult vertebrates. In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "Both  Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is not correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is not correct but Reason is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All vertebrates are chordates because they possess a notochord at least at some time during their life. All chordates are not vertebrates because protochordates have notochord but lack a vertebral column. Therefore, A ssertion and Reason  are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9189,'biology',87,1124,2696,'Which enzyme causes conversion of prothrombin into thrombin?','[{"text": "Thrombinase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prothrombinase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thrombokinase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fibrinogen", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Thrombins, in turn are formed from another inactive substance present in the plasma called prothrombin. An enzyme complex, thrombokinase, is required for this reaction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9191,'biology',86,979,2284,'Which one is incorrect statement from following?','[{"text": "Nasal chambers opens into a part of pharynx i.e., Nasophrynx", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pharynx is a common path of food and air.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epiglottis is a bony, flap like structure which covers glottis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Larynx is a cartilagenous box which produces sound", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'While swallowing food, glottis wall is covered by epiglottis which is a thin elastic cartilaginous flap. Epiglottis prevents entry of food into glottis',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9192,'biology',83,506,1024,'In which of the following animals, digestive tract has additional chambers like crop and gizzard?','[{"text": "<i>Bufo, Balaenoptera, Bangarus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Catia, Columbia, Crocodilus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pavo, Psittacula, Corvus</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Corvus, Columbia, Chameleon</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The digestive tract has two additional chambers, the crop and the gizzard, in birds (e.g., <i>Pavo, Psittacula, Corvus</i>).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9193,'biology',87,1124,2696,'Select the incorrect statement from the following:<br>I. Clot or coagulam formed mainly of a network of threads called fibrins in which living and damaged formed elements of blood are trapped<br>II. Inactive fibrinogen is converted to fibrin by the hormone thrombinase.','[{"text": "I is correct only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II is correct only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Clot or coagulam formed mainly of a network of threads called fibrins in which dead and damaged formed elements of blood are trapped. Inactive fibrinogen is converted to fibrin by the enzyme thrombin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9195,'biology',86,979,2284,'Nasal cavity serves all the following functions except','[{"text": "Cleaning the air", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "As initiator of the cough reflex", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Warming and humidifying the air", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "As a passageway for air movement", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Nasal cavity acts as a initiator of sneezing reflex.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9196,'biology',83,489,1003,'Radial symmetry is not found in adults of phylum ______.','[{"text": "Ctenophora", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hemichordata", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coelenterata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Echinodermata", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Hemichordates are bilaterally symmetrical animals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9197,'biology',87,1124,2696,'Select the correct statement from the following:','[{"text": "Calcium plays an important role in clotting", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "When injured tissue releases certain factor which initiate clotting it is known as extrinsic pathway.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Platelet or injured tissue release certain factors which initiate coagulation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements given above are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9199,'biology',86,981,2286,'A man\'s lung volume is 6 litres at maximum inspiration. His functional residual volume is 3.5 litres and expiratory reserve volume is 2 litres. What is his vital capacity?','[{"text": "6 litres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5 litres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4 litres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4.5 litres", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<br>$$\\mathrm{TLC}=6$$ litres; $$\\mathrm{FRC}=3.5$$ litres; $$\\mathrm{ERV}=2$$ litres;<br>$$\\mathrm{RV}=\\mathrm{FRC}-\\mathrm{ERV}=3.5-2=1.5$$ litres<br>$$\\mathrm{VC}=\\mathrm{TLC}-\\mathrm{RV}=6-1.5=4.5$$ litres',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9200,'biology',83,496,1012,'Match Column I with Column II.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <em>Taenia</em><br>B. <em>Paramoecium</em><br>C. <em>Periplaneta</em><br>D. <em>Pheretima</em></div><div class="column-right">P. Nephridia<br>Q. Contractile vacuole<br>R. Flame cells<br>S. Urecose gland</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Protonephridia or flame cells are the excretory structures in platyhelminthes. Nephridia are the tubular excretory structures of earthworms (Pheretima) and other annelids. Single celled organisms like Paramoecium have contractile vacuoles for excretion. Urecose glands are present in cockroach.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9201,'biology',87,1124,2696,'"This complex is formed by a series of linked enzymic reactions (cascade process) involving a number of factors present in the plasma in an inactive state." This statement talks about which component in the body?','[{"text": "Fibrinogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heparin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thrombokinase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Platelets", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Thrombins, are formed from another inactive substance present in the plasma called prothrombin. An enzyme complex, thrombokinase, is required for the above reaction. This complex is formed by a series of linked enzymic reactions (cascade process) involving a number of factors present in the plasma in an inactive state.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9203,'biology',86,979,2284,'Identify the component of the respiratory system which displays the features given below and choose the correct option<BR>i. Fluid contained in it reduces the friction on the lung surface<BR>ii. Its outer layer is in contact with thoracic wall<BR>iii. double layered<BR>iv. Its inner layer is in contact with lungs','[{"text": "Pleura", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Visceral organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Visceral layers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peritoneum cavity", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pleura are the membranes that covers lungs. Each lung has 2 pleural membranes, Parietal pleuron and visceral pleuron . It encloses the pleural cavity which is filled by pleural fluid.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9204,'biology',83,507,1025,'The unique mammalian characteristics are:','[{"text": "hairs, tympanic membrane and mammary glands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "hairs, pinna and mammary glands", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "hairs, pinna and indirect development", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "pinna, monocondylic skull and mammary glands", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Presence of hairs, pinna and mammary\nglands are unique features of mammals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9205,'biology',87,1124,2696,'Which of the following substances, would cause coagulation of blood at the site of its introduction?','[{"text": "Fibrinogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heparin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thrombokinase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Platelets", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Thrombokinase would cause coagulation of blood at the site of its introduction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9207,'biology',86,980,2285,'Read the statements<br>I. Diaphragm is very useful in both inspiration and expiration<br>II. On an average, healthy human breathes 12-16 times /minutes<br>III. The volume of air involved in the breathing movements can be estimated by spirometer<br>Which of the above statements are incorrect?','[{"text": "III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the three statements are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9208,'biology',83,500,1016,'Select the correct statements with reference to chordates.<br>I. Presence of a mid-dorsal, solid and double nerve cord.<br>II. Presence of closed circulatory system.<br>III. Presence of paired pharyngeal gill slits.<br>IV. Presence of dorsal heart<br>V. Triploblastic pseudocoelomate animals.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "I, III and IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV and V only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV and V only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statements II and III only are correct. Option (1), (3) and (4) are not correct. The chordate characters are presence of closed circulatory system and presence of pharyngeal gill slits. Nerve cord is dorsal, hollow and single. Heart is ventral. They are triploblastic and coelomate.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9209,'biology',87,1124,2696,'What is the correct order of these events?<br>1) Conversion of fibrinogen to fibrin<br>2) Trapping of dead and damaged formed elements of blood<br>3) Thrombokinase formation<br>4) Conversion of prothrombin to thrombin','[{"text": "$$3,2,1,4$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$3,4,1,2$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$3,4,2,1$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$4,1,3,2$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Clot or coagulam formed mainly of a network of threads called fibrins in which dead and damaged formed elements of blood are trapped. Fibrins are formed by the conversion of inactive fibrinogens in the plasma by the enzyme thrombin. Thrombins, in turn are formed from another inactive substance present in the plasma called prothrombin. An enzyme complex, thrombokinase, is required for the above reaction. This complex is formed by a series of linked enzymic reactions (cascade process) involving a number of factors present in the plasma in an inactive state.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9211,'biology',86,983,2288,'All of the following speed up breathing except','[{"text": "A slight increase in arterial $$\\\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A slight decrease in arterial $$\\\\mathrm{pH}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A slight increase in arterial $$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A slight decrease in arterial $$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Receptors associated with aortic arch and carotid artery can recognise changes in $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$concentration and send necessary signals to the rhythm it centre for remedial actions. The role of oxygen in the regulation of respiratory rhythm is quite insignificant.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9212,'biology',83,502,1020,'Which of the following is found exclusively in the sea water?','[{"text": "Prawns", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Trygon</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crabs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oysters", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Oysters are sedentary marine bivalve found in all seas except in colder ones. The Indian pearl oyster is Pinctada vulgaris that is known as for yielding precious pearls',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9213,'biology',87,1123,2695,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Blood group- A<br>B. Blood group-B<br>C. Blood group- AB<br>D. Blood group- O</div><div class="column-right">P. Universal donor<br>Q. Anti-A antibodies in plasma<br>R. Universal recipient<br>S. Anti-B antibodies in plasma</div></div>','[{"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Blood group A - Anti-B antibodies in plasma<br>Blood group B - Anti-A antibodies on plasma Blood group $$\\mathrm{AB}$$ - Universal recipient Blood group $$\\mathrm{O}$$ - Universal donor',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9215,'biology',86,984,2289,'Identify which of the following is incorrect?<br>i. Incase of forceful expiration, lungs become empty<br>ii. Exchange of gases in the lungs is interrupted during expiration.<br>iii. Chemosensitive area of respiratory centre in medulla is affected by excess $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$ions<br>iv. Respiratory movements are controlled by $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ concentration of arterial blood','[{"text": "ii and iii only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and ii only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii and iv only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In case of forceful expiration, lungs donot become empty, a residual volume of a sir remains in the lungs. During expiration exchange of gases in lungs is not interrupted.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9216,'biology',83,498,1014,'Which of the following is properly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Echinodermata - Asteroidea - Starfish", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Arthropoda - Insecta - Spider", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mollusca - Cephalopoda - <i>Unio</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Platyhelminthes - Trematoda - <i>Planaria", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Star fish comes under Asteroidea class of phylum Echinodermata<br>Spider belongs to Arachnida class of phylum Arthropoda<br>Unio comes under Bivalvia class of phylum Mollusca<br>Planaria belongs to Turbellaria class of phylum Platyhelminthes',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9217,'biology',87,1124,2696,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Thrombin<br>B. Thrombokinase<br>C. Calcium<br>D. Brown scum</div><div class="column-right">P. Conversion of prothrombin to thrombin<br>Q.Important role in blood clotting<br>R. Conversion of fibrinogen to fibrin<br>S. Clot formed mainly of a network of threads called fibrins</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S,D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P,D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-S,D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q,D-S", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Thrombin - Conversion of fibrinogen to fibrin<br>Thrombokinase - Conversion of prothrombin to thrombin<br>Calcium - Important role in Blood clotting<br>Brown scum - Clot formed mainly of a network of threads called fibrins',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9218,'biology',84,583,1170,'Which of the following is false about the nervous system of frog?','[{"text": "Mid-brain includes paired optic lobes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fore-brain includes olfactory lobes, paired cerebral hemispheres and unpaired diencephalon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There are 12 pairs of spinal nerves", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hind-brain includes cerebellum and medulla oblongata", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'There are 10 pairs of spinal nerves in frog.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9219,'biology',86,979,2284,'Analyze the statements regarding the functions of conducting part of human respiratory system.<br>I. Transports the atmospheric air to the alveoli and cools down the air<br>II. Humidifies the air and also brings the air to body temperature<br>III. Transports the atmospheric air to the alveoli and clears it from foreign particles','[{"text": "I and II are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and III are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement II and III are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9220,'biology',83,489,1004,'The cross section of the body of an invertebrate is given below. Identify the animal which has this body plan','[{"text": "Roundworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Planaria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Earthworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cockroach", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'It is showing body plan of acoelomate. These animals do not contain coelom. The space between the endoderm and ectoderm is filled with parenchyma, which is derived from mesoderm. The parenchymatous tissue leaves no space to accomodate for the development of visceral organs. For example, Planaria',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_9220_question_1.png'),
(9221,'biology',87,1125,2697,'Tissue fluid is known as','[{"text": "Blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interstitial fluid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasma", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Tissue fluid is known as interstitial fluid. It has the same mineral distribution as that in plasma. Exchange of nutrients, gases, etc., between the blood and the cells always occur through this fluid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9222,'biology',84,583,1168,'Read the following statements and find out the incorrect statement','[{"text": "Frog never drinks water.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In frog, neck and tail are absent.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eyes of frog are covered by nicitating membrane that protects them while in water.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The duodenum receives bile form gall bladder and pancreatic juices form the pancreas through the common bile duct.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The duodenum receives bile form gall bladder and pancreatic juices form the pancreas through the Hepato-pancreatic duct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9223,'biology',86,982,2287,'For completion of respiratory process, arrange the given stops in the sequential manner<br>i. Diffusion of gases $$\\left(\\mathrm{O}_{2}\\right.$$ and $$\\left.\\mathrm{CO}_{2}\\right)$$ across alveolar membrane<br>ii. Diffusion of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ between blood and tissues<br>iii. Transport of gases by the blood<br>iv. Pulmonary ventilation by which atmospheric air is drawn in and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ rich alveolar air is released out<br>v. Utilization of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ by the cells for catabolic reactions','[{"text": "iv, i, iii, ii, v", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iv, i, ii, v, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv, v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iii, iv, i, v", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The steps for completion of respiratory process has sequence as follow:<br>(1) Pulmonary ventilation by which atmospheric air is drawn in and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ rich alveolar air is released out<br>(2) Diffusion of gases $$\\left(\\mathrm{O}_{2}\\right.$$ and $$\\left.\\mathrm{CO}_{2}\\right)$$ across alveolar membrane<br>(3) Transport of gases by the blood<br>(4) Diffusion of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ between blood and tissues<br>(5) Utilization of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ by the cells for catabolic reactions',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9224,'biology',83,507,1025,'Pick the mammal with true placenta','[{"text": "Kangaroo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Echinda</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Platypus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mongoose", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Placenta is present in all mammals except marsupials and monotremes. Echinda and Platypus are monotreme that is egg laying mammals. Kangaroo is a marsupial, pouched mammal. Mongoose is the mammal which has a true placenta',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9225,'biology',87,1125,2697,'Lymph is a fluid that','[{"text": "Transports nutrients", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transports hormones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Returns interstitial fluid to blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The fluid present in the lymphatic system is called the lymph. Lymph is a colourless fluid containing specialised lymphocytes which are responsible for the immune responses of the body. Lymph is also an important carrier for nutrients, hormones, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9226,'biology',84,583,1168,'Which one is correct about the respiration of frog?<br>i. In frog, cutaneous and pulmonary respiration are found<br>ii. A pair of elongated pink hollow lungs are found in thorax<br>iii. Atmospheric $\\mathrm{O}_{2} \\rightarrow$ Nostril $\\rightarrow$ Buccal cavity $\\rightarrow$ Lungs<br>iv. During aestivation and hibernation, gaseous exchange takes place through skin','[{"text": "iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'All the given statements about the respiration of frog are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9227,'biology',86,983,2288,'Read the following statements<br>I. A person can expel all the air from the lungs by a forceful expiration<br>II. A rise of $\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$ increases the oxygenaffinity of haemoglobin<br>III. Vital capacity is a measure of maximum inspiration<br>IV. During gaseous exchange the gases diffuse from high partial pressure to low partial pressure.<br>Identify which of the statements are TRUE/ FALSE?<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}} {\\rm{I}}&amp;{{\\rm{II}}}&amp;{{\\rm{III}}}&amp;{{\\rm{IV}}} \\end{array}$','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{llll}\\\\mathrm{F} &amp; \\\\mathrm{F} &amp; \\\\mathrm{F} &amp; \\\\mathrm{T}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{llll}\\\\mathrm{F} &amp; \\\\mathrm{T} &amp; \\\\mathrm{F} &amp; \\\\mathrm{F}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{llll}\\\\mathrm{T} &amp; \\\\mathrm{T} &amp; \\\\mathrm{F} &amp; \\\\mathrm{F}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{llll}\\\\mathrm{F} &amp; \\\\mathrm{T} &amp; \\\\mathrm{T} &amp; \\\\mathrm{F}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{I - F,}}\\,{\\rm{II - F,}}\\,{\\rm{III - F,}}\\,{\\rm{IV - T}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9228,'biology',83,498,1014,'In which of the following phyla given as the adult shows radial symmetry, the larva shows bilateral symmetry?','[{"text": "Annelids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arthropods", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Molluscs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Echinodermata", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bodies of Echinodermata exhibit bilateral symmetry in larvae and pentamerous radial symmetry in adults',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9229,'biology',87,1125,2697,'The lymphatic vessel join up to form larger vessels which finally unite, the content of these duct reaches heart through','[{"text": "Inferior vena cava", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Superior vena cava", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pulmonary vein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pulmonary artery", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The lymphatic vessel join up to form larger vessels which finally unite, the content of these duct reaches heart through superior vena cava.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9230,'biology',84,583,1167,'Which of the following statements is incorrect about the frog?<br>I. The hind limbs end in four digits and they are larger and muscular than fore limbs that end in five digits.<br>II. Eyes are bulged out and covered by a nictitating membrane that protects them while in water.<br>III. On either side of the eyes a membranous tympanum (ear) receives sound signals<br>IV. Frogs exhibit sexual dimorphism<br>V. Feet have webbed digits and help in swimming','[{"text": "III and IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Fore limb of frog has 4 digits, Hind limb of frog are larger than fore limbs and the ends in 5 digits',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9231,'biology',86,983,2288,'Which of the following factors raise the P50 value and shifts the $$\\mathrm{HbO}_{2}$$ dissociation curve to right and vice versa :<br>i. Rise in $$\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$<br>ii. Fall in temperature<br>iii. Rise in $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}(=$$fall in $$\\mathrm{pH})$$<br>iv. Fall in diphosphoglyceric acid answer codes :','[{"text": "i and ii are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iii are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii and iv are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii and iii are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ of blood falls as its carbon dioxide content increases so that, when the $$\\mathrm{PCO}_{2}$$ rises, the oxygen-haemoglobin dissociation curve shifts to the right side and the P50 rises.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9232,'biology',83,498,1014,'Which one of the following groups of 3 animals each is correctly matched with their one characteristic morphological feature?<br>&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;\\[\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{Animals}}}\n\\end{array}}&{\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;{\\rm{Morphological}}\\;{\\rm{features}}}\n\\end{array}\\]<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{Centipede,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Prawn,}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{Sea}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{urchin}}\\n\\\\end{array}&\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{Jointed}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{appendages}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\n\\\\end{array}$<br><br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{Cockroach,}\\\\,}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{Locust,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Taenia}}\\\\,\\\\,\\n\\\\end{array}&\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Metameric}}\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Segmentation}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\n\\\\end{array}}$<br><br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{Scorpion,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Spider,}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{Cockroach}}\\\\,\\\\,\\n\\\\end{array}&\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Ventral}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{solid}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{ }}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{nervecord}}\\n\\\\end{array}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}\\n\\\\end{array}$<br><br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{Liver}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{fluke,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Sea}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{anemone,}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{Sea}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{cucumber}}\\n\\\\end{array}&{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Bilateral }}\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{symmetry}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Centipede and Prawn are arthropods and have jointed appendages, but sea urchin belongs to Echinodermata and have tube feet for locomotion<br>Cockroach and Locust are arthropods and exhibits metameric segmentation. Taenia belongs to platyhelminthes and their body is divided into three parts - head or scolex, unsegmented neck and segmented strobil<br>Scorpion, Spider and Cockroach are all arthropods that have a well - developed neural system consisting of cerebral ganglion, peripharyngeal connectives, subpharyngeal ganglion, nerve ring and solid double ganglionated ventral nerve cord<br>Liver fluke belongs to platyhelminthes and exhibit bilateral symmetry. Sea anemonebelongs to Cnidaria and Sea cucumber to Echinodermata and exhibit radial symmetry',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9233,'biology',87,1125,2697,'Tissue fluid has the ____ distribution as that in plasma.','[{"text": "Same mineral", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Same RBC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Same WBC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Tissue fluid has the same mineral distribution as that in plasma',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9234,'biology',84,583,1171,'Which of the following sequences is correct for the passage of sperms in frog (male)','[{"text": "Testis $\\\\rightarrow$ Vasa efferentia $\\\\rightarrow$ Bidder\'s canal $\\\\rightarrow$ Urinogenital duct $\\\\rightarrow$ Cloaca $\\\\rightarrow$ Cloacal aperture", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Testis $\\\\rightarrow$ Bidder\'s canal $\\\\rightarrow$ Vasa efferentia $\\\\rightarrow$ Urinogenital duct $\\\\rightarrow$ Cloaca $\\\\rightarrow$ Cloacal aperture", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testis $\\\\rightarrow$ Vasaefferentia $\\\\rightarrow$ Urinogenital duct $\\\\rightarrow$ Bidder\'s canal $\\\\rightarrow$ Cloaca $\\\\rightarrow$ Cloacal aperture", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testis $\\\\rightarrow$ Urinogenital duct $\\\\rightarrow$ Bidder\'s canal $\\\\rightarrow$ Vasa efferentia $\\\\rightarrow$ Cloaca $\\\\rightarrow$ Cloacal aperture", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'the following sequences is correct for the passage of sperms in frog (male)<br>Testis - Vasa efferentia - Bidder\'s canal - Urinogenital duct - cloaca - cloacal aperture',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9244,'biology',83,492,1008,'Identify the phylum X :','[{"text": "Aschelminthes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ctenophora", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hemichordata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Hemichordata, Aschelminthes and Platyhelminthes show organ system level of organisation, i.e., organs get associated to form functional systems, each system concerned with a specific physiology function.<br>Ctenophores have tissue grade level of organisation but are biradially symmetrical, i.e., ( radial + bilateral)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_9244_question_1.png'),
(9235,'biology',86,983,2288,'Which of the following statements are true/ false?<br>I. The blood transports $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ comparatively easily because of its highest solubility<br>II. Approximately $$8.9 \\%$$ of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is transported being dissolved in the plasma of blood<br>III. The $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ produced by the tissues, diffuses passively into the blood stream and passes into red blood corpuscles and react with water to form $$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{CO}_{3}$$<BR>IV. The oxyhaemoglobin $$\\left(\\mathrm{HbO}_{2}\\right)$$ of erythrocytes is basic<br>V. The chloride ions diffuse from plasma into the erythrocytes to maintain ionic balance','[{"text": "I, III and V are false, II and IV are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III and V are true, II and IV are false", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II and V are false, III and IV are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III are true, IV and V are false", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$$70 \\% \\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is transported being dissolved in the plasma of blood. Oxyhaemoglobin $$\\left(\\mathrm{HbO}_{2}\\right)$$ of erythrocytes is acidic.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9236,'biology',83,489,1004,'The kind of coelom represented in the diagram, given below is characteristics of','[{"text": "Earthworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cockroach", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Round worm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tape worm", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'This is pseudocoelomate. In the body cavity is not lined by mesoderm, instead mesoderm is present in scattered pouches in between ectoderm and endoderm. This is seen in aschelminthes or round worms',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_9236_question_1.png'),
