(9238,'biology',84,583,1168,'Consider the following statements about the respiratory system of frog<br>I. Dissolved oxygen is exchanged through the skin by the process of active transport.<br>II. Skin acts as a respiratory organ<br>III. Gaseous exchange takes place through the skin during hibernation and aestivation<br>IV. Lungs are paired and present in thorax.<br>Which of the statement given above are incorrect?','[{"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In frog dissolved oxygen is exchanged through the skin by the process of diffusion.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9239,'biology',86,983,2288,'Read the following statements and select the correct option stating TRUE (T) and FALSE (F) among themselves.<br>I. More $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ dissolves in the blood plasma than carried in RBC<br>II. $$100 \\mathrm{ml}$$ of blood enable to transport about $$3 \\mathrm{ml}$$ of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ in the form of carbonate<br>III. $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ accumulation in the blood is associated with decrease in $$\\mathrm{pH}$$<br>IV. $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ concentration in the blood is decreased by hyperventilation<BR>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{\\rm{I}}&{{\\rm{II}}}&{{\\rm{III}}}&{{\\rm{IV}}}\n\\end{array}$','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{T}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{T}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{F}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{F}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$$7 \\% \\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is dissolved in plasma, $$20-25 \\%$$ is carried by $$\\mathrm{RBC}$$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9240,'biology',83,507,1025,'The success of mammals on earth is largely beacuse','[{"text": "They can conform to the changes in the environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They can reduce metabolic activity and go into a state of dormancy during unfavourable conditions in the environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have the ability to maintain constant body temperature", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They can take of their young ones as they have mamary glands to suckle them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mammals are endothermic. Endothermy<br>( maintenance of internal temperature ) enable these animals to live at temperatures that other land vertebrates cannot bear',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
