(9242,'biology',84,583,1171,'For female frog, which of the following is false?<br>i. One pair of ovaries is situated in the kidneys<br>ii. Ovary has functional connection with kidney<br>iii. Convulated, tubular, ciliated and glandular oviduct opens into cloaca<br>iv. Oviduct and ureter open separately into the cloaca<br>v. A female frog can lay 2500-3000 ova at a time','[{"text": "only ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{i}$ and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iv and $v$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$i$ and ii", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The female reproductive organs include a pair of ovaries. The ovaries are situated near kidneys and there is no functional connection with kidneys.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9243,'biology',86,983,2288,'The graph show oxygen-dissociation curves of adult haemoglobin (Hb-a), foetal haemoglobin $$(\\mathrm{Hb}-\\mathrm{F})$$ and myoglobin $$(\\mathrm{Mb})$$. Choose the option that correctly identifies the three curves.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{A - Mb}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{B - Hb - F}}\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{C - Hb - a}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{A - Hb - a}}\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{B - Hb - F}}\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{C - Mb}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{A - Mb}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{B - Hb - a}}\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{C - Hb - F}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{A - Hb - F}}\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{B - Mb}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{C - Hb - a}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Oxygen-affinity of myoglobin is more than that of Hb-F than that of Hb-A.',NULL,'Hard','Graph/Figure',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/86_9243_question_1.png'),
