(9246,'biology',84,579,1159,'To which one of the following categories does adipose tissue belong?','[{"text": "Epithelial", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Connective", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Muscular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neural", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Adipose tissue belongs to Connective tissues Categories and is mesodermal in origin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9247,'biology',83,507,1025,'Match the animals of Column I with their respective classes in Colum II and choose the correct answer<br>Select the codde for the correct answer from the options given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <i>Aptenodytes</i><br>B. <i>Hemidactylus</i><br>C. <i>Carcharodon</i><br>D. <i>Pteropus</i></div><div class="column-right">P. Aves<br>Q. Chondrichthyes<br>R. Mammalia<br>S. Reptila<br>T. Osterchthyes</div></div>','[{"text": "A - T, B - Q, C - S, D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P, B - S, C - R, D - Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - T, B - P, C - Q, D - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P, B - S, C - Q, D - R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Aptenodytes commonly known as Penguin, belongs to the class Aves and sub class Neornithes<br>Hemidactylus, commonly known as house lizard, belongs to class Reptilia and sub - class Diapsida<br>Carcharodon is a genus of sharks, belongs to the super class pisces and class chondrichthyes<br>Pteropus, commonly known as flying fox, belongs to the class Mammalia and sub - class Theria, infra class Eutheria and order Chiroptera',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9248,'biology',86,984,2289,'Which of the following is incorrect regarding respiration :-','[{"text": "Role of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ is significant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemoreceptors present in aortic arch and carotid artery can detect the change of $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ in blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Herring bruer reflex prevents over dilation of lungs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pneumotaxic centre is present in Pons", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Herring Bruer reflex is a reflex that will prevent over inflation of lungs. Herring Bruer reflex is initiated by expansion of lungs which in turn excites stretch receptors. Stimulation of stretch receptors will send signals to medulla of brain to shorten inspiratory time.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9249,'biology',87,1126,2698,'In amphibia, without exception, the heart has','[{"text": "Two auricles and two ventricles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two auricles and one ventricle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One auricle and two ventricles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One auricle, one ventricle and one sinus venosus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Amphibians have a 3 -chambered heart with two atria and a single ventricle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9251,'biology',83,489,1004,'Which of the following phyla possess body cavity as shown in the diagram below?','[{"text": "Annelida", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Porifera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aschelminthes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coelenterata", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'This is pseudococelomate. In this body cavity is not lined by mesoderm, instead mesoderm is present in scattered poches in between ectoderm and endoderm. This is seen aschelminthes or round worms',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_9251_question_1.png'),
(9252,'biology',86,984,2289,'The respiratory process is regulated by respiratory rhythm centre present in medulla of the brain, which is?','[{"text": "Stimulated by lower $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$ concentration in aortic arch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimulated by higher $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and higher $$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$ concentration.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inhibited byhigher $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$concentration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimulated by lower $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$ concentration in carotid artery", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Respiratory rhythm centre is present in medulla region of brain. There is a chemosensitive area, adjacent to respiratory rhythm centre, it is sensitive to $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$ ions. Receptors associated with aortic arch and carotid artery also recognize changes in concentration of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$concentration and send signals to respiratory rhythm centre.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
