(9254,'biology',83,500,1018,'Observe the following simplified scheme and choose the correct option that matches with the letters given in the boxes\'<br><div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "p-Agnatha, q-Gnathostomata, r-Pisces, s - Tetrapoda", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "p -Gnathostomata , q-Agnatha, r - Tetrapoda, s - Pisces", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "p - Tetrapoda , q - Pisces, r - Gnathostomata,\\ns - Agnatha", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "p - Agnatha, q - Gnathostomata,\\nr - Tetrapoda, s - Pisces", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{p}$ - Agnatha, $\\mathrm{q}$ - Gnathostomata, $\\mathrm{r}$ - Pisces, s - Tetrapoda',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/83_9254_question_1.png'),
(9265,'biology',87,1126,2698,'Which of the following has a closed blood vascular system?','[{"text": "Apis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cockroach", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pila", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Earthworm", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Annelids and chordates have a closed circulatory system in which the blood pumped by the heart is always circulated through a closed network of blood vessels. Earthworm has a closed blood vascular system.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9255,'biology',86,985,2290,'Read the following symptoms of respiratory disorders-<br>1) Inflammation in bronchus and bronchioles and trachea<br>2) It is a chronic disorder<br>3) Smoking is one of the major cause of it<br>4)Fibrosis occurs in lungs.<br>5) It occurs in those person who works in stone industries.<br>6) In this disorder, alveolar wall is get damaged and decreased surface area of gaseous exchange.<br>Out of these how many symptoms are not related to "Emphysema"?','[{"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Five", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Six", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Emphysema is a respiratory disorder. It is a chronic disorder where the alveolar walls get damaged which will result in decrease of respiratory surface. Major cause for emphysema is smoking of cigarette. Statement (2) (3) and (6) are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9257,'biology',87,1126,2698,'Which one of the following has an open circulatory system?','[{"text": "<i>Pteropus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Balaenoptera</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Periplaneta</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Hirudinaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Open circulatory system is present in arthropods and molluscs in which blood pumped by the heart passes through large vessels into open spaces or body cavities called sinuses. Periplaneta (cockroach) an arthropod has an open circulatory system.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9258,'biology',83,506,1024,'Identify the correct statements regrading class aves<br>I. Forelimbs are modified into wings and hindlimbs are modified for walking and swimming<br>II. Heart is completely four - chambered<br>III. They are homeotherms<br>IV. They are oviparous and development is direct','[{"text": "Both I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements are correct for aves/ birds. Forelimbs are modified into wings and hindlimbs are modified for walking and swimming Heart is completely four -<br>chambered They are homeotherms They are oviparous and development is direct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9259,'biology',86,985,2290,'Read the following statements :-<br>I. It is chronic disorder.<br>II. Major cause of it is cigarette smoking.<br>III. It is an allergy.<br>IV. Alveolar walls are damaged.<br>V. Respiratory surface is decreased.<br>VI. It is due to inflammation of bronchi and bronchioles.<br>How many of above statements are correct about Emphysema disorder?','[{"text": "Two", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Emphysema is a chronic disorder where alveolar walls are damaged and it results in decrease of respiratory surface. Major cause for emphysema is cigarette smoking. Statement I, II, IV and V are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9261,'biology',87,1126,2698,'In an open circulatory system,','[{"text": "The heart is open", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The blood vessels are open", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There are open spaces or sinuses in the body", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Circulatory system keeps growing like cambium in plants", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In an open circulatory system, there are open spaces or sinuses in the body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9262,'biology',83,489,1003,'Select the correct match.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Porifera - Tissue level of organisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cnidaria - Bilateral symmetry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Echinodermata - Notochord", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Platyhelminthes - Triploblastic", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Phylum Platyhelminthes includes flatworms which are bilaterally symmetrical, triploblastic and acoelomate animals with organ level of organisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9263,'biology',86,980,2285,'During inspiration, air moves into lungs because','[{"text": "Pressure within the lungs is more than atmospheric pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pressure within the lungs and atmospheric air is same", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Passive flow of air takes air inside", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pressure within the lungs is less than atmospheric pressure in air", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Contraction of diaphragm and external intercostal muscles causes fall in intrapulmonary pressure, and create negative suction pressure to pull air into lungs.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9264,'biology',84,583,1170,'Match the followings and choose the correct answer in the frog<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Touch<br>B. Smell<br>C. Cranial nerves<br>D. Medulla oblongata</div><div class="column-right">1. Nasal epitheliumun<br>2. Foramen magnum<br>3. Sensory papillae<br>4. Peripheral nervous system<br></div></div>','[{"text": "A-3, B-1, C-2, D-4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-2, B-1, C-4, D-3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-3, B-4, C-2, D-1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-3, B-1, C-4, D-2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sensory papillae are touch receptors, Olfactory receptors present in nasal epithelium is for smell; Cranial nerves are a part of Peripheral neural system and Medulla Oblongata passes out through foramen magnum.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9321,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Mitral valve is found between','[{"text": "Left atrium and left ventricle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Right atrium and right ventricle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Right atrium and left ventricle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Left atrium and right ventricle", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bicuspid or mitral valve guards the opening between the left atrium and the left ventricle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9266,'biology',83,490,1006,'The type of movement that helps in the maintenance of water current in the canal system of sponges also helps for ____ in humans beings','[{"text": "Swimming of spermatozoa", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Diapedesis of leukocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peristalsis of the intestine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Swallowing of food", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Flagellar movement helps in the swimming of spermatozoa, maintenance of water current in the canal system of sponges and in locomotion of Protozoans like <i>Euglena</i>.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9267,'biology',86,979,2284,'The reason for change of voice pitch in males from high to low on puberty is','[{"text": "Thickening of vocal cords under the effect of androgens", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thickening of epiglottis under the effect of androgens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shortening of larynx", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shortening of vocal cords under the effect of androgens", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'At puberty, the vocal cords of boys are thickened due to effect of androgens. The vocal cords of males are longer and thicker in males, due to which they have low pitch voice.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9268,'biology',84,579,1158,'Which one of the following types of cell is involved in making of the inner walls of large blood vessels?','[{"text": "Cuboidal epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Columnar epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Squamous epithelium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stratified epithelium", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Inner walls of large blood vessels is formed by Squamous epithelium',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9269,'biology',87,1126,2698,'Single circulation occurs in','[{"text": "Fishes (1 auricle and 1 ventricles)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fishes (2 auricle)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fishes (2 ventricles)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fishes (1 auricle)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Fishes have a 2-chambered heart with an atrium and a ventricle. In fishes the heart pumps out deoxygenated blood which is oxygenated by the gills and supplied to the body parts from where deoxygenated blood is returned to the heart (single circulation).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9270,'biology',86,985,2290,'Which of the following statements is incorrect?','[{"text": "Emphysema can be caused due to deficiency of antitrypsin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Asthma is an allergic diseaes due to spasm of muscles in the walls of bronchi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "BCG vaccine is given at birth to prevent children from bronchitis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pneumonia is infection of alveoli caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bacillus Calmette Guerin (BCG) vaccine is given at birth to prevent children from tuberculosis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9271,'biology',83,500,1017,'Choose the correct statement.','[{"text": "All sponges are marine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All flatworms are endoparasites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All arthropods are dieocious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All protochordates are marine", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both urochordates and cephalochordates (collectively called protochordates) are marine. Some sponges live in freshwater (e.g., Spongilla). Some flatworms are free-living (e.g., planaria). Arthropods are mostly dioecious. Some crustaceans are bisexual.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9272,'biology',84,579,1159,'Which one of the following is not a connective tissue?','[{"text": "Bone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cartilage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Muscles", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bone, Cartilage and blood are Connective tissue and Muscle is not a connective tissue.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9273,'biology',87,1126,2698,'Four chambered heart is found in','[{"text": "Turtle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tortoise", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crocodile", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Crocodiles, birds and mammals possess a 4-chambered heart with two atria and two ventricles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9274,'biology',83,491,1007,'Cnidarians and ctenophores share which of the following characteristics?','[{"text": "Tissue level of organisation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metagenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cnidocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Comb plates", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both cnidarians and ctenophores are diploblastic with tissue level of organisation. Metagenesis and cnidocytes are absent in ctenophores. Comb plates are absent in cnidarians.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(9275,'biology',86,982,2287,'Which of the following is incorrect?','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ of deoxygenated blood is ${\\\\rm{40}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mmHg}}$ and ${\\\\rm{45}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mmHg}}$ respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ of alveolar air is ${\\\\rm{104}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mmHg}}$ and ${\\\\rm{40}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mmHg}}$ respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ of inhaled air is ${\\\\rm{116}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mmHg}}$ and ${\\\\rm{32}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mmHg}}$ respectively.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ of exhaled air is ${\\\\rm{159}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mmHg}}$ and ${\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.3}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mmHg}}$ respectively.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$$\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ of inhaled air is $$159 \\mathrm{mmHg}$$ while $$\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ is $$0.3 \\mathrm{mmHg}$$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9277,'biology',87,1126,2698,'In mammals and reptiles, the circulation is known as','[{"text": "Incomplete double circulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mammalian circulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Double circulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None is correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In amphibians and reptiles, the left atrium receives oxygenated blood from the gills/lungs/ skin and the right atrium gets the deoxygenated blood from other body parts. However, they get mixed up in the single ventricle which pumps out mixed blood (incomplete double circulation). And mammals show double circulation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10340,'biology',9,24,45,'In Rhodophyceae reserve food is','[{"text": "Starch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mannitol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Floridean starch", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Laminarin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The food in red algae is stored as floridean starch which is very similar to amylopectin and glycogen in structure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9278,'biology',83,491,1007,'Cnidarians are advanced over sponges by the presence of','[{"text": "Larval stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Division of labour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tissues", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In sponges, the cells are arranged as loose cell aggregates (cellularlevel of organisation). Cnidarians exhibit tissue level of organisation. Both sponges and cnidarians exhibit indirect development. Sponges also reproduce sexually. Division of labour occurs among the cells in sponges also.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9279,'biology',86,979,2283,'Which of the following statement is correct about respiratory organs of different animals?','[{"text": "The exchange of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ via simple diffusion across body surface occurs in aquatic arthropods", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A complex system of air tubes called trachea is present in earthworm for respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fishes have lungs for respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cutaneous respiration occurs in amphibians", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Lower invertebrates like sponges, coelenterates, flatworms, etc., exchange $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ with $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ by simple diffusion over their entire body surface. Earthworms use their moist cuticle and insects have a network of tubes (tracheal tubes) to transport atmospheric air within the body. Special vascularised structures called gills (branchial respiration) are used by most of the aquatic arthropods and molluscs whereas vascularised bags called lungs (pulmonary respiration) are used by the terrestrial forms for the exchange of gases. Among vertebrates, fishes use gills whereas amphibians, reptiles, birds and mammals respire through lungs. Amphibians like frogs can respire through their moist skin (cutaneous respiration) also.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9280,'biology',84,579,1159,'Haversian canals are found in','[{"text": "Matrix of mammalian bone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Matrix of amphibian bone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Matrix of reptilian bone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Haversian canals are found in matrix of mammalian bone.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9281,'biology',87,1126,2698,'Double circulation is found in','[{"text": "Birds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mammals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amphibians", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In birds and mammals, oxygenated and deoxygenated blood received by the left and right atria respectively passes on to the ventricles of the same sides. The ventricles pump it out without any mixing up, i.e., two separate circulatory pathways are present in these organisms, hence, these animals have double circulation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9282,'biology',83,494,1010,'Match the following genera with their respective phyla.<br>Select the correct option.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <i>Adamsia</i><br>B. <i>Sycon</i><br>C. <i>Pleurobrachia</i><br>D. <i>Ancylostoma</i></div><div class="column-right">P. Porifera<br>Q. Aschelminthes<br>R. Ctenophora<br>S. Cnidaria</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P B-S C-R D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S B-P C-R D-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q B-R C-P D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S B-P C-Q D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Adamsia</i> - Cnidaria<br><i>Sycon</i> - Porifera<br><i>Pleurobrachia</i> - Ctenophora<br><i>Ancylostoma</i> - Aschelminthes',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9283,'biology',86,979,2284,'Which of the following statement is incorrect about nasopharynx?','[{"text": "Internal nostrils open into nasopharynx", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is the passage for air only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is a portion of pharynx", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nasopharynx opens through the glottis of the larynx region into the trachea", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The pharynx is a common passage for food and air.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9285,'biology',87,1126,2698,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Open circulatory system<br>B. Closed circulatory system<br>C. 2-chambered heart<br>D. 3-chambered heart</div><div class="column-right">P. Annelids<br>Q. Arthropods<br>R. Pisces<br>S. Reptilia</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Open circulatory system - Arthropods<br>Closed circulatory system - Annelids<br>2-chambered heart - Pisces<br>3-chambered heart - Reptilia.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9286,'biology',83,495,1011,'Which of the following animal groups is correctly paired with its characteristic?','[{"text": "Annelida - Body is covered by chitinous exoskeleton", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aschelminthes - Fertilisation is external and development is direct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Platyhelminthes - Flame cells help in excretion and osmo-regulation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cnidaria - Free-swimming polyp and sessile medusa stages", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Platyhelminthes-Flame cells help in excretion and osmoregulation',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9287,'biology',86,980,2285,'Read the following statements.<br>I. The Intrapulmonary pressure is more than the atmospheric pressure<br>II. Increased thoracic volume and pulmonary volume.<br>In which of the above two situations inspiration takes place?','[{"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I or II", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The overall increase in the thoracic volume causes a similar increase in pulmonary volume. An increase in pulmonary volume decreases the intra-pulmonary pressure to less than the atmospheric pressure which forces the air from outside to move into the lungs, i.e., inspiration.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9288,'biology',84,579,1158,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Squamous epithelium consists of a single thin layer of flattened cells with irregular boundaries<br></div><div class="column-right">Squamous epithelium is involved in many functions like diffusion</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9289,'biology',87,1126,2698,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Single circulation<br>B. Incomplete double circulation<br>C. Double circulation</div><div class="column-right">P. Aves and mammalia<br>Q. Amphibians<br>R. Pisces</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Single circulation - Pisces<br>Incomplete double circulation - Amphibians<br>Double circulation - Aves and mammalia',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9290,'biology',83,493,1009,'Planarians possess<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Complete alimentary canal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "High regeneration capacity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hooks and suckers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "True coelom", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Planarians</i> possess high regeneration capacity. Their alimentary canal is incomplete. Hooks and suckers are present in parasitic flatworms (trematodes and cestodes) only. Platyhelminthes are acoelomates.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9291,'biology',86,979,2284,'Which of the following statement(s) is/are true for pleural membrane of lungs?','[{"text": "It is single -layered", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fluid contained in it reduces the friction on the lung surface", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Lungs are covered by a double layered pleura, with pleural fluid between them. It reduces friction on the lung-surface.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9292,'biology',84,579,1158,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Columnar epithelium is composed of single layer of tall and slender cells <br></div><div class="column-right">Columnar epithelium is commonly found in alveoli of mammalian lungs.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The columnar epithelium is commonly found in the lining of stomach and intestine and helps in secre-tion and absorption.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9293,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Heart is derived from ____, is situated in the ____, in between the two lungs, slightly tilted to the ____.','[{"text": "Endoderm, thoracic cavity, left", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ectoderm, abdominal cavity, left", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesoderm, thoracic cavity, left", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mesoderm, thoracic cavity, right", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Heart, the mesodermally derived organ, is situated in the thoracic cavity, in between the two lungs, slightly tilted to the left. It has the size of a clenched fist.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9294,'biology',83,498,1014,'Which of the following characteristic features always holds true for the corresponding group of animals?','[{"text": "Hooks and suckers - Platyhelminthes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Asymmetry - Porifera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calcareous skeleton - Coelenterata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Marine habitat - Echinodermata", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All echinoderms are marine. Hooks and suckers are present in parasitic flatworms (trematodes and cestodes) only. Most sponges are asymmetrical; some are radially symmetrical. Calcareous skeleton is present only coral forming coelenterates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9295,'biology',86,979,2284,'Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct for features of diaphragm in the respiratory tract?','[{"text": "Found in mammals and invertebrates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non muscular and fibrous partition, elevated towards the thorax like a dome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Separates abdominal and pelvic cavity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the given statements are wrong. The diaphragm is the primary muscle used in respiration, which is the process of breathing. This dome-shaped muscle is located just below the lungs and heart. It contracts continually as you breathe in and out.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9296,'biology',84,579,1161,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Neuroglia is made up of more one half the volume of neural tissue in our body<br></div><div class="column-right">Muscles are mesodermal in origin</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9297,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Apex of heart is','[{"text": "Upper and tilted toward left", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lower and tilted towards left", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Upper and tilted towards right", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lower and tilted towards right", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Heart, the mesodermally derived organ, is situated in the thoracic cavity, in between the two lungs, slightly tilted to the left. It has the size of a clenched fist.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9298,'biology',83,495,1011,'In which one of the following, the genus name and its two characters are correctly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Ctenoplana</i> belongs to the phylum Ctenophora. The body of ctenophores bears eight external rows of ciliated comb plates, which help in locomotion. Bioluminescence (the property of a living organism to emit light) is well-marked in ctenophores. Taenia is acoelomate. <i>Ascaris</i> lacks nephridia. Nereis is dioecious.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10131,'biology',89,1287,3108,'During muscular contraction, the myosin head binds to the exposed active sites on actin to form a','[{"text": "Motor unit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Motor end plate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cross arm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cross bridge", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During muscular contraction, the myosin head binds to the exposed active sites on actin to form a cross bridge.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9299,'biology',86,982,2287,'Which of the following option is not true?','[{"text": "The partial pressure of oxygen in oxygenated blood is $$95 \\\\mathrm{~mm} \\\\mathrm{Hg}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The partial pressure of oxygen in oxygenated blood is $$95 \\\\mathrm{~mm} \\\\mathrm{Hg}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The partial pressure of oxygen in deoxygenated blood is $$40 \\\\mathrm{~mm} \\\\mathrm{Hg}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The partial pressure of $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ in atmospheric air is $$40 \\\\mathrm{~mm} \\\\mathrm{Hg}$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The partial pressure of $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ in atmospheric air is $$159 \\mathrm{~mm} \\mathrm{Hg}$$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9301,'biology',87,1127,2699,'The heart is protected by a double walled membranous bag called ____.','[{"text": "Epicardium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endocardium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myocardium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pericardium", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The heart is protected by a double walled membranous bag called Pericardium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9302,'biology',83,495,1011,'Which of the following is true regarding <i>Nereis, Pheretima</i> and <i>Hirudinaria</i>?','[{"text": "<i>Hirudinaria</i> is aquatic whereas the other two are terrestrial", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pheretima</i> has setae which are absent in the other two", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Nereis</i> is dioecious whereas the other two are monoecious", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Hirudinaria</i> lacks parapodia which are present in the other two", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<i>Nereis</i> is dioecious, but earthworms and leeches are monoecious. <i>Nereis</i> and <i>Hirudinaria</i> are aquatic, but earthworms are terrestrial. Setae are present in <i>Nereis</i> and <i>Pheretima</i> but absent in leeches. Parapodia are present in <i>Nereis</i> but absent in earthworms and leeches.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9303,'biology',86,983,2288,'Read the following statements and identify the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ is the major factor which affects the binding of $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ with haemoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ is low and $$\\\\mathrm{pO}_{2}$$ is high in tissues", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "RBC contains a very high concentration of carbonic anhydrase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Every $$100 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$ of deoxygenated blood delivers approximately $$4 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$ of $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ to alveoli", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$$\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}(45 \\mathrm{mmHg})$$ is high and $$\\mathrm{pO}_{2}(40$$ $$\\mathrm{mmHg})$$ is low in tissues.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9305,'biology',87,1127,2699,'The right atrium and the right ventricle are separated by a ____ tissue called the ____ septum','[{"text": "Thick fibrous, ventricular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thick fibrous, atrio-ventricular", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thin fibrous, atrio-ventricular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thick elastic, atrio-ventricular", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The right atrium and the right ventricle are separated by a thick fibrous issue called the atrio-ventricular septum',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9306,'biology',83,489,1003,'Open circulatory system is present in','[{"text": "Annelids and arthropods", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hemichordates and cephalochordates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arthropods and hemichordates", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Molluscs and annelids", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Open circulatory system is present in Arthropoda, Mollusca (except cephalopods), Echinodermata, Hemichordata and Urochordata.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9307,'biology',86,979,2284,'Which of the following statements is correct regarding respiratory system?','[{"text": "Each terminal bronchiole gives rise to a network of bronchi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The alveoli are highly vascularised", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The lungs are covered by a single-layered membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The pleural fluid increases friction on the lung surface", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The alveoli are highly vascularized.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9322,'biology',83,501,1019,'Choose the false statement regarding <i>Petromyzon</i>.','[{"text": "Skull is without cranium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mouth is without jaws", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Skin is without scales", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo is without amnion", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Petromyzon</i> is a vertebrate (craniate). Cranium and vertebral column are cartilaginous. Only reptiles, birds and mammals are amniotes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9309,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Select the total number of thick structure out of the following:<br>1) Walls of atrium<br>2) Interventricular septum<br>3) Atrioventricular septum<br>4) Walls of ventricles<br>5) Interatrial septum','[{"text": "$$1,2,3$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$2,3,5$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$2,3,4$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$1,3,4$$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Interventricular septum, Atrioventricular septum, Walls of ventricles are thick walled structures.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9310,'biology',83,499,1015,'Which of the following animal groups is not correctly paired with its characteristic?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Arthropoda-Chitinous exoskeleton", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mollusca - Exoskeleton is absent", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Echinodermata-Excretory system is absent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hemichordata- Respiration through gills", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Molluscs have a calcareous shell (which represents their exoskeleton).',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9312,'biology',86,980,2285,'Arrange the given steps of expiration in the sequence of event occuring first.<br>I. Relaxation of the diaphragm and sternum<br>II. Reduction of the pulmonary volume.<br>III. Increase in intrapulmonary pressure.<br>IV. Expiration<br>Choose the correct option.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, III, II, I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, II, III, I", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Steps of expiration in the sequence of event occuring first is as follow-<br>(1) Relaxation of the diaphragm and sternum<br>(2) Reduction of the pulmonary volume.<br>(3) Increase in intrapulmonary pressure.<br>(4) Expiration.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9313,'biology',87,1127,2699,'The chordae tendinae are attached to which of the following','[{"text": "Right AV valve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Semilunar valve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Left AV valve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The chordae tendinae are attached to Right $$A V$$ valve and Left $$A V$$ valve.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9314,'biology',83,499,1015,'Select the option which shows correct combination of an organism and its feature.','[{"text": "<i>Echinus</i> - Well-developed excretory system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Dentalium</i> - Metameric segmentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Bombyx</i> - External fertilisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Balanoglossus</i> - Body is divided into proboscis, collar and trunk", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<i>Balanoglossus</i> is a hemichordate. In hemichordates, body is divided into a proboscis, collar and a long trunk. <i>Echinus</i> is an echinoderm. Special excretory organs area absent in echinoderms. <i>Dentalium</i> is a mollusc. Molluscs are unsegmented. Fertilization is mostly internal in arthropods (e.g. <i>Bombyx</i>), except a few aquatic forms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9315,'biology',86,980,2285,'Consider the following statements.<br>I. Thoracic chamber which contain lungs is anatomically an sound-tight chamber.<br>II. Change in the volume of thoracic cavity does not affect the pulmonary cavity.<br>Select the correct option.','[{"text": "I is true, II is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I is false, II is true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are false", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Thoracic chamber which contain lungs is anatomically an air-tight chamber.<br>Change in the volume of thoracic cavity affects the pulmonary cavity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9316,'biology',84,583,1169,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The RBCs, WBCs and platelets are enucleated in frogs.</div><div class="column-right">Frogs, are omnivores and nocturnal</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the statements are incorrect. In frog RBC\'s are nucleated and contain red coloured pigment namely haemoglobin. Frogs, are insectivores and nocturnal.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9317,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Which of the following organs has chordae tendinae and papillary muscles?','[{"text": "Lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heart", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Arteries", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aorta", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Heart has papillary muscles and chordae tendinae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9318,'biology',83,499,1015,'Which of the following is not a body part of <i>Balanoglossus</i>','[{"text": "Proboscis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trunk", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tail", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Body of <i>Balanoglossus</i> is divided in 3 parts only namely proboscis , collar, Trunk but not tail.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9319,'biology',84,583,1171,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">External ears are present in frog.<br></div><div class="column-right">There is presence of cloaca in male frogs for the excretion of urine, fecal matter and sperms</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'External ear is absent in frogs and only tympanum can be seen externally.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9320,'biology',86,983,2288,'Consider the folllowing statements.<br>I. Red coloured iron containing pigment in RBCs is haemoglobin.<br>II. $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ binds with haemoglobin reversible to form oxyhaemoglobin.<br>Select the correct option.','[{"text": "I is true, II is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are true", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I is false, II is true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are false", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9324,'biology',86,980,2285,'Read the following statements.<br>I. On an average a healthy human breathes 72times/minute<br>II. The volume of air involved in the breathing movements can be estimated by barometer<br>III. Diaphragm is very useful in both inspiration and expiration.<br>Which of the above statements are incorrect?','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'On an average, a healthy human breathes 12-16 times/minute.<br>The volume of air involved in breathing movements can be estimated by using a spirometer which helps in clinical assessment of pulmonary functions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9325,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Tricuspid valve is present between','[{"text": "Left atrium and left ventricle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Right atrium and right ventricle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Right atrium and left ventricle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Left atrium and right ventricle", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The opening between the right atrium and the right ventricle is guarded by a valve formed of three muscular flaps or cusps, the tricuspid valve.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9326,'biology',83,505,1023,'Which of the following animals does not undergo metamorphosis?','[{"text": "<i>Naja</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Rana</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Salpa</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pila</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Development in reptiles (e.g., <i>Naja</i>) is direct. In <i>Rana, Salpa and Pila</i>, development is indirect and includes a larval stage.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9327,'biology',86,983,2288,'Consider the following statements.<br>I. At the alveolar site, $$\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ is low due to which $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$$ are formed.<br>II. The $$\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ level at the tissue is high due to catabolism.<br>Select the correct option.','[{"text": "I is true, II is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I is false, II is true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are true", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both I and II are false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9329,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Ventricles are thick-walled as compared to atrium because','[{"text": "It is to receive blood from atria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is present on the posterior side", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It has to pump blood to far away distances", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ventricles are thick-walled as compared to atrium because it has to pump blood to far away distances.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9330,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which of the following represents the correct combination of a taxonomic group with its characteristics, without any exception?<br>Group Characteristics','[{"text": "Reptilia-Crawling mode of locomotion, all are terrestrial", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chondrichthyes-Placoid scales, electric organs, claspers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphibia-Tympanum, two pairs of limbs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mammalia-Mammary glands, lungs, direct development", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All mammals possess mammary glands, lungs and undergo direct development. Some reptiles are aquatic (e.g., sea snakes, turtles).<br>Electric organs are present only in some cartilaginous fishes (e.g.,<i>Torpedo</i>); not all. Some amphibians are limbless (e.g., Ichthyophis).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9331,'biology',84,583,1169,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Eyes of the frog are bulged and covered by nictiating membrane.<br></div><div class="column-right">Heart of the frog possesses sinus venosus and conus arteriosus</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9332,'biology',86,984,2289,'Consider the following statements.<br>I. Neural signals from pneumotaxic centre can reduce the duration of expiration and thus, alter the respiratory rate.<br>II. The role of oxygen in the regulation of respiratory rhythm is quite insignificant.<br>Select the correct option.','[{"text": "I is false, II is true", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both I and II are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I is true, II is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are false", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Neural signal from pneumotaxic centre can reduce the duration of inspiration and thereby alter the respiratory rate.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9333,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Which of the following has the thickest wall?','[{"text": "Left auricle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Left ventricle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Right auricle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Right ventricle", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'As it has to pump blood from heart to all the parts of the body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10132,'biology',9,24,43,'Cell wall of green algae is made up of','[{"text": "Cellulose only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pectose only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pectin and cellulose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellulose and pectose", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Green algae usually have a rigid cell wall made of an inner layer of cellulose and an outer layer of pectose.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9334,'biology',83,506,1024,'Which of the following animal groups is correctly paired with its characteristic?','[{"text": "Amphibia : Skin is without scales and eyes are without eyelids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osteichthyes : Marine and freshwater fishes with bony endoskeleton and ventral mouth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reptilia : Mostly terrestrial animals with dry and cornified skin, epidermal scales or scutes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aves : Feathered bipedal poikilotherms with pneumatic bones and air sacs", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Reptiles are mostly terrestrial animals with dry and cornified skin, epidermal scales or scutes. Amphibians have eyelids. Bony fishes have a terminal mouth. Aves are homeotherms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9335,'biology',84,583,1171,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Bidder canal is present in kidneys into which vasa efferentia opens in male frog.<br></div><div class="column-right">Development is indirect through tadpole larva in frog.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9336,'biology',86,979,2284,'The dorsal, ventral, lateral and lower side of thoracic chamber is bounded by ____ respectively','[{"text": "Vertebral column, sternum, ribs, diaphragm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vertebral column, ribs, sternum, diaphragm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diaphragm, ribs, sternum, vertebral column", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribs, diaphragm, sternum, vertebral column", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The thoracic chamber is formed dorsally by vertebral column, ventrally by the sternum, laterally by the ribs and on the lower side of the dome-shaped diaphragm',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9337,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Identify the valves which allow blood from ventricles into its respective blood vessels?','[{"text": "Aortic valve and mitral valve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bicuspid valves and semilunar valves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bicuspid and tricuspids valves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AV valves and semilunar valves", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The openings of the right and the left ventricles into the pulmonary artery and the aorta respectively are provided with the semilunar valves. The valves in the heart allows the flow of blood only in one direction, i.e., from the atria to the ventricles and from the ventricles to the pulmonary artery or aorta. These valves prevent any backward flow. AV valves and semilunar valves allow blood from ventricles into its respective blood vessels.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9338,'biology',83,506,1024,'Aves originated from reptiles. Which of the following is not an advancement of birds over reptiles?','[{"text": "Homeothermy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Complete double circulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insulated body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Scales on the hindlimbs", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Scales are present in reptiles also.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9339,'biology',84,583,1169,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Frog does not have hepatic portal system .<br></div><div class="column-right">Frog is not a poikilotherm</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the statements are incorrect. Frogs have hepatic portal system. Frog is a poikilothermic ani-mal.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9340,'biology',86,983,2288,'People who have migrated from the planes to an area adjoining Rohtang Pass about six months back','[{"text": "Are not physically fit to play games like football.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Have more RBC and their haemoglobin has a lower binding affinity to $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Have the usual RBC count but their haemoglobin has very high binding affinity to $$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Suffer from altitude sickness with symptoms like nausea, fatigue, etc.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'At higher altitude haemoglobin has a lower binding affinity to $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$. Hence, people who have migrated from planes to an area adjoining Rohtang pass (more than $$10000 \\mathrm{~m}$$ height) for about six months have more RBCs to compensate for the low binding affinity of haemoglogin to oxygen.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9341,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Which of the following valves come in contact with deoxygenated blood?<br>A. Semilunar pulmonary valve<br>B. Mitral<br>C. Bicuspid<br>D. Tricuspid<br>E. Semilunar aortic valve','[{"text": "A, B, C and E only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, D and E only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and D only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A, E and D only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Semilunar valve and tricuspid valve come in contact with deoxygenated blood.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9342,'biology',83,502,1020,'Consider following features:<br>(a) Internal fertilization<br>(b) A pair of jaws<br>(c) Mostly viviparous<br>Select the correct option of animal groups which possess all the above characteristics.','[{"text": "Chondrichthyes and Osteichthyes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reptilia and Mammalia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphibia and Mammalia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chondrichthyes and Mammalia", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both Chondrichthyes and Mammalia belong to Gnathostomata (have jaws). They are mostly viviparous and exhibit internal fertilisation. Osteichthyes, amphibians and reptiles are mostly oviparous.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9343,'biology',86,985,2290,'Identify the wrong statement:','[{"text": "Asthma is caused due to spasm of bronchial muscles.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Yawning occurs due to excess of oxygen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pneumotaxic centre for respiration is located in pons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Respiratory rhythm centre is located in medulla region of brain.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A yawning occurs when one\'s blood contains increased amounts of carbon dioxide and therefore becomes in need of the influx of oxygen (or expulsion of carbon dioxide) that a yawn can provide.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9374,'biology',83,494,1010,'Which of the following statements is correct with regard to <i>Ascaris</i>?','[{"text": "Nephridia help in excretion and osmoregulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alimentary canal is complete with a well developed muscular pharynx", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Males are longer than females", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Body cavity is lined by peritoneum", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In Aschelminthes, alimentary canal is complete with a well-developedmuscular pharynx. Nephridia are absent. Females are longer. Body cavity is pseudocoelom which is not lined by peritoneum.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
