(9347,'biology',86,985,2290,'Which one of the following is the correct staement for respiration in human','[{"text": "Neural signals from pneumotaxic centre in pons region of brain can increase the duration of inspiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cigarette smoking may lead of inflammation of bronchi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "About $$20-25 \\\\%$$ of carbon dioxide $$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}\\\\right)$$ is carried by haemoglobin as carbamino haemoglobin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Workers in grinding sandstone - breaking industries may suffer, from Asthma", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Nearly 20-25 per cent of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is transported by RBCs whereas 70 per cent of it is carried as bicarbonate. About 7 per cent of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is carried in a dissolved state through plasma.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
