(9350,'biology',83,490,1006,'Identify the correct characteristics of Porifera.<br>(i) Commonly known as sea walnuts.<br>(ii) Presence of ostia and collar cells.<br>(iii) Exhibit tissue level of characteristics.<br>(iv) It is the largest phylum of animal kingdom.<br>(v) The body is supported by spicules and spongin fibers.<br>(vi) Contains cnidocytes which is used for defense, anchorage and capturing of prey.','[{"text": "(ii), (v) only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(i), (ii), (vi) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i), (ii), (iii), (iv)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Porifera is commonly referred to as sponges. They are multicellular organisms that have bodies full of pores and channels allowing water to circulate through them, consisting of jelly-like sandwiched between two thin layers of cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9351,'biology',84,579,1159,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The cells of connective tissues except blood secrete fibres<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Fibres provide strength, elasticity and flexibility to the tissue','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Fibroblast are the cells which produce various types of fibres. Blood lacks fibroblast cells.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9352,'biology',86,983,2288,'The correct statements about respiration are<br>I. In cockroach gaseous exchanges occurs mainly between tracheoles and haemoymph<br>II. Increase in inspiratory capacity does not involve an increase in tidal volume<br>III. Partial pressure of oxygen in blood is less than that in alveoli<br>IV. Chloride shift in erythrocytes maintain the ionic balance','[{"text": "I, III and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Increase in inspiratory capacity does involve an increase in tidal volume as,<br>Inspiratory capacity $$=$$ tidal volume + inspiratory reserve volume.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9353,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Which of the following term does not apply to human heart?','[{"text": "Muscular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four chambered", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pericardium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neurogenic", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Heart is not neurogenic, heart is myogenic. Normal activities of the heart are regulated intrinsically, i.e., auto regulated by specialised muscles (nodal tissue), hence the heart is called myogenic.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9354,'biology',83,491,1007,'Cnidocytes do not help in','[{"text": "Regeneration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anchorage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Defence", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prey capture", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cnidarians have cnidoblasts or cnidocytes (which contain the stinging capsules ornemato cysts) on the tentacles and the body. Cnidoblasts are used for anchorage, defense and for the capture of prey.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9355,'biology',84,579,1159,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Tendons attach one bone to another<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Ligaments attach skeletal muscles to bones','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Tendon connects a skeletal muscle to a bone. Ligament connects a bone to another bone.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9356,'biology',86,984,2289,'The most important afferent (sensory) receptors for the respiratory response to systemic arterial carbon dioxide are the','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ receptors of the aortic and carotid bodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$receptors of the aortic and carotid bodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ receptors in the medulla of the brain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$receptors in the medulla of the brain", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The most important receptors in chemical regulation of ventilation by carbon dioxide are the hydrogen ion receptors in the medulla, since the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ of CSF and brain interstitial fluid are controlled by blood $$\\mathrm{pCO}_{2}$$ as $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ readily crosses the blood-brain barrier.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9357,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Heart<br>B. Pericardium<br>C. Atria<br>D. Ventricles</div><div class="column-right">P. Double walled membranous bag protecting heart<br>Q. Small upper chambers of heart<br>R. Larger lower chambers of heart<br>S. Mesoderm in origin</div></div>','[{"text": "A-S, B-P, C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-S, C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Heart - mesodermal in origin<br>Pericardium - Double walled membranous bag protecting heart<br>Atria - small upper chambers of heart<br>Ventricles - Larger lower chambers of heart.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
