(9363,'biology',86,981,2286,'Pick the correct statement.','[{"text": "Contraction of internal intercostal muscles lifts up the ribs and sternum.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RBCs transport oxygen only.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Healthy man can inspire approximately $$500 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$ of air per minute.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thoracic cavity is anatomically an air tight chamber.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Contraction of external intercostal muscles lifts up the ribs and sternum. RBCs transport both oxygen and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ Healthy mam can inspire approximately 6000-8000 mL of air per minute.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9393,'biology',83,504,1022,'Which one of the following is not a character of <i>Rana</i>?','[{"text": "Tympanum represents ear", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Body is divided into head, trunk and tail", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Skin is moist and lacks scales", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cloaca receives urine, faeces and gametes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In frogs (e.g.<i> Rana</i>), body is divided into head and trunk. Tails is absent. Tail is present in some amphibians (e.g., <i>salamanders</i>).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9365,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Bicuspid valve<br>B. Tricuspid valve<br>C. Semilunar valve</div><div class="column-right">P. Guards the opening of right and left ventricles into the pulmonary artery and aorta respectively<br>Q. Guards the opening between right atrium and right ventricle<br>R. Guards the opening between left atrium and the left ventricle</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bicuspid valve - Guards the opening between left atrium and left ventricle<br>Tricuspid valve - Guards the opening between right atrium and right ventricle<br>Semilunar valve - Guards the opening of right and left ventricles into the pulmonary artery and aorta respectively',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9366,'biology',83,495,1011,'In which one of the following, the genus name and its two characters are correctly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<i>Hirudinaria</i> is monoecious and exhibits metamerism. In Fasciola, alimentary canal is incomplete. <i>Meandrina</i> lacks comb plates. <i>Ancylostoma</i> is bilaterally symmetrical.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
