(10274,'biology',89,1287,3108,'In a running race, which is the major source of energy to the leg muscle?','[{"text": "Glycolysis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pyruvate and lactate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Starch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxidative metabolism", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In a running race, glycolysis is the major source of energy to the leg muscle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9821,'biology',87,1128,2700,'Read statements regarding cardiac system and choose the right option<br>I. Human heart is an ectodermal derivative<br>II. Mitral valve guards the left upper corner of the right atrium<br>III. SAN is located on the upper corner of the right atrium<br>IV. Cardiac output $$=$$ Heart rate $$\\times$$ Stroke volume','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The amount of blood pumped by heart per minute is called cardiac output. Cardiac output of humans is approximately 5 litres per minute. Cardiac output is also the volume of blood flowing through either the systemic or the pulmonary circuit per minute. It is determined by multiplying the heart rate with the volume of blood ejected by each ventricle during each beat, which is called the stroke volume. Cardiac output $$=$$ Heart rate $$\\times$$ Stroke volume',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9822,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Muscle is a tissue of ____ origin','[{"text": "Endodemal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesodermal", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ectodermal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Muscle is a specialised tissue of mesodermal origin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9823,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Glomerular filtrate doesnot contain','[{"text": "Albumin, blood cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glucose, water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NaCl}$$, urea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Creatinine, urea", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Glomerular filtrate contains all components of plasma except blood proteins and fats. Blood cells like RBCs, WBCs, platelets and albumins are not found in the filtrate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9824,'biology',87,1128,2700,'A normal healthy person is about to go for a run. What is his pulse rate at rest?','[{"text": "$$50-80$$ beats per minute", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$70-90$$ beats per minute", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$50-70$$ beats per minute", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$40-70$$ beats per minute", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Normal pulse rate ranges from $$70-90$$ per minute.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9825,'biology',89,1285,3106,'What percent of the body weight of a human adult is contributed by muscles?','[{"text": "$50-60$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$60-70$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$40-50$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$20-30$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'About $40-50$ percent of the body weight of a human adult is contributed by muscles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9826,'biology',88,1152,2759,'In a glomerulus','[{"text": "Afferent arteriole is thicker than efferent arteriole.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Afferent capillaries are thicker than efferent capillaries.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Afferent capillaries are thinner than efferent capillaries.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Afferent arteriole is thinner than efferent arteriole.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The afferent arteriole is larger in diameter than the efferent arteriole. Afferent arteriole being thicker compared to efferent arteriole, helps create filtration pressure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9827,'biology',87,1128,2700,'Choose the incorrect answer regarding pulse rate:<br>i. The normal pulse for healthy adults ranges from 60 to 100 beats per minute.<br>ii. The pulse rate does not fluctuate and increase with exercise illness, injury and emotions.<br>iii. Female aged 12 and older in general tend to have faster heart rates than males.<br>iv. Athletes such as runners, who do a lot of cardiovascular conditioning may have heart rates near 40 beats per minute and experience no problems.','[{"text": "ii only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{i}$ and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'ii only is incorrect. The normal pulse for healthy adults ranges from 60 to 100 beats per minute. The pulse rate may fluctuate and increase with exercise, illness, injury, and emotions. Females ages 12 and older, in<br>general, tend to have faster heart rates than do males. Athletes, such as runners, who do a lot of cardiovascular conditioning, may have heart rates near 40 beats per minute and experience no problems.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9828,'biology',89,1285,3106,'List the properties of muscles','[{"text": "Excitability", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contractility", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Extensibility", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'About 40-50 percent of the body weight of a human adult is contributed by muscles. They have special properties like excitability, contractility, extensibility and elasticity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9829,'biology',88,1152,2759,'The glomerular filtrate, i.e., the liquid collected in the cavity of Bowman\'s capsule is','[{"text": "Blood minus proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood minus proteins and corpuscles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Blood minus water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood minus urine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Blood is filtered so finely through the filtration membrane, that almost all the constituents of the plasma except the proteins and corpuscles pass onto the lumen of the Bowman\'s capsule.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9830,'biology',87,1128,2700,'Choose incorrect statement among the following:<br>I. Pulse is the mechanical pulse of blood flow through capillaries caused by the contractions of heart per minute.<br>II. Pulse can be measured from an ear lobe with a pulse meter containing a photocell sensor.<br>III. Pulse can also be measured by palpating during rest.<br>IV. A pulse is the expansion and contraction of an artery caused by the ejection of blood from the left side of the heart.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Palpating is not an accurate method to receive exercise heart rate. If one wants to check his/her exercise heart rate manually, the measurement should be done immediately after stopping because heart rate will start to slow down as the body recovers.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9831,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Based on their location, three types of muscles are identified. What are they?','[{"text": "Skeletal, Visceral and Pulmonary.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Muscular, Visceral and Cardiac.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Skeletal, Visceral and Cardiac.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Skeletal, Visceral and Hepatic.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Based on their location, three types of muscles are identified : (i) Skeletal (ii) Visceral and (iii) Cardiac.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9832,'biology',88,1152,2759,'The amount of the filtrate formed by the kidneys are','[{"text": "$$125 \\\\mathrm{ml} / \\\\mathrm{min}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "180 litre/day", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 litre/ day", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The amount of filtrate formed by the kidneys per minute is called glomerular filtration rate (GFR). GFR is a healthy individual is $$125 \\mathrm{~mL} /$$ $$\\min$$ or $$180 \\mathrm{~L} /$$ day.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9835,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Choose the correct option for the layers present between the glomerulus and Bowman\'s capsule.','[{"text": "Epithelium is the layer of glomerular blood vessels", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Basement membrane is present between the endothelium and epithelium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Endothelium is the layer of Bowman\'s capsule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Basement membrane is present between the endothelium and epithelium',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9836,'biology',87,1128,2700,'Which of the following statement is incorrect?','[{"text": "The body has the ability to alter the stroke volume as well as the heart rate and thereby the cardiac output.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In each minute a single cardiac cycle is performed.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "During each cardiac cycle two prominent sounds are produced.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cardiac cycle includes atrial systole, ventricular systole and joint diastole.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In each minute a 72 cardiac cycles are performed.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9837,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Skeletal muscles are controlled by','[{"text": "Autonomic nerves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parasympathetic nervous sytem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sympathetic nerves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Central nervous system", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Activities of skeletal muscles are under the voluntary control of the central nervous system, they are known as voluntary muscles too.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9838,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Select the correct matching.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "PCT $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Proximal Conducting Tube", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GFR $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Glomerular Filtration Ratio", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DCT $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Distal Convoluted Tubule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "JGA $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Juxtaglomerular Action", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The ascending limb of Loop of Henle continues as a highly coiled tubular region called distal convoluted tubule (DCT).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9839,'biology',87,1125,2697,'Select correct combination of statements for lymph:<br>I. It is contained in lymphatic vessels and lymphatic organs in mammals<br>II. It is derived from tissue fluid<br>III. It contains less antibodies than plasma<br>IV. It flows from tissue<br>V. It helps to conserve proteins and remove bacteria<br>VI. It helps to maintain fluid balance of the body','[{"text": "II,III, IV and V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III and V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "V, I, II, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Lymph destroys the invading microorganisms and foreign particles in the lymph nodes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9840,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Skeletal muscles have a striped appearance under the microscope and hence are called','[{"text": "Unstriated muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Striated muscles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Voluntary muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Smooth muscles", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Skeletal muscles have a striped appearance under the microscope and hence are called striated muscles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9841,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Juxta Glomerular Apparatus (JGA) which regulates the glomerular filtration rate is formed at the point of contact of','[{"text": "DCT and PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DCT and efferent arteriole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DCT and afferent arteriole", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Loop of Henle and DCT", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'JGA is a special sensitive region formed by cellular modifications in the Distal Convoluted Tubule (DCT) and the afferent arteriole at the location of their contact. The kidneys have built in mechanisms for the regulation of glomerular filtration rate. One such efficient mechanism is carried out by Juxta Glomerular Apparatus (JGA).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9842,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Select the correct answer<br>I. As their activities are under the voluntary control of the nervous system.<br>II. They are primarily involved in locomotory actions<br>III. They attach to the bone system of the body<br>The above statements reflect which muscle?','[{"text": "Unstriated muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cardiac muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Voluntary muscles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Smooth muscles", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Skeletal muscles are closely associated with the skeletal components of the body. They have a striped appearance under the microscope and hence are called striated muscles. As their activities are under the voluntary control of the nervous system, they are known as voluntary muscles too. They are primarily involved in locomotory actions and changes of body postures.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9843,'biology',87,1132,2704,'Symptoms of a heart attack can include','[{"text": "Dizziness, weakness, arm pain, pressure in the chest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heart palpations, shortness of breath, pressure in the chest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shortness of breath, pressure in the chest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Many symptoms of heart disease include fatigue, weakness, shortness of breath, weakness, shortness of breath, dizziness, palpitations, chest discomfort or pain, chest heaviness, nausea, vomiting and pain that radiates to jaw, arm and throat.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9844,'biology',88,1152,2759,'A ___ in GFR can activate the JG cells to release ____ which can stimulate the glomerular blood flow and thereby the GFR back to normal','[{"text": "rise, renin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "fall, renin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "fall, rennin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "rise, rennin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A fall in GFR can activate the JG cells to release renin which can stimulate the glomerular blood flow and thereby the GFR back to normal',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9845,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Which of the following muscles are primarily involved in locomotory actions and changes of body postures?','[{"text": "Skeletal muscles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Visceral muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cardiac muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Skeletal muscles are primarily involved in locomotary actions and changes of body postures.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9857,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Non striated muscles help in','[{"text": "Peristalsis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transfer of gametes through genital tract", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Micturition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Smooth muscles assist, for example, in the transportation of food through the digestive tract (peristalsis), transfer of gametes through the genital tract and micturition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9846,'biology',87,1132,2704,'Which of the following options correctly represents the heart conditions in heart failure and heart attack, respectively?','[{"text": "The heart stops beating; heart muscle is suddenly damaged by an inadequate blood supply", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The heart is not pumping blood effectively; the heart stops beating", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The heart is not pumping blood effectively; heart muscle is suddenly damaged by an inadequate blood supply", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Acute chest pain when no enough oxygen is reaching the heart muscle; the heart stops beating", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Heart failure means the state of heart when it is not pumping blood effectively enough to meet the needs of the body. In case of heart attack, the heart muscle is suddenly damaged by an inadequate blood supply.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9847,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Visceral muscles are also called','[{"text": "Smooth muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Involuntary muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Striated muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Visceral muscles do not exhibit any striation and are smooth in appearance. Hence, they are called smooth muscles (nonstriated muscle). The activities of smooth muscles are not under the voluntary control of the nervous system and are therefore known as involuntary muscles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9848,'biology',88,1152,2759,'The glomerular filtration rate would be increased by','[{"text": "Constriction of the efferent arteriole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "An increase in afferent arteriolar pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Constriction of the afferent arteriole", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "An increase in the renal blood flow", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Constrictory effects on blood vessels, brought by hormone like ADH, this causes an increase in blood pressure. An increase in blood pressure can increase the glomerular blood flow and thereby the GFR',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9849,'biology',87,1123,2695,'Which of the following transfusions would carry the least risk?','[{"text": "O- plasma to $$\\\\mathrm{AB}+$$ patient", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "O-whole blood to $$\\\\mathrm{AB}+$$ patient", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{O}+$$ packed cells to $$\\\\mathrm{A}+$$ patient", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B-whole blood to $$\\\\mathrm{O}+$$ patient", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$$\\mathrm{Ag}=$$ antigens; $$\\mathrm{Ab}=$$ antibodies In case (1) and (2), the antibodies in the plasma of the donor can clump A, B, D antigens on the RBC of the recipient. In case (3), donors $$\\mathrm{RBC}$$ have $$\\mathrm{D}$$ antigen but there is no anti-D antibody in the plasma of the recipient.Though recipient has A and $$\\mathrm{D}$$ antigens on $$\\mathrm{RBC}$$, there are no antibodies to clump them. What is donated is packed cells (only blood corpuscles but no plasma)In case (4), anti-B antibodies in the blood plasma of the recipient can clump donors $$\\mathrm{RBC}$$ which have $$\\mathrm{B}$$ antigen. Furthermore, anti-D antibodies in the donor\'s blood plasma can clump recipient $$\\mathrm{RBC}$$ which have $$\\mathrm{D}$$ antigen.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9850,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Visceral muscles are likely to be found in','[{"text": "Digestive system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reproductive tract", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Urinary system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Visceral muscles are located in the inner walls of hollow visceral organs of the body like the alimentary canal, reproductive tract, urinary system etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9851,'biology',88,1152,2759,'A fall in the GFR activates the','[{"text": "JG cells to release renin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "JG cells to release aldosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "JG cells to release epinephrin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "JG cells to release rennin", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Fall in Glomerular Blood Flow (GBF)/ Glomerular Blood Pressure (GBP)/ and low Glomerular Filtration Rate (GFR) activates the Juxta Glomerular (JG) cells in the kidneys to release renin which brings the GFR back to normal.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9852,'biology',87,1126,2698,'Which of the following is absent in an animal with a closed circulatory system?','[{"text": "Haemocoel", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood vessels", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hemoceol is absent in an animal with a closed circulatory system. In closed circulatory system, the blood pumped by the heart is always circulated through a closed network of blood vessels.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9853,'biology',89,1285,3106,'The activities of the visceral muscles are not under the voluntary control of the nervous system and are therefore known as','[{"text": "Non-striated muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Smooth muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Involuntary muscles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The activities of the visceral muscles are not under the voluntary control of the nervous system and are therefore known as involuntary muscles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9854,'biology',88,1152,2759,'GFR in a healthy individual is','[{"text": "$$125 \\\\mathrm{~mL} / \\\\mathrm{min}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$150 \\\\mathrm{~L} /$$ day", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$125 \\\\mathrm{~mL} / \\\\mathrm{sec}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$135 \\\\mathrm{~L} /$$ day", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Glomerular Filtration Rate (GFR) in a healthy individual is approximately $$125 \\mathrm{~mL} /$$ minute, i.e. 180 litres per day. GFR is the amount of the filtrate formed by the kidneys per minute.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9855,'biology',87,1126,2698,'Consider the following statements regarding open circulatory system:<br>I. In the open circulatory system blood flows into hemocoel with blood diffusing back to the cells.<br>II. Blood flow is sluggish.<br>III. Insects, molluscs and other invertebrates have an open system.<br>Which of the above are incorrect?','[{"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The open circulatory system is common to molluscs and arthropods. Open circulatory systems (evolved in crustaceans, insects, molluscs and other invertebrates) pumps blood into a hemocoel with the blood diffusing back to the circulatory system between cells. Blood is pumped by a heart into the body cavities, where tissues are surrounded by the blood.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9856,'biology',88,1152,2759,'How much percentage of the filtrate is reabsorbed if volume of filtrate formed per day is $$180 \\mathrm{~L}$$ and urine released is $$1.5 \\mathrm{~L}$$ ?','[{"text": "$$70-80 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$85 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$99 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$90 \\\\%$$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A comparison of the volume of the filtrate formed per day (180 L per day) with that of the urine released $$(1.5 \\mathrm{~L})$$, suggests that nearly $$99 \\%$$ of this filtrate has to be reabsorbed by the renal tubules.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9858,'biology',87,1127,2699,'It shows pulmonary circulation','[{"text": "Left atrium (deoxygenated blood) - Lungs (oxygenated blood) - Left atrium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Left atrium (oxygenated blood) - Lungs (deoxygenated blood) - Right atrium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Right atrium (deoxygenated blood) - Lungs (oxygenated blood) - Left atrium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Left atrium (oxygenated blood) - Lungs (deoxygenated blood) - Left atrium", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The pulmonary circulation is the portion of the circulatory system which carries deoxygenated blood away from the right ventricle of the heart, to the lungs, and returns oxygenated blood to the left atrium and ventricle of the heart.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9859,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Completely involuntary unstriated muscles occur in','[{"text": "Base of pinna", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abdomen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eye lids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pylorus", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pylorus is region of stomach that leads to duodenum of intestine, it is made of smooth muscles, which are completely involuntary and unstriated.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9860,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Reabsorption takes place in the?','[{"text": "Glomerulus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glomerulus and Bowman\'s capsule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glomerulus and Bowman\'s capsule and PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PCT, Loop of Henle, DCT, Collecting duct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Reabsorption is the second step of urine formation. It takes place in the renal tubules like PCT, DCT, Loop of Henle and collecting duct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9861,'biology',87,1132,2704,'How many statements are wrong?<br>i. Systemic circulation takes place between left ventricle and right atrium of heart.<br>ii. Adrenal medullary hormones can increase the cardiac output.<br>iii. Heart failure is not the same as cardiac arrest or heart attack<br>iv. The opening between the right atrium and the right ventricle is guarded by a valve formed by two muscular flops','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The opening between the right atrium and the right ventricle is guarded by bicuspid valve.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9862,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Muscles causing movement of food in stomach','[{"text": "Striated", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cardiac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unstriated", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Specialized", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Muscles that cause movement of food in stomach are the unstriated muscles. Unstriated muscles are the smooth muscles they are involuntary muscles which are under control of autonomic nervous system. Smooth muscles maintain prolonged contraction. The smooth muscles help in peristalsis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9863,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Substances like glucose, amino acids, $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$, etc., in the filtrate are reabsorbed ____ whereas the nitrogenous wastes are absorbed by ____ transport?','[{"text": "passively, passively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "actively, passively", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "passively, actively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "actively, actively", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Substances like glucose, amino acids, $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$, etc., in the filtrate are reabsorbed actively whereas the nitrogenous wastes are absorbed by passive transport.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9864,'biology',87,1127,2699,'In a study of a blood vessels $$\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{C}$$ and $$\\mathrm{D}$$ in man. Vessel \'A\' carried pure blood away from heart, Vessel \'B\' carried impure blood towards heart, Vessel \' $$C$$ \' carried pure blood into the heart musculature while Vessel \'D\' carried impure blood away from heart. The correct name of four vesssels can be','[{"text": "Systemic aorta - A, Vena cava - B, Coronary artery - C, Pulmonary artery-D", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coronary artery - A, Pulmonary vein - B, Pulmonary artery $$-\\\\mathrm{C}, \\\\mathrm{SVN}-\\\\mathrm{D}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pulmonary vein - A, Pulmonary artery B, Coronary artery - C, Vena cava - D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Systemic aorta - A, Pulmonary vein - B, Coronary artery $$-\\\\mathrm{C}$$, Pulmonary artery- D", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'b. Systemic aorta - A, Vena cava - B, Coronary artery $$-\\mathrm{C}$$, Pulmonary artery $$-\\mathrm{D}$$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9865,'biology',9,23,40,'Kingdom-Plantae includes classes','[{"text": "Algae, mosses, fungi bryophytes and pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae, liverworts, pteridophyte, gymnosperms and angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae, fungi, pteridophytes, gymnosperms and angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae, bryophyta, pteridophytes, gymnosperms and angiosperms", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Classes Algae, Bryophyta, Pteridophyta, Gymnosperm and Angiosperm are included in Kingdom Plantae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
