(9870,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Read the following 4- statements (I-IV) and accordingly mark the option that has both correct statements<br>I. Cardiac fibres are branched with one nucleus<br>II. Smooth muscles are unbranched and cylindrical<br>III. Striated muscles can be branched or unbranched<br>IV. Involuntary muscles are non-striated','[{"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cardiac fibres are branched with one nucleus. Involuntary muscles are non-striated are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9871,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Choose the correct statement about absorption in renal tubules from the following:','[{"text": "Glucose, amino acids and $$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$reabsorbed actively.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nitrogenous waste are absorbed by passive transport.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reabsorption of water also occurs passively in the initial segments of the nephron", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Substances like glucose, amino acids, $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$, etc., in the filtrate are reabsorbed actively whereas the nitrogenous wastes are absorbed by passive transport. Reabsorption of water also occurs passively in the initial segments of the nephron.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9872,'biology',87,1128,2700,'Which of the following statements are true of the cardiac cycle of a healthy young adult?<br>I. During ventricular diastole, the pressure in the left ventricle is close to $$80 \\mathrm{~mm} \\mathrm{Hg}$$ (10.5 kpa).<br>II. During ventricular systole, the pressure in the left ventricle reaches a maximum of about $$25 \\mathrm{~mm} \\mathrm{Hg}$$ (3.5 kpa).<br>III. During the initial stage of ventricular contraction the volume of the ventricle doesnot change.<br>IV. During ventricular systole, all the blood in the ventricles is ejected.','[{"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During the cardiac cycle the pressure in the left ventricle is around zero during diastole and $$120 \\mathrm{~mm}$$ of $$\\mathrm{Hg}$$ (16 Kpa) at the peak of systole.<br>Only about $$60 \\%$$ of the diastole volume is ejected during ventricular systole.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9873,'biology',9,23,40,'Artificial system of classification was given by','[{"text": "Benthan and Hooker", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carolus Linnaeus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Carolus Aristotle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Robert Linnaeus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The earliest systems of classification used only gross superficial morphological characters such as habit, colour, number and shape of leaves, etc. They were based mainly on vegetative characters or on the androecium structure. Such systems were artificial and were given by Carlos Linnaeus',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9874,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Match the columns I and II?<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Skeletal muscles<br>B. Smooth muscles<br>C. Cardiac muscles</div><div class="column-right">P. Nonstriated muscle<br>Q. Voluntary muscle<br>R. Striated but involuntary</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Skeletal muscles - Voluntary muscles<br>Smooth muscles - Non-striated muscles<br>Cardiac muscles - Striated but involuntary',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9875,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Tubular secretion secrete substances like ____ into the filtrate.','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}, \\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$and ammonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}, \\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$$and ammonia", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During urine formation, the tubular cells secrete substances like $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}, \\mathrm{K}^{+}$$and ammonia into the filtrate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9876,'biology',87,1128,2700,'The cardiac events that occur from the beginning of the heart beat to the next heart beat are called the cardiac cycle. During the cardiac cycle:','[{"text": "The atria and the ventricles contract simultaneously", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The atria contract before the ventricles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The ventricles contract before the atria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The period of time that begins with contraction of the atria and ends with ventricular relaxation is known as the cardiac cycle. The period of contraction that the heart undergoes while it pumps blood into circulation is called systole. The period of relaxation that occurs as the chambers fill with blood is called diastole. Both the atria and ventricles undergo systole and diastole, and it is essential that these components be carefully regulated and coordinated to ensure blood is pumped efficiently to the body.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9877,'biology',9,23,40,'The earliest classification used only','[{"text": "Gross physiological characters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gross anatomical characters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gross superficial morphological characters", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gross internal morphological characters", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The earliest systems of classification used only gross superficial morphological characters such as habit, colour, number and shape of leaves, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9878,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Intercostal muscle occurs is between','[{"text": "Abdomen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thigh", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Diaphragm", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Intercostal muscle occur in the ribs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9879,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Tubular secretion helps in','[{"text": "Ionic balance of body fluid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acid base balance of body fluid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Tubular secretion is an important step in urine formation as it helps in the maintenance of ionic and acid base balance of body fluids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9880,'biology',87,1128,2700,'Which of the following events do not occur during joint diastole?<BR>I. All 4 chambers of heart are in relaxed state<BR>II. Tricuspid and bicuspid valves open<BR>III. Action potential is conducted from SAN to AVN<br>IV. Blood from the pulmonary veins and vena cava flows into the left and right ventricles respectively through the left and right atria<br>V. The semilunar valves are closed','[{"text": "Only V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only I and II", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Action potential is conducted from SAN to AVN just before depolarization of ventricles (contraction).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9881,'biology',9,23,40,'The gross superficial morphological characters considered under artificial system classification were','[{"text": "Habit, colour, number and shape of leaves", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All morphological features of the plant.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only evolutionary evidences.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both evolutionary and morphological characters.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The gross superficial morphological characters considered under artificial system classification were  habit, colour, number and shape of leaves.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9882,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Which muscle go into fatigue?','[{"text": "Striped", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Unstriped", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cardiac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Involuntnary", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Skeletal muscle(striped muscles) get fatigue.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9883,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Podocytes<br>B. GFR<br>C. Blood filtered by kidneys per minute<br>D. Juxta Glomerular apparatus</div><div class="column-right">P. 125 ml/min<br>Q. 1100-1200 ml/min<br>R. Special sensitive region formed by cellular modifications in DCT and afferent arteriole<br>S. Form filtration slits</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-S, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-P, C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. Podocytes - S. Form filtration slits<br>B. GFR - P. ${\\rm{125}}\\,{\\rm{ml/min}}$<br>C. Blood filtered by kidneys per minute - Q. ${\\rm{1100 - 1200}}\\,{\\rm{ml/min}}$<br>D. Juxta Glomerular apparatus - R. Special sensitive region formed by cellular modifications in DCT and afferent arteriole',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9884,'biology',87,1129,2701,'During the cardiac cycle the opening of the aortic valve takes place at the','[{"text": "End of isovolumeric contraction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Beginning of systole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "End of diastasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "End of diastole", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During cardiac cycle the opening of the aortic valve takes place at the end of isovolumetric contraction. In cardiac physiology, isovolumetric contraction is an event occurring in early systole during which the ventricles contract with no corresponding volume change (isovolumetrically). This short-lasting portion of the cardiac cycle takes place whilst all heart valves are closed.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9885,'biology',9,23,40,'Artificial systems gave equal weightage to','[{"text": "Vegetative and asexual characters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vegetative and sexual characters", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vegetative and anatomical characters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Morphological and sexual characters", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The artificial systems gave equal weightage to vegetative and sexual characteristics; this was not acceptable since we know that often the vegetative characters are more easily affected by environment.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9886,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Which of the following statement is incorrect?','[{"text": "Cells of human body exhibits three main type of movement", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Locomotary structures need to be different from those affecting other type of movements", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Locomotion is generally for search of food, shelter, mate, suitable breeding ground, favorable climatic conditions or escape from enemies/predator", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Locomotion requires a perfect coordinated activity of muscular, skeletal and nervous system", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Locomotory structures need not to be different from those affecting other type of movements.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9887,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. A fall in GFR can activate<br>B. Volume of filtrate formed<br>C. Amount of urine released<br>D. Tubular reabsorption</div><div class="column-right">P. 180 L/ per day<br>Q. Renal tubules<br>R. JG cells to release renin<br>S. 1.5 L</div></div>','[{"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-P, C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<br>A. A fall in GFR can activate - R. JG cells to release renin<br>B. Volume of filtrate formed - P. $$180 \\mathrm{~L} / \\mathrm{per}$$ day<br>C. Amount of urine released - S. 1.5 L<br>D. Tubular reabsorption - Q. Renal tubules',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9888,'biology',87,1129,2701,'Choose the correct statement:<br>I. Phase of isometric contraction begins when the aortic valves open.<br>II. Aortic pressure falls to its diastolic pressure during isometric ventricular relaxation.<br>III. Phase of ventricular contraction approximately equal to the QT interval in ECG.<br>IV. Most of ventricular contraction approximately equal to the QT interval in ECG.','[{"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III only", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Aortic pressure falls to its diastolic pressure during isovolumetric ventricular relaxation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9889,'biology',9,23,40,'_______ characters are easily affected by environment','[{"text": "Sexual", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vegetative", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anatomical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Vegetative characters are more easily affected by environment.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9890,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Each organised skeletal muscle in our body is made of a number of','[{"text": "Muscle bundles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fascicles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sarcomere", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each organised skeletal muscle in our body is made of a number of muscle bundles or fascicles held together by a common collagenous connective tissue layer called fascia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9891,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Identify the given diagram in the question?','[{"text": "Renal corpuscle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glomerulus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Malpighian body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Glomerulus with Bowman\'s capsule as shown in the figure together form the Malphigian body/Renal Corpuscle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/88_9891_question_1.png'),
(9939,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Collecting duct of nephron extends from the cortex of kidney to','[{"text": "Capsule region", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inner part of medulla", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Outer part of medulla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Middle part of medulla", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The long collecting duct extends from the cortex of the kidney to the inner parts of the medulla.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9892,'biology',87,1129,2701,'If there is a blockage between the AV node and the AV bundle, how will this affect the appearance of the ECG?','[{"text": "There would be more P waves than QRS complexes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "PR interval would be smaller", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There would be more QRS complexes than aves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "QRS interval would be shorter", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'If there is a blockage between the AV node and the AV bundle there would be more $$\\mathrm{P}$$ waves than QRS complexes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9893,'biology',9,23,40,'The earliest system of classification given by ......, based on gross superficial morphological traits was called .........','[{"text": "Linnaeus, natural classification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linnaeus, artificial classification", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Whittaker, natural classification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Whittaker, artificial classification", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Carlos Linnaeus proposed the artificial system of classification. It was based on assessment of only gross superficial morphological characters like habit, colour,shape etc. They were based mainly on vegetative characters or on the androecium structure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9894,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Each muscle bundle contains a number of','[{"text": "Muscle fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Muscle cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each muscle bundle contains a number of muscles fibres i.e. muscle cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9895,'biology',88,1152,2759,'The given diagram is of renal corpuscle. Name the labeled parts A-D?','[{"text": "A-Afferent arteriole, B-Bowman\'s capsule, C-Efferent arteriole, D-PCT", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Bowman\'s capsule, B-PCT, C-Afferent arteriole, D- Efferent arteriole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Efferent arteriole, B-Bowman\'s capsule, C- PCT, D-Afferent arteriole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-PCT, B-Afferent arteriole, C-Efferent arteriole, D-Bowman\'s capsule", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. Afferent arteriole<br>B. Bowman\'s capsule<br>C. Efferent arteriole<br>D. PCT',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/88_9895_question_1.png'),
(9896,'biology',87,1129,2701,'Choose the correct statement among the following:<br>I. Atrio-ventricular node is the pacemaker that generates action potential and initiates the atrial systole.<br>II. During each cardiac cycle, the \'lubb\' sound is due to the closure of semilunar valves.<br>III. Stroke volume in each cardiac cycle is approximately $$170 \\mathrm{ml}$$ of blood.<br>IV. QRS complex in an ECG indicates depolarization of ventricles.','[{"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'SA node is the pacemaker that generates action potential and initiates the atrial systole.<br>The first heart sound (lub) is associated with the closure of the tricuspid and bicuspid valves whereas the second heart sound (dub) is associated with the closure of the semilunar valves.<br>Stroke volume in each cardiac cycle is approximately $$70 \\mathrm{ml}$$ of blood.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9897,'biology',9,23,40,'Classification by Linnaeus is based on','[{"text": "gynoecium structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "androecium structure", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sepal structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Petal structure", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Artificial classification system proposed by Linnaeus was mainly based on vegetative characters or on androecium structure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9898,'biology',89,1285,3106,'The fascicles are held together by connective tissue called','[{"text": "Intercalated disc", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myofibril", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fascia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each organised skeletal muscle in our body is made of a number of muscle bundles or fascicles held together by a common collagenous connective tissue layer called fascia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9899,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Which of the following is an incorrect statement about filtration?','[{"text": "Selective process", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-selective process", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Performed by glomerulus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It occurs through the usage of capillary (glomerulus) blood pressure", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Glomerular filtration depends on the effective pore size and glomerular hydrostatic pressure. The filtration membrane is not selective and filters everything in the blood except corpuscles and large blood proteins.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9900,'biology',87,1129,2701,'Choose the correct statement:<br>I. The T- wave in an ECG represents excitation of ventricles.<br>II. The sum of $$\\mathrm{P}$$ and $$\\mathrm{T}$$ waves in a given time period can determine the heartbeat rate of an individual. <br>III. The end of the P- wave marks the end of the systole.<br>IV. In a standard ECG, a person is connected to the machine using three electrical leads.','[{"text": "IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and  only IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The T-wave represents the return of the ventricles from excited to normal state (repolarisation). By counting the number of QRS complexes that occur in a given time period, one can determine the heart beat rate of an individual.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9901,'biology',9,23,40,'Natural system of classification was proposed by','[{"text": "Bentham and Linnaeus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bentham alone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Engler and Prantl", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bentham and Hooker", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Natural classification system for flowering plants was given by George Bentham and Joseph Dalton Hooker.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9902,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Fascia is made up of','[{"text": "Fibrous connective tissue layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Elastic connective tissue layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collagenous connective tissue layer", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Reticular connective tissue layer", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each organised skeletal muscle in our body is made of a number of muscle bundles or fascicles held together by a common collagenous connective tissue layer called fascia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9903,'biology',88,1153,2760,'PCT helps in the maintenance of $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ in the body fluid by','[{"text": "Selective secretion of $$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$ions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Selective secretion of ammonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Selective secretion of $$\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$$ions and absorption of $$\\\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}{ }^{-}$$ions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'PCT helps to maintain the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and ionic balance of the body fluids by selective secretion of hydrogen, potassium ions and ammonia into the filtrate and by absorption of $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$from it.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9904,'biology',87,1129,2701,'What is the heart rate in the following ECG?','[{"text": "80", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "75", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "85", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "70", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'By counting the number of QRS complexes that occur in a given time period, one can determine the heart rate of an individual (NCERT statement). In the given ECG, there are 8 QRS complexes over a span of 6 seconds. So, number of beats per minute ( 60 seconds) is $$8 \\times 10=80$$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/87_9904_question_1.png'),
(9905,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Which out of the following represent collagenous connective tissue','[{"text": "A - Sarcolemma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B - Fascicle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Fascicle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B - Sarcolemma", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Given is diagrammatic cross-sectional view of a muscle showing muscle bundles and muscle fibres. In which label A represents Fascicle, B represents muscle fibre (muscle cell).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/89_9905_question_1.png'),
(9906,'biology',9,23,40,'Natural classification system developed were based on','[{"text": "Natural affinities amongst organism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ultra structure and anatomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryology and phytochemistry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Natural classification systems were based on natural affinities among the organisms and consider not only the external features, but also internal features, like ultrastructure, anatomy, embryology and phytochemistry.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9907,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Reabsorption is minimum in which part of nephron?','[{"text": "PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collecting duct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ascending limbs of Henle\'s loop", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Reabsorption is minimum in the ascending limb of loop of Henle. However, this region plays a significant role in the maintenance of high osmolarity of medullary interstitial fluid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9908,'biology',87,1128,2700,'If someone\'s heart has a stroke volume of $$70 \\mathrm{ml}$$ and a heart rate of 90 beat/minute, the cardiac output would be','[{"text": "$$0.71 \\\\mathrm{~L} / \\\\mathrm{min}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$6.3 \\\\mathrm{~L} / \\\\mathrm{min}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$1.28 \\\\mathrm{~mL} / \\\\mathrm{min}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$70 \\\\mathrm{ml} / \\\\mathrm{min}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cardiac output $$=$$ Heart rate $$\\times$$ Stroke volume $$=90 \\times 0.07$$ litre $$/$$ beat $$=6.3 \\mathrm{~L} / \\mathrm{min}$$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9909,'biology',89,1285,3106,'The sarcolemma lines a','[{"text": "Muscle fibre", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fascia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Muscle bundle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Each muscle fibre is lined by the plasma membrane called sarcolemma enclosing the sarcoplasm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9910,'biology',9,23,40,'Natural system of classification was based upon<br>i. Structural embryology and ultrastructure<br>ii. Phytochemistry and anatomy<br>iii. Natural affinities among the organisms<br>iv. External features<br>v. Habit, colour, number and shape of leaves<br>vi. Androecium structure','[{"text": "i, ii, iii, iv, v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iii, iv, vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i , iii, v, vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Natural classification systems were based on natural affinities among the organisms and consider not only the external features, but also internal features, like ultrastructure, anatomy, embryology and phytochemistry.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9911,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Henle\'s loop of nephron plays a significant role in maitaining a high osmolarity in','[{"text": "Interestrial fluid of hilum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Medullary interstitial fluid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cortex interstitial fluid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Henle\'s loop of nephron plays a significant role in maintaining a high osmolarity in medullary interstitial fluid. This occurs due to the mechanism of counter-current occuring here.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9912,'biology',87,1128,2700,'The part of the hand that should not be used while checking someone else\'s pulse is','[{"text": "Thumb", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Index finger", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ring finger", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Central finger", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All of your digits have a pulse, which is felt as a surge in the digital arteries each time the heart beats. The reason not to use your thumb when taking someone else\'s pulse, as far as I understand, is that the digital artery of the thumb is larger and/or closer to the surface of the pad of the thumb, and more easily felt than the pulse in the other fingers. Therefore, if feeling another person\'s pulse with you thumb, you may confuse their pulse with your own and get an inaccurate reading. You\'re less likely to feel a pulse in your own fingertips (index and middle finger), and thus more likely to feel only the other person\'s pulse when you palpate with them',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9913,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Muscle fibre is a ____ as the sarcoplasm contains many nuclei.','[{"text": "Coencytic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Syncitium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Non-coenocytic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Muscle fibre is a syncytium as the sarcoplasm contains many nuclei.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9914,'biology',9,23,40,'Identify the classification based on evolutionary history','[{"text": "Natural classification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Artificial classification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Numerical classification", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phylogenetic classification", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Phylogenetic classification systems are based on evolutionary relationships between the various organisms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9915,'biology',88,1153,2760,'The part of loop of Henle that is impermeable to electrolytes is','[{"text": "Descending limb", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ascending limb", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The descending limb of loop of Henle is permeable to water but almost impermeable to electrolytes. This concentrates the filtrate as it moves down.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10021,'biology',9,24,42,'Algae possesing gametes similar in size and non- flagellated','[{"text": "<i>Ulothrix</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Volvox</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Spirogyra</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Udorina</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Spirogyra possesses isogamous, non-motile/ non-flagellated gametes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9916,'biology',87,1132,2704,'Identify the correct statement regarding circulatory system:<br>I. Arteries are thick walled and have narrow lumen as compared to veins<br>II. Angina is acute chest pain when the blood circulation to the brain is reduced<br>III. Persons with blood group $$\\mathrm{AB}$$ can donate blood to any person with any group under ABO system<br>IV. Calcium ions play a very important role in blood clotting','[{"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Angina is also called \'angina pectoris\'. A symptom of acute chest pain appears when no enough oxygen is reaching the heart muscle. Group \' $$\\mathrm{O}$$ \' blood can be donated to persons with any other blood group and hence \' $$\\mathrm{O}$$ \' group individuals are called \'universal donors\'. Persons with \'AB\' group can accept blood from persons with $$\\mathrm{AB}$$ as well as the other groups of blood. Therefore, such persons are called \'universal recipients\'.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9917,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Calcium ions in the muscle fibre is present in','[{"text": "Smooth endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Golgi complex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sarcoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The endoplasmic reticulum, i.e., sarcoplasmic reticulum of the muscle fibres is the store house of calcium ions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9918,'biology',9,23,40,'Phylogenetic system of classfication is based on','[{"text": "Genotypic characters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Similarities and differences between organisms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Evolutionary relationships", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Number of leaves present in the species", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Phylogenetic classification systems are based on evolutionary relationships between the various organisms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9919,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Transport of electrolytes through ascending limb of loop of Henle takes place through','[{"text": "Active transport", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Passive transport", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diffusion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The ascending limb is impermeable to water but allows transport of electrolytes. Therefore, as the concentrated filtrate pass upward, it gets diluted due to the passage of electrolytes to the medullary fluid. This transport of electrolytes takes place by diffusion actively/passively.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9920,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Which of the following sequences is truly a systemic circulation pathway?','[{"text": "Right auricle $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Left ventricle $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Aorta $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Tissues $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Veins $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Right auricle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Right ventricle $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Pulmonary aorta $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Tissues $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Pulmonary veins $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Left auricle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Left auricle $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Left ventricle $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Aorta $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Arteries $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Tissues $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Veins $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Right atrium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Left auricle $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Left ventricle $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Pulmonary aorta $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Tissues $$\\\\rightarrow$$ Right auricle", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Left auricle Left ventricle Aorta Arteries Tissues Veins Right atrium.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9921,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Sarcoplasmic reticulum is a storehouse of which ion','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The endoplasmic reticulum, i.e., sarcoplasmic reticulum of the muscle fibres is the store house of calcium ions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9922,'biology',9,23,40,'The characters used to classify organism when no fossil evidence is supportive is','[{"text": "Numerical taxonomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemotaxonomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytotaxonomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Numerical taxonomy, Chemotaxonomy and cytotaxonomy become important for classification when there is no supporting fossil evidence.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9923,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Main function of Distal Convoluted Tubule (DCT) of nephron is to maitain the','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pH}$$ in blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Na-K balance of blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Temperature of blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Conditional reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and water takes place in DCT. It is also capable of reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$and selective secretion of hydrogen and potassium ions and $$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$ to maintain the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and sodium-potassium balance in blood.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9924,'biology',87,1128,2700,'Select incorrect answer:','[{"text": "A higher heart rate implies more efficient heart pressure.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A normal resting heart rate for adult ranges from 60 to 100 beats a minute.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Consult your doctor if your resting heart rate is consistently above 100 beats a minute.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A lower heart rate implies more efficient heart function and better cardiovascular fitness.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Causes of tachycardia include: Heartrelated conditions such as high blood pressure (hypertension)<br>Poor blood supply to the heart muscle due to coronary artery disease (atherosclerosis), heart valve disease, heart failure, heart muscle disease (cardiomyopathy), tumours, or infections.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9925,'biology',89,1285,3106,'A characteristic feature of the muscle fibre is the presence of large number of parallel arranged filaments in the sarcoplasm called','[{"text": "Microfilaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microtubules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myofibrils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A characteristic feature of the muscle fibre is the presence of large number of parallelly arranged filaments in the sarcoplasm called microfilaments and myofibrils.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9926,'biology',9,23,40,'Numbers and codes are assigned to the characters in','[{"text": "Cytotaxonomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemotaxonomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Numerical taxonomy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phylogenetic taxonomy", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Numerical Taxonomy which is now easily carried out using computers is based on all observable characteristics. Number and codes are assigned to all the characters and the data are then processed. In this way each character is given equal importance and at the same time hundreds of characters can be considered.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9927,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Which segment helps in the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ maintenance of body fluid?','[{"text": "PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collecting duct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'PCT helps to maintain the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and ionic balance of the body fluids by selective secretion of hydrogen ions and ammonia into the filtrate and by absorption of $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$from it. DCT is capable of reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$and selective secretion of hydrogen and potassium ions and $$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$ to maintain the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and sodium-potassium balance in blood. The collecting duct plays a role in the maintenance of $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and ionic balance of blood by the selective secretion of $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$and $$\\mathrm{K}^{+}$$ions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9928,'biology',87,1125,2697,'Consider following statements (I -IV) regarding lymph. Which of the statements are correct;<br>I. Composition of lymph is very much like that of the blood<br>II. Lymph is responsible for immunity<br>III. Lymphocytes are added when lymph passes through small capillaries<br>IV. Lymph contains less fibrinogen than blood plasma','[{"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The lymphatic system performs these functions:It takes up excess tissue fluid and returns it to the bloodstream, absorbs fat in the intestinal villi and transports them to the bloodstream and defends the body against disease.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9929,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Sarcolemma<br>B. Sarcoplasmic reticulum<br>C. Myofibrils</div><div class="column-right">P. Alternate dark and light bands<br>Q. Plasma membrane<br>R. Store house of calcium</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sarcolemma - Plasma membrane<br>Sarcoplasmic reticulum - Store house of calcium<br>Myofibrils - Alternate dark and light band',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9930,'biology',9,23,40,'Classification on the basis of all observed characters is known as','[{"text": "Mathematical taxonomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Numerical taxonomy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bentham taxonomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Numerical information taxonomy", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Numerical Taxonomy which is easily carried out using computers is based on all observable characteristics.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9931,'biology',88,1153,2760,'DCT helps in','[{"text": "Conditional reabsorption of $$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Selective secretion of $$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$and $$\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$$and $$\\\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$reabsorption", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{pH}$$ maintenance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'DCT is capable of reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$ and selective secretion of hydrogen and potassium ions and $$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$ to maintain the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and sodium-potassium balance in blood.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9932,'biology',87,1132,2704,'In the heart, a clogged artery causes a heart attack. In the brain it causes a','[{"text": "Mental illness", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Migraine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seizures", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stroke", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A stroke occurs when blood flow to the brain is significantly impaired. A stroke that results from inadequate blood supply to the brain is referred to as ischemic stroke, when a blood vessel to the brain breaks open and bleeds, it causes a hemorrhagic stroke',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(9933,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Myofilaments or Myofibrils are','[{"text": "Laterally arranged filaments of muscle fibre", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parallelly arranged filaments of muscle fibre", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Horizontally arranged filaments of muscle fibre", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tangentially arranged filaments of muscle fibre", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A characteristic feature of the muscle fibre is the presence of a large number of parallelly arranged filaments in the sarcoplasm called myofilaments or myofibrils. Each myofibril has alternate dark and light bands on it. A detailed study of the myofibril has established that the striated appearance is due to the distribution pattern of two important proteins - Actin and Myosin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9934,'biology',9,23,40,'Chemotaxonomy is based on','[{"text": "Information of chromosome number, structure and behaviour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemical constituents of plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only Asexual characters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only sexual characters", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Chemotaxonomy uses the chemical constituents of the plant to resolve confusions and is used by taxonomists these days.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9935,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Which of the following segment allows the passage of small amount of urea into medullary interstitium to keep up the osmolarity?','[{"text": "Collecting duct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Loop of henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Large amounts of water could be reabsorbed from the collecting duct to produce a concentrated urine. This segment allows passage of small amounts of urea into the medullary interstitium to keep up the osmolarity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9936,'biology',87,1122,2694,'One of the common symptoms observed in people infected with Dengue fever is','[{"text": "Significant decrease in RBC count", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Significant decrease in WBC count", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Significant decrease in platelets count", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Significant increase in platelets count", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Low platelet count is used as diagnostic tool to assess the severity of dengue. The virus attacks on the platelets and reduce their count.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9937,'biology',89,1285,3106,'The light and dark regions of myofibril are called','[{"text": "A-band and I-band, respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Z-band and M-band, respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I-band and A-band, respectively", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-band and M-band, respectively", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A detailed study of the myofibril has established that the striated appearance is due to the distribution pattern of two important proteins - Actin and Myosin. The light bands contain actin and is called I-band or Isotropic band, whereas the dark band called \' A \' or Anisotropic band contains myosin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9940,'biology',87,1131,2703,'Cardiac activity could be moderated by the autonomous neural system. Tick the correct answer:','[{"text": "The parasympathetic system stimulates heart rate and stroke volume", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The sympathetic system stimulates heart rate and stroke volume", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The parasympathetic system decreases the heart rate but increase stroke volume", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The sympathetic system decreases the heart rate but increase stroke volume", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sympathetic system plays excitatory role, while parasympathetic system plays inhibitory role thus stimulate the heart rate.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9941,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Anisotropic band is made of','[{"text": "Myosin filaments", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Actin filaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Actin and myosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Anisotropic band is made of myosin filaments.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9942,'biology',9,23,40,'A) Phylogenetic system of classification is based upon evolutionary relationship of organisms<br>B) Phylogenetic classification systems are based on numbers and codes are assigned to it<br>C) Cytotaxonomy is based on cytological information like chromosome number, structure and behaviour.','[{"text": "A and C are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only C is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only A is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B and C are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Numerical taxonomy is the classification system based on numbers and codes assigned to it.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9943,'biology',88,1153,2760,'The function of collecting duct is to','[{"text": "Reabsorb water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maitain osmolarity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maitain $$\\\\mathrm{pH}$$ and ionic balance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Large amounts of water could be reabsorbed from the collecting duct to produce a concentrated urine. This segment allows passage of small amounts of urea into the medullary interstitium to keep up the osmolarity. It also plays a role in the maintenance of $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and ionic balance of blood by the selective secretion of $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$and $$\\mathrm{K}^{+}$$ ions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9944,'biology',89,1285,3106,'The light bands (I band) of a skeletal muscle are known as','[{"text": "Myofilaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cross arm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isotropic band", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anisotropic band", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A detailed study of the myofibril has established that the striated appearance is due to the distribution pattern of two important proteins - Actin and Myosin. The light bands contain actin and is called I-band or Isotropic band, whereas the dark band called \'A\' or Anisotropic band contains myosin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9945,'biology',9,23,40,'Which of the following systems of classification involves usage of one or few morphological characters for grouping of organisms?','[{"text": "Artificial system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linnaeus system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phylogenetic system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Artificial system proposed by Carlos Linnaeus was based on one or few morphological characters such as habit, colour, number and shape of leaves, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9946,'biology',87,1129,2701,'ECG depicts the depolarisation and repolarisation processes during the cardiac cycle. In the ECG of a normal healthy individual one of the following waves is not represented.','[{"text": "Depolarisation of atria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Repolarisation of atria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Depolarisation of ventricles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Repolarisation of ventricles", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$$\\mathrm{P}$$ wave shows depolarisation of atria. QRS complex shows depolarisation of ventricles $$T$$ wave shows repolarisation of ventricles.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9947,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Urine is first seen in?','[{"text": "PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ureters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Loop of Henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collecting duct (end)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Metabolic wastes is considered as urine first in the collecting duct. It gets transported to renal calyces and further renal pelvis before exiting the kidney and passing through the ureter.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9948,'biology',89,1285,3106,'The dark bands (A-bands) of a skeletal muscle are known as','[{"text": "Anisotropic bands", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Isotropic bands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myofilaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cross bridges", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The dark bands (A-bands) of a skeletal muscle are known as Anisotropic bands.<br>A-bands are made up of protein myosin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9949,'biology',9,23,40,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. R. H. Whittakar<br>B. Linnaeus<br>C. Natural classification system</div><div class="column-right">P. Artificial classi fication system<br>Q. 1969<br>R. George Bentham and J.D.Hooker</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R, B – P, C – Q,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – R, C – P,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – P, B – R, C – Q,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – P, C – R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. R. H. Whittakar - Q. 1969<br>B. Linnaeus - P. Artificial classification system<br>C. Natural classification system - R. George Bentham and J.D.Hooker',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9950,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Which one of the following blood cells is involved in antibody production.','[{"text": "B-Lymphocytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "T-Lymphocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{RBC}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neutrophils", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'B-lymphocytes assisted by T-Lymphocytes',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9951,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Reabsorption of glucose, ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$, amino acids<br>B. Reabsorption of nitrogenous wastes<br>C. Reabsorption of water</div><div class="column-right">P. Passively in the initial segments of nephron<br>Q. Active transport<br>R. Passive transport</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. Reabsorption of glucose, $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$, amino acids - Q. Active transport B. Reabsorption of nitrogenous wastes - R. Passive transport<br>C. Reabsorption of water - P. Passively in the initial segments of nephron',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9952,'biology',9,23,40,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Phylogenetic classification system<br>B. Chemotaxonomy<br>C. Cytotaxonomy</div><div class="column-right">P. Chemical  constituents of  the plant<br>Q. Evolutionary relationships<br>R.  Chromosome  number, structure, behaviour</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R , B – P , C – Q,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q , B – R , C – P,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – P , B – R , C – Q,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q , B – P , C – R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. Phylogenetic classification system - Q.Evolutionary relationships<br>B. Chemotaxonomy - P. Chemical constituents of the plant<br>C. Cytotaxonomy - R. Chromosome number, structure, behaviour',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9953,'biology',89,1285,3106,'The light bands contain____ and is called','[{"text": "Actin, Anisotropic band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myosin, Isotropic band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Actin, Isotropic band", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Myosin, Anisotropic band", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The light band contains Actin, and it is called as isotropic band.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9954,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Agranulocytes responsible for immune response of the body are','[{"text": "Basophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neutrophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eosinophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lymphocytes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Lymphocytes are responsible for immune response by producing antibodies.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9955,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. PCT<br>B. Ascending limb of Henle’s loop<br>C. Descending limb of Henle’s loop<br>D. DCT</div><div class="column-right">P. Conditional reabsorption of ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$<br>Q. Reabsorption of water only<br>R. Reabsorption of salts only<br>S. Reabsorption of ions, water and organic nutrients</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-S, C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. PCT - S. Reabsorption of ions, water and organic nutrientsB. Ascending limb of Henle\'s loop - R. Reabsorption of salts onlyC. Descending limb of Henle\'s loop - Q. Reabsorption of water onlyD. DCT - P. Conditional reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9956,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Actin and myosin filaments of muscles are also called ____ respectively','[{"text": "Thick and thin filaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thin and light filaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thin and thick filaments", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "White and dark filaments", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A detailed study of the myofibril has established that the striated appearance is due to the distribution pattern of two important proteins - Actin and Myosin. The light bands contain actin and is called I-band or Isotropic band, whereas the dark band called \' A \' or Anisotropic band contains myosin. Actin filaments are thinner as compared to the myosin filaments, hence are commonly called thin and thick filaments respectively.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9957,'biology',9,24,42,'Algae are','[{"text": "Saprotrophic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterotrophic but cholorphyll bearing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlorophyll bearing autotrophs", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Algae are chlorophyll-bearing, simple, thalloid, autotrophic and largely aquatic organisms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9958,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. PCT<br>B. Henle’s loop<br>C. DCT<br>D. Collecting duct</div><div class="column-right">P. Long duct extends from cortex of kidneys to inner medulla<br>Q. Maintain sodium - potassium balance in blood<br>R. Maintain pH and ionic balance of body fluids<br>S. Plays significant role in maintenance of high osmolarity of medullary interstitial fluid</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-S, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. PCT R. Maintain $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and ionic balance of body fluids<br>B. Henle\'s loop S. Plays significant role in maintenance of high osmolarity of medullary interstitial fluid<br>C. DCT Q. Maintain sodium potassium balance in blood<br>D. Collecting Duct P. Long duct extends from cortex of kidneys to inner medulla',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9959,'biology',87,1129,2701,'Which of the following correctly explains a phase/ event in cardiac cycle in a standard electrocardiogram?','[{"text": "QRS complex indicates atrial contraction.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "QRS complex indicates ventricular contraction.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Time between $$\\\\mathrm{S}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{T}$$ represents atrial systole.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P-wave indicates beginning of ventricular contraction.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The QRS complex in a standard ECG represents ventricular depolarization. $$\\mathrm{P}$$ wave represents atrial depolarization. $$\\mathrm{T}$$ wave represents ventricular repolarization.<br>Thus, the correct answer is \'QRS complex indicates ventricular contraction.\'',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9960,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Actin and myosin are arranged as rod-like structures____','[{"text": "Parallel to each other", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parallel to the longitudinal axis of the myofibrils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A detailed study of the myofibril has established that the striated appearance is due to the distribution pattern of two important proteins - Actin and Myosin. The light bands contain actin and is called I-band or Isotropic band, whereas the dark band called \'A\' or Anisotropic band contains myosin. Both the proteins are arranged as rod-like structures, parallel to each other and also to the longitudinal axis of the myofibrils.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9961,'biology',9,24,42,'Chlorophyll bearing, thalloid, simple, autotropic eukaryotic and largely aquatic organisms are','[{"text": "Bryophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chrysophyta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cyanobacteria", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Algae are chlorophyll-bearing, simple, thalloid, autotrophic and largely aquatic organisms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10043,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Secondary or thin filaments of striated muscle fibres are made up of all except','[{"text": "F-actin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Troponin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meromyosin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tropomyosin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Meromyosin is a component of primary or thick myofilaments.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9962,'biology',88,1153,2760,'The given diagram showing reabsorption and secretion of major substances at different parts of the nephron. Identify (A-D) in the diagram?','[{"text": "A- Water, B- Urea, C- Water, D- $$\\\\mathrm{NaCl}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Water, B-NaCl, C-Urea, D- water", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A- NaCl, B- Water, C- Water, D- Urea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Urea, B- NaCl, C- Water, D- Water", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Water<br>B. $$\\mathrm{NaCl}$$<br>C. Urea<br>D. Water',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/88_9962_question_1.png'),
(9963,'biology',87,1128,2700,'What would be the cardiac output of a person having 72 heart beats per minute and a stroke volume of $$50 \\mathrm{~mL}$$ ?','[{"text": "$$360 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$3600 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$7200 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$5000 \\\\mathrm{~mL}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Volume in one beat $$=50 \\mathrm{~mL}$$, Volume in 72 beats $$=72 \\times 50=3600 \\mathrm{~mL}$$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9964,'biology',89,1285,3106,'In the centre of each I-band, there is an elastic fibre called','[{"text": "I-line", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-line", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Z-line", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "H-zone", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In the centre of each \'I\' band is an elastic fibre called \' Z \' line which bisects it. The thin filaments are firmly attached to the \' Z \' line.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9965,'biology',9,24,42,'In algae, the photosynthetic pigments are present in','[{"text": "pyrenoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "cell membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "chloroplast", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "pellicle", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The photosynthetic pigments in algae are localised in definite chloroplasts.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9966,'biology',88,1153,2760,'The given diagram shows the reabsorption and secretion process of urine formation. Which molecules are actively reabsorbed in tubular segments?','[{"text": "Nitrogenous wastes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose, amino acids, $$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The tubular epithelial cells in different segments of nephron perform reabsorption either by active or passive mechanisms. Substances like glucose, amino acids, $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$, etc., in the filtrate are reabsorbed actively.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/88_9966_question_1.png'),
(9967,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Read the following statements and choose the correct option<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Atria receive blood from all parts of the body which subsequently flows to ventricles.<br></div><div class="column-right">Action potential generated at sino-atrial node passes from atria to ventricles.</div></div>','[{"text": "Action mentioned in Statement 1 is dependent on action mentioned in Statement 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Action mentioned in Statement 2 is dependent on action mentioned in Statement 1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Action mentioned in Statements 1 and 2 are independent of each other.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Action mentioned in Statements 1 and 2 are synchronous.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Action potential generated at the SA node causes the ventricles to contact and the blood goes to the lungs from the right ventricle and into the aorta from the left ventricle. After emptying of the venticles the blood enters the atrium. Hence action mentioned in statement 1 is dependent on action mentioned in statement 2 .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9968,'biology',89,1285,3106,'A thin fibrous membrane called \' $M$ \' line holds together','[{"text": "I band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A band", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Z band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}$ band", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The thick filaments in the \'A\' band are also held together in the middle of this band by a thin fibrous membrane called \' M \' line.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9969,'biology',9,24,42,'Which of the following are used as habitat by algae.<br>A. Aquatic environment<br>B. Moist stones<br>C. Moist soils<br>D. Moist wood','[{"text": " A and B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and C only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B, C and D", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Algae are found in aquatic environment, moist stones, moist soils	and moist wood',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9970,'biology',88,1153,2760,'The given diagram shows the reabsorption and secretion process of urine formation. Which molecules are passively reabsorbed in tubular segments?','[{"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nitrogenous wastes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose, amino acids, $$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The tubular epithelial cells in different segments of nephron perform reabsorption either by active or passive mechanisms. Substances like nitrogenous wastes are absorbed passively.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/88_9970_question_1.png'),
(9971,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Which of the following cells does not exhibit phagocytic activity?','[{"text": "Monocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neutrophil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Basophil", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Macrophage", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Basophils secrete histamine, serotonin, heparin etc. and are involved in inflammatory reactions and do not perform phagocytic activity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9972,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Centre of each ‘I’ band<br>B. Centre of each ‘A’ band<br>C. Not overlapped by thin filaments</div><div class="column-right">P. ‘Z’ line<br>Q. ‘H’ zone<br>R. ‘M’ line</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Centre of each I band -Z line<br>Centre of each A band - M line<br>Not overlapped by thin filament -H zone',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9973,'biology',9,24,42,'Sometimes algae are present in a non -aquatic environment. Identify them','[{"text": "Fungi (lichen)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Virus (lichen)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi (mycorrhizae)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Some of the fungi also occur in association with fungi (lichen), higher plants (mycorrhiza) and animals (sloth bear).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9974,'biology',88,1153,2760,'The given diagram shows the reabsorption and secretion process of urine formation. $$70-80 \\%$$ of electrolytes and water are reabsorbed by which segments?','[{"text": "A- DCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-PCT", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B- Henle\'s loop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C- DCT", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'PCT is lined by simple cuboidal brush border epithelium which increases the surface area for reabsorption. Nearly all of the essential nutrients, and 70-80 percent of electrolytes and water are reabsorbed by this segment. It is marked as $$\\mathrm{A}$$ in the figure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/88_9974_question_1.png'),
(9975,'biology',87,1128,2700,'Which among the followings is correct during each cardiac cycle?','[{"text": "The volume of blood pumped out by the $$\\\\mathrm{Rt}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{Lt}$$ ventricles is same.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The volume of blood pumped out by the $$\\\\mathrm{Rt}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{Lt}$$ ventricle is different", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The volume of blood received by each atrium is different", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The volume of blood received by the aorta and pulmonary artery is different", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Volume of blood entering the lungs is same as the volume leaving the lungs after oxygenation. Otherwise it will lead to congestive heart failure due to varying pressure.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9976,'biology',89,1285,3106,'In a resting state, the edges of thin filaments on either side of the ____ filaments partially overlap the free ends of the____filaments leaving the central part of the ____filaments. Fill in the blank','[{"text": "Thick", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thick or thin both", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In a resting state, the edges of thin filaments on either side of the thick filaments partially overlap the free ends of the thick filaments leaving the central part of the thick filaments. This central part of thick filament, not overlapped by thin filaments is called the \'H\' zone.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9977,'biology',9,24,42,'Filamentous forms of algae are','[{"text": "<i>Spirogyra</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ulothrix</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Chlamydomonas</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Algae has highly variable forms. Filamentous forms like<i>Ulothrix</i> and<i>Spirogyra</i> are also seen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9978,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Out of the four parts given below, which parts play significant role in forming concentrated urine in human?','[{"text": "Loop of Henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "vasa recta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collecting tubule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The ability to produce concentrated urine in humans is a function of loop of Henle and vasa recta. The flow of filtrate in the two limbs of Henle\'s loop is in opposite directions and thus forms a counter-current mechanism (the process due to which the urine is made hypertonic). Vasa recta also play a significant role in counter-current mechanism.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9979,'biology',87,1124,2696,'Mark the pair of substances among the following which is essential for coagulation of blood.','[{"text": "Heparin and calcium ions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calcium ions and platelet factors", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oxalates and citrates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Platelet factors and heparin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Calcium ions help in conversion of fibrinogen into fibrin so that blood can be coagulated.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9980,'biology',89,1285,3106,'The \'A\' and \'I\' bands are arranged ____throughout the length of the myofibrils.','[{"text": "Helically", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non alternately", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two of myosin and one of actin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alternately", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The \'A\' and \'I\' bands are arranged alternately throughout the length of the myofibrils.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9981,'biology',9,24,42,'<i>Volvox</i>  is a','[{"text": "Unicellular algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Colonial algae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Filamentous algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Symbiotic algae", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Algae has highly variable forms. Colonial forms like <i>Volvox</i> are present.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9982,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Vasa recta are minute vessel of peritubular capillaries network, which is','[{"text": "Also known as juxtaglomerular apparatus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Running parallel to loop of Henle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Running parallel to PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Running parallel to DCT", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A minute vessel of the peritubular capillaries network runs parallel to the Henle\'s loop forming a \' $$U$$ \' shaped vasa recta.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9983,'biology',87,1122,2694,'Which one of the following types of cells lack nucleus in humans?','[{"text": "RBC", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neutrophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eosinophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Erythrocytes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'RBC\'s are the only mammalian cell lacking nucleus and mitochondria.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9984,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Identify A, B and C','[{"text": "A - I band, B - A band, C - Z line", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - A band, B - I band, C - M line", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - A band, B - I band, C - Z line", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - I band, B - A band, C - M line", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The given diagram shows a sarcomere. Which can be labelled as A - A band, B - I band, $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{Z}$ line',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/89_9984_question_1.png'),
(9985,'biology',9,24,42,'In algae what are the modes of reproduction?','[{"text": "Vegetative", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Asexual", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sexual", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The algae reproduce by vegetative, asexual and sexual methods.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9986,'biology',88,1154,2761,'The counter-current mechanism operates in nephron','[{"text": "In ascending and descending limb of vasa recta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In ascending limb of Henle\'s loop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In Descending limb of Henle\'s loop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Within the loop of Henle and vasa recta", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The flow offiltrate in the two limbs of Henle\'s loop is in opposite directions and thus forms a counter current. The blood flow in the two limbs of vasa recta is also in a counter-current manner. With this mechanism, mammals are capable of producing concentrated urine.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9987,'biology',87,1127,2699,'The cardiac impulse is initiated and conducted further upto ventricle. The correct sequence of conduction of impulse is','[{"text": "SA Node, AV Node, Purkinje fiber, A V Bundle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "SA Node, Purkinje fiber, AV Node, A V Bundle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "SA Node, AV Node, AV Bundle, Purkinje fiber", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "SA Node, Purkinje fiber, AV Bundle, AV Node", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct sequence of conduction of impulse is SA Node - AV Node - AV Bundle - Purkinje fiber. The SAN generates an action potential which stimulates both the atria to undergo a simultaneous contraction - the atrial systole. The action potential is conducted to the ventricular side by the AVN and AV bundle from where the bundle of His transmits it through the entire ventricular musculature.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9988,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Select the correct statement:','[{"text": "A-band is made up of thick myosin filament", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "M-zone is present in the middle of A-band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Actin and myosin are polymerized sugars with contractility", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The dark bands (A-bands) of a skeletal muscle are known as Anisotropic bands.<br>A-bands are made up of protein myosin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9989,'biology',9,24,42,'In algae, vegetative reproduction mainly takes place by','[{"text": "budding", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "akinetes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "fragmentation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cyst formation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The algae reproduce by vegetative, asexual and sexual methods. Vegetative reproduction is by fragmentation. Each fragment develops into a thallus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9990,'biology',88,1154,2761,'The proximity between the Henle\'s loop and vasa recta, as well as the counter current in them help in maintaining ____','[{"text": "an increasing osmolarity towards the inner medullary interstitium.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "an increasing osmolarity towards the outer medullary interstitium.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "decreasing osmolarity towards the inner medullary interstitium.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "decreasing osmolarity towards the outer medullary interstitium.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The proximity between the Henle\'s loop and vasa recta, as well as the counter current in them help in maintaining an increasing osmolarity towards the inner medullary interstitium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9991,'biology',87,1128,2700,'The second heart sound (dubb) is associated with the closure of','[{"text": "Tricuspid valve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Semilunar valves", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bicuspid valve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tricuspid and bicuspid valves.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Dubb is the second heart sound which is sharp, high pitched of shorter duration and is produced due to closure of semilunar valves at the base of arteries.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9992,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Major protein in the thick filaments of skeletal muscle fibre is','[{"text": "Myosin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Actin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tropomyosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Troponin", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Major protein in the thick filaments of skeletal muscle fibre is Myosin. Each myosin filament is a polymerised protein, made up of monomeric protein units called meromyosin. Each meromyosin has 2 parts, a globular head with short arm and a tail. Head is called heavy meromyosin and tail is called light meromyosin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9993,'biology',9,24,42,'Which is the most common method of asexual reproduction in algae?','[{"text": "Aplanospore formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zoospore formation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Akinete formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autospore formation.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The most common method of asexual reproduction in algae is zoospore formation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9994,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Osmolarity in the cortex and inner medulla respectively are','[{"text": "$$300 \\\\mathrm{~m} \\\\mathrm{Osmol} \\\\mathrm{L}^{-1}, 1200 \\\\mathrm{~m} \\\\mathrm{Osmol} \\\\mathrm{L}^{-1}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$200 \\\\mathrm{~m} \\\\mathrm{Osmol} \\\\mathrm{L}^{-1}, 1300 \\\\mathrm{~m} \\\\mathrm{Osmol} \\\\mathrm{L}^{-1}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$1200 \\\\mathrm{~m} \\\\mathrm{Osmol} \\\\mathrm{L}^{-1}, 300 \\\\mathrm{~m} \\\\mathrm{Osmol} \\\\mathrm{L}^{-1}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The proximity between the Henle\'s loop and vasa recta, as well as the counter current in them help in maintaining an increasing osmolarity towards the inner medullary interstitium, i.e., from ${\\rm{300}}\\,{\\rm{mOsmol}}{{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$ in the cortex to about ${\\rm{1200}}\\,{\\rm{mOsmol}}{{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$ in the inner medulla.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9995,'biology',87,1123,2695,'Which of the following statements is incorrect?','[{"text": "A person of \' $$O$$ \' blood group has anti \' $$A$$ \' and anti \' $$\\\\mathrm{B}$$ \' antibodies in his blood plasma.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A person of \'B\' blood group can\'t donate blood to a person of \'A\' blood group.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood group is designated on the basis of the presence of antibodies in the blood plasma.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A person of $$\\\\mathrm{AB}$$ blood group is universal recipient.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Blood group is designated on the basis of the presence of antigens on the RBCs.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9996,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Sarcomere is the structural and functional unit of myofibril and area between','[{"text": "I to I band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Z}$ to $\\\\mathrm{Z}$ band", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I band to $Z$ line", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A to I band", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sarcomere is the portion of myofibril between two successive Z-lines. It is the structural and functional unit of myofibril.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9997,'biology',9,24,42,'In algae, the most common type of asexual spore is','[{"text": "aplanospore", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "algaspore", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "zoospore", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "oospore", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Algae produce different types of spores, the most common being the zoospores. These are motile, flagellated and give rise to new plants on germination.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9998,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Medullary gradient is mainly developed due to','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NaCl}$$ and urea", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NaCl}$$ and glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose and Ammonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ammonia and $$\\\\mathrm{NaCl}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The proximity between the Henle\'s loop and vasa recta, as well as the counter current in them help in maintaining an increasing osmolarity towards the inner medullary interstitium. This gradient is mainly caused by $$\\mathrm{NaCl}$$ and urea.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(9999,'biology',87,1127,2699,'Match the terms given under Column \' $$A$$ \' with their functions given under Column \' $$\\mathrm{B}$$ \' and select the answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Lymphatic system<br>B. Pulmonary vein <br>C. Thrombocytes<br>D. Lymphocytes</div><div class="column-right">P. Carries oxygenated blood<br>Q. Immune response<br>R. To drain back the tissue fluid to the circulatory system<br>S. Coagulation of blood</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - P,B - Q,C - R,D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R,B - P,C - S,D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R,B - P,C - Q,D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q,B - P,C - R,D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Lymphatic system - to drain back the tissue fluid to the circulatory system<br>Pulmonary vein - carries oxygenated blood Thrombocytes - Coagulation of blood<br>Lymphocytes - Immune response',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10000,'biology',89,1285,3106,'A sarcomere in the myofibrils of muscle is found in between two alternate','[{"text": "M-lines", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Z-lines", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "H-zones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sarcomere is present between two Z lines.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10001,'biology',9,24,42,'Identify the correct answer.<br>i. The most common spores in algae<br>ii. They are flagellated (motile) and on germination gives rise to new plants.','[{"text": "Aplanspores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zoospores", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hypnospores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phytospores", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Algae produce different types of spores, the most common being the zoospores. These are motile, flagellated and give rise to new plants on germination.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10002,'biology',88,1154,2761,'$$\\mathrm{NaCl}$$ transported by ascending limb of Henle\'s loop is exchanged with','[{"text": "Collecting tubule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Descending limb of limb of Henle\'s loop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ascending limb of vasa recta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Descending limb of vasa recta", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$$\\mathrm{NaCl}$$ is transported by the ascending limb of Henle\'s loop which is exchanged with the descending limb of vasa recta.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10003,'biology',87,1122,2693,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Blood is a special connective tissue consisting of a fluid matrix, plasma and formed elements.<br></div><div class="column-right">Plasma is a straw coloured, viscous fluid constituting nearly $$55 \\%$$ of the blood.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10004,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Sarcomere is a','[{"text": "Functional unit of contraction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Portion of myofibril present in between two Z-lines", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Complete bundle of muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The portion of the myofibril between two successive<br>\' Z \' lines is considered as the functional unit of contraction and is called a sarcomere',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10005,'biology',9,24,42,'Which of the following type of sexual reproduction is/are present in algae?','[{"text": "Isogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anisogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sexual reproduction takes place through fusion of two gametes. These gametes can be isogamous, anisogamous or oogamous.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10006,'biology',88,1154,2761,'$$\\mathrm{NaCl}$$ is returned to interstitium by','[{"text": "Ascending limb of Henle\'s loop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Descending limb of Henle\'s loop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ascending limb of vasa recta", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Descending limb of vasa recta", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$$\\mathrm{NaCl}$$ is transported by the ascending limb of Henle\'s loop which is exchanged with the descending limb of vasa recta. $$\\mathrm{NaCl}$$ is returned to the interstitium by the ascending portion of vasa recta.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10007,'biology',87,1122,2693,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Fibrinogens primarily are involved in defense mechanisms of the body<br></div><div class="column-right">Clotting factors are present in the plasma in an inactive form.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement A is wrong. Fibrinogens primarily are involved in blood coagulation mechanisms of the body.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10008,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Identify the diagram','[{"text": "Functional unit of contraction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Functional unit of excretion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Functional unit of conduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Functional unit of secretion", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The given diagram represents a functional unit of contraction i.e. sarcomere.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/89_10008_question_1.png'),
(10009,'biology',9,24,42,'Isogamous condition with nonflagellated gametes is found in','[{"text": "<i>Fucus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Udorina</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Spirogyra</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Volvox</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Non-flagellated/ non-motile gametes are found in <i>Spirogyra</i>.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10010,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Counter-current mechanism helps to maintain a concentration gradient. This gradient helps in','[{"text": "Easy passage of water between the collecting tubule and medulla and so dilute urine is formed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Easy passage of water from collecting tubule to interstitial fluid and thereby concentrating urine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Easy passage to water from medullary interstitial fluid to collecting tubule and there by diluting urine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Easy passage of water from medulla to collecting tubule and there by concentrating urine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Counter-current mechanism helps to maintain a concentration gradient. Presence of such interstitial gradient helps in an easy passage of water from the collecting tubule thereby concentrating the filtrate (urine). Human kidneys can produce urine nearly four times concentrated than the initial filtrate formed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10011,'biology',87,1122,2694,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Erythrocytes, leucocytes and platelets are collectively called formed elements and they constitute nearly 45% of the blood.</div><div class="column-right">WBCs are formed in the red bone marrow in the adults.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10012,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Functional unit of striated muscle is','[{"text": "I Band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Z}$ line", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myofilament", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sarcomere", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The portion of myofibril between two successive Z-lines is the functional unit of contraction, which is called as Sarcomere. <img src=\'/img/data/biology/89_10012_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10013,'biology',9,24,42,'Isogamy is seen in','[{"text": "<i>Ulothrix</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Spirogyra</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The mode of reproduction where gametes are similar in size, motile/ non-motile is known as isogamy. Isogamous gametes can be seen in<i>Ulothrix</i> and <i>Spirogyra</i>.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10014,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Which of the following is incorrect about counter-current mechanism?','[{"text": "The flow of filtrate in two limbs of vasa recta is in opposite direction.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The flow of blood in two limbs of vasa recta is also in opposite direction.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NaCI}$$ is transported by the ascending limb of henleys loop which is exchanged with the descending limb of vasa recta.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NaCI}$$ is returned to in interstitium by the ascending portion of vasa recta.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The flow of filtrate in the two limbs of Henle\'s loop is in opposite directions and thus forms a counter current. The blood flow in the two limbs of vasa recta is also in a countercurrent manner. $$\\mathrm{NaCl}$$ is transported by the ascending limb of Henle\'s loop which is exchanged with the descending limb of vasa recta. $$\\mathrm{NaCl}$$ is returned to the interstitium by the ascending portion of vasa recta.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10015,'biology',87,1122,2694,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">RBCs are devoid of nucleus in most of the mammals and are biconcave in shape.</div><div class="column-right">RBCs have red coloured, iron containing complex protein called hemoglobin, which play significant role in transport of respiratory gases.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10016,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Select the correct answer<br>I. The \'A\' and \'I\' bands are arranged alternately throughout the length of the myofibrils.<br>II. In a contracting state, the edges of thin filaments on either side of the thick filaments partially overlap the free ends of the thick filaments leaving the central part of the thick filaments.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In a resting state, the edges of thin filaments on either side of the thick filaments partially overlap the free ends of the thick filaments leaving the central part of the thick filaments. This central part of thick filament, not overlapped by thin filaments is called the \'H\' zone.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10017,'biology',9,24,42,'Algae possesing gametes similar in size and flagellated','[{"text": "<i>Ulothrix</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Volvox</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Spirogyra</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Udorina</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Ulothrix</i> possesses isogamous, motile/ flagellated gametes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10018,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Carefully observe the given figure and select the correct option?<BR>I. Mammals have the ability to produce a concentrated urine.<BR>II. Only Henle’s loop play a significant role in this mechanism.<BR>III. The flow of filtrate in the two limbs of Henle’s loop is in opposite directions and thus forms a counter current.<BR>IV. This mechanism helps to maintain a concentration gradient in the medullary interstitium.<BR>V. Human kidneys can produce urine diluted than the initial filtrate formed.','[{"text": "I, III, IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The Henle\'s loop and vasa recta both play a significant role in counter-current mechanism. Human kidneys can produce urine nearly four times concentrated than the initial filtrate formed.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/88_10018_question_1.png'),
(10019,'biology',87,1122,2694,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A healthy individual has 20-30 gms of hemoglobin in every 100 ml of blood.</div><div class="column-right">WBCs have an average life span of 120 days after which they are destroyed in the spleen.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the statements are incorrect. A healthy individual has 12-16 gms of haemoglobin in every $$100 \\mathrm{ml}$$ of blood. RBCs have an average life span of 120 days after which they are destroyed in the spleen.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10020,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Identify the part that contains (i) Both actin & myosin<br>(ii) Area not overlapped by thin filament during rest','[{"text": "(i) A-band&emsp;&emsp;(ii) M-line", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i) I-band&emsp;&emsp;(ii) H-zone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i) A-band&emsp;&emsp;(ii) M-zone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i) A-band&emsp;&emsp;(ii) H-zone", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A band contains both actin and myosin. Area overlapped by thin filament during rest is called as $\\mathrm{H}$ zone.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/89_10020_question_1.png'),
(10022,'biology',88,1154,2761,'The given diagram showing counter current mechanism. Which part of kidney is involved in this mechanism (A-C)?','[{"text": "A- Inner medulla, B- Outer medulla, C- Cortex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Cortex, B- Outer medulla, C- Inner medulla", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A- Cortex, B- Inner medulla, C- Outer medulla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Inner medulla, B- Cortex, C- Outer medulla", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Cortex<br>B. Outer Medulla<br>C. Inner Medulla',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/88_10022_question_1.png'),
(10023,'biology',87,1122,2694,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Neutrophils, eosinophils and basophils are different types of granulocytes, while lymphocytes and monocytes are the agranulocytes.<br></div><div class="column-right">Basophils are the most abundant cells (60-65%) of the total WBCs and neutrophils are the least (0.5-1%) among them.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement B is wrong. Neutrophils are the most abundant cells $$(60-65 %)$$ of the total WBCs and basophils are the least (0.5-1%) among them.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10024,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Component of actin filament of a sarcomere is','[{"text": "Actin, troponin and tropomyosin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Troponin and actin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Actin and myosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myosin and troponin", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Each actin (thin) filament is made of two \' F \' (filamentous) actins helically wound to each other. Each \' F \' actin is a polymer of monomeric \' G \' (Globular) actins. Two filaments of another protein, tropomyosin also run close to the \' F \' actins throughout its length. A complex protein Troponin is distributed at regular intervals on the tropomyosin. In the resting state a subunit of troponin masks the active binding sites for myosin on the actin filaments.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10025,'biology',9,24,42,'Male gamete is small and motile and female gamete is large and immotile in','[{"text": "<i>Fucus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Volvox</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ulothrix</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Fusion between one large, non-motile (static) female gamete and a smaller, motile male gamete is termed oogamous and is observed in Volvox and Fucus',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10026,'biology',88,1154,2761,'The diagram is showing mechanism of concentration of filtrate. Identify A and B in the diagram?','[{"text": "A- Vasa recta, B- cortex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Nephron, B- Vasa recta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Cortex, B- Medulla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Vasa recta, B- Nephron", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. Vasa Recta<br>B. Nephron',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/88_10026_question_1.png'),
(10027,'biology',87,1122,2694,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Neutrophils and monocytes are phagocytic cells which destroy foreign organisms entering the body.<br></div><div class="column-right">Basophils secrete histamine, serotonin, heparin etc and are involved in inflammatory reactions.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10028,'biology',89,1286,3107,'The proteins which in association with actin forms the thin filaments of muscles are','[{"text": "Tropomyosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Troponin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "F actin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Each actin (thin) filament is made of two \' F \' (filamentous) actins helically wound to each other. Each \' F \' actin is a polymer of monomeric \' G \' (Globular) actins. Two filaments of another protein, tropomyosin also run close to the \' F \' actins throughout its length. A complex protein Troponin is distributed at regular intervals on the tropomyosin. In the resting state a subunit of troponin masks the active binding sites for myosin on the actin filaments.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10029,'biology',9,24,42,'Both gametes in anisogamous are','[{"text": "Similar in size and non-motile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dissimilar in size", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Similar in size and motile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dissimilar in morphology", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Anisogamous means fusion of two morphologically dissimilar gametes, which may be motile or non-motile, e.g. in Eudorina.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
