(10046,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Osmoregulation is the function of','[{"text": "Oxytocin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ADH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasopressin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'ADH/Vasopressin is responsible for osmoregulation. It is released in response to the activation of osmoreceptors due to excessive loss of fluid from body. This hormone is released from the neurohypophysis and facilitates water reabsorption from latter parts of the tubule, thereby preventing diuresis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
