(10050,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Osmoregulators activated in response to excessive loss of fluid from body stimulate the release of','[{"text": "ADH from hypothalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renin from JG cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ADH from adenohypophysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ADH from neurohypophysis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Osmoreceptors in the body are activated by changes in the blood volume, body fluid volume and ionic concetration. An excessive loss of fluid from the body can activate these receptors, which stimulate the hypothalamus to release ADH (Anti Diuretic Hormone) or vasopressin from neurohypophysis (posterior lobe of pituitary).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
