(10059,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Actin binding sites are located on','[{"text": "Troponin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tropomyosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myosin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each myosin (thick) filament is also a polymerised protein. Many monomeric proteins called Meromyosin constitute one thick filament. Each meromyosin has two important parts, a globular head with a short arm and a tail, the globular head is an active ATPase enzyme and has binding sites for ATP and active sites for actin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
