(10066,'biology',88,1155,2762,'ADH causes','[{"text": "Increased water absorption from DCT and CT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increased GFR by increasing blood pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increases reabsorption of electrolyte from distal tubules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'ADH is released from the neurohypophysis and facilitates water reabsorption from latter parts of the tubule, thereby preventing diuresis. $$\\mathrm{ADH} /$$ Vasopressin can also affect the kidney function by its constrictory effects on blood vessels. An increase in blood pressure caused by constriction of blood vessels can increase the glomerular blood flow and thereby the GFR.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10067,'biology',89,1286,3107,'In the rest state, a subunit of troponin masks:-','[{"text": "Active binding sites for actin on the myosin filaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Active binding sites for myosin on the actin filaments", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Active binding sites for myosin on the myosin filaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Active binding sites for actin on the actin filaments", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During muscle contraction, calcium released from sarcoplasmic reticulum will bind to subunit of troponin of thin filament, binding of troponin to thin filament will expose (unmask) binding site for myosin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10068,'biology',87,1125,2697,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Lymph is a colourless fluid containing specialized lymphocytes which are responsible for the immune responses of the body.<br></div><div class="column-right">Lymph is also an important carrier for nutrients, hormones, etc. Fats are absorbed through lymph in the lacteals present in the intestinal villi.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10069,'biology',88,1155,2762,'In response to low GFR, rennin is released by','[{"text": "Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Posterior lobe of pitutary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "JG cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Rennin is a gastric, proteolytic enzyme responsible for milk digestion in children. Renin, on the other hand, released by JG cells in response to low GFR, converts angiotensinogen to angiotensin-I and further to angiotensin-II.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10070,'biology',9,24,42,'The alga used in space research is','[{"text": "All red algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Gelidium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Chlorella</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Gracilaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<i>Chlorella</i> is used for purifying air in space ships. It is also used as food supplements by space travellers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10071,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Identify the structure that masks the active binding site for myosin','[{"text": "A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{B}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Myosin itself", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In the rest state, a subunit of troponin labeled by letter \' $\\mathrm{C}$ \' masks the active binding site for myosin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/89_10071_question_1.png'),
(10072,'biology',87,1126,2698,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Open circulatory system is present in annelids and chordates in which blood pumped by the heart passes through large vessels into open spaces called sinuses.<br></div><div class="column-right">Closed circulatory system is present in arthropods and molluscs in which the blood pumped by the heart is always circulated through a closed network of blood vessels.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the statements are incorrect. Open circulatory system is present in arthropods and molluscs in which blood pumped by the heart passes through large vessels into open spaces called sinuses. Closed circulatory system is present in annelids and chordates in which the blood pumped by the heart is always circulated through a closed network of blood vessels.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10073,'biology',88,1155,2762,'The effect of antidiuretic hormone (ADH) on the kidney is to increase the','[{"text": "Excretion of water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Excretion of $$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Permeability of the distal nephron to water", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'An excessive loss of fluid from the body can activate the osmoreceptors which stimulate the hypothalamus to release antidiuretic hormone (ADH) or vasopressin from the neurohypophysis. ADH facilitates water reabsorption from latter parts of the tubule, thereby preventing diuresis. $$\\mathrm{ADH} /$$ Vasopressin can also affect the kidney function by its constrictory effects on blood vessels. An increase in blood pressure caused by constriction of blood vessels can increase the glomerular blood flow and thereby the GFR.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10074,'biology',9,24,42,'The algae rich in proteins and used as food by space travellers is','[{"text": "<i>Chlorella</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Porphyra</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Laminaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Chlorella</i>, a unicellular alga rich in proteins is used as food supplement even by space travellers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10075,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Each myosin (thick) filament is a ____ protein.','[{"text": "Monomerised", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dimerised", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polymerised", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Trimerised", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each myosin (thick) filament is a polymerised protein.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10076,'biology',87,1126,2698,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A muscular chambered heart is present in all vertebrates. Fishes have 2-chambered heart with an atrium and a ventricle.<br></div><div class="column-right">Amphibians and all reptiles including crocodiles have a 3-chambered heart with 2 atria and a single ventricle.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement $$B$$ is wrong. Amphibians and the reptiles (except crocodiles) have a 3-chambered heart with two atria and a single ventricle, whereas crocodiles, birds and mammals possess a 4-chambered heart with two atria and two ventricles',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10077,'biology',88,1155,2762,'The following reaction is brought about by Angiotensiogen $$\\rightarrow$$ Angiotensin-I $$\\rightarrow$$ Angiotensin-II.','[{"text": "Renin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{ADH}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasopressin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rennin", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Renin converts the angiotensinogen in blood to angiotensin-I and further to angiotensin-II. Renin is released by JG cells due to fall in GFR, in order to increase it.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10078,'biology',9,24,42,'Algae','[{"text": "Contributes to aquatic food", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contributes to dissolved oxygen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is used in production of commercial products like agar, hydrocolloids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Algae are useful to man in a variety of ways. Being photosynthetic they increase the level of dissolved oxygen in their immediate environment. They are of paramount importance as primary producers of energy rich compounds which form the basis of the food cycles of all aquatic animals. Many species of Porphyra, Laminaria and Sargassum are among the 70 species of marine algae used as food. Certain algae are used to obtain commericial products like agar-agar.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10079,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Myosin is made up of monomeric proteins called','[{"text": "Troponin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tropomyosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meromyosin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each myosin (thick) filament is also a polymerised protein. Many monomeric proteins called Meromyosin constitute one thick filament.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10080,'biology',87,1126,2698,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In fishes, the gills pump out deoxygenated blood which is oxygenated by the heart and supplied to the body parts from where deoxygenated blood is returned to gills.<br></div><div class="column-right">In incomplete double circulation, the left atrium receives oxygenated blood from gills or lungs and right atrium gets the deoxygenated blood from the other body parts. They get mixed up in the single ventricle.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement A is wrong. In fishes the heart pumps out deoxygenated blood which is oxygenated by the gills and supplied to the body parts from where deoxygenated blood is returned to the heart (single circulation).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10081,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which of the following is most likely to cause an increase in the glomerular filtration rates?','[{"text": "Blockage of ureter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dilation of the afferent arterioles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release of renin from the juxtaglomerular apparatus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Volume depletion", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A fall in glomerular blood flow/ glomerular blood pressure/GFR can activate the JG cells to release renin which converts angiotensinogen in blood to angiotensin I and further to angiotensin II. Angiotensin II, being a powerful vasoconstrictor, increases the glomerular blood pressure and thereby GFR.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10082,'biology',9,24,42,'Hydrocolloids are secreted by','[{"text": "All of the algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only brown algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both red and brown algae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only green algae", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Certain marine brown and red algae produce large amounts of hydrocolloids (water holding substances), e.g., algin (brown algae) and carrageen (red algae) which are used commercially.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10083,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Each meromyosin has two important parts. They are','[{"text": "A short arm and a tail", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A globular head and a tail", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A globular head with a short arm and a tail", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A globular head with a short arm", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each meromyosin has two important parts, a globular head with a short arm and a tail, the former being called the heavy meromyosin (HMM) and the latter, the light meromyosin (LMM).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10084,'biology',87,1127,2699,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Blood vascular system consists of a bony chambered heart, a network of closed branching blood vessels and the fluid blood.<br></div><div class="column-right">Heart is ectoderm in origin and is situated in the thoracic cavity in between two lungs, slightly tilted to the left.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the statements are incorrect. Human circulatory system, also called the blood vascular system consists of a muscular chambered heart, a network of closed branching blood vessels and blood, the fluid which is circulated. Heart, the mesodermally derived organ, is situated in the thoracic cavity, in between the two lungs, slightly tilted to the left.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10085,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Angiotensin-II increases the glomerular blood pressure and GFR as it is a/an','[{"text": "Osmoregulator", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasodilator", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasoconstrictor", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of there", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Angiotension-II, being a powerful vasoconstrictor, increases the glomerular blood pressure and thereby GFR. AngiotesinII also activates the adrenal cortex to release aldosterone.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10086,'biology',9,24,42,'Algin -a hydrocolloid is secreted by','[{"text": "All of the algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brown algae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Red algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both red and brown algae", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The hydrocolloid (water holding substance) – Algin is obtained from brown algae and is used commercially for various purposes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10087,'biology',89,1286,3107,'The globular head of HMM is an active ATPase enzyme and has<br>i. ATP binding sites<br>ii. Actin binding sites<br>iii. Myosin binding sites<br>iv. Troponin binding sites<br>v. Calcium binding sites','[{"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii and v", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The HMM component, i.e; the head and short arm projects outwards at regular distance and angle from each other from the surface of polymerised myosin filament and is known as cross arm. The globular head is an active ATPase enzyme and has binding sites for ATP and active sites for actin.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10165,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Binding of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ with ____ in the skeletal muscles and leads to the exposure of the myosin binding site for ____ on the filament','[{"text": "Troponin, actin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Troponin, myosin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Actin, troponin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tropomyosin, myosin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Binding of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ with troponin in the skeletal muscles and leads to the exposure of the myosin binding site for myosin on the filament.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10088,'biology',87,1127,2699,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Heart is protected by a double walled membranous bag, pleural membrane enclosing the pericardial fluid.<br></div><div class="column-right">Mammalian heart has four chambers, two relatively small upper chambers called atria and two larger lower chambers called ventricles.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement $$A$$ is wrong. Heart is protected by a double walled membranous bag, pericardium, enclosing the pericardial fluid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10089,'biology',9,24,42,'Carrageen is a','[{"text": "SCP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brown algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A hydrocolloid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Type of agar", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Carrageen is a hydrocolloid obtained from red algae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10090,'biology',88,1155,2762,'ANF (Anti Natriuretic Factor) is released by','[{"text": "Lung", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heart", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'An increase in blood flow can cause the release of Atrial Natriuretic Factor (ANF) from atrial walls of the heart. ANF can cause vasodilation (dilation of blood vessels) and thereby decrease the blood pressure. ANF mechanism, therefore, acts as a check on the renin-angiotensin mechanism.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10091,'biology',89,1286,3107,'The heavy meromyosin (HMM) component, i.e the head and short arm projects outwards at regular distance and angle form each other from the surface of a polymerised myosin filament and is known as','[{"text": "Cross arm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Motor unit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cross bridge", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neuromuscular junction", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The heavy meromyosin(HMM) component, i.e.; the head and short arm projects outwards at regular distance and angle from each other from the surface of polymerised myosin filament and is known as cross arm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10092,'biology',87,1127,2699,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Right and left atrium is separated by a thick muscular wall called inter-atrial septum.<br></div><div class="column-right">Left and right ventricle is separated by a thin-walled inter-ventricular septum.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the statements are incorrect. A thin, muscular wall called the interatrial septum separates the right and the left atria. a thickwalled, the inter-ventricular septum, separates the left and the right ventricles.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10093,'biology',88,1155,2762,'ANF mechanism checks on','[{"text": "Oxytocin-renin mechanism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Counter-current mechanims", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renin-angiotensin mechanism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oxytocin-angiotensin mechanism", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Atrial Natriuretic Factor (ANF) is produced by atria of heart during increased blood pressure/volume. It is responsible for causing vasodilation and thereby, decreasing the blood pressure. A decrease in blood pressure/ volume stimulates the hypothalamus to release $$\\mathrm{ADH}$$ (Anti Diuretic hormone) as well as JGA (Juxta Glomerular Apparatus) cells to release renin. Renin by renin-angiotensin mechanism activates the adrenal cortex to release aldosterone. Therefore, ANF mechanism acts as a check on renin-angiotensin mechanism.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10094,'biology',9,24,42,'Find out the mismatch pair<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Carrageen -red algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algin-brown algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Single celled protein-<em>Chlorella</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Agar -<em>Porphyra</em>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Agar-agar is obtained from <em>Gelidium</em> and <em>Gracilaria</em>.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10095,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Cross arms of the myosin monomer consist of','[{"text": "Outward projection of troponin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Outward projection of the tail region of meromyosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Outward projection of the head and arm region of meromyosin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (2) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each meromyosin has two important parts, a globular head with a short arm and a tail, the former being called the heavy meromyosin (HMM) and the latter, the light meromyosin (LMM). The HMM component, i.e.; the head and short arm projects outwards at regular distance and angle from each other from the surface of a polymerised myosin filament and is known as cross arm',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10096,'biology',87,1127,2699,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The atrium and the ventricle are separated by a thick fibrous tissue called atrio-ventricular septum.<br></div><div class="column-right">The opening between right atrium and the right ventricle is guarded by a valve formed of three muscular flaps called tricuspid valve.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10097,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Osmoreceptors in the body is activated by the changes in','[{"text": "Ionic concentration.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Body fluid volume", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood volume", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Osmoreceptors in the body are activated by changes in blood volume, body fluid volume and ionic concentration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10108,'biology',87,1128,2700,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Cardiac cycle is the sequential event in the heart which consists of systole and diastole of both the atria and ventricles.<br></div><div class="column-right">Ventricular systole decreases the ventricular pressure causing the closure of tricuspid and bicuspid valves.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement B is wrong. Ventricular systole increases the ventricular pressure causing the closure of tricuspid and bicuspid valve.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10098,'biology',9,24,42,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <em>Chlorella</em><br>B. <em>Laminaria </em>and <em>Sargassum</em><br>C. Algin <br>D. Carrageen<br>E. <em>Gelidium </em>and <em>Gracilaria</em></div><div class="column-right">P. Phaeophyceae<br>Q. SCP<br>R. Used as food<br>S. Agar<br>T. Rhodophyceae</div></div>','[{"text": "A &ndash; R, B &ndash; P, C &ndash; Q, D &ndash; T, E &ndash; S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A &ndash; Q, B &ndash; R, C &ndash; P, D &ndash; T, E &ndash; S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A &ndash; S, B &ndash; R, C &ndash; P, D &ndash; T, E &ndash; Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A &ndash; Q, B &ndash; T, C &ndash; P, D &ndash; R, E &ndash; S", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. <em>Chlorella</em> - Q. SCP<br>B. <em>Laminaria</em> and <em>Sargassum</em> - R. Used as food<br>C. Algin - P. Phaeophyceae<br>D. Carrageen - T. Rhodophyceae<br>E. <em>Gelidium</em> and <em>Gracilaria</em> - S. Agar',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10099,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Select the correct answer<br>I. Each myosin (thin) filament is also a polymerised protein<br>II. The globular head is an active ATPase enzyme and has binding sites for ATP and active sites for troponin.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Each myosin (thick) filament is also a polymerised protein. The globular head is an active ATPase enzyme and has binding sites for ATP and active sites for actin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10100,'biology',87,1127,2699,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The opening between left atrium and left ventricle is guarded by mitral valve.<br></div><div class="column-right">The opening of the right and left ventricles into the pulmonary artery and the aorta respectively are provided with the semi-lunar valves.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10101,'biology',88,1155,2762,'In deficiency of $$\\mathrm{ADH}$$, the rate of micturition','[{"text": "Decreases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Remains the same", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$$\\mathrm{ADH}$$ facilitates water reabsorption from latter parts of the tubule, thereby preventing diuresis (excessive production of urine). In deficiency of $$\\mathrm{ADH}$$, the rate of micturition increases.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10102,'biology',9,24,42,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Chlorophyceae<br>B. Phaeophyceae<br>C. Rhodophyceae</div><div class="column-right">P. Red algae<br>Q. Green algae<br>R. Brown algae</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R, B – P, C – Q,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – R, C – P,", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A – P, B – R, C – Q,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – P, C – R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Chlorophyceae - Q. Green algae<br>B. Phaeophyceae - R. Brown algae<br>C. Rhodophyceae - P. Red algae',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10103,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. ‘F’ actins<br>B. Tropomyosin<br>C. Troponin</div><div class="column-right">P. Run close to the ‘F’ actins throughout its length<br>Q. Masks the active binding sites<br>R. ‘G’ actins</div></div>','[{"text": "A–R, B–P, C–Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A–Q, B–R, C–P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A–P , B–R, C–Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A–Q, B–P, C–R", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'\'F\' actins - \'G\' actin<br>Tropomyosin - Run close to the \'F\' actins throughout it\'s length<br>Troponin - Masks the active binding sites.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10104,'biology',87,1127,2699,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">SA node is a special cardiac nodal which is present in the right upper corner of the right atrium.<br></div><div class="column-right">The SA node can generate the maximum number of action potentials $$40-45$$ per minute and is responsible for initiating and maintaining the rhythmic contractile activity of the heart.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement B is wrong. The SA node can generate the maximum number of action potentials $$70-72$$ per minute and is responsible for initiating and maintaining the rhythmic contractile activity of the heart.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10105,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Volume of urine is regulated by','[{"text": "Aldosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aldosterone and $$\\\\mathrm{ADH}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aldosterone, $$\\\\mathrm{ADH}$$ and testosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{ADH}$$ alone", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$$\\mathrm{ADH}$$ facilitates water reabsorption from latter parts of the tubule. Aldosterone causes reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{Na}+$$ and water from the distal parts of the tubule. Hence, both regulate the volume of urine produced.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10106,'biology',9,24,43,'The members of Chlorophyceae are commonly called','[{"text": "Red algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green algae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Brown algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blue-green algae", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All the species of green algae are clubbed together in the Class Chlorophyceae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10107,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Read the statements regarding muscle protein<br>I. Actin is a thin filament and is made up of two F-actins.<br>II. Complex protein, tropomyosin is distributed at regular intervals on the troponin.<br>III. Myosin is a thick filament which is also a polymerized protein.<br>IV. Globular head of meromyosin consists of light meromysin (LMM).<br>Of the above statements:','[{"text": "I, III and IV are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II and IV are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Complex protein, troponin is distributed at regular intervals on the tropomyosin.<br>Globular head of meromyosin consists of heavy meromyosin (HMM).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10201,'biology',89,1287,3108,'During muscle contraction','[{"text": "Size of sarcomere becomes smaller", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Size of A- band increases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Size of I -band decreases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During muscle contraction size of sarcomere becomes smaller.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10109,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Increase in blood pressure is caused by','[{"text": "$$\\\\uparrow$$ in Angiotensinogen II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\uparrow$$ in Aldosterone secretion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\uparrow$$ in $$\\\\mathrm{ADH}$$ secretion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Angiotensin II, being a powerful vasoconstrictor, increases the glomerular blood pressure and thereby GFR. ADH can also affect the kidney function by its constrictory effects on blood vessels. This causes an increase in blood pressure. Aldosterone causes reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and water from the distal parts of the tubule. This also leads to an increase in blood pressure and GFR.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10110,'biology',9,24,43,'Chlorophyceae are grass green due to the dominance of pigment','[{"text": "Chlorophyll a, c", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlorophyll a, b", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chlorophyll a, d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Xanthophyll", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Members of Chlorophyceae are usually grass green due to the dominance of pigments chlorophyll a and b.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10111,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Choose the incorrect pair.','[{"text": "Globular head of meromyosin - Active ATPase enzyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thin elastic membrane holding -M-line thick filaments in A-band", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dark bands - Anisotropic band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Each actin (thin) filament is made of two \'F\' (filamentous) actins", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The thin filaments are firmly attached to the \' Z \' line. The thick filaments in the \' A \' band are also held together in the middle of this band by a thin fibrous membrane called \' M \' line.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10112,'biology',87,1128,2700,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Stroke volume is the amount of blood which is pumped out by each ventricle during a cardiac cycle.<br></div><div class="column-right">Cardiac output is defined as the volume of blood pumped out by each ventricle per minute.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10113,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which of the following is true about ANF?','[{"text": "It causes vasodialtion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antagonistic to Renin-Angiotensin mechanism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decreases blood pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'An increase in blood flow to the atria of the heart can cause the release of Atrial Natriuretic Factor (ANF). ANF can cause vasodilation (dilation of blood vessels) and thereby decrease the blood pressure. ANF mechanism therefore, keeps a check on the renin-angiotensin mechanism by acting antagonistic to it.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10114,'biology',9,24,43,'The members of Chlorophyceae, phaeophyceae and rhodophyceae have a common pigment, identify it from the below option','[{"text": "chlorophyll-a", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "chlorophyll-b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "chlorophyll-a and b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "chlorophyll-c", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Chlorophyll-a, also known as the universal pigment is present in all plants. It is hence a common pigment in Chlorophyceae, Phaeophyceae and Rhodophyceae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10115,'biology',89,1287,3108,'During muscle contraction','[{"text": "Size of A-band remains the same", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Size of H-zone becomes larger", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diameter of fibre increases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Size of I-bands increase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The dark band of myofibril is called A- band (Anisotropic band). Thick myofibrils are confined to \' $\\mathrm{A}$ \' bands, it contains myosin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10116,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Stimulus for activation of JG cells to release renin is/are','[{"text": "$$\\\\downarrow$$ GFR", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\downarrow$$ Glomerular blood pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\downarrow$$ Glomerular blood flow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A fall in glomerular blood flow/glomerular blood pressure/GFR can activate the JG cells to release renin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10117,'biology',87,1129,2701,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Lub is associated with the closure of the tricuspid and bicuspid valve whereas dub is associated with the closure of the semilunar valves.<br></div><div class="column-right">ECG is a graphical representation of the electrical activity of the lungs during a cardiac cycle.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement B is wrong. ECG is a graphical representation of the electrical activity of the heart during a cardiac cycle.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10118,'biology',9,24,43,'Identify the different types of chloroplasts in Chlorophyceae?','[{"text": "Discoid and plate-like", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reticulate and cup-shaped", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spiral or ribbon-shaped", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The pigments in green algae are localized in definite chloroplasts. The chloroplasts may be discoid, plate-like, reticulate, cup-shaped, spiral or ribbon-shaped in different species.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10119,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Mechanism of muscle contraction is best explained by','[{"text": "Actin-Myosin filament theory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gliding filament theory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sliding filament theory", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Saltation filament theory", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mechanism of muscle contraction is best explained by the sliding filament theory which states that contraction of a muscle fibre takes place by the sliding of the thin filaments over the thick filaments.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10130,'biology',87,1131,2703,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Human heart is called myogenic because it is autoregulated by specialized nodal tissue called SA node.<br></div><div class="column-right">A special neural centre in the medulla oblongata can moderate the cardiac function through autonomic nervous system.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10120,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Bowman’s capsule<br>B. Contains more ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ and less urea<br>C. Anti-diuretic hormone<br>D. Contains more urea</div><div class="column-right">P. Renal artery<br>Q. Regulates amount of water excreted<br>R. Renal vein<br>S. Glomerulus</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. Bowman\'s capsule - S. Glomerulus<br>B. Contains more $$\\mathrm{CO} 2$$ and less urea - R. Renal vein<br>C. Anti-diuretic hormone - Q. Regulates amount of water excreted<br>D. Contains more urea - P. Renal artery',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10121,'biology',9,24,43,'Pyrenoids are located in','[{"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroplast", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Most of the members have one or more storage bodies called pyrenoids located in the chloroplasts. Pyrenoids contain protein besides starch.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10122,'biology',87,1129,2701,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The P-wave in ECG represents the depolarization of the atria which leads to the contraction of both the atria.<br></div><div class="column-right">The QRS complex represents the depolarization of the ventricles which initiates the ventricular contraction.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10123,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Contraction of muscle fibre takes place by the sliding of','[{"text": "Thin filaments over the actin filaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thick filaments over the thin filaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thick filaments over the myosin filaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thin filaments over the thick filaments", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'According to sliding filament theory of muscle contraction, thin myofilaments slide over the thick filament and penetrate deeper into A bands in the contracting muscle fibre.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10124,'biology',9,24,43,'Pyrenoids store','[{"text": "Protein and Starch", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only starch", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pyrenoids, a characteristic feature of the green algae help in the storage of proteins and starch.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10125,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Osmoreceptors<br>B. Hypothalamus<br>C. Juxtaglomerular cells<br>D. Angiotensin-II</div><div class="column-right">P. Releases vasopressin<br>Q. Activates adrenal cortex to release Aldosterone<br>R. Activated by changes in blood volume and ionic concentration<br>S. Release renin</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A. Osmoreceptors - R. Activated by changes in blood volume and ionic concentration<br>B. Hypothalamus - P. Releases vasopressin<br>C. Juxtaglomerular cells - S. Release renin<br>D. Angiotensin-II - Q. Activates adrenal cortex to release Aldosterone',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10126,'biology',87,1130,2702,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In pulmonary circulation, deoxygenated blood pumped from pulmonary artery to the lungs from where oxygenated blood is carried by the pulmonary veins to the left atrium.<br></div><div class="column-right">In systemic circulation, the oxygenated blood from aorta is carried to the tissues from where the deoxygenated blood is collected by vena cava and emptied into the right atrium.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the given statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10127,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Which of the following statement is correct regarding sliding filament theory?','[{"text": "Contraction of muscle fibre takes place by the sliding of thick filament over thin filament", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contraction of muscle fibre takes place by the sliding of thin filament over thick filament", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Contraction of muscle fibre takes place by the sliding of thick and thin filament on each other", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'H. E. Huxley, A. F. Huxley and Ralph gave the sliding filament theory of muscle contraction which states that the thin myofilaments slide over the thick filament and penetrate deeper into $\\mathrm{A}$ bands in the contracting muscle fibre.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10128,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Aldosterone<br>B. Anti-diuretic hormone<br>C. Renin<br>D. Atrial Natriuretic Factor</div><div class="column-right">P. Cause vasodilation of blood vessels<br>Q. Causes reabsorption of ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ and water from DCT<br>R. Prevent diuresis<br>S. Converts Angiotensinogen to Angiotensin-I</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-S, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Aldosterone Q. Causes reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{Na}+$$ and water from DCT<br>B. Anti-diuretic hormone R. Prevent diuresis<br>C. Renin S. Converts Angiotensinogen to Angiotensin-I<br>D. Atrial Natriuretic Factor P. Cause vasodilation of blood vessels',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10129,'biology',9,24,43,'How many pyrenoids are present in the members of class-chlorophyceae?','[{"text": "One", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hundreds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One to many", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pyrenoids are coverings of chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Most of the members of Chlorophyceae have one to many storage bodies called pyrenoids located in the chloroplasts. Pyrenoids contain protein besidesstarch.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10133,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Atria of heart<br>B. Adrenal cortex<br>C. JG cells of kidney</div><div class="column-right">P. Release renin<br>Q. Release ANF<br>R. Release aldosteron</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A. Atria of Heart - Q. Release ANF<br>B. Adrenal cortex - R. Release Aldosterone<br>C. JG cells of kidney - P. Release renin',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10134,'biology',87,1131,2703,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Neural signals through the sympathetic nerves can decrease the rate of heartbeat, the strength of ventricular contraction.<br></div><div class="column-right">Parasympathetic neural signals increase the rate of heartbeat, speed of conduction of action potential and thereby the cardiac output.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the statements are incorrect. Neural signals through the sympathetic nerves (part of ANS) can increase the rate of heartbeat, the strength of ventricular contraction and thereby the cardiac output. On the other hand, parasympathetic neural signals (another component of ANS) decrease the rate of heartbeat, speed of conduction of action potential and thereby the cardiac output.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10135,'biology',89,1287,3108,'What is the location of troponin in the process of muscle contraction?','[{"text": "Attached to calcium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Attached to tropomyosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Attached to myosin cross bridge", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In the event of muscle contraction, the $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ binding causes a conformational change in the troponin which results in pulling the tropomyosin away exposing the active sites on the actin filaments to which the myosin heads bind to initiate muscle contraction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
