(10136,'biology',9,24,43,'The members of chlorophyceae usually have a rigid cell wall made up of','[{"text": "Cellulose (outer layer) and algin (inner layer)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pectose (inner layer) and peptidoglycan (outer layer)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellulose (inner layer) and pectose (outer layer)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cellulose (inner layer) and pectin (outer layer", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Green algae usually have a rigid cell wall made of an inner layer of cellulose and an outer layer of pectose.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10137,'biology',88,1156,2763,'Which of these will be completely reabsorbed from glomerular filtrate under normal conditions in the nephrons?','[{"text": "Urea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Salts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Usually, under normal conditions, glucose is completely reabsorbed from glomerular filtrate. Presence of glucose in urine due to the malfunctioning of kidney causes Glycosuria.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10138,'biology',87,1132,2704,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Cardiac arrest means when the heart muscle is suddenly damaged by an inadequate blood supply.<br></div><div class="column-right">Heart failure means the state of heart when it is not pumping blood effectively enough to meet the needs of the body.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement A is wrong. When the heart stops beating it is called as cardiac arrest.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10139,'biology',88,1156,2763,'Identify the organ where urine is stored till a voluntary signal is given by','[{"text": "Ureter, CNS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Urinary bladder, CNS", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Urinary bladder, PNS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Urinary bladder, SNS", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Urine formed by the nephrons is ultimately carried to the urinary bladder where it is stored till a voluntary signal is given by the central nervous system (CNS).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10140,'biology',9,24,43,'Starch as stored food is present in','[{"text": "Members of chlorophyceae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Members of rhodophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Members of phaeophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Food is stored in the form of starch in chlorophyceae (green algae).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10141,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Motor unit is a','[{"text": "Neuron only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Muscle cell only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Motor neuron with muscle fibre", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Muscle fascicle", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A motor neuron along with the muscle fibres connected to it constitute a motor unit.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10142,'biology',87,1132,2704,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Coronary artery disease is caused by deposits of calcium, fat, cholesterol and fibrous tissues, which makes the lumen of arteries narrower.<br></div><div class="column-right">In angina pectoris, acute chest pain appears when enough oxygen is reaching the heart muscle.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement B is wrong. \'angina pectoris\', A symptom of acute chest pain appears when no enough oxygen is reaching the heart muscle.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10143,'biology',9,24,43,'Anteriorly placed, equal, 2-8, flagella are characteristic to','[{"text": "Members of chlorophyceae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Members of rhodophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Members of phaeophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Anteriorly placed, equal, 2-8, flagella are characteristic to the members of Chlorophyceae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10144,'biology',88,1156,2763,'The process of release of urine is called','[{"text": "Micturition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sweating", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Defecation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osmoregulation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The process of release of urine is called micturition and the neural mechanisms causing it is called the micturition reflex.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10147,'biology',88,1156,2763,'What happens in micturition reflex?','[{"text": "Contraction of striated muscles of bladder", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contraction of the urethral sphincter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release of urine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Micturition is defined as the process of release of urine. If the urine content of urinary bladder reaches more than $$300 \\mathrm{~mL}$$, micturition reflex activates CNS to contract smooth muscles and relax the urethral sphincter muscle that leads to the release of urine.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10148,'biology',9,24,43,'In chlorophyceae, vegetative reproduction takes place by','[{"text": "Fragmentation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Formation of different types of spores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zoospores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Vegetative reproduction in green algae usually takes place by fragmentation or by formation of different types of spores.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10149,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Skeletal muscle contraction is initiated by a signal sent by','[{"text": "ANS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PNS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "CNS", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neural transmitters", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Muscle contraction is initiated by a signal sent by the central nervous system (CNS) via a motor neuron.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10151,'biology',88,1156,2763,'An adult human excretes on an average','[{"text": "180 litres of urine per day", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-1.5 litres of urine per day", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2-5 litres of urine per day", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4-5 litres of urine per day", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'An adult human excretes, on an average, 1 to 1.5 litres of urine per day.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10152,'biology',9,24,43,'Zoospores are formed in algae and formed in','[{"text": "Zoophores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microsporangia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zoosporangia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Megasporangia", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Asexual reproduction in chlorophyceae is by flagellated zoospores produced in zoosporangia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10153,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Action potential in the sarcolemma of muscles is generated by','[{"text": "Methylcholine- a neurotransmitter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acetylcholine-a neurotransmitter", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Troponin- a neurotransmitter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acetylcholine-a neuroinhibitor", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A neural signal reaching this junction releases a neurotransmitter (Acetyl choline) which generates an action potential in the sarcolemma. This spreads through the muscle fibre and causes the release of calcium ions into the sarcoplasm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10155,'biology',88,1156,2763,'Human urine is acidic due to the presence of','[{"text": "Glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Urea", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ketone bodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uric acid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Urine formed is slightly acidic ( $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ 6.0) due to the presence of urea.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10156,'biology',9,24,43,'Sexual reproduction is of isogamous, anisogamous and oogamous in','[{"text": "Phaeophyceae and Rhodophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rhodophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlorophyceae and Phaeophyceae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chlorophyceae and Rhodophyceae", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In Chlorophyceae and Phaeophyceae, the sexual reproduction shows considerable variation in the type and formation of sex cells and it may be isogamous, anisogamous or oogamous. Whereas, in Rhodophyceae, only oogamous mode of reproduction is seen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10157,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Name the neurotransmitter which generates an action potential in the sarcolemma','[{"text": "Serotonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epinephrine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acetylcholine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adrenaline", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A neural signal reaching this junction releases a neurotransmitter (Acetyl choline) which generates an action potential in the sarcolemma. This spreads through the muscle fibre and causes the release of calcium ions into the sarcoplasm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10159,'biology',88,1156,2763,'On an average, the amount of urea in gram excreted out per day is','[{"text": "$20 - 25\\\\,{\\\\rm{gm}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$25 - 30\\\\,{\\\\rm{gm}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$25 - 30\\\\,{\\\\rm{mg}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$40 - 45\\\\,{\\\\rm{gm}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'On an average, 25-30 gm of urea is excreted out per day.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10160,'biology',9,24,43,'Which one of the following belongs to green algae?','[{"text": "<i>Udorina</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ectocarpus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ulothrix</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both 1 and 3. Ectocarpus is a brown algae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10161,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Chemical ions responsible for muscle contraction are','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$and $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$and $\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ and $\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ and $\\\\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Calcium ions play a significant role in muscle contraction. These activate the interaction of myosin and actin, through the intervention of tropomyosin and troponin. Magnesium, in muscle contraction, stimulates calcium re-uptake by the calcium-activated ATPase of the sarcoplasmic reticulum. It also affects the translocation of calcium ions through the smooth muscle cell membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10163,'biology',9,24,43,'Name the green algae which shows oogamous type sexual reproduction','[{"text": "<i>Sphagnum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Volvox</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Dictyota</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Spirogyra</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Fusion between one large, non-motile (static) female gamete and a smaller, motile male gamete is termed oogamous, e.g., Volvox.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10164,'biology',88,1156,2763,'Analysis of urine help in the diagnosis of','[{"text": "Metabolic disorders", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Malfunctioning of kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diabetes mellitus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Various conditions can affect the characteristics of urine. Analysis of urine helps in clinical diagnosis of many metabolic disorders eg. Diabetes mellitus as well as malfunctioning of the kidney.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10167,'biology',88,1156,2763,'Indication of diabetes mellitus is/are','[{"text": "The presence of glucose in urine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The presence of ketone bodies in urine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The presence of amino acid in urine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The presence of glucose (glycosuria) and ketone bodies (ketonuria) in the urine are indicative of diabeties mellitus. Analysis of urine helps in clinical diagnosis of many metabolic disorders as well as malfunctioning of the kidney.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10168,'biology',9,24,43,'Algae which form motile colony is','[{"text": "<i>Spirogyra</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Nostoc</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Volvox</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Chlamydomonas</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Colonial form of green algae is represented by Volvox.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10169,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Action potential in sarcolemma of muscles causes the release of which ions from sarcoplasmic reticulum?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A neural signal reaching this junction releases a neurotransmitter (Acetyl choline) which generates an action potential in the sarcolemma. This spreads through the muscle fibre and causes the release of calcium ions from sarcoplasmic reticulum into the sarcoplasm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10171,'biology',88,1156,2763,'Presence of glucose and ketone bodies in urine is called','[{"text": "Glycosuria and ketonuria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glucosuria and ketonuria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycosuria and ketonemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diabetes and ketonuria", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The presence of glucose (glycosuria) and ketone bodies (ketonuria) in the urine are both indicative of diabetes mellitus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
