(10192,'biology',88,1157,2764,'Other than kidney which other organs help in excretion?','[{"text": "Lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Skin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liver", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Other than the kidneys, lungs, liver and skin also help in the elimination of excretory wastes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10193,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Which of the following has ATPase activity on its head?','[{"text": "Tropomyosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myosin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Catin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Troponin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Each myosin (thick) filament is a polymerised protein called meromyosin. Each meromyosin has two important parts, a globular head with a short arm and a tail, the former being called the heavy meromyosin (HMM) and the latter, the light meromyosin (LMM). The globular head is an active ATPase enzyme and has binding sites for ATP and active sites for actin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10195,'biology',9,24,44,'In brown algae, brown colour is due to the presence of','[{"text": "Carotenoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Xanthophyll", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phycoerythrin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlorophyll", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Brown algae vary in colour from olive green to various shades of brown depending upon the amount of the xanthophyll pigment, fucoxanthin present in them.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10196,'biology',88,1157,2764,'Sweat produced by sweat glands is a watery fluid which contains','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NaCl}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Urea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lactic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sweat produced by the sweat glands is a watery fluid containing $$\\mathrm{NaCl}$$, small amounts of urea, lactic acid, etc. Though the primary function of sweat is to facilitate a cooling effect on the body surface, it also helps in the removal of some of the wastes mentioned above.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10197,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Identify the labeled parts from A, B, C from the diagram of myosin monomer','[{"text": "A-Head&emsp;B-Cross arm&emsp;C-ATP binding site", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Head&emsp;B-Cross arm&emsp;C-GTP binding site", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Cross&emsp;B-Head arm&emsp;C-ATP binding site", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Head&emsp;B-Cross arm&emsp;C-${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{a}}^{{\\\\rm{2 + }}}}$ binding site", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The labeled parts from A,B,C from the diagram of myosin monomer are head, cross arm and ATP binding site respectively.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/89_10197_question_1.png'),
