(10244,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Statements about the mechanism of muscle contraction are given below.<br>I. Acetycholine is released when the neural signal reaches the motor end plate<br>II. Muscle contraction is initiated by a signal sent by CNS via a motor neuron<br>III. During muscle contraction isotropic band gets elongated<br>IV. Repeated activation of the muscles can lead to pyruvic acid accumulation<br>Identify the correct statements','[{"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Muscle contraction is initiated by a signal sent by the central nervous system (CNS) via a motor neuron. A neural signal reaching neuromuscular junction releases a neurotransmitter (Acetyl choline) which generates an action potential in the sarcolemma. This spreads through the muscle fibre and causes the release of calcium ions into the sarcoplasm.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10245,'biology',88,1158,2765,'Which is the ultimate method for the correction of acute renal failure?','[{"text": "Haemodialysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renal transplantation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Blood transfusion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heparin injection", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Kidney/Renal transplantation is the ultimate method in the correction of acute renal failures (kidney failure). A functioning kidney is used in transplantation from a donor, preferably a close relative, to minimise its chances of rejection by the immune system of the host.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
