(10250,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Find the correct order of stages of muscle contraction?','[{"text": "Stimuli $\\\\rightarrow$ Release of Neurotransmitter $\\\\rightarrow$ Release of $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+} \\\\rightarrow$ Cross bridges formation $\\\\rightarrow$ Excitation of sarcolemma<br>$\\\\rightarrow$ Sliding of actin filaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimuli $\\\\rightarrow$ Release of Neurotransmitter<br>$\\\\rightarrow$ Cross bridges formation $\\\\rightarrow$ Excitation of sarcolemma $\\\\rightarrow$ Sliding of actin filaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimuli $\\\\rightarrow$ Excitation of sarcolemma<br>$\\\\rightarrow$ Release of Neurotransmitter $\\\\rightarrow$ Cross bridges formation $\\\\rightarrow$ Sliding of actin filaments $\\\\rightarrow$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimuli $\\\\rightarrow$ Release of Neurotransmitter $\\\\rightarrow$ Excitation of sarcolemma $\\\\rightarrow$ Release of $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+} \\\\rightarrow$ Cross bridges formation $\\\\rightarrow$ Sliding of actin filaments", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct order of stages of muscle contraction is as follow:<br>Stimuli-Release of Neurotransmitter<br>Excitation of sarcolemma-Release of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ -<br>Cross bridges formation - Sliding of actin filaments.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10251,'biology',9,24,44,'Vegetative reproduction in brown algae takes place by','[{"text": "Budding", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiple fission", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fragmentation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vegetative reproduction never occurs", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Vegetative reproduction in members of Phaeophyceae takes place by fragmentation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10253,'biology',88,1158,2765,'Uremia is treated by?','[{"text": "Haemodialysis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Renal transplantation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood transfusion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heparin injection", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Malfunctioning of kidneys can lead to accumulation of urea in blood, a condition called uremia, which is highly harmful and may lead to kidney failure. In such patients, urea can be removed by a process called hemodialysis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
