(10258,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Biomolecule that accumulates in a fatigued muscle is','[{"text": "Pyruvic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lactic acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{ADP}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Accumulation of lactic acid causes muscle fatigue. Reduction in force of contraction of a muscle after a prolonged stimulation is muscle fatigue. A muscle that has fatigue needs extra oxygen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10261,'biology',88,1158,2765,'Following are the steps of dialysis:<br>A. Blood is drained from convenient artery.<br>B. Blood is mixed with heparin.<br>C. Blood is mixed with anti-heparin.<br>D. Blood is passed into a vein.<br>E. Blood is passed through a coiled and porous cellophane tube bathing in dialysis fluid.<br>F. Removal of nitrogenous wastes from blood.<br>The correct sequence of steps is','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{D} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{B} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{F} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{E} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{A}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{A} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{B} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{E} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{F} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{D}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{A} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{E} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{B} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{F} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{D}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{D} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{E} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{F} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{B} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{A}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During the process of haemodialysis, the blood drained from a convenient artery is pumped into a dialysing unit called artificial kidney. Blood drained from a convenient artery is pumped into a dialysing unit after adding an anticoagulant like heparin. The unit contains a coiled cellophane tube surrounded by a fluid (dialysing fluid) having the same composition as that of plasma except the nitrogenous wastes. The porous cellophane membrane of the tube allows the passage of molecules based on concentration gradient. As nitrogenous wastes are absent in the dialysing fluid, these substances freely move out, thereby clearing the blood. The cleared blood is pumped back to the body through a vein after adding antiheparin to it.<br>Hence, the process of haemodialysis follows the sequence - A, B, E, F, C, D.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10262,'biology',89,1287,3108,'During strenuous exercise, glucose is converted into','[{"text": "Lactic acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pyruvic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Starch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycogen", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Repeated activation of the muscle can lead to the accumulation of lactic acid due to anaerobic breakdown of glycogen in them, causing fatigue.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10264,'biology',88,1158,2765,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Uremia<br>B. Renal calculi<br>C. Glomerulo-nephritis</div><div class="column-right">P. Insoluble mass of crystallized salts of oxalates<br>Q. Accumulation of urea in blood<br>R. Inflammation of glomeruli of kidney</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Uraemia - Q. Accumulation of urea in bloodB. Renal calculi - P. Insoluble mass of crystallized salts of oxalatesC. Glomerulonephritis - R. Inflammation of glomeruli of kidney',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10265,'biology',9,24,44,'The zoospores are characterised by one of the following feature. Identify it','[{"text": "Uniflagellate pear-shaped", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "biflagellate apple-shaped", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "biflagellate pear-shaped", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Uniflagellate apple -shaped", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Zoospores in responsible for asexual reproduction in phaeophyceae are biflagellate and pear-shaped.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10266,'biology',89,1287,3108,'During strenuous exercise which of the following process occurs','[{"text": "Anaerobic respiration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aerobic respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethanol fermentation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During strenuous exercise anaerobic respiration process occurs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10268,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Select the incorrect statement from the following:','[{"text": "Animals accumulate ammonia, urea, uric acid, $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and water by metabolic activities.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Animal accumulate substances like ions $$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}, \\\\mathrm{K}^{+}, \\\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}\\\\right)$$and urea, ammonia, uric acid, $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and water are removed totally or partially.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ammonia produced by metabolism is converted into urea in the liver of mammals.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kidneys play significant role in the removal of ammonia directly.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Animals accumulate ammonia, urea, uric acid, carbon dioxide, water and ions like $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$, $$\\mathrm{K}^{+}, \\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$$, phosphate, sulphate, etc., either by metabolic activities or by other means like excess ingestion. These substances have to be removed totally or partially. Ammonia produced by metabolism is converted to urea in the liver via Urea/Ornithine cycle. Urea produced is excreted by the kidneys in the form of urine.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10269,'biology',9,24,44,'Sexual reproduction shown by brown algae is','[{"text": "Isogamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anisogamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oogamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sexual reproduction in brown algae may be isogamous, anisogamous or oogamous. The gametes are pyriform (pear-shaped) and bear two laterally attached flagella.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10270,'biology',89,1287,3108,'The reaction which change lactic acid into glycogen come under','[{"text": "Calvin cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Krebs cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coricycle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glycolysis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Repeated activation of the muscles can lead to the accumulation of lactic acid due to anaerobic breakdown of glycogen in them, causing fatigue.<br>Fatigue is the inability of the muscle to contract due to deposition of lactic acid by repeated contraction. Lactic acid is transported to liver by blood and converted to glycogen through Cori\'s cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10272,'biology',88,1158,2765,'Select the incorrect statement from the following.','[{"text": "High-protein diet can increase the levels of urea in your blood.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diabetes mellitus decreases the levels of ketone bodies in the urine.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Foods like spinach that contain high levels of oxalate may lead to formation of renal calculi.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Drinking too much alcohol will increase the urine output", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Diabetes mellitus increases the levels of ketone bodies in the urine.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10273,'biology',9,24,44,'Fertilization in brown algae occurs in','[{"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Within the oogonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Air", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In sexual reproduction performed by brown algae, union of gametes or fertilization may take place in water or within the oogonium (oogamous species).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10276,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Characteristic shared by urea, uric acid and ammonia are<br>i. They are nitrogenous wastes.<br>ii. They need small amount of water for excretion<br>iii. They are equally toxic<br>iv. They are secreted in kidney alone','[{"text": "i, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ammonia, urea and uric acid are the major forms of nitrogenous wastes excreted by the animals. Ammonia is the most toxic form and requires large amount of water for its elimination, whereas uric acid, being the least toxic, can be removed with a minimum loss of water.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10277,'biology',9,24,44,'Pyriform gametes means','[{"text": "Pea-shaped gametes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pear shaped gametes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apple shaped gametes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Gametes that are pear-shaped are known as pyriform gametes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10278,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Myoglobin occurs in','[{"text": "Red muscle fibre", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "White fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cardiac muscle fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Red muscles are thin muscle fibres which are dark red in colour due to presence of large amount of myoglobin which is a red haemoprotein. Myoglobin stores oxygen as oxymyoglobin in red muscle fibres, it releases oxygen for utilisation during muscle contraction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10280,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Substances like amino acids and glucose in the filtrate are reabsorbed ____A____ in the tubular epithelial cells whereas the nitrogenous wastes are absorbed by____B____ transport,','[{"text": "A-actively; B-passive", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-passively; B-active", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-actively; B-active", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-passively; B-passive", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The tubular epithelial cells in different segments of nephron perform reabsorption either by active or passive mechanisms. For example, substances like glucose, amino acids, $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$, etc., in the filtrate are reabsorbed actively whereas the nitrogenous wastes are absorbed by passive transport.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10281,'biology',9,24,44,'Two laterally attached flagella are present in brown algae in which of the following structures?','[{"text": "Gametes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zoospores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Frond", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In brown algae, both zoospores (asexual reproduction) and gametes (sexual reproduction) bear two laterally attached flagella.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10282,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Which one is not a feature of "Red muscles"?','[{"text": "Red muscles contain more amount of myoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They has more mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They obtain energy anaerobically", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They has less amount of sarcoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Red muscles have mitochondria; hence they obtain energy aerobically.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10284,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Blood in the renal vein differs from that in renal artery in having','[{"text": "More $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$, less urea and more glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$, less urea and less glucose", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Less $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$, less urea, and less glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Less $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$, more urea and more glucose.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ is generally more in venous blood than in arterial blood. As kidneys excrete urea, concentration of urea in blood passing through the renal vein is less than that in the renal artery. Furthermore some glucose will consumed by the renal cells. So, there will be less glucose in the blood passing.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10285,'biology',9,24,44,'Pear-shaped gametes are found in','[{"text": "<i>Ectocarpus, Dictyota</i> and <i>Kelps</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Kelps, Spirogyra</i> and <i>Ectocarpus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ectocarpus, Gelidium </i>and <i>Gracilaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ectocarpus, Kelps</i> and <i>Volvox</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pyriform, biflagellate gametes are a characteristic of brown algae. The common forms are <i>Ectocarpus, Dictyota, Kelps</i>.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10286,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Which of the following is not the feature of red muscle fibres','[{"text": "They have high content of Myoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have plenty of mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are called aerobic muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have high amount of Sarcoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The red muscle fibres have high amount of myoglobin. White muscle fibres have high amount of sarcoplasmic reticulum.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10288,'biology',88,1156,2763,'Identify the correct statement from the following','[{"text": "Henle\'s loop plays on important role in concentrating the urine.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Micturition is carried out by reflex.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein -free fluid is filtered from blood plasma into the Bowman\'s capsule.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'1) The Henle\'s loop and vasa recta both play a significant role in the concentration of urine.<br>2) The process of release of urine is called micturition and the neural mechanisms causing it is called the micturition reflex.<br>3) Blood is filtered so finely through the filtration membrane that almost all the constituents of the plasma except the proteins pass onto the lumen of the Bowman\'s capsule.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10289,'biology',9,24,44,'<em>Sargassum </em>belongs to','[{"text": "Bryophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brown algae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<em>Sargassum</em> is a member of class Phaeophyceae, commonly known as brown algae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10303,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Identify the wrong statement about distal convoluted tubule<br>I. Reabsorb water $$50 \\%$$ of the water filtered by the glomeruli<br>II. Secrete hydrogen ions into the tubular lumen<br>III. Capable of reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$<br>IV. Selective secretion of hydrogen and potassium ions and $$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$','[{"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both III and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'DCT is capable of reabsorption of  ${\\rm{HC}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ and selective secretion of hydrogen and potassium ions and ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ to maintain the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and sodium-potassium balance in blood',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10290,'biology',89,1287,3108,'i. Number of mitochondria less.<br>ii. Number of mitochondria more<br>iii. Sarcoplasmic reticulum is abundant<br>iv. Myoglobin content high<br>v. Sarcoplasmic reticulum moderate<br>vi. Aerobic muscles<br>vii. Depend on anaerobic respiration for energy.<br>viii. Less myoglobin content<br>A. Red muscles&emsp;&emsp;B. White muscles<br>Identify above (i to viii) traits as characteristic of $A$ and $B$ types of muscles','[{"text": "A-i, iii, vii, viii; B-ii, iv, v, vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-i, iii, iv, vii; B-ii, v, vi, viii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-ii, iv, v, vi B-i, iii,vii, viii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-ii, v, vi, viii; B-i, iii, iv, vii", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Muscle contains a red coloured oxygen storing pigment called myoglobin. Myoglobin content is high in some of the muscles which gives a reddish appearance. Such muscles are called the Red fibres. These muscles also contain plenty of mitochondria which can utilise the large amount of oxygen stored in them for ATP production. These muscles, therefore, can also be called aerobic muscles. On the other hand, some of the muscles possess very less quantity of myoglobin and therefore, appear pale or whitish. These are the White fibres. Number of mitochondria are also few in them, but the amount of sarcoplasmic reticulum is high. They depend on anaerobic process for energy.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10291,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which one of the following enables the mammalian kidney to regulate water reabsorption during states of dehydration?','[{"text": "The cells of the tubules detect the osmotic pressure of the blood.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water is extracted from the glomerular filtrate in the proximal tubules.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The kidney produces a hypotonic urine.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ADH increase the permeability of the DCT and collecting ducts to water.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'An excessive loss of fluid from the body can activate the osmoreceptors which stimulate the hypothalamus to release antidiuretic hormone $$(\\mathrm{ADH})$$ or vasopressin from the neurohypophysis. $$\\mathrm{ADH}$$ facilitates water reabsorption from latter parts of the tubule i.e. DCT and CT, thereby preventing diuresis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10293,'biology',9,24,44,'Pear shaped gametes and pear shaped zoospores are found in which of the following algae?<br>I.<i> Sargassum</i><br>II. <i>Fucus</i><br>III. <i>Dictyota</i><br>IV.<i> Laminaria</i>','[{"text": "I, II, and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pyriform, biflagellate gametes are a characteristic of brown algae. The common forms are <i>Ectocarpus, Dictyota, Laminaria, Sargassum and Fucus</i>.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10294,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Mark the feature which is not associated with white muscle fibres?','[{"text": "Lighter in colour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These muscles have a fast rate of contraction but for a short period", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Less sarcoplasmic reticulum compared to red muscle fibres", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They depend mainly on glycolysis for energy production and soon get fatigued", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Abundant sarcoplasmic reticulum is present in white muscle fibres, whereas sarcoplasmic reticulum is less in red muscle fibres.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10295,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Loss of mitochondria in the ascending limb of the loop of Henle would result in.','[{"text": "Increased $$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and $$\\\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$$ions in the urine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Decreased $$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and $$\\\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$$ions in the urine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decreased only $$\\\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$$ions the urine.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decreased $$\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$$ ions in the urine", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The ascending limb is impermeable to water but allows transport of electrolytes actively or passively. With the death of mitochondria and loss of ATP, active transport will be hindered. $$\\mathrm{NaCl}$$ will not get transported in the medullary interstitial fluid and starts accumulating in urine.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10297,'biology',9,24,44,'Members of phaeophyceae are','[{"text": "<i>Ectocarpus, Dictyota, Kelps Fucus</i> and <i>Sargassum</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Ectocarpus, Dictyota, Fucus Kelps</i> and <i>Porphyra</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Chlamydomonas, Sargassum, Fucus, Volvox</i> and <i>Ulothrix</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Gracilaria, Fucus, Kelps</i> and <i>Gelidium</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Some members of the class Phaeophyceae are <i>Ectocarpus, Dictyota, Laminaria, Sargassum</i> and <i>Fucus</i>.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10298,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Anaerobic muscles and aerobic muscles are called ____ respectively','[{"text": "Red fibres; white fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "White fibres; red fibres", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "White fibres; yellow fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red fibres, yellow fibres", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Anaerobic muscles and aerobic muscles are called white muscle fibres and red muscle fibres respectively.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10299,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Which of the following statements is correct?','[{"text": "Substances like glucose, amino acids, $$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$, etc in the filtrate are reabsorbed actively.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Conditional reabsorption of $$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and water takes place in DCT.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DCT is capable of selective secretion of $$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}, \\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$$and $$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$ to maintain $$\\\\mathrm{pH}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}-\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$$balance in blood.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'1) Substances like glucose, amino acids, $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$, etc., in the filtrate are reabsorbed actively while nitrogenous wastes are reabsorbed passively.<br>2) DCT is capable of reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}$$ - and selective secretion of hydrogen and potassium ions and $$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$ to maintain the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and sodium-potassium balance in blood.<br>3) Conditional reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and water takes place in DCT.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10301,'biology',9,24,44,'Kelp (filamentous form) and ectocarpus (branched form) belong to','[{"text": "Green algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brown algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement is wrong", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Kelp (branched form) and ectocarpus (filamentous form) belong to brown algae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10302,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Muscle contains a red coloured oxygen containing pigment called','[{"text": "Sarcoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myoglobin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Haemocyanin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Muscle contains a red coloured oxygen containing pigment called myoglobin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10305,'biology',9,24,44,'Incorrect statement wrt to brown algae is','[{"text": "Presence of chlorophyll a and b", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They remain attached to substratum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Filamentous brown algae is ectocarpus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of fucoxanthin.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Brown algae possess chlorophyll a, c, carotenoids and xanthophylls.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10306,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Fatigue<br>B. Red fibres<br>C. White fibres</div><div class="column-right">P. Sarcoplasmic reticulum is high<br>Q. Anaerobic breakdown of glycogen<br>R. Plenty of mitochondria</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P , C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Fatigue - Anaerobic breakdown of glycogen<br>Red fibres - Plenty of mitochondria<br>White fibres - Sarcoplasmic reticulum is high.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10307,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Which of the following is a correct match?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "PCT- Brush bordered columnar epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PCT- Brush bordered cuboidal epithelium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "GFR- $$125 \\\\mathrm{~L} / \\\\mathrm{min}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renal vein - more urea", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'PCT- Brush bordered cuboidal epithelium',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10308,'biology',9,24,44,'In brown algae, union of gametes may take place in _________or within the _______.<br>The gametes____ are and bear ____attached flagella.','[{"text": "Air, oogonium, pyriform, two medially", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Air, oogonium, pyriform, one laterally", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Air, oogonium, pyriform, two laterally", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water, oogonium, pyriform, two laterally", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In brown algae, union of gametes may take place in water or within the oogonium (oogamous species). The gametes are pyriform (pear-shaped) and bear two laterally attached flagella.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10310,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Which is correct between white and red muscles fibre?','[{"text": "White muscle fibre- Less myoglobin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "White muscle fibre- Number of mitochondria is more", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red muscles fibre - Amount of sarcoplasmic reticulum is high", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aerobic muscle is white muscle fibre", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'White muscle fibres have less myoglobin as compared to red muscle fibre.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10311,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Which of these parts in vertebrates functionally corresponds to the contractile vacuole of protozoans?','[{"text": "Food vacuole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cloaca", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sweat glands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kidneys", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Contractile vacuoles are organelles in sponges and freshwater protozoans. It performs functions like osmoregulation, expulsion of excess water, etc. in a single cell. They are functionally similar to kidneys in vertebrates.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10312,'biology',9,24,45,'Rhodophyceae are red due to the presence of pigment','[{"text": "Algoerythrin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "r-phycocyanin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "r-phycoerythrin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "r-phaeoerythrin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The members of rhodophyceae are commonly called red algae because of the predominance of the red pigment, r-phycoerythrin in their body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10314,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Number of mitochondria are few in them, but the amount of sarcoplasmic reticulum is high. The following line refers to?','[{"text": "White muscle fibres", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Red muscle fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Number of mitochondria are few in them, but the amount of sarcoplasmic reticulum is high. The following line refers to white muscle fibres.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10315,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Find the correct answers about glomerular filtrate.<br>i. Formed continuously through ultrafiltration of blood.<br>ii. Lipid free fluid collects in the lumen of Bowman\'s capsule.<br>iii. Protein free fluid collects in the lumen of Bowman\'s capsule.<br>iv. Formed by process of ultrafiltration','[{"text": "i, ii, iii Correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii Correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iv Correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii, iv Correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The first step in urine formation is the filtration of blood, which is carried out by the glomerulus and is called glomerular filtration. Blood is filtered so finely through the filtration membranes that almost all the constituents of the plasma except the proteins pass onto the lumen of the Bowman\'s capsule. Therefore, it is considered as a process of ultrafiltration.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10316,'biology',9,24,45,'Most of the red algae','[{"text": "Unicellular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "May be multicellular and unicellular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multicellular", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The red thalli of most of the red algae are multicellular. Some of them have complex body organisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10319,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Read the following statements and find out the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "In fish, kidney plays a very significant role in the removal of $\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Uricotelic animals excrete nitrogenous wastes as uric acid in the form of pellet or paste with a minimum loss of water.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Some amount of urea may be retained in the kidney matrix of some of the ureotelic animals to maintain a desired osmolarity.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Fishes that are ammonotelic in nature, perform excretion via body surfaces and gill surfaces. Kidneys do not play a significant role in the excretion of ammonia.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10320,'biology',9,24,45,'Red algae are found in','[{"text": "Great depths", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seas with moderate temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Surface of water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Majority of the red algae are marine with greater concentrations found in the warmer areas. They occur in both well-lighted regions close to the surface of water and also at great depths in oceans where relatively little light penetrates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10323,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Vasopressin is also called ____and is synthesized by the ____','[{"text": "Atrial diuretic hormone, hypothalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antidiuretic hormone, pituitary gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antidiuretic hormone, hypothalamus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Atrial diuretic hormone, pituitary gland", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Vasopressin is also called Antidiuretic hormone and is synthesized by the Hypothalamus and is secreted by the pituitary gland.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10324,'biology',9,24,45,'Algae found in the areas where very less light penetrates is','[{"text": "Green algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blue - green algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red algae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Brown algae", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Red algae occur in both well-lighted regions close to the surface of water and also at great depths in oceans where relatively little light penetrates',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10327,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Which is correct?','[{"text": "Water reabsorption in descending limb and sodium reabsorption in ascending limb of Henle loop occur by active transport", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sodium reabsorption in ascending limb of loop and collecting duct are regulated in aldosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water reabsorption is facultative in DCT and collecting duct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Water reabsorption is obligation in descending limb of loop and collecting duct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Facultative reabsorption involves the reabsorption of water aimed at specific needs. It is stimulated by hormones like $$\\mathrm{ADH}$$ and aldosterone. These hormones act on the latter tubules of nephron i.e. DCT and CT.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10328,'biology',9,24,45,'Red algae is found in areas with','[{"text": "Abundant light as well as areas of great depths with relatively little light", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Less light as well as areas of great depths", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Very less light as well as areas of great depths with no light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abundant light as well as areas of great depths with a lot of light", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Red algae occur in both well-lighted regions close to the surface of water and also at great depths in oceans where relatively little light penetrates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10331,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Why terrestrial organisms excrete lesser toxic nitrogenous waste?','[{"text": "For conservation of water", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "For maintaining osmolarity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "To faciliate simple diffusion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is easy to excrete less toxic substances", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Terrestrial organisms excrete lesser toxic nitrogenous waste for conservation of water. This is due to the fact that terrestrial organisms are adapted to live in water deficient conditions and if water is eliminated in abundance, the organism can die.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10332,'biology',9,24,45,'Photosynthetic pigment(s) of class- Rhodophyceae is/are','[{"text": "Chlorophyll-a and b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlorophyll-a and d", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chlorophyll-a and r", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlorophyll-a and c", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Chlorophyll a and d are the major photosynthetic pigments in class Rhodophyceae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10335,'biology',88,1151,2758,'The extension of renal medulla in renal cortex is known as','[{"text": "Renal columns", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Columns of bertini", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The extension of renal cortex in renal medulla is known as Columns of bertini/ Renal columns',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10336,'biology',9,24,45,'Phycoerythin is present in','[{"text": "<i>Fucus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Laminaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Kelps</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Porphyra</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The red pigment, r-phycoerythrin is present in members of class Rhodophyceae (eg. Porphyra)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10339,'biology',88,1153,2760,'In human beings, the blood passing through which of the following blood vessels has maximum concentration of urea?','[{"text": "Renal vein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renal artery", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hepatic portal vein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hepatic vein", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Urea is synthesised in the liver. Hepatic vein drains blood from the liver into the inferior vena cava. So, concentration of urea is maximum in the blood passing through the hepatic veins. Concentration of urea is least in the blood passing through renal veins which drain blood from kidneys into the inferior vena cava.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10343,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Which term is used<br>1) Both for a part of kidney and a part of skeleton in the mammals<br>2) Both for a part of kidney and ovary?','[{"text": "1- Hilum 2 - cortex and medulla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-Pelvis 2 - cortex and medulla", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1-Cortex 2- medulla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-Hilum 2- medulla", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both for a part of kidney and a part of skeleton in the mammals- Pelvis. Both for a part of Kidney and ovary - cortex and medulla.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10344,'biology',9,24,45,'Floridean starch is stored food very similar to _________in structure.','[{"text": "Starch and glycogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amylopectin and starch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amylopectin and glycogen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Starch and cellulose", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The food in red algae is stored as floridean starch which is very similar to amylopectin and glycogen in structure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10347,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Which term is used both for a part of kidney and a part of ovule?','[{"text": "Hilum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pelvis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cortex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Medulla", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both for a part of kidney and a part of ovule is hilum.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10348,'biology',9,24,45,'Polysulphate esters are present in the cell wall of','[{"text": "<i>Ectocarpus</i> and<i> Gelidium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Porphyra and Gracilaria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gelidium and Sargassum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Spirogyra</i> and <i>Polysiphonia</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The cell wall is vegetative cells of red algae is composed of cellulose, pectin and polysulphate esters',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10351,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Which of the following is correct about ultrafiltration?','[{"text": "Podocytes are a part of the glomerulus.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood is filtered so finely through these membranes, that almost all the constituents of the plasma except the proteins pass onto the lumen of the Bowman\'s capsule.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Filtered fluid is hypertonic to blood plasma.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The last step in urine formation is the filtration of blood.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The first step in urine formation is the filtration of blood, which is carried out by the glomerulus and is called glomerular filtration. The glomerular capillary blood pressure causes filtration of blood through 3 layers, i.e., the endothelium of glomerular blood vessels, the epithelium of Bowman\'s capsule and a basement membrane between these<br>two layers. The epithelial cells of Bowman\'s capsule called podocytes are arranged in an intricate manner so as to leave some minute spaces called filtration slits or slit pores. Blood is filtered so finely through these membranes that almost all the constituents of the plasma except the proteins pass onto the lumen of the Bowman\'s capsule. Therefore, it is considered as a process of ultrafiltration. The filtrate is isotonic to blood plasma except that the proteins are absent.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10352,'biology',9,24,45,'Floridean starch is','[{"text": "Carbohydrate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aminoacid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Floridean starch (α-1,4-glycan) is a storage carbohydrate that stores food in red algae. It is very similar to amylopectin and glycogen in structure',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10355,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Choose the incorrect statement about absorption in renal tubules from the following:','[{"text": "Glucose, amino acids and $$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$reabsorbed passively always.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nitrogenous waste are absorbed by active transport.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reabsorption of water also occurs passively in the last segments of the nephron", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The tubular epithelial cells in different segments of nephron perform reabsorption either by active or passive mechanisms. For example, substances like glucose, amino acids, $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$, etc., in the filtrate are reabsorbed actively whereas the nitrogenous wastes are absorbed by passive transport. Reabsorption of water also occurs passively in the initial segments of the nephron.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10356,'biology',9,24,45,'The spores and gametes of red algae are','[{"text": "Motile gametes and non-motile spores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both non-motile", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are motile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Motile spores and non-motile gamete", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Spores (asexual reproduction) and gametes (sexual reproduction) in red algae are both non-motile due to absence of flagella.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10359,'biology',88,1153,2760,'In a healthy man, glucose is not found in urine. Which one of the following statements justifies this?','[{"text": "The filtration membrane is permeable to urea but impermeable to glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose is neither filtered nor secreted into the renal tubule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose is completely reabsorbed into the blood from the proximal convoluted tubule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tubular cells utilize glucose to generate ATP required for active transport", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Glucose is filtered because it is a micromolecule. It is a high threshold substance. Normally it is completely reabsorbed into the peritubular capillaries from PCT by active transport.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10360,'biology',9,24,45,'Sexual reproduction of oogamous type is found in','[{"text": "Red algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brown algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sexual reproduction is of isogamous, aniosgamous or oogamous in green and brown algae. In red algae, sexual reproduction is exclusively oogamous. Thus, we conclude that oogamous mode of sexual reproduction is common in all three classes of algae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10363,'biology',88,1154,2761,'If loop of Henle were absent from mammalian nephrons, which of the following is to be expected?','[{"text": "There will be no urine formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The urine will be more dilute", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "There will be hardly any change in quality and quantity of urine formed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The urine will be more concentrated", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Loop of Henle plays a significant role in the concentration of urine by its participation in the counter-current mechanism. If the loop of Henle is absent or too short, urine formed will be dilute in nature.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10364,'biology',9,24,45,'In Red algae _________type of sexual reproduction is found','[{"text": "Oogamous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anisogamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isogamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In red algae, sexual reproduction is exclusively of oogamous type.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10367,'biology',9,24,45,'The complex post-fertilization events are seen in','[{"text": "<i> Gracilaria</i> and <i>Porphyra</i> - green algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i> Gracilaria</i> and <i>Porphyra</i> - red algae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i> Gracilaria</i> and <i>Porphyra</i> - brown algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Oogamous mode of reproduction followed by complex post-fertilisation events is found in red algae like Gracilaria and Porphyra.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10368,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Which of the following is incorrect about PCT?','[{"text": "Lined with simple cuboidal brush border epithelium.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "70 to 80 percent of the electrolyte and water are absorbed .", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It helps in the $$\\\\mathrm{pH}$$ maintenance of body fluid by the selective secretion of $$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$$ion and by the absorption of $$\\\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It help in the maintenance of ionic balance of body fluid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'70 to 80 percent of the electrolyte and water are reabsorbed',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10371,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Select the incorrect statements about the loop of Henle.','[{"text": "It helps in the maintenance of high osmolarity in medullary interstitium.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ascending limb is impermeable to water.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It allows the transport of electrolyte only actively.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Descending limb is permeable to water.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The loop of Henle plays a significant role in the maintenance of high osmolarity of medullary interstitial fluid. The descending limb of loop of Henle is permeable to water but almost impermeable to electrolytes. The ascending limb is impermeable to water but allows transport of electrolytes actively or passively.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10372,'biology',9,24,45,'How many of the following algae belong to the category of red algae?<br> <i>Spirogyra, Gelidium, Laminaria, Polysiphonia, Porphyra, Fucus, Gracilaria</i>','[{"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The common members of red algae are Polysiphonia, Porphyra, Gracilaria and Gelidium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10375,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Choose the mismatched part of nephron with its function.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Counter current-Vasa recta and loop of Henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PCT-Reabsorption of $$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and $$\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DCT-Reabsorption of glucose", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Loop of Henle-Urine concentration", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Option (3) contains the mismatched pair. It can be corrected as<br>Distal Convoluted Tubule (DCT) performs conditonal reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and water. DCT is also capable of reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$and selective secretion of hydrogen and potassium ions and $$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$ to maintain the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and $$\\mathrm{Na}-\\mathrm{K}$$ balance in blood.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10376,'biology',9,24,45,'Match the columns I and II<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Chlorophyll a, b<br>B. Chlorophyll a, c<br>C. Chlorophyll a, d</div><div class="column-right">P. Rhodophyceae<br>Q. Chlorophyceae<br>R. Phaeophyceae</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R, B – P, C – Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – R, C – P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A – P, B – R, C – Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – P, C – R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Chlorophyll a, b - Q. Chlorophyceae<br> B. Chlorophyll a, c - R. Phaeophyceae<br> C. Chlorophyll a, d - P. Rhodophyceae',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10379,'biology',9,24,45,'In <i>Polysiphonia</i> and <i>Gelidium</i>, sexual reproduction is','[{"text": "Isogamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anisogamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oogamous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gelidium and Polysiphonia are types of red algae. In red algae, sexual reproduction is exclusively of oogamous type.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10380,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Which of the following statement is/are true?<br>I. Urine is hypertonic in distal convoluted tubule.<br>II. When the urine passes into the collecting tubule, it becomes hypotonic.<br>III. Urine is isotonic in proximal convoluted tubule<br>IV. Urine becomes more and more hypotonic as it passes through the descending limb of Henle\'s loop.','[{"text": "I and IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Nearly all of the essential nutrients, and 70-80 percent of electrolytes and water are reabsorbed by PCT with small luminal changes in osmolarity. This leaves the urine to be isotonic in nature.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10383,'biology',88,1155,2762,'____in the body are activated by changes in blood volume, body fluid volume and ionic concentration. An excessive ____ of fluid from the body can activate these receptors which stimulate the ____ to release antidiuretic hormone (ADH) or vasopressin from the neurohypophysis.','[{"text": "Osmoreceptors, loss, hypothalamus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Osmoreceptors, gain, hypothalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osmoreceptors, gain, neurohypophysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Baroreceptors, gain, neurohypophysis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Osmoreceptors in the body are activated by changes in blood volume, body fluid volume and ionic concentration. An excessive loss of fluid from the body can activate these receptors which stimulate the hypothalamus to release antidiuretic hormone (ADH) or vasopressin from the neurohypophysis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10384,'biology',9,24,45,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Carotenoids, fucoxanthin and xanthophylls<br>B. Chlorophyll a, b<br>C. Phycoerythrin</div><div class="column-right">P. <em>Polysiphonia</em><br>Q. <em>Sargassum</em><br>R. <em>Chlamydomonas</em></div></div>','[{"text": "A &ndash; R, B &ndash; P, C &ndash; Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A &ndash; Q, B &ndash; R, C &ndash; P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A &ndash; P, B &ndash; R, C &ndash; Q,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A &ndash; Q, B &ndash; P, C &ndash; R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Carotenoids, fucoxanthin and xanthophylls - Q. <em>Sargassum</em><br>B. Chlorophyll a, b - R. <em>Chlamydomonas</em><br>C. Phycoerythrin - P. <em>Polysiphonia</em>',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10387,'biology',9,24,45,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Pyrenoids<br>B. Mannitol and laminarin<br>C. Floridean starch</div><div class="column-right">P. <em>Fucus</em><br>Q. Contains protein besides starch<br>R.&nbsp;<em>Porphyra</em></div></div>','[{"text": "A &ndash; R, B &ndash; P, C &ndash; Q,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A &ndash; Q, B &ndash; R, C &ndash; P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A &ndash; P, B &ndash; R, C &ndash; Q,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A &ndash; Q, B &ndash; P, C &ndash; R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. Pyrenoids - Q. Contains protein besides starch<br>B. Mannitol and laminarin - P. <em>Fucus</em><br>C. Floridean starch - R. <em>Porphyra</em>',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10388,'biology',88,1152,2759,'The number of Bowman\'s capsules in a kidney is equal to the','[{"text": "Number of loop of Henle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sum of Bowman\'s capsules and glomeruli", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Double the number of nephrons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sum of PCT and DCT", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A nephron contains one Bowman\'s capsule and one loop of Henle. Thus, the number of Bowman\'s capsules will be equal to the number of loops of Henle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10391,'biology',9,24,45,'Which of the following is not matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "<i>Chlamydomonas</i> - unicellular green algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Sargassum</i> - Food", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Chlorella</i> - Unicellular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Volvox</i> - Non-colonial form", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Volvox is a colonial form of green algae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10392,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Which factor helps in maintaining an increasing osmolarity towards the inner medullary interstitium?<br>i. Counter current pattern in vasa recta<br>ii. Counter current pattern in Henle\'s loop<br>iii. Proximity between the Henle\'s loop and vasa recta','[{"text": "i, ii and iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii only", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The Proximity between the Henle\'s loop and vasa recta, as well as the counter current in them help in maintaining an increasing osmolarity towards the inner medullary interstitium i.e. from     ${\\rm{300}}\\,{\\rm{mOsmol}}{{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$ in the cortex to about ${\\rm{1200}}\\,{\\rm{mOsmol}}{{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$ in the inner medulla.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10395,'biology',9,24,45,'In the species given below, food is stored in the form of-','[{"text": "Starch", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mannitol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Laminarin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Floridean starch", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The given figure represents the green alga, Volvox. Food is stored in the form of starch in all green algae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_10395_question_1.png'),
(10396,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Which of the following statements is/are true?<br>1) DCT is capable of secreting bicarbonate<br>2) When the urine passes into the collecting tubule it becomes hypertonic.<br>3) Urine is isotonic in proximal convoluted tubule.','[{"text": "1 and 2 only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 and 3 only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'2 and 3 only<br>Nature of filtrate in various parts of nephron -<br>- PCT - Isotonic (70 to $$80 \\%$$ of electrolytes and water reabsorbed)<br>- Descending limb of $$\\mathrm{LOH}$$ - Hypertonic (Permeable to water)<br>- Ascending limb of $$\\mathrm{LOH}$$ - Hypotonic ( Impermeable to water)<br>- DCT - Hypertonic (action of ADH)<br>- $$\\mathrm{CT}$$ - Hypertonic (action of ADH)',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10399,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Which one of the following groups of structures/organs have similar function?','[{"text": "Typhlosole in earthworm, and contractile vacuole in amoeba.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nephridia in earthworm, Malpighian tubules in cockroach and kidney in human.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nephrons in earthworm, green glands in cockroach and kidney in human.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nephridia in cockroach, metanephridia in cockroach and kidney in human.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Nephridia in earthworm, Malpighian tubules in cockroach and kidney in human are all excretory ograns performing excretion and osmoregulation in various organisms.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10400,'biology',9,24,45,'Reproduction in species given below is_','[{"text": "Oogamous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anisogamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isogamous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The given figure represents the green alga, Volvox. Sexual reproduction in Volvox takes place by oogamous mode of reproduction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_10400_question_1.png'),
(10403,'biology',88,1151,2758,'What is the ratio of concentration of outer medulla to outer portion of inner medulla?','[{"text": "$$1 / 3$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$2 / 3$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$4 / 3$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$1 / 4$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Concentration in outer medulla is  ${\\rm{600}}\\,{\\rm{mOsmol}}{{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$, while concentration in outer part of inner medulla is ${\\rm{900}}\\,{\\rm{mOsmol}}{{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$. Thus, the ratio becomes $$600 / 900$$ or $$2 / 3$$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10404,'biology',9,24,45,'Name the diagram given below_','[{"text": "<i>Kelps</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Polysiphonia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Laminaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Dictyota</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The given diagram represents Dictyota, a member of Phaeophyceae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_10404_question_1.png'),
(10407,'biology',88,1156,2763,'Find the correct steps for micturition (arrange in order- from last step to start step ).<br>1) Urine filled in urinary bladder<br>2) Stretch-receptor activation<br>3) Wall of bladder send signal to CNS<br>4) Motor message from CNS to urinary bladder and urethral sphincter<br>5) Bladder contracts and sphincter dilates leads to micturition.','[{"text": "1→ 2 → 3 → 4→ 5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 → 3 →1 → 5 →4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5 → 4→ 3→ 2→ 1", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2→ 4 → 1 → 3 → 5", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The sequence of events occurring during micturition in a descending order are $$-5,4$$, $$3,2,1$$<br>(5) Bladder contracts and sphincter dilates leads to micturition<br>(4) Motor message from CNS to urinary bladder and urethral sphincter<br>(3) Wall of bladder send signal to CNS<br>(2) Stretch-receptor activation<br>(1) Urine filled in urinary bladder',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10408,'biology',9,24,45,'Label the diagram of <em>Laminaria </em>a, b and c respectively are_','[{"text": "a-Stipe, b-frond, c-holdfast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a-Holdfast, b-rhizoid, c-lamina", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a-Frond, b-holdfast, c-stipe", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a-Frond, b-stripe, c-holdfast", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'a-Frond, b-Holdfast, c-Stipe',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_10408_question_1.png'),
(10410,'biology',88,1150,2757,'A man takes large amount of proteins. He is likely to excrete a greater amount of','[{"text": "Urea", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Uric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sugar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Nitrogen is the main constituent of amino acids and proteins. Large intake of proteins and their catabolism leads to formation of a lot of nitrogenous wastes in the form of urea',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10411,'biology',9,24,45,'Select the correct option showing characteristics of given species_<br>(a) Oogamous &emsp; &emsp; (b) Isogamous<br>(c) unicellular  &emsp; &emsp; (d) colonial<br>(e) haplontic  &emsp; &emsp; (f) diplontic','[{"text": "b,c,e", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "c,d,e", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a,d,e", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a,d,f", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The given diagram represents Volvox, a green alga that lives in colonies. It carries out oogamous mode of sexual reproduction and exhibits a haplontic life cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_10411_question_1.png'),
(10413,'biology',9,24,45,'In which of the following pyrenoids are present<br>','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pyrenoids are present in green algae. The 3rd diagram represents Ulothrix (chlorophyceae), a member of Chlorophyceae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10414,'biology',88,1157,2764,'Which of the following functions is correct?','[{"text": "Sebaceous glands eliminate certain substances like sterols, hydrocarbons and waxes through sweat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sweat produced by the sweat glands is a watery fluid containing $$\\\\mathrm{NaCl}$$, small amounts of urea, pyruvic acid, etc", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Small amount of nitrogenous waste elimination through saliva", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The sweat and sebaceous glands in the skin can eliminate certain substances through their secretions. Sweat produced by the sweat glands is a watery fluid containing $$\\mathrm{NaCl}$$, small amounts of urea, lactic acid, etc. Sebaceous glands eliminate certain substances like sterols, hydrocarbons and waxes through sebum. Small amounts of nitrogenous wastes could be eliminated through saliva too.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10416,'biology',9,24,45,'Dominance of which pigment is found in following species?','[{"text": "xanthophylls", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "chlorophyll-b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "r-phycoerythrin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "fucoxanthin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Given diagram represents the red algae, Polysiphonia. The dominance of the red pigment, r-phycoerythrin makes the plant body red.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_10416_question_1.png'),
(10417,'biology',88,1157,2764,'Go through the following statements.<br>I. Least concentration of urea is present in renal vein.<br>II. The highest concentration of urea is found in Hepatic vein.<br>III. Vasa recta is well developed in cortical nephrons.<br>IV. Urethra is not the part of kidney.<br>V. Liver is the site of urea synthesis<br>How many of the above statements are correct?','[{"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Option iii is the only wrong statement. Vasa recta is poorly developed in cortical nephrons.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10419,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Choose the correct statement.','[{"text": "The ascending limb of Henle\'s loop continues as the DCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasa recta are well-developed in Juxtamedullary nephrons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The PCT and DCT are situated in the medulla of the kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'PCT and DCT are situated in the cortex of kidney while the loop of Henle dips in the medulla.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10420,'biology',9,25,46,'Bryophytes include','[{"text": "Liverworts and mosses", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sphenopsida and mosses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rhodophyceae and liverworts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liverworts and grasses", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bryophytes include various mosses and liverworts.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10422,'biology',88,1157,2764,'Select the correct statement from the following.','[{"text": "Liver is the largest heterocrine gland in our body.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liver is located in the pelvis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bile contains substance like bilirubin, biliverdin, cholesterol, degraded steroid hormones, vitamins and drugs are passed with digestive wastes.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Liver helps in excretion of urea.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Liver, the largest gland in our body and is exocrine in nature. It is located in the abdominal cavity. It helps in the synthesis of urea. It secretes bile-containing substances like bilirubin, biliverdin, cholesterol, degraded steroid hormones, vitamins and drugs. Most of these substances ultimately pass out along with digestive wastes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10423,'biology',9,25,46,'Bryophytes are found in','[{"text": "Icy cold places", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hilly areas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Moist and shady places", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fresh and marine water", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bryophytes are commonly found growing in moist shaded areas in the hills.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10425,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Which is not a part of renal tubule?<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {\\left( {\\rm{1}} \\right){\\rm{ PCT}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}&amp;{\\left( {\\rm{2}} \\right){\\rm{ Afferent}}\\,{\\rm{tubule}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}\\\\ {\\left( {\\rm{3}} \\right){\\rm{ DCT}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}&amp;{\\left( {\\rm{4}} \\right){\\rm{ Collecting}}\\,{\\rm{duct}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}\\\\ {\\left( {\\rm{5}} \\right){\\rm{ Efferent}}\\,{\\rm{tubule}}\\,\\,}&amp;{\\left( {\\rm{6}} \\right){\\rm{ Bowmans}}\\,{\\rm{capsule}}} \\end{array}$','[{"text": "$1,2,3,4$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2,3,4,5$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2, 5$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$2,3,5$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The renal tubule begins with a double walled cup-like structure called Bowman&rsquo;s capsule,PCT ,DCT ,Collecting duct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10426,'biology',9,25,46,'Plants referred to as amphibians of plant kingdom are','[{"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bryophytes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bryophytes are also called amphibians of the plant kingdom because these plants can live in soil but are dependent on water for sexual reproduction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10428,'biology',9,25,46,'Bryophytes are called ‘amphibians of the plant kingdom’ because','[{"text": "They have evolved from frogs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They grow only in water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These plants grow in soil, but are dependent on water for sexual reproduction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bryophytes are also called amphibians of the plant kingdom because these plants can live in soil but are dependent on water for sexual reproduction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10429,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Find out the names of the following<br>i. A chordate animal having flame cells as excretory structures.<br>ii. Cortical portions projecting between the medullary pyramids in the human kidney.<br>iii. A loop of capillary running parallel to the Henle\'s loop.','[{"text": "i-Man; ii-duct of Bellini; iii-renal tubules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i- Amphioxus; ii-collecting duct; iii-vasa recta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i-Lancelet; ii- columns of Bertini; iii-vasa recta", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i-Amphioxus; ii-columns of Bertini; iii-peritubular capillary", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<br>i. Flame cells or Protonephridia are excretory structures in Platyhelminthes, annelids and cephalochordates-Amphioxus or Lancelet<br>ii. The cortex extends in between the medullary pyramids as renal columns called Columns of Bertini<br>iii. A minute vessel of that runs parallel to the Henle\'s loop forming a \' $$U$$ \' shaped structure is Vasa recta.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10431,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Select the total number of excretory organs found in various animals from the following options<br>Protonephridia, nephridia, Hepatic Ceacae, Malpighian tubules, green glands, kidney, Yellow body, fat body, urecose glands.','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "7", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Protonephridia, nephridia, Malpighian tubules, green glands, kidney, fat body, urecose glands, these organs help in excretion.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10432,'biology',9,25,46,'Organisms that play an important role in plant succession on bare rocks are','[{"text": "Bryophyta", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bryophytes play an important role in plant succession on bare rocks/soil',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10434,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Identify the correct statement.','[{"text": "Large amount of water from renal filtrate is reabsorbed in DCT and a less amount is reabsorbed by PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hilum is divided into outer cortex and inner medulla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Medulla is divided into medullary pyramids and cortex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The cortex extends in between the medullary pyramids which is called as columns of Bertini", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The cortex extends in between the medullary pyramids which is called as columns of Bertini, is the only correct statement',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10437,'biology',88,1156,2763,'Which one of the following statement is correct?','[{"text": "The outer layer of the kidney is called hilum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The descending limb of loop of Henle is almost impermeable to $$\\\\mathrm{NaCl}$$ salt", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DCT and PCT are found in medulla region of kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The urine is slightly basic in nature", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The statement in option (2) is correct regarding excretion. Rest of the statement is incorrect and can be corrected as<br>- Conditional reabsorption of water takes place DCT and large amount of water is reabsorbed in PCT.<br>- Malphigian corpuscle is found in the cortical region of kidney.<br>The colour of urine is pale yellow and it $$\\mathrm{s}$$ acidic in nature.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10438,'biology',9,25,46,'Mosses (Bryophytes) occur in moist places because','[{"text": "They cannot grow on land", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They donot have pigment system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fusion of gametes occur in water", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They lack root and vascular tissue", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mosses can live in soil but are dependent on water for sexual reproduction. Hence, they usually occur in damp, humid and shaded localities.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10440,'biology',9,25,46,'The plants having more differentiated body than algae is','[{"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liverwort", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Monera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The plant body of bryophytes (liverworts and mosses) is more differentiated than that of algae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10441,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Filtration of the blood takes place at','[{"text": "PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collecting ducts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Malpighian body", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ultrafiltration/ Glomerular filtration takes place in glomerulus. Malpighian body is another name for glomerulus plus Bowman\'s capsule.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10443,'biology',88,1157,2764,'A large quantity of one of the following is removed from our body by lungs.','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}$$ only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ammonia", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Our lungs remove large amounts of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ (approximately $$200 \\mathrm{~mL} /$$ minute) and also significant quantities of water every day.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10444,'biology',9,25,46,'Rhizoids are found','[{"text": "in algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "in pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "in bryophytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "in gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Unicellular or multicellular rhizoids can be found in Bryophytes. They help in the attachment of plant body to the substratum.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(10446,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Different types of excretory structures and animals are given below. Match them appropriately and mark the correct answer from among those given:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Protonephridia<br>B. Nephridia<br>C. Malphigian tubules<br>D. Green gland or Antennal gland</div><div class="column-right">P. Prawn <br>Q. Cockroach<br>R. Earthworm<br>S. Flatworms</div></div>','[{"text": "D-P, C-Q, B-R, A-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B-P, D-Q, A-R, C-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D-P, C-Q, A-R, B-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B-P, C-Q, A-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. Protonephridia - (iv) Flatworms<br>B. Nephridia - (iii) Earthworm<br>C. Malphigian tubules - (ii) Cockroach<br>D. Green gland or Antennal gland - (i) Prawn',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10447,'biology',9,25,46,'The plant body of bryophytes is attached to substratum with the help of','[{"text": "Unicellular or multicellular root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unicellular or multicellular rhizoids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Multicellular rhizoids only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unicellular rhizoids only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Unicellular or multicellular rhizoids can be found in Bryophytes. They help in the attachment of plant body to the substratum.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10449,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Which of the following pairs is wrong?','[{"text": "Uricotelic ----- Birds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ureotelic ----- Insects", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ammonotelic ----- Tadpole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ureotelic ----- Elephant", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Insects are uricotelic.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10450,'biology',9,25,46,'Gametophytic generation is photosynthetic and dominant in','[{"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bryophytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The main plant body of bryophytes is represented by a gametophyte. It is free-living, green, haploid, dominant and can perform photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10452,'biology',88,1158,2765,'The condition of accumulation of urea in the blood is termed as','[{"text": "Renal Calculi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glomerulonephritis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uremia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ketonuria", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Malfunctioning of kidneys can lead to accumulation of urea in blood, a condition called uremia, which is highly harmful and may lead to kidney failure.<br>',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10453,'biology',9,25,46,'Mosses possess leaf like, root like and stem like structure. What structure does it represent?','[{"text": "Gametophyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diploid Gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The plant body of bryophytes may possess root-like, leaf-like or stem-like structures. The main plant body of the bryophyte is haploid. It produces gametes, hence is called a gametophyte.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10455,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Match the terms given in Column I with their physiological processes given in Column II and choose the correct answer<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Proximal convoluted<BR>B. Distal convoluted<BR>C. Henle’s loop<BR>D. Counter current<BR>E. Renal corpuscle</div><div class="column-right">1. Formation of tubule concentrated urine<BR>2. Filtration of blood tubule<BR>3. Reabsorption of 70-80% of electrolytes<BR>4. Ionic balance mechanism<BR>5. Maintenance of concentration gradient in medulla</div></div>','[{"text": "A – 3, B – 5, C – 4, D – 2, E – 1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – 3, B – 4, C – 1, D – 5, E – 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A – 1, B – 3, C – 2, D – 5, E – 4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – 3, B – 1, C – 4, D – 5, E – 2", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Proximal convoluted - 3. Reabsorption of $$70-80 \\%$$ of electrolytes<br>B. Distal convoluted - 4. Ionic balance mechanism<br>C. Henle\'s loop - 1. Formation of tubule concentrated urine<br>D. Counter current - 5. Maintenance of concentration gradient in medulla<br>E. Renal corpuscle - 2. Filtration of blood tubule',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10456,'biology',9,25,46,'The main plant body of bryophyte is','[{"text": "Triploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haploid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The main plant body of the bryophyte is haploid. It produces gametes, hence is called a gametophyte.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10458,'biology',88,1154,2761,'We can produce a concentrated/ dilute urine. This is facilitated by a special mechanism. Identify the mechanism.','[{"text": "Reabsorption from PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reabsorption from collecting duct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reabsorption/ Secretion in DCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Counter current mechanism in Henle\'s loop/ Vasa recta", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Counter current mechanism operates between the two limbs of loop of Henle and those of Vasa recta. The filtrate becomes concentrated when it moves down the descending limb but is diluted by the ascending limb.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10459,'biology',9,25,46,'Gametophyte of bryophyte is','[{"text": "Free living and parasitic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Free living and autotrophic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Free living and saprotrophic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The main plant body of bryophytes is represented by a gametophyte. It is free-living, green, haploid, dominant and can perform photosynthesis (autotrophic).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10461,'biology',88,1150,2757,'The following substances are the excretory products in animals. Choose the least toxic form among them?','[{"text": "Urea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uric acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ammonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbon dioxide", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Level of toxicity in decreasing order is: Ammonia $$>$$ Urea $$>$$ Uric acid',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10462,'biology',9,25,46,'Haploid state is dominant phase in the life cycle of','[{"text": "Hibiscus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rice", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Marchantia</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mango", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The main plant body, gametophyte is haploid in bryophytes. Eg. <em>Marchantia</em>',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10524,'biology',9,25,46,'The sporophyte of bryophyte develops after','[{"text": "Reduction division of zygote", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiplication in zygote", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Before the formation of zygote", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Any of the above mentioned processes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Zygote with multiple divisions forms a multicellular sporophyte.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10464,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which of the following statements is correct?','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{ADH}$$ - prevents conversion of angiotensinogen in blood to angiotensin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aldosterone - facilitates water reabsorption", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ANF - enhances sodium reabsorption", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renin - causes vasodilation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Renin activates angiotensinogen. It in turn activates adrenals to release aldosterone. It helps in absorption of $$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\mathrm{Na}{ }^{+}$$and Secretion of $$\\mathrm{K}^{+}$$ions.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10465,'biology',9,25,46,'The gametophyte of bryophyte develops from','[{"text": "A haploid gamete", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A diploid spore", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A haploid spore", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Some cells of the sporophyte undergo reduction division (meiosis) to produce haploid spores. These spores germinate to produce gametophyte.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10467,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Which one of the following statements is incorrect?','[{"text": "Birds and land snails are uricotelic animals.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mammals and frogs are ureotelic animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aquatic amphibians and aquatic insects are ammonotelic animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Birds and reptiles are ureotelic", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Birds and reptiles are uricotelic.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10468,'biology',9,25,46,'Which of the following plant lacks true roots, stem and leaves?','[{"text": "Monocots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicot", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lycopods", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mosses", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'True roots, stem and leaves having vascular supply are absent in bryophytes, but root-like, non-vascular rhizoids leaf-like and stem-like structures are present. Lycopods (members of Pteridophyta) and Angiosperms (monocots and dicots) bear true roots, true leaves and true stem.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10470,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Which one of the following statements is incorrect?','[{"text": "The medullary zone of kidney is divided into a few conical masses called medullary pyramids projecting into the calyces.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inside the kidney the cortical region extends in between the medullary pyramids as renal pelvis.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glomerulus along with Bowman\'s capsule is called the renal corpuscle.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renal corpuscle, proximal convoluted tubule (PCT) and distal convoluted tubule (DCT) of the nephron are situated in the cortical region of kidney.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Inside the kidney, the cortical region extends in between the medullary pyramids as columns of Bertini.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10471,'biology',9,25,46,'The sex organ in bryophytes are','[{"text": "Reduced to single celled stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multicellular", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Unicellular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "are never formed", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The sex organs in bryophytes are multicellular. The male sex organ is called antheridium. They produce biflagellate antherozoids. The female sex organ called archegonium is flask-shaped and produces a single egg.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10473,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which one of the following is also known as antidiuretic hormone?','[{"text": "Oxytocin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasopressin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adrenaline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calcitonin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Vasopressin facilitates water reabsorption from latter parts of the tubule, thereby preventing diuresis. Thus, it is known as antidiuretic hormone.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10474,'biology',9,25,46,'The male sex organ of bryophyte is called','[{"text": "Antherozoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antheridium", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The male sex organ in Bryophytes is called antheridium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10500,'biology',90,1330,3213,'The neural system is composed of highly specialised cells called neurons that can','[{"text": "Detect response", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Receive response", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transmit stimuli", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The neural system of all animals is composed of highly specialised cells called neurons which can detect, receive and transmit different kinds of stimuli.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
