(10487,'biology',90,1330,3213,'Which pair of systems jointly coordinate and integrate all the activities of organs, so that they function in a synchronised fashion?','[{"text": "Neural system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endocrine system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Circulatory system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The neural and endocrine system together coordinate and work in synchronised fashion. The neural system sense stimulus through neurons and endocrine system provides chemical integration through hormones.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10501,'biology',9,25,46,'Division in zygote results in the formation of _______ in bryophytes','[{"text": "Gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antherozoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporophyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Archegonium", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Zygotes in bryophytes do not undergo reduction division immediately. They produce a multicellular body called a sporophyte.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10488,'biology',88,1150,2757,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Many bony fishes, aquatic amphibians and aquatic insects are ammonotelic in nature.<br></div><div class="column-right">Ammonia, as it is not readily soluble, is generally excreted by diffusion across body surfaces or through gill surfaces as ammonium ions.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Many bony fishes, aquatic amphibians and aquatic insects are ammonotelic in nature. Ammonia, as it is readily soluble, is generally excreted by diffusion across body surfaces or through gill surfaces (in fish) as ammonium ions.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
