(10496,'biology',88,1150,2757,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Ammonia produced by metabolism is converted into uric acid in the liver of these animals and released into the blood which is filtered and excreted out by the kidneys.<br></div><div class="column-right">Some amount of ammonia may be retained in the kidney matrix of some of these animals to maintain a desired osmolarity.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ammonia produced by metabolism is converted into urea in the liver of these animals and released into the blood which is filtered and excreted out by the kidneys. Some amount of urea may be retained in the kidney matrix of some of these animals to maintain a desired osmolarity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10497,'biology',9,25,46,'Archegonium contains _______ egg cells in bryophytes','[{"text": "Many", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Archegonium, flask-shaped female sex organ in bryophytes produces a single egg.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10499,'biology',88,1150,2757,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Reptiles, birds, land snails and insects excrete nitrogenous wastes as uric acid in the form of pellet or paste with a minimum loss of water and uricotelic animals.<br></div><div class="column-right">Kidneys play important role in excretion of ammonium ions.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Reptiles, birds, land snails and insects excrete nitrogenous wastes as uric acid in the form of pellet or paste with a minimum loss of water and are called uricotelic animals. Kidneys do not play any significant role in the removal of ammonia.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10503,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Protonephridia or flame cells are the excretory structures in platyhelminthes, rotifers, some annelids and the cephalochordate-Amphioxus.<br></div><div class="column-right">Protonephridia are primarily concerned with ionic and fluid volume regulation.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Protonephridia or flame cells are the excretory structures in Platyhelminthes (Flatworms, e.g., Planaria), rotifers, some annelids and the cephalochordate-Amphioxus. Protonephridia are primarily concerned with ionic and fluid volume regulation, i.e., osmoregulation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
