(10509,'biology',9,25,46,'Bryophytes reproduce by','[{"text": "Vegetative reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Asexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bryophytes show vegetative, asexual and sexual modes of reproduction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10511,'biology',88,1150,2757,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Malpighian tubules are the excretory structures of most of the annelids.</div><div class="column-right">Antennal glands or green glands perform the excretory function in crustaceans like prawns.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Malpighian tubules are the excretory structures of most of the insects including cockroaches. Antennal glands or green glands perform the excretory function in crustaceans like prawns.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10512,'biology',9,25,46,'Spore in bryophytes are formed','[{"text": "On the gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In the capsule of sporophyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In the seta of sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In the foot of sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Some cells of the sporophyte undergo reduction division (meiosis) to produce haploid spores. These spores present in the capsule of sporophyte germinate to produce gametophyte.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10513,'biology',90,1330,3213,'Nervous system of <i>Hydra</i> is composed of','[{"text": "Brain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ganglion with nerves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Network of nerves", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Well - developed nervous system", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In Hydra, neural organisation comprises of network of neurons called nerve net. Nerve nets connects sensory photoreceptors and touch sensitive nerve cells located in the body wall and tentacles',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10515,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In humans, the excretory system consists of a pair of kidneys, one pair of ureters, a urinary bladder and a urethra.<br></div><div class="column-right">Kidneys are reddish brown, bean shaped structures situated between the levels of last thoracic and third lumbar vertebra close to the dorsal inner wall of the abdominal cavity.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In humans, the excretory system consists of a pair of kidneys, one pair of ureters, a urinary bladder and a urethra. Kidneys are reddish brown, bean shaped structures situated between the levels of last thoracic and third lumbar vertebra close to the dorsal inner wall of the abdominal cavity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10516,'biology',9,25,46,'_______ form gametophyte in bryophytes.','[{"text": "Zygote", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spores", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Spores produced by sporophyte germinate to form gametophyte',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10517,'biology',90,1331,3214,'In humans, neural system comprises of the','[{"text": "CNS only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PNS only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both CNS and PNS", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The human neural/nervous system comprises of both Peripheral Nervous System (PNS) and Cental Nervous System (CNS). PNS consists of all the nerves (cranial nerves and spinal nerves) associated with CNS.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10519,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Each kidney of an adult human measures $$10-12 \\mathrm{~cm}$$ in width, $$5-7 \\mathrm{~cm}$$ in length, 2-3 $$\\mathrm{cm}$$ in thickness with an average weight of 120-170 g.<br></div><div class="column-right">Towards the centre of the inner concave surface of the kidney is a notch called hilum through which ureter, blood vessels and nerve leaves.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Each kidney of an adult human measures $$10-12 \\mathrm{~cm}$$ in length, $$5-7 \\mathrm{~cm}$$ in width, $$2-3 \\mathrm{~cm}$$ in thickness with an average weight of 120$$170 \\mathrm{~g}$$. Towards the centre of the inner concave surface of the kidney is a notch called hilum through which ureter, blood vessels and nerves enter.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10520,'biology',9,25,46,'The bryophyte have an aquatic ancestry. Which of the following best explains this?','[{"text": "Thread-like protonema", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of rhizoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Some forms are aquatic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flagellated sperms", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bryophytes are also called amphibians of the plant kingdom because these plants can live in soil but are dependent on water for sexual reproduction. The male gametes, antherozoids are biflagellate and swim through the water to reach the female plant and ultimately, the egg.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10521,'biology',90,1331,3214,'Which of the following is known as the site of information processing and control?','[{"text": "Brain and spinal cord- CNS", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Brain and spinal cord-Autonomic nervous system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brain and spinal cord- PNS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Central nervous system is the main site of information processing and control. It includes brain and spinal cord.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10523,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Inner to the hilum is a broad funnel shaped space called the renal pelvis with projections called calyces.<br></div><div class="column-right">The outer layer of kidney is a tough capsule. Inside the kidney, there are two zones, an outer medulla and an inner cortex.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Inner to the hilum is a broad funnel shaped space called the renal pelvis with projections called calyces. The outer layer of kidney is a tough capsule. Inside the kidney, there are two zones, an outer cortex and an inner medulla.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10525,'biology',90,1331,3214,'The two types of nerve fibres of PNS found associated with brain and spinal cord are','[{"text": "Efferent fibres, mixed fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sensory fibres, mixed fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Afferent fibres, efferent fibres", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Afferent fibres, mixed fibres", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The nerve fibres of the PNS are of two types :<br>(a) afferent fibres<br>(b) efferent fibres',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10527,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The medulla is divided into a few conical masses called medullary pyramids projecting into the calyces.<br></div><div class="column-right">The cortex extends in between the medullary pyramids as renal columns called Columns of Bertini.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The medulla is divided into a few conical masses (medullary pyramids) projecting into the calyces. The cortex extends in between the medullary pyramids as renal columns called Columns of Bertini.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10528,'biology',9,25,46,'Sporophyte of bryophytes is<br> I. Multicellular body<br> II. Dependent on the gametophyte<br> III. Some cells of the capsule undergoes reduction division to form spores<br> IV. Non-dependent on the gametophyte','[{"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The sporophyte in bryophytes is a multicellular body formed by division in zygote. It is not free-living and depends on the gametophyte. The cells in capsule of sporophyte undergo division to form spores.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10529,'biology',90,1331,3214,'The afferent nerve fibres transmit impulses','[{"text": "From tissues/organs to the PNS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "From the CNS to the concerned peripheral tissues/organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "From the CNS to skeletal muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "From tissues/organs to the CNS", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The afferent nerve fibres transmit impulses from tissues/organs to the CNS',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10531,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Each kidney has nearly one million complex tubular structures called nephrons, which are the functional units.<br></div><div class="column-right">Each nephron has two partsthe glomerulus and the renal tubule.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each kidney has nearly one million complex tubular structures called nephrons, which are the functional units. Each nephron has two parts - the glomerulus and the renal tubule.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10532,'biology',9,25,46,'Select the correct answer about bryophyta<br> A. Some cells of the sporophyte undergo reduction division (mitosis) to produce haploid spores. <br>B. The sporophyte is not free-living but attached to the photosynthetic gametophyte and derives nourishment from it.','[{"text": "A is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Reduction division is meiosis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10533,'biology',90,1331,3214,'The efferent nerve fibres transmit impulses','[{"text": "From tissues/organs to the PNS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "From the PNS to the smooth muscles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "From the CNS to concerned peripheral tissues/organs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "From the PNS to the involuntary organs", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The efferent fibres transmit regulatory impulses from the CNS to the concerned peripheral tissues/organs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10535,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Glomerulus is a tuft of capillaries formed by the efferent arteriole- a fine branch of renal artery.<br></div><div class="column-right">Blood from the glomerulus is carried away by an efferent arteriole.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Glomerulus is a tuft of capillaries formed by the afferent arteriole - a fine branch of renal artery. Blood from the glomerulus is carried away by an efferent arteriole.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10536,'biology',9,25,46,'Peat moss is','[{"text": "<i>Funaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Marchantia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Sphagnum</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The older dead parts of Spagnum are slowly carbonised, compressed and fossilised over thousands of years to produce a dark spongy moss called peat.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10538,'biology',90,1331,3214,'The PNS includes','[{"text": "Central neural system, visceral neural system and  autonomic neural system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Somatic neural system, autonomic neural system and visceral neural system", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sympathetic neural system and autonomic neural system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Somatic neural system, visceral neural system and peripheral neural system", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The PNS is divided into two divisions called somatic neural system and autonomic neural system and Visceral nervous system is a part of the peripheral nervous system',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10539,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The renal tubule begins with a double walled cup-like structure called glomerulus, which encloses the Bowman\'s capsule.<br></div><div class="column-right">Glomerulus along with Bowman\'s capsule is called renal tubule.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The renal tubule begins with a double walled cup-like structure called Bowman\'s capsule, which encloses the glomerulus. Glomerulus alongwith Bowman\'s capsule, is called the malpighian body or renal corpuscle.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10540,'biology',9,25,46,'Peat used in transshipment is a product obtained from','[{"text": "Liverworts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pteridophyta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mosses", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Peat is obtained from the moss, Sphagnum. It helps in the transshipment of living material due to its water holding capacity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10542,'biology',90,1331,3214,'The system that trasmits impulse from the CNS to skeletal muscles is','[{"text": "Somatic neural system", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sympathetic neural system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parasympathetic neural system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autonomic neural system", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The somatic neural system relays impulses from the CNS to skeletal muscles',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10543,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The renal tubule continues further to form a highly coiled network - proximal convoluted tubule (PCT)<br></div><div class="column-right">A hairpin shaped Henle\'s loop is the next part of the renal tubule which has a descending and an ascending limb.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The tubule continues further to form a highly coiled network - proximal convoluted tubule. (PCT). A hairpin shaped Henle\'s loop is the next part of the tubule which has a descending and an ascending limb.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10544,'biology',9,25,46,'Peat which is used as fuel is a product obtained from','[{"text": "<i>Funaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species of <i>Sphagnum</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All mosses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All liverworts", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Species of Sphagnum, a moss, provide peat that have long been used as fuel.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10546,'biology',90,1331,3214,'The system that transmits impulse from the CNS to the involuntary organs and smooth muscles of the body','[{"text": "Sympathetic neural system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parasympathetic neural system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Somatic neural system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autonomic neural system", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The autonomic neural system transmits impulses from the CNS to the involuntary organs and smooth muscles of the body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10547,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The descending limb continues as another highly coiled tubular region called distal convoluted tubule.<br></div><div class="column-right">The DCTs of many nephrons open into a straight tube called collecting duct, many of which diverge and open into the renal pelvis through medullary pyramids in the calyces.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The ascending limb continues as another highly coiled tubular region called distal convoluted tubule (DCT). The DCTs of many nephrons open into a straight tube called collecting duct, many of which converge and open into the renal pelvis through medullary pyramids in the calyces.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10548,'biology',9,25,46,'Organisms which first colonizes the bare rocks is','[{"text": "Mosses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lichens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mosses along with lichens are the first organisms to colonise rocks and hence, are of great ecological importance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10550,'biology',90,1331,3214,'Visceral nervous system comprises the whole complex of ____ by which impulses travel from the central nervous system to the viscera and from the viscera to the central nervous system','[{"text": "Nerves and plexuses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nerves, ganglia, and plexuses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nerves, fibres, and plexuses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nerves, fibres, ganglia, and plexuses", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Visceral nervous system is the part of the peripheral nervous system that comprises the whole complex of nerves, fibres, ganglia, and plexuses by which impulses travel from the central nervous system to the viscera and from the viscera to the central nervous system',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10551,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The Malpighian corpuscle, PCT and DCT of the nephrons are situated in the cortical region of the kidney whereas the loop of Henle dips into the medulla.<br></div><div class="column-right">In majority of nephrons, the loop of Henle is too short and extends only very little into the medulla. Such nephrons are called juxta medullary nephrons.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The Malpighian corpuscle, PCT and DCT of the nephron are situated in the cortical region of the kidney whereas the loop of Henle dips into the medulla. In majority of nephrons, the loop of Henle is too short and extends only very little into the medulla. Such nephrons are called cortical nephrons.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10552,'biology',9,25,46,'Mosses along with lichen are of great ecological importance because','[{"text": "Help in eclogical succession", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prevent soil erosion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They colonise barren rocks and decompose rock", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mosses along with lichens are the first organisms to colonise rocks and hence, are of great ecological importance. They decompose rocks making the substrate suitable for the growth of higher plants. Since mosses form dense mats on the soil, they reduce the impact of falling rain and prevent soil erosion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10554,'biology',90,1331,3214,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Central Neural system<br>B. Peripheral Neural system<br>C. Autonomic Neural system<br>D. Somatic Neural system</div><div class="column-right">P. Relays impulses from CNS to skeletal muscles<br>Q. Includes brain & spinal cord<br>R. Transmits impulses from CNS to involuntary organs & smooth muscles<br>S. Comprises of all nerves associated with the CNS</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P,B-R,C-Q,D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q,B-P,C-S,D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P,B-Q,C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-Q, B-S, C-R, D-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10555,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In some of the nephrons, the loop of Henle is very long and runs deep into the medulla. These nephrons are called cortical nephrons.<br></div><div class="column-right">The efferent arteriole emerging from the glomerulus forms a fine capillary network around the renal tubule called the peritubular capillaries.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In some of the nephrons, the loop of Henle is very long and runs deep into the medulla. These nephrons are called juxta medullary nephrons. The efferent arteriole emerging from the glomerulus forms a fine capillary network around the renal tubule called the peritubular capillaries.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10556,'biology',9,25,46,'In which way, mosses affect the quality of soil?','[{"text": "Prevent soil erosion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Form dense mats on the soil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Promotes soil degradation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mince mosses form dense mats on the soil, they reduce the impact of falling rain and prevent soil erosion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10558,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A minute vessel of this network runs parallel to the Henle\'s loop forming C-shaped vasa recta.<br></div><div class="column-right">Vasa recta are present or highly coiled in cortical nephrons.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A minute vessel of this network runs parallel to the Henle\'s loop forming a \' $$U$$ \' shaped vasa recta. Vasa recta is absent or highly reduced in cortical nephrons.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10559,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Neuron is a ____ structure composed of three major parts____.','[{"text": "Macroscopic, cell body ,dendrites and axon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microscopic, cell body, dendrites and axon", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Microscopic, cyton, soma and dendrites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microscopic, soma, node of ranvier and dendrites", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A neuron is a microscopic structure composed of three major parts, namely, cell body,dendrites and axon',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10593,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Multipolar neurons are found in the','[{"text": "Retina of eye", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cerebral cortex", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Embryonic stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Multipolar (with one axon and two or more dendrites; found in the cerebral cortex)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10560,'biology',9,25,46,'Mosses are ecologically important.<br> I. The last organism to colonize base rocks.<br> II. It decompose rocks making suitable for the growth of higher plant.<br> III. It forms dense mats on soil.<br> IV. It increases the impact of falling rain and soil erosion. <br>Identify the correct answer','[{"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mosses along with lichens are the first organisms to colonise rocks and hence, are of great ecological importance. They decompose rocks making the substrate suitable for the growth of higher plants. Since mosses form dense mats on the soil, they reduce the impact of falling rain and prevent soil erosion.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10562,'biology',88,1152,2759,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Urine formation involves two main processes namely, glomerular filtration, reabsorption.<br></div><div class="column-right">The first step in urine formation is the filtration of blood, which is carried out by the glomerulus and is called glomerular filtration.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Urine formation involves three main processes namely, glomerular filtration, reabsorption and secretion, that takes place in different parts of the nephron. The first step in urine formation is the filtration of blood, which is carried out by the glomerulus and is called glomerular filtration.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10563,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Nissl\'s granules are found in all except','[{"text": "Cyton", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dendrites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Axon", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The cell body / cyton and the dendrites contain nissl\'s granules. They are absent in the axon.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10564,'biology',9,25,46,'Which of the following statement is incorrect with respect to bryophytes?','[{"text": "The plant body is thallus like, more differentiated than algae and attached to substratum by the help of holdfast.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bryophytes mostly occur in humid, damp and shaded localities", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote formed undergoes mitosis immediately", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have leaf like, stem like and root like structures.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The plant body of bryophytes is more differentiated than that of algae. It is thallus like and prostrate or erect, and attached to the substratum by unicellular or multicellular rhizoids',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10566,'biology',88,1152,2759,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">On an average, 1100-1200 ml of blood is filtered by the kidneys per minute which constitute roughly $$1 / 5$$ th of the blood pumped out by each ventricle of the heart in a minute.<br></div><div class="column-right">The glomerular capillary blood pressure causes filtration of blood through 2 layers i.e. endothelium of blood vessels and epithelium of blood vessels.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'On an average, 1100-1200 $$\\mathrm{ml}$$ of blood is filtered by the kidneys per minute which constitute roughly $$1 / 5$$ th of the blood pumped out by each ventricle of the heart in a minute. The glomerular capillary blood pressure causes filtration of blood through 3 layers, i.e., the endothelium of glomerular blood vessels, the epithelium of Bowman\'s capsule and a basement membrane between these two layers.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10567,'biology',90,1332,3215,'____transmit impulse towards cell body and ____ transmits impulse away from cell body.','[{"text": "Dendrites, axon", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dendrites, dendrites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Axon, axon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Axon, dendrites", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The dendrite fibres transmit impulses towards the cell body. The axons transmit nerve impulses away from the cell body to a synapse or to a neuro-muscular junction',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10568,'biology',9,25,47,'Which group of plants constitute the lower members of bryophytes?','[{"text": "Liverworts", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mosses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rhodophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bryophyceae", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bryophytes are classified into Liverworts, Hornworts and Mosses. Liverworts represent the lower members in bryophytes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10594,'biology',88,1153,2760,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">PCT is lined by simple columnar brush border epithelium which increases the surface area for reabsorption.<br></div><div class="column-right">Nearly all of the essential nutrients and 70-80 percent of electrolytes and water are reabsorbed by this segment.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'PCT is lined by simple cuboidal brush border epithelium which increases the surface area for reabsorption. Nearly all of the essential nutrients, and 70-80 percent of electrolytes and water are reabsorbed by this segment.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10570,'biology',88,1152,2759,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The epithelial cells of Bowman\'s capsule called podocytes are arranged in an intricate manner so as to leave some minute spaces called filtration slits or slit pores.<br></div><div class="column-right">Blood is filtered so finely through these membranes that almost all the constituents of the plasma pass onto the lumen of the Bowman\'s capsule is called ultra filtration.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The epithelial cells of Bowman\'s capsule called podocytes are arranged in an intricate manner so as to leave some minute spaces called filtration slits or slit pores. Blood is filtered so finely through these membranes that almost all the constituents of the plasma except the proteins pass onto the lumen of the Bowman\'s capsule. Therefore, it is considered as a process of ultrafiltration.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10571,'biology',9,25,47,'Liverworts are found in','[{"text": "Moist shady places, marshy ground", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Banks of streams, bark of trees", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Damp soil, and deep in the woods", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The liverworts grow usually in moist, shady habitats such as banks of streams, marshy ground, damp soil, bark of trees and deep in the woods.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10572,'biology',90,1332,3215,'The cytoplasm contained within the cell body of neuron is characterised by the presence of','[{"text": "Cell granules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Special mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nissl\'s granules", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The cell body contains cytoplasm with typical cell organelles and certain granular bodies called Nissl\'s granules.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10574,'biology',88,1152,2759,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The amount of the filtrate formed by the kidneys per minute is called glomerular filtration rate (GFR).<br></div><div class="column-right">GFR in a healthy individual is approximately $$125 \\mathrm{ml} /$$ minute i.e. 180 litres per day.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The amount of the filtrate formed by the kidneys per minute is called glomerular filtration rate (GFR). GFR in a healthy individual is approximately $$125 \\mathrm{ml} /$$ minute, i.e., 180 litres per day.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10575,'biology',9,25,47,'The thallus of liverworts are','[{"text": "Anterio-posterior and appressed to substrate.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dorsiventral and appressed to substrate.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lateroventral and appressed to substrate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dorsi-medial and appressed to substrate.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The thallus in liverworts is dorsiventral and closely appressed to the substrate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10576,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Dendrites of neurons are','[{"text": "Repeatedly branched, short fibres containing Nissl\'a granules", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Repeatedly branched, short fibres containing no Nissl\'a granules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unbranched, short and do not contain Nissl\'a granules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unrepeatedly branched, long process without cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Dendrites of neurons are highly branched, short fibres containing Nissl\'s granules. Short fibres which branch repeatedly and project out of the cell body also contain Nissl\'s granules and are called dendrites.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10578,'biology',88,1152,2759,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Juxtaglomerular apparatus is a special sensitive region formed by cellular modifications in the distal convoluted tubule and the afferent arteriole at the location of their contact.<br></div><div class="column-right">A rise in GFR can activate the JG cells to release rennin which can stimulate the glomerular blood flow and thereby the GFR back to normal.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'JGA is a special sensitive region formed by cellular modifications in the distal convoluted tubule and the afferent arteriole at the location of their contact. A fall in GFR can activate the JG cells to release renin which can stimulate the glomerular blood flow and thereby the GFR back to normal.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10579,'biology',9,25,47,'Which of the following liverworts has thalloid plant body?','[{"text": "<i>Marchantia</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Sphagnum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Funaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Polytrichum</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Marchantia is a liverwort with dorsiventral lobed thallus-like plant body. Rest option are mosses',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10580,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Synaptic knob is bulb-like structure which is present','[{"text": "At the end of axon terminal", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "At the node of Ranvier", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "At the end of cytonic terminal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "At the end of dendrites", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The axon is a long fibre, the distal end of which is branched. Each branch terminates as a bulb-like structure called synaptic knob which possesses synaptic vesicles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10582,'biology',88,1152,2759,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Volume of the filtrate formed per day is 180 litres with that of the urine released 1.5 litres, reflects that nearly $$99 \\%$$ of the filtrate has to be secreted by the renal tubules. This process is called tubular secretion.<br></div><div class="column-right">The tubular epithelial cells in different segments of nephrons perform tubular reabsorption either by active or passive mechanisms.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A comparison of the volume of the filtrate formed per day (180 litres per day) with that of the urine released (1.5 litres), suggest that nearly 99 percent of the filtrate has to be reabsorbed by the renal tubules. This process is called reabsorption. The tubular epithelial cells in different segments of nephron perform this either by active or passive mechanisms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10583,'biology',9,25,47,'Asexual reproduction in liverworts takes place by the formation of specialised structures called','[{"text": "Spores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gemmules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Receptacles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gemmae", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Asexual reproduction in liverworts takes place by the formation of specialised structures called gemmae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10584,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Synaptic vesicles contains chemicals called ____ and is present in ____','[{"text": "Synaptic fluid, axon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neurotrasmitters, cyton", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neurotrasmitters, axon", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neurotrasmitters, neuron", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each branch of the axon terminates as a bulb-like structure called synaptic knob which possess synaptic vesicles containing chemicals called neurotransmitters',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10586,'biology',88,1152,2759,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Substances like glucose, amino acids, $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$etc in the filtrate are reabsorbed actively whereas the nitrogenous wastes are absorbed by passive transport.</div><div class="column-right">Reabsorption of water also occurs passively in the initial segments of the nephrons.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Substances like glucose, amino acids, $$\\mathrm{Na}+$$, etc., in the filtrate are reabsorbed actively whereas the nitrogenous wastes are absorbed by passive transport. Reabsorption of water also occurs passively in the initial segments of the nephron.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10587,'biology',9,25,47,'Liverworts reproduce asexually by','[{"text": "Gemmae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fragmentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zoospores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Asexual reproduction in liverworts takes place by fragmentation of thalli, or by the formation of specialised structures called gemmae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10588,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Multipolar and bipolar neurons differ in','[{"text": "Number of cytons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence or absence of Nissl\'s granules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number of dendrites", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Neurons are classified on the basis of dendrites attached to it. Based on the number of axon and dendrites, the neurons are divided into three types, i.e.,multipolar(with one axon and two or more dendrites; found in the cerebral cortex), bipolar (with one axon and one dendrite, found in the retina of eye) and unipolar (cell body with one axon only; found usually in the embryonic stage).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10590,'biology',88,1153,2760,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">During urine formation, the tubular cells secrete substances like $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}, \\mathrm{K}^{+}$$and ammonia into the filtrate.<br></div><div class="column-right">Tubular secretion does not helps in the maintenance of ionic and acid base balance of body fluids.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During urine formation, the tubular cells secrete substances like $$\\mathrm{H}^{+}, \\mathrm{K}^{+}$$and ammonia into the filtrate. Tubular secretion is also an important step in urine formation as it helps in the maintenance of ionic and acid base balance of body fluids.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10591,'biology',9,25,47,'Gemmae are asexual buds, which originate from','[{"text": "Large receptacles called gemma cups", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Small receptacles called gemma cups.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Small receptacles called gemma plates.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Large receptacles called gemma plates.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Gemmae are green, multicellular, asexual buds, which develop in small receptacles called gemma cups located on the thalli.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10597,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Unipolar axons are found in','[{"text": "Respiratory epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Retina", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cerebral cortex", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Unipolar (cell body with one axon only; found usually in the embryonic stage',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10598,'biology',88,1153,2760,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">PCT also helps to maintain the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and ionic balance of the body fluids by selective secretion of hydrogen ions, ammonia and potassium ions into the filtrate and by absorption of $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$from it.<br></div><div class="column-right">Henle\'s loop plays significant role in the maintenance of high osmolarity of medullary interstitial fluid.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'PCT also helps to maintain the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and ionic balance of the body fluids by selective secretion of hydrogen ions and ammonia into the filtrate and by absorption of $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$from it. The loop of Henle plays a significant role in the maintenance of high osmolarity of medullary interstitial fluid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10599,'biology',9,25,47,'<i>Marchantia</i> is','[{"text": "Monoecious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dioecious", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both monoecious and dioecious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During sexual reproduction, male and female sex organs are produced either on the same or on different thalli. In Marchantia, archegoniophore and antheridiophore are on two different thalli. Hence, dioecious.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10601,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Bipolar axons are found in','[{"text": "Retina of eye", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cerebral cortex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesencephalon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryonic stag", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bipolar - with one axon and one dendrite, found in the retina of eye',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10602,'biology',88,1153,2760,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The descending limb of loop of Henle is impermeable to water but permeable to electrolytes. This concentrates the filtrate as it moves down.<br></div><div class="column-right">The ascending limb is permeable to water but allows transport of electrolytes actively or passively.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The descending limb of loop of Henle is permeable to water but almost impermeable to electrolytes. This concentrates the filtrate as it moves down. The ascending limb is impermeable to water but allows transport of electrolytes actively or passively.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10603,'biology',9,25,47,'The plant shown in given diagram is_','[{"text": "Sterile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dioecious", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Monoecious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bisexual", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The given figure represents the liverwort, Marchantia which is dioecious.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_10603_question_1.png'),
(10605,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Identify the correct pair','[{"text": "Multipolar - with one axon and two or more dendrites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unipolar - cell body with one axon only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bipolar- one axon and one dendrite", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Multipolar(with one axon and two or more dendrites; found in the cerebral cortex), bipolar (with one axon and one dendrite, found in the retina of eye) and unipolar (cell body with one axon only; found usually in the embryonic stage).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10606,'biology',88,1153,2760,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Conditional reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and water takes place in distal convoluted tubule.<br></div><div class="column-right">DCT is not capable of reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$and selective secretion of hydrogen and potassium ions.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Conditional reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and water takes place in this segment. DCT is also capable of reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$$and selective secretion of hydrogen and potassium ions and $$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$ to maintain the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and sodium-potassium balance in blood.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10607,'biology',9,25,47,'Sexual reproduction in liverworts takes place by','[{"text": "Gemmae formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Special spores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sexual reproduction is absent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fusion of male and female gametes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During sexual reproduction, male and female sex organs are produced either on the same or on different thalli. These sex organs produce gametes, which fuse to form zygote (sporophyte).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10609,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Schwann cell is absent in','[{"text": "Myelinated neuron", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non myelinated", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Astrocytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (2) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Astrocytes do not have schwann cell, they are glial cells and help in maintaining blood brain barrier.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10610,'biology',88,1154,2761,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Collecting duct extends from cortex of the kidney to the inner parts of the ureter.<br></div><div class="column-right">Large amounts of water could be reabsorbed from collecting duct to produce concentrated urine.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The collecting duct extends from the cortex of the kidney to the inner parts of the medulla. Large amounts of water could be reabsorbed from this region to produce a concentrated urine.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10611,'biology',9,25,47,'The sporophyte in liverworts','[{"text": "Is differentiated into foot, seta and capsule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Produces gemma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gives nutrition to the gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The sporophyte is differentiated into a foot, seta and capsule',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10613,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Myelinated nerve fibre is found in','[{"text": "Spinal nerve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cranial nerve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Myelinated nerve fibres are found in spinal and cranial nerves.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10614,'biology',9,25,47,'Select the correct answer about liverworts After_______, spores are produced within the capsule. These spores germinate to form____.','[{"text": "Mitosis, free-living gametophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis, free-living gametophytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Meiosis, dependent gametophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitosis, dependent gametophytes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'After meiosis, spores are produced within the capsule of sporophyte. These spores germinate to form free-living gametophytes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10615,'biology',88,1154,2761,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The flow of filtrate in the two limbs of Henle\'s loop is in opposite directions and thus forms a counter current.<br></div><div class="column-right">The proximity between the Henle\'s loop and vasa recta, as well as the counter current in them help in maintaining an increasing osmolarity towards the inner medullary interstitium.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The flow of filtrate in the two limbs of Henle\'s loop is in opposite directions and thus forms a counter current. The flow of blood through the two limbs of vasa recta is also in a counter current pattern. The proximity between the Henle\'s loop and vasa recta, as well as the counter current in them help in maintaining an increasing osmolarity towards the inner medullary interstitium.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10617,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Unmyelinated nerve fibres are commonly found in','[{"text": "ANS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Somatic neural system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Unmyelinated nerve fibre is enclosed by a Schwann cell that does not form a myelin sheath around the axon, and is commonly found in autonomous and the somatic neural systems.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10619,'biology',88,1154,2761,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Large amounts of urea enter the thin segment of the ascending limb of Henle\'s loop which is transported back to the interstitium by the collecting tubule.<br></div><div class="column-right">Human kidneys can produce urine nearly four times concentrated than the initial filtrate formed.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Small amounts of urea enter the thin segment of the ascending limb of Henle\'s loop which is transported back to the interstitium by the collecting tubule. Human kidneys can produce urine nearly four times concentrated than the initial filtrate formed.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10621,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Nerve fibres enveloped with Schwann cells are','[{"text": "Myelinated fibres", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Non-myelinated fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Medullated fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Efferent fibres", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Only medullated / myelinated neurons have axons with schwann cells and nodes of ranvier.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10622,'biology',9,25,48,'The predominant stage of the life cycle of a moss is the gametophyte which consists of____ stages, namely ____ and _________.','[{"text": "Two, protonema, leafy stage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Two, prothallus, leafy stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two, protonema, prothallus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two, protonema, secondary protonema", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The predominant stage of the life cycle of a moss is the gametophyte which consists of two stages. The first stage is the protonema stage, which develops directly from a spore. The second stage is the leafy stage, which develops from the secondary protonema as a lateral bud.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10623,'biology',88,1155,2762,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">An excessive loss of fluid from the body can activate osmoreceptors which stimulate the hypothalamus to release vasopressin from the neurohypophysis.<br></div><div class="column-right">ADH facilitates water reabsorption from latter parts of the tubule, thereby preventing diuresis.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'An excessive loss of fluid from the body can activate these receptors which stimulate the hypothalamus to release antidiuretic hormone $$(\\mathrm{ADH})$$ or vasopressin from the neurohypophysis. ADH facilitates water reabsorption from latter parts of the tubule, thereby preventing diuresis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10625,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Axons are different from the cyton is','[{"text": "Presence of nissl\'s granules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Absence of nissl\'s granules", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Presence of schwann cells always", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of nodes of ranvier always", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Axons do not possess nissl\'s granules.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10626,'biology',9,25,48,'On germination moss spores produce','[{"text": "Leafy stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protonema", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prothallus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary protonema", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Protonema directly develops from a spore after its germination.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10627,'biology',88,1155,2762,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">ADH can also affect the kidney function by its constrictory effects on blood vessels. This causes an increase in blood pressure.</div><div class="column-right">An increase in blood pressure can decrease the glomerular blood flow and thereby the GFR.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'ADH can also affect the kidney function by its constrictory effects on blood vessels. This causes an increase in blood pressure. An increase in blood pressure can increase the glomerular blood flow and thereby the GFR.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
