(10637,'biology',90,1332,3215,'The gaps between two adjacent myelin sheaths are called','[{"text": "Synapse", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synaptic gap", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nodes of ranvier", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sheath gap", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The gaps between two adjacent myelin sheaths are called nodes of Ranvier',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10638,'biology',88,1155,2762,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">An increase in blood flow to the atria of the heart can cause the release of Atrial Natriuretic Factor (ANF).<br></div><div class="column-right">ANF can cause vasodilation and thereby decrease the blood pressure.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'An increase in blood flow to the atria of the heart can cause the release of Atrial Natriuretic Factor (ANF). ANF can cause vasodilation (dilation of blood vessels) and thereby decrease the blood pressure.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10640,'biology',9,25,48,'The dominant stage of mosses consists of','[{"text": "Sporophyte -secondary protonema which develops from the lateral bud", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametophyte- A leafy stage developing from a spore", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametophyte- leafy stage developing from the secondary protonema", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (2) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The main plant body of mosses is the free-living gametophyte. The gametophyte has two stages – protonema stage developed from a spore and leafy stage developed from secondary protonema.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10641,'biology',88,1156,2763,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The signal for micturition is initiated by the stretching of the urinary bladder as it gets filled with urine.<br></div><div class="column-right">The CNS passes on motor messages to initiate the contraction of smooth muscles of the bladder and simultaneous contraction of the urethral sphincter causing the release of urine.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A signal is initiated by the stretching of the urinary bladder as it gets filled with urine. In response, the stretch receptors on the walls of the bladder send signals to the CNS. The CNS passes on motor messages to initiate the contraction of smooth muscles of the bladder and simultaneous relaxation of the urethral sphincter causing the release of urine.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10642,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Medullated nerve fibres are found in the nerves of','[{"text": "Cranial region only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spinal; cranial region", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Spinal; internal organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spinal region only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Myelinated/medullated, nerve fibres are covered by myelin sheath and these fibres are found in cranial and spinal region. Due to the presence of myelin sheath, the transmission of nerve impulse occur faster as compared to non-myelinated fibres.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10645,'biology',88,1156,2763,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">An adult human excretes on average 2-2.5 litres of urine per day.<br></div><div class="column-right">The urine formed is a light yellow coloured watery fluid which is slightly acidic and has a characteristic odour.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'An adult human excretes, on an average, 1 to 1.5 litres of urine per day. The urine formed is a light yellow coloured watery fluid which is slightly acidic<br>( $$\\mathrm{pH}-6.0)$$ and has a characterestic odour.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
