(10665,'biology',88,1158,2765,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Blood drained from a convenient artery is pumped into a dialysing unit after adding an anticoagulant like heparin.<br></div><div class="column-right">The unit contains a coiled cellophane tube surrounded by a dialysing fluid having the same composition as that of plasma except the nitrogenous wastes.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The blood drained from a convenient artery is pumped into a dialysing unit called artificial kidney. Blood drained from a convenient artery is pumped into a dialysing unit after adding an anticoagulant like heparin. The unit contains a coiled cellophane tube surrounded by a fluid (dialysing fluid) having the same composition as that of plasma except the nitrogenous wastes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10667,'biology',9,25,48,'Label the a,b,c correctly_','[{"text": "a-sporophyte c-gametophye b-rhizoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a-gametophyte b-sporophyte c-rhizoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b-gametophyte a-sporophyte c-rhizoids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a-fruit b-leaves c-roots", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'a. Sporophyte b. Gametophyte c. Rhizoids',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_10667_question_1.png'),
(10668,'biology',90,1333,3216,'Identify the correct statement<br>a. Neurons are excitable cells because their membranes are in a polarised state.<br>b. Different types of ion channels are present on the neural membrane.','[{"text": "a is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10669,'biology',88,1158,2765,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The porous cellophane membrane of the tube allows the passage of molecules based on concentration gradient.<br></div><div class="column-right">Kidney transplantation is the ultimate method in the correction of acute renal failures.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The porous cellophane membrance of the tube allows the passage of molecules based on concentration gradient. Kidney transplantation is the ultimate method in the correction of acute renal failures (kidney failure).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10671,'biology',9,25,48,'Vegetative reproduction in mosses takes place by','[{"text": "Fragmentation and budding in secondary protonema", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fragmentation and gemma in secondary protonema", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fragmentation and budding in primary protonema", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fragmentation and gemma in primary protonema", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Vegetative reproduction in mosses is by fragmentation and budding in the secondary protonema.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10672,'biology',90,1333,3216,'Identify the correct statement<br>a. When a neuron is not conducting any impulse, i.e., resting .<br>b. Different types of ion channels are selectively permeable to different ions.','[{"text": "a is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10673,'biology',88,1158,2765,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Renal calculi are insoluble mass of crystallized salts of oxalates formed within the kidney.<br></div><div class="column-right">Glomerulonephritis is the inflammation of glomeruli of kidney.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Renal calculi are stones or insoluble masses of crystallised salts (oxalates, etc.) formed within the kidney. Glomerulonephritis is the inflammation of glomeruli of kidney.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10675,'biology',9,25,48,'In mosses the sex organs are present','[{"text": "At the mid-point of the leafy shoots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "At the apex of the leafy shoots", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "At the base of the leafy shoots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anywhere in the leafy stage", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In sexual reproduction, the sex organs antheridia and archegonia are produced at the apex of the leafy shoots',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10676,'biology',90,1333,3216,'In resting stage, the axonal membrane is comparatively more permeable and nearly impermeable to','[{"text": "Sodium; potassium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sodium; calcium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Potassium; sodium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Potassium; calcium", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In resting stage, the axonal membrane is comparatively more permeable to potassium ions and nearly impermeable to sodium ions. Due to this, the inside of neuron remain negatively charged, while the other side remain positively charged.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10677,'biology',88,1158,2765,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Nephritis is the inflammation of kidney tissue.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Nephritis is usually caused by infection.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Nephritis is inflammation of the kidneys and may involve the glomeruli, tubules, or interstitial tissue surrounding the glomeruli and tubules. Nephritis is often caused by infections, and toxins, but is most commonly caused by autoimmune disorders that affect the major organs like kidneys.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10679,'biology',9,25,48,'Sporophyte of mosses is more elaborated from','[{"text": "<i>Sphagnum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Selaginella</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Polytrichum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Marchantia</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The sporophyte in mosses is more elaborate than that in liverworts. <i>Marchantia</i> is a liverwort.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10680,'biology',90,1333,3216,'In resting stage, the axonal membrane for negatively charged proteins found in axoplasm is','[{"text": "Permeable", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Partially permeable", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Impermeable", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Selectively permeable", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In resting stage, the axonal membrane is comparatively more permeable to potassium ions ${{\\rm{K}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ and nearly impermeable to sodium ions ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$. Similarly, the membrane is impermeable to negatively charged proteins present in the axoplasm',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10681,'biology',88,1150,2757,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Aquatic animals like whales and seals are said to be ureotelic animals.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It is because of the fact that their main nitrogenous waste product is urea.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ureotelism is the process of excretion of urea. Aquatic animals like whales and seals are said to be ureotelic animals because their major nitrogenous waste product is urea.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10683,'biology',9,25,48,'Spores in bryophytes are formed by','[{"text": "Meiosis in capsule of leafy stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis in capsule of gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis in zygote", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis in capsule of sporophyte", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Spores are formed after meiosis in the capsule cells of sporophyte.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10684,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Kidneys are retroperitoneal organs.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Peritoneum covers the kidneys on all sides.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Structures that lie behind the peritoneum are termed "retroperitoneal".',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10685,'biology',90,1333,3216,'In resting stage, the axoplasm inside the axon contains high concentration of','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{a}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}$ & ${{\\\\rm{K}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In resting stage, the axoplasm inside the axon contains high concentration of $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$ and negatively charged proteins and low concentration of ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10687,'biology',9,25,48,'Elaborate mechanism of spore dispersal is found in','[{"text": "Ferns", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liverworts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mosses", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fucus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The mosses have an elaborate mechanism of spore dispersal.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10688,'biology',88,1155,2762,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Kidneys maintain the osmotic concentration of the blood.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Kidneys eliminate either hypotonic or hypertonic urine according to the need of the body.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Kidneys play an important role in maintaining the concentration and osmotic pressure of the blood. When water intake of an animal is high, the urine excreted has to be hypotonic and lower in osmotic pressure than their blood in order to remove the excess of water. On the contrary when there is a shortage of water, the urine excreted needs to be hypertonic and higher in osmotic pressure than their blood to reduce the loss of water with urine',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10689,'biology',90,1333,3216,'In the resting stage of a neuron, concentration gradient generates due to the','[{"text": "The fluid inside the axon contains a low concentration of $\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$, a high concentration of $\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The fluid inside the axon contains a low concentration of $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{+2}$, a high concentration of $\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The fluid outside the axon contains a low concentration of $\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$, a high concentration of $\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The fluid outside the axon contains a low concentration of $\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$, a high concentration of $\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In contrast, the fluid outside the axon contains a low concentration of $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$, a high concentration of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$and thus form a concentration gradient.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10691,'biology',9,25,48,'In moss, the sporophyte is differentiated into','[{"text": "Seta, protonema and capsule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Foot, protonema and seta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Foot, seta and capsule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Protonema, foot and capsule", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In moss, the sporophyte is differentiated into foot, seta and capsule. Capsule bears spores which give rise to gametophyte after meiosis',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10692,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Urinary tract infection is less common in women than in men.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Urethra is longer in women than in men.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Urinary tract infections are more common in females than in males. This is because the urethra in women is shorter than men.<br>It becomes easy for the bacteria to enter a female\'s urinary bladder.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10694,'biology',90,1333,3216,'For the maintenance of the ionic gradients across the resting membrane, the sodium-potassium pump transports','[{"text": "$3 \\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$outwards for $2 \\\\mathrm{~K}^{+}$into the cell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$2 \\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$outwards for $2 \\\\mathrm{~K}^{+}$into the cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3 \\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$outwards for $3 \\\\mathrm{~K}^{+}$into the cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2 \\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$outwards for $3 \\\\mathrm{~K}^{+}$into the cell", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The ionic gradients across the resting membrane are maintained by the active transport of ions by the sodium-potassium pump which transports ${\\rm{3N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ outwards for ${\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{K}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ into the cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10695,'biology',9,25,48,'Which stage bears sex organs in the species given below-','[{"text": "Protonema stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leafy stage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All stages", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Juvenile stage", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The second stage in the life cycle of a gametophyte, that is the leafy stage bears sex organs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_10695_question_1.png'),
(10696,'biology',88,1150,2757,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Malpighian tubules are excretory organs in most of the insects.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> These help in excretion of urea and creatinine.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Assertion is true, but Reason is false and can be corrected as Insects are the members of phylum-Arthropoda, in which excretion takes place through Malpighian tubules. But, insects excrete uric acid (not urea) as their nitrogenous wastes in the form of pellet or paste which minimise the loss of water. Thus, insects are called uricotelics.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10698,'biology',90,1333,3216,'The electrical potential difference across the polarised plasma membrane during polarisation, is known as','[{"text": "Potential deficit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Resting potential", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Action potential", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The electrical potential difference across the resting plasma membrane is called as the resting potential.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10699,'biology',9,25,48,'<i>Sphagnum</i> belongs to','[{"text": "Ferns", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liverworts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mosses", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Common examples of mosses are Funaria, Polytrichum and Sphagnum.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10700,'biology',88,1152,2759,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In the blood of glomerular capillaries, a filtration pressure forces water and solutes into the Bowman\'s capsule.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Proteins in the glomerular blood exert osmotic pressure.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The Bowman\'s capsule (also called the glomerular capsule surround the glomerulus and is composed of visceral (simple squamous epithelial cells - inner) and parietal (simple squamous epithelial cells - outer) layers. The visceral layer lies just beneath the thickened glomerular basement membrane and is made of podocytes that form small slits in which the fluid passes through into the nephron. The size of the filtration slits restricts the passage of large molecules (such as albumin) and cells (such as red blood cells and platelets) that are the non-filterable components of blood.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10702,'biology',90,1333,3216,'When a stimulus is applied at a site on the polarised membrane, the membrane at that site becomes freely permeable to','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$and $\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{++}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When a stimulus is applied at a site on the polarised membrane, the membrane at the site A becomes freely permeable to $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10703,'biology',9,25,48,'<i>Funaria, Polytrichum</i> are the examples of','[{"text": "Ferns", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liverworts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mosses", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Common examples of mosses are Funaria, Polytrichum and Sphagnum.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10704,'biology',88,1150,2757,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Deamination takes place in the hepatocytes producing $$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Ornithine cycle combines $$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$ and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ to form urea in the hepatocytes.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When amino acids are absorbed by liver cells a series of chemical reactions begins. The amino acid is oxidised in the presence of an enzyme catalyst. At the same time the amine group, $$-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$$, and a hydrogen atom, $$\\mathrm{H}$$, are removed from the main structure of the amino acid. The important product of this reaction is ammonia. The amine group is reduced to ammonia by the addition of a hydrogen atom. This process is called deamination. The non-nitrogenous portion of the molecule is converted to carbohydrates or fats.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10706,'biology',90,1333,3216,'The electrical potential difference across the plasma membrane is called the____.<br>Which is infact termed as a nerve impulse.','[{"text": "Potential deficit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Resting potential", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Action potential", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The polarity of the membrane is reversed and hence depolarised. The electrical potential difference across the plasma membrane at the site is called the action potential, which is in fact termed as a nerve impulse',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10707,'biology',9,25,48,'In a moss, the sporophyte','[{"text": "Is parasitic on the gametophyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Is autotrophic and non -dependent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arises from a spore", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is saprotrophic in nature", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In mosses, the sporophyte is attached to the gametophyte and derives nourishment from it. In other words, the sporophyte is parasitic on the gametophyte.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10708,'biology',88,1154,2761,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Urine is hypertonic in the descending limb of loop of Henle, while urine is hypotonic in the ascending limb.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Ascending limb is impermeable to $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$whereas the descending limb is impermeable to $$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$$.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Counter current system is found in two limbs of loop of Henle. The ascending limb transports $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and some urea into surrounding medullary tissue. It is impermeable to water. So it makes urine dilute or hypotonic. The walls of descending limbs are permeable of water and salt, so $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and water from surrounding fluid are absorbed. The contents or urine become hypertonic.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10710,'biology',90,1333,3216,'Durig the propagation of a nerve impulse, the action potential results due to','[{"text": "Rapid influx of $\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rapid influx of $\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rapid influx of $\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rapid influx of $\\\\mathrm{K}^{+2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During the propagation of nerve impulse, when the stimulus of adequate strength is applied to a polarised membrane, the action potential results from the movement of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ ions from extracellular fluid to intracellular fluid. This is because the permeability of the membrane to $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ions is greatly increased at the point of stimulation and since $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ions are more in the extracellular fluid at resting state, there occurs influx of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ions through sodium ion channels by the diffusion. Since, there are more $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$entering than leaving, the electric potential of the membrane changes from $-70 \\mathrm{mV}$ towards $+30 \\mathrm{mV}$, i.e. action potential.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10711,'biology',9,25,48,'The moss plant is','[{"text": "Predominantly sporophyte with gametophyte attached to it", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reduced sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reduced gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Predominantly gametophyte with sporophyte attached to it", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The main plant body of a moss is a predominant gametophyte which provides nourishment to the sporophyte attached on it.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10742,'biology',9,25,46,'Bryophytes are not characterised by','[{"text": "Sporophyte multicellular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Independent gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Absence of rhizoids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dependent sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bryophytes have root-like structures called rhizoids which help in attachment of thallus to substratum. These rhizoids can be unicellular or multicellular.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10712,'biology',88,1154,2761,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> When the filtrate moves through the descending limb, it becomes hypertonic and as it passes through the ascending limb of Henle\'s loop, it becomes hypotonic.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The descending limb is permeable to sodium ions, while the ascending limb is impermeable to sodium ions.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The descending limb has low permeability to ions and urea, while being highly permeable to water. The loop has a sharp bend in the renal medulla going from descending to ascending thin limb. The thin ascending limb is impermeable to water, but it is permeable to ions.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10714,'biology',90,1333,3216,'Identify the correct statement which describes after events of depolarisation.<br>i. The rise in the stimulus-induced permeability to $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$is extremely shortlived.<br>ii. It is quickly followed by a rise in impermeability to $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$.','[{"text": "i is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'After events of depolarisation is the rise in the stimulus-induced permeability to $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ is extremely shortlived.<br>It is quickly followed by a rise in permeability to $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10715,'biology',9,25,48,'A dominant autotrophic gametophyte alternating with a dependent sporophyte is','[{"text": "<i>Sphagnum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Polytrichum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Funaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bryophytes exhibit haplontic life cycle. The gametophyte is the main plant body. It is free-living, green, autotrophic, haploid and dominant. The sporophyte attached to the gametophyte is parasitic and derives nourishment from it. Sphagnum, Polytrichum, Funaria are examples of bryophytes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10716,'biology',88,1151,2758,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Hilum is a part of human excretory system.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It is helpful in collection of urine.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Assertion is true, but Reason is false and it can be corrected as<br>Hilum is a notch present on the concave surface of the kidneys through which ureter, blood vessels and nerves enter into the kidneys. It is not concerned with collection of urine. Urine is stored in the urinary bladder.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(10718,'biology',90,1333,3216,'During the transmission of nerve impulse through a nerve fibre the potential on the inner side of the plasma membrane has which type of electric charge?','[{"text": "First positive then negative and continue to be negative", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "First negative then positive and continue to be negative", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "First positive then negative and continue to be positive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "First negative then positive and continue to be positive", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During the transmission of nerve impulse through a nerve fibre the potential on the inner side of the plasma membrane is first negative then positive and again back to negative.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10719,'biology',9,25,47,'If the rhizoids of <em>Marchantia </em>has 10 chromosomes, the primary protonema will have','[{"text": "10 chromosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5 chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "15 chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "20 chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Rhizoids are haploid structures that are responsible for the attachment of thallus to substratum. Primary protonema is a stage of gametophyte which is haploid too. Thus, both will have same number of chromosomes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10720,'biology',88,1154,2761,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In the collecting duct, the final reabsorption of water from the urine into the blood results in hyperosmotic urine.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The loop of Henle creates sodium gradient in the interstitial fluid in the renal medulla.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In response to dehydration (increased ECF osmolarity) the kidneys can save water and produce concentrated urine. The ability to excrete urine that is more concentrated than the extracellular fluid (ECF) depends on the creation of a hyperosmotic environment in the medulla. As the collecting duct descends through the medulla, the increasing osmolarity in the interstitial fluid drives water reabsorption. However, there is a tremendous variability in water excretion. The urine produced can be either concentrated, or very dilute. They do so by regulating water reabsorption in the collecting duct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10722,'biology',90,1333,3216,'The resting axonal membrane of a neuron:','[{"text": "Is not polarized", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is more permeable to sodium ions than to potassium ions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is more permeable to potassium ions than to sodium ions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cannot be excited by a stimulus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When a neuron is not conducting any impulse, i.e., resting, the axonal membrane is comparatively more permeable to potassium ions $\\left( {{{\\rm{K}}^{\\rm{ + }}}} \\right)$ and nearly impermeable to sodium ions $\\left( {{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}} \\right)$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10723,'biology',9,25,48,'If the chromosome number in the leaf of <i>Sphagnum</i> is 10, what will be the chromosome number in the spores?','[{"text": "10", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "15", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "20", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Leaf of <i>Sphagnum</i> is a part of gametophyte (n). Spore is formed after the reduction division of capsule cells of sporophyte (2n). Hence, the spore is haploid. Both leaf of Marchantia and spore will have same chromosome number.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10724,'biology',88,1155,2762,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Diabetes insipidus is marked by excessive urination and too much thirst of water.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Anti-diuretic hormone (ADH) is secreted by the posterior lobe of pituitary gland.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Anti-diuretic hormone acts to maintain blood pressure, blood volume and tissue water content by controlling the amount of water and hence the concentration of urine excreted by the kidney. It is secreted by the neurophysis/ posterior pituitary. Its deficiency indicates a condition called Diabetes insipidus which is marked by diuresis and continuous thirst of water.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10726,'biology',90,1333,3216,'Within a fraction of a ____ $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$diffuses ____ the membrane and restores the resting potential of the membrane at the site of excitation and the fibre becomes once more responsive to further stimulation.','[{"text": "Second, inside", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Minutes, outside", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Second, outside", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Minutes, inside", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Within a fraction of a second, ${{\\rm{K}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ diffuses outside the membrane and restores the resting potential of the membrane at the site of excitation and the fibre becomes once more responsive to further stimulation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10727,'biology',9,25,46,'Which of the following statement is incorrect regarding bryophytes?','[{"text": "Water is essential for sexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The main plant body is haploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They usually occur in damp, humid and shady localities.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The presence of autotrophic, independent sporophyte", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sporophyte is reduced, dependent and parasitic on gametophyte.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10728,'biology',88,1150,2757,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Protonephridia or Flame cells in flatworms help in osmoregulation.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> These serve as excretory organs only.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both Assertion and Reason are true, but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.<br>Protonephridia or Flame cells are the excretory structures in Platyhelminthes (flatworms, e.g. Planaria). These are also concerned with ionic and fluid volume regulation, i.e. osmoregulation in these animals.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10730,'biology',9,25,48,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Amphibians of the plant<br>B. Lichen<br>C. Archegonium<br>D. Antherozoid<br>E. Marchantia</div><div class="column-right">P. Produces single egg<br>Q. Bryophytes<br>R. Along with  mosses help in  ecological succession<br>S. Dioecious  liverwort <br>T. Biflagellated  gamete</div></div>','[{"text": "A - R, B - P, C - Q, D - T, E - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - R, C - P, D - T, E - S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - S, B - R, C - P, D - T, E - Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - T, C - P, D - R, E - S", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Amphibians of the plant -<br> Q. Bryophytes<br> B. Lichen – R. Along with mosses help in ecological succession<br> C. Archegonium - P. Produces single egg<br> D. Antherozoid - T. Biflagellated gamete<br> E. Marchantia - S. Dioecious liverwort',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10731,'biology',90,1333,3216,'Which of the following is true about neural membrane?','[{"text": "Same type of ion channels present.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ion channels are selectively impermeable.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are wrong", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are wrong',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10743,'biology',90,1333,3216,'Unidirectional transmission of the nerve impulse is maintained by','[{"text": "Interneurons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myelin sheath", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synapse", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Membrane polarity", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A nerve impulse is transmitted from one neuron to another through junctions called synapses which maintains the unidirectional flow of nerve impulse transmission.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10732,'biology',88,1153,2760,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Conditional reabsorption of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ and water takes place in distal convoluted tubule (DCT).<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The DCT allows passive absorption of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$and active absorption of $\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$along with water.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Assertion is true, but Reason is false and can be corrected as<br>In DCT, conditional reabsorption of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$and water occurs. Here, $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$is reabsorbed actively, while $\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$ions are reabsorbed passively along with $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10734,'biology',9,25,46,'Which one is wrong in respect to bryophytes?','[{"text": "They are dependent on water for sexual reproduction.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The presence of antheridium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The presence of uniflagellated sperms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They play an important role in plant succession on bare rocks", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Male gametes in bryophytes are biflagellate sperms called antherozoids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10735,'biology',90,1333,3216,'Depolarization occurs due to','[{"text": "Rapid influx of $\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rapid eflux of $\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Slow influx of $\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Slow eflux of $\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Depolarization occurs due to Rapid influx of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10736,'biology',88,1158,2765,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In haemodialysis, blood drained from a convenient artery is pumped into a dialyzing unit after adding an anticoagulant like heparin.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The cleared blood is pumped back to the body through an artery after adding anti-heparin to it.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Blood drained from a convenient artery is pumped into a dialysing unit after adding an anticoagulant like heparin. Routine addition of anticoagulant to patient\'s blood is necessary to prevent clotting during haemodialysis. After the process is complete and the blood is pumped back, anti-heparin is added to neutralise the previously added heparin and return the blood back in its original form.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10738,'biology',9,25,46,'Which of the following is correct about bryophytes?','[{"text": "They have rhizoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They contain antheridium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They possess archegonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sex organs is bryophytes are antheridium (male) and archegonium (female). Bryophytes have root-like structures called rhizoids which help in attachment of thallus to substratum. These rhizoids can be unicellular or multicellular.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10739,'biology',90,1333,3216,'The correct sequence for depolarization and return of polarization is(A) Stimulus applied at a site on polarized membrane(B) Increased $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$entry into the cell(C) Increase $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$entry out of the cell(D) Generation of action potential(E) Return of membrane potential','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{B} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{D} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{E}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{B} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{A} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{D} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{E}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{D} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{B} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{E}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{B} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{C} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{D} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{E}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-B-C-D-E',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10740,'biology',88,1155,2762,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> RAAS gets activated in a person suffering from diarrhoea.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Both loss of water and electrolytes takes place in such a patient.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.<br>The person suffering from diarrhoea losses water and electrolytes excessively from the body which results in decreased blood pressure. This can be fatal for the person. Thus, inorder to increase the blood pressure.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10817,'biology',9,26,49,'In pteridophyte, the sporophyte consists of\nleaf-like appendages which is called','[{"text": "Prothallus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporophylls", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Protonema", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporangia", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The sporophytes bear sporangia that are subtended by leaf-like appendages called sporophylls.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10744,'biology',88,1156,2763,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The stretch receptors on the wall of urinary bladder do not signal the CNS when the urinary bladder fills with urine.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Micturition is a in voluntary process.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Assertion is false, Reason is false Urine formed by the nephrons is ultimately carried to the urinary bladder where it is stored till a voluntary signals is given by the Central Nervous System (CNS).<br>This signal is initiated by the stretching of the urinary bladder as it gets filled with urine.<br>In response, the stretch receptors on the walls of the bladder send signals to the CNS. The CNS passes on motor messages to initiate the contraction of smooth muscles of the bladder and simultaneous relaxation of the urethral sphincter causing the release of urine, i.e. micturition. Thus, micturition is a voluntary process.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10746,'biology',9,25,46,'Plants producing embryo but multicellular dominant gametophyte','[{"text": "Bryophyta", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bryophytes are haplontic plants that have gametophyte as their main plant body. This gametophyte is dominant and produces gametes that fuse to form a zygote. Zygote after multiple divisions forms an embryo and ultimately a sporophyte.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10747,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Select the true statements from the following.','[{"text": "At a chemical synapse, the membrane of the pre- and post-synaptic neurons are separated by a fluid-filled space called synapsis.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "At chemical synapse, the membranes of pre- and post-synaptic neuron are in very close proximity.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transmission of an impulse across electrical synapses is very similar to impulse conduction along a single dendrite.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are wrong", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are wrong, they can be corrected as<br>(1) At a chemical synapse, the membrane of the pre- and post-synaptic neurons are separated by a fluid-filled space called synaptic cleft .<br>(2) At electrical synapse, the membranes of pre- and post-synaptic neuron are in very close proximity.<br>(3) Transmission of an impulse across electrical synapses is very similar to impulse conduction along a single axon.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10748,'biology',88,1158,2765,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Haemodialysis is used to clean the excretory products generated from the blood.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Dialysing fluid has same composition as that of plasma except nitrogenous wastes.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both Assertion and Reason are true, but Reason is not the correct explanation of Asserion.<br>Haemodialysis is a process in which blood is purified artificially if the kidneys fail to do their designated function. The dialysing fluid used in haemodialysis has same composition as that of plasma but it does not contain nitrogenous waste. Therefore, these wastes can freely pass from blood into dialysing fluid, thus, clearing blood.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10750,'biology',9,25,48,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Chlorophyceae<br>B. Phaeophyceae<br>C. Rhodophyceae<br>D. Mosses</div><div class="column-right">P. Flagella is absent<br>Q. Multicellular and branched rhizoids<br>R. 2 unequal and lateral flagella<br>S. 2-8 equal and apical flagella</div></div>','[{"text": "A - R, B - P, C - Q, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S, B - R, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - P, B - R, C - Q, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - P, C - R, D - S", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A.Chlorophyceae - S. 2-8 equal and apical flagella<br>B. Phaeophyceae - R. 2 unequal and lateral flagella <br>C. Rhodophyceae - P. Flagella is absent<br>D. Mosses - Q. Multicellular and branched rhizoids',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10751,'biology',90,1333,3216,'Following is the diagrammatic representation of impulse conduction through an axon. Identify the process of impulse conduction in $\\mathrm{A}$ ?','[{"text": "Action potential", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Resting potential", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Deporalisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'This is a representation of Action potential.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/90_10751_question_1.png'),
(10752,'biology',88,1156,2763,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> During urination, the back flow of urine into the ureters is prevented.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Urethral sphincters relax during urination','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both Assertion and Reason are true, but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.<br>The correct explanation would be during urination, the back flow of urine into the ureters is prevented by the presence of a one way valve at the urethral-bladder junction.<br>Urethral sphincters control the exit of the urine in the urinary bladder through the urethra. Thus, urethral sphincters relax during urination and constrict when not urinating.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10754,'biology',9,25,48,'Which of the following can be called as amphibians of the plant_','[{"text": "<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'1. Selaginella (pteridophyte)<br>2. Polysiphonia (algae)<br>3. Sphagnum (bryophyte &ndash; amphibians of Plant Kingdom)<br>4. Salvinia (pteridophhyte)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10755,'biology',90,1333,3216,'A wave of action potential travelling through the neuron is called as','[{"text": "Resting impulse", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nerve impulse", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Motor impulse", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Repolarisation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A wave of action potential travelling through the neuron is called as nerve impulse.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10756,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Uricotelism is found in','[{"text": "Mammals and birds<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fishes and fresh water protozoans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Birds, reptiles and insects", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Frogs and toads", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Reptiles, birds, land snails and insects excrete nitrogenous wastes as uric acid in the form of pellet or paste with a minimum loss of water and are called uricotelic animals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2004,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10758,'biology',9,25,48,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Liverworts<br>B. Gametes in Rhodophyceae<br>C. Gametes in Phaeophyceae<br>D. <em>Sphagnum</em><br>E. <em>Gelidium&nbsp;</em></div><div class="column-right">P. Pear shaped<br>Q. Non-flagellated<br>R. Peat moss<br>S. Agar<br>T. Gemmae</div></div>','[{"text": "A - R, B - P, C - Q, D - T, E - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - T, B - Q, C - P, D - R, E - S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - R, B - Q, C - P, D - T, E - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - T, C - P, D - R, E - S", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-T, B-Q, C-P, D-R, E-S',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10759,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Earthworms are<br>','[{"text": "Ureotelic when plenty of water is available", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uricotelic when plenty of water is available", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uricotelic under conditions of water scarcity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ammonotelic when plenty of water is available", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Lumbricus (commonly seen earthworm) produces both ammonia and urea. But when plenty of water is available they are ammonotelic.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10760,'biology',90,1334,3217,'A nerve impulse is transmitted from one neuron to another through junctions called','[{"text": "Synaptic cleft", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neuroreceptor junction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synapse", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A nerve impulse is transmitted from one neuron to another through junctions called synapses',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10762,'biology',9,26,49,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Presence of r-phycoerythrin<br>B. <em>Selaginella</em><br>C. Fern<br>D. <em>Chlorella</em></div><div class="column-right">P. Macrophylls<br>Q. SCP<br>R. Microphylls<br>S. <em>Gracilaria</em></div></div>','[{"text": "A &ndash; R, B &ndash; P , C &ndash; Q, D &ndash; S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A &ndash; S, B &ndash; R , C &ndash; P, D &ndash; Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A &ndash; P, B &ndash; R , C &ndash; Q, D &ndash; S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A &ndash; Q, B &ndash; P , C &ndash; R , D &ndash; S", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A.Presence of r-phycoerythrin -&nbsp;S. <em>Gracilaria</em><br>B. <em>Selaginella </em>- R. Microphylls<br>C. Fern - P. Macrophylls<br>D. <em>Chlorella </em>- Q. Scp',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10763,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Angiotensinogen is a protein produced and secreted by<br>','[{"text": "Macula densa cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endothelial cells (cells lining the blood vessels)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liver cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Juxtaglomerular (JG) cells", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Angiotensinogen is a plasma protein produced and secreted by the liver cells. Renin is secreted from juxtaglomerular cells and acts enzymatically on angiotensinogen to release 10 amino acid peptide angiotensin-I. Macula densa is actually a plaque in the wall at the end of thick ascending limb of nephrons.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10764,'biology',90,1334,3217,'The axons transmit nerve impulses away from the cell body to a ____.','[{"text": "Synapse", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synapsis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synapse or neuro-muscular junction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The axons transmit nerve impulses away from the cell body to a synapse or to a neuromuscular junction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10766,'biology',9,26,49,'The plants frequently grown as ornamentals and are used for medicinal purpose belong to','[{"text": "Angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bryophyta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pteridophytes are used for medicinal purposes and as soil-binders. They are also frequently grown as ornamentals.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10767,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Excretory product of spider is','[{"text": "Ammonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Guanine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Guanine is the excretory product of a spider. It is insoluble in water and contains compounds such as carbon, nitrogen, hydrogen and oxygen.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10769,'biology',90,1334,3217,'The synaptic cleft is found between the membrane of','[{"text": "Pre-synaptic nephron and a post-synaptic nephron", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pre-synaptic axon and a post-synaptic axon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pre-synaptic dendrite and a post-synaptic dendrite", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pre-synaptic neuron and a post-synaptic neuron", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A synapse is formed by the membrane of a pre-synaptic neuron and post-synaptic neuron. The space between these two membrane at synapse is called synaptic cleft.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10770,'biology',9,26,49,'Pteridophytes are also called','[{"text": "Amphibians of plant kingdom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "First terrestrial plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Seed producing plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pteridophytes are evolutionarily, the first terrestrial plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10771,'biology',88,1155,2762,'A person is on a long hunger strike and is surviving only on water, will have','[{"text": "More sodium in his urine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Less amino acids in his urine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More glucose in his blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Less urea in his urine", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Urea is an organic compound which is a waste product produced during body metabolism.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10773,'biology',90,1334,3217,'The two types of synapses are','[{"text": "Physical, chemical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Electrical, chemical", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Physical, electrical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Electrochemical, Biological", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Synapses are of two types, i.e. electrical synapses and chemical synapses. Eletrical synapse is mediated by electrical impulse. It is very fast but rate in humans. On the other hand, chemical synapse is mediated by chemicals such as neurotransmitter.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10774,'biology',9,26,49,'Evolutionarily, the first terrestrial plants to possess vascular tissues are','[{"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Green algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bryophytes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Evolutionarily, pteridophytes are the first terrestrial plants to possess vascular tissues – xylem and phloem.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10775,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Uric acid is the chief nitrogenous component of the excretory products of<br>','[{"text": "Man", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Earthworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cockroach", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Frog", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cockroach excrete uric acid as the chief nitrogenous excretory product. Man excrete urea as the chief nitrogenous excretory product. Earthworm excrete 40% urea and 20% ammonia and 40% amino acids. Frog excretes urea as the chief nitrogenous product.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10777,'biology',90,1334,3217,'At ____synapses, the membranes of pre- and post-synaptic neurons are in very close proximity.','[{"text": "Physical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Electrical", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chemical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biological", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'At electrical synapses, the membranes of pre- and post-synaptic neurons are in very close proximity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10778,'biology',9,26,49,'To which of the groups would you assign plant which has a primitive vascular supply but does not produce flowers and grown as ornamentals?','[{"text": "Gymmosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pteridophyta", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bryophyta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pteridophytes, frequently grown as ornamentals are the first plants to possess vascular tissues. They don’t bear flowers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10779,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which one of the following statements in regard to the excretion by the human kidneys is correct?<br>','[{"text": "Descending limb of loop of Henle is impermeable to water.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Distal convoluted tubule is incapable of reabsorbing $$\\\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}$$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nearly $$99 \\\\%$$ of the glomerular filtrate is reabsorbed by the renal tubule.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ascending limb of loop of Henle is impermeable to electrolytes.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The plasma fluid that filters out from glomerular capillaries into Bowman\'s capsule of nephron is called glomerular filtrate. A comparison of the volume of the filtrate formed per day $$(180 \\mathrm{~L} /$$ day $$)$$ with that of the urine released $$(1.5 \\mathrm{~L})$$, suggests that nearly $$99 \\%$$ of the filtrate has to reabsorbed by the renal tubules. This process is called reabsorption.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10781,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Impulse transmission across an electrical synapse is ____ to that across a chemical synapse','[{"text": "Always equal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Always slower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Always faster", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sometimes faster", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Impulse transmission across an electrical synapse is always faster than that across a chemical synapse.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10782,'biology',9,26,49,'Horsetails and ferns belong to','[{"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bryophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The Pteridophytes include horsetails and ferns.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10783,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Injury to adrenal cortex is not likely to affect the secretion of which one of the following?<br>','[{"text": "Aldosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both androstenedione and dehydroepiandrosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenaline", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cortisol", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The adrenal medulla synthesises two hormones adrenaline (epinephrine) and nonadrenaline (nonepinephric). These hormones are proteinaceous in nature and derived from amino acid tyrosine. Thus, injury to adrenal cortex will not affect the secretion of adrenaline.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10785,'biology',9,26,49,'Pteridophytes mostly occur in','[{"text": "Fresh and marine water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sandy-soil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cool, damp and shady places", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pteridophytes mostly occur in cool, damp and shady places. Pteridophytes are fundsmentally terrestrial plants, but they are dependent on an external source of water for completion of their life cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10786,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Transmission of a impulse across ____ is very similar to impulse conduction along a single axon.','[{"text": "Chemical synapses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Electrical synapses", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Electrical synapsis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemical synapsis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Transmission of a impulse across electrical synapses is very similar to impulse conduction along a single axon. Electrical synapse are rare in our system.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10787,'biology',88,1157,2764,'The principle nitrogenous excretory compound in humans is synthesised<br>','[{"text": "In kidneys but eliminated mostly through liver", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In kidneys as well as eliminated by kidneys", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In liver and also eliminated by the same through bile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In the liver but eliminated mostly through kidney", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In human beings, the principle nitrogenous excretory compound (i.e, urea) is synthesised in liver by Ornithine cycle and is eliminated mostly through one molecule of  ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ is activated by biotin and combines with two molecules of  ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ in the presence of carbamyl phosphate and one molecule of ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$ is released. Carbamyl phosphate reacts with Ornithine and forms Citrulline. Citrulline combines with another molecule of ammonia and form arginine that is broken into urea and Ornithine in the presence of an enzyme arginase and water.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10789,'biology',9,26,49,'Which of the following plant group doesnot possesses vascular tissues xylem and phloem?','[{"text": "Bryophytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bryophytes do not possess any vascular tissues. While pteridophytes, gymnosperms and angiosperms are all tracheophytes (vascular tissue bearing plants)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10790,'biology',90,1334,3217,'The fluid-filled space, contain neurotransmitters','[{"text": "They are released from vesicles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are found at chemical synapse only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are found at electrical synapse only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The fluid-filled space, i.e. synaptic cleft has neurotransmitters (chemicals) released from vesicles and is found in chemical synapse. Electrical synapses do not have neurotransmitters.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10803,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Column of Bertini of extension of<br><div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Cortex into medulla", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Medulla into cortex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renal pelvis into renal sinus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renal capsule into cortex", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The renal column (or Bertin column, or column of Bertin) is a medullary extension of the renal cortex in between the renal pyramids. It allows the cortex to be better anchored.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10791,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Which is wrongly matched<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "DCT-absorption of glucose", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bowman\'s capsule-Glomerular filtration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Henle\'s loop- Concentration of urine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PCT- Absorption of $$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and $$\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$$ions", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Conditional reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{Na}+$$ and water takes place in DCT. DCT is also capable of reabsorption of $$\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}$$ - and selective secretion of hydrogen and potassium ions and $$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$ to maintain the $$\\mathrm{pH}$$ and sodium-potassium balance in blood.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10793,'biology',9,26,49,'Vascular plants which do not bear seeds are','[{"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pterdiophytes are seedless tracheophytes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10794,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Unidirectional transmission of a nerve impulse through nerve fibre is due to the fact that','[{"text": "Neurotransmitters are released by the axon endings", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neurotransmitters are released by the cyton vesicles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neurotransmitters are released by dendrites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above statements are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Chemicals called neurotransmitters are involved in the transmission of impulses at these synapses. The axon terminals contain vesicles filled with these neurotransmitters',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10795,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Which one of the following correctly explains the function of a specific part of a human nephron?<br>','[{"text": "Henle\'s loop - Most reabsorption of the major substances from the glomerular filtrate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Distal convoluted tubule-Reabsorption of ions into the surrounding blood capillaries", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Afferent arteriole - Carries the blood away from the glomerulus towards renal vein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Podocytes- Create minute spaces (slit pores) for the filtration of blood into the Bowman\'s capsule", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Podocytes or visceral epithelial cells are the cells in Bowman\'s capsule in the kidneys that wrap around capillaries of glomerulus. They create minute pores (slit pores) for the filtration of blood into the Bowman\'s capsule.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10797,'biology',9,26,49,'Pteridophytes are also known as','[{"text": "Avascular cryptogams", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phanerogams", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphibious plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vascular cryptogams", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Plants carrying out conspicuous/hidden reproduction are known as cryptogams. Hidden reproduction is by the means of spores. These plants are seedless. Eg. Pteridophytes.<br>Pteridophytes possess vascular tissue like xylem and phloem , therefore they are vascular cryptogams.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10798,'biology',90,1334,3217,'The synaptic vesicle moves towards the membrane, where it fuses with plasma membrane and release neurotransmitter. The membrane from where the neurotransmitter released is ____','[{"text": "Special membrane of the axon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pre-synaptic membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Synaptic cleft membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Post-synaptic membrane", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When an impulse (action potential) arrives at the axon terminal, it stimulates the movement of the synaptic vesicles towards the membrane where they fuse with the plasma membrane and release their neurotransmitters in the synaptic cleft. The membrane from where the neurotransmitter is released is the pre-synaptic membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10799,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Uricotelic mode of passing out nitrogenous waste is found in','[{"text": "Birds and annelids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphibians and reptiles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insects and amphibians", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reptiles and birds<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Reptiles, birds, land snails and insects excrete nitrogenous waste as uric acid in the form of pellet of paste with a minimum loss of water and are called uricotelic animals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10801,'biology',9,26,49,'Which statement is incorrect about\npteridophyte?','[{"text": "Evolutionarily, they are the first terrestrial\\nplants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are found in cool damp and shady\\nplace", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The xylem posses vessels", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They flourish well in moist and shady\\ncondition", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Xylem vessels are a characteristic feature of flowering plants. They are absent in pteridophytes and gymnosperms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10802,'biology',90,1334,3217,'After a chemical synapse, the new potential developed is','[{"text": "Always excitatory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Always inhibitory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "May be excitatory or inhibitory", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None is correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'On post-synaptic membrane, the new action potential developed can be excitatory or inhibitory, depending upon the action of neurotransmitter.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10805,'biology',9,26,49,'The main plant body of pteridophytes is','[{"text": "Sporophyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gametophytes as well as sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thalloid", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In pteridophytes, the main plant body is a sporophyte which is differentiated into true root, stem and leaves',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10806,'biology',90,1334,3217,'The neurotransmitters binds to their specific receptors. This binding ____ ion channels allowing the ____of ions which can generate a new potential.','[{"text": "Opens, exit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Opens, entry", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Closes, entry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Closes, exit", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The neurotransmitters binds to their specific receptors, present on the post-synaptic membrane. This binding opens ion channels allowing the entry of ions which can generate a new potential in the post-synaptic neuron.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10807,'biology',88,1152,2759,'The maximum amount of electrolytes and water $$(70-80 \\%)$$ from the glomerular filtrate is reabsorbed in which part of the nephron?<br>','[{"text": "Ascending limb of loop of Henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Distal convoluted tubule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proximal convoluted tubule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Descending limb of loop of Henle", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'From the Bowman\'s capsule, the glomerular filtrate enters the proximal convoluted tubule (PCT). PCT is surrounded by a network of pertubular capillaries and is the seat of reabsorption. About $$75 \\%$$ of glomerular filtrate is normally reabsorbed in PCT before reaching the loop of Henle. The reabsorbed materials include glucose, amino acids, vitamins, hormones, sodium, potassium, chlorides, phosphates, bicarbonates, most of the water and some urea, etc.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10809,'biology',9,26,49,'The structure of the plant body of a pteridophyte','[{"text": "Is the most well-developed in plant\\nkingdom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Posses true root, leaves and stem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Is thalloid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Possess rhizoids", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pteridophytes are the first plants to bear true roots, steam and leaves.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10810,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Which one of the following is not a part of a renal pyramid?','[{"text": "Convoluted tubule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Collecting ducts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Loop of Henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peritubular capillaries<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Convoluted tubule is the highly convoluted segments of nephron located in the cortex region of the kidney. It is made up of proximal tubule leading from the Bowman\'s capsule to the descending limb of Henle\'s loop and distal tubule leading from the ascending limb of Henle\'s loop to a collecting tubule.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10811,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Electrical synapse<br>B. Chemical synapse<br>C. Receptors</div><div class="column-right">P. Where neurotransmitter bind<br>Q. Found rare in our body<br>R. Synaptic cleft is present</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P,B-R,C-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q,C-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-RB-Q,C-P", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Q, B-R, C-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10813,'biology',9,26,49,'Macrophylls are characteristics of','[{"text": "Mosses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Equisetum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ferns", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Selaginella", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The leaves in pteridophytes, especially ferns, are large in size and called macrophylls.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10814,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which one of the following statement is correct with respect to kidney function regulation?<br>','[{"text": "Exposure to cold temperature stimulates $$\\\\mathrm{ADH}$$ release", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "An increase in glomerular blood flow stimulate formation of angiotension-II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "During summer when body loses lot of water by evaporation, the release of $$\\\\mathrm{ADH}$$ is suppressed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "When someone drinks lot of water $$\\\\mathrm{ADH}$$ release is suppressed", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'When someone drinks lot of water which is not required by body, the osmoregulation of the blood will decrease. The decrease in osmoregulation will inhibit the release of $$\\mathrm{ADH}$$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10815,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Synapse<br>B. Synaptic cleft<br>C. Axon Terminal<br>D. Neurotransmitters</div><div class="column-right">P. The membranes of the pre- and post- synaptic neurons are separated by fluid filled space<br>Q. Junction through which nerve impulse is transmitted from one neuron to another<br>R. Chemicals involved in the transmission of impulses at synapse<br>S. Contain vesicles filled with acetylcholine</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10818,'biology',88,1155,2762,'During summer season, which hormone concentration is maintained at high level?<br>','[{"text": "Insulin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasopressin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oxytocin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corticoid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During summer season, due to continuous dehydration of the body, more water reabsorption is needed from the renal tubules. This is kept in check by ADH/Vasopressin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10819,'biology',90,1334,3217,'The following diagram show transmission of impulses from synapse. Identify structure in pre-synaptic and post-synaptic neuron (A-C).','[{"text": "A - Receptors, B-Synaptic vesicles, C - Axon terminal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Axon terminal, B - Receptors, C - Synaptic vesicles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Axon terminal, B-Synaptic vesicles, C - Receptors", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Synaptic vesicles, B - Receptors, C - Axon terminal", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A- Axon terminal, B- Vesicles, C- Receptor',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/90_10819_question_1.png'),
(10821,'biology',9,26,49,'The leaves in pteridophytes are small as in','[{"text": "Ferns", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Dryopteris</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Selaginella</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Azolla</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The leaves in pteridophyta are small (microphylls) as in Selaginella.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10822,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Pressure which favours filtration and one which opposes filtration of blood are ____ And ____ Respectively<br>','[{"text": "Capsular hydrostatic pressure and glomerular osmotic pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glomerular hydrostatic pressure and glomerular osmotic pressure", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glomerular osmotic pressure and Glomerular hydrostatic pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glomerular osmotic pressure and arterial pressure.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pressure which favours filtration and one which opposes filtration of blood are glomerular hydrostatic pressure and glomerular osmotic pressure respectively. The glomerular hydrostatic pressure is the blood pressure created by the glomerular blood and is about ${\\rm{60}}\\,{\\rm{mmHg}}$, Osmotic concentration of proteinaceous content of glomerular blood equivalent to ${\\rm{30}}\\,{\\rm{mmHg}}$ is called glomerular osmotic pressure.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10824,'biology',90,1334,3217,'The following diagram shows transmission of impulse through chemical synapse. The membranes involved in the synapse are (A-C).','[{"text": "A - Pre-synaptic membrane,<br>B - Synaptic cleft,<br>C - Post-synaptic membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Synaptic cleft,<br>B - Pre-synaptic membrane,<br>C - Post-synaptic membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Pre-synaptic membrane,<br>B - Post-synaptic membrane,<br>C - Synaptic cleft", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Synaptic cleft,<br>B - Post-synaptic membrane,<br>C - Pre-synaptic membrane", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A - Pre-synaptic membrane, B-Synaptic cleft, C-Post-synaptic membrane',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/90_10824_question_1.png'),
(10825,'biology',9,26,49,'Given diagram is of the_<br>','[{"text": "<i>Gracilaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Salvia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Salvinia </i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Selaginella</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The given diagram represents Selaginella.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_10825_question_1.png'),
(10826,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Which is common between humans and adult frog?<br>','[{"text": "Internal fertilization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleated RBC\'s", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four chambered heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ureotelic excretion", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Adult frog being terrestrial performs excretion as ureotelism. Adult frog and humans share the same mode of excretion i.e. ureotelism.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10828,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Identify structure and chemicals involved in chemical impulse A, B & $\\mathrm{C}$ in the given diagram?','[{"text": "A - Synapse,<br>B - Neurotransmitters,<br>C - Synaptic vesicles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Neurotransmitters,<br>B - Synaptic vesicles,<br>C - Synapse", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Neurotransmitters,<br>B - Synapse,<br>C - Synaptic vesicles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Synaptic vesicles,<br>B - Neurotransmitters,<br>C - Synapse", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A - Neurotransmitters, B - Synaptic vesicles C- Synapse',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/90_10828_question_1.png'),
(10829,'biology',9,26,49,'The leaves of following species are _','[{"text": "Sporophylls", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microphylls", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Macrophylls", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Strobili", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The given diagram represents Selaginella.It bears leaves that are small, also known as microsporophylls.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_10829_question_1.png'),
(10830,'biology',88,1155,2762,'A fall in glomerular filtration activates<br>','[{"text": "Juxta glomerular cells to release rennin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenal cortex to release aldosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Posterior pituitary to release vasopressin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adrenal medulla to release adrenaline", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A fall in glomerular blood flow/glomerular blood pressure/GFR can activate the JG cells to release renin which converts angiotensinogen in blood to angiotensin $$\\mathrm{I}$$ and further to angiotensin II. Angiotensin II, being a powerful vasoconstrictor, increases the glomerular blood pressure and thereby GFR.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10832,'biology',90,1335,3218,'Brain controls the','[{"text": "Voluntary movements & functioning of vital involuntary organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Balance of the body & thermoregulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hunger and thirst", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Brain controls the voluntary movements, balance of the body, funtioning of vital involuntary organs (e.g. lungs, heart, kidneys, etc.), thermoregulation, hunger and thirst, circadian (24-hours) rhythms of our body, activities of several endocrine glands and human behaviour. It is the site for processing of vision, hearing, speech, memory, intelligence, emotions and thoughts.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10833,'biology',9,26,49,'The leaves bearing sporangia are called','[{"text": "Macrophylls", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fronds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zoosporangia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporophylls", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The sporophytes bear sporangia that are subtended by leaf-like appendages called sporophylls.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10834,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Figure shows human urinary system with structure labelled A to D. Select option, which correctly identifies them and gives their characteristics and / of functions.<br>','[{"text": "A-Adrenal gland located at the anterior part of kidney. Secrete catecholamies, which stimulate glycogen breakdown", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B-Pelvis-broad funnel shaped space inner to hilum, directly connected to loops of Henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C-Medulla-inner zone of kidney and contains complete nephrons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D-Cortex-outer part of kidney and do not contain any part of nephrons", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Adrenal gland it is correctly mentioned. It is located at the anterior part of kidney. Secrete catecholamines which stimulate glycogen breakdown.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/88_10834_question_1.png'),
(10836,'biology',90,1335,3218,'Inside the bony structure____,  the brain is covered by','[{"text": "Skull, arachnoid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Skull, cranial meninges", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cranium, skull", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cranial meninges, cranium", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The human brain is well protected by the skull. Inside the skull, the brain is covered by cranial menings, comprising of durameter, arachnoid and piameter.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10837,'biology',9,26,49,'Cones in pteridophytes are formed in','[{"text": "<i>Salvinia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Selaginella</i> only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Equisetum</i> only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Selaginella</i> and<i> Equisetum</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In some cases sporophylls may form distinct compact structures called strobili or cones (Selaginella, Equisetum).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10838,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which of the following causes an increase in sodium reabsorption in the distal convoluted tubule?<br>','[{"text": "Increase in aldosterone levels", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Increase in antidiuretic hormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decrease in aldosterone levels", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decrease in antidiuretic hormone levels", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Increase in aldosterone levels cause an increase in sodium reabsorption in DCT. It is secreted by outer layer of adrenal gland when aldosterone is present in the blood and all the ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ ions in the filtrate are reabsorbed. Retaining ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ raises the osmotic pressure of the blood and reduces the water loss from the body.<br>',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10840,'biology',90,1335,3218,'Cranial menings from inner layer to outer layer are called','[{"text": "Piameter, arachnoid, durameter", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Durameter, arachnoid, piameter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arachnoid, durameter, piameter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arachnoid, piameter, durameter", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The correct sequence of menings from inside to outside is<br>Piameter $\\rightarrow$ Arachnoid $\\rightarrow$ Duramater',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10841,'biology',9,26,49,'Sporophytic, generation is dominant phase in the life cycle of','[{"text": "<i>Selaginella</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Equisetum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Salvinia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Dominant phase in Salvinia , Selaginella , Equisetum ,ferns is sporophyte (2n), which is differentiated into root, stem and leaf.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10842,'biology',88,1150,2757,'The body cells in cockroach discharge their nitrogenous waste in the haemolymph mainly in the form of<br>','[{"text": "Ammonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Potassium urate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Urea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calcium carbonate", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<br>$$\\square$$ Insects including cockroach excrete nitrogenous waste in the form of soluble potassium urate which is liberated into the haemolymph and taken up by the cells lining the Malpighian tubules.<br>$$\\square$$ The tubules facilitate the absorption of urate by stirring up the blood.<br>$$\\square$$ In the cells of the tubule the potassium urate reacts with water and carbon dioxide (from respiration) to form potassium hydrogen carbonate and uric acid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10846,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which of the following does not favour the formation of large quantities of dilute urine?<br>','[{"text": "Alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Caffeine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Atrial- natriuretic factor", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Renin secreted by JGA regulates the glomerular filtration rate by inducing multihormonal system i.e., RAAS (renin angiotensin-aldosterone system). Activation of this system increase the reabsorption rate of Sodium ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ and water, making the urine more concentrated. Alcohol decreases vasopressin level which lowers reabsorption of water thus making urine more dilute. ANF causes vasodilation and acts as check on RAAS.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10848,'biology',90,1335,3218,'The brain can be divided into three major parts:','[{"text": "Left brain, midbrain, and right brain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dorsal brain, midbrain, and ventral brain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Forebrain, midbrain, and hindbrain", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Medial brain, midbrain, and lateral brain", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The brain can be divided into three major parts: (i) forebrain, (ii) midbrain, and (iii) hindbrain',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10849,'biology',9,26,49,'In pteridophytes, spore germinates to give rise to','[{"text": "Photosynthetic sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporophyte called prothallus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametophyte called protonema", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametophyte called prothallus", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The spores germinate to give rise to inconspicuous, small but multicellular, freeliving, mostly photosynthetic thalloid gametophytes called prothallus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10850,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which one of the following is not a zymogen?<br>','[{"text": "Trypsinogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pepsinogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angiotensin -II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Procollaginase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Inactive precursors of enzymes are known as proenzymes or zymogen granules. It undergoes a chemical change to get activated. Some examples are trypsinogen, pepsinogen, procollagenase but angiotensin II is not a proenzyme but it is a vasoconstrictor that regulates blood pressure.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10852,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Forebrain consist of','[{"text": "Cerebrum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thalamus & Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpus callosum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of them are correct. corpus callosum joins the two cerebral hemispheres, so it also becomes a part of the forebrain.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10853,'biology',9,26,49,'Prothallus is the sporophyte of','[{"text": "Bryophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pteridophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Prothallus is a gametophyte that develops from a spore.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10854,'biology',88,1151,2758,'In mammals, which blood vessel would normally carry largest amount of urea?','[{"text": "Hepatic vein", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hepatic portal vein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renal vein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dorsal aorta", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Urea is synthesized in the liver. Hepatic vein carries blood from the liver into the inferior vena cava and thus has the largest amount of urea compared to any other blood vessel.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10856,'biology',90,1336,3219,'The cerebrum is made up of how many cerebral hemispheres?','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cerebrum is divided longitudinally into two halves, which are termed as the left and right cerebral hemispheres',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10857,'biology',9,26,49,'Mosses and ferns are found in moist and shady places because both','[{"text": "Require the presence of moisture for\\nbasic growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Do not need sunlight for photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Require the presence of water for\\nfertilization", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Require the presence of air", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mosses and ferns carry out zooidogamy (fertilization in water). Therefore, they grow in moist, damp places as they require water for sexual reproduction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10858,'biology',88,1155,2762,'A decrease in blood pressure/volume will not cause the release of :','[{"text": "Atrial natriuretic factor", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aldosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{ADH}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renin", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Atrial natriuretic factor (ANF) is secreted by the atrium of heart and it regulates composition of $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$in blood and controls uresis (urine output). It promotes excretion of $$\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$$and water, it also promotes retention of $$\\mathrm{K}^{+}$$. Activity of ANF will help to reduce blood volume and blood pressure i.e., it has a vasodilator effect.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10860,'biology',9,26,49,'Gametophyte of pteridophyte','[{"text": "Parasite on sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photosynthetic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photosynthetic and symbiotic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photosynthetic and free living", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Gametophytes of pteridophytes are not the main plant bodies but they are free-living and autotrophic.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10861,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Right and left cerebral hemispheres are connected via','[{"text": "Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpus callosum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpus luteum", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A deep cleft divides the cerebrum longitudinally into two halves, which are termed as the left and right cerebral hemisphere. The hemisphere are connected by a tract of nerve fibres called corpus callosum.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10862,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Match the items given in Column I with those in Column II and select the correct option given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Ultrafiltration<BR>B. Concentration of urine<BR>C. Transport of urine<BR>D. Storage of urine</div><div class="column-right">1. Henle’s loop<BR>2. Ureter<BR>3. Urinary bladder<BR>4. Malphighian corpuscle<BR>5. Proximal convoluted tubule</div></div>','[{"text": "A-5, B-4, C-1, D-2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-4, B-1, C-2, D-3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-4, B-5, C-2, D-3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-5, B-4, C-1, D-3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<br>A. (4) Ultrafiltration is the filtration of very fine particles having molecular weight less than 68,000 Daltons through Malpighian corpuscle.<br>B. (1) Urine formed gets concentrated as it passes along Henle\'s loop.<br>C. (2) Formed urine is transported from kidney to urinary bladder through Ureters.<br>D. (3) Urine is stored in urinary bladder.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10864,'biology',9,26,49,'Gametophyte of pteridophyte','[{"text": "Inconspicuous, small but multicellular", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inconspicuous, small but unicellular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Conspicuous, small but multicellular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Conspicuous, small but unicellular", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Gametophyte in pteridophytes is small, inconspicuous but multicellular. It is freeliving and can carry out photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10865,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Corpus callosum','[{"text": "Is a tract of connective tissue fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is a tract of dense muscular fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is a tract of dense irregular connective tissue fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None is correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Corpus callosum is a tract of nerve fibres',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10866,'biology',88,1158,2765,'Match the items given in Column I with those in Column II and select the correct option given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Glycosuria<br>B. Gout<br>C. Renal calculi<br>D. Glomerulonephritis</div><div class="column-right">1. Accumulation of uric acid in joints<br>2. Mass of crystalized salts within the kidney<br>3. Inflammation in glomeruli<br>4. Presence of glucose in urine</div></div>','[{"text": "A-2, B-3, C-1, D-4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-1, B-2, C-3, D-4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-3, B-2, C-4, D-1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-4, B-1, C-2, D-3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<br>A. (4) Glycosuria is presence of glucose in urine. When blood glucose level rises above ${\\rm{180}}\\,{\\rm{mg/100ml}}$ of blood it can be observed.<br>B. (1) Gout is caused by deposition of crystals of uric acid in a joint.<br>C. (2) Renal calculi is the formation of stone or insoluble mass of crystallised salts (oxalates, etc.) within the kidney.<br>D. (3) Glomerular nephritis is the inflammation of glomeruli of kidney.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10868,'biology',9,26,49,'Prothallus of the pteridophyta produces','[{"text": "Gametes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Spores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Prothallus is the gametophyte in pteridophytes. It produces gametes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10869,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Which part constitutes the major part of the brain?','[{"text": "Hindbrain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cerebrum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cerebellum", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cerebrum forms the major part of the human brain',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10870,'biology',88,1158,2765,'Presence of which of the following conditions in urine are indicative of Diabetes Mellitus?<br>','[{"text": "Uremia and Renal Calculi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ketonuria and Glycosuria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Renal calculi and Hyperglycaemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uremia and Ketonuria", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Presence of glucose (Glycosuria) and ketone bodies (Ketonuria) in urine are indicative of diabetes mellitus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10872,'biology',9,26,49,'Sex organs in pteridophytes are formed on the','[{"text": "Sporophyte.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dependent gametophyte phase of the\\nplant.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Free living gametophyte.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gametophyte dependent on sporophyte.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The gametophytes of pteridophytes bear male and female sex organs called antheridia and archegonia, respectively.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10873,'biology',90,1336,3219,'The folded layer of cells that covers the cerebral hemisphere is called as','[{"text": "White matter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cerebral cortex", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Corpus callosum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cerebral medulla", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The layer of cells which covers the cerebral hemisphere is called cerebral cortex and is thrown into prominent folds.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10874,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which of the following would help in prevention of diuresis?','[{"text": "Reabsorption of and water form renal tubules due to aldosterone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Atrial natriuretic factor causes vasoconstriction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decrease in secretion of renin by JG cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More water reabsorption due to undersecretion of $$\\\\mathrm{ADH}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Reabsorption of and water from renal tubules due to aldosterone.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10876,'biology',9,26,49,'The male and female sex organs of pteridophyte\nare called','[{"text": "Archegonia and antheridia respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testes and ovary respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anther and egg respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antheridia and archegonia respectively", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Male sex organ – Antheridia, Female sex organ - Archegonia',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10877,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Nitrogenous waste is excreted in the form of pellet or paste by:','[{"text": "<em>Salamandra</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Hippocampus</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Pavo</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<em>Ornithorhynchus</em>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Reptiles, birds, land snails and insects are uricotelic animals and excrete nitrogenous wastes as uric acid in the form of pellet of paste with a minimum loss of water. <em>Pavo </em>(peacock) is a bird. Note that <em>Salamandra </em>is an amphibian, not a reptile.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10878,'biology',90,1336,3219,'The cerebral cortex is referred to as','[{"text": "White matter-axon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "White matter- cell bodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Grey matter- axon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Grey matter- cell bodies", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The cerebral cortex is referred to as the grey matter. This is due to its greyish appearance. The neuron cell bodies are concentrated here giving it, its grey colour.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10880,'biology',9,26,49,'The zygote of pteridophyte','[{"text": "Produces unicellular sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Produces multicellular gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Produces multicellular sporophyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Undergoes immediate meiosis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fusion of male gamete with the egg present in the archegonium result in the formation of zygote. Zygote thereafter produces a multicellular well-differentiated sporophyte which is the dominant phase of the pteridophytes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10881,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Flame cells present in the members of platyhelminthes are specialized to perform,','[{"text": "Osmoregulation and excretion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Respiration and Excretion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Respiration and Osmoregulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osmoregulation and Circulation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Osmoregulation and Excretion',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10882,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Cerebral cortex consists of','[{"text": "Sensory areas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Motor areas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Association areas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The cerebral cortex contains motor areas, sensory areas and large regions that are neither clearly sensory nor motor in function. These regions called as the association areas',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10884,'biology',9,26,49,'In homosporous pteridophyte, the gametophyte\nis','[{"text": "Neither monoecious or dioecious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "May be monoecious or dioecious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dioecious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monoecious", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The spores when are present in homosporous condition (in both male and female parts only one type of gametophyte is present) then the gametophyte produced is called monoecious but when the spores are\npresent in heterozygous condition (male an female parts produce different gametophytes, the male produces microspores while female produces megaspores) then the gametophyte produced is called dioecious.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10885,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Read the Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct options given below:<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Nephrons are of two types: Cortical & Juxta medullary, based on their relative position in cortex and medulla.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Juxta medullary nephrons have short loop of Henle whereas, cortical nephrons have longer loop of Henle.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are  true and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is false but  Reason is true", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Assertion is true as there are two types of nephrons, i.e., cortical nephrons and juxtamedullary nephrons based on their relative position in the cortex and medulla. Reason is not correct as loop of Henle in\njuxtamedullary nephrons is very long and runs deep into the medulla. Therefore, Assertion is correct but Reason is false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10886,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Association areas of the brain are','[{"text": "Always clearly sensory areas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Always clearly motor areas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neither clearly sensory nor motor areas", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Association areas are the regions of brain that are neither clearly sensory nor motor in function.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10888,'biology',9,26,49,'Heterosporous plants are','[{"text": "Sexual and asexual spores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plants producing large and small spores.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Plants producing two type of spores which<br>\\nare similar in size.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haploid and diploid spores", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Genera which produce two kinds of spores, macro (large) and micro (small) spores, are known as heterosporous. The megaspores and microspores germinate and give rise to female and male gametophytes, respectively.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10889,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>I. An excessive loss of body fluid from the body switches off osmoreceptors.<br>II. ADH facilitates water reabsorption to prevent diuresis.<br>III. ANF causes vasodilation.<br>IV. ADH causes increase in blood pressure.<br>V. ADH is responsible for decrease in GFR.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "I and II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III and IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II and V only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV and V only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statements II, III and IV are true statements. ADH facilitates water reabsorption from DCT of nephron to prevent diuresis, which causes increase in blood pressure. ANF which is secreted by the heart is a vasodilator',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10890,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Functions of associations areas in which in cerebral cortex','[{"text": "Inter sensory association", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Memory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Communication", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Association areas are the regions of brain that are neither clearly sensory nor motor in function. These are responsible for complex functions like intersensory associations, memory and communication.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10892,'biology',9,26,49,'Heterosporous pteridophytes are','[{"text": "<i>Selaginella</i> and<i> Salvia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Selaginella </i>and <i>Lycopodium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Selaginella</i> and <i>Salvinia</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adiantum and Psilotum", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Genera Selaginella and Salvinia are heterosporous pteridophytes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10893,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Vasopressin released from the neurohyphysis is mainly responsible for','[{"text": "Facultative reabsorption of water through DCT", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Obligatory reabsorption of water through PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Facultative reabsorption of water through Henle\'s loop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Obligatory reabsorption of water through Bowman\'s capsule", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Facultative reabsorption is the removal of water in the distal convoluted tubule and collecting duct. It is regulated by the vasopressin (also called ADH) and the role of vasopressin is to make the collecting duct more permeable so that water can be osmotically drawn out of the filtrate. The conditions that favor maximizing facultative reabsorption are dehydration.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10895,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Thalamus in human brain is','[{"text": "A major centre for motor and sensory signaling", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Wraps the cerebrum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Found above the epithalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The cerebrum wraps around a structure called thalamus, which is a major coordinating centre for sensory and motor signaling',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10932,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Filtration of blood during urine formation takes place in','[{"text": "Glomerulus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collecting duct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Filtration of blood during urine formation takes place in Glomerulus. The glomerular filtrate is collected in the Bowmans capsule.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10896,'biology',9,26,49,'Pteridophytes are<br>I. Homosporous and produce only one kind of spores.<br>II. Zygote produces a multicellular well differentiated sporophyte<br>III. Heterosporus and produce small and large spores.<br>IV. Restricted to narrow geographical zone because of specific requirement of water.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II III and IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The spread of living pteridophytes is limited and restricted to narrow geographical regions because their need or water for fertilization. Pteridophytes can be homosporous (produce one kind of spore) or heterosporous (produce two different spores, small and large). For sexual reproduction, gametes fuse to form a zygote. This zygote divides to form a multicellular, well-diffrentiated sporophyte.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10897,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Curved portion of the Henle\'s loop of the Nephrons are lined by','[{"text": "Ciliated epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cubodial epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Squamous epithelium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Columnar epithelium", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Simple squamous epithelium have thin, flat, disc like cells closely fitted to each other. Hence, it is also called pavement epithelium. The squamous epithelium lines the Bowman\'s capsules, curved portion of Henle\'s loop of the urinary tubules and the alveoli of the lungs. Its function is protection, excretion, gas exchange and secretion of coelomic fluid',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10899,'biology',9,26,49,'In <span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><em>Selaginella</em></span> the embryo develops into','[{"text": "Gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporophyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Antheridium", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In Pteridophytes, like <em>Selaginella</em>, the zygote develops into embryo and further into a well differentiated sporophyte that acts the main plant body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10900,'biology',90,1336,3219,'The inner parts of cerebral hemisphere and a group of associated deep structures like form a complex structure called','[{"text": "Limbs system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Limbic system", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Corpora quadrigemina", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The inner parts of cerebral hemispheres and a group of associated deep structures like amygdala, hippocampus, etc., form a complex structure called the limbic lobe or limbic system.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10901,'biology',88,1153,2760,'A large quantity of fluid is filtered every day by the nephrons in the kidneys. Only about $1 \\%$ of it is excerted as urine. The remaining $99 \\%$ of the filtrate','[{"text": "It lost as sweat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is stored in the urinary bladder", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is reabsorbed into the blood", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gets collected in the renal pelvis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'On average, 1100 - 1120 millilitres of blood per minute is filtered by the kidney. More than $99 \\%$ of th glomerular filtrate return to the bloodstream via tubular reabsorption, so only about 1.5 litres is excerted as urine',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10903,'biology',9,26,49,'In pteridophytes, the megaspore germinates to form','[{"text": "Male sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Female gametophyte", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In heterosporous pteridophytes, the megaspores germinate and give rise to female gametophytes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10904,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Which part of the human brain controls the urge for eating and drinking?','[{"text": "Forebrain- Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Midbrain- Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Forebrain- Forethalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Forebrain- Thalamus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Forebrain consists of hypothamus, which controls the urge for eating and drinking.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10905,'biology',88,1150,2757,'The characteristic that is shared by urea, uric acid and ammonia is/are:<br>A. They are nitrogenous wastes<br>B. They all need very large amount of , water for excretion<br>C. They are all equally toxic<br>D. They are produced in the kidneys','[{"text": "A and D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, C and D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A and C", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ammonia, urea and uric acid are nitrogenous waste. Ammonia is produced by deamination of amino acid, urea is produced by ammonia and carbondioxide and uric acid is produced from nitrogenous bases.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10907,'biology',9,26,49,'The development of young embryos of pteridophytes within the female gametophytes is a precursor to the','[{"text": "Fruit habit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo habit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed habit", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Flower habit", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The development of the zygotes into young embryos take place within the female gametophytes. This event is a precursor to the seed habit considered an important step in evolution.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10908,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Hypothalamus controls','[{"text": "Body\'s thermostat", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mind\'s thermostat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The hypothalamus contains a number of centres which control body temperature, urge for eating and drinking.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10909,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Which substance is in higher concentration in blood than in glomerular filtrate?','[{"text": "Glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Urea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasma proteins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The fluid that enters the capsular space from glomerular capillaries is called the glomerul ar filtrate . A thin membrane, the slit membrane. extends across each filtration slit and permits the passage of molecules having a diameter smaller than $0.006-0.007$ microm . including water, glucose, vitamins, amino acids, very small plasma proteins, ammonia, urea and ions. Thus, plasma proteins are higher in concentration in blood than in glomerular filtrate.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10911,'biology',9,26,49,'In pteridophytes, fusion of gametes takes place in','[{"text": "External medium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antheridium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antherozoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Archegonium", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The male gametes from the antheridia are released to the mouth of archegonium. Fusionof male gamete with the egg takes placee in the archegonium resulting in the formation of zygote.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10912,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Thalamus is responsible for','[{"text": "Acting as coordinating centre for sensory and motor signal", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Acting as sensory and motor centre", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Urge for eating and drinking.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The cerebrum wraps around a structure called thalamus, which is a major coordinating centre for sensory and motor signaling.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10913,'biology',88,1154,2761,'Compare the statement A and B<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">When the urine moves through the descending limb, it becomes hypertonic and as it passes through the ascending limb of Henle\'s loop, it becomes hypotonic<br></div><div class="column-right">The descending limb is permeable to sodium ions, while the ascending limb is impermeable to sodium ions</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is wrong and Statement B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct and Statement B is wrong", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements A and B are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements A and B are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The filtrate moves from proximal convoluted tubule to the descending limb of the loop of Henle. The cells of the walls of the descending limb do not permit salt and urea to pass out of the tubule but they are freely permeable to water. As water passes out of the descending limb, it leaves behind a more concentrated filtrate, thus the tiltrate is hypertonic to blood plasma.In the ascending limb, active transport channels are present in the wall of the tubule that pump even more electrolytes out of the filtrate. Thus, the electrolyte concentration increases within the renal medulla. As ions not water molecules are reabsorbed, the osmolarity of the tubular fuid decreases progressively as fluid flows toward the end of the ascending limb. Sodium, potassium, calcium, magnesium and chloride are reabsorbed and the filtrate is hypotonie to blood plasma.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2010,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10915,'biology',9,26,49,'The female gametophytes are retained on the parent sporophyte in','[{"text": "Homosporous species of pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are never retained on sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homosporous and Heterosporous species\\nof pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterosporous species of pteridophytes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The female gametophytes in heterosporous pteridophytes are retained on the parent sporophytes for variable periods.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10916,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Effective filtration pressure in glomerulus is caused due to','[{"text": "Powerful pumping action of the heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretion of adrenalin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Afferent arteriole is slightly larger than efferent arteriole", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vacuum develops in proximal convoluted tubule and sucks the blood", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Efferent arterioles are smaller in diameter than afferent arterioles. As a result, pressurized blood enters the glomerulus through a relatively wide tube but is forced to exit through a narrower tube builds effective filtration pressure.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10917,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Which of the following is true about hypothalamus?','[{"text": "Controls urge for food", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contains neurosecretory cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Situated at the base of thalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The hypothalamus contains a number of centres which control body temperature, urge for eating and drinking. It also contains several groups of neurosecretory cells, which secrete hormones called hypothalamic hormones.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10919,'biology',9,26,49,'Seed habit is linked to','[{"text": "Homospory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterospory", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Seed habit takes place in heterosporous plants. In these plants, the development of zygote takes place in female gametophyte.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10920,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Juxta glomerular cells secrete $\\underline {\\text{A}} $ when there is a fall in $\\underline {\\text{B}} $ ion concentration. Choose the correct pair labelled as A and B','[{"text": "A: Renin B: Chloride", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A: Carbonic anhydrase B: Sodium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A: ATPase B: Potassium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A: Renin B: Sodium", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The regulation of the rate of glomerular filtration is done by juxta glomerular apparatus (JGA) which comprises macula densa cells and juxta glomerular ells. The juxta glomerular (JG) cells secrete renin which regulates the blood pressure, renal blood fow and rate of ultrafiltration. When glomerular filtration rate is low and thus a fall in the concentration of ions of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$and $\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$, the JG cells get activated and release more renin which stimulates the blood flow and increases GFR to normalcy by increasing reabsorption of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$and $\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10921,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Limbic system consists of all except ____','[{"text": "Amygdala", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hippocampus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inner parts of cerebral hemispheres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The inner parts of cerebral hemispheres and a group of associated deep structures like amygdala, hippocampus, etc., form a complex structure called the limbic lobe or limbic system.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10923,'biology',9,26,49,'The pteridophytes are further classified into four classes: Identify the wrong pair','[{"text": "Psilopsida (<i>Psilotum</i>)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lycopsida (<i>Selaginella, Lycopodium</i>)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pteropsida (<i>Dryopteris, Pteris, Adiantum</i>)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sphenopsida (Fern)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The class Sphenopsida has species like Equisetum.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10924,'biology',88,1155,2762,'A fall in glomerular filtration rate activates:','[{"text": "Juxtaglomerular cells to release renin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adrenal cortex to release aldosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenal medulla to release adrenaline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Posterior pituitary to release vasopressin -", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A fall in glomerular blood fiow/ glomerular blood pressure GFR can activate the JG cells to release renin which converts angiotensinogen in blood to angiotensin I and further to angiotensin II. Angiotensin II, being a powerful vasoconstrictor, increases the glomerular blood pressure and thereby GFR. Angiotensin II also activates the adernal cortex to release aldosterone. Aldosterone causes reabsorption of $\\mathrm{Na}$ and water from the distal parts of the tubule. This also leads to an increase in blood pressure and GFR This complex mechanism is generally known as the Renin-Angiotensin mechanism',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10925,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Limbic system controls','[{"text": "Sexual behaviour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Motivation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Affection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The limbic system is involved in the regulation of sexual behaviour, expression of emotional reactions (e.g., excitement, pleasure, rage and fear), and motivation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10927,'biology',9,26,49,'Which of the following group of pteridophytes belong to class-Pteropsida?','[{"text": "<em>Equisetum </em>and <em>Dryopteris</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Psilotum</em> and <em>Dryopteris</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Selaginella</em> and <em>Pteris</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Pteris </em>and <em>Adiantum</em>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'&nbsp;Class <em>Pteropsida </em>contains &nbsp;<em>Dryopteris</em>,<em>Pteris</em>, <em>Adiantum</em>.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10928,'biology',88,1153,2760,'The type of epithelium found in the inner lining of PCT is :','[{"text": "Squamous epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cuboidal epithelium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glandular epithelium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ciliated epithelium", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In proximal convoluted tubules (PCT), the cells are cuboidal epithelial cells with a prominent brush border of microvilli on their apical surface. These microvilli, like those of the small intestine, increase the surface area for reabsorption and secretion.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10929,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Cerebral medulla','[{"text": "Is the inner part", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Called as white matter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Consists of neurons are covered with the myelin sheath", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10931,'biology',9,26,49,'In which of the following distinct, independent gametophytic and sporophytic generations are found in their life cycle?<br>A.&nbsp;<em>Adiantum</em>	B.&nbsp;<em>Psilotum</em>	C.&nbsp;<em>Selaginella</em>','[{"text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B and C only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and C only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and C", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In the life cycle of all pteridophytes like <em>Adiantum</em>, <em>Psilotum </em>and <em>Selaginella</em>, both gametophyte and sporophyte are distinct, independent and multicellular.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10933,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Four rounded lobes in hindbrain are','[{"text": "Cerebral aqueduct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpora quadrigemina", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpora digemina", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The dorsal portion of the midbrain consists of four round swelligs (lobes) called corpora quadrigemina. The midbrain is located between the thalamus/hypothalamus of the forebrain and pons of the hindbrain.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10935,'biology',9,26,49,'Leaves of pteridophytes are:','[{"text": "Microphyllous only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phylloids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microphyllous in some and Megaphyllous in some others. ", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Megaphyllous only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Leaves of pteridophytes are microphyllous in some and megaphyllous in some others.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
