(10971,'biology',88,1155,2762,'The maximum percentage of filtered water is reabsorbed in','[{"text": "Proximal convoluted tubule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Loop of Henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Distal convoluted tubule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collecting duct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Nearly all of the essential nutrients and 70-80 per cent of electrolytes and water are reabsorbed from the filtrate in the proximal convoluted tubule.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10972,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Which of the following consists of fibre tracts interconnecting the different regions of brain?','[{"text": "Cerebellum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pons varolli", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Medulla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spinal cord", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pons consists of fibre tracts that interconnect different regions of the brain',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10974,'biology',9,26,49,'Following species produces_<br>','[{"text": "Micro spores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Macro spores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Similar spores", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 2 both", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Given diagram represents the homosporous pteridophyte, Equisetum. It bears only one type of spore, similar to each other.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_10974_question_1.png'),
(10975,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Ultrafiltration occurs in a glomerulus when','[{"text": "hydrostatic pressure exceeds osmotic pressure.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "osmotic pressure exceeds hydrostatic pressure.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "capsular hydrostatic pressure exceeds glomerular hydrostatic pressure.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Colloidal osmotic pressure plus capsular pressure remain less than glomerular hydrostatic pressure.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ultrafiltration is an entirely passive process. It occurs in glomerulus when colloidal osmotic pressure plus capsular pressure remain less than glomerular hydrostatic pressure.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10976,'biology',90,1335,3218,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Cranial meninges<br>B. Dura mater<br>C. Arachnoid<br>D. Pia mater</div><div class="column-right">P. Outer layer which is in contact with brain tissue<br>Q. Inner layer which is in contact with brain tissue<br>R. Brain is covered by membrane inside the skull<br>S. A very thin middle layer</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10978,'biology',9,26,49,'The precursor to the seed habit is found in_','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Precursor of seed habit is seen in heterosporous pteridophytes. Eg. Selaginella',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10979,'biology',88,1158,2765,'Dialysing fluid used in hemodialysis does not contain','[{"text": "Urea", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Dialysing fluid has the same composition as that of plasma except for the absence of nitrogenous wastes (e.g. urea, creatinine, uric acid).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10980,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Cerebral hemisphere<br>B. Corpus callosum<br>C. Cerebral cortex<br>D. Associated area</div><div class="column-right">P. Hemispheres are connected by a tract of nerve fibres<br>Q. Cerebrum longitudinally divides into two halves<br>R. Regions responsible for memory & communication<br>S. Contains motor areas, sensory areas & large regions that are neither sensory nor motor in function</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10981,'biology',89,1285,3106,'For the purpose of increase of expiratory capacity which muscles are responsible from following?<br>i. Radial muscles of diaphragm<br>ii. External intercostals muscles<br>iii. Internal intercoastal muscles<br>iv. Abdominal muscles. Option','[{"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii and iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Expiratory capacity is volume of air that can be exhaled forcefully after normal inspiration. During expiration, diaphragm relaxes and becomes convex.The external intercoastal muscles relax and pull ribs downwards and inwards which will decrease size of thoracic cavity.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10982,'biology',9,27,50,'Gymnosperms are characterised by','[{"text": "Seeds inside fruits", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Naked seeds", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Seeds with a special covering", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Winged sperms", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The name gymnosperm itself defines gymnos : naked, sperma : seeds i.e. plants bearing naked seeds.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10983,'biology',88,1158,2765,'In a kidney machine, which of the following passes from the blood to the dialysis fluid?','[{"text": "Glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasma protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red blood cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Urea", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During dialysis, as the patient\'s blood is passed through dialysing solution, most of the wastes like urea present in it pass through selectively permeable cellophane tubes into the dialysing solution. The clean fluid is then pumped back into the vein of patient\'s arm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10984,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Thalamus<br>B. Hypothalamus<br>C. Cerebrum<br>D. Limbic system</div><div class="column-right">P. Control body temperature, urge for eating & drinking<br>Q. Involved in regulation of sexual behavior, expression of emotional reactions<br>R. Major coordinating centre for sensory & motor signaling<br>S. Forms the major part of human brain</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(10985,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Put the following phrases in proper order to describe what occurs at the neuromuscular junction to trigger muscle contraction.<br>i. Receptor sites on sarcolemma<br>ii. Nerve impulses.<br>iii. Release of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ from sarcoplasmic reticulum<br>iv. The neurotransmitter acetylcholine is released<br>v. Sarcomere shortern<br>vi. Synaptic cleft<br>vii. Spread of impulses over sarcolemma on T-tubules','[{"text": "ii, iv, i, vi, vii, iii, v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv, v, vi, vii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iv, vi, i, vii, iii, v", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "vii, vi, v, iv, iii, ii, i", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Proper order of steps that occur at the neuromuscular junction to trigger muscle contraction is as follow:<br>(a) Nerve impulses<br>(b) The neurotransmitter acetylcholine is released<br>(c) Synaptic cleft<br>(d) Receptor sites on sarcolemma<br>(e) Spread of impulses over sarcolemma on T-tubules<br>(f) Release of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ from sarcoplasmic reticulum<br>(g) Sarcomere shorten',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10986,'biology',88,1151,2758,'The nephron shown in the picture given below is a','[{"text": "Cortical nephron because the loop of Henle is very short", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Juxtamedullary nephron because vasa recta are well-developed", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cortical nephron because vasa recta are poorly developed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Juxtamedullary nephron because Malpighian corpuscle is present", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Juxtamedullary nephrons have a long loop of Henle and well-developed vasa recta.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/88_10986_question_1.png'),
(10987,'biology',9,27,50,'Vascular plants, with seeds but no fruits are','[{"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gymnosperms are vascular plants with naked seeds.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10988,'biology',90,1337,3220,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Mid – Brain<br>B. Cerebral aqueduct<br>C. Corpora quadrigemina</div><div class="column-right">P. A canal passess through the midbrain.<br>Q. Midbrain consists mainly of four round lobes<br>R. Located between thalamus & hypothalamus of forebrain</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-R, B-P, C-Q',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10990,'biology',88,1155,2762,'$\\mathrm{ADH}$ receptors are mainly located in which two of the parts (A-E) shown in the following figure?','[{"text": "A and D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B and C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D and E", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "C and D", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{ADH}$ facilitates water reabsorption from the distal convoluted tubule $(\\mathrm{D})$ and the collecting duct $(\\mathrm{E})$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/88_10990_question_1.png'),
(10991,'biology',9,27,50,'Gymnosperms bear seeds but lack fruits because they lack','[{"text": "cotyledon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Integuments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ovule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ovary", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In gymnosperms, ovules are not enclosed by any ovary wall and remain exposed, both before and after fertilisation. The seeds that develop post-fertilisation, are not covered, i.e., are naked. They do not develop into fruits.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11003,'biology',9,27,50,'The first seeded plants are the','[{"text": "<i>Equisetum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Sequoia</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Marchantia</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Gymnosperms were the first seed bearing plants in the process of evolution. Sequoia is one of the tallest gymnosperms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10992,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Brain stem<br>B. Pons<br>C. Cerebellum<br>D. Medulla</div><div class="column-right">P. Contains centre which control respiration, cardiovascular reflexes & gastric secretions<br>Q. Consists of fibre tracts that interconnect different regions of the brain<br>R. Convoluted surface in order to provide the additional space for many more neurons<br>S. Formed by midbrain & hindbrain</div></div>','[{"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-S, B-Q, C-R, D-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10993,'biology',89,1287,3108,'The function of tropomyosin in skeletal muscles is','[{"text": "Sliding on actin filaments to shorten the muscle fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acting as \\"relaxing protein\\" at rest by covering up the sites where myosin binds to actin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Releasing $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{+2}$ after initiation of contraction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acting as ATPase essential for muscle contraction and relaxation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Tropomyosin is an $\\alpha$-helical rod having double strands and it is a fibrous molecule that will attach to F-actin. Tropomyosin masks the myosin binding sites of F-actin, keeping the muscle fibre relaxed. At a resting state, tropomyosin molecule will lie at the top of actin strands, such that contraction of the muscle does not take place.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10994,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Which one of the following options gives the correct categorization of three animals according to the type of nitrogenous waste they excrete?<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{{\\bf{Ammonotelic}}\\,\\,}&{{\\bf{Ureotelic}}\\,\\,\\,\\,}&{{\\bf{Uricotelic}}}\n\\end{array}$','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Land snail}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{Shark}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{King}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{crab}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Frog}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{Tadpole}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{Earthworm}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Sea}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{horse}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{Horse}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{Lamprey}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Rohu}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{Shark}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{Peacock}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Rohu, tadpole - Ammonotelic Shark, frog, earthworm, horse - Ureotelic Peacock, land snail - Uricotelic Lamprey - Ammonia and urea',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10995,'biology',9,27,50,'Ovules are not enclosed by the ovaries in','[{"text": "Bryophyta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In gymnosperms, ovules are not enclosed by any ovary wall and remain exposed, not developing into fruits.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10996,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Following diagram shows section of the human brain. The human brain can be divided into three major parts-','[{"text": "A - Midbrain, B - Hindbrain, C - Forebrain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Hindbrain, B - Forebrain, C - Midbrain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Midbrain, B - Forebrain, C - Hindbrain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Forebrain, B - Midbrain, C - Hindbrain", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Forebrain, B- Midbrain, C-Hindbrain',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/90_10996_question_1.png'),
(10997,'biology',89,1287,3108,'The diagram shows the length-tension relationship for a single sarcomere Why is the tension development maximal between points \\(\\mathrm{B}\\) and \\(\\mathrm{C}\\) ?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "The length of A-band decreases to minimum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The length of I-band increases to maximum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There is optimal overlap between the actin and myosin filaments", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The length of actin and myosin filaments decreases to minimum", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Contraction of a muscle fibre takes place by the sliding of the thin filaments over the thick filaments. Neither the thick filaments nor the thin filaments shorten. During contraction, I-bands get reduced while A-bands retain their length.',NULL,'Hard','Graph/Figure',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/89_10997_question_1.png'),
(10998,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Which of the following sets of animals produce the same substances as their chief excretory product?','[{"text": "Fish, pigeon and frog", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Camel, housefly and snake", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Frog, monkey and dog", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Amoeba</i>, ant and antelope", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Frog, monkey and dog, all are ureotelic animals. They excrete their wastes in the form of urea.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(10999,'biology',9,27,50,'Which of the following plants possess naked seeds?','[{"text": "<i>Cycas</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pinus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Gingko</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Gymnosperms possess naked seeds. Common examples are Cycas, Pinus, Gingko.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11000,'biology',89,1285,3106,'All the muscles in the body at a given time are never found in perfectly relaxed state. Although showing no outward signs of activity they are in a state of mild contraction which causes them to resist on being stretched. This activity of muscle is called','[{"text": "Conductibility", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tonicity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Twitch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tensility", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All the muscles in the body at a given time are never found in perfectly relaxed state. Although showing no outward signs of activity they are in a state of mild contraction which causes them to resist on being stretched. This activity of muscle is called tonicity.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11001,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Identify the labeled parts of human brain A-C in the given diagram?','[{"text": "A - Corpus callosum,<br>B - Cerebral aqueduct,<br>C - Cerebral hemisphere", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Cerebral aqueduct,<br>B - Cerebral hemisphere,<br>C - Corpus callosum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Cerebral hemisphere,<br>B - Corpus callosum,<br>C - Cerebral aqueduct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Corpus callosum,<br>B - Cerebral hemisphere,<br>C - Cerebral aqueduct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-Cerebral hemisphere, B- Corpus callosum, C-Cerebral aqueduct',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/90_11001_question_1.png'),
(11002,'biology',88,1157,2764,'Which of the following accessory excretory structure eliminates $\\mathrm{NaCl}$, lactic acid and urea?','[{"text": "Kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liver", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sebaceous gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sweat gland", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sweat glands are highly vascular and tubular glands that separate the waste products from the blood and excrete them in the form of sweat. Sweat excretes excess salt and water from the body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11004,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Which of the following options shows correct order of some stages of muscle contraction from the beginning to the end of the process?','[{"text": "Stimuli, Neurotransmitter secretion, cross bridges formation, Excitation of T-system, Sliding of actin filaments.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimuli, Excitation of T-system, Neurotransmitter secretion, cross bridges formation, Sliding of actin filaments, \'H\'- band diminishes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimuli, neurotransmitter secretion, Release of $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$, cross bridges formation, Excitation of T-system Sliding of actin filaments.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimuli, Neurotransmitter secretion, Excitation of T-system release of $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{+2}$ cross, bridges formation, Sliding of actin filaments, \' $\\\\mathrm{H}$ \' - band diminishes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The contraction of skeletal muscle includes biochemical and ultrastructural events. Ultrastructural events leads with stimuli excitation of T-system followed by cross bridge formation and the cross bridge breakage. Biochemical events explain that stimuli leads to neurotransmitter secretion, excitation of T-system and release of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11005,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Identify the labeled parts of forebrain A-C in the given diagram?','[{"text": "A - Cerebrum,B - Thalamus,C - Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Thalamus, B - Hypothalamus, C - Cerebrum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Hypothalamus, B - Thalamus, C - Cerebrum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Cerebrum, B - Hypothalamus, C - Thalamus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-Cerebrum, B- Thalamus, C-Hypothalamus',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/90_11005_question_1.png'),
(11006,'biology',9,27,50,'The tallest gymnosperm is','[{"text": "<em>Sequoia</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red wood tree", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Cycas</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sequoia (Red wood tree) is the tallest gymnosperm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11007,'biology',88,1150,2757,'Identify the set of animals which excrete the same substance as their chief nitrogenous waste.','[{"text": "Hydra, shark, rohu", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Frog, camel, locust", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lizard, parrot, silkworm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Catla, electric ray, cobra", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Reptiles (e.g., lizard), birds (e.g., parrot), insects (e.g., silkworm) and land snails are uricotelic.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11008,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Consider the following statements with blank<br>i. Globular head of meromyosin is an active ATPase enzyme and has binding sites for A and active sites for B<br>ii. This central part of thick filament not overlapped by thin filaments is called C<br>iii. Repeated activation of the muscles can lead to the accumulation of $\\mathrm{D}$ due to anaerobic breakdown of glycogen in them causing fatigue<br>Select the correct option correctly filling the concerned blanks','[{"text": "D-pyruvic acid, A- Troponin, C- A band B- myosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- ATP, B-actin, C- $\\\\mathrm{H}$ zone, D- lactic acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "D- glucose, C- A band, B- Actin, A- ATP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D- lactic acid, C-I band, A- ATP, B- Actin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'(i) Globular head of meromyosin is an active ATPase enzyme and has binding sites for ATP and active sites for actin.<br>(ii) The central part of thick filament not overlapped by thin filaments is called $\\mathrm{H}$ zone.<br>(iii) Repeated activation of the muscles can lead to the accumulation of lactic acid due to anaerobic breakdown of glycogen in them causing fatigue',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11009,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Following is a labeled diagram of human brain. Identify $(\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{C})$ the parts of hind brain-','[{"text": "A - Pons,B- Medulla ,C - Cerebellum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Pons, B-Cerebellum, C - Medulla", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Cerebellum, B - Pons, C - Medulla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Medulla, B-Cerebellum, C - Pons", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A- Pons , B- Cerebellum , C-Medulla',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/90_11009_question_1.png'),
(11010,'biology',9,27,50,'What type of root system is present in gymnosperms?','[{"text": "Tap root system", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fibrous root system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rhizoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rhizines", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The roots in gymnosperms are generally tap roots.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11011,'biology',88,1151,2758,'The projections of renal pelvis are called','[{"text": "hilus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "calyces", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "medullary pyramids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "renal columns", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Hilus leads to funnel shaped cavity called renal pelvis with projections called calyces.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11013,'biology',90,1339,3222,'In reflex action the entire process of response is to a ____.','[{"text": "CNS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spinal cord", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peripheral Nervous Stimulation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Voluntary response", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The entire process of response to a peripheral nervous stimulation, that occurs involuntarily, i.e., without conscious effort or thought and requires the involvment of a part of the central nervous system is called a reflex action.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11014,'biology',9,27,50,'Identify the gymnosperm having association\nwith ${N_2}$  fixing bacteria','[{"text": "<i>Pinus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Cycas</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Sequoia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Cedrus</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cycas bears small specialised roots called coralloid roots that are associated with N2 - fixing cyanobacteria.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11105,'biology',9,27,50,'In gymnosperms, the multicellular female gametophyte is retained within','[{"text": "Archegonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Female gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Megasporangium", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The multicellular female gametophyte is retained within megasporangium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11015,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Which one of the following is not a part of a renal pyramid?','[{"text": "Loops of Henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasa recta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Convoluted tubules", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Collecting ducts", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Convoluted tubules is not a part of renal pyramid but a portion of the nephron in the kidney that functions in concentrating urine and in maintaining salt, water, and sugar balance.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11016,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Study the following statements and select the correct option<br>I. The accumulation of lactic acid in the muscle causes fatigue<br>II. The phosphogen in the vertebrate muscle is arginine phosphate<br>III. Cori\'s cycle occurs in the muscle<br>IV. ATP is resynthesised in the muscle by the phosphorylation of ADP by a phosphogen','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Accumulation of lactic acid causes muscle fatigue.Phosphagen in vertebrate muscles is phosphoacreatine. Cori\'s cycle occurs in muscle and liver. During the process of glycolysis, lactic acid is produced in muscles where some of it is oxidized into water and carbon dioxide remaining is converted into glycogen.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11017,'biology',90,1339,3222,'The process of response to a peripheral nervous stimulation that occurs involuntarily is called','[{"text": "Resting membrane potential", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Action potential", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reflex action", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Activation energy", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The entire process of response to a peripheral nervous stimulation, that occurs involuntarily, i.e. without conscious efforts or thought and requires involvement of a part of the central nervous system is called a reflex action.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11018,'biology',9,27,50,'Which type of roots are present in <i>Cycas</i> which is in association with ${N_2}$fixing bacteria?','[{"text": "Coralloid roots", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tap root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fibrous root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mycorrhizae", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Small specialised roots called coralloid roots are associated with N2 - fixing cyanobacteria.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11019,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which of the following statements is not true about hormonal regulation of kidney function?','[{"text": "Kidneys secrete renin when blood pressure is low", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "High blood pressure causes kidneys to secrete aldosterone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Heart secretes ANP when blood volume increases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Excess intake of water reduces ADH secretion", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Aldosterone secreted by the adrenal cortex leads to an increase in blood pressure.A fall in blood pressure activates reninangiotensin-aldosterone pathway.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11021,'biology',90,1339,3222,'Identify the correct statement about the reflex action','[{"text": "Occurs involuntarily", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Requires the involvement a part of CNS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Requires peripheral stimulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The entire process of response to a peripheral nervous stimulation, that occurs involuntarily, i.e., without conscious effort or thought and requires the involvment of a part of the central nervous system is called a reflex action.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11022,'biology',9,27,50,'Which of the following gymnosperms, mycorrhizal association is found','[{"text": "<i>Cycas</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pinus</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Cedrus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Roots in some genera have fungal association in the form of mycorrhiza (Pinus)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11023,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Which of the following statement is not correct with respect to human kidney?','[{"text": "The peripheral region is called cortex and central region is medulla.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Malpighian capsules are present in the cortex region.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood enters glomerulus through efferent arterioles.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The concave part of kidney is called hilus.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Blood enters glomerulus through afferent arterioles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11025,'biology',9,27,50,'Gymnosperms','[{"text": "Have naked seeds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Have tap roots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leaves are well-adapted to withstand\\nextremes of temperature, humidity and\\nwind.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In gymnosperms, the seeds that develop post-fertilisation, are not covered, i.e., are naked. The roots are generally tap roots. The leaves are well-adapted to withstand extremes of temperature, humidity and wind.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11026,'biology',90,1339,3222,'The dorsal nerve root ganglion is a part of','[{"text": "Spinal cord", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Brain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cerebellum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cerebrum", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Dorsal nerve root into the CNS (at the level of spinal cord).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11027,'biology',88,1153,2760,'Select the correct option with regard to the function of the distal convoluted tubule of the nephron.','[{"text": "Reabsorption of $\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretion of $\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reabsorption of $\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reabsorption of $\\\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Reabsorption of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$, water, and $\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}{ }^{-}$ as well as secretion of $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$and $\\mathrm{H}^{+}$takes place in the DCT.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11029,'biology',9,27,50,'Which of the following are incorrect for gymnosperms?<br>I. Have tap root system.<br>II. The leaves in gymnosperms can with stand extreme temperature, humidity and wind.<br>III.<em>Cycas </em>has symbiotic association with ${N_2}$ fixing cyanobacteria.<br>IV. They include medium or tall sized trees and shrubs.','[{"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'No incorrect statements.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11030,'biology',90,1339,3222,'Reflex action is controlled by','[{"text": "PNS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "CNS", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Reflex pathway involves both ANS and CNS. In case of CNS, it may be spinal cord(spinal reflexes; more common) and brain (cerebral reflexes; less common).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11031,'biology',88,1154,2761,'The part of the nephron impermeable to water is.','[{"text": "Proximal tubule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Distal tubule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ascending limb of Henle\'s loop", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Collecting duct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The ascending limb of Henle\'s loop is impermeable to water but allows transport of electrolytes like sodium. So, the filtrate gets diluted.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11033,'biology',88,1154,2761,'If Henle\'s loop were absent from mammalian nephron which of the following event is to be expected?','[{"text": "There will be no urine formation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There will be hardly any change in the quality and quantity of urine formed.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The urine will be more concentrated.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The urine will be more dilute.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Henle\'s loop is a U-shaped tube that consists of a descending limb and ascending limb. Its primary role is to concentrate the salt in the interstitium, the tissue surrounding the loop. In the absence of Henle\'s loop, the urine will be more dilute.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11034,'biology',90,1339,3222,'The reflex pathway comprises','[{"text": "One afferent neuron only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One efferent neuron only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One afferent and one efferent neuron", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Motor neurons only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The reflex pathway comprises at least one afferent neuron, i.e. receptor and one efferent (effector or excitor) neuron appropriately arranged in a series.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11036,'biology',9,27,50,'<i>Cycas</i>- a gymnosperm','[{"text": "The stems are branched.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The palmately compound leaves persist for years.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Have symbiotic association with ${N_2}$ fixing fungi.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are wrong.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In Cycas the pinnate leaves persist for a few years. The stems are unbranched. Small specialised roots called coralloid roots are associated with N2 - fixing cyanobacteria.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11037,'biology',88,1153,2760,'From the medullary interstitium, urea diffuses into','[{"text": "Medullary collecting ducts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The thick segment of ascending limb of loop of Henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The thin segment of ascending limb of loop of Henle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ascending limb of vasa recta", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Small amounts of urea enter the thin segment of the ascending limb of Henle\'s loop which is transported back to the interstitium by the collecting tubule.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11205,'biology',91,1395,3337,'Identify the gland which acts as both exocrine and endocrine gland in given diagram?','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pancreas is an exocrine and endocrine gland, that represents label 2.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/91_11205_question_1.png'),
(11038,'biology',90,1339,3222,'In reflex action, the reflex arc is formed by','[{"text": "Muscle, Effector, brain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brain, spinal cord, Effector", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Receptor, spinal cord, Effector", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Receptor, Effector, spinal cord", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct pathway of reflex arc is<br>Sensory receptor $\\rightarrow$ Afferent neuron $\\rightarrow$ Dorsal nerve root $\\rightarrow$ CNS $\\rightarrow$ Effector neuron $\\rightarrow$ Effector organs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11040,'biology',9,27,50,'Which of the following shows branched stem?','[{"text": "<i>Pinus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Cedrus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cycas", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pinus and Cedrus show branched stems.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11041,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Which of the following statements is not true about ADH?','[{"text": "It increases the permeability of the collecting ducts to water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Its secretion is regulated by osmoreceptors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alcohol inhibits its secretion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It decreases blood pressure by dilating blood vessels", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{ADH}$ (vasopressin) increases blood pressure by constricting blood vessels.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11042,'biology',90,1339,3222,'Which of the following are due to reflex action?','[{"text": "Vomiting", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sneezing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coughing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are reflex actions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11044,'biology',9,27,50,'Which of the following statements are correct for conifers?','[{"text": "Needle like leaves to reduce surface area.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thick cuticle on leaves.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sunken stomata to reduce water loss.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In conifers, the needle-like leaves reduce the surface area. Their thick cuticle and sunken stomata also help to reduce water loss.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11045,'biology',88,1156,2763,'Human urine is usually acidic because','[{"text": "Potassium and sodium exchange generates acidity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrogen ions are actively secreted into the filtrate.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The sodium transporter exchanges one hydrogen ion for each sodium ion, in peritubular capillaries.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Excreted plasma proteins are acidic.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Human urine is acidic due to the secretion of hydrogen ions into the tubule.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11047,'biology',90,1339,3222,'Which of the following are example of reflexes?','[{"text": "Knee-jerk reflex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corneal reflex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pupillary reflex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are reflex actions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11048,'biology',9,27,50,'The gymnosperms are','[{"text": "Heterosporous- they produce haploid microspores and megaspores.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Heterosporous- they produce diploid microspores and megaspores.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homo sporous- they produce same haploid microspores and megaspores.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homo sporous- they produce same diploid microspores and megaspores.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The gymnosperms are heterosporous plants as they produce haploid microspores and megaspores.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11049,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Atrial natriuretic factor (ANF) is released in response to the increase in blood volume and blood pressure. Which of the followings is not the function of ANF?','[{"text": "It stimulates aldosterone secretion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It causes vasodilation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It decreases blood pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It acts as a counter check on reninangiotensin-aldosterone system", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'ANF is secreted by heart under the influence of too much blood in the circulatory system. ANF stimulates the loss of sodium in urine while aldosterone absorbs sodium from glomerular filtrate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11051,'biology',9,27,50,'In gymnosperms, two kinds of spores are produced within sporangia that are borne on sporophylls which______','[{"text": "Are arranged spirally along an axis to form compact strobili or cones only.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Are arranged spirally along an axis to form lax strobili or cones only.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Are arranged in a linear manner along an axis to form lax or compact strobili or cones.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Are arranged spirally along an axis to form lax or compact strobili or cones.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The two kinds of heterospores are produced within sporangia that are borne on sporophylls which are arranged spirally along an axis to form lax or compact strobili or cones.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11052,'biology',90,1339,3222,'White matter is____ in brain and____ in spinal cord in humans','[{"text": "Outside, inside", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inside, Outside", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inside, Inside", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Outside, Outside", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'White matter is inside in the brain and in spinal cord it is outside in humans.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11053,'biology',88,1151,2758,'Which of the following has the highest number of microvilli?','[{"text": "Proximal convoluted tubule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Distal convoluted tubule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Loop of Henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Collecting duct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The apical surface of cuboidal epithelial cells bears numerous microvilli forming a brush border. The microvilli increase the surface area for reabsorption and secretion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11055,'biology',9,27,50,'In gymnosperms, the male strobili consists of','[{"text": "Megasporophylls and microsporangia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microsporophylls and megasporangia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microsporophylls and microsporangia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The strobili bearing microsporophylls and microsporangia are called microsporangiate or male strobili.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11056,'biology',90,1339,3222,'Which of the following is not a reflex action?','[{"text": "Salivation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sweating", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Withdrawal of hand when pinched by needle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sweating is not a reflex action. It is the action under the control of brain to lower down body temperature,i.e. homeostasis.<br>Salivation and withdrawl of hand when pinched by the needle are reflex actions not controlled by brain.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11057,'biology',88,1155,2762,'Juxta-glomerular apparatus is formed by cellular modification in the.','[{"text": "Afferent arteriole and DCT", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Efferent arteriole and PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Afferent arteriole and PCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Efferent arteriole and DCT", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Juxta-glomerular apparatus is a microscopic structure located between the vascular pole of the renal corpuscle and the returning distal convoluted tubule of the same nephron. It is formed by cellular modification in the afferent arteriole and DCT.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11059,'biology',9,27,50,'In gymnosperms, the cones bearing microsporophylls are known as','[{"text": "Male strobili", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microsporangiate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Female strobili", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The strobili bearing microsporophylls and microsporangia are called microsporangiate or male strobili.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11060,'biology',90,1339,3222,'Interneuron is present in the','[{"text": "Gray matter of the spinal cord", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "White matter of the spinal cord", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dorsal region of the spinal cord", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ventral region of the spinal cord", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Interneuron is present in the gray matter of the spinal cord.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11220,'biology',91,1396,3338,'Hypothalamus directly regulates the ____ endocrine gland.','[{"text": "Hypophysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pineal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pituitary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Hypothalamus regulate the synthesis and secretion of pituitary hormones.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11061,'biology',88,1156,2763,'Micturition reflex is triggered by','[{"text": "Chemoreceptors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osmoreceptors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thermoreceptors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stretch receptors", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Stretching of the urinary bladder stimulates the stretch receptors in the walls of the bladder. The impulses are carried to the CNS and trigger the micturition reflex.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11062,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Which of the following actions is most likely to terminate an ongoing contraction of a skeletal muscle fibre?','[{"text": "Release of neurotransmitter at the neuromuscular junction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase in $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ concentration in sarcoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Influx of $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ into the axon terminal at the neuromuscular junction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Removal of $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ from sarcoplasm", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'When $\\mathrm{Ca}^{++}$ions removed from sarcoplasm, active sites on actin filaments are masked. This causes the return of \' $Z$ \' lines back to their original position (muscle relaxation).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11063,'biology',9,27,50,'In gymnosperms, the microspores develop into\na male gametophyte generation, which','[{"text": "Is highly reduced and confined to only a\\nlimited number of cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Is highly developed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is highly developed and confined to only a limited number of cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is highly reduced and has a huge number\\nof cells", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The male gametophytic generation is highly reduced and is confined to only a limited number of cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11064,'biology',90,1339,3222,'Given below are different components of reflex are.i. Effector neuronii. Dorsal nerve rootiii. CNSiv. Afferent neuronv. Sensory receptor vi. Effector organ<br>Arrange these in correct order of action potential that follows a sensory receptor stimulation.','[{"text": "v, iv, iii, ii, i, vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "v,iv, ii, iii , i, vi", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "v, iii, iv, i, ii, vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "v, ii , iv, iii ,i , vi", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct pathway of reflex arc is Sensory receptor $\\rightarrow$ Afferent neuron $\\rightarrow$ Dorsal nerve root $\\rightarrow$ CNS $\\rightarrow$ Effector neuron $\\rightarrow$ Effector organs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11065,'biology',88,1158,2765,'Match the items in column I with those in column II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Nephritis<br>B. Uremia<br>C. Oxalate crystals<br>D. Ketone bodies</div><div class="column-right">P. Diabetes\nmellitus<br>Q. Renal calculi<br>R. Dialysis<br>S. Glomerulus</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R, B - S, C - Q, D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - S, B - R, C - Q, D - P}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q, B - P, C - S, D - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - P, B - Q, C - R, D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Glomerulonephritis – Inflammation of glomeruli<br>\nUremia – Dialysis<br>\nOxalate crystals – Renal calculi<br>\nKetone bodies – Diabetes mellitus',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11066,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Which of the following statements about the molecular arrangement of actin and myosin in myofibrils is false?<br>I. Each actin (thin filament) is made of $2 \\mathrm{~F}$ (filamentous) actins<br>II. F-actin is the polymer of $\\mathrm{G}$ (globular) actin.<br>III. $2 \\mathrm{~F}$-actins are twisted into a helix.<br>IV. Two strands of tropomyosin (protein) lie in the grooves of F-actin.<br>V. Troponin molecules (complex proteins) are distributed at regular intervals on the tropomyosin<br>VI. Troponin forms the head of the myosin molecule<br>VII. The myosin is a polymerised protein','[{"text": "I, III, VII", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only VII", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "VI only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'HMM forms the head of the myosin molecule.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11067,'biology',9,27,50,'In gymnosperms, the reduced male gametophyte is called','[{"text": "Male gamete", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollen grain", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Microsporangia", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The male gametophytic generation is highly reduced and is confined to only a limited number of cells. This reduced gametophyte is called a pollen grain.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11068,'biology',90,1339,3222,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Stimulus<br>B. Receptor<br>C. Effector<br>D. Reflex action</div><div class="column-right">P. Muscle spindle<br>Q. Motor end plate<br>R. Extremely hot, cold objects<br>S. Knee jerk reflex</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-R, B-P, C-Q, D-S.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11069,'biology',88,1151,2758,'The given figure shows the longitudinal section of kidney with few structures labelled as I, II, III & IV identify renal vein in the given figure.','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The label II represents renal vein while label I represent renal artery, label III represents renal pelvisand label IV represents renal column.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/88_11069_question_1.png'),
(11070,'biology',89,1287,3108,'How does the troponin-tropomysin complex affect cross-bridge cycling?','[{"text": "The troponin-tropomyosin complex regenerates ATP for the myosin ATPase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "When $\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}\\\\right]$ is low, the troponintropomyosin complex blocks actin\'s binding site for myosin. When $\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}\\\\right]$ is high, the complex rolls out of the way, allowing myosin to bind to actin and initiate the cross-bridge cycle.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The troponin-tropomysin complex regulates calcium release from the terminal cisternae.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The troponin-tropomyosin complex binds to the myosin head, facilitating contact with the actin filaments", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When $\\left[\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}\\right]$ is low, the troponintropomyosin complex blocks actin\'s binding site for myosin. When $\\left[\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}\\right]$ is high, the complex rolls out of the way, allowing myosin to bind to actin and initiate the cross-bridge cycle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
