(11075,'biology',9,27,50,'In gymnosperms, the pollen chamber\nrepresents','[{"text": "A cell in the pollen grain in which the\\nsperms are formed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A cavity in the ovule in which pollen grains are stored after pollination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "An opening in the megagametophyte through which the pollen tube approches the egg", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The microsporangium in which pollen\\ngrains develop", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In gymnosperms, the pollen chamber is acavity in the ovule in which pollen grains are stored after pollination. Within this chamber, the generative cell divides to form two male gametes and the pollen cell starts elongating to\nform pollen tube.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
