(11077,'biology',89,1287,3108,'When muscle get fatigue, there is','[{"text": "Much ATP, more glycogen but much lactic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Little ATP and glycogen but much lactic acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "More ATP, no glycogen and no lactic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Little ATP, more glycogen and little lactic acid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Muscle fatigue is a condition where there is a reduction in force of contraction of muscle after a prolonged stimulation. Muscle fatigue is caused due to accumulation of lactic acid. A muscle that has undergone fatigue needs extra oxygen to remove excess lactic acid.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11078,'biology',88,1152,2759,'Select the correct match of a term with its description.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Macula densa - Modified smooth muscle fibres of afferent arteriole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glomerulus - A tuft of capillaries formed by the afferent arteriole", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "JG cells - Densely packed cells in the wall of the DCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasa recta-Blood capillaries around the PCT and DCT", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Glomerulus - A tuft of capillaries formed by the afferent arteriole<br>Macula densa - Densely packed cells in the wall of the DCT<br>JG cells $\\quad-\\quad$ Modified smooth muscle fibres of afferent arteriole<br>Vasa recta - Extensions of the efferent arteriole of a juxtamedullary nephron that run along side the loop of Henle of the nephron',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11079,'biology',9,27,50,'Which one is not the feature of <em>Cycas</em>?','[{"text": "Coralloid roots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pinnate leaves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The male or female may be borne on the different trees", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucellus is absent", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All gymnosperms have nucellus. The megaspore mother cell is differentiated from one of the cells of the nucellus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11080,'biology',90,1340,3223,'Select the correct answer<br>i. The sensory organs detect all types of changes in the environment and send appropriate signals to the CNS.<br>ii. Signals are then sent to different parts/ centres of the brain.','[{"text": "i is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The sensory organs detect all types of changes in the environment and send appropriate signals to the CNS, where all the inputs are processed and a analysed. Signals are then sent to different parts/centres of the brain. This is how you sense changes in the environment.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11081,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Read the following statement with two blanks (A and B) $\\underline {\\,{\\rm{A}}\\,} $ muscle fibers are adapted for activities such a marathon running. They are $\\underline {\\,{\\rm{B}}\\,} $. The one correct option for the two blanks is:<br>&emsp;$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{A}}}\n\\end{array}}&{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{B}}}\n\\end{array}}\n\\end{array}$','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{White}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Slow - twitch}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\\\\\\\\\n{}&{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{fatigue - resistant}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}$<br><br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Red}}\\\\,\\\\,}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Slow - twitch}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\\\\\\\\\n{}&{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{fatigue - resistant}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}$<br><br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{White}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Fast - twitch}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\\\\\\\\\n{}&{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{fatigue - prone}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}$<br><br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Red}}\\\\,\\\\,}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Fast - twitch}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\\\\\\\\\n{}&{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{fatigue - resistant}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Red muscle fibres contain high myoglobin content, and plenty of mitochondria. They can utilise the large amount of oxygen stored in them for ATP production. Because they rely on aerobic respiration, they are fatigue-resistant (no lactic acid production). They have a slow speed of contraction (slow-twitch).<br>They are capable of prolonged, sustained contractions for many hours. These fibres are adapted for maintaining posture and for aerobic, endurance-type activities like marathon running.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11082,'biology',88,1158,2765,'The term Uremia refers to','[{"text": "Accumulation of urea in blood.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Presence of glucose in the urine.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Accumulation of uric acid in blood.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Accumulation of uric acid in kidneys.<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Malfunctioning of Kidneys can lead to accumulation of urea in blood. This condition is called uremia. It is highly harmful and may lead to kidney failure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
