(11095,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Read the following events occurred during muscle contraction, arrange them in correct sequence and select the correct option given below<br>i. Hydrolysis of ATP and formation of cross bridge<br>ii. During power stroke, thin filaments moves towards the centre of A band<br>iii. Release of Acetylcholine<br>iv. Generation of action potential in sarcolemma<br>v. Release of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{+2}$ from sarcoplasmic reticulum, increases sarcoplasmic $\\mathrm{Ca}^{+2}$ level<br>vi. Binding of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{+2}$ with troponin and masking activities removed','[{"text": "ii $-\\\\mathrm{i}-\\\\mathrm{iii}-\\\\mathrm{iv}-\\\\mathrm{v}-\\\\mathrm{vi}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii $-\\\\mathrm{iv}-\\\\mathrm{v}-\\\\mathrm{vi}-\\\\mathrm{ii}-\\\\mathrm{i}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii $-\\\\mathrm{iv}-\\\\mathrm{v}-\\\\mathrm{vi}-\\\\mathrm{i}-\\\\mathrm{ii}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iii $-\\\\mathrm{iv}-\\\\mathrm{v}-\\\\mathrm{i}-\\\\mathrm{ii}-\\\\mathrm{vi}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct order of events occurred during muscle contraction is as follow:<br>iii - Release of Acetylcholine<br>iv - Generation of action potential in<br>sarcolemma<br>$\\mathrm{v}$ - Release of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{+2}$ from sarcoplasmic<br>reticulum, increases sarcoplasmic $\\mathrm{Ca}^{+2}$ level<br>vi-Binding of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{+2}$ with troponin and masking activities removed<br>$\\mathrm{i}$ - Hydrolysis of ATP and formation of cross<br>bridge<br>ii - During power stroke, thin filaments moves towards the centre of A band',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
