(11354,'biology',89,1287,3108,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Acetylcholine released in the myoneural junction communicates neuron with a myocyte.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Acetylcholine diffuses in the nerve muscle gap binds to the receptor on the sarcolemma which gets depolarized.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Biochemical event that occurs during muscle contraction involves action of acetylcholine. The nerve impulse stimulates a muscle fibre at a neuromuscular junction to produce acetylcholine which will bring about release of calcium ions into interior of muscle fibre.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11355,'biology',9,29,52,'Meiosis can take place in','[{"text": "Only haploid species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only diploid species", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both in haploid as well as diploid species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only triploid species", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Meiosis or reduction division can take place only in diploid or species with an even ploidy number. This is because haploid ploidy cannot be reduced any further. Also, odd number of ploidy cannot be equally divided.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
