(11382,'biology',89,1285,3106,'The H-Zone in the skeletal muscle fibre is due to','[{"text": "The central gap between actin filaments extending through myosin filaments in the A-band", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Extension of myosin filaments in the central portion of the A-band.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The absence of myofibrils in the central portion of A-band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The central gap between myosin filaments in the A-band.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'As per sliding filament theory, during muscle contraction, actin and myosin filaments slide over each other by formation of cross bridges and reduce length of a sarcomere. As the muscle contracts, Z-lines come closer, width of \'I\' band and \' H \'band decreases. But there is no change in length of \' A \' band.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
