(11401,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Stimulation of a muscle fibre by a motor neuron occurs at','[{"text": "The neuromuscular junction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Transverse tubules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The myofibril", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The sacroplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A motor neuron is a neuron that transmits stimulus to a muscle tissue. A muscle fibre along with the motor neuron that innervates muscle fibre forms a motor unit. Neuromuscular junction is formed by the axon terminals, motor end plate. Motor end plate is formed by nerve endings that lie beneath portion of sarcolemma.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
