(11408,'biology',9,29,52,'When both the phases of life cycle are multicellular, i.e., haploid and diploid phases','[{"text": "Life cycles are called haplodiplontic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "However, they differ in their dominant\\nphases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are seen in pteridophytes and\\nbryophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'An intermediate condition, where both gametophyte(n) and sporophyte (2n) are multicellular is known as Haplo-diplontic life cycle. It is exhibited by pteridophytes and bryophytes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
