(11450,'biology',91,1399,3341,'A flap of connective tissue which connects three lobes of thyroid is known as','[{"text": "Cristae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ampulla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isthmus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Thin flap of connective tissue which connects two lobes of thyroid is known as Isthmus',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11451,'biology',9,29,52,'Identify the following life cycle pattern_<br>','[{"text": "Haplontic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diplontic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Haplo-diplontic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The life cycle pattern represented in the figure is diplontic.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_11451_question_1.png'),
(11453,'biology',91,1399,3341,'The thyroid gland is composed of','[{"text": "Follicles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stromal tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trachea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The thyroid gland is composed of follicles and stromal tissue. Thyroid gland is the largest endocrine gland composed of two lobes connected by a isthmus. It has some 3 million follicles, arranged in lobules (40 follicles in each lobule) and embedded in stromal tissue rich in blood capillaries. Each thyroid follicle is composed of follicular cells, enclosing a cavity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11455,'biology',9,29,52,'Select the number of species which follow life cycle pattern depicted by given diagram____<br><em>Selaginella, Salvia, Salvinia, Ectocarpus, Funaria, Fucus, Polysiphonia, Kelps, </em>Coconut','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The given diagram represents diplontic life cycle. It is exhibited by gymnosperms, angiosperms and some algae. Some examples are - <em>Salvinia</em>, Coconut and <em>Fucus</em>. Total - 3',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_11455_question_1.png'),
(11457,'biology',91,1399,3341,'By which part of thyroid gland, $T_{3}$ and $T_{4}$ hormones are synthesised?','[{"text": "Follicles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stromal tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isthmus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The follicle cells of thyroid gland synthesise two hormones, tetraiodothyronine or thyroxine $\\left(\\mathrm{T}_{4}\\right)$ and tri-iodothyronine $\\left(\\mathrm{T}_{3}\\right)$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11459,'biology',9,29,52,'In the species following the life cycle pattern shown by the following diagram, meiosis occurs in _<br>','[{"text": "Gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spore", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Given figure represents a haplontic life cycle. Here, zygote is the unicelled sporophyte. It undergoes meiosis to produce 4 haploid spores.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_11459_question_1.png'),
(11460,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Which of the following statements are correct regarding skeletal muscle?<br>I. Muscle bundles are held together by collagenous connective tissue layer called fascicle.<br>II. Sarcoplasmic reticulum of muscle fibre is a store house of calcium ions.<br>III. Striated appearance of skeletal muscle fibre is due to distribution pattern of actin and myosin proteins.<br>IV. M line is considered as functional unit of contraction called sarcomere.<br>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "I, II and III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III and IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statements II and III are only correct\nstatements while I and IV are incorrect\nstatements.<br>Muscle bundles are held together by\ncollagenous connective tissue layer called\nfascia. Muscle bundles are called fascicles.\nThe portion of the myofibril between two\nsuccessive ‘Z’ lines is considered as functional\nunit of contraction called sarcomere.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11461,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Hypothyroidism and goitre is caused due to the deficiency of','[{"text": "Iodine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Calcium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroidinum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Iron", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hypothyroidism occurs due to the deficiency of iodine. In this enlargement of thyroid gland occurs, as a consequence of distress development by the body to tope in whatever iodine is available in the diet and produce more thyroxine. Iodine is essential for thyroxine hormone production.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11463,'biology',9,29,52,'The following life cycle pattern is followed by_<br>','[{"text": "Bryophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Some algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The given figure shows a haplo-diplontic life cycle. It is exhibited by bryophytes, pteridophytes and some algae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_11463_question_1.png'),
(11464,'biology',89,1285,3106,'The diagram given below represents the histology of a striped muscle. Label the parts $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{C}, \\mathrm{D}, \\mathrm{E}$ and $\\mathrm{F}$','[{"text": "A - Sarcoplasm, B - Nucleus, C - Sarcolemma, D - Myofibril, E - Dark band , F - Light band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Sarcoplasm, B - Light band, C - Myofibril, D - Sacrolemma, E - Nucleus, F - Dark Band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Light Band, B - Sarcoplasm, C - Myofibril, D - Sacrolemma, E - Nucleus, F - Dark band", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Sacrolemma, B - Nucleus, C - Dark Band, D - Light Band, E - Sacroplasm, F - Myofibril", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/biology/89_11464_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2011,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/89_11464_question_1.png'),
(11465,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Enlargement of thyroid gland is called','[{"text": "Hypothyroidism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hyperthyroidism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Goitre", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Enlargement of the thyroid gland, commonly called goitre',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11467,'biology',9,29,52,'The species which follow following life cycle pattern have_<br>','[{"text": "Dominant gametophytic phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dominant sporophytic phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Data is insufficient.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Given diagram represents a haplo-diplontic life cycle. We cannot determine which out of the two – gametophyte/sporophyte is the main plant body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_11467_question_1.png'),
(11777,'biology',91,1404,3346,'The male accessory sex organs are','[{"text": "Epididymis, Vas deferens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Urethra", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seminal vesicle, Prostate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The male accessory sex organs like epididymis, vas deferens, seminal vesicles, prostate gland, urethra etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11468,'biology',89,1286,3107,'The globular head of myosin contains','[{"text": "Calcium ions in large quantities", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Troponin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ATPase enzyme", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ATP", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The two projections of each myosin molecule (golf club heads) are called meromyosin heads that have a short arm (also known as heavy meromyosin or HMM). Each head is an active ATPase enzyme and contains actin active sites and ATP binding sites',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11469,'biology',91,1399,3341,'The features of cretinism includes','[{"text": "Stunted growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mental retardation and low IQ", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abnormal skin and deaf mutism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of them are correct. Hypothyroidism during pregnancy causes defective development and maturation of the growing baby leading to stunted growth (cretinism), mental retardation, low intelligence quotient, abnormal skin, deaf-mutism',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11470,'biology',9,29,52,'The life cycle of the species given below is_','[{"text": "Haplontic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haplo-diplontic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diplontic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Diplo-haplontic", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The diagram represents the brown algae, Fucus. It exhibits a diplontic life cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_11470_question_1.png'),
(11472,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Sacromere is the functional unit of contraction in a muscle fibre. Identify the portion of mofibril that constitute a scaromere','[{"text": "The portion of myofibril between two successive \' Z \' line", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The portion of myofibril between two successive \' I \' band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The portion of myofibril between two successive \' A \' band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The portion of myofibril between two successive \' M \' line", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Narrow, plate - shaped regions of dense protein material called Z line (or Krause\'s membrane) separate one sarcomere from the next. Thus, a sacromere extends from one Z line to the next $\\mathrm{Z}$ line',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11473,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Hypothyroidism during pregnancy causes defective development and maturation of growing baby leading to','[{"text": "Addison\'s disease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cretinism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pituitary dwarf", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tetany", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Hypothyroidism during pregnancy causes defective development and maturation of the growing baby leading to stunted growth (cretinism), mental retardation, low intelligence quotient, abnormal skin, deafmutism',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11474,'biology',9,23,40,'Identify the incorrect statement for artificial system of classification.','[{"text": "Artificial system was based mainly on vegetative characters or on androecium.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The artificial system did not give equal weightage to the vegetative and sexual characteristics", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It was proposed by Linnaeus.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Artificial system separated closely related species.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Artificial system of classification was one of the earliest systems of classification. It was proposed by Linnaeus. They were based mainly on vegetative characters or on the androecium structure. Such systems were artificial; they separated the closely related species since they were based on a few characteristics. Also, the artificial systems gave equal weightage to vegetative and sexual characteristics which was not acceptable',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11477,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Thyroid gland secretes','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{T}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{T}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "TCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The thyroid follicular cells synthesise two hormones, tetraiodothyronine or thyroxine ${\\text{(}}{{\\text{T}}_{\\text{4}}}{\\text{) }}$  and triiodothyronine ${\\text{(}}{{\\text{T}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{) }}$ and thyrocalcitonin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11478,'biology',9,24,42,'Read carefully the given statements about algae and identify the correct option.','[{"text": "Vegetative reproduction is absent.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mainly aquatic, and exclusively marine.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The plant body is complex and thread like.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Volvox is the colonial form of algae.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Algae are aquatic plants (both marine and freshwater). The plant body is simple and thalloid. Vegetative reproduction is carried out by fragmentation. One of the green algae, Volvox exists in colonial form.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11480,'biology',89,1287,3108,'During the contraction of a sarcomere,','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Z}$ lines are pulled towards the $\\\\mathrm{A}$ band", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thick filaments are pulled into the $\\\\mathrm{I}$ band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{M}$ lines are pulled towards the edges of $\\\\mathrm{A}$ band", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calcium ions are pumped into the sarcoplasmic cisternae", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During muscle contraction, crossbridges pull the attached actin filaments towards the centre of $\\mathrm{A}$ band. The $\\mathrm{Z}$ lines attached to these actins are also pulled inwards thereby causing a shortening of the sarcomere.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11481,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Thyroid hormone controls the metabolism of','[{"text": "Carbohydrates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Thyroid hormones control the metabolism of carbohydrates, proteins and fats.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11482,'biology',9,24,43,'Which of the statements given below are incorrect about green algae?','[{"text": "Algae store food in the form of mannitol in a specialised structure called pyrenoids located in chloroplast.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vegetative reproduction occurs through budding.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Given algae are green due to the presence of chlorophyll-a and b pigments localised in mitochondria.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Algae store food in the form of starch and oil in a specialised structure called pyrenoids located in chloroplast. Pigments are localized in chloroplasts of algae. Algae vegetatively reproduce by fragmentation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11483,'biology',89,1287,3108,'A motor unit consists of','[{"text": "All the muscle fibres in a fascicle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A motor neuron plus all the muscle fibres it stimulates", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All the motor neurons innervating a muscle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A motor end plate and the axon terminal that synapses with it", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A motor unit consists of a somatic motor neuron plus all the skeletal muscle fibers it stimulates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11485,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Removal of thyroid in early years of growth will cause','[{"text": "Iodine deficiency goitre", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cretinism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Exophthalmic goitre", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cretinism is caused by the deficiency of thyroid hormone in infants therefore, congential removal of thyroid will cause cretinism. It will also cause dwarfism and mental retardation slow body growth and reduced metabolic rate of body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11486,'biology',9,24,45,'Consider the following with respect to red algae and identify the incorrect statements.<br>I. r. phycoerythrin is the predominant pigment.<br>II. Food is stored in the form of Floridean starch, amylopectin and glycogen.<br>III. Cell wall has polysulphate esters.<br>IV. Motile cells have two unequal flagella on the lateral side.','[{"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Red algae have phycoerythrin as predominant pigment which imparts red colour to them. Food is stored in the form of a complex polysaccharide Floridean starch which structurally resembles the branched polysaccharides amylopectin and glycogen. Cell wall has polysulphate esters such as agar-agar. Motile cells or flagellated cells are absent. ',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11487,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Calcium is important in skeletal muscle contraction because it is needed for','[{"text": "Unmasking of actin-binding sites on myosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrolysis of ATP by myosin head", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unmasking of myosin-binding sites on actin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Polymerization of globular actins into filamentous actin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ binds to troponin on the thin filament, exposing the binding sites for myosin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11489,'biology',91,1399,3341,'The function of thyroxine is to','[{"text": "Regulate the basal metabolic rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Support the process of RBC\'s formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maintenance of water and electrolyte balance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Thyroxine plays an important role in the regulation of the basal metabolic rate. These hormones also support the process of red blood cell formation. Thyroid hormones control the metabolism of carbohydrates, proteins and fats. Maintenance of water and electrolyte balance is also influenced by thyroid hormones',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11490,'biology',9,24,44,'Consider the following statements about asexual reproduction in brown algae.<br>I. It takes place with the help of zoospores.<br>II. Vegetative reproduction takes by budding.<br>III. The gametes are cylindrical in shape and bear two laterally attached flagella.<br>Which of the statements given above are correct?','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In brown algae, sexual reproduction takes place by pyrenoid shaped, motile zoospores with two laterally attached flagella. Vegetative reproduction takes place by fragmentation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11491,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Sliding filament theory can be best explained as','[{"text": "Actin and myosin filaments do not shorten but rather slide pass each other.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "When myofilaments slide pass each other, myosin filaments shorten while actin filaments do not shorten.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "When myofilaments slide pass each other actin filaments shorten while myosin filaments do not shorten.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Actin and myosin filaments shorten and slide pass each other.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The sliding filament theory states that contraction of a muscle fibre takes place by the sliding of the thin filaments over the thick filaments. Neither thick nor thin filaments shorten.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11493,'biology',91,1399,3341,'The function of thyroid gland is to','[{"text": "Regulate the basal metabolic rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Controls metabolism of fats, proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Regulate the blood calcium level", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'It includes the functions of thyroxine and TCT also',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11494,'biology',9,24,44,'Which of the statements given below are incorrect about brown algae?','[{"text": "Brown algae stores food in the form of floridean starch.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brown algae have gelationous coating inside the cellulosic cell wall called algin.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The kelps are unbranched.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Brown algae stores food in the form of laminarin and mannitol. They have a gelatinous coating outside the cellulosic cell wall called algin. Kelps are branched, macroscopic forms of brown algae.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11497,'biology',91,1399,3341,'The function of thyroid gland is to secrete','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{T}_{3}$ and $\\\\mathrm{T}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\text{T}}_{\\\\text{3}}}{\\\\text{ , }}{{\\\\text{T}}_{\\\\text{4}}}$ and thyrocalcitonin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thyrocalcitonin only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyrocalcitonin and PTH", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$T_{3} T_{4}$ and thyrocalcitonin are secreted by thyroid gland',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11498,'biology',9,24,45,'Consider the following statements.<br> I. Usually reproduce by fragmentation.<br> II. Spores are produced asexually.<br> III. Increases the levels of dissolved oxygen in their immediate environment. <br>The above characteristics belong to which class of algae?','[{"text": "Chlorophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phaeophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rhodophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Given statements are characteristics of algae that includes members of Chlorophyceae, Phaeophyceae and Rhodophyceae',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11501,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Thyroid gland secretes a ____  hormone called ____  calcium levels which regulates the blood','[{"text": "Steroid, thyrocalcitonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Steroid, parathyroid hormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein, thyrocalcitonin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Protein, parathyroid hormone", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Thyroid gland also secretes a protein hormone called thyrocalcitonin (TCT) which regulates the blood calcium levels',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11502,'biology',9,24,45,'Match column I with column II and select the correct option from the codes given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Unicellular algae<br>B. Agar<br>C. Algin<br>D. Carrageen</div><div class="column-right">P. <em>Fucus</em><br>Q. <em>Chlorella</em><br>R. <em>Gelidium</em>, <em>Gracilaria</em><br>S. <em>Polysiphonia</em></div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. Unicellular algae - Q. <em>Chlorella</em><br>B. Agar - R. <em>Gelidium</em>, <em>Gracilaria</em><br>C. Algin - P. <em>Fucus</em><br>D. Carrageen - S. <em>Polysiphonia</em>',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11504,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Pineal gland<br>B. Melatonin<br>C. Thyroid gland<br>D. Isthmus</div><div class="column-right">P. Located on the dorsal side of forebrain<br>Q. Both lobes of thyroid gland are interconnected with a thin flap of connective tissue<br>R. Regulates sleep- wake cycle<br>S.  Located on either side of the trachea</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A - P,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - R,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - P,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - R,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - R,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - P,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - R,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-P, B-R, C-S, D-Q',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11506,'biology',9,24,45,'In which of the following grouped examples species belong to the different classes','[{"text": "<i>Fucus, Dictyota, Laminaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Porphyra, Polytrichum, Gracilaria</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Chlorella, Volvox, Ulothrix</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Chlamydomonas, Spirogyra, Chara</i>.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In option 2, Polytrichum is mentioned. Polytrichum is a moss and hence belongs to Bryophyta.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11508,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Thyroid gland<br>B. Grave\'s disease <br>C. Hypothyroidism</div><div class="column-right">P.  Deficiency of iodine in our diet<br>Q. Composed of follicles and stromal tissues <br>R. Enlargement of  thyroid gland</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A - Q,  B - R,  C - P}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - Q,  B - P,  C - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - R,  B - P,  C - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - R,  B - Q,  C - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-Q, B-R, C-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11510,'biology',9,24,42,'About prothallus, identify the correct statement from the following:<br>I) It is undifferentiated sporophyte of bryophytes developed from zygote.<br>II) Term used in pteridophytes.<br>III) First gametophytic stage of mosses.<br>IV) Inconspicuous, multicellular, small, free-living gametophyte developed from spore.','[{"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III and IV.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II and IV are correct. Prothallus is Inconspicuous, multicellular, small, free-living gametophyte of pteridophytes developed from spore.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11512,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Which of the following disease is caused due to over secretion of the structure marked as A?','[{"text": "Grave\'s disease", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Diabetic mellitus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diabetic Insipidus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gigantism", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Grave\'s disease  is caused by hypersecretion of thyroxine is secreted thyroid gland.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/91_11512_question_1.png'),
(11514,'biology',9,24,44,'Sonal once collected some algae and found that its cells contained chlorophyll c and mannitol, an algae must be_','[{"text": "cyanophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "chlorophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phaeophyceae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "rhodophyceae", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Phaeophyceae contains chlorophyll a and c, carotenoids and xanthophyll (fucoxathin) as pigments. It stores food in the form of laminarin and mannitol.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11516,'biology',91,1399,3341,'What does \' A \' indicate in the given diagram, and what is the function of the labeled region?','[{"text": "Thyroid, more secretion decreases BMR", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroid, regulate BMR", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Parathyroid, regulate $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{++}$level in blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parathyroid, regulate BMR", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A  is thyroid gland , that regulates BMR.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/91_11516_question_1.png'),
(11517,'biology',9,24,42,'Algae is ecologically important because_','[{"text": "They provide fuel for machine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are present in huge amount", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They increase dissolved oxygen in their immediate environment", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They are used to study photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Algae being photosynthetic increase the level of dissolved oxygen in their immediate environment. This is a significant ecological role of algae.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11518,'biology',90,1330,3213,'Select the incorrect statement:','[{"text": "In <i>Hydra</i> endocrinal organisation is composed of a network of neurons.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The neural system is better organised in insects, where a brain is present along with a single ganglia and neural tissues.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The neural system of all animals is composed of highly specialised cells called nephrons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are incorrect. They can be corrected as<br>(1) In Hydra neural organisation is composed of a network of neurons.<br>(2) The neural system is better organised in insects, where a brain is present along with a number of ganglia and neural tissues<br>(3) The neural system of all animals is composed of highly specialised cells called neurons',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11519,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Select the option that correctly identifies the following contractile protein along with its location.','[{"text": "Meromyosin - Thin filament", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tropomyosin - Thick filament", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meromyosin - Thick filament", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Actin - Thin filament", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The given figure represents meromyosin. About 300 meromyosin molecules form a single thick filament.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/89_11519_question_1.png'),
(11520,'biology',91,1399,3341,'The following figure shows view of the position of thyroid gland. Identify the location of gland.','[{"text": "Dorsal side of forebrain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Located on dorsal side of trachea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Located on the anterior part of each kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Located on either side of the trachea", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The thyroid gland is located on either side of the trachea.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/91_11520_question_1.png'),
(11521,'biology',9,25,46,'Which of the following characters are shown by bryophytes','[{"text": "A plant shows thallus level of organization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It needs water to complete its life cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rhizoids are haploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The plant body of bryophytes is more differentiated than that of algae. It is thallus like and prostrate or erect, and attached to the substratum by unicellular or multicellular haploid rhizoids. Bryophytes are also called amphibians of the plant kingdom because these plants can live in soil but are dependent on water for sexual reproduction.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11522,'biology',90,1332,3215,'A typical neuron is composed of','[{"text": "Malphigian body and renal tubule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dendrites and axon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Axon and nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell, axon and dendrites", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A neuron is a microscopic structure composed of three major parts, namely, cell body,dendritesandaxon',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11524,'biology',91,1400,3342,'The full form of PTH is','[{"text": "Parathyroid hormone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prethyroid hormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prothyroid hormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Perithyroid hormone", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The parathyroid glands secrete a peptide hormone called parathyroid hormone (PTH)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11525,'biology',9,25,46,'Which of the following statement/s about bryophytes is/are correct?','[{"text": "Zygotes undergo mitotic division immediately", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The sperms are released into water and fuse with the egg to produce the zygote inside the body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The sperms are biflagellate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Antheridia, the male sex organ in bryophytes produces biflagellate male gametes called antherozoids.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11526,'biology',90,1334,3217,'The new potential developed on post-synaptic membrane is','[{"text": "Excitatory always", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inhibitory always", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "May be excitatory or inhibitory", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neither excitatory nor inhibitory", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The new potential developed on postsynaptic membrane may be excitatory or inhibitory',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11528,'biology',91,1400,3342,'In humans, ____ parathyroid glands are present on the ____','[{"text": "Four, back side of the thyroid gland", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Two , back side of the thyroid gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four, front side of the thyroid gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two, front side of the thyroid gland", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In humans, four parathyroid glands are present on the back side of the thyroid gland, one pair each in the two lobes of the thyroid gland',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11529,'biology',9,25,47,'Which of the statements is correct about <em>Marchantia</em>?','[{"text": "Plant body is a thallus-like structure, closely attached to substrate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The leafy members have tiny leaf-like appendages in one row", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gemmae are sexual buds.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 and 3 both.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The plant body of a liverwort is thalloid, e.g., <em>Marchantia</em>. The thallus is dorsiventral and closely appressed to the substrate. The leafy members have tiny leaf-like appendages in two rows on the stem-like structures. Asexual reproduction in liverworts takes place by fragmentation of thalli, or by the formation of specialised structures called gemmae.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11530,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Select the correct statement :','[{"text": "Cerebral cortex, thrown into prominent folds known as sulci and gyri.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Concentrated neuron cell body gives grey color to the cerebral cortex.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fibres of the tract, constitute inner part of cerebral hemisphere.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11532,'biology',91,1400,3342,'$\\mathrm{PTH}$ is a ____ hormone and its chemical nature is ____','[{"text": "Hypercalcemic, peptide", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hypocalcemic, peptide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypocalcemic, protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypercalcemic, protein", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Parathyroid Hormone (PTH) is a hypercalcemic hormone, i.e. it increases of blood $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ levels.and it is a peptde hormone.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11533,'biology',9,25,48,'Which of the statements given below are correct about protonema?','[{"text": "Adult stage of moss is protonema", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It consists of slender, green, branching system of filaments", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Develops directly from a zygote", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The first stage of gametophyte in mosses is the protonema stage, which develops directly from a spore. It is a creeping, green, branched and frequently filamentous stage.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11534,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Which of the following is not the feature of white muscle fibre.','[{"text": "Less quantity of myoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Few mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have less amount of Sarcoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They are anaerobic muscles", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'White muscle fibres are one kind of skeletal muscles which contain less quantity of myoglobin, mitochondria and have more sarcoplasmic reticulum and are anaerobic in nature.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11535,'biology',90,1339,3222,'Read the sentence :<br>The entire process of response to a PNS stimulation, that occur involuntary i.e., without conscious effort and requires involvement of CNS part is called a reflex action:- Which one is not true about sentence-','[{"text": "Sensory stimuli passes through dorsal surface", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All involuntary reflexes are spinal reflex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All spinal reflexes are involuntary", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'All spinal reflexes are involuntary',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11536,'biology',91,1400,3342,'The process by which PTH increases blood $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ level','[{"text": "Acts on bones and stimulates the process of bone reabsorption/dissolution/ demineralization.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reabsorption of $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ by the renal tubules.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increases $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ absorption from the digested food.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Parathyroid hormone (PTH) increases the $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ levels in the blood. PTH acts on bones and stimulates the process of bone resorption (dissolution/ demineralisation). PTH also stimulates reabsorption of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ by the renal tubules and increases $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ absorption from the digested food',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11537,'biology',9,25,46,'Choose the incorrect statements for the sporophyte of bryophytes.<br> I. Sporophyte is multicellular, free-living, and provides nourishment to the gametophyte.<br> II. Some cells of the sporophyte undergo meiosis to produce haploid spores.<br> III. These spores germinate to produce sporophyte.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The sporophyte is parasitic, multicellular and differentiated into a foot, seta and capsule. After meiosis, haploid spores are produced within the capsule. These spores germinate to form free-living gametophytes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11538,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Myosin-binding site is present on','[{"text": "Troponin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Actin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tropomyosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Actinin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Myosin-binding sites are present on actin. When the muscleis relaxed, they are masked. During muscle contraction, they are exposed when $\\mathrm{Ca} 2+$ binds to $\\mathrm{TnC}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11539,'biology',90,1340,3223,'What is common between olfaction and gustation?','[{"text": "Retina is a very important organ involved in both", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The receptor cells for both are located in the taste buds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both involve detection of dissolved chemicals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The receptors of both do not have any connection with the neurons", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both nose and tongue detect dissolved chemicals. The neurons of the only olfactory epithelium extend from the outside environment directly into a olfactory bulbs in the brain. Gustatory receptor cells synapse with sensory neurons that carry the impulses to the CNS. Olfactory receptors are bipolar neurons; not specialised cells. Only gustatory receptors are present in the taste buds.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11540,'biology',91,1400,3342,'Secretion of PTH is regulated by the circulating levels of','[{"text": "TCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ ions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroxine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The parathyroid glands secrete a peptide hormone called Parathyroid Hormone (PTH). The secretion of PTH regulated by the circulating levels of calcium ions $\\left(\\mathrm{Ca}^{+}\\right)$in the blood.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11541,'biology',9,25,47,'Consider the following statements.<br> I. The leafy members of liverworts have tiny leaf-like appendages in two rows on the true stem.<br> II. The liverworts grow usually in moist, shady habitats such as banks of streams, marshy ground, damp soil, bark of trees and deep in the woods.<br>Choose the correct option','[{"text": "I is true, but II is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I is false, but II is true", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both I and II are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II are false", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The liverworts grow usually in moist, shady habitats such as banks of streams, marshy ground, damp soil, bark of trees and deep in the woods.The leafy members have tiny leaf like appendages in two rows on the stem-like structures.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11542,'biology',89,1287,3108,'The myosin head detaches from actin soon after','[{"text": "ATP is hydrolysed into ADP and Pi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ATP binds to myosin head", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Calcium binds to troponin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calcium binds to myosin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When a new ATP binds to the myosin head, the cross-bridge is broken.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11544,'biology',9,25,48,'Read the following statements carefully.<br>I. <em>Sphagnum</em>, provide peat and has been being used as fuel since long.<br>II. Gemma cups are located on thalli.<br>III. <em>Funaria </em>possesses multicellular rhizoids. <br>Which of the statements given above are correct?','[{"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Species of <em>Sphagnum</em>, a moss, provide peat that have long been used as fuel. Gemmae are green, multicellular, asexual buds, which develop in small receptacles called gemma cups located on the thalli. <em>Funaria</em>, a moss, possesses root-like structures called rhizoids that can be either unicellular or multicellular.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11545,'biology',91,1400,3342,'Which of the following hormones affect $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ ion metabolism?','[{"text": "TCT (Thyrocalcitonin)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parathyroid hormone (PTH)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cortisol", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both TCT and PTH regulate the metabolism of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{+2}$ in our body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11546,'biology',89,1287,3108,'The cross-bridges of the sarcomere in a skeletal muscle are made up of','[{"text": "Actin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Troponin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Light meromyosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heavy meromyosin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The head and short arm of a meromyosin are made up of heavy meromyosin. They project outwards at regular distance and angle from each other from the surface of a myosin filament and form a cross arm. They interact with the thin filament to form cross-bridges during muscle contraction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11547,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Read the given statements and select the correct option .','[{"text": "The thalamus wraps around a structure called cerebrum, which is major coordinating centre for sensory and motor signaling", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpus callosum is referred to as grey matter due to it\'s greyish appearance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arachnoid is the outer most layer of the meninges", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypothalamus lies at the floor of the thalamus", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Arachnoid is the middle layer of meninges. Corpus callosum connects two cerebral hemisphere. Hypothalamus lies at base of thalamus. The cerebrum wraps around a structure called thalamus, which is major coordinating centre for sensory and motor signaling',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11548,'biology',91,1400,3342,'In humans, parathyroid glands','[{"text": "Are four in number present on the back side of the thyroid gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One pair each in the two lobes of the thyroid gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In humans, four parathyroid glanda are present on the back side of the thyroid gland, one pair each in the two lobes of the thyroid gland. The parathyroid glands secrete a peptide hormone called Parathyroid Hormone (PTH).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11560,'biology',91,1400,3342,'The following figure shows view of the position of parathyroid gland. Identify the location of gland.','[{"text": "Dorsal side of forebrain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Present on the back side of the thyroid gland", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Located on the anterior part of each kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Located on either side of the kidney<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Parathyroid gland is present on the backside of the thyroid gland.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/91_11560_question_1.png'),
(11549,'biology',9,25,48,'In Funaria, 30 chromosomes are present in seta then the number of chromosomes in gametophyte, rhizoids and capsule will be','[{"text": "30,30,30 respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "15,30,30 respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "15,15,30 respectively", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "30,30,15 respectively", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Foot, seta, capsule are divisions of diploid sporophyte . Hence, cells of seta are diploid too. Seta = 2n = 30 , Gametophyte = n = 15, Rhizoids (gametophyte) = n = 15 , Capsule (sporophyte) = 2n = 30',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11550,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Which of the following types of muscle fibres will be the first to undergo fatigue?','[{"text": "White muscle fibres", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cardiac muscle fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red muscle fibres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aerobic muscle fibres", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'White muscle fibres depend on the anaerobic process for energy and hence are fatigue-prone.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11551,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Which of the following statements are false w.r.t. association areas of brain?<br>I. These areas are responsible for complex functions like intersensory associations, memory and communication<br>II. There are large regions present in cerebral cortex<br>III. It is constituted of white matter only<br>IV. These are clearly motor areas','[{"text": "I and II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The cerebral cortex contains motor areas, sensory areas and large regions that are neither clearly sensory nor motor in function. These regions called as the association areas are responsible for complex functions like intersensory associations, memory and communication.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11552,'biology',91,1400,3342,'The hormone released by \' A \' marked in the given diagram helps to restore \' $\\mathrm{B}$ \'. Identify $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{B}$.','[{"text": "A- Thyroxine,<br>B-Too much calcium in the blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Thymosins,<br>B- Decreased level of blood sugar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Parathormone,<br>B- lowered levels of calcium in blood", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Adrenaline,<br>B-Excessive loss of sodium in extracellular fluid<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A is parathyroid gland that secretes parathormone and along with calcitonin , they maintain the calcium balance in the  body.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/91_11552_question_1.png'),
(11553,'biology',9,26,49,'Which of the statements given below are correct about pteridophytes?','[{"text": "They are called vascular phanerogams", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They produce seeds rather than spores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The gametophyte bears both male and female sex organs.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The sporangia produce spores by mitosis.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pteridophytes are vascular cryptogams.They produce spores and exhibits an event precursor to seed habit. The gametophytes bear male and female sex organs called antheridia and archegonia, respectively. The sporangia produces spores by meiosis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11554,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Which of the following is an active ATPase in the skeletal muscle fibre?','[{"text": "Tropomyosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Actin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heavy meromyosin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Light meromyosin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The globular head of meromyosin is an active ATPase enzyme. The head and the short arm are made up of heavy meromyosin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11555,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Read the statement regarding synapse and select the correct option','[{"text": "At a synapse the membrane of axon and dendrite are not in physical contact with each other", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synapse is a junction between axon endings of one nerve fibre and dendrite of the other.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transmission of nerve impulse through chemical synapse is only one way", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11556,'biology',91,1400,3342,'What is related to region labeled as \' $\\mathrm{A}$ \' in the diagram?','[{"text": "Parathyroid hormone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thyroid stimulating hormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyrocalcitonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenaline", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A is a parathyroid gland that secretes Parathoromone.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/91_11556_question_1.png'),
(11557,'biology',9,26,49,'The peculiar character of pteridophyte is','[{"text": "Presence of roots, leaves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dominant sporophyte with an autotrophic gametophyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dominant sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametophyte reduced", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In pteridophytes, sporophyte and gametophyte are both multicellular, independent, photosynthetic structures. Although, sporophyte in the main plant body and bears true roots, stem and leaves.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11558,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Mark the feature which is not associated with white muscle fibres.','[{"text": "Lighter in colour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These muscles have a fast rate of contraction but for a short period", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They depend mainly on glycolysis for energy production and soon get fatigued", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Less sarcoplasmic reticulum compared to red muscle fibres", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Amount of sarcoplasmic reticulum is high in white muscle fibres.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11559,'biology',90,1337,3220,'Read all statements carefully and find out how many statement\'s are correct ?<br>1) Neural system provides an organised network of point to point connection\'s for a quick co-ordination<br>2) Impulse transmission across a chemical synapse is always faster than that across a electrical synapse<br>3) Cerebral aqueduct passes through the mid-brain<br>4) The hypothalamus contain centres which control respiration and gastric secretions','[{"text": "one", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "two", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "four", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement 2 and 4 are wrong. Impulse transmission across electrical synapse is always faster than that across chemical synapse. Hypothalamus of brain has centres for control of body temperature, urge for eating and drinking\'. Medulla of hind brain has centres that control respiration, cardiovascular reflex and gastric secretions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11639,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Identify the correct pair','[{"text": "Zona fasciculata - middle layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zona glomerulosa - outer layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zona reticularis - inner layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The adrenal cortex can be divided into three layers, called zona reticularis (inner layer), zona fasciculata (middle layer) and zona glomerulosa (outer layer)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11561,'biology',9,26,49,'In pteridophytes, to prevent self-fertilisation_','[{"text": "Plant becomes apomicitic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There is high degree of sterility", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antherozoids and eggs mature at different times", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They can’t prevent self-fertilisation.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pteridophytes exhibit dichogamy, the maturation of male and female sex organs at different times to prevent self fertilisation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11562,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Which of the following brings about the relaxation of a muscle fibre?','[{"text": "Unmasking of active sites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pumping of $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ into sarcoplasmic cisternae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sliding of the thin filaments towards $\\\\mathrm{M}$ line", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Binding of $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ to troponin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pumping of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ into sarcoplasmic cisternae results in the masking of active sites on actin filaments. This causes the return of thin filaments back to their original position leading to muscle relaxation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11563,'biology',90,1334,3217,'If the receptors are removed from postsynaptic membrane, then','[{"text": "Synaptic transmission will be faster", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemical synaptic transmission will become slow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemical synaptic transmission will not occur", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Synaptic transmission will not be affected", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Chemicals released cannot bind to the receptor if receptors are removed from post-synaptic membrane hence chemical transmission will not occur between presynaptic and post-synaptic neuron.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11564,'biology',91,1401,3343,'The thymus gland secretes the steroidal hormones called','[{"text": "Antibodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Androgens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thymosins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The thymus gland secretes the peptide hormones called thymosins.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(11565,'biology',9,26,49,'Which of the following is true about prothallus?','[{"text": "A gametophytic free living structure formed in bryophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A gametophytic free living structure formed in pteridophytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A structure in bryophytes formed before the thallus develops", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A primitive structure formed after fertilization in pteridophytes.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The spores in pteridophytes germinate to give rise to inconspicuous, small but multicellular, free-living, mostly photosynthetic thalloid gametophytes called prothallus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11567,'biology',91,1401,3343,'The thymus gland is a lobular structure located between','[{"text": "Lungs infront sternum on the dorsal side of aorta.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lungs behind sternum on the dorsal side of aorta.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lungs infront sternum on the ventral side of aorta.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lungs behind sternum on the ventral side of aorta.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The thymus gland is a lobular structure located between lungs behind sternum on the ventral side of aorta.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11568,'biology',90,1337,3220,'Which of the statement/s is/are correct?','[{"text": "Cerebral medulla is referred to as a white matter due to its whitish appearance.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Magnum canal passes through the mid brain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The thalamus contains a number of centres which control body temperature, urge for eating and drinking including respiratory and cardiovascular reflexes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cerebral medulla is referred to as a white matter due to its whitish appearance.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11569,'biology',9,27,50,'Identify the correct statement with regards to the gymnosperms.','[{"text": "The <i>Sequoia</i> is the tiny gymnosperm species.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In gymnosperms, ovules remain exposed, only before fertilisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leaves in gymnosperms are well-adapted to withstand extreme environmental conditions.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The gymnosperms are homosporous.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gymnosperms are heterosporous plants where the seeds remain naked pre and post fertilisation. Sequoia is an example of the tallest gymnosperm. These plants are well adapted to withstand extreme environmental\nconditions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11571,'biology',91,1401,3343,'Thymosin','[{"text": "Amino acid -hormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secreted by pituitary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Associated with auto immunity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Promote production of antibodies", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Thymosin promote production of antibodies',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11572,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Which of the following statements are correct in relation to Hind brain?<br>I. Consists of pons, cerebellum, medulla oblongata<br>II. Pons consists of fibre tracts that interconnect different regions of the brain<br>III. Cerebellum has visual area<br>IV. Medulla oblongata connected to spinal cord','[{"text": "I, II, IV are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'i, ii and iv are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11573,'biology',9,27,50,'Consider the following statements regarding gymnosperms and choose the correct statements.<br> I. The gymnosperms are homosporous.<br> II. In gymnosperms, the male and female gametophytes are dependent on sporophytes.<br>III. The unicellular female gametophyte is retained within the megasporangium.','[{"text": "I and II are true, but III is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III are false, but II is true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III are false, but I is true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III are true, but I is false", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In gymnosperms, the male and female gametophytes are dependent on sporophytes. The unicellular female gametophyte is retained within the megasporangium.The gymnosperms are heterosporous.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11575,'biology',91,1401,3343,'Which gland plays major role in the differentiation of T-lymphocyte?','[{"text": "Thyroid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thymus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adrenal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pituitary", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Thymosins play a major role in the differentiation of T-lymphocytes, which provide cell-mediated immunity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11576,'biology',9,27,50,'In gymnosperms, the endosperm is','[{"text": "diploid and formed before fertilization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "haploid and formed before fertilization", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "diploid and formed after fertilization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "haploid and formed after fertilization", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In gymnosperms, a haploid endosperm is formed before fertilisation. It is equivalent to female gametophyte.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11578,'biology',90,1333,3216,'Read the following given statements regarding $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}-\\mathrm{K}^{+}$and identify the correct option<br>I. Expels $3 \\mathrm{Na}^{+}$for every $2 \\mathrm{~K}^{+}$ions imported<br>II. Maintains resting potential<br>III. Works against a concentration gradient','[{"text": "Statement I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement II and III are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I, II and III are correct.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the given statement about $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}-\\mathrm{K}^{+}$ are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11579,'biology',91,1401,3343,'Immune response of old persons are weak because','[{"text": "Thymus is degenerated in old individual", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thymosin production decreases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thymosin production increases<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The thymus plays a major role in the development of the immune system. Thymus is degenerated in old individuals resulting in a decreased production of thymosin. As a result, the immune responses of old persons become weak.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11581,'biology',9,27,50,'Consider the following statements regarding gymnosperms and choose the incorrect option','[{"text": "In gymnosperms endosperm is formed before fertilisation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The multicellular female gametophyte is retained within megasporangium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The gymnosperms are heterosporous.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In gymnosperms, the male and female gametophytes have an independent existence", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In gymnosperms, male and female gametophyte are both dependent on sporophyte.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11583,'biology',91,1401,3343,'Which of the following is correct about thymus?','[{"text": "Lobular structure located on the ventral side of the heart and aorta.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Provides cell-mediated immunity.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The thymus size decreases with age.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct .Thymosin plays a major role in the differentiation of T-lymphocytes, which provides cell-mediated immunity. Thymus is degenerated in old individuals resulting in a decreased production of thymosin. As a result, the immune responses of old persons become weak.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11584,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Repeated activation of a skeletal muscle can cause fatigue due to the','[{"text": "Accumulation of lactic acid, a byproduct of anaerobic respiration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Accumulation of lactic acid, a byproduct of aerobic respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase in $\\\\mathrm{pH}$ due to the accumulation of $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synthesis of ATP from creatine phosphate", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Repeated activation of the muscles can lead to the accumulation of lactic acid due to anaerobic breakdown of glycogen in them, causing fatigue.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11824,'biology',91,1405,3347,'Identify the correct pair','[{"text": "Ovarian follicle - ovum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epididymis - male accessory organ", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Androgens - oogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ovarian follicle - ovum, Epididymis - male accessory organ, both are correct',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11585,'biology',9,27,50,'Select one of the following pairs of important features distinguishing <i>Cycas</i> from <i>Pinus</i>_','[{"text": "Presence of haploid endosperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of mycorrhiza", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "presence of vessels", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of coralloid roots", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In Cycas, small specialised roots called coralloid roots are associated with N2- fixing cyanobacteria. While in Pinus, mycorhizzal roots in association with fungi are present.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11586,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Chemicals called neurotransmitter are involved in conduction of impulses at a synapse. Which out of the following is the correct statement for electrical synapse','[{"text": "Axon terminals contain vesicles that are filled with neurotransmitter.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neurotransmitter is always released from axon endings and not by dendrites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transmission of nerve impulse through electrical synapse is fast", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Remaining statements provide information on chemical synapse.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11587,'biology',91,1401,3343,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A  Parathyroid  gland <br>B  Parathormone <br>C  Thymus gland <br>D  Thymosins</div><div class="column-right">P.  Lobular  structure located on the ventral side of  the heart and  aorta <br>Q.  Increases the ${\\text{C}}{{\\text{a}}^{{\\text{ +  + }}}}$ the blood<br>R.  Four glands are present on the  backside of  thyroid gland<br>S. Plays major  role in the  differentiation of  T-lymphocytes</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A - S,  B - Q,  C - R,  D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - R,  B - P,  C - Q,  D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - R,  B - Q,  C - P,  D - S}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - P,  B - Q,  C - R,  D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-R, B-Q, C-P, D-S.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11588,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Select the option which identifies any one part (A-C) of the following diagram and gives its correct description.','[{"text": "A: Troponin - A complex protein distributed at regular intervals on the actin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B: Troponin - Two filaments run close to the F-actins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C: G-actin - A polymer of monomeric F-actins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A: Myosin - ATP binds to it", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Troponin is a complex protein distributed at regular intervals on the actin molecule, masking its active sites.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/89_11588_question_1.png'),
(11589,'biology',9,26,49,'Salvia is considered to represent a significant step towards evolution of seed habit because','[{"text": "megapores possess endosperm and embryo surrounded by seed coat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "female gametophytes lack archegonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "female gametophyte is free and gets dispersed like seeds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Above consideration in question is wrong.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Salvia is an angiosperm. Evolution of seed habit was first shown by pteridophytes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11591,'biology',91,1401,3343,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A  Parathyroid  gland <br> B  Thymosins <br> C T- lymphocytes <br> D Degeneration of thymus gland</div><div class="column-right">P  Result in the wek immune response in old persons <br>Q  Stimulates the process of bone resorption<br>R  Also promotes production of antibodies to provide humoral immunity<br>S  Provide cell - mediated immunity</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A - Q,  B - R,  C - S,  D - P}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - Q,  B - R,  C - P,  D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - R,  B - Q,  C - S,  D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - R,  B - P,  C - Q,  D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11593,'biology',9,28,53,'Which of the following is absent in angiospermic plants_<br>I. Double fertilisation<br>II. Triploid endosperm<br>III. Diploid endosperm<br>IV. Syngamy','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Endosperm in angiosperms in triploid due to fusion of secondary nucleus (2n) and male gamete (n).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11595,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Adrenal gland is present in the','[{"text": "Anterior side of each kidney", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dorsal side of each kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Posterior side of each kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ventral side of each kidney", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Our body has one pair of adrenal glands, one at the anterior part of each kidney',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11640,'biology',90,1330,3213,'Nervous system is different from endocrine because it shows :-<br>i. Point to point effect<br>ii. Widely spread effect<br>iii. Slow speed of service<br>iv. Fast speed of service','[{"text": "i and iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'i and iv are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11596,'biology',89,1286,3107,'The functional unit of contraction is a','[{"text": "Portion of myofibril between two successive Z-lines", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Portion of myofibril between two successive M-lines", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centre of the H-zone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centre of the I-band", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The portion of the myofibril between two successive \' Z \' lines is considered as the functional unit of contraction and is called a sarcomere.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11597,'biology',9,28,53,'Find the odd man out w.r.t. ploidy','[{"text": "flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "seed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "leaf", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Primary endosperm cell", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Primary endosperm cell is formed after fusion of secondary nucleus and male gamete. It is triploid while other options are diploid.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11598,'biology',90,1336,3219,'What will happen if amygdala of a person is damaged?','[{"text": "Person will forget recent events and cannot commit anything to memory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Person will fail to recognise fearful expression of others / or to express fear in appropriate situation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Person fail to maintain body temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Person fails to feel hunger and thirst", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Amygdala is the structure present in the inner parts of cerebral hemisphere. It forms part of the limbic system. Amygdala is mainly associated with emotions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11599,'biology',91,1402,3344,'The term \'Medulla\' is used in','[{"text": "Cerebrum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenal gland, ovaries", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of them is correct, the inner part of these organs is called medulla.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11600,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Three types of muscles are given as and Identify the correct matching pair along with their location in human body: <br>Name of Muscle/location<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "(a) Smooth - Toes(b) Skeletal - Legs(c) Cardiac - Heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(a) Skeletal - Triceps(b) Smooth - Stomach(c) Cardiac - Heart", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(a) Skeletal - Biceps(b) Involuntary - Intestine(c) Smooth - Heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(a) Involuntary - Nose tip(b) Skeletal - Bone(c) Cardiac - Heart", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Figure (a) represents skeletal muscle fibres which are closely attached to skeletal bones. In a typical muscle such as triceps and biceps, striated muscle fibres are bundled together in a parallel fashion.<br>Figure (b) represents smooth muscle fibres which are present in the wall of internal organs such as the blood vessels, stomach and intestine.<br>Figure (c) represents cardiac muscle fibres which are exclusively present in the heart.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/89_11600_question_1.png'),
(11601,'biology',9,28,53,'Read the following statements and identify the incorrect option<br>(a) Triple fusion is unique event in angiosperms<br>(b) In angiosperms, the seeds are not enclosed by fruits<br>(c) Angiosperms range in size from microscopic <em>Wolffia</em> to tall trees of eucalyptus<br>(d) In angiosperms each cell of the synergids are diploid.<br>(e) In angiosperms, the zygote develops into an endosperm','[{"text": "a, c, d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "c, e, d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b, d, e", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a, b, d", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In angiosperms, seeds are enclosed inside fruit wall. Each synergid cell in female gametophyte (embryo sac) is haploid. Endosperm is developed after the fusion of secondary nucleus and male gamete.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11602,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Select the correct option :-<br>i. Unmyelinated nerve fibres are commonly found in autonomous and somatic neural system.<br>ii. Myelinated nerve fibres are found in spinal & cranial nerves.<br>iii. Unmyelinated nerve fibre is also enclosed by schwann cell that does not form a myelin sheath around axon.<br>iv. The gaps between two adjacent nonmyelinated sheaths are called synaptic cleft','[{"text": "i, ii & iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii & iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii & iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'i, ii and iii are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11603,'biology',91,1402,3344,'The centrally located tissue is called the adrenal ____ and outside this lies the adrenal ____.','[{"text": "Cortex, periphery", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cortex, cortex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Medulla, cortex", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cortex, medulla", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The centrally located tissue is called the adrenal medulla, and outside this lies the adrenal cortex',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11605,'biology',9,28,53,'If the chromosome number of endosperm of a flowering plant is 27, change to what would be the chromosome number in its synergid cell?','[{"text": "18", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "36", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "9", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "9+9", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Endosperm in angiosperms is triploid. 3n = 27<br>Synergid cell is haploid. n = 27/3 = 9.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11606,'biology',91,1402,3344,'The adrenal medulla secretes hormones These are commonly known as','[{"text": "Steroids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Terpenes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Catecholamine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hormoamines", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The adrenal medulla secretes two hormones called adrenaline or epinephrine and noradrenaline or norepinephrine. These are commonly called as catecholamines',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11641,'biology',9,28,53,'Pick out the incorrect statement:<br>(a) Double fertilization is unique to angiosperms.<br>(b) <em>Sequoia</em>, an angiosperm is one of the tallest tree<br>(c) <em>Dictyota</em> members possess chlorophyll, a,c, and 2 unequal laterally flagellated zoospores.<br>(d) In mosses adult stage is named as protonema stage','[{"text": "c, d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b, c", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b, d", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<em>Sequoia</em> is one of the tallest gymnosperm species. In mosses, the juvenile stage is named as protonema.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11609,'biology',9,29,52,'Consider the following statements about the gametophytic stage.<br> I. The generation which produces sporophyte.<br>II. Generation that produces the gametes.<br>III. Generation that is diploid<br>IV. Generation that produces the spores.<br>Choose the incorrect statements given above.','[{"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Gametophyte is a haploid plant body that produces haploid gametes. These gametes fuse to form zygote, which in turn develops into a sporophyte. Sporophyte is a diploid plant body that produces haploid spores.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11610,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Emergency hormone and hormones of fight are all except','[{"text": "Adrenalin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Noradrenaline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cortisol", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Emergency hormone and hormones of fight are Adrenalin and Noradrenaline',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11612,'biology',9,29,52,'In which of the following groups of plants, the gametophytic phase is not dominant, photosynthetic, independent and sexually reproducing.','[{"text": "<i>Funaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Marchantia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Lycopodium</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 2 both", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lycopodium is a pteridophyte. In this group of plants, sporophyte is the dominant, photosynthetic and independent plant body.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11613,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Epinephrine/adrenaline causes','[{"text": "Increase the strength of heart contraction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase rate of respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase the heart beat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Adrenalin and Noradrenaline, both the hormones increase the heart beat, the strength of heart contraction and the rate of respiration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11614,'biology',90,1337,3220,'Read the following four statements. How many statements are correct ?','[{"text": "Associated area are mixed area which are found in cerebellar cortex.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpora quadrigemina is a structure which is made up of optic lobes and are found in forebrain.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both cerebral hemisphere are connected with connecting strip of white collagen fibre, known as corpus callosum.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Corpora quadrigemina is part of the mid brain. Association area in a brain connects sensory and motor areas. Corpus callosum is part that connects the two cerebral hemispheres, it is composed of bundle of fibres.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11615,'biology',9,26,49,'Bryophytes and pteridophytes do not show similarity in which one of the following feature?','[{"text": "Haplo-diplontic alternation of generation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis in sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Main gametophytic plant body", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dependence on water for fertilisation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In bryophytes, gametophyte is the main plant body. Whereas, in pteridophytes, sporophyte is the main plant body.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11616,'biology',91,1402,3344,'A. Increase alertness<br>B. Sweating<br>C. Piloerection<br>D. Increase heart rate<br>E. Increase respiratory rate<br>F. Pupillary dilation<br>Which of the above are effects of emergency hormone?','[{"text": "All except C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All except B and D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All except A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Adrenalin and Noradrenaline ,these hormones increase alertness, pupilary dilation, piloerection (raising of hairs), sweating etc.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11617,'biology',90,1336,3219,'The inner part of cerebral hemisphere & group of associated deep structure form a complex structure called limbic system. The associated deep structures include:-<br>i. Amygdala<br>ii. Hippocampus<br>iii. Outer parts of cerebral cortex<br>iv. Association area','[{"text": "i & iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i & ii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i & iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii & iv", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The limbic system in human brain consists of Hippocampus, Amygdala , Mammillary body and an anterior nucleus of thalamus. Along with hypothalamus limbic system is involved in regulation of sexual behaviour, expression of emotional reactions. Hippocampus is located in temporal lobe, it is involved in long term memory. Amygdala is mainly associated with emotions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11618,'biology',9,25,48,'Read the following statements carefully<br> Mosses and ferns are found in moist and shady places because<br> (a) They get killed by sunlight<br> (b) They are dependent on water for asexual reproduction<br> (c) They are dependent on bacteria for their nutrition which survive only in shades<br> (d) They are dependent on water for fertilisation. <br>Select the incorrect statements.','[{"text": "a, b, d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b, c", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "b, c, d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, c, d", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mosses and ferns are found in moist and shady places because they are dependent on water for fertilisation. All other statements are incorrect.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11619,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Adrenaline causes','[{"text": "Lipolysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein breakdown", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycogenolysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Catecholamines also stimulate the breakdown of glycogen resulting in an increased concentration of glucose in blood. In addition, they also stimulate the breakdown of lipids and proteins',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11620,'biology',9,28,51,'Select the matching pair<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Precursor of seed habit – vascular cryptogams", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amphibians of plant kingdom– pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water required for fertilization – gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seeds enclosed in fruits – first terrestrial plants", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pteridophytes were the first plants to evolve an efficient vascular system. They don’t bear flowers, seeds, fruits and are hence known as cryptogams. The development of zygotes is carried out inside the female gametophyte. This event is a precursor to seed habit, which is observed in pteridophytes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11622,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Which of the following layers are present in the adrenal cortex from inner to outer?','[{"text": "Zona reticularis, zona fasciculata, zona glomerulosa", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Zona fasciculata, zona glomerulosis, zona reticularis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zona glomerulosa, zona reticularis, zona fasciculata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zona glomerulosa, zona fasciculata, zona reticularis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The adrenal cortex can be divided into three layers, called zona reticularis (inner layer), zona fasciculata (middle layer) and zona glomerulosa (outer layer), this are histological layers',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11623,'biology',9,27,50,'Which of the given sets are matched incorrectly?<br>a. <i>Polysiphonia</i> - Carrageen<br>b. <i>Pinus</i> - Mycorrhiza<br>c. <i>Cycas</i> - Coralloid root<br>d. <i>Gelidium</i> - Agar<br>e. <i>Adiantum</i> - Flying fern<br>f. <i>Lycopodium</i> - Cord moss<br>g. <i>Cedrus</i> - Dependent gametophyte<br>h. <i>Kelps</i> - Giant gymnosperm<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "a, d, f", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b, c, g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, c, d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "e, f, h", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Adiantum - Walking fern<br>Lycopodium – Club moss<br>Kelps - giant bryophytes',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11624,'biology',90,1336,3219,'The cerebrum wrap around a structure called ____A ____. Which is major coordinating centre for ____ B ____ signaling. Another very important part of the brain called ____ C ____  lie at the base of thalamus. Choose the correct option for A, B and C to complete the given statement','[{"text": "A- Thalamus, B- Sensory motor, C-Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Pons, B-Visual, C-Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Cerebellum, B-Smell, C- Epithalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Pons, B- Sensory motor, C-Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Thalamus is part of brain that is present just below cerebrum, its function is to receive sensory impulses (except for smell ). Hypothalamus is part of brain, present below thalamus, it controls different autonomic functions and help to maintain homeostasis of the body.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11625,'biology',91,1402,3344,'The adrenal cortex secretes many hormones commonly called','[{"text": "Catecholamine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peptide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corticoids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glucocorticoids", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The adrenal cortex secretes many hormones,commonly called as corticoids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11626,'biology',9,28,51,'Match column I with column II and select the correct option from the codes given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Non-vascular cryptogams<br>B. Phanerogams<br>C. Vascular cryptogams</div><div class="column-right">1. <em>Sequoia</em>, Rose<br>2. <em>Adiantum</em><br>3. <em>Dictyota</em>, <em>Polytrichum</em></div></div>','[{"text": "A-(3), B-(2), C-(1)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-(2), B-(1), C-(3)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-(3), B-(1), C-(2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-(2), B-(3), C-(1)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A. Non-vascular cryptogams - <em>Dicyota, Polytrichum</em><br>B. Phanerogams - <em>Sequoia</em>, Rose<br>C. Vascular cryptogams - <em>Adiantum</em>',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11627,'biology',90,1339,3222,'Given below are the different components of reflex arc. Arrange those in correct order of action potential that follows a sensory receptor stimulation.<br>i. Sensory receptor<br>ii. Sensory neuron<br>iii. Interneuron<br>iv. Motor neuron<br>v. Effector organ','[{"text": "iii- iv- i- ii- v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i-ii-iii-iv-v", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iii-ii-iv-i-v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii-iv-iii-i-v", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the reflex arc, impulse passes in the following manner<br>Sensory receptor $\\rightarrow$ Sensory neuron $\\rightarrow$ Interneuron $\\rightarrow$ Motor neuron $\\rightarrow$ effector organ',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11628,'biology',91,1402,3344,'The hormones, synthesised by adrenal cortex which are involved in carbohydrate metabolism are called ____.','[{"text": "Catecholamine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peptide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corticoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucocorticoids", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The corticoids, which are involved in carbohydrate metabolism are called glucocorticoids',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11629,'biology',9,28,51,'Which of the following is an example of cryptogams','[{"text": "<em>Eucalyptus</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Ginkgo</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Sphagnum</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hibiscus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cryptogams includes plants from class Algae, Bryophyta and Pteridophyta. <em>Sphagnum</em>, a moss is a cryptogam.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11630,'biology',90,1337,3220,'Read the following statement (A to D) carefully:-<br>How many statements are incorrect?','[{"text": "Four round swellings are found in midbrain towards anterior side", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neurotransmitter released from presynaptic membrane generates excitatory and inhibitory potentials at post synaptic membrane in electrical synapses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Association area are clearly sensory area for complex functions like intersensory association and memory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are incorrect Four round swellings are found is mid brain towards dorsal side. Neurotransmitter released from pre-synaptic membrane generates potentials at post synaptic membrane in chemical synapses .<br>Association area are neither clearly sensory nor motor in function.<br>They perform complex functions like intersensory association and memory',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11631,'biology',91,1402,3344,'In our body the main glucocorticoid is','[{"text": "Adrenaline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aldosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cortisol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glucocorticoids", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In our body, cortisol is the main glucocorticoid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11632,'biology',9,28,53,'Which of the following statements is true?','[{"text": "Trimerous condition of floral whorls is characterstic of dicotyledons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Adiantum</i> is also called flying fern", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In gymnosperms the vascular system consists of xylem without vessels and phloem with companion cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Riccia and Marchantia are liverworts.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'1. Trimerous condition of floral whorls is characterstic of monocotyledons.<br>2. Adiantum is also called walking fern.<br>3. In gymnosperms the vascular system consists of xylem without vessels and pholem with albuminous cells.<br>4. Riccia and Marchantia are liverworts. This statement is true.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11633,'biology',90,1338,3221,'A special neural centre in the ____can moderate the cardiac function through ____','[{"text": "Medulla oblongata, CNS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Medulla oblongata, ANS", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mid brain, PNS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mid brain, medulla oblongata", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A special neural centre in the Medulla oblongata can moderate the cardiac function through ANS.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11634,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Corticoids, which regulate the balance of water and electrolytes in our body are called ____','[{"text": "Adrenaline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mineralocorticoids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cortisol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucocorticoids", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Corticoids, which regulate the balance of water and electrolytes in our body are called mineralocorticoids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11635,'biology',9,26,49,'Antherozoids cannot be','[{"text": "biflagellated", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "multicilliated", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "photosynthetic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "motile", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Antherozoids are biflagellated male gametes. They are motile and might bear cilia. They are unicellular, haploid gametes that cannot be photosynthetic.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11636,'biology',90,1333,3216,'Read the statements and identify which is TRUE /FALSE<br>I. The axoplasm inside the axon contains low concentration of $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$.<br>II. The axoplasm inside the axon contains high concentration of $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$and negatively charged proteins.<br>III. The fluid outside the axon contains a low concentration of $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$<br>IV. The fluid outside the axon contains a low concentration of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$','[{"text": "I and IV are false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Axoplasm inside axon has a high concentration of $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$ and negatively charged proteins. Fluid outside axon has low concentration of $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$.  Axoplasm inside axon as low $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$concentration.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11637,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Identify the correct pair','[{"text": "Aldosterone-glucocorticoid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cortisol- mineralocorticoid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenal cortex- adrenaline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are wrong", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are wrong, the correct ones will be<br>(1) Aldosterone- mineralocorticoid<br>(2) Cortisol-glucocorticoid<br>(3) Adrenal cortex- corticoids',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11638,'biology',9,28,53,'In which of the following features, <i>Cycas</i> do not resemble with angiosperms?','[{"text": "Syngamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of vessels", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "triploid endosperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (2) and (3)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cycas is a gymnosperm. In this group of plants, vessels of xylem are absent. Endosperm is haploid and derived from female gametophyte. Syngamy, the fusion of gametes occurs in both gymnosperms and angiosperms.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12023,'biology',9,28,53,'Double fertilization is exhibited by','[{"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angiosperms", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Double fertilization is a characteristic feature exhibited by angiosperms. It involves syngamy and triple fusion.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11642,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Identify the correct statement<br>I. The adrenal cortex secretes many hormones, commonly called as corticoids.<br>II. The adrenal medulla secretes catecholamines.','[{"text": "I is correct only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II is correct only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct a. The adrenal cortex secretes many hormones, commonly called as corticoids. b. The adrenal medulla secretes catelcholamines.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11644,'biology',9,27,50,'Consider the following 4 statements whether they are correct or wrong<br>(a) The sporophyte in mosses is more elaborate than that in liverworts<br>(b) <i>Selaginella</i> is heterosporous<br>(c) The life cycle of all the algae is haplontic<br>(d) In <i>Pinus</i> male and female cones are borne on the same tree.<br>The correct statements are','[{"text": "a, c and d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b and d", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "b, c and d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Some algae are haplontic,<i>Fucus</i> is <i>diplontic</i>, Kelps, <i>Ectocarpus, Polysiphonia</i> is haplodiplontic.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11645,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Glucocorticoid causes all except','[{"text": "Proteolysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipolysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycogenolysis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gluconeogenesis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Glucocorticoids stimulate gluconeogenesis, lipolysis and proteolysis; and inhibit cellular uptake and utilisation of amino acids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11646,'biology',90,1339,3222,'How many of the statements are false with respect to reflex action?','[{"text": "Sudden withdrawal of body part from object which comes in contact may include in reflex action", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reflex pathway contains at least two afferent and one efferent neuron.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The afferent neuron receives signal from a sensory organ and transmits the impulse via a dorsal nerve root into the CNS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The reflex pathway comprises at least one afferent neuron (receptor) and one efferent (effector or excitor) neuron appropriately arranged in a series',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11647,'biology',9,27,50,'Which one of the following is an incorrect statement?','[{"text": "In mosses gametophyte has a protonemal and leafy stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In gymnosperms female gametophyte is free living", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Antheridiophores and archegoniophores are present in bryophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Origin of seed habit can be traced in pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In gymnosperms, both male and female gametophyte are dependent on sporophyte.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11648,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Which of the following is incorrect about glucocorticoid?','[{"text": "Inhibits cellular uptake and utilization of amino acids.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimulate gluconeogenesis, lipolysis and proteolysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucocorticoid stimulates gluconeogenesis, lipogenesis and proteolysis.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Glucocorticoids stimulate gluconeogenesis, lipolysis and proteolysis; and inhibit cellular uptake and utilisation of amino acids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11649,'biology',90,1330,3213,'Select the correct statement.','[{"text": "Neurons regulate endocrine activity but not vice-versa", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Endocrine glands regulate neural activity but not vice-versa.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endocrine glands regulate neural activity and nervous system regulates endocrine activity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neither hormones control neural activity nor the neurons control the endocrine activity.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement in option (1) is correct.<br>Neurons regulate the endocrine activity, but endocrine activity do not regulates the neural activity.<br>Rest statements are incorrectly written',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11650,'biology',9,27,50,'Read the statements i-v and question which follows<br>i) <i>Pinus</i> is monoecious<br>ii) Angiosperm and all ferns are heterosporous<br>iii) Sexual reproduction in <i>Fucus, Volvox</i> and <i>Albugo</i> is oogamous<br>iv) In liverworts, mosses and ferns, gametophytes are dependent on sporophyte<br>How many of the above statements are correct','[{"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Angiosperms and some ferns like Selaginella are heterosporous. In liverworts, mosses and ferns, gametophytes are not dependent on sporophytes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11651,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Which of the following organs are affected by cortisol?','[{"text": "Kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cardiovascular system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Skeletal system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cortisol is also involved in maintaining the cardio-vascular system as well as the kidney functions',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11652,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Which of the following regarding to nerve activity is true','[{"text": "The synaptic cleft does not prevent direct propagation of action potential from presynaptic neuron to post synaptic cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Information occurs when the synaptic cleft is transmitted by means of a chemical neurotransmitter from small vesicle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Combination of neurotransmitter with receptor site changes membrane potential without changing membrane permeability", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Synaptic cleft is the gap between presynaptic neuron and post- synaptic neuron. During chemical synapse, membrane of pre-synaptic neuron and post-synaptic neuron is separated by a fluid - filled space called Synaptic Cleft.Synaptic cleft will allow propagation of action potential from presynaptic neuron to post synaptic neuron. Neurotransmitter binds to specific receptor on post synaptic membrane which leads to opening of ion channels which will allow entry of ions and generates a new electrical potential. Neurotransmitter acts by changing membrane permeability.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11653,'biology',9,28,51,'Which is wrongly matched<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Terror of bengal - water hyacinth,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phycomycetes - <em>Rhizopus</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Sargassum</em> - chl b", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<em>Spirogyra</em> - non-motile gametes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<em>Sargassum</em>, a brown algae contains chlorophyll a and c as its major pigments.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
