(11655,'biology',90,1337,3220,'Read the given statements regarding mid brain. Identify the correct one.<br>I. Located between the thalamus / hypothalamus.<br>II. Posses a canal named cerebral aqueduct which passes through it. <br>III. Dorsal part consists of 4 lobes.','[{"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All statements regarding mid brain are correct.The midbrain is located between the thalamus/hypothalamus regions of forebrain and pons of hindbrain. It has canal called cerebral aqueduct. In its dorsal portion, midbrain consists four round swellings ( lobes) called as corpora quadregemina.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11656,'biology',9,27,50,'I) Diploid sporophyte is generally multicellular in algae<br> II) Ovules of gymnosperms are not enclosed by ovary wall<br>III) <i>Salvinia</i> is homosporous <br>IV) In phaeophyceae, food is stored as mannitol and laminarin <br>Of the above statements find the wrong statements','[{"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In algae, diploid sporophyte is represented by unicellular zygote. Salvinia is a heterosporous pteridophyte.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
