(11668,'biology',9,25,46,'A plant shows thallus level of organization. It shows rhizoids and is haploid. It needs water to complete its life cycle because the male gametes are motile. Identify the group to which it belongs to','[{"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monocots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bryophytes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Plants from monocots and gymnosperms do not need water for fertilization. Byrophytes and pteridophytes need water for fertilization. But pteridophytes have true roots. Hence,‘d’ is the correct option.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exempler','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11669,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Gluconeogenesis, lipolysis and proteolysis means','[{"text": "Synthesis of glucose and breakdown of lipids and proteins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Synthesis of glucose, lipids and proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Breakdown of glucose, lipids and proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Glucocorticoids are steroid hormones secreted by zona glomerulosa of adrenal cortex. The hormones are involved in metabolism of carbohydrates, proteins and fats.<br>These function in gluconeogenesis or synthesis of glucose from sources other than carbohydrates, breakdown of fats (lipolysis) and proteolysis (formation of amino acids from proteins).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11670,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Read the following statements :-<br>I. Impulse transmission across an electrical synapse is always faster than that across a chemical synapse<br>II. Limbic system is composed of pons, medulla and cerebellum.<br>III. Cerebral cortex is made up of white matter because myelinated axons are concentrated here.<br>IV. Association areas are responsible for memory, intersensory association and communication<br>V. At the site of excitation, $\\mathrm{Ca}^{+2}$ ions channels open and restore the resting potential of the membrane<br>Which statements are correct?','[{"text": "I, II and V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'At the site of excitation, $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ion channels close and restore the resting membrane potential Cerebral cortex is made up of grey matter, it is made of non- myelinated fibres. Limbic system is made up of amygdala, hippocampus, septal nuclei and mammilary bodies. Pons, medulla and cerebellum are parts of hind brain.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
