(11676,'biology',9,28,53,'If the diploid number of a flowering plant is 36. What would be the chromosome number in its endosperm','[{"text": "36", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "18", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "54", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "72", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Endosperm is formed after fusion between a haploid male gamete and diploid secondary nucleus. Thus, endosperm has triploid nucleus; which will have three times the number of chromosomes as in a haploid nucleus. Here, 2n = 36. Therefore, 3n = 54.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exempler','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
