(11823,'biology',90,1334,3217,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The released neurotransmitters bind to their specific receptors, present on the post-synaptic membrane.<br></div><div class="column-right">The new potential developed may be either excitatory or inhibitory.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11826,'biology',9,24,45,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Carrageen is a good emulsifying agent.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It is got from <em>Sargassum </em>and <em>Porphyra</em>.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Carrageens are got from <em>Chondrus</em> and <em>Gigartina</em>; it is a good emulsifier in ice creams, chocolates, toothpastes, sauces and cosmetics. It is also used as clearing and finishing agent.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11827,'biology',90,1335,3218,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The human brain is well protected by the skull.<br></div><div class="column-right">Inside the skull, the brain is covered by cranial meninges consisting of an inner layer called dura mater, a very thin middle layer called arachnoid and an outer layer called pia mater.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement-A is correct. Inside the skull, the brain is covered by cranial meninges consisting of an outer layer called dura mater, a very thin middle layer called arachnoid and an inner layer called pia mater.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11828,'biology',91,1405,3347,'Identify the correct pair','[{"text": "Ovary - scrotum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testis - In pelvic cavity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'(1) Ovary- scrotum<br>(2) Testis - In pelvic cavity both are incorrect, the correct answer would be<br>(1) Ovary- In pelvic cavity<br>(2) Testis -scrotum',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11829,'biology',9,24,44,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Algin is a hydrocolloid.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It is obtained from <em>Laminaria </em>and <em>Fucus</em>.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Algin is hydrocolloid obtained from brown algae <em>Laminaria, Alaria</em> and <em>Fucus</em>. It is a thickner and gelating agent.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11830,'biology',90,1336,3219,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The cerebral hemispheres are connected by a tract of nerve fibres called corpus callosum.<br></div><div class="column-right">Cerebrum forms the major part of the human brain.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11831,'biology',91,1405,3347,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Testis<br>B. Leydig cells<br>C. Ovaries<br>D. Corpus luteum</div><div class="column-right">P. Produces testosterone<br>Q. Ruptured follicle formed after ovulation <br>R. Composed of seminiferous tubules and stromal tissue<br>S. Composed of ovarian follicles & stromal tissues</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A - R,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - P,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - S, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - R, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - R,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - P,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - Q, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B -S,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - P, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11833,'biology',9,27,50,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cycas has two types of root, taproot system and corolloid roots.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Coralloid roots contain Anabaena.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In <i>Cycas</i>, the primary root persists and forms a tap root system, some of lateral roots branch repeatedly to form dwarfed dichotomous branching, they are called the corolloid roots or corallorhiza. They become inhibited by blue green alga <i>Anabeana cycadacearum</i>. The blue green algae fixes atmospheric nitrogen and thus plants get fixed nitrogen.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11834,'biology',91,1405,3347,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A.Testosterone<br>B. Estrogen<br>C. Progesterone</div><div class="column-right">P. Secreted mainly by growing ovarian follicles<br>Q. Play major role in the process of spermatogenesis<br>R. Supports pregnancy</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  R,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B  -  P,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  R,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B  -  Q,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  Q,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B  -  R,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  Q,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B  -  P,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Q, B-P, C-R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11835,'biology',90,1336,3219,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The cerebrum wraps around a structure called thalamus<br></div><div class="column-right">The cerebral cortex is referred to as the grey matter and has axons.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement-A is correct. The cerebral cortex is referred to as the grey matter and has cell bodies.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11837,'biology',9,24,42,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Isogamy is a primitive type of sexual reproduction.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The gametes are of different sizes.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The fusing gametes in the lower forms of algae are alike in size, structure and behaviour, they are indistinguishable as to sex, and such gametes are called isogametes. Sexual reproduction which involves the fusion of isogametes is termed as isogamy; it is a primitive type of sexual reproduction.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11838,'biology',91,1406,3348,'By which organ the hormones are secreted which serve non endocrine functions otherwise?','[{"text": "Heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kidney", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GIT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of the options are correct - heart, kidney and GIT.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11839,'biology',90,1336,3219,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The limbic system is located between the thalamus/ hypothalamus of the forebrain and pons of the hindbrain.<br></div><div class="column-right">The cerebral medulla is referred to as the white matter and has axons .</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement-B is correct.The midbrain is located between the thalamus/hypothalamus of the forebrain and pons of the hindbrain.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11840,'biology',9,25,46,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> All Bryophytes are land dwellers.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Water is not necessary to complete their life cycle.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both are incorrect. All Bryophytes are not land dwellers. Water is necessary to complete their life cycle.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11842,'biology',91,1406,3348,'Select the incorrect matching:<br>Hormone Target organ<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Secretin &nbsp; - &nbsp; &nbsp;Pancreas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "CCK - &nbsp;Pancreas and Gallbladder", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ANF &nbsp;- &nbsp; Atrial wall", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gastrin - &nbsp; Gastric glands", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'ANF - atrial wall is incorrect, its target organ is blood vessels, vaso dilator.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11843,'biology',90,1338,3221,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Pons consists of fibre tracts that interconnect different regions of the brain<br></div><div class="column-right">Cerebellum has a very convoluted surface in order to provide the additional space for many more neurons.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11844,'biology',9,25,46,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> <em>Sphagnum </em>is slowly carbonised, compressed and fossilised over thousands of years to produce a dark spongy mass called peat.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Peat helps to keep soil porous and it also improves water holding capacity of soil.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<em>Sphagnum</em> peat mass is slowly carbonised, compressed and fossilised over thousands of years to produce a dark spongy mass called peat. It has a remarkable ability to manage water efficiently and holds to nutrients that would otherwise leach out of the soil.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11845,'biology',91,1406,3348,'Which of the following peptide hormone is secreted by non-endocrine gland?','[{"text": "ANF", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Erythropoietin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gastric inhibitory peptide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Endocrine cells present in different parts of the gastro-intestinal tract secrete four major peptide hormones, namely gastrin, secretin, cholecystokinin (CCK) and gastric inhibitory peptide (GIP), ANF, Erythropoietin are also peptide hormones',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11846,'biology',90,1338,3221,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Three major regions make up the brain stem; midbrain, pons and medulla of the cerebrum.<br></div><div class="column-right">Brain stem forms the connections between the brain and spinal cord.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement-B is correct. Three major regions make up the brain stem; midbrain, pons and medulla oblongata.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11848,'biology',9,24,45,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Red algae contribute in producing coral reefs.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Some red algae secrete and deposit calcium carbonate over their walls.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Red algae make an important contribution to the growth of coral reefs, some red algae deposits calcium carbonate in their cell walls.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11849,'biology',91,1406,3348,'Which of the following are peptide hormones?','[{"text": "Cholecystokinin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gastrin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Endocrine cells present in different parts of the gastro-intestinal tract secrete four major peptide hormones, namely gastrin, secretin, cholecystokinin (CCK) and gastric inhibitory peptide (GIP)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11851,'biology',9,27,50,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Sporocarps are of two types, microsporangia bearing microsporophyll and megasporangia bearing megasporophylls.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It is called as Heterospory.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Heterospory is the phenomenon in which two kinds of spores are borne by the same plant. These spores differ in size, the smaller one is known as microspore and the larger one is megaspore. The microspore germinates to form the male gametophyte and megaspore germinates to form female gametophyte. The male gametophyte releases the male gametes and these reach the female gametophyte to fuse with the egg. The development of the zygote takes place inside the female gametophyte this ensures proper development of zygote. The zygote develops into future sporophyte. Heterospory is thus considered an important step in evolution as it is a precursor to seed habit.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11852,'biology',91,1406,3348,'The hormone ANF is secreted by','[{"text": "Graafian follicle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Atrial wall of heart", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The hormone, \'Atrial Natriuretic Factor\' is secreted by Atrial wall of heart',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11853,'biology',90,1339,3222,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The entire process of response to a peripheral nervous stimulation that never occurs involuntarily, i.e., without conscious effort or thought is called a reflex action.<br></div><div class="column-right">Reflex action.never requires the involvement of a part of the central nervous system.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both statements are incorrect. The entire process of response to a peripheral nervous stimulation that occurs involuntarily, i.e., without conscious effort or thought is called a reflex action. Reflex action.requires the involvement of a part of the central nervous system.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11854,'biology',9,23,40,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Chemotaxonomy uses chemical constituents and secondary metabolites.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It uses the chemical constituents of the plants to resolve confusions.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'It is a branch of taxonomy that uses chemical constituents for plant classification; it uses chemical constituents and secondary metabolites for finding out relationships amongst plants.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11855,'biology',91,1406,3348,'ANF means','[{"text": "Anti -natriuretic factor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Atrial Natriuretic Factor", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arterial Natriuretic Factor", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'ANF means Atrial Natriuretic Factor',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12008,'biology',91,1405,3347,'Fall in levels of oestrogen and progesterone in blood stimulate the production of','[{"text": "GH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prolactin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "TSH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GnRH", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{GnRH}$ is secreted from hypothalamus in response to low levels of sex hormones oestrogen and progesterone.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11857,'biology',90,1339,3222,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">PNS processes and analyses all the sensory inputs<br></div><div class="column-right">Receptors receive motor impulses</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both statements are incorrect. CNS processes and analyses all the sensory inputs Receptors receive stimulus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11858,'biology',9,25,46,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Bryophyta dominant stage is gametophyte<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Gametophyte is green and performs photosynthesis','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The main plant body of the bryophyte is haploid. It produces gametes, hence is called a gametophyte. It is free-living.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11859,'biology',91,1406,3348,'\'ANF\' is a hormone, which','[{"text": "Is secreted in response to increased BP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decreases BP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Causes vasodilation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Atrial Natriuretic Factor (ANF) is a hormone which decreases blood pressure. ANF is secreted when blood pressure is high and causes dilation of the blood thus, option(4) is correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11861,'biology',90,1340,3223,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Olfactory epithelium that consists of three kinds of cells.<br></div><div class="column-right">Olfactory bulb are a pair of broad bean-shaped organ</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement-A is correct.Olfactory bulbs are a pair of broad bean-sized organs.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11862,'biology',9,28,53,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Angiosperms have two classes: Dicotyledonae and Monocotyledonae.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Dicotyledonae are advanced in evolutionary history.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Monocotyledons are rather small group of plants compared to genetically diverse dicotyledons. Monocots have more genes, moved from chloroplast genome with better controlled photosynthesis. Adding  ${C_4}$ mechanism, average monocot is better adaptable to diverse and harsh environment comparing to average dicot. Monocots do not show secondary growth yet considered more advanced.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11863,'biology',91,1406,3348,'Juxtaglomerular cells secrete','[{"text": "ANF", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Erythropoietin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rennin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The juxtaglomerular cells of kidney produce a peptide hormone called renin, which increases blood pressure through agiotensin-II and crythropoietin which stimulates the formation of RBCs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11865,'biology',9,28,53,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Bryophytes and tracheophytes have an embryo stage in their lifecycle.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Embryophytes are terrestrial plants.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Bryophytes and tracheophytes possess an embryo stage; they are collectively termed as embryophyta. Bryophytes and tracheophytes are terrestrial plants, nonvascular and vascular respectively.',NULL,'Hard','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11919,'biology',9,27,50,'Examine the figures A, B, C and D. In which one of the four options all the items A, B, C and D are correct?<br>','[{"text": "<i> A - Chara, B - Marchantia, C - Fucus, D - Pinus </i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i> A - Equisetum, B - Ginko, C - Selaginella, D - Lycopodium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i> A - Selaginella, B - Equisetum, C - Salvinia, D - Ginko </i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i> A - Funaria, B - Adiantum, C - Salvinia, D - Riccia </i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A - Selaginella, B - Equisetum, C -  Salvinia, D - Gingko',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_11919_question_1.png'),
(11867,'biology',91,1406,3348,'The hormone, erythropoietin','[{"text": "Stimulates erythropoiesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inhibits erythropoiesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inhibits platelet formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Breaks down RBC", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Erythropoietin is a glyoprotein hormone that controlserythropoiesis or red blood cells production. It is a cytokine(protein signaling molecule) for erythrocytes (red blood cells) precursors in the bone marrow.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11869,'biology',9,28,53,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Double fertilization is unique to angiosperms.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Triple fusion occurs in double fertilization.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'S.G. Nawaschin was the first to show that the sperms released by a pollen tube are involved in fertilization, they fertilize two different elements of the embryo sac, the phenomenon is unique to angiosperms and it is\ncalled as double fertilization. The nucleus of the one of sperm fuses with the egg nucleus and that of the other migrates to the central product, the secondary nucleus. Most of the plants have two polar nuclei, consequently the second fertilization involves the fusion of 3 nuclei, and the phenomenon is called triple fusion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11870,'biology',91,1406,3348,'Gastrin hormone acts on gastric glands and','[{"text": "Stimulates the secretion of $\\\\mathrm{HCl}$ and pepsinogen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inhibits the secretion of pepsinogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimulates the secretion of $\\\\mathrm{HCl}$ and pepsin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Gastrin hormone acts on gastric glands and stimulates the secretion of $\\mathrm{HCl}$ and pepsinogen, and not pepsin (active form of pepsinogen)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11873,'biology',9,29,52,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> <em>Spirogyra</em> shows haplontic life cycle.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Zygotic meiosis occurs in <em>Spirogyra</em>.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Life cycle characterized by a haploid thallus and zygotic meiosis is called haplontic life cycle. It is called as haplobiontic because only a single type of free living individual is involved in the life cycle and <em>Spirogyra</em> shows haplontic life cycle and therefore, it also shows zygotic nucleus.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11874,'biology',91,1406,3348,'Which hormone acts on the exocrine part of pancreas and stimulates the secretion of water and bicarbonate ions?','[{"text": "Gastric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "CCK", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pancreatin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Secretin, a digestive hormone secreted by the wall of the upper part of the small intestine(the duodenum) acts on the exocrine pancreas and stimulates secretion of water and bicarbonate ions. Secretin is a polypeptide made up of 27 amino acids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11967,'biology',9,27,50,'Male gametophyte with least number of cells is present in','[{"text": "<i>Pteris</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Funaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Lilium</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Pinus</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lilium, an angiosperm bears the least called male gametophyte as compared to Funaria (bryophyte). As we progress from algae to angiosperms, gametophytes get reduced.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11876,'biology',9,24,42,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Bryophytes possess archegonium as a female sex organ.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Algae also possess the archegonium.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The female sex organ of the bryophytes i s a remarkable structure, it appears for the first time in the liverworts and mosses, it continues in the pteridophytes. Archegonium is absent in thallophytes (algae and fungi). Sex organs in them are male gametes and female gametes.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11878,'biology',91,1406,3348,'GIP (Gastric Inhibitory Peptide)','[{"text": "Stimulates the gastric secretion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inhibits the gastric secretion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inhibits the gastric secretion and motility", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gastric inhibitory Polypeptide (GIP), functions to neutralise stomach acid to protect the small intestine from acid damage. It reduces the rate at which food is transferred through the stomach and inhibit the GI motility and secretion of hydrochloric acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11879,'biology',9,25,48,'In a moss the sporophyte','[{"text": "is partially parasitic on the gametophyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Produces gametes that given rise to the gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arises from a spore produced from the gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Manufactures food for itself, as well as for the gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In mosses, the sporophyte is not free-living. It is parasitic, attached to the photosynthetic gametophyte and derives nourishment from it.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11881,'biology',91,1406,3348,'Cholecystokinin (CCK) acts on','[{"text": "Pancreas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gall bladder", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Liver", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'CCK acts on both pancreas and gall bladder and stimulate the secretion of pancreatic enzyme and bile juice, respectively',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11883,'biology',9,25,46,'Moss peat is used as a packing material for sending flowers and live plants to distant places because-','[{"text": "It is easily available", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is hygroscopic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It reduces transpiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It serves as a disinfectant", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Species of Sphagnum, a moss, provide peat that have long been used as fuel, and as packing material for trans-shipment of living material because of their capacity to hold water (hygroscopic).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11884,'biology',91,1406,3348,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Atrial natriuretic factor <br>B. Erythropoietin<br>C. Gastrin<br>D. Secretin</div><div class="column-right">P. Stimulates formation of RBC<br>Q. Causes dilation of the blood vessels<br>R. Stimulates secretion of water and bicarbonate ions<br>S. Stimulates the secretion of ${\\text{HCl}}$ and pepsinogen</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A - P,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - R, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - P,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - S, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - R,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - Q, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - P, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11887,'biology',9,27,50,'In gymnosperms, the pollen chamber represents','[{"text": "A cavity in the ovule in which pollen grains are stored after pollination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "An opening in the mega gametophyte through which the pollen approaches the egg", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The megasporangium in which pollengrains develop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A cell in the pollen grain in which the sperms are formed.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In gymnosperms, the pollen chamber is a cavity in the ovule in which pollen grains are stored after pollination. Within this chamber, the generative cell divides to form two male gametes and the pollen cell starts elongating to form pollen tube.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11888,'biology',91,1406,3348,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Cholecystokinin<br>B. Gastric inhibitory peptide<br>C. Growth factors<br>D. Juxtaglomerular cells</div><div class="column-right">P. Secretes  peptide harmone called erythropoietin<br>Q. Stimulates secretion of pancreatic enzyme and bile juice<br>R. Inhibits gastric secretion and motility<br>S. Essential for normal growth of tissues and repairing</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A - P,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - R,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - Q, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - P,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - R, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - R,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - S, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - P}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - R,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - Q, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11889,'biology',90,1334,3217,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Transmission of a nerve impulse across a synapse is brought by a neurotransmitter.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> A neurotransmitter is necessary to transmit a nerve impulse across a synapse because there is a small gap, the synaptic cleft between the two neurons at the synapse.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The action potential simply travels from one cell to the next through specialised channels, called gap junctions, which connect the two cells. Most cells, however, communicate via chemical synapses. Such cells are separated by a space called a synaptic cleft and thus cannot transmit action potentials directly. Instead, chemicals called neurotransmitters are used to communicate the signal from one cell to the next. Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11890,'biology',9,26,49,'In the prothallus of a vascular cryptogam, the antherozoids and eggs mature at different times, as a result','[{"text": "There is high degree of sterility", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One can conclude that the plant is apomictic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Self fertilisation is prevented", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "There is no change in success rate of fertilisation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pteridophytes exhibit dichogamy, the maturation of male and female sex organs at different times to prevent self fertilization.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
