(11897,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Intracellular receptors are mostly','[{"text": "Cytoplamic receptors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Membrane receptors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nuclear receptors", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Hormone receptors present on the cell membrane of the target cellsare called membrane bound receptors and receptors preset inside the target cells are called intracellular receptors, which are mostly nuclear receptors (present in the nucleus).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11898,'biology',9,29,52,'In which one of the following male and female gametophytes do not have free - living independent existence?','[{"text": "<i>Polytrichum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Cedrus</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Pteris</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Funaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cedrus, a gymnosperm has dependent male and female gametophytes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11899,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Among the following sets of hormones, which one contain only peptide hormones?','[{"text": "Epinephrine, cortisol, pituitary hormones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "TSH, hypothalamic hormones, oestradiol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insulin, progesterone, cortisol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insulin, glucagon, pituitary hormones", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Set of hormones given in option (4)contain only peptide hormones. These insulin, glucagon and pituitary hormone.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11900,'biology',90,1333,3216,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Imbalance in $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}, \\mathrm{K}^{+}$and proteins generate the resting potential.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> To maintain unequal distribution of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$and $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$neurons use electrical energy.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In a resting neuron, there are concentration gradients across the membrane for $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$and $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$. Ions move down their gradients via channels, leading to a separation of charge that creates the resting potential. The membrane is much more permeable to $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$than to $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$so the resting potential is close to the equilibrium potential of $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$. Both Assertion and Reason are false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11902,'biology',9,26,49,'Which one of the following is a vascular cryptogam?','[{"text": "<i>Ginkgo</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Marchantia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Cedrus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Equisetum</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In this, Equisetum is pteridophyte so it considered as vascular cryptogam.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
