(11908,'biology',90,1336,3219,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Amygdala are present in superficial region of cerebral hemisphere.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> They do not form a part of limbic system like hippocampus','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The amygdala is one of two almond- shaped groups of nuclei located deep and medially with in the temporal lobes of the brain in complex vertebrates like humans. The limbic system is a complex set of structures that lies on both sides of the thalamus, just under the cerebrum. It includes the hypothalamus, the hippocampus, the amygdala, and several other nearby areas.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11909,'biology',9,26,49,'Which one of the following is considered important in the development of seed habit?','[{"text": "Heterospory", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Haplontic life cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Free - living gametophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dependent sporophyte", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Heterospory, first observed in pteridophytes Salvinia and Selaginella is a precursor to seed habit.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11910,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Following hormones are iodothyronines','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{T}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{T}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "TCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'iodothyronines are thyroid hormones',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11912,'biology',90,1333,3216,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Acetylcholine transmits the nerve impulse across a synapse<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Acetylcholine is secreted by adrenergic neurons','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Acetylcholine is a neurotransmitter released from nerve endings (terminals) in both the peripheral and the central nervous systems. It is synthesised within the nerve terminal from choline. Most neuromuscular junctions use the neurotransmitter, acetylcholine, which is broken down by the enzyme acetylcholinesterase. Hence, the given Assertion is true but the Reason is false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11913,'biology',9,28,53,'Which one of the following plants is monoecious?','[{"text": "<i>Pinus</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Cycas</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Papaya", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Marchantia</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pinus is a monoecious gymnosperm.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11914,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Which is steroid hormone?','[{"text": "GH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insulin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aldosterone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Epinephrine", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Aldosterone is steroid hormone of the adrenal cortex.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11915,'biology',90,1340,3223,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Stimulus is interpreted by the brain and not by sense organs.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Sense organs act as transducers transforming the stimulus energy.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The sensory nervous system is a part of the nervous system responsible for processing sensory information. A sensory system consists of sensory neurons (including the sensory receptor cells), neural pathways, and parts of the brain involved in sensory perception. Thus, both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11917,'biology',9,24,45,'Algae have cell wall made up of','[{"text": "Cellulose, Galactans and Mannans", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hemicellulose, Pectins and Proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pectins, Cellulose and Proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellulose, Hemicellulose and Pectins", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Majority of algae possess definite cellwall. It is made up of different chemical components namely Cellulose, Galactans and Mannans.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11918,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Which of the following hormones do not act by a second messenger system?','[{"text": "GH and FSH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epinephrine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insulin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oestrogen", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Oestrogen is a hormones which interact with intracellular receptors e.g., steroid hormones, iodothyronines, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11980,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Following is the diagram of mechanism of steroid hormone. Identify type of hormone and receptor in given diagram.','[{"text": "A- FSH, B- Membrane bound receptor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Estrogen, B- membrane bound receptor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Estrogen, B- Nuclear receptor", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A- FSH, B- Nuclear receptor", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-Estrogen, B- Nuclear receptor',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/91_11980_question_1.png'),
(11920,'biology',90,1333,3216,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In depolarisation process, there is a positive charge on the outer side of the fibre and a negative charge on its inner side.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> During depolarisation, permeability of plasma membrane increase for sodium ions, so $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ ions move to outer side of the membrane and $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$enter the nerve fibre.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During depolarisation, the charge within the cell rapidly shifts from negative to positive. For this rapid change to take place within the interior of the cell, several events must occur along the plasma membrane of the cell as well. While the sodium potassium pump continues to work, the voltage gated ion channels that had been closed while the cell was at resting potential have been opened by an electrical stimulus. As the sodium rushes back into the cell the positive sodium ions raise the charge inside the cell from negative to positive. Once the interior of the cell becomes positively charged, depolarisation of the cell is complete. Thus, both Assertion and Reason are false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11922,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Chemically epinephrine is','[{"text": "Amino acid derivative", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Peptide hormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Steroid hormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Iodothyronines", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'amino-acid derivatives (e.g., epinephrine)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11923,'biology',9,29,52,'The gametophyte is not an independent, freeliving generation in','[{"text": "<em>Polytrichum</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Adiantum</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Marchantia</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Pinus</em>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pinus - gymnosperms do not have free living , independent gametophytes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11924,'biology',90,1332,3215,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Myelin sheath insulates nerve fibre and prevents its depolarisation.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Nerve impulses are conducted more rapidly in non-myelinated fibres than myelinated ones.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Myelin acts as an insulator that prevents current from leaving the axon, increasing the speed of action potential conduction. By insulating the axon for particular lengths and then having nodes for ion exchange, the myelin sheath increases the speed of transmission of an impulse. Thus, both Assertion and Reason are false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11925,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Which of the following endocrine glands produce hormones that are peptides, amines?','[{"text": "Testes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenal medulla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anterior pituitary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Hormones of adrenal medulla - adrenaline and Anterior pituitary- peptide hormone',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11927,'biology',9,29,52,'Male and female gametophytes are independent and free-living in','[{"text": "Mustard", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Castor</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pinus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Sphagnum</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Gametophytes are free-living in bryophytes such as Sphagnum (bog moss).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11928,'biology',90,1340,3223,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Human sense of smell is relatively poor<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Olfactory receptors are limited to only small areas of the nasal chambers.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The human sense of smell is commonly believed to be relatively poor compared to that of other mammals, including great apes. Olfactory receptors are limited to only small areas of the nasal chambers. Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11929,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Hormones, which interact with membrane bound receptors normally','[{"text": "Generate secondary messengers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Do not enter the target cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Hormones, which interact with membrane bound receptor normally do not enter the target cell, but generate secondary messenger (e.g. cyclic AMP, $\\mathrm{IP}_{3} \\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$, etc.), which in turn regulate cellular metabolism.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11930,'biology',9,27,50,'Consider the following four statements whether they are correct or incorrect<br>A. The sporophyte in liverworts is more elaborate than that in mosses<br>B. <i>Salvinia</i> is heterosporous<br>C. The life cycle in all seed bearing plants is diplontic<br>D. In <i>Pinus</i> male and female cones are borne on different trees.<br>The two wrong statements together are','[{"text": "A and C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and D", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B and C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and B", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The sporophyll in mosses is more elaborate than liverworts. The male and female cones or strobili are borne on the same tree in pinus. In cycas, male cones and megasporophyll are borne on different trees.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11933,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Which one of the following is a second messenger in hormone action?','[{"text": "Calcium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{IP}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "cAMP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Second messengers are cyclic $\\mathrm{AMP}, \\mathrm{IP}_{3}$, calcium ions, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11934,'biology',9,26,49,'Archegoniophore is present in','[{"text": "<em>Marchantia</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<em>Chara</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Adiantum</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prothallus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<em>Marchantia </em>is dioecious; consist of Archegoniophore and Antheridiophore in separate thallus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11936,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Steroid hormones typically alter the activity of target cells by','[{"text": "Activating primary messenger", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Activating secondary messenger", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interacting with nuclear receptors", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Steroid hormones are the lipid soluble hormones and are categorised as hydrophobic hormones. They directly pass through the cell membrane and interact with intracellular receptors present inside the cell (generally within the nucleus).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11938,'biology',9,25,47,'Examine the figure given below and select the correct option giving all the four parts (A, B, C, D) rightly identified:<br>','[{"text": "A - Archegoniophore, B - Female thallus, C - Gemma cup, D - Rhizoids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Archegoniophore, B - Female thallus, C - Bud, D - Food", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Seta, B - Sporophyte, C - Protonema, D - Rhizoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Archegoniophore, B - Male thallus, C - Globule, D - Roots", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The given diagram is the female thallus of marchantia in which A, B, C, D are <br> Archegoniophore, Female thallus, Gemma cups and Rhizoids.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/9_11938_question_1.png'),
(11939,'biology',91,1407,3349,'What is the mechanism of action of steroid hormones?','[{"text": "They enter into the target cells and bind with specific receptor and activate specific gene expression or chromosome function", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They bind to cell membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hormones which interact with intracellular receptors (e.g., steroid hormones, iodothyronines, etc.) mostly regulate gene expression or chromosome function by the interaction of hormone-receptor complex with the genome',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11982,'biology',9,28,53,'Male gametophyte in angiosperms produces','[{"text": "Three sperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two sperms and a vegetative cell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Single sperm and a vegetative cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Single sperm and two vegetative cells", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mature male gametophyte is three celled.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11940,'biology',90,1332,3215,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Multipolar neurons have two or more axons and one dendrite.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Bipolar neurons are found usually in the cerebral cortex.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Based on the number of axons and dendrites, the neurons are divided into three types, i.e., multipolar (with one axon and two or more dendrites; found in the cerebral cortex), bipolar (with one axon and one dendrite; found in the retina of eye) and unipolar (cell body with one axon only: found usually in the embryonic stage).',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11942,'biology',9,25,46,'Compared with the gametophytes of the bryophytes, the gametophytes of vascular plants tend to be','[{"text": "Smaller but to have sex organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Larger but to have smaller sex organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Larger and to have larger sex organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Smaller and to have smaller sex organs", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Compared with the gametophytes of the bryophytes, the gametophytes of vascular plants tend to be smaller and have smaller sex organs.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11943,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Progesterone and testosterone hormones bind to','[{"text": "Cytoplasmic receptors", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Membrane receptors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Enzyme linked proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Progesterone and testosterone are female and male sex hormones, respectively. Chemically, these are steroid hormones (lipid soluble) which easily pass through the cell membrane and bind to specific (cytoplasmic) intracellular receptors.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11944,'biology',90,1333,3216,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The resting membrane of the neuron exhibits polarity of charges.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The outer surface of the axonal membrane possesses a negative charge while its inner surface becomes positively charged.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When a nueron is not conducting any impulse, i.e., resting, the axonal membrane is comparatively more permeable to potassium ions $\\left( {{{\\rm{K}}^{\\rm{ + }}}} \\right)$ and nearly impermeable to sodium ionw $\\left( {{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}} \\right)$. Similarly, the membrane is impermeable to negatively charged proteins present in the axoplasm. Consequently, the axoplasm inside the axon contains high concentration of ${{\\rm{K}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ and negatively charged proteins and low concentration of ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$. These ionic gradients across the resting membrane are maintained by the active transpoprt of ions by he sodium - potassium pump which transports ${\\rm{3N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ outwards for ${\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{K}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ into the cell. As a result, the outer surface of the axonal membrane possesses a positive charge while its inner surface becomes negatively charged and therefore is polarised.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11945,'biology',9,26,49,'<i>Selaginella</i> and <i>Salvinia</i> are considered to represent a significant step towards evolution of seed habit because','[{"text": "Female gametophyte is free and gets dispersed - like seeds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Female gametophyte lacks archegonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Megaspores possess endosperm and embryo sorrunded by coat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo develops in female gametophyte which is retained on parent sporophyte", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Selaginella and Salvinia produce two kinds of spores: macro and micro spores known as heterosporous. It germinates and gives rise to male and female gametophytes, the female gametes in these plants are retained on the parent sporophytes for variable period. This event is significant step towards evolution of seed habit.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11947,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A  Hormone receptors<br>B  Membrane bound receptors<br>C  Nuclear receptors</div><div class="column-right">P  Present in the nucleus of target cells<br>Q  Located in target tissues only<br>R  Present on the cell membrane of the target cells</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  P,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B  -  R,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  Q,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B  -  R,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  R,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B  -  P,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  Q,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B  -  P,}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Q, B-R, C-P.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11993,'biology',91,1394,3336,'Select the incorrect statement from the following:','[{"text": "Neural coordination is short-lived.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neural coordination is fast.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neural system provides point to point rapid coordination among organs.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nerve fibres innervates all the cells of body so cellular function be continuously regulated.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The neural coordination is fast but shortlived. As the nerve fibres do not innervate all cells of the body and the cellular functions need to be continuously regulated',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11948,'biology',90,1336,3219,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Association areas are neither clearly sensory nor motor in function.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Association areas are responsible for complex functions like intersensory associations, memory and communication.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The cerebral cortex contains motor areas, sensory areas and large regions that are neither clearly sensory nor motor in function. These regions are called the association areas which are responsible for complex functions like intersensory associations, memory and communication. Association area is concerned with the reception of sensory impulses and start of motor impulses.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11949,'biology',9,25,46,'Which one of the following is common to multicellular fungi, filamentous algae and protonema of mosses?','[{"text": "Diplontic life cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Members of kingdom plantae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mode of nutrition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiplication by fragmentation", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Multicellular fungi, filamentous algae and protonema of mosses multiply by fragmentation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11950,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A  Protein hormone<br>B  Steroids hormone<br>C  Iodothyronines hormone<br>D  Amino acid derivatives hormone</div><div class="column-right">P  Thyroid harmones<br>Q  Cortisol and estradiol<br>R  Epinephrine and nor-epinephrine<br>S  Insulin and Glucagon</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - P, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - R, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - P, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - P,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - R,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - S, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-S, B-Q, C-P, D-R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11951,'biology',90,1338,3221,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Medulla contains centres which control respiration, cardiovascular reflexes and gastric secretions.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Medulla contains several neurosecretory cells which secrete hormones.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The medulla contains centres which control respiration, cardiovascular reflexes are gastric secretions. The hypothalamus is the basal part of diencephalon (forebrain) which contains several groups of neurosecretory cells called nuclei that produce hormones.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11953,'biology',9,25,46,'The plant body is thalloid in','[{"text": "<i>Sphagnum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Salvinia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Marchantia</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Funaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Marchantia belongs to hepaticopsida. These are bryophytes in which the thallus is dorsiventrally flattened and closely appressed to the substrate.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11954,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A Membrane bound receptors<br>B Intracellular receptors<br>C FSH receptors<br>D Estrogen receptors</div><div class="column-right">P &nbsp;Present on ovarian cell membrane<br>Q &nbsp;Generate secondary messengers like Cyclic AMP<br>R &nbsp;Present in uterine cytoplasm<br>S &nbsp;Regulate gene expressions or chromosome function</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A - P,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - Q, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - R, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - S,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - P, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - P,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - R,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - S, }}\\\\,{\\\\text{D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-P , B-S, C-Q, D-R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11955,'biology',90,1339,3222,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Reflex arc comprises of at least one afferent neuron, one efferent neuron and a part of PNS.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The afferent neuron receives signal from a sensory organ and transmits the motor impulse via a dorsal nerve root into the CNS.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The reflex pathway comprises at least one afferent neuron (receptor) and one efferent (effector or excitor) neuron appropriately arranged in a series. The afferent neuron receives signal from a sensory organ and transmits the sensory impulse via a dorsal nerve root into the CNS (at the level of spinal cord). The efferent neuron then carries signals from CNS to the effector. The stimulus and response thus forms a reflex arc.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(11956,'biology',9,28,53,'Which one of the following pairs is wrongly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Mustard – Synergids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ginkgo</i> –Archegonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Salvinia</i> – Prothallus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Viriods – RNA", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The Salvinia is advanced and plant body is differentiated.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
