(12030,'biology',90,1338,3221,'The human hind brain comprises three parts, one of which is<br>','[{"text": "Spinal cord", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpus callosum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cerebellum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Hindbrain, also called rhombencephalon, region of the developing vertebrate brain that is composed of the medulla oblongata, the pons, and the cerebellum.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12031,'biology',9,25,46,'Which one is wrongly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Gemma cups &ndash; <em> Marchantia</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biflagellate zoospores &ndash; <em> </em>Brown algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uniflagellate gametes &ndash; <em> Polysiphonia</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Unicellular organism &ndash; <em> Chlorella</em>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<em>Polysiphonia </em>belongs to class Rhodophyceae (red algae), where they have non-motile or non-flagellated gametes',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12032,'biology',91,1398,3340,'Identify the correct statement about melatonin','[{"text": "Pineal gland located in midbrain secretes melatonin.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Melatonin influences metabolism, pigmentation, the menstrual cycle as well as our defense capability", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Melatonin plays a very important role in the regulation of a 12-hour (diurnal) rhythm of our body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Melatonin influences metabolism, pigmentation, the menstrual cycle as well as our defense capability is the correct statement.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12033,'biology',90,1334,3217,'A person entering an empty room suddenly finds a snake right in front on opening the door. Which one of the following is likely to happen in his neurohormonal control system?<br>','[{"text": "Neurotransmitters diffuse rapidly across the cleft and transmit a nerve impulse.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sympathetic nervous system is activated releasing epinephrine and norepinephrine from adrenal medulla.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hypothalamus activates the parasympathetic division of brain.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sympathetic nervous system is activated releasing epinephrine and norepinephrine from adrenal cortex.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Epinephrine and norepinephrine are secreted by adrenal medulla in response to stress or during emergency. These are called emergency hormones or hormones of flight, fright or fight.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12035,'biology',9,27,50,'Which of the following statements is correct?','[{"text": "Horsetails are gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Selaginella</i> is heterosporous, while Salvinia is homosporous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovules are not enclosed by ovary wall in gymnosperms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stems are usually unbranched in both <i> Cycas </i>and <i>Cedrus</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gymnosperms are naked seeded plants because the ovule is not enclosed by ovarian wall. Horsetails are Pteridophytes. Both Selaginella and Salvinia are heterosporous. Stem in Cycas is unbranched and Stem in Cedrus is branched.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12036,'biology',91,1400,3342,'Identify the correct set of hormones<br>i. weakens the bone<br>ii. strengthens the bones','[{"text": "i- TCT ii- PTH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i- PTH ii- PTH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i- TCT ii- TCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i- PTH ii- TCT", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{PTH}$ increases calcium resorption to increase blood calcium levels and TCT increases calcium deposition in the bones.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12038,'biology',9,26,49,'From evolutionary point of view, retention of the female gametophyte with developingyoung embryo on the parent sporophyte for some time, is first observed in','[{"text": "Liverworts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mosses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In Pteridophyte, megaspore is retained for some times in female gametophyte, however the permanent retention is required for seed formation in Gymnosperms. That’s why Pteridophytes exhibit precursor to seed habit only.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12040,'biology',91,1399,3341,'A. Oxytocin causes milk ejection from mammary gland.<br>B. In adult women, hypothyroidism may cause menstrual cycle to become irregular.<br>C. Protein hormone secreted by thyroid, TCT (Thyrocalcitonin) regulates the blood calcium level.<br>D. Maintenance of water and electrolytes balance is also influenced by thyroid hormone.<br>Select the correct statement:','[{"text": "A, B and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B, C only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All except D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct statements.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12042,'biology',9,27,50,'<em>Pinus </em>seed cannot germinate and established without fungal association. This is because :','[{"text": "its embryo is immature.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "it has obligate association with mycorrhizae.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "it has very hard seed coat.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "its seeds contain inhibitors that present germination.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Fungus associated with roots of <em>Pinus </em>increases minerals &amp; water absorption for the plant by increasing surface area and in turn fungus gets food from plant. Therefore, mycorrhizal association is obligatory for <em>Pinus </em>seed germination.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12043,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Identify the hormones responsible for<br>(1)  RBC Synthesis <br>(2)  WBC differentiation','[{"text": "1-Thyroxine, Thymosins, glucocorticoids, 2-Erythropoeitin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-Thyroxine, Erythropoeitin, glucocorticoids, 2- Thymosins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1-Thyroxine, Thymosins, 2-Erythropoeitin, glucocorticoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'RBC synthesis- erytjropoeitin, thyroxine, glucocorticoids, WBC differentiation thymosins.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12045,'biology',90,1334,3217,'A diagram showing axon terminal and synapse is given. Identify correctly at least two of A-D.','[{"text": "A- Neurotransmitter, B- Synaptic Cleft", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C- Neurotransmitter, D- $\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{++}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Receptor, C- Synaptic vesicles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B- Synaptic connection, D- $\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A- Receptor and C-Synaptic vesicles',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/90_12045_question_1.png'),
(12046,'biology',9,27,50,'Phloem in gymnosperms lacks :','[{"text": "Albuminous cells and sieve cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sieve tubes only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Companion cells only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both sieve tubes and companion cells", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Phloem in Gymnosperms lacks both sieve tube and companion cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12047,'biology',91,1400,3342,'Delay in blood coagulation is due to the deficiency of which hormone?','[{"text": "Adrenaline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "TCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parathormone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thyroxine", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Parathyroid Hormone (PTH) regulate $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ ions level in body. These ions plays a significant role in blood clotting. Thus, deficiency of PTH would lead to deficiency of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ ions. Due to this, the process of blood clotting would be delayed and bleeding time would increase.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12049,'biology',90,1333,3216,'The most abundant intracellular cation is<br>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ca}^{++}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The most abundant cation in the intracellular fluid (ICF) is potassium $\\left(\\mathrm{K}^{+}\\right)$; whereas, the most abundant cation (or positively charged ion) in the extracellular fluid (ECF) is sodium $\\left(\\mathrm{Na}^{+}\\right)$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12050,'biology',9,25,47,'Gemmae are present in:','[{"text": "Mosses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Some Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Some Liverworts", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Most liverworts can reproduce asexually by means of gemmae. The gemmae are held in special organs known as gemma cups and are dispersed by rainfall.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12051,'biology',91,1398,3340,'The brain associated structures that function as \'master clock\' are<br>${\\text{i}}{\\text{. Forebrain           ii}}{\\text{. Pituitary gland}}$<br>${\\text{iii}}{\\text{. Adrenal           iv}}{\\text{. Pineal gland}}$<br>In above options which are correct?','[{"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pineal secretes a hormone called melatonin. Melatonin plays a very important role in the regulation of a 24-hour (diurnal) rhythm of our body. For example, it helps in maintaining the normal rhythms of sleep-wake cycle, body temperature.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12052,'biology',9,26,49,'Genera like <i>Selaginella</i> and <i>Salvinia</i> produce two kinds of spores. Such plants are known as:','[{"text": "Homosorus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterosorus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homosporous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterosporous", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Selaginella and Salvinia are heterosporous as they produce two kinds of spores - microspores and megaspores.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12053,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Injury localised to the hypothalamus would most likely disrupt','[{"text": "Short term memory<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Co-ordination during locomotion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Executive functions, such as decision making", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Regulation of body temperature", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Thermoregulation centre of body is present in hypothalamus of brain.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12055,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Hypothyroidism is caused by','[{"text": "Cancer of thyroid gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Development of nodule of thyroid gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Iodine deficiency", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Deficiency of iodine in our diet results in hypothyroidism and enlargement of the thyroid gland, commonly called goitre.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12056,'biology',9,24,45,'Which of the following algae produce Carrageen?','[{"text": "Green algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brown algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red algae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Blue-green algae", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Carrageen is a Phycocolloid produced from red algae. E.g., Chondrus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12058,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Which of the following is incorrect about thyroid gland?','[{"text": "It is composed of follicles and stromal tissues.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It secretes tetraiodothyronine or thyroxine (T4) and triiodothyronine (T3), TCT.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Each thyroid follicle is composed of follicular cells, enclosing a cavity.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is stimulated by the hormone TSH from hypothalamus .", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Thyroid is stimulated by the hormone TSH from anterior pituitary .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
