(12075,'biology',9,27,50,'Match the Column &ndash; I with Column &ndash; II<br>choose the correct option from the following<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Bryophyta <br>B. Gymnosperm <br>C. Algae <br>D. Pteridophyta</div><div class="column-right">P. <em>Pinus</em><br>Q. <em>Adiantum</em><br>R. <em>Sphagnum</em><br>S. <em>Ectocarpus</em></div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12076,'biology',91,1402,3344,'The heartbeat increases at the time of results of the NEET exams due to','[{"text": "Secretion of adrenaline and noradrenaline", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Secretion of adrenaline and corticotropic hormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretion of adrenaline and renin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretion of adrenaline and cortisol", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The heartbeat increases at the time of results of the neet exams due to secretion of adrenaline and noradrenaline',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12079,'biology',9,25,48,'Read the Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct options given below:<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> The first stage of gametophyte in the life cycle of moss is protonema stage.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Protonema develops directly from spores produced in capsule.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is not correct but  Reason is correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.<br>The predominant stage of the life cycle of a moss is the gametophyte which consists of two stages. The first stage is the protonema stage, which develops directly from a spore. Capsule of the sporophyte contains spore which gives rise to protonema.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12080,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Hypothyroidism causes','[{"text": "Irregular menstrual cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reduced BMR", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reduced production of RBC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12081,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Receptor sites for neurotransmitters are present in','[{"text": "Pre-synaptic membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tips of axons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Post synaptic membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Membranes of synaptic vessels", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In postsynaptic cells, neurotransmitter receptors receive signals that trigger an electrical signal, by regulating the activity of ion channels.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12082,'biology',9,26,49,'Identify the pair of heterosporous pteridophytes among the following :','[{"text": "<i>Lycopodium and Selaginella</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Selaginella and Salvinia</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Psilotum and Salvinia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Equisetum and Salvinia</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Selaginella</i> and <i>Salvinia</i> are heterosporous pteridophytes. They produces two different kind of spores. Psilotum, Lycopodium and Equisetum are homosporous pteridophytes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12084,'biology',91,1401,3343,'A child with following issues could have problems with which gland<br>1.A weak immune system<br>2. Short height','[{"text": "1. Thymus, 2. Thyroid gland only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1. Thymus, 2. Pituitary/Parathyroid gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1. Thymus, 2. Thyroid/ pituitary", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1. Thymus, 2. Pituitary only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Thymus gland provides antibody-mediated immunity or humoral immunity. Thus, a child with weak immune system could have problem in his thymus gland.Thyroid/ pituitary hormone deficiencies lead to dwarfism .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12094,'biology',9,24,42,'Which one of the following is an example of chlorophyllous thallophyte?','[{"text": "<i>Volvariella</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Spirogyra</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Nephrolepis</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Gnetum</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Spirogyra is a green-algae belonging to the class chlorophyceae. Volvariella is a genus of mushrooms. Nephrolepis is a genus of pteridophytes. Gnetum is a genus of gymnosperms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12086,'biology',9,27,50,'Read the Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct options given below:<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> In gymnosperms the pollen grains are released from the microsporangium and carried by air currents.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Air currents carry the pollen grains to the mouth of the archegonia where the male gametes are discharged and pollen tube is not formed.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are  true and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but  Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is false but  Reason is true", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Assertion is true but Reason is false as in gymnosperms the pollen grains are released from the microsporangium and they are carried in air currents. They come in contact with the opening of the ovules borne on megasporophylls. The pollen tube carrying the male gametes grows towards archegonia in the ovules and discharge their contents near the mouth of the archegonia.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12087,'biology',91,1400,3342,'Hormone that stimulates $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ reabsorption by renal tubules and increases $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ absorption from the digested food is','[{"text": "Calcitonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parathormone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vit D", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Parathyroid hormone (PTH) increases the $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ levels in the blood. PTH acts on bones and stimulates the process of bone resorption (dissolution/demineralisation). PTH also stimulates reabsorption of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ by the renal tubules and increases $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ absorption from the digested food. It is, thus, clear that PTH is a hypercalcemic hormone',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12089,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Myelin sheath is produced by:','[{"text": "Astrocytes and Schwann cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oligodendrocytes and Osteoclasts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osteoclasts and Astrocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Schwann cells and Oligodendrocytes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Myelin is made by two different types of support cells. In the central nervous system (CNS) i.e., the brain and spinal cord cells called oligodendrocytes wrap their branch-like extensions around axons to create a myelin sheath. In the nerves outside of the spinal cord, Schwann cells produce myelin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12090,'biology',9,25,46,'Bryophytes resemble algae in the following aspects:','[{"text": "Differentiation of plant body into root, stem and leaves and autotrophic nutrition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thallus like plant body, presence of roots and autotrophic nutrition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thallus like plant body, lack of vascular tissues and auto trophic nutrition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Filamentous body, presence of vascular tissues and auto-trophic nutrition", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The similarities between bryophyte and green alage are as follows:<br>• Both lack vascular tissues and roots and have similar flagella in motile forms.<br>• They have thallus plant body and the dominant phase in the life cycle is the gametophyte.<br>• They are autotrophic and have identical chloroplast pigments in the vegetative cells.<br>•Guard cells swell due to an increase in their water potential.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12091,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Gluconeogenesis, lipolysis and proteolysis processes are stimulated by','[{"text": "Glucocorticoids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mineralocorticoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenaline and nor adrenaline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Glucocorticoids are steroid hormones secreted by zona glomerulosa of adrenal cortex. The hormones are involved in metabolism of carbohydrates, proteins and fats.<br>These function in gluconeogenesis or synthesis of glucose from sources other than carbohydrates, breakdown of fats (lipolysis) and proteolysis (formation of amino acids from proteins).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12092,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Which of the following structures or regions is incorrectly paired with its functions?<br><br>','[{"text": "Hypothalamus : production of releasing hormones and regulation of temperature, hunger and thirst.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Limbic system : consists of fibre tracts that interconnect different regions of brain; controls movement.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Medulla oblongata : controls respiration and cardiovascular reflexes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpus callosum : band of fibers connecting left and right cerebral hemispheres.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Limbic system is part of human brain. Limbic system consists of Hippocampus, Amygdalo, Mammilliary bodies, anterior nucleus of thalamus, Function of Limbic system includes control of emotions.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12095,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Adrenal cortex secretes','[{"text": "Cortisol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aldosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Androgenic steroid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct. Adrenal cortex secretes Cortisol, Aldosterone, Androgenic steroid',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12097,'biology',9,27,50,'<i>Pinus</i> belongs to the class:','[{"text": "Gnetopsida", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cycadopsida", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coniferopsida", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sphenopsida", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pinus belong to the class Coniferospdia. They have needle like leaf structure and grow in Coniferous forests.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12099,'biology',91,1405,3347,'What is the role-played by luteinizing hormones in males and females respectively?','[{"text": "Activation of interstitial cells / secretion of progesterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Activation of leydig cells /stimulate ovulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synthesis of androgens / development of corpus luteum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct, luteinizing hormones in males -Activation of interstitial cells, Synthesis of androgens; luteinizing hormones in females secretion of progesterone, stimulate ovulation, development of corpus luteum',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12100,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Nissl bodies are mainly composed of','[{"text": "Nucleic acids and SER", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA and RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteins and lipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Free ribosomes and RER<br><br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Nissl granules (Nissl bodies ) are present in cyton (cell body) of neuron, it is composed of free ribosomes and rough endoplasmic reticulum (RER), due to presence of ribosomes and RER, protein synthesis takes place.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12101,'biology',9,25,47,'Gametophyte is the dominant phase in the lifecycle of:','[{"text": "<i>Hibiscus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Nephrolepis</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Cycas</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Riccia</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Gametophyte is a dominant phase in life cycle of only bryophytes. Riccia is a genus of liverworts, thus it belongs to bryophytes.<br>Their main body is haploid. Nephrolepis is a genus of pteridophytes, Cycas is a genus of gymnosperms and Hibiscus is a genus of angiosperms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12102,'biology',91,1407,3349,'The following are peptide hormones except','[{"text": "Insulin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucagon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thymosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenaline", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Adrenaline is a catecholamine',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12104,'biology',9,26,49,'Pteridophytes are called vascular cryptogams, because they are non-seeded plants containing:','[{"text": "Xylem and pholem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only xylem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only pholem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphibians of plant kingdom", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Vascular - mean having xylem and phloem tissues, Pteridophyta has xylem and phloem. Pteridophytes are seedless cortex is produced on the inner side of phellogen. It is made of living cells. Its cells take part in storage of food.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12105,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Which part of the brain is responsible for thermoregulation?<br>','[{"text": "Cerebrum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Corpus callosum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Medulla oblongata", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Hypothalamus in the thermoregulatory centre of our brain. It is responsible for maintaining constant body temperature.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12106,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Cortisol is involved in','[{"text": "Maintaining the cardio-vascular system and kidney functions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Produces anti-inflammatory reactions and suppresses the immune response.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimulations of RBC\'s production", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cortisol is involved in maintaining the cardio-vascular system as well as kidney function. Glucocorticoids, particularly cortisol, produces anti-inflammatory reactions and supresses the immune response.Cortisol also stimulates the RBCs production.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12107,'biology',9,26,49,'Mosses and ferns are:','[{"text": "Thallophytes of plant kingdom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angiosperms of plant kingdom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gymnosperms of plant kingdom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphibians of plant kingdom", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mosses and ferns predominantly grow in humid environment. Both ferns and mosses depend on water for fertilisation. Therefore, they are called "amphibians of plant kingdom". However, mosses show lack of vascular tissues thus they show greater dependence on amphibious environment.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12109,'biology',91,1403,3345,'Insulin and glucagon have','[{"text": "Synergistic action", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antagonistic action", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Similar action", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Insulin and glucagon have antagonistic action, insulin increases the cellular uptake of glucose and glucagon convert glycogen to glucose',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12111,'biology',9,27,50,'Match the words of Column I with that of Column II and choose the correct answer given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Algae<br>B. <i>Riccia</i><br>C. <i>Spirogyra</i><br>D. <i>Gnetum</i></div><div class="column-right">P. Gymnospersm<br>Q. Pond scum<br>R. Autotrophic<br>S. Livewort</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-S, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-S, C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-P, C-R, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'• Algae are autotrophic as they make their own food by photosynthesis.<br>• Riccia is an example of acquatic bryophyte. It comes under the class of hepaticopsida (liverwort)<br>• Spirogyra from masses that float near the surface of streams and ponds, buoyed by oxygen bubbles released during photosynthesis.<br>• Gnetum comes under the sub-class Gnetophyta under Gymnosperms.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2013,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12112,'biology',91,1403,3345,'A patient of diabetes mellitus excretes glucose in urine even when he is kept on a carbohydrate free diet. It is because','[{"text": "Fats are catabolised in adipose tissue to form glucose", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amino acid are catabolised in kidney to form glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycogen is catabolised from muscles and is released in blood stream", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None is correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A patient of diabetes mellitus excretes glucose in urine even, when he is kept on a carbohydrate free diet. It is because fats are catabolised in adipose tissues to form glucose.<br>Glucose moves from hepatocytes and adipocytes into the blood in a patient of diabetes mellitus, which increases blood glucose level(hyperglycemia).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12115,'biology',9,28,53,'Match the plant structures given in the Column I with their plants given in Column II. <br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Prothallus<br>B. Microsporophyll<br>C. Protonema<br>D. PEN</div><div class="column-right">P. Bryophytes<br>Q. Pteridophytes<br>R. Angiosperms<br>S. Gymnosperms</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R; B-P; C-S; D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S; B-R; C-P; D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q;B-S;C-R;D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q; B-S; C-P; D-R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'• In pteriodophytes, each spore upon germination gives rise to a free-living, green multicellular gametophyte called prothallus.<br>• In gymnosperms, the microsporophyll bears microsporangia on the abaxial surface that are attached to it by a short stalk.<br>• In mosses, a gametophytic structure called protonema, a green filamentous structure bearing buds is formed. Each bud grows into an adult gametophytic plant.<br>• In angiosperm, the sperm nucleus fuses with the diploid secondary nucleus (this is called triple fusion) of the embryosac, producing a triploid primary endosperm nucleus (PEN).',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2016,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12116,'biology',91,1403,3345,'Identify the exception to the pair of antagonist hormone','[{"text": "Adrenaline and noradrenaline", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Insulin and glucagon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PTH and TCT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Adrenaline and noradrenaline are synergistic hormones .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12118,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Select incorrect statement regarding synapses:<br><br>','[{"text": "Electrical current can flow directly from one neuron into the other across the electrical synapse.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemical synapses use neurotransmitters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Impulse transmission across a chemical synapse is always faster than that across an electrical synapse.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The membranes of presynaptic and postsynaptic neurons are in close proximity in an electrical synapse.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Impulse transmission across an electrical synapse is always faster than across chemical synapse.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(12119,'biology',9,27,50,'In which of the following groups do the male and female gametophytes have independent, free living existence?','[{"text": "Bryophytes and Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bryophytes and Pteridophytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pteridophytes and Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Algae and Gymnosperms", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Unlike bryophytes and pteridophytes, in gymnosperms the male and the female gametophytes do not have an independent free-living existence. The male and female gametophytes remain within the microsporangium and megasporangium. The gametophytes are dependent on the sporophytes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12120,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Find out the correct statement<br>(I) Hormones interact with membrane bound receptors that normally do not enter the target cells.<br>(II) Steroid hormones generate second messengers.<br>(III) Iodothyronines have membrane bound receptors','[{"text": "I is correct only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and II are correct only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III are correct only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III are correct only", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hormones interact with membrane bound receptors that normally do not enter the target cells. This is the only correct statement.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12121,'biology',90,1336,3219,'The parts of human brain that helps in\nregulation of sexual behaviour, expression of\nexcitement, pleasure, rage, fear etc. are:','[{"text": "Limbic system and hypothalamus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Corpora quadrigemina and hippocampus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brain stem and epithalamus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpus callosum and thalamus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Limbic system along with hypothalamus\nregulate the sexual behaviour, expression of\nexcitement, pleasure, rage, fear, etc.<br>Corpora\nquadrigemina is a part of the midbrain and\nconsists of four round swellings. Corpus\ncallosum is a tract of nerve fibres that connects\nright and left cerebral hemispheres. Midbrain,\npons and medulla oblongata together form the\nbrain stem. Thalamus is a major coordinating\ncentre in the forebrain for sensory and motor\nsignalling.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12122,'biology',9,25,48,'Plants like <i>Marchantia</i> and <i>Funaria</i> produce gametes by mitosis, because:','[{"text": "They are gametophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plant body is haploid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They are dioecious", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametophyte is diploid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Marchantia</i> and <i>Funaria</i> are bryophytes. The leafy thallus of the bryophyte is haploid and produces gametes by mitosis and is called the gametophyte.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12124,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Mark the mismatch<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Peptide- Pituitary hormones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Androgen- Peptide hormones", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amine hormone - Thyroxine derivative", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The 2nd option can be corrected as Androgen--Steroid hormones.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12125,'biology',90,1338,3221,'In the diagram of the lateral view of the human brain, parts are indicated by alphabets. Choose the answer in which those alphabets have been correctly matched with the parts which they indicate<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A - Temporal lobe; B - Parietal lobe;<br>C - Cerebrum; D - medulla oblongata;<br>E - Frontal lobe", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Frontal lobe; B - Temporal lobe;<br>C - Cerebellum; D - Medulla oblongata;<br>E - Parietal lobe", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Temporal lobe; B - Paretial lobe;<br>C - Cerebellum; D - Medulla oblongata;<br>E - Frontal lobe", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Frontal lobe; B - Temporal lobe;<br>C - Cerebrum; D - Medulla oblongata; E - Occipital lobe", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A\' represents frontal lobe<br> \' $\\mathrm{B}$ \' represents temporal lobe<br> \' $\\mathrm{C}$ \' represents cerebellum<br> \'  $\\mathrm{D}$ \' represents medulla oblongata.<br>\'  $\\mathrm{E}$ \' represents parietal lobe.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/90_12125_question_1.png'),
(12126,'biology',9,24,44,'The plant body having holdfast, stipe and frond is a characterstic of','[{"text": "<i>Laminaria</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Volvox</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Gelidium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Porphyra</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Laminaria - a brown algae has holdfast holding the plant body to substratum, stipe the stalk and the photosynthetic frond.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12127,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Which of the following is incorrect w.r.t catecholamines?','[{"text": "They are secreted by adrenal cortex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They cause fall in blood glucose in emergency conditions.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adrenaline and noradrenaline are examples of catecholamines.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The following statements are incorrect.<br>(1) They are secreted by adrenal cortex and<br>(2) They cause fall in blood glucose in emergency conditions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12129,'biology',90,1336,3219,'A man is admitted to a hospital. He is suffering from an abnormally low body temperature, loss of appetite and extreme thirst. His brain scan would probably show a tumour in','[{"text": "Pons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cerebellum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Medulla Oblongata", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The hypothalamus regulates food intake. It contains s feeding centre, which promotes eating, and a satiety centre, which causes a sensation of fullness and cessation of eating It also contains a thirst centre. It also functions as the body thermostat. If the temperature of blood flowing through the hypothalamus is above or below normal, the hypothalamus directs the ANS to control it. Thus, the person is likely to have tumour in hypothalamus',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12130,'biology',9,24,45,'Phycoerythrin and Floridean starch is found in<br>','[{"text": "Brown algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blue-green algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red algae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Green algae", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Phocoerythrin is a pigment in red algae and floridean starch is stored food in red alage.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12131,'biology',91,1403,3345,'Select the incorrect matching.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Thyroxine - decreases RBC production, causes inflammation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\alpha$-cell - Glucagon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\beta$-cell - Insulin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Thyroxine - $\\downarrow$ es RBC production, causes inflammation, this is incorrect statement<br>Thyroxine - play an important role in the regulation of the basal metabolic rate. These hormones also support the process of red blood cell formation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12133,'biology',9,24,45,'Match the storage products listed under Column I with the organisms given under Column II: Choose the appropriate option from the given choices.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Glycogen<br>B. Pyrenoids<br>C. Laminarin and\nmanitol<br>D. Floridean\nstarch</div><div class="column-right">P. <i>Sargassum</i><br>Q. <i>Nostoc</i><br>R. <i>Polysiphonia</i><br>S. <i>Spirogyra</i><br>T. <i>Agaricus</i></div></div>','[{"text": "A-R; B-S; C-P; D-T", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S; B-R; C-T; D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-T; B-S; C-P; D-R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q; B-P; C-S; D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<br>Agaricus has mannitol, trehalose and other storage compounds, such as glycogen and fatty acids.<br>Spirogyra contains pyrenoid and reserve food is starch like plants.<br>Laminarin and mannitol are present as food reserves in Sargassum.<br>Floridean starch is the stored food reserve in Polysiphonia.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2015,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12134,'biology',90,1338,3221,'The brainstem is made up of','[{"text": "Midbrain, Pons, cerebellum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Midbrain, Pons, medulla oblongata", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Diencephalon, medulla oblongata, cerebellum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cerebellum, cerebrum, medulla oblongata", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The brain stem consists of the midbrain, pons, and medulla oblongata. It controls the flow of messages between the brain and the rest of the body, and it also controls basic body functions such as breathing, swallowing, heart rate, blood pressure.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12135,'biology',91,1407,3349,'If receptor molecules are removed from target organs, then the target organ will','[{"text": "Not respond to the hormone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Continue to respond to the hormone, but will require higher concentration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Continue to respond to the hormone, but in the opposite way", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hormone will not be released from its respective gland", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Binding of a hormone to its receptor leads to the formation of a hormone receptor complex which causes certain biochemical changes in the target tissue. Thus, if receptor molecules are removed from the target organs, then the target organ will not respond to the hormone.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12137,'biology',90,1336,3219,'Hypothalamus of the brain is not involved in this function:','[{"text": "Sleep-wake cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osmoregulation and thirst", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Temperature control", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Accuracy of muscular movement", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Hypothalamus controls and integrates activities of autonomic neural system<br>It regulates emotional and behavioural pattens (together with limbic system)<br>It contains feeding and satiety centres (regulates eating), thirst centre ( regulates drinking)<br>It controls body temperature by serving as body thermostat',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12138,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Synergistic set of hormones includes','[{"text": "Prolactin and oxytocin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenaline and noradrenaline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parathormone and calcitonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Estrogen, progesterone, prolactin and oxytocin are synergistic hormones involved in lactation. Estrogen and progesterone help in development of breast and production of milk, prolactin milk secretion, oxytocin release of milk from breast.Adrenaline and noradrenaline are also synergistic.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12139,'biology',9,24,45,'Which of the following class of algae is mostly found in salt water?','[{"text": "Phaeophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rhodophyceae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chlorophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Rhodophyceae are commonly called as red algae because of the predominance of the redpigment (rphycoerythrin) in their body. They are mostly found in salt water.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12140,'biology',91,1403,3345,'Identify the correct match?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Gigantism--Deficiency of growth hormone in adults ---Increased growth of body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diabetes insipidus----Hyposecretion of vasopressin---Diuresis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Diabetes mellitus ---Hypersecretion of insulin---ketonuria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Diabetes insipidus----Hypersecretion of vasopressin---Diuresis, this is the corrected statement.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12141,'biology',90,1337,3220,'In which part of the human brain corpora quadrigemina is located?','[{"text": "Forebrain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hindbrain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Midbrain", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cerbral hemisphere", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Corpora quadrigemina are four rounded swellings in the mid brain.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12143,'biology',9,27,50,'i. In rhodophyceae, food is stored in the form of mannitol and laminarin.<br>ii. The ovules of Gymnosperms are not enclosed by ovary wall.<br>iii. <i>Salvinia</i> is heterosporous.<br>iv. In the diplontic life-cycle, the free living gametophyte represents the dominant phase','[{"text": "ii and iv are correct but i and iii are wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii are correct but i and iv are wrong", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i and ii are correct but iii and iv are wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii and iv are correct but i and ii are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In diplontic life cycle the sporophyte is dominant',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12144,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Which hormone directly affect transcription by acting on gene?','[{"text": "FSH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "LH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testosterone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Testosterone is a steroid hormone so it will act intracellularly and affect gene transcription.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12145,'biology',90,1330,3213,'A simple neural organisation, with a network\nof neurons, is found in','[{"text": "<i>Scypha</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pheretima</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Hydra</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Salamandra</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In cnidarians (e.g., Hydra) have the simplest neural organisation, with a network of neurons. The neural system is better organised in insects, where a brain is present along with a number of ganglia and neural tissues. The vertebrates have a more developed neural system.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12146,'biology',9,24,44,'<i>Ectocarpus, Dictyota, Laminaria, Sargassum</i> and <i>Fucus</i> belongs to','[{"text": "Phaeophyceae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chlorophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyanophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rhodophyceae", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ectocarpus,Dictyota,Laminaria, Sargasassum and Fucus belongs to Phaeophyceae and it is called as Brown algae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12148,'biology',91,1401,3343,'Major role of thymus gland in human is/are','[{"text": "Differentiation of T-lymphocytes to provide cell mediated immunity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Differentiation of B-lymphocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Production of antibodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Thymus gland secretes the peptide hormones called thymosins. Thymosin plays a major role in the differentiation of T-lymphocytes, which provides cell-mediated immunity.<br>In addition, thymosins also promote the production of antibodies to provide humoral immunity.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12149,'biology',9,24,45,'Find the correct match<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Green algae<br>B. Brown algae<br>C. Red algae<br>D. Blue green algae</div><div class="column-right">P. <i>Volvox</i><br>Q. <i>Dictyota</i><br>R. <i>Polysiphonia</i><br>S. <i>Nostoc</i></div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-S, C-R, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All the algal classes are classified based on presence of pigments, Green algae contains chlorophyll a, b, Volvox belongs to chlorophyceae, Red algae contain Chlorophyll a, d and Phycoerythrin and Polysiphonia belongs to red algae, Blue green algae contains chlorophyll c, phycocyanin and belongs to cyanophyceae.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12150,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Which of the following is incorrect regarding\ndendrites?','[{"text": "They are short fibres which project out of\\nthe cell body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are unbranched", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They contain Nissl’s granules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They transmit impulses towards the cell\\nbody", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The dendrites are branched. They are the short fibres which branch repeatedly and project out of the cell body. They contain Nissl\'s granules. They transmit impulses towards the cell body (afferent processes).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12152,'biology',91,1402,3344,'The outer layer of adrenal cortex and inner layer of adrenal medulla are ____  and ____  respectively','[{"text": "Zona glomerulosa, zona reticularis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zona reticularis, zona glomerulosa", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zona fasciculata, zona reticularis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zona glomerulosa, Nothing", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The outer layer of adrenal cortex are zona glomerulosa and and adrenal medulla doesnot have such differentiation of layers .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12153,'biology',9,25,47,'Which of the statement is correct about <i>Marchantia</i>?<br>I. Plant body is thallus-like structure attached to the substrate<br>II. Foot, seta and capsule differentiation is seen in the sporophyte<br>III. Gemma cup is located on the thalli','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "only II", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Marchantia is a liver wort.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
