(12180,'biology',90,1334,3217,'The figure given below is a diagrammatic sketch of a synapse. Select the option which correctly identifies one of the labelled parts along with its characteristic feature.','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{A : Dendrite }}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{-Carries\\\\,impulses}}\\\\,\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{towards\\\\,the\\\\,cyton}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{B : Synaptic}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{vesicle - Filled\\\\,with\\\\,a}}\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{neurotransmitter}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{C : Presynaptic}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - Contains\\\\,receptors}}\\\\,\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{ }}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{for}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{membrane\\\\,the}}\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{neurotransmitter}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{D : Synaptic\\\\,cleft }}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{- Enveloped\\\\,by}}\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{myelin\\\\,sheath}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{{\\rm{A:Axon}}}&{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{-}}\\,{\\rm{Carries\\,impulses}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}\\\\\n{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}&{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{away\\,from\\,the\\,cyton}}}\n\\end{array}$<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{{\\rm{B}}:{\\rm{Synaptic }}}&{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{\\rm{Filled}}\\,{\\rm{with}}\\,{\\rm{a}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}\\\\\n{{\\rm{vesicle}}}&{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{neurotransmitter}}}\n\\end{array}$\n<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{{\\rm{C:Presynaptic}}}&{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{ -Does\\,not\\,have\\,receptors}}\\,\\,\\,\\,}\n\\end{array}}\\\\\n{}&{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{membrane\\,for\\,the}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}\n\\end{array}}\\\\\n{}&{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{neurotransmitter}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}\n\\end{array}}\n\\end{array}$<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{{\\rm{D}}\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{:Postsynaptic}}}\n\\end{array}}&{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{- Has\\,receptors\\,for\\,the}}\\,\\,}\n\\end{array}\\,}\n\\end{array}}\\\\\n{}&{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{membrane}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}\n\\end{array}}\\\\\n{}&{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{neurotransmitter}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}\n\\end{array}}\n\\end{array}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/90_12180_question_1.png'),
(12181,'biology',91,1405,3347,'Choose the statements which correctly indicates functioning of gonads.','[{"text": "Androgens produce catabolic effects on carbohydrate and protein metabolism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Androgens influence both male and female sex behaviours.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovary produces one ovum during each menstrual cycle and produce three groups of steroid hormones called androgens, oestrogen and progesterone.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Androgens stimulate growth of facial hairs and axillary hairs, muscular growth, low pitch of voice, etc., in males.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ovary produces one ovum during each menstrual cycle and produces two groups of steroid hormones called oestrogen and progestrone, Androgens influence male sex behaviour (libido) and not female sex behaviour. Androgens produce anabolic (synthetic) effects on carbohydrate and protein metabolism',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12183,'biology',9,27,50,'Consider the following statements regarding gymnosperms and choose the correct option.<br>I. In gymnosperms, the male and female gametophytes have an independent existence.<br>II. The multicellular female gametophyte is retained within the megasporangium.<br>III. The gymnosperms are heterosporous<br>Of these statements','[{"text": "I and II are correct but III is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III are correct but II is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III are incorrect but I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III are correct but I is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In gymnosperms, the male and female gametophytes never grow independently but develop within the sporophyte structures Gymnosperms are heterosporus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12184,'biology',90,1335,3218,'The following figure shows a diagrammatic T.S. of a certain part of the central nervous system (ignore the shading, shape and proportions). Select the option that correctly identifies the part as well as the labels A and B. &emsp; &emsp;$\\,\\,\\,{\\bf{Part}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\bf{ A}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\bf{ B}}$<br>','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Spinal cord}}}&{\\\\,{\\\\rm{Grey}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{matter}}}&{{\\\\rm{White}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{matter}}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Cerebrum}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Grey}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{matter}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{ White}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{matter}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Medulla}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{ Pia}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mater}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{ Dura}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mater}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Cerebrum}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{White\\\\,matter}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Grey\\\\,matter}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The cerebrum and cerebellum have an outer grey matter an inner white matter. In the spinal cord, the grey matter is inner and the white matter is outer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/90_12184_question_1.png'),
(12185,'biology',91,1397,3339,'Which of the following hormones is not secreted by anterior pituitary gland?','[{"text": "Growth hormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Follicle stimulating hormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxytocin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adrenocorticotrophic hormone", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Oxytocin is produced by posterior pituitary gland.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12186,'biology',9,27,50,'What is the similarity between gymnosperms and angiosperms?','[{"text": "Phloem of both have companian cells.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endosperm is formed before fertilization in both.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Origin of ovule and seed is similar in both.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both have leaves, stem and roots.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Gymnosperms (including conifers) and angiosperms both have advanced support tissues true leaves, stems and roots they also are the two groups that produce pollen and seeds.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12188,'biology',91,1402,3344,'The steroid hormone responsible for balance of water and electrolytes in our body is','[{"text": "Insulin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Melatonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aldosterone", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Aldosterone stimulates reabsorption of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$and water and excretion of $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$and phosphate ions. Thus, it maintains balance of water and electrolytes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12189,'biology',90,1333,3216,'How many of the following are true about a polarized axonal membrane?<br>A. The outer surface possesses a positive charge.<br>B. It is impermeable to negatively charged proteins present in the axoplasm.<br>C. The inner surface possesses a negative charge.<br>D. It is more permeable to $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$and nearly impermeable to $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$.','[{"text": "A, C, and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and C only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B, C and D", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The outer surface of a resting axonal membrane possesses a positive charge while its inner surface possesses a negative charge. It is comparatively more permeable to $\\mathrm{K}+$ and nearly impermeable to sodium ions $\\mathrm{Na}+$. It is impermeable to negatively charged proteins present in the axoplasm.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12190,'biology',9,26,49,'Match the classes of pteridophytes given in column I with their examples given in column II and choose the correct option<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Psilopsida<br>B. Lycopsida<br>C. Sphenopsida<br>D. Pteropsida</div><div class="column-right">P. <i>Selaginella</i><br>Q.  <i>Psilotum</i><br>R.  <i>Dryopteris</i><br>S.  <i>Equisetum</i></div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pteridophytes are the vascular plants (those having xylem and phloem tissues) that reproduce by releasing spores rather than seeds, and they include the highly diverse true ferns and other graceful, primarily forest-dwelling plants. The pteridophytes are further classified into four classes: psilopsida (eg, Psilotum), lycopsida (eg, Selaginella), sphenopsida (eg, Equisetum) and pteropsida (eg, Dryopteris).',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12192,'biology',91,1407,3349,'In the mechanism of action of a protein hormone, one of the second messengers is','[{"text": "Cyclic AMP", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Insulin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\text{T}}_{\\\\text{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gastrin", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hormones which interact with membrane-bound<br>receptors normally do not enter the target cell, but generate second messengers (Cyclic AMP, $\\mathrm{IP}^{3}, \\mathrm{Ca}^{++}$, etc.)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12193,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Arrange the following events of synaptic transmission in a proper sequence.<br>A. Binding of neurotransmitter to specific receptors on the postsynaptic membrane.<br>B. Generation of a new potential in the postsynaptic neuron.<br>C. Release of neurotransmitter into the synaptic cleft.<br>D. Opening of ion channels in the postsynaptic membrane.','[{"text": "A, C, D, B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C, A, B, D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C, A, D, B", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{D}, \\\\mathrm{A}, \\\\mathrm{C}, \\\\mathrm{B}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When an action potential arrives at the axon terminal, it stimulates the release of neurotransmitters from the synaptic vesicles into the synaptic cleft. The released neurotransmitters bind to their specific receptors, present on the postsynaptic membrane. This binding opens ion channels allowing the entry of ions which can generate a new potential in the postsynaptic neuron.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12194,'biology',9,24,45,'Choose the correct order of colour with respect to pigments Chlorophyll-b, Fucoxanthin and Phycoerythrin','[{"text": "Green, Brown and Red", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Green, Red and Brown", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green, Blue and Red", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green, Red and Blue", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Chlorophyll,Fucoxanthinand Phycoerythin are Green, Brown and Red pigments respectively.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
