(12196,'biology',90,1337,3220,'The cerebral aqueduct passes through the','[{"text": "Midbrain", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cerebrum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cerebellum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diencephalon", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A canal called the cerebral aqueduct (aqueduct of Sylvius or iter) passes through the midbrain. It connects the diocoel (in the diencephalon) with the myelocoel (in the medulla).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12197,'biology',9,24,45,'Algin, carrageen and proteins are obtained\nfrom','[{"text": "red algae, brown algae, green algae\\nrespectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "brown algae, red algae, green algae\\nrespectively", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "red algae, green algae, brown algae\\nrespectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "green algae, brown algae, red algae\\nrespectively", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Certain marine brown and red algae produce largeamounts of hydrocolloids (water holding substances), e.g., algin (brown algae) and carrageen (red algae) which are used commercially. Chlorella and Spirullina are unicellular green algae, which are rich in proteins and used as food supplements.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12199,'biology',91,1398,3340,'A hormone responsible for normal sleep-wake cycle is','[{"text": "Epinephrine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gastrin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Melatonin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Insulin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A hormone responsible for normal sleep wake cycle is melatonin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12200,'biology',9,24,42,'Which of the following statements with respect to algae are correct.<br>I. Fusion between one large, non-motile female gamete and a smaller, motile male gamete is termed as oogamous.<br>II. Fusion of two gametes similar in size is termed as oogamous.<br>III. Fusion of two gametes similar in size is called anisogamous.<br>IV. In Chlorophyceae, the major pigments are chlorophyll $\\mathrm{a}$ and $\\mathrm{b}$, and the food is stored as starch.<br>V. In rhodophyceae, the major pigments are chlorophyll a and d, and the food is stored as mannitol.','[{"text": "I and V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Isogamous fertilization is the fusion of two similar gametes while anisogamous fertilization is fusion of two morphologically dissimilar motile gametes.In rhodophyceae, the major pigments are chlorophyll\' $a$ \' and \' $d$ \' but the stored food is floridean starch.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
