(12217,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Given below are two statements:<br>Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The cerebral hemispheres are connected by nerve tract known as corpus callosum.</div><div class="column-right">The brain stem consists of the medulla oblongata, pons and cerebrum.<br></div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are\\ntrue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are\\nfalse", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is true but Statement B is\\nfalse", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is false but Statement B is\\ntrue", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement A is correct but statement B is incorrect.<br>In human brain, a deep cleft divides the cerebrum longitudinally into two halves, which are termed as the left and right cerebral hemispheres. The cerebral hemispheres are connected by a tract of nerve fibres called corpus callosum.<br>Three major regions make up the brain stem <i>i.e.</i> mid brain, pons and medulla oblongata. Cerebrum is a part of forebrain which does not form brain stem.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
