(12315,'biology',94,781,1686,'Monomer of DNA is','[{"text": "Nucleoside", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fatty acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleotide", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amino acids", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Monomer of DNA is Nucleotide',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12382,'biology',93,271,529,'In his classic experiments on pea plants, Mendel did not use','[{"text": "Seed shape", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed colour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flower position", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Podlength", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mendel observed seven traits that are easily recognized as- flower color, flower position, stem length , seed shape, seed color, pod shape, pod colour. Therefore, pod length was not a character of garden pea plant which Mendel selected for his experiment.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12317,'biology',91,1407,3349,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Thyroid hormones are iodothyronines while epinephrine is amino acid derivatives in nature.<br></div><div class="column-right">Hormone receptors present inside the target cell in nucleus, are called intracellular receptors.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12318,'biology',93,278,536,'What map unit (Centimorgan) is adopted in the construction of genetic maps?','[{"text": "A unit of distance between two expressed genes representing 10% cross over.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A unit of distance between two expressed genes representing 100% cross over.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A unit of distance between genes on chromosomes, representing 1% cross over.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A unit of distance between genes on chromosomes, representing 50% cross over.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'1 map unit represent 1 % cross over. Map unit is used to measure genetic distance. This genetic distance is based on average number of cross over frequency.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12319,'biology',94,781,1686,'RNA has additional roles as well. It functions as','[{"text": "Adapter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Structural", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "As a catalytic molecule.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'RNA though it also acts as a genetic material in some viruses, mostly functions as a messenger. RNA has additional roles as well. It functions as adapter, structural, and in some cases as a catalytic molecule',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12320,'biology',91,1407,3349,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Membrane-bound receptors normally do not enter the target cell, but generate secondary messengerlikecAMP,IP3, $\\mathrm{Ca}^{++}$ which in turn regulate cellular <br>\nmetabolism.<br></div><div class="column-right">Intracellular receptors mostly regulate gene expression by the interaction of hormonereceptor complex with the genome.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12322,'biology',93,281,539,'Select the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "Male fruit fly is heterogametic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In male grasshoppers 50% of sperms have no sex-chromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In domesticated fowls, sex of progeny depends on the type of sperm rather than egg", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Human males have one of their sexchromosome much shorter than the other", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In domesticated fowls, female is heterogametic (ZW) and produces two types of ova (half have Z chromosome while the other half have W chromosome). Male is homogametic (ZZ) and all the sperms carry Z\nchromosome. Sex of the offspring depends on the type of ovum but not the sperm.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12323,'biology',94,781,1686,'DNA can make an exact copy of itself','[{"text": "Replication", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Translation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trancription", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transduction", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Replication - DNA can make an exact copy of itself',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12324,'biology',91,1399,3341,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Irregularities in thyroid gland can alter BMR.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Thyroxine regulates oxidation and ATP production.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Since hormones secreted by the thyroid regulate the rate of cellular metabolism, they have a marked effect on the Basal metabolic rate i.e., BMR. Thus, both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12325,'biology',93,285,550,'What is the genetic disorder in which an individual has an overall masculine development gynaecomastia, and is sterile ?','[{"text": "Turner’s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Klinefelter’s syndrome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Edward syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Down’s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Individuals with Klinefelter’s syndrome havetrisomy of sex chromosome as 44 + XXY (47).They show overall masculine development,gynaecomastia and are sterile.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12327,'biology',94,781,1686,'The process of protein synthesis inside the cell is called as','[{"text": "Transduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Translation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Transcription", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transformation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The process of protein synthesis inside the cell is called as Translation',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12350,'biology',94,781,1686,'Genetic material is','[{"text": "Any nucleic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A nucleic acid made from a nucleic acid template that has been or is capable of being used as a template in replication only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A nucleic acid  capable of being used as a template in transcription only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A nucleic acid  capable of being used as a template in replication and transcription", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Genetic material is the hereditary material present in the nucleus of eukaryotic cells. It is stable, capable of being expressed when needed, is also capable of proper replication and it must be transmitted from parent to progeny without any change.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12328,'biology',91,1402,3344,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Aldosterone stimulate reabsorption of water, and $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ ions.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Deficiency of aldosterone causes diabetes mellitus.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When there is a decreased blood pressure, the adrenal gland gets stimulated and releases aldosterone. This hormone helps in the reabsorption of sodium from the urine, gut and sweat. This increases the osmolarity in the extracellular fluid and helps in regaining a normal blood pressure. Thus, here the Assertion is true but Reason is false because diabetes mellitus occurs due to the deficiency of insulin.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12329,'biology',93,278,536,'Select the correct statement','[{"text": "Spliceosomes take part in post transcription.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Punnett square was developed by a British scientist", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Franklin Stahl coined the term ‘‘linkage’’", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transduction was discovered by S. Altman", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Punnett Square: It was developed by a British geneticist, Reginald C. Punnett.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12331,'biology',94,781,1686,'The connecting link between two generations is','[{"text": "Ribonucleic acid only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Deoxyribonucleic acid only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ribonucleic acid + Deoxyribonucleic acid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The DNA and RNA carries and transfers the genetic information from one generation to another.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12332,'biology',91,1399,3341,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> If tadpole is kept in water containing a weak solution of iodine it undergoes rapid metamorphosis.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The process of metamorphosis is controlled by thyroxine hormone.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The growth and development of animals like tadpoles is controlled by the hormone thyroxine. Thus, both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12333,'biology',93,283,541,'A woman has an X-linked condition on one of her X chromosomes. This chromosome can be inherited by','[{"text": "Only grandchildren", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only sons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only daughters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both sons and daughters", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Women has X-linked condition on one of her X chromosomes so she is a carrier of the disease. Chromosome can be inherited by both sons and daughters. But disease will be effected to the son only.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12334,'biology',94,781,1686,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Process of making RNA from DNA<br>B. Process of protein synthesis<br>C. Determination of complete nucleotide sequence</div><div class="column-right">P. Human genome project<br>Q. Transcription<br>R. Translation</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}$, $\\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}$, $\\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$, $\\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}$, $\\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{P}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12336,'biology',91,1403,3345,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Insulin is not given orally.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Insulin cannot be digested in the gut.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Insulin cannot be given orally because it is a protein and is broken down in the stomach before it can be absorbed.That is the reason why insulin must be injected. Thus, Assertion is true but Reason is false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12337,'biology',93,281,539,'Which of the following pairs is wrongly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "XO type sex : Grasshopper determination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ABO blood grouping : Co-dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Starch synthesis in pea : Multiple alleles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "T.H. Morgan : Linkage", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Starch synthesis in pea is controlled by pleiotropic gene.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12338,'biology',94,781,1686,'The genetic material found in most of organisms is','[{"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribonucleic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Deoxyribonucleic acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Enzymes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'DNA acts as the genetic material in most of the organisms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12339,'biology',91,1405,3347,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The regulation of $\\mathrm{RBC}$ production is accomplished by the hormone FSH.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> This hormone circulates to redbone marrow where it increases stem cell mitosis and speeds up the RBC development.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Erythropoietin, which is produced by peritubular capillary lining cells of the kidney, is critical to the production of red blood cells. Endogenously produced erythropoietin circulates in the plasma to act on specific target cells in the marrow through cell surface receptors. Thus, both Assertion and Reason are false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12340,'biology',93,275,533,'Which of the following characteristics represent ‘Inheritance of blood groups’ in humans?<br>A. Dominance<br> B. Co-dominance<br>C. Multiple allele<br>D. Incomplete dominance<br>E. Polygenic inheritance','[{"text": "B, D and E", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and C", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B, C and E", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, C and E", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'•  ABO blood groups are controlled by the gene I. Gene (I ) has three alleles IA, IB and i (Multiple alleles)<br>•  IA and IB are completely dominant over i. when IA and i are present only IA expresses and similarly when IB and i are present IB expresses (Dominant – recessive relationship)<br>•  When IA and IB are present together they both express their own types of sugars: this is because of co-dominance.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12342,'biology',94,781,1686,'Which nucleic acid in some viruses can also act as genetic material?','[{"text": "DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "mRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "tRNA", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'RNA though it also acts as a genetic material in some viruses',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12343,'biology',91,1401,3343,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Thymosin promotes production of antibodies.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Thymosin provides cell mediated immunity.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Thymosins play a major role in the differentiation of T-lymphocytes, which provide cell-mediated immunity. In addition, thymosins also promote production of antibodies to provide humoral immunity',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12344,'biology',93,271,529,'Among the following characters, which one was not considered by Mendel in his experiments on pea?','[{"text": "Trichomes - Glandular or non-glandular", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Seed - Green or Yellow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pod - Inflated or Constricted", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stem - Tall or Dwarf", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Gregor Johann Mendel also called as Father of Genetics conducted artificial pollination/ cross pollination experiments using several true breeding pea lines. He selected 7 characters for the experiments.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12346,'biology',94,781,1686,'The process of transfer of genetic information from DNA to RNA/formation of RNA from DNA is','[{"text": "Transversion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transcription", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Translation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Translocation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The process of making RNA from DNA (transcription)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12347,'biology',91,1402,3344,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cortisol is a protein hormone that regulates gluconeogenesis and lowers blood pressure.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> High levels of cortisol promotes release of $\\mathrm{ACTH}$.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cortisol is a steroid hormone, It increases BP. No explanation why \' $A$ \' is is wrong. No discussion of Reason. High levels of cortisol inhibits release of ACTH. Thus, both Assertion and Reason are false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12348,'biology',93,275,533,'The genotypes of a husband and wife are IAIB and IAi. Among the blood types of their children, how many different genotypes and phenotypes are possible?','[{"text": "3 genotypes ; 4 phenotypes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4 genotypes ; 3 phenotypes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4 genotypes ; 4 phenotypes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 genotypes ; 3 phenotypes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Husband - IA IB Wife –IA i ${\\rm{IA{I^B} \\times IAi}}$<br> Genotypes: IA IA, IA IB, IA i, IB i<br>Blood group : A, AB, B (Phenotype)<br>$Blood\\,group\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,Genotypes$<br>$A$ &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; $IA\\,IA:IAi$<br>$AB$ &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; $IA\\,IB$<br>$B$ &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; $IBi$<br>Hence there are 4 genotypes and 3 phenotypes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12351,'biology',91,1405,3347,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Corpus luteum secretes mainly progesterone.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Progesterone causes milk ejection from the mammary gland.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ejection of milk from mammary gland is caused by action of oxytocin hormone',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12352,'biology',93,284,547,'Thalassemia and sickle cell anemia are caused due to a problem in globin molecule synthesis. Select the correct statement :','[{"text": "Both are due to a quantitative defect in globin chain synthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thalassemia is due to less synthesis of globin molecules", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are due to a qualitative defect in globin chain molecules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are due to a qualitative defect in globin chain synthesis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Thalassaemia is a inherited autosomal codominant blood disease. In Thalassaemia , genetic defect lead to reduced rate of synthesis of one of the globin chains which make up the haemoglobin. Hence there will be formation of abnormal haemoglobin molecule leading to Thalassaemia. Sickle cell anaemia is an autosome linked recessive trait. This defect is caused by substitution of amino acid glutamic acid (Glu) by Valine (Val) in the 6th position of beta globin chain of haemoglobin molecule.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12353,'biology',94,781,1686,'DNA is not directly involved in the synthesis of the following:','[{"text": "Protein", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "mRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "rRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "tRNA", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'DNA is not directly involved in protein synthesis. Instead, DNA base sequence is "transcribed" to an RNA base sequence. It is involved indirectly as it provides the pattern after which RNA is formed. Though it sends information to mRNA molecules which goes to ribosomes to initiate protein synthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12354,'biology',91,1397,3339,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Pituitary gland is ectodermal in origin.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Both parts of pituitary develop from nervous tissue.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Reason is wrong',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12356,'biology',93,285,548,'A disease caused by an autosomal primary nondisjunction is :','[{"text": "Klinefelter’s Syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Turner’s Syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sickle Cell Anemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Down’s Syndrome", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Nondisjunction is the failure of homologous chromosomes or sister chromatids to separate properly during cell division. Downs syndrome is a autosomal primary nondisjunction disease or a genetic disorder which\nis caused by presence of extra copy of chromosome number 21( trisomy of 21).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12357,'biology',94,782,1687,'Haploid content of human DNA is ____','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{\\\\rm{.65 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{\\\\rm{9}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{bP}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{3}}{\\\\rm{.1 - 3}}{\\\\rm{.3 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{\\\\rm{9}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{bP}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{4}}{\\\\rm{.6 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{\\\\rm{9}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{bP}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{3}}{\\\\rm{.3 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{\\\\rm{9}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{bP}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'haploid content of human DNA is ${\\rm{3}}{\\rm{.3 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{9}}}\\,{\\rm{bp}}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12358,'biology',91,1397,3339,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{MSH}$ and melatonin are antagonistic hormones.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> MSH help in the dispersion of melanin in melanocytes while melatonin concentrates the melanin in melanocyte.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both are correct and reason is the correct explanation',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12359,'biology',93,271,529,'Which one from those given below is the period for Mendel’s hybridization experiments?','[{"text": "1840-1850", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1857-1869", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1870-1877", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1856-1863", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mendel conducted hybridization experiments on garden peas for seven years i.e from 1856 to 1863.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12361,'biology',94,782,1687,'Find the incorrect match.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\phi \\\\times 174$ phage -5368 deoxyribose sugar in its genetic material", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haploid content of human DNA is ${\\\\rm{6}}{\\\\rm{.6 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{\\\\rm{9}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{bp}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>E.coli</em>&nbsp;- $4.6 \\\\times 10^{6}$ base pairs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'a bacteriophage known as $\\varphi \\times 174$ has 5386 nucleotides and the haploid content of human DNA is $3.3 \\times 10^{9} \\mathrm{bp}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12552,'biology',94,782,1687,'The base paired structure of DNA implies that it','[{"text": "Can be used to make more copies of DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Used as a template to make RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is the hereditary material", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The base paired structure of DNA implies that it can be used to make more copies of DNA and used as a template to make RNA',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12362,'biology',91,1402,3344,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Over secretion of adrenal cortex hormones result in development of facial hair.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> This is due to increase secretion of androgenic steroid along with other cortical hormone.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hypersecretion of androgens from the adrenal cortex cause a condition called adrenogenital syndrome. In this excess of adrenal sex hormones are secreted causing secondary sexual characters to develop early in male children and female children become masculinised. Thus, both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12363,'biology',93,278,536,'In a test cross involving  ${F_1}$ dihybrid flies, more parental-type offspring were produced than the recombinant type offspring. This indicates','[{"text": "The two genes are linked and present on the same chromosome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The two genes are located on two different chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosomes failed to separate during meiosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both of the characters are controlled by more than one gene", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Linked genes sit much closer together on a chromosome, making them probably to be inherited together. This signifies that the two genes are linked and present on the same chromosome.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12365,'biology',94,782,1687,'The length of DNA is usually defined as','[{"text": "Number of nucleosides in one turn only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number of nitrogen bases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number of nucleotides", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Number of nucleotides in one turn only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The length of DNA is usually defined as number of nucleotides (or a pair of nucleotide referred to as base pairs) present in it.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12366,'biology',91,1397,3339,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Oxytocin is called birth hormone.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It induces contractions of smooth muscles during parturition.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Oxytocin is released into the bloodstream as a hormone in response to stretching of the cervix and uterus during labor. It helps in the contraction of the smooth muscles of the uterus. Thus, both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12367,'biology',93,280,538,'A pleiotropic gene','[{"text": "Controls a trait only in combination with another gene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is expressed only in primitive plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Controls multiple traits in an individual", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Is a gene evolved during Pliocene.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A single gene can have two or more phenotypic expressions. The multiple phenotypic effect of a single gene is called Pleiotropy. And a gene that has multiple, probably unrelated, phenotypic traits is termed as a pleiotropic gene. Thus, in a pleiotropic gene a mutation might have an effect on several traits together due to the gene coding for a product used by countless cells which have the same signaling function. The most\nwidely known examples in humans are phenylketonuria and sickle cell anaemia.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12368,'biology',91,1403,3345,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In advanced diabetes mellitus R.Q. is about 0.7 . <br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In absence of insulin mostly fats are burnt.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In some conditions the fats are burnt chiefly by the body like in cases of starvation or advanced diabetes mellitus; the respiratory quotient (RQ) will be about 0.7 . Whereas, in carbohydrate combustion the RQ will be 1 . Thus, both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12369,'biology',94,782,1687,'Genetic material of Bacteriophage lambda contain','[{"text": "4502 base pairs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5386 nucleotides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "48502 base pairs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5386 base pairs", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bacteriophage lambda has 48502 base pairs (bp)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12371,'biology',93,272,530,'Alleles are :','[{"text": "Different phenotype", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "True breeding homozygotes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Different molecular forms of a gene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Heterozygotes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Different molecular forms of a gene are called alleles. This results because the arrangement of nucleic acids can differ between copies of the same gene It was used in the early days of genetics to describe variant forms of a gene detected as different phenotypes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12372,'biology',91,1405,3347,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Steroid hormones are similar to cholesterol in structure.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Oestrogen is a steroidal hormone.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Oestrogen is a steroidal hormone and it has a sructure similar to cholesterol, so both are correct and the reason is the correct explanation of the assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12373,'biology',94,782,1687,'Genetic material of bacteriophage $\\phi  \\times {\\rm{174}}$ and it has ____ nucleotides','[{"text": "ss DNA, 5386", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ss RNA, 5386", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ds DNA,5368", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ss DNA, 5368", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'bacteriophage known as $\\varphi \\times 174$ has 5386 nucleotides',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12375,'biology',93,282,540,'Which is the most common mechanism of genetic variation in the population of a sexually reproducing organism','[{"text": "Recombination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chromosomal aberrations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic drift", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transduction", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Recombination is a very important origin of genetic variation between individuals of sexually reproducing species, and the driving force for the process of natural selection.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12376,'biology',91,1403,3345,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> On secretion of insulin glucose level in blood decreases.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> As it causes rapid movement of glucose from blood to hepatocyte.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Insulin keeps blood glucose levels from becoming too high. It causes glucose to move from the blood into cells, where it is either used for respiration or stored in liver and muscle cells as glycogen. Thus, both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12377,'biology',94,782,1687,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Bacteriophage $\\phi &nbsp;\\times {\\rm{174}}$<br>B. Bacteriophage lambda<br>C.&nbsp;<em>Escherichia coli</em><br>D. Human DNA haploid</div><div class="column-right">P. 5386 nucleotides<br>Q. ${\\rm{4}}{\\rm{.6 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{bp}}$<br>R. 48502 base pairs<br>S. ${\\rm{3}}{\\rm{.3 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{9}}}\\,{\\rm{bp}}$</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-P, B-R, C-Q, D-S',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(12378,'biology',93,275,533,'Multiple alleles are present:','[{"text": "On different chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "On non-sister chromatids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "At the same locus on the chromosome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "At different loci on the same chromosome", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Multiple alleles are present at the same locus of chromosome. Though only two of the alleles can be present in a single organism. Multiple alleles is a condition where a gene exist in more than two allelic forms which are present on the same locus of the chromosome. For example - ABO system in humans.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12380,'biology',91,1398,3340,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Pineal gland influences our defense capability.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It secretes a hormone called melatonin.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Melatonin is secreted by the pineal gland and it influences our defense capabilities. Both are correct nd the reason is not the correct explanation of the assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12381,'biology',94,782,1687,'A nucleoside differs from nucleotide in not having the','[{"text": "Phosphate group", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sugar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nitrogenous base", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A nucleoside contains a nitrogenous base covalently attached to a sugar but without the phosphate group. Whereas, a nucleotide contains a nitrogenous base, a sugar and one to three phosphate groups.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12384,'biology',94,782,1687,'A nucleoside consists of','[{"text": "Nitrogen Base", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sugar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phosphate group", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 & 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A nucleoside contains a nitrogenous base covalently attached to a sugar but without the phosphate group.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12385,'biology',91,1403,3345,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Insulin act as a hypoglycemic hormone.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Deficiency of insulin produces polyuria condition.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both the statements are correct but the reason is not the correct explantion of the assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12386,'biology',93,285,550,'An abnormal human baby with ‘XXX’ sex chromosomes was born due to','[{"text": "Formation of abnormal sperms in the father", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fusion of two sperms and one ovum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fusion of two ova and one sperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Formation of abnormal ova in the mother", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'An abnormal baby with XXX sex chromosomes was born because of an extra X chromosome, formed by fusion of abnormal XX ovum with a normal X sperm. Formation of abnormal XX sperm is impractical as males\nhave only XY genotype, and in case they produce abnormal sperms, then also XY and O sperms is formed. When a blend of multiple gametes takes place, at that instant the baby will bear triploid genotype and not the trisomy of sex chromosomes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12387,'biology',91,1397,3339,'MSH is secreted by:','[{"text": "Anterior lobe of pituitary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Middle lobe of pituitary", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Posterior lobe of pituitary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endostyle", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Melanocyte-stimulating hormone (MSH peptides are secreted specifically by the intermediate lobe (middle lobe) of the pituitary gland.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2000,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12388,'biology',94,782,1687,'A nucleotide is formed by','[{"text": "Purines, pyrimidines and phosphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "sugar and phosphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nitrogen base, sugar and phosphate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pyrimidines and sugar", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Nitrogen base + sugar + phosphate',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12390,'biology',93,272,530,'When a gene exists in more than one form, the different forms are called','[{"text": "Heterozygous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alleles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Complementary genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genotypes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Alleles are the different forms of the same gene. A genetic locus is that point on the chromosome where alleles for a specific gene can be found.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12391,'biology',91,1398,3340,'Melatonin is secreted by:','[{"text": "Pineal body", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Skin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pituitary Gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroid", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The pineal gland (epiphysis) secretes the hormonemelatonin which regulates the working of gonads by inhibiting gonadotrophins and their effects. Its production is inhibited by exposure of animal to light.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2000,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12392,'biology',94,782,1687,'Identify the pyrimidines found in DNA are','[{"text": "Adenine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytosine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thymine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 & 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Adenine is a purine.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12393,'biology',93,284,544,'Select the incorrect statement with regard to haemophilia','[{"text": "A single protein involved in the clotting of blood is affected", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is a sex linked disease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is a dominant disease", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is a recessive disease", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Haemophilia is an inherited genetic disorder, due to presence of a recessive allele on the X -chromosome.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12429,'biology',91,1400,3342,'A person is having problems with calcium and phosphorous metabolism in his body. Which one of the following glands may not be functioning properly?','[{"text": "Parotid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pancreas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parathyroid", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Parathyroid gland secretes the parathormone which regulates the calcium and phosphate ion balance in the blood and other tissues of the body.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12395,'biology',91,1405,3347,'When both ovaries of rat are removed then which hormone is decreased in blood : --','[{"text": "Oxytocin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prolactin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estrogen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gonadotrophic releasing factor", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ovaries secrete 2 hormones, Oestrogen before ovulation and Progesterone after ovulation. Hence estrogen decreases in blood when both the ovaries are removed. Oxytocin and Prolactin are pituitary hormones. Gonadotrophic releasing factor are released by hypothalamus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2002,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12396,'biology',94,782,1687,'Identify $\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{R}$.','[{"text": "P - Phosphate group, Q-Deoxyribose sugar, R-Nitrogen base", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P-Nitrogen base, Q-Deoxyribose sugar, R-Phophate group", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "P-Nitrogen base, Q-Ribose sugar, R-Phosphate group", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P-Phosphate group, Q-Ribose sugar, R-Nitrogen base", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'P-Nitrogen base, Q-Deoxyribose sugar, R-Phophate group',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/94_12396_question_1.png'),
(12397,'biology',93,284,543,'A colour blind man marries a woman with normal sight who has no history of colour blindness in her family. What is the probability of their grandson being colour blind','[{"text": "0.25", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.5", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The daughters of the colour blind man and normal sighted woman pair will have normal eye sight and carrier if one of the carrier daughter marries with a normal eyed man.than their son 25% may be affected.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12399,'biology',91,1403,3345,'Which one of the following pairs correctly matches a hormone with a disease resulting from its deficiency: -<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Relaxin - Gigantism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prolactin-Cretinism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parathyroid hormone - Tetany", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Insulin - Diabetes insipidus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Hyposecretion of parathyroid gland leads to hypocalcaemic tetany, it is also called Parathyroid tetany. It occurs when calcium concentration in body is less than normal. There will be an increase in excitability of nerves and muscles causing sustained contractions or tetany of muscles.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2003,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12400,'biology',94,782,1687,'Which one of the following pairs of nitrogenous bases of nucleic acids, is correctly matched with the category mentioned against it?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Cytosine, Adenine - Purines", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adenine, Thymine - Purines", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thymine, Uracil - Pyrimidines", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adenine, Cytosine - Pyrimidines", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Thymine, cytosine and uracil are pyrimidines.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12401,'biology',93,285,548,'A person who is trisomic for twenty first pair of chromosome is','[{"text": "Down’s syndrome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Klienefelter’s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Turner’s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Down syndrome is also known as trisomy 21. It is a genetic disorder caused due to the presence of a part of a third copy of chromosome 21',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12403,'biology',91,1403,3345,'Which one of the following pair\'s correctly matches a hormone with a disease resulting from its deficiency<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Insulin - Diabetes insipidus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroxine - Tetany", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parathyroid hormone - Diabetes mellitus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Luteinizing hormone - Failure of ovulation", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ovulation occurs under the influence of LH and FSH of anterior pituitary gland, Disease Deficiency<br>Diabetes mellitus - Insulin<br>Tetany - Parathormone<br>Diabetes insipidus - ADH',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2004,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12404,'biology',94,782,1687,'Find the correct answer','[{"text": "Adenine, Guanine - Pyrimidines", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytosine, Adenine - Purines", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thymine, cytosine - pyrimidines", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thiamine, Uracil - Purines", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Thymine, cytosine and uracil are pyrimidines.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12405,'biology',93,275,533,'When both alleles express their effect on being present together, the phenomenon is called','[{"text": "Dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pseudodominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aphidominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Codominance", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In codominance, neither allele is dominant or recessive and both get expressed. In this, the contributions of both alleles are visible in the phenotype. Blood types are excellent examples of codominance. A person’s blood type can be A, B,AB or O. If a person has type A protein they have type A blood, if a person has type B protein, they have type B blood , and if a person has type O blood neither protein is present, if a person is type AB then they have both type A and type B proteins present in their blood.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12430,'biology',94,782,1687,'Hydrogen bonds between cytosine and guanine are:','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Three hydrogen bonds are formed between cytosine and guanine and two hydrogen bonds are formed between adenine and thymine.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12406,'biology',91,1394,3336,'Which one of the following statements is correct?','[{"text": "Endocrine glands regulate neural activity, but not vice versa.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neurons regulate endocrine activity, but not vice versa.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endocrine glands regulate neural activity, and nervous system regulates endocrine glands.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neither hormones control neural activity nor the neurons control the endocrine activity.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The endocrine glands regulate neural activity as the neurosecretory cells of the hypothalamus helps it to regulate many functions like reproduction, homeostasis, metabolism, eating, etc. Again, the nervous system is responsible for the regulation of endocrine glands as the hypothalamus again controls the anterior pituitary to release or inhibit secretion of hormones which in turn controls other glands.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12407,'biology',94,782,1687,'Ribose sugar has an additional ____ present at _____ carbon:','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{OH}, 3$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{OH}, 4$ \'", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{OH}, 2$ \'", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{OH}, 1$ \'", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In RNA, every nucleotide residue has an additional-OH group present at 2\'-position in the ribose',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12409,'biology',93,274,532,'${F_2}$ generation in a Mendelian cross showed that both genotypic and phenotypic ratios are same as 1:2:1. It represents a case of :','[{"text": "Dihybrid cross", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiple allelism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monohybrid cross with complete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monohybrid cross with incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In Mirabilis jalapa which produces red flowers (RR) when they are crossed with plants having white flowers (rr), the ${F_1}$ plants (Rr) produce pink flowers. Although when such ${F_1}$ hybrid plants are self fertilized or crossed, the resultant ${F_2}$ plants are of 3 kinds on the basis of colour of the flower they bear. Thus the phenotypic ratio of plants with red: pink: white colour is 1:2:1 respectively. The effect of dominant character ( i.e., red colour) is incomplete in the hybrid pink flowered plants due to the diluting effect of recessive character (i.e., white colour) .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12410,'biology',91,1402,3344,'A steroid hormone which regulates glucose metabolism is','[{"text": "Cortisone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cortisol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Corticosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "11-deoxycorticosterone", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Glucocorticoids are steroid hormones that regulate multiple aspects of glucose homeostasis. Glucocorticoidspromote gluconeogenesis in liver,whereas in skeletal muscle and white adipose tissue they decrease glucose uptake and utilisation by antagonising insulin response.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12411,'biology',94,782,1687,'RNA serves an important role in','[{"text": "Protein synthesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fat synthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbohydrate synthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'rRNA (ribosomal RNA) form ribosomes associating with a set of proteins. This complex structure moves along an mRNA molecule, catalyze the assembled amino acids into protein chains. They combine with tRNAs and different accessory molecules important for protein synthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12412,'biology',93,275,533,'Which idea is depicted by a cross in which the ${F_1}$ generation resembles both the parents?','[{"text": "Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inheritance of one gene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Codominance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Complete dominance", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Codominance is a genetic sequence where neither allele is dominant or recessive and both get expressed equally in the heterozygote. In this both the alleles are capable of expressing themselves independently when present together results in a phenotype which is median between both the parental homozygous phenotypes, with that resembling both of them. Example of codominance is red coat colour in cattle.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12414,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Which hormone causes dilation of blood vessels, increased oxygen consumption and glycogenolysis?','[{"text": "Glucagon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ACTH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insulin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenaline", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The stress responses in the body are initiated by the Adrenaline. It increases heart rate and the blood pressure and also the metabolic rate. It dilates the blood vessels and increases the breathing rate.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12415,'biology',94,782,1687,'The first genetic material could be:','[{"text": "DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fats", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RNA", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The first genetic material could be: RNA',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12428,'biology',93,275,533,'If two persons with ‘AB’ blood group marry and have sufficiently large number of children could be classified as ‘A’ blood group : ‘AB’ blood group: ‘B’ blood group in 1:2:1 ratio. Modern technique of protein electrophoresis reveals presence of both ‘A’ and ‘B’ type proteins in ‘AB’ blood group individuals. This is an example of','[{"text": "Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Co-dominance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Complete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Partial dominance", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Blood group AB is an example of codominance and such persons carry both antigens A and B on their RBCs (plasmalemma). Both alleles of a gene pair in heterozygote are completely expressed and neither is dominant or recessive to the other.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12416,'biology',93,278,536,'Which of the following statements is not true of two genes that show 50 % recombination frequency?','[{"text": "The genes may be on different chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The gene show independent assortment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "If the genes are present on the same chromosome, they undergo more than one crossovers in every meiosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The genes are tightly linked", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The two genes which exhibit 50 % recombination frequency are tightly linked. When two genes are close together on the same chromosome, are called linked genes and they do not assort independently. While genes based on distinct chromosomes assort independently and have a recombination frequency of 50%, linked genes have a recombination frequency that is less than 50%. Though independent assortment is not shown by the linked genes but they remain together and are inherited all together producing only parental type of progeny.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12418,'biology',91,1407,3349,'Which one of the following is not a secondary messenger in hormone action?','[{"text": "cAMP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "cGMP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calcium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sodium", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sodium is not a secondary messenger.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12419,'biology',94,782,1687,'Find the correct functions of RNA.','[{"text": "It is a carrier of genetic information from DNA to ribosomes synthesis polypeptides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It carries amino acids to ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is a part of ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'It is a carrier of genetic information from DNA to ribosomes for synthesis of polypeptides. t RNA - It carries amino acids to ribosomes. r - RNA - It is a part of ribosomes',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12420,'biology',93,282,540,'Genetic variation in a population arises due to','[{"text": "Reproductive isolation and selection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Recombination only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutations as well as recombination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mutations only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Genetic variation can be caused by mutation, random mating, random fertilization, and recombination between homologous chromosomes during meiosis .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12421,'biology',91,1397,3339,'Which of the following is an accumulation and release centre of neurohormones?','[{"text": "Anterior pituitary lobe", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Posterior pituitary lobe", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Intermediate lobe of the pituitary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypothalamus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The neurohormones in most mammals (like oxytocin and vasopressin) are produced in the hypothalamic region of the brain and secreted into the blood by the neurohypophysis i.e., posterior part of the pituitary gland.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12423,'biology',94,782,1687,'Match the columns I and II with respect to DNA.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Base pairing<br>B. Deoxyribose<br>C. Thymine</div><div class="column-right">P. Sugar of DNA<br>Q. Unique property<br>R. Nitrogen base of DNA</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Q, B-P, C-R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12424,'biology',93,281,539,'In our society woman are blamed for producing female children. Choose the correct answer for the sex determination in human','[{"text": "Due to some defect like aspermia in man", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Due to the genetic make-up of the egg", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Due to the genetic make-up of the particular sperm which fertilizes the egg", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Due to some defect in the woman", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The sex of an individual is determined by the type of the male gamete (X or Y), which fuses with the X chromosome of the female. If the fertilizing sperm is X, then the baby will be a girl and if it is Y, then the baby will be a boy. Sex is determined at fertilization by the nature of the sperm that fertilizes the egg. Hence, it is incorrect to blame a woman for the gender of the child.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12425,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Feeling the tremors of an earthquake a scared resident of seventh floor of a multistoreyed building starts climbing down the stairs rapidly. Which hormone initiated this action?','[{"text": "Adrenaline", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glucagon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gastrin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroxine", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Adrenaline is a catecholamine thatis known to cause general physiological changes that prepare the body for physical activity and fight-or-flight response. Some typical effects include- increase in heart rate, blood pressure, blood glucose levels and sweating, etc.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12426,'biology',94,782,1687,'Thymosin is a','[{"text": "Nucleoside", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nitrogen base", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleotide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'It is a protein made by the thymus gland.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12431,'biology',93,272,530,'When two unrelated individual lines are crossed, the performance of F1 hybrid is often superior to both its parents. This phenomenon is called','[{"text": "Splicing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transformation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metamorphosis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Whenever two homozygous inbreeds of geneticallyndissimilar constituents are crossed together, the emerging hybrids obtained from the crossed seeds are commonly strong, vigorous, productive and taller than their\nparents. This improved productivity or superiority over the parents is known as heterosis or hybrid vigour. or outbreeding enhancement. It is the superiority of  ${F_1}$ hybrid over both the parents in terms of yield or some other character.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12433,'biology',91,1404,3346,'Compared to a bull, a bullock is docile because of','[{"text": "Higher levels of thyroxine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Higher levels of cortisone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lower levels of blood testosterone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lower levels of adrenaline /noradrenaline in its blood", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A bullock is docile because its blood has lower levels of blood testosterone.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12434,'biology',94,782,1687,'The backbone of DNA double helix consists of:','[{"text": "Sugar-Base", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrogen bond", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sugar-Phosphate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nitrogen base", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The backbone of a polynucleotide chain is formed due to sugar and phosphates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12435,'biology',93,278,536,'Select the correct statement from the ones given below with respect to dihybrid cross','[{"text": "Genes far apart on the same chromosome show very few recombination’s", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "genes loosely linked on the same chromosome show similar recombination’s as the tightly linked ones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tightly linked genes on the same chromosomes show very few recombination’s", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tightly linked genes on the same chromosomes show higher recombination’s", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Recombination is a rearrangement of genes during the process of meiosis, if genes are tightly linked on the same chromosome, they show very few recombination.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12436,'biology',91,1397,3339,'In human adult females, oxytocin','[{"text": "Is secreted by anterior pituitary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimulates the growth of mammary glands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimulates pituitary to secrete vasopressin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Causes strong uterine contractions during parturitions", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In human adult females, the hormone oxytocin secreted by the hypothalamus but stored in the posterior pituitary when released in the blood stimulates the contractions of uterus during parturition.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12438,'biology',94,782,1687,'Identify the purine out of the structure.','[{"text": "B - Adenine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Adenine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "C - Adenine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Guanine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A - Adenine is double ring structure.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/94_12438_question_1.png'),
(12439,'biology',93,272,530,'The genotype of a plant showing the dominant phenotype can be determined by','[{"text": "dihybrid cross", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "pedigree analysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "test cross", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "back cross", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gregor Mendel , the genetic, first brought in the term test cross which involves the breeding of an individual with a phenotypically recessive individual, in accordance to determine the zygosity of the former by\nanalysing proportions of offspring phenotypes. Simply, it is a cross between an individual featuring the dominant phenotype of a trait and an individual who is homozygous recessive for that particular trait in order to determine the genotype of the dominant individual .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12440,'biology',91,1399,3341,'The blood calcium level is lowered by the deficiency of','[{"text": "Both calcitonin and parathormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calcitonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parathormone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thyroxine", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Parathyroid hormone $(\\mathrm{PTH})$ increases the $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ levels in the blood. PTH acts on bones and stimulates the process of bone resorption',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12441,'biology',94,782,1687,'The successive nucleotides of DNA are covalently linked through','[{"text": "Peptide bonds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phosphodiester bonds", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hydrogen bonds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycosidic bonds", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The successive nucleotides of DNA are covalently linked through phosphate group bridges. Especially, the 5\'-hydroxyl group of one nucleotide unit is joined to the 3 \'-hydroxyl group of the next nucleotide by a phosphodiester linkage.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12453,'biology',94,782,1687,'Which one is incorrect statement?','[{"text": "In the polymer the ribose has a free ${\\\\rm{3\' - OH}}$ group is the 3 \'-end of the polynucleotide chain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A nitrogenous base is linked to pentose sugar by hydrogen linkage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adenosine, guanosine, and cytidines are nucleosides.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA is a polynucleotide", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A nitrogenous base is linked to pentose sugar by $\\mathrm{N}$ - glycosidic bond.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12443,'biology',93,272,530,'A cross in which an organism showing a dominant phenotype is crossed with the recessive parent in order to know its genotype is called','[{"text": "Test cross", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Monohybrid cross", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Back cross", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dihybrid cross", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A test cross is a cross that involves the mating of  ${F_1}$ individual with the homozygous recessive parent. A test cross can help decide whether a dominant phenotype is homozygous or heterozygous for a specific\nallele. The genotype of an organism with a dominant phenotype is either homozygous or heterozygous for the dominant allele.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12444,'biology',91,1395,3337,'Which one of the following pairs of organs includes only the endocrine glands?','[{"text": "Thymus and testes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenal and ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parathyroid and adrenal", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pancreas and parathyroid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Parathyroid and adrenal glands are only the endocrine glands. The pancreas and the gonads (both ovaries and testes) are examples of organs that have both endocrine and exocrine functions. Exocrine function of the pancreas is the production of digestive enzymes which travel down a duct or tube from the pancreas into the small intestine. The exocrine function of the gonads is the production of the gametes (sperm or eggs) which travel through ducts to the exterior or interior site of use.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12445,'biology',94,782,1687,'The structure of DNA is characterized by a','[{"text": "Left - handed single helix", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Right handed helix and antiparallel strands", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Right handed single helix", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Right handed single helix and parallel strands", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The structure of DNA is characterized by a Right handed helix and antiparallel strands',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12446,'biology',93,284,545,'Sickle cell anaemia is','[{"text": "Characterized by elongated sickle cell like RBCs with a nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Caused by substitution of valine by glutamic acid in the beta globin chain of haemoglobin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Caused by a change in a single base pair of DNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "An autosomal dominant trait", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Sickle cell anemia is a blood disorder caused by an inherited abnormal hemoglobin which causes distorted sickled red blood cells. Haemoglobin, a protein in RBCs carries oxygen around the body is coded by â HB gene. A mutation in HBB brings a change in one of the bass in the DNA sequence from an A to AT. Then , the amino acid present in the Hb protein changes from glutamic acid to valine. As a consequence, the body produces a new type of haemoglobin called HbS . The HbS formed causes the RBCs to occur abnormally and become sickle shaped . Therefore, Sickle cell anaemia is caused due to a change in a single base pair of DNA.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12448,'biology',91,1399,3341,'A health disorder that results from the deficiency of thyroxine in adults and characterised by (i) a low metabolic rate, (ii) increase in body weight and (iii) tendency to retain water in tissues is','[{"text": "Simple goitre", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myxoedema", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cretinism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypothyroidism", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Myxoedema causes the swelling of the skin and underlying tissues giving it a waxy consistency. It is a symptoml of patients with underactive thyroid glands. The type of hypothyroidism, includes weight gain, mental dullness, and sensitivity to cold.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12449,'biology',94,782,1687,'Identify the bond in the diagram.','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{X}}$ - Phospho-diester $\\\\mathrm{Y}$ - Hydrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{X}}$ - Hydrogen bond, $\\\\mathrm{Y}$ - Phospho-ester", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{X}}$ - phosphoester, $\\\\mathrm{Y}$ - phospho-diester", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{X}$ - phospho-diester $\\\\mathrm{Y}$ - phosphoester", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'X - phospho-diester Y - phosphoester',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/94_12449_question_1.png'),
(12450,'biology',93,278,536,'Select the incorrect statement from the following.','[{"text": "Baldness is a sex limited trait.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Small population size results in random genetic drift in a population", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linkage is an exception to the principle of independent assortment in heredity.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Galactosemia is an inborn error of metabolism.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Sex-influenced traits are autosomal traits that are affected by sex. If a male has one recessive allele, he will reflect that trait, but for the female to reflect that same trait it will require two recessive alleles. But these are dominant in males and recessive in females. One such gene is pattern baldness. Those men who inherit the gene from either parent lose hair (get bald) as they age, though women have them only if they inherit it from both parents and are therefore, homozygotes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12452,'biology',91,1397,3339,'Foetal ejection reflex in human female is induced by','[{"text": "Pressure exerted by amniotic fluid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release of oxytocin from pituitary", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fully developed foetus and placenta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Differentiation of mammary glands", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The main actions of oxytocin in the body are contraction of the uterus during childbirth and lactation. Oxytocin stimulates the uterine muscles to contract and also increases production of prostaglandins, which increase the contractions further.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12454,'biology',93,285,549,'Which of the following conditions in human is correctly matched with its chromosomal abnormality/ linkage?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Klienefelter’s syndrome - 44 autosomes + XXY", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Down’s syndrome - 44 autosomes + XO", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Erythroblastosisfoetalis - X linked", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Colour blindness - Y linked", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Klienefelter’s syndrome is a type of genetic disorder that has three sex chromosomes, XXY instead of the normal XX or XY chromosomes, though the atosome number is normal that i.e. 44. Mostly male are affected by this syndrome. The observable symptoms include weaker muscles, greater height, small testes, failure of normal spleen production, enlarged breasts like females gynaecomastia and absence of facial and body hair.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12455,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Injury to adrenal cortex is not likely to affect the secretion of which one of the following?','[{"text": "Aldosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both aldostenedione and dehydroepiandrosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenaline", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cortisol", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Adrenaline is a stress hormone released from the adrenal medulla.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12457,'biology',94,782,1687,'The double helical model of DNA resembles a twisted ladder in which the rungs of the ladder are :','[{"text": "A purine paired with a pyrimidine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A paired G and C paired with T", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sugar phosphate paired with sugar phosphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2) are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The double helical model of DNA resembles a twisted ladder in which the rungs of the ladder consist of four nitrogenous bases viz., adenine, guanine, thymine and cytosine that are attached to a sugar molecule on each side of the ladder. Adenine and thymine pair together, so as guanine and cytosine pair together',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12458,'biology',93,282,540,'Haploids are more suitable for mutation studies than the diploids. This is because','[{"text": "Haploids are more abundant in nature than diploids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haploids are reproductively more suitable than diploids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All mutations whether dominant or recessive are expressed in haploids.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mutagens penetrate in haploids more effectively than in diploids", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Haploid plants are formed in large number by anther and ovary cultures. As haploids have only one set of chromosome hence alleles. So, they can be used for isolation of mutants, after all, even recessive mutant alleles would be expressed in the mutagen treated generation itself.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12459,'biology',91,1405,3347,'Which one of the following pairs is incorrectly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Glucagon - Beta cells (source)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Somatostatin - Delta cells (source)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpus luteum - Relaxin (secretion)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insulin - Diabetes mellitus (disease)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hormones secreted from the pancreatic islets of Langerhans are insulin and glucagon. Glucose stimulates insulin secretion from betacells but suppresses the release of glucagon from the alphacells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12460,'biology',94,782,1687,'Total amount $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{T}$ in DNA is $45 \\%$ Amount of guanine will be ...','[{"text": "$22.5 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$27.5 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$35 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$55 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{T}+\\mathrm{G}+\\mathrm{C}=100 \\%$<br>Since $\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{T}=45 \\%$<br>$45 \\%+\\mathrm{G}+\\mathrm{C}=100 \\%$<br>$\\mathrm{G}+\\mathrm{C}=100 \\%-45 \\%$<br>$\\mathrm{G}+\\mathrm{C}=55 \\%$<br>$\\mathrm{G} / \\mathrm{C}=55 / 2$<br>$\\mathrm{G}=27.5 \\%$<br>Hence answer is $27.5 \\%$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12462,'biology',93,272,530,'Phenotype of an organism is the result of','[{"text": "Cytoplasmic effects and nutrition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutations and linkages", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genotype and environment interactions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Environmental changes and sexual dimorphism", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The combination of an organism’s observable physical or biochemical traits like their morphology,development, biochemical or physiological properties, behaviour as well as the products formed due to the behavior\n(such as a bird’s nest). A phenotye is the result of an organism’s genetic code, its genotype, the impact of environmental factors (for example : height, weight and skin colour) in addition to the interactions between the two. To conclude, existence of phenotype can be distinguished by genotype and environmental factors.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12463,'biology',91,1399,3341,'Toxic agents present in food which interfere with thyroxine synthesis lead to the development of','[{"text": "Thyrotoxicosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Toxic goiter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cretinism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Simple goiter", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Toxic agents in food which interfere with thyroxine synthesis will lead to simple goitre. Thyrotoxicosis and toxic goitre are under the category of hyperthyroidism.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12723,'biology',94,783,1688,'Chromosomes contain a region of chromatin which is loosely packed known as:','[{"text": "Heterochromatin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Euchromatin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both of them", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In a typical nucleus, some region of chromatin are loosely packed (and stains light) and are referred to as euchromatin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12464,'biology',94,782,1687,'The length of DNA having 23 base pairs is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{74}}{\\\\rm{.8}}\\\\,\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{o}} $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{78}}\\\\,\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{o}} $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{78}}{\\\\rm{.4}}\\\\,\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{o}} $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{78}}{\\\\rm{.2}}\\\\,\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{o}} $", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{1}}\\,{\\rm{helix}}\\,{\\rm{length = 34}}\\,\\mathop {\\rm{A}}\\limits^{\\rm{o}} \\,{\\rm{with}}\\,{\\rm{10}}\\,{\\rm{bp}}$. The length of DNA having 23 base pairs is ${\\rm{78}}{\\rm{.2}}\\,\\mathop {\\rm{A}}\\limits^{\\rm{o}} $ .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12465,'biology',93,284,545,'Both sickle cell anaemia and Huntington’s chorea are','[{"text": "Congenital disorders", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bacterial related diseases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Virus related diseases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollutant induced disorders", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A congenital disorder is a condition that exists at or before birth regardless of cause. It is also known as congenital disease, deformity, birth defect or anomally. Sickle-cell disease (SCD) is a group of genetic blood disorders that is generally inherited from a person’s parents. The most common type is known as sickle-cell anaemia (SCA). People suffering from SCD have abnormal hemoglobin, called hemoglobin S or sickle shaped hemoglobin, in their RBCs. When a person is having two hemoglobin S genes( Haemoglobin SS) the disease is called sickle cell anemia. Huntington’s disease (HD) is also known as Huntington’s chorea . It is an inherited disorder which results in death of brain cells. The earliest symptoms are often subtle problems with mood or mental abilities. Mental abilities mostly decline into dementia.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12467,'biology',91,1400,3342,'Low $\\mathrm{Ca}^{++}$in the body fluid may be the cause of','[{"text": "Tetany", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anaemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angina pectoris", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gout", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hypocalcemia: It is the primary cause of tetany. Low ionised calcium levels in the extracellular fluid increase the permeability of neuronal membranes to sodium ion, causing a progressive depolarisation, which increases the possibility of action potentials.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12468,'biology',94,782,1687,'If there are 120 adenine molecules in B-DNA double helical structure showing 20 coils, what is pyrimidine nucleotides forming three hydrogen bonds in it ...','[{"text": "80", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "100", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "120", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "140", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'20 coils means $20 \\times 10 \\times 2=400$ base pairs. 120 adenine means 120 thymine $=240$, remaining 160 is guanine and cytosine which forms 3 hydrogen bonds, therefore only the pyrimidine part would be 80',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12469,'biology',93,283,541,'The recessive genes located on X-chromosome in humans are always','[{"text": "Expressed in males", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sub-lethal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lethal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Expressed in females", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The recessive genes located on the X-chromosome in humans are always expressed in females, because they have two of them and therefore, can be homozygous or heterozygous for any locus on this chromosome. On the other hand, males are hemizygous for the X chromosome, because they have only one copy of every gene on the X chromosome.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12470,'biology',91,1403,3345,'Select the correct matching of a hormone, its source and function.<br>Hormone / Source / Function<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Vasopressin/Posterior pituitary / increases loss of water through urine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Norepinephrine / Adrenal medulla / increases heart beat, rate of respiration and alertness", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glucagon / Beta cells of islets / stimulates glycogenelysis of Langerhans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prolactin / Posterior / pituitary regulates growth of mammary glands and milk formation in females", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Norepinephrine is secreted by the adrensl medullaand causes increased heart beat and respiration.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12472,'biology',94,782,1687,'How many nucleotides are present in one spiral of DNA?','[{"text": "20", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "10", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "25", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The double helix DNA is right-handed having about 10-10.5 base pairs per turn. This reads about 20-21 nucleotides per turn or in one spiral.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12473,'biology',93,278,536,'The salivary gland chromosomes in the dipteran larvae are useful in gene mapping because','[{"text": "These are fused", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These are much longer in size", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have endore duplicated chromosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "These are easy to stain", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Endoreduplicated chromosomes are found in the salivary gland hormones in the dipteran larvae which are useful in gene mapping. These chromosomes are formed because of endoduplication or endopolyploidy\nor endomitosis, in this process the nuclear membrane doesn’t rupture but the chromosomes are doubled and they don’t get separated from each other.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2005,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12530,'biology',91,1398,3340,'The amino acid tryptophan is the precursor for the synthesis of','[{"text": "Thyroxine and Triiodothyronine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estrogen and Progesterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Melatonin and Serotonin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cortisol and Cortisone", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Amino acid tryptophan acts as building blocks in protein synthesis. It functions as a biochemical precursor to the neurotransmitters serotonin and melatonin',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12474,'biology',91,1405,3347,'Match the source gland with its respective hormone and function and select the correct option.<br>Source gland / Hormone / Function<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Anterior pituitary / Oxytocin / Contraction of uterus muscles during childbirth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Posterior pituitary / Vasopressin / Stimulates reabsorption of water in the distal tubules in the nephron", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Corpus luteum / Oestrogen / Supports pregnancy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroid / Thyroxin / Regulate blood calcium level", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Posterior pituitary secretes vasopressin which stimulates resorption of water in the distal tubules in the nephron.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
