(12617,'biology',94,782,1687,'The coiling of double strands in B-DNA is:','[{"text": "Right- handed", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Parallel", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Left -handed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Symmetrical", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The double helical form of DNA is righthanded. It is twisted tightly in a right handed direction until the helix forms a knot.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12618,'biology',93,284,546,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Phenylketonuria patients have high level of phenylpyruvic acid in their urine</div><div class="column-right">Phenylketonuria is an inborn error of metabolism and it is an autosomal dominant trait.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'PKU is a recessive hereditary disease caused due to absence of PAH which changes phenylalanine into tyrosine. as a result there is higher concentration of phenylpyruvic acid in blood tissue fluids and urine.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12969,'biology',96,1159,2772,'Which microorganism is growing on potato dextrose agar containing petri plate?','[{"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Virus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viriods", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Fungi is growing on potato dextrose agar containing petri plate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/96_12969_question_1.png'),
(12620,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Which one of the following hormones also produces anti-inflammatory reactions in man and suppresses the immune response in addition to its primary functions?','[{"text": "Cortisol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thymosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyrocalacitonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Erythropoietin", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Glucocorticoids (cortisol) inhibit white blood cells that paricipate in infammatory responses. Unforunately glucocortcoids also retard tissue repair, and as a result, they slow wound healing',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12621,'biology',94,782,1687,'Form of B-DNA is','[{"text": "Right handed with 11 bp per turn", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Left handed with 10 bp per turn", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Right handed with 10 bp per turn", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Left handed with 9 bp per turn", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Form of B-DNA is Right handed with 10 bp per turn',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12622,'biology',93,281,539,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Grasshopper is an example of XO type of sex determination</div><div class="column-right">X-chromosome in humans is present in female as well as males.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12623,'biology',91,1397,3339,'Facultative absorption of water from primary urine is influenced by the hormone:','[{"text": "Androgens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epinephrine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasopressin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thyroxine", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Antidiuretic hormone (or vasopressin), released by the neurohypophysis (posterior pituitary), regulates facultative water reabsorption by increasing the water permeability principle of cells in the last part of DCT and principal throughout the collecting duct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12624,'biology',94,782,1687,'Given the figure represent the DNA double helix model as proposed by Watson and Crick (1953). Select the option that shows correct measurement of A, B and C.','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - 3}}{\\\\rm{.4\\\\,nm,\\\\,B - 0}}{\\\\rm{.34\\\\,nm,C - 2\\\\,nm}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - 34}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{nm,B - 3}}{\\\\rm{.4}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{nm,C - 20}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{nm}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - 3}}{\\\\rm{.4}}\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{o}} {\\\\rm{,B - 0}}{\\\\rm{.34}}\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{o}} {\\\\rm{,C - 20}}\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{o}} $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - 34}}\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{o}} {\\\\rm{,B - 3}}{\\\\rm{.4}}\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{o}} {\\\\rm{,C - 2}}\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{o}} $", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{A - 3}}{\\rm{.4\\,nm,\\,B - 0}}{\\rm{.34\\,nm,C - 2\\,nm}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/94_12624_question_1.png'),
(12626,'biology',93,276,534,'In the ${F_2}$ generation of a Mendelian dihybrid cross the number of phenotypes and genotypes are:','[{"text": "Phenotypes - 4; genotypes - 16", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenotypes - 9; genotypes - 4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenotypes - 4; genotypes - 8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenotypes - 4; genotypes - 9", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Let us take example of dihybrid cross between round yellow (RRYY) and wrinkled green (rryy). In F2 generation there were four Phenotypes: round yellow, round green, wrinkled yellow and wrinkled green. The genotypes were; RRYY, RRYy, RRyy,RrYY, RrYy, Rryy, rrYY, rrYy and rryy. Option ‘4’ is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12627,'biology',91,1402,3344,'The hormones of "Fright, Fight and Flight"" are:','[{"text": "Thyroxin and oxytocin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroxin and melatonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenalin and nor-adrenalin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gastrin and secretin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In stressful situations and during exercise, impulses from the hypothalamus stimulate sympathetic preganglionie neurons which in tun stimulate the chromaffin cells to secrete epinephrine and norepinephrine, also called adrenaline and noradrenaline respectively. These two hormones greatly augment the fight-or-flight response.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
