(12628,'biology',94,783,1688,'Length of DNA in E. coli is','[{"text": "$2.2 \\\\mathrm{~m}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1.36 \\\\mathrm{~mm}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$1.36 \\\\mathrm{~m}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3.4 \\\\mathrm{~mm}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The length of E. coli DNA is $1.36 \\mathrm{~mm}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12906,'biology',93,285,548,'Any change in sex chromosome is not involved in','[{"text": "Super female", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Super male", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Down’s syndrome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Turner’s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Down’s Syndrome ,there is presence of an additional copy of the chromosome number 21 (trisomy of 21), no involvement of sex chromosome.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12630,'biology',93,275,533,'Mother and father of a person with ‘O’ blood group have ‘A’ and ‘B’ blood group, respectively. What would be the genotype of both mother and father?','[{"text": "Mother is homozygous for ‘A’ blood\\ngroup and father is heterozygous for ‘B’", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mother is heterozygous for ‘A’ blood\\ngroup and father is homozygous for ‘B’", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both mother and father are heterozygous\\nfor ‘A’ and ‘B’ blood group, respectively", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both mother and father are homozygous\\nfor ‘A’ and ‘B’ blood group, respectively", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Possible genotype of parents are; IAi (A blood group) and IBi (B blood group) and phenotype of offspring is ii (O blood group).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12631,'biology',91,1404,3346,'A boy after attaining sexual maturity shows muscular growth, growth of facial and axillary hair, aggressive and low pitch or voice. These changes are attributed to ____ hormone','[{"text": "Estrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testosterone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Secretin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucagon", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'At puberty, testosterone and dihydrotestosterone bring about development and enlargement of the male sex organs, secondarysex organs such as epididymis, vas deferens, seminal vesicles prostate gland, penis, urethra, etc., and the development of male secondary sexual characteristics such as muscular and skeletal growth resulting in wide shoulders and narrow hips, facial and chest hair and more hair on other parts of the body; thickening of the skin; increased sebaceous (oil) gland secretion; and enlargement of the larynx and deepening of the voice',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12632,'biology',94,783,1688,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A.&nbsp;<em>E.coli</em> DNA lengths<br>B. Human DNA length<br>C.&nbsp;<em>E.coli</em> area<br>D. Human nucleus area</div><div class="column-right">P. 1.36 mm<br>Q. 1 &micro;m<br>R. 2.2 m<br>S. 5 &micro;m</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{D}-\\mathrm{S}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12633,'biology',93,273,531,'It is said that Mendel proposed that the factor controlling any character is discrete and independent. His proposition was based on the','[{"text": "Results of ${F_3}$ generation of a cross.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Observations that the offspring of a\\ncross made between the plants having two\\ncontrasting characters shows only one\\ncharacter without any blending.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Self pollination of ${F_1}$ offsprings", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cross pollination of Cross pollination of F1 generation with\\nrecessive parent generation with\\nrecessive parent", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During dihybrid cross, Mendel observed that when tw opairs of contrasting charcters were selected for analysis; it was found that a particular character behave dindependently from another character. Hence, option ‘b’ is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12635,'biology',91,1405,3347,'A girl after attaining sexual maturity shows development of growing ovarian follicles, development of mammary glands and high pitch of voice. These changes are attributed to ____ hormones','[{"text": "Melatonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estrogens", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Progesterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Androgens", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Estrogens are female sex hormone produced by the ovary. It acts on the stimulation of growth, activities of female secondary sex organs, development of growing ovarian follicles, the appearance of female secondary sex characters (e.g., the high pitch of voice, etc.) and mammary gland development. Estrogens also regulate female sexual behaviour',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12636,'biology',94,783,1688,'The typical nucleus dimension is','[{"text": "Approximately $10^{-6} \\\\mathrm{~nm}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Approximately $10^{-5} \\\\mathrm{~m}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Approximately $10^{-6} \\\\mathrm{~m}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Approximately $10^{-9} \\\\mathrm{~m}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A typical nucleus (approximately $10^{-6} \\mathrm{~m}$ )',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12637,'biology',93,278,536,'Two genes ‘A’ and ‘B’ are linked. In a dihybrid cross involving these two genes, the ${F_1}$ heterozygote is crossed with homozygous recessive parental type (aa bb). What would be the ratio of offspring in the next generation?','[{"text": "$1{\\\\rm{ }}:{\\\\rm{ }}1{\\\\rm{ }}:{\\\\rm{ }}1:{\\\\rm{ }}1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$9{\\\\rm{ }}:{\\\\rm{ }}3{\\\\rm{ }}:{\\\\rm{ }}3{\\\\rm{ }}:{\\\\rm{ }}1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3{\\\\rm{ }}:{\\\\rm{ }}1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1{\\\\rm{ }}:{\\\\rm{ }}1$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Heterozygous when crossed recessive parent (test cross) gives 1:1.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12638,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Match the hormones of Column I with its functions in Column II<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Catecholamines<br>B.MSH <br>C. Thymosins<br>D. Melatonin</div><div class="column-right">P. Diurnal rhythm<br>Q. Immune response<br>R. Pigmentation<br>S. Stress hormone</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  Q, C  -  S, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  S, C  -  S, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  Q, C  -  S, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  P}}$, stress hormones are chemically catelcholamines, MSH causes pigmentation, Thymosins are responsible for immunity and melatonin causes diurnal rhythm of the body.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12640,'biology',94,783,1688,'The electric charge on DNA and histones is:','[{"text": "Both are positive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are negative", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Negative and positive, respectively", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neutral molecules", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The electric charge on DNA and histones is: Negative and positive, respectively',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12641,'biology',91,1397,3339,'Select the incorrect statement about the pituitary gland.','[{"text": "The pituitary gland is located in a bony cavity called the sella turcica", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The pituitary gland is attached to the hypothalamus by a stalk called infundibulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The adenohypophysis consists of pars distalis and pars intermedia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In humans, the pars intermedia is almost merged with the pars nervosa", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In humans, the pars intermedia is almost merged with the pars distalis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12642,'biology',93,283,541,'The inheritance pattern of a gene over generations among humans is studied by the pedigree analysis. Character studied in the pedigree analysis is equivalent to:','[{"text": "Quantitative trait", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mendelian trait", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Polygenic trait", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maternal trait", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The pattern of inheritance of Mendelian disorders can be traced through pedigree analysis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12643,'biology',94,783,1688,'The DNA in nucleoid is organised in','[{"text": "Large loops held by histones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Large loops held by nucleotides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Large loops held by sugar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Large loops held by proteins", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The DNA in nucleoid is organised in large loops held by proteins',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12645,'biology',91,1400,3342,'Calcium homeostasis is maintained by<br>A. Thyroxine<br>B. Calcitonin<br>C. Parathormone<br>D. Aldosterone','[{"text": "A and B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B and C", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "C and D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and D", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Calcium homeostasis is maintained by parathormone (hypercalcemic hormone) and calcitonin (hypocal-cemic hormone) through a feedback loop.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12646,'biology',93,281,539,'In a certain taxon of insects some have 17 chromosomes and the others have 18 chromosomes. The 17 and 18 chromosomebearing organisms are:','[{"text": "Males and females, respectively", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Females and males, respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All males", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All females", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'XO type of sex determination is seen in these insects. In such cases, the males have onlyone X-chromosome and the females have apair of X-chromosome.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12647,'biology',94,783,1688,'What is nucleosome?','[{"text": "They are similar to endosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A structure formed by wrapping of negatively charged DNA around positively charged histone octamer", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A structure formed by wrapping of positively charged DNA around negatively charged histone octamers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A structure formed by wrapping of positively charged histones around negatively charged DNA", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Each nucleosome is made of DNA wrapped around eight histone proteins which function as a spool and are thus, called a histone octamer. Each histone octamer consists two copies of histone proteins i.e., H2A, H2B, $\\mathrm{H} 3$, and $\\mathrm{H} 4$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12649,'biology',91,1396,3338,'GnRH is produced by the','[{"text": "Hypothalamus and stimulates the posterior pituitary to secrete gonadotropins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypothalamus and stimulates the anterior pituitary to secrete $\\\\mathrm{GH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypothalamus and stimulates the anterior pituitary to secrete gonadotropins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adenohypophysis and stimulates the ovaries to secrete oestrogens", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'GnRH is produced by the hypothalamus and stimu-lates the anterior pituitary to secrete gonadotropins (FSH and LH).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12650,'biology',93,276,534,'Mendel’s Law of independent assortment holds good for genes situated on the:','[{"text": "Non-homologous chromosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Homologous chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Extra nuclear genetic element", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Same chromosome", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Independent assortment cannot take place in case of options (2), (3) and(4).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12651,'biology',94,783,1688,'Match the columns I and II with respect to nucleosome.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Typical nucleosome<br>B. Histones<br>C. DNA</div><div class="column-right">P. Negatively charged<br>Q. 200 bp<br>R. Basic amino acid lysine and arginines</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{P}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12652,'biology',91,1404,3346,'Increased secretion of which hormone starts the process of sperm formation at the time of puberty?','[{"text": "GH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "TSH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PRL", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GnRH", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Gonadotropin-releasing hormone $(\\mathrm{GnRH})$ is released from the anterior pituitary. GnRH activity is very low during childhood, and is activated at puberty or adolescence. At the puberty increased secretion of GnRH start the process of sperm formation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12654,'biology',93,280,538,'Occasionally, a single gene may express more than one effect. The phenomenon is called:','[{"text": "Multiple allelism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mosaicism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pleiotropy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Polygeny", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Occasionally, a single gene may express more than one effect,this phenomenon is called as pleiotropy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12655,'biology',94,783,1688,'DNA is associated with highly basic proteins called','[{"text": "Globulins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-histones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Histones", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Albumins", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Histones are a group of basic proteins which are associated with DNA in the nucleus and help condense it into chromatin. They are the main protein components of chromatin, which acts as spools around which DNA winds, and plays a significant role in gene regulation',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12656,'biology',91,1397,3339,'The hormone that supports pregnancy and stimulates mammary glands for the formation of alveoli for storing milk, is secreted from','[{"text": "Anterior pituitary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Posterior pituitary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Graafian follicle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpus luteum", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Corpus luteum secretes the hormone progesterone that supports pregnancy and stimulates mammary glands for formation of alveoli for storing milk.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12657,'biology',93,276,534,'In a dihybrid cross, if you get 9:3:3:1 ratio it denotes that:','[{"text": "The alleles of two genes are interacting with each other", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is a multigenic inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is a case of multiple allelism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The alleles of two genes are segregating independently.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'This shows the perfect dihybrid ratio according to Mendel. Hence, the alleles of two genes are segregating independently.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12658,'biology',94,783,1688,'Lysine, Arginine are found in ?','[{"text": "Sugars", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acidic proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non histone chromosomal proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Histones", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Histones are rich in the basic amino acid residues lysine and arginine',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12660,'biology',91,1397,3339,'Gorilla-like man with large head, hands and protrud-ing jaws, is produced due to','[{"text": "Over secretion of thyroxin.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Over secretion of growth hormone in adult.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Excess of vitamin \' C \' in diet.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Excess secretion of TSH.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Excess secretion of growth hormone in adults especially in middle age can result in severe disfigurement (especially of the face) called acromegaly.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12661,'biology',93,278,536,'Which of the following will not result in variations among siblings?','[{"text": "Independent assortment of genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crossing over", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linkage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mutation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Linkage happens in al cases whenever two genes are located on the same chromosome and are close to each other. Thus, linkage has nothing to do with variation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12662,'biology',94,783,1688,'Biochemically what are Lysine, Arginine?','[{"text": "Nitrogen bases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fatty acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sugars", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amino-acids", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Histones are rich in the basic amino acid residues lysine and arginine',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12664,'biology',91,1398,3340,'The hormone that regulates circadian rhythms in the body is','[{"text": "Thymosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Melatonin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oxytocin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroxine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Melatonin plays a very important role in the regulation of a 24-hour (diurnal) rhythm of our body. For example, it helps in maintaining the normal rhythms of the sleep-wake cycle and body temperature.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12665,'biology',93,281,539,'Z Z / ZW type of sex determination is seen in:','[{"text": "Platypus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Snails", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cockroach", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peacock", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'This type of sex determination is seen in birds. The female has a ZW combination while the male has ZZ combination.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12666,'biology',94,783,1688,'Identify the structure &amp; labelled parts A, B.','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {{\\\\rm{Nucleus - A - H1}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{{\\\\rm{B - Octamer}}} \\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {{\\\\rm{Nucleus - A - Octamer}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{{\\\\rm{B - H1}}} \\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {{\\\\rm{Nucleosome}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ A - H1}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{{\\\\rm{B - Octamer}}} \\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {{\\\\rm{Nucleosome - A\\\\, Octamer}}}&amp;{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&amp;{{\\\\rm{B - H1}}} \\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Nucleosome A - H1 B - Octamer',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/94_12666_question_1.png'),
(12667,'biology',91,1407,3349,'How do peptide hormones influence cellular activities?','[{"text": "By binding to intracellular receptors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "By activating a second messenger inside the target cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "By influencing gene expression", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "By catalyzing biochemical reaction inside the cell", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Water-soluble hormones (e.g., peptide hormones) interact with membrane-bound receptors. They normally do not enter the target cell but generate second messengers which, in turn, regulate cellular metabolism.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12668,'biology',93,284,545,'In sickle cell anaemia glutamic acid is replaced by valine. Which one of the following triplets codes for valine?','[{"text": "G G G", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A A G", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "G A A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "G U G", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The substitution of amino acid in the globin protein results due to the single base substitution at the sixth codon of the beta globin gene from GAG to GUG. Codon GUG codes for valine which results in sickle cell\nanaemia.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12670,'biology',94,783,1688,'In a nucleosome, there are ____ histones and are organised in____ structure?','[{"text": "8 ,Octamer", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "8 , Hexamer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6, Octamer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "9,Octamer", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Histones are organised to form a unit of eight molecules called histone octamer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12671,'biology',91,1405,3347,'Which of the following is a steroid hormone?','[{"text": "Epinephrine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Enterocrinin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estradiol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Erythropoietin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Estradiol is a steroid hormone. Epinephrine is an amino acid derivative. Enterocrinin and erythropoietin are peptide/ protein hormones.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12672,'biology',93,272,530,'A cross between two tall plants resulted in offspring having few dwarf plants. What would be the genotypes of both the parents?','[{"text": "TT and Tt", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tt and Tt", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "TT and TT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tt and tt", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In case of TT and Tt; all offspring would be tall (TT, Tt). In case of option ‘c’ no gene for dwarf is present, so all offspring will be tall. Incase of option ‘d’ one of the parent plant is dwarf, so it is incorrect. In case of option ‘b’ most of the off spring will be tall and a few will be dwarf (TT, Tt, tt). Option ‘b’ is the correct answer.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12673,'biology',94,783,1688,'Typical nucleosome consists of how many base pairs:','[{"text": "146", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "200", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "54", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "246", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A typical nucleosome contains $200 \\mathrm{bp}$ of DNA helix.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12675,'biology',91,1397,3339,'An impairment affecting the synthesis or release of ADH results in','[{"text": "Diabetes insipidus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Addison\'s disease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diabetes mellitus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Graves\' disease", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'An impairment affecting the synthesis or release of ADH results in a diminished ability of the kidney to conserve water leading to water loss and dehydration (diabetes Insipidus).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12676,'biology',93,275,533,'Person having genotype ${I^A}{I^B}$ would show the blood group as AB. This is because of:','[{"text": "Pleiotropy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Co-dominance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Segregation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When ${F_1}$ generation resembles both parents, this is called co-dominance. This is often seen in ABOblood grouping. Since both A and B sugars are dominant, hence it results in AB blood group.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12677,'biology',94,783,1688,'Nucleosome contains:','[{"text": "Both DNA and histone protein", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only histone protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both DNA and RNA", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The nucleosome contains 146 DNA base pairs wrapped in super helical turns around a histone octamer that consists of 2 copies each of the core histones H2A, H2B, $\\mathrm{H} 3$, and $\\mathrm{H} 4$ and linker DNA contain 54, total $200 \\mathrm{Npb}$ in some Nucleosome',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12679,'biology',91,1404,3346,'Secretion of which hormone suddenly decreases when an animal is castrated?','[{"text": "Thyroxine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Growth hormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testosterone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thymosin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Castration is the removal of testes. It results in a fall in serum testosterone levels. You might be aware that testosterone is produced by the Leydig cells of the testes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12680,'biology',93,278,536,'Distance between the genes and percentage of recombination shows:','[{"text": "A direct relationship", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "An inverse relationship", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A parallel relationship", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No relationship", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Distance between the genes and percentage of recombination shows a direct relationship.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12681,'biology',94,783,1688,'In prokaryotes, DNA is held together by which proteins?','[{"text": "Negatively charged proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-histone chromosomal proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Positively charged proteins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Histone proteins", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In prokaryotes, such as, E. coli, though they do not have a defined nucleus, the DNA is not scattered throughout the cell. DNA (being negatively charged) is held with some proteins (that have positive charges) in a region termed as \'nucleoid\'.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12682,'biology',91,1402,3344,'The hormone that stimulates gluconeogenesis, lipolysis, proteolysis is','[{"text": "Aldosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cortisol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glucagon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epinephrine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Glucocorticoids stimulate gluconeogenesis, lipolysis and proteolysis. Cortisol is the principal glucocorticoid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12684,'biology',93,284,542,'If a genetic disease is transferred from a phenotypically normal but carrier female to only some of the male progeny, the disease is:','[{"text": "Autosomal dominant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autosomal recessive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sex-linked dominant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sex-linked recessive", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In this case, the defective gene is present on the X-chromosome but the disease is manifested in men and women are carriers.So, it is a sex-linked recessive disease. Haemophilia is one example and is also referred to as X-linked recessive disease',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12685,'biology',94,783,1688,'Histones are rich in which sugar?','[{"text": "Cysteine, Arginine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysine, Arginine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysine, methionine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "none of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Histones are rich in the basic amino acid residues lysine and arginine, $\\mathrm{n}$ not sugars.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12686,'biology',91,1401,3343,'Which of the following endocrine glands grow to the maximum size at puberty and then diminishes gradually?','[{"text": "Thymus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pituitary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adrenal", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Thymus starts functioning in the embryonic stage itself, becomes active during childhood and undergoes regression and gradually stops functioning in old individuals. So, production of thymosins decreases. As a result, immune responses of old persons become weak.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12687,'biology',93,278,536,'All genes located on the same chromosome:','[{"text": "Form different groups depending upon their relative distance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Form one linkage group", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Will not form any linkage groups", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Form interactive groups that affect the phenotype", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Form one linkage group Morgan showed that genes located on the same chromosome formed one linkage group. But linkage or no linkage depends on proximity of two genes. Genes which are closer show more likelihood of linkage. Hence, option‘b’ is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12699,'biology',93,284,546,'Which of the following statement is false w.r.t phenylketonuria?','[{"text": "Inborn error of metabolism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autosomal dominant disorder", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Affected individual lacks enzyme PAH that converts the amino acid phenylalanine to tyrosine.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenylalanine is accumulated and converted into phenylpyruvic acid and other derivatives.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Phenylketonuria : This inborn error of metabolism is also inherited as the autosomal recessive trait.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12688,'biology',94,783,1688,'Name the proteins required by chromatin at all level of coiling?','[{"text": "Histone only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non histone chromosomal proteins only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Histone and Non histone chromosomal proteins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only basic amino acid containing proteins", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Histone and Non histone chromosomal proteins are required for all levels of coiling. DNA is packed by histones. The packaging of chromatin at higher level requires additional set of proteins that collectively are referred to as Non-histone Chromosomal (NHC) proteins.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12690,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Catecholamines cause all of the following, except','[{"text": "Increased heart rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Piloerection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Constriction of bronchioles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Breakdown of glycogen", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Catecholamines cause bronchodilation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12691,'biology',93,285,548,'Conditions of a karyotype 2n +1, 2n –1 and 2n + 2, 2n – 2 are called:','[{"text": "Aneuploidy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Polyploidy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Allopolyploidy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monosomy", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Failure of segregation of chromatids during cell division cycle results in gain or loss of chromosome. This condition is called aneuploidy',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT EXEMPLAR','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12692,'biology',94,783,1688,'Chromatin fibres coil and condense at stage of cell division to form','[{"text": "Metaphase, Nucleosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metaphase, Chromosome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metaphase, Chromatin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metaphase, Chromatid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Chromatin fibers that are further coiled and condensed at metaphase stage of cell division to form chromosomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12694,'biology',91,1404,3346,'Which of the following statements is not correct about the function of androgens?','[{"text": "They stimulate the formation of spermatozoa.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They act on the central neural system and influence male sexual behaviour (libido).", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They produce anabolic effects on protein and carbohydrate metabolism.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They stimulate muscular growth, aggressiveness, the high pitch of voice", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Androgens are responsible for the low pitch of voice in males. Due to the influence of androgens, vocal folds are thicker and longer in males than in females. So, they vibrate more slowly. This is the reason why men have a lowpitch voice compared to females.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12695,'biology',93,284,547,'Find the incorrect statement w.r.t. thalassemia:','[{"text": "It is qualitative problem of synthesizing an incorrectly functioning globin.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alpha thalassemia is due to mutations of HBA1 and HBA2.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Beta thalassemia is controlled by a single gene HBB present on chromosome 11.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Caused by defects in the synthesis of globin polypeptidein RBC.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Thalassemia differs from sickle-cell anaemia in that the former is a quantitative problem of synthesising too few globin molecules while the latter is a qualitative problem of synthesising an incorrectly functioning globin.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12696,'biology',94,783,1688,'Packaging of DNA helix in eukaryotes','[{"text": "Is more complex in eukaryotes than prokaryotes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Occurs with the help of histone and NHC proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Requires acidic proteins that help in coiling of DNA in prokaryotes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both (1) and (2) are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12697,'biology',91,1403,3345,'Prolonged hyperglycemia leads to a complex disorder called','[{"text": "Diabetes insipidus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diabetes mellitus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Exophthalmic goitre", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Addison\'s disease", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Prolonged hyperglycemia leads to a complex disorder called diabetes mellitus which is associated with loss of glucose through urine and formation of harmful compounds known as ketone bodies.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12700,'biology',94,783,1688,'Which part of chromatin is transciptionally inactive and active respectively?','[{"text": "Heterochromatin and Euchromatin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleosome and Euchromatin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Euchromatin and heterochromatin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosome and Euchromatin", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Euchromatin is said to be transcriptionally active chromatin, whereas heterochromatin is inactive.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12701,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Select the most appropriate matching of a hormone and its target.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Epinephrine}}\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{SA}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{node}}}&{}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Oxytocin}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{DCT}}}&{}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Insulin}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Pancreas}}}&{}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{FSH}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Leydig}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{cells}}}&{}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Epinephrine acts on the SA node and accelerates the heart rate. Oxytocin stimulates the contraction of smooth muscles. Insulin acts mainly on the hepatocytes and the adipocytes. FSH acts on the Sertoli cells while LH acts on the Leydig cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12702,'biology',93,273,531,'‘Gametes are never hybrid’. Which law explains the following concept','[{"text": "Dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Independent assortment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Segregation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mutation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Law of segregation explains that gametes are never hybrid.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12704,'biology',94,783,1688,'Read the statements and select the correct option<br>I. A set of positively charged, basic proteins called histones are used in packaging.<br>II. Densely packed and dark stained region of chromatin is called as euchromatin<br>III. Loosely packed and lightly stained region of chromatin is called heterochromatin','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Densely packed and dark stained region of chromatin is called as heterochromatin and loosely packed and lightly stained region of chromatin is called as Euchromatin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12705,'biology',91,1400,3342,'Which of the following pair of hormone and its disorder is correctly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Parathormone}}\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Cretinism}}}&{}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Thyroxine}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Rickets}}}&{}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Insulin}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}&{{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Diabetes}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{insipidus}}}&{}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Corticosteroids }}}&{{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Cushings}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{disease}}}&{}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Over secretion of cortisol causes Cushing\'s disease. This disease mainly occurs in females and causes obesity hypertension, glycosuria, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12706,'biology',93,285,550,'An individual shows the following characteristics:<br>A. Sterile females<br>B. Rudimentary ovaries<br>C. lack of secondary sexual characters<br>D. 44 + XO<br>The individual suffers from','[{"text": "Edward’s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Down’s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Turner’s syndrome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Klinefelter syndrome", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Turner’s Syndrome : Such a disorder is caused due to the absence of one of the X chromosomes, i.e., 45 with X0, Such females are sterile as ovaries are rudimentary besides other features including lack of other secondary sexual characters.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12708,'biology',94,783,1688,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Non-histone chromosomal (NHC) proteins<br>B. Euchromatin<br>C. Heterochromatin</div><div class="column-right">P. Loosely packed chromatin<br>Q. Higher level packaging of chromatin<br>R. Transcriptionally inactive</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{R}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12709,'biology',91,1406,3348,'The hormone secretin is produced in','[{"text": "Pancreas and influences conversion of glycogen into glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Small intestine and stimulates pancreas", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adrenal glands and accelerates heartbeat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testes and produces male secondary sexual", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Secretin is a hormone which is released into the bloodstream by the wall of the upper part of the small intestine (the duodenum) under the influence of stomach acid. It stimulates secretion of water and bicarbonates from the pancreas.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12710,'biology',93,278,536,'Incorrect statement is:','[{"text": "Chromosomes as well as genes occur in triplet", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mendel could not provide any physical proof for the existence of factors.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In the Mendelian dihybrid cross, segregation of one pair of characters are independent from the segregation of the pair of characters.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linkage was given by Morgan", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Chromosomes and genes will always occur in pairs.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12713,'biology',91,1402,3344,'The figure below shows the structure of an endocrine gland with two parts labelled A and B. Select the option that correctly identifies a part along with its function.','[{"text": "A: Adrenal medulla -Brings about fight or flight response", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B: Adrenal cortex - Secretes corticosteroids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A: Adrenal cortex - Secretes corticoids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B: Adrenal medulla -Secretes two protein hormones", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The gland shown in the picture is the adrenal gland. \'A\' represents the adrenal cortex whereas \' $\\mathrm{B}$ \' represents the adrenal medulla. The adrenal cortex produces steroid hormones called corticoids. The adrenal medulla produces epinephrine and norepinephrine which are amino acid derivatives.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/91_12713_question_1.png'),
