(12778,'biology',93,278,536,'In a cross Drosophila, the heterozygous animal with grey body $\\left( {{b^ + }} \\right)$ and long wings $\\left( {v{g^ + }} \\right)$ was crossed with black body and vestigeal wings, the progeny has the animals in the following ratio : grey vestigeal 24; grey long 126; black long 26; black vestigeal 124.What is the frequency of recombinations in the population?','[{"text": "$16.7\\\\% $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$15.8\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$14.5\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$17.5\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In a cross Drosophila, the heterozygous animal with Gray body $\\left( {{b^ + }} \\right)$ and Long wing $\\left( {v{g^ + }} \\right)$ was cross with black body &amp; vestigial wings, the Recombination are gray vestigial 24, Black long 26, so, total Recombination 50, according to Recombination frequency formula<br>$R.F = \\frac{{{\\rm{Total}}\\,{\\rm{no}}{\\rm{.}}\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,{\\rm{Recombinants}}}}{{No.\\,of\\,progency}}$<br>$R.F = \\frac{{{\\rm{50}}}}{{{\\rm{300}}}} \\times 100 = 16.7\\% $',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12779,'biology',91,1402,3344,'Match Column I with Column II :<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Exophthalmic goitre<br>B. Acromegaly <br>C. Cushing\'s syndrome<br>D. Cretinism</div><div class="column-right">P. Excess secretion of cortisol<br>Q. Hypo secretion of thyroid hormone and stunted growth<br>R. Hyper secretion of thyroid hormone & protruding eye balls.<br>S. Excessive secretion of growth hormone</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  Q, C  -  P, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  Q, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  P, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-R , B-S, C-P, D-Q is the correct option.<br>A. Exophthalmic goiter - R - Hyper secretion of thyroid hormone and characterized by protruding eye balls<br>B. Acromegaly - S - Excessive secretion of growth hormone<br>C. Cushing\'s syndrome - P- Excess secretion of cortisol, moon face and hyperglycaemia<br>D. Cretinism - Q - Hyposecretion of thyroid hormone and characterized by stunted growth.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
