(12887,'biology',94,787,1693,'Isotopes used for proving semi-conservative replication of DNA are','[{"text": "${ }^{14} \\\\mathrm{N}$ and ${ }^{31} \\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${ }^{14} \\\\mathrm{~N}$ and ${ }^{14} \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Radioisotopes ${ }^{14} \\\\mathrm{~N}$ and ${ }^{15} \\\\mathrm{~N}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heavy isotopes ${ }^{14} \\\\mathrm{~N}$ and ${ }^{15} \\\\mathrm{~N}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Meselson and Stahl proved this by using cultured in E. coli in a cultural medium containing $^{{\\rm{15}}}{\\rm{N}}$ isotopes of heavy nitrogen . After the DNA replication of E.coli for some generations in $^{{\\rm{15}}}{\\rm{N}}$ medium, it was found that both strands of DNA had $^{{\\rm{15}}}{\\rm{N}}$ as constituent of purines and pyrimidines. Therefore, such DNA formed was found to be hybrid as one strand was made up of $^{{\\rm{15}}}{\\rm{N}}$ (old) and the other was made up of $^{{\\rm{14}}}{\\rm{N}}$ (new)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12888,'biology',93,285,549,'A man having Klinefelter’s syndrome is','[{"text": "Intersex with secondary sexual characters on the side of female", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Female with secondary sexual characters of male", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male with secondary sexual characters of female", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Normal fertile male", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Klinefelter syndrome is a chromosomal disorder, also known as 47, XXY or XXY. This condition result from two or more X chromosomes in males. Such individuals are counted as males phenotypically, but they can\nexhibit some female secondary characters (breast growth, less body hair)and are commonly sterile.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(12891,'biology',94,787,1693,'Matthew Meselson and Franklin Stahl grew_____ in a medium containing ${ }^{15} \\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}$ $\\left({ }^{15} \\mathrm{N}\\right.$ is the ___ isotope of nitrogen) as the only nitrogen source for many generations. The result was that______ was incorporated into newly synthesised DNA (as well as other nitrogen containing compounds).','[{"text": "<i>E. coli</i>, heavy, ${ }^{15} \\\\mathrm{N}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "bacteriophage, heavy, ${ }^{15} \\\\mathrm{N}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>E. coli</i>, radioactive, ${ }^{15} \\\\mathrm{N}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "bacteriophage, radioactive, ${ }^{15} \\\\mathrm{N}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Matthew Meselson and Franklin Stahl grew E. coli in a medium containing ${}^{{\\rm{15}}}{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{Cl}}\\,{\\rm{(15\\,N}}$ is the heavy isotope of nitrogen) as the only nitrogen source for many generations. The result was that ${ }^{15} \\mathrm{~N}$ was incorporated into newly synthesised DNA (as well as other nitrogen containing compounds).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
