(13005,'biology',96,1159,2772,'The puffed-up appearance of dough is due to the production of','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Water vapour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The puffed up appearance is due to production of $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ gas. Yeast produces 3 types of enzymes Amylase, Maltase & Zymase complex. Amylase changes small amount of starch into maltose, Maltase changes maltose to glucose, Zymase complex acts on glucose to form bubbles of ethyl alcohol and carbon dioxide.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13006,'biology',94,787,1694,'The molecular scissors of DNA are','[{"text": "Exonucleases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ligases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endonucleases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Polymerases", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The chemical knives/molecular scissors or genetic scalpels of DNA are endonucleases. The restriction enzymes are mostly used to cut the plasmids and DNA fragment at distinct points in such a way so as to carry sticky ends in both the molecules. Due to this, these enzymes are of great use in genetic engineering.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
