(13079,'biology',93,284,545,'Marriage between two sickle-cell carriers results into normal and sickle-cell carrier progenies in the ratio of','[{"text": "$2:1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1:2$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$3:1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1:2:1$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Three types of progenies are produced from marriage between sickle-cell carriers are one normal, two sickle-cell carriers and one sickle cell anaemic. The one sickle-cell anaemic diesleaving behind one normal and\ntwo sickle-cell carriers. Therefore, the ratio is 1 : 2.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
