(13088,'biology',96,1160,2774,'Identify the bacteria and fungi which was growing on in the culture plate which were plated by Alexander Fleming?','[{"text": "<i>Staphylococci, Penicillium notatum</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Streptococci, Penicillium notatum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Staphylococci, Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Streptococci, Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Alexander Fleming while working on Staphylococci bacteria, observed a mould growing in one of his unwashed culture plates around which Staphylococci could not grow. $$\\mathrm{He}$$ found out that it was due to a chemical produced by the mould and he named it Penicillin after the mould Penicillium notatum',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13090,'biology',94,788,1695,'Molecule into which the coded information in DNA is transcribed is','[{"text": "tRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "rRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "snRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "mRNA", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Messenger RNA or mRNA are the special type of RNA which carry the information stored in DNA to other parts of the cell. A portion of the cell\'s DNA serves as a template in creating an RNA molecule during transcription. In some cases, the newly formed RNA molecule in itself a finished product, and serves as a useful function within the cell while in other cases, messages are carried by RNA molecule from the DNA to other parts of the cell for processing.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13091,'biology',93,284,545,'Sickle-cell anaemia is caused by the substitution of _________ by _____ aminoacid. It occurs at the________position of _______ globin chain of haemoglobin molecule.','[{"text": "Valine, glutamic acid, sixth, beta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glutamic acid, valine, sixth, alpha", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glutamic acid, valine, sixth, beta", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Valine, glutamic acid, sixth, alpha", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Sickle cell anaemia is caused by the substitution of Glutamic acid (Glu) by Valine (Val) at the sixth position of the beta globin chain of the haemoglobin molecule.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
