(13095,'biology',94,788,1695,'Amino acid sequence, in protein synthesis is decided by the sequence of','[{"text": "mRNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "cDNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "rRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "tRNA", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The sequence of mRNA is decided by amino acid sequence in protein synthesis. The mRNA enters the cytoplasm taking the information from DNA and translating it into the specific sequence of amino acids. The translation starts with codons; which is a sequence of three nucleotides in the mRNA.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13096,'biology',96,1160,2774,'Name the scientist who received Nobel prize in 1945 for the discovery of penicillin as an antibiotic?','[{"text": "Alexander Fleming, Ernst Chain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ernst Chain, Howard Florey", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Howard Florey, Alexander Fleming, Ernst Chain", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alexander Fleming, Ernst Chain, Norman Borlaug", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Penicillin was the first antibiotic to be discovered by Alexander Fleming (1928). The antibiotic was, however, commercially extracted by efforts of Ernst Chain and Howard Florey. Fleming, Chain and Florey were togehter awarded Nobel Prize in 1945, for this discovery.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13108,'biology',94,788,1695,'If the coding strand has the sequence 5\'-ATCGATCG - 3\' then find out the sequence of non-coding strand.','[{"text": "3\'-TAGCTAGC - 5\'", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5\'- TACGTACG - 3\'", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5\'- UAGGUACG - 3\'", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5\'- UACFUACG - 3\'", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'If the coding strand has the sequence<br>5\'-ATCGATCG - 3\' then find out the sequence of non-coding strand.<br>(1) 3\'-TAGCTAGC-5\'',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13098,'biology',94,788,1695,'If both the strands copied during transcription, then what will happen?','[{"text": "The segment of DNA would be coding for two different proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two RNA will be produced simultaneously complementory to each other.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There will be formation of double helical RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'First, if both strands act as a template, they would code for RNA molecule with different sequences (Remember complementarity does not mean identical), and in turn, if they code for proteins, the sequence of amino acids in the proteins would be different. Hence, one segment of the DNA would be coding for two different proteins, and this would complicate the genetic information transfer machinery. Second, the two RNA molecules if produced simultaneously would be complementary to each other, hence would form a double stranded RNA. This would prevent RNA from being translated into protein and the exercise of transcription would become a futile one.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13099,'biology',93,284,544,'Match the columns I and II.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Hemophilia<br>B. Colour blindness<br>C. Pedigree analysis<br>D. Sickle cell anaemia</div><div class="column-right">P. Absence of particular pigments in cones<br>Q. Clotting protein<br>R. Identify inheritance in families<br>S. Mutation</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R, B – P , C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – R, C – P, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – P , B – R, C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – P , C – R, D – S", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Q, B-P,C-R, D-S',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
