(13104,'biology',94,788,1695,'The strand which do not code for anything is called','[{"text": "Coding strand", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Non-coding strand", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Template strand", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nonsense strand", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The strand which has the polarity $\\left(5^{\\prime} \\rightarrow 3^{\\prime}\\right)$ and the sequence same as RNA (except thymine at the place of uracil), is displaced during transcription. Strangely, this strand (which does not code for anything) is referred to as coding strand.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
