(13123,'biology',93,284,544,'Name the disease in which a single protein that is a part of the cascade of proteins involved in the clotting of blood is affected?','[{"text": "Haemophilia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sickle cell anemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Beta-thalasemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Color blindness", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hemophilia- In this disease, a single protein that is a part of the cascade of proteins involved in the clotting of blood is affected. Due to this, in an affected individual a simple cut will result in non-stop bleeding',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13124,'biology',94,788,1695,'The promoter site and the terminator site for transcription are located at:','[{"text": "3\' (downstream) end and 5\' (upstream) end, respectively of the transcription unit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5\' (upstream) end and 3\' (downstream) end, respectively of the transcription unit", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3\' (upstream) end and 5\' (downstream) end, respectively of the transcription unit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5\' (downstream) end and 3\' (upstream) end, respectively of the transcription unit", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The promoter is said to be located towards 5 \'-end (upstream) of the structural gene (the reference is made with respect to the polarity of coding strand). The terminator is located towards 3\'-end (downstream) of the coding strand and it usually defines the end of the process of transcription',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
