(13144,'biology',94,788,1695,'Why both the strands of DNA are not copied during transcription?','[{"text": "Because RNA molecule with different sequences will be formed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Because RNA molecule with same sequences will be formed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Because protein molecule with different aminoacid sequence will be formed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'If both strands act as a template, they would code for RNA molecule with different sequences (Remember complementarity does not mean identical), and in turn, if they code for proteins, the sequence of amino acids in the proteins would be different.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
