(13365,'biology',96,1164,2779,'The organisms which are used to enrich the nutrient quality of the soil are','[{"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyanobacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Microorganisms which act as biofertilisers are bacteria, cyanobacteria (blue green algae) and mycorrhizal fungi. Bacteria and cyanobacteria have the property of nitrogen fixation while mycorrhizal fungi preferentially withdraw minerals from organic matter for the plant with which they are associated.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
