(13401,'biology',96,1164,2779,'The symbiotic association of fungi with the roots of higher plants is called','[{"text": "Cyanobacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Commensalism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mycorrhiza", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lichen", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A mycorrhiza is a symbiotic (mutually beneficial) association between a fungus and the roots of a vascular higher plant. These are important components of soil life and soil chemistry.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13402,'biology',94,789,1698,'_____, gave the concept of genetic code is a combination of three nucleotides.','[{"text": "George Gamow", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nirenberg", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hargobind Khorana", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Severo Ochoa", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'George Gamow, gave the concept of genetic code is a combination of three nucleotides.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13404,'biology',93,281,539,'Identify the wrong statement','[{"text": "In domesticated fowls the sex of the\\nprogeny depends on the type of sperm\\nthat fertilizes the egg", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The human males have one of their sex\\nchromosomes much shorter than the other", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Usually female birds produce two types\\nof gametes based on sex chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In male grasshoppers 50% of the sperms\\nhave no sex chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In Birds, the females have one Z and one W chromosome, whereas males have a pair of Z-chromosomes besides the autosomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13405,'biology',96,1164,2779,'Fungi belonging to genus ____ takes part in mycorrhiza is ____','[{"text": "<i>Glomus</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Nostoc</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Azolla</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ulothrix</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Glomus</i> is a genus of arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi which forms endomycorrhiza, a symbiotic association with plant roots. The fungal symbiont in these associations absorbs phosphorous from soil and passes it to the plant. Plants having such associations show other benefits also, such as resistance to rootborne pathogens, tolerance to salinity and drought and an overall increase in plant growth and development.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13406,'biology',93,281,539,'Choose the incorrect pair with respect to sex determination in different organisms.','[{"text": "Grasshopper = XX-XY type", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Honey bee = Haplo-diploid type", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Drosophila </em>= XX-XY type", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Human = XX-XY type", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Grasshopper is an example of XO type of sex determination in which the males have only one X-chromosome besides the autosomes, whereas females have a pair of X-chromosomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13408,'biology',96,1164,2779,'Glomus is a','[{"text": "Genus of the kingdom cyanobacterium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus of the kingdom monera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genus of the kingdom fungi", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genus of the kingdom protista", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Glomus is a genus of Kingdom Fungi, and all species form symbiotic relationships (mycorrhizae) with plant roots.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13409,'biology',94,789,1698,'Genetic code translates the language of','[{"text": "Proteins into that of RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amino acids into that of RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RNA into that of proteins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "RNA into that of DNA", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The process of turning the genetic code in mRNA into an amino acid chain in preparation to make proteins is called translation. It starts with mRNA that is coded sequence of nucleotide bases called by A, G, C and U.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13410,'biology',93,281,539,'The unfertilised eggs in honey bees develop\ninto','[{"text": "Worker", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Queen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Males", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'An unfertilised egg develops as a male (drone) by means of parthenogenesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13412,'biology',96,1164,2779,'Mycorrhizae help in uptake of following nutrients','[{"text": "Sulpahtes and Manganese", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phosphorus and Nitrogen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nitrogen and Calcium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calcium and Selenium", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mycorrhizae are able to create a vast connection between the roots of a plant and with the soil around them which allows the fungus to uptake nutrients such as Nitrogen and Phosphorous for the plant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13413,'biology',94,789,1698,'The genetic code is present on the','[{"text": "polypeptide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "r-RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "t-RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "m-RNA", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The genetic code is present on the m-RNA.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13414,'biology',93,281,539,'Haplodiploid sex-determination system is seen\nin ______','[{"text": "Grass hopper", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Birds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Honey bees", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Humans", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The sex determination in honey bee is based on the number of sets of chromosomes an individual receives, Haplo-diploid system.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13416,'biology',96,1164,2779,'Symbiotic association helps the plants in what ways?','[{"text": "Resistance to root-borne pathogens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tolerance to salinity and drought", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase in growth and development", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of them are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13417,'biology',94,789,1698,'The scientist who gave the genetic code was a','[{"text": "Phycisist", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Geneticist", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biologist", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biochemist", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'George Gamow, a physicist, who argued that since there are only 4 bases and if they have to code for 20 amino acids, the code should constitute a combination of bases. He suggested that in order to code for all the 20 amino acids, the code should be made up of three nucleotides.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13418,'biology',93,281,539,'In honey bees, females are (i) and have (ii) chromosomes and males are (iii) and have (iv) chromosomes.','[{"text": "i-Haploid, iii- diploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i- diploid , iii- haploid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii- 32, iv - 16", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 & 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In honey bees, the males have half the number of chromosomes than that of a female. The females are diploid having 32 chromosomes and males are haploid, i.e., having 16 chromosomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13419,'biology',96,1164,2779,'A nitrogen fixing microbe associated with <i>Azolla</i> in rice fields is','[{"text": "<i>Frankia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Rhizobium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Spriulina</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Anabaena</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Anabaena azollae, a cyanobacterium that lives in symbiotic association with the freefloating water fern Azolla. Anabaena azollae can grow Photo-autotrophically and fixes atmospheric nitrogen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13421,'biology',94,789,1698,'_____cell-free system for protein synthesis finally helped the genetic code to be deciphere:','[{"text": "George Gamow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Marshal Nirenberg", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Har Gobind Khorana", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "J.D. Watson", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Marshall Nirenberg\'s cell-free system for protein synthesis finally helped the code to be deciphered.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13422,'biology',93,281,539,'In honey bee males produce sperms by______\nand females produce eggs by','[{"text": "Meiosis, Meiosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meiosis, mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "mitosis, Meiosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "mitosis, mitosis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In honey bee males produce sperms by mitosis and have 16 chromosomes in their gametes and females produce eggs by meiosis and have 16 chromosomes in the gametes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13423,'biology',96,1164,2779,'Which one of the following statements is correct?','[{"text": "Both <i>Azotobactor</i> and <i>Rhizobium</i> fix atmospheric nitrogen in root nodules of plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyanobacteria such as Anabaena and Nostoc are important mobilizers of phosphates and for plant nutrition in soil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biofertilisers are chemical fertilisers that enrich the nutrient quality of the soil.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Extensive use of chemical fertilizers may lead to eutrophication of nearby water bodies", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Root nodules are formed when nitrogenfixing bacteria called Rhizobia enter the cells of a host leguminous plant. Azotobacter is a genus of free-living diazotrophic bacteria whose resting stage is a cyst. It is primarily found in neutral to alkaline soils, in aquatic environments, and on some plants. It helps in atmospheric nitrogen fixation by conversion to ammonia. Cyanobacteria, Anabaena and Nostoc are mobilizers of nitrates and plant nutrition in soil. Organic fertilizers can be used to grow maize. Unlike chemical fertilizers, organic fertilizers reduce acidity in the soil and do not cause leaching. They do not kill beneficial micro-organisms in the soil. The prime contaminants are nitrates and phosphates, which act as plant nutrients and causes the excessive growth of algae which reduces the dissolved oxygen from water, vital to other aquatic life.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13425,'biology',94,789,1698,'The chemical method developed by____ was instrumental in synthesizing RNA molecules with defined combination of bases (homopolymers and copolymers):','[{"text": "Marshal Nirenberg", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "George Gamow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Har Gobind Khorana", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sanger", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The chemical method developed by Har Gobind Khoranawas instrumental in synthesizing RNA molecules with defined combination of bases (homopolymers and copolymers)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13426,'biology',93,281,539,'An offspring formed from the union of a sperm and an egg develops as a ________, and an unfertilised egg develops as a _________ by means of parthenogenesis.','[{"text": "Queen or worker, drone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only queen, drone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Drone, queen or worker", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only worker, drone", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'An offspring formed from the union of a sperm and an egg develops as a female (queen or worker), and an unfertilised egg develops as a male (drone) by means of parthenogenesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13427,'biology',96,1160,2774,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Kali khansi<br>B. Galghotu<br>C. Kusht rog</div><div class="column-right">P. Leprosy<br>Q. Pertussis<br>R. Diphtheria</div></div>','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A] Kali khansi - Pertussis<br>B] Gal ghotu - Diphtheria<br>C] Kusht rog - Leprosy',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13429,'biology',94,789,1698,'_______(polynucleotide phosphorylase) was also helpful in polymerising_____ with defined sequences in a template independent manner (enzymatic synthesis of RNA).','[{"text": "Marshal Nirenberg enzyme, DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Marshal Nirenberg enzyme, RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Severo Ochoa enzyme, DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Severo Ochoa enzyme, RNA", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Severo Ochoa enzyme (polynucleotide phosphorylase) was also helpful in polymerising RNA with defined sequences in a template independent manner (enzymatic synthesis of RNA).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13430,'biology',93,281,539,'What concept do the following sentences explain?<br>i. During spermatogenesis, two types of gametes are produced. 50 per cent of the sperm produced carry the X-chromosome and the rest 50 per cent has Y-chromosome.<br>ii. Females, produce only one type of ovum with an X-chromosome<br>iii. Genetic makeup of the sperm determines the sex of the child','[{"text": "Sex Determination in Grasshopper", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sex Determination in Honey bees", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sex Determination in Birds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sex Determination in Humans", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In humans, sex determining mechanism in case of humans is XY type. The genetic makeup of the sperm that determines the sex of the child.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13431,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <em>Aspergillus niger</em><br>B. <em>Clostridium butylicum</em><br>C. <em>Acetobacteraceti</em></div><div class="column-right">P. Citric acid<br>Q. Acetic acid<br>R. Butyric acid</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$,", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A] <em>Aspergillus niger </em>- Citric acid<br>B] <em>Clostridium butylicum </em>- Butyric acid<br>C] <em>Acetobacter</em> <em>Aceti </em>- Acetic acid',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13433,'biology',94,789,1698,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. George Gamow<br>B. Har Gobind Khorana<br>C. Marshal Nirenberg<br>D. Severo Ochoa</div><div class="column-right">P. Physicist<br>Q. Cell-free system for protein synthesis<br>R. Homopolymers &amp; copolymers<br>S. Polynucleotide phosphorylase</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{D}-\\mathrm{S}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13434,'biology',93,281,539,'A medical technician while observing a human\nblood smear under the microscope notes the\npresence of barr body close to the nuclear\nmembrane in the WBC. This indicates that\nperson under investigation is','[{"text": "Normal female", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Colourblind", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haemophilic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Normal male", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A Barr body is the inactive X-chromosome in a female somatic cell. A normal human female has only one Barr body per somatic cell',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13436,'biology',93,281,539,'Which of the following is incorrect regarding ZW-ZZ type of sex determination?','[{"text": "It occurs in birds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Females are heterogametic and males are\\nhomogametic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1:1 sex ration is produced in the offsprings", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13437,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Among the below given biomolecules how many of them are produced by heterotropes<br>Citric acid, Streptomycin, Ethylalcohol, Gibberellic acid, Statins, Cyclosporine - A, streptokinase, Roquefort Cheese, Swiss Cheese','[{"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "9", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All are heterotrophs. Streptokinase is a medication and enzyme which is used in the treatment of thrombosis. It is obtained from Streptococci bacteria.<br>Cyclosporin A is an immunosuppresant medication. It is used during transplantation. It is obtained from fungus Trichoderma polysporum.<br>Statin is a medication which is used for lowering the lipid levels. It is obtained from fungus Aspergillus terreus.<br>Swiss cheese is one of the varieties of cheese. There are 3 bacteria involved in the process of making Swiss cheese. These are Streptococcus thermophilus, Lactobacillus helveticus and Propionibacterium shermanii.<br>Citric acid is an organic acid. It is produced by the action of fungus Aspergillus niger on molasses.<br>Acetic acid is also called as vinegar. It is used in preparing food. It is obtained from Acetobacter.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13438,'biology',94,789,1698,'Most of the amino acids are represented by more than one codons, the genetic code is said to be','[{"text": "Degenerate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Deaminated", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Comma less", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Overlapping", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Each of the 20 amino acids is represented by at least one codon In the genetic code. Most of the amino acids are coded for by more than one codon. This is specified as degeneracy of the code.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13439,'biology',93,281,539,'Individuals having homomorphic sex\nchromosomes produce','[{"text": "Two different types of gamete", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One type of gametes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only X containing gametes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two gametes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Individuals having homomorphic sex chromosomes produce one type of gametes',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13440,'biology',96,1159,2772,'Select the correct answer<br>i. The LAB produce acids that coagulate and partially digest the milk proteins.<br>ii. Inoculum or starter contains millions of LAB is not necessary for conversion of milk to curd .<br>iii. LAB improves nutritional quality of fermented milk by increasing vitamin $$\\mathrm{B}_{12}$$.<br>iv. $$\\mathrm{LAB}$$ performs Anaerobic respiration releasing Lactic acid and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$.','[{"text": "Only i and iii are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only ii and iv are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Microbes such as. Lactobacillus and others commonly called lactic acid bacteria (LAB) grow in milk and convert it into curd. During growth, such bacteria produce adds (mainly lactic add) that coagulate and partially digest the milk proteins. A small amount of curd, known as starter, is added to the milk and kept at a suitable temperature, where lactic acid bacteria multiply in millions and converts milk into curd that also improves its nutritional quality by increasing vitamin BI2. It also checks the growth of disease-causing microbes in the stomach.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13442,'biology',94,789,1698,'Degeneracy refers to','[{"text": "One amino acid has more than one code triplet", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One amino acid has only one code triplet", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Codons which specify the same amino acids defer only in the third base of the triplet", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Some amino acids are coded by more than one codon, hence the code is degenerate, the codons generally differ in third base - wobble base.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13443,'biology',93,281,539,'Female heterogamety is seen in','[{"text": "Humans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Drosophila", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Grasshopper", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Birds", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In birds, the females have one Z and one W chromosome, whereas males have a pair of Z-chromosomes besides the autosomes.so female are heterogamous.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13446,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Identify the incorrect statement about biological control of pests/diseases using microbes?','[{"text": "The majority of baculoviruses used as biological control agents are in the genus Nucleopolyhedrovirus.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Trichoderma</i> species are free-living fungi that are very common in the shoot ecosystems.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lady bird beetle against mosquitoes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Trichoderma</i> sp. against certain plant pathogens", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Trichoderma sp are free living fungi that are effective biocontrol agents of several pathogens in root ecosystem.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13451,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Which of the following statements is correct?<br>I. Single cell protein is rich in high quality proteins but poor in fat.<br>II. BOD is the amount of oxygen that would be consumed if all the inorganic matter in one litre of water were oxidised by bacteria.<br>III.&nbsp;<em>Trichoderma</em> sp are free living fungi that are effective biocontrol agents of several pathogens.<br>IV. Baculoviruses are pathogens that attack insects and other arthropods.<br>V.&nbsp;<em>Bacillus thuringiensis</em> is first used biopesticide.<br>VI. Lactase enzyme is used in alcoholic fermentation.<br>VII. Mycorrhiza is a symbiotic association between fungi e.g.&nbsp;<em>Glomus </em>and vascular plant.','[{"text": "II, III, VI, VII", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V, VII", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'BOD is the amount of oxygen that would be consumed if all the organic matter in one litre of water were oxidised by bacteria. Invertase enzyme is used in alcoholic fermentation. This are corrected statements.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
