(13471,'biology',96,1162,2777,'Pollution from animal excreta and organic waste from kitchen can be most profitably minimized by','[{"text": "Using them for producing biogas", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Using them directly as biofertilizer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Using them directly as bioinsecticide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Organic farming", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Pollution from animal excreta and organic waste from kitchen can be most profitably minimized by using them for producing biogas.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13473,'biology',93,281,539,'The barr body is observed in','[{"text": "Neutrophils of males", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neutrophils of females", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Eosinophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Basophils of males", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The presence of barr body can be seen in the neutrophils (i.e. polymorphonuclear leucocytes) of 3 -5 % cells in females, but can’t be seen in males.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13475,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Which one of the following is false statement on sustainable agriculture and organic farming?','[{"text": "Sustainable agriculture is an agriculture practice which uses renewable resources and causes minimum pollution and maintains optimum yield level.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sustainability of agriculture will be enhanced if there is reduction in use of non-renewable resources and decrease in the level of pollution.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sustainable agriculture and organic farming causes negative impacts on soil health.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It includes usage of biofertilizers, biopesticides, bioherbicides and vermicomposting.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Sustainable agriculture and organic farming imroves on soil health by increase of fertility and doesnot cause any negative impacts on yield, soil etc, and it is ecofriendly.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13477,'biology',93,281,539,'&nbsp;In &nbsp;<em>Drosophila</em>, the sex is determined by','[{"text": "X and Y chromosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only by X chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only by Y chromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Whether the egg is fertilized", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In human beings and in <em>Drosophila </em>the males have one X and one Y chromosome, whereas females have a pair of X-chromosomes besides autosomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13479,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Fill up blanks by selecting the correct option<br>i. ____ have been commercialized as blood cholesterol lowering agent<br>ii. ____ used as an immunosuppressive agent in organ transplant patients<br>iii.____ is a tissue plasminogen activator','[{"text": "Statins, Cyclosporin A, Streptokinase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cyclosporin A, Statins, Chymosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyclosporin A, Citric acid, Butyric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'i. Statins, ii. Cylosporine A, iii. Sterptokinase',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13481,'biology',93,281,539,'In humans, chromosomal condition of male is','[{"text": "44 AA + XX", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "44 AA + XO", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "44 AA + XY", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "44 AA + XXY", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In human males, 22 chromosome pairs (i.e., 44) called autosomes are there and a XY pairing sex chromosome. Thus, 44 AA (autosomes)+ XY (sex chromosomes) chromosomes are present in males.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13483,'biology',96,1160,2774,'In 1928, a scientist discovered the first effective antibiotic, scientist and antibiotic are','[{"text": "Flemming- streptomycin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flemming- penicillin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Waksman- pencillin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Waksman- streptomycin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In September 1928 when Alexander Fleming observed his Petri dishes of the bacterial culture he notice that the culture of bacteria <i>Staphylococcus</i> has a mould growing over it which has inhabited its growth in that area. Upon observing he found that the mould was a strain of fungus Penicillium notatum and its was secreting some substance which inhibited the growth of the bacteria. He named it penicillin after the organism from which it is secreted.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13485,'biology',93,281,539,'A family of five daughters only is expecting sixth issue. The chance of its being son is','[{"text": "Zero", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$50\\\\% $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$25\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$100\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Always there will be 50% chance tohave either X or Y chromosome in the Human sperm. Hence male gamete genotype is basis of Sex- determination in Humans.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13487,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Which of the following statement is incorrect w.r.t. pectinases?','[{"text": "They are used in clearing of fruit juices", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These are enzymes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are obtained from by <i>Saccharomyces flavous</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They are used in retting of fibres", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In bottle fruit juices that our ability may occur due to the presence of pulp or plant residues. Pectinase is an enzyme which is used in breaking down the polysaccharide pectin which is present in cell walls. This can completely remove the turbidity of the bottled fruit juices.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13489,'biology',93,281,539,'In XO type of sex determination.','[{"text": "Females produce two different types of\\ngametes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male produce two different types of\\ngametes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Females produce gametes with Y\\nchromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Males produce gametes with Y\\nchromosome", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In XO type, all eggs bear an additional X-chromosome besides the other chromosomes (autosomes). Some of the sperms bear the X-chromosome whereas some do not',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13491,'biology',96,1161,2776,'Select incorrect w.r.t sewage teatment plants.','[{"text": "In anaerobic sludge digester, gases like methane, $$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{~S}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ are also produced.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacterial flocs are allowed to sediment in setting tank when BOD of sewage is high.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Primary treament of sludge is based on sequential filtration and sedimentation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Activated sludge is pumped into anaerobic sludge digesters to digest the bacteria and fungi", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The effluent from aeration tank is passed into a settling tank where the aerobic bacterial \'flocs\' are allowed to sediment and the sediment is called activated sludge, when the BOD of sewage is high. Biogas is produced by the activity of anaerobic bacteria on activated sludge.<br>Methano bacterium is an anaerobic bacteria found in rumen of cattle.<br>Biogas is a mixture of gases such as methane, hydrogen sulphide and carbon dioxide.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13493,'biology',93,281,539,'Sex-determination is controlled by ....A....and\nthe remaining chromosomes which are not\ninvolved in sex-determination are .....B.....','[{"text": "Allosomes Autosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sex-chromosomes  Autosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sex-chromosomes  Allosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sex-determination is controlled by Allosomes (Sex-chromosomes) and the remaining chromosomes which are not involved in sex-determination are Autosomes',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13495,'biology',96,1164,2779,'Farmers have reported over $$50 \\%$$ higher yields of rice by using the biofertilizer :','[{"text": "Mycorrhiza", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Azolla pinnata</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cyanobacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Legume-<i>Rhizobium</i> symbiosis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Anabaena azollae</i>, a cyanobacterium living in the cavities of fern Azolla, fixes atmospheric nitrogen and releases it into the leaf cavity of the fern. Farmers have reported over 50% higher yields by using <i>Azolla pinnata</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13497,'biology',93,281,539,'XO type of sex determination is seen in','[{"text": "Man", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Drosophila</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Birds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Grasshopper", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The XO sex-determination system is the system which decides the sex of offspring among grasshoppers . There is only one sex chromosome in this system, referred to as X. Males only have one X chromosome (X0), whereas females have a pair or two (XX) chromosomes . The zero (frequently, the letter O) indicates the lack of a second X.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13499,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Study the following table<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{{\\rm{Table}}\\,{\\rm{ - 1}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}&{}&{}\\\\\n{{\\rm{i}}{\\rm{.}}\\,Aspergillus\\,niger}&{{\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{fungus}}\\,\\,\\,}&{{\\rm{Citric}}\\,{\\rm{acid}}\\,\\,}\\\\\n{{\\rm{ii}}{\\rm{.}}\\,Saccharomyces\\,\\,}&{{\\rm{Algae}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}&{{\\rm{Ethanol}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}\\\\\n{cerevisiae\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}&{}&{}\\\\\n{{\\rm{iii}}{\\rm{.}}\\,Lactobacillus\\,\\,\\,}&{{\\rm{Bacterium}}}&{{\\rm{Pencillin}}\\,\\,\\,\\,}\\\\\n{delbruchii\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}&{}&{}\\\\\n{{\\rm{iv}}{\\rm{.}}\\,Streptococcus\\,\\,\\,}&{{\\rm{Bacterium}}}&{{\\rm{Clot}}\\,{\\rm{buster}}}\\\\\n{sps\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}&{}&{}\n\\end{array}$<br>The correct combination is','[{"text": "i & ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i & iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i & iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii & iv", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Aspergillus</i> produces citric acid Saccharomyces is a fungi uses sugars to form alcohols.<br><i>Lactobacillus</i> is a genus of Gram-positive, facultative anaerobic, rod-shaped, nonspore-forming bacteria. They convert sugars to lactic acid. <i>Streptococci</i> produces clot buster streptokinase.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13501,'biology',93,281,539,'Grasshopper is an example of XO type of sex\ndetermination in which the males have','[{"text": "One X chromosome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One Y chromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two X chromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No X chromosome", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Grasshopper is an example of XO type of sex determination in which the males have only one X-chromosome besides the autosomes, whereas females have a pair of X-chromosomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13503,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Tissue plasminogen activator is','[{"text": "An enzyme", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amino acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A vitamin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A chemical that stimulate tissue differentiation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Tissue plasminogen activator is a serine protease found on endothelial cells involved in the break down of blood clots.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13505,'biology',93,281,539,'Due to the involvement of the X-chromosome in the determination of sex, it was designated to be the________, and the rest of the chromosomes were named as_________.','[{"text": "Autosomes ,sex chromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sex chromosome, autosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Due to the involvement of the X-chromosome in the determination of sex, it was designated to be the sex chromosome, and the rest of thechromosomes were named as autosomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
