(13509,'biology',93,281,539,'Name the scientist who traced a specific\nnuclear structure all through spermatogenesis\nin a few insects?','[{"text": "Henking (1981)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Henking (1891)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Henking (1819)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Henking (1918)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Henking (1891) could trace a specific nuclear structure all through spermatogenesis in a few insects.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13511,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Which of the following statements about mycorrhizae is false?<br>I. Gymnosperms may also possess mycorrhizae<br>II. The mycorrhizal association of fungus and the plant may have had importance in the evolution of land plant<br>III. The mycorrhizal association is a mutualistic symbiosis<br>IV. Fungal partner is associated with the only roots of the higher plants (like angiosperms)<br>V. Only advanced modern plants such as angiosperms possess mycorrhizae','[{"text": "Only IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II and V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The mycorrhizal symbiosis is arguably the most important symbiosis on earth. Fossil records indicate that arbuscular mycorrhizal interactions evolved 400 to 450 million years ago and that they played a critical role in the colonization of land by plants. Approximately $$80 \\%$$ of all known land plant species form mycorrhizal interactions with ubiquitous soil fungi. The majority of these mycorrhizal interactions is mutually beneficial for both partners and is characterized by a bidirectional exchange of resources across the mycorrhizal interface. The mycorrhizal fungus provides the host plant with nutrients, such as phosphate and nitrogen, and increases the abiotic (drought, salinity, heavy metals) and biotic (root pathogens) stress resistance of the host. In return for their beneficial effect on nutrient uptake, the host plant transfers between 4 and $$20 \\%$$ of its photosynthetically fixed carbon to the mycorrhizal fungus',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13513,'biology',93,281,539,'Sex- linked characters are usually','[{"text": "Recessive", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Non-inherited", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dominant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lethal", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In both segments of X and Y-chromosomes, genes for sex linked characters occur. About 120 sex linked characters are found in man. Mostly these characters are recessive.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13515,'biology',96,1161,2776,'Formation of flocs means','[{"text": "Association of virus with the bacterial remains in water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria which is associated with the mycorrhiza of the fungus of soil", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria which is associated with the mycorrhiza of the fungus of water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria which is associated with the fungi in solid waste of the water", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Formation of flocs means bacteria associated with fungi in the solid waste of the water.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13517,'biology',93,281,539,'The concept of sex-linked inheritance was\nintroduced by?','[{"text": "T H Morgan", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hugo de Vries", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "G Pontecarno", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (2) and (1)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The concept of sex-linked inheritance was introduced by T.H. Morgan in Drosophila melanogaster. While experimenting, on dihydrid cross between eye colour & body colour in one cross and eye colour and wing\nsize in other.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13519,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Which of the following microbial organisms can be used as biocontrol agents?<br>i. Lady bird beetle and NPV,<br>ii. Dragon flies,<br>iii. Bt and&nbsp;<em>Gambusia</em>&nbsp;fish,<br>iv.&nbsp;<em>Trichoderma</em>&nbsp;&amp; Bt','[{"text": "iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iv", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<em>Trichoderma </em>&amp; <em>Bacillus thuringiensis </em>are microbes, used as biocontrol agents.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13520,'biology',93,280,538,'Pleiotropic gene','[{"text": "One gene regulates many phenotypic\\ncharacters", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One gene one character", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiple allelism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polygenic inheritance", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A single gene can exhibit multiple phenotypic expression. Such a gene is called a pleiotropic gene.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
