(13524,'biology',93,280,538,'What concept do the following sentences explain?<br> i. The effect of the gene is on metabolic pathways which contribute towards different phenotypes<br> ii. Phenylketonuria and sickle cell anaemia\nare examples of this type of inheritance<br> iii. Starch synthesis in pea seeds is also an example','[{"text": "Polygenetic inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pleiotropy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Multiple alleles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Co - dominance", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All of the following statements indicate pleiotropy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13527,'biology',96,1164,2779,'Biofertilizers include','[{"text": "Blue green algae, <em>Rhizobium</em> and other $\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ fixing bacteria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Blue green algae, <em>Rhizobium</em> and lichens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Rhizobium</em>, other $\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ fixing bacteria and lichen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blue green algae, <em>Rhizobium</em> and <em>Saccharomyces</em>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Blue green algae, <em>Rhizobia</em> and other $\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ fixing bacteria are used as biofertilizers.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13528,'biology',93,281,539,'The initial clue about the genetic/chromosomal mechanism of sex determination can be traced back to some of the experiments carried out in','[{"text": "Birds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Humans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fishes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insects", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The initial clue about the genetic/ chromosomal mechanism of sex determination can be traced back to some of the experiments carried out in insects.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13531,'biology',96,1162,2777,'Select the correct statements from the following','[{"text": "Activated sludge - sediment in settling tanks of sewage treatment plant is a rich source of aerobic bacteria.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Biogas to produced by the activity of virus on animal waste", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Methanobacteria</i> is an aerobic bacterium found in rumen of cattle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bio-gas, commonly called gobar gas, is pure methane", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Methanobacterium are anaerobic organisms.<br>Biogas refers to a mixture of different gases produced by the breakdown of organic matter in the absence of oxygen.<br>Activated sludge-sediment in settlement tanks of sewage treatment plant is a rich source of aerobic bacteria. Biogas can be produced by anaerobic digestion with anaerobic bacteria.\'Activated sludge- sediment in settlement tanks of sewage treatment plant is a rich source of aerobic bacteria\'.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13532,'biology',93,278,536,'Genetic maps are beneficial as they were','[{"text": "Extensively used as a starting point in the\\nsequencing of whole genomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It helps to measure the distance between\\ngenes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mapping the position of genes on\\nchromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13535,'biology',96,1159,2772,'The most abundant prokaryotes helpful to humans in making curd from milk and in production of antibiotics are the one categoriged as','[{"text": "Chemosynthetic autotrophs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterotrophic bacteria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cyanobacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Archaebacteria", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Heterotrophic bacteria require an organic carbon source for growth (i.e., they derive energy and carbon from organic compounds). Economically important uses of heterotrophic bacteria are:<br>They enhance the fertility of the soil by nitrogen fixation.<br>Production of curd and yogurt from milk, cheese, butter, wine, Production of antibiotics. They form an essential part of biogeochemical cycles during which they release essential elements, such as nitrogen and carbon for recycling. Cleaning of oil spills',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13536,'biology',93,280,538,'Occasionally a single gene may express more than one effect, this is','[{"text": "Polygenetic inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pleiotropy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Multiple alleles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Co - dominance", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A single gene can exhibit multiple phenotypic expression. Such a gene is called a pleiotropic gene and the process is called pleiotropy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13551,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Which microorganism is useful to obtain short chain fatty acids?','[{"text": "<i>Saccharomyces cereviseae</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Azotobacter aceti</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Clostridium butyricum</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Aspergillus niger</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Short chain fatty acids- Butyric acid = is produced by Clostridium butyricum',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13539,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Which one (s) is/are correct about Cyclosporin A?','[{"text": "It is produced by the fungus <em>Trichoderma polysporum</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is used as an immuno suppressive agent during organ transplantation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is produced by a type of yeast, <em>Monascus purpureus</em>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cyclosporin is an effective immunosuppressant used in the treatment of autoimmune disorders (such as rheumatoid arthritis) and in organ transplantation to prevent rejection. Cyclosporin lowers the activity of T-cells and hence, suppressing the activity of the immune system. Cyclosporin is isolated from the fungus <em>Trichoderma polysporum</em>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13540,'biology',93,278,536,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Law of segregation<br>B. Dihybrid test cross<br>C. Dihybrid cross fruit fly<br>D. Re-discovery of Mendel’s work</div><div class="column-right">P. Purity of gametes<br>Q. Morgan<br>R. Mendel<br>S. de Vries</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R , B – P , C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q , B – R , C – P, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – P , B – R , C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A – Q , B – P , C – R , D – S", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-P , B-R, C-Q, D-S',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13543,'biology',96,1159,2772,'Read the following four statements to find out certain mistakes in two of them :<br>I. Dough, which is used for making foods such as dosa and idlii is fermented by fungi and algae<br>II. Toddy, a traditional drink of southern India is made by fermenting sap from palms<br>III. Large holes in Swiss cheese are due to production of large amount of methane by&nbsp;<em>Propionibacterium shermanii<br></em>IV. In our stomach, lactic acid bacteria play very benficial role in checking disease causing microbes<br>Which are the two statements having mistakes?','[{"text": "Statements I &amp; III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statements I &amp; II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statements II &amp; III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statements III &amp; IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I. Dough, which is used for making foods such as dosa and idli is fermented by fungi and bacteria.<br>III. Large holes in \'Swiss cheese\' are due to production of large amount of $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ by <em>Propionibacterium shermanii</em>',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13544,'biology',93,278,536,'The distance between the genes is measured\nby','[{"text": "Centimetres", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Map unit", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dobson unit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Millimetre", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The distance between the genes is measured by map unit.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13547,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Benefits of mycorrhizae are<br>i. Resistance to root-borne pathogens<br>ii. Tolerance to salinity and absorption of phosphorus<br>iii. Tolerance to drought<br>iv. Overall increase in the plant growth and development','[{"text": "Only i and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii and iv", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mycorrhiza is a symbiotic association between fungus and the roots of higher plants. In this association, the fungal hyphae form a closely woven mass around the rootlets or penetrate the cells of the root and enhance nutrition and water uptake by the roots of the plants. Such plants are resistant to water stress, root borne pathogens, salinity etc. The roots in turn provide essential nutrients for the growth of the fungi.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13548,'biology',93,278,536,'If Mendel had an idea of linkage, then which\nof the following laws, he would not have been\nable to explain?','[{"text": "Law of indominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of independent assortment", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Law of segregation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of purity of gametes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mendel was not able to get any linkage due to the Law of independent assortment.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13552,'biology',93,278,536,'How many of the following sentences are not\ntrue with regards to Morgan?','[{"text": "He carried out several dihybrid crosses in\\nDrosophila", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "He coined the term linkage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Morgan coined term recombination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mendel carried out dihybrid crosses on\\nPisum", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mendel carried out dihybrid crosses on Pisum, this is not related to Morgan.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13555,'biology',96,1161,2776,'Match the Column I with Column II-<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. The stage in which physical treatment of sewage is done<BR>B. The stage in which biological treatement of sewage is done<BR>C. The names of sediment and supernatant in primary treatment<BR>D.___is carried to aeration tanks from primary settling<BR>E. Site of flocs growth<BR>F. Name of the sediment of secondary settling<BR>G. The function of sludge digester</div><div class="column-right">P. Anaerobic digestion of activated sludge and production of biogas<BR>Q. Activated sludge<BR>R. Aeration tanks<BR>S. Primary effluent<BR>T. Primary sludge, effluent<BR>U. Secondary treatment<BR>V. Primary treatment</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - P,\\\\,B - R,C - T,D - V,E - Q,\\\\,F - S,G - U}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - V,\\\\,B - U,C - T,D - S,E - R,\\\\,F - Q,G - P}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - P,\\\\,B - Q,C - R,D - S,E - T,\\\\,F - U,G - V}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - V,\\\\,B - U,C - P,D - Q,E - R,\\\\,F - S,G - T}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{A - V,\\,B - U,C - T,D - S,E - R,\\,F - Q,G - P}}$',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
