(13603,'biology',93,278,536,'A fruitfly has two genes for eye colour, but each of its sperm cell has only one. This illustrates','[{"text": "Independent assortment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linked genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pleiotropy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Segregation", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A fruitfly has two genes for eye colour, but each of its sperm cell has only one. This illustrates the law of segregation. As according to law of segregation, when an organism produces gametes, then each gamete gets one gene copy only, that is chosen randomly.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13604,'biology',96,1161,2776,'What would happen if oxygen availability to activated sludge flocs is reduced?','[{"text": "It will slow down the rate of degradation of organic matter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The center of flocs will become anoxic, which would cause death of bacteria and eventually breakage of flocs.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Flocs would increase in size as anaerobic bacteria would grow around flocs.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protozoa would grow in large numbers.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The center of flocs will become anoxic, which would cause death of bacteria and eventually breakage of flocs.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
