(13609,'biology',93,278,536,'Find out the incorrect sentence:<br>a. Sutton and Boveri argued that the pairing and separation of a pair of chromosomes would lead to the segregation of a pair of factors they carried.<br>b. Theodore Sutton and Walter Boveri noted that the behaviour of chromosomes was parallel to the behaviour of genes and used chromosome movement to explain Mendel’s laws<br>c. Morgan found that the genes for colour of the body and colour of the eye were very tightly linked and showed only 1.3 percent recombination','[{"text": "a", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a,b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b,c", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statement b is incorrect, the correct statement is - Walter Sutton and Theodore Boveri noted that the behaviour of chromosomes was parallel to the behaviour of genes and used chromosome movement to explain Mendel’s laws',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
