(13688,'biology',93,271,529,'Mendel investigated characters in the garden pea plant that were manifested as ______traits','[{"text": "Three similar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three opposing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two similar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two opposing", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mendel investigated characters in the garden pea plant that were manifested as two opposing traits, e.g., tall or dwarf plants, yellow or green seeds.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13670,'biology',96,1164,2779,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Nitrogen fixing enzyme in legume root nodules functions at low oxygen concentration.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Low oxygen concentration is provided by Leghaemoglobin.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Oxygen is required to generate sufficient respiratory energy to drive $$\\mathrm{N}_{2}$$ fixation, but too much oxygen inactivates nitrogenase. Biological nitrogen fixation occurs when atmospheric nitrogen is converted to ammonia by a pair of bacterial enzyme called nitrogenase. In root nodules the $$\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$ level is regulated by special haemoglobin (leghaemoglobin).The globin protein is encoded by plant genes but the heme factor is made by the symbiotic bacteria. This is produced only when the plant is infected with Rhizobium. The plant root cells convert sugar to organic acids which they supply to the bacteroids. In exchange, the plant receives Amino acids.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
