(13673,'biology',96,1160,2775,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> A person admitted to hospital as he had myocardial infarction. A cardiologist injected him \'Streptokinase\'.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> \'Streptokinase\' is tissue plasminogen activator.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Streptokinase is also called as tissue plasminogen activator or TPA which is obtained from haemolytic Streptococcus species. It is used as Fibrinolytic and also used in Myocardial infarction and Transient ischemic attack.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13676,'biology',93,271,529,'The technique of removal of stamens in hybridisation used by Mendel was','[{"text": "Emasculation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Back cross", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Double cross", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Single cross", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A process in which plants belonging to different species are artificially cross pollinated is called hybridisation. Emasculation is the important step which was used by Mendel , it means removal of anthers or stamens before anthesis to prevent self pollination in bisexual flowers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13677,'biology',96,1163,2778,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Nowadays production/use of herbicide resistant GM crops has increased.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It eliminates weeds from the field without the use of manual labour.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The main objective of using herbicide resistant GM crops is to reduce herbicide accumulation in food articles for health safety.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13680,'biology',93,271,529,'Emasculation is','[{"text": "Removal of carpels from Unisexual flowers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Removal of anther from bisexual flower bud after it dehisces using a pair of forceps", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Removal of anther from bisexual flower bud before it dehisces using a pair of forceps", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Removal of carpels from bisexual flowers.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Emasculation means removal of anthers or stamens before anthesis to prevent self pollination in bisexual flowers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13681,'biology',96,1160,2775,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> produces acetic acid.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i> produces blood cholesterol lowering agent.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Saccharomyces cerevisiae is used for commercial production of ethanol,<br>Monascus purpureus have been commercialised as blood-cholesterol lowering agents.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13684,'biology',93,271,529,'Find the correct statement w.r.t. Mendel’s investigations into inheritance','[{"text": "It was for the first time that statistical analysis and mathematical logic were applied to problems in biology.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "His experiments had a small sampling size, which gave greater credibility to the data that he collected.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The confirmation of his inferences from experiments on successive generations of his test plants, proved that his results pointed to general rules of inheritance rather than being unsubstantiated ideas.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 & 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Option 1 and 3 are correct , so option 4 is correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13685,'biology',96,1159,2772,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Curdling is required in the manufacture of cheese.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Lactic acid bacteria are used for the purpose.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The manufacture of cheese requires two main steps: curdling and ripening. In curdling the milk protein forms a solid material from which the water is drained. The curdling process is microbiological, since production of lactic acid bacteria is sufficient to coagulate milk proteins.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13690,'biology',96,1160,2775,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Organ transplantation patients are given immunosuppressive drugs.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Transplanted tissue has antigens which stimulate immune response of the patient.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'An organ transplant is the transfer of organ or tissue including bone marrow from a living person or a cadaver to another living person to replace his non-functioning organ. Immune suppressants dampen the immune system components. They are primarily used to prevent allograft rejection after organ transplantation. Foreign blood or tissue can trigger a blood transfusion reaction or transplantation, the match is usually not perfect. No two people have identical tissue antigens. Suppressing the immune response can treat and prevent transplant rejection.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13692,'biology',93,271,529,'Select the correct statement for truebreeding line _____','[{"text": "Undergoes continuous self-pollination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shows stable trait inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Expression for several generations.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A truebreeding line is one that, having undergone continuous self-pollination, shows the stable trait inheritance and expression for several generations.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13693,'biology',96,1164,2779,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Nowadays people realised that there is a large pressure to switch to organic farming.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Biofertilizers are organisms that enrich the nutrient quality of soil.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Organic farming is an agriculture practice which uses renewable resources, causes minimum pollution and maintains optimum yield. The various components of organic farming are Biofertilizers, Biopesticides and non-use of artificial fertilizers and chemical pesticides.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13696,'biology',93,271,529,'Match the columns I (Characters) and II.\n(Contrasting Traits)<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Flower colour<br>B. Pod shape<br>C. Pod colour<br>D. Seed shape</div><div class="column-right">P. White<br>Q. Yellow<br>R. Constricted<br>S. Wrinkled</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R, B – P, C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – R, C – P, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – P , B – R, C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A – Q, B – P, C – R, D – S", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-P, B-R, C-Q, D-S',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13697,'biology',96,1160,2774,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> While working on <em>staphylococci</em>, Alexander Fleming observed that Penicillium notatum inhibits the growth of the bacteria.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> This inhibiting chemical was commercially extracted and its full potential was established by Alexander Fleming.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Alexander Fleming while working on&nbsp;<em>Staphylococci bacteria</em>, once observed a mould growing in one of his unwashed culture plates around which&nbsp;<em>Staphylococci</em>&nbsp;could not grow. He found that it was due to a chemical produced by the mould and he named it Penicillin after the mould Penicillium notatum. However, its full potential as an effective antibiotic was established by Ernest chain and Howard florey.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13700,'biology',93,271,529,'The dominant flower colour in Pea is','[{"text": "Pink", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "White", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Yellow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Violet", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Violet is the dominant flower colour and white is recessive.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13702,'biology',96,1163,2778,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> A gene <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> is incorporated in plant genome to increase their yield.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> has $$\\mathrm{Bt}$$ toxin producing gene, which will kill the larva of insects.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bacillus thuringiensis is a gram positive soil dwelling bacterium, commonly used as biological pesticide. In 1976 Robert A Zakharyan reported the presence of a plasmid in a strain and suggested the plasmid involvement in endospore and crystal formation. Spores and crystalline produced by this have been used to control pests so plant yield also increased e.g, Cotton.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
