(13803,'biology',99,1322,3205,'A functional unit of nature, where living organisms interact among themselves and also with the surrounding physical environment is','[{"text": "Community", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecosystem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biosphere", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ecosystem is structural and functional unit of biosphere, consisting of community of living organisms and physical environment by interacting and exchanging materials between them',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13817,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Biotic components refer to','[{"text": "Decomposers only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Producers only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Living organisms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Consumers only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The biotic components of an ecosystem refer to all living organisms like plants, animals and microbes, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13804,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Which of the following are the critical research areas of biotechnology?','[{"text": "Providing best catalyst", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Creating optimal conditions for catalyst function", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Downstreaming processing technique", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Three critical research areas of biotechnology are:<br>(i) Providing the best catalyst in the form of improved organism usually a microbe or pure enzyme.<br>(ii) Creating optimal conditions through engineering for a catalyst to act, and<br>(iii) Downstream processing technologies to purify theprotein/organic compound.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13805,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Ecosystem is','[{"text": "The community of organisms interacting with one another", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The community of organisms together with the environment in which they live", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Part of the earth and its atmosphere which inhibits living organisms.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ecosystem is structural and functional unit of biosphere, consisting of community of living organisms and physical environment by interacting and exchanging materials between them .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13806,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Out of the following which method/ process is used for increasing food production?','[{"text": "Agrochemical based agriculture, Organic agriculture", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetically engineered crop-based agriculture", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Using high quantities of chemical fertilisers and pesticides", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Three options that can be thought for increasing food production<br>(i) agro-chemical based agriculture;<br>(ii) organic agriculture; and<br>(iii) genetically engineered crop-based agriculture.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13807,'biology',99,1322,3205,'The basic categories of ecosystem are','[{"text": "Aquatic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Terrestrial", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aerial and desert", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The basic categories of ecosystem are aquatic and terrestrial. The terrestrial ecosystem could be forest, grassland, desert, etc. Wehreas aquatic ecosystem are ponds, lake, sea, wetland, freshwater streams, estuaries, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13808,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Organic agriculture is a technique of raising crops for','[{"text": "Increased food production", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reduced use of chemical based fertilisers and pesticides", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Increasing the use of agrochemicals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Organic agriculture is the technique of raising crops, which is aimed at reducing the need for chemical fertilisers and pesticides, which are harmful to both mankind and environment. Food production in organic agriculture is compatatively low as compared to other methods, which include the use of pesticides and herbicides.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13809,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Example of man-made ecosystem are?','[{"text": "Crop field", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aquarium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Desert", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Crop field and aquarium both are man made',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13810,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Plants, bacteria, fungi and animals whose genes have been altered by manipulation are called','[{"text": "Recombinant organisms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hybrid organism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetically modified organisms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Super-organisms", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Plants, bacteria, fungi and animals whose genes have been altered by manipulation are called Genetically Modified Organisms (GMO).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13811,'biology',99,1322,3205,'What is the original source of energy of the living organisms?','[{"text": "DNA and RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ATP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sunlight", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sun light is the ultimate source for all living organisms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13812,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Use of genetically modified crops in crop field may','[{"text": "Crops more tolerant to abiotic stresses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maximise yield", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reduce post harvest losses.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'GM plants have been useful in many ways. Genetic modification has:<br>(i) Made crops more tolerant to abiotic stresses (cold, drought, salt, heat).<br>(ii) Reduced reliance on chemical pesticides (pest-resistant crops).<br>(iii) Helped to reduce post harvest losses. (iv) maximise yield',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13813,'biology',99,1322,3205,'The two components of an ecosystem are','[{"text": "Biotic and abiotic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Weeds, trees and man", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Energy flow and Decomposers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plants and animals", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Biotic and abiotic components are a part of ecosystem',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13814,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Which of the following statements is not correct regarding the genetic modification of crops?','[{"text": "It results in decreased efficiency of mineral usage by plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It helps to reduce post harvest losses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It increases the nutritional value of food", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'GM increases efficiency of mineral usage by plants (this prevents early exhaustion of fertility of soil).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13815,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Abiotic components refer to','[{"text": "Only sunlight", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Living physico-chemical factors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gases produced by industries", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-living physico-chemical factors", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Abiotic components refer to the non-living physio-chemical factors of the environment. Abiotic factors also include inorganic substances, organic compounds, climatic factors and edaphic factors.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13816,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Main objective of production of pest resistant plants is to','[{"text": "Increase the nutritional value of food", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eliminate weeds from the field", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase the amount of chemical pesticide used", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decrease the amount of chemical pesticide used", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Main objective of production of pest resistant plants is to decrease the amount of pesticide used',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13818,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Which ingredient was present in high concentrations in genetically modified (GM) rice as compared to the usual rice?','[{"text": "Protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbohydrates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vitamin A", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'GM enhanced nutritional value of food, e.g., golden rice, i.e., Vitamin \'A\'enriched rice.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13819,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Stability of ecosystem depends on','[{"text": "Number of producers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number of consumers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interaction between producers and consumers", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Stability of ecosystem depends upon interchange between producers and consumers.Their interaction leads to formation of trophic levels and energy flow in an ecosystem',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13820,'biology',98,1187,2846,'GMO which are good example of pest resistant crop is','[{"text": "Bt-cotton", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Golden rice", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transgenic tobacco plant with nematode genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bt toxin gene has been cloned from the bacteria and been expressed in plants to provide resistance to insects without the need for insecticides; in effect created a bio-pesticide. Examples are Bt cotton, Bt corn, rice, tomato, potato and soyabean etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13821,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Select the correct answer<br>I. Interaction of biotic and abiotic components result in a physical structure that is characteristic for each type of ecosystem.<br>II. Identification and enumeration of plant and animal species of an ecosystem gives its stratification.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Identification and enumeration of plant and animal species of an ecosystem gives its species composition',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13822,'biology',98,1187,2846,'A protoxin is','[{"text": "A denatured toxin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "inactive toxin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Primitive toxin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "An active toxin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Protoxin is a inactive toxin or a chemical compound which becomes toxin only after it is altered.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13823,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Stratification is :-','[{"text": "Identification and enumeration of plant and animal species of an ecosystem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Species composition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vertical distribution of different species occupying different levels", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Active nature of all the components of the ecosystem as a unit", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Stratification refers to the formation of vertical layers. Vertical distribution of different species occupying different levels is called as Stratification.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13824,'biology',98,1187,2846,'What does <i>Bt</i> means?','[{"text": "<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Barium treated cotton seeds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria terminator", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacillus tuberculae", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> is in short called as $B t$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13825,'biology',99,1322,3205,'The stratification pattern in a community is well illustrated by a','[{"text": "Aquatic community", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Desert community", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Forest community", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Grassland community", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In forest trees occupy top vertical strata, shrubs, second and herbs & grasses occupy bottom layers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13826,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Which bacterium was the first to be used as biopesticides?','[{"text": "<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Escherichia coli</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Nitrosomonas</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Agrobacterium tumefaciens</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i>, spores were first used as biopesticides on a commercial scale in the world.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13827,'biology',99,1322,3205,'The functioning of an ecosystem is governed by:-','[{"text": "The interactions of plants and animals only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only decomposers composition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The climatic and other abiotic factor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The interaction of abiotic and all the life forms", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The functioning of an ecosystem is governed by the interaction of abiotic and all the life forms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13828,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Which of the following crops are modified using <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i>?','[{"text": "Corn and soybean", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tomato and rice", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Potato and cotton", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Crops modified using Bacillus thuringiensis are $\\mathrm{Bt}$ cotton, Bt corn, rice, tomato, potato and soyabean etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13829,'chemistry',15,185,404,'An organic compound contains carbon hydrogen and oxygen. Its elemental analysis gave C, 38.71%, and H, 9.67%. The empirical formula of the compound would be','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{CHO}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Thus empirical formula is ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{O}}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13830,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Productivity, decomposition, energy flow and nutrient cycling are the :-','[{"text": "Physical structure of ecosystem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Functions of ecosystem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only Biotic components of ecosystem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only Abiotic components of ecosystem", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Productivity, decomposition and nutrient cycling are the functions of an ecosystem.Productivity is the rate of biomass production, it includes primary productivity and secondary productivity. Decomposition is the process of breakdown of complex organic matter into inorganic substances like $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}, \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$. Nutrient cycling refers to the process of movement of nutrient elements through various components of an ecosystem. Nutrient cycling is also referred as Biogeochemical cycles and it includes gaseous cycles and sedimentary cycles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13831,'biology',98,1187,2846,'$B t$ toxins are','[{"text": "Intracellular polypeptides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intracellular lipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intracellular crystalline proteins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Extracellular crystalline proteins", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$B t$ toxins are Intracellular crystalline proteins which exist as inactive protoxins but once an insect ingest the inactive toxin. It is converted into active form of toxin due to alkaline $\\mathrm{pH}$ of the gut which solubilize the crystals.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13832,'chemistry',15,186,405,'The volume of oxygen required for complete combustion of 0.25 mole of methane at STP is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{22}}{\\\\rm{.4}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{d}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{11}}{\\\\rm{.2}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{d}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{7}}{\\\\rm{.46}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{d}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{5}}{\\\\rm{.6}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{d}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Given,<br>Volume of methane = 0.25 mol = 5.6 L<br>[Multiply mole value by molar volume constant, 22.4 L]<br>Combustion of methane ${\\rm{(C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{)}}$<br>$\\mathop {{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}}\\limits_{{\\rm{Methane}}} {\\rm{ + 2}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}} \\to {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ + 2}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2020,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13833,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Maximum primary productivity of pond is achieved by','[{"text": "Decomposers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zooplankton", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Floating plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phytoplankton", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Phytoplanktons are the chief producers of the aquatic ecosystem.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13834,'biology',98,1187,2846,'<i>Bt</i> toxin is harmful to insects like?','[{"text": "Lepidopterans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diptera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coleopterans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bacillus thuringiensis produce proteins that kill certain insects such as lepidopterans (tobacco budworm, armyworm), coleopterans (beetles) and dipterans (flies, mosquitoes).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13835,'chemistry',15,186,405,'For the reaction, ${\\rm{F}}{{\\rm{e}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ + 3CO}} \\to {\\rm{2Fe + 3C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ the volume of carbon monoxide required to reduce one mole of ferric oxide is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{67}}{\\\\rm{.2}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{d}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{11}}{\\\\rm{.2}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{d}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{22}}{\\\\rm{.4}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{d}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{44}}{\\\\rm{.8}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{d}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{F}}{{\\rm{e}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{ + }}\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{3CO}}\\,\\,\\, \\to \\,\\,\\,{\\rm{2Fe}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{ + }}\\,\\,{\\rm{3C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>$\\,\\,{\\rm{1}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{vol}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{3}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{vol}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{2}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{vol}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{3}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{vol}}{\\rm{.}}$<br>$\\,{\\rm{1}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mol}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{3}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mol}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{2}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mol}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{3}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mol}}{\\rm{.}}$<br>$\\left( {{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\because {\\text{vol\\%  = mol\\% }}} \\right)$<br>One gram mol of any gas occupies 22.4 L at NTp. 1 ml of ${\\rm{F}}{{\\rm{e}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ requires 3 mol of CO for its reduction i.e., 1 mol of${\\rm{F}}{{\\rm{e}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ requires ${\\rm{3 \\times 22}}{\\rm{.4L}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{or}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{67}}{\\rm{.2d}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{CO}}$ to get itself reduced.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13836,'biology',99,1322,3205,'In a pond ecosystem, the autotrophic components are','[{"text": "Algae and phytoplanktons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zooplanktons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Submerged and marginal plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Algae, phytoplanktons, submerged plants and marginal plants are all producers in a pond ecosystem.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13837,'biology',98,1187,2846,'<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> forms protein crystal during a particular phase of their growth which contain','[{"text": "Insecticidal protein", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bactericidal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Herbicidal protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'B. thuringiensis forms protein crystals during a particular phase of their growth. These crystals contain a toxic insecticidal protein.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13838,'chemistry',15,186,405,'What is the quantity of hydrogen gas liberated when 46g sodium reacts with excess ethanol? (Given atomic mass of Na = 23)','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}{\\\\rm{.4 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 3}}}}{\\\\rm{kg}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}{\\\\rm{.0 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 3}}}}{\\\\rm{kg}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{4}}{\\\\rm{.0 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 3}}}}{\\\\rm{kg}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}{\\\\rm{.4 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 2}}}}{\\\\rm{kg}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The reaction of ethanol with water is as follows.<br>${\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{OH(l) + 2Na(s)}} \\to $<br>${\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{\\bar ON}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{(g)}} \\uparrow $<br>2 mole of Na (46 g) = 1 mole of ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 2g = 2 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 3}}}}{\\rm{kg}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2017,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13839,'biology',99,1322,3205,'What are the abiotic component in the pond ecosystem?<br>i. Dissolved inorganic and organic substances<br>ii. Rich soil deposit at the bottom of the pond.<br>iii. The solar input, the cycle of temperature,<br>iv. Day-length and other climatic conditions','[{"text": "i, iii only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iii only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The abiotic component in the pond ecosystem are Dissolved inorganic and organic substances ,Rich soil deposit at the bottom of the pond.,The solar input, the cycle of temperature, Day-length and other climatic conditions',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13840,'biology',98,1187,2846,'<i>Bt</i> toxin protein crystals present in bacterium <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i>, do not kill the bacterium because','[{"text": "Bacteria are resistant to the toxin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria enclose toxins in a special sac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Toxins occur as inactive protoxins in bacteria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bt toxin protein crystals present in bacterium, Bacillus thuringiensis, do not kill the bacterium itself. This is because the toxin occurs as inactive protoxin in bacterium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13851,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Match the columns I and II wrt the pond.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Consumers<br>B. Decomposers<br>C. Autotrophs</div><div class="column-right">P. Bacteria and flagellates<br>Q. Zooplankton<br>R. Phytoplankton</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Q, B-P, C-R is correct',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
