(13841,'chemistry',15,186,405,'1.0 g of Mg is burnt with 0.28 g of ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ in a closed vessel. Which reactant is left in excess and how much?','[{"text": "Mg, 5.8 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mg, 0.58 g", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$, 0.24 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$, 2.4 g", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Balanced reaction can be given as<br>$\\mathop {{\\rm{2Mg}}}\\limits_{{\\rm{24 \\times 2 = 48}}} {\\rm{ + }}\\mathop {{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}\\limits_{{\\rm{32}}}  \\to {\\rm{2MgO}}$<br>32 g of ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ is required to burn 48 g Mg<br>So, ${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.28}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ will be required for $\\frac{{{\\rm{48}}}}{{{\\rm{32}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 0}}{\\rm{.25 gMg = 0}}{\\rm{.42}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Mg}}$<br>Thus, Mg will remain in excess<br>${\\rm{ = 1 - 0}}{\\rm{.42 = 0}}{\\rm{.58}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13842,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Name the decomposers abundant in the bottom of the pond?','[{"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flagellates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The decomposers are the fungi, bacteria and flagellates especially abundant in the bottom of the pond.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13843,'biology',98,1187,2846,'<i>Bt</i> toxin kills insect by','[{"text": "Causing nervous problems", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Generating excessive heat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inhibiting protein synthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Creating pores in the midgut epithelial cell to cell swelling and lysis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Bt toxin protein exist as inactive protoxins but once an insect ingest the inactive toxin, it is converted into an active form of toxin due to the alkaline $\\mathrm{pH}$ of the gut which solubilise the crystals. Activated toxin binds to the surface of midgut epithelial cells and creates pores that cause cell swelling and lysis and cause death of the insect.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13844,'chemistry',15,186,405,'In the reaction<br>${\\rm{4N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{(g) + 5}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{(g)}} \\to {\\rm{4NO(g) + 6}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O(l)}}$<br>When 1 mole of ammonia and 1 mole of ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ are made to react to completion.','[{"text": "1.0 mole of ${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$ is produced", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.0 mole of NO will be produced", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "all the oxygen will be consumed", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "all the ammonia will be consumed", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'According to stoichiometry they should react as follow<br>${\\rm{4N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ + 5}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}} \\to {\\rm{4NO + 6}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$<br>4 mole of ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ requires 5 mole of ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>1 mole of ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}$  requires ${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{5}}}{{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.25}}$ moleof ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$.<br>Hence ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ is consumed completely.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13845,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Select the correct answer<br>i. Conversion of inorganic into organic material with the help of the radiant energy of the sun by the autotroph<br>ii. Consumption of the autotrophs by heterotrophs;<br>iii. Decomposition and mineralisation of the dead matter to release them back for reuse by the autotrophs<br>The above events occur in a','[{"text": "Population", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Individual", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecosystem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only pond", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Different events and processes occur within an ecosystem.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13846,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Select the correct answer<br>I. Bt toxin protein exist as inactive protoxins in the bacteria.<br>II. Once an insect ingest the inactive toxin, it is converted into an active form of toxin due to the acidic $\\mathrm{pH}$ of the gut which solubilise the crystals.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bt toxin protein exist as inactive protoxins but once an insect ingest the inactive toxin, it is converted into an active form of toxin due to the alkaline $\\mathrm{pH}$ of the gut which solubilise the crystals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13848,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Match the columns I and II<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Terrestrial ecosystem<br>B. Aquatic ecosystem<br>C. Man made ecosystems</div><div class="column-right">P. Aquarium<br>Q. Grassland<br>R. Estuary</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Q, B-R, C-P is correct',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13849,'biology',98,1187,2846,'The activated $\\mathrm{Bt}$ toxin binds to the surface of midgut epithelial cells and eventually causes death of the insect by','[{"text": "Creating pores in the gut cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Causing cell swelling in the gut cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Causing lysis of the gut cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The activated toxin binds to the surface of midgut epithelial cells and create pores that cause cell swelling and lysis and eventually cause death of the insect.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13850,'chemistry',15,177,387,'Which of the following statements about a compound is incorrect?','[{"text": "A molecule of a compound has atoms of different elements.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A compound cannot be separated into its constituent elements by physical methods of separation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A compound retains the physical properties of its constituent elements.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The ratio of atoms of different elements in a compound is fixed.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A compound is a pure substance containing two or more than two elements combined together in a fixed proportion by mass and which can be decomposed into its constituent elements by suitable chemical methods.<br>Further, the properties of a compound are quite different from the properties of constituent elements. e.g., water is a compound containing hydrogen and oxygen combined together in a fixed proportion. But the properties of water are completely different from its constituents, hydrogen and oxygen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13852,'biology',98,1187,2846,'The choice of genes of <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> which is to be incorporated into crop depends upon','[{"text": "Crop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Targeted pest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Toxin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The choice of genes depends upon the crop and the targeted pest, as most Bt toxins are insect-group specific.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13854,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Match the columns I and II<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Consumers<br>B. Decomposers<br>C. Autotrophs</div><div class="column-right">P. Mineral cycling<br>Q. Own food<br>R. Depend on others</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-R , B-P, C-Q is correct.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13855,'biology',98,1187,2846,'The genes obtained from <i>B. thuringiensis</i> is called','[{"text": "Cry gene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nif gene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bac gene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bt gene", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The cry genes is obtained from $\\mathrm{B}$, thuringiensis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13857,'biology',99,1322,3205,'What happens if all green plants on earth are destroyed','[{"text": "There will no changes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only herbivores die", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All animals will die", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "all weeds get destroyed", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'As green plants are the producers and all the others including primary, secondary and tertiary consumers depends on the producers.<br>So if green plants are destroyed then all animals will be destroyed',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13858,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Proteins encoded by gene <i>cryIAb</i> controls','[{"text": "Bollworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insects", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corn borer", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nematodes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Some strains of <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> produce proteins that kill certain insects. It contains $B t$ toxin coded by gene \'cry\'. Protein encoded by cryIAb controls corn borer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13860,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Choose the incorrect statement','[{"text": "Sun is the ultimate source of energy for any ecosystem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecosystem is self sustaining and dynamic structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In an artificial ecosystem flow of energy is not unidirectional", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ecosystem is an open system.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Flow of energy in an artificial ecosystem is unidirectional.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13861,'biology',98,1187,2846,'The protein products of the $B t$ toxin genes <i>cryIAc</i> and <i>cryIIAb</i> are responsible for controlling','[{"text": "Fruit fly", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corn borer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bollworm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Moth", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Two cry genes, cryIAc and cryIIAb have been incorporated in cotton. These genes control cotton bollworms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13863,'biology',99,1323,3206,'Primary production is','[{"text": "Expressed in terms of weight $\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{gm}^{-2}\\\\right)$ or energy $\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{kcal}}\\\\,{{\\\\rm{m}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 2}}}}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The amount of biomas or organic matter produced per unit area over a time period by plants during photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The amount of inorganic matter produced per unit area over a time period by plants during photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Primary production is defined as the amount of biomass or organic matter produced per unit area over a time period by plants during photosynthesis. It is expressed in terms of weight $\\left(\\mathrm{g}^{-2}\\right)$ or energy $\\left( {{\\rm{k}}\\,{\\rm{cal}}\\,{{\\rm{m}}^{{\\rm{ - 2}}}}} \\right)$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13864,'biology',98,1187,2846,'<em>cryIab</em> and <em>cryIIAb</em> produce toxins that control','[{"text": "Cotton bollworms and corn borer, respectively.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corn borer only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cotton bollworms only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corn borer and Cotton bollworms, respectively", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The proteins encoded by the genes cryIAc and cryIIAb control the cotton bollworms, that of cryIAb controls corn borer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13866,'biology',99,1323,3206,'The rate of biomass production is','[{"text": "Productivity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nutrient cycling", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decomposition", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The rate of biomass production is called productivity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13867,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Insect resistant transgenic cotton has been produced by inserting a piece of DNA from','[{"text": "Insecta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prokaryote", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Protista", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A virus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Insect resistant transgenic cotton has been produced by inserting a piece of DNA from a bacterium -prokaryote Bacillus thuringiensis into the genome of cotton.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13869,'biology',99,1323,3206,'The productivity is expressed in terms of','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{gm}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 2}}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{y}}{{\\\\rm{r}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{kcal}}\\\\,{{\\\\rm{m}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 2}}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{y}}{{\\\\rm{r}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{kcal}}\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{m}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 2}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Productivity is expressed in terms of ${{\\rm{g}}^{{\\rm{ - 2}}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{y}}{{\\rm{r}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{or}}\\,\\,{\\rm{(kcal}}\\,{{\\rm{m}}^{{\\rm{ - 2}}}}{\\rm{)}}\\,\\,{\\rm{y}}{{\\rm{r}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13870,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Cry gene containing crops needs','[{"text": "No insecticide", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Little amount of insecticide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Large amount of insecticide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'cry gene containing crops need no insecticide because cry gene produces protein which makes the plant pest resistance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13872,'biology',99,1323,3206,'Net primary productivity (NPP) is given by the formula','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NPP}=\\\\mathrm{GPP} \\\\times \\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NPP}=\\\\mathrm{GPP}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NPP}=\\\\mathrm{GPP}-\\\\mathrm{R} / 100$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NPP}=\\\\mathrm{GPP} \\\\times 100$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{NPP}=\\mathrm{GPP}$ - $\\mathrm{R}$ is correct',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13894,'biology',98,1188,2847,'Which method of cellular defense is common in all eukaryotic organisms?','[{"text": "RNA interference", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Reverse transcription", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "VNTR", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phagocytosis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'RNAi takes place in all eukaryotic organisms as a method of cellular defense.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13873,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Identify the correct statements','[{"text": "Bt-toxins are insect-group specific", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Proteins encoded by gene <em>CryIAb </em>controls cotton boll worms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>CryIAc</em> &amp; <em>CryIIAb </em>genes encode proteins that control corn borers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bt-toxin genes cannot be introduced in food crops", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All insects cannot be controlled by Btgene. Hence group specific.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13875,'biology',99,1323,3206,'Identify the correct formula regarding NPP and GPP','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NPP}=\\\\mathrm{GPP}+$ Animal respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NPP}=\\\\mathrm{GPP}-$ Plant respiration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NPP}=\\\\mathrm{GPP}+$ Plant respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NPP}=\\\\mathrm{GPP}-$ Animal respiration", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Net primary productivity is gross production minus the losses by the way of respiration and decomposition. Gross primary productivity of an ecosystem is the rate of production of organic matter during photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13876,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Which one of the following option is correct?','[{"text": "The proteins encoded by the genes <i>cryIAc</i> and <i>cryIIAb</i> control cotton bollworms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein encoded by <i>cryIAb</i> controls corn borer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Proteins encoded by <i>cryIAc</i> and <i>cryIAb</i> control flies", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The toxin is coded by a gene cryIAc named cry. There are a number of them, for example, the proteins encoded by the genes cryIAc and cryIIAb control the cotton bollworms, that of cryIAb controls corn borer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13878,'biology',99,1323,3206,'Net primary productivity is equal to','[{"text": "Organic matter synthesised by photosynthesis only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Organic matter synthesised by photosynthesis minus utilisation in respiration and other losses", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rate of respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rate of respiration + photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Net primary productivity is equal to organic matter synthesised by photosynthesis minus utilisation in respiration and other losses. It can also be defined as the available biomass for the consumption to heterotrophs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13879,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Identify the correct statement about Bt toxin?','[{"text": "Bt toxin on mid-gut epithelial cells, creates pores, leading to swelling and lysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bt is produced by a prokaryote", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Bt}$ is produced in its inactive state", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of them are correct',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13881,'biology',99,1323,3206,'In an ecosystem producers are all, except','[{"text": "Green plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemolithotrophs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photo organotrophs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterotrophs", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Heterotrophs are not producers and are dependent on plants or other animals for food',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13882,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Identify the part labelled A and B','[{"text": "A-Fully mature cotton ball, B-Destroyed by bollworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Destroyed by bollworm, B-Fully mature cotton ball", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A- Destroyed by <em>M.incognitia</em>, B-Fully mature cotton ball", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- Destroyed by <em>B. thuringiensis</em>, B-Fully mature cotton ball", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A- Destroyed by bollworm, B-Fully mature cotton ball',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/98_13882_question_1.png'),
(13884,'biology',99,1323,3206,'Primary productivity depends upon','[{"text": "Availability of nutrients", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photosynthetic capacity of plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Respiration", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Primary productivity depends upon availibility of nutrients and photosynthetic capability of plants. Other factors which affect primary productivity are temperature, water, moisture, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13885,'biology',98,1188,2847,'Name the organism that infects tobacco plant and decrease its yield','[{"text": "<i>Meluidugyne incognita</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Meloidegyne incognita</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Meloidagyne incognita</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Mycobacterium incognita</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A nematode Meloidegyne incognitia infects the roots of tobacco plants and causes a great reduction in yield.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13887,'biology',99,1325,3208,'What is the trophic level of rat in a food chain?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{T} 1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{T} 2$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{T} 3$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{T} 4$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Rat belongs to ${\\rm{T 2}}$ because it depends on grains / plants',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13888,'biology',98,1188,2847,'Which of the following part of the plant is infected by the nematode and reduces the production?','[{"text": "Roots of tobacco plant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Leaves of tobacco plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Roots of cotton plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flowers of cotton plant", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Roots of tobacco plant are infected by the nematode and reduces the production.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13890,'biology',99,1323,3206,'The primary consumers sustain on','[{"text": "Gross primary production", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Net secondary production", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Net community production", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Net primary production", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Net primary productivity is the available biomass for the consumption of herbivores & decomposers (or) primary consumers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13891,'biology',98,1188,2847,'A novel strategy was adopted to prevent $M$. incognita infection in tobacco plants that was based on the process of','[{"text": "DNA interference", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RNA interference", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "RNA replication", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA replication", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A novel strategy was adopted to prevent this infestation which was based on the process of RNA interference (RNAi).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13893,'biology',99,1323,3206,'Secondary productivity is rate of formation of new organic matter by','[{"text": "Consumers", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Decomposers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Producers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parasites", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Secondary productivity is rate of formation of new organic matter by consumers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13896,'biology',99,1323,3206,'The rate of production of organic matter by consumers is','[{"text": "Secondary productivity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Net primary productivity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Primary productivity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gross primary productivity", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Secondary productivity is the rate at which food energy is assimilated at the trophic level of consumers or rate of synthesis of organic matter by consumers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13897,'biology',98,1188,2847,'RNA interference involves','[{"text": "Interference of RNA in synthesis of DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synthesis of mRNA from DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synthesis of cDNA and RNA using reverse transcriptase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Silencing of specific mRNA due to complementary dsRNA", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'RNA interference takes place in all eukaryotic organisms as a method of cell defense. This method involves silencing of a specific mRNA. Using vectors, Nematode specific genes are introduced into host plant. The introduction of DNA produced both sense and antisense RNA in host cells. The two RNAs being complimentary to each other formed a dsRNA that initiated RNAi.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13899,'biology',99,1323,3206,'Generally, the major factor that limits primary productivity in most oceans is','[{"text": "Oxygen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nutrients", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Nutrients (nitrogen, phosphorus and iron) limit primary production in most oceans and lakes.Concentrations of these nutrients are typically lowin the photic zone because they are rapidly taken up by phytoplankton and because detritus tends to sink.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13900,'biology',98,1188,2847,'In RNA, genes are silenced using','[{"text": "ss DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ds DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ss RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ds RNA", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'This method involves silencing of a specific mRNA due to a complementary dsRNA molecule that binds to and prevents translation of the mRNA (silencing).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13902,'biology',99,1323,3206,'All are highly productive ecosystems, except','[{"text": "Tropical rain forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coral reefs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sugarcane field", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Deep sea", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Deep sea has limited reach of sunlight, so less primary production therefore less productive ecosystem.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13903,'biology',98,1188,2847,'In which of the following plants, resistance against a nematode was introduced by implying RNAi?','[{"text": "<i>Nicotiana</i>-fabaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Nicotiana</i> -solanaceae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Nicotiana</i> -liliaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Nicotiana</i> -brassicaceae", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Tobacco plants have been made resistant to nematodes using RNAi, its botanical name is Nicotiana tabacum-solanaceae',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13905,'biology',99,1323,3206,'The annual net primary productivity of the whole biosphere is approximately____ tons (dry weight) of organic matter. Of this, despite occupying about____ of the surface, the productivity of the oceans are only____ tons.','[{"text": "55 billion, 70 per cent, 55 billion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "170 million, 70 per cent, 55 million", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "55 million, 70 per cent, 55 million", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "170 billion, 70 per cent, 55 billion", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The annual net primary productivity of the whole biosphere is approximately 170 billion tons (dry weight) of organic matter. Of this, despite occupying about 70 per cent of the surface, the productivity of the oceans are only 55 billion tons.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
