(13957,'biology',98,1189,2848,'The main challenge for production of insulin using rDNA techniques was getting insulin assembled into a mature form. Why was it so?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{B}$ - peptide is absent in mature insulin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{B}$ - peptide is added to proinsulin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}$ - peptide is absent in mature insulin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}$ - peptide is added to proinsulin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Insulin consists of two short polypeptide chains, Chain A and chain B linked together by disulphide bridges. Pro- hormone or Pro insulin contains extra stretch called $\\mathrm{C}$ peptide. In mature insulin, $\\mathrm{C}$ peptide is been removed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
