(13960,'biology',98,1189,2848,'Which polypeptide chain is removed during the maturation of proinsulin into insulin?','[{"text": "A - chain (21 amino acids)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B - chain (30 amino acids)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C - chain (33 amino acids)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A and C-chains", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'This $\\mathrm{C}$ peptide is not present in the mature insulin and is removed during maturation into insulin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13962,'biology',99,1324,3207,'Decomposers are very important in the ecosystems because they','[{"text": "Transduce light energy into chemical energy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Return energy from higher trophic levels back to the producers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Convert organic matter in the detritus into inorganic compounds usable by primary producers", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Synthesize organic compounds from inorganic compounds", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Decomposers breakdown complex dead organic matter into inorganic substances like carbondioxide, water and nutrients to release them back for reuse by the autotrophs. If this does not happen, producers (and hence consumers) cannot continue to exist forever',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(13963,'biology',98,1189,2848,'Human Insulin is being commercially produced from a transgenic species of','[{"text": "<i>Rhizobium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Saccharomyces</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Mycobacterium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Escherichia coli</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In 1983, Eli Lily an American Company first prepared two DNA sequences corresponding to A and B chains of human insulin and introduced them in plasmids of <i>Escherichia coli</i> to produce insulin chains. Chains A and B were produced separately extracted and combined by creating disulfide bonds to form human insulin( Humulin).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
