(14011,'biology',98,1189,2849,'Which of the following statements is incorrect about gene therapy in ADA deficiency?','[{"text": "Patient does not require periodic infusion of genetically engineered lymphocytes.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lymphocytes are then introduced in the body of patient.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A functional ADA cDNA using a retroviral vector is introduced into these lymphocytes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lymphocytes from patients\' blood are taken out and cultured.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In gene therapy, lymphocytes from the blood of patient are grown in culture outside body. Later a functional ADA cDNA is introduced in lymphocytes which are returned in patients body. The cells are immortal and hence patient requires periodic infusion of genetically engineered lymphocytes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14013,'biology',99,1325,3208,'Organisms that depend on plants (directly or indirectly) for food are called','[{"text": "Decomposers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Producers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Consumers", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Grazers", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'All the animals that depend for food on plants (directly or indirectly) are called consumers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14014,'biology',98,1189,2849,'Gene therapy performed for correction of disorders','[{"text": "Is always a temporary cure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Could be permanent if gene is introduced in the early embryonic stages", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Has not been tried for humans <br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Involves removal of defective genes & introduction of functional genes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In ADA deficiency, lymphocytes are extracted from blood, cultured and are introduced with functional ADA cDNA which are later introduced in patients. but this process is not immortal as the patient requires periodic infusion of such genetically engineered lymphocytes. However, if the gene isolate from marrow cells producing ADA is introduced into cells at early embryonic stages, it could be a permanent cure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14016,'biology',98,1189,2849,'In order for gene therapy to be most effective, genes should be inserted in?','[{"text": "WBC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RBC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stem cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In order for gene therapy to be most effective, genes should be inserted in stem cells- cells from which all other cells with specialized functions are generated.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
