(14035,'chemistry',15,187,412,'A metallic chloride contain 47.22% metal. Calculate the equivalent weight of metal','[{"text": "39.68", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "31.76", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "36.35", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "33.46", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Suppose weight of metallic chloride =100 g<br>Then weight of metal = 47.22 g<br>Weight of chlorine = 100 – 47.22 = 52.78 g<br>$\\therefore $  Equivalent weight of metal = $\\left( {\\frac{{{\\rm{Mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Metal}}}}{{{\\rm{Mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{chloride}}}}} \\right){\\rm{ \\times 35}}{\\rm{.5}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{47}}{\\rm{.22}}}}{{{\\rm{52}}{\\rm{.78}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 35}}{\\rm{.5 = 31}}{\\rm{.76}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
