(14077,'chemistry',15,186,405,'0.4 g of dihydrogen is made to react with 7.1 g of dichlorine to form hydrogen chloride. The volume of hydrogen chloride formed at 273 K and 1 bar pressure is','[{"text": "4.54 L", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "90.8 L", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "45.4 L", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "9.08 L", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{2(g)}}}}{\\rm{ + C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{{\\rm{2(g)}}}} \\to {\\rm{2HC}}{{\\rm{l}}_{{\\rm{(g)}}}}$<br>${\\rm{2}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ required to react with ${\\rm{7}}{\\rm{.1}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{2 \\times 7}}{\\rm{.1}}}}{{{\\rm{71}}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.2}}\\,\\,{\\rm{g}}$<br>$\\therefore {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ is the limiting reagent.<br>${\\rm{71}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ produces ${\\rm{2 \\times 22}}{\\rm{.7L}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{HC}}{{\\rm{l}}_{{\\rm{(g)}}}}$<br>$\\therefore $ Volume of ${\\rm{HC}}{{\\rm{l}}_{{\\rm{(g)}}}}$  produce ${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{2 \\times 22}}{\\rm{.7 \\times 7}}{\\rm{.1}}}}{{{\\rm{71}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 4}}{\\rm{.54}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{L}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
