(14134,'chemistry',15,183,402,'The volume of 1 mole of any pure gas at standard temperature and pressure is always equal to','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.022414}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{22}}{\\\\rm{.414}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}{\\\\rm{.2414}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.22414}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The volume of 1 mole of any pure gas at standard and pressure (STP) is equal to 22.414 L<br>${\\rm{1L = 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 3}}}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}$<br>$\\therefore {\\rm{22}}{\\rm{.4}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{L = 0}}{\\rm{.022414}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2019,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14135,'biology',99,1326,3209,'Ascending trophic level in grazing food chain pyramid represents','[{"text": "Gradual decrease in biomass from base to the apex", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "No change in biomass", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gradual increase of the biomass from producers to the tertiary consumers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "gradual decrease in biomass from apex to the base", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ascending trophic level in grazing food chain pyramid represents Gradual decrease in biomass from base to the apex, At the apex, there will be least bio mass',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14137,'chemistry',15,183,402,'Mass of 0.1 mole of methane is','[{"text": "1.6 g", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.1 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "16 g", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{No}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{moles = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{substance}}}}{{{\\rm{molecular}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{substance}}}}$<br>${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.1 = }}\\frac{{\\rm{w}}}{{{{\\rm{M}}_{{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}}}}}$<br>${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.1 = }}\\frac{{\\rm{w}}}{{{\\rm{16}}}}$$\\left( {\\because {{\\text{M}}_{{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{4}}}}}{\\text{ = 16}}} \\right)$<br>$ \\Rightarrow {\\rm{w = 1}}{\\rm{.6g}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14138,'biology',99,1326,3209,'Which of the following is not used for construction of an ecological pyramid?','[{"text": "Dry weight", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rate of energy flow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Individuals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fresh weight", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Commonly pyramids used for constructing ecological pyramids are number of individuals (pyramid of numbers), dry weight (pyramid of biomass) or rate of energy flow (pyramid of energy) at successive trophic levels.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14139,'biology',98,1191,2852,'Organisms used to gain commercial benefits are called','[{"text": "Bio resources", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Beneficial resources", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemical resources", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Financial resources", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Organisms used to gain commercial benefits are called Bio resources.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14140,'chemistry',15,180,395,'The combining ratios of hydrogen and oxygen in water and hydrogen peroxide are 1 : 8 and 1 : 16. Which law is illustrated in this example?','[{"text": "Law of definite proportions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of conservation of mass", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gay Lussac’s law of combining volumes of gases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of multiple proportions", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The combining ratios of hydrogen and oxygen in water and hydrogen peroxide are 1: 8 and 1: 16. It is an example of law of multiple proportions. According to this law, if two elements combine together to form several compounds then weight of one of these elements, which combines with a fixed weight of the other, are in ratio of simple whole numbers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2019,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14141,'biology',99,1326,3209,'Pyramid of energy is always upright which indicates that','[{"text": "Producers have lowest energy conversion efficiency", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Energy conversion efficiency is same for all trophic levels.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Herbivores have better energy conversion efficiency than carnivores.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Carnivores have better efficiency than herbivores", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pyramid of energy is always upright indicates that herbivore is consumed by a carnivore. Here herbivore is primary consumer and carnivore is the secondary consumer. As energy passes into higher trophic levels along with food, its amount decreases because of its dissipation as heat and use in overcoming entropy as well as for performing various body activities',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14142,'biology',98,1191,2852,'A permission granted to an individual who has invented a new and useful article, invented a new process is called','[{"text": "Bioethics", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biopatency", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Biopiracy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bionorm", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Biopatents or Biopatency, also referred to as patents of life, are defined as patents of living organisms that can include plant and animal species, and related biological and biotechnology-enabled inventions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14143,'chemistry',15,180,394,'The percentage of copper and oxygen in samples of CuO obtained by different methods were found to be the same. This illustrates the law of','[{"text": "constant proportions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "conservation of mass", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "multiple proportions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "reciprocal proportions", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'According to law of constant proportions a pure chemical compound always contains same elements combined together in the same definite proportion of weight.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14144,'biology',99,1326,3209,'Limitation of ecological pyramids is/are :-','[{"text": "It does not take into account the same species belonging to two or more trophic levels", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It assumes a simple food chains, it does not accommodate a food web", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Saprophytes are not given any place in ecological pyramids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'There are certain limitations of ecological pyramids such as it does not take into account the same species belonging to two or more trophic levels. It assumes a simple food chain, something that almost never exists in nature, it does not accommodate a food web. Saprophytes are not given any place in ecological pyramid even though they play a vital role in the ecosystem.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14145,'biology',98,1191,2852,'Unauthorized exploitation of their bioresources and traditional knowledge can be prevented by','[{"text": "GEAC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biopiracy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biopatency", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Biopatency prevents bio piracy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14146,'chemistry',15,180,398,'${\\rm{10}}\\,{\\rm{d}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}$ of ${{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}$  gas and ${\\rm{10}}\\,\\,{\\rm{d}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}$ of gas x at the same temperature contain the same number of molecules, the gas X is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{CO}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{NO}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The number of molecules of ${{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ and X are same. Hence they must have the same molecular weights.<br>$\\therefore {\\rm{X}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{is}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{CO}}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14147,'biology',99,1326,3209,'(P) ${\\rm{10 kcal/}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{/yr}}$<br>(Q) ${\\rm{100 kcal/}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{/yr}}$<br>(R) ${\\rm{1000 kcal/}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{/yr}}$<br>(S) ${\\rm{1,00,000 kcal/}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{/yr}}$<br>In the above energy pyramid, rate of primary production is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{1000}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{kcal/}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{/yr}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{110}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{kcal/}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{/yr}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uncertain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{100}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{kcal/}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{/yr}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The plants- primary producer the rate of primary production will be ${\\rm{1000}}\\,{\\rm{kcal/}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{/yr}}{\\rm{.}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/99_14147_question_1.jpg'),
(14149,'chemistry',15,182,400,'An element X has the following isotopic composition:<br>$^{{\\rm{200}}}{\\rm{X:90}}{{\\rm{\\% }}^{{\\rm{199}}}}{\\rm{X:8}}{\\rm{.0}}{{\\rm{\\% }}^{{\\rm{202}}}}{\\rm{X:2}}{\\rm{.0\\% }}$<br>The weighted average atomic mass of the naturally occurring element X is closest so','[{"text": "201 amu", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "202 amu", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "199 amu", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "200 amu", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Average isotopic mass of<br>${\\rm{X = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{200 \\times 90 + 199 \\times 8 + 202 \\times 2}}}}{{{\\rm{90 + 8 + 2}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{18000 + 1592 + 404}}}}{{{\\rm{100}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{19996}}}}{{{\\rm{100}}}}{\\rm{ = 199}}{\\rm{.96}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{amu}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14150,'biology',99,1326,3209,'Given below is one of the types of ecological pyramid. This represents.','[{"text": "Pyramid of numbers in a grassland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Energy pyramid in a spring", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pyramid of biomass in a fallow land", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pyramid of biomass in a lake", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In a pond, No. of producers is small, but the no. of primary consumers is more',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/99_14150_question_1.jpg'),
(14151,'biology',98,1191,2852,'Biopatents are<br>i. Right to use manufacture clothes<br>ii. Prevention of exploitation of bioresources and traditional knowledge of developing countries<br>iii. Right to use invention<br>iv. Right to use biological entities','[{"text": "iv and ii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iii and i", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iv", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Biopatents are right to use biological entities. They refers to patents obtained by individuals, group or country to establish exclusive right over the origin of particular organism or plant. It also prevents exploitation of bioresources and traditional knowledge of developing countries.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
