(14211,'chemistry',15,185,404,'0.30 g of an organic compound containing C, H and O on combustion yields 0.44 g ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ and 0.18 g ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$. If one mol of compound weight 60, then the molecular formula of the compound is','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{8}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{6}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Percentage of<br>${\\rm{C = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{12}}}}{{{\\rm{44}}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.44}}}}{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.30}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 100 = 40\\% }}$<br>${\\rm{Percentage}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{H = }}\\frac{{\\rm{2}}}{{{\\rm{18}}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.18}}}}{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.30}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 100 = 6}}{\\rm{.6\\% }}$<br>${\\rm{Percentage}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{O = 100 - (40 + 6}}{\\rm{.6) = 53}}{\\rm{.4\\% }}$<br>Hence, empirical formula ${\\rm{ = C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$<br>${\\rm{n = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{Molecular}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mass}}}}{{{\\rm{Empirical}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{formula}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mass}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{60}}}}{{{\\rm{30}}}}{\\rm{ = 2}}$<br>$ \\Rightarrow $ Molecular formula of the compound<br>${{\\rm{(C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O)}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
