(14241,'biology',99,1328,3211,'The following explains about a particular element that is released by these activities . Identify the element?<br>i. Decomposers<br>ii. Burning of wood<br>iii. Forest fire and combustion of organic matter, fossil fuel,<br>iv. Volcanic activity','[{"text": "Carbondioxide", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sulphur", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nitrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phosphorus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A considerable amount of carbon returns to the atmosphere as $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ through respiratory activities of the producers and consumers. Decomposers also contribute substantially to $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ pool by their processing of waste materials and dead organic matter of land or oceans. Some amount of the fixed carbon is lost to sediments and removed from circulation. Burning of wood, forest fire and combustion of organic matter, fossil fuel, volcanic activity are additional sources for releasing $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ in the atmosphere',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
