(14258,'chemistry',45,424,844,'The period consisting of lanthanides starts with the filling of','[{"text": "7s orbitals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6s orbitals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4f orbitals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5d orbitals", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The elements in which differentiating electron enters into the 4f-orbital are known as 4f - series elements or the lanthanides. These elements are placed in the 6th period of the periodic table because 4f-orbital is filled only after 6s is filled. And the 6th period starts with filling of 6s-orbital.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
