(14297,'biology',99,1327,3210,'Identify the correct statement.','[{"text": "The succession resulting from changes brought about by factors external to community is called allogenic succession", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The diversity of species tends to in with succession.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biomass and standing crop of organic matter increase with succession.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements are correct. The succession resulting from changes brought about by factors external to community is called allogenic succession. The diversity of species tends to increase with succession.. Biomass and standing crop of organic matter increase with succession.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14298,'chemistry',45,430,856,'If the atomic radius of non-metal bromine is ${\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.14}}\\mathop {\\rm{A}}\\limits^{\\rm{^\\circ }} $, its covalent radius is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{\\\\rm{.14}}\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{^\\\\circ }} $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{\\\\rm{.12}}\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{^\\\\circ }} $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{\\\\rm{.16}}\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{^\\\\circ }} $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.57}}\\\\mathop {\\\\rm{A}}\\\\limits^{\\\\rm{^\\\\circ }} $", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The term covalent radius is used to represent the atomic radius of non-metal.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14299,'chemistry',15,180,398,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Volume of a gas is inversely proportional to the number of moles of gas.</div><div class="column-right">The ratio by volume of gaseous reactants and products is in agreement with their mole ratio.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'We know that from the reaction ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ + C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}} \\to {\\rm{2HCl}}$ that the ratio of the volume of gaseous reactants and products is in agreement with their molar ratio. The ratio of ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{:C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{:HCl}}$ volume is 1: 1: 2 which is the same as their molar ratio. Thus volume of gas is directly related to the number of moles. Therefore, Statement A is incorrect but statement B is correct',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14300,'biology',98,1189,2850,'A probe which is a molecule used to locate homologous sequences in a mixture of DNA or RNA molecules could be:','[{"text": "A ssRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A ssDNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Either RNA or DNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Can be ssDNA but not ssRNA", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Either RNA or DNA',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERTExemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14301,'biology',99,1323,3206,'Arrange the following ecosystems in increasing order of their mean NPP (tons/ha/ year)<br>i. Temperate coniferous forest<br>ii. Temperate deciduous forest<br>iii. Tropical deciduous forest<br>iv. Tropical rain forest','[{"text": "i < ii < iii < iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii < iii < i < iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i < iv < ii < iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii < i < iv < iii", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Net primary productivity (NPP) is the biomass or storage of energy by green plants. It is equal to the gross primary productivity minus loss due to respiration. The productivity generally increases from polar regions toward the tropics because of the increasing sunlight and temperature, so this is the correct order i $ < $ ii $ < $ iii $ < $ iv',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14302,'chemistry',45,430,856,'The correct order of radii are','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{N &lt; Be &lt; B}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\text{F}}^{\\\\text{ - }}} &lt; {{\\\\text{O}}^{{\\\\text{2}} - }} &lt; {{\\\\text{N}}^{{\\\\text{3}} - }}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Na &lt; Li &lt; K}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{F}}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{{\\\\rm{3 + }}}}{\\\\rm{ &lt; F}}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{{\\\\rm{2 + }}}}{\\\\rm{ &lt; F}}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{{\\\\rm{4 + }}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In Isoelectronic species, ionic radii decreases as atomic number increases.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14304,'biology',98,1189,2849,'The site of production of ADA in the body is:','[{"text": "Erythrocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lymphocytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Blood plasma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osteocytes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Lymphocytes are involved in secretion of ADA.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERTExemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14305,'biology',99,1325,3208,'Study the following statements<br>I. Removal of carnivores resulted in increased herbivores<br>II. Removal of phytoplanktons resulted in decreased productivity in a lake <br>III. Removal of tigers from an area resulted in increased growth of vegetation<br>IV. Removal of decomposers resulted in decreased primary productivity','[{"text": "Only one statement is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only two statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only three statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Removal of tigers from an area resulted in increased growth of vegetation, this statement is wrong, which means 3 statements are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14306,'chemistry',45,430,856,'The covalent and van der Waals radii of hydrogen respectively are','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.37A^\\\\circ ,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{1}}{\\\\rm{.2A^\\\\circ }}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.37A^\\\\circ ,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.37A^\\\\circ }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{\\\\rm{.2A^\\\\circ ,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{1}}{\\\\rm{.2A^\\\\circ }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{\\\\rm{.2A^\\\\circ ,}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.37A^\\\\circ }}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'van der Waal’s radius by definition is always larger than covalent radius.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(14307,'chemistry',15,185,404,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Molecular formula shows the exact number of different types of atoms present in a compound.</div><div class="column-right">Molecular formula can be obtained directly from empirical formula which represents the simplest whole number ratio of various atoms present in a compound.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Molecular formula can be obtained from empirical formula if molar mass is known.<br>Molecular formula ${\\rm{ = n \\times }}$ Empirical formula<br>where, ${\\rm{n = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{Molar}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mass}}}}{{{\\rm{Empirical}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{formula}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mass}}}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14308,'biology',98,1189,2850,'Pathophysiology is the:','[{"text": "Study of physiology of pathogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Study of normal physiology of host", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Study of altered physiology of host", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pathophysiology is a combination of pathology and physiology. While physiology is about various biological processes, pathology is about diseased state.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERTExemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14309,'biology',99,1323,3206,'Which of the following statement is true?','[{"text": "GPP utilizes $1-5 \\\\%$ of PAR", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GPP utilizes $2-10 \\\\%$ of incident radiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "NPP utilizes $1.6-8 \\\\%$ of incident radiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GPP utilizes $2-10 \\\\%$ of PAR", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Of the total solar radiation less than $50 \\%$ of it is PAR (400 nm - $700 \\mathrm{~nm}$ ). Gpp utilizes $2-10 \\%$ of PAR (photosynthetic active radiation)',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14310,'chemistry',45,425,851,'Which of the following is the wrong statement?','[{"text": "All the actinide elements are radioactive.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alkali and alkaline earth metals are s-block elements.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chalcogens and halogens are p-block elements.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The first member of the lanthanide series is lanthanum.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'First member of lanthanide series is Cerium, Ce',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14311,'chemistry',15,177,387,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Components of a homogeneous mixture cannot be separated by using physical methods.</div><div class="column-right">Composition of homogeneous mixture is uniform throughout as the components react to form a single compound.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In homogeneous mixture, the components completely mix with each other and hence the composition is uniform throughout. Formation of homogeneous mixture is a physical change as no chemical reaction occurs between the componenets and no new compound is formed hence the components can be separated by physical methods.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14312,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Golden rice is:','[{"text": "A variety of rice grown along the yellow river in China", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Long stored rice having yellow colour tint", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A transgenic rice having gene for carotene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Wild variety of rice with yellow coloured grains", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A transgenic rice having gene for beta carotene is called golden rice due to its colour.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERTExemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14313,'biology',99,1323,3206,'Read the given statements and select the correct options<br>I. The amount of biomass or organic matter produced per unit area over a time period in plants during photosynthesis is called primary production.<br>II. Gross primary productivity of an ecosystem is the rate of production of organic matter during photosynthesis.<br>III. Productivity is expressed in ${{\\rm{gm}}^{{\\rm{ - 2}}}}{\\rm{y}}{{\\rm{r}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\rm{or}}\\,\\,{\\rm{(kcal}}\\,{{\\rm{m}}^{{\\rm{ - 2}}}}{\\rm{)y}}{{\\rm{r}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$<br>IV. Net primary productivity is the available biomass for the consumption to heterotrophs','[{"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III and IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14314,'chemistry',45,430,857,'The ionic radius of Cr is minimum in which or the following compounds?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{Cr}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{CrC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{r}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{Cr}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cr has maximum oxidation number (+6) in ${{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{Cr}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ and thus, has minimum ionic radius. More is the positive charge on the cation smaller is the size.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14315,'chemistry',15,177,386,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Solids have definite volume and shape.</div><div class="column-right">In solids, the constituent particles are very close to each other and there is not much freedom of movement.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14316,'biology',98,1189,2849,'The first clinical gene therapy was done for the treatment of:','[{"text": "AIDS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cancer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cystic fibrosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "SCID (Severe Combined Immuno<br>Deficiency resulting from deficiency of ADA)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The first clinical gene therapy was given in 1990 to a 4-year old girl with adenosine deaminase (ADA) deficiency.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERTExemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14317,'biology',99,1327,3210,'Secondary ecological succession can occur in<br>i. Newly cooled larva<br>ii. Bare rock<br>iii. Burned or cut forest<br>iv. Newly created ponds<br>v. Abandoned farm Land','[{"text": "i, iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iii, iv and v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii & V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii and iv", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Secondary succession occurs in an areas that some how lost all the biotic communities that existed there.It occurs in areas as in burned or cut forests and abandoned farm lands. In secondary succession climax community reached more quickly because this succession is much faster as compared to primary succession.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14318,'chemistry',45,430,858,'Correct orders of 1st I.P. are<br>(i) Li < B < Be < C<br>(ii) O < N < F<br>(iii) Be < N < Ne','[{"text": "(i), (ii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(ii), (iii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i), (iii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i), (ii), (iii)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Due to stability of half-filled and completely filled orbitals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14328,'biology',98,1189,2848,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Humulin is better than conventional insulin<br></div><div class="column-right">Insulin is required for uptake of protein</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Humulin is more effective than the insulin produced by conventional methods. Humilin is absorbed rapidly in the blood than the conventionally produced insulin. Insulin is required for carbohydrate, fat, and protein to be metabolized. With respect to carbohydrate from a clinical standpoint, the major determinate of the glycemic response is the total amount of carbohydrate ingested rather than the source of the carbohydrate. Statement-A is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14319,'chemistry',15,177,386,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">On heating, a solid usually changes to a liquid and the liquid on further heating changes to the gaseous state.</div><div class="column-right">Arrangement of constituent particles is different in solid, liquid and gaseous state.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'On heating, the interparticle distance and freedom of movement of particles increase and interparticle forces decrease. Hence, on heating solids changes to liqids, where the particles are comparatively less close to each other and the particles are comparatively less close to each other and hence can move around. Liquids on further heating changes to gaseous state, in which the particles are far apart as compared to solids or liquids and their movement is easy and fast.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14320,'biology',98,1188,2847,'Silencing of a gene could be achieved through the use of:','[{"text": "RNAi only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antisense RNA only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both RNAi and antisense RNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both RNAi and antisense RNA',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERTExemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14321,'biology',99,1327,3210,'Read the following statements carefully.<br>I. Primary succession is a very slow process taking thousands of years for the climax to be reached.<br>II. Energy at a higher trophic level is always more than at a lower level.<br>III. Bacterial and fungal enzymes degrade detritus into simpler inorganic substances. This process is called fragmentation.<br>IV. All succession whether taking place in water or on land, proceeds to a similar climax community the mesic.<br>Which of the two above statements are correct?','[{"text": "II & III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I & II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III & IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I & IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I and IV are correct these two statements in the question are wrong and can be corrected as<br>II. Energy at a higher trophic level is always less than at a lower level.<br>III. Bacterial and fungal enzymes degrade detritus into simpler inorganic substances. This process is called catabolism.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14322,'chemistry',45,430,858,'Which of the following is incorrect?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{I}}{{\\\\rm{E}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Be < I}}{{\\\\rm{E}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{B}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{I}}{{\\\\rm{E}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Li < I}}{{\\\\rm{E}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Be}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{I}}{{\\\\rm{E}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Li < I}}{{\\\\rm{E}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Na}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{I}}{{\\\\rm{E}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{He < I}}{{\\\\rm{E}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Ne}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Electronic configuration of ${\\rm{Be:1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}$<br>Electronic configuration of ${\\rm{B:1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{1}}}$<br>Due to completely filled 2s orbital of Be element, ${\\rm{I}}{{\\rm{E}}_{\\rm{1}}}$ of Be is greater than ${\\rm{I}}{{\\rm{E}}_{\\rm{1}}}$ of B .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14323,'chemistry',15,185,404,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The empirical mass of ethyne is half of its molecular mass.</div><div class="column-right">The empirical formula represents the simplest whole number ratio of various atoms present in a compound.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14324,'biology',98,1189,2849,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">ADA gene provides instructions for producing enzyme adenosine aminase<br></div><div class="column-right">Adenosine aminase enzyme is found in the lymphocytes</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{ADA}$ gene provides instructions for producing the enzyme adenosine deaminase. Enzyme is produced in all cells, but the highest levels of adenosine deaminase occur in immune system cells called lymphocytes, which develop in lymphoid tissues. This enzyme is produced in all cells, but the highest levels of adenosine deaminase occur in immune system cells called lymphocytes, which develop in lymphoid tissues. These lymphoid tissues include the thymus, which is a gland located behind the breastbone, and lymph nodes, which are found throughout the body. So,both statements are incorrect.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14325,'biology',99,1325,3208,'Standing crop is -<br>i. Biomass in a unit area<br>ii. Number of living organism in unit area<br>iii. Amount of nutrient such as carbon, nitrogen, calcium in unit area<br>iv. Amount of Detritus in unit area','[{"text": "Only i", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i & ii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iv", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Each trophic level has a certain mass of living material at a particular time called as the standing crop. The standing crop is measured as the mass of living organisms (biomass) or the number in a unit area.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14326,'chemistry',45,430,858,'Elements X, Y and Z have atomic numbers 19, 37 and 55 respectively. Which of the following statement is true about them?','[{"text": "Their ionization potential would increase with increasing atomic number", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "\'Y\' would have an ionisation potential between those of X and Z.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Z would have the highest ionisation potential", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Y would have the highest ionisation potential", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All of the them are s-block elements',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14327,'chemistry',15,187,410,'Read the following statements and choose the correct statements<br>(I) Molality is preferred over molarity in expressing the concentration of a solution in case of temperature variation.<br>(II) The SI unit of molarity is mol ${\\rm{d}}{{\\rm{m}}^{{\\rm{ - 3}}}}$<br>(III) The molar volumes of a gases do not change with their molar masses','[{"text": "Only (I)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only (II)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only (III)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I), (II), (III)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14329,'biology',99,1324,3207,'Dead remains of animals including faecal matter, drop over soil and dried plant parts like leaves, bark, flowers etc constitute<br>i. Litter fall<br>ii. Below ground detritus<br>iii. Above ground detritus','[{"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'i and iii are correct, Litter fall and Above ground detritus will have dead remains of animals including faecal matter, drop over soil and dried plant parts like leaves, bark, flowers.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14330,'chemistry',45,430,858,'Which of the following metals require radiation of highest frequency to cause emission of electrons?','[{"text": "Na", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mg", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "K", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ca", "isCorrect": false}]',1,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14332,'biology',98,1187,2846,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Genetically engineered crop-based agriculture is used for increasing food production<br></div><div class="column-right">Genomes of many plants are manipulated or altered by combining them with other genes to get deisred traits.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Crops are genetically modified to allow higher yields due to the production of molecules that are toxic to insect pests, but have no effect on animals and humans. These crops are not devoured by insect pests, and lead to higher incomes for farmers due to better crop yield and lowered use of chemical pesticides. Genetic engineering (also called genetic modification) is a process that uses laboratory-based technologies to alter the DNA makeup of an organism. This may involve changing a single base pair (A-T or C-G), deleting a region of DNA or adding a new segment of DNA. Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14333,'biology',99,1325,3208,'Select the incorrect statement','[{"text": "Energy captured by plants does not revert back to solar input", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Energy flow is greatly reduced from T1 to $\\\\mathrm{T} 2$ level but increses from T2 to T4 level", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Energy flow is unidirectional", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pyramid of energy in always up right.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'There is a reduction in the amount of energy passing from one trophic level to another because at each step in food chain . Food is broken down to release energy and only a small amount of energy will enter body of organism. Hence there will be reduction in amount of energy from T2 to T4 level.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14334,'chemistry',45,430,858,'From the ground state electronic configurations of the elements given below, pick up the one with highest value of second ionisation enthalpy','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{6}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{3}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{6}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{3}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{1}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{6}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{5}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Here, ${\\rm{I}}{{\\rm{E}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ involves the removal of an electron from the inert gas configuration $\\left( {{\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}} \\right)$. So, it has highest value of second ionisation enthalpy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14335,'chemistry',15,181,399,'Consider the following statements<br>(i) Atoms of H, O, N and C have identical properties but different mass<br>(ii) Matter is divisible into atoms which are further indivisible<br>(iii) The ratio of N : H in ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ is 1 : 3 and N:O in nitric oxide is 2 : 1<br>(iv) Dalton’s atomic theory support law of conservation of mass<br>Which of the following pairs of statements is true according to Dalton’s atomic theory?','[{"text": "(i) and (ii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(ii) and (iii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(ii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(i) and (iv)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'For statement (i) : H, O, C, N = All have different chemical properties<br>For statement (ii) : It is true as per Dalton’s postulate.<br>For statement (iii) : N : O = 1 : 1(NO)<br>For statement (iv) : Dalton’s postulate says, atoms can neither be created nor destroyed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14336,'biology',98,1187,2846,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A crop expressing cry gene is usually resistant to specific insects<br></div><div class="column-right">cry\' proteins produced from <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> is toxic to certain insects</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Each Cry protein is toxic to a different group of insects. The gene encoding Cry protein, that is cry gene has been isolated and transferred into several crops. A crop expressing a cry gene is usually resistant to the groups of insects.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14337,'chemistry',45,430,859,'Electron affinity is a','[{"text": "Relative strength to attract the shared electron pair", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Necessary energy required to remove the electron from the ultimate orbit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Energy released when an electron is added to the outermost shell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Energy released when an electron is added to the inner shell", "isCorrect": false}]',2,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14338,'biology',99,1325,3208,'Choose the correct statements from the following<br>I. A man eating curd belongs to 3rd trophic level<br>II. A sparrow feeding on a herbivorous insect is a secondary consumer<br>III. Rabbit and deer belong to the same trophic level','[{"text": "I, II, III only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I. A man eating curd belongs to 3rd trophic level as curd is obtained from milk of herbivore $\\mathrm{T} 2$<br>II. A sparrow feeding on a herbivorous insect is a secondary consumer<br>III. Rabbit and deer belong to the same trophic level- herbivore, all the statements are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14339,'chemistry',15,180,398,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Equal moles of different substances contain same number of constituent particles.</div><div class="column-right">Equal weights of different substances contain the same number of constituent particles.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Equal moles of different substances contain same number of constituent particles but equal weights of different substances do not contain the same number of constituent particles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14340,'biology',98,1190,2851,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">\'Silencing of mRNA molecule\' in order to control the production of a harmful protein has been used in the protection of plants from armyworm<br></div><div class="column-right">$\\alpha$-1-antitrypsin gene was introduced in the first transgenic cow</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Silencing of mRNA has been used in producing transgenic plants resistant to nematodes.<br>Rosie was the first transgenic cow and it was produced in 1997. The gene for human protein alpha-lactalbumin was introduced in this cow. Both statements are incorrect.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14341,'chemistry',45,430,859,'Second electron affinity of an element is','[{"text": "Always exothermic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endothermic for few elements", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Exothermic for few elements", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Always endothermic", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14342,'biology',99,1325,3208,'Study the following statements about food chain and choose the correct option<br>I. The length of grazing food chains is general limited to 3-4 trophic levels due to energy loss<br>II. Removal of most of the carnivores resulted in an increased population of deers<br>III. The length of food chains may vary from 2-8 trophic levels<br>IV. Removal of $80 \\%$ tigers from an area resulted in greatly increased growth of vegetation.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement III and IV are wrong as trophic levels do not reach 8th step and removel of tigers - carnivore - consumer will result in increase in herbivores, consuming the vegetation and decreasing it.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14343,'chemistry',15,186,405,'Match the column I with column II and mark the appropriate choice.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Mass of ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ produced when 0.5 mole of zinc reacts with excess of HCl<br>B. Mass of all atoms of a compound with formula ${{\\rm{C}}_{{\\rm{70}}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{22}}}}$<br>C. Number of molecules in ${\\rm{35}}{\\rm{.5}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>D. Number of molecules in ${\\rm{64}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$</div><div class="column-right">P. ${\\rm{3}}{\\rm{.01 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{molecules}}$<br>Q. ${\\rm{6}}{\\rm{.023 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{molecules}}$<br>R. ${\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.43 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 21}}}}{\\rm{g}}$<br>S. ${\\rm{1}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}$</div></div>','[{"text": "A - Q, B - P, C - S, D - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P, B - Q, C - R, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S, B - R, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - S, B - R, C - Q, D - P", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'(A) ${\\rm{Zn + 2HCl}} \\to {\\rm{ZnC}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>1 mole of Zn produces 2g of ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>0.5 mole of Zn will produce 1g of ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>(B) molar mass of ${{\\rm{C}}_{{\\rm{70}}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{22}}}}{\\rm{ = 862}}$<br>Mass of atoms = ${\\rm{862/6}}{\\rm{.023 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.43 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 21}}}}{\\rm{g}}$<br>(C) 71g of ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 6}}{\\rm{.023 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}$ molecules<br>(D) molar mass of ${\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 64 = 1mole}}$<br>64g of ${\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 6}}{\\rm{.023 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}$ molecules',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14344,'biology',98,1188,2847,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">RNAi is a cellular defence mechanism in prokaryotes.<br></div><div class="column-right">It is silencing of a specific r-RNA.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'RNAi is a self-defense mechanism of eukaryotic cells, which specially prevent infection evoked by viruses. It can inhibit the expression of crucial viral proteins by targeting viral mRNA for degradation through cellular enzymes . In fact, RNAi does work effectively as an antiviral agent in plants. Antisense RNA is a single stranded oligonucleotide complementary to a protein coding mRNA. It forms a ds structure with the mRNA thus, blocking the process of translation. RNA interference technique silences the targeted mRNA molecule using a ds RNA Both statements are incorrect.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14345,'biology',99,1326,3209,'Study the following statements and select the incorrect one.','[{"text": "The pyramid of biomass is upright in an grassland ecosystem and the pyramid of numbers is upright in a parasitic food chain", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Topographic factors are the ecological factors connected with physical geography of earth with respect to that habitat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A food chain can not represent food web also", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The pyramid of biomass is upright in an grassland ecosystem and the pyramid of numbers is upright in a parasitic food chain, this statement si wrong as pyramid of number is inverted in parasitic food chain.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14346,'chemistry',45,430,859,'Highest electron affinity is shown by','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{L}}{{\\\\rm{i}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{a}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{F}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14348,'biology',98,1187,2846,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left"><i>Bacillus tumefaciens</i> is popularly used in genetic engineering because it can deliver genes to dicots<br></div><div class="column-right">Using  <i>Agrobacterium</i> as vector, the genes can be transferred in biotechnological techniques.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Agrobarcterium is well known for its ability to transfer DNA between itself and plants, and for this reason it has become an important tool for genetic engineering. Agrobacterium tumefaciens is a plant pathogen and most effective as plant genetic engineer. It causes the formation of crown gall in plants. The tumor-inducing plasmid Ti can be used as a useful cloning vector in gene cloning in plants. It introduces a piece of DNA which transforms normal plant cells into tumor cells. The Ti plasmid contains genes for the synthesis of auxin and cytokinin hormone and thus its introduction in a plant helps it to produce its own nutrient machinery. Statement-B is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14349,'chemistry',45,430,859,'In which of the following process maximum energy is released?','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right)}}{\\\\rm{ + }}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}} \\\\to {\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right)}^{\\\\rm{ - }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right)}^{\\\\rm{ - }}{\\\\rm{ + }}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}} \\\\to {\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right)}^{{\\\\rm{ - 2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right)}}{\\\\rm{ + }}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}} \\\\to {\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right)}^{\\\\rm{ - }}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right)}^{\\\\rm{ - }}{\\\\rm{ + }}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}} \\\\to {\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right)}^{{\\\\rm{ - 2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14350,'biology',99,1323,3206,'What type of pyramid would be obtained with the following data?<br>A. Secondary consumers: $2.6 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{m}^{2}$<br>B. Primary consumers: $48 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{m}^{2}$<br>C. Primary producers: $763 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{m}^{2}$','[{"text": "Upright pyramid of energy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inverted pyramid of energy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Upright pyramid of biomass", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inverted pyramid of biomass", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Biomass of $\\mathrm{PP}(763)>\\mathrm{PC}(48)>\\mathrm{SC}$ (2.6). So, the given data produces an upright pyramid of biomass.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14351,'chemistry',15,183,402,'Match the mass of elements given in column I with the number of moles given in column II and mark the appropriate choice. Choose the correct codes from the options given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. 28 g of He<br>B. 46 g of Na<br>C. 60 g of Ca<br>D. 27 g of Al</div><div class="column-right">P. 2 moles<br>Q. 7 moles<br>R. 1 mole<br>S. 1.5 mole</div></div>','[{"text": "A - S, B - R, C - Q, D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P, B - R, C - Q, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - R, B - Q, C - Q, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - P, C - S, D - R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{A:28}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{He = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{28}}}}{{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{7mol}}$<br>${\\rm{B:46g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Na = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{46}}}}{{{\\rm{23}}}}{\\rm{2mol}}$<br>${\\rm{C:60g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Ca = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{60}}}}{{{\\rm{40}}}}{\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.5mol}}$<br>${\\rm{D:27g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Al = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{27}}}}{{{\\rm{27}}}}{\\rm{1mol}}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14352,'biology',98,1190,2851,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Recombinant therapeutics do not induce unwanted immunological responses. <br></div><div class="column-right">Animals whose DNA is manipulated to possess and express an extra (foreign) gene are known as Transgenic animals</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The recombinant therapeutics do not induce unwanted immunological responses as is common in case of similar products isolated from non-human sources. A : Recombinant DNA technologies process has been less effective in therapeutic drug production. Animals that have had their DNA manipulated to possess and express an extra (foreign) gene are known as transgenic animals. Transgenic rats, rabbits, pigs, sheep, cows and fish have been produced, although over 95 percent of all existing transgenic animals are mice. Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14353,'biology',99,1324,3207,'Earthworms are regarded as farmer\'s friends because','[{"text": "They help in fragmentation of detritus and loosening of soil", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They help in leaching", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They reduce the rate of decomposition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Earthworms are regarded as farmer\'s friends because they help in fragmentation of detritus and loosening of soil, also the feacal matter - vermicompost is rich in nutrients.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14363,'chemistry',45,430,860,'Which one of the following is incorrect?','[{"text": "An element which has high electronegativity always has high electron gain enthalpy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Electron gain enthalpy is the property of an isolated atom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Electronegativity is the property of a bonded atom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both electronegativity and electron gain enthalpy are usually directly related to nuclear charge and inversely related to atomic size", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14354,'biology',98,1189,2849,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">ADA deficiency disorder is caused due to the excessive synthesis of gene for adenosine deaminase.<br></div><div class="column-right">It affects the human immune system.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Adenosine deaminase deficiency is caused by mutations in the ADA gene. This gene provides instructions for producing the enzyme adenosine deaminase. This enzyme is found throughout the body but is most active in specialized white blood cells called lymphocytes. Adenosine deaminase (ADA) deficiency is an inherited disorder that damages the immune system and causes severe combined immunodeficiency (SCID). People with SCID lack virtually all immune protection from bacteria, viruses, and fungi. Statement-B is correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14355,'biology',99,1325,3208,'Select the correct statement from the following.','[{"text": "Herbivores are secondary producers in an ecosystem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The mass of living material at a particular time in a trophic level is referred to as standing state", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The difference between GPP and NPP is the dfraction of PAR that plants cannot capture", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Net primary productivity of oceans is much higher than that of land because $71 \\\\%$ of carbon is dissolved in oceans", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Autotrophs are the primary producers. Herbivores are sometimes called secondary producers because they produce the biomass for their predators (primary carnivores).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14356,'chemistry',45,430,859,'The electron affinity of sulphur is -200 kJ/mole. Then the electron affinity of oxygen is','[{"text": "-142 kJ/mole", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "-702 kJ/mole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "-332 kJ/mole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "-348 kJ/mole", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14357,'chemistry',15,187,411,'Match the column I with column II and mark the appropriate choice.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Molarity<br>B. Mole fraction<br>C. Mole<br>D. Molality</div><div class="column-right">P. mol<br>Q. ${\\rm{mol}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{k}}{{\\rm{g}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$<br>R. ${\\rm{mol}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$<br>S. Unitless</div></div>','[{"text": "A - S, B - R, C - Q, D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A- R, B - S, C - Q, D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - R, B - S, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - P, B - Q, C - R, D - S", "isCorrect": false}]',2,NULL,NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14358,'biology',98,1190,2851,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Transgenic animals are those which have foreign RNA in all of their cells<br></div><div class="column-right">Of all the existing transgenic animals, $95 \\%$ are rats</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Transgenic organism is one that has become transformed following the introduction of novel genes into its genome. It is most frequently achieved by integration of doned DNA sequences following their injection into the fertilised egg. This fertilised egg divides mitotically to form the whole organism so that all the cells of the organism will carry the transferred genes. The transferred genes are known as transgenes. Over 95 percent of all transgenic animals are mice although transgenic rats, rabbits, pigs, sheep, cows and fish have also been produced. Statement-B is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14359,'chemistry',45,430,859,'Ionisation of energy of ${{\\rm{F}}^{\\rm{ - }}}\\,\\,{\\rm{is}}\\,\\,{\\rm{320}}\\,{\\rm{kJ}}\\,{\\rm{/}}\\,{\\rm{mole}}$. The electron gain enthalpy of fluorine would be','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{ - 320}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{kJ}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mo}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ - 160}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{kJ}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mo}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ + 320}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{kJ}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mo}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{160}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{kJ}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mo}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14360,'biology',99,1325,3208,'The first trophic level in grazing food chain is always a green plant because','[{"text": "They along have capability to fix atmospheric $\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rich in chlorophyll", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Of wide distribution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Their capacity to convert light energy to chemical energy", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Members of first trophic level are autotrophs- green plants as they convert light energy to chemical energy',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14361,'chemistry',15,182,401,'Match the formulas given in Column I with the molar mass given in Column II and mark the appropriate option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. ${{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{6}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>B. ${{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{6}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{6}}}$<br>C. ${{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{6}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{12}}}}$<br>D. ${\\rm{CaC}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}$</div><div class="column-right">P. 84<br>Q. 100<br>R. 93<br>S. 78</div></div>','[{"text": "A - S, B - R, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - R, B - S, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - S, B - P, C - S, D - Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - S, C - R, D - P", "isCorrect": false}]',1,NULL,NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14362,'biology',98,1190,2851,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">$\\alpha$-lactalbumin was introduced into the first transgenic cow to produce human protein enriched milk.<br></div><div class="column-right">An organism that contains and expresses a trangene is called transgenic organism.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Rosie was the first transgenic cow and it was produced in 1997. The gene for human protein alpha-lactalbumin was introduced in this cow. Thus, the cow could produce protein-enriched milk. This milk was nutritionally more balanced than natural cow milk. Transgenic organisms contain foreign DNA that has been introduced using biotechnology. Foreign DNA (the transgene) is defined here as DNA from another species, or else recombinant DNA from the same species that has been manipulated in the laboratory then reintroduced. Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14364,'biology',99,1323,3206,'Net primary productivity is the gross primary productivity less','[{"text": "That which is consumed by herbivores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "That which is consumed by producer in Metabolism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Secondary productivity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Loss due to mortality", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Gross primary productivity minus respiration losses ( $\\mathrm{R})$, is the net primary productivity (NPP). GPP $-\\mathrm{R}=\\mathrm{NPP}$, respiratory loss is the energy used in metabolism .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14365,'chemistry',15,183,402,'Match the data given in Column I with the corresponding moles in Column II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. ${\\rm{88}}\\,{\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>B. ${\\rm{6}}{\\rm{.022 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}$ molecules of ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$<br>C. 5.6 litres of ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ at STP<br>D. 96 g of ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$</div><div class="column-right">P. 0.25 mol<br>Q. 2 mol<br>R. 1 mol<br>S. 3 mol</div></div>','[{"text": "A - Q, B - R, C - P, D - S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - S, B - R, C - Q, D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P, B - R, C - Q, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - R, B - S, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-Q; Number of moles of ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{Mass}}}}{{{\\rm{Molar}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mass}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{88}}}}{{{\\rm{44}}}}{\\rm{ = 2}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mol}}$<br>B-R;${\\rm{1mol}}\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,{{\\rm{H}}_2}{\\rm{O}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{ = }}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{6}}.{\\rm{022}} \\times {\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{molecules}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$<br>C-P; ${\\rm{22}}.{\\rm{4}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{L}}\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}\\,{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{at}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{STP}} = 1{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mol}}{\\mkern 1mu} $<br>${\\rm{5}}.{\\rm{6}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{L}}\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}\\,{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{at}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{STP}}\\,\\,{\\rm{ = }}\\,{\\mkern 1mu} \\frac{{{\\rm{5}}.{\\rm{6}}}}{{{\\rm{22}}.{\\rm{4}}}}\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{ = }}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{0}}.{\\rm{25}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{mol}}$<br>D-S; Number of moles of ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{Mass}}}}{{{\\rm{Molar}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mass}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{96}}}}{{{\\rm{32}}}}{\\rm{ = 3}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mol}}$',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14366,'biology',98,1190,2851,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">ELISA is based on the principle of antigen-antibody interaction.<br></div><div class="column-right">The milk containing the human $\\alpha$-lactalbumin is nutritionally a more balanced product for human babies than natural cow milk.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'ELISA technique is based on the principles on the antigen-antibody interaction, used for diagnosis of AIDS. Rosie was the first transgenic cow which produced human protein-enriched milk (2.4 $\\mathrm{g} / \\mathrm{L})$. It was developed in the year 1997. Its milk proved to be nutritionally more balanced for human babies than any other natural cow milk because the milk contained the human alpha-lactalbumin. Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14367,'chemistry',45,430,860,'Electronic configuration of most electronegative element is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{5}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{6}}}{\\\\rm{3}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{1}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{6}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{3}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{3}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{5}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{6}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{3}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{3}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{6}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{5}}}$ is the electronic configuration of the Fluorine which is the most electronegative element in the periodic table.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14368,'chemistry',15,186,405,'If a rocket runs on a fuel ${\\rm{(}}{{\\rm{C}}_{{\\rm{15}}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{30}}}}{\\rm{)}}$ and liquid oxygen, the weight of oxygen required and ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ released for every litre of fuel respectively are: (Given: density of the fuel is 0.756 g/mL)','[{"text": "1188 g and 1296 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2376 g and 2592 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2592 g and 2376 g", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3429 g and 3142 g", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${{\\rm{C}}_{{\\rm{15}}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{30}}}}{\\rm{ + }}\\frac{{{\\rm{45}}}}{{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}} \\to {\\rm{15C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ + 15}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$<br>${\\rm{Mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{fuel = density \\times V}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{(mL)}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.756 \\times 1000g}}$<br>${\\rm{No}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{moles}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{fuel = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.756 \\times 1000}}}}{{{\\rm{210}}}}{\\rm{moles}}$<br>${\\rm{Wt}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{oxygen = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.756 \\times 1000}}}}{{{\\rm{210}}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}\\frac{{{\\rm{45}}}}{{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ \\times 32 = 2592g}}$<br>${\\rm{Wt}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.756 \\times 1000}}}}{{{\\rm{210}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 15 \\times 44 = 2376g}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2022,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14369,'biology',99,1326,3209,'Read the statements and select the best option<br>I. Pyramid of energy can never be inverted<br>II. A trophic level represents one species<br>III. Saprophytes are included in the lower most bar in an energy pyramid<br>IV. Ecological pyramids hold true only for simple food chains.','[{"text": "All are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I is true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III and IV are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV are true", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statement I and IV are correct as the remaining two statements can be corrected as a trophic level represent the group of organisms based on the type of nutrition or food consumed, saprophytes are never a part of pyrami system.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14377,'biology',99,1324,3207,'Which one of the following processes during decomposition is correctly described?','[{"text": "Catabolism - Last step in the decomposition under fully anaerobic condition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leaching- Water soluble inorganic nutrients rise to the top layers of soil.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fragmentation - Carried out by organism such as earth worm.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Humification -Leads to the accumulation of a dark coloured substance humus which undergoes microbial action at a very fast rate.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Breakdown of complex organic matter into inorganic substances is called decomposition.Dead plants remains, dead animals are called detritus, which is the raw material for decomposition. Fragmentation is the breakdown of detritus into small particles with the help of detritivores. Leaching is the process in which water soluble inorganic nutrients go down into the soil horizon and get precipitated as unavailable salts. Degradation of detritus into simpler inorganic substances with the help of bacterial and fungal enzymes is called Catabolism',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14370,'biology',98,1187,2846,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The inactive protoxin gets converted into active form in the insect gut<br></div><div class="column-right">Bt proteins exist as active toxins in the <i>Bacillus</i></div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bacillus thuringiensis is biopesticide, commonly known as $\\mathrm{Bt}$, is a naturally occurring, gram-positive, spore-forming soil bacterium. Bt has been known to be reservoir of several insecticidal proteins, such as endotoxins, cytolytic proteins, vegetative insecticidal proteins, etc.<br>During sporulation, it synthesizes a cytoplasmic inclusion containing one or more proteins that are toxic to insect larvae. Upon completion of sporulation the parent bacterium lyses to release the spore and the inclusion. In these inclusions, the toxins exist as inactive protoxins. When the inclusions are ingested by insect larvae, the alkaline $\\mathrm{pH}$ solubilizes the crystal. The protoxin is then converted in to an active toxin after processing by the host proteases present in the midgut. Bacillus thuringiensis (Bt) is a Gram-positive bacterium that produces crystals during sporulation. These crystals comprise of one or a small number of $\\sim 130 \\mathrm{kDa}$ protoxins called as crystal proteins and exists as inactive protoxin in the Bacillus. These proteins are potent and highly specific insecticides. Statement-A is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14371,'chemistry',45,430,860,'Regarding electronegativity<br>(i) The element with maximum electronegativity : Fluorine<br>(ii) In Pauling scale, the reference element is : Silicon<br>(iii) Elements with stable configuration have high electronegativity<br>(iv) The element with maximum electropositivity:Hydrogen','[{"text": "Only (i) correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only (ii) correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only (iii) correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only (iv) is correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14372,'chemistry',15,186,405,'A sample of ${\\rm{NaCl}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ is converted by heat to NaCl with a loss of 0.16 g of oxygen. The residue is dissolved in water and precipitated as AgCl . The mass of AgCl (in g) obtained will be: (Given: Molar mass of ${\\rm{AgCl = 143}}{\\rm{.5mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$)','[{"text": "0.35", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.54", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.41", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.48", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{2NaCl}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}} \\to {\\rm{2NaCl + 3}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.16}}$<br>$\\frac{{{{\\rm{n}}_{{\\rm{NaCl}}}}}}{{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{n}}_{{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}{{\\rm{3}}}$ [n = number of moles]<br>${{\\rm{n}}_{{\\rm{NaCl}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.16}}}}{{{\\rm{32}}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}\\frac{{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{200}}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}\\frac{{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{300}}}}$<br>${\\rm{NaCl}} \\to {\\rm{AgCl}}$<br>${\\rm{POAC}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Cl}}$<br>${\\rm{1 \\times }}{{\\rm{n}}_{{\\rm{NaCl}}}}{\\rm{ = 1 \\times }}{{\\rm{n}}_{{\\rm{AgCl}}}}$<br>$\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{300}}}}{\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{n}}_{{\\rm{AgCl}}}}$<br>Weight of ${\\rm{AgCl = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{143}}{\\rm{.5}}}}{{{\\rm{300}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.48g}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2018,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
