(14378,'biology',98,1189,2848,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Human insulin is made up of 50 amino acids arranged in two polypeptide</div><div class="column-right">C-peptide is present in the mature insulin</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Human insulin is made up of 51 amino acids arranged in two polypeptide chains; A chain with 21 amino acids and B chain with 30 amino acids. The two chains are interconnected by disulphide bridges. In mammals, insulin is synthesised in a pro-enzyme form called pro-insulin. $\\mathrm{C}$ peptide is not seen in mature insulin and eliminated during maturation into insulin. Both statements are incorrect.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14379,'chemistry',45,430,860,'The bond dissociation energies of ${\\rm{H}}\\, - \\,{\\rm{H,}}\\,{\\rm{C}}\\, - \\,{\\rm{C}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{\\rm{C}}\\, - \\,{\\rm{H}}$ bonds respectively are ${\\rm{104}}{\\rm{.2,}}\\,{\\rm{83}}{\\rm{.1}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{\\rm{98}}{\\rm{.8}}\\,\\,{\\rm{kcal}}\\,\\,{\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\rm{.}}$ The electronegativity of carbon is','[{"text": "2.59", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2.51", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}{\\\\rm{.50}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2.52", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${^{\\rm{E}}{\\rm{H}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{{\\rm{H}}^{{\\rm{ \\times E}}}}{\\rm{C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{C}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 98}}{\\rm{.8 - }}{\\left[ {\\left( {{\\rm{104}}{\\rm{.2}}} \\right){\\rm{ \\times }}\\left( {{\\rm{83}}{\\rm{.1}}} \\right)} \\right]^{{\\rm{1/2}}}}{\\rm{ = 5}}{\\rm{.75}}\\,{\\rm{k}}\\,{\\rm{cal}}$<br>${{\\rm{x}}_{\\rm{C}}}{\\rm{ - }}{{\\rm{x}}_{\\rm{H}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.208}}\\sqrt {\\rm{\\Delta }} {\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.208}}\\,{\\left( {{\\rm{5}}{\\rm{.75}}} \\right)^{{\\rm{1/2}}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.49}}$<br>$\\therefore \\,{{\\rm{x}}_{\\rm{C}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.49 + }}{{\\rm{x}}_{\\rm{H}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.49 + 2}}{\\rm{.1 = 2}}{\\rm{.59}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14380,'chemistry',15,183,402,'An unknown chlorohydrocarbon has 3.55% of chlorine. If each molecule of the hydrocarbon has one chlorine atom only; chlorine present in 1g of chlorohydrocarbon are: (Atomic wt. of Cl u = 35.5u ; Avogadro number<br>${\\rm{ = 6}}{\\rm{.023 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$)','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{6}}{\\\\rm{.023 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{\\\\rm{9}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{6}}{\\\\rm{.023 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{23}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{6}}{\\\\rm{.023 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{21}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{6}}{\\\\rm{.023 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{20}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{x}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{y}}}{\\rm{Cl}}$ is the formula of chorohydrocarbon.<br>Given, % Cl = 3.55%<br>Weight of ${\\rm{Cl = 1 \\times }}\\frac{{{\\rm{3}}{\\rm{.55}}}}{{{\\rm{100}}}}$<br>${{\\rm{n}}_{{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1 \\times 3}}{\\rm{.55}}}}{{{\\rm{100 \\times 35}}{\\rm{.5}}}}$<br>No of ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\rm{ion = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1 \\times 3}}{\\rm{.55}}}}{{{\\rm{100 \\times 35}}{\\rm{.5}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 6}}{\\rm{.023 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 6}}{\\rm{.023 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{20}}}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2018,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14381,'biology',99,1326,3209,'Which of the following statement is correct?','[{"text": "Pyramid of number in grassland ecosystem is upright.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pyramid of number in aquatic ecosystem is inverted.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pyramid of biomass in tree ecosystem is inverted.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pyramid of biomass in aquatic ecosystem is upright", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In a grassland ecosystem, number of plants or grasses or herbs will support fewer number of grasshoppers that will support still lesser number of frogs, still lesser number of snakes etc. Hence pyramid of number in a grassland ecosystem is upright.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14382,'biology',98,1189,2848,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The two polypeptide chains are interconnected by disulphide bridges<br></div><div class="column-right">In mammals including humans, insulin is synthesised as a prohormone, which contains an extra stretch called the C-peptide</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Two peptide chains as referred to $A$ and B chains are linked together by two disulfide bonds while the additional disulfide is created within the A Chain. Hence, we can say that two polypeptides of human insulin are linked together by Disulfide bridges. In mammals, including humans, insulin is synthesised as pro-hormone which needs to be processed before it becomes a fully mature and functional hormone. It contains an extra stretch called the $\\mathrm{C}$ peptide which is removed during maturation into insulin. Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14383,'chemistry',45,432,864,'The order in which the following oxides are arranged according to decreasing basic nature is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{a}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{MgO,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{A}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{CuO}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{CuO,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{A}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{MgO,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{a}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{CuO,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{MgO,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{a}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{CuO,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{MgO,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{a}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{A}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'As we move from left to right in a period the basic character of the oxides of s-and p_x0002_block elements decreases while their acidic character increases. The basic character of oxides of d-block elements is, however, lower than alkali and alkaline earth metals. Thus, ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$ is most basic followed by ${\\rm{MgO,}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{and}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{A}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$ while ${\\rm{CuO}}$ is least basic.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14384,'chemistry',15,187,411,'A solution of sodium sulphate contains 92 g of ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ ions per kilogram of water. The molality of ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$  ions in that solution in ${\\rm{mol}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{k}}{{\\rm{g}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$ is','[{"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{Molality}}\\,{\\rm{ = }}\\,\\frac{{{\\rm{mass}}\\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,\\,{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}}}{{{\\rm{At}}{\\rm{.}}\\,\\,{\\rm{wt}}{\\rm{.}}\\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,\\,{\\rm{Na \\times mass}}\\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,\\,{\\rm{solvent(kg)}}}}$<br>${\\rm{Molality = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{92}}}}{{{\\rm{23}}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = 4mol/kg}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
