(14393,'biology',99,1325,3208,'Read the given statements regarding food chain<br>I. The length of food chains is generally limited to 3-4 trophic levels due to energy loss.<br>II. Removal of $80 \\%$ tigers from an area resulted in greatly increased growth of vegetation.<br>III. The length of food chains may vary from 2 to 8 trophic levels.<br>IV. Removal of most of carnivores resulted in an increased population of herbivores animals like deer<br>Which of the two statements are correct?','[{"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'By removal of $80 \\%$ of tiger from the area, there will be decrease in growth of vegetation, as primary and secondary consumers will feed on plants. Removal of carnivores will increase of population of herbivores animals like deer.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
