(14404,'chemistry',15,187,412,'The volume of 0.1 N dibasic acid sufficient to neutralise 1 g of a base that gives 0.04 mole of ${\\rm{O}}{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$ in aqueous solution:','[{"text": "400 mL", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "600 mL", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "200 mL", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.125 mL", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Applying law of equivalence,<br>Equivalence of acid = Equivalence of base<br>${(NV)_{acid}} = {(n \\times ch\\arg e)_{base}}$<br>$0.1 \\times V = 0.04 \\times 1$<br>$V = 0.4L = 0.4 \\times 1000 = 400mL$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14405,'biology',99,1325,3208,'Number of trophic levels in food chains is restricted because','[{"text": "Trophic efficiency of animals is less than that of plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "About $90 \\\\%$ of the energy in a trophic level is lost as it passes to the next higher level", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Predator animals are larger than prey animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number of organisms always decreases from lower to higher trophic levels", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The number of trophic levels in the grazing food chain is restricted as the transfer of energy follows 10 per cent law - only 10 per cent of the energy is transferred to each trophic level from the lower trophic level.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14406,'biology',98,1187,2846,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> \'Cry\' proteins are named so because they are crystal proteins.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In alkaline environment of insect midgut \'Cry\' proteins are solubilized and then release toxic core fragments after proteolytic action.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The cry gene of Bacillus thuringiensis produces a protein, that forms crystalline inclusions i.e., is crystal in nature in the bacterial spores. Due to their crystal nature these proteins are named \'cry\' proteins and are responsible for the insecticidal activities of the bacterial strains. In alkaline environment of insect midgut \'Cry\' proteins are solubilized. Then to release core toxic fragments these proteins undergo proteolytic digestion. These toxins bind to receptors in brush border of midgut epithelial cells. As a result, brush border, membrane develop pores, most likely nonspecific in nature and cause influx of ions and water into the cells resulting in their swelling and eventual lysis.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14407,'chemistry',45,432,865,'Aqueous solutions of two compounds ${\\rm{M}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{O}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{H}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{M}}^{\\rm{\'}}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{O}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{H}}$ have been prepared in two different beakers. If the electronegativity of ${\\rm{M = 3}}{\\rm{.5,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{M}}^{\\rm{\'}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.72,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{O = 3}}{\\rm{.0}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{\\rm{H = 2}}{\\rm{.1,}}$ then the solutions respectively are','[{"text": "Acidic, acidic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acidic, basic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Basic, basic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Basic, acidic", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the compound ${\\rm{M}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{O}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{H}}$, if IE or E.N. of M is low, the compound will act as a base and if the IE or E.N of M is high, the compound will behave as an acid',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14408,'chemistry',15,186,405,'The amount of arsenic pentasulphide that can be obtained when 35.5 g arsenic acid is treated with excess ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{S}}$ in the presence of conc. HCl (assuming 100% conversion) is:','[{"text": "0.25 mol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.50 mol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.333 mol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.125 mol", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathop {{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{As}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}}\\limits_{\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{2moles}}}\\\\{{\\kern 1pt} {\\rm{1}}{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\rm{mole}}}\\end{array}} {\\rm{ + 5}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{S}}\\mathop {{\\rm{A}}{{\\rm{s}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{5}}}}\\limits_{\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\rm{1mole}}}\\\\{{\\rm{1/2mole}}}\\end{array}} {\\rm{ + 8}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}} <br>$\\therefore $ Number of moles of ${H_3}As{O_4} = \\frac{{35.5}}{{142}} = 0.25$ moles<br>$\\therefore $ Number of moles of $A{s_2}{S_5} = \\frac{{0.25}}{2}$<br>$ = 0.125\\,\\,moles$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2016,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14409,'biology',99,1323,3206,'The rate of biomass production is called productivity it may be primary or secondary productivity. Primary productivity does not depends on :-','[{"text": "Plant species inhabitating a particular area", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Predation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Environmental factors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photo synthetic capacity", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Predation is not a factor $n$ which productivity of an ecosystem depends.<br>Predation is an interaction where one animal which acts as predator will kill consume another animal.(prey)',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14410,'biology',98,1187,2846,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> <i>Agrobacterium</i> is a genetic engineer.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It is a vector used for transfer of genes.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Assertion : Agrobacterium is a genetic engineer. Reason : It is a vector used for transfer of genes. Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14411,'chemistry',45,421,841,'The first list of 23 elements was compiled in the late 1790s by','[{"text": "Dimitri Medeleev", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lother Meyer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antione Lavoisier", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "John New land", "isCorrect": false}]',2,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14412,'chemistry',15,186,405,'A sample of a hydrate of barium chloride weighing 61 g was heated until all the water of hydration is removed. The dried sample weighed 52 g. The formula of the hydrated salt is:<br>(atomic mass : Ba = 137 amu , Cl = 35.5 amu)','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{BaC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{.4}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{BaC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{.3}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{BaC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{.}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{BaC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{.2}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Weight of hydrated $BaC{l_2}$ = 61 g<br>Weight of anhydrous $BaC{l_2}$ = 52 g<br>Loss in mass = 9g<br>Assuming $BaC{l_2}.x{H_2}O$ as hydrate<br>Moles of ${H_2}O = \\frac{9}{{18}} = 0.5$<br>Gram molecular weight of $BaC{l_2}$ = 208 % of ${H_2}O$ in this hydrated<br>$BaC{l_2} = \\frac{9}{{61}} \\times 100 = 14.75\\%  = \\frac{{18x}}{{208 + 18x}} \\times 100$<br>On solving, x = 2<br>So, the formula is $BaC{l_2}.2{H_2}O$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14413,'biology',99,1326,3209,'Go through the statements.<br>I. In terrestrial ecosystem, maximum energy is present in $\\mathrm{T} 1$.<br>II. In grassland ecosystem, the pyramid of biomass is upright.<br>III. In pyramid of food, the producers occupy the base/ bottom.<br>IV. Energy flow in an ecosystem is bidirectional.<br>V. If all green plants of earth are destroyed, all animals shall die ultimately.<br>VI. The typical biome of an area having 50 to $100 \\mathrm{~cm}$ of rainfall is grassland.<br>How many of the above statements (s) is/are wrong?','[{"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The flow of energy in the ecosystem is unidirectional because lost as heat from the living organism of a food chain cannot be renewed by the plants in photosynthesis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14414,'biology',98,1190,2851,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Transgenic plant is a product of plant tissue culture.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> An organism that contains and expresses a transgenic organism.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plant tissue culture has various applications in the different fields of biology. An example of this is the production of transgenic plants and animals. Transgenic organisms contain genes, which are transferred into them through the genetic engineering. These genes are known as transgenic.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14415,'chemistry',45,422,842,'The final contributor to the modern periodic table was','[{"text": "Glenn Seaborg", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lother Meyer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Henry Mosely", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dimitri Medeleev", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14416,'chemistry',15,186,405,'${\\rm{A + 2B + 3C}} \\to {\\rm{A}}{{\\rm{B}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{3}}}$<br>Reaction of 6.0 g of A, ${\\rm{6}}{\\rm{.0 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}$ atoms of B, and 0.036 mol of C yields 4.8 g of compound ${\\rm{A}}{{\\rm{B}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{3}}}$. If the atomic mass of A and C are 60 and 80 amu, respectively, the atomic mass of B is $\\left( {{\\rm{Avogadro}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{no}}{\\rm{. = 6 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}} \\right)$:','[{"text": "50 amu", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "60 amu", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "70 amu", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "40 amu", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$A + 2B + 3C \\to A{B_2}{C_3}\\left( 1 \\right)$<br>No. of moles of $B = \\frac{{6.0g}}{{60g/mol}} = 0.1mol$<br>No. of moles of $A = \\frac{{6.0 \\times {{10}^{23}}}}{{6 \\times {{10}^{23}}}} = 0.1mol$<br>No. of moles of $C = 0.036\\,mol$<br>$A{B_2}{C_3}$ is formed accordingly to C, which is a limiting reagent.<br>Since, 3 moles of C are used in (1)<br>So it gives 1 mole of $A{B_2}{C_3}$<br>${n_{A{B_2}{C_3}}} = \\frac{{0.036}}{3} = 0.012 = \\frac{{Given\\,\\,mass\\,\\,\\left( {4.8} \\right)}}{{Molecular\\,\\,mass\\,\\,\\left( {M.M} \\right)}}$<br>$Mol.\\,\\,mass = \\frac{{4.8}}{{0.012}} = 400$<br>Let assume the atomic mass of B is ‘x’.<br>$400 = 60 + \\left( {2 \\times x} \\right) + \\left( {80 \\times 3} \\right)$<br>$x = 50$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2015,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14417,'biology',99,1322,3205,'How many of given ecosystem are natural and man made ecosystem respectively','[{"text": "5,3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3,5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4,4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6,2", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Natural ecosystem $=5$ (forest, grassland, river, estuary, lake)<br>Man made ecosystem $=3$ (Crop field, fishery tank, Aquaria)',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/99_14417_question_1.jpg'),
(14418,'biology',98,1187,2846,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> A crop expressing a cry gene is usually resistant to a group of insects.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Cry proteins produced from <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> is non toxic to the bacillus','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Bacillus thuringiensis (Bt), a soil bacterium produces a Cry protein (crystal protein). This protein is toxic to the larvae of certain insects. There are several kinds of Cry proteins. Each Cry protein is toxic to a different group of insects. The gene encoding Cry protein, i.e., cry gene has been isolated and transferred into several crops. A crop expressing a cry gens is usually resistant to the groups of insects.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14419,'chemistry',45,421,841,'The element cited as an example to prove that validity of Mendeleev’s periodic law is','[{"text": "Germanium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Scandium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gallium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The discovery of these elements were made later on. However, Mendeleev left blank spaces in periodic table and predicted their properties.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14420,'chemistry',15,187,410,'Dissolving 120 g of a compound of molar mass 60 in 1000 g of water gave a solution of density 1.12 g/mL. The molarity of the solution is:','[{"text": "1.00 M", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2.00 M", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2.50 M", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4.00 M", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Given<br>Mass of solute $({w_2}) = 120\\,\\,g$<br>Mass of solvent $({w_1}) = 1000\\,\\,g$<br>Mol. mass of solute $ = 60\\,\\,g\\,\\,mo{l^{ - 1}}$<br>Density of solution $ = 1.12\\,\\,g/ml$<br>From the given data,<br>Mass of solution $ = 1000 + 120 = 1 = 120\\,\\,g$<br>Volume of the solution, $V = \\frac{{Mass\\,\\,of\\,\\,the\\,\\,solution}}{{Density\\,\\,of\\,\\,the\\,\\,solution}}$<br>$V = \\frac{{1120}}{{60 \\times 1}} = 1000\\,\\,mL = 1L$<br>Now, Molarity $(M) = \\frac{{{W_2}}}{{Mol \\cdot mass \\times V(lit)}}$<br>$ = \\frac{{120}}{{60 \\times 1}} = 2M$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14421,'biology',99,1328,3211,'Which in not correct statement from the following','[{"text": "Food web shows the pattern of energy or nutrient flow throughout the community", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbon cycle does not necessarily have to involve decomposers", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The organisms, which attack dead animals are present at the starting of food chain, e.g. detritus food chain and are known as decomposers.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cropland ecosystem is a man made ecosystem. Here genetic diversity is least and food web is simple", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Carbon cycle is a type of gaseous cycle. In carbon cycle, decomposers are involved in decomposition of organic wastes and dead bodies to release carbon.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14422,'biology',98,1188,2847,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> By insertion of gene encoding complementary RNA only the RNAi can be introduced in an organism.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In vitro there are no methods by which synthesised complementary RNA can be inserted in an organism to induce RNAi (RNA interference).','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both Assertion and Reason are false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14424,'chemistry',15,185,404,'A gaseous compound of nitrogen and hydrogen contains 12.5 % by mass of hydrogen. The density of the compound relative to hydrogen is 16. The molecular formula of the compound is:','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{H}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Given, % of H = 12.5%<br>$\\therefore \\% \\,\\,of\\,\\,N = 100 - 12.5 = 87.5\\% $2$ \\times $ vapour density = Mol.wt<br>$Mol.wt. = 16 \\times 2 = 32$<br>Molecular formula $ = n \\times empirical\\,\\,formula\\,\\,mass$<br>$n = \\frac{{32}}{{16}} = 2$<br>$\\therefore $ Molecular formula of the compound will be $ = {(N{H_2})_2} = {N_2}{H_4}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14425,'biology',99,1322,3205,'Read the following statements and choose the correct set of options w.r.t ecosystem<br>I. Various ecosystem are interconnected by flow of energy and transfer of materials<br>II. It is self sustained and self regulated segment of nature<br>III. Energy flow is always cyclic while flow of nutrients in unidirections<br>IV. Density of ecosystem is governed by degree of biogeochemical cycling and the amount of nutrients','[{"text": "I, II and IV are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II and III are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Energy flow is always unidirectional while the flow of nutrients is cyclic.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14426,'biology',98,1188,2847,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cellular defence mechanism in eukaryotes is RNAi.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> RNAi is silencing of a specific tRNA.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'RNAi is the silencing of a specific mRNA.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14427,'chemistry',45,422,842,'The statement that is not true for the long form of the periodic table is','[{"text": "It reflects the sequence of filling electrons in the order of sub-energy levels s, p, d and f.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It reflects trends in physical and chemical properties of the elements", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It helps to predict the stable valence states of the elements", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It helps to predict the relative ionicity of the bond between any two elements.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14428,'chemistry',15,187,410,'10 mL of 2M NaOH solution is added to 200 mL of 0.5 M of NaOH solution. What is the final concentration?','[{"text": "0.57 M", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5.7 M", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "11.4 M", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.14 M", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'From molarity equation<br>${M_1}{V_1} + {M_2}{V_2} = M{V_{(total)}}$<br>$2 \\times \\frac{{10}}{{100}} + 0.5 \\times \\frac{{200}}{{1000}} = M \\times \\frac{{210}}{{1000}}$<br>$120 = M \\times 210$<br>$M = \\frac{{120}}{{210}} = 0.57M$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2013,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14429,'biology',99,1323,3206,'The following table shows net productivities of various trophic levels in one ecosystem in Silver Springs, Florida receiving sunlight at a rate of  ${\\rm{1,700,000}}\\,{\\rm{kcal/}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{/yr}}$.<br>${\\rm{Primaryproducers}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{7168}}\\,{\\rm{kcal/}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{/yr}}$<br>${\\rm{Primaryconsumers}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{1103}}\\,\\,{\\rm{kcal/}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{/yr}}$<br>${\\rm{Secondaryconsumers111}}\\,\\,{\\rm{kcal/}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{/yr}}$<br>${\\rm{Tertiaryconsumers}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{5}}\\,\\,{\\rm{kcal/}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{/yr}}$<br>The efficiency energy transfer is the highest between','[{"text": "Primary producers and primary consumers", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Primary consumers and secondary consumers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Solar energy and primary producers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary consumers and tertiary consumers", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Sunlight to PP<br>$=\\dfrac{7168}{1700000} \\times 100 \\approx 0.42 \\%$<br>PP to $\\mathrm{PC}=\\dfrac{1103}{7168} \\times 100 \\approx 15 \\%$<br>PC to $\\mathrm{SC}=\\dfrac{111}{1103} \\times 100 \\approx 10 \\%$<br>$\\mathrm{SC}$ to $\\mathrm{TC}=\\dfrac{5}{111} \\times 100 \\approx 4.5 \\%$<br>Therefore, efficiency energy transfer is the highest between PP and PC.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14430,'biology',98,1188,2847,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Tobacco plant yield is highly reduced because of damage to roots.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Nematode <i>Meloidogyne incognita</i> infects the root.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Meloidogyne incognita infects the root of tobacco plant that leads to the degradation of cell walls of the roots and reduce the yield.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14431,'chemistry',45,421,837,'Which of the following is not a Dobereiner triad?','[{"text": "Cl,Br,I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ca,Sr,Ba", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Li, Na,K", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fe,Co, Ni", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Dobereiner triads consist of elements of the same groups and hence Fe, Co, Ni do not constitute a Dobereiner triad.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14432,'chemistry',15,183,402,'The amount of oxygen in 3.6 moles of water is:','[{"text": "115.2 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "57.6 g", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "28.8 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "18.4 g", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'1 mole of water contains = 16gm of oxygen<br>$\\therefore $ 3.6 mole of water contains<br>$ = 16 \\times 3.6 = 57.6\\,\\,g$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14467,'biology',98,1190,2851,'Transgenic plants are','[{"text": "Grown in artificial medium after hybridization in the field", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Generated by introducing foreign DNA into a cell and regenerating a plant from that cell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Produced after protoplast fusion in artificial medium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Produced by somatic embryo in artificial medium.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Transgenic plants are plants that are produced by genetically engineering contain a foreign gene. Recombinant DNA Techniques are used to improve crop plants by increasing their productivity, disease resistance etc.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14433,'biology',99,1327,3210,'Consider the following statements regarding ecological succession and select the correct option.<br>I. Reproductive structures from any previous community are absent in primary succession.<br>II. Primary succession takes less time than secondary succession for its completion<br>III. Landslide or earthquake can be a reason for secondarily bared area.<br>IV. Newly submerged areas and newly exposed sea floor are some of the examples of secondary succession.<br>$\\,\\,\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{\\rm{I}}&{{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{II}}}&{{\\rm{III}}}&{{\\rm{IV}}}\\end{array}$','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\,{\\\\rm{T}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{F}}}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\,{\\\\rm{T}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{T}}}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\,{\\\\rm{T}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{F}}}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\,{\\\\rm{T}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{F}}}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II and IV statement is false and can be corrected as Primary succession takes more time than secondary succession for its completion Newly submerged areas and newly exposed sea floor are some of the examples of primary succession.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14434,'biology',98,1190,2851,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Biotechnology produces transgenic micro-organisms that acts as microfactories for proteins.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> To produce proteins of human use like insulin. Transgenic microorganisms can be developed.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'By inserting genes (or desired protein products transgenic micro-organisms can be developed using recombinant DNA technology. These transgenic organisms acts as living microfactories that produce proteins like human insulin, human growth hormone, etc. Production of proteins from such organisms is easier, more efficient and cost effective.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14435,'chemistry',45,421,838,'The discovery of which of the following group of elements gave a death blow to the Newland Law of Octaves.','[{"text": "Inert gases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alkaline earths", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rare earths", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Actinides", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'With the discovery of inert gases (Group zero in Mendeleev’s periodic table), the law of octaves lost its original significance since it was now the nineth element which had properties similar to the first one.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14436,'chemistry',15,187,410,'The amount of ${\\rm{BaS}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ formed upon mixing 100 mL of 20.8% ${\\rm{BaC}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ solution with 50 mL of 9.8% ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ solution with 50 mL of 9.8% ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ solution will be:','[{"text": "23.3 g", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1.65 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "30.6 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "33.2 g", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathop {{\\rm{BaC}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}}\\limits_{\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{208}}\\,{\\rm{g}}}\\\\{{\\rm{20}}{\\rm{.8}}\\,{\\rm{g}}}\\end{array}} {\\rm{ + }}\\mathop {{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{SO}}}\\limits_{\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{98}}\\,{\\rm{g}}}\\\\{{\\rm{9}}{\\rm{.8}}\\,{\\rm{g}}}\\end{array}}  \\to \\mathop {{\\rm{BaS}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}}\\limits_{\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{233}}\\,{\\rm{g}}}\\\\{{\\rm{23}}{\\rm{.3}}\\,{\\rm{g}}}\\end{array}} {\\rm{ + }}\\mathop {{\\rm{2HCl}}}\\limits_{\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{73}}\\,{\\rm{g}}}\\\\{{\\rm{7}}{\\rm{.3}}\\,{\\rm{g}}}\\end{array}} $',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14437,'biology',99,1327,3210,'Pick out of the correct option from (1) to (4).<br>i. Primary succession begins in areas where natural communities have been destroyed.<br>ii. Hydrarch succession takes place in water.<br>iii. He climax community is the community that is in near equilibrium with the immediate environment<br>iv. In newly cooled lava secondary succession occurs.','[{"text": "ii and iii are correct, i and iv are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i and ii are correct, iii and iv are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii only is correct, i, iii and iv are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iv are correct, ii and iii are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'II and III are correct, I and IV are incorrect',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14438,'biology',98,1189,2848,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Using biotechnology human insulin can be produced into bacterial cells.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> To produce human insulin the $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}$ and $\\mathrm{C}$ polypeptides of the human insulin are produced in the bacterial cells, separately extracted and combined by creating disulfide bonds.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Adult onset diabetes management is possible by taking insulin at regular time intervals, but insulin from other animals could elicit immune response in body. Biotechnology has helped to overcome this problem. Transgenic bacteria have been produced that translate the constituting polypeptide chains of human insulin from the bacterial cells. These polypeptides can be extracted and combined to produce human insulin, by creating disulfide bonds. In humans, insulin is produced as a prohormone with three polypeptides A, B and C. After processing, the $\\mathrm{C}$ peptide is removed and mature insulin is formed. When transgenic bacteria are used, instead of producing extra stretch of C peptide, only A and B polypeptides are produced and then linked directly to produce mature insulin.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14439,'chemistry',45,421,838,'Which of the following set of elements obeys Newland’s octave rule?','[{"text": "Na, K, Rb", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mg, Ca, Sr", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cl,Br, I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Be, Mg, Ca", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14440,'chemistry',15,183,402,'Number of atoms in the following samples of substances is the largest in:','[{"text": "4.0 g of hydrogen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "7.10 g of chlorine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "127.0 g of iodine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "48.0 g of magnesium", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'(1) 4g of hydrogen = 4 mole of hydrogen atoms $ = 4 \\times 6.023 \\times {10^{23}}\\,\\,atoms$<br>(2) 71.0 gm of chlorine $ = \\frac{{71.0}}{{71.0}}$<br>= 1 moleof chlorine<br>$ = 6.023 \\times {10^{23}}\\,\\,atoms$<br>(3) 127 gm of iodine =1 mole of I atoms $ = 6.023 \\times {10^{23}}\\,\\,atoms$<br>(4) 48.0 gm of magnesium $ = \\frac{{48.0}}{{24.0}}$<br>2 moles of Mg $ = 2 \\times 6.023 \\times {10^{23}}\\,\\,atoms$<br>$\\therefore $ 4.0 gm ${H_2}$ has the largest number of atoms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2013,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14441,'biology',99,1324,3207,'Leaching, fragmentation and catabolism are some of the important steps of decomposition. Select the correct options w.r.t. the given statements<br>i. Water soluble inorganic nutrients go into the soil and get precipitated as unavailable salts.<br>ii. Detritivores breakdown detritus into smaller particles<br>iii. Decomposers excrete digestive enzymes and degrade detritus into simple inorganic substances.<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{Leaching}}}&{{\\rm{Fragmentation}}}&{{\\rm{Catabolism}}}\\end{array}$','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{ii}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{i}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{iii}}}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{iii}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{i}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{ii}}}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{i}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{ii}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{iii}}}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{i}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{iii}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{ii}}}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Decomposition is process of breakdown of complex organic matter into inorganic substances . Process of decomposition includes<br>(1) Fragmentation of detritus<br>(2) Catabolism<br>(3) Leaching. Fragmentation of detritus is a process where the detrivores (earthworm, beetle) breakdown the detritus into smaller particles. Catabolism is process in which decomposers excrete digestive enzymes over detritus which will change insoluble complex organic substance into simple and soluble substances. The process of leaching, the soluble substances formed are passed to deeper layers by percolating water.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14442,'biology',98,1189,2849,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Due to excessive synthesis of gene for adenosine deaminase ADA deficiency disorder is caused.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It affects the human digestive system.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'ADA disorder is caused because of lack of gene for adenosine deaminase. It affects the human immune system.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14443,'chemistry',45,421,841,'By taking chemical equivalents into consideration, the atomic weights of the following elements were corrected by Mendeleev','[{"text": "Te & I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ar & K", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Co & Ni", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Be & In", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14444,'chemistry',15,187,411,'The density of 3M solution of sodium chloride is ${\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.252g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{m}}{{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$. The molality of the solution will be: (molar mass of, ${\\rm{58}}{\\rm{.5}}\\,\\,{\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$)','[{"text": "260 m", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2.18 m", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2.79 m", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3.00 m", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The relation between molarity (M) and molality (m) is $d = M\\left( {\\frac{1}{m} + \\frac{{{M_2}}}{{1000}}} \\right),\\,\\,{M_2} = Mol$. mass of solute On substituting value<br>$1.252 = 3\\left( {\\frac{1}{m} + \\frac{{58.5}}{{1000}}} \\right)$<br>on solving $m = 2.79m$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2013,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14445,'biology',99,1324,3207,'Decomposers like fungi and bacteria are :-<br>i. Autotrophs<br>ii. Heterotrophs<br>iii. Saprotrophs<br>iv. Chemo-autotrophs','[{"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Heterotrophs are organisms which cannot manufacture their own food and depend on autotrophs for nutrition. Saprotrophs are organisms that depends on dead and decaying matter for its survival.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14446,'biology',98,1189,2849,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The ADA gene gives instruction for producing the enzyme adenosine deaminases.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Throughout the body this enzyme is found but is most active in lymphocytes.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The $\\mathrm{ADA}$ gene gives instructions for producing the enzyme adenosine deaminase. In all cells this enzyme is produced, but the highest levels of adenosine deaminase takes place in immune system cells called lymphocytes, that develop in lymphoid tissues. Lymphocytes form the immune system, that defends the body against potentially harmful invaders, such as viruses or bacteria.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
