(14449,'biology',99,1327,3210,'Read the following statements and select the option stating which ones are true (T) and which ones are false (F).<br>I. Rooted plants which occur in shallow waters are called macrophytes.<br>II. Submerged hydrophytes have higher photosynthetic rate than the floating hydrophytes.<br>III. Detritus is the dried fallen plant matter.<br>IV. Primary productivity is the rate of synthesis of organic matter by producers.<br>$\\,\\,\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{I}}}&{{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{II}}}&{{\\rm{III}}}&{{\\rm{IV}}}\\end{array}$','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{T}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{F}}}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{T}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{F}}}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{F}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{T}}}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{\\\\rm{T}}&{\\\\rm{F}}&{\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{T}}}&{\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{T}}}\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{T}}\\,\\,{\\rm{F}}\\,\\,{\\rm{F}}\\,\\,{\\rm{T}}$ is the correct option, and second statement can be corrected as Submerged plants have a lower rate of photosynthesis than floating hydrophytes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
