(14461,'biology',99,1325,3208,'G F C\'s are<br>i. Also called predatory food chains<br>ii. Begin with detritus<br>iii. Begin with producers<br>iv. The major conduit for energy flow in aquatic ecosystems<br>v. The major conduit for energy flow in terrestrial ecosystem','[{"text": "i, ii, iii are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii, iv, v are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii, iv are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii, iv, v are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In an aquatic ecosystem, GFC is the major conduit for energy flow. As against this, in a terrestrial ecosystem, a much larger fraction of energy flows through the detritus food chain than through the GFC.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14462,'chemistry',45,424,844,'The 6th period of the periodic table contains','[{"text": "Two s-block and six p-block elements", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fourteen f-block elements", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ten d-block elements", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the three above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'6 th period contains 32 elements of which 2 are s-block, 6 are p-block, 10 are d-block and 14 are f-block elements.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14463,'biology',98,1187,2846,'The bacterium <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> is widely used in contemporary biology as a','[{"text": "Insecticide", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Indicator of water pollution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Agent for production of diary products", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Source of industrial enzyme", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The bacterium Bacilius thuringiensis or $\\mathrm{Bt}$ is a gram positive bacteria of the genus Bacillus residing in soil. It generates a parasporal insecticidal crystal protein. Thus, Bt is used as an insecticide in contemporary biology.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14465,'biology',99,1326,3209,'Read the following statements and select the correct option<br>I. Producers constitute the first trophic level of a detritus food chain<br>II. Productivity of an aquatic system is less than that of a terrestrial system<br>III. A given species may occupy more than one trophic level in the same ecosystem at the same time','[{"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Producers constitute the first trophic level of a detritus food chain is wrong<br>A simple grazing food chain (GFC) is depicted below:<br>Grass (Producer) ---Goat (Primary Consumer)--- Man (Secondary consumer)',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14466,'chemistry',45,426,852,'The quantum numbers of the last electron in an element are l = 3, m = -2 and s = +1/ 2. In which block of the periodic table this element is present ?','[{"text": "s-Block", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "p-Block", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "d-Block", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "f-Block", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Since the last electron enters f-orbital (l = 3), therefore the element must belong to f-block.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14468,'biology',99,1326,3209,'The given pyramid shows the relative biomass of zooplanktons and phytoplankton in a marine ecosystem. The biomass of the zooplantktons is higher than that of the phytoplantktons because____','[{"text": "The zooplanktons have a shorter life cycle than the phytoplanktons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The zooplanktons have more energy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The phytoplanktons have extermely high turnover rate of energy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The phytoplanktons are individually much smaller that the zooplanktons", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The phytoplanktons are individually much smaller that the zooplanktons',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/99_14468_question_1.jpg'),
(14470,'biology',98,1187,2846,'What is true about $B t$ toxin?','[{"text": "The activated toxin enters the ovaries of the pest, sterilize it and thus, prevent its multiplication", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The concerned bacillus has antitoxins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The inactive protoxin gets converted into active form in the insect gut", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bt protein exists as active toxin in the Bacillus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cry gene of Bacillus thuringiensis produces $B t$ proteins which form crystalline inclusion in bacteria spores. $B t$ toxin protein exist as inactive protoxins but once an insect ingest the inactive toxin, it is converted into an active form of toxin due to the alkaline $\\mathrm{pH}$ of the gut which solubilise the crystals. Activated toxin binds to the surface of midgut epithelial cells and creates pores that cause cell swelling and lysis and cause death of the insect',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14471,'chemistry',45,426,852,'Identify the correct statement','[{"text": "Filling of 5d orbital begins with Hf in ${{\\\\rm{5}}^{{\\\\rm{th}}}}$ period.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Filling of 4f orbital begins with Ce in ${{\\\\rm{6}}^{{\\\\rm{th}}}}$ period.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Filling of 5d orbital begins with La in ${{\\\\rm{5}}^{{\\\\rm{th}}}}$ period.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Filling of 4f orbital begins with La in ${{\\\\rm{6}}^{{\\\\rm{th}}}}$ period.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,NULL,NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14472,'biology',99,1326,3209,'$1 \\mathrm{~S}$ : pyramid of biomass is more accurate than pyramid of numbers<br>$2 \\mathrm{~S}$ : pyramid of energy gives the best picture of over all view of ecosystem','[{"text": "Both 1 S & 2 S are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 S is correct, 2 S incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 S & 2 S are wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 S incorrect, 2 S correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both the statements are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
