(14475,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Some of the characteristics of Bt cotton are','[{"text": "High yield and resistance to bollworms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "High yield and production of toxic protein crystals which kill dipteran pests", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Long fibre and resistance to beetle pests", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Long fibre and resistance to aphids", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bt toxin genes were segregated from Bacillus thuringiensis and were included in cotton plant for forming genetically modified crop called Bt cotton. Bt cotton has high yield and $\\mathrm{Bt}$ toxins in it gives resistance against certain pest like Bollworm, corn borer.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14476,'biology',99,1326,3209,'Which of the following statements regarding ecological pyramid is true?','[{"text": "Ecological pyramids demonstrate a loss in energy at each step of the trophic level", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ecological pyramids show that carnivore are more than herbivores.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecological pyramid depict the total biomass of an ecosystem minus total energy used in respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More than one option is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Transfer of energy from one trophic level to another trophic level follows the 10 percent law which says that $10 \\%$ of energy is transferred to each trophic level from the lower trophic level.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14477,'chemistry',45,423,843,'Identify the correct symbolic notation for the given name of the elements','[{"text": "Ununbium - Uuu", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unbinilium - Ubn", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "nunpentium - Uuh", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ununhexium - Unh", "isCorrect": false}]',1,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14478,'biology',98,1191,2852,'An improved variety of transgenic basmati rice','[{"text": "Gives high yield and is rich in vitamin A", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Is completely resistant to all insect pests and diseases of paddy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Does not require chemical fertilizers and growth hormones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gives high yield but has no characteristic aroma", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Transgenic basmati rice contains $\\beta$-carotene. It is precursor of Vitamin A and also gives high yield.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14480,'biology',99,1326,3209,'The pyramid of biomass in marine ecosystem is generally inverted because','[{"text": "Primary productivity of marine ecosystems is lesser than that of terrestrial ecosystems", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The size of individual organisms decreases from lower trophic levels to higher trophic levels", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Compared to primary consumers, phytoplankton synthesize less biomass per unit time per unit area", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The standing crop of phytoplankton at any given moment is lower than that of primary consumers", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Phytoplankton have shorter lifespan and they multiply much faster. Zooplankton have longer lifespan. A single generation of zooplankton consume several generations of phytoplankton. Hence at any given moment, the standing crop of zooplankton is higher than that of phytoplankton (Standing crop is the mass of biomass at a particular time in a trophic level).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14481,'biology',98,1190,2851,'Genetic engineering has been successfully used for producing<br>','[{"text": "Animals like bulb for farm work as they have super power", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transgenic mice for testing safety of polio vaccine before use in humans", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Transgenic models for studying new treatments for certain cardiac diseases.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transgenic cow- Rosie, which produces high fat milk for making ghee.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Transgenic models are used as a model for human diseases like cancer etc. so that investigation of new treatment are made. Transgenic mice are being developed for use in testing the safety of vaccines before they are used on humans.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14484,'biology',99,1324,3207,'The process of mineralisation by micro organisms helps in the release of:','[{"text": "Inorganic nutrients from humus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both organic and inorganic nutrients from detritus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Organic nutrients from humus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inorganic nutrients from detritus and formation of humus.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mineralisation by organisms helps in formation of inorganic nutrients from Humus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14486,'chemistry',45,430,857,'In the isoelectronic species the ionic radii $\\left( {\\mathop {\\rm{A}}\\limits^{\\rm{^\\circ }} } \\right)\\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{N}}^{{\\rm{3 - }}}}{\\rm{,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{O}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}}{\\rm{,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{F}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$ are respectively given by','[{"text": "1.36, 1.71, 1.40", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.36, 1.40, 1.71", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.71, 1.36, 1.40", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.71, 1.40, 1.36", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14487,'biology',98,1187,2846,'<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> forms protein crystals which contain insecticidal protein<br>','[{"text": "Is activated by acid $\\\\mathrm{pH}$ of the foregut of the insect pest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is coded by several genes including the gene cry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Binds with epithelial cells of midgut of the insect pest ultimately killing it", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Does not kill the carrier bacterium which is itself resistant to this toxin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bacillus thuringiensis forms protein crystals which contain insecticidal protein because they have the ability to bind with the midgut epithelium of the insect pest and create pores killing it.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14488,'biology',99,1326,3209,'An inverted pyramid of biomass can be found in which ecosystem?','[{"text": "Forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Marine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Grass land", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tundra", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'An inverted pyramid of biomass can be found in marine ecosystem, because the size of fish is much bigger than phytoplankton.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14490,'chemistry',45,430,857,'Which of the following is the correct order of size of given species?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{H > }}{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}{\\\\rm{ > H}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{H > }}{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}{\\\\rm{ > H > }}{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Anion is larger in size than its neutral atom. Cation is smaller in size than its neutral atom.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14491,'biology',98,1188,2847,'Silencing of mRNA has been used in producing transgenic plant resistant to','[{"text": "Bollworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nematode", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bacterial blight", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "White rusts", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A Nematode called Meloidogyne incognita infects root of tobacco plants and causes reduction in yield. RNA interference is a method involves silencing of a specific mRNA. Using Agrobacterium vectors nematode specific genes were introduced into host plant. These two RNA\'s being complementary to each other formed double stranded (dsRNA) that initiated RNAi and this silenced specific mRNA of the nematode. Parasite could not survive in transgenic host expressing specific interfering RNA. Hence the transgenic plant gets protected from the parasite.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14492,'biology',99,1323,3206,'Which of the following ecosystems is most productive in terms of net primary production?','[{"text": "Deserts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tropical rain forests", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oceans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estuaries", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Tropical rain forests have high density of green plant population. Hence, net primary production is high.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14495,'biology',98,1190,2851,'Read the following four statement (I-IV) and identify the certain mistakes in two of them<br>I. The first transgenic buffalo, Rosie produced milk which was human alphalact- albumin enriched<br>II. Restriction enzymes are used in isolation of DNA from other macromolecules<br>III. Downstream processing is one of the steps of R-DNA technology<br>IV. Disarmed pathogen vectors are also used in transfer of R-DNA into the host','[{"text": "Statements I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statements I and II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement III and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In statement A, it should be the first transgenic cow was named as Rosie. And in Statement B, Restriction endonucleases are used for cutting the DNA at specific points.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14496,'biology',99,1325,3208,'Approximately how much of the solar energy that falls on the leaves of a plant is converted to chemical energy by photosynthesis?','[{"text": "Less than $1 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2-10 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$30 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$50 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plants absorb only $2-10 \\%$ of PAR and only this amount of energy sustains the entire living world.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14498,'chemistry',45,430,856,'In which one of the following sets, elements have nearly same atomic radii ?','[{"text": "Li, Be, B, C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mg, Ca, Sr, Ba", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fe, Co, Ni, Cu", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "O, S, Se, Te", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In 3d-elements particularly from Fe to Cu, the contractive effect of the increased nuclear charge is almost balanced by increase in size due to increasing shielding effect. As a result, elements, Fe, Co, Ni, Cu all have nearly the same atomic radii.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
