(14502,'biology',98,1189,2848,'The first human hormone produced by recombinant DNA technology is','[{"text": "Estrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insulin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Progesterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroxin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In 1983, Eli lilly an American company prepared two DNA sequences corresponding to $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{B}$, chains of human insulin and introduced them in plasmids of E.coli to produce insulin chains. Chains A and B were produced separately, extracted and combined by creating disulphide bonds to form human insulin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
