(14518,'biology',98,1189,2848,'The two polypeptides of human insulin are linked together by','[{"text": "Phosphodiester bond", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Covalent bond", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Disulphide bridges", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hydrogen bridges", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Human insulin consists of two short polypeptides chains linked together by disulphide bridges.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14519,'chemistry',15,187,410,'The mass of potassium dichromate crystals required to oxidise ${\\rm{750}}\\,{\\rm{c}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.6}}\\,{\\rm{M}}$ Mohr’s salt solution is (molar mass = 392 )','[{"text": "0.49 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.45 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "22.05 g", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2.2 g", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mohr’s salt is ${\\rm{FeS}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}} \\cdot {\\left( {{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}} \\right)_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}} \\cdot {\\rm{6}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$ Only oxidisable part ${\\rm{F}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}$ is<br>$\\left[ {{\\rm{F}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}} \\to {\\rm{F}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{3 + }}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}} \\right]{\\rm{ \\times 6}}$<br>${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{r}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{7}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}{\\rm{ + 14}}{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{ + 6}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}} \\to {\\rm{2C}}{{\\rm{r}}^{{\\rm{3 + }}}}{\\rm{ + 7}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$<br>${\\rm{6F}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}{\\rm{ + C}}{{\\rm{r}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{7}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}{\\rm{ + 14}}{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ + }}} \\to {\\rm{6F}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{3 + }}}}{\\rm{ + 2C}}{{\\rm{r}}^{{\\rm{3 + }}}}{\\rm{ + 7}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$<br>${\\rm{Millimoles}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{F}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}{\\rm{ = 750 \\times 0}}{\\rm{.06 = 450}}$<br>${\\rm{F}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{450}}}}{{{\\rm{1000}}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.450}}\\,{\\rm{mol}}$<br>${\\rm{6}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mol}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{F}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mol}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{r}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{7}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}$<br>$\\therefore {\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.450}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mol}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{F}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.450}}}}{{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.075}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mol}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{r}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{7}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.075 \\times 294}}\\,{\\rm{g = 22}}{\\rm{.05}}\\,{\\rm{g}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14520,'biology',99,1329,3212,'Which of the following is an ecosystem service provided by a natural ecosystem?','[{"text": "Cycling of nutrients", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prevention of soil erosion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollutant absorption and reduction of the threat of global warming", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The products of ecosystem processes are named as ecosystem services, for example, healthy forest ecosystems purify air and water, mitigate droughts and floods, cycle nutrients, generate fertile soils, provide wildlife habitat, maintain biodiversity, pollinate crops, provide storage site for carbon and also provide aesthetic, cultural and spiritual values.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14521,'chemistry',45,430,857,'Consider the ions ${{\\rm{K}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{,}}\\,{{\\rm{S}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}}{\\rm{,}}\\,{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}^{\\rm{ - }}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{a}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}$. The radii of these ionic species follow the order','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{a}}^{{\\\\rm{2 + }}}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{K}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}{\\\\rm{ > C}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{S}}^{{\\\\rm{2 - }}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{S}}^{{\\\\rm{2 - }}}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{K}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}{\\\\rm{ > C}}{{\\\\rm{a}}^{{\\\\rm{2 + }}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{a}}^{{\\\\rm{2 + }}}}{\\\\rm{ > C}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{K}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{S}}^{{\\\\rm{2 - }}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}^{{\\\\rm{2 - }}}}{\\\\rm{ > C}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{K}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}{\\\\rm{ > C}}{{\\\\rm{a}}^{{\\\\rm{2 + }}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In case of isoelectronic species, radius is inversely proportional to the atomic number.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14522,'biology',98,1191,2852,'A \'new\' variety of rice was patented by a foreign company, though such varieties have been present in India for a long time. This is related to','[{"text": "Lerma Rojo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sharbati Sonora", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Co-667", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Basmati<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'RiceTec an American company got patent rights on Basmati rice through the US patent and trademark. But Basmati was actually a Indian Variety. The patent was originally accepted by the US Patent Office in 1997. Indian basmati was crossed with semidwarf varieties and claimed as an invention or a novelty. Sharbati Sonora and Lerma Rojo are varieties of wheat.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
