(14523,'chemistry',15,187,410,'The molarity of a solution obtained by mixing 750 mL of 0.5 M HCl with 250 mL of 2M HCl will be','[{"text": "0.875 M", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1.00 M", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.75 M", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.0975 M", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The molarity of a resulting solution is given by ${\\rm{M = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{M}}_{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{V}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{M}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{V}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{{{{\\rm{V}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{V}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{750 \\times 0}}{\\rm{.5 + 250 \\times 2}}}}{{{\\rm{750 + 250}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{875}}}}{{{\\rm{1000}}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.875M}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14524,'biology',99,1323,3206,'Productivity is the rate of production of biomass expressed in terms of:<br>i. ${\\rm{(kcal}}\\,{{\\rm{m}}^{{\\rm{ - 3}}}}{\\rm{)y}}{{\\rm{r}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$<br>ii. ${{\\rm{g}}^{{\\rm{ - 2}}}}\\,{\\rm{y}}{{\\rm{r}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$<br>iii. ${{\\rm{g}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}\\,{\\rm{y}}{{\\rm{r}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$<br>iv. ${\\rm{(kcal}}\\,{{\\rm{m}}^{{\\rm{ - 2}}}}{\\rm{)y}}{{\\rm{r}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$','[{"text": "ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The rate of biomass production is called productivity. It is expressed in terms of $\\mathrm{g}^{-2} \\mathrm{yr}^{-1}$ or $\\left( {{\\rm{kcal}}\\,{{\\rm{m}}^{{\\rm{ - 2}}}}} \\right){\\rm{y}}{{\\rm{r}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14525,'chemistry',45,430,858,'Three elements X, Y and Z have atomic numbers 19, 37 and 55 respectively. Then the correct statement is','[{"text": "Their ionisation potential would increase with increasing atomic numbers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Z would have the highest ionisation potential", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Y would have the highest ionisation potential", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Y would have an ionisation potential between those of X and Z", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14526,'biology',98,1191,2852,'Use of bioresources by multinational companies and organisations without authorization from the concerned country and its people is called','[{"text": "Biodegradation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biopiracy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bio-infringement", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bioexploitation<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Biopiracy is the use of bioresources by multinational companies and other organisations without proper authorization from countries and people concerned without compensatory payment.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14527,'chemistry',15,187,410,'The density of a solution prepared by dissolving 120g of urea (mol. mass = 60u ) in 1000g of water is 1.15 g/mL. The molarity of this solution is','[{"text": "0.50 M", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.78 M", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.02 M", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2.05 M", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Total mass of solution = 1000 g water + 120 g urea = 1120 g<br>Thus, volume of solution<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{mass}}}}{{{\\rm{density}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1120}}\\,\\,{\\rm{g}}}}{{{\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.15}}\\,\\,{\\rm{g/mL}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 973}}{\\rm{.91}}\\,\\,{\\rm{mL = 0}}{\\rm{.974}}\\,\\,{\\rm{L}}$<br>${\\rm{Moles}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{solute = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{120}}}}{{{\\rm{60}}}}{\\rm{ = 2mol}}$<br>${\\rm{Molarity = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{moles}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{solute}}}}{{{\\rm{volume(L)of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{solution}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{2}}\\,\\,{\\rm{mol}}}}{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.974}}\\,\\,{\\rm{L}}}}{\\rm{ = 2}}{\\rm{.05}}\\,\\,{\\rm{mol}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14528,'biology',99,1325,3208,'Which of the following is not a producer?','[{"text": "$Spirogyra$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$Agaricus$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$Volvox$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$Nostoc$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$Agaricus$ belongs to fungi hence it is not a producer. It is a saprophyte.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14529,'chemistry',45,430,858,'The incorrect statement among the following is','[{"text": "The first ionisation potential of Al is less than the first ionisation potential of Mg.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The second ionisation potential of Mg is greater than the second ionisation potential of Na.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The first ionisation potential of Na is less than the first ionisation potential of Mg.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The third ionisation potential of Mg is greater than third ionisation potential of Al.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$_{{\\rm{11}}}{\\rm{Na:1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}\\,{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{1}}}$<br>$_{{\\rm{12}}}{\\rm{Mg = 1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}\\,{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{:1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}$<br>$_{{\\rm{13}}}{\\rm{Al = 1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}\\,{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{1}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14530,'biology',98,1191,2852,'In India, the organisation responsible for assessing the safety of introducing genetically modified organisms for public use is<br>','[{"text": "Research Committee on Genetic Manipulation (RCGM)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Council for Scientific and Industrial Research (CSIR)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic Engineering Appraisal Committee (GEAC)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Indian Government has set up organisations such as GEAC (Genetic Engineering Approval Committee), which will make decisions regarding the validity of GM research and the safety of introducing Genetically modified organisms for public services',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14651,'biology',99,1325,3208,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Recycling of materials is must for maintenance of biosphere.<br></div><div class="column-right">Energy flows bidirectionally in a food chain</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Energy flows unidirectionally.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14531,'chemistry',15,185,404,'A gaseous hydrocarbon gives upon combustion, 0.72 g of water and 3.08 g of ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ the empirical formula of the hydrocarbon is','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{6}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{7}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{8}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\rm{18g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$ contains 2g H<br>$\\therefore {\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.72g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$ contains 0.08 g H<br>${\\rm{44g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ contains 12g C<br>$\\therefore {\\rm{3}}{\\rm{.08g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ contains 0.84 g C .<br>$\\therefore {\\rm{C:H = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.84}}}}{{{\\rm{12}}}}{\\rm{:}}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.08}}}}{{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.07:0}}{\\rm{.08 = 7:8}}$<br>$\\therefore $ Empirical formula ${\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{7}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{8}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14532,'biology',99,1326,3209,'Pyramid of numbers is:','[{"text": "Always upright", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Always inverted", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Either upright or inverted", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neither upright nor inverted.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pyramid of Number is either upright or inverted When small number of herbivores feeding on large number of plants give an upright pyramid. Large number of insects taking food from a treat gives an inverted pyramids.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14533,'chemistry',45,428,854,'The order of penetrating effect of electrons of s, p, d and f orbitals of a given shell of an atom on its outer shell electrons is','[{"text": "s > p > d > f", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "f > d > p > s", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "p < d < s > f", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "f > p > s > d", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14534,'biology',98,1189,2848,'Which of the following glucose transporters is insulin-dependent?','[{"text": "GLUT I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GLUT II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GLUT III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GLUT IV<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'GLUT-IV is insulin dependent and is responsible for majority of glucose transport into muscle and adipose cells in anabolic conditions. GLUT-I, GLUT-II and GLUT-III are insulin independent.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14535,'chemistry',15,183,402,'The ratio masses of oxygen and nitrogen in a particular gaseous mixture is 1 : 4. The ratio of number of their molecule is','[{"text": "$1:4$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1:8$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$7:32$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$3:16$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The number of moles is given by<br>${\\rm{n = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{weight}}\\,\\,{\\rm{(W)}}}}{{{\\rm{molecular}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{weight}}\\,\\,{\\rm{(M)}}}}$<br>Thus, ratio of moles of  ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{and}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ is given by<br>$\\frac{{{{\\rm{n}}_{{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}_{{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{\\frac{{{{\\rm{W}}_{{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}{{{{\\rm{M}}_{{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}}}{{\\frac{{{{\\rm{W}}_{{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}{{{{\\rm{M}}_{{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}}}} \\right){\\rm{ = }}\\left( {\\frac{{{{\\rm{W}}_{{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}{{{{\\rm{W}}_{{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}} \\right){\\rm{ = }}\\left( {\\frac{{{{\\rm{M}}_{{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}{{{{\\rm{M}}_{{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}} \\right)$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\left( {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{4}}}} \\right){\\rm{ \\times }}\\left( {\\frac{{{\\rm{28}}}}{{{\\rm{32}}}}} \\right){\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{7}}}{{{\\rm{32}}}}$<br>Hence, ratio of ${{\\rm{n}}_{{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{and}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{n}}_{{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{is}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{7:32}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14536,'biology',99,1324,3207,'Among the following, where do you think the process of decomposition would be the fastest?','[{"text": "Tropical rain forest", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Antarctic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dry arid region", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alpine region", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In tropical rain forest, the warm and moist environment and plenty of sugar in the detritus will be there. Due to this the rate of decomposition is fast.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14538,'biology',98,1187,2846,'What triggers activation of protoxin to active $\\mathrm{Bt}$ toxin of <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> in boll worm?','[{"text": "Body temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Moist surface of midgut", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alkaline $\\\\mathrm{pH}$ of gut", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Acidic $\\\\mathrm{pH}$ of stomach", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bacillus thuringiensis forms protein crystals during a particular phase of their growth. These crystals contain a toxic insecticidal protein. These protein exist as inactive protoxins but once an insect ingest the inactive toxin, it is converted into an active form of toxin due to alkaline $\\mathrm{pH}$ of the gut which solubilize the crystals. The activated toxin binds to the surface of midgut epithelial cells and create pores that cause cell swelling and lysis and eventually cause death of insect.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14556,'biology',99,1322,3205,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">An ecosystem can be visualised as a functional unit of nature<br></div><div class="column-right">Crop fields and an aquarium cannot be considered as manmade ecosystems.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Crop fields and an aquarium may also be considered as man-made ecosystems.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
