(14562,'biology',98,1189,2850,'For effective treatment of the disease, early diagnosis and understanding its pathophysiology is very important. Which of the following molecular diagnostic techniques is very useful for early detection.<br>','[{"text": "Western Blotting Technique", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Southern Blotting Technique", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ELISA Technique", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hybridization Technique", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'ELISA or Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay is based upon antigen-antibody reactions. By detecting the presence of antigens (pathogen proteins) in the patient\'s serum, or by detecting antibodies produced against the pathogen, ELISA may diagnose infections. An early diagnosis opens the door to future care and treatment. It helps people to plan ahead while they are still able to make important decisions on their care and support needs and on financial and legal matters.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14563,'chemistry',15,185,404,'Two elements X (At. wt. = 75) and Y (At. wt. = 16) combine to give a compound having 75.8% of X. The formula of the compound is:','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{XY}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{X}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{Y}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{X}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{Y}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{X}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{Y}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/15_14563_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Formula of the compound is ${{\\rm{X}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{Y}}_{\\rm{3}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14564,'biology',99,1322,3205,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The components of the ecosystem cannot be seen to function as a unit when we consider energy flow.<br></div><div class="column-right">Pond is a small, selfsustainable unit of ecosystem but it cannot be an example that explains complex interactions that exist in an aquatic ecosystem.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The components of the ecosystem are seen to function as a unit when we consider productivity, energy flow, decomposition and nutrient cycling. Pond is fairly a selfsustainable unit and rather simple example that explain even the complex interactions that exist in an aquatic ecosystem.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14565,'chemistry',45,430,858,'Among the following processes, the one that requires largest amount of energy is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{Al}}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right) \\\\to {\\\\rm{A}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ + }}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right) \\\\to {\\\\rm{A}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{2 + }}}}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ + }}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{2 + }}}}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right) \\\\to {\\\\rm{A}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{3 + }}}}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{g}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ + }}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All the above processes require same amount of energy", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ionization energy of ion is directly proportional to the charge on the ion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
