(14575,'chemistry',15,185,404,'0.145 g of hydrocarbon is heated with dry copper (II) oxide and ${\\rm{224}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{c}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}$ of ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ was collected at STP. The empirical formula of the hydrocarbon is','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{{\\\\rm{10}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{8}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Sample of hydrocarbon contains carbon and hydrogen<br>At STP, ${\\rm{22400}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{c}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mole}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = }}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{1}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mole}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C = 12}}$<br>${\\rm{224}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{c}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.01}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mole}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.01}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mole}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C = 00}}{\\rm{.12}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}$<br>${\\rm{Mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C = 0}}{\\rm{.12}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}$<br>${\\rm{Mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{H = 0}}{\\rm{.45 - Mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C = 0}}{\\rm{.12 - 0}}{\\rm{.145 = 0}}{\\rm{.025}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}$<br>Formula of the compound is ${{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{5}}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14567,'chemistry',15,187,412,'3.92 g of ferrous ammonium sulphate crystals are dissolved in 100 mL of water. 20 ml of this solution requires 18 mL of potassium permanganate during titration for complete oxidation. The weight of ${\\rm{KMn}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ present in one litre of the solution of','[{"text": "34.76 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12.38 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.238 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3.476 g", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Eq . wt of ferrous ammonium sulpate = 392<br>$\\therefore $ Normality of salt sol.<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{3}}{\\rm{.92}}}}{{{\\rm{392}}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{100}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 1000 = 0}}{\\rm{.1N}}$<br>20 mL of 0.1 N salt sol. $ \\equiv {\\rm{18}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{ml}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{pf}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{KMn}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{sol}}$<br>$\\therefore $ Normality of ${\\rm{KMn}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ sol ${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{20 \\times 0}}{\\rm{.1}}}}{{{\\rm{18}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{9}}}{\\rm{N}}$<br>Eq. wt. of ${\\rm{KMn}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ = 31}}{\\rm{.6}}$<br>$\\therefore $ Strength of ${\\rm{KMn}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{sol = }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{9}}}{\\rm{ \\times 31}}{\\rm{.6 = 3}}{\\rm{.5g}}{{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$ approx.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14568,'biology',99,1322,3205,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In pond ecosystem, the abiotic component is the water with all the dissolved inorganic and organic substances and the rich soil deposit at the bottom of the pond.</div><div class="column-right">The solar input, the cycle of temperature, day-length and other climatic conditions regulate the rate of function of the entire pond.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct statements.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
