}}}{\\rm{Cr}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}$<br>${\\rm{\\% }}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{yield}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{A}}{{\\rm{g}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{Cr}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{Actual}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{yield}}}}{{{\\rm{Theoretical}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{yield}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 100}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.4}}}}{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.488}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 100 = 82\\% }}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14596,'chemistry',45,430,859,'Among halogens, the correct order of amount of energy released in electron gain (electron gain enthalpy) is','[{"text": "F > Cl > Br > I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "F < Cl < Br < I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "F < Cl > Br > I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "F > Cl < Br < I", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'F experience greater inter electronic repulsion on addition of electron due to smaller size compared to Cl. Hence F electron affinity is less than Cl.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
