(14622,'chemistry',15,187,412,'3 g of activated charcoal was added to 50 mL of acetic acid solution 0.06N in a flask. After an hour it was filtered and the strength of the filtrate was found to be 0.042 N. The amount of acetic acid adsorbed (per gram of charcoal) is:','[{"text": "42 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "54 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "18 mg", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "36 mg", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Let the weight of acetic acid initially be ${{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{1}}}$ in 50 mL of 0.060 N solution.<br>Let the ${\\rm{N = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ \\times 1000}}}}{{{\\rm{M}}{\\rm{.wt}}{\\rm{. \\times 50}}}}$<br>${\\rm{(Normality = 0}}{\\rm{.06N)}}$<br>${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.06 = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ \\times 1000}}}}{{{\\rm{60 \\times 50}}}}$<br>$ \\Rightarrow {{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.06 \\times 60 \\times 50}}}}{{{\\rm{1000}}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.18g = 180}}\\,\\,{\\rm{mg}}$<br>After an hour, the strength of acetic acid = 0.042 N<br>so, let the weight of acetic acid be ${{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\rm{N = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ \\times 1000}}}}{{{\\rm{60 \\times 50}}}}$<br>${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.042 = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ \\times 1000}}}}{{{\\rm{3000}}}}$<br>$ \\Rightarrow {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.126 g = 126 mg}}$<br>So amount of acetic acid adsorbed per 3 g = 180 - 126 mg = 54 mg<br>$\\therefore $  Amount of acetic acid absorbed per<br>${\\rm{g = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{54}}}}{{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ = 18g}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
