(14627,'chemistry',15,182,401,'A mixture of gas "X" (mol. wt. 16) and gas “Y” (mol. wt. 28) in the mole ratio a : b has a mean molecular weight 20. What would be mean molecular weight if the gases are mixed in the ratio b : a under identical conditions (gases are non reacting)?','[{"text": "24", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "20", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "26", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "40", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\frac{{{\\rm{a \\times 16 + b \\times 28}}}}{{{\\rm{a + b}}}}{\\rm{ = 20}}$<br>${\\rm{16a + 28b = 20a + 20b}}$<br>${\\rm{4a = 8b}} \\Rightarrow {\\rm{a = 2b}} \\Rightarrow {\\rm{a/b = 2}}$<br>${\\rm{Now}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\frac{{{\\rm{16b + 28a}}}}{{{\\rm{b + a}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{16 + 28a/b}}}}{{{\\rm{1 + a/b}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{16 + 28 \\times 2}}}}{{{\\rm{1 + 2}}}}{\\rm{ = 24}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
