(14793,'chemistry',15,187,411,'An X molal solution of a compound in benzene has mole fraction of solute = 0.2. The value of X is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{14}}{\\\\rm{.0}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3.2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1.4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}{\\\\rm{.0}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mole fraction of solute, ${{\\rm{X}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.2}}$.<br>Therefore, mole fraction of solvent, ${{\\rm{X}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.8}}$<br>$\\frac{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.2}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{and}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\frac{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.8}}$<br>$\\frac{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.2}}}}{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.8}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{4}}}$<br>Now, if ${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}$ (solvent moles) ${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1000}}}}{{{\\rm{78}}}}{\\rm{ = 12}}{\\rm{.8}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{moles}}$<br>${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{12}}{\\rm{.8}}}}{{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ = 3}}{\\rm{.2}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{moles}}$. Therefore, 3.2 moles of the compound are present in one Kg of solvent benzene and so molality = 3.2 m.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
