(14794,'biology',99,1325,3208,'If 20 J of energy is trapped at producer level, then how much energy will be available to peacock as food in the following chain?<br>Plant $\\rightarrow$ Mice $\\rightarrow$ Snake $\\rightarrow$ Peacock','[{"text": "$0.02 \\\\mathrm{~J}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$0.002 \\\\mathrm{~J}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0.2 \\\\mathrm{~J}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0.0002 \\\\mathrm{~J}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'According to $10 \\%$ law of Lindeman, if a herbivore is eaten by carnivores animal it retains only $10 \\%$ of the energy remaining it utilizes for maintenance of its body etc. Hence if a plant trapped 20J of energy, mice will get $2 \\mathrm{~J}$, snake will have $0.2 \\mathrm{~J}$ and Peacock will get $0.02 \\mathrm{~J}$ of energy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14795,'chemistry',45,430,857,'In which of the following compounds manganese show maximum radius?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{Mn}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{KMn}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{MnO}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{[Mn(CN}}{{\\\\rm{)}}_{\\\\rm{6}}}{\\\\rm{]}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Oxidation number of Mn$ \\propto \\frac{1}{{{\\rm{Radius}}}}$<br>oxidation number of  "Mn" is ${\\rm{Mn}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{,}}\\,{\\rm{KMn}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{,}}\\,{\\rm{MnO}}$, and ${{\\rm{K}}_3}\\left[ {{\\rm{Mn(CN}}{{\\rm{)}}_{\\rm{6}}}} \\right]$ are +4, +7, +2 and +3 respectively.<br>The order of radius is ${\\rm{K}}\\left[ {{\\rm{Mn(CN}}{{\\rm{)}}_{\\rm{6}}}} \\right] &gt; {\\rm{Mn}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}} &gt; {\\rm{KMn}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}$. Hence, the maximum radius is shown by ${\\rm{MnO}}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
