(14856,'biology',99,1326,3209,'Identify the incorrect statement regarding the flow of energy between various components of the food chain','[{"text": "Energy flow is unidirectional", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green plants capture about 10% of the solar energy that falls on leaves", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Each trophic level loses some energy as heat to the environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The amount of energy available at each trophic level is 10% of previous trophic level", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plants capture only 2 to 10 percentage of PAR and this small amount of energy sustains the entire living world.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14857,'chemistry',15,186,405,'1 g alloy Cu and Zn reacted with excess of dil. ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ to give ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ gas which occupies 60 Ml at STP. The percentage of Zn in the alloy is','[{"text": "$17\\\\% $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$34\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$83\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$40\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Only Zn reacts with dil. ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ to give ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ gas.<br>${\\rm{Zn + }}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}} \\to {\\rm{ZnS}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>Let the weight of Zn in the alloy be x g.<br>Eq. of Zn = Eq. of ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>$\\frac{{{\\rm{2x}}}}{{{\\rm{65}}{\\rm{.3}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{60}}}}{{{\\rm{11200}}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\left[ {{\\rm{Eq}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{wt}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Zn = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{65}}{\\rm{.3}}}}{{\\rm{2}}}} \\right]$<br>${\\rm{x = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{60 \\times 65}}{\\rm{.3}}}}{{{\\rm{11200 \\times 2}}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.1749}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}$<br>${\\rm{\\% }}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Zn = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.1749 \\times 100}}}}{{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = 17}}{\\rm{.49\\% }}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14858,'chemistry',46,437,875,'If ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ ion is larger than ${\\rm{M}}{{\\rm{g}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}$ ion, and ${{\\rm{S}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}}$ ion is larger than ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$ ion, which of the following will be less soluble in water?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{NaCl}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{a}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{MgC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{MgS}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'MgS is more covalent, so less soluble',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14859,'chemistry',45,432,864,'The basic character of ${\\rm{MgO,}}\\,{\\rm{SrO,}}\\,{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{\\rm{NiO}}$ increases in the order','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O < SrO < MgO < NiO}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{NiO < MgO < SrO < }}{{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{MgO < NiO < SrO < }}{{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O < MgO < NiO < SrO}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14860,'biology',99,1324,3207,'Identify the correct statements:<br>I. Detrivores perform fragmentation.<br>II. The humus is further degraded by some microbes during mineralization.<br>III. Water soluble inorganic nutrients go down into the soil and get precipitated by a process called leaching.<br>IV. The detritus food chain begins with living organisms.<br>V. Earthworms break down detritus into smaller particles by a process called catabolism.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "I, II, III only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V, I only", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The detritus food chain begins with detritus that is dead organic matter. The saprotrophic bacteria and fungi breakdown detritus into simpler inorganic substances by a process called catabolism.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14861,'chemistry',15,185,404,'Which of the following statements about the molecular formula is correct?','[{"text": "Molecular formula shows the exact number of different types of atoms present in a molecule.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Molecular formula can be obtained from empirical formula if molar mass is known.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Percentage composition of a compound can be calculated from its molecular formula.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A molecular formula shows the actual number of atoms of each element present in single molecule of compound. Molecular formula can be determined from empirical formula by knowing molar mass using the following relation:<br>Molecular formula = n $ \\times $ Empirical formula<br>By knowing the molecular formula, we can calculate the % composition of elements.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
