(14867,'chemistry',45,431,863,'Both lithium and magnesium display several similar properties due to the diagonal relationship; however, the one which is incorrect is :','[{"text": "Both form basic carbonates", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both form soluble bicarbonates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both form nitrides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nitrates of both Li and Mg yield ${\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ on heating", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mg can form basic carbonate like<br>${\\rm{3MgC}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{.Mg}}{\\left( {{\\rm{OH}}} \\right)_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{.3}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}} \\downarrow $<br>While Li can form only carbonate $\\left( {{\\rm{L}}{{\\rm{i}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}} \\right)$ not basic carbonate.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14868,'biology',99,1324,3207,'A detrivorous animal of economic importance is:<br>','[{"text": "Caterpillar larva", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leech", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Earthworm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Giriraja fowl", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The earthworms improve the fertility of soil in different ways and, therefore, they are of utmost importance in agriculture. Actually, the borrowing and soil feeding habits of earthworms make the soil porous which permit both aeration and quick absorption of water. It also permits easy and deep penetration of the plant roots.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
