(14880,'biology',99,1324,3207,'The process of decomposition delays when:<br>','[{"text": "The detritus is made up of sugars and nitrogen compounds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aeration is sufficient", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Warm and moist environment exists", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Detritus is rich in lignin and chitin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The nutrients in organic matter are broken down by a group of processes known as decomposition, which also return carbon dioxide or water to the atmosphere, where it can be reused by autotrophs for photosynthesis.<br>Substances such as amino acids and sugars decompose readily.<br>Cellulose and hemicellulose, which are broken down more slowly.<br>Compounds which are more resistant to decay, like lignin or chitin .<br>Thus, rate of decomposition is slower if detritus is rich in lignin and chitin and faster if detritus is rich in nitrogen and water-soluble substances like sugars.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
