(14909,'chemistry',15,183,402,'How many valence electrons are present in 0.53 g of ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ ?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{40 \\\\times 6}}{\\\\rm{.023 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{23}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.2 \\\\times 6}}{\\\\rm{.023 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{23}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.4 \\\\times 6}}{\\\\rm{.023 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{23}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2 \\\\times 6}}{\\\\rm{.023 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{23}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}$, sodium exists as ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ and carbonate exists as ${\\rm{CO}}_{\\rm{3}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}$. In ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$, number of valence electrons are 8. In ${\\rm{CO}}_{\\rm{3}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}$, number of valence electrons are 24.<br>Total number of valence electrons in ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ = 2}}\\left( {\\rm{8}} \\right){\\rm{ + 24 = 40}}$<br>Hence, 106 g of  ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ contains ${\\rm{40 \\times 6}}{\\rm{.023 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}$ valence electrons.<br>$ \\Rightarrow {\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.53}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{contains}}$<br>${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.53 \\times }}\\frac{{{\\rm{40}}}}{{{\\rm{106}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 6}}{\\rm{.023 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.2 \\times 6}}{\\rm{.023 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}$ valence electrons.<br>Note : Number of valence electrons in Na is 1 but in ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ is 8.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
