(14929,'chemistry',45,430,858,'The first ionisation enthalpies of Na, Mg, Al and Si are in the order:','[{"text": "Na < Mg > Al < Si", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Na > Mg > Al > Si", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Na < Mg < Al < Si", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Na > Mg > Al < Si", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Na, Mg, Al and Si belongs to the same period i.e., 3rd period.<br>I.P. increases as we move along a period from left to right due to decrease in atomic size.<br>Hence, the trend in I.P. should be Si > Al > Mg > Na<br>However, it is seen that Mg has higher ionization potential than Al because of its stable electronic configuration.<br>So, the true order of first I.P. is Na < Mg > Al < Si.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
