(14958,'chemistry',15,183,402,'P and Q are two elements which form ${{\\rm{P}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{Q}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ and ${\\rm{P}}{{\\rm{Q}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ molecules. If 0.15 mole of ${{\\rm{P}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{Q}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ and ${\\rm{P}}{{\\rm{Q}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ weighs 15.9 and 9.3g, respectively, what are atomic mass of P and Q ?','[{"text": "26, 18", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "18, 26", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "26, 26", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "18, 18", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Let at. mass of P and Q be a and b respectively,<br>$\\therefore {\\rm{Mol}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{P}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{Q}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ = 2a + 3b}}$<br>and Mol. mass of<br>$\\therefore {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\left( {{\\rm{2a + 3b}}} \\right){\\rm{ \\times 0}}{\\rm{.15 = 15}}{\\rm{.9}}$<br>${\\rm{and}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\left( {{\\rm{a + 2b}}} \\right){\\rm{ \\times 0}}{\\rm{.15 = 9}}{\\rm{.3}}$<br>${\\rm{a = 26,}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{b = 18}}$<br>Atomic mass of P = 26<br>Atomic mass of Q = 18',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
