(14967,'chemistry',15,180,393,'In an experiment, ${\\rm{5}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{CaC}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ on heating gave ${\\rm{2}}{\\rm{.8}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{CaO}}$ and ${\\rm{2}}{\\rm{.2}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$. The results are in accordance with the','[{"text": "Law of conservation of mass", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Law of constant proportion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of multiple proportion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of reciprocal proportion", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mass of ${\\rm{CaC}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ = Mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{CaO + Mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\rm{5}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g = 2}}{\\rm{.8}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{ + 2}}{\\rm{.2}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g = 5g}}$<br>Hence, given data obey’s law of conservation of mass',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
