(14976,'chemistry',15,180,395,'In compound A, 1.0 g nitrogen combines with 0.57 g oxygen. In compound B, 2.0 g nitrogen unite with 2.24 g oxygen and in compound C, 3.0 g nitrogen combine with 5.11 g oxygen. These results obey the law of:','[{"text": "Multiple proportions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Constant proportions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reciprocal proportions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Given that,<br>Compound A, 1 g of Nitrogen combine with 0.57 of Oxygen<br>Compound B, 2 g of Nitrogen combine with 2.24 g of Oxygen<br>1 g of Nitrogen combine with ${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1 \\times 2}}{\\rm{.24}}}}{{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.12g}}$ of Oxygen<br>Compound C, 3 g of Nitrogen combine with 5.11 g of Oxygen<br>1 g of Nitrogen combine with ${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1 \\times 5}}{\\rm{.11}}}}{{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.70g}}$of Oxygen<br>The ratio of Oxygen in A, B, and C = 0.57 : 1.12 : 1.7 = 1 : 2 : 3.<br>Therefore, given results obey law of multiple proportions.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(14977,'chemistry',46,444,890,'The dipole moment of HCl is 1.03 D, if H - Cl bond distance is ${\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.26}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{A^\\circ }}$, what is the percentage of ionic character in the H - Cl bond ?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{60\\\\% }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{39\\\\% }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{29\\\\% }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{17\\\\% }}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{\\% }}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{ionic}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{character = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{\\mu }}_{{\\rm{exp}}}}}}{{{{\\rm{\\mu }}_{{\\rm{theoretical}}}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 100}}{\\rm{.}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\left[ {\\frac{{{\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.03}}}}{{{\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.26 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 8}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 4}}{\\rm{.8 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 10}}}}}}} \\right]{\\rm{ \\times 100 = 17\\% }}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
