(14982,'chemistry',15,180,395,'Two samples of lead oxide were separately reduced to metallic lead by heating in a current of hydrogen. The weight of lead from one oxide was half the weight of lead obtained from the other oxide. The data illustrates','[{"text": "Law of reciprocal proportions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of constant proportions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of multiple proportions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Law of equivalent proportions", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'This shows that the weights of lead combining with fixed weight of oxygen are in the ratio $\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{:1}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{or}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{1:2}}$ which is in accordance with law of multiple proportions.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
