(14985,'chemistry',15,187,412,'An element forms an oxide in which the oxygen is 20% of the oxide by weight, the equivalent weight of the given element will be','[{"text": "32", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "40", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "60", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "128", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{1}}}$ gm of the metal gave ${{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ gm of its oxide.<br> Hence equivalent weight of the metal is $\\frac{{{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{1}}}}}{{{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ - }}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{1}}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 8}}$<br>According to the given data, equivalent weight of metal is $\\frac{{{\\rm{80}}}}{{{\\rm{100 - 80}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 8 = 32}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
