(14987,'chemistry',45,430,858,'Consider the following ionisation enthalpies of two elements ‘A’ and ‘B’.<br>(A) Element 1st - 899 &emsp; &emsp; Ionisation 2nd - 1757 &emsp; &emsp; enthalpy(kJ/mol) 3rd - 14847<br>(B) Element 1st - 737 &emsp; &emsp; Ionisation 2nd - 1450 &emsp; &emsp; enthalpy(kJ/mol) 3rd - 7731<br>Which of the following statements is correct?','[{"text": "Both ‘A’ and ‘B’ belong to group-1 where ‘B’ comes below ‘A’.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both ‘A’ and ‘B’ belong to group -1 where ‘A’ comes below ‘B’.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both ‘A’ and ‘B’ belong to group -2 where ‘B’ below ‘A’.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both ‘A’ and ‘B’ belong to group -2 where ‘A’ comes below ‘B’.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Generally, the ionisation enthalpies or energy increases from left to right in a period and decreases from top to bottom in a group. Several factors such as atomic radius, nuclear charge, shielding effect are responsible for change of ionisation enthalpies.<br>Here,1st ionisation enthalpy of A and B is greater than group I $\\left( {{\\rm{Li}}\\,\\,{\\rm{520}}\\,\\,{\\rm{kJ}}\\,\\,{\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{to}}\\,\\,{\\rm{Cs}}\\,\\,{\\rm{374}}\\,\\,{\\rm{kJ}}\\,\\,{\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}} \\right){\\rm{,}}$ which means element A and B belong to group-2 and all three given ionisation enthalpy values are less for element B means B will come below A.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
