(14999,'chemistry',15,177,387,'Which of the following is not a compound?','[{"text": "Marble", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ozone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Carborundum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Quicklime", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ozone ${\\rm{(}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{)}}$ consists of only one kind of atom oxygen. The structure formed by only one type of atom is called a molecule not compound.<br>A compound is a combination of more than one element.<br>Marble, ${\\rm{CaC}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ is made by the combination of calcium, carbon and oxygen.<br> Carborundum, ${\\rm{SiC}}$ is a compound and quicklime, ${\\rm{CaO}}$ is also compound.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15000,'chemistry',46,449,905,'Which of the following order of energies of molecular orbitals of ${{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ is correct?','[{"text": "$\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{\\\\pi 2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{y}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ < }}\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{\\\\sigma 2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{z}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ < }}\\\\left( {{{\\\\rm{\\\\pi }}^{\\\\rm{*}}}{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{x}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ = }}\\\\left( {{{\\\\rm{\\\\pi }}^{\\\\rm{*}}}{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{y}}}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{\\\\pi 2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{y}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ > }}\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{\\\\sigma 2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{z}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ > }}\\\\left( {{{\\\\rm{\\\\pi }}^{\\\\rm{*}}}{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{x}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ = }}\\\\left( {{{\\\\rm{\\\\pi }}^{\\\\rm{*}}}{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{y}}}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{\\\\pi 2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{y}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ < }}\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{\\\\sigma 2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{z}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ > }}\\\\left( {{{\\\\rm{\\\\pi }}^{\\\\rm{*}}}{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{x}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ = }}\\\\left( {{{\\\\rm{\\\\pi }}^{\\\\rm{*}}}{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{y}}}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{\\\\pi 2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{y}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ > }}\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{\\\\sigma 2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{z}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ < }}\\\\left( {{{\\\\rm{\\\\pi }}^{\\\\rm{*}}}{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{x}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ = }}\\\\left( {{{\\\\rm{\\\\pi }}^{\\\\rm{*}}}{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{y}}}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15001,'chemistry',45,425,850,'Consider the following statements:<br>I. s-block elements are found pure in nature<br>II. d-block elements form coloured ions exhibit variable valence and paramagnetism<br>III. Lanthanoids contains the elements from Ce(Z = 58) to Lu (Z = 71)<br>IV. Actinoids contains the elements from Th(Z = 90) to Lr(Z = 103)<br>Choose the option with all the correct statements:','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III and IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statements II, III and IV are correct, while the statement I is incorrect.<br>It’s correct form is as follows:<br>s-block elements are never found in pure nature because of their high reactivity. So, the option (4) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15003,'chemistry',46,449,905,'In which pair, the stronger bond found in the first species<br>(I) ${\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ - }}{\\rm{,}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>(II) ${{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{.N}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ + }}$<br>(III) ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{O}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{,N}}{{\\rm{O}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$','[{"text": "(I) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(II) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I) and (III) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(II) and (III) only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'B.O. is directly proportional to the strength of the bond.<br>(I) B.O. of ${\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ - }}$ is 1.5 and ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ is 2<br>(II) B.O. of ${{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ is 3 and ${\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ + }}$ is 2.5<br>(III) B.O. of ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{O}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ is 3 and ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{O}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$ is 2.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15005,'chemistry',45,432,867,'Consider the following statement:<br>I. Metals comprise more than 78% of all known elements and appear on the left side of the periodic table.<br>II. Most non-metallic solids are brittle and are neither malleable nor ductile.<br>III. The elements become more metallic as we go down a group.<br>IV. The non-metallic character decreases as one goes from left to right across the periodic table.<br>Choose the option with all correct statements:','[{"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statements I, II and III are correct, while the statement IV is incorrect.<br>It’s correct form is as follows:<br>The non-metallic character increases as one goes from left to right across the periodic table. So, the option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15007,'chemistry',46,449,905,'The bond length of ${\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ + }}{\\rm{,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ - }}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ are in the order','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{ > H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{ > H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}{\\\\rm{ > H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{ > H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}{\\\\rm{ > H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'B.O. of ${\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ + }}$ is 0.5, ${\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ - }}$ is 0.5 and B.O. of ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ is 1.<br>${\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ + }}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ - }}$ have same bond order. However in ${\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ - }}$, the ${{\\rm{3}}^{{\\rm{rd}}}}$ electron is entering an ABMO, making it less stable than the former. So, Greater the B.O., shorter the bond and species is more stable.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15009,'chemistry',45,430,861,'Consider the following statements<br>I. The radius of an anion is larger than that of the parent atom.<br>II. The ionization energy generally increases with increasing atomic number in a period.<br>III. The electronegativity of elements increases on moving down across a group.<br>Which of the above statements is/are correct?','[{"text": "I alone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II alone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement I, II are correct, while statement III is incorrect. It’s correct form is the E.N. of elements decreases on moving down in a group.<br>So, the option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15011,'chemistry',46,449,905,'Which of the following statement is correct about ${{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ molecule?','[{"text": "It has a bond order of 3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The number of unpaired electrons present in it is zero and hence it is diamagnetic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The order of filling of MOs is ${\\\\rm{\\\\pi }}\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{x}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ = \\\\pi }}\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{y}}}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{,\\\\sigma }}\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{p}}_{\\\\rm{z}}}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15013,'chemistry',45,430,861,'Consider the following statements<br>I. The radius of an cation is larger than that of the parent atom.<br>II. The ionization energy generally increases with increasing atomic number in a group.<br>III. The electronegativity of an element is the tendency of an isolated atom to attract an electron.<br>Which of the above statements is/are correct?','[{"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement III is only correct. The correct statements are as follows:<br>I. The radius of an cation is smaller than that of parent atom<br>II. The ionization energy generally decreases in a group. So, the option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
