(15045,'chemistry',45,430,858,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Second ionization enthalpy will be higher than the first ionization enthalpy.</div><div class="column-right">Ionization enthalpy is a quantitative measure of the tendency of an element to lose electron.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but statement B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but statement B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'It is difficult to remove an electron frrom a positively charged ion than a neutral atom due to which ${\\rm{I}}{{\\rm{E}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ > I}}{{\\rm{E}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{.}}$ So, the option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15046,'chemistry',15,187,409,'Three statements are given about mole fraction<br>i) Mole fraction of a solute + mole fraction of solvent = 1<br>ii) Equal weights of Helium and methane are present in a gaseous mixture. The mole fraction of He is $\\frac{{\\rm{4}}}{{\\rm{5}}}$<br>iii) The mole fraction of 40% by mass of NaOH solution is 0.5','[{"text": "i and ii are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii and iii are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iii are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "all are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'(i) Sum of the mole fraction of all the components in solution is 1.<br>(ii) Let us assume weight of He and ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}$  as 1 g each.<br>Mole fraction of ${\\rm{He = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{n}}_{{\\rm{He}}}}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}_{{\\rm{He}}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{n}}_{{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{4}}}}}{{\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ + }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{16}}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{4}}}{{\\rm{5}}}$<br>(iii) 40% by mass of NaOH means 40 g of NaOH present in 100 g of solution or 60 g of water.<br>Mole fraction of NaOH<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{n}}_{{\\rm{NaOH}}}}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}_{{\\rm{NaOH}}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{n}}_{{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\left( {\\frac{{{\\rm{40}}}}{{{\\rm{40}}}}} \\right)}}{{\\left( {\\frac{{{\\rm{40}}}}{{{\\rm{40}}}}} \\right){\\rm{ + }}\\left( {\\frac{{{\\rm{60}}}}{{{\\rm{18}}}}} \\right)}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.23}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15047,'chemistry',45,430,856,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Covalent radius of an element is always lesser than its van der Waal’s radius.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Covalent radius is one half the distance between the nuclei of two covalently bonded atoms of the same element in a molecule whereas van der Waal’s radius is one half the distance between the nuclei of two non-bonded isolated atoms.','[{"text": "If both Assertion & Reason are true and the reason is the correct explanation of the assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "If both Assertion & Reason are true but the reason is not the correct explanation of the assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "If Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "If Assertion is false but Reason is true.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion & Reason are true but reason is the correct explanation of the assertion.<br>So the option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15050,'chemistry',15,187,412,'The weight of ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{.2}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$ required to prepare 500 mL of 0.2N solution is','[{"text": "1.26g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6.3g", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1.575g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3.15g", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${{\\rm{W}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{N \\times E}}{{\\rm{W}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ \\times V(mL)}}}}{{{\\rm{1000}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.2 \\times 63 \\times 500}}}}{{{\\rm{1000}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 6}}{\\rm{.3}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
