(15058,'chemistry',15,187,410,'Two binary solutions have the same molarity.<br>Which of the following statements is true?','[{"text": "Equal volumes of the two solutions contain equal number of solute molecules.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Equal weights of the two solutions contain equal number of solute molecules.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The two solutions must have the same molality", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The two solutions must have the same mole fraction.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{Molarity = }}\\frac{{\\rm{w}}}{{{\\rm{MW \\times V}}}}$<br>For two solutions having molarity,<br>$\\frac{{{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{1}}}}}{{{\\rm{M}}{{\\rm{W}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}{{\\rm{V}}_{\\rm{1}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{{{\\rm{M}}{{\\rm{W}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}{{\\rm{V}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}$<br>${\\rm{If}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{V}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{V}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{,}}\\frac{{{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{1}}}}}{{{\\rm{M}}{{\\rm{W}}_{\\rm{1}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{{{\\rm{M}}{{\\rm{W}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}$<br>Thus, solutions contain equal number of moles of solute and hence equal number of molecules.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
