(15236,'chemistry',15,187,412,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Equvivalent weight of base ${\\text{ =  }}\\frac{{{\\text{molecular}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{weight}}}}{{{\\text{acidity}}}}$<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Acidity is the number of replaceable hydrogen atom in one molecule of the base','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Equivalent weight of a base is calculated by dividing its molecular mass with its acidity. Acidity is defined as the number of replaceable hydroxyl group in one molecule of the base.<br>Hence, Assertion  is correct but Reason  is incorrect.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2008,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
