(15244,'chemistry',45,430,857,'In the ions ${{\\rm{P}}^{{\\rm{3 - }}}}{\\rm{,}}{{\\rm{S}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}}$ and ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$, the increasing order of size is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\\\rm{,}}{{\\\\rm{S}}^{{\\\\rm{2 - }}}}{\\\\rm{,}}{{\\\\rm{P}}^{{\\\\rm{3 - }}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{P}}^{{\\\\rm{3 - }}}}{\\\\rm{,}}{{\\\\rm{S}}^{{\\\\rm{2 - }}}}{\\\\rm{,C}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}^{{\\\\rm{2 - }}}}{\\\\rm{,C}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}{\\\\rm{,}}{{\\\\rm{P}}^{{\\\\rm{3 - }}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}^{{\\\\rm{2 - }}}}{\\\\rm{,}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{{\\\\rm{3 - }}}}{\\\\rm{,C}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15245,'chemistry',15,183,402,'$\\mathrm{10^{21}}$ molecules are removed from $\\mathrm{200 \\mathrm{mg}}$ of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CO}_{2}}$. The moles of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CO}_{2}}$ left are','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{2.88 \\\\times 10^{-3}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{28.8 \\\\times 10^{-3}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{288 \\\\times 10^{-3}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{28.8 \\\\times 10^{3}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'1 mole of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CO}_{2}}$ molecule<br>$\\mathrm{=6.023 \\times 10^{23}}$ molecules of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CO}_{2}}$<br>$\\mathrm{=44 \\mathrm{~g}}$ of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CO}_{2}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\therefore 10^{21}}$ molecules of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CO}_{2}}$<br>$\\mathrm{=\\dfrac{44}{6.023 \\times 10^{23}} \\times 10^{21} \\mathrm{gCO}_{2}}$<br>$\\mathrm{=7.31 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~g}=73.1 \\mathrm{mg}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\therefore \\mathrm{CO}_{2}}$ left $\\mathrm{=200-73.1=126.9 \\mathrm{mg}}$<br>$\\mathrm{=126.9 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~g}}$<br>Hence, moles of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CO}_{2}}$ left $\\mathrm{=\\dfrac{\\text { given mass }}{\\text { molar mass }}}$<br>$\\mathrm{=\\dfrac{126.9 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~g}}{44 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{mol}}}$<br>$\\mathrm{=2.88 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~mol}}$<br>',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15246,'chemistry',46,446,892,'The orientation of electron pairs and the shape of molecule is different in','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{BeC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{BC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{CC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Due to the presence of two lone pairs.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15293,'chemistry',46,444,890,'Among the following, the molecule with highest dipole moment is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{Cl}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{CHC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{CC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15248,'chemistry',45,430,857,'Which of the following orders of ionic radii is correctly represented?','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}{\\\\rm{ > H > }}{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{a}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{F}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{O}}^{{\\\\rm{2 - }}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{F}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{O}}^{{\\\\rm{2 - }}}}{\\\\rm{ > N}}{{\\\\rm{a}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{3 + }}}}{\\\\rm{ > M}}{{\\\\rm{g}}^{{\\\\rm{2 + }}}}{\\\\rm{ > }}{{\\\\rm{N}}^{{\\\\rm{3 - }}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All the options (b,c and d) are incorrect<br>${\\rm{(1)}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\rm{ > }}{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{ > H}}$<br>It is known that radius of a cation is always smaller than that of a neutral atom due to decrease in the number of orbits. Whereas the radius of anion is always greater than a cation due to decrease in effective nuclear charge. Hence the correct order is<br>${{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\rm{ > }}{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{ > H}}$<br>${\\rm{(2)}}\\,\\,{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{ > }}{{\\rm{F}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\rm{ > }}{{\\rm{O}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}}$<br>The given species are isoelectronic and they are in contact with the same number of electrons. For isoelectronic species,<br>${\\rm{Ionic}}\\,\\,{\\rm{radii}}\\,\\, \\propto \\,\\,\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{atomic}}\\,\\,{\\rm{number}}}}$<br>$\\therefore $ The correct order of ionic radii is<br>${{\\rm{O}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}}{\\rm{ > }}{{\\rm{F}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\rm{ > N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$<br>(3) Similarly, the correct option is<br>${{\\rm{O}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}}{\\rm{ > }}{{\\rm{F}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\rm{ > N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$<br>(4) The correct order is ${{\\rm{N}}^{{\\rm{3 - }}}}{\\rm{ > M}}{{\\rm{g}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}{\\rm{ > A}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{3 + }}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15249,'chemistry',15,187,412,'$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{x}}$ moles of potassium dichromate oxidises 1 mole of ferrous oxalate in acidic medium. Here $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{x}}$ is','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1.0", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The reaction of oxidation of ferrous oxalate by potassium dichromate in acidic medium is written as<br>${\\rm{2Fe}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ + C}}{{\\rm{r}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{7}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}{\\rm{ + 14}}{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ + }}} \\to $<br>${\\rm{2F}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{3 + }}}}{\\rm{ + 2C}}{{\\rm{r}}^{{\\rm{3 + }}}}{\\rm{ + 4C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ + 7}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\because 2}$ moles of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{FeC}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{4}}$ are oxidised by $\\mathrm{=1}$<br>mole of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}^{2-}}$.<br>$\\mathrm{\\therefore 1}$ mole of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{FeC}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{4}}$ will be oxidised by<br>$\\mathrm{=\\dfrac{1}{2}=0.5}$ mole of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}^{2-}}$<br>',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
