(15276,'chemistry',45,430,861,'Which of the following is incorrect statement?','[{"text": "The first ionisation potential of Al is less than the first ionisation potential of Mg", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Radius of hydrated ${\\\\rm{L}}{{\\\\rm{i}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}$ is more than that of hydrated ${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The formation of ${{\\\\rm{S}}^{{\\\\rm{2 - }}}}$ is an endothermic process", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{Mg}}\\,{\\rm{ = }}\\,{\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{,2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{,2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{,3}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{;}}\\,{\\rm{Al}}\\,{\\rm{ = }}\\,{\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{,2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{,2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{,3}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{1}}}$<br>Because electron is to be removed from stable completely filled s-orbital of Mg as compared to partially filled p-orbital of Al.<br>(2) ${\\rm{L}}{{\\rm{i}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$  due to small in size attracts more number of water molecules and thus have bigger hydrated ion.<br>(3) Addition of 2nd ${{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$ to an anion (same\ncharge) is difficult due to the electrostatic repulsion.<br>All statements are true.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
