(15284,'chemistry',45,430,859,'The electron gain enthalpies of halogens are as follows:<br>F = –332, Cl = – 349, Br = –324,<br>${\\rm{I =  - 295}}\\,{\\rm{kJ}}\\,{\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$<br>The less negative value for F as compared to that of Cl is due to','[{"text": "strong electron-electron repulsions in the compact 2-p subshell of F.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "weak electron-electron repulsions in the bigger 3-p sub shell of Cl", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "smaller electronegativity value of F than Cl", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Due to small size of F atom, the electron_x0002_electron repulsions in compact 2-p subshell are large; hence, the incoming electron is not accepted with the same ease as is the case with Cl (less electron-electron repulsions).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
