(15300,'chemistry',45,432,867,'Which of the following order is correct?','[{"text": "F > N > C > Si > Ga: non-metallic character", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "F > Cl > O > N: oxidising property", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C< Si > P > N: electron affinity value", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'C = –121; Si = –135; P = –60; N = 31.<br>(1) As electronegativity increases, non-metallic  character increases.<br>(2) It is based on their SRP values, which in turns depends on bond energies, hydration energies and electron affinity values.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15301,'chemistry',15,183,402,'How many gram of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}}$ are present in $\\mathrm{0.25 \\mathrm{~mol}}$ of it?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{0.25 \\\\mathrm{~g}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{5.4 \\\\mathrm{~g}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{4.5 \\\\mathrm{~g}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{6.1 \\\\mathrm{~g}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{1 \\mathrm{~mol}}$ of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}=18 \\mathrm{~g}}$ (molar mass)<br>$\\mathrm{\\therefore 0.25 \\mathrm{~mol}}$ of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}=\\dfrac{18 \\times 0.25}{1}=4.5 \\mathrm{~g}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
