(15426,'chemistry',45,430,861,'Which one of the following is an incorrect statement?','[{"text": "The first ionisation potential of nitrogen is greater than that of oxygen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The electron affinity of fluorine is greater than that of chlorine.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The ionization potential of beryllium is greater than that of boron", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The electronegativity of fluorine is greater than that of chlorine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The electron affinity of chlorine is greater than fluorine. The lower E.A. of fluorine is due to small size and more electronic repulsions.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
