(15428,'chemistry',15,177,387,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Element and compound are the examples of pure substances.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Element contains one kind of atoms while a compound contains more than one kind of elements or atoms.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Elements are fundamental pure substances with distinct properties, indivisible by chemical or physical processes, while compounds are also pure substances formed by combining two or more elements in fixed proportions. So, the option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
