(15581,'chemistry',45,430,860,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> For hydrogen like species, energy of an electron in a particular orbit decreases with increase in value of ${\\text{Z}}$.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Electronegativity decreases across a period.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'For hydrogen-like species, the energy of an electron in the nth orbit is determined by the equation:<br>$\\mathrm{E}=\\dfrac{-13.6 \\times \\mathrm{Z}^{2}}{\\mathrm{n}^{2}}$<br>Electronegativity increases across a period. So option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
