(15610,'chemistry',15,183,402,'The highest number of helium atoms is in','[{"text": "4 mol of helium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4 u of helium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4 g of helium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2.271098 L of helium at STP", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'(1) 4 mol of  ${\\rm{He}} = 4 \\times 6.022 \\times {10^{23}}\\,{\\rm{He}}$ atoms<br>(2) ${\\rm{4}}\\,{\\rm{u}}\\,\\,{\\rm{of }}\\,{\\rm{He = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{4u}}}}{{{\\rm{4u}}}}{\\rm{ = 1He}}$ atom<br>(3) <br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n{\\rm{4g}}\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,{\\rm{Helium}} = \\frac{{4\\,{\\rm{g}}}}{{4\\,{\\rm{g}}}}{\\rm{mole}} = 1{\\rm{mole}}\\\\\n = 6.022 \\times {10^{23}}{\\mkern 1mu}\\, {\\rm{He}}\\,{\\rm{atoms}}.\n\\end{array}$<br>(4) 2.2710982 L of He at STP<br>$=\\dfrac{2.271}{22.710982}$ mole<br>$=0.1$ mole (or) $6.022 \\times 10^{22} \\,\\mathrm{He}$ atoms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
