(15645,'chemistry',45,430,857,'The correct increasing order of the ionic radii is','[{"text": "${\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{a}}^{2 + }} < {{\\\\text{K}}^ + } < {\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{l}}^ - } < {{\\\\text{S}}^{2 - }}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\text{K}}^ + } < {{\\\\text{S}}^{2 - }} < {\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{a}}^{2 + }} < {\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{l}}^ - }$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\text{S}}^{2 - }} < {\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{l}}^ - } < {\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{a}}^{2 + }} < {{\\\\text{K}}^ + }$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{l}}^ - } < {\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{a}}^{2 + }} < {{\\\\text{K}}^ + } < {{\\\\text{S}}^{2 - }}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In case of isoelectronic species, as the – ve charge increases radii increases and as the + ve charge increases radii decreases. Hence, the correct order is ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{a}}^{2 + }} < {{\\rm{K}}^ + } < {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}^ - } < {{\\rm{S}}^{2 - }}.$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
