(15653,'chemistry',45,422,842,'It is observed that characteristic X-ray spectra of elements show regularity. When frequency to the power " n " i.e. $\\mathrm{v}^{\\mathrm{n}}$ of X-rays emitted is plotted against atomic number \'Z\', following graph is obtained. The value of " n " is','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1/2$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The relation between the atomic number and frequency for the X -rays is given by Moseley as<br>${\\mathrm{\\sqrt{v}=a(Z-b)}}$<br>(or) ${\\mathrm{\\sqrt{v} \\propto Z}}$<br>So, ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{n}=\\dfrac{1}{2}}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/45_15653_question_1.png'),
