(15704,'chemistry',15,186,405,'446 g of PbO, 46 g of ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ and 16 g of ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>are allowed to react according to the equation $\\mathrm{PbO}+2 \\mathrm{NO}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_{3}\\right)_{2}$. The amount of $\\mathrm{Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_{3}\\right)_{2}$ that can be produced is<br>(At. wt. of $\\mathrm{Pb}=207$ )','[{"text": "331 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "662 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "165.5 g", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "132.5 g", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{PbO}+2 \\mathrm{NO}_{2}+\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_{3}\\right)_{2}$$\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{PbO}}=\\dfrac{446}{(207+16)}=\\dfrac{446}{223}=2$<br>$\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{NO}_{2}}=\\dfrac{46}{46}=1$<br>$\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{O}_{2}}=\\dfrac{16}{32}=0.5$<br>1 mole PbO needs 2 mole $\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$<br>$\\therefore 2$ moles PbO needs ?<br>$=\\dfrac{2 \\times 2}{1}=4$ mole $\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$<br>So, PbO is excess<br>2 mole $\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ needs $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ mole $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$<br>1 mole $\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ needs ?<br>$ = \\frac{{2 \\times 2}}{1} = 4\\,\\,{\\rm{mole}}\\,\\,{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>So, PbO is excess<br>2 mole ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ needs $\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,{\\rm{mole}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{O}}_2}$<br>1 mole ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ needs ?<br>$ = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2} = 0.25\\,\\,{\\rm{mole}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{O}}_2}$<br>but given is 0.5 mole $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$, So It is excess.<br>$\\therefore \\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ is limiting reagent.<br>2 mole $\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ forms $=1 \\mathrm{~mole} \\mathrm{~Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_{3}\\right)_{2}$<br>1 mole $\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ forms $=0.5$ mole $\\mathrm{Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_{3}\\right)_{2}$<br>$\\mathrm{wt}_{\\mathrm{PbNO}_{3}}=\\mathrm{n} \\times \\mathrm{MM}$<br>$=0.5 \\times 331=165.5 \\mathrm{~g}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15706,'chemistry',46,444,890,'The dipole moment of HBr is ${\\rm{2}}{\\rm{.6 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 30}}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{C - m}}$ and the interatomic spacing is ${\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.41}}\\,\\,\\mathop {\\rm{A}}\\limits^{\\rm{^\\circ }} $. The percentage of ionic character in HBr is','[{"text": "10.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "11.5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "12.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "13.5", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'% Ionic character<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{Observed}}\\,\\,{\\rm{dipole}}\\,\\,{\\rm{moment}}}}{{{\\rm{Theoretical}}\\,\\,{\\rm{dipole}}\\,\\,{\\rm{moment}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 100}}$<br>Theoretical dipole moment of a 100% ionic\ncharacter ${\\rm{ = q \\times d = }}\\left( {{\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.6 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 19}}}}{\\rm{C}}} \\right){\\rm{ \\times }}\\left( {{\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.41 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 10}}}}\\,{\\rm{m}}} \\right)$<br>${\\rm{ = 2}}{\\rm{.256 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 29}}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{cm}}$<br>% Ionic character<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{2}}{\\rm{.6 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 30}}}}}}{{{\\rm{2}}{\\rm{.256 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 29}}}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 100 = 11}}{\\rm{.5\\% }}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15707,'chemistry',45,430,861,'Match Column I with Column II and choose the correct combination from the options given.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{ A}} - {\\\\rm{P}},{\\\\rm{ B}} - {\\\\rm{R}},{\\\\rm{ C}} - {\\\\rm{S}},{\\\\rm{ D}} - {\\\\rm{Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A}} - {\\\\rm{R}},{\\\\rm{ B}} - {\\\\rm{P}},{\\\\rm{ C}} - {\\\\rm{S}},{\\\\rm{ D}} - {\\\\rm{Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A}} - {\\\\rm{R}},{\\\\rm{ B}} - {\\\\rm{Q}},{\\\\rm{ C}} - {\\\\rm{P}},{\\\\rm{ D}} - {\\\\rm{S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A}} - {\\\\rm{R}},{\\\\rm{ B}} - {\\\\rm{S}},{\\\\rm{ C}} - {\\\\rm{P}},{\\\\rm{ D}} - {\\\\rm{Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'(A) Across a period 1.E. increases in general. Ionization enthalpy of Be is higher than B because of the presence of fullyfilled 2s-orbital.<br>(B) Atomic radius decreases across the period.<br>(C) Metallic character increases down the group and decreases across the period.<br>(D) In group 16 ,sulphur has the highest negative electron gain enthalpy and oxygen has the least.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/45_15707_question_1.png'),
