(15723,'chemistry',15,185,404,'In a compound, A containing carbon, hydrogen, and oxygen, the $\\%$ of hydrogen is one sixth that of carbon which is 1.5 times that of oxygen. What is the simplest formula for the compound?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{4} \\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{4} \\\\mathrm{O}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6} \\\\mathrm{O}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4} \\\\mathrm{O}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/15_15723_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>So, empirical formula is $\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{4} \\mathrm{O}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15725,'chemistry',46,442,887,'The Cl - O bond order in perchlorate ion','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.75", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2.5", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Perchlorate ion is ${\\rm{ClO}}_{\\rm{4}}^{\\rm{ - }}{\\rm{.}}$ It has 4 resonating structures. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_15725_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> ${\\rm{Bond}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Order}}\\,{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\left( {\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\begin{array}{l}{\\rm{No}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{bonds}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{between}}\\\\{\\rm{any}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{two}}\\,\\,{\\rm{atoms}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{in}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{all}}\\end{array}\\\\{{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{resonating}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{structures}}}\\end{array}} \\right)}}{{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{7}}}{{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.75}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15726,'chemistry',45,430,859,'Which will have the maximum value of electron affinity ${{\\rm{O}}^{\\rm{x}}},{{\\rm{O}}^{\\rm{y}}},{{\\rm{O}}^{\\rm{z}}}$ (x, y and z respectively are $0,-1$ and $-$2 ?','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{O}}^{\\\\rm{x}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{O}}^{\\\\rm{y}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{O}}^{\\\\rm{z}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All have equal", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Less -ve charge, more is electron affinity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15729,'chemistry',45,430,859,'$\\mathrm{N}_{0} / 2$ atoms of $\\mathrm{X}(\\mathrm{g})$ are converted into $\\mathrm{X}^{+}(\\mathrm{g})$ by energy $\\mathrm{E}_{1} \\cdot \\mathrm{N}_{0} / 2$ atoms of $\\mathrm{X}(\\mathrm{g})$ are converted into $\\mathrm{X}^{-}(\\mathrm{g})$ of energy $\\mathrm{E}_{2}$. Hence, ionization energy and electron affinity of $\\mathrm{X}(\\mathrm{g})$ are:','[{"text": "$\\\\dfrac{2 \\\\mathrm{E}_{1}}{\\\\mathrm{~N}_{0}}, \\\\dfrac{2\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{E}_{1}-\\\\mathrm{E}_{2}\\\\right)}{\\\\mathrm{N}_{0}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\dfrac{2 \\\\mathrm{E}_{1}}{\\\\mathrm{~N}_{0}}, \\\\dfrac{2 \\\\mathrm{E}_{2}}{\\\\mathrm{~N}_{0}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\frac{{\\\\left( {{{\\\\text{E}}_{\\\\text{1}}} - {{\\\\text{E}}_{\\\\text{2}}}} \\\\right)}}{{{{\\\\text{N}}_{\\\\text{0}}}}},\\\\frac{{2{{\\\\text{E}}_{\\\\text{2}}}}}{{{{\\\\text{N}}_{\\\\text{0}}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Let $\\mathrm{IE}=\\mathrm{I}$ and $\\mathrm{EA}=\\mathrm{E}$<br>$\\mathrm{X}(\\mathrm{g}) \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{X}^{+}(\\mathrm{g})+\\mathrm{e}$<br>$\\frac{{{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{0}}}}}{2} \\times {\\rm{I}} = {{\\rm{E}}_1}\\quad \\therefore {\\rm{I}} = \\frac{{2{{\\rm{E}}_1}}}{{\\,{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{0}}}}}$<br>$\\mathrm{X}^{+}(\\mathrm{g}) \\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{e}^{-}} \\mathrm{X}(\\mathrm{g})$<br>$\\frac{{{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{0}}}{\\rm{E}}}}{2} = {{\\rm{E}}_2}\\quad \\therefore {\\rm{E}} = \\frac{{2{{\\rm{E}}_2}}}{{\\,{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{0}}}}}$<br>So $\\dfrac{2 \\mathrm{E}_{1}}{\\mathrm{~N}_{\\mathrm{0}}}, \\dfrac{2 \\mathrm{E}_{2}}{\\mathrm{~N}_{\\mathrm{0}}}$ is correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15731,'chemistry',15,187,409,'Read Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct option given below.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> The weight percentage of a compound A in a solution is given by<br>${\\rm{\\% }}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{A = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{Mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{A}}}}{{{\\rm{Total}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{solution}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 100}}$<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The mole fraction of a component A is given by, Mole fraction of A <br>$ = \\frac{{{\\rm{No}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{moles}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{A}}}}{{{\\rm{Total}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{no}}{\\rm{.of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{moles}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{all}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{components}}}}$','[{"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both assertion and reason are with correct formula for $\\%$ mass and mole fraction, but there is no relation between them.',NULL,'Easy','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15733,'chemistry',45,430,861,'Which of the following is correct option?<br>(P) Same number of electrons in d-subshell $(\\mathrm{Mn}, \\mathrm{Cr}$ )<br>(Q) Same value of ${{\\rm{Z}}_{{\\rm{eff }}}}\\left( {{\\rm{L}}{{\\rm{i}}^{\\rm{ + }}}\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{B}}^{\\rm{ + }}}} \\right)$<br>(R) Same value of shielding constant, ${\\text{(}}\\,{\\text{L}}{{\\text{i}}^ + }\\,\\,{\\text{and}}\\,\\,{\\text{B}}{{\\text{e}}^{{\\text{2 + }}}})$<br>(S) Same value of electronegativity ( P and H )<br>(T) Same value of electron affinity ( F and Cl )','[{"text": "(P) (R) and (T)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(R), (S) and (T)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(P), (R) and (S)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct statements", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{Mn} \\rightarrow[\\mathrm{Ar}] 4 \\mathrm{~s}^{2} 3 \\mathrm{~d}^{5}, \\mathrm{Cr} \\rightarrow[\\mathrm{Ar}] 4 \\mathrm{~s}^{1} 3 \\mathrm{~d}^{5}$,<br>So d-electrons in Mn and $\\mathrm{Cr}=5$.<br>$\\mathrm{Li}^{+}$and $\\mathrm{B}^{+} \\rightarrow$ different $\\mathrm{Z}_{\\text {eff }}$<br>(inner shell $\\mathrm{e}^{-}$different)<br>$\\mathrm{Li}^{+}$and $\\mathrm{Be}^{2+} \\rightarrow$ same value of screening constant, $\\sigma$ as $\\sigma_{\\text {net }}$ inner shell electrons are same<br>P and H both have same value of electronegativity.<br>EA of $\\mathrm{Cl}(-349 \\mathrm{~kJ} /$ mole $) \\& \\mathrm{~F}(-333 \\mathrm{~kJ} /$ mole $)$.<br>$\\therefore$ (P),(R), and (S) only correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15734,'chemistry',46,451,910,'KF combines with HF to form ${\\rm{KH}}{{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{2}}}$. The compound contains the species','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{K}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}{\\\\rm{,}}\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{F}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{K}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}{\\\\rm{,}}\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{F}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{HF}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{K}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{H}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}} \\\\right]^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{KHF}}} \\\\right]^{\\\\rm{ + }}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${{\\rm{F}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$ forms H-bond with HF, therefore, the species ${\\left[ {{\\rm{F}}....{\\rm{H - F}}} \\right]^{\\rm{ - }}}$ or ${\\rm{HF}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ - }}$ exists.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15735,'chemistry',15,186,405,'1.12 mL of a gas is produced at STP by the action of 4.12 mg of alcohol, with methyl magnesium iodide. The molecular mass of alcohol is','[{"text": "16.0", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "41.2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "82.4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "156.0", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{ROH}+\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{MgI} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{CH}_{4}+\\mathrm{MgROI}$<br>$\\therefore 1$ mole alcohol gives 1 mole $\\mathrm{CH}_{4}$.<br>According to data,<br>1.12 L(at STP) $\\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ is obtained from 4.12 g alcohol.<br>$\\therefore 22.4 \\mathrm{~L}$ (at STP) $\\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ is obtained from<br>$=\\dfrac{22.4 \\times 4.12}{1.12}=82.4 \\mathrm{~g}$<br>So, $82.4 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-}$is the molar mass of alcohol.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15750,'chemistry',45,430,861,'Consider the following statements:\n(I) The radius of an anion is larger than that of the parent atom\n(II) The IE increases left to right in a period\n(III) The electronegativity of an element is the tendency of an isolated atom to attract an electron.\nThe correct statements are:','[{"text": "I alone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II alone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only I and II are correct options as $\\mathrm{M}^{-}>\\mathrm{M}$ is order for radii and IE increase from left to right in period but EN is the property of bonded atoms to attract the shared electron pair towards itself.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15737,'chemistry',45,426,852,'Match column I with column II.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\quad \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\quad \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\quad \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\quad \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\quad \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\quad \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\quad \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\quad \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\quad \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\quad \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\quad \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\quad \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'(A-S) $\\mathrm{ns}^{2} \\mathrm{np}^{5}$ is general valence shell electron configuration of halogens. So this configuration belongs to bromine.<br>(B-Q) $(\\mathrm{n}-1) \\mathrm{d}^{10} \\mathrm{~ns}^{1}$ is for copper $\\left([\\mathrm{Ar}] 4 \\mathrm{~s}^{1} 3 \\mathrm{~d}^{10}\\right)$<br>(C-P) $(\\mathrm{n}-1) \\mathrm{d}^{5} \\mathrm{~ns}^{1}$ configuration belongs to chromium. $\\left([\\mathrm{Ar}] 4 \\mathrm{~s}^{1} 3 \\mathrm{~d}^{5}\\right)$<br>(D-R) Noble gases has valence shell electron configuration ${\\rm{(n}} - {\\rm{1)}}{{\\rm{d}}^{1 - 10}}$ $\\mathrm{ns}^{2} \\mathrm{np}^{6}$, so it belongs to krypton.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/45_15737_question_1.png'),
(15740,'chemistry',15,186,405,'Which statement is false for the balanced equation given below?<br>$\\mathrm{CS}_{2}+3 \\mathrm{O}_{2} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{SO}_{2}+\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$','[{"text": "One mole of $\\\\mathrm{CS}_{2}$ will produce one mole of $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The reaction of 16 g of oxygen produces 7.33 g of $\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The reaction of one mole of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ will produce $2 / 3$ mole of $\\\\mathrm{SO}_{2}$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Six molecules of oxygen requires three molecules of $\\\\mathrm{CS}_{2}$.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'3 moles of $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ react with 1 mole of $\\mathrm{CS}_{2}$.<br>So, 6 moles of $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ react with 2 moles of $\\mathrm{CS}_{2}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15741,'chemistry',46,442,887,'The bond order of S-O bond in ${\\rm{SO}}_{\\rm{4}}^{{\\rm{ - 2}}}$ is','[{"text": "1.25", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{B}}{\\rm{.O}}{\\rm{. = }}\\frac{{\\left( \\begin{array}{l}{\\rm{Total}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{no}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{bonds}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{between}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Cl - O}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\\\{\\rm{in}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{all}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{resonance}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{structrues}}\\end{array} \\right)}}{{{\\rm{Total}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{no}}{\\rm{.}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{resonance}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{structures}}}}$<br>$\\left( {{\\rm{or}}} \\right)\\,\\,\\frac{{{\\rm{No}}{\\rm{.}}\\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,\\,{\\rm{all}}\\,\\,{\\rm{bonds}}}}{{{\\rm{No}}{\\rm{.}}\\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,\\,{\\rm{all}}\\,\\,{\\rm{attached}}\\,\\,{\\rm{atoms}}}}{\\rm{.}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{6}}}{{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.5}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15742,'chemistry',45,425,851,'Match Column I (atomic number of elements) with Column II (position of elements in periodic table) and select the correct answer using the codes given below the lists.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{ A}} - {\\\\rm{P}},{\\\\rm{ B}} - {\\\\rm{Q}},{\\\\rm{ C}} - {\\\\rm{R}},{\\\\rm{ D}} - {\\\\rm{S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A}} - {\\\\rm{S}},{\\\\rm{ B}} - {\\\\rm{R}},{\\\\rm{ C}} - {\\\\rm{Q}},{\\\\rm{ D}} - {\\\\rm{P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A}} - {\\\\rm{S}},{\\\\rm{ B}} - {\\\\rm{R}},{\\\\rm{ C}} - {\\\\rm{P}},{\\\\rm{ D}} - {\\\\rm{Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A}} - {\\\\rm{Q}},{\\\\rm{ B}} - {\\\\rm{P}},{\\\\rm{ C}} - {\\\\rm{R}},{\\\\rm{ D}} - {\\\\rm{S}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$19 \\rightarrow 1 \\mathrm{~s}^{2} 2 \\mathrm{~s}^{2} 2 \\mathrm{p}^{6} 3 \\mathrm{~s}^{2} 3 \\mathrm{p}^{6} 4 \\mathrm{~s}^{1} \\rightarrow$ s $ - $ block<br>$22 \\to {\\text{ }}1{{\\text{s}}^2}2{{\\text{s}}^2}2{{\\text{p}}^6}3{{\\text{s}}^2}3{{\\text{p}}^6}4{{\\text{s}}^2}3{{\\text{d}}^2} \\to {\\text{d}} - {\\text{block}}$<br>$32 \\to {\\text{ }}1{{\\text{s}}^2}2{{\\text{s}}^2}2{{\\text{p}}^6}3{{\\text{s}}^2}3{{\\text{p}}^6}4{{\\text{s}}^2}3{{\\text{d}}^{10}}4{{\\text{p}}^2} \\to {\\text{p}} - {\\text{block}}$<br>$64 \\rightarrow 1 \\mathrm{~s}^{2} 2 \\mathrm{~s}^{2} 2 \\mathrm{p}^{6} 3 \\mathrm{~s}^{2} 3 \\mathrm{p}^{6} 4 \\mathrm{~s}^{2} 3 \\mathrm{~d}^{10} 4 \\mathrm{p}^{6} 5 \\mathrm{~s}^{2}$$4 \\mathrm{~d}^{10} 5 \\mathrm{p}^{6} 6 \\mathrm{~s}^{2} 5 \\mathrm{~d}^{1} 4 \\mathrm{f}^{7} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{f}$-block',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/45_15742_question_1.png'),
(15761,'chemistry',46,449,905,'What is the effect of the following processes on the bond order in ${{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ ?<br>i) ${{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}} \\to {\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ + }}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$<br>ii) ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}} \\to {\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{ + }}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$','[{"text": "Decreases in both (i) & (ii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increases in both (i) & (ii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increases in (i) but decreases in (ii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decreases in (i) but increases in (ii)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15744,'chemistry',15,185,404,'A compound having the formula ${\\rm{B}}{{\\rm{r}}_{\\rm{3}}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{6}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\left( {{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{3}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{8}}}} \\right)_{\\rm{n}}}$ contains $10.46\\,\\% \\,\\,{\\rm{Br}}$ by mass; the value of n is','[{"text": "54", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "65", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "45", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "35", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'10.46 g Br is present in 100 g compound $3 \\times 80 \\mathrm{~g}$ \' Br \' is present in?<br>$ = \\frac{{3 \\times 80 \\times 100}}{{10.46}} = 2294.45\\,\\,{\\text{gram}}$<br>$\\therefore$ Mass of $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{3} \\mathrm{H}_{8}\\right)_{\\text {n }}$<br>$=2294.45-[(3 \\times 80)+(6 \\times 12)+(3 \\times 1)]$<br>$=1979.45$<br>$\\therefore \\mathrm{n}=\\dfrac{1979.45}{44}=45$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15745,'chemistry',46,442,884,'Select the incorrect statement about N - N bond length will be highest?','[{"text": "In ${{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}{\\\\rm{,}}$ d-orbitals are contracted by electronegative fluorine atoms, but d orbitals contraction is not possible by H - atoms in ${{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The N-N bond energy in ${{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$ is more than N-N bond energy in ${{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The N-N bond length in ${{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$ is more than that of in ${{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The N-N bond length in ${{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$  is less than that of in ${{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'It can be explained on the basis of Bent’s rule.<br>In ${{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}$, N - N bond has more s-character; hence, bond length decreases.<br>While in ${{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}$, N - N bond has less s-character (i.e., more p-character);<br>hence bond length increases.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15746,'chemistry',45,432,864,'Read Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct option given below.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{O}$ is an acidic oxide while $\\mathrm{Cl}_2 \\mathrm{O}_7$ is a basic oxide.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Oxides of metals are generally acidic and oxides of non-metals are generally basic.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and the Reason is the correct explanation of the assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true, but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true, but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Oxides of metals are basic in nature and oxides of nonmetals are acidic in nature. Hence, $\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$ is a basic oxide and $\\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}$ is an acidic oxide.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15748,'chemistry',15,187,410,'50 mL of $20.8 \\%(\\mathrm{w} / \\mathrm{V}) \\mathrm{BaCl}_{2}$ (aq) and 100 mL of $9.8 \\%(\\mathrm{w} / \\mathrm{V}) \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4}(\\mathrm{aq})$ solutions are mixed. Molarity of $\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$ions in the resulting solution is (At. wt. of $\\mathrm{Ba}=137$ )','[{"text": "0.333 M", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.666 M", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.1 M", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.33 M", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$50\\,\\,{\\text{ml}}\\,\\,20.8\\% \\,\\,\\frac{{\\text{w}}}{{\\text{v}}}\\,{\\text{ BaC}}{{\\text{l}}_2}$ solution<br>${\\text{M}} = \\frac{{20.8}}{{208}} \\times \\frac{{1000}}{{50}} = 2$<br>$\\therefore \\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$concentration $=4 \\mathrm{M}$. (As each molecule of $\\mathrm{BaCl}_{2}$ has $2 \\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$ions)<br>from Dilution law :<br>$50 \\times 2=150 \\times \\mathrm{M}_{2}$<br>$\\mathrm{M}_{2}=0.666$<br>(Here no need of any reaction, Question is about chloride ion concentration only, which is diluted from 50 ml to 150 mL )',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(15749,'chemistry',46,442,885,'Which of the following bond angle order is not correct?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{BC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{ > PC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{ > AsC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{S < S}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{ < N}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{ < B}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O < O}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{ < C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{OC}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{PO}}_{\\\\rm{4}}^{{\\\\rm{3 - }}}{\\\\rm{ < SO}}_{\\\\rm{4}}^{{\\\\rm{2 - }}}{\\\\rm{ < ClO}}_{\\\\rm{4}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All have same bond angle',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
