(16233,'chemistry',46,446,892,'Which of the following is the correct increasing order of lone pair of electrons on the central atom?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{I}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{7}}}{\\\\rm{ < I}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}{\\\\rm{ < Cl}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{ < Xe}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{I}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{7}}}{\\\\rm{ < Xe}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{ < Cl}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{ < I}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{I}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{7}}}{\\\\rm{ < Cl}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{ < Xe}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{ < I}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{I}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{7}}}{\\\\rm{ < Xe}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{ < I}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}{\\\\rm{ < Cl}}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The number of lone pairs of electrons on central atom in various given species are<br>&emsp; Species &emsp; &emsp; Number of lone pairs on central atom<br>&emsp; &emsp; ${\\rm{I}}{{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{7}}}$ &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; nil<br>&emsp; &emsp; ${\\rm{I}}{{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{5}}}$ &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; 1<br>&emsp; &emsp; ${\\rm{Cl}}{{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; 2<br>&emsp; &emsp; ${\\rm{Xe}}{{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; 3<br>Thus the correct increasing order is<br>${\\rm{I}}{{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{7}}}{\\rm{ < I}}{{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{ < Cl}}{{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ < Xe}}{{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>$\\,{\\rm{0}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{1}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{2}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{3}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16235,'chemistry',48,749,1610,'The gas in a refrigerator causes cooling on expansion because','[{"text": "Work done by the gas is converted into heat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heat of the gas is lost as work done by the gas", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The heat is spread over a large space", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Imagine the gas was in a cylinder and expanded by pushing against a piston. The movement would involve work being done. This work would need energy, which would come from the kinetic energy of the gas molecules hitting the piston- reducing their average speed. Taking KE away corresponds to lowering the temperature of the gas.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
