(16340,'chemistry',46,449,905,'Which of the following statements is<br>INCORRECT?','[{"text": "Bond length of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2} < $ bond length of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2-}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bond order of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}>$ bond order of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2-}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bond length of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}>$ bond length of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bond order of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{+} < $bond order of $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2-}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_16340_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  B.L $\\propto \\dfrac{1}{\\text { B.O }}$<br>B.O $=\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{+2}>\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{+}>\\mathrm{O}_{2}>\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{-}>\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2-}$<br>B.L $=\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2+} < \\mathrm{O}_{2}^{+} < \\mathrm{O}_{2} < \\mathrm{O}_{2}^{-} < \\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2-}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16341,'chemistry',48,761,1654,'The enthalpy of vaporisation of chloroform is $\\mathrm{29.4 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol}}$ at its normal boiling point of $\\mathrm{61.7^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}$. What is the entropy of condensation of chloroform at this temperature ?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{ - 57}}{\\\\rm{.3}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ - 10}}{\\\\rm{.6}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ - 1}}{\\\\rm{.18}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{10}}{\\\\rm{.6}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{R}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{\\Delta_{v a p} H^{\\circ}=29.4 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol}}$ and<br>$\\rm{T_{\\text {boiling }}=334.7 \\mathrm{~K}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\Rightarrow \\Delta_{v a p} S^{\\circ}=\\dfrac{\\Delta_{v a p} H^{\\circ}}{T_{\\text {boiling }}}=87.84 \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}=10.6 \\mathrm{R}}$<br>$\\rm{\\left(R=8.314 J^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\right)}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\Rightarrow \\Delta_{\\text {condensation }} S^{\\circ}=-10.6 R}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16343,'chemistry',46,442,885,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{S}-\\mathrm{H}$ bond angle in $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}$ is closer to $90^{\\circ}$ but $\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{O}-\\mathrm{H}$ bond angle in $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$ is $104.5^{\\circ}$.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Lone pair - lone pair repulsion is stronger in $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}$ than in $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_16343_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Oxygen is more electronegative than sulphur due to which there is less lone pair - lone pair repulsion in $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$ while more lone pair - lone pair repulsion in $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}$. Hence both Assertion  and  Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2007,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16344,'chemistry',48,761,1652,'Calculate the entropy change in surroundings when $\\mathrm{1.00 \\mathrm{~mol}}$ of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}(\\mathrm{l})}$ is formed under standard conditions. $\\mathrm{\\Delta_{\\mathrm{f}} \\mathrm{H}^{\\circ}=-286 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$.','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{960}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{J}}\\\\,{{\\\\rm{K}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\\\rm{\\\\,mo}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{960}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{k}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{J}}\\\\,{{\\\\rm{K}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\\\rm{\\\\,mo}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1048}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{J}}\\\\,{{\\\\rm{K}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\\\rm{\\\\,mo}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1048}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{k}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{J}}\\\\,{{\\\\rm{K}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\\\rm{\\\\,mo}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Enthalpy change for the formation of 1 mole of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}(\\mathrm{l})}$,<br>$\\rm{ \\mathrm{H}_{2(g)}+\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2(g)} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{(l)} ; \\\\ \\Delta_{f} H^{\\circ}=-286 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$<br>Energy released in the above reaction, is absorbed by the surroundings. It means $\\mathrm{q_{\\text {surr }}=+286 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$.<br>$\\mathrm{\\Delta S=\\dfrac{q_{\\text {surr }}}{T}=\\dfrac{+286 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}{298 \\mathrm{~K}}}$<br>$\\rm{=0.9597 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}=959.7 \\mathrm{JK}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16346,'chemistry',46,444,889,'Bond polarity of diatomic molecule is because of','[{"text": "Difference in electron affinities of two atoms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Difference in electronegativities of two atoms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Difference in ionisation potentials", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In case of diatomic molecule, the greater difference of electronegativities of the two atoms leads to greater polarity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2013,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16347,'chemistry',48,762,1658,'$\\mathrm{\\Delta G=-177 \\mathrm{kcal}}$ for $\\mathrm{2 \\mathrm{Fe}_{(s)}+\\dfrac{3}{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Fe}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3(\\mathrm{~s})}}$ and $\\mathrm{\\Delta G=-19 \\mathrm{kcal}}$ for $\\mathrm{4 \\mathrm{Fe}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3(\\mathrm{~s})}+\\mathrm{Fe}_{(\\mathrm{s})}}$ $\\mathrm{\\rightarrow 3 \\mathrm{Fe}_{3} \\mathrm{O}_{4(\\mathrm{~s})}}$<br>what is the Gibb\'s free energy of formation of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Fe}_{3} \\mathrm{O}_{4}}$ ?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{+229.6 \\\\mathrm{kcal} / \\\\mathrm{mol}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-242.4 \\\\mathrm{kcal} / \\\\mathrm{mol}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-727 \\\\mathrm{kcal} / \\\\mathrm{mol}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-229.6 \\\\mathrm{kcal} / \\\\mathrm{mol}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<br>(i) $\\mathrm{2 \\mathrm{Fe}_{(s)}+\\dfrac{3}{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2(g)} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Fe}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3(S)} ; \\Delta G=-177 \\mathrm{kcal}}$<br>(ii) $\\mathrm{4 \\mathrm{Fe}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3(s)}+\\mathrm{Fe}_{(s)} \\rightarrow 3 \\mathrm{Fe}_{3} \\mathrm{O}_{4(s)} \\quad \\Delta G=-19 \\mathrm{kcal}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\Delta G_{r}=3 \\Delta G_{f}\\left(\\mathrm{Fe}_{3} \\mathrm{O}_{4}\\right)-4 \\Delta G_{f}(\\mathrm{Fe}, S)}$<br>$\\mathrm{3 \\Delta G_{f}\\left(F_{3} O_{4}, S\\right)=-19+4 \\times(-177)}$<br>$\\mathrm{3 \\Delta G_{r}\\left(\\mathrm{Fe}_{3} \\mathrm{O}_{4}, S\\right)=-\\dfrac{727}{3}=-242.4 \\mathrm{kcal} / \\mathrm{mol}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16349,'chemistry',46,446,892,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{SeCl}_{4}$ does not have a tetrahedral structure.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> $\\mathrm{Se}$ in $\\mathrm{SeCl}_{4}$ has two lone pairs.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{SeCl}_{4}$ has see - saw geometry, i.e. distorted trigonal pyramidal geometry. The distortion in shape is due to he presence of one lone pair of electrons and it is $\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\mathrm{~d}$ hybridised. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_16349_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Hence, both Assertion  and Reason are incorrect',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2005,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16350,'chemistry',48,762,1659,'Which of the following is true for the reaction $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}(\\mathrm{l}) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}(\\mathrm{g})}$ at $\\mathrm{100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}$ and 1 atmosphere?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{S}=0}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{H}=0}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{H}=\\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{U}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{H}=\\\\mathrm{T} \\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{S}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'At equilibrium, $\\mathrm{\\Delta G=0}$<br>Hence, $\\mathrm{0=\\Delta H-T \\Delta S}$ or $\\mathrm{\\Delta H=T \\Delta S}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16352,'chemistry',46,448,898,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}$ bond in ethyne is shorter than $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}$ bonds in ethene.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> ( $\\mathbf{R})$ Carbon atom in ethene is $\\mathrm{sp}$ hybridised while it is $\\mathrm{sp}^{2}$ in ethyne.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The carbon atoms in ethene is $\\mathrm{sp}^{2}$ hybridised due to <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_16352_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> t  while it is sp in ethyne due to  $ - {\\text{C}} \\equiv {\\text{C}} - $ <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_16352_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Hence,  Assertion is correct but Reason  is incorrect.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2007,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16353,'chemistry',48,763,1661,'Gibbs energy change $\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{G}}$ is related to equilibrium constant \' $\\mathrm{K}$.\' as','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{\\\\Delta G^\\\\circ  =  - RT}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ln}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{K}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{\\\\Delta G^\\\\circ  = RT}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ln}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{K}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ln}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{K =  - }}\\\\frac{{{\\\\rm{RT}}}}{{{\\\\rm{\\\\Delta G^\\\\circ }}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ln}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{K =  - }}\\\\frac{{{\\\\rm{\\\\Delta G^\\\\circ }}}}{{{\\\\rm{RT}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The relationship between $\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{G}, \\Delta \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}}$ and Reaction quotient, $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Q}}$ is as follows:<br>$\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{G}=\\Delta \\mathrm{G}^{\\mathrm{o}}+\\mathrm{RT} \\operatorname{In} \\mathrm{Q}}$<br>At equilibrium, $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Q}=\\mathrm{K}, \\Delta \\mathrm{G}=0}$<br>Upon substitution, we get<br>$\\mathrm{0=\\Delta \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}+\\mathrm{RT} \\operatorname{InK}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}=-\\mathrm{RT} \\operatorname{InK}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16355,'chemistry',46,448,899,'The hybridisation scheme for the central atom includes a d - orbital contribution in','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{I}_{3}^{-}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{PCl}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NO}_{3}^{-}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Se}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_16355_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   Hence, in $\\mathrm{I}_{3}^{-}, \\mathrm{d}$ - orbitals are used in hybridisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2009,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16456,'chemistry',46,442,885,'In which of the following species, the angle around the central atom is exactly equal to $109^{\\circ} 28^{\\prime}$ ?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{SF}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{4}^{+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{NH}_{4}^{+}$is $\\mathrm{sp}^{3}$ hybridised without lone pairs. So, it\'s bond angle is $109^{0} 28^{1}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16356,'chemistry',48,763,1661,'Find out the value of equilibrium constant for the following reaction at $\\mathrm{298 \\mathrm{~K}}$.<br>$\\rm{2 \\mathrm{NH}_{3(\\mathrm{~g})}+\\mathrm{CO}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{NH}_{2} \\mathrm{CONH}_{2(\\mathrm{aq})}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{(\\mathrm{l})}}$<br>Standard Gibb\'s energy change, $\\mathrm{\\Delta_{\\mathrm{r}} \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}}$ at the given temperature is $\\mathrm{-13.6 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$.','[{"text": "200", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "220", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "240", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "280", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'We know, $\\mathrm{\\log K=\\dfrac{-\\Delta_{r} G^{\\circ}}{2.303 R T}}$<br>$\\rm{=\\dfrac{\\left(-13.6 \\times 10^{3} \\mathrm{Jmol}^{-1}\\right)}{2.303\\left(8.314 J \\mathrm{~K}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\right)(298 \\mathrm{~K})}=2.38}$<br>Hence, $\\mathrm{K=\\operatorname{antilog} 2.38=2.4 \\times 10^{2}=240}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16358,'chemistry',46,446,892,'The ion which is not tetrahedral in shape is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{BF}_{4}^{-}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{4}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Cu}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{4}\\\\right]^{2+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{NiCl}_{4}\\\\right]^{-2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{BF}_{4}^{-}, \\mathrm{NH}_{4}^{+},\\left[\\mathrm{NiCl}_{4}\\right]^{2-}$ all are tetrahedral in shape but $\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{4}\\right]^{2+}$ is not tetrahedral but square planar  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_16358_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16359,'chemistry',48,747,1601,'Thermodynamics is not concerned about','[{"text": "Energy changes involved in a chemical reaction.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The extent to which a chemical reaction proceeds.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The rate at which a reaction proceeds.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The feasibility of a chemical reaction.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The rate at which a reaction proceeds explained by Chemical kinetics',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16360,'chemistry',49,615,1229,'What will be the correct order of vapour pressure of water, acetone and ether at $30^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. Given that among these compounds, water has maximum boiling point and ether has minimum boiling point?','[{"text": "Water $ < $ ether $ < $ acetone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water $ < $ acetone $ < $ ether", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ether $ < $ acetone $ < $ water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acetone $ < $ ether $ < $ water", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Greater the boiling point, less is the vapour pressure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16362,'chemistry',46,448,899,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In $\\mathrm{SF}_{6}$, molecule, $\\mathrm{F}-\\mathrm{S}-\\mathrm{F}$ bond angle is $90^{\\circ}$.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> $\\mathrm{SF}_{6}$ molecule has octahedral geometry with $\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\mathrm{~d}^{2}$ hybridisation.<br>','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Formation of $\\mathrm{SF}_{6}: \\mathrm{InSF}_{6}$, the central sulphur atom has the ground state outer electronic configuration  ${\\text{3}}{{\\text{s}}^{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ 3}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{4}}}$  In the excited state, the available six orbitals i.e. one $\\mathrm{s}$, three $\\mathrm{p}$ and two $\\mathrm{d}$ are singly occupied by electrons. These orbitals hybridise to form six new $\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\mathrm{~d}^{2}$ hybrid orbitals which are projected towards the six corners of a regular octahedron in $\\mathrm{SF}_{6}$. In this, $\\mathrm{F}-\\mathrm{S}-\\mathrm{F}$ bond angle are $90^{\\circ}$ and $180^{\\circ}$.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2017,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16363,'chemistry',48,748,1602,'Which of the following is closed system?','[{"text": "Jet engine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tea placed in a steel kettle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rocket engine during propulsion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pressure cooker", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Closed\n  system only allows energy to be exchanged with the surroundings but not mass.\n  Tea in the steel kettle loses heat over time.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16364,'chemistry',49,614,1227,'Which of the following is a characteristic property of equilibrium?','[{"text": "Number of moles of reactants and products is always equal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Catalyst affects the equilibrium state", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It never proceeds to completion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rate of forward and backward reactions are not equal", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'(1)Number of moles of reactants and products is always not same<br>(2) Catalyst fastens the existence of equilibrium but does not affect the equilibrium state.<br>(4) At equilibrium, rate of forward reaction is equal to the rate of backward reaction. So option 3 is correct',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16366,'chemistry',46,446,892,'The structure of $\\mathrm{IF}_{7}$ is','[{"text": "Square pyramidal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trigonal bipyramidal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Octahedral", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pentagonal bipyramidal", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The structure of $\\left(\\mathrm{IF}_{7}\\right)$ is pentagonal bipyramidal. It can be depicted as follows:<br>$\\mathrm{I}(\\mathrm{Z}=53)($ Ground state $)=$  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_16366_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Here, $\\mathrm{X}$ denotes electrons of $\\mathrm{F}$ - atoms. The structure of $\\mathrm{IF}_{7}$ is shown below:<br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_16366_explanation_2.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>Pentagonal bipyramidal structure',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2018,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21134,'chemistry',55,1240,3017,'The dipole moment of benzene is:','[{"text": "Zero", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Less than p-dichloro benzene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Greater than p-dichloro benzene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Equal to that of chloro benzene", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'It is a symmetrical molecule, so dipole moment is zero.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16370,'chemistry',46,449,905,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> ${{\\text{B}}_{\\text{2}}}$  molecule is diamagnetic<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The highest occupied molecular orbital is of  $\\sigma$  type.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The total number of electrons in  ${{\\text{B}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ = 10}}$<br>Molecular orbital configuration:<br>$\\sigma 1 {{\\text{s}}^2},\\mathop \\sigma \\limits^* 1 {{\\text{s}}^2},\\sigma 2 {{\\text{s}}^2},\\mathop \\sigma \\limits^* 2 {{\\text{s}}^2},\\pi 2{\\text{p}}_{\\text{x}}^1 \\approx \\pi 2{\\text{p}}_{\\text{y}}^1$<br>It has two unpaired electrons.<br>$\\therefore$ It is paramagnetic and the highest occupied molecular orbital is of $\\pi$ type.<br>Hence, both $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{R}$ are incorrect',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2005,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16371,'chemistry',48,748,1608,'For the process to occur under adiabatic conditions, the correct condition is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{T}=0}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{p}=0}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{q=0}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{w}=0}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'For the process to occur under adiabatic conditions, $\\mathrm{q=0}$, i.e., heat cannot flow system to surroundings or vice-versa.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16372,'chemistry',49,617,1236,'If   ${{\\text{N}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ + 3}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{2N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{(I)}}$ &<br>${{\\text{N}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ + 3}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}\\mathop  \\rightleftharpoons \\limits^{{\\text{Fe}}} {\\text{2N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{(II)}}$ are in equilibrium at same temperature, then','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}_{\\\\mathrm{C}}$ of I = $\\\\mathrm{K}_{\\\\mathrm{C}}$ of II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}_{\\\\mathrm{C}}$ of I = $\\\\mathrm{K}_{\\\\mathrm{P}}$ of II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}_{\\\\mathrm{C}}$ of I $ < \\\\mathrm{K}_{\\\\mathrm{C}}$ of II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}_{\\\\mathrm{P}}$ of II $>\\\\mathrm{K}_{\\\\mathrm{P}}$ of I", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm {\\mathrm{K}}$ value does not vary with catalyst.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
