(16376,'chemistry',49,617,1241,'At equilibrium, the concentrations of $\\mathrm{N}_{2}=3.0 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{M}, \\mathrm{O}_{2}=4.2 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{M}$ and $\\mathrm{NO}=2.8 \\times$ $10^{-3} \\mathrm{M}$ in a sealed vessel at $800 \\mathrm{~K}$. What will be  ${{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{C}}}$ for the reaction${{\\text{N}}_{{\\text{2(g)}}}}{\\text{  +  }}{{\\text{O}}_{{\\text{2(g)}}}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{2N}}{{\\text{O}}_{{\\text{(g)}}}}?$','[{"text": "0.322", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3.22", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.622", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "6.22", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'For the reaction equilibrium constant, $\\mathrm {K_{C}}$ can be written as<br>$\\rm{K_{C}=\\dfrac{[N O]^{2}}{\\left[N_{2}\\right]\\left[O_{2}\\right]}}$ <br> = $\\dfrac{\\left(2.8 \\times 10^{-3} \\rm{M}\\right)^{2}} {\\left(3.0 \\times 10^{-3} \\rm{M}\\right)\\left(4.2 \\times 10^{-3} \\rm{M}\\right)}$ =0.622.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
