(16464,'chemistry',46,442,884,'The bond length of the $\\mathrm{S}-\\mathrm{O}$ bond is maximum in which of the following compound?<br>$\\mathrm{SOBr}_{2}, \\mathrm{SOCl}_{2}, \\mathrm{SOF}_{2}$','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{SOCl}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{SOBr}_{2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{SOF}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All have same length", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_16464_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> In $\\mathrm{SOBr}_{2}, \\mathrm{~S}-\\mathrm{O}$ bond has maximum bond length in comparison to $\\mathrm{S}-\\mathrm{O}$ bond lengths in $\\mathrm{SOF}_{2}$ and $\\mathrm{SOCl}_{2}$, because in $\\mathrm{SOBr}_{2}$, S-O bond has been formed by hybrid orbital containing less s-character.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
