(16525,'chemistry',48,758,1642,'The heats of combustion of rhombic and monoclinic sulphur are respectively 70.96 and $\\mathrm{71.03 \\mathrm{k}}$ cal. What will be the heat of conversion of rhombic sulphur to monoclinic?','[{"text": "70960 calories", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "71030 calories", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "-70 calories", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "+70 calories", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Given: (1) $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{S}_{(\\text {rhombic) }}+\\mathrm{O}_{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{SO}_{2}}$<br>$\\rm{\\Delta H=-70.96 \\mathrm{kcal}}$<br>(2) $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{S}_{\\text {(monoclinic) }}+\\mathrm{O}_{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{SO}_{2}, \\quad \\Delta H=-71.03 \\mathrm{kcal}}$<br>Eqn. (1) - Eqn (2) gives $\\mathrm{S_{(\\text {rhombic) }} \\rightarrow S_{\\text {(monoclinic) }}}$<br>$\\rm{(\\Delta) \\mathrm{H}=71.03-70.96=0.07 \\mathrm{kcal}=70 \\mathrm{cal}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
