(16541,'chemistry',49,624,1267,'The degree of ionisation of $0.05{\\text{M}}\\,\\,{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_3}$ at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ in a solution of $\\mathrm{pH}=11\\left(\\mathrm{~K}_{\\mathrm{b}}=1.76 \\times 10^{-5}\\right)$ is','[{"text": "0.0173", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.173", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.73", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "17.3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {}&{{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{4}}}{\\text{OH}}\\,\\, \\rightleftharpoons }&{{\\text{NH}}_{\\text{4}}^{\\text{ + }}}&{\\text{ + }}&{{\\text{O}}{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ - }}}\\,}&{} \\\\ \n  {{\\text{At time t  = }}\\,{\\text{0}}}&{\\text{C}}&{\\text{0}}&{}&{\\text{0}}&{} \\\\ \n  \\begin{gathered}\n  {\\text{At}} \\hfill \\\\\n  {\\text{Equilibrium}} \\hfill \\\\ \n\\end{gathered} &{{\\text{C}(1 - \\mathrm{\\alpha})}}&{{\\text{C}\\alpha }}&{}&{{\\text{C}\\alpha }}&{} \n\\end{array}$<br> $\\mathrm {p O H=14-11=3}$<br>Then, $\\mathrm {\\left[\\mathrm{OH}^{-}\\right]=10^{-3}}$<br>$\\mathrm {\\therefore \\quad K_{\\mathrm{b}}=\\dfrac{C \\alpha\\left[\\mathrm{OH}^{-}\\right]}{C(1-\\alpha)}=\\dfrac{0.05 \\times \\alpha\\left[10^{-3}\\right]}{0.05(1-\\alpha)}}$<br>$\\mathrm {1.76 \\times 10^{-5}=\\dfrac{\\alpha 10^{-3}}{(1-\\alpha)}}$<br>$\\mathrm {1.76 \\times 10^{-2}(1-\\alpha)=\\alpha}$<br>$\\mathrm {1.76 \\times 10^{-2}=1.0176 \\alpha}$<br>$\\mathrm {\\alpha=\\dfrac{0.0176}{1.0176}=0.01729}$<br>$\\mathrm {=0.0173}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16550,'chemistry',49,630,1283,'The hydrolysis constant of ammonium acetate is given by','[{"text": "$\\\\dfrac{{{{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{w}}}}}{{{{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{a}}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\dfrac{{{{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{w}}}}}{{{{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{b}}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\dfrac{{{{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{w}}}}}{{{{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{a}}}{\\\\rm{.}}{{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{b}}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{a}}}{\\\\rm{.}}{{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{b}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ammonium acetate is salt of weak acid and weak base. So, the hydrolysis constant for ammonium acetate is $\\mathrm {\\dfrac{K_{w}}{K_{a} K_{b}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16542,'chemistry',46,449,905,'In which of the following sets, all the species are diamagnetic in nature?','[{"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2-}, \\\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2+}, \\\\mathrm{N}_{2}^{2-}\\\\right]$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{C}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2-}, \\\\mathrm{N}_{2}^{2+}\\\\right]$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2-}, \\\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{+}, \\\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2+}\\\\right]$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}^{+}, \\\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{2+}, \\\\mathrm{B}_{2}\\\\right]$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{C}_{2}-12 \\mathrm{e}^{-}, \\mathrm{O}_{2}^{-2}-18 \\mathrm{e}^{-}, \\mathrm{N}_{2}^{+2} \\rightarrow 12 \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow$ all are diamagnetic<br>$\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{-2}-18 \\mathrm{e}^{-}, \\mathrm{O}_{2}^{+2}-14 \\mathrm{e}^{-}(\\mathrm{Dia}) \\&$<br>$\\mathrm{N}_{2}^{-2}\\left(16 \\mathrm{e}^{-}\\right)$paramagnetic<br>$\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{-2}-18 \\mathrm{e}^{-}, \\mathrm{O}_{2}^{+2}-14 \\mathrm{e}^{-}($Dia $) \\&$<br>$\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{+}\\left(15 \\mathrm{e}^{-}\\right)$paramagnetic<br>$\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{+2}-14 \\mathrm{e}^{-}$,diamagnetic,<br>$\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\rightarrow 10 \\mathrm{e}^{-}, \\mathrm{N}_{2}^{+} \\rightarrow 13 \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\Rightarrow$ paramagnetic<br>Hint: All odd no. $\\mathrm{e}^{-}, 10,16 \\rightarrow$ paramagnetic<br>All even no. of $\\mathrm{e}^{-}$(except 10,16) $\\rightarrow$<br>Diamagnetic',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16544,'chemistry',49,624,1268,'A 0.1 molar solution of weak base $\\mathrm{BOH}$ is $1 \\%$ dissociated. If 0.2 mole of $\\mathrm{BCl}$ is added in 1 litre solution of $\\mathrm{BOH}$, the degree of dissociation of $\\mathrm{BOH}$ will become','[{"text": "$2 \\\\times 10^{-3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$5 \\\\times 10^{-5}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.05", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.02", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm {K_{b}=C \\alpha^{2}=1 \\times 10^{-5}}$<br>In the presence of 0.2 moles $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{BCl}}$<br>$\\rm {\\underset{0.1-0.1 \\alpha}{\\mathrm{BOH}} \\rightleftharpoons \\underset{0.1 \\alpha+0.2}{\\mathrm{~B}^{+}}+\\underset{0.1 \\alpha}{\\mathrm{OH}^{-}}}$<br>$\\mathrm {0.1 \\alpha+0.2 \\approx 0.2}$. Due to common ion, $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{B}^{+}}$ ion concentration due to $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{BOH}}$ is negligible. <br>$\\mathrm {0.1-0.1 \\alpha=0.1}$ Since $\\mathrm {\\alpha}$ is very less.<br>$\\rm {K_{b}=\\dfrac{0.2 \\times 0.1 \\alpha}{0.1} \\Rightarrow 10^{-5}=2 \\times 10^{-1} \\times \\alpha \\\\ \\therefore \\quad \\alpha=5 \\times 10^{-5}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16545,'chemistry',46,449,905,'Which of the following statement is not correct from the view point molecular orbital theory?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Be}_{2}$ is not a stable molecule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{He}_{2}$ is not stable but $\\\\mathrm{He}_{2}^{+}$is expected to exist", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bond strength of $\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ is maximum amongst the homonuclear diatomic molecules belonging to the second period", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The order of energies of molecular orbitals in $\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ molecule is", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct order of energies of molecular orbitals in $\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ molecule is<br>$\\sigma 1 \\mathrm{~s} < \\sigma^{*} 1 \\mathrm{~s} < \\sigma 2 \\mathrm{~s} < \\sigma^{*} 2 \\mathrm{~s} < \\left(\\pi 2 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{x}} \\approx \\pi 2 \\mathrm{py}\\right)$<br>$ < \\sigma 2 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{z}} < \\pi^{*} 2 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{x}}=\\pi^{*} 2 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{y}} < \\sigma^{*} 2 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{z}}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16546,'chemistry',48,762,1659,'Given that $\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{H}=0}$ for mixing of two gases. The diffusion of these gases into each other in a closed container is','[{"text": "A non spontaneous process", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A spontaneous process", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insufficient data", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'It is spontaneous process. Although enthalpy change is zero but randomness or disorder (i.e., $\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{S}}$ ) increases. Therefore, in equation $\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{G}=\\Delta \\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{T} \\Delta \\mathrm{S}}$, the term $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{T} \\Delta \\mathrm{S}}$ will be negative. Hence, $\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{G}}$ will be negative.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
