(16698,'chemistry',50,844,1885,'$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{E}^{\\circ}}$ values of some redox couples are given below. On the basis of these values choose the correct option.<br>$\\mathrm{E^{\\circ}}$ values: $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Br}_{2} / \\mathrm{Br}^{-}=+1.90 ; \\mathrm{Ag}^{+} / \\mathrm{Ag}(s)=+0.80}$<br>$\\rm{C u^{2+} / C u(s)=+0.34 ; I_{2}(s) / I^{-}=+0.54}$','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cu}}$ will reduce ${\\\\rm{B}}{{\\\\rm{r}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cu}}$ will reduce $\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Ag}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cu}}$ will reduce $\\\\mathrm{I^{-}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cu}}$ will reduce $\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Br}_{2}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16699,'chemistry',46,442,884,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Molecular nitrogen is less reactive than molecular oxygen.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The bond length of $\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ is shorter than that of oxygen.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\underset{\\text { Dinitrogen }}{\\mathrm{N} \\equiv \\mathrm{N}} \\quad \\underset{\\text { Dioxygen }}{\\mathrm{O}=\\mathrm{O}}$<br>Molecular nitrogen has a triple bond. Whereas, molecular oxygen has a double bond. Triple bond is shorter than the double bond. Shorter the bond , higher the bond dissociation energy, higher the stability and lesser the reactivity. So the option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
