(16705,'chemistry',48,756,1632,'In Harber\'s process of ammonia manufacture :<br>$\\rm{\\mathrm{N}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})}+3 \\mathrm{H}_{2(g)} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{NH}_{3(g)} ; \\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}^{o}=-92.2 \\mathrm{~kJ}}$<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{Molecule}}}&{{{\\rm{N}}_{{\\rm{2(g)}}}}}&{{{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{2(g)}}}}}&{{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{3(g)}}}}}\\\\{{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{P}}}{\\rm{J/}}\\left( {{\\rm{K}}\\,{\\rm{mol}}} \\right)}&{{\\rm{29}}{\\rm{.1}}}&{{\\rm{28}}{\\rm{.8}}}&{{\\rm{35}}{\\rm{.1}}}\\end{array}$<br>If $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{p}}}$ is independent of temperature, then reaction at $\\mathrm{100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}$ as compared to that of $\\mathrm{25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}$ will be :','[{"text": "More endothermic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Less endothermic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More exothermic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Less exothermic", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{H}^{\\circ}=-92.2 \\mathrm{~kJ}}$<br>$\\rm{\\Delta \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{P}}= 2 \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{P}}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}, \\mathrm{~g}\\right)-\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{P}}\\left(\\mathrm{N}_{2}, \\mathrm{~g}\\right)-3 \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{p}}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\right) \\\\ =2 \\times 35.1-29.1-3 \\times 28.8 \\\\ =70.2-29.1-86.4 \\\\ =-45.3 \\mathrm{~J} / \\mathrm{K}}$<br><br>$\\rm{ \\Delta H_{100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}^{o}=\\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}^{o}+\\Delta \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{P}}(\\Delta \\mathrm{T}) \\\\ =-92.2-\\dfrac{45.3 \\times 75}{1000} \\\\ \\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}^{o}=-92.2-3.3975 \\\\ \\mathrm{H}_{100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}^{o}=-95.59 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol}}$<br>Then the reaction at $\\mathrm{100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}$ will be more exothermic compared to that at $\\mathrm{25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(18874,'chemistry',54,1214,2912,'Most stable carbanion is :','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}^{-}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}^{-}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Carbanion is stabilised by electron withdrawing groups.<br>Due to $-\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ group in benzene ring, <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_18874_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> is most stable carbanion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
