(16718,'chemistry',48,751,1612,'According to the first law of the thermodynamics, $\\mathrm{\\Delta U=q+w}$. In special cases the statement can be expressed in different ways. Which of the following is not a correct expression?','[{"text": "At constant temperature, $\\\\mathrm{q=-w}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "When no work is done, $\\\\mathrm{\\\\Delta U=q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In gaseous system, $\\\\mathrm{\\\\Delta U=q+P \\\\Delta V}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "When work is done by the system : $\\\\mathrm{\\\\Delta U=q+w}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Acc $\\mathrm{1^{\\text {st }}}$ law of thermodynamics<br>$\\Delta {\\rm{U = q + w}}$<br>$\\Delta {\\rm{U = q - P}}\\Delta {\\rm{V}}\\,\\,\\left( {{\\rm{w =  - P}}\\Delta {\\rm{V}}} \\right)$<br>Hence, option (3) is incorrect.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
