(16723,'chemistry',46,445,891,'Order of covalent bond :<br>A.  ${\\rm{KF}} > {\\rm{KI}}\\,;{\\rm{LiF}} > {\\rm{KF}}$<br>B. ${\\rm{KF}} < {\\rm{KI}}\\,;{\\rm{LiF}} > {\\rm{KF}}$<br>C. ${\\rm{SnC}}{{\\rm{l}}_4} > {\\rm{SnC}}{{\\rm{l}}_2};{\\rm{CuCl}} > {\\rm{NaCl}}$<br>D. ${\\rm{LiF}} > {\\rm{KF}}\\,;{\\rm{CuCl}} < {\\rm{NaCl}}$<br>E.  ${\\rm{KF}} < {\\rm{KI}}\\,;{\\rm{CuCl}} > {\\rm{NaCl}}$<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.','[{"text": "C, E only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, C, E only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B, C only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Large cation, small anion, low charge favour ionic bond. Large anion, small cation ,higher charges favour covalent bond. Covalent character of:<br>$ \\bullet $  ${\\rm{KF}} < {\\rm{KI}}$ since ${{\\rm{I}}^ - }$ has larger size than ${{\\rm{F}}^ - }$.<br>$ \\bullet $ ${\\rm{LiF}} > {\\rm{KF}}$ since  ${\\rm{L}}{{\\rm{i}}^ + }$ has smaller size than ${{\\rm{K}}^ + }$<br>$ \\bullet $ ${\\rm{SnC}}{{\\rm{l}}_4} > {\\rm{SnC}}{{\\rm{l}}_2}$ since ${\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{n}}^{4 + }}$  has more positive charge than  ${\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{n}}^{2 + }}$.<br>$ \\bullet $ ${\\rm{CuCl}} > {\\rm{NaCl}}$ since ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{u}}^ + }$  has smaller size than ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^ + }$.<br>So, the correct order of covalent bond is given in B, C and E only.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
