(16796,'chemistry',48,757,1634,'Oxidising power of chlorine in aqueous solution can be determined by the parameters indicated below:<br>$\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}({\\rm{g}}) \\to {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{   -   }}}}({\\rm{aq}})$<br>(using the data,<br>$\\mathrm{\\Delta_{\\text {diss }} H_{C l_{2}}^{o}=240 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}, \\Delta_{e g} H_{C l}^{o}=-349 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$,<br>$\\mathrm{\\left.\\Delta_{h y d} H_{C l^{-}}^{o}=-381 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\right)}$, will be','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{+152 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-610 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-850 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{+120 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The energy involved in the conversion of $\\mathrm{\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})}$ to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cl}^{-1}(\\mathrm{aq})}$ is given by<br>$\\mathrm{\\Delta H=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\Delta_{\\text {diss }} H_{C l_{2}}^{(-)}+\\Delta_{e g} H_{C l}^{(-)}+\\Delta_{h y l} H_{C l}^{(-)}}$<br>Substituting various values from given data, we get<br>$\\mathrm{\\Delta H=9\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2} \\times 240\\right)+(-349)+(-381) k J m o l^{-1}}$<br>$\\mathrm{=(120-349-381) \\mathrm{kJ} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}=-610 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
