(16813,'chemistry',48,763,1661,'At $\\mathrm{60^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}$, dinitrogen tetroxide is fifty percent dissociated. The standard free energy change at this temperature and at one atmosphere is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-578 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{764 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{578 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-764 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{4(\\mathrm{~g})} \\rightleftharpoons 2 \\mathrm{NO}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})}}$<br>If $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{4}}$ is $\\mathrm{50 \\%}$ dissociated, the mole fraction of both the substances is given by<br>$\\mathrm{X_{\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{4}}=\\dfrac{1-0.5}{1+0.5} ; X_{\\mathrm{NO}_{2}}=\\dfrac{2 \\times 0.5}{1+0.5}}$<br>$\\mathrm{p_{\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{4}}=\\dfrac{0.5}{1.5} \\times 1 \\mathrm{~atm}, p_{\\mathrm{NO}_{2}}=\\dfrac{1}{1.5} \\times 1 \\mathrm{~atm}}$<br>The equilibrium constant $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{p}}}$ is given by<br>$\\rm{K_{p}=\\dfrac{\\left(p_{\\mathrm{NO}_{2}}\\right)^{2}}{p_{\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{4}}}=\\dfrac{1.5}{(1.5)^{2}(0.5)}=1.33 \\mathrm{~atm}}$<br>Since, $\\mathrm{\\Delta_{r} G^{\\circ}=-R T \\ln K_{p}}$<br>$\\rm{\\Delta_{r} G^{\\circ}=  \\left(-8.314 \\mathrm{JK}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\right) \\times(333 \\mathrm{~K}) \\\\ \\times(2.303) \\times(0.1239) \\\\= -763.8 \\mathrm{kJ} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}.}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
