(16914,'chemistry',49,617,1243,'Dihydrogen gas used in Haber\'s process is produced by reacting methane from natural gas with high temperature steam. The first stage of two stage reaction involves the formation of $\\mathrm{CO}$ and $\\mathrm{H}_{2}$. In second stage, $\\mathrm{CO}$ formed in first stage is reacted with more steam in water gas shift reaction, <br>${\\text{C}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\left( {\\text{g}} \\right)}}{\\text{ + }}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\left( {\\text{g}} \\right)}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{C}}{{\\text{O}}_{{\\text{2}}\\left( {\\text{g}} \\right)}}{\\text{ + }}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{2}}\\left( {\\text{g}} \\right)}}$<br>If a reaction vessel at $400^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is charged with an equimolar mixture of $\\mathrm{CO}$ and steam such that  ${{\\text{p}}_{{\\text{CO}}}}{\\text{ = }}{{\\text{p}}_{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}}}{\\text{ = 4}}{\\text{.0}}$  bar, what will be the partial pressure of $\\mathrm{H}_{2}$ at equilibrium? ${{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{P}}}$ =10.1 at $400^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$.','[{"text": "1 bar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 bar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 bar", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4 bar", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/49_16914_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> ${\\text{ }}{{\\text{K}}_{\\text{P}}}{\\text{ = }}\\frac{{{{\\text{p}}_{{\\text{C}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}}} \\cdot {{\\text{p}}_{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}}}}}{{{{\\text{p}}_{{\\text{CO}}}} \\cdot {{\\text{p}}_{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}}}}}{\\text{ = }}\\frac{{{\\text{p}} \\cdot {\\text{p}}}}{{({\\text{4 - p}}) \\cdot ({\\text{4 - p}})}}$ <br>${\\text{10}}.{\\text{1 = }}\\frac{{{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{2}}}}}{{{{({\\text{4 - p}})}^{\\text{2}}}}} \\Rightarrow \\sqrt {{\\text{10}}.{\\text{1}}} {\\text{ = }}\\frac{{\\text{p}}}{{({\\text{4 - p}})}}$ <br>${\\text{3}}.{\\text{17 = }}\\frac{{\\text{p}}}{{({\\text{4 - p}})}}<br>{\\text{p = }}\\frac{{{\\text{12}}.{\\text{71}}}}{{{\\text{4}}.{\\text{17}}}}{\\text{ = 3}}.{\\text{04}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{bar}}$<br>Hence, ${{\\text{p}}_{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{\\text{ = 3}}.{\\text{04 bar}}.$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
