(16916,'chemistry',48,758,1646,'The standard enthalpy of formation of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NH}_{3}}$ is $\\mathrm{-46.0 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol}}$. If the enthalpy of formation of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2}}$ from its atoms is $\\mathrm{-436 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol}}$ and that of $\\mathrm{N_{2}}$ is $\\mathrm{-712 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol}}$, the average bond enthalpy of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{N}-\\mathrm{H}}$ bond in $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NH}_{3}}$ is:','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-1102 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} / \\\\mathrm{mol}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-964 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} / \\\\mathrm{mol}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{+352 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} / \\\\mathrm{mol}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{+1056 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} / \\\\mathrm{mol}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Given<br>$\\rm{ \\dfrac{1}{2} N_{2}+\\dfrac{3}{2} H_{2} \\rightarrow N_{3} \\Delta H=-46.0 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol} \\\\ 2 H \\rightarrow H_{2} \\Delta H=-436.0 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol} \\\\ 2 N \\rightarrow N_{2} \\Delta H=-712 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol} \\\\ \\Delta H_{r}=\\sum B E_{R}-\\sum B E_{P} \\\\-46= {\\left[\\dfrac{1}{2}(+712)+\\dfrac{3}{2}(436)\\right]-3 B E_{N-H} } \\\\-46=(356+3 \\times 218)-3 B E_{N-H} \\\\ 3 B E_{N-H}=(356+654)+46 \\\\=1010+46}$<br><br>$\\rm{B E_{N-H}=\\dfrac{1056}{3}=+352 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
