(16918,'chemistry',49,617,1243,'The value of ${{\\text{K}}_{\\text{P}}}$ for the reaction, $\\mathrm{CO}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})}+\\mathrm{C}_{(\\mathrm{s})} \\rightleftharpoons 2 \\mathrm{CO}_{(\\mathrm{g})}$ is 3.0 at $1000 \\mathrm{~K}$. If initially ${{\\text{p}}_{{\\text{C}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{\\text{ = 0}}{\\text{.48}}$ bar and ${{\\rm{p}}_{{\\rm{CO}}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}$ bar and pure graphite is present, calculate the equilibrium partial pressures of $\\mathrm{CO}$ and $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$.','[{"text": "0.66 bar, 0.15 bar", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.66 bar, 0.66 bar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.15 bar, 0.15 bar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.15 bar, 0.66 bar", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'For the reaction, let \' $\\mathrm {x}$ \' be the decrease in pressure of <br>${\\text{C}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{,}}$ then<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}<br>&nbsp; {}&amp;{{\\text{C}}{{\\text{O}}_{{\\text{2(g)}}}}}&amp;{{\\text{ &nbsp;+ &nbsp;}}}&amp;{{\\text{C(s)}}}&amp; \\rightleftharpoons &amp;{{\\text{2CO(g)}}}&amp;{}&amp;{} \\\\&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; {{\\text{Intial}}}&amp;{}&amp;{}&amp;{{\\text{0}}{\\text{.48 bar}}}&amp;{}&amp;{\\text{0}}&amp;{}&amp;{} \\\\&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; {{\\text{At}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{equi}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{m:}}}&amp;{}&amp;{}&amp;{{\\text{(0}}{\\text{.48 &nbsp;- &nbsp;x)}}}&amp;{}&amp;{{\\text{2x}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{bar}}}&amp;{}&amp;{}&nbsp;<br>\\end{array}$<br>$\\rm {K_{P}=\\dfrac{\\left(P_{C O}\\right)^{2}}{P_{C O_{2}}} \\\\ K_{P}=(2 x)^{2} /(0.48-x)=3 \\\\ 4 x^{2}=3(0.48-x) \\\\ 4 x^{2}=1.44-3 x \\\\ 4 x^{2}+3 x-1.44=0} \\\\ \\mathrm{a}=4, \\mathrm{~b}=3, \\mathrm{c}=-1.44$<br>${\\text{ x &nbsp;= &nbsp;}}\\frac{{\\left( {{\\text{ &nbsp;- &nbsp;b}} \\pm \\sqrt {{{\\text{b}}^{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ &nbsp;- &nbsp;4ac}}} } \\right)}}{{{\\text{2a}}}}\\frac{{\\left[ {{\\text{ &nbsp;- &nbsp;3}} \\pm \\sqrt {{{({\\text{3}})}^{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ &nbsp;- &nbsp;4}}({\\text{4}})({\\text{ &nbsp;- &nbsp;1}}.{\\text{44}})} } \\right]}}{{{\\text{2}} \\times {\\text{4}}}}{\\text{ }}$<br>${\\text{ = &nbsp;}}({\\text{ &nbsp;- &nbsp;3}} \\pm {\\text{5}}.{\\text{66}}){\\text{/8 &nbsp;= &nbsp;}}({\\text{ &nbsp;- &nbsp;3 &nbsp;+ &nbsp;5}}.{\\text{66}}){\\text{/8}}$ as value of x cannot be<br>negative hence we neglect that value)<br>$\\rm {x=2.66 / 8=0.33}$<br>The equilibrium partial pressures are,<br>${\\text{ }}{{\\text{p}}_{{\\text{CO}}}}{\\text{ &nbsp;= &nbsp;2x &nbsp;= &nbsp;2}} \\times {\\text{0}}{\\text{.33 &nbsp;= &nbsp;0}}{\\text{.66 &nbsp;bar}}$<br>${{\\text{p}}_{{\\text{C}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{\\text{ = &nbsp;0}}{\\text{.48 &nbsp;- }} \\times {\\text{ = &nbsp;0}}{\\text{.48 &nbsp;- 0}}{\\text{.33 = 0}}{\\text{.15 bar}}{\\text{.}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
