(16974,'chemistry',48,758,1635,'At $\\mathrm{25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}$ and 1 atm pressure, the enthalpies of combustion are as given below:<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{Substance}}}&{{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}}&{{\\rm{C}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\left( {{\\rm{graphite}}} \\right)}&{{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{6}}}\\left( {\\rm{g}} \\right)}\\\\{\\frac{{{\\Delta _{\\rm{C}}}{\\rm{H}}^\\circ }}{{{\\rm{k}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{J}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{  -  1}}}}}}}&{{\\rm{  -  286}}{\\rm{.0}}}&{{\\rm{  -  394}}{\\rm{.0}}}&{{\\rm{  -  1560}}{\\rm{.0}}}\\end{array}$<br>The enthalpy of formation of ethane is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{+54.0 \\\\mathrm{kJmol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-68.0 \\\\mathrm{kJmol}{ }^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-86.0 \\\\mathrm{kJmol}{ }^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{+97.0 \\\\mathrm{kJmol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<br>$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}(\\mathrm{~g})+\\dfrac{7}{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{CO}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})+3 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}(l)}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\Delta_{\\mathrm{c}} \\mathrm{H}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}\\right)=2 \\Delta_{\\mathrm{f}} \\mathrm{H}\\left(\\mathrm{CO}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})\\right)+3 \\Delta_{\\mathrm{f}} \\mathrm{H}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}, l\\right)}$<br>$\\mathrm{-\\Delta_{\\mathrm{f}} \\mathrm{H}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}, \\mathrm{~g}\\right)}$<br>$\\mathrm{-1560=2(-394)+3(-286)-\\Delta_{\\mathrm{f}} \\mathrm{H}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}, \\mathrm{~g}\\right)}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\Delta_{\\mathrm{f}} \\mathrm{H}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}, \\mathrm{~g}\\right)=-86 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mole}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16975,'chemistry',46,442,887,'The bond order of the $\\mathrm{N}-\\mathrm{O}$ bonds in $\\mathrm{NO}_{3}^{-}$ ion is','[{"text": "0.33", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.00", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.33", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1.50", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The resonance structures of  ${\\rm{NO}}_3^ - $ ions are as : <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_16975_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  ${\\rm{The}}\\,{\\rm{N - O}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{bond}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{order}}$<br>$ = \\frac{{{\\rm{ number}}\\,{\\rm{ of }}\\,{\\rm{bonds}}\\,{\\rm{ between  two}}\\,{\\rm{ atoms }}}}{{{\\rm{ total }}\\,{\\rm{number}}\\,{\\rm{ of }}\\,{\\rm{resonating }}\\,{\\rm{structure }}}}$<br>$=\\dfrac{4}{3}=1.33$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16978,'chemistry',46,444,890,'Which of the following fluoride of xenon has zero dipole moment?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{XeF}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{XeF}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{XeF}_{4}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{XeF}_{6}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Symmetrical structures have zero dipole moment. Among the given compounds, $\\mathrm{XeF}_{4}$ has square planar structure as : <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_16978_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Thus, its dipole moment is zero.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16979,'chemistry',50,837,1867,'Oxidation state of $\\rm{{{\\rm{N}}^{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{N}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{N}}^{\\rm{3}}}}$ in the compound ${\\rm{H}}{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ (hydrazoic acid), shown in below figure, are:','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{0,0,3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{0,0,-1}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{1,1,-3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-3,-3,-3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/50_16979_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> $\\mathrm{N^{1}}$ and $\\mathrm{N^{2}}$ has oxidation state zero because they<br>are linked to each other.<br>For $\\mathrm{N^{3}, X+0+0+1=0}$<br>$\\rm{X=-1}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/50_16979_question_1.png'),
(16980,'chemistry',48,755,1629,'Consider the following statements for the given reactions:<br>(I) $\\mathrm{\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{~N}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})+\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{NO}(\\mathrm{g})}$;<br>$\\rm{\\Delta_{\\mathrm{r}} \\mathrm{H}^{\\mathrm{o}}=90 \\mathrm{kJmol}^{-1}}$<br>(II) $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NO}(\\mathrm{g})+\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{NO}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})}$;<br>$\\rm{\\Delta_{\\mathrm{r}} \\mathrm{H}^{\\circ}=-74 \\mathrm{kJmol}^{-1}}$<br>I. In reaction (I), $\\mathrm{N O(g)}$ is unstable because the energy is released and unstable $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NO}(\\mathrm{g})}$ changes into the stable $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NO}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})}$.<br>(II) The energy is absorbed in reaction (i) , $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NO}(\\mathrm{g})}$ is unstable and unstable $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NO}(\\mathrm{g})}$ changes into the stable $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NO}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})}$.<br>Select the correct statements and choose the correct option','[{"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement II is correct, while the other statements are incorrect.<br>Corrected form are as follows:<br>In reaction (i) energy is absorbed, hence NO become unstable.<br>So, in reaction (ii) transform to stable $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NO}_{2}}$ by releasing energy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(16981,'chemistry',49,624,1266,'Calculate the degree of ionisation of ${\\text{0}}{\\text{.05}}\\,\\,{\\text{M}}$  acetic acid in ${\\text{0}}{\\text{.01}}\\,\\,{\\text{M}}$ ${\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{HCl}}$  if its  ${\\rm{p}}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{a}}}$  value is 4.74.','[{"text": "$1.82 \\\\times 10^{-2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1.82 \\\\times 10^{-3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$1.82 \\\\times 10^{-4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1.82 \\\\times 10^{-5}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm {\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{a}}=-\\log \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{a}}}$<br>$\\mathrm {4.74=-\\log \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{a}}}$<br>$\\mathrm {\\log \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{a}}=-4.74=\\overline{5} .26}$<br>${{\\text{K}}_{\\text{a}}}{\\text{  =  antilog}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\overline {\\text{5}} {\\text{.26  =  1}}{\\text{.82 }} \\times {\\text{1}}{{\\text{0}}^{{\\text{  -  5}}}}$ <br>In the presence of ${\\text{0}}.{\\text{01 M }}{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ + }}}$<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {}&{{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{COOH}}}& \\rightleftharpoons &{{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CO}}{{\\text{O}}^{\\text{ - }}}\\,{\\text{ + }}}&{{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ + }}}} \\\\ \n  {{\\text{Initial}}\\,{\\text{conc}}{\\text{.}}}&{{\\text{0}}{\\text{.005}}\\,{\\text{M}}}&{}&{\\text{0}}&{\\text{0}} \\\\ \n  {{\\text{Equili}}\\,{\\text{conc}}{\\text{.}}}&{{\\text{0}}{\\text{.05-C} \\alpha}}&{}&{{\\text{C}\\alpha}}&{{\\text{C} \\alpha}} \n\\end{array}$<br>$\\rm {(\\mathrm{C} \\alpha+0.01) \\approx 0.05 \\approx 0.01}$<br>$\\mathrm {\\left[\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOH}\\right.}$ is a weak acid and $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{HCl}}$ is a strong acid so we can assume that $\\mathrm {(\\mathrm{C} \\alpha+0.01) \\approx 0.01]}$<br>$\\rm {\\therefore \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{a}}=\\dfrac{\\left[\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COO}^{-}\\right]\\left[\\mathrm{H}^{+}\\right]}{\\left[\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOH}\\right]}}$<br>$\\mathrm {1.82 \\times 10^{-5}=\\dfrac{\\mathrm{C} \\alpha \\times 0.01}{0.05}}$<br>$\\mathrm {\\mathrm{C} \\alpha=\\dfrac{1.82 \\times 10^{-5} \\times 0.05}{0.01}=9.1 \\times 10^{-5}}$<br>$\\mathrm {\\mathrm{C} \\alpha=9.1 \\times 10^{-5}}$<br>$\\mathrm {\\alpha=\\dfrac{9.1 \\times 10^{-5}}{0.05}=1.82 \\times 10^{-3}}$<br>In the presence of strong acid, dissociation of weak acid i.e., $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOH}}$ decreases due to common ion effect.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
