(16986,'chemistry',46,448,898,'What is hybridisation of ${\\rm{\'O\'}}$ in $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$ ?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{sp}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{sp}^{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{sp}^{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No hybridisation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In gaseous state, water exists as discrete $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$ molecule, in which the central $\\mathrm{O}$-atom contains four $\\mathrm{sp}^{3}$-hybridised orbitals, two of which are half - filled and used in overlapping with 1s orbital of $\\mathrm{H}$-atom to give two $\\mathrm{sp}^{3}-\\mathrm{s}, \\mathrm{O}-\\mathrm{H}, \\sigma$-bond while the remaining two exist as lone pair. The geometry of the molecule is angular or $\\mathrm{V}$-shape. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_16986_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
