(17045,'chemistry',46,449,905,'The common features among the species $\\mathrm{CN}^{-}, \\mathrm{CO}$ and $\\mathrm{NO}^{+}$are','[{"text": "bond order three and isoelectronic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "bond order three and weak field ligands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "bond order two and $\\\\pi$-acceptor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "isoelectronic and weak field ligands", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{CN}^{-}$ion Total number of electrons <br>$6+7+1=14$<br>MO configuration is<br>$\\sigma 1\\,{{\\rm{s}}^2},\\mathop \\sigma \\limits^*1 {{\\rm{s}}^2},\\mathop \\sigma \\limits^{} 2\\,{{\\rm{s}}^2},\\mathop \\sigma \\limits^ *  2\\,{{\\rm{s}}^2},\\pi 2{\\rm{p}}_{\\rm{x}}^2$<br>$\\approx \\pi 2 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{y}}^{2}, \\sigma 2 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{z}}^{2}$<br>Bond order $=\\dfrac{10-4}{2}=3$<br>CO molecule Total number of valence electrons<br> $=6+8=14$<br>MO configuration is<br>$\\sigma {\\rm{1}}\\,{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}},\\mathop \\sigma \\limits^{\\rm{*}} {\\rm{1}}\\,{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}},\\sigma {\\rm{2}}\\,{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}},\\mathop \\sigma \\limits^{\\rm{*}} {\\rm{2}}\\,{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}},\\pi {\\rm{2p}}_{\\rm{x}}^{\\rm{2}},$<br>$\\pi 2{\\rm{p}}_{\\rm{y}}^2,\\sigma 2{\\rm{p}}_{\\rm{z}}^2$<br>Bond order $ = \\frac{{10 - 4}}{2} = 3$<br>$\\mathrm{NO}^{+}$ion Total number of valence electrons$=7+8-1=14$<br>MO configuration is<br>$\\sigma 1\\,{{\\rm{s}}^2},\\mathop \\sigma \\limits^* 1\\,{{\\rm{s}}^2},\\sigma 2\\,{{\\rm{s}}^2},\\mathop \\sigma \\limits^* 2\\,{{\\rm{s}}^2},\\pi 2{\\rm{p}}_{\\rm{x}}^2$,<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, \\approx \\pi 2{\\rm{p}}_{\\rm{y}}^2,\\sigma 2{\\rm{p}}_{\\rm{z}}^2$<br>Bond order $ = \\frac{{10 - 4}}{2} = 3$<br>All $\\mathrm{CN}^{-}, \\mathrm{CO}$ and $\\mathrm{NO}^{+}$ion have bond order 3 and they are isoelectronic',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
