(17064,'chemistry',48,758,1646,'The bond dissociation energies of $\\mathrm{X_{2}, Y_{2}}$ and $\\mathrm{X Y}$ are in the ratio of $\\mathrm{1: 0.5: 1 . \\Delta H}$ for the formation of $\\mathrm{X Y}$ is $\\mathrm{-200 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$. The bond dissociation energy of $\\mathrm{X_{2}}$ will be','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{800 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{400 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{100 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{200 \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{X_{2}: Y_{2}: X Y}$<br>Let B.E. $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{x} \\quad \\dfrac{x}{2} \\quad x}$<br>Formation of $\\mathrm{X Y}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\dfrac{1}{2} X_{2}+\\dfrac{1}{2} Y_{2} \\rightarrow X Y ; \\Delta H=-200 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$ $\\mathrm{\\therefore \\Delta H_{\\text {reaction }}=B . E}$. of reactant ${\\rm{ -  B}}{\\rm{.E}}{\\rm{.}}$ of product<br>$\\mathrm{\\therefore \\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{\\text {reaction }}=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{x}+\\dfrac{\\mathrm{x}}{4}-\\mathrm{x}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\therefore-200 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}=\\dfrac{2 x+x-4 x}{4}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\therefore \\quad-800=2 x+x-4 x}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\therefore \\quad x=800 \\mathrm{~kJ}}$ mole<br>$\\mathrm{\\therefore}$ Bond dissociation energy is $\\mathrm{800 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mole}^{-1}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
