(17082,'chemistry',50,836,1862,'Identify the compound among the following that cannot act as a reducing agent is','[{"text": "Sulfur dioxide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sulfuric acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hydrogen peroxide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrogen", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Oxidation state of sulfur in sulfuric acid is its maximum $\\mathrm{(+6)}$ exhibited in any of its compounds. Hence it cannot be further oxidised to any higher oxidation state by acting as a reducing agent.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17083,'chemistry',49,617,1243,'At a certain temperature and total pressure of $10^{5} \\mathrm{~Pa}$, iodine vapour contains $40 \\%$ by volume of ${\\text{ I}}$  atoms ${{\\text{I}}_{{\\text{2(g)}}}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{2}}{{\\text{I}}_{\\left( {\\text{g}} \\right)}}$<br>Calculate ${{\\text{K}}_{\\text{P}}}$ for the equilibrium.','[{"text": "${\\\\text{2}}{\\\\text{.67 x 1}}{{\\\\text{0}}^{\\\\text{4}}}{\\\\text{ bar}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2.67 \\\\times 10^{3} \\\\mathrm{~Pa}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2.67 \\\\times 10^{4} \\\\mathrm{~Pa}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{2}}{\\\\text{.67 x 1}}{{\\\\text{0}}^{\\\\text{3}}}{\\\\text{ bar}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${{\\text{P}}_{\\text{I}}}{\\text{   =   }}\\frac{{{\\text{40 }} \\times {\\text{ 1}}{{\\text{0}}^{\\text{5}}}}}{{{\\text{100}}}}{\\text{Pa;}}$ ${{\\text{P}}_{{{\\text{I}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{\\text{   =   }}\\frac{{{\\text{60  }} \\times {\\text{1}}{{\\text{0}}^{\\text{5}}}}}{{{\\text{100}}}}{\\text{Pa}}$<br>$\\rm {K_{P}=\\dfrac{p_{I}^{2}}{p_{I_{2}}}}$<br>${\\text{ = }}\\frac{{{{\\left( {\\frac{{{\\text{40}} \\times {\\text{1}}{{\\text{0}}^{\\text{5}}}}}{{{\\text{100}}}}} \\right)}^2}}}{{\\frac{{{\\text{60}} \\times {\\text{1}}{{\\text{0}}^{\\text{5}}}}}{{{\\text{100}}}}}}$<br>${\\text{ = }}\\frac{{{\\text{16}} \\times {\\text{1}}{{\\text{0}}^{{\\text{12}}}}}}{{{\\text{6}} \\times {\\text{1}}{{\\text{0}}^{\\text{8}}}}}$<br>${\\text{  =  2}}{\\text{.67}} \\times {\\text{1}}{{\\text{0}}^{\\text{4}}}{\\text{ Pa}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17084,'chemistry',48,751,1617,'Which of the following $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{p}-\\mathrm{V}}$ curve represents maximum work done?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{p}-\\mathrm{V}}$ graph, area under the curve represent magnitude of work.<br>It is maximum in graph-1, So, correct answer is (1).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17085,'chemistry',46,446,892,'The bond angles of $\\mathrm{NH}_{3}, \\mathrm{NH}_{4}^{+}$and $\\mathrm{NH}_{2}^{-}$ are in the order','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}^{-}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{4}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{4}^{+}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}^{-}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}^{-}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{4}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{4}^{+}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}^{-}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'As the number of lone pairs of electrons increases, bond angle decreases. Thus, the order of bond angle is<br>$\\mathrm{NH}_{4}^{+}>\\mathrm{NH}_{3}>\\mathrm{NH}_{2}^{-}$<br>$\\text { (no l.p.) } \\quad \\text { (1 l.p.) } \\quad \\text { ( } 2 \\text { l.p.) }$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
