(17162,'chemistry',48,757,1633,'For the thermochemical equation, $\\mathrm{2 \\mathrm{H}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})}+\\mathrm{O}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{(1)}: \\Delta \\mathrm{H}=-571.6 \\mathrm{~kJ}}$<br>Heat of decomposition of water is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-571.6 \\\\mathrm{~kJ}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{+571.6 \\\\mathrm{~kJ}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-1143.2 \\\\mathrm{~kJ}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{+285.8 \\\\mathrm{~kJ}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{(1)} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})}+\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})}}$;<br>$\\rm{\\Delta \\mathrm{H}=\\dfrac{571.6}{2}=285.8 \\mathrm{~kJ}}$<br>Since, the forward reaction is exothermic, backward has to be endothermic.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
