(17166,'chemistry',48,756,1631,'If $\\mathrm{38.55 \\mathrm{~kJ}}$ of heat is absorbed, when 6.0 of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{O}_{2}}$ react $\\mathrm{C l F}$ according to reaction.<br>$\\mathrm{2 \\mathrm{CIF}(\\mathrm{g})+\\mathrm{O}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})+\\mathrm{OF}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})}$<br>What is the standard enthalpy of reaction?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{102.8 \\\\mathrm{~kJ}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{49.80 \\\\mathrm{~kJ}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{72.28 \\\\mathrm{~kJ}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{205.6 \\\\mathrm{~kJ}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Given, Enthalpy change for a given mass $\\mathrm{=38.55 \\mathrm{~kJ}}$ Mass of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{O}_{2}=6.0 \\mathrm{~g}}$<br>Number of moles of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{O}_{2}=\\dfrac{\\text { Mass of } \\mathrm{O}_{2}}{\\text { Molar mass of } \\mathrm{O}_{2}}}$<br>$\\rm{=\\dfrac{6 \\mathrm{~g}}{32 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}=0.1875 \\mathrm{~mol}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\therefore}$ Enthalpy change for 1 mole $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{O}_{2}}$<br>$\\rm{=\\dfrac{38.55 \\mathrm{~kJ}}{0.1875}=205.6 \\mathrm{~kJ}}$<br>From the reaction, 2 moles of CIF react with 1 mole of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{O}_{2}}$.<br>So, the standard enthalpy of reaction is +205.6 $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{kJ}}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
