(17183,'chemistry',48,761,1652,'For a process, entropy change of a system is expressed as','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{H}-\\\\mathrm{TS}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\dfrac{q_{\\\\text {rev }}}{T}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\dfrac{\\\\mathrm{T}}{\\\\mathrm{q}_{\\\\mathrm{rev}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{q_{\\\\text {rev }} \\\\times T}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'For an isothermal reversible process, let the system absorbs $\\mathrm{q}$ amount of heat from surroundings at temperature T. Thus, the entropy change of system will be $\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{System}}=\\dfrac{\\mathrm{q}_{\\mathrm{rev}}}{\\mathrm{T}}}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2019,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
