(17219,'chemistry',49,629,1278,'The $\\mathrm{pH}$ of an acid buffer can be raised by 2 units by','[{"text": "Increasing the concentration of both weak acid and salt by two moles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increasing the concentration of both the acid and salt by 10 times", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diluting the solution by 10 times", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increasing the concentration of the salt by 10 times and decreasing concentration of the acid by 10 times.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\rm {{\\text{p}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{1}}}{\\text{ = p}}{{\\text{K}}_{\\text{a}}}{\\text{ + log}}\\left( {\\dfrac{{{\\text{ Salt }}}}{{{\\text{ Acid }}}}} \\right)}$<br>$\\rm {{\\text{p}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{1}}}{\\text{ = p}}{{\\text{K}}_{\\text{a}}}{\\text{ + log}}\\left( {\\dfrac{{{{\\text{x}}_{\\text{1}}}}}{{{{\\text{y}}_{\\text{1}}}}}} \\right)}$, $\\rm {{\\text{p}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ = p}}{{\\text{K}}_{\\text{a}}}{\\text{ + log}}\\left( {\\dfrac{{{{\\text{x}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{{{{\\text{y}}_{\\text{2}}}}}} \\right)}$<br>$\\rm {{\\text{p}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ - p}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{1}}}{\\text{ = log}}\\dfrac{{{{\\text{x}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{{{{\\text{y}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{\\text{ - log}}\\dfrac{{{{\\text{x}}_{\\text{1}}}}}{{{{\\text{y}}_{\\text{1}}}}}}$$\\rm {{\\text{2 = log}}\\left( {\\dfrac{{{{\\text{x}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{/}}{{\\text{y}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{{{{\\text{x}}_{\\text{1}}}{\\text{/}}{{\\text{y}}_{\\text{1}}}}}} \\right)}$ $\\therefore \\dfrac{{{{\\text{x}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{/}}{{\\text{y}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{{{{\\text{x}}_{\\text{1}}}{\\text{/}}{{\\text{y}}_{\\text{1}}}}}{\\text{  =  1}}{{\\text{0}}^{\\text{2}}}{\\text{  =  100}}$<br>This is only possible, if the concentration of salt is increased by 10 times and the concentration of acid is decreased by 10 times.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17221,'chemistry',48,748,1608,'A cycle tyre bursts suddenly. What is the type of this process?','[{"text": "Isochoric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isothermal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isobaric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adiabatic", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'For an isochoric process, work done by the gas $\\mathrm{=-\\mathrm{P} \\Delta \\mathrm{V}}$<br>$\\rm{\\begin{gathered}\\Delta \\mathrm{U}=\\mathrm{q}+\\mathrm{w} \\\\\\Delta \\mathrm{U}=\\mathrm{q}-\\mathrm{P} \\Delta \\mathrm{V}\\end{gathered}}$<br>when $\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{V}=0, \\Delta \\mathrm{U}=\\mathrm{q}}$ or qv<br>(2) For an adiabatic process, $\\mathrm{q=0, \\Delta U=w}$<br>(3) For an isothermal process,<br>$\\rm{\\Delta \\mathrm{U}=0, \\mathrm{q}=-\\mathrm{w}}$<br>(4) For a cyclic process, $\\mathrm{\\Delta U=0}$<br>$\\rm{\\therefore \\mathrm{q}=-\\mathrm{w}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
