(17230,'chemistry',49,632,1293,'Specify if addition of the second substance in each of the following increases (i) or decreases (D), <br>the solubility of the first substance.<br>(I) $\\mathrm{Al}(\\mathrm{OH})_{3}, \\mathrm{NaOH}$  <br>(II) $\\mathrm{PbCl}_{2}, \\mathrm{~Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_{3}\\right)_{2}$  <br>(III) $\\mathrm{CuSO}_{4}, \\mathrm{NH}_{3}$','[{"text": "I -D, II-i, III-i", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I-i, II-D, III-i", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I-i, II-D, III-i", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I-D, II-D, III-i", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'(I) Adding $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{NaOH}}$ increases solubility of $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{Al}(\\mathrm{OH})_{3}}$ by forming complex $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{Na}\\left[\\mathrm{Al}(\\mathrm{OH})_{4}\\right]}$ <br>(II) Adding $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_{3}\\right)_{2}}$ to saturated $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{PbCl}_{2}}$ will decrease solubility by common ion effect<br>(III) Adding ammonia will increase solubility by forming $\\mathrm {\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{4}\\right]^{2+}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17233,'chemistry',48,751,1612,'Which among the following equations represents the first law of thermodynamics under isobaric conditions?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{U}=\\\\mathrm{q}_{\\\\mathrm{p}}-\\\\mathrm{p}_{\\\\mathrm{ex}} \\\\cdot \\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{V}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{q}_{\\\\mathrm{v}}=\\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{U}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\Delta U=W}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{W  =   -  q}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'According to first law of thermodynamics, $\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{U}=\\mathrm{q}+\\mathrm{W}}$. In case of isobaric conditions, change of state is brought about at constant pressure, i.e. $\\mathrm{d p=0}$. Moreover, work done for a process is given as $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{W}=-\\mathrm{p}_{\\text {ext. }} \\Delta \\mathrm{V}}$.<br>Substituting the value of \' $\\mathrm{W}$ \' in first law of thermodynamics<br>$\\rm{\\Delta \\mathrm{U}=\\mathrm{q}_{\\mathrm{p}}-\\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{ext} .} \\cdot \\Delta \\mathrm{V}}$<br>So, option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17234,'chemistry',49,632,1290,'Which expression correctly represents solubility product for,<br>${\\text{Ba(OH}}{{\\text{)}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{.8}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O(s)}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{B}}{{\\text{a}}^{{\\text{2  +  }}}}{\\text{(aq)  +  2O}}{{\\text{H}}^{{\\text{  -  }}}}{\\text{(aq)  +  8}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O(l)?}}$','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{K}}_{{\\\\rm{SP}}}}{\\\\rm{ = }}\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{B}}{{\\\\rm{a}}^{{\\\\rm{2 + }}}}} \\\\right]{\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{O}}{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}} \\\\right]^{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{K}}_{{\\\\rm{SP}}}}{\\\\rm{ = }}\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{B}}{{\\\\rm{a}}^{{\\\\rm{2 + }}}}} \\\\right]{\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{2O}}{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}} \\\\right]^{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{K}}_{{\\\\rm{SP}}}}{\\\\rm{ = }}\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{B}}{{\\\\rm{a}}^{{\\\\rm{2 + }}}}} \\\\right]{\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{O}}{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}} \\\\right]^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\left[ {{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}} \\\\right]^{\\\\rm{8}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{K}}_{{\\\\rm{SP}}}}{\\\\rm{ = }}\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{B}}{{\\\\rm{a}}^{{\\\\rm{2 + }}}}} \\\\right]{\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{O}}{{\\\\rm{H}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}} \\\\right]^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{8}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}} \\\\right]^{\\\\rm{8}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hydration does not influence the$\\rm {{{\\rm{K}}_{{\\rm{sp}}}}}$ value.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17236,'chemistry',50,837,1867,'Which of the following arrangements represent increasing oxidation number of the central atom?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{CrO}_{2}^{-}, \\\\mathrm{ClO}_{3}^{-}, \\\\mathrm{CrO}_{4}^{2-}, \\\\mathrm{MnO}_{4}^{-}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{ClO}_{3}^{-}, \\\\mathrm{CrO}_{4}^{2-}, \\\\mathrm{MnO}_{4}^{-}, \\\\mathrm{CrO}_{2}^{-}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{CrO}_{2}^{-}, \\\\mathrm{ClO}_{3}^{-}, \\\\mathrm{MnO}_{4}^{-}, \\\\mathrm{CrO}_{4}^{2-}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{CrO}_{4}^{2-}, \\\\mathrm{MnO}_{4}^{-}, \\\\mathrm{CrO}_{2}^{-}, \\\\mathrm{ClO}_{3}^{-}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'O.N of<br>$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cr}}$ in $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CrO}_{2}^{-}}$is +3<br>$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cl}}$ in $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{ClO}_{3}^{-}}$is +5<br>$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cr}}$ in $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CrO}_{4}^{2-}}$ is +6<br>$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Mn}}$ in $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{MnO}_{4}^{-}}$is +7',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17237,'chemistry',48,751,1612,'Based on first law of thermodynamics which of the following is correct ?','[{"text": "for an isobaric process, $\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{q}_{\\\\mathrm{p}}=\\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{U}+\\\\mathrm{w}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "for an adiabatic process, $\\\\mathrm{\\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{U}=-\\\\mathrm{W}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "for an isochoric process, $\\\\mathrm{\\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{U}=-\\\\mathrm{q}_{\\\\mathrm{v}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "for an isothermal process, $\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{q}=+\\\\mathrm{w}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In isobaric process, pressure is constant and volume increases from $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{V}_{1}}$ to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{V}_{2}}$ due to the absorption of heat. According to the first law of thermodynamics, $\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{U}=\\mathrm{q}+\\mathrm{W}}$<br>At constant pressure, $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{q}_{\\mathrm{p}}=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}-\\mathrm{W}}$<br>${{\\rm{q}}_{\\rm{p}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\Delta {\\rm{U - p}}\\Delta {\\rm{V}}$<br>${{\\rm{q}}_{\\rm{p}}}{\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{U}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ - }}{{\\rm{U}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\left( {{\\rm{ - p}}\\left( {{{\\rm{V}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ - }}{{\\rm{V}}_{\\rm{1}}}} \\right)} \\right)$<br>${{\\rm{q}}_{\\rm{p}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\left( {{{\\rm{U}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ + p}}{{\\rm{V}}_{\\rm{2}}}} \\right){\\rm{ - }}\\left( {{{\\rm{U}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ + p}}{{\\rm{V}}_{\\rm{1}}}} \\right)$<br>${{\\rm{q}}_{\\rm{p}}}{\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ - }}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{1}}}$<br>${{\\rm{q}}_{\\rm{p}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\Delta {\\rm{H}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{(1)}}$<br>As we know, $\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{H}=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}+\\mathrm{p} \\Delta \\mathrm{V}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{H}=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}+\\mathrm{W}}$<br>Putting the value of $\\Delta {\\rm{H}}\\,\\,in\\,\\,(1)$<br>$\\rm{\\mathrm{q}_{\\mathrm{p}}=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}+\\mathrm{W}}$<br>Other corrected options are as follows:<br>$ \\bullet $ For adibatic process, $\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{U}=\\mathrm{W}}$<br>$ \\bullet $ For an isochoric process, $\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{U}=\\mathrm{q}_{\\mathrm{v}}}$<br>$ \\bullet $ For an isothermal process $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{q}=-\\mathrm{W}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2010,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17238,'chemistry',49,632,1291,'The solubility product constant of $\\mathrm{Ag}_{2} \\mathrm{CrO}_{4}$ and $\\mathrm{AgBr}$ are $1.1 \\times 10^{-12}$ and $5.0 \\times 10^{-13}$ respectively. Calculate the ratio of the solubilities of their saturated solutions.','[{"text": "72", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "82", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "92", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "112", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\text{A}}{{\\text{g}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{Cr}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{2A}}{{\\text{g}}^{\\text{ + }}}{\\text{ + CrO}}_{\\text{4}}^{{\\text{2 - }}}{\\text{;}}{{\\text{K}}_{{\\text{sp}}}}{\\text{ = 1}}{\\text{.1  1}}{{\\text{0}}^{{\\text{ - 12}}}}$<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{S}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{2S}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{S}}$<br>(solubility of $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{AgBr}}$ is $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{S} \\mathrm{mol} \\mathrm{L}^{-1}}$ )<br>$\\mathrm {\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}=\\left[A g^{+}\\right]\\left[B r^{-}\\right]=S . S=S^{2}}$<br>or $\\mathrm {S=\\sqrt{K_{s p}}=\\sqrt{5.0 \\times 10^{-13}}=\\sqrt{50 \\times 10^{-14}}}$<br>$\\mathrm {S=7.07 \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{M}}$<br>Ratio of their solubilities<br>$\\mathrm {\\dfrac{S\\left(\\mathrm{Ag}_{2} \\mathrm{CrO}_{4}\\right)}{S(\\mathrm{AgBr})}=\\dfrac{6.50 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{M}}{7.07 \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{M}}=91.93 \\approx 92}$<br>$\\mathrm {\\mathrm{Ag}_{2} \\mathrm{CrO}_{4}}$ is 92 times more soluble than $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{AgBr}}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17239,'chemistry',46,446,892,'In a regular octahedral molecule, $\\mathrm{SF}_{6}$, the number of $\\mathrm{F}-\\mathrm{M}-\\mathrm{F}$ bonds at $180^{\\circ}$ is ____.','[{"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/46_17239_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{{{\\rm{F}}^{\\rm{1}}} - {\\rm{M}} - {{\\rm{F}}^{\\rm{3}}}}&{{{\\rm{F}}^{\\rm{2}}} - {\\rm{M}} - {{\\rm{F}}^{\\rm{4}}},}\\\\\n{{{\\rm{F}}^{\\rm{5}}} - {\\rm{M}} - {{\\rm{F}}^{\\rm{6}}}}&{{\\rm{Each}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} 180^\\circ .}\n\\end{array}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
