(17306,'chemistry',46,444,890,'Bond length in HCl is 1.275 $ \\mathop {\\rm{A}}^{\\circ}  $ and experimental value of dipole moment is 1.03 D . Percentage ionic character of HCl will be?','[{"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "10", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "21.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "16.83", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{For}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{HCl}}\\,{{\\rm{\\mu }}_{{\\rm{exp}}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}.{\\rm{03D}}$<br>${\\rm{Bond}}\\,{\\rm{length = 1}}.{\\rm{275}}$$ \\mathop {\\rm{A}}^{\\circ}  $<br>$ = 1.275 \\times {10^{ - 8}}\\,{\\rm{cm}}$<br>${\\rm{Charge}}\\,{\\mkern 1mu}\\, {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{electron}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{ = }}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{4}}.{\\rm{8}} \\times {\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 10}}}}{\\rm{esu}}$<br>$1{\\rm{D}} = {10^{ - 18}}{\\rm{ esu \\, cm}}$<br>${\\rm{\\% \\, Ionic}}{\\kern 1pt} \\,{\\rm{character}}\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,{\\rm{HCl}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1}}.{\\rm{03}} \\times {\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 18}}}} \\times {\\rm{100}}}}{{{\\rm{4}}.{\\rm{8}} \\times {\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 10}}}} \\times {\\rm{1}}.{\\rm{275}} \\times {\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 8}}}}}}$<br>$ = 16.83\\% $',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17308,'chemistry',50,836,1860,'Which of the following statements is/are correct about reduction reaction?<br>I. Removal of electronegative element.<br>II. Removal of electropositive element.<br>III. Adition of electronegative element.<br>IV. Addition of electropositive element.<br>Select the correct option','[{"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Reduction is the process which involves removal of oxygen or electronegative element from a substance or addition of hydrogen or electropositive element to a substance.<br>Therefore, statement I and IV are correct and, hence option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17311,'chemistry',48,757,1634,'The following two reaction are known<br>${\\rm{F}}{{\\rm{e}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}({\\rm{s}}){\\rm{ + 3CO}}({\\rm{g}}) \\to {\\rm{2Fe}}({\\rm{s}}){\\rm{ + 3C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}({\\rm{g}});$<br>$\\Delta {\\rm{H =  - 26}}.{\\rm{8}}\\,{\\rm{kJ}}$<br>${\\rm{FeO}}({\\rm{s}}){\\rm{ + CO}}({\\rm{g}}) \\to {\\rm{Fe}}({\\rm{s}}){\\rm{ + C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}({\\rm{g}});$<br>$\\Delta {\\rm{H =  - 16}}.{\\rm{5}}\\,{\\rm{kJ}}$<br>The value of $\\mathrm{\\Delta H}$ for the following reaction $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Fe}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}(s)+\\mathrm{CO}(\\mathrm{g}) \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{FeO}(s)+\\mathrm{CO}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})}$ is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{+10.3 \\\\mathrm{~kJ}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-43.3 \\\\mathrm{~kJ}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{-10.3 \\\\mathrm{~kJ}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{6.2 \\\\mathrm{~kJ}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Given<br>${\\text{F}}{{\\text{e}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{ + 3CO}} \\to {\\text{2Fe + 3C}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}};$<br>$\\Delta {\\rm{H  =    - 26}}.{\\rm{8}}\\,{\\rm{kJ}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{(1)}}$<br>${\\text{FeO + CO}} \\to {\\text{Fe + C}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}};$<br>$\\Delta {\\rm{H  =    - 16}}.{\\rm{5}}\\,{\\rm{kJ}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{(2)}}$<br>Aim, $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Fe}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}+\\mathrm{CO} \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{FeO}+\\mathrm{CO}_{2} ; \\mathrm{\\Delta H}=}$ ?<br>eq. (1) $\\mathrm{-2 \\times e q}$. (2) gives the required eq.<br>With, $\\mathrm{\\Delta H=-26.8+33=6.2 \\mathrm{~kJ}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17312,'chemistry',50,838,1874,'When chlorine gas passes through a concentrated solution of alkali.<br>I. $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}}$ is oxidised to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{ClO}^{-}}$ <br>II. $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}}$ is reduced to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}}$<br>III. Products formed are $\\mathrm{5 \\mathrm{Cl}^{-}, \\mathrm{ClO}_{3}^{-}}$and $\\mathrm{3 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}}$.<br>Which of the above statement is/are correct?','[{"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statement II and III are correct, while the statement I is incorrect. Its correct form is as follows<br>When chlorine gas passes through a concentrated solution of alkali, the following chemical reaction occurs.<br>$\\rm{\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}+\\mathrm{OH}^{-}(\\mathrm{aq}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Cl}^{-1}(\\mathrm{aq})+\\mathrm{ClO}_{3}^{-}}$<br>Thus, $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}}$ is reduced.<br>After balancing this equation, we have<br>$\\rm{\\underset{3 \\mathrm{~mol}}{3 \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}}+\\underset{6 \\mathrm{~mol}}{6 \\mathrm{OH}^{-}}(\\mathrm{aq}) \\rightarrow 5 \\mathrm{Cl}^{-}(\\mathrm{aq})+\\mathrm{ClO}_{3}^{-}(\\mathrm{aq})+3 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
