(17459,'chemistry',49,629,1279,'$50 \\mathrm{~mL}$ of ${\\text{0}}{\\text{.2}}\\,\\,{\\text{M}}$  ammonia solution is treated with $25 \\mathrm{~mL}$ of $0.2{\\rm{M}}\\,\\,{\\rm{HCl}}$. If  ${\\rm{p}}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{b}}}$ of ammonia solution is ${\\text{4}}{\\text{.75,}}$  the $\\mathrm{pH}$ of the mixture will be','[{"text": "3.75", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4.75", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8.25", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "9.25", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm {\\mathrm{NH}_{3}+\\mathrm{HCl} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}}$<br>moles of<br>$\\rm {\\mathrm{HCl}=0.2 \\mathrm{M} \\times 25 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~L}=0.005 \\text { moles } \\mathrm{HCl}}$<br>(total consumed)<br>moles of $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{NH}_{3}=0.2 \\mathrm{M} \\times 50 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~L}=0.01 \\mathrm{moles}}$<br>$\\mathrm {\\mathrm{HCl}}$ excess $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{NH}_{3}=0.01-0.005=0.005}$ moles<br>1 mole ammonia $\\mathrm {=1}$ mole $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}}$<br>${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.005}}\\,$ ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ ${\\rm{ = }}\\,\\,{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.005}}\\,\\,$ ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{Cl}}$<br>Total volume $\\mathrm {=V_{H C l}+V_{N H_{3}}=25+50=75 \\mathrm{~mL}}$<br>$\\rm {\\left[\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right]=\\left[\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}\\right]=\\dfrac{0.005 \\mathrm{~mole}}{75 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~L}}=0.066 \\mathrm{M}}$<br>$\\rm {p O H=p K_{b}+\\log \\dfrac{\\left[\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}\\right]}{\\left[\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right]}}$<br><br>$\\rm { p O H=4.75+\\log \\dfrac{[0.066]}{[0.066]} \\\\ p O H=4.75 \\\\ p H=14-p O H \\Rightarrow p H=9.25}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2017,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17462,'chemistry',50,839,1878,'For the reaction:<br>$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NH}_{3}+\\mathrm{OCl}^{-} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{4}+\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}}$in basic medium, the coefficients $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NH}_{3}, \\mathrm{OCl}}$ and $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{4}}$ for the balanced equation are respectively.','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{2,2,2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{2,2,1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{2,1,1}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{4,4,2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The balanced equation :<br>${\\rm{2N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ + OC}}{{\\rm{l}}^{\\rm{ - }}} \\to {{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ + C}}{{\\rm{l}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17463,'chemistry',49,619,1247,'At  ${\\text{320 K,}}$  a gas ${{\\text{A}}_{\\text{2}}}$  is  ${\\rm{20}}\\% $   dissociated to ${\\rm{A(g)}}$. The standard free energy change at $320 \\mathrm{~K}$ and $1 \\mathrm{~atm}$ in ${\\text{J}}\\,{\\text{mo}}{{\\text{l}}^{{\\text{ - 1}}}}$ is approximately:<br>${\\text{(R  =  8}}{\\text{.314J }}{{\\text{K}}^{{\\text{  -  1}}}}\\,{\\text{mo}}{{\\text{l}}^{{\\text{  -  1}}}}{\\text{; ln2  =  0}}{\\text{.693 ; ln3  =  1}}{\\text{.098)}}$','[{"text": "1844", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2068", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4281", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4763", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm {A_{2}(g) \\rightleftharpoons 2 A(g)\\{20 \\%}$ means $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{x}=0.2\\}}$<br>$\\mathrm {1 \\quad 0}$<br>$\\mathrm {1-\\mathrm{x} \\quad \\mathrm{x}}$<br>$\\mathrm {1-0.2 \\quad 2(0.2)=0.4}$<br>$\\mathrm {\\begin{array}{ll}0.8 & 0.4\\end{array}}$<br>$\\mathrm {K_{p}=\\dfrac{\\left(p_{A}\\right)^{2}}{\\left(p_{A_{2}}\\right)}=\\dfrac{0.4 \\times 0.4}{0.8}=0.2}$<br>$\\mathrm {\\Delta G^{0}=-2.303 \\times 8.314 \\times 320 \\log _{10} 0.2=4281 \\mathrm{~J} / \\mathrm{mole}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2018,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17466,'chemistry',50,844,1885,'Consider the folowing reduction processes<br>$\\mathrm{Z n^{2+}+2 e \\rightarrow Z n(S) ; E^{\\circ}=-0.76 \\mathrm{~V}}$<br>${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{a}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}{\\rm{ + 2e}} \\to {\\rm{Ca}}({\\rm{s}});{\\rm{E}}^\\circ {\\rm{ =  - 2}}.{\\rm{87}}\\,{\\rm{V}}$<br>${\\rm{M}}{{\\rm{g}}^{{\\rm{ + 2}}}}{\\rm{ + 2e}} \\to {\\rm{Mg}}({\\rm{s}});{\\rm{E}}^\\circ {\\rm{ =  - 2}}.{\\rm{36}}\\,{\\rm{V}}$<br>${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{i}}^{{\\rm{ + 2}}}}{\\rm{ + 2e}} \\to {\\rm{Ni}}({\\rm{s}});{\\rm{E}}^\\circ {\\rm{ =  - 0}}.{\\rm{25}}\\,{\\rm{V}}$<br>The reducing power of the metals increases inorder:','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Ni} < \\\\mathrm{Zn} < \\\\mathrm{Mg} < \\\\mathrm{Ca}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C a < Z n < M g < N i}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Zn} < \\\\mathrm{Mg} < \\\\mathrm{Ni} < \\\\mathrm{Ca}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Ca} < \\\\mathrm{Mg} < \\\\mathrm{Zn} < \\\\mathrm{Ni}}$<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The higher the value of reduction potential, the higher will be the oxidising power whereas the lower the value of reduction potential the higher will be reducing power.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17476,'chemistry',46,449,901,'Read the Statement ${\\mathrm{A}}$ and Statement  B carefully to mark the correct options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A ${\\mathrm{\\pi}}$ bonding MO has lower electron density above and below the internuclear axis.</div><div class="column-right">The ${{\\rm{\\pi }}^{\\rm{*}}}$ anti-bonding MO has a node between the nuclei.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Molecular orbitals obtained from ${\\mathrm{2 p_{x}}}$ and ${\\mathrm{2 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{y}}}}$ orbitals are not symmetrical around the bond axis because of the presence of positive lobes above and negative lobes below the molecular plane. Such molecular orbitals, are labelled as ${\\mathrm{\\pi}}$ and ${\\mathrm{\\pi^{*}}}$. A ${\\mathrm{\\pi}}$ bonding MO has larger electron density above and below the internuclear axis. The antibonding MO has a node between the nuclei.<br> So, the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
