(17649,'chemistry',49,621,1255,'For the reversible reaction,<br>${{\\text{N}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{(g) + 3}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{(g)}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{2N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{(g) + }}$ heat<br>The equilibrium shifts in backward direction','[{"text": "By increasing the concentration of ${\\\\text{N}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{3}}}{\\\\text{(g)}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "By decreasing the pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "By decreasing concentration of  ${{\\\\text{N}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{(g)}}\\\\,$ and  ${{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{(g)}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Given reaction is exothermic reaction. hence according to Le Chatelier\'s principle low temperature favours the forward reaction and on decreasing pressure equilibrium will shift towards more number of moles, i.e., backward direction. By increasing concentration of $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{NH}_{3}}$ and by decreasing concentration of $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{N}_{2}, \\mathrm{H}_{2}}$ favours backward reaction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(17650,'chemistry',48,751,1614,'Which of the following reactions shows work of compression?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3(\\\\mathrm{~g})}+\\\\mathrm{HCl}_{(\\\\mathrm{g})} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\\\mathrm{Cl}_{(\\\\mathrm{s})}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6(\\\\mathrm{~g})} \\\\rightarrow 2 \\\\mathrm{C}_{(\\\\mathrm{s})}+3 \\\\mathrm{H}_{2(\\\\mathrm{~g})}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2 \\\\mathrm{SO}_{3(\\\\mathrm{~g})} \\\\rightarrow 2 \\\\mathrm{SO}_{2(\\\\mathrm{~g})}+\\\\mathrm{O}_{2(\\\\mathrm{~g})}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2 \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{2(\\\\ell)} \\\\rightarrow 2 \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{(\\\\ell)}+\\\\mathrm{O}_{2(\\\\mathrm{~g})}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When gases convert into solids, it is a work of compression.<br>$\\mathrm{NH}_{3(\\mathrm{~g})}+\\mathrm{HCl}_{(\\mathrm{g})} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}_{(\\mathrm{s})}$<br>In this reaction, gaseous reactants converted into solid product which results in a decrease of volume and shows work of compression.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
