(17705,'chemistry',49,618,1246,'In the reaction ${\\text{Fe(OH}}{{\\text{)}}_{\\text{2}}}_{{\\text{(S)}}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{Fe}}_{{\\text{(aq)}}}^{{\\text{3  +  }}}{\\text{  +  3OH}}_{{\\text{(aq)}}}^{{\\text{  -  }}}$<br>If the concentration of $\\mathrm{OH}^{-}$ions is decreased by $1 / 4$ times, then the equilibrium concentration of $\\mathrm{Fe}^{3+}$ will increase by','[{"text": "8 times", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "16 times", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "64 times", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4 times", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${{\\text{K}}_{\\text{c}}}{\\text{ = }}[{\\text{x}}]{[{\\text{3x}}]^{\\text{3}}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,({\\text{I}})$<br>When concentration of $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{OH}^{-}}$ions is decresed<br>by $\\frac{{\\text{1}}}{{\\text{4}}}{\\text{times, }}{{\\text{K}}_{\\text{c}}}{\\text{ = }}\\left[ {{{\\text{x}}^{\\text{\'}}}} \\right]{\\left[ {\\frac{{{\\text{3x}}}}{{\\text{4}}}} \\right]^{\\text{3}}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{(II)}}$<br>Equation eq. (I) and (II)<br>$\\rm { x \\times(3 x)^{3}=x^{\\prime}\\left(\\dfrac{3 x}{4}\\right)^{3} \\\\ 64 x=x^{\\prime}}$<br>So, $\\mathrm {\\mathrm{x}^{\\prime}=64 \\mathrm{x}}$ or 64 times',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
