(18319,'chemistry',49,621,1255,'At constant temperature, the equilibrium constant $\\left(\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{p}}\\right)$ for the decomposition reaction, $\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{4}(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightleftharpoons 2 \\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ is expressed by,<br>$\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{p}}=\\dfrac{\\left(4 \\mathrm{x}^{2} \\mathrm{P}\\right)}{\\left(1-\\mathrm{x}^{2}\\right)}$<br>where $\\mathrm{P}=$ pressure, $\\mathrm{x}=$ extent of decomposition. Which of the following statements is true.','[{"text": "${{{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{P}}}}$ increases with increase in $\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{P}}}}$ increases with increase in $\\\\mathrm{x}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{{\\\\rm{K}}_{\\\\rm{P}}}}$ increases with decrease in $\\\\mathrm{x}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}_{\\\\mathrm{p}}$ remains constant with change in $\\\\mathrm{P}$ or $\\\\mathrm{x}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${{\\text{K}}_{\\text{P}}}$ is a characteristic constant for a given reaction and changes only with temperature.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
