(18328,'chemistry',48,752,1621,'Heat required to raise the temperature of 1 mole of a substance by $1^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is called','[{"text": "specific heat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "water equivalent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "specific gravity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "molar heat capacity", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The amount of heat required to raise the temperature of one mole of a substance through$1^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is called molar heat capacity.<br>$\\mathrm{C}=\\dfrac{\\mathrm{q}}{\\mathrm{T}_{2}-\\mathrm{T}_{1}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(18333,'chemistry',48,762,1659,'When the heat of reaction at constant pressure is $-2.5 \\times 10^{3} \\mathrm{cal}$ and entropy change is 7.4 caldeg ${ }^{-1}$ at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, the reaction is predicted as','[{"text": "reversible", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "spontaneous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "non-spontaneous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "irreversible", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'For the reaction at constant pressure,$\\Delta {\\rm{H}} =  - 2.5 \\times {10^3}{\\rm{cal}}$<br>${\\rm{\\Delta S}} = 7.4\\,{\\rm{cal}}\\,{\\rm{de}}{{\\rm{g}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$<br>$\\therefore \\Delta {\\rm{G}} = \\Delta {\\rm{H}} - {\\rm{T}}\\Delta {\\rm{S}}$<br>$ = ( - )2.5 \\times {10^3} - 298 \\times 7.4$<br>$ = ( - )2.5 \\times {10^3} - 2205.2\\Delta {\\rm{G}}$<br>${\\rm{\\Delta G}} =  - 4705 \\cdot 2\\,{\\rm{cal}}$<br>$\\therefore$ Reaction is spontaneous.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
