(18838,'chemistry',49,626,1274,'If $50 \\mathrm{~mL}$ of $0.1 \\mathrm{HBr}$ is mixed with$50\\,{\\rm{mL}}\\,0.2{\\rm{M}}\\,{\\rm{NaOH}}$, find $\\mathrm{pH}$ of resulting mixture','[{"text": "2.7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12.7", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "10.7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {{{\\text{N}}_{{\\text{Mix}}}}{{\\text{V}}_{{\\text{Mix}}}} = {{\\text{N}}_{\\text{1}}}\\,{{\\text{V}}_1} - {{\\text{N}}_{\\text{2}}}\\,{{\\text{V}}_{{\\text{2   }}}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,(1)} \\\\ \n  {{\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,({\\text{Base}}){\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,({\\text{Acid}})} \n\\end{array}$<br>Given, $\\mathrm{M}_{1}=0.2 \\mathrm{M}, \\mathrm{N}_{1}=0.2 \\mathrm{~N}$<br>$\\begin{aligned}& \\mathrm{M}_{2}=0.1 \\mathrm{M}, \\mathrm{N}_{2}=0.1 \\mathrm{~N} \\\\& \\mathrm{~V}_{1}=50 \\mathrm{~mL}, \\mathrm{~V}_{2}=50 \\mathrm{~mL}, \\mathrm{~V}_{\\text {mix }}=100 \\mathrm{~mL}\\end{aligned}$<br>On substituting the given values in equation (1)<br> $\\mathrm{N}_{\\text {mix }} \\times 100=50 \\times 0.2-50 \\times 0.1$<br>${{\\rm{N}}_{{\\rm{mix }}}} = \\frac{5}{{100}} = 5 \\times {10^{ - 2}}$$\\therefore\\left[\\mathrm{OH}^{-}\\right]=5 \\times 10^{-2}$<br>Now, $\\quad$ pOH $=-\\log \\left[\\mathrm{OH}^{-}\\right]=-\\log \\left[5 \\times 10^{-2}\\right]$$=2-\\log 5=1.3$<br>Also, $\\mathrm{pH}+\\mathrm{pOH}=14$$\\mathrm{pH}=14-1.3=12.7$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
