(18866,'chemistry',49,631,1285,'The rapid changes of $\\mathrm{pH}$ near the stoichiometric point of an acid base titration is the basis of indicator detection. $\\mathrm{pH}$ of the solution is related to ratio of the concentrations of the conjugate acid ${\\text{(HIn)}}$ and base ( $\\mathrm{In}^{-}$) forms of the indicator given by the expression','[{"text": "$\\\\log \\\\dfrac{\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{In}^{-}\\\\right]}{[\\\\mathrm{HIn}]}={\\\\rm{p}}{{\\\\rm{K}}_{{\\\\rm{ln}}}}-\\\\mathrm{pH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\log \\\\dfrac{[\\\\mathrm{HIn}]}{\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{In}^{-}\\\\right]}={\\\\rm{p}}{{\\\\rm{K}}_{{\\\\rm{ln}}}}-\\\\mathrm{pH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{log}}\\\\frac{{[{\\\\rm{HIn}}]}}{{\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{I}}{{\\\\rm{n}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}} \\\\right]}} = {\\\\rm{pH}} - {\\\\rm{p}}{{\\\\rm{K}}_{{\\\\rm{ln}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{log}}\\\\frac{{\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{I}}{{\\\\rm{n}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}} \\\\right]}}{{{\\\\rm{[HIn]}}}} = {\\\\rm{pH}} - {\\\\rm{p}}{{\\\\rm{K}}_{{\\\\rm{ln}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Acid indicators are generally weak acids. The dissociation of indicator ${\\text{ HIn}}$ takes place as follows:<br>$\\begin{aligned}& \\mathrm{HIn} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{H}^{+}+\\mathrm{In} \\\\& \\therefore \\quad \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{In}}=\\dfrac{\\left[\\mathrm{H}^{+}\\right]\\left[\\mathrm{In}^{-}\\right]}{[\\mathrm{HIn}]} \\\\& \\text { or }\\left[\\mathrm{H}^{+}\\right]=\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{In}} \\dfrac{[\\mathrm{HIn}]}{\\left[\\mathrm{In}^{-}\\right]} \\\\& \\because \\quad \\mathrm{pH}=-\\log \\left[\\mathrm{H}^{+}\\right] \\\\& \\therefore \\quad \\mathrm{pH}=-\\log \\left(\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{In}} \\cdot \\dfrac{[\\mathrm{HIn}]}{\\left[\\mathrm{In}^{-}\\right]}\\right) \\\\& =-\\log \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{In}}+\\log \\dfrac{\\left[\\mathrm{In}^{-}\\right]}{[\\mathrm{HIn}]} \\\\& =\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{In}}+\\log \\dfrac{\\left[\\mathrm{In}^{-}\\right]}{[\\mathrm{HIn}]}\\end{aligned}$<br>or $\\log \\dfrac{\\left[\\mathrm{In}^{-}\\right]}{[\\mathrm{HIn}]}=\\mathrm{pH}-\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{In}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
