(18954,'chemistry',49,617,1237,'For the reaction, <br> $2{{\\text{A}}_{({\\text{g}})}} + {{\\text{B}}_{2({\\text{g}})}} \\rightleftharpoons 2{\\text{A}}{{\\text{B}}_{({\\text{g}})}}$ <br>the equilibrium constant, ${{\\text{K}}_{\\text{p}}}$ at $300 \\mathrm{~K}$ is 16.0. The value of ${{\\text{K}}_{\\text{p}}}$ for ${\\text{A}}{{\\text{B}}_{2({\\text{g}})}} \\rightleftharpoons {{\\text{A}}_{({\\text{g}})}} + 1/2{{\\text{B}}_{2({\\text{g}})}}$ is','[{"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.25", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.125", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "32", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{A}}_{{\\rm{(g)}}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{B}}_{{\\rm{2(g)}}}}{\\rm{2A}}{{\\rm{B}}_{{\\rm{(g)}}}}$<br>${{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{p}}} = 16.0$<br>On reversing the equation,<br>$2{\\text{A}}{{\\text{B}}_{{\\text{(g)}}}} \\rightleftharpoons 2{{\\text{A}}_{{\\text{(g)}}}} + {{\\text{B}}_{{\\text{2(g)}}}}$<br>${\\text{K}}_{\\text{p}}^{\\text{\'}} = \\frac{1}{{{{\\text{K}}_{\\text{p}}}}} = \\frac{1}{{16}}$<br>Dividing the equation by 2<br>${\\text{A}}{{\\text{B}}_{{\\text{(g)}}}} \\rightleftharpoons {{\\text{A}}_{{\\text{(g)}}}} + \\frac{1}{2}{{\\text{B}}_{{\\text{2(g)}}}}$<br>${\\text{K}}_p^{\\prime \\prime } = \\sqrt {{\\text{K}}_p^\\prime }  = \\sqrt {\\frac{1}{{16}}}  = \\frac{1}{4} = 0.25$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
