(18981,'chemistry',49,624,1268,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> ${\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{b}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{\\,}}{{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ is not soluble in yellow ammonium sulphide.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The common ion effect due to $\\mathrm{S}^{2-}$ ions reduces the stability of $\\mathrm{Sb}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}_{3}$.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Due to common ion effect the $\\left[\\mathrm{S}^{2-}\\right]$ is reduced and only group 2 cations are precipitated as sulphides. The common ion is $\\mathrm{H}^{+}$[From HCl and $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}$ ]. So correct option is (4).',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
