(19058,'chemistry',49,630,1283,'${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{a}}}}$ of a weak acid (HA) and ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{b}}}}$ of a weak base ${\\mathrm{(\\mathrm{BOH})}}$ are 3.2 and 3.4 respectively. The ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{pH}_{\\text {}}}}$ of their salt ( ${\\mathrm{A \\mathrm{~B}}}$ ) solution is ____ .','[{"text": "7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6.9", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "10", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The given salt is of weak acid and weak base. pH of the salt solution is given by:<br>$\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{pH} & =\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{w}}+\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{a}}-\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{b}} \\\\& =\\dfrac{1}{2} \\times 14+\\dfrac{1}{2}3.2-\\dfrac{1}{2}(3.4)=6.9\\end{aligned}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
