(19379,'chemistry',49,629,1278,'pH of an aqueous solution of ${\\mathrm{0.6\\, \\mathrm{M}\\, \\mathrm{NH}_{3}}}$ and ${\\mathrm{0.4 \\, \\mathrm{M} \\, \\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}}}$ is 9.4 ${\\rm{(p}}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{b}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\,{\\rm{4}}.{\\rm{74}})$. The new pH when ${\\mathrm{0.1 \\mathrm{M} \\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2}}}$ solution is added to it is','[{"text": "9.86", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3.75", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "7.25", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "10.5", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Since ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2}}}$ is completely ionised. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/49_19379_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> \nBBB rule: On adding base,to hte basic buffer,cocentration of base increases and salt decreases.<br>$\\therefore $ New concentartaion of base and salt are:<br>${\\mathrm{[}}$ Base ${\\mathrm{]=\\left[\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right]=0.6+0.2=0.8 \\mathrm{M}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{[}}$ Salt ${\\mathrm{]=\\left[\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}\\right]=0.4-0.2=0.2 \\mathrm{M}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore \\mathrm{pOH}=\\mathrm{p} K_{b}+\\log \\left[\\dfrac{\\text { Salt }}{\\text { Base }}\\right]}}$<br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n{\\rm{pOH}} = 4.74 + \\log \\left( {\\frac{{0.2}}{{0.8}}} \\right)\\\\\n\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, = 4.74 - 2\\log 2 = 4.74 - 2 \\times 0.30\\\\\n\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, = 4.14\\\\\n{\\rm{pH}} = 14 - 4.14 = 9.86\n\\end{array}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
