(19449,'chemistry',49,630,1283,'Read statement-A and statement-B carefully to mark the correct options given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">: Aqueous solution of ammonium carbonate is basic.</div><div class="column-right">:Acidic/basic nature of salt solution of a salt of weak acid and weak base depends on ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K_{a}}}}$ and ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K_{b}}}}$ values of acid and the base forming it.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{OH}: \\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{b}}=4.74}}}$<br>$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{CO}_{3}: \\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{a}}=6.35$<br>As ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{b}}>\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{a}}}}}$, it\'s aqueous solution is basic. pH of salt of weak acid & weak base is given by<br>$\\mathrm{pH}=7+\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{a}}-\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{b}}$<br>It means pH depends on ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{a}} \\& \\mathrm{~K}_{\\mathrm{b}}}}}$ values.So, the correct option is (3).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
