(19453,'chemistry',49,617,1237,'The equilibrium constant for the reaction, <br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{SO}_{3(\\mathrm{~g})} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{SO}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})}+\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})}}}}$ is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{c}}=4.9 \\times 10^{-2}}}}$.<br>The value of  ${{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{c}}}$ for the reaction given below is <br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{2 \\mathrm{SO}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})}+\\mathrm{O}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})} \\rightleftharpoons 2 \\mathrm{SO}_{3(\\mathrm{~g})}}}}$ is','[{"text": "416", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4.9", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "41.6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "49", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{{\\text{3}}(\\,{\\text{g}})}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{{\\text{2}}(\\,{\\text{g}})}}{\\text{ + }}\\frac{{\\text{1}}}{{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{{\\text{2}}(\\,{\\text{g}})}};{{\\text{K}}_{\\text{c}}}{\\text{ = 4}}.{\\text{9}} \\times {\\text{1}}{{\\text{0}}^{{\\text{ - 2}}}}\\,(1)$<br>Reversing and multiplying equation (1) by 2, the desired equation will be obtained<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{2 \\mathrm{SO}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})}+\\mathrm{O}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})} \\rightleftharpoons 2 \\mathrm{SO}_{3(\\mathrm{~g})} ; \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{c}}^{\\prime}=}}}$ ?<br>$\\therefore {{\\rm{K}}_c}^\\prime {\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\left( {{\\rm{\\,}}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{c}}}} \\right)}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\left( {{\\rm{4}}.{\\rm{9}} \\times {\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 2}}}}} \\right)}^{\\rm{2}}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{4}}}}}{{{\\rm{4}}.{\\rm{9}} \\times {\\rm{4}}.{\\rm{9}}}}{\\rm{ = 416}}.{\\rm{49}}$<br>So, the correct option is (1).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
