(19459,'chemistry',53,994,2327,'The reducing character of hydrides of group 14 elements is :','[{"text": "Maximum for $$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}$$ and minimum for $$\\\\mathrm{PbH}_{4}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maximum for $$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}$$ and minimum for $$\\\\mathrm{SnH}_{4}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maximum for $$\\\\mathrm{PbH}_{4}$$ and minimum for $$\\\\mathrm{SiH}_{4}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maximum for $$\\\\mathrm{PbH}_{4}$$ and minimum for $$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}$$<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19461,'chemistry',49,617,1241,'${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{At}-20^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}}}$ and 1 atm pressure, a cylinder is filled with equal number of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2}, \\mathrm{I}_{2}}}}$ and HI molecules for the reaction,<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})}+\\mathrm{I}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})} \\rightleftharpoons 2 \\mathrm{HI}_{(\\mathrm{g})}}}}$, the ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{p}}}}}$ for the process is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{x} \\times 10^{-1} . \\mathrm{x}=}}}$ ____<br>[Given : ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{R}=0.082 \\mathrm{L\\,atm} \\,\\mathrm{K}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}}}$ ]','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "10", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.01", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K_{p}=K_{c} \\cdot(R T)^{\\Delta n}}}}$<br>$\\begin{gathered}\\text { as } \\Delta \\mathrm{n}_{(\\mathrm{g})}=0 ; \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{p}}=\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{c}} \\\\\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{P}}=\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{c}}=\\dfrac{[\\mathrm{HI}]^{2}}{\\left[\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\right]\\left[\\mathrm{I}_{2}\\right]}=1 \\text { (or) } 10 \\times 10^{-1}\\end{gathered}$<br>$\\left[[\\mathrm{HI}]=\\left[\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\right]=\\left[\\mathrm{I}_{2}\\right]\\right]$<br>So, the correct option is (3).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19465,'chemistry',49,617,1240,'The ratio ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\dfrac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{p}}}{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{c}}}}}}$ for the reaction,<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CO}_{(\\mathrm{g})}+\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{CO}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})}}}}$ is','[{"text": "RT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{\\\\dfrac{1}{\\\\sqrt{\\\\mathrm{RT}}}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{(\\\\mathrm{RT})^{\\\\frac{1}{2}}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K_{p}=K_{c}(R T)^{\\Delta n(g)}}}}$<br>Here, ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{g}}=1-\\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)=-\\dfrac{1}{2}}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\therefore \\dfrac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{p}}}{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{c}}}=(\\mathrm{RT})^{-\\dfrac{1}{2}}=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{\\mathrm{RT}}}}}}$<br>So, the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19467,'chemistry',53,995,2336,'Which is /are true statements?','[{"text": "Diamond is unaffected by conc. acids but graphite reacts with hot conc. $$\\\\mathrm{HNO}_{3}$$ forming mellitic acid, $$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6}(\\\\mathrm{COOH})_{6}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}$$ is toxic because it forms a complex with haemoglobin in the blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{C}_{3} \\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$$, carbon suboxide, is a foul-smelling gas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are true statements", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19468,'chemistry',49,617,1237,'For the given hypothetical reactions, the equilibrium constants are as follows:<br>${\\text{X}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{Y;}}{{\\text{K}}_1} = 1.0$<br>${\\text{Y}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{Z}};{{\\text{K}}_2} = 2.0$<br>${\\text{Z}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{W}};{{\\text{K}}_3} = 4.0$<br>The equilibrium constant for the reaction, ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{X} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{W}}}}$ is','[{"text": "12.0", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6.0", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8.0", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "7.0", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'By adding given three equations, desired equation is obtained. When equations are added, rate constants are multiplied to get resultant rate constant.<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{X} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{Y} ; \\mathrm{K}_{1}=1.0}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Y} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{Z} ; \\mathrm{K}_{2}=2.0}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Z} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{W} ; \\quad \\mathrm{K}_{3}=4.0}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{X} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{W} ; \\quad \\mathrm{K}=\\mathrm{K}_{1} \\times \\mathrm{K}_{2} \\times \\mathrm{K}_{3}}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K=1 \\times 2 \\times 4=8}}}$<br>So, the correct option is (3).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
