(19560,'chemistry',53,989,2312,'In the following sets of reactants which two sets best exhibit the amphoteric character of $$\\mathrm{Al}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}, x \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$$ ?<br>Set 1: $$\\mathrm{Al}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3} \\cdot \\mathrm{xH}_{2} \\mathrm{O}(\\mathrm{s})$$ and $$\\mathrm{OH}^{-}$$(aq)<br>Set 2: ${\\rm{A}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{.x}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O(s)}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O(l)}}$<br>Set 3:${\\text{A}}{{\\text{l}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{.X}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O(s)}}\\,\\,{\\text{and}}\\,\\,{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ + }}}{\\text{(aq)}}$<br>Set 4: $$\\mathrm{Al}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3} \\cdot \\mathrm{XH}_{2} \\mathrm{O}(\\mathrm{s})$$ and $$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$ (aq)','[{"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2 and 4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 and 4", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Aluminium oxide is amphoteric oxide because it shows the properties of the both acidic and basic oxides. It reacts with both acids and bases to form salt and water.<br>${\\text{A}}{{\\text{l}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{.x}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O + 2NaOH}} \\to {\\text{NaAl}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ + }}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}$<br>${\\text{A}}{{\\text{l}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{.x}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O + HCl}} \\to {\\text{AlC}}{{\\text{l}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{ + }}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19563,'chemistry',53,996,2341,'Example of a three-dimensional silicate is:','[{"text": "Zeolites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ultramarines", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Feldspars", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Beryls", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The feldspares are most abundant aluminosilicate minerals in the earth surface. The silicon atoms and aluminium atoms occupy the centres of interlinked tetrahedra of $$\\mathrm{SiO}_{4}^{4-}$$ and $$\\mathrm{AlO}_{4}^{5-}$$. These tetrahedra connect at each corner to other tetrahedra forming an intricate, three dimensional, negatively charged framework. The sodium cations sit within the voids in this structure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19565,'chemistry',54,1214,2917,'Among the following the unstable molecule is','[{"text": "Benzyl free radical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tert-butyl carbocation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tert-butyl carbanion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Allyl carbanion", "isCorrect": false}]',2,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19566,'chemistry',53,995,2331,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Among the carbon allotropes, diamond is an insulator, whereas, graphite is a good conductor of electricity.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Hybridization of carbon in diamond and graphite are ${\\text{s}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{3}}}\\,$ and  ${\\text{s}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{2}}}$, respectively.<br>','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In diamond, each C-atom is covalently bonded to four other $$\\mathrm{C}$$-atoms to give a tetrahedral unit. In diamond each C-atom is ${\\text{s}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{3}}}$ hybridized. Therefore each $$\\mathrm{C}$$-atom forms four sigma bonds with neighbouring $$\\mathrm{C}$$-atoms. In diamond each $$\\mathrm{C}$$-atom utilizes its four unpaired electrons in bond formation.<br>These bonding electrons are localized. Due to this reason diamond is a bad conductor of electricity. In graphite each C-atom is covalently bonded to three $$\\mathrm{C}$$-atoms to give trigonal geometry. Each C-atom in graphite is    ${\\text{s}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{2}}}$ hybridized. Three out of four valence electrons of each C-atom are used in bond formation while the fourth electron is free to move in the structure of graphite. Due to this reason graphite is a good conductor of electricity.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2016,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19568,'chemistry',54,1213,2907,'Consider the following compounds,<br>(I) (II) (III) (IV) The order of basic strength of their conjugate base is','[{"text": "II $>$ I $>$ IV $>$ III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II $>$ IV $>$ I $>$ III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III $>$ IV $>$ I $>$ II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III $>$ IV $>$ II $>$ I", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/54_19568_question_1.png'),
(19569,'chemistry',53,996,2343,'Match the items in Column I with its main use listed in Column II<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A  Silica gel<br>B  Silicon<br>C  Silicone<br>D  Silicate</div><div class="column-right">P  Transistor<br>Q  Ion-exchanger<br>R  Drying agent<br>S   Sealant</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  R,  B  -   P,   C  -   S,  D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  S,  B  -   P,   C  -   Q,  D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  Q,  B  -   P,   C  -   S,  D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  Q,  B  -   S,   C  -   P,  D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A - Silica gel packets are used to absorb moisture and keep things dry i.e., as drying agent.<br>B - Silicon is a semiconductor and is used in transistors.<br>C - Silicone is used as sealant.<br>D - Silicates are widely used in ion-exchange beds in domestic and commercial water purification, softening, and other applications.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2016,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19571,'chemistry',54,1213,2907,'Mesomeric effect involve delocalisation of','[{"text": "$\\\\pi$-electrons", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\sigma$-electrons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neutrons", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mesomeric effect involves complete transfer of $\\pi$ or lone pair of electrons to the adjacent atom or covalent bond. Hence, it involves delocalisation of $\\mathrm{pi}(\\pi)$ electrons.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
