(19572,'chemistry',53,992,2315,'A group 13 element \' $$\\mathrm{X}$$ \' reacts with chlorine gas to produce a compound $$\\mathrm{XCl}_{3}. \\mathrm{XCl}_{3}$$ is electron deficient and easily reacts with $$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$ to form $$\\mathrm{Cl}_{3} \\mathrm{X} \\leftarrow \\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$ adduct; however, $$\\mathrm{XCl}_{3}$$ does not dimerize. $$\\mathrm{X}$$ is:','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{B}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{Al}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\ln$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{Ga}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/53_19572_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19574,'chemistry',54,1213,2910,'Among the following, the most basic compound is','[{"text": "Benzamide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Butanamine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nitrobenzene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aniline", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Basicity increases with ${\\rm{ + I}}$ (inductive) effect and also presence of lone pairs which are available for protonation. Out of the given compounds, butanamine is most basic.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19575,'chemistry',53,996,2340,'Correct statements among  ${\\text{A}}\\,\\,{\\text{to}}\\,\\,{\\text{D}}$ regarding silicones are<br>(A) They are polymers with hydrophobic character<br>(B) They are biocompatible<br>(C) In general, they have high thermal stability and low dielectric strength<br>(D) Usually, they are resistant to oxidation and used as greases','[{"text": "(A), (B), (C) and (D)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(A) and (B) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(A), (B) and (C) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(A), (B) and (D) only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19577,'chemistry',54,1213,2910,'Correct order of basic nature is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'(i) $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ is more basic than $\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ due to presence of electron donating methyl group.<br>(ii) $\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ is less basic than $\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ due to presence of electron withdrawing phenyl group.<br>$\\therefore$ Correct order of basic nature is<br>$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{NH}_{2}>\\mathrm{NH}_{3}>\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{NH}_{2}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19578,'chemistry',53,986,2295,'Aluminium is usually found in +3 oxidation state.In contrast, thallium exists in +1 and +3 oxidation states. This is due to','[{"text": "Lattice effect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lanthanoid contraction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inert pair effect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Diagonal relationship.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Due to inert pair effect, last elements of Gr. 13, 14, 15 show lower oxidation state.<br>Ex:  ${\\text{Tl + 1,}}\\quad {\\text{Pb + 2,}}\\quad {\\text{Bi + 3}}{\\text{.}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2019,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19580,'chemistry',54,1213,2906,'Among the following, the one that has least ${\\rm{p}}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{a}}}$ value is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CCl}_{3} \\\\mathrm{COOH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{ClCOOH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CF}_{3} \\\\mathrm{COOH}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{COOH}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{CF}_{3} \\mathrm{COOH}$ is the strongest acid due to greatest $-\\mathrm{I}$ effect of $-\\mathrm{F}$ atom among $-\\mathrm{Cl}$ and $-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19581,'chemistry',53,988,2307,'Identify the correct statement for $$\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$$ from those given below.<br>(A) In $$\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$$, all B-H bonds are equivalent.<br>(B) In $$\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$$ there are four 3-centre-2-electron bonds.<br>(C) $$\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$$ is a Lewis acid.<br>(D) $$\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$$ can be synthesized from both $$\\mathrm{BF}_{3}$$ and $$\\mathrm{NaBH}_{4}$$.<br>(E) $$\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$$ is a planar molecule.<br>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :','[{"text": "(A) and (E) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(B), (C) and (E) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(C) and (D) only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(C) and (E) only<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/53_19581_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   (A), (B):<br>Two 3 centre -2 - electron bonds<br>(C) $$\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$$ is  ${\\text{e  - }}$ deficient species<br>(E) $$\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$$ is non - Planar molecule<br>(D) $$\\mathrm{BF}_{3}+\\mathrm{LiAlH}_{4} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{~B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}+3 \\mathrm{LiF}+3 \\mathrm{AlF}_{3}$$<br>$$\\mathrm{NaBH}_{4}+\\mathrm{I}_{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}+2 \\mathrm{NaI}+\\mathrm{H}_{2}$$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
