(19584,'chemistry',53,988,2304,'Consider the given statements regarding the properties of boron.<br>I. It is a hard refractory solid.<br>II. It has low melting point and high density.<br>III. It shows high electrical conductivity<br>Choose the correct statement(s).','[{"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement I  is correct regarding the properties of boron, while the statements II and III are incorrect. Corrected form are as follows:<br>II. Boron has high melting point and low density.<br>III. Boron shows low electrical conductivity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19586,'chemistry',54,1214,2912,'The ascending order of stability of the carbanion $\\mathrm{C}^{-} \\mathrm{H}_{3}(\\mathrm{P}), \\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{C}^{-} \\mathrm{H}_{2}(\\mathrm{Q}),\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{C}^{-} \\mathrm{H}(\\mathrm{R})$ and<br>$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{C}^{-}-\\mathrm{CH}=\\mathrm{CH}_{2}(\\mathrm{~S})$ is','[{"text": "P $ < $ R $ < $ S $ < $ Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "R $ < $ P $ < $ S $ < $ Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "R $ < $ P $ < $ Q $ < $ S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P $ < $ R $ < $ Q $ < $ S", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Stability of carbanions is enhanced by<br>(i) Presence of conjugation<br>(ii) Presence of group existing -I effect<br>So correct order is<br>${{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{6}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{5}}}{{\\rm{C}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ > }}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{C}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\rm{ - CH = C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ > }}{{\\rm{C}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ > }}{\\left( {{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}} \\right)_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{C}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\rm{H}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19587,'chemistry',53,986,2294,'Which of the following statements is correct regarding group 13 elements?<br>(I) Density increases down the group from B to $$\\mathrm{Ga}$$ and then decreases upto $$\\mathrm{Tl}$$<br>(II) Boiling point of gallium is very high (2676 $$\\mathrm{K})$$<br>(III)Boron is a soft non-metal<br>(IV) Melting point of gallium is very high (3030 K)','[{"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only IV<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement II is correct, while other statements are incorrect. Corrected form are as follows:<br>I Density of the group-13 elements increases down the group from boron to thallium.<br>III Boron is a har non-metal.<br>IV Melting point of Ga is unusually low (i.e. $$303 \\mathrm{~K})$$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19588,'chemistry',54,1214,2912,'The stability of carbanions in the following is','[{"text": "(I) $>$ (II) $>$ (III) $>$ (IV)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(II) $>$ (III) $>$ (IV) $>$ (I)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(IV) $>$ (II) $>$ (III) $>$ (I)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I) $>$ (III) $>$ (II) $>$ (IV)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When s-character increases, then electrons becomes more closer to the nucleus and structure is of lower energy and is more stable. The stability order of carbanions is as<br>${\\rm{RC}} \\equiv {{\\rm{C}}^ \\odot } > {{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{H}}_5^ \\odot  > {{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}} = \\mathop {{\\rm{ C}}}\\limits^ \\odot  {\\rm{H}} > {{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{C}} - \\mathop {\\rm{C}}\\limits^ \\odot  {{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/54_19588_question_1.jpg'),
