(19594,'chemistry',53,995,2331,'Consider the following statements.<br>I. Graphite has planar hexagonal layers of carbon atoms in which each carbon atom undergoes ${\\text{s}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{2}}}$  hybridisation.<br>II. Fullerence have smooth structure having \'danglings\' bond.<br>III. In diamond, each atom is linked tetrahedrally to four other carbon atoms by ${\\text{s}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{3}}}$ hybridised bonds.<br>The correct statement(s) is/are','[{"text": "Both I and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statements I and III are correct while statement II is incorrect. It\'s correct form is as follows:<br>Fulleren are the only pure form of carbon because they have smooth structure without having \'dangling\' bonds.<br>',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
