(19688,'chemistry',55,1240,3014,'The carbon-carbon bond length in benzene is','[{"text": "same as in $\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "in between $\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6}$ in $\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "in between $\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{4}$ and $\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "in between $\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6}$ and $\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{4}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In benzene, due to delocalisation of $\\pi$ - electrons, all the $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$ bond lengths are equal as each $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$ bond has some double bond character and thus the bond length is between single and double bond, i.e., between $\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$ and $\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{4}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(19689,'chemistry',53,995,2331,'Choose the correct statement :','[{"text": "Diamond is covalent and graphite is ionic.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diamond is $$\\\\mathrm{sp}^{3}$$ hybridized and graphite is $$\\\\mathrm{sp}^{2}$$ hybridized.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both diamond and graphite are used as dry lubricants.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diamond and graphite have two dimensional network.<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In diamond each carbon is bonded with four other carbon atoms. So, hybridisation of carbon atom is $$\\mathrm{sp}^{3}$$.<br>In graphite each carbon is bonded with three other carbon atoms. So, hybridisation of carbon atom is $$\\mathrm{sp}^{2}$$.<br>',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
