(19732,'chemistry',55,1237,2984,'Identify the following compound which exhibits geometrical isomerism','[{"text": "But-2-ene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "But-1-ene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Butane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Iso-butane", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The necessary and sufficient condition for a compound to exhibit geometrical isomerism is that the two groups attached to the same double bonded carbon must be different, i.e., alkenes of the following types show cis-trans isomerism. $\\mathrm{abC}=\\mathrm{Cab}, \\mathrm{abC}=\\mathrm{Ccd}, \\mathrm{abC}=\\mathrm{Cax}, \\mathrm{abC}=\\mathrm{Cbx}$<br>Thus, out of the given examples, only but-2-ene exhibits geometrical isomerism.  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_19732_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
