(19773,'chemistry',55,1234,2970,'What is the range of number of carbon atoms in alkanes found in paraffin wax?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{21}$ to $\\\\mathrm{C}_{30}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{19}$ to $\\\\mathrm{C}_{20}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6}$ to $\\\\mathrm{C}_{8}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{17}$ to $\\\\mathrm{C}_{18}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Carbon twenty $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{20}\\right)$ to carbon thirty $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{30}\\right)$ range of carbon atoms in alkanes found in paraffin wax. It is a soft colourless solid derived from petroleum, coal or shale oil that consists of a mixture of hydrocarbon molecules. It is used in candles, wax paper, polishes, cosmetics and electrical insulators.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
