(19849,'chemistry',53,995,2336,'Gas A is bubbled through slaked lime when a white precipitate is formed. On prolonged bubbling the precipitate is dissolved. On heating the resultant solution, the white precipitate appears with evolution of gas B. The gases A and $$\\mathrm{B}$$ respectively are','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{CO}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{CO}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{CO}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{and}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'According to the question,<br>$$\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2}+\\mathrm{CO}_{2} \\rightarrow \\underset{\\text { White ppt }}{\\mathrm{CaCO}_{3}}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$$<br>$$\\begin{aligned}& \\mathrm{CaCO}_{3}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}+\\mathrm{CO}_{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Ca}\\left(\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\\\& \\mathrm{Ca}\\left(\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\stackrel{\\Delta}{\\longrightarrow} \\mathrm{CaO}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}+2 \\mathrm{CO}_{2}\\end{aligned}$$<br>Hence, the gas ${\\text{A}}\\,\\,{\\text{and}}\\,\\,{\\text{B}}$ are $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ and $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ respectivley.<br>',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
