(19888,'chemistry',55,1234,2968,'Which one of the following conformations of ethane is more stable?','[{"text": "staggered", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "eclipsed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "both are equally stable", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "skew", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The half-chair can be attained by moving the carbons $\\mathrm{C}_{1}, \\mathrm{C}_{2}, \\mathrm{C}_{3}$ and $\\mathrm{C}_{4}$ of a chair, conformation into one plane and $\\mathrm{C}_{6}$ above the plane and $\\mathrm{C}_{5}$ below the plane. It contains many eclipsed carbon-hydrogen bonds. The half chair conformer lies about $10.8\\,\\,{\\text{kcal}}$ above the chair form.<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_19888_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
