(19910,'chemistry',53,987,2300,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{SiF}_{6}^{2-}$ is known but $\\mathrm{SiCl}_{6}^{2-}$ is not.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Size of fluorine is small and its lone pair of electrons interacts with d- orbitals of<br>${\\text{Si }}$ strongly.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason is Incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{SiF}_{6}^{2-}$ is known, as $\\mathrm{F}$ has small size and thus, the ion is quite stable unlike $\\mathrm{SiCl}_{6}^{2-}$ in which size of $\\mathrm{Cl}$ - atom is large which destabilises it.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2005,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
