(19916,'chemistry',55,1234,2969,'The compound which is not formed when a mixture of ${\\text{n}}$-butyl bromide and ethyl bromide treated with sodium metal in the presence of dry ether is','[{"text": "butane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "octane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "hexane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ethane", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'When a mixture of n-butyl bromide and ethyl bromide is treated with sodium metal in the presence of dry ether, then ethane cannot be formed because reaction follows Wurtz-Fittig reaction. It is a type of coupling reaciton.<br>$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{Br}+\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{Br}+2 \\mathrm{Na} \\underset{\\text { Ether }}{\\stackrel{\\text { Dry }}{\\longrightarrow}}$<br>$\\mathop {{{\\text{C}}_4}{{\\text{H}}_9} - {{\\text{C}}_4}{{\\text{H}}_9}}\\limits_{{\\text{Octane}}}  + \\mathop {{{\\text{C}}_4}{{\\text{H}}_9} - {{\\text{C}}_2}{{\\text{H}}_5}}\\limits_{{\\text{ Hexane }}}  + \\mathop {{{\\text{C}}_2}{{\\text{H}}_5} - {{\\text{C}}_2}{{\\text{H}}_5}}\\limits_{{\\text{ Butane }}} $',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2016,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
