(19963,'chemistry',55,1244,3025,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Alkynes are more reactive than alkenes towards catalytic hydrogenation<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Alkynes are less reactive towards electrophilic reaction than alkenes','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Alkynes are more reactive than alkenes towards catalytic hydrogenation because<br>they are more easily adsorbed on the catalytic surface due to less steric hinderance around the<br>multiple bonds.<br>Alkynes are less reactive than alkenes towards electrophilic substitution because the pi electrons<br>are tightly held in the more compact triple bond as compared to a double bond. Thus, both<br>assertion and reason are true but reason is the correct explanation of the assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
