(19998,'chemistry',55,1234,2971,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Iodination of alkanes is reversible.</div><div class="column-right">Iodination is carried out in presence of iodic acid.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Iodination is reversible since formed $\\mathrm{HI}$ is a strong reducing agent and reduces the alkyl iodide back to alkane.<br>$\\mathrm{CH}_{4}+\\mathrm{I}_{2} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{I}+\\mathrm{HI}$<br>Iodination can be done only in presence of strong oxidising agents like iodic acid which destroys the hydriodic acid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
