(20005,'chemistry',55,1240,3018,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In the electrophilic substitution of aryl halides, the incoming electrophile gets attached to the meta position.</div><div class="column-right">Aryl halides are moderately deactivating.<br></div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the electrophilic substitution of aryl halides, the incoming electrophile gets attached to the ortho and/or para position. This is because, even though aryl halides shows ${\\text{ - I}}$ -effect, the electron density on ortho and para positions is greater than that at meta position due to resonance.<br>Hence, the incoming electrophile is directed at the ortho and/or para position.<br>So, the option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20006,'chemistry',53,987,2300,'The exhibition of highest coordination number depends on the availability of vacant orbitals in the central atom. Which of the following elements is not likely to act as central atom in $\\mathrm{MF}_{6}^{3-}$ ?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{B}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Al}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ga}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{In}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Boron can show maximum coordination number of 4 . Thus, ${\\text{B}}$ can not form complex of the type $\\mathrm{MF}_{6}^{3-}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20007,'chemistry',54,1213,2910,'The most polar compound among the following is:','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20007_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> the bond dipole vector of $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{F}$ bond is not subtractive.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2018,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20008,'chemistry',55,1240,3018,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Nitration of benzene with nitric acid requires the use of concentrated sulphuric acid.<br></div><div class="column-right">The mixture of concentrated sulphuric acid and concentrated nitric acid produces the electrophile, $\\mathrm{NO}_{2}^{+}$.<br></div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The reaction is given below:  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20008_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   So, the option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20009,'chemistry',53,988,2307,'A compound $\\mathrm{X}$, of boron reacts with $\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ on heating to give another compound $\\mathrm{Y}$ which is called inroganic benzene. The compound X can be prepared by treating $\\mathrm{BF}_{3}$ with lithium aluminium hydride. The compounds $\\mathrm{X}$ and $\\mathrm{Y}$ are represented by the formulae','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6}, \\\\mathrm{~B}_{3} \\\\mathrm{~N}_{3} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{~B}_{3} \\\\mathrm{~N}_{3} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{BF}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{~B}_{3} \\\\mathrm{~N}_{3} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{B}_{3} \\\\mathrm{~N}_{3} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6}, \\\\mathrm{~B}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'(i) $\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6} \\cdot 2 \\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ which is formulated as $\\left[\\mathrm{BH}_{2}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{2}\\right]^{+}\\left[\\mathrm{BH}_{4}\\right]^{-}$ formed by the reaction of ammonia with diborane initially further on heating it changes into borazine, $\\mathrm{B}_{3} \\mathrm{~N}_{3} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$<br>$\\mathop {{\\text{3}}{{\\text{B}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{6}}}}\\limits_{{\\text{(x)}}} {\\text{ +  6N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{473 K}}}}{\\text{2}}\\mathop {{\\text{}}{{\\text{B}}_{\\text{3}}}{{\\text{N}}_{\\text{3}}}{{\\text{N}}_{\\text{6}}}}\\limits_{{\\text{(y)}}} {\\text{ + 12}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}$<br>Borazole has cyclic structure and is isoelectronic and isosteric with benzene and thus called inorganic benzene.<br>ii) By the reduction of $\\mathrm{BF}_{3}$ with lithium aluminium hydride in diethyl ether diborane can be prepared.<br>$4 \\mathrm{BF}_{3}+3 \\mathrm{LiAlH}_{4} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{~B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}+3 \\mathrm{AlF}_{3}+3 \\mathrm{LiF}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20011,'chemistry',55,1240,3015,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The compound cyclooctatetraene has the following structural formula.<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20011_qtext_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  It is cyclic and conjugated $8\\pi $- electron system but it is not an aromatic compound.</div><div class="column-right">$\\left( {{\\text{4n  +  2}}} \\right){\\text{ }}\\pi {\\text{  -  }}$ electron rule does not hold good and ring is not planar.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20011_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  is cyclic and conjugated<br>$8 \\pi$ - electron system but it is not an aromatic compound because ${\\text{(4n  +  2) }}\\pi {\\text{ }}$ - electrons rule does not hold good and ring is not planar.<br>So, the option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20012,'chemistry',53,988,2311,'A gas other than $\\mathrm{HCl}$ is obtained in','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}+\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\xrightarrow[\\\\text { discharge }]{\\\\text { Silentelric }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{LiAlH}_{4}+\\\\mathrm{BF}_{3} \\\\rightarrow$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) & (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$2 \\mathrm{BCl}_{3}+6 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}+6 \\mathrm{HCl}$<br>$3 \\mathrm{LiAlH}_{4}+4 \\mathrm{BF}_{3} \\rightarrow 3 \\mathrm{LiF}+3 \\mathrm{AlF}_{3}+2 \\mathrm{~B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20014,'chemistry',55,1241,3021,'Which of the following statement is incorrect regarding nitration of aromatic compounds?<br>I. The rate of nitration of benzene decreases at 323-333 K.<br>II. The rate of nitration of toluene is greater than that of benzene.<br>III. The rate of nitration of chlorobenzene is greater than that of benzene.<br>IV. Nitration is an electrophilic substitution reaction.<br>Choose the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statements I and III are incorrect.<br>Its correct form is as follows:<br>I. The rate of nitration of benzene increases at high temperature, i.e., 323-333 K.<br>III. The rate of nitration of chlorobenzene is lower than that of benzene.<br>So, the option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
