(20029,'chemistry',55,1244,3025,'Given below are two statements.<br>Statement I : The presence of weaker $\\pi$-bonds make alkenes less stable than alkanes.<br>Statement II : The strength of the double bond is greater than that of carbon-carbon single bond.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below.','[{"text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2022,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20030,'chemistry',53,988,2311,'Which one of the following is the correct statement?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6} \\\\cdot 2 \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ is known as \'inorganic benzene\'", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Boric acid is a protonic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Beryllium exhibits coordination number of six", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlorides of both beryllium and aluminium have bridged chlorine structures in solid phase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{BeCl}_{2}$ and $\\mathrm{AlCl}_{3}$ have bridged chlroine structures.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20032,'chemistry',55,1234,2969,'Which of the following statements are correct regarding Kolbe\'s electrolytic process?<br>I. Alkanes containing even number of C-atoms are prepared.<br>II. Sodium or potassium salts of carboxylic acids are taken as substrate.<br>III. Methane can be prepared by this method.<br>IV. $\\mathrm{H}_{2}$ gas is liberated at anode.<br>Choose the correct statement.','[{"text": "Both I and II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statements I and II are correct, while the statements III and IV are incorrect<br>Corrected form are as follows:<br>III. Methane cannot be prapared by Kolbe\'s electrolytic process.<br>IV. $\\mathrm{CH}_{2}$ gas is liberated at cathode.<br>Kolbe\'s electrolytic reaction:<br>${\\text{RCOONa}}\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}}}\\mathop {{\\text{R -  R  +  C}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}}\\limits_{{\\text{At}}\\,\\,{\\text{Anode}}} {\\text{ + }}\\mathop {{\\text{NaOH  +  }}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}}\\limits_{{\\text{At}}\\,\\,{\\text{Cathode}}} $<br>So, the option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20033,'chemistry',53,987,2299,'Which of the following reactions does not liberate gaseous product?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{AlCl}_{3}+\\\\mathrm{NaOH} \\\\rightarrow$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NaOH}+\\\\mathrm{P}($ white $)+\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O} \\\\rightarrow$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{Al}} + {\\\\text{NaOH}}\\\\xrightarrow{\\\\Delta }$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{Zn}} + {\\\\text{NaOH}}\\\\xrightarrow{\\\\Delta }$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{AlCl}_{3}+3 \\mathrm{NaOH} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Al}(\\mathrm{OH})_{3}+3 \\mathrm{NaCl}$<br>$\\mathrm{P}_{4}+3 \\mathrm{NaOH}+3 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{PH}_{3}+3 \\mathrm{NaH}_{2} \\mathrm{PO}_{2}$<br>$2 \\mathrm{Al}+2 \\mathrm{NaOH}+2 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{NaAlO}_{2}+3 \\mathrm{H}_{2}$ $\\mathrm{Zn}+2 \\mathrm{NaOH} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{ZnO}_{2}+\\mathrm{H}_{2}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20034,'chemistry',54,1211,2901,'Which of the following statements is/are correct?<br>I. When two or more compounds have similar molecular formula but different carbon skeletons they are referred as chain isomers.<br>II. When two or more compounds differ in the position of substituent atom or functional group on the carbon skeleton, they are called functional isomers.<br>III. The isomerism which arises due to the presence of different alkyl chains on either side of the functional group in the molecule is referred to as metamerism.<br>Choose the correct option.','[{"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statement I and III are correct, while statement II is incorrect.<br>Its correct form is as follows:<br>When two or more compounds differ in the position of substituent atom or functional group on the carbon skeleton, they are called position isomers.<br>So, the option (4) is correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20036,'chemistry',54,1207,2888,'Consider the following statements:<br>I. The presence of functional group disables systematisation of organic compound into different classes.<br>II. In polyfunctional compounds, one of the functional group is chosen as the principal functional group.<br>III.The order of priority for functional group is<br>$-\\mathrm{COCl}>-\\mathrm{COOR}>-\\mathrm{SO}_{3} \\mathrm{H}>-\\mathrm{COOH}$<br>IV. $\\mathrm{CH}_{2}(\\mathrm{OH}) \\mathrm{CH}_{2}(\\mathrm{OH})$ is named as ethane -1 , 2- diol.<br>Read the given statements and choose the correct option.','[{"text": "Both I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both II and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement II and IV are correct, while the statement I and III are incorrect.<br>Corrected form are as follows:<br>I. The presence of functional group enables systematisation of organic compound into different classes.<br>III. The order of priority of functional groups is<br>$-\\mathrm{COOH}>-\\mathrm{SO}_{3} \\mathrm{H}>-\\mathrm{COOR}>-\\mathrm{COCl}$.<br>So, the option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20037,'chemistry',53,986,2296,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The first member of a group of elements compared to that of the subsequent members in the same group shows different chemical behaviour.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The first member of a group has small size, high electronegativity and no ${\\text{d}}$-orbital.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Besides its small size and high electronegativity, the first member of each group has only four valence orbitals ${\\text{( 2s and 2p )}}$  available for bonding, meaning there is no expansion of the valence shell to accommodate more than four pairs of electrons, So, option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20038,'chemistry',55,1234,2972,'Statement-1 : 2-Methylbutane is oxidised by $\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4}$ to give 2-Methyl butan-2-ol.<br>Statement-2 : An alkane is easily oxidised by $\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4}$.','[{"text": "Both Statement - 1 and Statement - 2 are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement - 1 and Statement -2 are false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement - 1 is correct and Statement - 2 is false", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement -1 is false and Statement -2 is correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2021,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20039,'chemistry',54,1213,2907,'Consider the following statements.<br>I. The resonance structure have different positions of nuclei.<br>II. Resonance structures have the same number of unpaired electrons.<br>III. Among the resonance structures, the one which has more number of covalent bonds, all the atoms with octet of electrons and more dispersal of charge is more stable than others.<br>Read the given statements and choose the incorrect option.','[{"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement I is incorrect.<br>Its correct form is as follows:<br>The following rules are applied while writing resonance structures:<br>The resonance structures have same positions of nuclei.<br>So, the option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20040,'chemistry',53,987,2300,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Anhydrous $\\mathrm{AlCl}_{3}$ is covalent but hydrated $\\mathrm{AlCl}_{3}$ is ionic.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In water, $\\mathrm{Al}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}_{6}$ dissociates into hydrated $\\mathrm{Al}^{3+}$ and $\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$ions due to high heat of hydration of these ions.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When anhydrous $\\mathrm{AlCl}_{3}$ is dissolved in water, it changes to hydrated $\\mathrm{AlCl}_{3}$, which is ionic in nature. The dimeric formula is retained in a non-polar solvent but is broken into $\\mathrm{Al}^{+3}$ and $\\mathrm{Cl}^{-1}$ ions upon dissolution in water, due to the high heat of hydration. So, option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20042,'chemistry',55,1240,3015,'Which of the following will satisfy aromaticity?<br>a) b) c) d)','[{"text": "a, b and c", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a and b", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a, b and d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "c and d", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Conditions for aromaticity:<br>(a) Molecule must be cyclic, planar ( $\\mathrm{sp}^{2}$ hybridised)<br>(b) Molecule must be conjugate<br>(c) Molecule must satisfy Huckel\'s rule i.e., ${\\text{(4 n + 2)}}$  rule',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_20042_question_1.png'),
(20043,'chemistry',54,1207,2879,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">IUPAC name of the following organic compound is 3,4,7 - trimethyloctane https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764953539/preptracker/questions/q_20043_col1_1764953539051.jpg</div><div class="column-right">The numbering is done in such a way that the branched carbon atoms get the lowest possible numbers.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct name of the given compound is 2, 5, 6 - trimethyloctane. So, the option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20044,'chemistry',53,987,2300,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Trihalides of boron family fume in moist air.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Trihalides of group-13 elements are hygroscopic.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Trihalides of boron family undergo hydrolysis producing hydrogen halide due to which they fume in moist air. So, option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20046,'chemistry',55,1237,2990,'Correct statement about A & B is -','[{"text": "A is more stable and formed with faster rate.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B is more stable and formed with faster rate.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A is less stable and formed with slow rate.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{B}$ is less stable and formed with faster rate.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$2^{\\circ}$ carbocation is more stable than $1^{\\circ}$ carbocation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',2021,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_20046_question_1.png'),
(20047,'chemistry',54,1209,2890,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Chain isomerism is observed in compounds containing four or more than four carbon atoms<br></div><div class="column-right">Only alkanes show chain isomerism</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Chain isomerism shown by other functional groups also. So, the option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20069,'chemistry',55,1240,3015,'Which of the following compounds will show highest dipole moment?<br> (I) (II) (III) (IV)','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20069_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  A dipolar resonance structure has aromatic character in the ring and would be expected to make a major contribution to the overall structure.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2017,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_20069_question_1.png'),
(20049,'chemistry',53,988,2310,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$ contains three centre two electron bonds.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> $\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$ is electron deficient molecule.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Diborane does not have sufficient electrons to form normal covalent bonds, therefore it forms three centre - 2electron bonds. So, option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20050,'chemistry',55,1244,3025,'In the given reactions sequence, the major product \' $\\mathrm{C}$ \' is<br>${{\\text{C}}_{\\text{8}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{10}}}}\\xrightarrow[{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}}]{{{\\text{HN}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{3}}}}}{\\text{A}}\\xrightarrow[\\Delta ]{{{\\text{B}}{{\\text{r}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{\\text{B}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{KOH}}}]{{{\\text{ alcoholic }}}}{\\text{C}}$','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20050_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2022,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20051,'chemistry',54,1209,2891,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">But - 1- ene and 2 - methylprop - 1 - ene are position isomers.<br></div><div class="column-right">Position isomers have same molecular formula but differ in position of functional group</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'But-1-ene and 2-methyl prop-l-ene are chain isomers. So, the option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20053,'chemistry',53,988,2306,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Boric acid acts as a strong acid in presence of catechol.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Boric acid does not act as a proton donor but behaves as a Lewis acid.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Metaborate ion gets complexed with catechol. So boric acid acts as strong acid in the presence of catechol. $\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{BO}_{3}$ is not a proton donar as all $\\mathrm{H}$ - atoms are with hydrogen bonds. But its a lewis acid due to vacant orbital availablity. So, option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20054,'chemistry',55,1237,2987,'Consider the following reactions:<br>(a) ${\\left( {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CCH(OH)C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{ conc}}{\\text{. }}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}}}$<br>(b) ${\\left( {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{CHCH(Br)C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{ alc}}{\\text{. KOH }}}}$<br>(c) ${\\left( {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{CHCH(Br)C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}\\xrightarrow{{{{\\left( {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)}_{\\text{3}}}{{\\text{O}}^\\Theta }{{\\text{K}}^ \\oplus }}}$<br> (d) Which of these reaction (s) will not produce saytzeff product ?','[{"text": "(d) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(c) only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(b) and (d)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(a), (c) and (d)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Bulky base and weak leaving group always prefer Hoffmann product',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_20054_question_1.png'),
(20055,'chemistry',54,1213,2907,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Benzene exhibit two different bond lengths between carbon and carbon<br></div><div class="column-right">Actual structure of benzene is a hybrid of following two structures. https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764953541/preptracker/questions/q_20055_col2_1764953540773.png</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Benzene has a uniform $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$ bond distance of $139 \\mathrm{pm}$, a value intermediate between the $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$ single bond $(154 \\mathrm{pm})$ and <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20055_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> double (134 pm) bonds. So, the option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20057,'chemistry',55,1237,2989,'The major product of the following reaction is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20057_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20057_explanation_2.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2019,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_20057_question_1.png'),
(20058,'chemistry',53,986,2293,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The ionisation energy of gallium remains nearly same as that of aluminium. <br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> This is due to shielding of outer shell electrons from the nucleus by the d-electrons of gallium.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In case of $\\mathrm{Ga}$, there are $10 \\mathrm{~d}$-electrons in the penultimate energy shell which shield the nuclear charge less effectively. The outer electron is held firmly by the nucleus. As a result the ionisation energy remains nearly the same as that of aluminium. So, option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20059,'chemistry',54,1213,2907,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Energy of resonance hybrid is equal to the average of energies of all canonical forms.<br></div><div class="column-right">Resonance hybrid cannot be represented by a single structure.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Resonance hybrid can be represented by a single structure. So, the option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20061,'chemistry',55,1237,2990,'The major product of the following reaction is:','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20061_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_20061_question_1.png'),
(20065,'chemistry',55,1241,3021,'The increasing order of nitration of the following compounds is:','[{"text": "(1) $ < $ (2) $ < $ (4) $ < $ (3)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(1) $ < $ (2) $ < $ (3) $ < $ (4)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(2) $ < $ (1) $ < $ (3) $ < $ (4)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(2) $ < $ (1) $ < $ (4) $ < $ (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Here the aniline is the least reactive due to formation of anilinium ion in acidic medium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2018,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_20065_question_1.png'),
(20066,'chemistry',53,987,2300,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{BF}_{3}$ is weaker Lewis acid than $\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}$.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> ${\\text{p}}\\pi {\\text{  -  p}}\\pi $ backbonding is stronger in $\\mathrm{BF}_{3}$ than in $\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}$.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{BF}_{3}$ is a weaker Lewis acid than $\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}$ due to the stronger electron-donating tendency (back bonding) of fluorine in $\\mathrm{BF}_{3}$ compared to chlorine in $\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}$. So availability of vacant orbital in $\\mathrm{BF}_{3}$ is less compared to $\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}$. So, option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20070,'chemistry',53,987,2303,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{B}(\\mathrm{OH})_{3}$ is acidic while $\\mathrm{In}(\\mathrm{OH})_{3}$ is basic.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> $\\mathrm{B}(\\mathrm{OH})_{3}$ has highly H-bonded network structure.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Due to small size and high ionisation enthalpy, $\\mathrm{B}$ in $\\mathrm{B}(\\mathrm{OH})_{3}$ accepts $\\mathrm{OH}^{-}$ ion from $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$ and thus, acts as a Lewis acid. However, due to large size and low ionisation enthalpy of ${\\text{In}}$, the ${\\text{ In  -  OH}}$ bond readily breaks and releases $\\mathrm{OH}^{-}$ ion, and $\\mathrm{In}(\\mathrm{OH})_{3}$ acts as a base. Boric acid has $\\mathrm{H}$ - bonded network structure. So, option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(20073,'chemistry',55,1237,2993,'The major product of the following reaction is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20073_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_20073_question_1.png'),
(20074,'chemistry',53,995,2331,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In $\\mathrm{C}_{60}$ fullerene is an allotrope of carbon.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In $\\mathrm{C}_{60}$ fullerene, five-membered rings are isolated from each other.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Fullerene, an allotrope of a carbon comprising carbon atoms arranged in spherical or ellipsoidal structures, which often includes isolated five-membered rings. It has soccer ball shape with 20 hexagons and 12 pentagons, which fuse only with hexagons. So, option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20075,'chemistry',54,1203,2874,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Acyclic compounds consist of straight or branched chain compounds.<br></div><div class="column-right">Alicyclic compounds contain carbon atoms joined in the form of a ring.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Acyclic or open chain compounds are also called aliphatic compounds and consist of straight or branched chain of carbon atoms. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20075_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Alicyclic or closed chain or ring compounds contain carbon atoms joined in the form of a ring (homocyclic). So, the option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20077,'chemistry',55,1240,3015,'Which of the following compounds is most reactive to an aqueous solution of sodium carbonate?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20077_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20078,'chemistry',53,995,2332,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Carbon monoxide is extremely toxic.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Carbon monoxide forms a stable complex with haemoglobin present in red blood cells.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Carbon monoxide $(\\mathrm{CO})$ is an extremely toxic gas due to its ability to bind strongly with hemoglobin in the blood, forming carboxyhemoglobin, which reduces the blood\'s  capacity to transport oxygen. So, option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20089,'chemistry',55,1237,2986,'The reagent needed for converting','[{"text": "Cat.Hydrogenation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2}$ /Lindlar catalyst", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Li} / \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{LiAlH}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'With Lithium in liquid ammonia, trans-alkene is almost an exclusive product.   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20089_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_20089_question_1.png'),
(20079,'chemistry',54,1212,2902,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A covalent bond may be cleaved either by heterolytic cleavage or by homolytic cleavage.<br></div><div class="column-right">Heterolytic cleavage of $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{Br}$ will given $\\mathop {\\rm{C}}\\limits^{\\rm{ + }} {{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\mkern 1mu} $ and ${\\rm{B}}{{\\rm{r}}^ - }$</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A covalent bond may be cleaved either by heterolytic cleavage or by homolytic cleavage.<br>In heterolytic cleavage, the bond breaks in such a fashion that the shared pair of electrons remains with one of the fragments. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20079_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> In homolytic cleavage, one of the electrons of the shared pair in a covalent bond goes with each of the bonded atoms. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20079_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> So, the option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20081,'chemistry',55,1237,2989,'Bromination of cyclohexene under conditions given below','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In presence of sunlight alkene undergoes free radical substitution.  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20081_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2016,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_20081_question_1.png'),
(20082,'chemistry',53,996,2340,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Silane is more reactive than methane.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The $\\mathrm{Si}$ and $\\mathrm{C}$-atoms are both $\\mathrm{sp}^{3}$ hybridized in the two compounds.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Silane $\\left(\\mathrm{SiH}_{4}\\right)$ is more reactive than methane $\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{4}\\right)$ primarily due to the difference in electronegativity between carbon and silicon, as well as the nature of the silicon-hydrogen ( $\\mathrm{Si-}$ $\\mathrm{H})$ bond compared to the carbon-hydrogen $(\\mathrm{C-}$ $\\mathrm{H})$ bond. $\\mathrm{C}$ and $\\mathrm{Si}$ both are $\\mathrm{sp}^{3}$ hybridised in $\\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ and $\\mathrm{SiH}_{4}$ respectively. So, option (2) is correct',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20083,'chemistry',54,1213,2910,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Inductive effect and resonance effect cause permanent polarisation of bond.<br></div><div class="column-right">Inductive effect involve electron displacements due to the influence of an atom or a substituted group present in the molecule.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The electron displacements in an organic molecule due to the influence of an atom or a substituted group present in the molecule cause permanent polarisation of the bond. Inductive effect and resonance effect are examples of this type of electronic displacement.<br>So, the option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20085,'chemistry',55,1237,2995,'The gas liberated in the electroysis of dipotassium succinate solution is','[{"text": "Ethane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethyne", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Propene", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ethene is obtained by electrolysis of dipotassium succinate as follows    <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20085_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />    <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20085_explanation_2.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   At anode : <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20085_explanation_3.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   At cathode:<br>${\\text{2}}{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ + }}}{\\text{ + 2}}{{\\text{e}}^{\\text{ - }}} \\to {\\text{[2H]}} \\to {{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20086,'chemistry',54,1205,2876,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Ethane and propane are homologues.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Ethane and propane have same general formula.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ethane formula: $\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}$<br>Propane formula : $\\mathrm{C}_{3} \\mathrm{H}_{8}$ Both ethane and propane are differ by $>\\mathrm{CH}_{2}$ group so, they are homologous. Ethane and propane are examples of alkane and have the general formula i.e., $\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{n}} \\mathrm{H}_{2 \\mathrm{n}+2}$. Homologous series molecules have same general formula. Assertion & Reason are true and the reason is the correct explanation for assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20087,'chemistry',53,986,2294,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Boron is metalloid.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Boron shows metallic nature.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Boron is metalloid. Metalloids possess metallic as well as non-metallic nature. So, option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20090,'chemistry',54,1209,2891,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Pent- 1- ene and pent- 2- ene are position isomers.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Position isomers differ in the position of functional group or a substituent.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Assertion and Reason are true and the reason is the correct explanation of the assertion. So, the option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20092,'chemistry',53,994,2326,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{CCl}_{4}$ is inert towards hydrolysis but $\\mathrm{SiCl}_{4}$ is readily hydrolysed.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Carbon cannot expand its octet but silicon can expand its octet.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{SiCl}_{4}$ readily undergoes hydrolysis with water because of the polarity of the $\\mathrm{Si}-\\mathrm{Cl}$ bonds and the nature of the central silicon atom. $\\mathrm{CCl}_{4}$ on the other hand, is inert towards hydrolysis because of the non-polar $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{Cl}$ bonds and the stability of carbon in its covalent compounds. And also due to non - availability of empty d orbitals So, option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20093,'chemistry',55,1234,2971,'The major product obtained in the photo catalysed bromination of 2-methylbutane is','[{"text": "1-Bromo-2-methylbutane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-Bromo-3-methylbutane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2-Bromo-3-methylbutane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2-Bromo-2-methylbutane", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The order of substitution in different alkanes is $3^\\circ  > 2^\\circ  > 1^\\circ $<br>Thus the bromination of 2- methyl butane mainly gives 2-Bromo -2-Methyl butane   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20093_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20093_explanation_2.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20094,'chemistry',54,1207,2880,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20094_qtext_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> is called cyclohexancarbonitrile.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It is an aromatic compound.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cyclohexanecarbonitrite is a saturated cyclic compound. So, the option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20096,'chemistry',53,995,2331,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Diamond is a bad conductor. <br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Graphite is a good conductor.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Diamond\'s poor conductivity is due to each carbon atom being tetrahedrally bonded in a hybridized state with no mobile electrons. Graphite\'s conductivity results from a hexagonal planar structure, leaving one p-electron per carbon atom free for heat and electricity conduction. So, option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20097,'chemistry',55,1239,3008,'Which one of the following class of compounds is obtained by polymerisation of acetylene?','[{"text": "Poly-yne", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Poly-ene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Poly-ester", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Poly-amine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Poly-ene. e.g<br>$\\mathop {3{\\text{CH}}}\\limits_{{\\text{ acetylene }}}  \\equiv {\\text{CH}} \\to \\mathop {{{\\text{C}}_6}{{\\text{H}}_6}}\\limits_{{\\text{ Benzene }}} $ <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20097_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20098,'chemistry',54,1210,2897,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Trans-1-chloropropene has higher dipole moment than cis-1-chloropropene.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The resultant of the two vectors in trans-1-chloropropene is more than in cis-1-chloropropene.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Trans is more polar due to the higher value of dipole moment due to the additive nature of $\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$ and $\\mathrm{Cl}$ vectors and have a higher dipole moment than cis. Both assertion and reason are correct and the reason is the correct explanation for assertion. So, the option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20100,'chemistry',53,988,2306,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In water, orthoboric acid behaves as a weak monobasic acid.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In water, orthoboric acid acts as a proton donor.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In water orthoboric acid accepts the hydroxyl ion by leaving proton and behaves as weak monobasic acid. But it cannot release it\'s own hydrogen as proton. So, option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20101,'chemistry',55,1237,2990,'In the hydroboration - oxidation reaction of propene with diborane, $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2}$ and $\\mathrm{NaOH}$, the organic compound formed is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{OH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CHOHCH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{OH}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{3} \\\\mathrm{COH}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CH = C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}\\xrightarrow[{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{,NaOH}}}]{{{{\\text{B}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{6}}}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{OH}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20102,'chemistry',54,1201,2868,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> All the hydrogen atoms in But-2-ene lie in one plane.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Carbon atoms in it are ${\\rm{s}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{\\rm{s}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ - }}$ hybridised.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The hydrogen atoms in but-2-ene are not present in the same plane. So, the option (4) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20104,'chemistry',53,993,2321,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{Pb}^{4+}$ compounds are stronger oxidizing agents than $\\mathrm{Sn}^{4+}$ compounds.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The higher oxidation states for the group 14 elements are more stable for the heavier members of the group due to inert pair effect.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The oxidizing action shows the following order $\\mathrm{Pb}^{4+}>\\mathrm{Sn}^{4+}>\\mathrm{Ge}^{4+}$<br>The lower oxidation state for the group 14 elements is more stable for heavier elements in the group due to inert pair effect. So, option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20105,'chemistry',55,1237,2990,'In the presence of peroxide, $\\mathrm{HCl}$ and $\\mathrm{HI}$ do not give anti-Markovnikoff\'s addition of alkenes because','[{"text": "One of the steps is endothermic in $\\\\mathrm{HCl}$ and $\\\\mathrm{HI}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both $\\\\mathrm{HCl}$ and $\\\\mathrm{HI}$ are strong acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HCl}$ is oxidising and the $\\\\mathrm{HI}$ is reducing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the steps are exothermic is $\\\\mathrm{HCl}$ and $\\\\mathrm{HI}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Anti-Markovnikov\'s addition is possible only in case of $\\mathrm{HBr}$ and not in $\\mathrm{HCl}$ and $\\mathrm{HI}$. In $\\mathrm{HBr}$ both the chain initiation and propagation steps are exothermic, while in $\\mathrm{HCl}$, first step is exothermic, and second step is endothermic and in $\\mathrm{HI}$, no step is exothermic. Hence $\\mathrm{HCl}$ and $\\mathrm{HI}$ do not undergo anti-Markovnikov\'s addition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20106,'chemistry',54,1212,2904,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{NO}_{2},-\\mathrm{CN},-\\mathrm{CNO}$ act as ambident nucleophiles <br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> These consist atoms of same period','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both assertion and reason are true and the reason is not the correct explanation of the assertion. So, the option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20108,'chemistry',53,986,2296,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{Al}$ forms $\\left[\\mathrm{AlF}_{6}\\right]^{3-}$ but $\\mathrm{B}$ does not form $\\left[\\mathrm{BF}_{6}\\right]^{3-}$.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> B does not react with fluorine.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Boron does not expand its octet due to non availability of vacant d-orbitals (sub-shell) in its valence shell, but alluminium can . Boron reacts with $\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ to form boron trifluorides. So, option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20109,'chemistry',55,1237,2990,'The addition of $\\mathrm{HI}$ in the presence of peroxide catalyst does not follow anti-Markovnikov\'s rule because','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HI}$ is a strong reducing agent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "H-I bond is too strong to be broken homolytically", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I atom combines with $\\\\mathrm{H}$ atom to give back $\\\\mathrm{HI}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Iodine atom is not reactive enough to add across a double bond", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{HI}$ does not exhibit peroxide effect. HI bond although dissociates easily into iodine radicals, they being bigger in size are not much reactive but recombine together to form iodine molecule.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20110,'chemistry',54,1213,2910,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Inductive and electomeric effects require polar nature in the molecule.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Polar nature in inductive effect is a must but not necessarily in electomeric effect.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Assertion is false, but reason is true. So, the option (4) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20112,'chemistry',53,995,2331,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Diamond and graphite do not have the same crystal structure.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Diamond is crystalline while graphite is amorphous.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Diamond is polymeric giant $3 \\mathrm{D}$ molecule where has graphite as two dimensional layer like structure with hexagonal rings. Diamond and graphite both are crystalline forms of carbon. So, option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20113,'chemistry',55,1234,2972,'Some oxidation reactions of methane are given below. Which of them is/are controlled oxidation reactions?','[{"text": "${\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{4}}}{\\\\text{(g) + 2}}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{(g)}} \\\\to {\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{(g) + 2}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{O(l)}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{4}}}{\\\\text{(g) + }}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{(g)}} \\\\to {\\\\text{C(s) + 2}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{O(l)}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{4}}}{\\\\text{(g)   +   }}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{(g)}}\\\\xrightarrow{{{\\\\text{M}}{{\\\\text{o}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{3}}}}}{\\\\text{HCHO   +   }}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{O}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{2C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{4}}}{\\\\text{(g) + }}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{(g)}}\\\\xrightarrow{{{\\\\text{Cu/100 atm}}}}{\\\\text{2C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{3}}}{\\\\text{OH}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20114,'chemistry',54,1214,2912,'The pair of electron in the given carbanion, $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{C} \\equiv \\mathrm{C}^{\\Theta}$, is present in which of the following orbitals?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{sp}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2p}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20114_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> ( $2 \\sigma+2 \\pi$, -ve charge is considered to be sigma)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20116,'chemistry',53,987,2299,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Al becomes passive in conc. $\\mathrm{HNO}_{3}$.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Conc. $\\mathrm{HNO}_{3}$ has no action on aluminium metal.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Aluminum (Al) becomes passive when treated with concentrated $\\mathrm{HNO}_{3}$ because concentrated $\\mathrm{HNO}_{3}$ is an oxidizing agent that produces a protective layer of oxide on the surface of aluminum metal. So, option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
