(20129,'chemistry',53,992,2315,'For compound having the formula $\\mathrm{GaAlCl}_{4}$, the correct option from the following is','[{"text": "Ga is more electronegative than Al and is present as a cationic part of the salt  ${\\\\rm{GaAlC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_4}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oxidation state of Ga in the salt  ${\\\\rm{GaAlC}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_4}$  is +3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ga is coordinated with Cl in $\\\\mathrm{GaAlCl}_{4}$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cl forms bond with both Al and Ga in $\\\\mathrm{GaAlCl}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Gallous tetrachloro aluminate is $\\mathrm{Ga}^{+} \\mathrm{AlCl}_{4}^{-}$<br>$2 \\mathrm{Ga}+\\mathrm{Ga}^{+} \\mathrm{GaCl}_{4}^{-}+2 \\mathrm{Al}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}_{6} \\xrightarrow{190^{\\circ}} 4 \\mathrm{Ga}^{+} \\mathrm{AlCl}_{4}^{-}$<br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/53_20129_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>Ga is cationic part of salt $\\mathrm{GaAlCl}_{4}$.<br>Electronegativity of Al and Ga respectively are 1.61 and 1.81 .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
