(20137,'chemistry',53,988,2309,'The incorrect statement from the following for borazine is','[{"text": "It has electronic delocalization.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It can react with water.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is a cyclic compound.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It contains banana bonds.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/53_20137_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>Due to grater difference in electronegativity values of \' B \'  &  \' N \' atoms electrons are partially delocalised in borazine. It has no banana bond. It is non-polar, cyclic and reacts with water :<br>$\\left[\\mathrm{B}_{3} \\mathrm{~N}_{3} \\mathrm{H}_{6}+9 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\rightarrow 3 \\mathrm{NH}_{3}+3 \\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{BO}_{3}+3 \\mathrm{H}_{2}\\right]$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
