(20145,'chemistry',53,995,2336,'Read Assertion and Reason carefully and mark correct option.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Carbon forms two important oxides -CO and $\\mathrm{CO}_{2} . \\mathrm{CO}$ is neutral whereas $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ is acidic in nature.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ can combine with water in a limited way to form carbonic acid, while CO is sparingly soluble in water.','[{"text": "Assertion is not correct but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is not correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'CO - neutral $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ - acidic<br>CO is slightly soluble in water, $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ on dissolving in water form carbonic acid.',NULL,'Easy','Assertion and Reason',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20149,'chemistry',53,988,2305,'During the borax bead test with $\\mathrm{CuSO}_{4}$,  a  blue green colour of the bead was observed in oxidising flame due to the formation of','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Cu}_{3} \\\\mathrm{~B}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Cu}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{BO}_{2}\\\\right)_{2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "CuO", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cu", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When $\\mathrm{CuSO}_{4}$ is heated on a loop of Pt wire with borax, blue green coloured $\\mathrm{Cu}\\left(\\mathrm{BO}_{2}\\right)_{2}$ bead is formed.<br>${\\text{CuS}}{{\\text{O}}_4}\\xrightarrow{\\Delta }{\\text{CuO}} + {\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_3}$<br>${\\text{CuO}} + {{\\text{B}}_2}{{\\text{O}}_3} \\to \\mathop {{\\text{Cu}}{{\\left( {{\\text{B}}{{\\text{O}}_2}} \\right)}_2}}\\limits_{{\\text{ Blue - green colour }}} $',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
