(20154,'chemistry',53,986,2293,'Read the Statement A and Statement B carefully and mark the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The decrease in first ionisation enthalpy from B to Al is much larger than that from Al to Ga .</div><div class="column-right">The d – orbitals in Ga are completely filled.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is incorrect but statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements A and B are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct but statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements A and B are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The decrease in first ionisation enthalpy from B to Al is associated with increase in size. The discontinuity between Al and Ga is due to low screening effect of d – electrons.<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n  {{{\\text{I}}^{{\\text{st }}}}{\\text{Ionisation}}\\,\\,{\\text{enthalpy}}\\,({\\text{kJ}}/{\\text{mol}})}&{\\text{B}}&{{\\text{Al}}}&{{\\text{Ga}}} \\\\ \n  {}&{801}&{577}&{579} \n\\end{array}$<br>In $\\mathrm{Ga}:[\\mathrm{Ar}] 3 \\mathrm{~d}^{10} 4 \\mathrm{~s}^{2} 4 \\mathrm{p}^{1}, \\mathrm{~d}$ – orbitals in Ga are completely filled.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
