(20160,'chemistry',55,1240,3020,'Toluene is nitrated and the resulting product is reduced with tin and hydrochloride acid. The product so obtained is diazotised and then heated with cuprous bromide. The reaction mixture so formed contains','[{"text": "Mixture of o- and p- bromotoluenes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mixture of o- and p-dibromobenzenes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mixture of o- and p-bromoanilines", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mixture of o- and m-bromotoluenes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Toluene   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20160_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />    contains ${\\text{ - C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}$ group  which is o-, p-directing group so on nitration of toluene the $-\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ group will occupy o-, p- positions.<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20160_explanation_2.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />    On reduction with $\\mathrm{Sn} / \\mathrm{HCl}$ they will form corresponding anilines in which $-\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ group changes to $-\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$. The mixture now contains  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20160_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   These anilines when diazotized and then treated with $\\mathrm{CuBr}$ forms o-, p-Bromotoluenes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
