(20171,'chemistry',53,987,2300,'The Lewis acid character of boron trihalides follows the order','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{BF}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{BBr}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{BI}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{BI}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{BBr}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{BF}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{BBr}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{BI}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{BF}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{BF}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{BBr}_{3}>\\\\mathrm{BI}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Extent of back bonding reduces down the group leading to more Lewis acidic strength.<br>$\\mathrm{BF}_{3}>\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}>\\mathrm{BBr}_{3}>\\mathrm{BI}_{3}$ (Extent of back bonding)<br>( $2 \\mathrm{p}-2 \\mathrm{p}) \\quad(2 \\mathrm{p}-3 \\mathrm{p}) \\quad(2 \\mathrm{p}-4 <br>\\mathrm{p}) \\quad(2 \\mathrm{p}-5 \\mathrm{p})$<br>So, $\\mathrm{BF}_{3} < \\mathrm{BCl}_{3} < \\mathrm{BBr}_{3} < \\mathrm{BI}_{3}$ (Lewis acidic nature).<br>On the basis of small bonding smaller be the halide atom, more effective the back bonding  & shows less tendency  to accept a pair of electrons.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20172,'chemistry',55,1237,2991,'Ozonolysis of an organic compound \'A\' produces acetone and propionaldhyde in equimolar mixture. Identify \' A \' from the following compounds','[{"text": "1 - Pentene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 - Pentene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2- Methyl - 2 - pentene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2 - Methyl - 1 - pentene", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'From the products formed it is clear that the compound has 5 carbon atoms with a double bond and methyl group on $2^{\\text {nd }}$ carbon atom.<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20172_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20172_explanation_2.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
