(20188,'chemistry',55,1240,3018,'For preparing monoalkyl benzene, acylation process is preferred than direct alkylation because','[{"text": "In alkylation, a poisonous gas is evolved", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In alkylation, large amount of heat is evolved", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In alkylation, polyalkylated product is formed", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alkylation is very costly", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'For preparing monoalkylbenzene, acylation route is preferred rather than direct alkylation. This is because of the fact that during alkylation, alkyl group is introduced, which being ring activating group, accelerates further alkylation to form di-, tri- and tetra- poly alkylated product.    <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20188_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  On the other hand, during acylation we get acylbenzene (e.g. acetylbenzene); acyl group, being deactivating group does not allow further acylation easily. Hence the reaction stops at the monoacyl stage which then can be reduced to alkyl benzene easily.<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20188_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20189,'chemistry',54,1211,2901,'Match the column I with column II and choose the correct option<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. $\\begin{array}{l}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{COOH}}\\,\\,{\\rm{\\&amp; }}\\\\{\\rm{HCOOC}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}\\end{array}$<br>B. 1  - butene &amp; 2 - butene<br>C. diethyl ether &amp; methyl propyl ether<br>D. Butene and 2 - methyl propane</div><div class="column-right">P. Chain isomers<br>Q. Metamers<br>R. Position isomers<br>S. Functional isomers</div></div>','[{"text": "A - S, B - R, C - Q, D - P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Q, B - R, C - S, D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - S, C - P, D - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - P, C - S, D - R", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'(A) $\\mathop {{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{COOH}}}\\limits_{\\left( {{\\rm{Acid}}} \\right)} $ and $\\underset{\\text { (Esid) }}{\\mathrm{HCOOCH}_{3}}$ : Function isomers<br>(B) 1-Butene and 2-Butene: Position isomers (Due to difference in position of double bond)<br>C - Q; <br>$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{OCH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{3}$ and $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{OCH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{3}$ : Metamers<br> D - P;<br> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20189_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> So, the option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
