(20193,'chemistry',54,1210,2897,'Geometrical isomerism is shown by','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$-\\\\mathrm{C} \\\\equiv \\\\mathrm{C}-$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$-\\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{C}-$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "none of these.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Geometrical isomerism is shown by molecule with same molecular formula but differ in arrangement of atoms or groups in space due to hindered rotation around the double bonded atoms <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20193_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> When two group attached to a carbon atom are different. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20193_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2007,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
