(20196,'chemistry',55,1241,3021,'Which order is correct for the decreasing reactivity for ring monobromination of the following compounds?<br>$\\begin{gathered}\n  {{\\text{C}}_{\\text{6}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{,}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\text{C}}_{\\text{6}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}}{\\text{COOH,}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\text{C}}_{\\text{6}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{6}}}{\\text{,}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\text{C}}_{\\text{6}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}}{\\text{N}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{?}} \\hfill \\\\\n  {\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{I}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{II}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{III}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{IV}} \\hfill \\\\ \n\\end{gathered} $','[{"text": "I $>$ II $>$ III $>$ IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I $&gt;$ III $&gt;$ II $&gt;$ IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II $>$ III $>$ IV $>$ I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III $>$ I $>$ II $>$ IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{CH}_{3}$ is most reactive due to the presence of $-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$ group (a + I group), followed by benzene due to absence of any - I group, followed by benzoic acid due to - $\\mathrm{COOH}$ group (a weaker -I group) and then nitrobenzene (having $-\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$, a strong - I group).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
