(20216,'chemistry',54,1214,2913,'The total number of electrons around the carbon atom of methyl free radical are','[{"text": "nine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "six", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "seven", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "eight", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The total number of electrons around the carbon atom of methyl free radical $\\left(\\stackrel{*}{\\mathrm{C}} \\mathrm{H}_{3}\\right)$ is seven. It\'s structure is shown below. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20216_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Each $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}$ bond two electrons and one unpaired electron on carbon atom.<br>Total electrons present $=3 \\times 2+1=7$ electrons',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2020,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
