(20301,'chemistry',53,995,2331,'Which of the following statement is correct for isotope of carbon?','[{"text": "Graphite is conductor of electricity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diamond have all $\\\\mathrm{sp}^{3}$ hybridised carbon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Graphite is more stable thermodynamically than diamond", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The explanation of given statements are as follows : <br>(1) Graphite is conductor of electricity because it has 1 free valence electron which does not participate in bonding. Thus, statement (1) is correct. <br>(2) Diamond has a three dimensional structure in which $\\mathrm{sp}^{3}$-hybridised $\\mathrm{C}$-atoms are arranged tetrahedrally. Thus, statement (2) is correct. <br>(3) Graphite is thermodyiamically more stable than diamond and its free energy of formation is less than that of diamond. However, entropy of graphite is more than that of diamond.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
