(20314,'chemistry',54,1209,2892,'Methoxy methane and ethanol are','[{"text": "functional isomers", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "optical isomers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "position isomers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "chain isomers.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20314_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Both compounds have the same molecular formula but posses different functional group. Methoxy methane has -O- (ether group) whereas ethanol has<br>-OH group. So, they are functional isomer to each other.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
