(20324,'chemistry',55,1234,2973,'Which of the following compounds liberate methane when treated with excess of methyl magnesium iodide in dry ether?<br>(A) $\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{OH}$<br>(B) $\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{C} \\equiv \\mathrm{CH}$<br>(C) $\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{CO}_{2} \\mathrm{H}$<br>(D) $\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{CHO}$','[{"text": "A, B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B, C", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The compounds which have active hydrogen atom liberate methane when treated with $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{MgI}$.<br>${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{ - C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ -  C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ -  OH  +  C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{ -  MgI}}$   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20324_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />    ${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{ -  C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ -  C}} \\equiv {\\text{CH  +  C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{MgI}}$  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20324_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  ${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{ -  C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ -  COOH  +  C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{MgI}}$  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20324_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20325,'chemistry',54,1211,2901,'Identify the correct statement in the following:','[{"text": "Dimethyl ether and ethanol are chain isomers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethanoic acids and methyl methnoate are position isomers.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "n- butane and isobutane are functional isomers.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Propan-1-ol and propan-2-ol are position isomers.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'(1) Alcohols and ethers are functional isomers :<br>$\\underset{\\substack{\\text { Dimethyl ether } \\\\ \\text { (Ether) }}}{\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{O}-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}}, \\quad \\underset{\\substack{\\text { Ethanol } \\\\ \\text { (Alcohol) }}}{\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{OH}}$<br>(2) Acids and esters are Functional isomers :<br>$\\mathop {{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{COOH}}}\\limits_{\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{Ethanoic}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{acid}}}\\\\{\\left( {{\\rm{Carboxylic}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{acid}}} \\right)}\\end{array}} $ <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20325_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> (3) n-Butane and isobutane are chain isomers :<br>$\\mathop {{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}\\,\\, - \\,\\,{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\,\\, - \\,\\,{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\,\\, - \\,\\,{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}}\\limits_{{\\rm{n}}\\,\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,\\,{\\rm{Butane}}} $ <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20325_explanation_2.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
