(20329,'chemistry',54,1210,2897,'Which of the following is correct set of physical properties of the geometrical isomers?<br>[DM - Dipole Moment, BP - Boiling Point, MP - Melting point, S - Stability]','[{"text": "DM - I > II, BP - I > II, MP - II > I, S - I > II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DM - II > I, BP - II > I, MP - II > I, S - II > I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DM - I > II, BP - I > II, MP - I > II, S - I > II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DM - II > I, BP - II > I, MP - I > II, S - I > II", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20329_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20329_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> first has more dipole moment than the second. Therefore, its boiling point will be higher. Melting point depends on symmetry; therefore, I was higher melting point than II. Steric crowding in I is more than II; therefore, I is more stable than II. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20329_explanation_3.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/54_20329_question_1.png'),
