(20434,'chemistry',55,1234,2969,'In which of the following reaction in the preparation of ethane a new $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$ bond is formed?','[{"text": "Sabatier-Senderen\'s reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reduction of ethyl iodide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decarboxylation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kolbe\'s electrolysis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20389,'chemistry',54,1213,2906,'Base strength of<br>(A) $\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{C} \\stackrel{\\oplus}{\\mathrm{C}} \\mathrm{H}_{2}$<br>(B) $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{C}=\\stackrel{\\oplus}{\\mathrm{C}} \\mathrm{H}$ and<br>(C) ${\\rm{H}} - {\\rm{C}} \\equiv \\mathop {\\rm{C}}\\limits^ \\oplus  $ is in the order of','[{"text": "$\\\\left( {\\\\rm{C}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ > }}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{B}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ > }}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{A}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left( {\\\\rm{A}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ > }}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{C}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ > }}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{B}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left( {\\\\rm{A}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ > }}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{B}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ > }}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{C}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left( {\\\\rm{B}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ > }}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{A}} \\\\right){\\\\rm{ > }}\\\\left( {\\\\rm{C}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The stronger is the acid, the weaker is its conjugate base.<br>Acidic nature:<br>$\\mathrm{CH} \\equiv \\mathrm{CH}>\\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\\mathrm{CH}_{2}>\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$<br>Conjugate basic:<br>$\\mathrm{CH} \\equiv \\mathrm{C}^{-} < \\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\\mathrm{CH}^{-} < \\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}^{-}$ nature.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20390,'chemistry',55,1237,2995,'Ethylene adds on a molecule of sulphur monochloride to give a poisonous gas used in war, known as:','[{"text": "Calor gas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isocyanide gas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liquefied petroleum gas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mustard gas", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ethylene adds on a molecule of sulphur monochloride to give a poisonous gas, known mustard gas and was used for the first time in first world war (1914-18)  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20390_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20393,'chemistry',54,1213,2907,'Consider the following compounds The correct order of basic strength is','[{"text": "i $>$ ii $>$ iii $>$ iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii $>$ iv $>$ ii $>$ i", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iv $>$ i $>$ iii $>$ ii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iv $>$ iii $>$ ii $>$ i", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'+ I nature of $\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$ group increases electrons density on $\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ group.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/54_20393_question_1.jpg'),
(20394,'chemistry',55,1237,2990,'In the presence of peroxide, hydrogen chloride and hydrogen iodide do not give anti-Markovnikov\'s addition to alkenes because','[{"text": "Both are highly ionic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One is oxidising and the other is reducing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One of the steps is endothermic in both cases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All steps are exothermic in both cases.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The reaction of $\\mathrm{HCl}$ with carbon radical in case of $\\mathrm{HCl}$, and addition of iodine radical to double bond in case of HI are endothermic steps.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20397,'chemistry',54,1215,2918,'Which of the following reactions is an example of nucleophilic substitution reaction?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{RX + Mg}} \\\\to {\\\\rm{RMgX}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{RX}+\\\\mathrm{KOH} \\\\longrightarrow \\\\mathrm{ROH}+\\\\mathrm{KX}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$2 \\\\mathrm{RX}+2 \\\\mathrm{Na} \\\\longrightarrow \\\\mathrm{R}-\\\\mathrm{R}+2 \\\\mathrm{NaX}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{RX}+\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\longrightarrow \\\\mathrm{RH}+\\\\mathrm{HX}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{KOH} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{K}^{+}+\\mathrm{OH}^{-}$<br>$\\mathrm{RX}+\\mathrm{OH}^{-} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{R}-\\mathrm{OH}+\\mathrm{X}^{-}$<br>Nucleophiles are either negatively charged or lone pair of electrons heaving species<br>e.g., ${\\text{O}}{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ - }}},\\mathop {\\text{N}}\\limits^{..} {{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}$, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20398,'chemistry',55,1237,2995,'An alkyl chloride (A) produces a single alkene on reaction with sodium ethoxide and ethanol. The alkene further undergoes hydrogenation to yield 2-methylbutane. The alkyl chloride (A) is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{ClCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{ClCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{ClCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right) \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{C}(\\\\mathrm{Cl})\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right) \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20398_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20399,'chemistry',53,1000,2349,'How many molecules of water of crystallization are present in one molecule of borax?','[{"text": "8", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "10", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The formula of borax is ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{B}}_{\\rm{4}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{7}}} \\cdot {\\rm{10}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$ However, it contains tetranuclear unit${\\left[ {{{\\rm{B}}_{\\rm{4}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{5}}}{{\\left( {{\\rm{OH}}} \\right)}_{\\rm{4}}}} \\right]^{{\\rm{2}} - }}$. So, the formula is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Na}_{2}\\left[\\mathrm{~B}_{4} \\mathrm{O}_{5}(\\mathrm{OH})_{4}\\right] \\cdot 8 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}}}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20401,'chemistry',54,1215,2921,'The conversion of 2-methylpropan-1-ol to 2-methylpropan-2-ol is','[{"text": "addition reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "rearrangement reaction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "substitution reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "elimination reaction", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The conversion of 2-methylpropan-1-ol to 2-methylpropan-2-ol is a rearrangement reaction. In these reactions, the carbon skeleton of a molecule is rearranged to give a structural isomer of the original molecule. Here, the alcohol group of 2-methylpropan-1-ol moves from one atom to another atom in the same molecule to give 2-methylpropan-2-ol. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20401_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
