(20465,'chemistry',53,993,2319,'Consider these two sets of bond enthalpies (in $\\mathrm{kJ} / \\mathrm{mol}$ ):<br>$\\mathrm{X}=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc}\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C} & \\mathrm{Si}-\\mathrm{Si} & \\mathrm{Ge}-\\mathrm{Ge} & \\mathrm{Sn}-\\mathrm{Sn} \\\\240 & 260 & 297 & 348\\end{array}\\right]$<br>(corresponding values are not in the same order)<br>$\\mathrm{Y}=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc}\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{F} & \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{Cl} & \\mathrm{Si}-\\mathrm{F} & \\mathrm{Si}-\\mathrm{Cl} \\\\326 & 360 & 439 & 536\\end{array}\\right]$<br>Sum of bond enthalpies for $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$ and $\\mathrm{Si}-\\mathrm{F}$ bond is ____.','[{"text": "348", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "536", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "884", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1080", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$(\\mathrm{X})$ The reason of high catenation tendency of carbon is its high bond energy.<br>Bond energy for $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}=348 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol}$<br>(Y) The difference in electronegativity is highest for $\\mathrm{Si}-\\mathrm{F}$ bond.<br>Hence, bond energy for $\\mathrm{Si}-\\mathrm{F}=536 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol}$<br>Sum of bond enthalpies $=348+536$<br>$=884 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
