(20503,'chemistry',55,1240,3015,'An aromatic compound contains ____ $\\pi$-electrons','[{"text": "$4 \\\\mathrm{n}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{4 n + 1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{4 n + 2}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{4 n + 3}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'An aromatic compound contains  ${\\text{(4n + 2)}}\\,\\,\\pi $ electrons. It is according to Huckel\'s rule, which represents the aromaticity of the molecules. Aromatic compounds possess a sweet smell which is characteristic and different from other fragments.<br>The term aromatic compounds is now used for benzene and the compounds structurally related to benzene, even if they do not possess a sweet smell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
