(20514,'chemistry',55,1243,3024,'Propyne and Propene can be distinguished by','[{"text": "Conc. $\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{SO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$ in $\\\\mathrm{CCl}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{Dil KMn}}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{4}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{AgN}}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{3}}}\\\\,{\\\\text{in N}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{3}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ammonical silver nitrate and ammonical cuprous chloride give precipitate, only with terminal alkynes (propyne, $\\left.\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{C} \\equiv \\mathrm{CH}\\right)$ and the same reactions not given by the propene.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20515,'chemistry',54,1209,2895,'Maximum enol content is in','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20515_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  In acetyl acetone, the enol form is stabilised by $\\mathrm{H}$ - bonding, hence it has more enol content than others.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20518,'chemistry',55,1239,3009,'Propyne on ozonolysis in the presence of ${{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}$ is<br>(1) Ethanoic acid<br>(2) Methanoic acid<br>(3) Propanoic acid<br>(4) None<br>The correct answer is -','[{"text": "1, 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2, 3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3, 4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1, 3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20518_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />    <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20518_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  ${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{COOH}}\\,{\\text{ + }}\\,{\\text{HCOOH}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20519,'chemistry',54,1210,2897,'Among the following, the most stable compound is','[{"text": "cis-1, 2-Cyclohexanediol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "trans-1,2-Cyclohexanediol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "cis-1,3-Cyclohexanediol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "trans-1,3-Cyclohexanediol", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Among 1,2 and 1, 3 configurations, 1, 3 is more stable due to less repulsion. Further among cis and trans configurations, the trans is more stable due to less crowding. Hence trans-1, 3Cyclohexanediol is the most stable among the given compounds.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20522,'chemistry',54,1211,2901,'$\\mathrm{C}_{8} \\mathrm{H}_{16}$ that can form cis-trans geometrical isomers and also has a chiral centre, is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20522_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Compound (1) will exhibit geometrical isomerism and have chiral centre so exhibits optical isomerism, while compound (2) exhibits geometrical isomerism but cannot exhibit optical isomerism due to absence of chiral carbon.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2008,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20523,'chemistry',55,1239,3006,'Acetylenic hydrocarbons are acidic because','[{"text": "Sigma electron density of ${\\\\text{C  -  H}}$  bond in acetylene is nearer a carbon which has $50 \\\\%$ s-character", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Acetylene has only one hydrogen atom at each carbon atom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acetylene contains least number of hydrogen atoms among the possible", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acetylene belongs to the class of alkynes with formula $\\\\mathrm{C}_{n} \\\\mathrm{H}_{2 n-2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The acidic character of $\\mathrm{H}$ is, ${\\text{F -  H  >  O  -  H  >  }} \\equiv {\\text{ C  -  H  >  N  -  H ; H}}$ atom attached on F, O, N and triply bonded carbon is acidic.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20526,'chemistry',54,1210,2897,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Boiling points of cis-isomers are higher than trans-isomers.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Dipole moments of cis-isomers are higher than trans-isomers.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Boiling points of isomeric compounds depend on dipole - dipole interactions and cis isomers have greater dipole moments (more polar) than trans - isomers (less polar).<br>Thus, both Assertion  and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Easy','Assertion and Reason',2008,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20527,'chemistry',55,1239,3007,'The number of structural and stereoisomers of a bromo compound, formed by the addition of one $\\mathrm{HBr}$ molecule to 2-Pentyne respectively are:','[{"text": "6 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 and 4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4 and 6", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The addition of $\\mathrm{HBr}$ to 2-pentyne gives two<br>structural isomers (I) and (II).  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20527_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />    Each one of these structures (I and II) will exist as a pair of geometrical isomers.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20528,'chemistry',53,995,2332,'What is the bond order of carbon monoxide?','[{"text": "0.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2.5", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n\\left( {\\sigma {\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\sigma ^{\\rm{*}}}{\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\sigma {\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\sigma ^{\\rm{*}}}{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\pi {\\rm{2p}}_{\\rm{x}}^{\\rm{2}} \\equiv \\pi {\\rm{2p}}_{\\rm{y}}^{\\rm{2}}\\sigma {\\rm{2p}}_{\\rm{z}}^{\\rm{2}}} \\right)\\\\\n{\\rm{ Bond order }} = \\frac{1}{2}\\left( {\\,{{\\rm{N}}_b} - {{\\rm{N}}_a}} \\right)\\\\\n\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, = \\frac{1}{2}(10 - 4) = 3.0\n\\end{array}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20530,'chemistry',54,1210,2897,'Which will not show geometrical isomerism?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}=\\\\mathrm{NOH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HO}-\\\\mathrm{N}=\\\\mathrm{N}-\\\\mathrm{OH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}=\\\\mathrm{NOH}$<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Compounds having either $\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{C}$ or $\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{N}$ exhibit geometrical isomerism but the other main condition for exhibiting geometrical isomerism is the presence of two different groups on double bonded carbon atoms.<br>Since in ketoxime, $\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{NOH}$, two same $\\left(-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)$ groups are present on double bonded carbon atom, its other form is not possible and it doesn\'t exhibit geometrical isomerism.<br>Compounds with $\\mathrm{N}=\\mathrm{N}$ having two<br>geometrical forms are as follows: <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20530_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20531,'chemistry',55,1237,2986,'In the given reaction<br>${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{  -  C}} \\equiv {\\text{C  -  C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{Na/N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{(e)}}}}[{\\text{X}}]$<br>$[{\\text{X}}]$  will be','[{"text": "Butane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "trans-2-Butene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "cis-2-Butene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-Butene", "isCorrect": false}]',1,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
