(20542,'chemistry',54,1210,2898,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Diastereomers have different physical properties.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> They are non - superimposable mirror images.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The optical isomers which are not related to each other as object and mirror images are known as diastereomers. They may differ in physical and chemical properties. So, Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.<br>',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2006,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20543,'chemistry',55,1239,3007,'The product that results when one mole of 1-pentyne is first treated with one mole of $\\mathrm{HCl}$ and then with one mole of $\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{Br}$ is','[{"text": "1-Chloro-2-bromopentane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2-Chloro-1-bromopentane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2-Bromo-2-chloropentane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1-Chloro-1-bromopentane", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both $\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{Cl}$ and $\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{Br}$ add in Markovnikoff\'s fashion   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20543_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
