(20591,'chemistry',53,994,2324,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{SiO}_{2}}}}$ and ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{GeO}_{2}}}}$ are acidic while SnO and PbO are amphoteric in nature.</div><div class="column-right">Allotropic forms of carbon are due to property of catenation and ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{p} \\pi-\\mathrm{d} \\pi}}}$ bond formation.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{SiO}_{2}}}}$ and ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{GeO}_{2}}}}$ are acidic while SnO and PbO are amphoteric in nature. Due to property of catenation and ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{p} \\pi-\\mathrm{p} \\pi}}}$ bond formation, carbon is able to show allotropic forms. So, the correct option is (2)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
