(20599,'chemistry',53,993,2318,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The electronegativity of group 14 elements from Si to Pb , gradually decreases.</div><div class="column-right">Group 14 contains non-metallic, metallic, as well as metalloid elements.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Electronegativity values do not decrease in a regular manner in group 14.<br>Group 14 contains non-metal (carbon), metalloids (Si and Ge) and metals ( ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Sn}, \\mathrm{Pb}}}}$ ). So, the correct option is (2)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
