(20622,'chemistry',55,1237,2986,'The conversion of 2, 3-Dibromobutane to 2- Butene with $\\mathrm{Zn}$ and alcohol is','[{"text": "Redox reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\alpha$ - elimination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\beta$-elimination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CHBrCHBrC}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{ Zn/alcohol }}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CH = CHC}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}$<br>Since two bromine atoms are lost from adjacent carbon atoms, the reaction is known as $\\beta$ - elimination.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
