(20613,'chemistry',53,992,2315,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Group 13 trivalent halides get easily hydrolyzed by water due to their covalent nature.</div><div class="column-right">${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{AlCl}_{3}}}}$ upon hydrolysis in acidified aqueous solution forms octahedral ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{Al}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{3+}}}}$ ion.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Most of the group 13 halides being covalent, are hydrolysed in water. Aluminium chloride in acidified aqueous solution forms geometry ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{Al}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{3+}}}}$ ion with octahedral geometry. So, the correct option is (3)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
