(20616,'chemistry',54,1209,2891,'Which of the following pairs of alkenes is an example of position isomers?','[{"text": "But-1-ene and 2-Methylprop-1-ene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "But-1-ene and 2-Methylbut-1- ene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "But-1-ene and But-2-ene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "But-2- ene and 2-Methylprop-1-ene", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{CH}=\\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$ and<br>But-2-ene<br>$\\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$<br>But-1-ene (difference in position of double bond).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20617,'chemistry',53,987,2298,'Identify the correct statements about p -block elements and their compounds.<br>(I) Non-metals have higher electronegativity than metals.<br>(II) Non-metals have lower ionisation enthalpy than metals.<br>(III) Compounds formed between highly reactive non-metals and highly reactive metals are generally ionic.<br>(IV) The non-metal oxides are generally basic in nature.<br>(V) The metal oxides are generally acidic or neutral in nature.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.','[{"text": "(IV) and (V) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I) and (III) only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(II) and (IV) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(II) and (III) only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Non-metals have higher ionisation enthalpy than metals. Non-metallic oxides are generally acidic, while metallic oxides are basic in nature. So, the correct option is (2)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20618,'chemistry',55,1237,2988,'The most stable diene among the following is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both the double bonds are disubstituted and in trans configuration which minimises steric repulsion and enhances conjugation in   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20618_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20620,'chemistry',54,1211,2901,'Identify the isomerism exhibited by methoxyethane and propan-1-ol','[{"text": "Position isomerism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chain isomerism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Functional group isomerism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metamerism", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\underset{\\text { Methoxyethane }}{\\mathrm{CH}_{2}}-\\mathrm{O}-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$ (ether) and<br>$\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\underset{\\text { Propan-1-ol }}{\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}}-\\mathrm{OH}(\\text { alcohol })$<br>Both have same molecular formual $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{3} \\mathrm{H}_{8} \\mathrm{O}\\right)$ but different functional groups.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20621,'chemistry',53,986,2293,'The correct order of the first ionisation enthalpy is','[{"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Al}>\\\\mathrm{Ga}>\\\\mathrm{Tl}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Tl}>\\\\mathrm{Ga}>\\\\mathrm{Al}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Ga}>\\\\mathrm{Al}>\\\\mathrm{B}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{>\\\\mathrm{Al}>}}}$ Ga<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/53_20621_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  The ionisation enthalpy decreases from B to Al due to increase in atomic size. The ionisation energy of Ga is slightly higher than that of Al due to ineffective screening of 3 d -electrons.<br> In Tl , the nuclear charge increases considerably which outweighs the screening effect of all the electrons of the inner shells. Hence, ionisation enthalpy of Tl is much higher than ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Al}, \\mathrm{Ga}}}}$, In.<br>So, correct order is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{\\mathrm{B}>\\mathrm{Tl}>\\mathrm{Ga}>\\mathrm{Al}>\\mathrm{In}}}}$. So, the correct option is (2)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20624,'chemistry',54,1203,2874,'Which from the following statements is true for tetrahydrofuran?','[{"text": "It is homocyclic aromatic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is heterocyclic aromatic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is aromatic non - benzenoid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is heterocyclic nonaromatic", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'It is heterocyclic nonaromatic compound  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_20624_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
