(20634,'chemistry',55,1234,2973,'One gram of an aliphatic bromide was completely reacted with $\\mathrm{Mg}$ and then treated with water, ${\\text{182}}\\,\\,{\\text{ml}}$  at STP, of a gas evolved in the process. The gas was found to be stable to $\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4}$. The hydrocarbon is','[{"text": "Propane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Butane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isobutane", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'No. of moles of gas evolved $=\\dfrac{182}{22400}$<br>No. of moles of bromide $=\\dfrac{1}{\\mathrm{M}}$<br>$\\frac{{\\text{1}}}{{\\text{M}}}{\\text{ = }}\\frac{{{\\text{182}}}}{{{\\text{22400}}}}\\quad {\\text{M = 123}}$<br>Molecular mass of the hydrocarbon $=123-80$ $=43$<br>Where 80 is the atomic mass of the bromine radical<br>Molecular mass of the hydrocarbon $=44$<br>The hydrocarbon therefore is $\\mathrm{C}_{3} \\mathrm{H}_{8}$ i.e., propane.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
