(20783,'chemistry',55,1237,2991,'An unsaturated hydrocarbon \' ${\\text{(A)}}$ \' adds to two molecules of $\\mathrm{H}_{2}$ and on reductive ozonolysis gives Butane-1, 4-dial, Ethanal and Propanone. Give the structure of \' ${\\text{(A)}}$ \', with its IUPAC name.','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Two molecules of hydrogen add on \' ${\\text{A}}$ \' this shows that \' $\\mathrm{A}$ \' is either an alkadiene or an alkyne.<br>On reductive ozonolysis \' ${\\text{A}}$ \' gives three fragments, one of which is dialdehyde. Hence, the molecule has broken down at two sites. Therefore, \'A\' has two double bonds.<br>It gives the following three fragments:<br>$\\mathrm{OHC}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{CHO}, \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CHO}$ and $\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{CO}-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$<br>Hence, its structure as deduced from the three fragments must be  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20783_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20783_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(20785,'chemistry',54,1213,2906,'Correct order of $\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{a}}$ in the following compounds is','[{"text": "IV $>$ I $>$ II $>$ III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III $>$ IV $>$ I $>$ II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II $>$ I $>$ IV $>$ III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV $>$ III $>$ II $>$ I", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'EWG like $-\\mathrm{NO}_{2}, \\mathrm{Cl}$ increases acidic strength.<br>-I groups at closer distances increases acidic strength.<br>Acidity or Acidic strength $\\alpha \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{a}} \\alpha \\dfrac{1}{\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{a}}}$<br>So, correct order is II > I > IV > III.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/54_20785_question_1.png'),
(20786,'chemistry',55,1237,2989,'The correct order of heat of hydrogenation of given molecules is :<br>(A) (B) (C) (D)','[{"text": "${\\\\text{D  >  C  >  A  >  B}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{D  >  C  >  B  >  A}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{B  >  A  >  C  >  D}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{D  >  A  >  C  >  B}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The reaction associated with the least negative enthalpy has the most stable reactant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_20786_question_1.png'),
