(20790,'chemistry',55,1237,2990,'The intermediate carbocation formed in the reactions of $\\mathrm{HI}, \\mathrm{HBr}$ and $\\mathrm{HCl}$ with propene is the same and the bond energy of $\\mathrm{HCl}, \\mathrm{HBr}$ and $\\mathrm{HI}$ is $430.5 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}, 363.7 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ and 296.8 $\\mathrm{kJ} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$ respectively. What will be the order of reactivity of these halogen acids?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HI}>\\\\mathrm{HBr}>\\\\mathrm{HCl}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HBr}>\\\\mathrm{HI}>\\\\mathrm{HCl}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HCl}>\\\\mathrm{HBr}>\\\\mathrm{HI}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HI}>\\\\mathrm{HBr} < \\\\mathrm{HCl}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Bond dissociation energy is least for $\\mathrm{HI}$ and maximum for $\\mathrm{HCl}$ therefore,order of reactivity will be $\\mathrm{HI}>\\mathrm{HBr}>\\mathrm{HCl}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
