(20826,'chemistry',55,1237,2986,'During debromination of meso-dibromobutane, the major compound formed is','[{"text": "n-butane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-butene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "cis-2-butene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "trans-2-butene", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20826_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />     <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20826_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_20826_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   In debromination reaction, we have to ensure that the two leaving groups, i.e., the two $\\mathrm{Br}$ atoms, are $180^{\\circ}$ to each other in the same plane before they are lost. From the above conformations of meso-dibromobutane drawn on Newmann projection, it is clear that debromination results in the formation of trans-2-Butene.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
