(20865,'chemistry',54,1201,2866,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Carbon possesses property of catenation.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Carbon atoms form double as well as triple bonds during catenation.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Catenation is the ability of an element to form long chains or rings of itself. Carbon has good catenation capacity due to its small size, tetravalency and strength of $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$, single, double and triple bonds. So , the option (2) is correct',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
