(21161,'chemistry',54,1214,2911,'The decreasing order of hydride affinity for following carbocations is<br> <br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "A, C, B, D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C, A, D, B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, C, D, B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C, A, B, D", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct hydride affinity order of the carbocations will be decided by the stability of the carbocation. Higher the stability of carbocation, lower will be hydride affinity. The stability order of carbocations is,<br>$\\mathrm{C} < \\mathrm{A} < \\mathrm{B} < \\mathrm{D}$. Thus, the decreasing order of hydride affinity<br>is $\\mathrm{C}>\\mathrm{A}>\\mathrm{B}>\\mathrm{D}$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/54_21161_question_1.png'),
(21162,'chemistry',55,1237,2989,'Select the correct statements:','[{"text": "Addition of $\\\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$ on trans-2-Butene gives erythro product", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Addition of $\\\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ on cis 2-Butene gives threo product", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Addition of $\\\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$ on cis-2- Butene gives racemic mixture", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Halogenation (addition of $\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ or $\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$ ) is anti addition.<br>Cis-anti-racemic mixture,<br>Trans-anti-mesoform.<br>Two same groups-same side-erythro<br>Two same groups-opposite side-threo.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
