(21640,'chemistry',58,172,380,'The mass of glucose that should be dissolved in 50 g of water in order to produce the same lowering of vapour pressure as is produced by dissolving 1 g of urea in the same quantity of water is','[{"text": "1 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 g", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "6 g", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "18 g", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\frac{{{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{^\\circ }}}{\\rm{ - }}{{\\rm{p}}_{\\rm{s}}}}}{{{{\\rm{p}}_{\\rm{s}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{M}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{{{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{M}}_{\\rm{1}}}}}$<br>To produce same lowering of vapour pressure<br>$\\left( {\\frac{{{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{^\\circ }}}{\\rm{ - }}{{\\rm{p}}_{\\rm{s}}}}}{{{{\\rm{p}}_{\\rm{s}}}}}} \\right)$<br>term will be same for both the cases<br>(solvent is same).<br>$\\therefore \\frac{{{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{g}}}{\\rm{ \\times 18}}}}{{{\\rm{50 \\times 180}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{u}}}{\\rm{ \\times 18}}}}{{{\\rm{50 \\times 60}}}}$<br>$\\left( {{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{g}}}{\\rm{ = weight}}\\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,\\,{\\rm{glucose,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{u}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\,\\,{\\rm{weight}}\\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,\\,{\\rm{urea}}} \\right)$<br>${\\rm{or,}}\\,\\,\\frac{{{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{g}}}{\\rm{ \\times 18}}}}{{{\\rm{50 \\times 180}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1 \\times 18}}}}{{{\\rm{50 \\times 60}}}}{\\rm{or,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{w}}_{\\rm{g}}}{\\rm{ = 3}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
