(21661,'chemistry',58,169,370,'Which among the following salts, solubility decreases with increase in temperature?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{a}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{S}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{NaBr}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{NaCl}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{KCl}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'For ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ salt, solubility decreases with increase in temperature because reaction of ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ with water is an exothermic reaction, i.e. ${{\\rm{\\Delta }}_{{\\rm{sol}}}}{\\rm{H < 0}}$. As a result solubility decreases. For NaBr, NaCl and KCl, the dissolution process is endothermic.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21664,'chemistry',55,1237,2995,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Propene and cyclopropane both give substitution reactions only.</div><div class="column-right">Propene and cyclopropane are ring chain isomers.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Propene gives addition and substitution reactions both. Propene and cyclopropane have same molecular formula $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{3} \\mathrm{H}_{6}\\right)$ and are ring chain isomers.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21666,'chemistry',58,169,372,'The relation between solubility of a gas in liquid at constant temperature and external pressure is stated by which law?','[{"text": "Raoult’s law", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "van’t Hoff-Boyle’s law", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "van’t Hoff-charles’ law", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Henry’s law", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The relationship between solubility of a gas in liquid at constant temperature and external pressure is given by Henry’s law. $X \\propto $ Partial pressure of the gas, p<br>${\\rm{p = }}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{H}}}{\\rm{x}}$<br>Here, ${{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{H}}}{\\rm{ = }}$ Henry’s law constant<br>More the value of ${{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{H}}}$, lower is the solubility of gas.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2016,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21667,'chemistry',54,1207,2888,'For which of the following, both the empirical formula and molecular formula are the same?','[{"text": "Naphthalene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sucrose", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-Butene", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sucrose $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{12} \\mathrm{H}_{22} \\mathrm{O}_{11}\\right)$ has the same molecular and empirical formulae.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21668,'chemistry',55,1234,2969,'Match Column I with Column II and choose the correct combination from the options given.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A - R,\\tB - P,\\tC - S,\\t\\tD - Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - P, \\tB - S,\\tC - R, \\tD - Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S,\\tB - Q,\\tC - P, \\t\\tD - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q,\\tB - P,\\tC - S,\\t\\tD - R", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{H}_{2}, \\mathrm{Pd} / \\mathrm{Pt}} \\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$ (reduction)<br>$\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{Cl} \\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{Zn} / \\mathrm{H}^{+}} \\mathrm{CH}_{4}+\\mathrm{HCl}$ (reduction)<br>$2{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{Br}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{ Na}},{\\text{ dry}}\\,\\,{\\text{ether }}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}} - {\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}} + 2{\\text{NaBr}}$<br>(WURTZ reaction)<br>${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CO}}\\overline {\\text{O}} {\\text{N}}\\mathop {\\text{a}}\\limits^ +  \\xrightarrow[{{\\text{CaO}}}]{{{\\text{NaOH}}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{4}}} + {\\text{N}}{{\\text{a}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{3}}}$ (Decarboxylation)',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_21668_question_1.png'),
(21670,'chemistry',58,170,374,'The correct option for the value of vapour pressure of a solution at ${\\rm{4}}{{\\rm{5}}^{\\rm{^\\circ }}}{\\rm{C}}$ with benzene to octane in molar ratio ${\\rm{3:2}}$ is :<br>[At ${\\rm{4}}{{\\rm{5}}^{\\rm{^\\circ }}}{\\rm{C}}$ vapour pressure of pure benzene is 280 mm Hg and that of pure octane is 420 mm Hg. Assume Ideal gas]','[{"text": "168 mm of Hg", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "336 mm of Hg", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "350 mm of Hg", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "160 mm of Hg", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{P}}_{\\rm{A}}^{\\rm{0}}$ for benzene = 280 mm of Hg<br>${\\rm{P}}_{\\rm{B}}^{\\rm{^\\circ }}$ for octane = 420 mm of Hg<br>$\\frac{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{A}}}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{B}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{3}}}{{\\rm{2}}}$<br>According to Raoult’s law,<br>${\\rm{P}}\\,{\\rm{ = }}\\,{\\rm{P}}_{\\rm{A}}^{\\rm{0}}{{\\rm{X}}_{\\rm{A}}}\\,{\\rm{ + }}\\,{{\\rm{P}}_{\\rm{B}}}{{\\rm{X}}_{\\rm{B}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 280 \\times }}\\frac{{\\rm{3}}}{{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{ + 420 \\times }}\\frac{{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{840 + 840}}}}{{\\rm{5}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1680}}}}{{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{ = 336mm}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Hg}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21672,'chemistry',55,1234,2972,'Match Column I with Column II and choose the correct combination from the options given.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A - P,\\tB - Q,\\tC - R,\\tD - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P,\\tB - Q,\\tC - S,\\tD - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - R,\\tB - P,\\tC - Q,\\tD - S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - R,\\tB - P,\\tC - S,\\tD - Q", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{CH}_{4}+\\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\xrightarrow{\\text { hv }} \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{Cl}+\\mathrm{HCl}$ (Halogenation)<br>$\\mathrm{CH}_{4}+\\mathrm{O}_{2} \\xrightarrow{\\Delta} \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}+\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ (Combustion)<br>$\\mathrm{CH}_{4}+\\mathrm{O}_{2} \\xrightarrow[\\Delta]{\\mathrm{Mo}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}} \\mathrm{HCHO}$ (Oxidation)<br>n - hexane $\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{ }}10{\\kern 1pt}  - 20{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} \\,{\\text{atm }}}]{{{\\text{C}}{{\\text{r}}_2}{{\\text{O}}_3}/{\\text{A}}{{\\text{l}}_2}{{\\text{O}}_3}{\\kern 1pt} ,{\\kern 1pt} \\,\\Delta {\\kern 1pt} 773{\\kern 1pt} \\,{\\text{K}}}}$Benzene (aromatization)',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_21672_question_1.png'),
(21674,'chemistry',58,168,366,'The molarity of urea (molar mass ${\\rm{60}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$) solution by dissolving 15 g of urea in ${\\rm{500}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{c}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}$ of water is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{mol}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{d}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 3}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.5}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{mol}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{d}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 3}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.125}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{mol}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{d}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 3}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.0005}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{mol}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{d}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 3}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Given, mass of urea = 15 g<br>Molar mass of urea ${\\rm{ = 60}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$<br>${\\rm{Volume = 500}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{c}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ = 500mL = 0}}{\\rm{.5L}}$<br>$\\because $ ${\\rm{1c}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ = 1mL = 1000}}\\,{\\rm{L}}$<br>$\\therefore {\\rm{Molarity}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{Mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{solute}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{in}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{grams(w)}}}}{{{\\rm{Molar}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mass}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{solute(M) \\times Volume}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{solution}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{V(L))}}}}$<br>${\\rm{Molarity}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{of}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{urea = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{15g}}}}{{{\\rm{60}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 0}}{\\rm{.5L}}}}$<br>$ \\Rightarrow {\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.5}}\\,\\,{\\rm{mol/L = 0}}{\\rm{.5}}\\,\\,{\\rm{mol/d}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}$<br>$\\left( {{\\rm{1L = 1d}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{3}}}} \\right)$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2018,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
