(21699,'chemistry',54,1210,2900,'Which of the following exhibits stereoisomerism?<br>(i) 1,2-Dichloroethylene<br>(ii) 2-Hydroxypropanoic acid<br>(iii) 1, 1-Dichloroethylene<br>(iv) 2-Methylpropane','[{"text": "(i) and (iv)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(ii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i) and (ii)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(iii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'1, 2-Dichloroethylene :  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_21699_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  It can show cis-and trans-forms. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_21699_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  2-Hydroxypropanoic acid :  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_21699_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Due to presence of chiral carbon it can show optical isomerism.<br>1, 1-Dichloroethylene :  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_21699_explanation_4.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  It cannot show geometrical isomerism due to presence of similar groups on two double bonded carbon atoms.<br>2-Methylpropane :  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_21699_explanation_5.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  It cannot show optical isomerism due to achiral carbon.<br>Hence, (1) and (2) will show stereoisomerism.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
