(21724,'chemistry',55,1239,3007,'<br>Which of the following statements is/are correct for these two reactions?','[{"text": "The rate of first hydrohalogenation is faster than that of second hydrohalogenation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The rate of first hydrohalogenation is slower than that of second hydrohalogenation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alkynes are more reactive than vinyl halide toward an electrophile.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_21724_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>The rate of first hydrohalogenation is faster than second because alkynes are more reactive than vinyl halide.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_21724_question_1.png'),
