(21822,'chemistry',54,1213,2906,'How many atoms or group of atoms given below will exhibit  ${\\rm{ + I }}$ effect?<br>${\\text{Zn}},{\\text{CO}}{{\\text{O}}^ - },{\\text{R}} - {{\\text{S}}^ - },{\\text{I}},{\\text{Be}}, - {\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{H}}, - {\\text{C}}{({\\text{Et}})_{\\text{3}}},$<br>$ - {\\text{COOH}}$','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "9", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\text{Zn,CO}}{{\\text{O}}^ - },{\\text{R}} - {{\\text{S}}^ - },{\\text{Be}}, - {\\text{C}}{\\left( {{\\text{Et}}} \\right)_{\\text{3}}}$ are electron donating groups and exhibit ${\\rm{ + I}}$ effect. On the other hand ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{I},-\\mathrm{SO}_{3} \\mathrm{H}}}$ and $ - {\\rm{COOH}}$ are electron withdrawing groups and exhibit $ - {\\rm{I}}$ effect.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21823,'chemistry',55,1239,3006,'Among the given compounds, one which can be distinguished by $\\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}$ is','[{"text": "ethane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ethylene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "acetylene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "diethyl ether", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only acetylene reacts with $\\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}$ and gives white precipitate of silver acetylide among the given compounds. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_21823_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Thus, it is distinguished by $\\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21824,'chemistry',58,170,374,'The solubility of ${{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ in water at 300 K and 500 torr partial pressure is ${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.01g}}{{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$. The solubility $\\left( {{\\rm{in}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{g}}{{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}} \\right)$ at 750 torr partial pressure is :','[{"text": "0.02", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.015", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.0075", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.005", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'According to Henry’s law<br>$\\frac{{{{\\rm{P}}_{\\rm{1}}}}}{{{{\\rm{P}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{1}}}}}{{{{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}$<br>$\\therefore {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{1}}}\\,{\\rm{\\& }}\\,\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{2}}}$  are solubility of gas (g/L)<br>$\\frac{{{\\rm{500}}}}{{{\\rm{750}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.01}}}}{{{{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}$<br>$\\therefore {{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{750 \\times 0}}{\\rm{.01}}}}{{{\\rm{500}}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.015g/L}}$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2016,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
