(21852,'chemistry',58,176,385,'In comparison to a 0.01m solution of glucose, the depression in freezing point of a 0.01m ${\\rm{MgC}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ solution is ........ .','[{"text": "The same", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "About twice", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "About three times", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "About six times", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'As we know depression in freezing point is directly related to Van’t Hoff factor (i) according to which greater the value of i greater will be the depression in freezing point.<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{Solution}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{i}}$<br>${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.01}}\\,\\,{\\rm{m}}\\,\\,{\\rm{glucose}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{1}}$<br>${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.01}}\\,\\,{\\rm{m}}\\,\\,{\\rm{MgC}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{3}}$<br>Hence, depression in freezing point of glucose is about 3 times of glucose.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exampler','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
