(21883,'chemistry',58,176,385,'Increasing amount of \\[{\\rm{Hg}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\] is added to 1 litre of an aqueous solution containing 0.1 mole of KI. Which of the following graphs does represent the variation of depression in freezing point of the resulting solution with the amount of \\[{\\rm{Hg}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\] added ?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\rm{2K}}{{\\rm{I}}_{\\left( {{\\rm{aq}}} \\right)}}{\\rm{ + Hg}}{{\\rm{I}}_{{\\rm{2}}\\left( {\\rm{s}} \\right)}} \\to {{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{Hg}}{{\\rm{I}}_{{\\rm{4}}\\left( {{\\rm{aq}}} \\right)}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{or}}$<br>${\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{K}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{ + 2}}{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\rm{ + Hg}}{{\\rm{I}}_{{\\rm{2}}\\left( {\\rm{s}} \\right)}} \\to {\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{K}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{ + }}{\\left[ {{\\rm{Hg}}{{\\rm{I}}_{\\rm{4}}}} \\right]^{{\\rm{2 - }}}}$<br>As a result of complex ion formation, the no. of mole particles in the solution decreases in the ratio ${\\rm{4:3}}$.<br>So ${\\rm{\\Delta }}{{\\rm{T}}_{\\rm{f}}}$ decreases until all the ${{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$ ions are consumed with 0.05 moles of ${\\rm{Hg}}{{\\rm{I}}_{\\rm{2}}}$. The excess of ${\\rm{Hg}}{{\\rm{I}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ remain insoluble. Hence after 0.05 moles of ${\\rm{Hg}}{{\\rm{I}}_{\\rm{2}}}$, the F.P. of solution remains constant.',NULL,'Hard','Graph/Figure',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21884,'chemistry',55,1240,3018,'The effective electrophile in aromatic sulphonation is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HSO}_{4}^{-}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{SO}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{SO}_{2}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{SO}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_21884_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21887,'chemistry',58,170,373,'Vapour pressure diagram of some liquids plotted against temperature are shown below. Most volatile liquid is<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Medium','Graph/Figure',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/58_21887_question_1.png'),
(21888,'chemistry',55,1240,3018,'Most reactive compound towards electrophilic substitution is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During electrophilic substitution, the substituent already present in the benzene ring directs the incoming group either to ortho and para or to meta position and the reaction may be faster or slower as compared to benzene. All groups which activate the ring, i.e. increase the reaction rate are o , p-directing.Activating groups increase the electron density in the benzene nucleus either due to inductive effect (+ I effect) or resonance or both. Therefore, electrophile will attack on benzene nucleus easily.Halogens are exceptions in the sense that they deactivate the ring, but are o,p -directing.Hence, $-\\mathrm{OC}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5}$ is the most activating group while $-\\mathrm{Cl}$-\\mathrm{COCH}_{3}$ are deactivating groups.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21890,'chemistry',58,169,372,'At 300 K, solubility of a gas in a liquid was measured at different partial pressures.<br>Mole fraction of gas 0.010 0.015 0.020 Partial pressure of gas (kPa) 82 122 166<br>Which of the following graph is correct accordance with Henry’s law?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Henry’s law of constant can be verified for the given graph ${\\rm{p = }}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{H}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}{{\\rm{X}}_{{\\rm{gas}}}}{\\rm{.}}$',NULL,'Medium','Graph/Figure',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21891,'chemistry',55,1241,3021,'electrophilic substitution will occur at','[{"text": "meta in second ring", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ortho/para in the first ring", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "meta in the first ring", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ortho/para in the second ring", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The second ring has o/p directing $\\mathrm{O}$-atom and first ring has m-directing <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_21891_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> group.  ${\\text{o/p}}$ directing group activate the benzene nucleus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_21891_question_1.png'),
(21896,'chemistry',55,1237,2984,'Which is a pair of geometrical isomers?','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II and IV are the geometrical isomers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_21896_question_1.png'),
(21898,'chemistry',55,1239,3006,'Arrange the following in order of decreasing<br> basicity. <br> A. $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{MgBr}$<br> B. $\\mathrm{HC} \\equiv \\mathrm{CMgBr}$<br> C. $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{OMgBr}$','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}>\\\\mathrm{C}>\\\\mathrm{B}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A $>$ B $>$ C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}>\\\\mathrm{B}>\\\\mathrm{A}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{B}>\\\\mathrm{A}>\\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}\\overline {\\rm{C}} {{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ > HC}} \\equiv {{\\rm{C}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\rm{ > C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$ <br> basic character. The acid character being<br>${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{OH > HC}} \\equiv {\\rm{CH > C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}$.<br>The weaker the acid, the stronger the base (conjugate pair).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21899,'chemistry',54,1213,2907,'$\'{\\rm{P}}\'$ and ‘Q’ are the number of resonating structures of the following two molecules.<br> <br>sum of P,Q is ____.','[{"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "10", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_21899_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>Hence, $\\mathrm{P}+\\mathrm{Q}=3+5=8$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/54_21899_question_1.png'),
(21902,'chemistry',55,1239,3000,'Name of following reaction is','[{"text": "Claisen Condensation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diel\'s Alder reaction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dieckmann cyclisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Michael addition reaction", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The given reaction is Diel\'s Alder reaction.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_21902_question_1.png'),
(21904,'chemistry',58,169,372,'Variation of \\[{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{H}}}\\] (Henry’s law constant) with temperature T is shown by following graphs I - IV.<br>Correct representation is<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Partial pressure, ${\\rm{p = }}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{H}}}{\\rm{X}}$<br>If temperature is lowered, solubility of gases increases at a given pressure. Thus, ${{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{H}}}$ increases with increase in temperature. It is due to this reason that aquatic species are more comfortable in cold water rather than in warm water.',NULL,'Medium','Graph/Figure',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/58_21904_question_1.png'),
(21907,'chemistry',55,1237,2991,'The unsaturated hydrocarbon which on<br> ozonolysis gives one mole each of formaldehyde,<br> acetaldehyde and methyl glyoxal $\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COCHO}\\right)$<br> is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\\\mathrm{CH}=\\\\mathrm{C}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\\\\mathrm{CH}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{CH}=\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\\\\mathrm{CH}-\\\\mathrm{C}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)=\\\\mathrm{CH}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}=\\\\mathrm{CH}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_21907_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(21910,'chemistry',54,1201,2868,'In the compound 7-ethyl 3-nonene-2, 5, 8-tricarboxylic acid, how many atoms are in ${\\rm{s}}{{\\rm{p}}^2} - $hybridisation state?','[{"text": "8", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All three carbon of three $-\\mathrm{COOH}$ are ${\\rm{s}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{2}}}$.<br>Three oxygen, one in each $-\\mathrm{COOH}$ are  ${\\rm{s}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{2}}}$.<br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_21910_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>Both C-3 and C-4 carbons are ${\\rm{s}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{2}}}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
