(21967,'chemistry',58,176,385,'${{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{4}}}\\left[ {{\\rm{Fe}}{{\\left( {{\\rm{CN}}} \\right)}_{\\rm{6}}}} \\right]$ is supposed to be 40% dissociated when 1M solution prepared. Its boiling point is equal to another 20% mass by volume of non electrolytic solution A. Considering molality = molarity. The molecular weight of A is','[{"text": "77", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "67", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "57", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "47", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Given that the boiling point of both the solution is same i.e., ${\\rm{\\Delta }}{{\\rm{T}}_{\\rm{b}}}$ values also same.<br>${\\left( {{\\rm{\\Delta }}{{\\rm{T}}_{\\rm{b}}}} \\right)_{{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{4}}}\\left[ {{\\rm{Fe}}{{\\left( {{\\rm{CN}}} \\right)}_{\\rm{6}}}} \\right]}}{\\rm{ = }}{\\left( {{\\rm{\\Delta }}{{\\rm{T}}_{\\rm{b}}}} \\right)_{\\rm{A}}}$<br>${\\left( {{\\rm{i}}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{b}}}{\\rm{m}}} \\right)_{{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{4}}}\\left[ {{\\rm{Fe}}{{\\left( {{\\rm{CN}}} \\right)}_{\\rm{6}}}} \\right]}}{\\rm{ = }}{\\left( {{\\rm{i}}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{b}}}{\\rm{m}}} \\right)_{\\rm{A}}}$<br>${\\rm{\'i\'}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{value}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{for}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{4}}}\\left[ {{\\rm{Fe}}{{\\left( {{\\rm{CN}}} \\right)}_{\\rm{6}}}} \\right]{\\rm{ = }}$<br>${\\rm{1 + }}\\left( {{\\rm{n - 1}}} \\right){\\rm{\\alpha  = 1 + }}\\left( {{\\rm{5 - 1}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.4}}} \\right){\\rm{ = 2}}{\\rm{.6}}$<br>${\\rm{\'i\'}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{value}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{for}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{4}}}\\left[ {{\\rm{Fe}}{{\\left( {{\\rm{CN}}} \\right)}_{\\rm{6}}}} \\right]{\\rm{ = 1}}$<br>(as it is non-electrolyte)<br>${\\left( {{\\rm{2}}{\\rm{.6 \\times 1}}} \\right)_{{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{4}}}\\left[ {{\\rm{Fe}}{{\\left( {{\\rm{CN}}} \\right)}_{\\rm{6}}}} \\right]}}{\\rm{ = }}{\\left( {{\\rm{1 \\times }}\\frac{{{\\rm{20 \\times 1000}}}}{{{\\rm{MW \\times 100}}}}}