(22097,'chemistry',58,169,372,'Ratio of ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ in the air is $1:4$. Find out th ratio of solubilities in terms of mole fraction of ${{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{and}}{\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ dissolved in water at atmospheric pressure and room temperature.<br>$\\left[ {\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}{{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{H}}}\\left[ {{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}} \\right]{\\rm{ = 3}}{\\rm{.30 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{7}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{torr}}}\\\\{{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{H}}}\\left[ {{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}} \\right]{\\rm{ = 6}}{\\rm{.60 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{7}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{torr}}}\\end{array}} \\right]$.','[{"text": "$1:2$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$2:1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1:1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${{\\rm{p}}_{{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{ \\times 1 = 0}}{\\rm{.2}}\\,\\,{\\rm{bar}}$<br>${{\\rm{p}}_{{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{4}}}{{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{ \\times 1 = 0}}{\\rm{.8}}\\,\\,{\\rm{bar}}$<br>${\\rm{P = }}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{H}}}{\\rm{X}}\\,\\,\\left( {{\\rm{Henry\'s}}\\,\\,{\\rm{law}}} \\right)$<br>$\\frac{{{{\\rm{X}}_{{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}{{{{\\rm{X}}_{{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{p}}_{{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}{{{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{H}}}\\left( {{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}} \\right)}}{\\rm{ \\times }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{H}}}\\left( {{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}} \\right)}}{{{{\\rm{P}}_{{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.2 \\times 6}}{\\rm{.60 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{7}}}}}{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.8 \\times 3}}{\\rm{.30 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{7}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(22101,'chemistry',58,170,373,'Which combination of following terms is matched correctly?<br>(I) Vapour pressure<br>(II) Intermolecular forces<br>(III) Latent heat of vaporisation<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "High - I, Weak - II, Small - III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "High - I, Strong - II, Large - III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Low - I, Weak - II, Large - III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Low - I, Strong - II, Small - III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\text{Liquid}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{Vapour}}$<br>(1) If vapour pressure is high, it means equilibrium is in forward side. This is attained when intermolecular forces holding the molecules are of weak nature. Low heat is required to convert liquid into vapour. Thus, (1) is correct.<br>(2) Thus, incorrect.<br>(3) When vapour pressure is low, it means inter molecular forces are strong hence (3) is incorrect.<br>(4) When, vapour pressure is low, intermolecular forces are strong, hence large heat is required thus, option (4) is incorrect.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
