(22309,'chemistry',54,1213,2907,'The correct arrangement for decreasing order of electrophilic substitution for above compounds is','[{"text": "(IV) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (I) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (II) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (III)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(III) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (IV) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (II) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (I)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(II) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (IV) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (III) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (I)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(III) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (I) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (II) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (IV)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Methoxy group strongly activates benzene ring towards electrophilic aromatic substitution due to + R effect. Methyl group weakly activates benzene ring due to its ${\\rm{ + I}}$ and +H effects. ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CF}_{3}}}$ group strongly deactivates the benzene ring due to $ - {\\rm{I}}$ and $-$ H effects. Electron donating groups will enhance the electrophilic substitution on the ring. Thus, the correct order will be<br> III ${\\mathrm{>}}$ I ${\\mathrm{>}}$ II ${\\mathrm{>}}$ IV.<br> So, the correct option is (4).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/54_22309_question_1.png'),
