(22395,'chemistry',59,373,697,'The number of moles of electrons passed when currect of 2 A is passed through a solution of electrolyte for 20 minutes is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{4}}{\\\\rm{.1 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 4}}}}{\\\\rm{mol}}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{\\\\rm{.24 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 2}}}}{\\\\rm{mol}}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}{\\\\rm{.487 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 2}}}}{\\\\rm{mol}}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}{\\\\rm{.487 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\\\rm{mol}}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Given, i = 2A, and t = 20 min, i.e, 1200 s. As we know, Q = l.t.<br>${\\rm{Q = 2 A \\times 1200 s}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 2400 A - s = 2400 C}}$<br>Using, Q = ne<br>where, Q = quantity of charge<br>n = number of electrons<br>${\\rm{e = 1}}{\\rm{.6 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 19}}}}{\\rm{C}}$<br>${\\rm{So,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{Q = n \\times 1}}{\\rm{.6 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 19}}}}{\\rm{C}}$<br>${\\rm{n = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{2400C}}}}{{{\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.6 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{19}}}}{\\rm{C}}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.5 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{22}}}}$<br>The number of electrons passed when current 2A is passed through a solution of electrolyte for 20 min is ${\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.5 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{22}}}}$<br>Number of moles of electrons $\\frac{{{\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.5 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{22}}}}}}{{6.022 \\times {{10}^{23}}}}$<br>${\\rm{2}}{\\rm{.487 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 2}}}}{\\rm{mol}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(22396,'chemistry',55,1237,2984,'Read the  Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct option out of the options given below.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Cis form of alkene is found to be more polar than the trans form.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Dipole moment of trans isomer of 2-butene is zero.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Dipole moment is a vector quantity and for a molecule not dipole moment is the sum of all bond dipoles, therefore dipole moment of cis is higher than trans form.    <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_22396_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  So, the correct option is (1).',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(22398,'chemistry',59,373,697,'What is the SI unit for electrochemical equivalent?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{J}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{J}}{{\\\\rm{C}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{kgC}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{kg}}{{\\\\rm{C}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The SI unit for electro-chemical equivalent is ${\\rm{kg}}{{\\rm{C}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$<br>Electrochemical equivalent<br>${\\rm{(Z) = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{mass}}}}{{{\\rm{1}}\\,\\,{\\rm{coulomb}}\\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,\\,{\\rm{electrical}}\\,\\,{\\rm{charge}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{kg}}}}{{\\rm{C}}}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
