(22404,'chemistry',55,1237,2984,'The incorrect statement regarding the geometrical isomers of 2-butene is','[{"text": "cis-2-butene and trans-2-butene are not interconvertible at room temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "cis-2-butene has less dipole moment than trans-2-butene.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "trans-2-butene is more stable than cis-2-butene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "cis-2-butene and trans-2-butene are stereoisomers.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'cis-2-butene has more dipole moment than trans-2-butene ${\\mathrm{(\\mu=0)}}$. So, the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(22406,'chemistry',59,373,697,'In the electrolysis of acidulated water, it is desired to obtain 1.12 cc of hydrogen per second under S.T.P condition. The current to be passed is','[{"text": "9.65 A", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "19.3 A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.965 A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.93 A", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'No. of moles of ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.12}}}}{{{\\rm{22400}}}}$<br>$\\therefore $ No. of equivalents of hydrogen<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.12 \\times 2}}}}{{{\\rm{22400}}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 4}}}}$<br>No. of Faradays required ${\\rm{ = 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 4}}}}$<br>$\\therefore $ Current to be passed in 1 sec. ${\\rm{ = 96500 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 4}}}}$<br>= 9.65 A',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
