(22432,'chemistry',55,1239,3006,'The ascending acidity order of the following ${\\mathrm{H}}$ atoms is','[{"text": "(III) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (IV) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (II) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (I)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(I) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (II) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (III) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (IV)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (II) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (IV) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (III)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(IV) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (III) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (II) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (I)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Acidity ${\\mathrm{\\propto-I}}$ effect ${\\mathrm{\\propto s \\%}}$ character<br>${\\mathrm{\\propto \\dfrac{1}{+ \\text { Ieffect }}}}$<br>In <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_22432_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  is attached to ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{sp}}}}$.<br>In <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_22432_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   is attached to ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{sp}^{2}}}}$.<br>Where as in <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_22432_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  and <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_22432_explanation_4.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  H  is attached to ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{sp}}{ }^{3}}}$. <br>${\\mathrm{\\%}}$ of s character : ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{sp}>\\mathrm{sp}^{2}>\\mathrm{sp}^{3}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{3}}}$ shows +I effect. In ${\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{3} \\mathrm{C}^{-}, 3 \\mathrm{CH}_{3}}}$ groups are attached, which destabilise the ${\\mathrm{3^{\\circ}}}$ carbanion. Whereas in ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}^{-}}}$, only one ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{3}}}$ group is attached, so ascending acidity order of H atoms is <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_22432_explanation_5.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/55_22432_explanation_6.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Therefore, the correct order will be (III)  <  (IV) ${\\mathrm{ < }}$ (II) ${\\mathrm{ < }}$ (I). So, the correct option is (1).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_22432_question_1.png'),
