(22446,'chemistry',59,373,696,'Which among the following is correct for electrolysis of brine solution?','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ gas is liberated at cathode", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sodium metal is collected at anode", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ gas is liberated at cathode", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ gas is liberated at cathode", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In electrolysis of brine solution, ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ gas is liberated at cathode. The solution contains four ions.<br>${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{,}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}^{\\rm{\\Theta }}}{\\rm{,}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{and}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\mathop {\\rm{O}}\\limits^{\\rm{\\Theta }} {\\rm{H}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{ions}}$. There occurs a race amongst them for their discharge at their respective electrodes.<br>Following electrode reactions are possible:<br>Cathode<br>${\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O(1) + 2}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}} \\to {{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{(g) + 2O}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{H(aq)}}$<br>${\\rm{Anode}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{2C}}{{\\rm{l}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\rm{(aq)}} \\to {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{(g) + 2}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$<br>In this electrolysis, ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ at cathode and ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ at anode are given off.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2019,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
