(22449,'chemistry',55,1240,3015,'Which of the following are aromatic?','[{"text": "(III) and (IV) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(II) and (IV) only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(I) and (III) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I) and (II) only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Compound 1 is non-aromatic as it contains ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{sp}^{3}}}$ hybridised carbon centre which makes it non-planar and compound 3 is nonaromatic due to severe non-bonded interactions between the internal hydrogen atoms. Due to these interactions ring acquires non-planar geometry. So, the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/55_22449_question_1.png'),
(22450,'chemistry',59,373,696,'In the electrolysis of aqueous sodium chloride solution, which of the half cell reaction will occur at anode?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{Cl}}_{{\\\\rm{(aq)}}}^{\\\\rm{ - }} \\\\to \\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{l}}_{{{\\\\rm{2}}_{{\\\\rm{(q)}}}}}}{\\\\rm{ + }}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}{\\\\rm{;E}}_{{\\\\rm{cell}}}^{\\\\rm{o}}{\\\\rm{ = 1}}{\\\\rm{.36}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{volts}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{{\\\\rm{(1)}}}} \\\\to {{\\\\rm{O}}_{{{\\\\rm{2}}_{{\\\\rm{(q)}}}}}}{\\\\rm{ + 4H}}_{{\\\\rm{(aq)}}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}{\\\\rm{ + 4}}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}}{\\\\rm{;E}}_{{\\\\rm{cell}}}^{\\\\rm{o}}{\\\\rm{ = 1}}{\\\\rm{.23}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{volts}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Na}}_{{\\\\rm{(aq)}}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}{\\\\rm{ + }}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}} \\\\to {\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{a}}_{{\\\\rm{(s)}}}}{\\\\rm{;}}{{\\\\rm{E}}^{\\\\rm{o}}}{\\\\rm{ =  - 2}}{\\\\rm{.71}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{volts}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{H}}_{{\\\\rm{(aq)}}}^{\\\\rm{ + }}{\\\\rm{ + }}{{\\\\rm{e}}^{\\\\rm{ - }}} \\\\to \\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{;E}}_{{\\\\rm{cell}}}^{\\\\rm{o}}{\\\\rm{ = 0}}{\\\\rm{.00}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{volts}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During electrolysis of aqueous NaCl following oxidation reactions are possible :<br>${\\rm{Cl}}_{{\\rm{(aq)}}}^{\\rm{ - }} \\to \\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{{\\rm{2(g)}}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\rm{;E}}_{{\\rm{cell}}}^{\\rm{o}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.36}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Volts}}$<br>${\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{{\\rm{(1)}}}} \\to {{\\rm{O}}_{{\\rm{2(g)}}}}{\\rm{ + 4H}}_{{\\rm{(aq)}}}^{\\rm{ + }}{\\rm{ + 4}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\rm{;E}}_{{\\rm{cell}}}^{\\rm{o}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.23}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Volts}}$<br>The reaction at anode with lower value of ${{\\rm{E}}^{\\rm{o}}}$ is preferred and therefore, water should get oxidised in preference to ${\\rm{Cl}}_{{\\rm{(aq)}}}^{\\rm{ - }}$. However, on account of overpotential of oxygen, reaction (1) is preferred. Thus,<br>Cathode<br>${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{{\\rm{(1)}}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}} \\to \\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{2(g)}}}}{\\rm{ + OH}}_{{\\rm{(aq)}}}^{\\rm{ - }}$<br>${\\rm{Anode:Cl}}_{{\\rm{(aq)}}}^{\\rm{ - }} \\to \\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{{\\rm{2(g)}}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
