(22478,'chemistry',58,168,366,'A student has 100 mL of 0.1 M KCl solution. To make it 0.2 M, he has to','[{"text": "evaporate 50 mL of the solution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "add 0.01 mole of KCl", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "both (1) and (2) can be used", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "neither (1) nor (2) can be used", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'100 mL of 0.1 M KCl contains 0.01 mole of KCl<br>On evaporating 50 mL of solution, now conc.<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.01}}}}{{{\\rm{50}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 1000 = 0}}{\\rm{.2M}}$<br>On adding 0.01 mole of KCl, now KCl present = 0.02 mole<br>$\\therefore $  Concentration ${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.02}}}}{{{\\rm{100}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 1000 = 0}}{\\rm{.2M}}$<br>Thus, both (1) and (2) can be used.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
