(22712,'chemistry',58,170,374,'In which case Raoult\'s law is not applicable?','[{"text": "$1 \\\\mathrm{M} \\\\mathrm{NaCl}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$1 \\\\mathrm{M}$ urea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1 \\\\mathrm{M}$ glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1 \\\\mathrm{M}$ sucrose", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Raoult\'s law is not applicable, if total number of particles of solute changes in the solution due to association or dissociation. Among the given compounds, $\\mathrm{NaCl}$ undergoes dissociation and forms $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$and $\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$ions, thus Raoult\'s law is not applicable to $\\mathrm{NaCl}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2012,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(22619,'chemistry',59,373,697,'A current of 2 A was passed for one hour through a solution of ${\\rm{CuS}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{.0}}{\\rm{.237g}}\\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,\\,{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{u}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}$ ions was discharged at cathode. The current efficiency is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{40}}{\\\\rm{.01\\\\% }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{10\\\\% }}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{42}}{\\\\rm{.2\\\\% }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{26}}{\\\\rm{.1\\\\% }}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{W - }}\\frac{{{\\rm{63}}{\\rm{.5}}}}{{{\\rm{2 \\times 96500}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 2 \\times 60 \\times 60 = 2}}{\\rm{.37 g}}$<br>${\\rm{\\% }}\\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,\\,{\\rm{efficiency = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.237}}}}{{{\\rm{2}}{\\rm{.37}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 100 = 10\\% }}$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(22621,'chemistry',60,587,1179,'The following data is obtained during the first order thermal decompsoition of<br>$2 \\mathrm{~A}_{(\\mathrm{g})} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{B}_{(\\mathrm{g})}+\\mathrm{C}_{(\\mathrm{s})}$<br>at constant volume and temperature.<br>The rate constant in ${\\rm{mi}}{{\\rm{n}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$ is','[{"text": "0.0693", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "6.93", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.00693", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "69.3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathop {{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{A}}_{\\left( {\\rm{g}} \\right)}}}\\limits_{\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{2(l - x)}}}\\\\{{\\rm{(2 - 2x)}}}\\end{array}} \\mathop {{{\\rm{B}}_{{\\rm{(g)}}}}}\\limits_{\\rm{x}} {\\rm{  +   }}{{\\rm{C}}_{{\\rm{(s)}}}}$<br>$2(1-x)$$(2-2 x)$<br>At the end of reaction, only 1 mole of gas is present whose pressure is 200 pascal.<br>$=2-2 x+x=2-x$<br>But the pressure of 2 moles $=400$ pascal<br>$\\therefore 400-x=300 \\Rightarrow x=100$<br>$\\therefore$ Pressure due to $2-2 \\mathrm{x}$ moles of $\\mathrm{A}$<br>$=400-200=200$ pascal<br>$\\therefore \\mathrm{k}=\\dfrac{2.303}{\\mathrm{t}} \\log \\left[\\dfrac{\\mathrm{a}}{\\mathrm{a}-\\mathrm{x}}\\right]=\\dfrac{2.303}{10} \\log \\left[\\dfrac{400}{200}\\right]$<br>$=\\dfrac{2.303}{10} \\log 2=\\dfrac{0.693}{10}=0.0693 \\mathrm{~min}^{-1}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/60_22621_question_1.png'),
(22622,'chemistry',58,168,365,'Three statements are given about mole fraction<br>i. Mole fraction of a solute + mole fraction of solvent = 1<br>ii. Equal weights of Helium and methane are present in a gaseous mixture. The mole fraction of He is 4/5<br>iii. The mole fraction of $40\\% $ by mass of NaOH solution is 0.5','[{"text": "i and ii are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii and iii are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iii are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "all are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'(i) Sum of the mole fraction of all the components in solution is 1.<br>(ii) Let us assume weight of ${\\rm{HE}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{and}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ as 1 g Mole fraction of ${\\rm{HE = }}\\frac{{\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{4}}}}}{{\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ + }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{6}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{4}}}{{\\rm{5}}}$.<br>(iii) 40% by mass of NaOH means 40 g of NaOH present in 100 g of solution.<br>Mole fraction of ${\\rm{NaOH = }}\\frac{{\\frac{{{\\rm{40}}}}{{{\\rm{40}}}}}}{{\\left( {\\frac{{{\\rm{40}}}}{{{\\rm{40}}}}} \\right){\\rm{ + }}\\left( {\\frac{{{\\rm{60}}}}{{{\\rm{18}}}}} \\right)}}{\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.23}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
