(22888,'chemistry',60,589,1186,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Rate constant determined from arrhenius equation are fairly accurate for simple as well as complex molecules.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Reactant molecules undergo chemical change irrespective of their orientaion during collision.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Assertion is correct, but reason is incorrect.<br>Rate constant determined from arrhenius equation are fairly accurate for simple and complex molecules because only those molecules which have proper orientation during collision (i.e., effective collision) and sufficient kinetic energy lead the chemical change.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(22890,'chemistry',59,368,681,'The Gibbs energy for the decomposition of ${\\rm{A}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{at}}\\,\\,{\\rm{500^\\circ C}}$ is as follows<br>$\\frac{2}{3}A{l_2}{O_3} \\to \\frac{4}{3}Al + {O_2}{\\Delta _r}G =  + 966 kJ\\,\\,mo{l^{ - 1}}$<br>The potential difference needed for electrolytic reduction of ${\\rm{A}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{at}}\\,\\,{\\rm{500^\\circ C}}$ is at least','[{"text": "5.0 V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2.5 V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4.5 V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3.0 V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\frac{{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{A}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}} \\to \\frac{{\\rm{4}}}{{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{Al + }}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\rm{Thus,}}\\,\\,\\frac{{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ \\times 3}}\\left( {{{\\rm{O}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}}} \\right)$<br>${\\rm{i}}{\\rm{.e}}{\\rm{.,}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{O}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}} \\to {{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ + 4}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} $ ${\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\left[ {{\\mkern 1mu} \\because {\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{n = 4}}} \\right]$<br>${\\rm{\\Delta G =  + 966}}\\,\\,{\\rm{kJ}}\\,\\,{\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\rm{ = 966 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{3}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{J}}\\,\\,{\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$<br>${\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\because \\,\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{\\Delta G =  - nF}}{{\\text{E}}_{{\\text{cell}}}}$<br>$ \\Rightarrow \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,966 \\times {10^3} =  - 4 \\times 96500 \\times {E_{cell}}$<br>$ \\Rightarrow \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{E_{cell}} = 2.5 V$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
