(22939,'chemistry',60,587,1180,'For a first order reaction, the time required for completion of 90% reaction is \'${\\rm{x}}$\' times the half life of the reaction. The value of \'${\\rm{x}}$\' is<br>(Given: $\\ln 10=2.303$ and $\\log 2=0.3010$ )','[{"text": "1.12", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2.43", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3.32", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "33.31", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Given, $\\mathrm{t}_{90 \\%}=\\mathrm{xt}_{1 / 2}$<br>$\\dfrac{t_{90 \\%}}{t_{1 / 2}}=x$<br>$\\dfrac{\\dfrac{2.303}{k} \\cdot \\log \\dfrac{100}{10}}{\\dfrac{0.693}{k}}=x \\Rightarrow x=3.32$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(22910,'chemistry',60,584,1172,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">It is not always convenient to determine the instantaneous rate.</div><div class="column-right">Instantaneous rate is measured by the determination of slope of the tangent at point \' $t$ \' in concentration versus time plot.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'It is not always convenient to determine the instantaneous rate, as it is measured by determining the slope of the tangent at point \' $t$ \' in concentration $v s$ time plot. This generally makes it difficult to determine the rate law and hence, the order of the reaction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
