(23036,'chemistry',58,167,360,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Amalgam is a homogeneous solution.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Amalgam is a solution in which mercury is solute and zinc is solvent.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'An amalgam is an alloy of mercury with another metal. It may be liquid, a soft paste or a solid, depending upon the proportion of mercury. In an amalgam, the solute metal and solvent mercury form a homogeneous mixture with uniformly dispersed metal atoms. So option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23038,'chemistry',60,589,1186,'For the chemical process energies are plotted in graph.','[{"text": "It is the exothermic reaction, $\\\\Delta \\\\mathrm{H}=\\\\mathrm{b}-\\\\mathrm{a}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Threshold energy, e $=\\\\mathrm{a}+\\\\mathrm{c}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left(E_{a}\\\\right)_{f} < \\\\left(E_{a}\\\\right)_{b}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/60_23038_question_1.png'),
(23039,'chemistry',58,174,382,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Molecular mass of polymers cannot be calculated by using boiling point or freezing point method.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Polymer solutions possess a low boiling point or freezing point.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Polymer solutions show minimal changes in boiling and freezing points due to the large size of polymer molecules. Measurement of osmotic pressure method is preferred for the determination of molar masses of polymers as it is carried out at room temperature, which does not require heating. Heating may change the nature of the polymer. So option (3)is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23040,'chemistry',59,373,695,'When electric current is passed through a cell having an electrolyte, the positive ions move towards the cathode and the negative ions towards the anode. If the cathode is pulled out of the solution','[{"text": "The positive and negative ions will move towards the anode", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The positive ions will start moving towards anode, the negative ions will stop moving", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The negative ions will continue to move towards the anode, the positive ions will stop moving", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The positive and negative ions will start moving randomly", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'After removing cathode no net charge will flow but ions move randomly.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
