rm{AgCl}}\\,\\,\\left( {\\rm{s}} \\right)$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23213,'chemistry',60,587,1180,'The rate equation for the reaction ${\\text{2A + B}} \\to {\\text{C}}$ is found to be: rate${\\text{  = k[A][B]}}$. The correct statement in relation to this reaction is','[{"text": "Unit of k must be $s^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$t_{1 / 2}$ is a constant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rate of formation of $\\\\mathrm{C}$ is twice the rate of disappearance of $\\\\mathrm{A}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Value of $\\\\mathrm{k}$ is independent of the initial concentrations of $\\\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\\\mathrm{B}$.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The overall order of the reaction is 2 .<br>(1) Unit of $\\mathrm{k}$ is $\\mathrm{mol}^{-1} \\mathrm{~L}^{1} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$ (2) $t_{\\dfrac{1}{2}}$ of second order reaction is inversely proportional to the initial concentration<br>(3) Rate of formation of $\\mathrm{C}$ is half of the rate of disappearance of A.<br>(4) Rate constant vary with temperature',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23216,'chemistry',59,372,694,'The resistance of 0.01 N solution of an electrolyte was found to be 220 ohm at 298 K using a conductivity cell with a cell constant of ${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.88}}\\,\\,{\\rm{c}}{{\\rm{m}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$. The value of equivalent conductance of solution is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{400}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{ohm}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{c}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{g}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{e}}{{\\\\rm{q}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{295}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{ohm}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{c}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{g}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{e}}{{\\\\rm{q}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{419}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{ohm}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{c}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{g}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{e}}{{\\\\rm{q}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{425}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{ohm}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{c}}{{\\\\rm{m}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{g}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{e}}{{\\\\rm{q}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${{\\rm{\\Lambda }}_{{\\rm{eq}}}}{\\rm{ = \\kappa  \\times }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1000}}}}{{\\rm{N}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{R}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}\\frac{{\\rm{l}}}{{\\rm{a}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1000}}}}{{\\rm{N}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{R}}}{\\rm{ \\times cell}}\\,\\,{\\rm{constant \\times }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1000}}}}{{\\rm{N}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{220}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 0}}{\\rm{.88 \\times }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1000}}}}{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.01}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 400}}\\,\\,{\\rm{ohm}}\\,\\,{\\rm{c}}{{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{g}}\\,\\,{\\rm{e}}{{\\rm{q}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23217,'chemistry',60,585,1174,'For the reaction : $2 \\mathrm{~A}+\\mathrm{B} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{A}_{2} \\mathrm{~B}$ the rate $=$ $\\mathrm{k}[\\mathrm{A}][\\mathrm{B}]^{2}$ with $\\mathrm{k}=2.0 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-2} \\mathrm{~L}^{2} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$. The initial rate of the reaction when $[\\mathrm{A}]=0.1 \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{~L}^{-}$ ${ }^{1},[\\mathrm{~B}]=0.2 \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{~L}^{-1}$ is','[{"text": "$4.0 \\\\times 10^{-9} \\\\mathrm{~mol} \\\\mathrm{~L}^{-1} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2.0 \\\\times 10^{-9} \\\\mathrm{~mol} \\\\mathrm{~L}^{-1} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$8.0 \\\\times 10^{-9} \\\\mathrm{~mol} \\\\mathrm{~L}^{-1} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$1.6 \\\\times 10^{-9} \\\\mathrm{~mol} \\\\mathrm{~L}^{-1} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Rate $=\\mathrm{k}[\\mathrm{A}][\\mathrm{B}]^{2}$<br>$\\begin{array}{r}=\\left(2.0 \\times 10^{-6}\\right) \\times(0.1) \\times(0.2)^{2} \\\\=8.0 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{~L}^{-1} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}\\end{array}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
