(23290,'chemistry',58,175,383,'A solution of a substance containing 1.05 g per 100 mL was found to be isotonic with $3 \\%$ glucose solution. The molecular mass of the substance is','[{"text": "31.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6.3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "63", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "630", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\pi_{x}=\\pi_{\\text {glucose }}$<br>$\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{x}} \\mathrm{RT}=\\mathrm{C}_{\\text {glucose }} \\mathrm{RT}$<br>$\\therefore \\dfrac{1.05}{\\text { M.W }}=\\dfrac{3}{180}$<br>$\\therefore$ M.W $=180 \\times \\dfrac{1.05}{3}$<br>$=63$ gram $\\mathrm{mole}^{-}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23291,'chemistry',60,589,1186,'Two reactions ${{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{1}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ have identical preexponential factors. Activation energy of ${{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{1}}}$ exceeds that of ${{\\text{R}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{by10}}\\,{\\text{kJ}}\\,{\\text{mo}}{{\\text{l}}^{{\\text{ - 1}}}}$.<br>If ${{\\text{k}}_{\\text{1}}}$ and ${{\\text{k}}_{\\text{2}}}$ and ${{\\text{R}}_{\\text{2}}}$ are rate constants for reaction ${{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{1}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ respectively at 300 k, then ${\\rm{in}}\\left( {{{\\rm{k}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{/}}{{\\rm{k}}_{\\rm{1}}}} \\right)$ is equal to :- $\\left( {{\\rm{R = 8}}{\\rm{.314\\,J\\,mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\rm{\\,}}{{\\rm{K}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}} \\right)$','[{"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'From Arrhenius equation,<br>$\\mathrm{k}=\\mathrm{A} \\cdot \\mathrm{e}^{\\dfrac{-\\mathrm{Ea}}{\\mathrm{RT}}}$<br>so,<br>$\\begin{aligned}&amp; \\mathrm{k}_{1}=\\mathrm{A} \\cdot \\mathrm{e}^{-\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{a}_{1 /} / \\mathrm{RT}}} \\\\&amp; \\mathrm{k}_{2}=\\mathrm{A} \\cdot \\mathrm{e}^{-\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{a}_{2} / \\mathrm{RT}}}\\end{aligned}$<br>so, equation (2)/ (1) $\\Rightarrow \\dfrac{\\mathrm{k}_{2}}{\\mathrm{k}_{1}}=\\mathrm{e}^{\\dfrac{\\left(\\mathrm{E}_{1}-\\mathrm{Ea}_{2}\\right)}{\\mathrm{RT}}}$<br>(As pre-exponential factors of both reactions is same)<br>$\\ln \\left(\\dfrac{\\mathrm{k}_{2}}{\\mathrm{k}_{1}}\\right)=\\dfrac{\\mathrm{Ea}_{1}-\\mathrm{Ea}_{2}}{\\mathrm{RT}}=\\dfrac{10000}{8.314 \\times 300}=4$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
