(23365,'chemistry',58,176,385,'Match the columns.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A - R, B - Q, C - S, D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - R, B - S, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - P,\\tB - Q,\\tC - R,\\tD - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S,\\tB - R,\\tC - Q,\\tD - P", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Osmotic pressure $({\\rm{\\pi }}) = {\\rm{i}}\\,{\\rm{CRT}}\\,;\\,{\\rm{i}} = $ van\'t Hoff factor<br>(A – R) i  is 1 for glucose, urea, fructose<br>(B - S) for $\\mathrm{NaCl}, \\mathrm{i}=2$ for $\\mathrm{MgCl}_{2}$ and        $\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4}, \\mathrm{i}=3$<br>(C - P) for $\\mathrm{K}_{4}\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\right]$ and  $\\mathrm{Al}_{2}\\left(\\mathrm{SO}_{4}\\right)_{3}, \\mathrm{i}=5$; for $\\mathrm{Na}_{3} \\mathrm{PO}_{4}, \\mathrm{i}=4$<br>(D - Q) for Glucose, $\\mathrm{i}=1$; for $\\mathrm{NaCl}, \\mathrm{i}=2$<br>for $\\mathrm{CaCl}_{2}, \\mathrm{i}=3$',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/58_23365_question_1.png'),
(23337,'chemistry',60,585,1174,'The rate law for a reaction between the substances A and B is given by<br>${\\rm{rate = k[A}}{{\\rm{]}}^{\\rm{n}}}{{\\rm{[B]}}^{\\rm{m}}}$<br>On doubling the concentration of A and halving the concentration of B, the ratio of the new rate to the earlier rate of the reaction will be as','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{2}}^{{\\\\rm{(n - m)}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1/}}{{\\\\rm{2}}^{{\\\\rm{(m + n)}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left( {{\\\\rm{m + n}}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{(n - m)}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Given, $(\\text { rate })_{1}=\\mathrm{k}[\\mathrm{A}]^{\\mathrm{n}}\\left[\\dfrac{\\mathrm{B}}{2}\\right]^{\\mathrm{m}}$<br>On doubling the concentration of A and halving the concentration of $\\mathrm{B}$, the rate can be represented as, $(\\text { rate })_{2}=\\mathrm{k}[2 \\mathrm{~A}]^{\\mathrm{n}}[\\mathrm{B} / 2]^{\\mathrm{m}}$<br>$\\dfrac{(\\text { rate })_{2}}{(\\text { rate })_{1}}=\\dfrac{k[2 A]^{n}\\left[\\dfrac{B}{2}\\right]^{m}}{k[A]^{n}[B]^{m}}=2^{n-m}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23338,'chemistry',58,175,383,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">If red blood cells were removed from the body and placed in pure water, pressure inside the cells increases.</div><div class="column-right">The concentration of salt content in the cell increases.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The pressure inside the cell increases due to osmosis. Water enters the cell due to higher concentration inside the cell. This results in lowering of concentration of salt content inside the cell. Correct Option is 3 .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23339,'chemistry',59,373,696,'${{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ gas cannot be obtained by the electrolysis of any aqueous fluoride salt because','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ is the strongest oxidising agent", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ easily combines with ${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ readily combines with the electrodes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ being strong oxidising agent and thus\nas soon as it is formed it gets reduced.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23341,'chemistry',58,171,379,'Match column I with column II.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A}} - {\\\\text{P;B}} - {\\\\text{P,Q;C}} - {\\\\text{P,S;D}} - {\\\\text{P,R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{Q;B}} - {\\\\rm{P,Q;C}} - {\\\\rm{S;D}} - {\\\\rm{P,R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{P;B}} - {\\\\rm{P,Q;C}} - {\\\\rm{R;D}} - {\\\\rm{S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{P;B}} - {\\\\rm{P,Q;C}} - {\\\\rm{P,Q;D}} - {\\\\rm{P,R}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Relative lowering of vapour pressure,  $\\frac{{{\\rm{P}}^\\circ  - {{\\rm{P}}_{\\rm{s}}}}}{{{\\rm{P}}^\\circ }} = {\\rm{i}}.{{\\rm{X}}_{{\\rm{solute }}}}$<br>Elevation in boiling point, $\\Delta \\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{b}}=\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{b}}-\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{b}}^{\\circ}=\\mathrm{i} . \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{b}} \\cdot \\mathrm{m}$<br>Depression in freezing point, $\\Delta \\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{f}}=\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{f}}^{\\circ}-\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{f}}=\\mathrm{i} . \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{f}} \\cdot \\mathrm{m}$<br>Osmotic pressure, $\\pi=$ iCRT .',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/58_23341_question_1.png'),
(23342,'chemistry',60,584,1172,'For a hypothetical reaction, ${\\rm{A + 3B}} \\to {\\rm{P}}\\quad {\\rm{\\Delta H =  - 2x\\,kJ/}}$ mole of A & ${\\rm{M}} \\to {\\rm{2Q + R}}\\quad {\\rm{\\Delta H =  + x\\,kJ/}}$ mole of M If these reactions are carried simultaneously in a reactor such that temperature is not changing. If rate of disappearance of B is ${\\rm{y}}\\,\\,{\\rm{M}}\\,\\,{\\rm{se}}{{\\rm{c}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$ then rate of formation (in ${\\rm{Mse}}{{\\rm{c}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$ ) of $\\mathrm{Q}$ is:','[{"text": "$\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{y}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{3}}}{{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{y}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{4}}}{{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{y}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{3}}}{{\\\\rm{4}}}{\\\\rm{y}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Multiply second equation by 2',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23343,'chemistry',59,373,696,'A solution of sodium sulphate in water is electrolysed using inert electrodes. The products at the cathode and anode are respectively','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{,}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{,}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{,Na}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{,S}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Water is reduced at the cathode and oxidised at the anode instead of ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{\\rm{SO}}_{\\rm{4}}^{{\\rm{2 - }}}$.<br>${\\rm{Cathode}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{:}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}\\,\\,{\\rm{ + }}\\,\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}\\,\\, \\to \\,\\,{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{ + }}\\,\\,{\\rm{2O}}{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$<br>${\\rm{Anode}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{:}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}\\,\\, \\to \\,\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ + }}}\\,\\,{\\rm{ + }}\\,\\,\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{O}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{ + }}\\,\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
