(23355,'chemistry',60,584,1172,'Contact process is used in the formation of sulphur trioxide, ${\\text{2S}}{{\\text{O}}_{{\\text{2(}}\\,{\\text{g)}}}}{\\text{  +  }}{{\\text{O}}_{{\\text{2(}}\\,{\\text{g)}}}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{2S}}{{\\text{O}}_{{\\text{3(}}\\,{\\text{g)}}}}$<br>The rate of reaction can be expressed as<br>\n$\\frac{{{\\rm{ - \\Delta }}\\left[ {{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}} \\right]}}{{{\\rm{\\Delta t}}}}{\\rm{ = 2}}{\\rm{.5 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 4}}}}{\\rm{\\,mol\\,}}{{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\rm{\\,}}{{\\rm{s}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$.<br>\nThen rate of disappearance of ${\\rm{S}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ will be','[{"text": "$50.0 \\\\times 10^{-5} \\\\mathrm{~mol} \\\\mathrm{~L}^{-1} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$3.75 \\\\times 10^{-4} \\\\mathrm{~mol} \\\\mathrm{~L}^{-1} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2.5 \\\\times 10^{-4} \\\\mathrm{~mol} \\\\mathrm{~L}^{-1} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4.12 \\\\times 10^{-4} \\\\mathrm{~mol} \\\\mathrm{~L}^{-1} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\dfrac{-\\Delta\\left[\\mathrm{SO}_{2}\\right]}{\\Delta \\mathrm{t}}=2\\left(-\\dfrac{\\Delta\\left[\\mathrm{O}_{2}\\right]}{\\Delta \\mathrm{t}}\\right)$<br>${\\rm{ = 2 \\times 2}}{\\rm{.5 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 4}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 5 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 4}}}}\\,{\\rm{mol}}\\,{{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}\\,{{\\rm{s}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 50 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 5}}}}\\,{\\rm{mol}}\\,{{\\rm{L}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}\\,{{\\rm{s}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\rm{.}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23357,'chemistry',59,365,676,'${E^o}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} for{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {F_2} + 2e \\to 2{F^ - }{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} is{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,2.8{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} V,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} $<br>${E^o}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} for{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\frac{1}{2}{F_2} + e \\to {F^ - }{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} is$','[{"text": "&ndash; 1.4 V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "&ndash; 2.8 V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2.8 V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1.4 V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${{\\rm{E}}^{\\rm{o}}}$ is intensive property and it does not depend on stoichiometry of ${F_2}$ taking part.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23358,'chemistry',58,170,377,'Read Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct option given below.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{CCl}_{4}$ and $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$ are immiscible.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> $\\mathrm{CCl}_{4}$ is a polar solvent.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{CCl}_{4}$ is a non-polar solvent.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23359,'chemistry',60,584,1172,'For the reaction $4 \\mathrm{P}+\\mathrm{Q} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{R}+2 \\mathrm{~S}$. Which of the following statement(s) is/are true ?<br>I. Rate of appearrance of $\\mathrm{S}$ is double the rate of the disappearance of $\\mathrm{Q}$.<br>II. Rate of disappearance $\\mathrm{Q}$ is one fourth the rate of disappearance of $P$<br>III. Rate of formation of $\\mathrm{R}$ is equal to the rate of formation of $\\mathrm{S}$.<br>Choose the correct option.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Given, $4 \\mathrm{P}+\\mathrm{Q} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{R}+2 \\mathrm{~S}$<br>Rate $=\\dfrac{1}{4}\\left[-\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}[\\mathrm{P}]}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right]=\\left[-\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}[\\mathrm{Q}]}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right]=$<br>$\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left[\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}[\\mathrm{R}]}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right]=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left[\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}[\\mathrm{S}]}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right]$<br>I. $\\left[-\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}[\\mathrm{Q}]}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right]=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left[\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}[\\mathrm{S}]}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right] \\Rightarrow$<br>$\\left[\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}[\\mathrm{S}]}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right]=2\\left[-\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}[\\mathrm{Q}]}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right]$<br>II. $\\dfrac{1}{4}\\left[-\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}[\\mathrm{P}]}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right]=\\left[-\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}[\\mathrm{Q}]}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right]$<br>III. $\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left[\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}[\\mathrm{R}]}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right]=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left[\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}[\\mathrm{S}]}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right]$<br>All the given statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23361,'chemistry',59,374,702,'Some of the batteries are rechargeable:<br>I. Fuel cell<br>II. Dry cell,<br>III. Lead-storage<br>IV. Nickel-Cadmium,<br>V. Lithium<br>Select the batteries which can be recharged','[{"text": "II, IV and V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV and V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'III. Lead-storage, IV. nickel-cadmium and V. lithium batteries are rechargeable',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23362,'chemistry',58,175,383,'An electrolyte A  gives 3 ions and B  is a nonelectrolyte. If 0.1 M solution of B produces an osmotic pressure P , then 0.05 M solution of A will produce pressure, assuming that the electrolyte is completely ionised.','[{"text": "1.5 P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.5 P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.75 P", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${{\\rm{i}}_{\\rm{A}}} = 3\\,,\\,{{\\rm{i}}_{\\rm{B}}} = 1$<br>$\\frac{{{{\\rm{\\pi }}_{\\rm{A}}}}}{{{{\\rm{\\pi }}_{\\rm{B}}}}} = \\frac{{{{\\rm{i}}_{\\rm{A}}} \\times {{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{A}}}}}{{{{\\rm{i}}_{\\rm{B}}} \\times {{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{B}}}}}$<br>$\\dfrac{\\pi_{\\mathrm{A}}}{\\mathrm{P}}=\\dfrac{3 \\times 0.05}{1 \\times 0.1} \\Rightarrow \\pi_{\\mathrm{A}}=1.5 \\mathrm{P}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23363,'chemistry',60,589,1186,'Activation energy $\\left( {{{\\rm{E}}_{\\rm{a}}}} \\right)$ and rate constants ${\\rm{(}}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{)}}$ and $\\left.k_{2}\\right)$ of a chemical reaction at two different temperatures $\\left( {{{\\rm{T}}_{\\rm{1}}}} \\right)$ and $\\left( {{{\\rm{T}}_{\\rm{2}}}} \\right)$are related by','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{log}}\\\\frac{{{{\\\\rm{k}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}}}{{{{\\\\rm{k}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}}}{\\\\rm{ =  - }}\\\\frac{{{{\\\\rm{E}}_{\\\\rm{a}}}}}{{\\\\rm{R}}}\\\\left( {\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\\\rm{T}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}}}{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\\\rm{T}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}}}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{log}}\\\\frac{{{{\\\\rm{k}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}}}{{{{\\\\rm{k}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}}}{\\\\rm{ =  - }}\\\\frac{{{{\\\\rm{E}}_{\\\\rm{a}}}}}{{\\\\rm{R}}}\\\\left( {\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\\\rm{T}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}}}{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\\\rm{T}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}}}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\ln \\\\dfrac{k_{2}}{k_{1}}=-\\\\dfrac{E_{a}}{R}\\\\left(\\\\dfrac{1}{T_{1}}-\\\\dfrac{1}{T_{2}}\\\\right)$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ln}}\\\\frac{{{{\\\\rm{k}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}}}{{{{\\\\rm{k}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}}}{\\\\rm{ =  - }}\\\\frac{{{{\\\\rm{E}}_{\\\\rm{a}}}}}{{\\\\rm{R}}}\\\\left( {\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\\\rm{T}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}}}{\\\\rm{ - }}\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\\\rm{T}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}}}} \\\\right)$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'On integrating within limits $k_{1}$ to $k_{2}$ and $T_{1}$ to $T_{2}$<br>$\\begin{aligned}& \\int_{k_{1}}^{k_{2}} \\ln k=-\\dfrac{E_{a}}{R} \\int_{T_{1}}^{T_{2}} \\dfrac{1}{T} \\\\& \\ln \\dfrac{k_{2}}{k_{1}}=\\dfrac{E_{a}}{R}\\left[\\dfrac{1}{T_{2}}-\\dfrac{1}{T_{1}}\\right]=\\dfrac{E_{a}}{R}\\left[\\dfrac{1}{T_{1}}-\\dfrac{1}{T_{2}}\\right] \\\\& \\text { or } \\ln \\dfrac{k_{2}}{k_{1}}=\\dfrac{E_{a}}{R}\\left[\\dfrac{1}{T_{1}}-\\dfrac{1}{T_{2}}\\right]\\end{aligned}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23367,'chemistry',60,589,1186,'The Arrhenius equation for trans isomerisation of 2-butene and 1-butene nitrile are given as follows:<br>\n(i) For 2-butene; ${\\rm{k}}\\left( {{{\\rm{s}}^{{\\rm{  -  1}}}}} \\right){\\rm{  =  1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{13}}{\\rm{.8}}}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{(  -  263}}{\\rm{.5}}\\,{\\rm{kJ/mol//RT)}}}}$<br>\n(ii) For 2-butene nitrile ; ${\\text{k\'}}\\left( {{{\\text{s}}^{{\\text{ - 1}}}}} \\right){\\text{ = 1}}{{\\text{0}}^{{\\text{11}}}}{\\text{ex}}{{\\text{p}}^{{\\text{ - 214}}{\\text{.5kmo}}{{\\text{\\Gamma }}^{{\\text{ - 1/RT}}}}}}$<br>The temperature at which ${\\text{k = k\'}}$ is','[{"text": "$913.87 \\\\mathrm{~K}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$533.43 \\\\mathrm{~K}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1000.02 \\\\mathrm{~K}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$407.05 \\\\mathrm{~K}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$10^{13.8} \\exp ^{-263.5 k J m o \\Gamma^{1 / R T}}=10^{11} \\exp ^{-214.5 k J m o I^{-1 / R T}}$<br>or<br>$\\begin{gathered}10^{13.8-11}=\\exp \\dfrac{[(-214.5)-(-263.5)] \\mathrm{kJmol}^{-1}}{8.314 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{kJmol}^{-1} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1} \\times T} \\\\\\quad \\text { or } 630.957=\\exp \\dfrac{5.893 \\times 10^{3}}{T} \\\\\\therefore 2.303 \\log 630.957=\\dfrac{5.893 \\times 10^{3}}{T} \\\\\\therefore \\quad T=\\dfrac{5.893 \\times 10^{3}}{2.303 \\times 2.8}=913.87 \\mathrm{~K}\\end{gathered}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
