(23371,'chemistry',60,589,1186,'The rate constant for the first order decomposition of the ethylene oxide into $\\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ and $\\mathrm{CO}$ is described by $\\log \\mathrm{k}\\left(\\mathrm{s}^{-1}\\right)=14.34-\\dfrac{12.5 \\times 10^{4} \\mathrm{~K}}{\\mathrm{~T}}$<br>Then the activation energy of the reaction is','[{"text": "$2.39 \\\\times 10^{5} \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2.39 \\\\times 10^{3} \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$4.78 \\\\times 10^{5} \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4.78 \\\\times 10^{2} \\\\mathrm{~kJ} \\\\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\log \\mathrm{k}=\\log \\mathrm{A}-\\dfrac{\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{a}}}{2.303 \\mathrm{RT}}$<br>$\\log \\mathrm{k}=14.34-\\dfrac{12.5 \\times 10^{4} \\mathrm{~K}}{\\mathrm{~T}}$<br>From Eqs. (1) and (2)<br>$\\dfrac{\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{a}}}{2.303 \\mathrm{R}}=12.5 \\times 10^{4} \\mathrm{~K}$<br>$\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{a}}=\\left(12.5 \\times 10^{4} \\mathrm{~K}\\right) \\times 2.303 \\times 8.314 \\mathrm{JK}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$<br>$=239 \\times 10^{4} \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$<br>$=2.39 \\times 10^{6} \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$<br>$=2.39 \\times 10^{3} \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/60_23371_question_1.png'),
