(23378,'chemistry',58,172,380,'The solubility of a specific non-volatile salt is 4 g in 100 g of water at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. If $2.0 \\mathrm{~g}, 4.0 \\mathrm{~g}$ and 6.0 g of the salt is added to 100 g of water at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, in system $\\mathrm{X}, \\mathrm{Y}$ and Z , respectively. The vapour pressure would be in the order','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{X} < \\\\mathrm{Y} < \\\\mathrm{Z}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{X}} > {\\\\rm{Y}} > {\\\\rm{Z}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Z}} > {\\\\rm{X}} = {\\\\rm{Y}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{X}} > {\\\\rm{Y}} = {\\\\rm{Z}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Solubility of salt is 4 g in $100\\,{\\rm{g}}\\,{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$.<br>So, if salt is less than 4 g , its vapour pressure will be high but on increasing solute to 4 g vapour pressure will decrease to maximum. On further adding solute (more than 4 g ), it won\'t affect the V.P. as now solute won\'t be a part of solution and will remain separated as ppt.<br>So, V.P. order: $\\mathrm{X}>\\mathrm{Y}=\\mathrm{Z}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(23379,'chemistry',60,589,1186,'In the equilibrium ${\\text{P + Q}} \\rightleftharpoons {\\text{R + S}}$, the activation energy for forward reaction is ${\\rm{15}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{k}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{cal/mole}}$ and that of backward reaction is ${\\rm{25}}\\,{\\rm{k}}\\,{\\rm{cal/mole}}$. Which one of the following statement is correct?','[{"text": "It is an exothermic process", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is an endothermic process", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is reaction for which ${\\\\rm{\\\\Delta H = 0}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is a sublimation process", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Activation energy of forward reaction is lesser than that of backward reaction. Hence the reaction is exdothermic.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
