(23433,'chemistry',58,172,380,'The relative lowering of vapour pressure is equal to the ratio between the number of','[{"text": "solute molecules to the solvent molecules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "solute molecules to the total molecules in the solution", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "solvent molecules to the total molecules in the solution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "solvent molecules to the total number of ions of the solute", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'According to Raoult\'s law, relative lowering in vapour pressure is directly proportional to the mole fraction of solute, i.e.$\\frac{{{\\rm{p^\\circ }} - {\\rm{p}}}}{{{\\rm{p^\\circ }}}} = {{\\rm{\\chi }}_{\\rm{s}}}$<br> where,<br>${{\\rm{\\chi }}_{\\rm{s}}} = \\frac{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{s}}}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{s}}} + {\\rm{N}}}} = \\frac{{{\\rm{moles\\,of\\,solute}}}}{{{\\rm{total\\,number\\,of\\,moles}}}}$<br>$\\therefore$ Relative lowering of vapour pressure<br>$ = \\frac{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ + }}\\,{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}}} = \\frac{{{\\rm{solute}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{molecules}}}}{{\\left( {\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{total}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{molecules}}}\\\\\n{{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{in}}\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{the}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{solution}}}\n\\end{array}} \\right)}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
