(23713,'chemistry',58,175,383,'The Osmotic pressure of the aq. solution of the given solute at $27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ if depression in freezing point is $0.90^{\\circ}$ is ____.(approx.)<br>(Molal depression constant of water is $1.86\\,{\\rm{K}}\\,{\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{ - 1}}\\,{\\rm{kg}}?$  Assume molality as molarity.)','[{"text": "12", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "18", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "25", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\Delta {{\\rm{T}}_{\\rm{f}}} = {{\\rm{k}}_{\\rm{f}}} \\times {\\rm{molarity}},$  $\\pi  = {\\rm{molarity}} \\times {\\rm{RT}}$<br>$\\therefore \\frac{{\\Delta {{\\rm{T}}_{\\rm{f}}}}}{\\pi } = \\frac{{{{\\rm{k}}_{\\rm{f}}}}}{{{\\rm{RT}}}}$<br>$\\frac{{0.9}}{\\pi } = \\frac{{1.86}}{{0.0821 \\times 300}}$<br>$\\pi=11.918$ atm',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
