(23726,'chemistry',60,587,1180,'8 g of the radioactive isotope, Cs - 137 were collected on Feb 1, 2011 at 10 atm and kept in a sealed tube. On july 1, 2011 at 10 atm it was found that only $0.25 \\mathrm{~g}$ of it remained. The half life period of the isotope is','[{"text": "25 days", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "30 days", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "37.5 days", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "50 days", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Number of days of disintegration $=$ number of months $\\times 30=150$ days<br>$8 \\rightarrow 4 \\rightarrow 2 \\rightarrow 1 \\rightarrow 0.5 \\rightarrow 0.25$<br>i.e., number of Half-lives $=5$<br>$\\mathrm{t}_{1 / 2}=\\dfrac{150}{5}=30 \\text { days }$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
