(23759,'chemistry',58,174,382,'One molal aqueous solution of urea freezes at $-1.86^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. Aqueous solution of ${{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{n}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{2n}}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{n}}}$  $36\\% $ by mass of water freezes at $-3.72^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. What is the value of n ?','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Molality of urea solution $=1 \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{~kg}^{-1}$<br>$\\Delta {{\\text{T}}_{\\text{f}}}({\\text{urea}}) = 0 - \\left( { - 1.86^\\circ } \\right) = 1.86^\\circ $<br>$\\Delta {{\\text{T}}_{\\text{f}}} = \\left( {\\frac{{1000\\,{{\\text{W}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{{{{\\text{M}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{W}}_{\\text{1}}}}}} \\right){{\\text{K}}_{\\text{f}}} = {\\text{molality}}\\,\\,{{\\text{K}}_{\\text{f}}}$<br>$\\therefore 1.86^\\circ  = {{\\text{K}}_{\\text{f}}} \\times 1\\,{\\text{mo}}{{\\text{l}}^{ - 1}}\\,{\\text{kg}}$<br>$\\therefore {{\\text{K}}_{\\text{f}}} = 186^\\circ {\\text{mo}}{{\\text{l}}^{ - 1}}\\,{\\text{kg}}$<br>${{\\text{C}}_{\\text{n}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{2n}}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{n}}} = 36{\\text{g}}\\,\\,{\\text{in}}\\,\\,100\\,\\,{\\text{g}}\\,\\,{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}$<br>$\\Delta {{\\text{T}}_{\\text{f}}} = \\left( {{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{n}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{2n}}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{n}}}} \\right) = \\frac{{1000\\,{{\\text{K}}_{\\text{f}}}{{\\text{W}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{{{{\\text{M}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{W}}_{\\text{1}}}}}$<br>$\\therefore {{\\text{M}}_{\\text{2}}}\\left( {{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{n}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{2n}}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{n}}}} \\right) = \\frac{{1000\\,{{\\text{K}}_{\\text{f}}}{{\\text{W}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{{\\Delta {{\\text{T}}_{\\text{f}}}{{\\text{W}}_{\\text{1}}}}}$<br>$ = \\frac{{1000 \\times 1.86 \\times 36}}{{3.72 \\times 100}}$<br>${{\\text{M}}_{\\text{2}}}\\left( {{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{n}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{2n}}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{n}}}} \\right) = 180\\,{\\text{g}}\\,\\,{\\text{mo}}{{\\text{l}}^{ - 1}}$<br>$12{\\text{n}} + 2{\\text{n}} + 16{\\text{n}} = 180$<br>$\\therefore 30\\,{\\text{n}} = 180$<br>${\\text{n}} = 6$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
