(24274,'chemistry',60,585,1176,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The overall order of the reaction is the sum of the exponents of all the reactants in the rate expression.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> There are many higher order reactions.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Higher-order reactions, with reaction orders beyond two, are uncommon due to the statistical improbability of multiple molecules colliding simultaneously in a specific way. This makes first and second order reactions more frequently observed and studied. So option (3) is correct',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24276,'chemistry',59,370,691,'The equivalent conductivity of a solution containing 2.54 grams of $\\mathrm{CuSO}_{4}$ per litre is $91.0 \\Omega^{-1} \\mathrm{~cm}^{2} \\mathrm{eq}^{-1}$. Its conductivity would','[{"text": "$2.9 \\\\times 10^{-3} \\\\Omega^{-1} \\\\mathrm{~cm}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$1.8 \\\\times 10^{-2} \\\\Omega^{-1} \\\\mathrm{~cm}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2.4 \\\\times 10^{-4} \\\\Omega^{-1} \\\\mathrm{~cm}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3.6 \\\\times 10^{-3} \\\\Omega^{-1} \\\\mathrm{~cm}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\text{k}} = {\\Lambda _{{\\text{eq}}}} \\times {\\text{C}}$<br> $ = \\left( {91{\\Omega ^{ - 1}}\\,{\\rm{c}}{{\\rm{m}}^2}{\\rm{e}}{{\\rm{q}}^{ - 1}}} \\right)\\left( {\\frac{{2.54}}{{(159/2) \\times 1000}}{\\rm{eq}} \\cdot {\\rm{c}}{{\\rm{m}}^{ - 3}}} \\right)$ <br> $ = 2.9 \\times {10^{ - 3}}{\\Omega ^{ - 1}}\\,{\\rm{c}}{{\\rm{m}}^{ - 1}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
