(24278,'chemistry',60,585,1175,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Rate of reaction doubles when concentration of reactant is doubled if it is a first order reaction.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Rate constant also doubles.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'For a given reaction, rate constant is constant and independent of the concentration of reactant.<br>For first order raection :<br>$\\mathrm{r}_{1}=\\mathrm{K}[\\mathrm{R}]$<br>According to equation, $\\mathrm{r}_{2}=2 \\mathrm{r}_{1}$<br>$\\mathrm{r}_{2}=\\mathrm{k}\\left[\\mathrm{R}_{2}\\right] \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{r}_{2}=\\mathrm{k}\\left[2 \\mathrm{R}_{1}\\right]$<br>$\\mathrm{r}_{2}=2 \\mathrm{k}\\left[\\mathrm{R}_{1}\\right]$<br>$\\mathrm{r}_{2}=2 \\mathrm{r}_{1}$<br>Rate constants depends only on temperature not on concentrations. So option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24280,'chemistry',59,365,677,'For the cell reaction, $2{\\text{C}}{{\\text{e}}^{4 + }} + {\\text{Co}} \\to 2{\\text{C}}{{\\text{e}}^{3 + }}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{o}}^{2 + }};\\,\\,{\\text{E}}{^\\circ _{{\\text{cell}}}}{\\text{is}}\\,\\,1.89\\,{\\text{V}}.$ if ${{\\text{E}}_{{\\text{C}}{{\\text{o}}^{2 + }}/{\\text{Co}}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} $ is ${\\mkern 1mu}  - 0.28{\\text{V}},$ What is the value of ${\\text{E}}{^\\circ _{{\\text{C}}{{\\text{e}}^{{\\text{4 + }}}}{\\text{/}}\\,\\,{\\text{C}}{{\\text{e}}^{{\\text{3 + }}}}}}$?','[{"text": "$0.28 \\\\mathrm{~V}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1.61 \\\\mathrm{~V}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$2.17 \\\\mathrm{~V}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$5.29 \\\\mathrm{~V}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{E}}{{\\rm{^\\circ }}_{{\\rm{Cell}}}}{\\rm{ = E}}{{\\rm{^\\circ }}_{{\\rm{Cel}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{4 + }}}}{\\rm{/C}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{3 + }}}}}}{\\rm{ - E}}{{\\rm{^\\circ }}_{{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{o}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}{\\rm{/Co}}}}$<br>$ \\Rightarrow 1.89 = {\\rm{E}}{^\\circ _{{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{/C}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{3 + }}}}}} - ( - {\\rm{0}}.{\\rm{28}})$<br>$ \\Rightarrow \\,\\,{\\rm{E}}{^\\circ _{{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{4 + }}}}{\\rm{/C}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{3 + }}}}}} = 1.89 - 0.28 = 1.61\\,{\\rm{V}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24281,'chemistry',63,823,1820,'Noble gases have very low boiling points because','[{"text": "Interatomic forces are negligible", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Interatomic forces are stronger", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are inert", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have completely filled valency shell", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Noble gases being monoatomic have no interatomic forces except weak dispersion forces and therefore, they are liquefied at very low temperatures. Hence, they have low boiling points.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24284,'chemistry',59,373,697,'A constant current of $30 \\mathrm{~A}$ is passed through an aqueous solution of $\\mathrm{NaCl}$ for a time of $1.00 \\mathrm{~h}$. What is the volume of $\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ gas produced at STP?','[{"text": "$30.00 \\\\mathrm{~L}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$25.08 \\\\mathrm{~L}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$12.54 \\\\mathrm{~L}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$1.12 \\\\mathrm{~L}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Due to electrolysis,<br>${\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{{\\rm{(l)}}}}{\\rm{ + 2}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}} \\to {{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{2(g)}}}}{\\rm{ + 2OH}}_{{\\rm{(aq)}}}^{\\rm{ - }}$<br>${\\rm{2Cl}}_{{\\rm{(aq)}}}^{\\rm{ - }} \\to {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{{\\rm{2(g)}}}}{\\rm{ + 2}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$<br>${\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{{\\rm{(l)}}}}{\\rm{ + 2C}}{{\\rm{l}}^{\\rm{ - }}}_{{\\rm{(aq)}}} \\to {{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{2(g)}}}}{\\rm{ + C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{{\\rm{2(g)}}}}{\\rm{ + 2OH}}_{{\\rm{(aq)}}}^{\\rm{ - }}$<br>${\\rm{O}}{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$ formed = NaOH formed = Z I T <br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{E}}}{{{\\rm{96500}}}}{\\rm{ \\times I \\times t = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{40}}}}{{{\\rm{96500}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 30 \\times 1 \\times 60 \\times 60}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 44}}{\\rm{.77}}\\,{\\rm{g}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{44}}{\\rm{.77}}}}{{{\\rm{40}}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.12}}\\,{\\rm{mol}}$<br>${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_2}$ formed =$\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}\\,$ mol of NaOH formed <br>$ = \\frac{{1.12}}{2} = 0.56\\,{\\rm{mol}}$<br>$ = 0.56 \\times 22.4\\,{\\rm{L}}\\,\\,{\\rm{at}}\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{STP}} = 12.54\\,{\\rm{L}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
