(24292,'chemistry',59,370,692,'The equivalent conductance of silver nitrate solution at $250^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ for an infinite dilution was found to be 133.3 $\\Omega^{-1} \\mathrm{~cm}^{2}$ equiv ${ }^{-1}$. The transport number of $\\mathrm{Ag}^{+}$ions in very dilute solution of $\\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}$ is 0.464 . Equivalent conductances of $\\mathrm{Ag}^{+}$ and $\\mathrm{NO}_{3}^{-}$(in $\\Omega^{-1} \\mathrm{~cm}^{2}$ equiv ${ }^{-1}$ ) at infinite dilution are respectively','[{"text": "$195.2,133.3$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$61.9,71.4$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$71.4,61.9$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$133.3,195.2$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\Lambda _{{\\text{eq}}\\left( {{\\text{A}}{{\\text{g}}^{{\\text{  +  }}}}} \\right)}^\\infty  = $ transport number ${\\text{A}}{{\\text{g}}^{{\\text{ }} + {\\text{ }}}} \\times \\Lambda _{{\\text{eq}}\\left( {{\\text{AgN}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)}^\\infty $<br>$ = 0.464 \\times 133.3 = 61.9\\,{\\Omega ^{ - 1}}\\,{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{equi}}{{\\text{v}}^{ - 1}}$<br> By Kohlrausch\'s law,<br>${\\rm{\\Lambda }}_{{\\rm{eq}}\\left( {{\\rm{AgN}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}} \\right)}^\\infty {\\rm{ = \\Lambda }}_{{\\rm{eq}}\\left( {{\\rm{A}}{{\\rm{g}}^{\\rm{ + }}}} \\right)}^\\infty {\\rm{ + \\Lambda }}_{{\\rm{eq}}\\left( {{\\rm{NO}}_{\\rm{3}}^{\\rm{ - }}} \\right)}^\\infty $<br>${\\rm{\\Lambda }}_{{\\rm{eq}}\\left( {{\\rm{NO}}_{\\rm{3}}^{\\rm{ - }}} \\right)}^\\infty {\\rm{ = \\Lambda }}_{{\\rm{eq}}\\left( {{\\rm{AgN}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}} \\right)}^\\infty {\\rm{ - \\Lambda }}_{{\\rm{eq}}\\left( {{\\rm{A}}{{\\rm{g}}^{\\rm{ + }}}} \\right)}^\\infty $<br> $ = 133.3 - 61.9$<br>$ = 71.4{\\Omega ^{ - 1}}\\,{\\rm{c}}{{\\rm{m}}^2}{\\rm{ equiv}}{{\\rm{ }}^{ - 1}}$<br>So, the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
