(24295,'chemistry',60,588,1184,'A student has studied the decomposition of a gas $\\mathrm{AB}_{3}$ at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. He obtained the following data.<br> <br>The order of the reaction is','[{"text": "0", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${{\\text{t}}_{1/2}} \\propto {\\left( {{{\\text{C}}_0}} \\right)^{1 - {\\text{n}}}}$<br>In terms of pressure,<br>$\\dfrac{\\left(\\mathrm{t}_{1 / 2}\\right)_{1}}{\\left(\\mathrm{t}_{1 / 2}\\right)_{2}}=\\left(\\dfrac{\\mathrm{p}_{1}}{\\mathrm{p}_{2}}\\right)^{1-\\mathrm{n}}$<br>$\\dfrac{4}{2}=\\left(\\dfrac{50}{100}\\right)^{1-n}$<br>or $(2)^{1}=\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{1-n}$<br>or $(2)^{1}=(2)^{\\mathrm{n}-1}$<br>On equating, we get<br>$1=\\mathrm{n}-1$<br>$\\mathrm{n}=2$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/60_24295_question_1.png'),
