(24363,'chemistry',59,367,680,'At temperature of 298 K , the emf of the following electrochemical cell<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Zn}_{(\\mathrm{s})}\\left|\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}(0.1 \\mathrm{M}) \\| \\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}(0.01 \\mathrm{M})\\right| \\mathrm{Cu}_{(\\mathrm{s})}}}$ will be  <br>V . (Given ${\\mathrm{\\left.\\mathrm{E}_{\\text {cell }}^{\\circ}=1.10 \\mathrm{~V}\\right)}}$','[{"text": "1.07V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1.1 V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.03 V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.75 V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'For the given electrochemical cell, the cell reaction will be as follows:<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Zn} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}+2 \\mathrm{e}^{-}}}$ (Oxidation at anode)<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}+2 \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{Cu}}}$ (Reduction at cathode)<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}+\\mathrm{Zn} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{Cu}+\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}}}$(Overall cell reaction)<br>The e.m.f. of the cell is given by<br>$\\mathrm{E}_{\\text {cell }}=\\mathrm{E}_{\\text {cell }}^{\\circ}-\\dfrac{0.0591}{\\mathrm{n}} \\log _{10} \\dfrac{\\left[\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}\\right]}{\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}\\right]}$<br>Substituting the values in above equation,<br>${{\\rm{E}}_{{\\rm{cell }}}} = 1.10 - \\frac{{0.0591}}{2}{\\rm{lo}}{{\\rm{g}}_{10}}\\frac{{(0.1)}}{{(0.01)}}$<br>$ = 1.10 - \\frac{{0.0591}}{2}{\\rm{lo}}{{\\rm{g}}_{10}}10$<br>$ = 1.10 - \\frac{{0.0591}}{2}$<br>$ = 1.10 - 0.0296$<br>$ = 1.07\\,{\\rm{V}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24365,'chemistry',63,810,1763,'White ${{\\rm{P}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ is more reactive than $\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ because','[{"text": "Ionisation energy of $\\\\mathrm{P}$ is low", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{P}-\\\\mathrm{P}$ bond is weaker than $\\\\mathrm{N} \\\\equiv \\\\mathrm{N}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Electronegativity of ${{\\\\rm{P}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}$ is low", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'White ${{\\rm{P}}_{\\rm{4}}}$ is more reactive than $\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ because $\\mathrm{P}-\\mathrm{P}$ bond is weaker than $\\mathrm{N} \\equiv \\mathrm{N}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
