(24422,'chemistry',60,585,1174,'Consider a chemical reaction involving compounds A and B , which is found to be second order in A and first order in B. At what rate, will the reaction occur in experiment 2 ?<br>','[{"text": "$1.8\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{M}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{ - 1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0.6\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{M}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{ - 1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1.2\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{M}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{ - 1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2.4\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{M}}{{\\\\rm{s}}^{ - 1}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{R}} = {\\rm{k}}{[{\\rm{A}}]^2}[{\\rm{B}}]$<br>From experiment 1,<br>$0.1=\\mathrm{k}(0.5)^{2}(2)$<br>$\\mathrm{k}=0 \\cdot 2$<br>and for experiment 2,<br>Rate $ = (0 \\cdot 2)\\,{(2)^2}(3) = 2 \\cdot 4\\,{\\rm{M}}{{\\rm{s}}^ - }$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/60_24422_question_1.png'),
(24423,'chemistry',59,367,680,'The standard e.m.f. of a cell, involving two electrons transfer is found to be 1.182 V at ${\\mathrm{25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}}$. The equilibrium constant of the reaction is','[{"text": "$1 \\\\times {10^{10}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1.5 \\\\times {10^{20}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2 \\\\times {10^{30}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1 \\\\times {10^{40}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Standard e.m.f. of the cell ${\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{E}^{\\circ}\\right)}}$<br>$ = \\frac{{2.303\\,{\\rm{RT}}}}{{{\\rm{nF}}}}{\\rm{lo}}{{\\rm{g}}_{{\\rm{10}}}}{\\rm{K}}$<br>$ = \\frac{{0.0591}}{{\\rm{n}}}{\\rm{lo}}{{\\rm{g}}_{{\\rm{10}}}}{\\rm{K}}$<br>$\\therefore 1.182 = \\frac{{0.0591}}{{\\rm{n}}}{\\rm{lo}}{{\\rm{g}}_{{\\rm{10}}}}{\\rm{K}}$<br>$\\therefore \\,\\,\\frac{{1.182 \\times 2}}{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.0591}}}}{\\rm{lo}}{{\\rm{g}}_{{\\rm{10}}}}{\\rm{K}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore}}$ Equilibrium constant ${\\mathrm{(\\mathrm{K})}}$<br>$ = {10^{\\left[ {\\frac{{1.182 \\times 2}}{{0.0591}}} \\right]}} = 1.0 \\times {10^{40}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
