(24426,'chemistry',60,585,1174,'For the reaction, $\\mathrm{A} \\rightarrow$ products, $-\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}[\\mathrm{A}]}{\\mathrm{dt}}=\\mathrm{k}$ and at different time interval, [A] values are<br> <br>At 20 minute, rate will be','[{"text": "$12 \\\\mathrm{~mol} / \\\\mathrm{min}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$10 \\\\mathrm{~mol} / \\\\mathrm{min}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$8 \\\\mathrm{~mol} / \\\\mathrm{min}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0.4 \\\\mathrm{~mol} / \\\\mathrm{min}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'At 20 min , moles of \'A\' will be 12 mol ,<br>So, rate $=\\dfrac{(20-12) \\mathrm{mol}}{20 \\mathrm{~min}}=0 \\cdot 4 \\mathrm{~mol} / \\mathrm{min}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/60_24426_question_1.png'),
