(24430,'chemistry',60,587,1179,'In the following first order reactions, $({\\text{A}})\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{k}}_{\\text{1}}}}}$ product, $({\\text{B}})\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{k}}_{\\text{2}}}}}$ product, the ratio $\\mathrm{k}_{1} / \\mathrm{k}_{2}$ if $90 \\%$ of (A) has been reacted in time \' $t$ \' while $99 \\%$ of (B) has been reacted in time $2 t$ is','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\dfrac{1}{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{k}_{1}=\\dfrac{1}{\\mathrm{t}} \\ln \\left(\\dfrac{\\mathrm{A}_{0}}{0.1 \\mathrm{~A}_{0}}\\right)$<br>$\\mathrm{k}_{2}=\\dfrac{1}{2 \\mathrm{t}} \\ln \\left(\\dfrac{\\mathrm{B}_{0}}{0.01 \\mathrm{~B}_{0}}\\right)$<br>$\\dfrac{\\mathrm{k}_{1}}{\\mathrm{k}_{2}}=2 \\dfrac{\\ln (10)}{\\ln (100)}=\\dfrac{2 \\ln (10)}{\\ln (10)^{2}}=\\dfrac{2 \\ln (10)}{2 \\ln (10)}$<br>$\\Rightarrow \\dfrac{\\mathrm{k}_{1}}{\\mathrm{k}_{2}}=1$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
