(24439,'chemistry',60,588,1184,'$\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{B} \\rightarrow$ Product, $\\frac{{{\\text{dx}}}}{{{\\text{dt}}}} = {\\text{k}}{[{\\text{A}}]^{\\text{a}}}{[{\\text{B}}]^{\\text{b}}}$.  If $\\left( {\\frac{{{\\rm{dx}}}}{{{\\rm{dt}}}}} \\right) = {\\rm{k}},$  then order of reaction is','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\frac{{{\\rm{dx}}}}{{{\\rm{dt}}}} = {\\rm{k}},$  means both $a, b$ are equal to zero.<br>So, it\'s zero order reaction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24440,'chemistry',63,813,1778,'How is $\\mathrm{O}_{3}$ estimated quantitatively?','[{"text": "Iodometry using borate buffer", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Permanganometry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acid base titration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Precipitation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ozone reacts with an excess of potassium iodide solution buffered with a borate buffer ( $\\mathrm{pH} 9.2)$, iodine is liberated which can be titrated against a standard solution of sodium thiosulphate. This is a quantitative method for estimating $\\mathrm{O}_{3}$ gas.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24443,'chemistry',60,585,1174,'The reaction, $\\mathrm{X}+2 \\mathrm{Y}+\\mathrm{Z} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{N}$ occurs by the following mechanism:<br>(P) $\\mathrm{X}+\\mathrm{Y} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{M}$ (rapid equilibrium)<br>(Q) $\\mathrm{M}+\\mathrm{Z} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{P}$ (slow)<br>(R) $\\mathrm{O}+\\mathrm{Y}+\\mathrm{P} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{N}$ (very fast)<br>What is the rate law for this reaction?','[{"text": "Rate $=\\\\mathrm{k}[Z]$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rate $=\\\\mathrm{k}[\\\\mathrm{X}][\\\\mathrm{Y}]^{2}[\\\\mathrm{Z}]$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rate $=\\\\mathrm{k}[\\\\mathrm{N}]$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rate $=\\\\mathrm{k}[\\\\mathrm{X}][\\\\mathrm{Y}][\\\\mathrm{Z}]$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Slow step is R.D.S<br>Rate $ = {{\\rm{K}}^\\prime }[{\\rm{M}}][{\\rm{Z}}]\\quad (1)$<br>but \' M \' is intermediate. So [M] can be taken from e.q. (1)<br>$[\\mathrm{M}]=\\dfrac{[\\mathrm{X}][\\mathrm{Y}]}{\\mathrm{k}_{\\mathrm{C}}}$<br>By Substituting [M] in e.q(1)<br>Rate $=\\dfrac{\\mathrm{k}^{\\prime}[\\mathrm{X}][\\mathrm{Y}]}{\\mathrm{k}_{\\mathrm{C}}}$. $[\\mathrm{Z}]$ or $\\mathrm{k}[\\mathrm{X}][\\mathrm{Y}][\\mathrm{Z}]$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24446,'chemistry',59,367,680,'The relationship between standard reduction potential of cell (in volts) and equilibrium constant at ${\\mathrm{25{ }^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}}$ is shown by ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{cell}}^{\\circ}=\\dfrac{5.91 \\times 10^{-\\mathrm{x}}}{\\mathrm{n}} \\log _{10} \\mathrm{~K}}}$. The value of \' X \' is ____ .','[{"text": "10", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\mathrm{E_{\\text {cell }}^{o}=\\dfrac{0.0591}{n} \\log _{10} \\mathrm{~K}=\\dfrac{5.91 \\times 10^{-2}}{\\mathrm{n}} \\log _{10} \\mathrm{~K}}}$ ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{X}=2}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24447,'chemistry',60,589,1186,'At room temperature, the reaction between NO and $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ to give $\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ is fast, while that between CO and $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ is slow. It is due to','[{"text": "CO is smaller in size than NO", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "CO is poisonous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The activation energy for the reaction, $2 \\\\mathrm{NO}+\\\\mathrm{O}_{2} \\\\rightarrow 2 \\\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ is less than<br>$2 \\\\mathrm{CO}+\\\\mathrm{O}_{2} \\\\rightarrow 2 \\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'If activation energy to form activated complex is low, then rate of reaction will be higher.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
