(24458,'chemistry',59,367,680,'At temperature of 298 K , the emf of the following electrochemical cell<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Zn}_{(\\mathrm{s})}\\left|\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}\\left(10^{-4} \\mathrm{M}\\right) \\| \\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}\\left(10^{-4} \\mathrm{M}\\right)\\right| \\mathrm{Cu}_{(\\mathrm{s})}}}$ will be ____ ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{V} .\\left(\\right.}}$ Given ${\\mathrm{\\left.\\mathrm{E}_{\\text {cell }}^{\\circ}=1.10 \\mathrm{~V}\\right)}}$','[{"text": "0", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.07", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.65", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.1", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'For the given electrochemical cell, the cell reaction will be as follows:<br>${\\mathrm{\\begin{array}{ll}\\mathrm{Zn} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}+2 \\mathrm{e}^{-} & \\text {(Oxidation at anode) } \\\\ \\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}+2 \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{Cu} & \\text { (Reduction at cathode) }\\end{array}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}+\\mathrm{Zn} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{Cu}+\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}}}$(Overall cell reaction)${\\mathrm{\\therefore \\quad}}$ The e.m.f. of the cell is given by${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{E}_{\\text {cell }}=\\mathrm{E}_{\\text {cell }}^{\\circ}-\\dfrac{0.0591}{\\mathrm{n}} \\log _{10} \\dfrac{\\left[\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}\\right]}{\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}\\right]}}}$<br>Substituting the values in above equation,<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{E}_{\\text {cell }}=1.10-\\dfrac{0.0591}{2} \\log _{10} \\dfrac{10^{-4}}{10^{-4}}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{=1.10-\\dfrac{0.0591}{2} \\times 0}}$<br>${\\mathrm{=1.10 \\mathrm{~V}}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
