(24496,'chemistry',60,587,1178,'Consider the following statement in respect of zero order reaction.<br>I. The rate of the reaction is independent of reactant concentration.<br>II. The rate of the reaction is independent of temperature.<br>III. Rate law expression: $\\mathrm{R}=\\mathrm{k}[\\mathrm{A}]^{0}$ and unit of $\\mathrm{k}=\\mathrm{s}^{-1}$<br>IV. The rate constant of reaction is independent of reactant concentration.<br>Choose the correct statements/s','[{"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'For a zero-order reaction, rate and rate constant are independent of reactant concentration. Units of K are mol. $1 \\mathrm{lit}^{-} \\mathrm{sec}^{-}$.In general, rate increases with increase in temp.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24502,'chemistry',60,586,1177,'Read Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct option given below.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> As mole is the basic chemical unit, the concentration of the dissolved solute is usually specified in terms of number of moles of solute.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The total number of molecules of reactants involved in a balanced chemical equation is known as molecularity of the reaction.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The number of moles of a solute present in one litre of solution is known is as molarity (M). The total no. of molecules of reactants present in a balanced chemical equation is known as molecularity. For example,<br>$\\mathrm{PCl}_{5} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{PCl}_{3}+\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ (Unimolecular)<br>$2 \\mathrm{HCl} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}_{2}+\\mathrm{I}_{2}$ (Biomolecular)<br>$\\therefore$ Molarity and molecularity are used in different sense. There is no relation between assertion and reason.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
