(24533,'chemistry',60,587,1179,'For reaction, $2 \\mathrm{~N}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{5} \\rightarrow 4 \\mathrm{NO}_{2}+\\mathrm{O}_{2}$, the rate is directly proportional to $\\left[\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{5}\\right]$. At $45^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}, 90 \\%$ of the $\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{5}$ reacts in 3600 seconds. The value of the rate constant is','[{"text": "$3.2 \\\\times 10^{-4} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$6.4 \\\\times 10^{-4} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$8.5 \\\\times 10^{-4} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$12.8 \\\\times 10^{-4} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Reaction is of first order as given rate is proportional to $\\left[\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{5}\\right.$ ]only. <br>So, $\\quad \\ln \\left( {\\frac{{\\text{a}}}{{{\\text{a}} - {\\text{x}}}}} \\right) = {\\text{kt}}$<br>where, ${\\text{a}} = $ initial concentration<br>${\\text{a}} = 100{\\text{ (Let)}}$<br>$ \\Rightarrow ({\\text{a}} - {\\text{x}}) = 10\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,(\\because {\\text{x}} = 90\\% )$<br>${\\text{a}} - {\\text{x}} = $ concentration at an instant<br>${\\rm{ln}}\\left( {\\frac{{100}}{{10}}} \\right) = {\\rm{k}} \\times 3600\\,\\,\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\kern 1pt} ({\\rm{t}} = 3600\\,{\\rm{s}})$<br>$2.303\\,\\log 10 = {\\text{k}} \\times 3600\\quad (\\log 10 = 1)$<br>${\\text{k}} = \\frac{{2.303}}{{3600}} = 6.4 \\times {10^{ - 4}}\\,{{\\text{s}}^{ - 1}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
