(24609,'chemistry',60,589,1186,'In the presence of a catalyst, activation energy of a reaction is lowered by 2 k cal at $27 ^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. Hence, rate will be','[{"text": "20 times", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "28 times", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "14 times", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "remain the same", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Arrhenius equation is<br>${\\rm{k}} = {\\rm{A}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{  -  }}{{\\rm{E}}_{\\rm{a}}}{\\rm{/RT}}}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} (1)$<br>In the presence of catalyst,rate constant <br>${{\\rm{k}}^\\prime } = {\\rm{A}}{{\\rm{e}}^{ - {\\rm{E}}_a^\\prime {\\rm{/ RT}}}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} (2)$<br>On dividing Eq. (2) by Eq. (1), we get<br>$\\frac{{{{\\text{k}}^\\prime }}}{{\\text{k}}} = {{\\text{e}}^{\\left( {{{\\text{E}}_{\\text{a}}} - {{\\text{E}}_a}^\\prime } \\right)}}/{\\text{RT}}$<br>$\\frac{{{{\\text{k}}^\\prime }}}{{\\text{k}}} = {{\\text{e}}^{\\left( {\\frac{{2000}}{{2 \\times 300}}} \\right)}} = {{\\text{e}}^{3.33}}$<br>$\\left[ {\\because {{\\text{E}}_{\\text{a}}} - {{\\text{E}}_{\\text{a}}}^\\prime  = 2000\\,{\\text{cal (given)}}} \\right]$<br>$\\because$ On taking log both sides,<br>$\\log \\frac{{{{\\text{k}}^\\prime }}}{{\\text{k}}} = \\frac{{3.33}}{{2.303}}$<br>$\\frac{{{{\\text{k}}^\\prime }}}{{\\text{k}}} = \\operatorname{antilog} 1.446 = 27.92 \\approx 28$<br>We know that, rate ${\\text{(R)}} \\propto {\\text{k}}$<br>$\\therefore \\quad {{\\text{R}}^\\prime }/{\\text{R}} = {{\\text{k}}^\\prime }/{\\text{k}} = 28$<br>$\\therefore \\quad {{\\text{R}}^\\prime } = 28{\\text{R}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
