(24636,'chemistry',60,585,1176,'For the reaction system :<br> $2 \\mathrm{NO}(\\mathrm{g})+\\mathrm{O}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g}) \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{NO}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})<br> \\text { volume is }$suddenly reduced to half of its value by<br> increasing the pressure on it. If the reaction is of<br> first order with respect to $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ and second order<br> with respect to $\\mathrm{NO}$, the rate of reaction will','[{"text": "diminish to one-fourth of its initial value", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "diminish to one-eighth of its initial value", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "increase to eight times of its initial value", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "increase to four times of its initial value", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Rate law ${\\rm{ = k}}\\left[ {{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}} \\right]{{\\rm{[NO]}}^{\\rm{2}}}$<br> If volume is reduced to half, concentrations<br> will get double.<br>$\\therefore {\\rm{Rate = k}}\\left[ {{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}} \\right]{{\\rm{[2NO]}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 8}}\\,\\,{\\rm{times}}$<br>So, the correct option is (3).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
