(24657,'chemistry',60,589,1186,'Consider the following reaction, The reaction is of first order in each diagram, with an equilibrium constant of ${10^4}$. For the conversion of chair form to boat form ${{\\text{e}}^{{\\text{ - E/aRT}}}} = 4.35 \\times {10^{ - 8}}$ at 298 K with pre-exponential factor of ${10^{12}}{\\mkern 1mu} {{\\text{s}}^{ - 1}}.$ Apparent rate constant $( = {{\\text{k}}_{\\text{A}}}/{{\\text{k}}_{\\text{B}}})$ at 298 K is','[{"text": "$4.35 \\\\times 10^{4} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4.35 \\\\times 10^{8} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$4.35 \\\\times 10^{-8} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4.35 \\\\times 10^{12} \\\\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${{\\text{k}}_{\\text{B}}} = {\\text{A}}{{\\text{e}}^{ - {{\\text{E}}_{\\text{a}}}{\\text{/RT}}}}$<br>$ = {10^{12}} \\times 4.35 \\times {10^{ - 8}} = 4.35 \\times {10^4}\\,{{\\text{s}}^{ - 1}}$<br>Also equilibrium constant, ${\\text{K}} = \\frac{{{{\\text{k}}_{\\text{A}}}}}{{{{\\text{k}}_{\\text{B}}}}} = {10^4}$<br>$\\therefore \\,\\,\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\kern 1pt} {{\\text{k}}_{\\text{A}}} = {{\\text{k}}_{\\text{B}}} \\times {10^4} = 4.35 \\times {10^8}\\,{{\\text{s}}^{ - 1}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/60_24657_question_1.png'),
