(24676,'chemistry',59,373,697,'The quantity of silver deposited when one coulomb charge is passed through ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}}}$ solution','[{"text": "1 chemical equivalent of silver", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.1 g atom of silver", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 electrochemical equivalent of silver", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "l g of silver.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The quantity deposited by 1 coulomb is known as electrochemical equivalent.<br>$\\begin{aligned}& \\mathrm{W}=\\mathrm{ZQ} \\\\& \\text { when } \\mathrm{Q}=1\\end{aligned}$<br>$\\therefore \\quad \\mathrm{W}=\\mathrm{Z}$<br>So, the correct option is (3).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24677,'chemistry',60,587,1179,'The activity of an old piece of wood is just $25 \\%$ of the fresh piece of wood. If ${{\\text{t}}_{1/2}}$ of $\\mathrm{C}-14$ is $6000\\,{\\text{yr}}$, the age of piece of wood is','[{"text": "$6000\\\\,{\\\\text{yr}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3000\\\\,{\\\\text{yr}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$9000\\\\,{\\\\text{yr}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$12000\\\\,{\\\\text{yr}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{k = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.693}}}}{{{{\\rm{t}}_{{\\rm{1/2}}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.693}}}}{{{\\rm{6000}}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.155 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 4}}}}$<br>${\\text{t}} = \\frac{{2.303}}{{\\text{k}}}\\log \\frac{{{{\\text{N}}_0}}}{{\\text{N}}}$<br>$ = \\frac{{2.303}}{{1.155 \\times {{10}^{ - 4}}}}{\\text{log}}\\frac{{100}}{{25}} = 12005\\,\\,{\\text{yr}} \\approx 12000\\,\\,{\\text{yr}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24678,'chemistry',60,587,1179,'In a first order reaction, it takes 40.5 minutes for the reactant to be $24 \\%$ decomposed. Find the rate of the reaction.','[{"text": "$9.4 \\\\times 10^{-3} \\\\mathrm{~min}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$7.0 \\\\times 10^{-3} \\\\mathrm{~min}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$25.2 \\\\times 10^{-3} \\\\mathrm{~min}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$10.5 \\\\times 10^{-3} \\\\mathrm{~min}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'For a first order reaction,<br>${\\rm{k}} = \\frac{{2.303}}{{\\rm{t}}}{\\rm{log}}\\frac{{\\rm{a}}}{{{\\rm{a}} - {\\rm{x}}}}$ <br>24% decomposition means,${\\rm{x}} = 24\\% \\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,{\\rm{a}} = 0.24\\,{\\rm{a}}$<br>${\\rm{Hence}},{\\rm{k}} = \\frac{{2.303}}{{40.5}}{\\rm{log}}\\frac{{\\rm{a}}}{{{\\rm{a}} - 0.24{\\rm{a}}}}$<br>$ = \\frac{{2.303}}{{40.5}} \\times {\\rm{log}}\\frac{{100}}{{76}}{\\rm{mi}}{{\\rm{n}}^{ - 1}}$<br>$ = \\frac{{2.303}}{{40.5}} \\times 0.12$<br>$ = 6.82 \\times {10^{ - 3}}\\,{\\rm{mi}}{{\\rm{n}}^{ - 1}} \\simeq 7.0 \\times {10^{ - 3}}\\,{\\rm{mi}}{{\\rm{n}}^{ - 1}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24679,'chemistry',63,808,1755,'On reaction with $\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$, phosphorus forms two types of halides \'${\\rm{A}}$\' and \'${\\rm{B}}$\'. Halide ${\\rm{A}}$ is yellowish-white powder but halide \' $B$ \' is colourless oily liquid. Compounds " $\\mathrm{A}$ ", " $\\mathrm{B}$ " and their hydrolysis products are, respectively','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}, \\\\mathrm{PCl}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{PO}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{PO}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{PCl}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{PO}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{PO}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{PCl}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{PO}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{PO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{PCl}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{PO}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{PO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{A}$ is $\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}$ (It is yellowish white powder)<br>$\\mathrm{P}_{4}+10 \\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\rightarrow 4 \\mathrm{PCl}_{5}$<br>$\\mathrm{B}$ is $\\mathrm{PCl}_{3}$ (It is a colourless oily liquid)<br>$\\mathrm{P}_{4}+6 \\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\rightarrow 4 \\mathrm{PCl}_{3}$<br>Hydrolysis products are formed as follows :<br>$\\begin{aligned}& \\mathrm{PCl}_{3}+3 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{PO}_{3}+3 \\mathrm{HCl} \\\\& \\mathrm{PCl}_{5}+4 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{PO}_{4}+5 \\mathrm{HCl}\\end{aligned}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24742,'chemistry',63,819,1813,'Among the following, the one that can do glass etching is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HIO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{SiF}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HF}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HNO}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'HF is the only acid that reacts with silica<br>$\\mathrm{SiO}_{2}+6 \\mathrm{HF} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SiF}_{6}+2 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24680,'chemistry',59,370,688,'A conductivity cell with two electrodes (dark side) are half filled with infinitely dilute aqueous solution of a weak electrolyte. If volume is doubled by adding more water at constant temperature, the molar conductivity of the cell will','[{"text": "depend upon type of electrolyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "increase sharply", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "remain same or cannot be measured accurately", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "decrease sharply.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In general, molar conductivity increases with dilution as mobility of ions increases but given is already at infinity dilution, so further dilution has no effect on molar conductivity. So, the correct option is (3).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/59_24680_question_1.png');
