(24681,'chemistry',60,587,1178,'In a zero order reaction, when ${\\rm{ d x / d t}}$  is plotted against (a-x) ____ is obtained.','[{"text": "a line passing through the origin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a curve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a parabola", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a line parallel to x-axis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In a zero order reaction, rate is independent of concentration. Hence, plot of rate vs concentration will be a horizontal line. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/60_24681_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24682,'chemistry',59,365,675,'How can an electrochemical cell be converted into an electrolytic cell?','[{"text": "Exchanging the electrodes at anode and cathode.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Applying an external opposite potential greater than ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{E}_{\\\\text {cell }}^{\\\\circ}}}$.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Applying an external opposite potential lower than ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{E}_{\\\\text {celll }}^{\\\\circ}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reversing the flow of ions in salt bridge.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'If ${\\mathrm{E_{\\text {ext }}>E_{\\text {cell }}^{\\circ}}}$ an electrochemical cell acts as an electrolytic cell. The entire cell reaction will be reversed. During this the the oxidised species will be reduced and reduced species will be oxidised. So, the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24683,'chemistry',63,808,1759,'In the compounds of the type $P O X_{3}, P$ atoms show multiple bonding of the type is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{p\\\\pi  - p\\\\pi }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{d\\\\pi  - d\\\\pi }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{p\\\\pi  - d\\\\pi }}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24684,'chemistry',59,371,693,'The molar conductivity for electrolytes ${\\mathrm{A}}$ and ${\\mathrm{B}}$ are plotted against ${\\mathrm{C^{1 / 2}}}$ as shown below. Electrolytes A and B respectively are','[{"text": "A - Weak electrolyte<br>B - Strong electrolyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Weak electrolyte<br>B - Weak electrolyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Strong electrolyte<br>B - Weak electrolyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Strong electrolyte<br>B - Strong electrolyte", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\mathrm{\\Lambda_{\\mathrm{m}}}}$ increases continously with dilution for weak electrolytes (A) and for strong electrolytes, no much change is noticed with dilution (B). So, the correct option is (1).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/59_24684_question_1.png'),
(24685,'chemistry',63,808,1757,'Among the following, the incorrect statement is','[{"text": "pyrophosphorus acid, ${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}{{\\\\rm{P}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}$ is dibasic and reducing agent.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "hypophosphorus acid, $\\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{PO}_{2}$ is monobasic and a very strong oxidizing agent", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "impure orthophosphoric acid, $\\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{PO}_{4}$ is prepared on a large scale by treating phosphate rock with conc. $\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{SO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "phosphorus in the phosphorus acid $\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{PO}_{3}\\\\right)$ is in +3 oxidation state and has a $\\\\mathrm{P}-\\\\mathrm{H}$ bond and is therefore a reducing agent", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{PO}_{2}$ is monobasic and strong reducing agent.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24686,'chemistry',60,584,1173,'Which one of the factors does not affect rate of the reaction?','[{"text": "Molecularity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Concentration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nature of reactants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Temperature", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Molecularity does not affect the rate of the reaction.<br>So, the correct option is (1).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24687,'chemistry',59,371,693,'Which out of the following is a correct equation to show change in molar conductivity with respect to concentration for a weak electrolyte, if the symbols carry their usual meaning?','[{"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\Lambda_{\\\\mathrm{m}}^{2} \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{K}_{\\\\mathrm{a}} \\\\Lambda_{\\\\mathrm{m}}^{\\\\circ 2}+\\\\mathrm{K}_{\\\\mathrm{a}} \\\\Lambda_{\\\\mathrm{m}} \\\\Lambda_{\\\\mathrm{m}}^{\\\\circ}=0}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\Lambda_{\\\\mathrm{m}}-\\\\Lambda_{\\\\mathrm{m}}^{\\\\circ}-\\\\mathrm{AC}^{1 / 2}=0}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\Lambda_{m}-\\\\Lambda_{m}^{\\\\circ}+\\\\mathrm{AC}^{1 / 2}=0}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\Lambda_{\\\\mathrm{m}}^{2} \\\\mathrm{C}+\\\\mathrm{K}_{\\\\mathrm{a}} \\\\Lambda_{\\\\mathrm{m}}^{\\\\circ 2}-\\\\mathrm{K}_{\\\\mathrm{a}} \\\\Lambda_{\\\\mathrm{m}} \\\\Lambda_{\\\\mathrm{m}}^{\\\\circ}=0}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'For weak electrolyte ${\\mathrm{K_{a}=\\dfrac{C \\alpha^{2}}{1-\\alpha}}}$ <br>$({\\rm{Degree}}\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,{\\rm{dissociation}})\\alpha {\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\Lambda _{\\rm{m}}}}}{{{\\Lambda _{\\rm{m}}}^\\circ }}$<br>${{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{a}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{C}}{{\\left( {\\frac{{{\\Lambda _{\\rm{m}}}}}{{\\Lambda {^\\circ _{\\rm{m}}}}}} \\right)}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{{{\\rm{1}} - \\frac{{\\Lambda {{\\rm{^\\circ }}_m}}}{{\\Lambda {{\\rm{^\\circ }}_m}}}}}$<br>${{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{a}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{C}}\\Lambda _{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}}}{{{\\rm{\\Lambda }}{{\\rm{^\\circ }}_{\\rm{m}}}\\left( {{\\rm{\\Lambda }}{{\\rm{^\\circ }}_{\\rm{m}}} - {{\\rm{\\Lambda }}_{\\rm{m}}}} \\right)}}$<br>${{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{a}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{C}}\\Lambda _{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}}}{{{\\rm{\\Lambda }}{{\\rm{^\\circ }}^{\\rm{2}}}_{\\rm{m}} - {{\\rm{\\Lambda }}_{\\rm{m}}}{\\rm{\\Lambda }}{{\\rm{^\\circ }}_{\\rm{m}}}}}$<br>${{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{a}}}\\left( {{\\rm{\\Lambda }}{{\\rm{^\\circ }}^{\\rm{2}}}_{\\rm{m}} - {\\rm{\\Lambda }}{{\\rm{^\\circ }}_{\\rm{m}}}{{\\rm{\\Lambda }}_{\\rm{m}}}} \\right){\\rm{ = C}}\\Lambda _{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}$<br>${\\rm{\\Lambda }}_{\\rm{m}}^{\\rm{2}}{\\rm{C}} - {{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{a}}}{\\rm{\\Lambda }}{{\\rm{^\\circ }}^{\\rm{2}}}_{\\rm{m}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{a}}}{\\rm{\\Lambda }}{{\\rm{^\\circ }}_{\\rm{m}}}{{\\rm{\\Lambda }}_{\\rm{m}}}{\\rm{ = 0}}$<br>${\\rm{So,the}}\\,{\\rm{correct}}\\,{\\rm{option}}\\,{\\rm{is(1)}}{\\rm{.}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24688,'chemistry',63,808,1758,'Which of the following statements is not valid for oxo-acids of phosphorus?','[{"text": "Orthophosphoric acid is used in the manufacture of triple superphosphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All oxo-acids contain tetrahedral four coordinated phosphorus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypophosphorus acid is a diprotic acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All oxo-acids contains atleast one $\\\\mathrm{P}=\\\\mathrm{O}$ unit and one $\\\\mathrm{P}$ - $\\\\mathrm{OH}$ group", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Hypophosphorus acid is monoprotic acid as only one $\\mathrm{H}$ is attached on oxygen atom. $\\mathrm{H}$ atoms attached to $\\mathrm{O}$ are ionisable.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
