(24710,'chemistry',60,587,1179,'In a first order reaction, the plot of log (a-x) against time \' t \' gives','[{"text": "a straight line with positive slope", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a straight line with negative slope", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a straight line passing through origin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a curve.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'For a first order reaction,<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{log}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{[A]}} = \\frac{{ - {\\rm{k}}}}{{2.303}}{\\rm{t}} + {\\rm{log}}\\,{{{\\rm{[A]}}}_0}}\\\\\n{{\\mkern 1mu} \\left. {\\quad {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} ({\\rm{where}}\\,{{{\\rm{[A]}}}_{\\rm{0}}} = {\\rm{a ,}}\\,{\\rm{[A}}] = {\\rm{a}} - {\\rm{x}}} \\right)}\n\\end{array}$  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/60_24710_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Thus, a plot of log(a - x) and \'t\' gives a straight line with a negative slope.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
