(24721,'chemistry',59,374,701,'The reaction at cathode in the cells commonly used in clocks involves','[{"text": "reduction of Mn from +4 to +3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "oxidation of Mn from +2 to +7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "reduction of Mn from +7 to +2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "oxidation of Mn from +3 to +4 .", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Dry cell is commonly used in clocks. The reaction at cathode is given by<br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n2{\\rm{Mn}}{{\\rm{O}}_{2(\\,{\\rm{s}})}} + 2{\\rm{NH}}_{4({\\rm{aq}})}^ +  + 2{{\\rm{e}}^ - } \\to \\\\\n\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{M}}{{\\rm{n}}_2}{{\\rm{O}}_{3(\\,{\\rm{s}})}} + 2{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{3(\\,{\\rm{g}})}} + {{\\rm{H}}_2}{\\rm{O}}\n\\end{array}$<br>Thus, in the reaction, manganese ${\\mathrm{(\\mathrm{Mn})}}$ is reduced from the +4 oxidation state to the +3 state. So, the correct option is (1).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
