(24725,'chemistry',59,368,681,'For the electrochemical cell : ${\\mathrm{M\\left|M^{2+} \\| X\\right| X^{2-}}}$ If, ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{E}_{\\left(\\mathrm{M}^{2+} / \\mathrm{M}\\right)}^{\\circ}=0.46 \\mathrm{~V}}}$ and ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{E}_{\\left(\\mathrm{x} / \\mathrm{x}^{2-}\\right)}^{\\circ}=0.34 \\mathrm{~V}}}$. <br>Which of the following is correct?','[{"text": "${\\\\mathrm{M^{2+}+X^{2-} \\\\rightarrow M+X}}$ is a spontaneous reaction.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{M}+\\\\mathrm{X} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{M}^{2+}+\\\\mathrm{X}^{2-}}}$ is a spontaneous reaction.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{E}_{\\\\text {cell }}=0.80 \\\\mathrm{~V}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{E}_{\\\\text {cell }}=-0.80 \\\\mathrm{~V}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{E}_{\\text {cell }}^{\\circ}=\\mathrm{E}_{\\text {cathode }}^{\\circ}-\\mathrm{E}_{\\text {anode }}^{\\circ}}}$<br>$=0.34-0.46=-0.12 \\mathrm{~V}$<br>Now, ${\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}=-\\mathrm{nFE}{ }^{\\circ}}}$<br>As ${\\mathrm{E_{\\text {cell }}^{\\circ}}}$ of the reaction ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{M}+\\mathrm{X} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{M}^{+2}+\\mathrm{X}^{2-}}}$ is negative, ${\\mathrm{\\Delta \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}}}$ will be positive hence this reaction will be non-spontaneous.<br>For the reverse reaction,<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{M}^{2+}+\\mathrm{X}^{2-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{M}+\\mathrm{X}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{E}_{\\text {cell }}^{\\circ}=+0.12 \\mathrm{~V}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\Rightarrow \\Delta \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}=-\\mathrm{ve}}}$<br>Thus the reaction ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{M}^{2+}+\\mathrm{X}^{2-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{M}+\\mathrm{X}}}$, will be spontaneous. So, the correct option is (1).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
