(24728,'chemistry',64,188,1904,'I : The three series of the transition metals are ${\\rm{3d}}$ series $\\mathrm{(\\mathrm{Sc}}$ to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cu}}$ ), ${\\rm{4d}}$ series ( $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Y}}$ to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cd}}$ ) and ${\\rm{5d}}$ series (La, Hf to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Hg}}$).<br>II : The two series of the inner transition metals (4f and 5f) are known as lanthanoids and actinoids respectively.<br>The above mentioned correct statement(s) is/ are','[{"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neither I nor II", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The three main series of the transition metals are $\\mathrm{3 \\mathrm{~d}}$ series ( $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Sc}}$ to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Zn}}$ ), $\\mathrm{4 \\mathrm{~d}}$ series ( $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Y}}$ to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cd})}$ and ${\\rm{5d}}$ series ( ${\\rm{La}}\\,\\,{\\rm{\\&amp; }}\\,\\,{\\rm{Hf}}\\,\\,{\\rm{to}}\\,\\,{\\rm{Hg}}$ ). The two series of the inner transition metals, (4f and 5f) are known as lanthanoids and actinoids respectively.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24729,'chemistry',59,367,680,'The emf of cell ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Tl}\\left|\\underset{(0.001 \\mathrm{M})}{\\mathrm{Tl}^{+}} \\| \\underset{(0.01 \\mathrm{M})}{\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}}\\right| \\mathrm{Cu}}}$ is 0.83 V at 298K. It could be increased by','[{"text": "increasing concentration of ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}}}$ ions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "increasing concentration of ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Tl}^{+}}}$ions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "decreasing concentration of both ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Tl}^{+}}}$and ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}}}$ ions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "increasing concentration of both ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Tl}^{+}}}$and ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}}}$ ions.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'At anode $\\left[ {{\\rm{T}}{{\\rm{l}}_{({\\rm{s}})}} \\to {\\rm{Tl}}_{{\\rm{(aq) }}}^{\\rm{ + }}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{e}}^ - }} \\right] \\times {\\rm{2}}$<br>At cathode ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cu}_{(\\text {aq })}^{2+}+2 \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Cu}_{(\\mathrm{s})}}}$<br>Overall redox reaction<br>${\\mathrm{2 \\mathrm{Tl}_{(\\mathrm{s})}+\\mathrm{Cu}_{\\text {(aq) }}^{2+} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{Tl}_{(\\mathrm{aq})}^{+}+\\mathrm{Cu}_{(\\mathrm{s})}}}$<br>From Nernst equation,<br>$\\mathrm{E}_{\\text {cell }}=\\mathrm{E}_{\\text {cell }}^{\\circ}-\\dfrac{0.059}{2} \\log \\dfrac{\\left[\\mathrm{Tl}^{+}\\right]^{2}}{\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}\\right]}$<br>If concentration of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}}}$ ion increases, emf of the cell increases.<br>So, the correct option is (1).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24730,'chemistry',63,826,1829,'Correct bond angles are in the order of','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{OF}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{OCl}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}>\\\\mathrm{ClO}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{ClO}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}>\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}>\\\\mathrm{OF}_{2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{OF}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}>\\\\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}>\\\\mathrm{ClO}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}>\\\\mathrm{OF}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}>\\\\mathrm{ClO}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In $\\mathrm{ClO}_{2}$, due to larger size of chlorine atom, repulsion between non-bonding electrons on the chlorine atoms overcome the lone pairlone pair repulsion. Hence, the order of bond angle is<br>$\\mathrm{ClO}_{2}>\\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\mathrm{O}>\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}>\\mathrm{OF}_{2} .$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
