(24739,'chemistry',60,587,1179,'Consider a first order gas phase decomposition reaction given below:<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{A}_{(\\mathrm{g})} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{B}_{(\\mathrm{g})}+\\mathrm{C}_{(\\mathrm{g})}}}$<br>The initial pressure is 6.0 atm . The pressure drops to 3.0 atm after 6.93 min . How much time (in minutes) would it take to lower the partial pressure of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{A}_{(\\mathrm{g})}}}$ by 4.0 atm ? <br>[Consider: ${\\mathrm{\\log _{10}(3)=0.48}}$ ]','[{"text": "4 min", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "11 min", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "8 min", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 min", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Since the partial pressure reduces to half after 6.93 minutes, the half-life, ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{t}_{1 / 2}=6.93 \\mathrm{~min}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{k=\\dfrac{0.693}{t_{1 / 2}}=\\dfrac{0.693}{6.93}=0.10 \\mathrm{~min}^{-1}}}$<br>For a gas phase first order reaction,${\\mathrm{k=\\dfrac{2.303}{t} \\log _{10}\\left(\\dfrac{p_{i}}{p_{A}}\\right)}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{i}}=6.0 \\mathrm{~atm} ; \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{A}}=6.0-4.0=2.0 \\mathrm{~atm}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore \\quad 0.10=\\dfrac{2.303}{\\mathrm{t}} \\log _{10}\\left(\\dfrac{6.0}{2.0}\\right)}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore \\quad t=23.03 \\log (3.0)=11.05 \\mathrm{~min}}}$<br>$ \\approx 11\\,\\min $',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
