(24766,'chemistry',64,191,1918,'$\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{Ti}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{3+}}$ absorbs green and yellow region part of visible light. The colour of the compound is','[{"text": "Blue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Purple", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Green", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'We know that white light is composed of many different colours. When white light is allowed to fall on $\\rm{{\\left[ {{\\text{Ti}}{{\\left( {{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}} \\right)}_{\\text{6}}}} \\right]^{{\\text{3 + }}}}}$ ion, this ion  absorbs the light of green and yellow colour and transmits almost purple colour. The purple colour of the transmitted light is called complimentary colour of that of absorbed light.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24784,'chemistry',64,191,1917,'Which one of the following sets correctly represents the increase in the paramagnetic property of the ions?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cr}^{+2}>\\\\mathrm{V}^{+2}>\\\\mathrm{Cu}^{+2}>\\\\mathrm{Mn}^{+2}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cu}^{+2} < \\\\mathrm{Cr}^{+2} < V^{+2} < \\\\mathrm{Mn}^{+2}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cu}^{+2} < \\\\mathrm{V}^{+2} < \\\\mathrm{Cr}^{+2} < \\\\mathrm{Mn}^{+2}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{V}^{+2} < \\\\mathrm{Cu}^{+2} < \\\\mathrm{Cr}^{+2} < \\\\mathrm{Mn}^{+2}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Paramagnetic property depends upon the number of unpaired electrons.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24768,'chemistry',63,825,1828,'Among the following incorrect statement is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{XeO}_{3}$ has four $\\\\sigma$ and four $\\\\pi$ bonds.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "the hybridization of $\\\\mathrm{Xe}$ in $\\\\mathrm{XeF}_{4}$ is ${\\\\rm{s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}{{\\\\rm{d}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "among the noble gases the occurrence (percent by weight) of argon is highest in air", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "liquid helium is used in cryogenic liquids.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/63_24768_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> $\\mathrm{XeO}_{3}$ has three $\\sigma$ and three $\\pi$-bonds. There is one lone pair of electrons on the central Xe atom.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24769,'chemistry',64,191,1921,'The type of holes occupied by $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}}$ and $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}}$ or $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{N}}$ in interstitial compounds are respectively','[{"text": "Tetrahedral and octahedral", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Octahedral and tetrahedral", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Octahedral and octahedral", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tetrahedral and tetrahedral", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Due to small size of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}}$ and large size of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}}$ or $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{N}}$, occupy tetrahedral and octahedral holes, respectively.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24771,'chemistry',63,824,1825,'Among the following, planar molecule is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{XeF}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{XeOF}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{XeO}_{2} \\\\mathrm{~F}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{XeF}_{4}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/63_24771_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> In the formation of ${\\rm{Xe}}{{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{s}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{3}}}{{\\rm{d}}^{\\rm{2}}}$ hybridization occurs which gives the molecule an octahedral structure. The xenon and four fluorine atoms are coplanar while the two equatorial positions are occupied by the two lone pairs of electrons.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24772,'chemistry',64,188,1904,'Platinum, palladium and iridium are called noble metals because','[{"text": "They are used as catalysts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are inert towards many common reagents", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They are shining lustrous pleasing to look at", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are found in active state", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Pt}, \\mathrm{Pd}}$ and Ir are called noble metals because they are inert towards many common reagents.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(24773,'chemistry',60,585,1175,'The unit of rate constant, ${\\mathrm{k}}$ for a third order reaction is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{mol}^{-\\mathrm{X}} \\mathrm{L}^{\\mathrm{X}} \\mathrm{s}^{-1}}}$. The value of \' X \' is ____.','[{"text": "$\\\\frac{1}{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\frac{3}{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$ - 1$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Unit of rate constant of ${\\mathrm{n^{\\text {th }}}}$ order reaction:<br>${\\left( {{\\rm{mol\\,}}{{\\rm{L}}^{ - 1}}} \\right)^{1 - {\\rm{n}}}}{{\\rm{s}}^{ - 1}} = {\\left( {{\\rm{mol}}\\,{{\\rm{L}}^{ - 1}}} \\right)^{1 - 3}}\\,{{\\rm{s}}^{ - 1}}$<br>$ = {\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{ - 2}}\\,{{\\rm{L}}^2}{\\rm{\\,}}{{\\rm{s}}^{ - 1}}$.<br>Hence, the value of \' X \' is 2 .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
