(24813,'chemistry',60,585,1175,'The rate constant of the reaction ${\\mathrm{A \\longrightarrow B}}$ is ${\\mathrm{1.0 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{M} \\mathrm{s}^{-1}}}$. After 100 min , if the concentration of A is 4.40 M , then concentration of ${\\mathrm{B}}$ will be ____ M .','[{"text": "0.44", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4.4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.6", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'For the reaction, ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{A} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{B}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{k}=1 \\times 10^{-4} \\,\\mathrm{M} \\mathrm{s}^{-1}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore}}$ Since the units of k is M ${{\\rm{s}}^{ - 1}}$, it is a zero order reaction.<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore k=\\dfrac{[\\mathrm{A}]_{0}-[\\mathrm{A}]_{\\mathrm{t}}}{\\mathrm{t}}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore \\mathrm{t}=100 \\mathrm{~min}=6000 \\mathrm{~s}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore 1 \\times 10^{-4}=\\dfrac{[\\mathrm{A}]_{0}-4.40}{6000}}}$<br>$\\begin{aligned}& {[\\mathrm{A}]_{0}=5.00 \\mathrm{M}} \\\\& {[\\mathrm{B}]_{\\mathrm{t}}=[\\mathrm{A}]_{0}-[\\mathrm{A}]_{\\mathrm{t}}=5.00-4.40=0.60 \\mathrm{M}}\\end{aligned}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
