(24832,'chemistry',60,587,1180,'The ratio of the rate at the start of the reaction if half life $\\left( {{{\\rm{t}}_{\\rm{1}}}} \\right)$ of the first order reaction and half life $\\left( {{{\\rm{t}}_{\\rm{2}}}} \\right)$ of the second order reaction are equal is ____.','[{"text": "0.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6.93", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.0693", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.693", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'For ${\\text{I}}$ order. ${{\\text{k}}_{\\text{1}}} = \\frac{{0.693}}{{[{{\\text{t}}_{1/2}}]}}$;<br>For ${\\text{ Il}}$ order. $\\mathrm{k}_{2}=\\dfrac{1}{\\left(\\mathrm{t}_{1 / 2}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{a}}$<br>If  ${\\left( {{{\\text{t}}_{1/2}}} \\right)_1} = {\\left( {{{\\text{t}}_{1/2}}} \\right)_2}$ then $\\frac{{{{\\text{k}}_{\\text{1}}}}}{{{{\\text{k}}_{\\text{2}}}}} = 0.693{\\text{a}}$<br>Initially  $\\,\\,\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\kern 1pt} {{\\text{r}}_1} = {{\\text{k}}_{\\text{1}}}{[{\\text{a}}]^1},\\,\\,\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\kern 1pt} {{\\text{r}}_{\\text{2}}} = {{\\text{k}}_{\\text{2}}}{[{\\text{a}}]^2}$<br>$\\therefore \\frac{{{{\\text{r}}_{\\text{1}}}}}{{{{\\text{r}}_{\\text{2}}}}} = \\frac{{{{\\text{k}}_{\\text{1}}}}}{{{{\\text{k}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{a}}}} = \\frac{{{{\\text{k}}_{\\text{2}}} \\times 0.693 \\times {\\text{a}}}}{{{{\\text{k}}_{\\text{2}}} \\times {\\text{a}}}} = 0.693$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
