(24841,'chemistry',60,585,1174,'A drop of solution (volume $0.06 \\mathrm{~mL}$ ) contains $3 \\times 10^{-6}$ mole $\\mathrm{H}^{+}$ ions. If the rate of disappearance of the $\\mathrm{H}^{+}$ ions is $1 \\times {10^7}{\\rm{mol}}\\,\\,{\\rm{litr}}{{\\rm{e}}^{ - 1}}{\\rm{se}}{{\\rm{c}}^{ - 1}},$ then time taken for $\\mathrm{H}^{+}$ions in the drop to disappear is ____.','[{"text": "$5 \\\\times {10^{ - 3}}\\\\sec $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$5 \\\\times {10^{ - 1}}\\\\sec $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$5 \\\\times {10^{ - 9}}\\\\sec $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$5 \\\\times {10^{ - 6}}\\\\sec $", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Concentration of drop $=\\dfrac{\\text { mole }}{\\text { volume in } \\mathrm{mL}} \\times 1000$<br>$ = \\frac{{3 \\times {{10}^{ - 6}}}}{{0.06}} \\times 1000 = 0.05\\,{\\text{mol}}\\,\\,{\\text{litr}}{{\\text{e}}^{ - 1}}$<br>Rate of disappearance $=\\dfrac{\\text { conc. change }}{\\text { time }}$<br>$1 \\times 10^{7}=\\dfrac{0.05}{\\text { time }}$<br>Time $=5 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{sec}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
