(24924,'chemistry',60,587,1182,'The initial concentrations of both the reactants of a second order reaction are equal and ${\\mathrm{60 \\%}}$ of the reaction gets completed in 30 s . How much time will be taken in ${\\mathrm{20 \\%}}$ completion of the reaction?','[{"text": "5 min", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.5 sec", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5 sec", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5 hr", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'For second order:<br>$\\begin{align*}k_{2} & =\\dfrac{1}{t} \\cdot \\dfrac{x}{a(a-x)} \\\\& =\\dfrac{1}{30 \\mathrm{~s}} \\times \\dfrac{0.6}{1(1-0.6)}=\\dfrac{1}{30} \\times \\dfrac{0.6}{0.4}\\end{align*}$<br>Now for ${\\mathrm{20 \\%}}$ completion,<br>${\\mathrm{k_{2}=\\dfrac{1}{t} \\cdot \\dfrac{x}{a(1-x)}}}$<br>(Since ${\\mathrm{k_{2}}}$ is constant)<br>${\\mathrm{\\dfrac{1}{30} \\times \\dfrac{0.6}{0.4}=\\dfrac{1}{t} \\times \\dfrac{1}{4}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{t=\\dfrac{30}{0.6} \\times \\dfrac{0.4}{4}=5 \\mathrm{~s}}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
