le=\'max-width:100%;\' />  i.e., $\\mathrm{t}_{2 \\mathrm{~g}}^{5} \\mathrm{e}_{\\mathrm{g}}^{2}$<br>$\\mathrm{Co}^{2+}=3 \\mathrm{~d}^{7}$<br>Number of unpaired electrons $=3$<br>$\\sqrt {3(3 + 2)}  = \\sqrt {15}  = 3.87{\\text{BM}}$<br>${\\left[ {{\\text{Co}}{{({\\text{CN}})}_6}} \\right]^{3 - }}$   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/65_24953_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   i.e., $\\mathrm{t}_{2 \\mathrm{~g}}^{6} \\mathrm{e}_{\\mathrm{g}}^{0}$<br>$\\mathrm{Co}^{3+}=3 \\mathrm{~d}^{6}$<br>Number of unpaired electrons are zero so diamagnetic.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
