(25098,'chemistry',65,954,2218,'Consider the following complex $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{5} \\mathrm{CO}_{3}\\right] \\mathrm{ClO}_{4}$. The coordination number, Oxidation number. number of d-electrons and number of unpaired d-electrons on the metal are respectively','[{"text": "$6,3,6,0$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$7,2,7,1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$7,1,6,4$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$6,2,7,3$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{5} \\mathrm{CO}_{3}\\right] \\mathrm{ClO}_{4}$ Six monodentate ligands are attached to $\\mathrm{Co}$ hence $\\mathrm{C}$. N. of $\\mathrm{Co}=6$; ${\\text{O}}{\\text{.N}}.{\\text{ = x + 5}} \\times ({\\text{0}}){\\text{ + 1}} \\times ({\\text{ - 2}}){\\text{ + 1}} \\times ({\\text{ - 1}}){\\text{ = 0}}$<br>$\\therefore {\\text{x =  + 3;}}$<br>Electronic configuration of $\\mathrm{Co}^{3+}[\\mathrm{Ar}] 3 d^{6} 4 s^{0}$ hence number of $\\mathrm{d}$ electrons is 6 . All d electrons are paired due to strong ligand hence unpaired electron is zero.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
