(25119,'chemistry',63,805,1736,'I. Covalency of $\\mathrm{N}$ is restricted to four<br>II. $\\mathrm{N}$ cannot form $\\mathrm{d} \\pi-\\mathrm{p} \\pi$ bond as the heavier element.<br>III. $\\mathrm{P}$ and As cannot form $\\mathrm{d} \\pi-\\mathrm{p} \\pi$ bond with transition elements when their compounds like $\\mathrm{P}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5}\\right)_{3}$ and $\\mathrm{As}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5}\\right)_{3}$ act as ligands.<br>Which of the above statements are true? Choose the correct option.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{P}$ and As form $\\mathrm{d} \\pi-\\mathrm{p} \\pi$ bond with transition elements when their compounds like $\\mathrm{P}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5}\\right)_{3}$ and $\\operatorname{As}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5}\\right)_{3}$ act as ligands. So, the option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
