(25121,'chemistry',64,190,1911,'Transition elements show high melting points because','[{"text": "d-electrons are involved in interatomic metallic bond in addition to $\\\\mathrm{s}$ electrons", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are hard metals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Generally metals have high MP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They show a transition from metals to non metals", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The high melting points of transition metals are attributed to the involvement of greater number of electrons in the interatomic metallic bonding from (n-1) d-orbitals in addition to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{ns}}$ electrons.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
