(25137,'chemistry',63,808,1755,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">$\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}$ is covalent in gaseous and liquid state but ionic in solid state.<br></div><div class="column-right">$\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}$ in solid state consists of tetrahedral $\\left[\\mathrm{PCl}_{4}\\right]^{+}$cation and octahedral $\\left[\\mathrm{PCl}_{6}\\right]^{-}$anion.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}$ is trigonal bipyramidal molecule containing $\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\mathrm{~d}$-hybridised $\\mathrm{P}$-atom in liquid and gaseous state. Whereas, in solid state it consists of tetrahedral $\\left[\\mathrm{PCl}_{4}\\right]^{+}$cation and octahedral $\\left[\\mathrm{PCl}_{6}\\right]^{-}$anion. So, the option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
