(25152,'chemistry',65,957,2228,'The hybridisation state of $\\mathrm{Fe}$ in<br>$\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{5} \\mathrm{NO}_{3} \\mathrm{SO}_{4}\\right.$ is (At. $\\mathrm{No}$. of $\\mathrm{Fe}=26$ )','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{dsp}^{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\\\mathrm{~d}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\\\mathrm{~d}^{2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{d}^{2} \\\\mathrm{sp}^{3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{Fe}$ is $\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\mathrm{~d}^{2}$ hybridised in $\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{5} \\mathrm{NO}\\right]^{2+}$ complex. $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$ is weak ligand',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25144,'chemistry',64,192,1923,'I. As the oxidation number of a metal increases, ionic character decreases.<br>II. In case of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Mn}, \\mathrm{Mn}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}}$ is a covalent green oil which possess predominantly acidic character and it gives $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{HMnO}_{4}}$.<br>III. $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{V}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{5}}$ is amphoteric, it gives $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{VO}_{4}^{3-}}$ as well as $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{VO}_{2}^{+}}$salts.<br>IV. $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CrO}}$ is basic while $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}}$ is amphoteric.<br>The correct set of statements is (choose the appropriate option)','[{"text": "I, II, III and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'As the oxidation number of a metal increases ionic character decreases. In case of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Mn}, \\mathrm{Mn}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}}$ is a covalent green oil which possess predominantly acidic character and it given $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{HMnO}_{4} \\cdot \\mathrm{V}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{5}}$ is amphoteric, it gives $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{VO}_{4}^{3-}}$ as well as $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{VO}_{2}^{+}}$salts. $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CrO}}$ is basic while $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}}$ is amphoteric.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25145,'chemistry',63,805,1735,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The stability of +5 oxidation state decreases and that of +3 state increases down the group-15.<br></div><div class="column-right">Inert pair effect is more prone in case of heavier members of p-block.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The stability of +5 oxidation state decreases and that of +3 state increases down the group due to inert pair effect. Inert pair effect is more effective in heavy members of p-block elements due to poor shielding effect of d - & f orbital electrons. So, the option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
