(25147,'chemistry',64,191,1914,'Consider the following statements,<br>I. Sc has a low value of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{E}^{\\circ}\\left(\\mathrm{M}^{3+} / \\mathrm{M}^{2+}\\right)}$.<br>II. $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Zn}}$ has the highest value of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{E}^{\\circ}\\left(\\mathrm{M}^{3+} / \\mathrm{M}^{2+}\\right)}$.<br>III. Mn and Fe have comparatively high and low values respectively.<br>The correct set of statements is (choose the appropriate option)','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sc has a low value of ${{\\rm{E}}^{\\rm{^\\circ }}}\\left( {{{\\rm{M}}^{{\\rm{3 + }}}}{\\rm{/}}{{\\rm{M}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}} \\right)$. ${\\rm{Zn}}$ has the highest value of ${{\\rm{E}}^{\\rm{^\\circ }}}\\left( {{{\\rm{M}}^{{\\rm{3 + }}}}{\\rm{/}}{{\\rm{M}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}} \\right)$. Mn and Fe have comparatively high and low values respectively.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
