(25193,'chemistry',65,957,2229,'The spin only magnetic moment of $\\left[\\mathrm{MnBr}_{4}\\right]^{2-}$ is 5.9 BM. The geometry of the complex ion is','[{"text": "Tetrahedral", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Square planar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pyramidal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Octahedral", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Since the coordination number of $\\mathrm{Mn}^{2+}$ ion in the complex ion is 4 , it will be either tetrahedral ( $\\mathrm{sp}^{3}$ hybridisation) or square planar (dsp ${ }^{2}$ hybridisation). But the fact that the magnetic moment of the complex ion is $5.9 \\mathrm{BM}$, it should be tetrahedral in shape rather than square planar because of the presence of five unpaired electrons in the d-orbitals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
