(25204,'chemistry',64,192,1924,'Consider the following statements,<br>I. Sodium dichromate is less soluble than potassium dichromate. <br>II. Crystals of potassium dichromate are of orange colour.<br>III. The chromates and dichromates are interconvertible in aqueous solution depending upon $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{pH}}$ of the solution.<br>IV. The oxidation state of chromate and dichromate is different.<br>The correct statements are','[{"text": "I, II, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I, II and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only I and II", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Sodium dichromate is less soluble than potassium dichromate. Colour of sodium dichromate and potassium dichromate is orange.<br>The chromates and dichromates are interconvertible in aqueous solution depending upon $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{pH}}$ of the solution. The oxidation state of chromate and dichromate is same.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
