(25206,'chemistry',65,958,2232,'Give the electronic configuration of the following complexes on the basis of Crystal Field Splitting theory.<br>$\\left[\\mathrm{CoF}_{6}\\right]^{3-},\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\right]^{4-}$ and $\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{2+}$','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{t}_{2 \\\\mathrm{~g}}^{4} \\\\mathrm{e}_{\\\\mathrm{g}}^{2}, \\\\mathrm{t}_{2 \\\\mathrm{~g}}^{6} \\\\mathrm{e}_{\\\\mathrm{g}}^{0}, \\\\mathrm{t}_{2 \\\\mathrm{~g}}^{6} \\\\mathrm{e}_{\\\\mathrm{g}}^{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{t}_{2 \\\\mathrm{~g}}^{6} \\\\mathrm{e}_{\\\\mathrm{g}}^{0}, \\\\mathrm{t}_{2 \\\\mathrm{~g}}^{6} \\\\mathrm{e}_{\\\\mathrm{g}}^{3}, \\\\mathrm{t}_{2 \\\\mathrm{~g}}^{4} \\\\mathrm{e}_{\\\\mathrm{g}}^{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{t}_{2 \\\\mathrm{~g}}^{6} \\\\mathrm{e}_{\\\\mathrm{g}}^{3}, \\\\mathrm{t}_{2 \\\\mathrm{~g}}^{4} \\\\mathrm{e}_{\\\\mathrm{g}}^{2}, \\\\mathrm{t}_{2 \\\\mathrm{~g}}^{6} \\\\mathrm{e}_{\\\\mathrm{g}}^{0}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{t}}_{{\\\\text{2g}}}^{\\\\text{4}}\\\\,{\\\\text{e}}_{\\\\text{g}}^{\\\\text{2}}{\\\\text{,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{t}}_{{\\\\text{2g}}}^{\\\\text{6}}\\\\,{\\\\text{e}}_{\\\\text{g}}^{\\\\text{3}}{\\\\text{,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{t}}_{{\\\\text{2g}}}^{\\\\text{6}}\\\\,{\\\\text{e}}_{\\\\text{g}}^{\\\\text{0}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\left[\\mathrm{CoF}_{6}\\right]^{3-}, \\mathrm{Co}^{3+}\\left(\\mathrm{d}^{6}\\right) \\mathrm{t}_{2 \\mathrm{~g}}^{4} \\mathrm{e}_{\\mathrm{g}}^{2}$,<br>$\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\right]^{4-}, \\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}\\left(\\mathrm{d}^{6}\\right) \\mathrm{t}_{2 \\mathrm{~g}}^{6} \\mathrm{e}_{\\mathrm{g}}^{0}$,<br>$\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{2+}, \\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}\\left(\\mathrm{d}^{9}\\right) \\mathrm{t}_{2 \\mathrm{~g}}^{6} \\mathrm{e}_{\\mathrm{g}}^{3}$,',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25207,'chemistry',66,1028,2422,'Alkyl bromide is formed as a result of heating the dry silver salt of carboxylic acid with bromine. What will be the order of formation w.r.t alkyl bromide?','[{"text": "$$1^{\\\\circ}>3^{\\\\circ}>2^{\\\\circ}$$ bromides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$1^{\\\\circ}>2^{\\\\circ}>3^{\\\\circ}$$ bromides", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$3^{\\\\circ}>2^{\\\\circ}>1^{\\\\circ}$$ bromides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$3^{\\\\circ}>1^{\\\\circ}>2^{\\\\circ}$$ bromides", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$$\\mathrm{RCOOAg}+\\mathrm{Br}_{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{RBr}+\\mathrm{CO}_{2}+\\mathrm{AgBr}$$<br>The yield of alkyl bromide has the following order: $$1^{\\circ}>2^{\\circ}>3^{\\circ}$$<br>Since the mechanism of this reaction involves formation of free radicals.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25208,'chemistry',64,192,1924,'When orange solution containing $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}^{2-}}$ ion is treated with an alkali, a yellow solution is formed and when $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}^{+}}$ions are added to yellow solution, an orange solution is obtained. Explain why does this happen?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{7}^{2-}}$ changes to $\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{CrO}_{4}^{2-}}$ in basic medium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{CrO}_{4}^{2-}}$ changes to $\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{7}^{2-}}$ in acid medium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are in equillibrium hence addition of acid or base shift the equillibrium, hence the colour change.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{\\underset{\\text { Dichromate(Orange) }}{\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}^{2-}} \\underset{\\mathrm{H}^{+}}{\\stackrel{\\mathrm{OH}^{-}}{\\rightleftharpoons}} \\underset{\\text { Chromate(Yellow) }}{2 \\mathrm{CrO}_{4}^{2-}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25209,'chemistry',63,812,1772,'Which is the correct thermal stability order for${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{E}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{(E = O,}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{S,}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Se,}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{Te}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{\\rm{Po)}}$ ?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{~S} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Se} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Te} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Po}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{~S} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Se} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Te} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Po}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Po} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Te} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Se} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{~S} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Se} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Te} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Po} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O} < \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{~S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'On going down the group thermal stability order for $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{E}$ decreases because H-E bond energy decreases<br>$\\therefore \\quad$ Order of stability would be :<br>$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{Po} < \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{Te} < \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{Se} < \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S} < \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25210,'chemistry',66,1028,2419,'Analyse the following reaction and identify the structure of A and B','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25210_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Formation of $$\\mathrm{A}$$ is an electrophilic addition reaction<br>(i) $$\\mathrm{HBr} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}^{+}+\\mathrm{Br}^{-}$$<br>(ii) <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25210_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> ${\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ + }}}\\,\\, \\to $ <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25210_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25210_explanation_4.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Formation of B is a free radical addition reaction<br>(i) $$\\mathrm{HBr} \\stackrel{\\mathrm{hv}}{\\longrightarrow} \\dot{\\mathrm{H}}+\\dot{\\mathrm{Br}}$$<br>(ii) <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25210_explanation_5.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> (iii) <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25210_explanation_6.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/66_25210_question_1.png'),
