(25239,'chemistry',64,194,1935,'Identify the wrong statement/s considering Lanthanoid contraction as the basis.<br>(i) As the size decreases covalent character increases. Therefore, $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{La}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}}$ is more ionic and $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Lu}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}}$ is more covalent.<br>(ii) As the size decreases from $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{La}}$ to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Lu}}$, stability of oxosalts also decreases.<br>(iii) Stability of complexes increases as the size of lanthanoids decreases.<br>(iv) Radii of ${\\rm{4d}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{\\rm{5d}}$ block elements will be almost same.<br>(v) Acidic character of oxides decreases from La to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Lu}}$.','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{i}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii,iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{v}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii,iv", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Acidic character of oxides increases from $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{La}}$ to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Lu}}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
