(25241,'chemistry',63,826,1829,'The element that does not form acidic oxide is','[{"text": "carbon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "phosphorus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "chlorine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "barium", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The acidic oxides are formed by the nonmetals (group 14-17) whereas basic oxides are formed by the metals of group 1 and group 2 elements. As the atoms get larger, the ionisation energy decreases and the elements also become more basic. $\\mathrm{BeO}$ is an amphoteric oxide, $\\mathrm{MgO}$ is weakly basic while $\\mathrm{BaO}$ is highly basic oxide.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
