(25259,'chemistry',65,959,2237,'Arrange the following complexes in increasing order towards the wavelength of light they absorb? Where $\\mathrm{M}$ is metal ion.<br>${\\left[ {{\\text{M}}\\left( {{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)} \\right]^{{\\text{3 + }}}}{\\text{ = a}},{\\left[ {{\\text{M}}{{({\\text{CN}})}_{\\text{6}}}} \\right]^{{\\text{3 - }}}}{\\text{ = b}},{\\left[ {{\\text{M}}{{\\left( {{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}} \\right)}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right]^{{\\text{3 - }}}}$<br>${\\text{ = c}},{\\left[ {{\\text{M}}{{\\text{F}}_{\\text{6}}}} \\right]^{{\\text{3 - }}}}{\\text{ = d}},$','[{"text": "d, c, a, b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "d, a, c, b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b, a, c, d", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a, b, c, d", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Energy for excitation<br>$(\\Delta ) = \\frac{{{\\text{hc}}}}{{{\\text{ wave length }}}}{\\text{. }}$<br>Therefore lower the wavelength of light higher will be the energy for excitation i.e., crystal field splitting energy.<br>$\\therefore$ Correct order will be $\\mathrm{b} < \\mathrm{a} < \\mathrm{c} < \\mathrm{d}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25260,'chemistry',63,807,1750,'Match the column I with column II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A.Used in manufacture of calcium cyanamie<br>B.used in manufacture in nitric acid<br>C.Used in pickling of stainless steel</div><div class="column-right">P.Ammonia<br>Q.Nitric acid<br>R.Dinitrogen</div></div>','[{"text": "A - R, B - P, C - Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A -P, B - R, C - Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P, B - Q, C - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - P, C - R", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'(A) $\\mathrm{CaC}_{2}+\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{CaCN}_{2}$ [Calcium cyanamide]<br>(B) In the manufacture of $\\mathrm{HNO}_{3}$, first step is involved by $\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$<br>(C) $\\mathrm{HNO}_{3}$ is used in pickling of stainless steel<br>So, the option (1) is correct',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
