(25285,'chemistry',63,808,1755,'Formation of $\\mathrm{PCl}_{3}$ is explained on the basis of what hybridisation of phosphorus atom?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{sp}^{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{sp}^{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\\\mathrm{~d}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}{{\\\\rm{d}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The type of hybridisation in an atom can be determined by using the formula<br>$\\mathrm{H}=\\dfrac{1}{2}[\\mathrm{~V}+\\mathrm{Y}-\\mathrm{C}+\\mathrm{A}]$<br>Here, $V=$ valence shell electrons of the central atom<br>$\\mathrm{Y}=$ number of monovalent atom<br>$\\mathrm{C}=$ total positive charge<br>and $\\mathrm{A}=$ total negative charge<br>In case of $\\mathrm{PCl}_{3}$,<br>$\\mathrm{H}=\\dfrac{1}{2}[5+3]=4$<br>$\\therefore$ Hybridisation of phosphorus atom is $\\mathrm{sp}^{3}$. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/63_25285_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Pyramidal shape (due to presence of one lone pair of electron.)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2018,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25286,'chemistry',64,190,1912,'In the series $\\mathrm{\\operatorname{Sc}(Z=21)}$ to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Zn}(Z=30)}$, the enthalpy of atomisation of zinc is the lowest, i.e., $\\mathrm{126 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}$. Why?','[{"text": "No 3d electrons involve in metallic bond", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is not a transition element", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It has psedo inert gas configuration in +2 state", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is soft metal", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In the formation of metallic bonds, no electrons from $\\mathrm{3 \\mathrm{~d}}$-orbitals are involved in case of zinc, while in all other metals of the $\\mathrm{3 \\mathrm{~d}}$ series, electrons from the d-orbitals are always involved in the formation of metallic bonds.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25287,'chemistry',65,956,2224,'Which of the following square planar complexes will form two geometrical isomers?','[{"text": "${\\\\text{M}}{{\\\\text{A}}_{\\\\text{4}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{M}}{{\\\\text{A}}_{\\\\text{3}}}{\\\\text{B}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{MA}}{{\\\\text{B}}_{\\\\text{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{M}}{{\\\\text{A}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{{\\\\text{B}}_{\\\\text{2}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
