(25289,'chemistry',63,812,1772,'Which among the following compounds does not act as reducing agent?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{~S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Se}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{Te}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All the hydrides, except water $\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)$ of group 16 elements acts as a reducing agents. The reducing character increases from $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}$ to $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{Te}$. This is due to decrease in stability of hydride.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25290,'chemistry',64,191,1922,'I. An alloy is a blend of metals prepared by mixing the components.<br>II. Alloys may be homogeneous solid solutions in which the atoms of one metal are distributed randomly among the atoms of the other.<br>III. Chromium, vandium, tungsten are ferrous alloys.<br>The correct set of statement(s) is/are (choose the appropriate option)','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'An alloy is a blend of metals prepared by mixing the components. These may be homogeneous solid solutions in which the atoms of one metal are distributed randomly among the atoms of the other.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
