(25300,'chemistry',63,814,1784,'Which of the following molecular formula represents Marshall\'s acid?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{~S}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{7}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{~S}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{6}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{~S}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{8}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Peroxodisulphuric acid $\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{8}\\right)$<br>represents Marshall\'s acid. It is a inorganic compound. It contain sulphur in its +6 oxidation state and a peroxide group. It\'s structure is as follows:<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/63_25300_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25301,'chemistry',64,191,1916,'Which of the following statements is not correct?','[{"text": "Copper liberates hydrogen from acids.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In its higher oxidation states, manganese forms stable compounds with oxygen and fluorine.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Mn}^{3+}}$ and $\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Co}^{3+}}$ are oxidising agents in aqueous solution.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Ti}^{2+}}$ and $\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cr}^{2+}}$ are reducing agents in aqueous solution.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Copper does not liberates hydrogen from acids as it is present below hydrogen in electrochemical series.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
