(25347,'chemistry',63,805,1734,'Which among the group- 15 elements does not exists as tetra atomic molecule?','[{"text": "Nitrogen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phosphorus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arsenic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antimony", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Nitrogen due to smaller size, high ionisation energy high electronegativity and the absence of d-orbital does not exist as a tetra atomic molecule.<br>Nitrogen cannot form $\\mathrm{d} \\pi-\\mathrm{p} \\pi$ bond due to absence of d-orbital, so it cannot expand its covalency beyond four as the heavier members of this group can.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25348,'chemistry',64,191,1922,'I. The most of durable metal plating on iron to protect against corrosion is zinc plating.<br>II. German silver is an alloy of copper, $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Zn}}$ and $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Ni}}$.<br>III. Bordeaux used as fungicide is a mixture of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CuSO}_{4}+\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2}}$.<br>IV. Turn bull\'s blue is a compound called ferrous ferricyanide.<br>The incorrect statements are (choose the appropriate option)','[{"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The most durable metal plating on iron to protect against corrosion is zinc plating.<br>German silver is an alloy of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cu}, \\mathrm{Zn}}$ and $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Ni}}$.<br>Bordeaux used as fungicide is a mixture of<br>$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CuSO}_{4}+\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2}}$.<br>Turnbull\'s blue is a compound called ferrous ferricyanide.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25351,'chemistry',63,805,1735,'Which among the following group 15 element forms most stable pentavalent compound?','[{"text": "Phosphorus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Antimony", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bismuth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arsenic", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Phosphorus being the group 15 element which forms most stable pentavalent compound due to the presence of vacant d-orbital to overlap with it.<br>e.g. $\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}$<br>It also favours $\\mathrm{p} \\pi-\\mathrm{d} \\pi$ bonding which has the strongest overlapping between the orbital $1 \\mathrm{~s}$, for a stable bond formation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25352,'chemistry',64,190,1911,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) Chromium has the highest melting point among the ${\\rm{3d}}$ series metals<br>(II) Number of unpaired electrons is greater in Cr than other elements of ${\\rm{3d}}$ series.<br>(III) In any row the melting point of transition metal increases as the atomic number increases.','[{"text": "(I) and (III)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I) and (II)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(II) and (III)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I), (II) and (III)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In any row the melting points of transition metals rise to a maximum at $\\mathrm{d^{5}}$ except for anomalous values of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Mn}}$ and Te and falls regularly as the atomic number increases.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25354,'chemistry',66,1027,2418,'The $$\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{Cl}$$ bond in Ethyl chloride is formed by the overlapping of','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{ - s}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{ - p}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{d - p}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{ - p}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{Cl}$$<br>$$\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{Cl}$$ bond is formed by the overlapping of ${\\rm{s}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{ - p}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25355,'chemistry',63,805,1735,'In which oxidation state, group 15 elements act as Lewis base?','[{"text": "+5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "+4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "-3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ + 3}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Group 15 elements acts as Lewis base in -3 oxidation state due to avilability of lone pair of electrons on the central atom. This basic character of group 15 decreases down the group with an increase in the size of the central atom.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2019,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25356,'chemistry',64,192,1925,'${\\text{KMn}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{R}}{\\text{.A}}{\\text{.}}}]{{{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ + }}}}}{{\\text{M}}^{{\\text{x + }}}}$<br>${\\text{KMn}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{R}}{\\text{.A}}}]{{{\\text{0}}{{\\text{H}}^{{\\text{ - 1}}}}}}{\\text{M}}{{\\text{n}}^{{\\text{y + }}}}$<br>${{\\text{K}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{r}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{7}}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{O}}{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ - }}}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{r}}^{{\\text{z + }}}}$ $\\left( {{\\text{x + y + z}}} \\right)$ value is:<br>(here $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{x}, \\mathrm{y}}$ and $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{z}}$ are oxidation states)','[{"text": "20", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "15", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "30", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4} \\underset{R . A .}{\\stackrel{H^{+}}{\\longrightarrow}} M^{+2}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4} \\underset{\\text { R.A. }}{\\stackrel{O H^{-}}{\\longrightarrow}} \\mathrm{Mn}^{+4}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7} \\stackrel{\\mathrm{OH}^{-}}{\\longrightarrow} \\mathrm{Cr}^{+6}}$<br>$\\mathrm{x+y+z=12}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25358,'chemistry',66,1026,2417,'Number of isomers possible (including stereoisomers) with molecular formula $$\\mathrm{C}_{3} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{Cl}_{3}$$ is','[{"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25358_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25358_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25358_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25358_explanation_4.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25358_explanation_5.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25358_explanation_6.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
