(25370,'chemistry',65,962,2242,'In quantitative analysis of second group in laboratory, $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}$ gas is passed in acidic medium for precipitation. When $\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}$ and $\\mathrm{Cd}^{2+}$ react with $\\mathrm{KCN}$, then for product true statement is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}_{2}\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Cu}(\\\\mathrm{CN})_{4}\\\\right]$ more soluble", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}_{2}\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Cd}(\\\\mathrm{CN})_{4}\\\\right]$ less stable", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}_{2}\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Cd}(\\\\mathrm{CN})_{3}\\\\right]$ more stable", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}_{3}\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Cu}(\\\\mathrm{CN})_{4}\\\\right]$ less stable", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In $K_{3}\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}(\\mathrm{CN})_{4}\\right]$ copper is in +1 oxidation state while in $\\mathrm{K}_{2}\\left[\\mathrm{Cd}(\\mathrm{CN})_{2}\\right]$ cadmium is in +2 oxidation state. The more the oxidation state of the central metal atom, the more is the stability of the complex.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
