(25372,'chemistry',64,191,1913,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) As a result of lanthanoid contraction members of ${\\rm{4d}}\\,\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{\\rm{5d}}$ series exhibit similar radii.<br>(II) $\\mathrm{I E_{2}}$ is high for $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cr}}$ and $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cu}}$ whereas $\\mathrm{I E_{3}}$ is very high for $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Zn}}$.<br>(III) Heavier members of d-block elements like p-block elements favours lower oxidation states.<br>(IV) In any transition series maximum number of oxidation states is shown by middle elements or elements near middle elements.','[{"text": "(I) and (II)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I), (II) and (IV)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(I), (II) and (III)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(II) and (IV)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Heavier members of d-block elements unlike p-block elements shows higher oxidation states. For example, W(VI) is more stable than $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cr}(\\mathrm{VI})}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
