(25376,'chemistry',64,194,1937,'Consider the following statements<br>(I) $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{La}(\\mathrm{OH})_{3}}$ is the least basic among hydroxides of lanthanides.<br>(II) $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Zr}^{4+}}$ and $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Hf}^{4+}}$ possess almost the same ionic radii.<br>(III) $\\mathrm{C e^{4+}}$ can act as an oxidizing agent.<br>Which of the above is/are true?','[{"text": "(I) and (III)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(II) and (III)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(II) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I) and (II)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'As a result of lanthanoid contraction $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Zr}^{4+}}$ and $\\mathrm{H f^{4+}}$ possess almost the same ionic radii. $\\mathrm{C e^{4+}}$ is an oxidising agent. $\\mathrm{C e^{4+}}$ gains electron to acquire more stable $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Ce}^{3+}}$ state. $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{La}(\\mathrm{OH})_{3}}$ is the most basic among lanthanide hydroxides.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
