(25405,'chemistry',65,955,2222,'Which of the following pairs of name and formula of complexes is not correct?','[{"text": "Tetraamminecopper (II) sulphate$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Cu}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{4}\\\\right] \\\\mathrm{SO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diamminesilverv (I) chloride$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Ag}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2}\\\\right] \\\\mathrm{Cl}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Potassium hexacyanidoferrate (III) $\\\\mathrm{K}_{4}\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Fe}(\\\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\\\right]$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Potassium amminepentachloridoplatinate (IV)- $\\\\mathrm{K}\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Pt}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right) \\\\mathrm{Cl}_{5}\\\\right]$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct formula of Potassium hexacyanido ferrate (III) is ${{\\text{K}}_{\\text{3}}}\\left[ {{\\text{Fe(CN}}{{\\text{)}}_{\\text{6}}}} \\right]$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25406,'chemistry',63,814,1786,'Which of the following oxyacids of sulphur contain four $\\mathrm{S}=\\mathrm{O}$ bonds?','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{S}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{SO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{~S}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{~S}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{6}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{6}$ oxyacids of sulphur contain four $\\mathrm{S}$ $=\\mathrm{O}$ bonds. It is shown as bellow:<br>Dithionic acid $\\left( {{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{S}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{6}}}} \\right)$ <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/63_25406_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25408,'chemistry',66,1028,2419,'The reaction of $$\\mathrm{SOCl}_{2}$$ on alkanols to form alkyl chlorides gives good yield because','[{"text": "Alkyl chlorides are immiscible with $$\\\\mathrm{SOCl}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The other products of the reaction are gaseous and escape out", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alcohol and $$\\\\mathrm{SOCl}_{2}$$ are soluble in water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The reaction occurs via intermediate formation of an alkyl chloro sulphite.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The reaction of $$\\mathrm{SOCl}_{2}$$ in alcohols to form alkyl chlorides gives good yield because the other products of the reaction are gaseous and escape out $$\\left(\\mathrm{HCl}, \\mathrm{SO}_{2}\\right)$$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25409,'chemistry',65,957,2227,'$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{3+}$ is an inner orbital complex whereas $\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{2+}$ is an outer orbital complex because','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Co}^{3+}$ has $\\\\mathrm{d}^{6}$ whereas $\\\\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}$ has $\\\\mathrm{d}^{8}$ hence pairing is not possible in $\\\\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ammonia behaves differently with both the metals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The approach of ligands to central metal ion is different.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No scientific reason", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the presence of $\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$, the $3 \\mathrm{~d}$ electrons pair up leaving two d-orbitals empty to be involved in $\\mathrm{d}^{2} \\mathrm{sp}^{3}$ hybridisation forming inner orbital complex in case of $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{3+}$.<br>In $\\mathrm{Ni}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}{ }_{6}+$, $\\mathrm{Ni}$ is in +2 oxidation state and has $\\mathrm{d}^{8}$ configuration, the hybridisation involved is $\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\mathrm{~d}^{2}$ forming outer orbital complex.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25410,'chemistry',63,814,1786,'Which oxoacid of sulphur contains ${\\rm{S - S}}$ bond in its structure?','[{"text": "Disulphurous acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Disulphuric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Perdisulphuric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sulphurous acid", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Disulphurous acid contains one S-S bond in its structure. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/63_25410_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/63_25410_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/63_25410_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/63_25410_explanation_4.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25412,'chemistry',66,1028,2422,'In Hunsdiecker reaction','[{"text": "A sodium salt of an acid reacts with bromine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A calcium salt of an acid reacts with $$\\\\mathrm{HBr}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A silver salt of an acid reacts with bromine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A silver salt of an acid reacts with $$\\\\mathrm{HBr}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In Hunsdiecker reaction, a silver salt of an acid reacts with bromine in the presence of $$\\mathrm{CCl}_{4}$$.<br>It is an important method of preparing an alkyl halide from a silver salt of an alkanoic acid.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25413,'chemistry',65,957,2229,'Among the following complexes ( $\\mathrm{K}$ to $\\mathrm{P}$ ), $\\mathrm{K}_{3}\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\right](\\mathrm{K}),\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}_{3}(\\mathrm{~L})$, $\\mathrm{Na}_{3}\\left[\\mathrm{Co}(\\text { oxalate })_{3}\\right](\\mathrm{M}),\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{6}\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}(\\mathrm{~N})$, $\\mathrm{K}_{2}\\left[\\mathrm{Pt}(\\mathrm{CN})_{4}\\right](\\mathrm{O})$, and $\\left[\\mathrm{Zn}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{6}\\right]\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_{3}\\right)_{2}(\\mathrm{P})$, the diamagnetic complexes are:','[{"text": "K, L, M, N", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "K, M, O, P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "L, M, O, P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "L, M, N, O", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$[\\mathrm{K}]: {{\\text{K}}_{\\text{3}}}\\left[ {{\\text{Fe(CN}}{{\\text{)}}_{\\text{6}}}} \\right] : \\mathrm{Fe}^{3+}$ has ${\\text{3}}{{\\text{d}}^{\\text{5}}}$ configuration; $\\mathrm{CN}^{-}$is strong field ligand and thus four electrons are paired leaving one unpaired electron with ${{\\text{d}}^{\\text{2}}}{\\text{s}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{3}}}$  hybridisation and thus paramagnetic.<br>[L]: $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}_{3}: \\mathrm{Co}^{3+}$ has configuration; $\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ is strong field ligand thus all six electrons are paired with ${{\\text{d}}^{\\text{2}}}{\\text{s}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{3}}}$ hybridisation and therefore diamagnetic.<br>$[\\mathrm{M}]: \\mathrm{Na}_{3}\\left[\\mathrm{Co}(\\mathrm{ox})_{3}\\right]: \\mathrm{Co}^{3+}$ configuration; $\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{4}^{2-}$ is strong field ligand and thus all the six electrons are paired with ${{\\text{d}}^{\\text{2}}}{\\text{s}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{3}}}$  hybridisation and therefore diamagnetic.<br>[N]: $\\quad\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{6}\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}: \\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}$ has ${\\text{3}}{{\\text{d}}^{\\text{8}}}$  configuration with two unpaired electrons. $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$ is weak field ligand and thus ${\\text{s}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{3}}}{{\\text{d}}^{\\text{2}}}$ hybridisation and paramagnetic.<br>[O]: ${{\\text{K}}_{\\text{2}}}\\left[ {{\\text{Pt(CN}}{{\\text{)}}_{\\text{4}}}} \\right]$. ${\\text{;}}{{\\text{P}}^{{\\text{2 + }}}}$  has ${\\text{3}}{{\\text{d}}^{\\text{8}}}$  Configuration. ${\\text{C}}{{\\text{N}}^{\\text{ - }}}$ is strong ligand and thus all the eight electrons are paired with ${\\text{ds}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{3}}}$  hybridiastion and therefore diamagnetic .<br>${\\text{[P]:}}\\left[ {{\\text{Zn}}{{\\left( {{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}} \\right)}_{\\text{6}}}{{\\left( {{\\text{N}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{:Z}}{{\\text{n}}^{{\\text{2 + }}}}} \\right.$ has ${\\text{3}}{{\\text{d}}^{{\\text{10}}}}$ Configuration and thus all paired showing ${\\text{s}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{3}}}{{\\text{d}}^{\\text{2}}}$ hubridisation and so diamagnetic.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
