(25476,'chemistry',65,959,2237,'The octahedral complex of a metal ion ${{\\text{M}}^{{\\text{3 + }}}}$ with four monodentate ligands ${{\\text{L}}_{\\text{1}}}{\\text{,}}{{\\text{L}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{,}}{{\\text{L}}_{\\text{3}}}$ and ${{\\text{L}}_{\\text{4}}}$ absorbs wavelengths in the region of red, green, yellow and blue respectively. The increasing order of ligand strength of the four ligands is:','[{"text": "${{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{3}}}{\\\\text{ < }}{{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{ < }}{{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{4}}}{\\\\text{ < }}{{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{1}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{4}}}{\\\\text{ < }}{{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{3}}}{\\\\text{ < }}{{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{ < }}{{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{1}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{1}}}{\\\\text{ < }}{{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{3}}}{\\\\text{ < }}{{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{ < }}{{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{4}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{1}}}{\\\\text{ < }}{{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{ < }}{{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{4}}}{\\\\text{ < }}{{\\\\text{L}}_{\\\\text{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/65_25476_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Coloured regions of visible light (VIBGYOR) are arranged in the increasing order of wavelength or decreasing order of energy $[E \\propto 1 / \\lambda]$. Therefore,<br>$\\begin{gathered}\n  {{\\text{E}}_{{\\text{Red }}}}{\\text{ < }}{{\\text{E}}_{{\\text{yellow }}}}{\\text{ < }}{{\\text{E}}_{{\\text{green }}}}{\\text{ < }}{{\\text{E}}_{{\\text{blue }}}} \\hfill \\\\\n  \\left( {{{\\text{L}}_{\\text{1}}}} \\right)\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\left( {{{\\text{L}}_{\\text{2}}}} \\right)\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\left( {{{\\text{L}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)\\quad \\,\\left( {{{\\text{L}}_{\\text{4}}}} \\right) \\hfill \\\\ \n\\end{gathered} $<br>This suggests that $L_{4}$ will absorbs higher energy wavelength followed by ${{\\text{L}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{,}}{{\\text{L}}_{\\text{3}}}\\,{\\text{and}}\\,\\,{{\\text{L}}_{\\text{1}}}$. Since, higher absorbed energy corresponds to greater extent of crystal field splitting and, thus, higher field strength to the ligand.<br>Hence, the increasing order of ligand strength of the four ligands is<br>${{\\text{L}}_{\\text{1}}}{\\text{ < }}{{\\text{L}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{ < }}{{\\text{L}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ < }}{{\\text{L}}_{\\text{4}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
