(25555,'chemistry',63,816,1794,'Correct order of bond dissociation energy is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Br}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{F}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{I}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{F}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{F}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{I}_{2}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In general, bond enthalpy or bond dissociation energy of halogen molecules $\\left(\\mathrm{X}_{2}\\right)$ decreases down the group from $\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ to $\\mathrm{I}_{2}$.<br>$\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}>\\mathrm{Br}_{2}>\\mathrm{F}_{2}>\\mathrm{I}_{2}$<br>$\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ is an exception due to lone pair-lone pair electronic repulsions.<br>',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2019,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
