(25563,'chemistry',63,818,1806,'$\\underset{\\text { (Excess) }}{8 \\mathrm{NH}_{3}}+3 \\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{X}$<br>$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}+\\underset{\\text { (Excess) }}{3 \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Y}$<br>What are $\\mathrm{X}$ and $\\mathrm{Y}$ in the above reactions?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{X}=6 \\\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\\\mathrm{Cl}+\\\\mathrm{N}_{2} ; \\\\mathrm{Y}=\\\\mathrm{NCl}_{3}+3 \\\\mathrm{HCl}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{X}=\\\\mathrm{NCl}_{3}+3 \\\\mathrm{HCl} ; \\\\mathrm{Y}=6 \\\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\\\mathrm{Cl}+\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{X}=\\\\mathrm{NCl}_{3}+\\\\mathrm{N}_{2} ; \\\\mathrm{Y}=6 \\\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\\\mathrm{Cl}+3 \\\\mathrm{HCl}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{X}=6 \\\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\\\mathrm{Cl}+3 \\\\mathrm{HCl} ; \\\\mathrm{Y}=\\\\mathrm{NCl}_{3}+\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}$<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\underset{\\text { (Excess) }}{8 \\mathrm{NH}_{3}}+3 \\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\rightarrow 6 \\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}+\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\uparrow$<br>$\\mathrm{NH}_{3}+\\underset{(\\text { Excess) }}{3 \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{NCl}_{3}+3 \\mathrm{HCl}$<br>',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25564,'chemistry',66,1032,2440,'The order of reactivity of the following alcohols towards concentrated hydrochloric acid is.','[{"text": "IV $$>$$ III $$>$$ II $$>$$ I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I $$>$$ II $$>$$ III $$>$$ IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III $$>$$ II $$>$$ I $$>$$ IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV $$>$$ II $$>$$ I $$>$$ III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The order of reactivity depends upon the stability of the carbocation formed from the alcohols. The greater the stability, higher the reactivity of alcohol. The increasing order of stability of carbocations formed from the alcohols is<br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25564_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>Hence order of reactivity is IV $$>$$ III $$>$$ II $$>$$ I. Therefore option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/66_25564_question_1.jpg'),
(25565,'chemistry',65,962,2242,'Which one of the following statement is correct?','[{"text": "From a mixed precipitate of $\\\\mathrm{AgCl}$ and $\\\\mathrm{AgI}$, ammonia solution dissolves only $\\\\mathrm{AgCl}$.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Manganese salt give a violet borax test in reducing flame.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "On boiling a solution having $\\\\mathrm{K}^{+}, \\\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ and $\\\\mathrm{HCO}_{3}^{-}$ions, we get a precipitate of $\\\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Ca}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CO}_{3}\\\\right)_{2}$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ferric ions give a deep green precipitate on adding potassium ferrocyanide solution.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{AgCl}+2 \\mathrm{NH}_{3} \\longrightarrow\\left[\\mathrm{Ag}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{2}\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}$ Soluble complex',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
