(25607,'chemistry',65,954,2214,'A chelating agent has two or more than two donor atoms to bind to a single metal ion. Which of the following is not a chelating agent?','[{"text": "Thio sulphate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oxalato", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycinato", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethane-1,2-diamine", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25608,'chemistry',63,813,1777,'Identify amphoteric oxide from the following','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{SO}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Al}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{SO}_{3}-$ Acidic, $\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{O}-$ Basic<br>$\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$ - Neutral, $\\mathrm{Al}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}-$ Amphoteric',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25609,'chemistry',64,191,1917,'The spin only magnetic moment of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Mn}^{4+}}$ ion is approximately','[{"text": "3 B.M.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6 B.M.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4 B.M.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "5 B.M.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{M n^{4+} \\rightarrow 1 s^{2} 2 s^{2} 2 p^{6} 3 s^{2} 3 p^{6} 3 d^{3}}$<br>Magnetic moment $\\mathrm{=\\sqrt{n(n+2)}}$ B.M.<br>Number of unpaired electrons, $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{n}=3}$ Magnetic moment $\\mathrm{=}$<br>$\\rm{\\sqrt{3(3+2)}=\\sqrt{3(5)}=\\sqrt{15}=3.89=4 \\text { B.M }}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2010,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25610,'chemistry',66,1031,2433,'Which one of the following compounds undergoes predominantly ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}{\\rm{2}}$ reaction with aqueous $$\\mathrm{NaOH}$$ in a polar aprotic solvent?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In primary halide<br>${\\rm{Rate}}\\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}^{\\rm{2}}\\, \\propto {\\rm{EWG}}\\, \\propto \\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{ERG}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ - OC}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{(ERG), - N}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{(EWG), - N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{(ERG)}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25613,'chemistry',64,191,1917,'The spin only magnetic moment of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}}$ ion (in B.M.) is approximately','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}}$ ion electronic configuration is $\\mathrm{4 s^{0} 3 d^{6}}$ and has 4 unpaired electrons, so magnetic moment is<br>${\\rm{\\mu  = }}\\sqrt {{\\rm{n(n + 2)}}} {\\rm{B}}{\\rm{.M}}{\\rm{. = }}\\sqrt {{\\rm{4(4 + 2)}}} {\\rm{ = }}\\sqrt {{\\rm{24}}} $<br>${\\rm{ = 4}}{\\rm{.898 B}}{\\rm{.M}}{\\rm{. }} \\approx {\\rm{5 B}}{\\rm{.M}}{\\rm{.}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\therefore}$ The magnetic moment of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}}$ ion is approximately equal to 5 .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2011,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25614,'chemistry',66,1031,2432,'Consider the following bromides :<br>The correct order of ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}{\\rm{1}}$ reactivity is','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{B}>\\\\mathrm{C}>\\\\mathrm{A}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B $$>$$ A $$>$$ C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C $$>$$ B $$>$$ A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A $$>$$ B $$>$$ C", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25614_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Since ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}^{\\rm{1}}$ reactions involve the formation of carbocation as intermediate in the rate determining step, more is the stability of carbocation higher will be the reactivity of alkyl halides towards ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}^{\\rm{1}}$ route. Now we know that stability of carbocations follows the order:<br>$$3^{\\circ}>$$ $$2^{\\circ}>1^{\\circ}$$, so ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}^{\\rm{1}}$ reactivity should also follow the same order.<br>$$3^{\\circ}>2^{\\circ}>1^{\\circ}>\\operatorname{Methyl}\\left(S_{N}{ }^{1}\\right.$$ reactivity)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/66_25614_question_1.jpg'),
(25615,'chemistry',63,820,1814,'Which among the following compounds in NOT a colourless gas?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CIF}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{IF}_{7}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{IF}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CIF}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{IF}_{3}$ - Yellow powder, remaining are colourless gases.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25616,'chemistry',65,955,2222,'According to IUPAC nomenclature sodium nitroprusside is named as','[{"text": "Sodium pentacyanonitrosyl ferrate (II)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sodium nitroferrocyanide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sodium nitroferricyanide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sodium pentacyanonitrosyl ferrate (III)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Sodium pentacyanonitrosyl ferrate (II), $\\mathrm{Na}_{2}\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_{5} \\mathrm{NO}\\right]$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25617,'chemistry',64,191,1917,'In a transition series, with the increase in atomic number, the paramagnetism','[{"text": "increases gradually", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "decreases gradually", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "first increases to a maximum and then decreases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "first decreases to a minimum and then increases.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In transition series, paramagnetism first increases due to increase in the number of unpaired electrons. Beyond manganese, number of unpaired electrons decreases. So, paramagnetism decreases.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25618,'chemistry',66,1031,2433,'The organic chloro compound, which shows complete stereochemical inversion during a ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}{\\rm{2}}$ reaction, is','[{"text": "$$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{CHCl}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{3} \\\\mathrm{CCl}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{CHCl}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{Cl}$$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}^2$ reaction is favoured by small groups on the carbon atom attached to halogen.<br>${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}^2$ reaction is shown to maximum extent by primary halides. The only primary halides given is $$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{Cl}$$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25619,'chemistry',63,824,1826,'Identify use of argon from the following','[{"text": "In supersonic wind tunnels", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "For magnetic resonance imaging", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "For producing inert atmosphere in welding", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "For production of lasers", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Argon is used to produce inert atmosphere in welding.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25620,'chemistry',64,191,1917,'Identify the set of paramagnetic ions among the following:','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}, \\\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}, \\\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Ti}^{3+}, \\\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}, \\\\mathrm{Mn}^{3+}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Sc}^{3+}, T i^{3+}, V^{3+}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{V}^{2+}, \\\\mathrm{Co}^{2+}, \\\\mathrm{Ti}^{4+}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{{ }_{22} T i \\Rightarrow[A r] 3 d^{2} 4 s^{2}}$<br>$\\mathrm{T i^{3+} \\Rightarrow[A r] 3 d^{1} 4 s^{0} \\Rightarrow}$ paramagnetic due to one unpaired electron.<br>$\\mathrm{{ }_{29} C u \\Rightarrow[A r] 3 d^{10} 4 s^{1}}$<br>$\\mathrm{C u^{2+} \\Rightarrow[A r] 3 d^{9} 4 s^{0}}$<br>Paramagnetic due to one unpaired electron.<br>$\\mathrm{{ }_{25} M n \\Rightarrow[A r] 3 d^{5} 4 s^{2}}$<br>$\\mathrm{M n^{3+} \\Rightarrow[A r] 3 d^{4} 4 s^{0}}$<br>Paramagnetic due to four unpaired electrons.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25621,'chemistry',65,955,2222,'The correct IUPAC name of the complex:','[{"text": "Dichlorodimethylglyoximatocobalt (II)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bis (dimethylglyoxime) dichlorocobalt (II)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dimethylglyoximecobalt (II) chloride", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dichlorodimethylglyoxime-N,N-cobalt(II)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/65_25621_question_1.png'),
(25630,'chemistry',66,1031,2432,'The order of decreasing ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}{\\rm{1}}$ reactivity of following compounds is','[{"text": "I $$>$$ II $$>$$ III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I $$>$$ III $$>$$ II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II $$>$$ III $$>$$ I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III $$>$$ I $$>$$ II", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Rate of ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}^1$ reaction $$\\propto$$ stability of carbocation<br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25630_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>Aromatic<br>(I)<br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25630_explanation_2.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>Anti Aromatic<br>(II)<br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25630_explanation_3.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>Non Aromatic<br>(III)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/66_25630_question_1.jpg'),
(25631,'chemistry',63,817,1799,'Which element from the following combines with hydrogen to form compound having lowest acidic strength?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Cl}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Br}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "F", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Acidic strength of halogen acids increases in the order :<br>$\\mathrm{HF} < \\mathrm{HCl} < \\mathrm{HBr} < \\mathrm{HI}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25622,'chemistry',66,1031,2435,'Consider the reactions:<br>(i) ${\\left( {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{CH - C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{Br}}\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}}{\\text{OH}}}}$<br>$$(\\mathrm{CH})_{2} \\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{OC}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5}+\\mathrm{HBr}$$<br>(ii) ${\\left( {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{CH - C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{Br}}\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}}{{\\text{O}}^{\\text{ - }}}}}$<br>$$\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{OC}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5}+\\mathrm{Br}^{-}$$<br>The mechanisms of reactions (i) and (ii) are respectively:','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{N}}}{\\\\rm{1}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{N}}}{\\\\rm{2}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{N}}}{\\\\rm{1}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{N}}}{\\\\rm{1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{N}}}{\\\\rm{1}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{N}}}{\\\\rm{1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{N}}}2\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{N}}}{\\\\rm{1}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A strong nucleophile favours the ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}^2$ reaction and a weak nucleophile favours the ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}^1$ reaction. First reaction is ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}^1$ reaction because $$\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{OH}$$ is used as solvent which is a weak nucleophile.<br>Second reaction is ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}^2$ reaction because $$\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{O}^{-}$$is strong nucleophile.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25623,'chemistry',63,815,1790,'Which from the following statements is true for group 16 elements?','[{"text": "All elements of this group form $\\\\mathrm{EO}_{2}$ type oxides.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It includes all the nonmetals.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxides of all elements of this group are gaseous at room temperature.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reducing properties of dioxides of this group element decreases from $\\\\mathrm{SO}_{2}$ to $\\\\mathrm{TeO}_{2}$.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'From $\\mathrm{SO}_{2}$ to $\\mathrm{TeO}_{2}$, reducing properties decrease.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25624,'chemistry',64,191,1917,'Magnetic moment of ${\\rm{2}}{\\rm{.83}}\\,\\,{\\rm{BM}}$ is shown by which of the following ions?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Cr}^{3+}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Mn}^{2+}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{T i^{3+}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{N i^{2+}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${{\\rm{(2}}{\\rm{.83)}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = n(n + 2)}}$<br>${\\rm{8 = n(n + 2)}}$<br>${\\rm{n = 2}}$<br>Thus, it is given by  ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{i}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}$ ion ${\\rm{(3}}{{\\rm{d}}^{\\rm{8}}}{\\rm{)}}$ <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/64_25624_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25625,'chemistry',65,955,2222,'Correct formula of tetraamminechloronitroplatinum(IV) sulphate can be written as','[{"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Pt}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{4}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NO}_{2}\\\\right) \\\\mathrm{Cl}\\\\right] \\\\mathrm{SO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left.\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Pt}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{4}\\\\right](\\\\mathrm{ONO}) \\\\mathrm{Cl}\\\\right] \\\\mathrm{SO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Pt}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{4} \\\\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\\\mathrm{NO}_{2}\\\\right]_{2} \\\\mathrm{SO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{PtCl}(\\\\mathrm{ONO}) \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{SO}_{4}\\\\right)\\\\right]$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'As per IUPAC rule.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25626,'chemistry',66,1031,2435,'Which of the following statements is correct?','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{N}}}{\\\\rm{2}}$ reactions of optically active halides are accompained by inversion of configuration.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{N}}}{\\\\rm{1}}$ reactions of optically active halides are accompained by racemisation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbocation formed in ${{\\\\rm{S}}_{\\\\rm{N}}}{\\\\rm{1}}$ reaction is ${\\\\rm{s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}$ hybridized.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In case of optically active alkyl halides, the product formed as a result of ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}^1$ mechanism has the inverted configuration as compared to the reactant. This is because the nucleophile attaches itself on the side opposite to the one where the halogen atom is present.<br>In case of optically active alkyl halides, ${{\\rm{S}}_{\\rm{N}}}^1$ reactions are accompanied by racemisation. The carbocation formed in the slow step being ${\\rm{s}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{2}}}$ hybridised is planar (achiral).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
