(25629,'chemistry',65,955,2222,'Which among the following will be named as dibromidobis-(ethylenediamine) chromium (III) bromide?','[{"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Cr}(\\\\text { en })_{3}\\\\right] \\\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Cr}(\\\\mathrm{en})_{2} \\\\mathrm{Br}_{2}\\\\right] \\\\mathrm{Br}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Cr}(\\\\mathrm{en}) \\\\mathrm{Br}_{4}\\\\right]^{-}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[ {{\\\\rm{Cr(}}} \\\\right.{\\\\rm{en}}\\\\left. {{\\\\rm{)B}}{{\\\\rm{r}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}} \\\\right]{\\\\rm{Br}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Two $\\mathrm{Br}$, two (en) and one $\\mathrm{Cr}$ are parts of complex.<br>Charge on the complex is<br>$\\left. \\begin{gathered}\n  {\\text{2(Br)   =     - 2}} \\hfill \\\\\n  {\\text{2(en)}}\\,\\,\\,{\\text{ = }}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{0}} \\hfill \\\\\n  {\\text{1(cr)}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{ = }}\\,\\,\\,{\\text{ + 3}} \\hfill \\\\ \n\\end{gathered}  \\right\\}{\\text{ =  + 1}}$<br>Thus, complex ion is $\\left[\\mathrm{Cr}(\\mathrm{en})_{2} \\mathrm{Br}_{2}\\right]^{+}$.<br>Since anion is bromide thus, complex is<br>$$\\left[\\mathrm{Cr}(\\mathrm{en})_{2} \\mathrm{Br}_{2}\\right] \\mathrm{Br}$$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
