(25640,'chemistry',64,191,1918,'Identify the metal that forms colourless compounds.','[{"text": "Iron $\\\\mathrm{(Z=26)}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Chromium}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{(Z = 24)}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vanadium $\\\\mathrm{(Z=23)}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Scandium $\\\\mathrm{(Z=21)}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'d-block elements show +3 as the most common oxidation state. For scandium $\\mathrm{(Z=21)}$, electronic configuration is $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{d}^{1}, \\mathrm{~s}^{2}}$. After the removal of +3 electrons $\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{Sc}^{3+}\\right)}$, it acquires a stable configuration $\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{d}^{0}\\right)}$. Hence, it forms colourless compounds.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2016,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
