(25660,'chemistry',64,192,1925,'The formula mass of Mohr\'s salt is 392. The iron present in it is oxidised by $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4}}$ in acid medium. The equivalent mass of Mohr\'s salt is','[{"text": "392", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "31.6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "278", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "156", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mohr\'s salt is $\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{4}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4} \\cdot \\mathrm{FeSO}_{4} \\cdot 6 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}}$. Oxidation of ferrous salt is as follows,<br>$\\mathrm{5 \\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}+\\mathrm{MnO}_{4}^{-}+8 \\mathrm{H}^{+} \\rightarrow 5 \\mathrm{Fe}^{3+}+\\mathrm{Mn}^{2+}+4 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}}$<br>Total change in oxidation number of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Fe}=(+3)}$ $\\mathrm{-(+2)=+1}$<br>Equivalent weight of Mohr\'s salt<br>$\\rm{=\\dfrac{\\text { Molecular wt of Mohr\'s salt }}{1}=\\dfrac{392}{1}=392}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25652,'chemistry',64,192,1924,'How is sodium chromate converted into sodium dichromate in the manufacture of potassium dichromate form chromite ore?','[{"text": "By the action of concentrated sulphuric acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "By roasting with soda ash", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "By the action of sodium hydroxide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "By the action of limestone", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'By the action of concentrated sulphuric acid, sodium chromate gets converted into sodium dichromate in the manufacture of potassium dichromate.<br>Various steps involved are:<br>Step I concentration of the chromite ore by Wilfley method.<br>Step II Conversion of the concentrated chromite ore into $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{CrO}_{4}}$. Concentrated chromite ore is fused with molten $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{CO}_{3}}$ in the presence of air when $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{CrO}_{4}}$ and $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Fe}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}}$ are formed.<br>Step III Conversion of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{CrO}_{4}}$ into $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}}$. Aqueous solution of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{CrO}_{4}}$ is acidified to obtain $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}}$.<br>${\\text{N}}{{\\text{a}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{Cr}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}{\\text{ + }}\\mathop {{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}}\\limits_{\\left( {{\\text{Dil}}{\\text{.}}} \\right)} \\xrightarrow{{}}{\\text{N}}{{\\text{a}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{r}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{7}}}{\\text{ + }}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
