(25774,'chemistry',64,192,1925,'When a mixture of manganese dioxide, potassium hydroxide and potassium chlorate is fused, the product obtained is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\\\mathrm{SO}_{4}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\\\mathrm{MnO}_{3}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\\\mathrm{MnO}_{4}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When a mixture of maganese dioxide, potassium hydroxide and potassium chlorate is fused then potassium chlorate first decomposes to give potassium chloride and oxygen gas. The formed $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{O}_{2}}$ gas then reacts with $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{MnO}_{2}}$ and $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{KOH}}$ to give $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{MnO}_{4}}$. The equations for the above reaction can be written as :<br>${\\rm{2KCl}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}(\\,{\\rm{s}})\\frac{\\Delta }{{{\\rm{Mn}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{2KCl}}({\\rm{s}}){\\rm{ + 3}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}(\\,{\\rm{g}})$<br>${\\rm{2Mn}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ + 4KOH + }}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}} \\to {\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{Mn}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ + 2}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
