(25790,'chemistry',64,192,1924,'The incorrect statement with respect to chromyl chloride test is','[{"text": "formation of lead chromate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "formation of chromyl chloride", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "liberation of chlorine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "formation of red vapours.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Chromyl chloride test is used to confirm the presence of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}}$in qualitative inorganic analysis. When a small amount of the substance (salt) is heated with conc. $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4}}$ in presence of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}}$, deep red vapours of chromyl chloride are evolved.<br>$\\rm{\\begin{gathered}\\mathrm{NaCl}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{NaHSO}_{4}+\\mathrm{HCl} \\\\\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}+2 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{KHSO}_{4}+2 \\mathrm{CrO}_{3}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\\\\\mathrm{CrO}_{3}+2 \\mathrm{HCl} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{CrO}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\end{gathered}}$<br>Chromyl chloride<br>These vapours are passed through $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NaOH}}$ solution and yellow coloured solution of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{CrO}_{4}}$ is abtained.<br>$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CrO}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}+4 \\mathrm{NaOH} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{CrO}_{4}+2 \\mathrm{NaCl}+2 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}}$<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\left( {{\\rm{Yellow}}\\,\\,{\\rm{colour}}} \\right)$<br>This yellow solution is neutralised with acetic acid and on addition of lead acetat gives a yellow ppt. of lead chromate. <br>${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{Cr}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ + Pb}}{\\left( {{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{COO}}} \\right)_{\\rm{2}}} \\to $<br>${\\rm{PbCr}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ + 2C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{COONa}}$<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{Yellow ppt}}{\\rm{.}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
