(25794,'chemistry',64,192,1925,'Aqueous solution of a salt (A) forms a dense white precipitate with $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{BaCl}_{2}}$ solution. The precipitate dissolves in dilute $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{HCl}}$ to produce a gas (B) which decolourises acidified $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4}}$ solution. A and $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{B}}$ respectively are','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{BaS}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}{\\\\rm{,}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{BaS}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{,}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{BaS}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{4}}}{\\\\rm{,S}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{BaS}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{,S}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<br>$\\rm{\\begin{gathered}\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{3(a q)}+\\mathrm{BaCl}_{2(a q)} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{BaSO}_{3} \\underset{\\text { (White ppt) }}{\\downarrow}+2 \\mathrm{NaCl}_{(a q)} \\\\\\mathrm{BaSO}_{3(s)}+2 \\mathrm{HCl}_{(\\text {dil. })} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{BaCl}_{2}+\\mathrm{SO}_{2(g)}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\end{gathered}}$<br>$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{BaCl}_{2}}$ is soluble in water, hence white precepitate disappears.<br>$\\mathrm{5 \\mathrm{SO}_{2}+2 \\mathrm{MnO}_{4}^{-}+2 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\rightarrow \\underset{\\text { colourless }}{5 \\mathrm{SO}_{4}^{2-}+4 \\mathrm{H}^{+}}}$<br>$\\rm{+2 \\mathrm{Mn}^{2+}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
