(25840,'chemistry',66,1038,2461,'Compound (A), $$\\mathrm{C}_{8} \\mathrm{H}_{9} \\mathrm{Br}$$ gives a light yellow precipitate when warmed with alcoholic $$\\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}$$. Oxidation of (A) gives an acid (B), $$\\mathrm{C}_{8} \\mathrm{H}_{6} \\mathrm{O}_{4}$$ (B) easily forms anhydride on heating. Identify the compound (A).','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Compound A gives light yellow precipitate with alcoholic $$\\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}$$, so it must contain $$\\mathrm{Br}$$ in side chain. On oxidation, it gives $$\\mathrm{C}_{8} \\mathrm{H}_{6} \\mathrm{O}_{4}$$, which shows the presence of two alkyl chains attached directly with the benzene nucleus.<br>Since compound B gives anhydride on heating, the two alkyl substituents must occupy adjacent $$(1,2)$$ positions.<br>Thus, A must be <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25840_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> and the reactions are as follows <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_25840_explanation_2.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(25842,'chemistry',63,818,1806,'Identify ${\\text{B}}$  in the given reaction .<br>$\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2} \\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{Cl}_{2},-\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}} \\mathrm{A}$<br>$\\xrightarrow{\\text { Auto Oxidation }} \\mathrm{CaCl}_{2}+\\mathrm{B}$','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CaOCl}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ca}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{ClO}_{3}\\\\right)_{2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ca}(\\\\mathrm{OH})_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ca}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{ClO}_{2}\\\\right)_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\xrightarrow[\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}]{\\stackrel{\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}}{\\longrightarrow}}$<br>$\\mathop {{\\text{CaOC}}{{\\text{l}}_{\\text{2}}}}\\limits_{\\mathop {\\text{A}}\\limits_{\\left( {{\\text{bleaching}}\\,\\,{\\text{powder}}} \\right)} } \\xrightarrow[{{\\text{oxidation}}}]{{{\\text{Auto}}}}{\\text{CaC}}{{\\text{l}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{  +  }}\\mathop {{\\text{Ca}}{{\\left( {{\\text{Cl}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)}_{\\text{2}}}}\\limits_{\\text{B}} $',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
