(25850,'chemistry',63,820,1814,'$\\mathrm{IBr}_{7}$ cannot exist but $\\mathrm{IF}_{7}$ exists. This fact can be explained on the basis of:','[{"text": "Ionisation potential", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Electron affinities", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ratio of radii of atoms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Reducing abilities", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Around \'I\', seven small \'  $\\mathrm{F}$ \' atoms can be accommodated where as big \' $\\mathrm{Br}$ \' atoms are not easily accommodated. On the basis of electronegativity also it can be explained. \' $\\mathrm{F}$ \' due to high e.n, can form $\\mathrm{IF}_{7}$ where as $\\mathrm{IBr}_{7}$ is not possible due to less electronegativity of $\\mathrm{Br}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
