(25862,'chemistry',63,805,1732,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Nitrogen has higher ionization energy than that of oxygen.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Nitrogen has smaller atomic size than that of oxygen.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Nitrogen has highy stable half filled  $\\mathrm{p}$ orbital. Thus, it has more ionization energy.<br>Oxygen has smaller atomic size than nitrogen due to its stronger nuclear charge.Therefore, option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
