(25866,'chemistry',63,807,1747,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{HNO}_{3}$ is a stronger acid than $\\mathrm{HNO}_{2}$.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In $\\mathrm{HNO}_{3}$ there are two nitrogen  oxygen bonds while in $\\mathrm{HNO}_{2}$ it is only one.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/63_25866_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  The acid strength of $\\mathrm{HNO}_{3}$ is higher than that of $\\mathrm{HNO}_{2}$ due to the higher oxidation state of nitrogen ( +5 in $\\mathrm{HNO}_{3}$ compared to +3 in $\\mathrm{HNO}_{2}$ ). Therefore, option (3) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
