(25870,'chemistry',63,806,1740,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Although $\\mathrm{PF}_{5}, \\mathrm{PCl}_{5}$ and $\\mathrm{PBr}_{5}$ are known, the pentahalides of nitrogen have not been observed.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Phosphorus has lower electronegativity than nitrogen','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Nitrogen does not have d orbitals, due to which it cannot have covalency beyond four. Therefore it cannot form pentahalides. Electronegativity of \' $\\mathrm{N}$ \' is more than \' $\\mathrm{P}$ \'. But it is not the reason for given assertion. So option (2) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
