(25964,'chemistry',63,824,1822,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Xenon forms fluorides.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Because 5d- orbitals are available for valence shell expansion.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Xenon forms fluorides primarily because only fluorine and oxygen are electronegative enough to excite electrons of Xenon into its vacant 5d-orbitals and allow bonding. So option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
