(26269,'chemistry',66,1031,2437,'Identify the catalyst $$\\mathrm{X}$$ used in following reaction.<br>$$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{Br}+2[\\mathrm{H}] \\stackrel{\\mathrm{x}}{\\longrightarrow} \\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}+\\mathrm{HBr}$$','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{7}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CaO}, \\\\Delta$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{Zn}-\\\\mathrm{Cu}$$ couple in alcohol", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{Br + 2[H]}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{Alcohol}}}]{{{\\text{zn}}{\\text{.Cu(X)}}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{ - C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{ + HBr}}$ $$[\\mathrm{X}]$$ is $$\\mathrm{Zn}-\\mathrm{Cu}$$ couple in alcohol. In the reaction, when ethyl bromide is reacted with $$\\mathrm{Zn}$$-Cu couple and alcohol, ethyl bromide reduced to give ethane. This is more or less a redox reaction. In it, ethyl bromide is reduced to give an ethyl organo metallic and $$\\mathrm{Br}^{-}$$subsequently, the ethanol protonates the ethyl organo metallic to give ethane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2020,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
