(26333,'chemistry',64,191,1913,'The set of correct statements is<br>(i)  Manganese exhibits $+ 7$ oxidation state in its oxide.<br>(ii) Ruthenium and Osmium exhibit $+ 8$ oxidation state in their oxides.<br>(iii) Sc shows $ + \\,4$ oxidation state which is oxidizing in nature.<br>(iv) Cr shows oxidising nature in $+ 6$ oxidation state.','[{"text": "(ii), (iii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i) and (iii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(ii) and (iii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i), (ii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$ \\bullet $  Mn shows $+ 7$ oxidation state in $\\mathrm{Mn}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}$<br>$ \\bullet $  Ruthenium and Osmium exhibit +8 oxidation state.<br>$ \\bullet $  Maximum oxidation state of Sc is $+ 3$ .<br>$ \\bullet $  $+ 6$ is the highest oxidation state of Cr and in this it can only act as an oxidising agent.<br>Thus, statements (i), (ii) and (iv) are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(26334,'chemistry',66,1031,2436,'Which of the following pairs are correctly matched?<br>\\[\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{Reactants}}}&{{\\rm{Products}}}\\\\{{\\rm{I}}{\\rm{.}}\\,\\,{\\rm{RX}}\\,{\\rm{ + }}\\,{\\rm{AgO}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\left( {{\\rm{aq}}} \\right)}}}&{{\\rm{RH}}}\\\\{{\\rm{II}}{\\rm{.}}\\,\\,{\\rm{RX}}\\,{\\rm{ + }}\\,{\\rm{AgC}}{{\\rm{N}}_{\\left( {{\\rm{alc}}} \\right)}}}&{{\\rm{RNC}}}\\\\{{\\rm{III}}{\\rm{.}}\\,\\,{\\rm{RX}}\\,{\\rm{ + }}\\,{\\rm{KC}}{{\\rm{N}}_{\\left( {{\\rm{alc}}} \\right)}}}&{{\\rm{RNC}}}\\\\{{\\rm{IV}}{\\rm{.}}\\,\\,{\\rm{RX}}\\,{\\rm{ + }}\\,{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\left( {{\\rm{ether}}} \\right)}}}&{{\\rm{R - R}}}\\end{array}\\]<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I alone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'(I) $$\\mathrm{R}-\\mathrm{X}+\\mathrm{AgOH}_{(\\mathrm{ar})} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{R}-\\mathrm{OH}+\\mathrm{AgX}$$<br>$$\\begin{aligned}& \\text { (II) } \\mathrm{R}-\\mathrm{X}+\\mathrm{AgCN}_{\\text {(alc) }} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{RNC}+\\mathrm{AgX} \\\\& \\text { (IV) } 2 \\mathrm{R}-\\mathrm{X}+2 \\mathrm{Na} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{R}-\\mathrm{R}+2 \\mathrm{NaX} \\\\& \\text { (III) } \\mathrm{R}-\\mathrm{X}+\\mathrm{KCN} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{RCN}+\\mathrm{KX}\\end{aligned}$$<br>II and IV reactions are correctly matched with its products.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
