(26348,'chemistry',63,823,1820,'Noble gases are adsorbed by','[{"text": "anhydrous calcium chloride.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ferric hydroxide.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "conc. $\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{SO}_{4}$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "activated coconut charcoal.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Noble gases are adsorbed by coconut charcoal. The adsorption of different noble gases occur at different temperatures. Hence, charcoal is used to separate these gases. Helium is not adsorbed by charcoal as it is very difficult to liquefy the gas.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
