(26352,'chemistry',64,194,1934,'Which of the following elements have half-filled f-orbitals in their ground state? <br>(Given : atomic numbers  ${\\rm{Sm}} = 62;{\\rm{Eu}} = 63;{\\rm{Tb}} = 65$<br>${\\rm{Gd}} = 64,{\\rm{Pm}} = 61)$<br>$\\begin{array}{lllll}\\text { A. } \\mathrm{Sm} & \\text { B. Eu } & \\text { C. } \\mathrm{Tb} & \\text { D. Gd } & \\text { E. Pm }\\end{array}$<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and E only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B and D only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "C and D only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Half-filled configuration of f - orbitals will have 7 electrons.<br>$({\\text{A}})\\,\\,{\\text{Sm}}\\,(62)\\quad \\left[ {{\\text{Xe}}} \\right]4{{\\text{f}}^6}6{{\\text{s}}^2}$<br>$({\\text{B}})\\,\\,{\\text{Eu}}\\,(63)\\quad \\,\\,\\left[ {{\\text{Xe}}} \\right]4{{\\text{f}}^7}6{{\\text{s}}^2}$<br>$({\\text{C}})\\,\\,{\\text{Tb}}\\,(65)\\quad \\,\\,\\left[ {{\\text{Xe}}} \\right]4{{\\text{f}}^9}6{{\\text{s}}^2}$<br>$({\\text{D}})\\,\\,{\\text{Gd}}\\,(64)\\quad \\,\\left[ {{\\text{Xe}}} \\right]4{{\\text{f}}^7}5{{\\text{d}}^1}6{{\\text{s}}^2}$<br>$({\\text{E}})\\,\\,{\\text{Pm}}\\,(61)\\quad \\,\\left[ {{\\text{Xe}}} \\right]4{{\\text{f}}^5}6{{\\text{s}}^2}$<br>Hence, Europium and Gadolinium have halffilled f-subshell.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(26353,'chemistry',63,811,1769,'The compounding not acting as a reducing agent is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{S}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Se}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Te}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Group 16 elements are O,S,Se,Te.Due to inert pair of effect stability of +4,+6 oxidation state decreases on moving down the group.Hence ${\\rm{T}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{4 + }}}}$ is more stable than ${\\rm{T}}{{\\rm{e}}^{{\\rm{6 + }}}}$. Hence${\\rm{Te}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$will act as on oxidising agent and not as reducing agent.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
