(26356,'chemistry',64,192,1924,'Read Statement A and Statement B carefully and mark correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Aqueous solution of $\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}$ is preferred as a primary standard in volumetric analysis over $\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}$ aqueous solution.</div><div class="column-right">$\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}$ has a higher solubility in water than $\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}$.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is false but statement B is true.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statement A and statement B are true.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is true but statement B is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Aqueous solution of $\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}$  is preferred as a primary standard in volumetric analysis over $\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}$ aqueous solution. $\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}$ is hygroscopic while the $\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}$  is not. Sodium dichromate is more soluble in water than potassium dichromate due to smaller size of sodium ions, as compared to potassium ions. Hence, statement A is true, but statement B is false.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
