(26559,'chemistry',65,954,2220,'Identify homoleptic complex from the following','[{"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Co}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{6}\\\\right]^{3+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Co}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{5} \\\\mathrm{Cl}\\\\right] \\\\mathrm{SO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Co}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{4} \\\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}\\\\right]^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Co}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}\\\\right)\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{5}\\\\right] \\\\mathrm{I}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{3+}-$ Here only one type of ligands surrounds the $\\mathrm{Co}^{3+}$ ion, so, it is homoleptic complex. Rest options are heteroleptic complexes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(26560,'chemistry',64,192,1924,'When hydrogen peroxide is added to acidified solution of dichromate $\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}^{2-}$, a deep blue coloured complex of chromic peroxide $\\mathrm{CrO}_{5}$ is formed. Oxidation state of $\\mathrm{Cr}$ in $\\mathrm{CrO}_{5}$ is','[{"text": "+5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "+3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "+6", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "-10", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2}$ is added to an acidified solution of dichromate $\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}^{2-}$, a deep blue complex chromic peroxide, $\\mathrm{CrO}_{5}$ is formed.<br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{r}}_2}{\\rm{O}}_7^{2 - } + 2{{\\rm{H}}^ + } + 4{{\\rm{H}}_2}{{\\rm{O}}_2} \\to \\\\\n\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{\\rm{CrO}}{\\left( {{{\\rm{O}}_2}} \\right)_2} + 5{{\\rm{H}}_2}{\\rm{O}}\n\\end{array}$<br>This deep blue coloured complex has the following structure  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/64_26560_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   In $\\mathrm{CrO}\\left(\\mathrm{O}_{2}\\right)_{2}$, let the oxidation state of $\\mathrm{Cr}$ be $x$.<br> $\\therefore \\,\\,\\,{\\mkern 1mu} {\\kern 1pt} {\\rm{x}} + ( - 1)4 + ( - 2) = 0$<br>${\\rm{x}} - 6 = 0 \\Rightarrow {\\rm{x}} =  + 6$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
