(27124,'chemistry',65,957,2229,'Nickel $({\\rm{Z}} = 28)$ combines with a uninegative monodentate ligand $\\mathrm{X}^{-}$to form a  paramagnetic complex $\\left[\\mathrm{NiX}_{4}\\right]^{2-}$. The number of unpaired electrons in the nickel and geometry of this complex ion are, respectively','[{"text": "One and tetrahedral", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two and tetrahedral", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One and square planar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two and square planar", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{NiX}_{4}\\right]^{2-}}}$ is paramagnetic complex.<br>So, ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Ni}^{+2}}}$ will have ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{d}^{8}}}$ configuration with 2 unpaired electrons. It undergoes ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{sp}^{3}}}$ hybridization and has tetrahedral geometry.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27125,'chemistry',66,1038,2461,'A saturated alkyl halide ${\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{3} \\mathrm{H}_{7} \\mathrm{X}\\right)}}$ heated with dry silver oxide ${\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{Ag}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)}}$ forms 1-propoxypropane. The number of moles of alkyl halide consumed per mole of 1-propoxypropane formed is ____ .','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathop {{\\text{2}}{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}} - {\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{Cl}}}\\limits_{\\mathop {{\\text{n   -   Propyl}}\\,{\\text{chloride}}}\\limits_{{\\text{(1   -   Chloropropane)}}} }  + \\mathop {{\\text{A}}{{\\text{g}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}}\\limits_{\\mathop {{\\text{Dry}}}\\limits_{{\\text{silver}}\\,{\\text{oxide}}} } \\,\\xrightarrow{\\Delta }\\,\\,\\,$<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\mathop {{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}} - {\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}} - {\\text{O}} - {\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}}\\limits_{{\\text{1  -  Propoxypropane}}}  - {{\\text{C}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}}{\\text{  +  2AgCl}}$<br>From above reaction, we say that 2 moles of n-propyl chloride is required.<br>So, the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
