(27126,'chemistry',67,1076,2569,'The increasing order of boiling points of the below mentioned alcohols is<br>I. 1, 2-dihydroxybenzene<br>II. 1, 3-dihydroxybenzene<br>III. 1, 4-dihydroxybenzene<br>IV. Hydroxybenzene','[{"text": "IV $$ < $$ II $$ < $$ I $$ < $$ III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV $$ < $$ I $$ < $$ II $$ < $$ III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I $$ < $$ II $$ < $$ IV $$ < $$ III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I $$ < $$ II $$ < $$ III $$ < $$ IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Among the given compounds, hydroxybenzene (IV) has least molar mass and therefore possess least boiling. 1, 2dihydroxybenzene (I) forms intramolecular $$\\mathrm{H}$$- bonding with result that it will not form intermolecular H-bonding leading to lowest boiling point. On the other hand 1, 3dihydroxybenzene (II) and 1, 4dihydroxybenzene (III) does not undergo chelation, hence they will involve extensive intermolecular $$\\mathrm{H}$$-bonding leading to higher boiling point. Further intermolecular hydrogen bonding is stronger in the p-isomer than the $$\\mathrm{m}$$- isomer hence former has highest b.p. Thus the decreasing order of boiling points is III $$>$$ II $$>$$ I $$>$$ IV.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27127,'chemistry',68,1113,2670,'${\\text{CH}} \\equiv {\\text{CH}}\\xrightarrow[{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}}]{{{\\text{HS}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}}}{\\text{A}}\\xrightarrow[{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}}]{{{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{Mgr}}}}{\\text{B}}\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{P}}_{{\\text{Br}}}}{\\text{B}}{{\\text{r}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{\\text{C}}$. Here \' $$\\mathrm{C}$$ \' is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Br}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\\\\mathrm{CH}-\\\\mathrm{Br}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{Br}-\\\\mathrm{CH}=\\\\mathrm{CH}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_27127_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27128,'chemistry',65,957,2229,'Magnetic moment of complexes<br>(I) $\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{CN})_{3}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{3}\\right]^{1-}$<br>(II) $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{3} \\mathrm{~F}_{3}\\right]^{0}$<br>(III) $\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_{3}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{3}\\right]^{1-}$<br>(IV) $\\left[\\mathrm{Cr}(\\mathrm{CN})_{3}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{3}\\right]^{0}$<br>are respectively (in B.M. units)','[{"text": "$\\\\sqrt{8}, 0,0$, and $\\\\sqrt{15}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0, \\\\sqrt{24}, \\\\sqrt{24}$, and 0", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0,0,0$, and $\\\\sqrt{15}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\sqrt{8}, \\\\sqrt{24}, 0$, and $\\\\sqrt{15}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'1. ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Ni}^{+2}: \\mathrm{d}^{8}: 2}}$ unpaired ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\sqrt{8}}}$ B.M.<br>2. ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Co}^{+3}: \\mathrm{d}^{6}: 4}}$ unpaired ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\sqrt{24}}}$ B.M.<br>3. ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Fe}^{+2}: \\mathrm{d}^{6}:}}$ (strong ligand) – 0 unpaired ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow 0}}$<br>4. ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cr}^{3+}: \\mathrm{d}^{3}: 3}}$ unpaired ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\sqrt{15}}}$ B.M.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
