(27171,'chemistry',65,957,2229,'Match Column I with Column II and choose the correct combination from the options given.<br><div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A - P,R,T, B - P,Q,S, C - P,R,S,D - R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - P,R, B - P,S,T, C - R, D - P,Q,S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P,Q,R,\\t B - P,Q,T,\\tC - P,Q,T,  D - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P,Q, B - P,T, C - P,S, D - R", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'(A) ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{DMG})_{2}}}$ is a square planar complex stabilized by two intra molecular hydrogen bonds. It has chelation and is diamagnetic.<br>(B) ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{4}^{-2}}}$ forms chelation. Fe in +3 oxidation state contains unpaired electrons so is paramagnetic and the complex is a conductor as it is ionic. ${\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{4}^{-2}\\right.}}$ is weak field ligand)<br>(C) ${\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{en})_{2}\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}}}$ ionic complex, so is a conductor. Due to \'en\'  group, chelation is there. ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Ni}^{+2}}}$ has ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{d}^{8}}}$ configuration which has no unpaired electrons due to \'en\' group (strong ligand) and is diamagnetic.<br>(D) ${\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{CO})_{4}\\right] \\mathrm{sp}^{3}-}}$ tetrahedral-diamagnetic (no unpaired electrons)',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/65_27171_question_1.png'),
