(27178,'chemistry',65,954,2216,'Read Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct option given below.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Charge on the complex of ferric ion with EDTA is minus one.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> EDTA is a hexadentate ligand.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is false but reason is true.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Reason should be EDTA charge is – 4 . Given assertion, reason both statements are true statements, but not the correct explanation.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27183,'chemistry',65,956,2223,'Which among the following statements are true for the complex $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}\\right]\\left[\\mathrm{Cr}(\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\right]$ ?<br>(A) It is a non-electrolyte.<br>(B) The magnitude of the charge on each complex ion is three.<br>(C) The complex will not conduct current in aqueous solution.<br>(D) The complex will exhibit co-ordination isomerism.<br>(E) The magnitude of the charge on each complex ion is one.','[{"text": "A and D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C and E", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B and D", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{3+}\\left[\\mathrm{Cr}(\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\right]^{3-}}}$<br>This compelx can show coordination isomerism as both anionic and cationic parts are complex ions. Due to charges it is an electrolyte and conducts electricity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27186,'chemistry',66,1032,2440,'15.7 g of 1-chloropropane is treated with alcoholic KOH . What mass of propene (in grams) is obtained if the yield is ${\\mathrm{50 \\%}}$ ?','[{"text": "4.2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2.1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8.4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.4", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When 1-chloropropane is heated with alcoholic KOH , propene is obtained.$\\mathop {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{Cl}}}\\limits_{{\\text{1  -  Chloropropane}}} {\\text{  +  }}\\mathop {{\\text{KOH}}}\\limits_{\\left( {{\\text{Alc}}{\\text{.}}} \\right)} \\xrightarrow{\\Delta }$<br>$\\mathop {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CH}}}\\limits_{{\\text{Propane}}} {\\text{ = C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ + KCl + }}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}$<br>Molar mass of ${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{Cl}} = {\\text{78}}{\\text{.5}}\\,{\\text{g/mol}}$    and molar mass of propene ${\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}=\\mathrm{CH}_{2}\\right)=42 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{mol}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore}}$ Number of moles of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}=\\dfrac{15.7 \\mathrm{~g}}{78.5 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{mol}}=0.2 \\mathrm{~mol}}}$<br>0.2 mol of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}}}$ will give 0.2 mol of propene.<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore}}$ Mass of propene obtained will be ${\\mathrm{0.2 \\times 42=8.4 \\mathrm{~g}}}$<br>However, the yield is ${\\mathrm{50 \\%}}$.<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore}}$ Mass of propene obtained ${\\mathrm{=8.4 \\times \\dfrac{50}{100}=4.2 \\mathrm{~g}}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27187,'chemistry',65,954,2216,'Select the complex which has all the following characteristics.<br>(1)  1:1 type electrolyte (number of cation to number of anion ratio)<br>(2)  Heteroleptic complex<br>(3)  Does not give AgCl with $\\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}$ (solution)','[{"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Pt}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{3} \\\\mathrm{Cl}_{3}\\\\right] \\\\mathrm{Cl}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Pt}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right) \\\\mathrm{Cl}_{5}\\\\right]$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}_{2}\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{PtCl}_{6}\\\\right]$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Pt}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{Cl}_{4}\\\\right]$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K}\\left[\\mathrm{Pt}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right) \\mathrm{Cl}_{5}\\right]}}$ gives 2 ions (1:1 type).<br>It can\'t give AgCl ppt as it is not providing ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}}}$ ions.<br>It has different ligands. So heteroleptic.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
