(27204,'chemistry',68,1118,2677,'In the compound given below, the correct order of acidity of the positions (X), $(\\mathrm{Y})$ and $(\\mathrm{Z})$ is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{Z &gt; X &gt; Y}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{X &gt; Y &gt; Z}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{X &gt; Z &gt; Y}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Y &gt; X &gt; Z}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Position (X) is most acidic due to &ndash; COOH group. &nbsp;$ - {\\rm{NH}}_{\\rm{3}}^{\\rm{ + }}$ group at position Y is more acidic than at Z because of presence of electron withdrawing &ndash; COOH group in close proximity. &nbsp;Hence, &nbsp;the &nbsp;$ - {\\rm{NH}}_{\\rm{3}}^{\\rm{ + }}$ group at position Z is least acidic as it is far away from th ecaboxylic acid group.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_27204_question_1.png'),
