(27208,'chemistry',68,1118,2677,'Arrange the following acids in the decreasing order of the acidic strength.<br>Choose the correct option','[{"text": "I $$>$$ II $$>$$ III $$>$$ IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I $$ < $$ II $$ < $$ III $$ < $$ IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I $$>$$ III $$>$$ II $$>$$ IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I $$>$$ IV $$>$$ III $$>$$ II", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Acidity increases as the electronegativity of the carbon atom directly attached to $$-\\mathrm{COOH}$$ group increases or the hybridisation of the carbon atom directly attached to $$\\mathrm{COOH}$$ changes from $$\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{sp}^{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{sp}$$. The acidic strength decreases in the order I $$>$$ II $$>$$ III $$>$$ IV.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_27208_question_1.png'),
