(27250,'chemistry',68,1113,2668,'Compound (A), $$\\mathrm{C}_{9} \\mathrm{H}_{10} \\mathrm{O}$$, is inert to $$\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$$ in $$\\mathrm{CCl}_{4}$$. Vigorous oxidation with hot alkaline $$\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4}$$ yields benzoic acid. Compound "A" gives red precipitate with 2,4-dinitrophenylhydrazine and yellow with $$\\mathrm{NaOI}$$. The possible structure of compound (A) will be :','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{PhCOCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{PhCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{COCH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{PhCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CHO}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{PhCH}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right) \\\\mathrm{CHO}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'(A) must be a ketone having $$-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$$ group attached to carbonyl group because only methyl ketones will give yellow precipitate with $$\\mathrm{NaOI}$$.<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_27250_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27251,'chemistry',65,956,2223,'$[{\\rm{Co}}{({\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_3})_4}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}]{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,[{\\rm{Co}}{({\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_3})_4}{\\rm{ClN}}{{\\rm{O}}_2}]{\\rm{Cl}}$exhibit which type of isomerism','[{"text": "Geometrical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Optical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linkage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ionisation", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}\\right] \\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ and $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{4} \\mathrm{ClNO}_{2}\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}$ give different ions when subjected to ionisation.<br>Thus, these are ionisation isomers and they exhibit ionisation isomerism.<br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n\\left[ {{\\rm{Co}}{{\\left( {{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_3}} \\right)}_4}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_2}} \\right]{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{O}}_2} \\to \\\\\n\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\left[ {{\\rm{Co}}{{\\left( {{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_3}} \\right)}_4}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_2}} \\right]^ + } + {\\rm{NO}}_2^ - \\\\\n\\left[ {{\\rm{Co}}{{\\left( {{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_3}} \\right)}_4}{\\rm{ClN}}{{\\rm{O}}_2}} \\right]{\\rm{Cl}} \\to \\\\\n\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\left[ {{\\rm{Co}}{{\\left( {{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_3}} \\right)}_4}{\\rm{ClN}}{{\\rm{O}}_2}} \\right]^ + } + {\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}^ - }\n\\end{array}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
