(27289,'chemistry',65,957,2229,'Choose the correct statement.','[{"text": "$\\\\left[ {{\\\\text{Co}}{{\\\\left( {{\\\\text{N}}{{\\\\text{H}}_3}} \\\\right)}_6}} \\\\right]_{}^{2 + }$ is oxidised to diamagnetic $\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Co}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{6}\\\\right]^{3+}$ by the oxygen in air", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tetrahedral complexes are more stable than octahedral complexes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Fe}(\\\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\\\right]^{3-}$ is stable but $\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{FeF}_{6}\\\\right]^{3-}$ is unstable", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The $\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Cu}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{4}\\\\right]^{2+}$ ion has a tetrahedral geometry and is diamagnetic<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'(1)${\\left[ {{\\rm{Co}}{{\\left( {{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}} \\right)}_{\\rm{6}}}} \\right]^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}{\\rm{ = [Ar]}}\\,{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{d}}^{\\rm{7}}}$ <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/65_27289_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   <br>(2) Tetrahedral complexes are less stable than octahedral complexes.<br>(3) $\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\right]^{3-}$ and $\\left[\\mathrm{FeF}_{6}\\right]^{3-}$ both are stable but former is more stable, since it forms inner orbital complex.<br>(4) $\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{4}\\right]^{2+}$ has square planar geometry and is paramagnetic.<br>So, the correct option is (1).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
