(27294,'chemistry',65,958,2234,'The magnitude of crystal field stabilisation energy in tetrahedral complexes ${\\rm{(CFSE}}\\,\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{\\Delta }}_{\\rm{t}}}{\\rm{)}}$ is considerably less than that in the octahedral field because','[{"text": "there are only four ligands instead of six so the ligand field is only $2 / 3$ the size, hence the $\\\\Delta_{t}$ is $2 / 3$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "the direction of the orbitals does not coincide with the direction of the ligands. This reduce the crystal field stabilisation energy $(\\\\Delta)$ by further $2 / 3$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both points (1) and (2) are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both points (1) and (2) are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both (a) and (b) statements are correct.<br>(a) There are only four ligands instead of six. So, the ligand field is only $2 / 3$ the size, hence the $\\Delta_{t}$ is $2 / 3$.<br>(b) The direction of the orbital does not coincide with the direction of the ligands. This reduces the crystal field stabilisation energy $(\\Delta)$ by further $2 / 3$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
