(27298,'chemistry',65,958,2234,'The crystal field stabilisation energy (CFSE) is highest for','[{"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{CoF}_{4}\\\\right]^{2-}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Co}(\\\\mathrm{NCS})_{4}\\\\right]^{2-}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Co}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{6}\\\\right]^{3+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{CoCl}_{4}\\\\right]^{2-}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Higher the oxidation state of the metal, greater the crystal field splitting. In options (a), (b) and (d), Co is present in +2 oxidation state and in (c) it is present in +3 oxidation state and hence, $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{3+}$ has a higher value of CFSE.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27299,'chemistry',66,1036,2451,'${{\\text{EtN}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{  +  MeMgI}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{ temp}}{\\text{. with pyridine }}}]{{{\\text{Heated}}{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\text{at}}{\\kern 1pt} {\\text{high}}}}{\\text{Gas(A)}}}$<br>The volume of gas (A) obtained at STP when<br> 0.45 g of ${{\\rm{EtN}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}}$ reacts with ${\\text{ MeMgI}}$ is ____ .','[{"text": "0.45", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.9", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "10", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_27299_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  One mole of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Et}-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}}}$ reacts with 2 moles of MeMgI to give 2 mol . of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{4}(\\mathrm{~g})}}$<br>Mol. mass of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Et}-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}=45 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}}}$<br>So, ${\\mathrm{45 \\mathrm{~g} \\,\\mathrm{Et}-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}}}$ gives ${\\mathrm{2 \\times 22.4 \\mathrm{~L}}}$ of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{4}}}$ at STP<br>$0.45\\,{\\text{g of Et}} - {\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_2}{\\text{ gives C}}{{\\text{H}}_4}$<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, = \\frac{{2 \\times 22.4 \\times 0.45}}{{45}} = 0.448\\,{\\text{L}} = 0.45\\,{\\text{L}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
