(27308,'chemistry',65,957,2228,'Among $\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{CO})_{4}\\right],\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{CN})_{4}\\right]^{2-},\\left[\\mathrm{NiCl}_{4}\\right]^{2-}$ species, the hybridisation states of $\\mathrm{Ni}$ atom are, respectively.(Atomic number of $\\mathrm{Ni}=28$ )','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^3},{\\\\rm{ds}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^2},{\\\\rm{ds}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{,ds}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{,s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{,s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{,ds}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ds}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{,s}}{{\\\\rm{p}}^{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{,sp}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'(a) $\\operatorname{In}\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{CO})_{4}\\right]$, nickel is ${\\text{s}}{{\\text{p}}^{\\text{3}}}$ -hybridised because in it oxidation state of $\\mathrm{Ni}$ is zero. So, its electronic configuration is<br>${}_{{\\text{28}}}{\\text{Ni}}$=${\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{,2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{,3}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{d}}^{\\rm{8}}}{\\rm{,4}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}$ <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/65_27308_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />    (b) $\\operatorname{In}\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{CN})_{4}\\right]^{2-}$, nickel is present as $\\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}$ so its configuration is<br>${\\rm{ = 1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{,2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{,3}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{d}}^{\\rm{8}}}$}  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/65_27308_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  $\\mathrm{CN}^{-}$is a strong field ligand, hence it makes $\\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}$ electrons to be paired up.<br>(III) $\\mathrm{In}\\left[\\mathrm{NiCl}_{4}\\right]^{2-}$ species, nickel is present as $\\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}$, so its configuration is<br>${\\rm{ = 1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{,2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{,3}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{d}}^{\\rm{8}}}$ <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/65_27308_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   $\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$is a weak field ligand, hence $\\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}$ electrons are not paired.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
