(27350,'chemistry',65,954,2216,'Which of the following is not an anionic complex?','[{"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Cu}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\\\right)_{4}\\\\right] \\\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}_{4}\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Fe}(\\\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\\\right]$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}_{3}\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{Fe}(\\\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\\\right]$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left[\\\\mathrm{NiCl}_{4}\\\\right]^{2-}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Positive charge if appears on the coordination sphere, the complex thus obtained is known as cationic complex.<br>$\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{4}\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\rightleftharpoons\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{4}\\right]^{2+}+2 \\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$<br>$\\mathrm{K}_{4}\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\right] \\rightleftharpoons 4 \\mathrm{~K}^{+}+\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\right]^{-}$$\\mathrm{K}_{3}\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\right] \\rightleftharpoons 3 \\mathrm{~K}^{+}+\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_{6}\\right]^{3-}$<br>$\\left[\\mathrm{NiCl}_{4}\\right]^{2-}$<br>Therefore, $\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{4}\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$ is not an anionic complex, it is a cationic complex.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
