(27404,'chemistry',66,702,2415,'Read the Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct option out of the options given below.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{Cl}}}$ is an example of allyl halide.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Allyl halides are the compounds in which the halogen atom is attached to ${\\rm{s}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{2}}}$ hybridised carbon atom.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Allyl halides are the compounds in which halogen atom is attached to ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{sp}^{3}}}$ hybridised carbon atom adjacent to a carbon-carbon double bond. So, the correct option is (3) .',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
