(27418,'chemistry',68,1118,2677,'The correct order of increasing acid strength of the compounds<br>(A) $$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CO}_{2} \\mathrm{H}$$<br>(B) $$\\mathrm{MeOCH}_{2} \\mathrm{CO}_{2} \\mathrm{H}$$<br>(C) $$\\mathrm{CF}_{3} \\mathrm{CO}_{2} \\mathrm{H}$$<br>(D)','[{"text": "(D) $$ < $$ (A) $$ < $$ (B) $$ < $$ (C)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(D) $$ < $$ (C) $$ < $$ (B) $$ < $$ (A)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(A) $$ < $$ (B) $$ < $$ (C) $$ < $$ (D)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(A) $$ < $$ (D) $$ < $$ (C) $$ < $$ (B)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The correct order of increasing acid strength<br>$$\\begin{gathered}\\mathrm{CF}_{3} \\mathrm{COOH}>\\mathrm{MeOCH}_{2} \\mathrm{COOH}>\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOH} \\\\>(\\mathrm{Me})_{2} \\mathrm{CH} . \\mathrm{COOH}\\end{gathered}$$<br>Electron withdrawing groups increase the acid strength and electron donating groups decrease the acid strength.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_27418_question_1.jpg'),
