(27459,'chemistry',67,1073,2559,'Which of the following reactions will yield propan-2-ol?','[{"text": "${\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{ = CH - C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{3}}}{\\\\text{ + HCl}}\\\\xrightarrow{{{{\\\\text{H}}^{\\\\text{ + }}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{3}}}{\\\\text{ - CHO}}\\\\xrightarrow{{{\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{3}}}{\\\\text{MgBr/HOH}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{O}}\\\\xrightarrow{{{{\\\\text{C}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{5}}}{\\\\text{MgI/HOH}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{ = CH - C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{3}}}\\\\xrightarrow{{{\\\\text{Neutral KMn}}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{4}}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Acetaldehyde on reaction with Grignard reagent gives a secondary alcohol.<br>i.e., Propan-2-ol $\\left( {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CH(OH)C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27460,'chemistry',66,1031,2435,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 2}}$ reactions are\n\'stereospecific\', indicating that they result in the formation of only one stereo-isomer as the product.</div><div class="column-right">${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 1}}$ reactions generally result in formation of product as racemic mixtures.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Inversion of configuration occurs in ${\\mathrm{S_{N} 2}}$reaction and ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 1}}$ reaction proceeds via carbocation intermediate, it produces racemic mixture. Hence, both statements are true. So, the correct option is (3) .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27462,'chemistry',65,956,2224,'The number of geometrical isomers possible for a square planar complex of the type ${\\left[ {{\\rm{Mabcd}}} \\right]^{{\\rm{n \\pm }}}}$ is \' ${\\mathrm{x}}$ \'. The number of geometrical isomers possible for octahedral complex of the type ${\\left[ {{\\rm{M}}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{4}}}{{\\rm{b}}_{\\rm{2}}}} \\right]^{{\\rm{n}} \\pm }}$ is<br>\' ${\\mathrm{y}}$ \'. Sum of ${\\mathrm{x}}$ and ${\\mathrm{y}}$ is ____. (a,b, c, d are monodentate ligands)','[{"text": "5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The square planar complex ${{\\rm{[Mabcd]}}^{{\\rm{n}} \\pm }}$ forms three geometric isomers whereas octahedral complex ${{\\rm{[M}}{{\\rm{a}}_{\\rm{4}}}{{\\rm{B}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{]}}^{{\\rm{n}} \\pm }}$ forms two geometric isomers.<br>i.e.x+y=5.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
