(27474,'chemistry',66,1031,2436,'Read the Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct option out of the options given below.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Haloalkanes react with KCN to form alkyl cyanides as a main product while with AgCN form isocyanide as the main product.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> KCN and AgCN both are highly ionic compounds','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'KCN is predominantly ionic and provides cyanide ions in solution. Although both carbon and nitrogen atoms are in a position to donate electron pairs, the attack takes place mainly through carbon atom and not through nitrogen atom since ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}}}$ bond is more stable than ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{N}}}$ bond. However, AgCN is mainly covalent in nature and nitrogen is free to donate electron pair forming isocyanide as the main product. So, the correct option is (3) .',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
