(27478,'chemistry',66,1031,2435,'The correct statement regarding nucleophilic substitution reaction in a chiral alkyl halide is','[{"text": "retention occurs in ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{S}_{\\\\mathrm{N}} 1}}$ reaction and inversion occurs in ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{S}_{\\\\mathrm{N}} 2}}$ reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "racemisation occurs in ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{S}_{\\\\mathrm{N}} 1}}$ reaction and retention occurs in ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{S}_{\\\\mathrm{N}} 2}}$ reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "racemisation occurs in both ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{S}_{\\\\mathrm{N}} 1}}$ and ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{S}_{\\\\mathrm{N}} 2}}$ reactions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "racemisation occurs in ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{S}_{\\\\mathrm{N}} 1}}$ reaction and inversion occurs in ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{S}_{\\\\mathrm{N}} 2}}$ reaction.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'As ${\\mathrm{S_{N} 1}}$ reaction proceeds via the formation of a planar carbocation intermediate, it allows attack by nucleophile from either direction leading to racemisation.<br>On the other hand, in ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 2}}$ reaction attack by nucleophile occurs from the backside leading to inversion of configuration of the chiral alkyl halide. So, the correct options is (4) .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
