(27482,'chemistry',66,1031,2432,'Which among the following halides will not show ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 1}}$ reaction?<br>(I) ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}}}$<br>(II) ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{CH}=\\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{Cl}}}$<br>(III) (IV) Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "(I) and (II) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(II) only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(I), (II) and (IV) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(II) and (III) only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Carbocation intermidiates are formed during ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 1}}$ mechanism. <br>(I) forms stable allyl carbocation ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\\mathrm{CH}-\\stackrel{+}{\\mathrm{C}} \\mathrm{H}_{2}}}$,<br>(II) forms highly unstable vinyl carbocation ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{CH}=\\stackrel{+}{\\mathrm{C}} \\mathrm{H}}}$,<br>(III)forms benzyl carbocation <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/66_27482_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  which is stable due to resonance, and <br>(IV) forms secondary carbocation ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\stackrel{+}{\\mathrm{C}} \\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}}}$.<br>Hence, (${\\text{II}}$) will not show ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 1}}$ reaction. So, the correct options is (2) .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/66_27482_question_1.png'),
