(27503,'chemistry',67,1075,2566,'For the preparation of $$t$$-butylmethylether by Williamson\'s method the correct choice of reagents is','[{"text": "Methoxide and $$t$$-butylbromide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Methanol and 2-bromobutane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2-Butanol and methylbromide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "t-Butoxide and methylbromide", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Williamson\'s synthesis is not given by teriary alkyl halide as they undergo elimination reaction.To prepare t-alkyl ether, t- alkoxide and a primary alkyl halide should be used.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27505,'chemistry',68,1116,2673,'Carbonation of methyl magnesium bromide gives an organic compound which can also be obtained by','[{"text": "Hydrolysis of acetonitrile with mineral acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oxidation of methyl alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrolysis of methyl isocyanide with mineral acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrolysis of methyl formate with mineral acid", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOH}$$ is the acid formed in both the cases.<br>${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{MgBr  +  C}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}\\xrightarrow[{{{\\text{H}}^{{\\text{  +  }}}}}]{{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O,}}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{COOH  + }}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{Mg}}\\left( {{\\text{OH}}} \\right){\\text{Br }}$<br>${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CN}}\\xrightarrow[{{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ + }}}}]{{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O,}}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{COOH + N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27507,'chemistry',67,1074,2562,'${\\text{Cumene}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{ii) }}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O/}}{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ + }}}}]{{{\\text{i) }}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{\\text{(X)}}\\,\\,{\\text{and}}\\,\\,{\\text{(Y)}}$  respectively are','[{"text": "Toluene, propene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Toluene, propylchloride", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenol, acetone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phenol, acetaldehyde", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cumene on aerial oxidation followed by hydrolysis gives phenol and acetone.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27508,'chemistry',65,953,2212,'A coordination compound ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CrCl}_{3} .4 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}}}$ precipitates silver chloride with silver nitrate solution. The molar conductivity of the solution corresponds to a total number of two ions. The number of chloride ions within the coordination sphere of the compound is _____ .','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Since the coordination compound gives precipitate with silver nitrate, there should be at least one chloride ion outside the coordination sphere. Further, the conductivity of the compound corresponds to two ions. This implies, the formula of the compound will have:${\\left[ {{\\rm{complex}}\\,{\\rm{ion}}} \\right]^ + } + {\\rm{one}}\\,{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}^ - }$ ion<br>So, the formula of the compound will be:<br>${\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{CrCl}_{2}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{4}\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}}}$<br>Therefore, the number of chloride ions within the coordination sphere of the compound is 2 .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27509,'chemistry',68,1113,2659,'Which of the following conversions can be carried out by Clemmensen Reduction?<br>(i) Benzaldehyde into benzyl alcohol<br>(ii) Cyclohexanone into cyclohexane<br>(iii) Benzoyl chloride into benzadehyde<br>(iv) Benzophenone into diphenyl methane','[{"text": "(ii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(i) and (iv)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i) and (iii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(iii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Carbonyl compound into alkane',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27514,'chemistry',67,1073,2559,'The reagent required to convert propene to 1 propanol is','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6}$$ followed by $$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{2} / \\\\mathrm{NaOH}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Conc. $$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{SO}_{4}$$ followed by hydrolysis with boiling water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{HBr}$$ followed by hydrolysis with aqueous $$\\\\mathrm{KOH}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{Hg}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{OCOCH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2}$$ followed by reduction with $$\\\\mathrm{NaBH}_{4}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Anti-Markovnikov\'s hydration by hydroboraton-oxidation of alkenes.<br>${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CH    =    C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{ (ii) }}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{/O}}{{\\text{H}}^{{\\text{    -    }}}}}]{{{\\text{(i)}}{{\\text{B}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{6}}}}}\\mathop {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{OH}}}\\limits_{{\\text{Anti}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{-Markonikov\'s}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\text{product}}} $<br>Other three options will lead Markovnikov\'s hydration, i.e. $$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}=\\mathrm{CH}_{2}$$ $$\\rightarrow \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CHOHCH}_{3}$$.<br>',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27515,'chemistry',68,1113,2663,'Which of the following gives Cannizzaro reaction?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Ph}}\\\\,\\\\, - \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{CH}}\\\\,\\\\, = \\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Aldehydes having no $\\alpha-H$ give Cannizzaro reaction. Chloral gives chloroform when treated with a base. Thus only <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_27515_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> gives Cannizzaro\'s reaction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27517,'chemistry',67,1073,2559,'The compound obtained by the reaction of ethene with diborane followed by hydrolysis with alkaline hydrogen peroxide is','[{"text": "Ethanol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Propanol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethanal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Triethyl boride", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\text{3C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ = C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{B}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{6}}}}}{\\left( {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}} \\right)_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{B}}\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{/O}}{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ - }}}}}{\\text{3C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{OH}}$<br>Hydroboration-oxidation of alkenes leads to hydration according to anti Markownikov\'s rule.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27518,'chemistry',68,1113,2659,'Consider the following reaction: The product (A) is:','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Reduction of ester group is not affected by weak reducing agent $$\\mathrm{NaBH}_{4}$$ <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_27518_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_27518_question_1.jpg'),
(27519,'chemistry',65,954,2215,'EDTA ${\\mathrm{^{4-}}}$ forms very stable complexes with most of the transition metals. In an octahedral ${\\mathrm{[\\mathrm{M}(\\text { EDTA })]^{2-}}}$ complex where M is in +2 oxidation state, the number of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{M}-\\mathrm{O}}}$ bonds is/are ____ .','[{"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The donor atoms in EDTA ${\\mathrm{{ }^{4-}}}$ are 2 N -atoms and 4 negatively charged O -atoms. When <br>EDTA ${\\mathrm{{ }^{4-}}}$ ion bonds to a metal ion ${\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{M}^{n+}\\right)}}$, it forms six bonds (i.e., ${\\mathrm{2 \\,\\mathrm{M}-\\mathrm{N}}}$ bonds and ${\\mathrm{4\\, \\mathrm{M}-\\mathrm{O}}}$ bonds).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27520,'chemistry',67,1073,2559,'2-Phenylethanol may be prepared by the reaction of phenyl magnesium bromide with','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{HCHO}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CHO}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{COCH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'2-Phenylethanol, $$\\mathrm{HOC}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\stackrel{2}{\\mathrm{C}} \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5}$$, is a $$1^{\\circ}$$ alcohol which can be prepared from $$\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{MgBr}$$ by treating with ethylene oxide (note that $$\\mathrm{HCHO}$$ will introduce only one carbon atom, i.e., it will give $$\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{OH}$$ and not $$\\left.\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{OH}\\right)$$. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_27520_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  ${{\\text{C}}_6}{{\\text{H}}_5}{\\text{MgBr}} + {\\text{HCHO}} \\to {{\\text{C}}_6}{{\\text{H}}_5}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_2}{\\text{OH}}.$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27521,'chemistry',68,1113,2670,'A compound (X) of molecular formula $$\\mathrm{C}_{3} \\mathrm{H}_{6} \\mathrm{O}$$ forms bisulphate complex, gives iodoform test but does not reduce Tollen\'s reagent. (X) on reaction with $$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{MgBr} / \\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{O}^{+}$$gives a compound (Y) that cannot','[{"text": "Give red with CAN", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Give white turbidity immediately with Lucas reagent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Give iodoform test", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Be dehydrated to alkene on reaction with heated $$\\\\mathrm{Cu}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In given condition ${\\rm{X}}\\left( {{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{3}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{O}}} \\right)$ should be methyl ketone. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_27521_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_27521_explanation_2.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27523,'chemistry',67,1073,2559,'To prepare 3-ethylpentan-3-ol, the reagents needed are','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{MgBr}+\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{COCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{MgBr}+\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{COCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{MgBr}+\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{COCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{MgBr}+\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{COCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{MgBr  +  C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{COC}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}} \\to $   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_27523_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
