(27536,'chemistry',68,1113,2670,'A compound (A), $$\\mathrm{C}_{4} \\mathrm{H}_{8} \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$$, on hydrolysis gives a product (B) which forms a 2, 4-DNP derivative but does not reduce Tollens reagent. The compound (A) has the structure','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CHClCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Cl}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CCl}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CHCl}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{ClCH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Cl}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ketone group forms 2, 4, DNP derivative but does not reduce Tollen\'s reagent. Hence ${\\rm{A}}\\left( {{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{4}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{8}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{2}}}} \\right)$ must be non-terminal geminal di chloride. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_27536_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
