(27545,'chemistry',68,1113,2668,'Compound (A), $$\\mathrm{C}_{5} \\mathrm{H}_{10} \\mathrm{O}$$, forms a<br>phenylhydrazone and gives negative Tollen\'s and iodoform tests. Compound (A) on reduction gives n-pentane. Compound (A) would be','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CHO}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{COCH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{COCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{OH}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'(A) forms 2, 4-DNP derivative. Therefore, it is an aldehyde or a ketone. Since it does not reduce Tollens\' reagent, (A) must be a ketone. (A) does not responds to iodoform test. Therefore, it does not contain a methyl keto group $$\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CO}^{-}\\right)$$. On reduction gives n-pentane, it is straight chain compound. So, the compound is $$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{COCH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{3}$$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
