(27552,'chemistry',67,1070,2551,'Identify the correct IUPAC name of the compound given below.','[{"text": "2-Chloro-5-hydroxyhexane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2-Hydroxy-5-chlorohexane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5-Chlorohexan-2-ol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2-Chlorohexan-5-ol", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\begin{gathered}\n  {\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CH(Cl)C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{CH(OH)C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}} \\hfill \\\\\n  \\,\\,\\,\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {\\text{6}}&{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{5}}}&{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{4}}}&{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{3}}}&{\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{2}}}&{\\,\\,{\\text{1}}} \n\\end{array} \\hfill \\\\ \n\\end{gathered} $<br>$$-\\mathrm{OH}$$ group is higher prior than -Cl group, so it gets lowest possible number.<br>Name of the compound is 5-chlorohexan-2-ol<br>',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/67_27552_question_1.png'),
