(27606,'chemistry',67,1083,2591,'Which of the following is the strongest acid?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Due to greater electron-withdrawing effect of $$\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$$, and also due to additional resonance due to $$-\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$$ group in the phenoxide ion, nitrophenols are stronger acids than chlorophenol. Further since resonance in p-nitrophenoxide ion is more important than that in m-nitrophenoxide ion, former is more stable, hence $$\\mathrm{p}$$-nitrophenol is more acidic than $$\\mathrm{m}$$ -nitrophenol. o-Nitrophenol is less acidic than $$\\mathrm{p}$$- nitrophenol because of intramolecular $$\\mathrm{H}$$ bonding.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
