(27675,'chemistry',68,1113,2670,'An organic compound (A) does not react with sodium but reacts with $$\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}$$. (A) also undergoes haloform reaction and gives 3-methylbut - 2-enoic acid on acidification of products. On hydrogenation (A) gives 2-methylpentane. The compound $$(\\mathrm{A})$$ is','[{"text": "$$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}=\\\\mathrm{CHCOCH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}=\\\\mathrm{CHCOCH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}=\\\\mathrm{CHCOOH}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{3} \\\\mathrm{C}=\\\\mathrm{CHCOOH}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'(A) does not react with sodium but reacts with $$\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}$$, hence it should be a carbonyl compound. Also (A) undergoes haloform reaction, hence it must be a $$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CO}$$ - unit.<br>Reduction of (A) gives 2-methylpentane i.e.,<br>$$\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{CHCH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{3}$$.<br>During haloform reaction an acid salt is formed which yields on acidification:<br>$$\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{CHCOOH}$$<br>Based on the above data, structure of (A) will be $$\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{CHCOCH}_{3}$$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
