(27754,'chemistry',65,953,2212,'An octahedral complex with the formula ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CoCl}_{3} \\cdot \\mathrm{nNH}_{3}}}$ upon reaction with excess of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}}}$ solution gives 2 moles of AgCl .Consider the oxidation state of Co in the complex is x . The value of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{n}}}$ is ____.','[{"text": "8", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The given complex will have the structure ${\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{5} \\mathrm{Cl}\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}}}$ as it gives 2 moles of AgCl with ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}}}$. So, the value of \' ${\\mathrm{n}}$ \' is 5.<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore}}$ Oxidation state of cobalt is +3 , i.e., ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{x}=3}}$<br>$\\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{n}=8$<br>So, the correct option is (1).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
