(27816,'chemistry',69,1174,2810,'The IUPAC name of the amine produced by the Hoffman degradation of benzamide is','[{"text": "Phenol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Benzenamine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Benzene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "N - Phenyl formamide", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'N-ethyl phthalimide on hydrolysis forms ethylamine. It is called Gabriel phthalimide reaction. It is an important method of preparing primary amines. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_27816_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27817,'chemistry',68,1113,2656,'The order of reactivity of the following compounds with $$\\mathrm{PhMgBr}$$ is<br>(I) $$\\mathrm{PhCOPh}$$<br>(II) $$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CHO}$$<br>(III) $$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COCH}_{3}$$','[{"text": "(I) $$>$$ (II) $$>$$ (III)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(III) $$>$$ (I) $$>$$ (II)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(II) $$>$$ (I) $$>$$ (III)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(II) $$>$$ (III) $$>$$ (I)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Reaction of carbonyl compounds with $$\\mathrm{PhMgBr}$$ is based on electrophilicity of carbonyl group and steric crowding around it. Based on electrophilicity and crowding, $$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CHO}$$ is most reactive. The least reactive will be $$\\mathrm{PhCOPh}$$ due to excessive steric crowding.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27818,'chemistry',65,957,2228,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{PF}_{5}}}$ and ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{BrF}_{5}}}$ both exhibit ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\mathrm{~d}}}$ hybridisation.</div><div class="column-right">Both ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{SF}_{6}}}$ and ${\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{3+}}}$ exhibit ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\mathrm{~d}^{2}}}$ hybridisation.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Hybridisation of ${\\mathrm{P}}$ in ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{PF}_{5}}}$ is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{sp}^{3} d}}$ but the hybridisation of Br in ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{BrF}_{5}}}$ is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\mathrm{~d}^{2}}}$. Thus, statement A is incorrect.<br>Hybridisation of S in ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{SF}_{6}}}$ is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{sp}^{3} \\mathrm{~d}^{2}}}$ but the hybridisation of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Co}^{3+}}}$ in ${\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{3+}}}$ is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{d}^{2} \\mathrm{sp}^{3}}}$ as ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NH}_{3}}}$ is a strong field ligand So, statement ${\\mathrm{B}}$ is also incorrect. So, the correct option is (4).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
