(27820,'chemistry',69,1174,2811,'Formaldoxime on reaction with $\\mathrm{Na} / \\mathrm{EtOH}$ gives','[{"text": "$1^{\\\\circ}$ Amine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$2^{\\\\circ}$ Amine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3^{\\\\circ}$ Amine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Formaldoxime on reaction with $\\mathrm{Na} / \\mathrm{EtOH}$ gives $1^{\\circ}$ amine. The reaction is representated as follows :<br>$\\begin{gathered}{\\text{H - CH = N - OH}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{4H}}}]{{{\\text{Na/EtOH}}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ + }}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}} \\hfill \\\\{\\text{formaldoxime}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{methyl}}\\,\\,{\\text{amine}} \\hfill \\\\ \\end{gathered} $<br>formaldoxime methyl amine<br>This method is used for the preparation of primary amines.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27821,'chemistry',68,1113,2656,'Which factors will increase the reactivity of $$>\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{O}$$ group?<br>(i) Presence of a group with positive inductive effect<br>(ii) Presence of a group with negative inductive effect<br>(iii) Presence of large alkyl group','[{"text": "Only (i)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only (ii)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (i) & (iii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (ii) & (iii)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Reactivity of carbonyl compounds can be increased by increase in number of -I effect groups.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(27822,'chemistry',65,958,2233,'Match Column I with Column II<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{R,B}} - {\\\\rm{P,C}} - {\\\\rm{S,D}} - {\\\\rm{Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{S,B}} - {\\\\rm{R,C}} - {\\\\rm{P,D}} - {\\\\rm{Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{P,B}} - {\\\\rm{R,C}} - {\\\\rm{S,D}} - {\\\\rm{Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{R,B}} - {\\\\rm{S,C}} - {\\\\rm{Q,D}} - {\\\\rm{P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'(A) Ti in ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{TiCl}_{4}}}$ is in +4 oxidation state having ${\\mathrm{3 \\mathrm{~d}^{0}}}$ or ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{e}^{0} \\mathrm{t}_{2}^{0}}}$ configuration (R).<br>(B) Fe in ${\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{FeO}_{4}\\right]^{2-}}}$ is in +6 oxidation state having ${\\mathrm{3 \\mathrm{~d}^{2}}}$ or ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{e}^{2} \\mathrm{t}_{2}^{0}}}$ configuration ${\\mathrm{(\\mathrm{P})}}$.<br>(C) Fe in ${\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{FeCl}_{4}\\right]^{-}}}$is in +3 oxidation state having ${\\mathrm{3 \\mathrm{~d}^{5}}}$ or ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{e}^{2} \\mathrm{t}_{2}^{3}}}$ configuration ${\\mathrm{(\\mathrm{S})}}$.<br>(D) Co in ${\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{CoCl}_{4}\\right]^{2-}}}$ is in +2 oxidation state having ${\\mathrm{3 \\mathrm{~d}^{7}}}$ or ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{e}^{4} \\mathrm{t}_{2}^{3}}}$ configuration ${\\mathrm{(\\mathrm{Q})}}$.<br>So, the correct option is (1).',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/65_27822_question_1.png'),
