(27829,'chemistry',68,1112,2653,'Arrange the following compounds in the increasing order of their boiling points.<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{CHO(I)}}}&{{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{OH}}\\,\\,{\\rm{(II)}}}\\\\{{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{5}}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{5}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{(III)}}}&{{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{(IV)}}}\\end{array}$','[{"text": "IV $$ < $$ I $$ < $$ II $$ < $$ III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV $$ < $$ III $$ < $$ II $$ < $$ I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV $$ < $$ III $$ < $$ I $$ < $$ II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV $$ < $$ II $$ < $$ III $$ < $$ I", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The boiling point of butan-1-ol would be highest, due to extensive intermolecular hydrogen bonding. Butanal is more polar than ethoxyethane. The intermolecular dipole-dipole attraction is stronger in the butanal. n-pentane molecules have only weak van der Waal\'s forces. The increasing order of boiling point of the given compounds are IV $$ < $$ III $$ < $$ I $$ < $$ II.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
