(27831,'chemistry',67,1083,2591,'Which one of the following properties is exhibited by phenol?','[{"text": "It is soluble in aq. $$\\\\mathrm{NaOH}$$ and evolves $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ with aq. $$\\\\mathrm{NaHCO}_{3}$$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is soluble in aq. $$\\\\mathrm{NaOH}$$ and does not evolve $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ with aq. $$\\\\mathrm{NaHCO}_{3}$$.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is not soluble in aq. $$\\\\mathrm{NaOH}$$ but evolves $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ with aq. $$\\\\mathrm{NaHCO}_{3}$$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is insoluble in aq. $$\\\\mathrm{NaOH}$$ and does not evolve $$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ with aq. $$\\\\mathrm{NaHCO}_{3}$$.<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Phenol is soluble in aq. $$\\mathrm{NaOH}$$ forming sodium phenoxide.<br>$$\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{OH}+\\mathrm{NaOH} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{ONa}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$$<br>But phenol does not evolve $$\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$$ with aq. $$\\mathrm{NaHCO}_{3}$$ and aq.  $$\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{CO}_{3}$$ because phenol is weaker acid than carbonic acid.<br>',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
