(27851,'chemistry',65,957,2229,'Consider the following complex ions<br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n{\\rm{         P}} = {\\left[ {{\\rm{Fe}}{{\\rm{F}}_6}} \\right]^{3 - }}\\\\\n{\\rm{         Q}} = {\\left[ {{\\rm{V}}{{\\left( {{{\\rm{H}}_2}{\\rm{O}}} \\right)}_6}} \\right]^{2 + }}\\\\\n{\\rm{         R}} = {\\left[ {{\\rm{Fe}}{{\\left( {{{\\rm{H}}_2}{\\rm{O}}} \\right)}_6}} \\right]^{2 + }}\n\\end{array}$<br>The correct order of the complex ions, according to their spin only magnetic moment values (in B.M.) is','[{"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{R} < \\\\mathrm{P} < \\\\mathrm{Q}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{R} < \\\\mathrm{Q} < \\\\mathrm{P}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Q ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ P ${\\\\mathrm{ < \\\\mathrm{R}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Q} < \\\\mathrm{R} < \\\\mathrm{P}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{P}=\\left[\\mathrm{FeF}_{6}\\right]^{3-}: \\mathrm{Fe}}}$ is in +3 oxidation state ${\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{d}^{5}\\right)}}$ forms outer orbital complex, so it has 5 unpaired electrons.<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Q}=\\left[\\mathrm{V}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{2+}: \\mathrm{V}}}$ is in +2 oxidation state${\\mathrm{\\left(d^{3}\\right)}}$ and form inner orbital complex, so it has 3 unpaired electrons.<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{R}=\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)_{6}\\right]^{2+}: \\mathrm{Fe}}}$ is in +2 oxidation state ${\\mathrm{\\left(d^{6}\\right)}}$ and forms outer orbital complex, so it has 4 unpaired electrons.<br>Spin only magnetic moment ${\\mathrm{\\propto}}$ no. of unpaired electrons. Hence, the correct order of spin only magnetic moment is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Q} < \\mathrm{R} < \\mathrm{P}}}$. So, the correct option is (4).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
