(27856,'chemistry',65,957,2230,'The correct statements from following are<br>(I) The strength of anionic ligands can be explained by crystal field theory.<br>(II) Valence bond theory does not give a quantitative interpretation of kinetic stability of coordination compounds.<br>(III) The hybridisation involved in formation of ${\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{CN})_{4}\\right]^{2-}}}$ complex is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{dsp}^{2}}}$.<br>(IV) The number of possible isomer(s) of ${\\mathrm{\\operatorname{cis}\\left[\\mathrm{PtCl}_{2}(\\mathrm{en})_{2}\\right]^{2+}}}$ is one.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below','[{"text": "(I), (IV)only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(II), (III) only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(II), (IV)only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I), (III) only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The statements II and III are correct. The correct statements of I and IV are given below: <br>The strength of anionic ligands is not explained by crystal field theory. It is explained by ligand field theory.<br>cis- ${\\mathrm{\\left[\\mathrm{PtCl}_{2}(\\mathrm{en})_{2}\\right]^{2+}}}$ shows optical activity. So exists in two forms ${\\mathrm{(d, 1)}}$.So, the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
