(27886,'chemistry',65,962,2242,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Dimethyl glyoxime forms a sixmembered covalent chelate when treated with ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NiCl}_{2}}}$ solution in presence of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{OH}}}$.</div><div class="column-right">Prussian blue precipitate contains iron both in ${\\mathrm{(+2)}}$ and ${\\mathrm{(+3)}}$ oxidation states.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/65_27886_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  The covalent bonded rings are five membered, so the chelate formed is five membered, but not of six membered.<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Fe}^{3+}}}$ ions are tested by adding potassium ferrocyanide solution to the salt solution when ferriferrocyanide or prussian blue complex is formed.  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/65_27886_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  So, the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
