(28032,'chemistry',69,1174,2810,'For the elimination of group of amide following reaction is used','[{"text": "Hoffmann hypobromite reaction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Kolbe reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hunsdiecker reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liebermann\'s reaction", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'For the formation of $\\mathrm{RNH}_{2}$ from $\\mathrm{RCONH}_{2}, \\mathrm{NaOH}$ and $\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$ are used as reagent. It is called Hofmann hypobromite reaction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/69_28032_question_1.jpg'),
(28022,'chemistry',67,1076,2569,'Arrange the following compounds in increasing order of boiling point. Propan-1-ol, butan-1-ol, butan-2-ol, pentan-1-ol','[{"text": "Propan-1-ol, butan-2-ol, butan-1-ol, pentan- 1-ol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Propan-1-ol, butan-1-ol, butan-2-ol, pentan- 1-ol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pentan-1-ol, butan-1-ol, propan-1-ol, butan- 2-ol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Propan-1-ol, butan-1-ol, pentan-2-ol, butan- $$1-\\\\mathrm{ol}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Boiling point increases with increase in the number of carbon atoms because of increase in molecular mass. So, the boiling point of pentan-1-ol is more than that of all boiling points than $$2^{\\circ}$$ alcohols because of higher surface area in $$1^{\\circ}$$ alcohols. Therefore, boiling point increase in the order<br>Propan-1-ol $$ < $$ butan-2-ol $$ < $$ butan-1-ol $$ < $$ pentan1-ol',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(28023,'chemistry',69,1176,2819,'Bond order of gas evolved out when $\\left[\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{NH}_{2}+\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{CHNH}_{2}\\right]$ is treated with sodium nitrite and $\\mathrm{HCl}$ is','[{"text": "2.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Primary amine and $\\mathrm{HNO}_{2}$ produces nitrogen gas.<br>$\\mathrm{RNH}_{2}+\\mathrm{HNO}_{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{ROH}+\\mathrm{N}_{2}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$<br>$\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ bond order is 3',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
