(28037,'chemistry',67,1089,2613,'Which one of the following statements is not correct ?','[{"text": "The bond angle in methanol as shown in figure &nbsp;is<br>$108.9^{\\\\circ}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acid strength of alcohols decreases in the following<br>order: $1^\\\\circ {\\\\text{ }} &gt; {\\\\text{ }}2^\\\\circ {\\\\text{ }} &gt; {\\\\text{ }}3^\\\\circ $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alcohols are weaker acids than water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbon - oxygen bond length in methanol,<br>$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{OH}$ is shorter than of $\\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{O}$ bond length<br>in phenol", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The carbon&ndash; oxygen bond length (136 pm) in phenol is slightly less than that in<br>methanol (142pm). This is due to<br>(i) partial double bond character on account of the conjugation of unshared electron pair of<br>oxygen with the aromatic ring.<br>(ii) sp2 hybridised state of carbon to which oxygen is attached. &nbsp; <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_28037_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> &nbsp;<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_28037_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
