(28076,'chemistry',69,1174,2812,'An alkyl amine is prepared by the following reaction<br>$\\mathrm{RCOOH}+\\mathrm{N}_{3} \\mathrm{H} \\stackrel{\\text { Conc. } \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4}}{\\longrightarrow} \\mathrm{RNH}_{2}+\\mathrm{CO}_{2}+\\mathrm{N}_{2}$<br>Name of the above reaction is :','[{"text": "Schmidt reaction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stephan\'s reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Schotton-Baumann reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reimer- Tiemann reaction", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The given reaction is represented as $\\underset{\\text { alkanoic acid }}{\\mathrm{RCOOH}}+\\underset{\\text { hydrazoic acid }}{\\mathrm{N}_{3} \\mathrm{H}} \\stackrel{\\text { Conc. } \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4}}{\\longrightarrow} \\underset{\\text { alkyl amine }}{\\mathrm{RNH}_{2}}+\\mathrm{CO}_{2}+\\mathrm{N}_{2}$<br>The above reaction is known as Schmidt reaction. This is an important method of preparing primary amines.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
