(28110,'chemistry',69,1176,2822,'The acid used for the determination of molecular weights of amines is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{PtCl}_{6}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Picric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HAuCl}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{SO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The acid used is $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{PtCl}_{6}$. It is a solution of platinic chloride, $\\mathrm{PtCl}_{4}$ in con. $\\mathrm{HCl}$<br>${\\rm{2R - N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}\\left[ {{\\rm{PtC}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{6}}}} \\right] \\to \\mathop {{{\\left[ {{\\rm{R}}\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}} \\right]}_{\\rm{2}}}^{\\rm{ + }}{{\\left[ {{\\rm{PtC}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{6}}}} \\right]}^{{\\rm{ - 2}}}}}\\limits_{{\\rm{alkyl amine platinichloride}}} $<br>Chloroplatinates on ignition leave a residue of metallic Pt. This reaction is employed in determining molecular weight of amines.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
