(28116,'chemistry',67,1075,2566,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">ter - Butyl methyl ether is not prepared by the reaction of ter - butyl bromide with sodium methoxide.</div><div class="column-right">Sodium methoxide is a strong nucleophile.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement A is true because ter-butyl methylether is not typically prepared by the reaction of ter-butyl bromide with sodium methoxide. During the above reaction, isobutene is formed as a major product. Statement B is also true as sodium methoxide is indeed a strong nucleophile.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(28117,'chemistry',69,1176,2816,'Considering the basic strength of amines in aqueous solution, which one has the smallest $p K_{b}$ value?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{NH}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{3} \\\\mathrm{~N}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'It is known that, $p K_{b}=-\\log K_{b}$<br>Thus, larger the value of $K_{b}$ smaller is the value of $p K_{b}$, hence, stronger is the base.<br>The order of basic strength of amines is as follows:<br>${\\left( {{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}} \\right)_{\\rm{2}}}\\mathop {\\rm{N}}\\limits^{..} {\\rm{H > C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}\\mathop {\\rm{N}}\\limits^{..} {{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ > }}{\\left( {{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}} \\right)_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{\\,}}\\mathop {\\rm{N}}\\limits^{..} {\\rm{ > }}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{6}}}{{\\rm{\\ddot H}}_{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>The basic strength of amines depends on the inductive effect as well as steric hindrance of alkyl groups. Hence, ${\\left( {{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}} \\right)_{\\rm{2}}}\\mathop {\\rm{N}}\\limits^{..} {\\rm{H}}$ [secondary amine] possesses the smallest value of ${\\rm{p}}{{\\rm{K}}_{\\rm{b}}}{\\rm{.}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
