(28120,'chemistry',67,1077,2572,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In esterification reaction, $$\\mathrm{HCOOH}$$ is the most reactive acid among carboxylic acids.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Alcohol acts as nucleophile.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$$\\mathrm{HCOOH}$$ is the most reactive acid among the carboxylic acid. Alcohol acts as nucleophile.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(28121,'chemistry',69,1176,2817,'A compound with molecular mass $180 u$ is acylated with $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COCl}$ to get a compound with molecular mass $390 u$. The number of amino groups present per molecule of the former compound is','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During acetylation, one $H$ atom with atomic mass 1 amu of $-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ group is replaced by an acetyl group $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CO}$ [molecular mass $=434 u]$. Thus, $-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}+\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COCl} \\rightarrow-\\mathrm{NHCOCH}_{3}+\\mathrm{HCl}$<br>The above equation suggests that the acylation of each $-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ group increases the mass by $42 u[43-1]$. If the molecular mass of the organic compound is $180 u$, while that of the acylated product is $390 u$, then the increase in the mass due to acylation is given by<br>$390-180=210 u$<br>Hence, the number of $-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ groups $=\\dfrac{210 u}{42 u}=5$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
