(28130,'chemistry',68,1112,2654,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Lower aldehydes and ketones are soluble in water but the solubility decreases as the molecular mass increases.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Aldehydes and ketones are separated by Fehling\'s solution.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Lower aldehydes and ketones are soluble in water due to polar effect of $$>\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{O}$$ which makes hydrogen bonds with water molecules. As the size of the aldehydes and ketones increases the hydrophobic part, i.e., alkyl chain increases which weakens the $$\\mathrm{H}-$$ bond formations with $$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$$ molecules and decreases the solubility.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
