(28147,'chemistry',68,1113,2657,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The reaction of aldehydes and ketones with pure $$\\mathrm{HCN}$$ is very slow to yield cyanohydrin.<br></div><div class="column-right">The above reaction is catalysed by a base and generated cyanide ion being a weaker nucleophile adds to carbonyl compounds to yield, corresponding cyanohydrin.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Aldehydes and ketones react with hydrogen cyanide to yield cyanohydrins. This reaction occurs very slowly with pure $$\\mathrm{HCN}$$.<br>Therefore, it is catalysed by a base and the generated cyanide ion $$\\left(\\mathrm{CN}^{-}\\right)$$being a stronger nucleophile readily adds to carbonyl compounds to yield corresponding cyanohydrin.<br>${\\rm{HCN + O}}{{\\rm{H}}^{\\rm{ - }}} \\to \\overline {\\rm{C}} {\\rm{N + }}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}$ <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_28147_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
