(28155,'chemistry',68,1109,2643,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The carbonyl carbon is a nucleophilic and carbonyl oxygen is an electrophilic centre.<br></div><div class="column-right">The carbon-oxygen double bond is polarised due to higher electronegativity of oxygen relative to carbon.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The carbon-oxygen double bond is polarised due to higher electronegativity of oxygen relative to carbon. The carbonyl carbon is an electrophilic (Lewis acid) and the carbonyl oxygen is a nucleophilic (Lewis base) centre. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_28155_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
