(28170,'chemistry',68,1118,2678,'The following steps are given for the mechanism of esterification of carboxylic acids.<br>I. The protonated esters looses a proton to give the ester.<br>II. Protonation of the carbonyl oxygen activates the carbonyl group towards nucleophilic addition of the alcohol.<br>III. Proton transfer in the tetrahedral intermediate occurs.<br>Arrange the following steps in their correct sequence.','[{"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III and I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, II and I", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Protonation of the carboxyl oxygen activates the carbonyl group toward nucleophilic addition of the alcohol. Proton transfer in the tetrahedral intermediate converts the hydroxyl group into $$-\\mathrm{OH}_{2}$$ group which being a better leaving group, is eliminated as neutral water molecule. The protonated ester so formed finally loses a proton to give the ester. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_28170_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
