(28199,'chemistry',67,1083,2591,'Given below are two statements:<br>Statement I:<br>The acidic strength of monosubstituted nitrophenol is higher than phenol because of electron withdrawing nitro group.<br>Statement II:<br>o-nitrophenol, m-nitrophenol and p-nitrophenol will have same acidic strength as they have one nitro group attached to the phenolic ring.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Acidic strength of phenolic group increases due to electron withdrawing groups. Order of acidic strength:   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_28199_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
