(28203,'chemistry',67,1078,2579,'Given below are two statements :<br>Statement I :<br>In Lucas test, primary, secondary and tertiary alcohols are distinguished on the basis of their reactivity with conc. $$\\mathrm{HCl}+\\mathrm{ZnCl}_{2}$$, known as Lucas Reagent.<br>Statement II:<br>Primary alcohols are most reactive and immediately produce turbidity at room temperature on reaction with Lucas Reagent.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$$1^{\\circ}, 2^{\\circ}, 3^{\\circ}$$ alcohols are distinguished by Lucas test on the basis of the time taken for turbidity to appear${\\text{R - C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ - OH}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{Conc}}{\\text{.HCl + Anhy}}{\\text{.ZnC}}{{\\text{l}}_{\\text{2}}}}}\\mathop {{\\text{R - C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ - Cl}}}\\limits_{\\left( {{\\text{Turbidity}}\\,\\,{\\text{in}}\\,\\,{\\text{30min}}{\\text{.}}} \\right)} $  $1^\\circ {\\text{Alcohol}}$     <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_28203_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_28203_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Reactivity of alcohol towards Lucas reagent $$\\Rightarrow 3^{\\circ}>2^{\\circ}>1^{\\circ}$$ Alcohol<br>',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
