(28252,'chemistry',67,1077,2577,'Match the following alcohols given in column I with the product formed during their reaction with $$\\mathrm{Cu} / 573 \\mathrm{~K}$$ in column II and choose the correct option from the codes given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A  $$1^{\\circ}$$ alcohol <br>B  $$2^{\\circ}$$ alcohol <br>C   $$3^{\\circ}$$ alcohol</div><div class="column-right">P   Ketone<br>Q   Alkene<br>R   Aldehyde</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  R,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B  -  P,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B  -  P,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B  -  R,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  R,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B  -  Q,}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_28252_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(28253,'chemistry',69,1174,2810,'An organic compound $\\mathrm{A}$ on reacting with $\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ gives $\\mathrm{B}$. On heating $\\mathrm{B}$, it gives $\\mathrm{C}$. $\\mathrm{C}$ in the presence of $\\mathrm{KOH}$ reacts with $\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$ to give $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{NH}_{2}$. A is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{COOH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{COOH}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{COOH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{A} \\stackrel{\\mathrm{NH}_{3}}{\\longrightarrow} \\mathrm{B} \\stackrel{\\Delta}{\\longrightarrow} \\mathrm{C} \\stackrel{\\mathrm{KOH} / \\mathrm{Br}}{\\longrightarrow} \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{NH}_{2}$<br>The reaction of $\\mathrm{C}$ with $\\mathrm{KOH} / \\mathrm{Br}_{2}$ to give amine is called Hoffmann bromamide reaction. this reaction is given by acid amides only in which <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_28253_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> group undergoes rearrangement along with the loss of $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ molecule. Thus, the<br>compound $\\mathrm{C}$ must be acid amide with three carbon atoms. Hence, the compound $\\mathrm{C}$ is <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_28253_explanation_2.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Since, all the options show that $\\mathrm{A}$ is an acid and it forms acid amide on reaction with $\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$. Thus, acid must contain three carbon atoms. Hence the compound $\\mathrm{A}$ is $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{COOH}$. The complete series of reactions can be represented as<br>$\\mathop {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{COOH}}}\\limits_{\\left( {\\text{A}} \\right)} \\xrightarrow{{{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}}}\\mathop {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{CO}}{{\\text{O}}^{\\text{ - }}}\\mathop {\\text{N}}\\limits^{\\text{ + }} {{\\text{H}}_{\\text{4}}}}\\limits_{\\left( {\\text{B}} \\right)} $ <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_28253_explanation_3.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
