(28327,'chemistry',68,1113,2668,'Silver mirror test is given by which one of the following compounds?','[{"text": "Benzophenone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Formaldehyde", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2-Butanone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acetone", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All aldehydes including reducing sugar (as glucose, fructose) gives silver mirror test (with Tollen\'s reagent)<br>${\\text{RCHO + 2}}{\\left[ {{\\text{Ag}}{{\\left( {{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)}_{\\text{2}}}} \\right]^{\\text{ + }}}{\\text{ + 3O}}{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ - }}}\\xrightarrow{{\\text{\\Delta }}}$<br>${\\text{RCO}}{{\\text{O}}^{\\text{ - }}}{\\text{ + }}\\mathop {{\\text{2Ag}}}\\limits_{{\\text{ Silver mirror }}}  \\downarrow {\\text{ + 4N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{ + 2}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}\\quad \\left( {{\\text{R = H,C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}} \\right)$<br>Thus, acetaldehyde and formaldehyde give silver mirror test.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
