(28334,'chemistry',68,1120,2687,'An organic compound has an empirical formula $$\\mathrm{C}_{5} \\mathrm{H}_{10} \\mathrm{O}$$. This liquid gives a pale yellow precipitate on warming with iodine in alkaline KI solution. The resulting salt upon acidification gives an acid which easily undergoes decarboxylaction on mild heating. The structural formula of the organic liquid could be','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{COCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}=\\\\mathrm{CHCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}(\\\\mathrm{OH}) \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CHO}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{OCH}=\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Given compound gives iodoform test, a characteristic of methyl ketones or secondary alcohol $$\\left(-\\mathrm{CH}(\\mathrm{OH}) \\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)$$. It may be option (1) or (2).<br>Acid undergoes decarboxylation by forming carbanion as an intermediate. Allylic carbanion is more stable.<br>$$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{CHCH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}(\\mathrm{OH}) \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{CHCH}_{2} \\mathrm{COOH}$$<br>$$\\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{CHCH}_{3}$$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
