(28356,'chemistry',67,1077,2577,'An oxygen containing organic compound upon oxidation forms a carboxylic acid as the only organic product with its molecular mass higher by 14 units. The organic compound is','[{"text": "an aldehyde", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a primary alcohol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a secondary alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a ketone", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The difference in mass between<br>$$-\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{OH}$$ group and - $$\\mathrm{COOH}$$ group is 14 . Thus the compound which undergoes oxidation is a primary alcohol.<br>$\\begin{gathered}\n  {\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{OH}}\\xrightarrow{{[{\\text{O}}]}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{COOH}} \\hfill \\\\\n  \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{46g}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{60g}} \\hfill \\\\ \n\\end{gathered} $',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2010,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
