(28476,'chemistry',69,1176,2819,'Given below are two statements.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Primary aliphatic amines react with $\\mathrm{HNO}_{2}$ to give unstable diazonium salts.</div><div class="column-right">Primary aromatic amines react with $\\mathrm{HNO}_{2}$ to form diazonium salts which are stable even above $300 \\mathrm{~K}$.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</div></div>','[{"text": "Both Statement-A and Statement-B are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement-A and Statement-B are correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{R}-\\mathrm{NH}_{2} \\stackrel{\\mathrm{HNO}_{2}}{\\longrightarrow} \\mathrm{R}-\\mathrm{N}_{2}^{\\Theta}$<br>Alkyl diazoniumion (unstable) <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_28476_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
