(28479,'chemistry',67,1077,2578,'${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{  -  CHO}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{(ii)}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}}]{{{\\text{(i)C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{MgBr}}}}{\\text{(A)}}\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}},\\Delta }}{\\text{(B)}}$<br> $\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{ Hydroboration oxidation }}}}{\\text{(C)}}$<br>In the above  reaction (A) and (C) are','[{"text": "Identical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Positional isomers", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Functional isomers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Optical isomers", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_28479_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Hence \' $\\mathrm{A}$ \' and \' $\\mathrm{C}$ \' are positional isomers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2017,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
