(28490,'chemistry',69,1174,2810,'Which of the following would undergo Hoffmann reaction to give a primary amine?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{RCONHCH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{RCONH}_{2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{RCOOR}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When a primary amide is heated with an aqueous solution of $\\mathrm{KOH}$ and $\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$, it gives a primary amine with one carbon atom less.<br>$\\begin{aligned}& \\underset{\\text { amide }}{\\mathrm{RCONH}_{2}}+\\mathrm{Br}_{2}+4 \\mathrm{KOH} \\stackrel{\\Delta}{\\longrightarrow} \\\\& \\underset{1^{\\circ} \\text { amine }}{\\mathrm{RNH}_{2}}+2 \\mathrm{KBr}+\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{CO}_{3}+2 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\end{aligned}$<br>This is known as Hoffmann degradation reaction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2006,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
