(28505,'chemistry',67,1076,2569,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Alcohols have higher boiling points than ethers of comparable molecular masses.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Alcohols and ethers are isomeric in nature','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Alcohols have higher boiling points than ethers because intermolecular $\\mathrm{H}$ - bonding is present in alcohols and not in ethers. Further, alcohols are isomeric with ethers but it is not the correct reason for assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2007,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
