(28508,'chemistry',68,1113,2657,'Observe the following compounds<br>The correct reactivity order of below compounds towards nucleophilic addition reaction is','[{"text": "III $$>$$ I $$>$$ II $$>$$ IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II $$>$$ IV $$>$$ I $$>$$ III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III $$>$$ II $$>$$ IV $$>$$ I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV $$>$$ II $$>$$ I $$>$$ III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Reactivity $$\\propto$$ Amount of positive charge at carbonyl carbon or ${\\rm{ - I}}\\, \\cdot \\,\\,{\\rm{Effect}}\\,\\,{\\rm{or}}\\,\\,{\\rm{ - R}} \\cdot \\,\\,{\\rm{Effect}}{\\rm{.}}$<br>Aldehydes are more reactive than ketones.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_28508_question_1.png'),
(28509,'chemistry',67,1075,2566,'In which of the following reactions, the product obtained is tert - butyl methyl ether?','[{"text": "${\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{3}}}{\\\\text{OH +  HO  -  C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{ -  C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{3}}}\\\\xrightarrow{{{\\\\text{ Conc}}{\\\\text{. }}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{S}}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{4}}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'tert - butyl methyl ether is a mixed ether and for the preparation of mixed ethers in high yield, the essential condition is the use of primary alkyl halide. Thus, <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_28509_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  This reaction is Williamson\'s ether synthesis. $3^{\\circ}$ alkyl halides undergo elimination to form alkenes under the same conditions.<br>',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2008,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(28510,'chemistry',69,1176,2823,'Match the column I (reaction condition) with column II (nature of amine) and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Gabriel phthalimide reaction<br>B. Reduction with ${\\rm{LiAl}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{4}}}$<br>C. Reduction of nitrobenzene with ${\\rm{Sn + HCl}}$<br>D. ${{\\rm{1}}^{\\rm{o}}}$ Amide with ${\\rm{B}}{{\\rm{r}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ + KOH}}$</div><div class="column-right">P. Used for ascent amine series preparation<br>Q. ${{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{6}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$<br>R. One carbon less amine than the reactant<br>S. ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}$</div></div>','[{"text": "A - S, B - P, C - Q, D - R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - S, B - P, C - R, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S, B - R, C - Q, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - P, C - R, D - S", "isCorrect": false}]',0,NULL,NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(28511,'chemistry',68,1113,2670,'A compound $$[\\mathrm{A}]$$ has the molecular formula $$\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}_{3} \\mathrm{OH}$$. It reduces Fehling\'s solution and on oxidation gives a monocarboxylic acid [B]. [A] is obtained by the action of $$\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}$$ on ethyl alcohol. [A] is','[{"text": "Chloral", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chloroform", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloromethane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroacetic acid", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Compound [A] must be an aldehyde. ${{\\text{C}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}}{\\text{OH}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{C}}{{\\text{l}}_{\\text{2}}}}}{\\text{CC}}{{\\text{l}}_{\\text{3}}} \\cdot {\\text{CHO}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{[IO]}}}}{\\text{CC}}{{\\text{l}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{COOH}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
