(28516,'chemistry',67,1070,2553,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> IUPAC name of the compound https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764954906/preptracker/questions/q_28516_col1_1764954905656.png<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In IUPAC nomenclature, ether is regarded as hydrocarbon derivative in whcih a hydrogen atom is replaced by $-\\mathrm{OR}$ or $-\\mathrm{OAr}$ group [where, $\\mathrm{R}=$ alkyl group and $\\mathrm{Ar}=$ aryl group].','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'IUPAC name of the given compound is correct, i.e. 1-(2-Propoxy) propane. In this compound, hydrogen atom is replaced by $-\\mathrm{OR}$ group and thus named ether. Therefore, both Assertion and Reason is correct and reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2018,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
