(28521,'chemistry',69,1176,2816,'The basicity of aniline is less than that of cyclohexylamine. This is due to','[{"text": "$+\\\\mathrm{R}$ effect of $-\\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ group", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "-I effect of $-\\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ group", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$-\\\\mathrm{R}$ effect of $-\\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ group", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "hyperconjugation effect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ has a $+\\mathrm{R}$ effect, it donates electrons to the benzene ring. As a result of resonance, the lone pair of electrons on the $\\mathrm{N}$ atom gets delocalized over the benzene ring and thus it is less readily available for protonation. Hence aniline is a weaker base than cyclohexyl amine. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_28521_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2006,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(28523,'chemistry',68,1113,2663,'Predict the product (s) formed in the following reaction.','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$$\\mathrm{OH}^{-}$$ can attack any of the three $$-\\mathrm{CHO}$$ groups, but nucleophilic addition $${ }^{-} \\mathrm{OH}$$ ion occurs on that $$-\\mathrm{CHO}$$ group which is located at parapositions w.r.t to the other. The $$\\mathrm{p}-\\mathrm{CHO}$$ group is oxidised while the $$\\mathrm{m}-\\mathrm{CHO}$$ group is reduced. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_28523_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_28523_question_1.png'),
(28524,'chemistry',67,1083,2593,'Identify the compound obtained in following reaction?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ar}-\\\\mathrm{Cl}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ar}-\\\\mathrm{O}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\text{Phenol + acidchloride}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{ pyridine }}}}{\\text{ester}}$  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_28524_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/67_28524_question_1.png'),
(28525,'chemistry',69,1176,2816,'The correct order of increasing basic nature for the bases $\\mathrm{NH}_{3}, \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ and $\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{NH}$ in aqueous solutions is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2} < \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3} < \\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{NH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2} < \\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{NH} < \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{NH} < \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3} < \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3} < \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2} < \\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{NH}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Due to $+\\mathrm{I}$ effect of methyl group $2^{0}$ amine are more basic than $1^{0}$ amine.<br>Hence, order of basicity of methyl amine in aqeuous solution is : $\\mathrm{NH}_{3} < \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{NH}_{2} < \\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{NH}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
