(28568,'chemistry',69,1174,2812,'Alkyl cyanides on reduction by sodium and ethanol give primary amines. This reaction is called as','[{"text": "Hell-Vohlard-Zelinsky reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Clemmensen reduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wolff-Kishner reduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mendius reduction", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\text{R - }}\\mathop {{\\text{C}} \\equiv {\\text{N + 4}}}\\limits_{{\\text{Alkyl cyanide}}} \\left[ {\\text{H}} \\right]\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{Na Ethanol}}}}{\\text{R - }}\\mathop {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{ - N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}}\\limits_{{\\text{Primary amine}}} $<br>Given, reaction is called Mendius reduction. In this reaction the reduction of cyano group $(-\\mathrm{C} \\equiv \\mathrm{N})$ takes place by nascent hydrogen in the presence of sodium and alcohol. Here nascent hydrogen breaks $\\mathrm{X}$ bond of cyano group.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
