(28609,'chemistry',68,1118,2683,'Which of the following reagents is used to distinguish phenol and benzoic acid?','[{"text": "aq. $\\\\mathrm{NaOH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tollen\'s reagent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Molisch reagent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neutral $\\\\mathrm{FeCl}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Neutral $\\mathrm{FeCl}_{3}$ is used to distinguish phenol and benzoic acid. It gives violet colour with phenol and buff - coloured precipitate with benzoic acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2017,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(28610,'chemistry',67,1069,2550,'Identify simple ether from the following.','[{"text": "Methoxymethane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Methoxyethane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-Propoxybenzene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anisole", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'If same alkyl or aryl groups are attached to the oxygen atom in ether then it is called simple or symmetrical ether.<br>${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_3} - {\\text{O}} - {\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_3} - {\\text{O}} - {{\\text{C}}_2}{{\\text{H}}_5}$<br>${\\text{Methoxymethane}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{Methoxyethane}}$<br>${\\text{(Simple ether)}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{(Mixed ether)}}$   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_28610_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2022,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
