(28614,'chemistry',68,1118,2677,'Consider the following acids :<br>(i) $\\mathrm{F}_{3} \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{COOH}$               (ii) $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOH}$<br>(iii) $\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{COOH}$              (iv) $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{COOH}$<br>Correct order of $\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{a}}$ values is','[{"text": "(i) $>$ (iii) $>$ (ii) $>$ (iv)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(iv) $>$ (ii) $>$ (iii) $>$ (i)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(iv) $>$ (iii) $>$ (ii) $>$ (i)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i) $>$ (ii) $>$ (iv) $>$ (iii)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Higher the $\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{a}}$ value or smaller the $\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{a}}$ value, weaker is the acid.<br>Acidic strength $\\alpha-$-I\'groups and<br>$\\alpha \\dfrac{1}{+ \\text { \'I\'groups }}$.<br>\' $-\\mathrm{F}$ \' is strong \' $-\\mathrm{I}$ \' group.<br>$-\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5}$ group is electron withdrawing group.<br>$-\\mathrm{CH}_{3},-\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5}$ are \'+I\' groups<br>So, order of acidic nature is (i) $>$ (iii) $>$ (ii) $>$ (iv).<br>Hence, correct order of $\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{a}}$ values is<br>(iv) $>$ (ii) $>$ (iii) $>$ (i).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
