(28683,'chemistry',69,1176,2816,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Anilinium chloride is more acidic than ammonium chloride.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Anilinium ion is resonance stabilised.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and  Reason are  incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Anilinium chloride is more acidic than ammonium chloride because it forms salt with water and liberates amine when treated with strong base.<br>$\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{NH}_{3}^{+} \\mathrm{Cl}^{-}+\\mathrm{NaOH} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{NH}_{2}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}+\\mathrm{NaCl}$<br>Anilinium ion does not show resonance because charge dispersion at ring may involve pentavalent nitrogen structure.<br>Hence, Assertion  is correct and Reason is incorrect.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2006,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(28684,'chemistry',67,1077,2576,'Which of the following alcohols gives the best yield of dialkyl ether on being heated with a trace of sulphuric acid?','[{"text": "2-Pentanol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2-Methyl-2 butanol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1-Pentanol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2-Propanol", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Primary alcohols  i.e., 1-Pentanol  readily form ether when heated with conc. $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4} \\cdot 2^{\\circ}$ and $3^{\\circ}$ alcohols prefer to form alkenes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(28685,'chemistry',68,1111,2649,'Which of the following reagents is used in the reaction shown below?<br>Benzoyl chloride $\\stackrel{?}{\\longrightarrow}$ Benzaldehyde','[{"text": "DIBAl - H", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{SnCl}_{2} / \\\\mathrm{HCl}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} / \\\\mathrm{Pd}-\\\\mathrm{BaSO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dimethyl cadmium", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'It is Rosenmund reduction <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_28685_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
