(28689,'chemistry',68,1111,2649,'Identify the name of the following reaction.<br>Toluene + Chromyl chloride<br>$\\stackrel{\\mathrm{CS}_{2}}{\\longrightarrow}$ complex $\\stackrel{\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{O}^{+}}{\\longrightarrow}$ Benzaldehyde','[{"text": "Stephen reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rosenmund reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Etard reaction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Wolff - Kishner reaction", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'It is ETARD reaction. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_28689_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(28690,'chemistry',69,1176,2816,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Amines are more basic than esters and ethers.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Nitrogen is less electronegative than oxygen and it is in better position to accommodate the positive charge on the proton<br>','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and  Reason are  incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Amines are more basic than esters and ethers because the nitrogen atom is less electronegative than oxygen, thus, it is in better position to accommodate the positive charge on the proton. Hence, both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2007,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(28691,'chemistry',67,1075,2567,'In the reaction,<br>$2 \\mathrm{~A}+$ dry silver oxide $\\stackrel{\\Delta}{\\longrightarrow}$ ether $+2 \\mathrm{AgX}$.<br>A is an/a:','[{"text": "Primary alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alkyl halide", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alcohol", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'On heating an alkyl halide with dry silver oxide, ether is formed.<br>$2{\\text{R}} - \\mathop {\\text{X}}\\limits_{{\\text{ Alkyl halide }}}  + {\\text{A}}{{\\text{g}}_2}{\\text{O}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{ Dry }}}]{\\Delta }\\Delta  - {\\text{O}} - \\mathop {\\text{R}}\\limits_{{\\text{ Ether }}}  - 2{\\text{AgX}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
